window.PFC_RELEASES=[{"id":"2026080301","title":"Stephen Thomas Creates Unforgettable West Virginia Performance Celebrating Legacy, Community, and DJ Unk","date":"2026-08-03","lead":"Stephen Thomas delivered a high energy performance at the Woody Fest featuring DaBaby, Waka Flocka Flame, and the Ying Yang Twins.","hero":"images/2026080301/hero.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Stephen Thomas delivered a high energy performance at the Woody Fest featuring DaBaby, Waka Flocka Flame, and the Ying Yang Twins."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>CHARLESTON, WV</strong> (August 3, 2026) - Recording artist <strong><a href=\"https://linktr.ee/stephentmusic?utm_source=ig&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_content=link_in_bio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Stephen Thomas</a></strong> delivered a milestone performance in his home state of West Virginia, creating a night centered around gratitude, community, and legacy. After years of expanding his career across multiple genres and reaching audiences beyond state lines, Thomas returned to the stage in West Virginia with a vision to create more than just a concert... he wanted to create a moment."},{"t":"p","html":"For Thomas, the performance represented an opportunity to celebrate the people, businesses, and supporters who have continued to stand behind him while honoring the artists who helped inspire his journey. The evening became a reflection of his growth as an artist, his appreciation for his roots, and his commitment to using music to bring people together."},{"t":"p","html":"A major part of that vision included honoring the late multi-platinum recording artist <strong>DJ Unk</strong> known for HITS 2 Step and Walk It Out, who was not only an influence in music but also a close friend of Thomas. The tribute carried special meaning after the two had planned to collaborate on the “Outstanding” music video before DJ Unk’s passing. Through the performance, Thomas celebrated his friend’s legacy and reminded audiences of the importance of appreciating every opportunity, every relationship, and every moment."},{"t":"quote","html":"Life is too short not to live it to the fullest.","cite":"- Stephen Thomas"},{"t":"p","html":"Understanding that a memorable performance begins long before stepping on stage, Thomas and his team prioritized wellness and preparation. In partnership with <strong>Vital Flow</strong>, Stephen, his band, and production team received IV hydration therapy before the performance to ensure they were physically prepared to deliver their best."},{"t":"p","html":"The performance was also made possible through the support of several local partners who helped bring Thomas’ vision to life. <strong>Calvin Broyles Jewelers</strong> helped create a memorable fan experience by providing the opportunity for Thomas to present a gold rose during the event, while <strong>Young Floral</strong> donated a dozen roses that became part of the emotional connection between Thomas and the audience. Together with Vital Flow, these partnerships represented the community-driven spirit behind the event."},{"t":"p","html":"The tribute served as a heartfelt reminder that life is precious and that music has the power to unite, heal, and inspire."},{"t":"p","html":"The performance also highlighted Thomas’ remarkable versatility as he showcased seven different musical genres throughout the evening. Fans experienced selections from his latest EP, <strong><em>The Universal Me</em></strong>, alongside original songs including “<strong>Feening For Love</strong>,” “<strong>Breaking Hearts</strong>,” “<strong>Come Home To Me</strong>,” and “<strong>Life Equals Purpose (Peace. Love. Unity.)</strong>.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Adding to the unforgettable experience were performances of songs made popular by <strong>Machine Gun Kelly</strong>, <strong>The Kid LAROI</strong>, <strong>Zedd</strong>, <strong>Jimmie Allen</strong>, <strong>Kanye West</strong>, <strong>T-Pain</strong>, and <strong>Chris Brown</strong>, demonstrating Thomas’ ability to seamlessly move between genres while making each performance uniquely his own."},{"t":"p","html":"One of the evening’s most memorable moments came during “<strong>Feening For Love</strong>,” when Thomas invited a fan on stage and presented her with a gold rose just off the side of the stage."},{"t":"p","html":"More than just a concert, the event showcased Thomas’ commitment to excellence both on and off the stage. From prioritizing wellness with Vital Flow before the first note was played to delivering an emotionally charged tribute to DJ Unk and connecting personally with fans throughout the evening, the performance reflected an artist dedicated to every aspect of his craft."},{"t":"p","html":"With a sound that bridges contemporary pop, rock, hip-hop, R&amp;B, country, alternative, and inspirational music, Stephen Thomas continues to prove that great music transcends genres. His performances are immersive experiences designed to encourage audiences to embrace life, value relationships, prioritize wellness, and never lose hope."},{"t":"quote","html":"I want every performance to leave people with more hope than they had when they walked in.","cite":"- Stephen Thomas"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-01.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas receiving IV hydration therapy with Vital Flow before the performance","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-01.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-02.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas with the Vital Flow team at the event","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-02.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-03.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas at the Woody Fest","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-03.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-04.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas at the Woody Fest","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-04.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-05.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas with a supporter at the event","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-05.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-06-full.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas performing on stage at the Woody Fest with a heart visual on the screen behind him","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-06.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-07-full.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas welcomes a fan on stage during his Woody Fest performance","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-07.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-08-full.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas singing at the mic stand during his Woody Fest performance","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-08.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-09-full.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas facing the crowd from the stage at the Woody Fest","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-09.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-10-full.jpg","alt":"The crowd gathered at the stage during Stephen Thomas' Woody Fest performance","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-10.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-11-full.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas' keyboardist performing at the Woody Fest","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-11.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-12-full.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas backstage with a member of his team at the Woody Fest","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-12.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-13-full.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas and a member of his team seated backstage at the Woody Fest","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-13.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080301/gallery-14-full.jpg","alt":"Stephen Thomas with his mom at the Woody Fest","thumb":"images/2026080301/gallery-14.jpg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephen:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/StephenTMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/StephenThomas1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"2026080302","title":"Rob Carranza Returns with Powerful New Single About Family and Finding Purpose","date":"2026-08-03","lead":"Houston rock artist Rob Carranza releases a heartfelt single celebrating fatherhood and sacrifice.","hero":"images/2026080302/hero.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Houston rock artist Rob Carranza releases a heartfelt single celebrating fatherhood and sacrifice."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>HOUSTON, TX</strong> - Houston-based alternative rock singer songwriter <strong><a href=\"https://www.carranzaband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rob Carranza</a></strong> delivers one of his most personal releases to date with his new single, “<strong>Realign</strong>,” a powerful anthem about choosing family over personal ambition while discovering that dreams never truly disappear, they simply evolve."},{"t":"p","html":"Drawing from his own life, Carranza tells the story of a young college student whose life changes overnight when he becomes a father. Trading textbooks for timecards, late-night rehearsals for late-night feedings, and campus dreams for long work shifts, the song captures the quiet heroism of everyday sacrifice. Rather than viewing those sacrifices as the end of a dream, Carranza reframes them as the beginning of a new one."},{"t":"quote","html":"Going to school with big dreams and then here comes a baby. IS IT THE END... no it is just a new beginning. Dreams don’t die, they re-align.","cite":"- Carranza"},{"t":"img","src":"images/2026080302/img-01.jpg","alt":"Photo credit to Melanie Carranza"},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, the single blends melodic singer-songwriter storytelling with late ’90s alternative rock energy, recalling artists such as <strong>Brian Vander Ark</strong>, <strong>John Mayer</strong>, and <strong>Johnny Cash</strong>, while channeling the radio-ready spirit of <strong>Gin Blossoms</strong>, <strong>Goo Goo Dolls</strong>, <strong>Incubus</strong>, <strong>Foo Fighters</strong>, and <strong>Jimmy Eat World</strong>. The result is an uplifting, emotionally resonant track that speaks to anyone who has ever had to redefine success without giving up on their passions."},{"t":"p","html":"The release continues Carranza’s decades long musical journey. He first gained national attention as founder of the Houston rock band StarFX, whose album <em>Changes</em> earned moderate national success in 2000. That same year, Carranza recorded with acclaimed producer <strong>Dave Ahlert</strong> (<strong>The Jacksons</strong>, <strong>Fleetwood Mac</strong>, <strong>Sugar Ray</strong>, <strong>Blue October</strong>, <strong>Earth to Andy</strong>), leading to six record label offers with guidance from legendary music attorney <strong>Al Staehely</strong>, whose clients have included <strong>Stevie Ray Vaughan</strong>, <strong>King’s X</strong>, and <strong>Blue October</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"In 2004, Carranza and his wife, former <strong>Sony/BMG</strong> executive <strong>Melanie Carranza</strong>, formed a new group and performed at <strong>SXSW</strong> in Austin, Texas. Together they co-wrote the song “<strong>Where Did I Go</strong>” before Melanie stepped away from performing to focus on raising their son, Diego. Today, Rob continues that musical legacy through his solo project, Carranza, creating authentic songs rooted in family, perseverance, and everyday life."},{"t":"quote","html":"Choose a job you love and you will never have to work a day in your life. Once kids come along in your life you will be clock’n in to work for real...you better find something you like.","cite":"- Carranza"},{"t":"p","html":"Unlike many coming of age songs that focus on what was lost, Carranza’s latest release celebrates what was gained. It’s a tribute to parents who traded one dream for another and discovered both can coexist."},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded entirely by Carranza, the project showcases his complete artistic vision. He wrote, performed, produced, recorded, mixed, and mastered every element of the track himself."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Rob Carranza:"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston, Texas singer-songwriter Rob Carranza has spent more than two decades crafting honest, guitar-driven rock rooted in resilience, family, and the pursuit of purpose. Blending the melodic edge of late ’90s alternative rock with timeless singer-songwriter storytelling, his music has drawn comparisons to Foo Fighters, Jimmy Eat World, Incubus, Gin Blossoms, and Goo Goo Dolls, while echoing the heartfelt songwriting of artists like Brian Vander Ark, John Mayer, and Johnny Cash."},{"t":"p","html":"Carranza first gained national attention as the founder of the Houston rock band StarFX, whose 2000 release <em>Changes</em> earned moderate national success. In 2004, Rob joined forces with his wife, Melanie Carranza, to form a new band and co-write the song “Where Did I Go” before Melanie stepped away from performing to focus on raising their son."},{"t":"p","html":"Today, Rob continues his musical journey under the Carranza name, writing songs that celebrate hard work, faith, family, and the everyday moments that define a life well lived. His latest music reflects the belief that while life may change our plans, our dreams never truly disappear, they simply find a new direction."},{"t":"p","html":"Every Rob Carranza release is a true independent effort. He writes, performs, records, produces, mixes, and masters his own music, bringing an authentic voice and hands-on artistry to every song."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Rob:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/carranzamusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/robcarranzamusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.carranzaband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"2026080303","title":"When the Anger Becomes the Healing: A Blues Rock Anthem for Moving On","date":"2026-08-03","lead":"Hallie Marie channels heartbreak into an unforgettable statement of resilience and self-worth.","hero":"images/2026080303/hero.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Hallie Marie channels heartbreak into an unforgettable statement of resilience and self-worth."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>WASHINGTON, DC</strong> - Up-and-coming musician <strong>Hallie Marie</strong> shifts from a pop sound to a blues rock vibe in her latest track “<strong>A Small Man’s Pride</strong>.” She delivers a powerful, heartfelt anthem that turns pain into resilience. More than a breakup song, the release is an unapologetic statement about self-respect, healing, and refusing to let anyone diminish the power of expressing the full range of human emotion."},{"t":"p","html":"A powerful new blues rock release transforms the pain of heartbreak into a declaration of strength, resilience, and self-worth. Built on a driving 6/8 blues guitar pulse, infused with alternative rock energy, soulful lead vocals, and soaring gospel-inspired harmonies, the song captures the moment when grief gives way to freedom and the opinions of an emotionally immature former partner no longer carry any weight."},{"t":"p","html":"Rather than dwelling on loss, the track celebrates the liberation that follows the end of a relationship that had long since run its course. It explores the relief of shedding emotional dead weight and embracing the confidence that comes from no longer seeking validation from someone incapable of offering it. At its heart, the song is about reclaiming personal power and refusing to apologize for emotions that deserve to be heard."},{"t":"quote","html":"The idea was to convey my heartache as well as an empowered vulnerability. Like yeah, I feel anger, I feel betrayal but I also feel strong and wiser instead of smaller and more insecure.","cite":"- Hallie Marie"},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, the record blends classic blues rock influences with modern alternative rock textures, anchored by soulful vocals and rich gospel-style backing harmonies that amplify both its vulnerability and its defiance. The result is a timeless yet contemporary anthem that balances raw emotion with undeniable strength."},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond its musical impact, the release speaks to broader conversations about emotional honesty and the double standards women often face when expressing anger. It challenges the expectation that feminine emotion must always be softened or made comfortable for others, instead embracing anger as a healthy and necessary part of healing."},{"t":"quote","html":"Immediately I knew that this is the kind of song where the vocals have got to be tight. They’ve got to be powerful, they’ve got to be the gravity.","cite":"- Hallie Marie"},{"t":"p","html":"The song was brought to life by an accomplished creative team, featuring sound engineer <strong>Ken Schubert</strong>, guitarist <strong>Buddy Speir</strong>, drummer <strong>Andy Hamburger</strong>, and bassist <strong>Eric Bass</strong>, whose performances create a powerful foundation for the song’s emotional intensity and dynamic blues rock sound."},{"t":"quote","html":"This is a song primarily about female rage. People have no problem with a woman’s sadness, grief, or heartbreak but every woman has experienced disregard or pushback when they express emotions that are not traditionally associated with femininity and softness. This is not a rejection of anyone else’s power. It’s an affirmation of the healing that happens when you are listened to instead of dismissed as a ‘bitch’ or ‘overreacting’ the moment we raise our voice. It is empowering to finally say, ‘No, I will not take on the entire burden of being hurt when you have hurt me. We all have to take responsibility for how our actions affect others.’","cite":"- Hallie Marie"},{"t":"p","html":"This release is more than a breakup song, it’s an anthem for anyone who has found the courage to stop carrying someone else’s emotional baggage, speak their truth without apology, and move forward stronger than before."},{"t":"quote","html":"I’m lost here without you babe but you can be sure I won’t sit here and cry over a small man’s pride.","cite":"- Lyrics from “A Small Man’s Pride”"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits:"},{"t":"p","html":"Singer: <strong>Hallie Marie</strong><br>Songwriter: <strong>Hallie Marie</strong><br>Guitar: <strong>Buddy Speir</strong><br>Drums: <strong>Andy Hamburger</strong><br>Bass: <strong>Eric Scott</strong><br>Sound Engineer: <strong>Ken Schubert</strong>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hallie Marie:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Hallie Marie</strong> is an intellectually curious spirit who explores the complexities of human emotions by creating music that moves fluidly between the highs of love and joy to the depths of melancholy. Inspired by the likes of <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>, <strong>Billy Joel</strong>, and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, Hallie Marie merges pop, rock, and folk elements to write musical anecdotes that foster genuine connections through heartfelt lyrics, which has caught the attention of major indie tastemakers and listeners alike."},{"t":"quote","html":"An artist who knows how to bring brevity to difficult concepts.","cite":"- Earmilk"},{"t":"quote","html":"Hallie builds a body of work grounded in truth and emotional resonance.","cite":"- Neon Music"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Hallie Marie</strong> is a multifaceted Washington DC-based artist whose music critics have described as both “sad and hopeful” with an emotional weight that lingers long after the final note."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hallie Marie:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/halliemariemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/people/Hallie-Marie/100068917929503/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qv9RFavvRmeHdVLljnpMBQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"2026080304","title":"Riconoflow Turns the “lights on” with New Single","date":"2026-08-03","lead":"Puerto Rico-based artist blends bilingual house and trap influences into a bold anthem celebrating intimacy, confidence, and authentic connection.","hero":"images/2026080304/hero.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Puerto Rico-based artist blends bilingual house and trap influences into a bold anthem celebrating intimacy, confidence, and authentic connection."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>SAN JUAN, PUERTO RICO</strong> - Brazilian artist <strong>Riconoflow</strong> returns with his infectious new single, “<strong>lights on</strong>,” arriving on Friday, August 7, 2026. The bilingual house record serves as the latest installment in the waterfall release leading to his debut EP, <strong><em>Disruptive Beauty</em></strong>, a seven-song project exploring confidence, vulnerability, and modern relationships through dance floor-ready production."},{"t":"img","src":"images/2026080304/img-01.jpg","alt":"“lights on” cover art"},{"t":"p","html":"Built around pulsing house rhythms and melodic trap influences, “lights on” channels the sleek, late-night energy of <strong>Drake’s</strong> “<strong>Honestly, Never Mind</strong>” while carving out a sound uniquely Riconoflow’s own. Blending English and Portuguese lyrics with infectious hooks, the track captures the exhilaration of chemistry, attraction, and the freedom that comes from being fully yourself with someone else. Rather than framing intimacy as something hidden in the dark, Riconoflow flips the narrative."},{"t":"quote","html":"Everyone thinks intimacy starts when the lights go off...I think real intimacy starts when the lights are on, when you’re comfortable enough to let someone see who you really are.","cite":"- Riconoflow"},{"t":"p","html":"That perspective fuels the song’s central message. Beneath its club-ready production and flirtatious swagger lies a celebration of vulnerability, genuine connection, and the confidence to embrace authenticity without reservation."},{"t":"p","html":"The single continues the artistic vision behind <em>Disruptive Beauty</em>, a project that balances polished electronic production with deeply personal themes. Each release reveals another side of Riconoflow’s evolving identity as a singer songwriter, pairing infectious grooves with stories about self-expression, attraction, and emotional honesty."},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Medeirin</strong>, “lights on” seamlessly moves between hypnotic house grooves and bilingual vocal performances, creating an atmosphere equally suited for late-night clubs, rooftop parties, and intimate moments. The result is a record that feels both sensual and uplifting, designed as much for movement as for meaningful connection."},{"t":"quote","html":"‘lights on’ is about chemistry that goes beyond appearances, it’s about letting your guard down and finding someone who makes you feel completely comfortable being yourself.","cite":"- Riconoflow"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"images/2026080304/gallery-01.jpg","alt":"Photo by Grey Hernandez","thumb":"images/2026080304/gallery-01.jpg"},{"full":"images/2026080304/gallery-02.jpg","alt":"Photo by Grey Hernandez","thumb":"images/2026080304/gallery-02.jpg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Riconoflow:"},{"t":"p","html":"Riconoflow doesn’t fit the genre box the algorithm keeps trying to put him in, so he built his own: trap com house. House beats underneath, hip-hop and trap flow on top, feel-good substance with Brazilian flavor, warm, romantic, modern music made for daylight, not the two-a.m. club."},{"t":"p","html":"Born Ricardo Vieira in Belo Horizonte, Brazil, and raised between Miami, Irvine, and now San Juan, Puerto Rico, he writes what he actually knows: songs about being in love, falling into it, and falling out of it. The optimism running through his catalog isn’t the absence of hard things, it’s what he chooses to do with them. The point, as he’ll tell you, is for you to walk away lighter than you came."},{"t":"p","html":"That good feeling is real, and it’s earned. Riconoflow doesn’t drink, surfs, holds a jiu-jitsu black belt, trains six days a week, and is a husband and father. He’s out to prove something simple: you can make art and still live a healthy and happy life. The proof is stacking up. His music has landed editorial support on Apple Music and a Deezer playlist cover, he’s an approved Symphonic partner, five of his tracks have passed 50,000 streams, and outlets from Tinnitist to Hip-Hop Dose have taken notice. With his debut EP rolling out now, riconoflow is building the kind of career that compounds, consistent, durable, flowing over time. Because, as the name says, he’s big in flow."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Riconoflow:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/riconoflow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://instagram.com/riconoflow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4m4MscUJ91TKgdNy6sbYwz?si=7wD9xtLjTeeyToh87-xKSw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"2026080305","title":"EMÜ Announces “Hurt Like This,” a Dreamy Afro-R&B Single About Quiet Heartbreak","date":"2026-08-03","lead":"New release draws from East African roots, contemporary R&B, and the emotional cost of loving on someone else’s terms.","hero":"images/2026080305/hero.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"New release draws from East African roots, contemporary R&amp;B, and the emotional cost of loving on someone else’s terms."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>LOS ANGELES, CA</strong> - Los Angeles-based Afro-soul and R&amp;B artist <strong><a href=\"https://www.officialemu.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EMÜ</a></strong> releases her new single, “<strong>Hurt Like This</strong>,” on Friday, July 31, 2026. Rooted in personal experience and shaped by her Kenyan upbringing and life in the United States, the track reflects on an on-and-off relationship marked by mixed signals, uneven commitment, and the slow realization that love can also mean losing parts of yourself."},{"t":"p","html":"With dreamy Afro-R&amp;B production and Afrosoul influence, “Hurt Like This” pairs intimate storytelling with contemporary African rhythms and smooth melodies. The song sits near the emotional depth of <strong>Tems</strong> and the polished R&amp;B edge of <strong>Elaine</strong>, while remaining distinct in its focus on the quiet pressure of waiting for someone to choose you."},{"t":"quote","html":"I wanted ‘Hurt Like This’ to give a voice to the quiet heartbreak, the kind that happens when someone’s promises don’t match their actions.","cite":"- EMÜ"},{"t":"img","src":"images/2026080305/img-01.jpg","alt":"Photo by Maries Danila"},{"t":"p","html":"The single centers on the tension between hope and self-recognition. In the verses, EMÜ traces the emotional unraveling of a relationship that moved on one person’s schedule, while the chorus lands on the repeated realization that love, at its worst, can leave lasting marks."},{"t":"p","html":"That perspective is consistent with EMÜ’s broader artistic identity. Emü (pronounced Emma) is a Kenyan-born Afrosoul and R&amp;B artist whose music bridges East African roots and contemporary global sounds. Born in Kenya and raised in the United States from the age of nine, she draws inspiration from both cultures, blending soulful storytelling, rich melodies, and honest emotion. Her work often explores love, heartbreak, healing, and self-discovery through a lens shaped by heritage and belonging."},{"t":"p","html":"“Hurt Like This” was produced by <strong>Spromson</strong>, with recording, mixing, and mastering by <strong>Rebecca Marti</strong>. Artwork photography is credited to Maries Danila. A visual video for the single is coming soon, adding another layer to a release that leans into both vulnerability and restraint."},{"t":"quote","html":"Sometimes the deepest heartbreak isn’t being left, it’s realizing how much of yourself you gave away while hoping someone would choose you.","cite":"- EMÜ"},{"t":"img","src":"images/2026080305/img-02.jpg","alt":"EMÜ"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About EMÜ:"},{"t":"p","html":"EMÜ, pronounced Emma, is the recording name of Kenyan-born Afrosoul and R&amp;B artist Emma Ngula, a Los Angeles-based singer and songwriter whose work bridges East African roots and contemporary global sounds. Born in Kenya and raised in the United States from age nine, she brings a perspective shaped by migration, memory, and the experience of living between more than one world."},{"t":"p","html":"Her music is built on soulful storytelling, rich melodies, and direct emotional detail. EMÜ writes about love, heartbreak, healing, and self-discovery with a calm, honest voice that gives weight to everyday emotions and the quiet shifts that come with growing up, moving forward, and learning where home lives."},{"t":"p","html":"Across her work, EMÜ offers a voice grounded in lived experience and cultural continuity. Her songs reflect heritage and growth without separating one from the other, creating music that feels personal, measured, and connected to the spaces where identity is formed."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with EMÜ:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.officialemu.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/emma_mueniii\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7sU3hLhSvqbhAvmGcLAwfE?si=oeCj7qb3R7-aiW1X-F3YtA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"2026080306","title":"Reese Weil & Nef The Pharaoh Keep the Momentum Rolling with Their Latest Single, “Money”","date":"2026-08-01","lead":"One release after another, the duo return this time around by turning heartbreak into an anthem.","hero":"images/2026080306/hero.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"One release after another, the duo return this time around by turning heartbreak into an anthem."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>CHICO, CA</strong> (August 1, 2026) - Reese Weil joins forces with Bay Area heavyweight <strong>Nef The Pharaoh</strong> once again for their new single, “<strong>Money</strong>,” arriving August 1, 2026. Blending melodic West Coast hip-hop with Bay Area bounce, polished hooks, warm synth textures, deep 808s, and radio-ready production, the record delivers an honest look at the emotional cost of giving everything to someone who never gives the same in return."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Zi3EV89aof6OMz8SHTxDN?si=givd5naNQzuyPQ6YSFOnsQ","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"images/2026080306/img-01.jpg","alt":"Photo by Dana Hocking"},{"t":"p","html":"Built around themes of dating, relationships, red flags, self-worth, and knowing when it’s time to walk away, “Money” captures the frustration of investing emotionally and financially into a relationship that ultimately leaves one person feeling unappreciated. Rather than dwelling on heartbreak, the song embraces the freedom that comes with choosing peace over one-sided love."},{"t":"p","html":"The collaboration came together organically during Nef The Pharaoh’s visit to Chico, California, where he was in town for a performance and to film the music video for “The One” with Reese Weil and <strong>Cotati7z</strong>. Reese had written the hook and developed the foundation for “Money” just hours before Nef arrived. Produced by <strong>Dana Hocking</strong>, the session quickly turned into lightning in a bottle as Nef stepped into the booth and delivered his verse within minutes. The result is a natural chemistry between Reese Weil’s melodic songwriting and Nef The Pharaoh’s unmistakable Bay Area swagger, creating a record that feels both personal and instantly memorable."},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Money’ is about realizing that no amount of giving can make someone love you back. At some point you have to choose your own peace and walk away.","cite":"- Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"Reflecting on how effortlessly the collaboration unfolded, Reese adds, “I wrote the hook just a couple hours before Nef got to Chico. The whole record came together naturally, sometimes the best songs happen when you don’t overthink them.”"},{"t":"p","html":"With infectious melodies, relatable storytelling, and an authentic West Coast sound, “Money” showcases Reese Weil’s continued evolution as an artist while pairing him with one of Northern California’s most recognizable voices. The single is positioned to resonate with fans of melodic hip-hop, relationship-driven storytelling, and contemporary West Coast rap."},{"t":"quote","html":"Working with Nef The Pharaoh is easy. Watching him step into the booth and knock out his verse in just a few minutes was unreal.","cite":"- Reese Weil"},{"t":"img","src":"images/2026080306/img-02.jpg","alt":"Photo by Dana Hocking"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Reese Weil:"},{"t":"p","html":"Reese Weil is a Northern California born artist, songwriter, and producer whose genre-blending sound bridges West Coast hip-hop, melodic pop, and alternative rock. Known for smooth, breathy vocals and groove-driven production, Weil crafts music that feels both laid-back and polished, which captures the spirit of California while reaching a global audience."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil’s musical journey began early. At just four years old, he picked up a guitar in his hometown of Chico, California, laying the foundation for a lifelong dedication to songwriting and performance. His talent and work ethic eventually earned him a scholarship to the prestigious Berklee College of Music, where he refined his skills in music production, composition, and modern songwriting. The experience helped shape the versatile creative voice that defines his work today."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil has built an impressive list of accomplishments. He has opened for <strong>The Wailers</strong>, the legendary band associated with <strong>Bob Marley</strong>, and contributed songwriting for international pop icon <strong>Enrique Iglesias</strong>. His music has also found a home on television, with placements on series such as <strong><em>Bones</em></strong> and <strong><em>Twisted</em></strong>. In addition, his work has been published through the music company Pulse Music Group, further expanding his reach as a songwriter and producer."},{"t":"p","html":"With a growing catalog, high-profile collaborations, and a steadily expanding fan base, Reese Weil continues to carve out his place as a dynamic modern artist. His music brings an energy designed for stages, screens, and playlists around the world."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Reese Weil:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reeseweilmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Zi3EV89aof6OMz8SHTxDN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"463228","title":"When the Prey Becomes the Predator: Riah Hunts in One Unbroken Take on \"Lestat\"","date":"2026-07-27","lead":"The Denver dark-pop artist directs and stars in a single-shot descent through a vampire den, where a seductive summer anthem reveals the innocent outsider was the monster all along.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/463228/ed20de7ba21ebb60501dafb726e41d62.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Denver dark-pop artist directs and stars in a single-shot descent through a vampire den, where a seductive summer anthem reveals the innocent outsider was the monster all along."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>DENVER, CO</strong> (July 27, 2026) – There is a moment in every vampire story when the hunt reverses. The one who seemed lost, wide-eyed and wandering among beautiful monsters, turns out to know exactly where the exits are and exactly who she came to find. “<strong>Lestat</strong>” lives in that turn, in the half-second before the prey shows her teeth."},{"t":"p","html":"Out July 27, 2026, the official music video for “Lestat” is the most visually ambitious release yet from Denver dark-pop artist <strong>Riah</strong>, featuring <strong>Cadiel</strong>. Directed by Riah and <strong>Luke Ostermiller</strong> and captured in a continuous shot, it immerses viewers in a decadent world of vampires, desire, and deception. At first Riah appears to be an innocent outsider searching for a mysterious man in a den of beautiful monsters. As the night unfolds, the truth arrives: she was never lost. She is the Queen."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/9umgYwdOIQI","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Artists like <strong>Rihanna</strong>, <strong>Kim Petras</strong>, <strong>Zara Larsson</strong>, and <strong>Hayley Kiyoko</strong> have pulled pop toward something darker and more cinematic, where sensuality carries a sharper edge. “Lestat” steps into that conversation and adds its own gothic theater: a summer anthem about power, temptation, and embracing the monster within."},{"t":"quote","html":"\"This was my first music video with a full cast of extras and my first time attempting a one-shot concept. We wanted the audience to feel like they were wandering through a vampire den with me in real time.\"","cite":"Riah"},{"t":"p","html":"Riah built “Lestat” around her eclectic tastes. The video features an ensemble cast of diverse performers, including queer and non-binary characters in celebration of Pride, alongside members of Denver's vampire scene. As both a co-director and a producer of her own work, she belongs to a growing wave of women shaping their releases from behind the camera as well as in front of it.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840347/large-f5fcecd21060a3639ae696a4a9fc8371.jpeg","alt":"Images by Ren Matthews"},{"t":"p","html":"The song moves like the night it depicts. Cold-skinned verses give way to a chorus that repeats \"they call you parasite\" until devotion and danger blur, and Cadiel's verse pulls the temptation closer, all flashing lights and instincts screaming to run. Across the single take, the camera never blinks, following Riah from outsider to Queen as the den reveals who was hunting whom. \"I love stories that subvert expectations,\" says Riah. \"You think you're watching a woman searching for a man, but really she's hunting.\""},{"t":"p","html":"“Lestat” is an early signal of something larger. The track belongs to Riah's forthcoming album, Insurrection, which she plans to pair with a fully scripted immersive show in collaboration with <strong>DejaView Productions</strong>, <strong>Medusa's Curse</strong>. The one-take video, with its theatrical staging, 'campy' feel, and ensemble world-building, reads as a first glimpse of that ambition: pop songs built to be staged, inhabited, and walked through rather than simply streamed. \"One take means there's nowhere to hide. The energy had to be real, and everyone involved brought so much life to the world we created.\" By the time the take ends, the question the video opens with has answered itself. She was never the prey."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840351/large-557ed887c2972d2f7a5e7f3802ba9a56.jpeg","alt":"IMG_1940.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840351/preview-0a64e58935567564a2a1a709ca925a91.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840352/large-31779f12c5ba351a0071286cfb9da403.jpeg","alt":"159AE67D-0137-4590-8C21-E2F8D68228DF.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840352/preview-2be8d6dbaf3b098f318684bdda755def.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840348/large-dbf9c4f3598cd0677c3f29834af46ba6.jpeg","alt":"IMG_1939.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840348/preview-3e7d10513006bc38055cacde094d50ca.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840349/large-eeaf2b7c71c1d0708a64466d680757b1.jpeg","alt":"IMG_1938.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840349/preview-8c6272b3f6dbc60cdcc8536998430910.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840350/large-dcb8e721ed27ecbf17bef85fd02506ec.jpeg","alt":"IMG_1937.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/840350/preview-57111a014b39ddb98ce4e4ed5950ccaa.jpeg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Ren Matthews"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Riah:"},{"t":"p","html":"Riah, a rising force in the Bedroom Pop scene, is crafting introspective and evocative music that resonates with the complexities of love, sex, loss, and a distinctive \"villain energy.\" Drawing from personal life experiences, Riah channels deep emotion into every lyric and melody, creating an intimate connection with listeners.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Starting in the Los Angeles entertainment industry at the tender age of 17, Riah faced the harsh realities of the pre-Me Too era, which fueled her desire for autonomy and control over her artistic vision. After years of enduring the industry's darker side, she stepped back, determined to return to music only on her own terms. Now, as an accomplished entrepreneur, Riah has reclaimed her voice and is ready to make waves with a fresh and authentic sound."},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to her musical journey, Riah has captivated audiences at numerous festivals, clubs, and acoustic venues. Her passion for performance extends beyond music, as she is also a competitive pole dancer, having won in her division and heels categories in the prestigious PSO Mountain competition in 2023.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a unique blend of vulnerability and power, Riah is poised to leave a lasting impact on the music world, bringing a new level of depth and intensity to the Bedroom Pop genre."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Riah:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4W98Etru2ErpE95smqDdfh?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/riahmusic1991\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/riahmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@Riah-Music-1991\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"462537","title":"Between the Acoustic and the Electric, Colorado Duo Woven Hollow Arrives at Last with Figure of Light","date":"2026-07-17","lead":"Glenwood Springs folk/indie duo Woven Hollow releases their debut full-length, a multi-genre 33-minute journey through human connection, technological duality, and the stubborn weight of love.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/462537/a882e7caf50374ac0de2dbc240f27697.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Glenwood Springs folk/indie duo Woven Hollow releases their debut full-length, a multi-genre 33-minute journey through human connection, technological duality, and the stubborn weight of love."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>GLENWOOD SPRINGS, CO</strong> (July 17, 2026) - There is a space between the pluck of a guitar string and the hum of a synthesizer where something quietly unresolvable lives. Not conflict, exactly. More like the feeling of standing at the edge of two worlds and refusing to step fully into either one. It is the space where human longing resists the clean logic of the digital, where old things and new things press against each other without quite making peace. Some artists spend a career dancing around that tension. <strong>Woven Hollow</strong> - the Colorado-based folk duo of <strong>Anna Murphy</strong> and <strong>Van Wampler</strong> - firmly plant a flag in the middle of that tension with their debut full-length album, <strong><em>Figure of Light</em></strong>, on July 17, 2026."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/466buRykNZGHjz7d0XNzZt?si=es40Mdm5TouG-VpwBPZt7w","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Artists like Shovels &amp; Rope, The Civil Wars, and Hozier have carved out a vital lane for folk music that refuses to stay put - pairing raw acoustic intimacy with production choices that widen the lens without losing the room. Woven Hollow belongs to that conversation, drawing equally on the orchestral intimacy of Sufjan Stevens, the austere vocal chemistry of The Secret Sisters, and the atmospheric production instincts of Frou Frou and Lana Del Rey. <em>Figure of Light&nbsp;</em>doesn't land squarely inside any one of those reference points., but rather is assembled from pieces of all of them, filtered through the specific experience of two people building a life together in the mountains of Colorado."},{"t":"quote","html":"The record has grown so much from what we originally set out to make. The songs have changed, the sound has grown, but the theme has largely remained true to the original goal. It's a journey through acoustic spaces and genres that complement each other while also reflecting the battle between life and technology, and the ups and downs of relationships and human bonds.","cite":"- Van Wampler and Anna Murphy"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837859/large-13bab542827d62b2706b5b2060a35526.jpg","alt":"'Figure of Light' Cover Art"},{"t":"p","html":"Anna Murphy and Van Wampler are based in Glenwood Springs, Colorado, a small city tucked into the western slope of the Rockies, and the album carries that geography in its bones - the open space, the distance between people, the way isolation can feel like freedom until it doesn't. The duo married in 2024, and the closing track, <strong>\"Chaparral,\"</strong> takes its name from the street where they live. They began tracking this album in 2019 and finished it across studios, states, and a global pandemic - coordinating a roster of more than a dozen collaborators in person and remotely to build out a record they were unwilling to rush. Anna, a multi-instrumentalist who expanded her range to tenor guitar and banjo in the course of making the record, brings melodic precision and harmonic intuition. Van serves as the project's primary architect - engineering, producing, and writing the majority of the material at his <strong>CinemaRaven Studios</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"The sonic world of <em>Figure of Light </em>is wider than its folk foundation suggests. Ambience is woven into the record's DNA: the sustained, shimmering textures that run beneath many of the tracks were built by lightly bowing discordant harmonics on stringed instruments, creating a human-made electronic quality that echoes the album's central tension between the organic and the digital. Fiddle, banjo, tenor guitar, classical guitar, trumpet, flugelhorn, violin, viola, cello, and field snare share space with production choices drawn from pop and electronic music. Mastered by <strong>Idania Valencia</strong> at <strong>Sterling Sound</strong>, and mixed across three different engineers - including <strong>Jason Richmond</strong> on four tracks and <strong>Stu Stapleton</strong> on two - the record maintains cohesion while allowing each song to occupy its own corner of the emotional spectrum."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>\"Figure of Light,\"</strong> the opening title track, establishes the album's central image immediately: a light that leads, that beckons, that stays just out of reach. Its ambient shimmer - built almost entirely from those bowed harmonics - signals immediately that this is not a standard folk record. <a href=\"https://wovenhollow.bandcamp.com/album/ten-feet-under\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\"Ten Feet Under\"</strong></a> broadens the record's emotional range, moving through grief, longing, and the strange consolation of knowing time is finite. The song's bridge - <em>\"we don't have much time around / it may not seem so profound / but I guess you'll know what I mean once you're in the ground\"</em> - sits with the listener the way the best folk lyrics do: plainly worded, quietly devastating. <strong>\"Battle Line,\"</strong> featuring bridge vocals from New Jersey-based artist <strong>42RAE</strong> alongside field snare by Denver's&nbsp;<strong>Wes Barton</strong> and strings by<strong>&nbsp;Jess Townsend&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Tom McCluskey</strong>, is the record's most sonically ambitious track, expanding into a full ensemble arrangement that traces the quiet wars fought between people who love each other. A music video for <strong>\"Reruns\"</strong> - which syncs clips from classic television with the song's lyrics about nostalgia and the inability to let go of the past - has earned festival recognition and is already in circulation."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/9vQFu2BhENM","height":""},{"t":"quote","html":"Van has put in countless hours to ensure this is an album you can listen to top to bottom. It was pretty cool to hear about all the people he coordinated both in-person and virtually. He also inspired me to learn more instruments to help round out the sound - I picked up tenor guitar and banjo outside of my usual classical guitar.","cite":"Anna Murphy"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Figure of Light</em> features contributions from a cohort of accomplished Colorado musicians, including bassist <strong>Jeanette Adams</strong>, drummer <strong>Leor Manelis</strong>, banjoist <strong>Mac Benning</strong>, and fiddlers <strong>Camille Backman</strong> and&nbsp;<strong>Delaney Meyers</strong>, alongside collaborators who tracked remotely from across the country and internationally. Nashville vocalist <strong>Rochelle Riser</strong> delivers the lead on <strong>\"Don't Worry Darling,\"</strong> the album's most open-handed song - an invitation to release shame, to let someone in, to stop waiting for the end before finally opening the door."},{"t":"p","html":"By the time <em>Figure of Light </em>reaches its closing notes, the tension it has held throughout the record - between connection and isolation, acoustic warmth and electronic cool, the past and what's still possible - doesn't resolve so much as settle. What lingers is what the best records always leave behind: the sense that someone sat down and told the truth about something, and that the telling cost them something real."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/774460/large-622454f118623c534ac9acd3f7d1a07f.jpg","alt":"Van Wampler and Anna Murphy of Woven Hollow"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Woven Hollow:"},{"t":"p","html":"The sound of music and the beauty of the Rocky Mountains led the winding paths of Anna Murphy and Van Wampler to cross in 2017. A few recording sessions together quickly blossomed into an ongoing collaboration which quickly solidified itself as Woven Hollow. After recording a few songs and playing a short tour in 2019, the duet set out to record its first full-length album during the Covid lock down of 2020. Years of work on the album would see a number of incredible musicians adding their talent to Woven Hollow's compositions, and what started as a simple folk record grew into an adventurous project that can hardly be described by a single genre.&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"CONNECT WITH WOVEN HOLLOW:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.WovenHollow.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/wovenhollowmusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3EC1U6eXrn2Yj3SEQLPvnA?si=UTZVOfzqSL6Dhtl9cUhJxA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@wovenhollow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3EC1U6eXrn2Yj3SEQLPvnA?utm_source=generator","height":"352"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"462956","title":"Aidan Leclaire Dives Into the Deep End of Growing Up on 'Diving'","date":"2026-07-17","lead":"The Northern Virginia alt-pop band's most expansive record yet swings from raw, blink-182-charged rock to hushed folk, tracing the cost of people-pleasing and the strange weight of coming of age in an uncertain world.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/462956/66abf499c65207e8cb7fd82fbff91dd8.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Northern Virginia alt-pop band's most expansive record yet swings from raw, blink-182-charged rock to hushed folk, tracing the cost of people-pleasing and the strange weight of coming of age in an uncertain world."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Vienna, VA (July 17, 2026)&nbsp;</strong>- There is a particular kind of falling that happens in your twenties, when you step into something you cannot see the bottom of and only realize mid-air that you are already committed. You do the things that keep the peace, that keep people close, that keep the surface calm, and then one day you look up and find you have drifted somewhere you never meant to go. That feeling, of being pushed into unfamiliar emotional water and bracing for a landing that may not come, runs through every song on <strong><em>Diving</em></strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Out July 17, 2026, <em>Diving</em> is the new album from Northern Virginia alt-pop artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aidan Leclaire</strong></a>, a seven-track record that moves between the urgency of late-night rock and the quiet of early-morning reckoning. Written and recorded across four studios with a rotating cast of producers and the full involvement of Leclaire's band, it is the most ambitious project the group has put to tape."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/3EOlpzL1IhSmrySzOnAUnC?si=c_9qas6TRdybQ_Rbzsgr2A","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Artists like <strong>blink-182</strong>, <strong>Brand New</strong>, and <strong>Green Day</strong> built a tradition where loud guitars and bruised honesty live in the same three minutes, where a hook can carry a confession. <em>Diving</em> steps into that lineage on its opening run and then keeps walking, past the noise and into something softer and stranger, until the record ends somewhere closer to folk than to punk."},{"t":"quote","html":"This album has been the most expansive work that we have done. From the number of different recording engineers and producers to the scope of involvement by the band members in shaping the songs, this has been the most professional collaboration and the most fulfilling journey to produce a collection of songs.","cite":"Aidan Leclaire"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/842629/large-1414074606f23f8de17672527542a4fb.jpg","alt":"Album Cover for 'Diving' by Abby Jover"},{"t":"p","html":"Leclaire first emerged in the Washington, DC-area scene in 2023, playing throughout Northern Virginia, Maryland, and DC before assembling the band that now backs the live show. Over the last year the group has built a following across DC, Richmond, Boston, and New York, selling more than 600 tickets across their last four local shows, including two sellouts. Their July 2025 debut album <strong><em>Hail to the Dogs</em></strong> drew praise from indie outlets including Indie Boulevard, which called it \"intelligent, thoughtful, and thoroughly engaging.\" <em>Diving</em> is the sound of that band stretching its range."},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, the record refuses to sit still. The first three tracks, <strong>\"2:02,\"</strong> <strong>\"Dive Slow,\"</strong> and <strong>\"Talk,\"</strong> hit fast and loud, raw alt-rock and pop with the in-your-face energy of the band's punk influences. Then <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0DhP1a8MxJebVB8BuonChS?si=9cdc9a3c8a3e4dd4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\"Lucy\"</strong></a> breaks the surface into pure, sunny pop. From there the album sinks into its second half: <strong>\"Parfait\"</strong> and<strong>&nbsp;\"Fishbowl\"</strong> turn low and mellow, soulful and unhurried, and the closer, <strong>\"Nature's Tune,\"</strong> drifts into something close to folk."},{"t":"p","html":"That descent is the point. \"Dive Slow\" sets the album's tone early, all forward motion and white lies and the refusal to keep \"playing their calls,\" a song about no longer performing for people who never had your interests at heart. \"Lucy\" is the record's brightest moment, a carefree pop high about a fascination that pulls you somewhere you know you should not stay. \"Nature's Tune\" lands the album in stillness, the band stripped back to its most exposed and acoustic, the last word after the noise has burned off."},{"t":"quote","html":"\"I initially tried to balance the album with an even mix of harder-edged, up-tempo songs and softer, mellower ones, but I realized that kind of symmetry doesn't reflect real emotional life. We aren't steady or consistent day to day. We move through highs and lows, sometimes staying in one longer than the other. Sequencing the album so it begins with the heavier tracks and ends with the quieter ones felt truer to the emotional rollercoaster behind it.\"","cite":"Aidan Leclaire"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831657/large-4ea36903e703da61ef38b6f5ccb6962b.jpg","alt":"God Boy - Colin.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831657/preview-4c0180739a34e8885cbbfcd9e832a53d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831658/large-eb8a8ae2da114b9a9cdfc0aa44dca4d3.jpg","alt":"Good Boy - Izzy.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831658/preview-202e06a0cdc6239e8bcaded481fe287b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831659/large-58a843f96f89fc6fe59370a257d292db.jpg","alt":"Colin.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831659/preview-8115dc6abbb433c3211a91ba440c156d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831660/large-7beb947e321d228ebc11f099fd4b0356.jpg","alt":"Figure 8 - 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831660/preview-0c97125d12f16099c0464c1e0cea317e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831661/large-62a60129543a2056047177175568a189.jpg","alt":"Good Boy - Will.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831661/preview-fe7ceffce8fa832f669fd3a0db8ca5a9.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Band photos by Abby Jover"},{"t":"p","html":"Underneath the shifting sound is a single thread: the instinct to please and appease because it feels like the only way to hold a relationship together, and the slow discovery that it leads somewhere you never intended, sometimes hurting yourself or the people you love. <em>Diving&nbsp;</em>also sits in the tension between private struggle and public scale, the guilt of feeling your own troubles loom large against a world of wars and climate and a future that looks bleaker than the one you were promised as a child. The cover art holds the same uncertainty and the sense of not quite knowing where, or when, you are; its blurred, crimson haze making the familiar feel distant and unsteady."},{"t":"p","html":"The album arrives as Leclaire continues to gain ground on the East Coast indie circuit, known for energetic sets and a grassroots fanbase grown through word of mouth and a collaborative stage presence that carries the intimacy of the recordings into a room full of people. With <em>Diving</em>, the band makes its widest, most honest statement yet."},{"t":"p","html":"You can spend a record bracing for the landing. <em>Diving</em> is what it sounds like to stop bracing, and to find that the falling itself was the part worth listening to."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831656/large-38a1b9a6f6cc8f1c9685d3ede1ede788.jpg","alt":"Photo by Aidan"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Aidan Leclaire"},{"t":"p","html":"Aidan Leclaire is a Northern Virginia singer-songwriter crafting indie rock and alt-pop songs rooted in emotional honesty, sharp songwriting, and energetic live performance. Influenced by artists ranging from Arctic Monkeys to Joni Mitchell, Leclaire combines introspective storytelling with infectious hooks and modern indie production."},{"t":"p","html":"Leclaire first emerged in the Washington, DC-area music scene in 2023, performing throughout Northern Virginia, Maryland, and DC before forming the band that now backs his live performances. Over the last year, the group has cultivated a growing regional audience across DC, Richmond, Boston, and New York, selling more than 600 tickets across their last four local shows, including two sellouts."},{"t":"p","html":"In July 2025, the band released their debut album, <em>Hail to the Dogs</em>, earning praise from indie music outlets including<strong>&nbsp;Indie Boulevard</strong>, which described the project as “intelligent, thoughtful, and thoroughly engaging,” while noting it “positions Aidan Leclaire firmly within today’s indie-rock landscape.”"},{"t":"p","html":"While Leclaire writes and produces the material, the band plays a central role in shaping the arrangements and translating the songs into dynamic live performances that continue to resonate with audiences and tastemakers alike."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR?utm_source=generator&si=338ce43db7b94def","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://aidanleclaire.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> |<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/the_leclaires\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">&nbsp;Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"462528","title":"Windows Down, Volume Up: Reese Weil and Nef The Pharaoh Deliver the Summer's Most Carefree Anthem","date":"2026-07-06","lead":"West Coast hip-hop collides with nightlife energy as Reese Weil and Nef The Pharaoh deliver a confident, club-ready single about tuning out the noise and living in the moment.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/462528/106bed4f9176dd0a24a947e702410173.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"West Coast hip-hop collides with nightlife energy as Reese Weil and Nef The Pharaoh deliver a confident, club-ready single about tuning out the noise and living in the moment."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>CHICO, CA (July 4, 2026)</strong> - There is a particular freedom that comes with cruising the city after dark, windows down, music rattling the speakers, the weight of everything that does not matter falling further behind with every mile. It is a feeling less explained than lived - and on a good night, with the right record on, it becomes a philosophy. <strong>Reese Weil </strong>channels exactly that energy on his new single <strong>\"I Ain't Worried,\"</strong> available everywhere July 4, 2026, featuring fellow West Coast standout <strong>Nef The Pharaoh</strong> alongside artists <strong>Derek King </strong>and <strong>Cotati7z</strong>."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/3LON0I316GGGVlsZ7RCmQJ?si=b36af4f5f1e64eec","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837850/large-87d0133e99608ea98f705b9e29dcbf3e.jpg","alt":"Cover art by Dana Hocking"},{"t":"p","html":"The track lands at the intersection of West Coast cool and club-floor momentum - a hypnotic, hook-driven anthem that settles into its own groove and refuses to leave. Think Bruno Mars' melodic ease stacked against E-40's Bay Area authority, filtered through the laid-back, nightlife-saturated world of Shoreline Mafia and G-Eazy. It is the kind of record that sounds equally natural coming out of a house party speaker at midnight or a festival stage at golden hour."},{"t":"quote","html":"\"At its core, 'I Ain't Worried' is about confidence - not arrogance. It's about trusting yourself.\"","cite":"Reese Weil"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837855/large-f42e4b420085c4f4c0fdb9434811ade8.jpg","alt":"reese-studio.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837855/preview-4fbc67a3cfebfe28c8dab020c2218eb7.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837853/-6624f98562cff690b322ee45a6783548.jpg","alt":"IMG_3396.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837853/preview-28f530ecf0dd26cd8aac8fe878d25dff.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837854/large-a53129ad68f87eda477ec4fd7a4229eb.jpg","alt":"reese-green.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837854/preview-8f8bd00ab425d9c9e3906c7b5dcd09fd.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837851/large-13d75861ebd53ec768722da844237580.jpg","alt":"IMG_3397-2b.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837851/preview-a3c4504983ee4793d8b8e9d52b9afba8.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837852/large-c8628a35f44424b17931773d73d61f6c.jpg","alt":"IMG_3351-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837852/preview-6ca6718f4dbc92a8bd4da564ac0aa7b3.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Reese Weil is a Chico, CA-based artist and producer with deep roots across the California corridor - from the Bay to Los Angeles. That geography is embedded in his sound: Bay Area swagger, LA polish, and the kind of unpretentious confidence that can only come from earning your place in a scene as competitive as West Coast hip-hop. As both the primary artist and producer on \"I Ain't Worried,\" Weil commands every layer of the record - writing, performing, and shaping the sonic environment that makes the track feel inevitable."},{"t":"p","html":"Nef The Pharaoh brings his South Vallejo credibility and signature double-time bravado to the second verse, grounding the track in authentic Bay Area identity. Derek King and Cotati7z round out the lineup, each adding a distinct dimension that keeps the record moving and unpredictable beneath its polished, effortless surface. Production is handled by Weil and Dana Hocking, with mastering by Carter Boy - a team that delivers a finished sound clean enough for radio and raw enough for the streets."},{"t":"quote","html":"\"Working with Nef The Pharaoh, Derek King, and Cotati7z was special because everybody brought a completely different flavor. That's what gives the record its character and makes it feel alive.\"","cite":"Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"\"I Ain't Worried\" arrives as a preview of Weil and Nef The Pharaoh's forthcoming collaborative album <strong><em>Valet</em></strong>, a project that promises to expand on the chemistry and West Coast world-building the two artists began here. For fans of the region's hip-hop lineage - and for any listener who knows the particular freedom of a late night drive with nowhere else to be - this is the record that sets the tone."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/830951/large-e2c9280b05b508e050f531a16e07e708.jpg","alt":"Reese Weil"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"Reese Weil is a Northern California born artist, songwriter, and producer whose genre-blending sound bridges West Coast hip-hop, melodic pop, and alternative rock. Known for smooth, breathy vocals and groove-driven production, Weil crafts music that feels both laid-back and polished which captures the spirit of California while reaching a global audience."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil’s musical journey began early. At just four years old, he picked up a guitar in his hometown of Chico, California, laying the foundation for a lifelong dedication to songwriting and performance. His talent and work ethic eventually earned him a scholarship to the prestigious Berklee College of Music, where he refined his skills in music production, composition, and modern songwriting. The experience helped shape the versatile creative voice that defines his work today."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1Zi3EV89aof6OMz8SHTxDN?utm_source=generator&si=64d1605526524b14","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Weil has built an impressive list of accomplishments. He has opened for <strong>The Wailers</strong>, the legendary band associated with <strong>Bob Marley</strong>, and contributed songwriting for international pop icon <strong>Enrique Iglesias</strong>. His music has also found a home on television, with placements on series such as <em><strong>Bones</strong></em> and <strong><em>Twisted</em></strong>. In addition, his work has been published through the music company Pulse Music Group, further expanding his reach as a songwriter and producer."},{"t":"p","html":"With a growing catalog, high-profile collaborations, and a steadily expanding fan base, Reese Weil continues to carve out his place as a dynamic modern artist. His music brings an energy designed for stages, screens, and playlists around the world."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reeseweilmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Zi3EV89aof6OMz8SHTxDN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>​"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"456728","title":"Bird x Butterfly Announces Debut Album 'Origami Hotel,' Where Every Room Holds a Different Kind of Love","date":"2026-06-26","lead":"An intimate, cinematic exploration of love, memory, and emotional transformation","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/456728/f20bb7cdabd82342d8c6c329ca12abc1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An intimate, cinematic exploration of love, memory, and emotional transformation&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>CHICAGO, IL (June 26, 2026)</strong> - Korean-American duo <strong>Bird x Butterfly</strong>, the collaborative project of <strong>Frances Kang</strong> and <strong>Paul Kim</strong>, announce the release of their highly anticipated debut album <em><strong>Origami Hote</strong></em><em><strong>l</strong></em>, arriving Friday, June 26, 2026. Blending cinematic indie pop with singer-songwriter intimacy, the record captures a deeply personal journey through love, loss, and the fragile beauty of human experience."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/38dYcptEaBZnp2WD1IQg4G?utm_source=generator&si=767dc5727b7e44cd","height":"352"},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/38dYcptEaBZnp2WD1IQg4G?si=XA_vyYlWQ0GDE7qnFx8OVQ","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Built on the premise that life unfolds as a series of emotional “rooms,” <em>Origami </em><em>Hotel </em>invites listeners to step inside moments of joy, grief, nostalgia, and quiet revelation. Each of the album’s nine tracks reflects a different emotional landscape, brought to life through lush, orchestral arrangements (strings, harp, brass, and layered synths) while remaining grounded in the duo’s signature vocal closeness."},{"t":"quote","html":"“The fragility and uncertainty in life is a beautiful thing.”","cite":"Kang and Kim"},{"t":"p","html":"Known for their rare musical chemistry, Kang and Kim create a sound that feels both intimate and expansive. Their voices don’t simply harmonize... they merge, forming a singular emotional presence that anchors the album’s sweeping production. The result is a sound that feels cinematic yet deeply personal, evoking artists like <strong>Bon Ive</strong><strong>r</strong>, <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>, <strong>Billie Eilish</strong>, <strong>Lizzy McAlpine</strong>, and <strong>The Civil Wars</strong>."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/828653/large-1903fc93ba61678549144e9f6a1d9e5a.jpg","alt":"Photo by Ayaka Sano"},{"t":"quote","html":"“We are very lucky to have made it here as both a musical duo and partners in life. We've spent a lot of time thinking about how we got here, what we’ve been through and what we’re still going through, while writing this album.”","cite":"Kang and Kim"},{"t":"p","html":"The album opens with “<strong>Baby’s Breath</strong>,” a tender reflection on devotion inspired by the duo’s own wedding day, while “<strong>Thousand Cranes</strong>” draws from the Japanese tradition of folding paper cranes as a symbol of healing and hope. Tracks like “<strong>Loom</strong>” and “<strong>Versailles</strong>” explore themes of temptation and external pressure, while “<strong>Robin</strong>” captures the fleeting warmth of young summer love and the longing to be truly seen. On “<strong>Serenade</strong>,” the duo confronts fear and vulnerability, asking whether we can move forward despite uncertainty, and “<strong>Looking Glass</strong>” closes the emotional arc with a meditation on love realized over time."},{"t":"p","html":"The influence of legendary composer <strong>Ryuichi Sakamoto</strong> also looms quietly over the record. “He passed away on Paul’s birthday,” they note. “He was on our hearts throughout the entire writing process.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded with a diverse ensemble of collaborators,&nbsp;<em>Origami Hote</em><em>l </em>balances intricate instrumentation with emotional immediacy. The album also features a reimagined cover of <strong>The Smashing Pumpkins'</strong> “<strong>1979</strong>,” further underscoring the duo’s ability to reinterpret nostalgia through their own lens."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/828654/large-36f017a69da6b88b2fedb0aef43f2e39.jpg","alt":"Album Cover - Ayaka Sano"},{"t":"p","html":"Bird x Butterfly’s music has been described as “a photograph you can’t quite place; familiar and unresolved all at once,” a fitting metaphor for a record that lingers in the in-between spaces of memory and feeling."},{"t":"p","html":"With <em>Origami Hotel</em>, Bird x Butterfly offers a debut that is both sonically expansive and emotionally unguarded. A collection of songs that invites listeners not just to hear, but to feel."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Production Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Origami Hotel</em> is anchored by the core performances of Frances Kang (piano, keys, and synths) and Paul Kim (guitars, synths, percussion, and piano), whose multi-instrumental work shapes the album’s intimate yet cinematic sound."},{"t":"p","html":"Across the record, they are joined by a rotating ensemble of collaborators, including drummers <strong>Brendan Tan</strong> and <strong>Evan Hutchings</strong>, and bassists <strong>Sean Hurley</strong> and <strong>Adrian Walther</strong>. Additional textures come from <strong>Benjamin Tennikoff</strong>, <strong>Jesse Dunn</strong>, and <strong>Peter James</strong> on synths and keys."},{"t":"p","html":"The album’s orchestral depth is brought to life through contributions from violinist <strong>Jinty McTavish</strong> and cellist <strong>Genevieve Tabby&nbsp;</strong>-<strong>&nbsp;</strong>both<strong>&nbsp;</strong>a part of<strong>&nbsp;ATLYS String Quartet</strong> - &nbsp;as well as brass and woodwind players <strong>Victor Garcia</strong> (trumpet/flugelhorn), <strong>Eric Brink</strong> (flute/clarinet), <strong>Caleb McMahon</strong> (trombone), and <strong>Ben Roidl-Ward</strong> (bassoon)."},{"t":"p","html":"The special instrumentation by <strong>Tal Vaknine</strong> (harp), <strong>Tokiko Kimura</strong> (koto), and <strong>Sam Wilson</strong> (pedal steel guitar) adds unique tonal color throughout the project."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/828655/large-31d18a394503347f1327251be061da43.jpg","alt":"Photo by Ayaka Sano"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Bird x Butterfly"},{"t":"p","html":"Bird x Butterfly is a Korean-American musical duo based in Chicago. Frances Kang and Paul Kim write and perform together with a rare intimacy: two voices that don’t harmonize so much as merge, becoming something neither could make alone."},{"t":"p","html":"Shaped by years of collaboration, Bird x Butterfly has developed a sound that feels both cinematic and deeply personal. Their music blends singer-songwriter vulnerability with expansive, orchestral textures; strings, synths, and delicate arrangements that frame the quiet intensity at the core of their work. The result is a sonic world that feels like a half-remembered photograph: familiar, nostalgic, and just out of reach."},{"t":"p","html":"Their debut album, Origami Hotel, embodies this sensibility. Built on the idea that life unfolds as a series of emotional rooms, the record moves through moments of love, doubt, grief, and fleeting joy with unguarded honesty. Each track captures a distinct feeling, while together forming a cohesive journey through the fragility and beauty of human connection."},{"t":"p","html":"At the heart of Bird x Butterfly is a shared history, one that informs not only their songwriting, but the way they listen to each other. Their music is less about performance and more about presence: two voices meeting in the same space, holding tension, tenderness, and truth in equal measure."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://birdxbutterfly.com/about/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/birdxbutterfly/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1sgIEgILYuzvQz9OQg7DSn?si=rIS7OwVbTtmrl0BI2D6xeQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"458551","title":"Emerging Black Trans Duo TRANSonic Announce Self-Titled Debut Album","date":"2026-06-26","lead":"A fearless Black trans hip-hop soul statement built on transformation, intimacy, resistance, and joy","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/458551/768408be82bca6cc1eb6bb8f139ee938.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A fearless Black trans hip-hop soul statement built on transformation, intimacy, resistance, and joy"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>(Friday, Jun 26, 2026)</strong> - Emerging Black trans hip-hop soul duo Transonic are set to release their self-titled debut album <em><strong>Transonic</strong></em> on Friday, June 26, 2026. This release is an emotionally expansive, genre-bending project that turns transition into sound."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/65bORB8GXzqQCCHpHGpT0D?utm_source=generator&si=68f7a49edd7f4c93","height":"352"},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/65bORB8GXzqQCCHpHGpT0D?si=lc-_IcaETbGAG_wv_xyfjQ","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Blending hip-hop, alternative soul, smoky intimacy, sharp lyricism, and fearless vulnerability, <em>Transonic</em> is both deeply personal and defiantly communal. Across nine tracks, the duo explore gender, Blackness, love, anxiety, pleasure, ambition, survival, and self-creation with a voice that feels entirely their own."},{"t":"p","html":"From the unapologetic swagger of “<strong>HookJab</strong>” and “<strong>I Need Dat</strong>” to the hazy tenderness of “<strong>Metadicinal</strong>” and “<strong>Heatwave</strong>,” the album moves fluidly between confrontation and comfort. Songs like “<strong>Fly Away With Me</strong>” and “<strong>Transitions_voicememo</strong>” offer some of the project’s most vulnerable moments, confronting mental health, visibility, and the emotional labor of existing while trans in America."},{"t":"p","html":"At its core, <em>Transonic</em> asks listeners a powerful question: have you ever heard yourself change?"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/834480/large-434a4ff3b05419787315084dceae050c.png","alt":"Front Cover Art"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This album is the culmination of life lived unashamedly. Transition is beautifully complicated. It’s expansive. It’s personal. Undefinable. It’s as constant as change. This is that. That is Transonic.”","cite":"Meysha"},{"t":"p","html":"Entirely Black trans-made, the project centers community at every level of creation. From production and songwriting to artwork, mixing, and mastering, <em>Transonic</em> intentionally uplifts the labor, artistry, and vision of Black trans creatives."},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, <em>Transonic</em> feels like “shared intimacy like smoking together - smooth like honey but also in your face speaking with confidence.” The album’s textured production, led by <strong>Korbin Hawkins</strong>, creates a world where sharp bars, soul melodies, weed smoke, bedroom confessions, and political clarity coexist naturally."},{"t":"p","html":"With themes of releasing old patterns, renewed inspiration, and the limitless worlds Black trans people create for themselves, <em>Transonic</em> arrives not only as an album, but as a declaration."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Have you ever heard yourself change? Listened to every audible detail of the shedding of your last self? Yeah. This album for us is just that. And some joy mixed in too.”","cite":"The duo shares."},{"t":"p","html":"Adding to the momentum surrounding the release, Transonic were recently selected by <strong>Tidal</strong> as the featured emerging artist on its <strong>Melodies and Bars</strong> playlist! This marks the duo’s first official playlist placement. The recognition highlights the growing impact of Transonic’s boundary-pushing sound and arrives as an early industry co-sign for a project already resonating through its fearless honesty, sharp lyricism, and genre-defying approach to hip-hop and soul."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/834481/large-3b005641cdeb56beeedc8c0ac4d09a5d.png","alt":"Back Cover Art"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Production: <strong>Korbin Hawkins</strong><br>Album Artwork:<strong> Arien Marley</strong><br>Lyricist/vocalist:<strong> Meysha</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"quote","html":"“There’s quite literally no one like us. We don’t sound like anything you’ve heard before and we invite the world to vibe with us. No need to compare us to any others - listen to us anew.”","cite":"Korbin and Meysha"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Transonic"},{"t":"p","html":"Transonic is a Black trans hip-hop soul duo creating music that feels both radically intimate and impossible to ignore. Blending hip-hop, alternative soul, sharp lyricism, smoky vulnerability, and experimental storytelling, the duo craft songs that move between tenderness, confrontation, pleasure, grief, humor, ambition, and transformation - often all at once."},{"t":"p","html":"Entirely Black trans-made, Transonic’s work centers authenticity at every level of creation. From production and songwriting to visual direction and engineering, the duo intentionally build art rooted in community, self-definition, and liberation. Their sound is fluid and emotionally layered: smooth like honey one moment, razor-sharp the next. Whether delivering confident rap cadences, vulnerable confessions, or hypnotic soul melodies, Transonic refuse easy categorization."},{"t":"p","html":"More than a music project, Transonic is a declaration. One rooted in survival, expansion, and self-invention. Their work speaks directly to people learning how to become themselves in public, while still making space to dance, smoke, laugh, heal, and dream bigger."},{"t":"p","html":"This isn’t music asking for permission.<br>It’s music arriving fully as itself."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/transonicmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5aq0OT6Fbs0Sn7OWpHnrrV?si=qhhWkXOeR5K0Etx3QAEelg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>​"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"461400","title":"Erin Lunsford Shares a Love Letter to Appalachian Roots in New Album \"Rhinestones\"","date":"2026-06-26","lead":"Virginia-based folk-americana artist steps into her own voice with a genre-defying record about love, loss, career, and the complicated pull of home","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/461400/da26797a4603dbf16aa21e140b06d3a4.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Virginia-based folk-americana artist steps into her own voice with a genre-defying record about love, loss, career, and the complicated pull of home"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>RICHMOND, VA (JUNE 26, 2026)</strong> - After five years, a pandemic-derailed debut, and a season of life that handed her more material than she bargained for, <strong>Erin Lunsford</strong> is back. Her sophomore album, <em><strong>Rhinestones </strong></em>(Friday June 26, 2026), arrives as a fully realized artistic statement from an artist who has stopped apologizing for who she is. With a blend of Americana, folk, and pop, the album explores the journey of an unyielding artist.... specifically the painful rejections, the hopeful dreams, and the quiet resilience of staying the course.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3MGBOry0b2Ferz3CO2jLSK?utm_source=generator&si=f5ba9da6c4b044d8","height":"352"},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/3MGBOry0b2Ferz3CO2jLSK?si=8MGPbQl4Sia7mER5S9W-hg","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Where her first record caught Lunsford still searching, <em>Rhinestones</em> finds her with something to say and the skill to say it plainly. A love letter to the artist's Appalachian roots while honoring creativity beyond bluegrass, the album moves through career disappointment, romantic love and loss, family tension, friendship, mental health, and the particular grief of growing up and moving away from a small Appalachian hometown. It is a record that trusts the listener and trusts itself. \"I have fixed rhinestones in my hair, I have glued sequins to my guitar, I have tried to make my body smaller and more socially acceptable, I have bedazzled my music persona for years trying to get my music to the people,\" Lunsford says. \"And I finally let all that rawness and realness come through in the most honest album I've ever made. This album is ultimately an expression of gratitude for my career and how much I love making music for a living.\""},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837173/large-adc627cfb25ff5988be9639c61b4057e.png","alt":"Photography by Aspen DeRosa, Graphic Design by Christina Swanson"},{"t":"quote","html":"The title track, \"Rhinestones,” wades through the troubled headspace that I find myself in when I'm questioning the milestones of my career. I can get caught up in the glamour, the aesthetics, and the perceived success of my music instead of grounding myself in the simple blessing of connecting with others through song. Sometimes the negative self-talk, social media comparisons, impossible double standards for women in music, and spinning wheels make the disappointments feel insurmountable. But every time I perform and am able to share my music with people, I am reminded that my music is a calling and it’s a privilege to make art for a living. The fire to make music burns brightly in my spirit whether or not I fit the narrow industry standard of a star. As an independent woman in music, sometimes \"my rhinestones won't stick, my diamonds won't shine, and my sequins catch in my hair,” but I don’t intend on stopping anytime soon.","cite":"Lunsford explains the purpose behind her title track."},{"t":"p","html":"Resembling a wholesome voyage of return, as well as an adventurous path forward, <em>Rhinestones</em> features extremely personal anecdotes that truly embodies Lunsford as both a person and an artist. With stories spanning from family dysfunction, friendship, mental health, career disappointments, massive heartbreak, romantic achievements, to the complexities of maturing and moving away from a small hometown, the release meticulously captures the nuances of each episode of the artist's life.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/837174/large-bb3fef9ac79ffafb172c7de13b1e3bb6.webp","alt":"Photography by Aspen DeRosa"},{"t":"quote","html":"This album feels like a snapshot of life in my 30’s: we wind through career highs and lows, searching for a romantic love, finding a life partner, fighting and making up with my mom, accepting my identity in a big city while mourning the loss of my quaint hometown ties, and welcoming community and friendship as absolutely vital pillars for my wellbeing.","cite":"Lunsford dives deeper into what this album means to her."},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically speaking, the album is birthed from a combination of pop-folk, singer-songwriter, and country Americana, while featuring influences reminiscent of Kacey Musgraves, Milk Carton Kids, Dolly Parton, Sierra Ferrell, Gillian Welch, Lucy Clearwater, and Watchhouse. Warm and plainspoken, with arrangements that breathe, Lunsford's Appalachian roots anchor every track without confining them. The result is a record that feels like a homecoming and a departure at the same time."},{"t":"p","html":"This marks Lunsford's first major record after her debut album in 2020, and will be the first time her solo music is printed on a vinyl, which is&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.erinlunsford.com/merch/p/pre-order-rhinestones-on-vinyl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">available for pre-order now</a>. The artist will also be hosting three big, full-band release show in Virginia:"},{"t":"p","html":"- <strong>July 11</strong> at <strong>The Spot</strong> on Kirk in Roanoke with Amelia Empson<br>- <strong>July 30</strong> at <strong>Potter's Craft Cider</strong> in Charlottesville, presented by 106.1 The Corner and Pandemonium Air with Sally Rose and Model House<br>- <strong>July 31</strong> at <strong>The Camel</strong> in Richmond featuring Sasha Landon of Palmyra."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits:"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by Jacob Ungerleider and Lunsford herself, <em>Rhinestones</em> was recorded with a full band including Summer Valentine, Ryan Lipps, Stephen Roach, Caroline Vain, Shannon Bielski, Wynton Davis, Morgan Stewart, and Rome Pratt. The record was mixed by Alex DeJong at Spacebomb Studios, with engineering by Curtis Fye and John Trainum, and mastered by Danny Kalb."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Erin Lunsford"},{"t":"p","html":"Erin Lunsford is an award-winning singer-songwriter from Fincastle, Virginia, now based in Richmond, whose work blends Appalachian roots with Americana, folk, and country influences. She has earned praise from NPR Music, \"mesmerizing voice and fantastic vocal technique\" and \"impressive, expressive voice and some serious guitar chops.\" A semi-finalist in the Songwriters Guild of America Country Song Contest for her song “Rhinestones,” Lunsford has built a reputation as a compelling storyteller. Her 2025 run of singles further defined her nostalgic, emotionally rich Americana sound, with Country Music News International calling “Last I Heard” a “meticulously crafted emotional time capsule… a gut-punch of a breakup song,” while The Auricular praised her ability to turn personal misfortune into “universal reflection” with “emotionally brilliant” vocals."},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond songwriting, Lunsford uses her platform to foster community impact. Her single “Strawberries” inspired a regional tour that raised over $16,000 for local food pantries, with Richmond Grid noting her work as “a model of artist-led community organizing… turning release celebrations into opportunities for collective support.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Most widely known for her role as the frontwoman of Erin &amp; The Wildfire featured by Rolling Stone Country as one of the “10 Best Things We Saw at FloydFest”, Lunsford has performed at major festivals and alongside artists such as Maggie Rose, Bruce Hornsby, and The Infamous Stringdusters. With her forthcoming full-length album set for Summer 2026, she continues to emerge as a rising voice in country and Americana, crafting songs that bridge personal storytelling with a deep sense of place and purpose."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/erinlunsfordmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@erinlunsfordmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.erinlunsford.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/erinlunsfordmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@erinlunsfordmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/erinlunsfordmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6VQmzs195HRiyaBhz9JMlv?si=Uy1oWYtGQhODypXZc5kE0Q&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=5b7a850956994217\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"460568","title":"INDVGO Captures the Quiet Tension of a Summer Situationship on New Single \"Slide In\"","date":"2026-06-12","lead":"Brooklyn Alt R&B Artist Returns with Hypnotic Summer Single, Out June 12","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/460568/b8dd6ff8eff7cc81b4311c132c60e0b1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Brooklyn Alt R&amp;B Artist Returns with Hypnotic Summer Single, Out June 12"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>BROOKLYN, NY (June 12, 2026)</strong> — Brooklyn, NY artist INDVGO captures the push and pull of a summer situationship with new song \"<strong>Slide In,</strong>\" releasing <strong>June 12, 2026</strong>, on all major streaming platforms. Hypnotic, sultry, and nocturnal, this Alt-R&amp;B track explores the tension of mixed signals and quiet confidence. \"Slide In\" marks INDVGO's second release of 2026, signaling an active chapter and setting the tone for the warm, emotionally grounded R&amp;B sound listeners can expect in her upcoming projects."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/5PrtXNCBUaDsX8FifhfJWK?si=6fbc9066d2b34143","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"I wanted it to feel like a thought you can't stop replaying, like you already know what's happening between you and somebody, but neither of you are saying it out loud yet. That's the whole energy.","cite":"INDVGO expresses."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Slide In\" heavily focuses on the emotional tension of a situationship in motion: the moment when someone's patterns betrays them before they've verbally admitted their feelings. With lines like \"you decide, you could slide,\" the artist leaves the door open without chasing, delivering calm and self-aware energy that leaves space for the other person to decide. \"Pick a side\" becomes the emotional core of the record, where a playful but direct call for clarity from someone who has already clocked everything."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/834758/large-4859071aa28d959f1035f597e782024a.webp","alt":"Slide_In_-_INDVGO_at7lrp.webp"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Slide In\" carries a looping, replay-heavy production that mirrors the feeling of running a situation back in your head late at night. Sonically inspired by Bryson Tiller, PARTYNEXTDOOR, Drake, SZA, and PnB Rock, INDVGO delivers smooth, atmospheric R&amp;B that is soft on the surface but self-aware and quietly dangerous underneath."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6KhPQmEWZGlpuaJRO7Dk22?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded, Mixed, and Mastered: Jorelle Montes&nbsp;<br>Producer: februxry"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About INDVGO"},{"t":"p","html":"INDVGO is an alternative R&amp;B artist from Brooklyn, NY known for balancing soulful and cinematic noir influences. Her music centers around themes of emotional restraint, narcissistic relationships, and self-awareness, resonating with listeners by creating a sanctuary for thoughts to unfold."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/61Se7XU0y8Gi4T64t1nfMA?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with INDVGO <a href=\"https://beacons.ai/indvgo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</strong>"}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"458331","title":"Reese Weil Teams Up with Nef The Pharaoh and Derek King for New West Coast Anthem “High Rise”","date":"2026-06-05","lead":"Northern California artist blends melodic pop and West Coast hip-hop on a groove-driven new release.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/458331/f161993c3cd844cd0bf315245cb8865e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Northern California artist blends melodic pop and West Coast hip-hop on a groove-driven new release."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>CHICO, CA (June 5, 2026)</strong> - Rising artist <strong>Reese Weil</strong> joins forces with Bay Area heavyweight <strong>Nef The Pharaoh</strong> and melodic hitmaker <strong>Derek King</strong> for the release of their new single “<strong>High Rise</strong>,” arriving everywhere on Friday, June 5, 2026."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/4B3CsgVnlofRlnbhbErA8W?si=d6815e72f13948c6","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/830952/large-7f1064deb6edeedf6c6968cedab28624.jpg","alt":"Cover Art by Dana Hocking"},{"t":"p","html":"Blending alternative hip hop, melodic rap, and late-night West Coast energy, “High Rise” captures the feeling of escaping into the moment; rooftop parties, city lights, luxury romance, and the freedom that comes alive after dark. Built around Reese Weil’s hypnotic hook and layered with sweeping basslines, melodic guitars, and polished vocals, the single delivers a crossover sound that feels equally at home in Bay Area nightlife and mainstream radio playlists."},{"t":"p","html":"“High Rise” began with Reese Weil in Chico, California, crafting a song centered around feeling fully alive in the nighttime atmosphere. The record quickly evolved into a multi-city West Coast collaboration, with Derek King bringing smooth confidence and luxury romance to the track while Nef The Pharaoh injects his signature Bay Area charisma, humor, and high-energy swagger."},{"t":"p","html":"Together, the three artists create a soundtrack for nights that feel endless - balancing celebration, loyalty, friendship, ambition, and carefree living into one cohesive record."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/830953/large-f1de6d507d71cd729d3f5b3bc4614a6f.jpg","alt":"Artwork by Dana Hocking"},{"t":"quote","html":"“High Rise is about freedom to do what you need to do when you need to do it and feeling alive at the same time.”","cite":"Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"“High Rise” is a vibe comparable to the crossover appeal of <strong>G-Eazy</strong> and <strong>E-40</strong> with the melodic accessibility of <strong>Maroon 5</strong>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Main Artist: <strong>Reese Weil&nbsp;</strong><br id=\"isPasted\">Main Artist: <strong>Nef The Pharaoh</strong><br>Featured Artist: <strong>Derek King</strong><br>Producer: <strong>Dana Hocking&nbsp;</strong><br>Mastering Engineer: <strong>Carter Boy</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Artwork &amp; Photography: <strong>Dana Hocking</strong> &amp; <strong>Reese Weil</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/830951/large-e2c9280b05b508e050f531a16e07e708.jpg","alt":"Reese Weil"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"Reese Weil is a Northern California born artist, songwriter, and producer whose genre-blending sound bridges West Coast hip-hop, melodic pop, and alternative rock. Known for smooth, breathy vocals and groove-driven production, Weil crafts music that feels both laid-back and polished which captures the spirit of California while reaching a global audience."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil’s musical journey began early. At just four years old, he picked up a guitar in his hometown of Chico, California, laying the foundation for a lifelong dedication to songwriting and performance. His talent and work ethic eventually earned him a scholarship to the prestigious Berklee College of Music, where he refined his skills in music production, composition, and modern songwriting. The experience helped shape the versatile creative voice that defines his work today."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil has built an impressive list of accomplishments. He has opened for The Wailers, the legendary band associated with Bob Marley, and contributed songwriting for international pop icon Enrique Iglesias. His music has also found a home on television, with placements on series such as Bones and Twisted. In addition, his work has been published through the music company Pulse Music Group, further expanding his reach as a songwriter and producer."},{"t":"p","html":"With a growing catalog, high-profile collaborations, and a steadily expanding fan base, Reese Weil continues to carve out his place as a dynamic modern artist. His music brings an energy designed for stages, screens, and playlists around the world."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reeseweilmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Zi3EV89aof6OMz8SHTxDN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>​"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"457139","title":"Erin Lunsford Shares Vulnerable New Single “Name So Pretty”","date":"2026-05-29","lead":"RICHMOND, VA (May 29, 2026) - Richmond-based singer-songwriter Erin Lunsford returns with her latest single, “Name So Pretty”. Blending elements of pop, folk, and country, the track delivers an intimate yet expansive sonic landscape. Anchored by acoustic guitar, laid-bac...","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/457139/b9b579381fd13019a885b97ba5828b50.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"p","html":"<strong>RICHMOND, VA (May 29, 2026)</strong> - Richmond-based singer-songwriter <strong>Erin Lunsford</strong> returns with her latest single, “<strong>Name So Pretty</strong>”. Blending elements of pop, folk, and country, the track delivers an intimate yet expansive sonic landscape. Anchored by acoustic guitar, laid-back vocals, and a swelling full-band arrangement that blooms into a celestial, groove-driven finish."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/1NzAGkIy9lKXdr3WosXkh9?si=c1677689d4d941d3","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Drawing sonic comparisons to artists like <strong>Kacey Musgraves</strong>, <strong>Lana Del Rey</strong>, <strong>Rayland Baxter</strong>, <strong>Hannah Cohen</strong>, and <strong>Maggie Rogers</strong>, “Name So Pretty” captures a delicate balance between introspective songwriting and lush, immersive production."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/829492/large-4d1ab76e8120c3bb1eae003e4f898274.jpg","alt":"Photo by Aspen DeRosa"},{"t":"quote","html":"'Name So Pretty' is one of the most vulnerable songs on the record, for me. I explore a complicated web of an argument I had with my mom while fighting the urge to revert to my child self both lyrically and emotionally,”","cite":"Lunsford"},{"t":"p","html":"At its core, the song explores the emotional complexities of family relationships; specifically the tension between personal growth and generational perspectives. Inspired by a real-life argument with her mother, Lunsford channels themes of body positivity, boundaries, and the struggle to be understood."},{"t":"p","html":"While rooted in familial conflict, the song’s accompanying visual takes a creative turn, reframing the narrative through a romantic lens. The music video centers on a queer love story set in a local garden center, marking the first time Lunsford publicly shares her bisexuality through her art."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/829493/large-6bc219c05bbcf0819cc82645061980ab.jpg","alt":"Photo by Aspen DeRosa"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wrote this one about an argument I had with my mom about body positivity and boundaries and it was brutal! So I had to make the music video about my bisexuality and shift away from the depressing family dynamic.”","cite":"Lunsford"},{"t":"p","html":"This layered storytelling transforms “Name So Pretty” into both a personal confession and a broader meditation on identity, autonomy, and emotional growth."},{"t":"p","html":"“Name So Pretty” navigates the fragile terrain of mother-daughter relationships, generational divides, and the process of outgrowing familial expectations. With poignant lyricism and evocative imagery - “It’s not her garden, definitely not her weeds” - Lunsford captures the push and pull between love and independence, vulnerability and self-definition."},{"t":"p","html":"The single serves as the final release ahead of Lunsford’s forthcoming album, due June 26, 2026."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/829494/large-63e5ab3e1b1b3ab3adecafce06e8aae1.jpg","alt":"Photo by Aspen DeRosa"},{"t":"h3","html":"Production Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Producer: <strong>Erin Lunsford </strong><br>Performed by: <strong>Summer Valentine</strong>, <strong>Ryan Lipps</strong>, <strong>Stephen Roach</strong>, <strong>Erin Lunsford</strong>, and <strong>Wynton Davis</strong><br>Mastered by:<strong>&nbsp;Danny Kalb</strong><br>Mixed by: <strong>Alex DeJong</strong>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Visual Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Photo &amp; Video: <strong>Aspen DeRosa</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/829495/large-bc9020d3b99feb3743eb3880a5a86512.jpg","alt":"Photo by Aspen DeRosa"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Erin Lunsford"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Erin Lunsford</strong> is an award-winning singer-songwriter from Fincastle, Virginia, now based in Richmond, whose work blends Appalachian roots with Americana, folk, and country influences. She has earned praise from <strong>NPR Music:</strong>"},{"t":"quote","html":"mesmerizing voice and fantastic vocal technique","cite":"NPR Music"},{"t":"p","html":"and"},{"t":"quote","html":"impressive, expressive voice and some serious guitar chops","cite":"NPR Music"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>A semi-finalist in the Songwriters Guild of America Country Song Contest</strong> for her song “Rhinestones,” Lunsford has built a reputation as a compelling storyteller. Her 2025 run of singles further defined her nostalgic, emotionally rich Americana sound, with Country Music News International calling “Last I Heard” a “meticulously crafted emotional time capsule… a gut-punch of a breakup song,” while The Auricular praised her ability to turn personal misfortune into “universal reflection” with “emotionally brilliant” vocals."},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond songwriting, Lunsford uses her platform to foster community impact. Her single “Strawberries” inspired a regional tour that <strong>raised over $16,000</strong> for local food pantries, with Richmond Grid noting her work as “a model of artist-led community organizing… turning release celebrations into opportunities for collective support.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Formerly the frontwoman of Erin &amp; The Wildfire featured by <strong>Rolling Stone Country as one of the “10 Best Things We Saw at FloydFest”</strong>, Lunsford has performed at major festivals and alongside artists such as <strong>Maggie Rose, Bruce Hornsby, and The Infamous Stringdusters</strong>. With her forthcoming full-length album set for Summer 2026, she continues to emerge as a rising voice in country and Americana, crafting songs that bridge personal storytelling with a deep sense of place and purpose."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Erin Lunsford</strong>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/erinlunsfordmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@erinlunsfordmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://www.erinlunsford.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/erinlunsfordmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@erinlunsfordmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/erinlunsfordmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6VQmzs195HRiyaBhz9JMlv?si=Uy1oWYtGQhODypXZc5kE0Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"459586","title":"Glass Dream Teases New Release And Reveals Behind-the-Scenes of ‘Tonight, Forever’.","date":"2026-05-27","lead":"Glass Dream unveils the story behind the atmospheric EP while previewing the next chapter of its darkly cinematic sound.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/459586/bd71a485fd2976d06e4ec2088c94ecf1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Glass Dream unveils the story behind the atmospheric EP while previewing the next chapter of its darkly cinematic sound."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ATLANTA, GA&nbsp;</strong>(March 31, 2026) - Atlanta native <strong>Glass Dream&nbsp;</strong>steps into the spotlight with EP <em><strong>Tonight, Forever</strong></em>. These powerful and deeply emotional new tracks blur the lines between indie rock, dream pop, shoegaze, and electronic noir. It is a mix of release and challenge, offering a preview of their upcoming debut album, set for release later this year."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/2WfBGU5s09CuNXzAFlp6l8?si=fvUCcGViR6KWzjk3-mTqlw","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Constructed using various layers of gleaming synthesizers, cinematic guitars, and heartfelt vocal performance, <em>Tonight, Forever</em> captures the emotional intensity of musicians such as <strong>M83</strong>, <strong>Slowdive</strong>, <strong>Beach House</strong>, <strong>The Antlers</strong>, and <strong>Radiohead</strong> while establishing a unique sound of its own - a genre Glass Dream refers to as “synthgaze” or “nightmare pop.”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/835726/large-9170d3fd0324fd7158f5d529a122f0a6.jpg","alt":"03.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"Originally conceived from demos recorded nearly a decade ago in a storage unit outside <strong>Athens, Georgia,</strong> the music behind <em>Tonight, Forever</em> and the forthcoming album remained buried &nbsp;for years as its creator struggled with anxiety, depression, addiction, and personal upheaval. Following a period marked by loss, displacement, and eventual sobriety, Glass Dream revisited the material through a radically different emotional lens."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2WfBGU5s09CuNXzAFlp6l8?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“These songs lived in the shadows for a long time. I was too scared of being judged, too scared of my thoughts and feelings being an open book for anyone to read. The creation of this album became part of my therapy. This record represents not only my rebirth as a person, but also my rebirth and introduction as an artist.”","cite":"Glass Dream"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Tonight, Forever</em> stands as the emotional centerpiece of that transformation. Pulsing with desperation and vulnerability beneath arena-sized instrumentation, the EP captures the tension between collapse and redemption."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/835727/large-8039de0e072929fe1a66b646c970cf8d.jpg","alt":"08.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"Too ominous to be dream pop and too synth-driven to fit neatly into shoegaze, Glass Dream occupies a liminal space between beauty and dread. Across <em>Tonight, Forever</em>, towering walls of sound collide with intimate confessions, pulling listeners through themes of alienation, mental health, substance abuse, and recovery before ultimately arriving somewhere hopeful... or at least honest."},{"t":"p","html":"Written and recorded entirely by Glass Dream and mixed/mastered by Ben Etter at Maze Studios in Atlanta, the forthcoming LP transforms deeply personal trauma into widescreen emotional release. The result is music that feels simultaneously familiar and alien: melancholic but massive, dark yet deeply human."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I hope this resonates with anyone who has struggled mentally or battled addiction.”","cite":"Glass Dream"},{"t":"p","html":"“Tonight, Forever” is available now."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/835728/large-304dca70af432a201de987f73f4ddc3d.jpg","alt":"07.jpg"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Written and Recorded by: <strong>Glass Dream</strong><br>Mixed and Mastered by: <strong>Ben Etter</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2IYe4cBSWi3e87v0iIsj1T?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Glass Dream"},{"t":"p","html":"Glass Dream is the solo project of an Atlanta via New York-based multi-instrumentalist crafting immersive, emotionally charged music from the darker corners of electronically driven indie rock. Glass Dream exists somewhere in a sound the artist describes as “synthgaze” or “nightmare pop.”"},{"t":"p","html":"The origins of the project trace back nearly a decade to a storage unit on the outskirts of Athens, Georgia, where the earliest demos for what would eventually become the debut album were first recorded. Though the songs remained hidden for years, life continued to unravel in the background. Long stretches of unfulfilling office jobs, mounting anxiety and depression, and escalating alcohol and substance abuse gradually pushed music further away. An apartment fire, a series of personal losses, and an overwhelming confrontation with mortality eventually culminated in a mental breakdown marked by existential dread and emotional collapse."},{"t":"p","html":"Following a stint in rehab in 2025 and encouragement through therapy, the artist behind Glass Dream returned to the abandoned demos with a renewed sense of purpose. Re-recorded and rewritten through the lens of sobriety, recovery, and self-examination, the songs evolved into a deeply personal exploration of mental health, addiction, impermanence, and healing."},{"t":"p","html":"What emerged was not only the completion of a ten-song debut LP, but a creative rebirth. Through towering synths, expansive guitars, and intimate lyricism, Glass Dream transforms years of buried emotion into cathartic, widescreen indie rock that feels both haunting and profoundly human."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://aidanleclaire.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"></a><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/glass_dream_band/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2IYe4cBSWi3e87v0iIsj1T?si=towlAPLGRhu_OgvYPPCW6A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"458844","title":"Aidan Leclaire Captures the Chaos of Young Love on “Lucy”","date":"2026-05-22","lead":"An upbeat indie-pop track with deeper themes of identity, ambition, and connection beneath its carefree surface.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/458844/7214e70b61d078c73eeb26079ab534f2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An upbeat indie-pop track with deeper themes of identity, ambition, and connection beneath its carefree surface."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Vienna, VA (May 22, 2026)&nbsp;</strong>- Northern Virginia indie-pop artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aidan Leclaire</strong></a> returns with “<strong>Lucy</strong>,” a vibrant yet emotionally layered alt-pop single arriving May 22, 2026. Blending sunny hooks, carefree summer-night energy, and introspective lyricism, “Lucy” explores the emotional push-and-pull of modern relationships and self-discovery through an infectious indie-rock lens."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/0DhP1a8MxJebVB8BuonChS?si=9cdc9a3c8a3e4dd4","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Written collaboratively by Aidan Leclaire and band member <strong>Izzy Vega</strong>, “Lucy” reflects on the complexities of trying to establish identity, ambition, and emotional connection all at once."},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, “Lucy” channels the melodic immediacy of modern alt-pop while drawing influence from indie-rock staples like <strong>Arctic Monkeys</strong> and the emotionally candid songwriting tradition of <strong>Joni Mitchell</strong>. The track’s repeated “uh!” refrain gives the song a loose, carefree spirit that mirrors the feeling of late-night city adventures and fleeting summer romance."},{"t":"p","html":"Built around shimmering guitars, driving percussion, and an effortlessly memorable vocal refrain, “Lucy” balances polished indie-pop production with the rawness of live-band chemistry. The track moves with the energy of a spontaneous night out while subtly revealing deeper emotional tensions beneath the surface. That contrast between brightness and uncertainty gives the song much of its emotional weight."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831654/compressed_original-410e4cf34bc10815b3cb3531daad5626.jpg","alt":"Photo by Aidan"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song is about today’s dating environment and the challenge of balancing a relationship while trying to establish a place for yourself in the world while also going through a self-discovery process. It’s not necessarily a new struggle, but I think this generation is more conscious of that interplay and more expressive about it.”","cite":"Leclaire says"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831657/large-4ea36903e703da61ef38b6f5ccb6962b.jpg","alt":"God Boy - Colin.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831657/preview-4c0180739a34e8885cbbfcd9e832a53d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831658/large-eb8a8ae2da114b9a9cdfc0aa44dca4d3.jpg","alt":"Good Boy - Izzy.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831658/preview-202e06a0cdc6239e8bcaded481fe287b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831659/large-58a843f96f89fc6fe59370a257d292db.jpg","alt":"Colin.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831659/preview-8115dc6abbb433c3211a91ba440c156d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831660/large-7beb947e321d228ebc11f099fd4b0356.jpg","alt":"Figure 8 - 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831660/preview-0c97125d12f16099c0464c1e0cea317e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831661/large-62a60129543a2056047177175568a189.jpg","alt":"Good Boy - Will.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831661/preview-fe7ceffce8fa832f669fd3a0db8ca5a9.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"The release arrives as Aidan Leclaire continues to gain momentum as a live act throughout the East Coast indie circuit. Known for energetic performances and a growing grassroots fanbase, the band has steadily expanded its reach through word-of-mouth buzz, emotionally charged sets, and a collaborative stage presence that translates the intimacy of the recordings into a larger communal experience."},{"t":"p","html":"With “Lucy,” Aidan Leclaire further establishes himself as one of the emerging young voices in the indie scene. An artist capable of pairing accessible hooks with thoughtful songwriting and emotionally grounded storytelling. As anticipation continues to build around the band’s growing live presence, “Lucy” signals another confident step forward in Leclaire’s evolution as both a songwriter and performer."},{"t":"p","html":"Leclaire is currently working on a forthcoming album set for release later this year, continuing the emotionally honest songwriting and energetic indie-pop sound showcased on “Lucy.” More details will be announced soon."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Written by: <strong>Aidan Leclaire</strong> &amp; <strong>Izzy Vega</strong><br id=\"isPasted\">Guitar, Drums, and Bass: <strong>Izzy Vega<br></strong>Additional Guitar: <strong>David McCallum</strong><br>Recorded, Produced, Mixed:<strong>&nbsp;Ben Green</strong> at Ivakota Studios&nbsp;<br>Mastered by: <strong>Gabi GrellaCover</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Art/photo by: <strong>Babak Yektafar</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/831656/large-38a1b9a6f6cc8f1c9685d3ede1ede788.jpg","alt":"Photo by Aidan"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Aidan Leclaire"},{"t":"p","html":"Aidan Leclaire is a Northern Virginia singer-songwriter crafting indie rock and alt-pop songs rooted in emotional honesty, sharp songwriting, and energetic live performance. Influenced by artists ranging from Arctic Monkeys to Joni Mitchell, Leclaire combines introspective storytelling with infectious hooks and modern indie production."},{"t":"p","html":"Leclaire first emerged in the Washington, DC-area music scene in 2023, performing throughout Northern Virginia, Maryland, and DC before forming the band that now backs his live performances. Over the last year, the group has cultivated a growing regional audience across DC, Richmond, Boston, and New York, selling more than 600 tickets across their last four local shows, including two sellouts."},{"t":"p","html":"In July 2025, the band released their debut album, <em>Hail to the Dogs</em>, earning praise from indie music outlets including<strong>&nbsp;Indie Boulevard</strong>, which described the project as “intelligent, thoughtful, and thoroughly engaging,” while noting it “positions Aidan Leclaire firmly within today’s indie-rock landscape.”"},{"t":"p","html":"While Leclaire writes and produces the material, the band plays a central role in shaping the arrangements and translating the songs into dynamic live performances that continue to resonate with audiences and tastemakers alike."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://aidanleclaire.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> |<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/the_leclaires\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">&nbsp;Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"454277","title":"Melissa D’s “Songbird” Is a Gentle Rebellion Against the Noise of Modern Life","date":"2026-05-15","lead":"A Gentle Anthem for Daydreamers, Nature Lovers, and Quiet Rebels","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/454277/f985dd4ac569d66373a3f31b4cf43389.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A Gentle Anthem for Daydreamers, Nature Lovers, and Quiet Rebels"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>MIDDLEBURY, VT (May 15, 2026)</strong> - Independent folk-pop artist Melissa D (Melissa Durkee Moorhouse) announces the release of her new single, “Songbird,” arriving May 15, 2026. Rooted in the lush landscapes of Vermont’s Green Mountains, the track is a soothing, nature-infused reflection on self-trust, renewal, and the quiet power of one’s inner voice."},{"t":"button","href":"https://melissadsings.bandcamp.com/track/songbird","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Known for creating “songs for daydreamers &amp; gentle rebels,” Melissa D continues to carve a deeply personal and independent path. A classically trained vocalist, her musical journey has spanned from fronting the rock band The Alley Katz to collaborating on the folk-rock project CHILL. Since 2016, she has focused on releasing solo work from her rural New England home, choosing an intentional, soul-driven approach over traditional industry routes."},{"t":"p","html":"Despite working without a label or major promotional backing, Melissa’s music has resonated with thousands of listeners worldwide and has been featured on outlets such as Vermont Public, Women of Substance Radio, and Sip-N-Stream. Her song “Little Girl” earned a nomination for Best Song of America (American Roots) at the 2021 InterContinental Music Awards."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/824548/large-aff95841a26525a38353493f10de4c68.jpg","alt":"Arielle Thomas Photography"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The more I watched and listened, the more I realized this song wasn’t just about the bird—it was about remembering my own voice.”","cite":"Melissa D"},{"t":"p","html":"“Songbird” is a gently transportive, nature-soaked track inspired by the wood thrush and its return to Vermont each spring. Through vivid sensory details and poetic imagery, the song invites listeners into a quiet moment of wonder and connection with the natural world. Unfolding like a soft conversation between human and bird, it blends curiosity, admiration, and introspection."},{"t":"p","html":"Written during a period of personal reflection, the song became a pathway back to presence and self-trust. At its heart, “Songbird” serves as both a tribute to nature and a tender reclaiming of one’s own voice."},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, the track features warm, expressive vocals layered over acoustic guitar, mandolin, viola, and silky percussion. The sound is delicate yet grounded—evoking a sense of calm, like sitting on a back deck watching birds drift through the sky. With subtle hints of classic vocal warmth and an intimate folk sensibility, “Songbird” offers a lilting, daydream-like listening experience."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/824549/large-0fe594499d6f1239cabb5b19ae94fa7e.jpg","alt":"Arielle Thomas Photography"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I started ‘Songbird’ on my back deck, cloud-watching when a bird flew so close overhead I could hear this subtle whip sound as the wings were flapping. That moment sparked everything.”","cite":"Melissa D"},{"t":"p","html":"Melissa D’s work is rooted in her identity as “The Daydreamer”, an artist who creates for introspective listeners, quiet creatives, and those seeking refuge from the noise of hustle culture. Her music celebrates sensitivity, imagination, and emotional depth, offering a sense of belonging to those who often feel out of place in louder spaces.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond music, Melissa has dedicated over 20 years to public service as a counselor and advocate, alongside ongoing commitments to animal rescue and humanitarian causes."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/824550/large-41a6db10751d97f541466a8309753285.jpg","alt":"Arielle Thomas Photography"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"list","items":["Vocals: Melissa D","Produced by: Colin McCaffrey","Harmony Vocals: Marianne Donahue Perchlik","Written by: Melissa D Moorhouse (BMI Publishing)","Cover Art: Jason Bemis","Photography: Arielle Thomas"]},{"t":"p","html":"This project is supported in part by the Vermont Arts Council and the Vermont Community Foundation."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"With “Songbird,” Melissa D invites listeners to slow down, reconnect with nature, and rediscover the quiet strength of their own inner rhythm, a timely message of radical joy, self-care, and gentle rebellion."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/824551/large-c9d28b0ce8672a5ca4ed3eb5cfa1035d.jpg","alt":"Arielle Thomas Photography"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Melissa Durkee Moorhouse"},{"t":"p","html":"Melissa Durkee Moorhouse, known artistically as Melissa D, hails from the rolling hills of rustic Vermont, USA. Her music is earthy, chill, and holistic. It's perfect for those seeking calm, connection, and a touch of lighthearted fun."},{"t":"p","html":"A classically trained vocalist, Melissa’s journey spans from fronting the rock band The Alley Katz, where she shared the stage with musicians like Joe Moore (Pork Tornado: Jon Fishman of Phish) and Benjamin Orr (The Cars), to co-creating the folk-rock collaboration CHILL with Michael Cressey"},{"t":"p","html":"Since 2016, Melissa has quietly forged her own musical path, recording and releasing her solo work from her small rural home in New England. Partnering with producers Clint Bierman (The Grift), Kristina Stykos, Phil Henry and most recently Colin McCaffrey, she has chosen to bypass the traditional industry grind, big tours, record deals, and relocation in favor of an independent, soul-driven approach."},{"t":"p","html":"Despite no label, corporate sponsorship, or major promotion, Melissa D's soothing, heartfelt songs have reached thousands of listeners worldwide. Her music has been featured on Vermont Public, Women of Substance Radio, and Sip-N-Stream, among others. Her song “Little Girl” (the title track from her solo EP) was nominated for Best Song of America (American Roots genre) in the 2021 InterContinental Music Awards."},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond music, Melissa is deeply committed to animal rescue and humanitarian causes. She dedicated 20 years to public service as a counselor and advocate, making a lasting impact on countless lives."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://melissadmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/melissadsings/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@melissadsings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Youtube</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"453262","title":"“Shifting Gears”: Kenny Hotopp Reflects on Change, Sobriety, and Self-Discovery in New Video","date":"2026-05-13","lead":"Americana artist Kenny Hotopp pairs introspective songwriting with striking visuals in his new music video “Shifting Gears,” a compelling portrait of personal change and creative renewal.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/453262/74ea54146f26fe441a3ab619b977d48f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Americana artist Kenny Hotopp pairs introspective songwriting with striking visuals in his new music video “Shifting Gears,” a compelling portrait of personal change and creative renewal."},{"t":"p","html":"WATERFORD, WI (May 12, 2026) - &nbsp;Americana folk-soul artist <strong>Kenny Hotopp</strong> will release the official music video for his new single <strong>“Shifting Gears”</strong> on May 12, delivering a deeply personal and visually intimate reflection on growth, sobriety, and self-discovery. Blending raw storytelling with warm, Nashville-inspired tones, the song captures a pivotal moment of change and clarity in Hotopp’s life."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/PpTqxLL29ns","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"The video offers a unique, day-in-the-life perspective, beginning with quiet morning scenes filmed over coffee at Hotopp’s home before shifting into live concert footage captured later that evening during a performance in Milwaukee. This contrast between the everyday and the stage highlights both the human side of being an artist and the emotional release that music provides. The result is an authentic visual narrative that mirrors the song’s themes of transition and renewal."},{"t":"p","html":"“Shifting Gears” is a relaxed yet powerful Americana track that leans into reflection while pushing forward with purpose. Written during a period of personal reassessment, the song was inspired by a milestone birthday and the realization that it was time to make meaningful life changes. Influenced in part by seeing musical heroes embrace sobriety and reach new creative heights, Hotopp channeled that spirit into a song about letting go, moving on, and rediscovering oneself."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/823245/large-6016ae6d766f31488819fa55e137da37.jpg","alt":"Image from \"Shifting Gears\" music video"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Last year I hit a milestone birthday which led me to reflect on where I was at in my life and what comes next. I also saw so many of my musical heroes stepping into sobriety and reaching new creative heights. That inspired me to make changes of my own—it was time to level up and shift gears.”","cite":"– Kenny Hotopp"},{"t":"p","html":"With its easy groove, soulful chord progressions, and heartfelt delivery, “Shifting Gears” carries the essence of the Nashville sound while staying grounded in modern Americana storytelling. Lyrics like <em>“Now I’m shifting gears / My sight lines clear / On where it is that I need to be”</em> reinforce the song’s core message of clarity, release, and personal evolution."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/823246/large-2eac3ea713ba56ca3e7eaccfef55e309.jpg","alt":"Image from \"Shifting Gears\" music video"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This is a heartfelt song about finding yourself again. It’s rooted in that classic Nashville sound, but it’s really about personal evolution. Sometimes you have to let go of what’s holding you back to discover who you really are.”","cite":"- Kenny Hotopp"},{"t":"p","html":"The single is part of an upcoming 12-song album that continues to explore themes of reflection, resilience, and renewal, blending elements of Americana, folk, and soul into a cohesive and emotionally resonant collection. The music video was filmed and produced by Chad Hensiak and Drake Hensiak of CAH Promotions, LLC, capturing both the intimacy and energy that define Hotopp’s artistry."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/823247/large-d5710faf2840c1a41d2e3594803f2af0.jpg","alt":"Image from \"Shifting Gears\" music video"},{"t":"h2","html":"About Kenny Hotopp:"},{"t":"p","html":"Based in Waterford, Wisconsin, Kenny Hotopp writes and sings soul-felt songs about family, love, memory, and the lifelong search for peace. His music blends genres from Americana and folk to blues and country but always centers on authenticity, heart, and lived experience. Every track is a story, every lyric an invitation to connect."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5TqcNmIwGgh7URsT0DvZ09?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Kenny Hotopp</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://kennyhotopp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/kenny_hotopp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=10234333295046619&amp;set=a.10201021262586627\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"457822","title":"Micah Edwards Brings the 'Texas Soul Tour' Home This Fall - With Rising Country Star Madeline Edwards in Houston","date":"2026-05-12","lead":"Edwards - who has logged 150M+ streams and two Grand Ole Opry appearances - launches a multiple-city Texas run behind his debut album Texas Soul, with a landmark Houston show alongside his sister, country breakout Madeline Edwards","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/457822/14aab0b2a282f3cdc1acf0bfb0785f0c.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Edwards - who has logged 150M+ streams and two Grand Ole Opry appearances - launches a multiple-city Texas run behind his debut album <em><strong>Texas Soul</strong></em><strong>,</strong> with a landmark Houston show alongside his sister, country breakout Madeline Edwards"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>HOUSTON, TX (May 2026)&nbsp;</strong>- Houston songwriter <strong>Micah Edwards</strong> is coming home. This fall, Edwards launches the <a href=\"https://www.mrtexassoul.com/tour\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Texas Soul&nbsp;</em>Tour</strong></a>, a fourteen-city run across the state - Houston, Austin, Fort Worth, Dallas, and San Antonio - behind his debut album <a href=\"https://too.fm/er3r14a?utm_source=ig&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_content=link_in_bio&amp;fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQMMjU2MjgxMDQwNTU4AAGn39COGDf2S0tdY4QVU-HMYBoIWDu8zlcNbe4BwTgYJp6Xgu8_VvJmbWvJ4rA_aem_lyVopUhDPbkdJ43A9Ywquw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Texas Soul</em></strong></a>, out now on all major platforms. The tour's most anticipated stop is Houston, where Edwards will share the stage with his sister <a href=\"https://www.madelineedwardsmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Madeline Edwards</strong></a>, one of country music's fastest-rising stars. As Micah has been carving his own lane in the space where country, soul, and borderland Texas music meet, the Houston show brings both artists to the same stage for what promises to be one of the most talked-about Texas music moments of the fall. It's a homecoming show and a family affair - a rare opportunity to see two siblings at pivotal moments in their careers, on their home turf."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/830252/large-7b8317c16dcb14aeba041d9bc4f9fc20.jpg","alt":"Micah Edwards - SQUARE.jpg"},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.mrtexassoul.com/tour","label":"Tour Tickets + Info","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Texas Soul</em> is not a genre experiment - it's a recognition. Edwards grew up between California and Houston, half Black and half white, and spent years learning that Texas music has always resisted easy categories. Honky-tonks, soul clubs, borderland boleros, Hill Country dance halls: the state has long been a crossroads where country and R&amp;B exist as neighbors, not rivals. Edwards makes that collision feel inevitable. The album - produced with <strong>Kendrick Ballard</strong>, <strong>Anthony Farrell</strong>, <strong>Jack Gulielmetti</strong>, <strong>Cameron Jaymes</strong>, and <strong>Andrew Trube</strong> - moves from rockabilly to '60s R&amp;B to '80s country, with pedal steel drifting across jazz chord progressions and horn sections swelling beneath Americana storytelling. Each side of the vinyl is named after a Texas community that shaped Edwards' life: <strong>Pasadena</strong> (once home to Gilley's, the world's largest honky-tonk), <strong>Concan</strong> (on the Frio River), <strong>Mission</strong> (in the Rio Grande Valley), and <strong>Galveston</strong>, where Edwards married his wife and filmed his first music video."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/prerelease/5mpcUWtIA2DbXaOj2HL0UV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“When I say 'Texas Soul' is a spectrum, I mean it. This record moves from boleros to rockabilly, from ’60s R&amp;B to ’80s country, and somehow it all still feels like the same story. Texas has always been a crossroads, and I wanted the album to sound like that - wide, textured, and big enough to hold all of it.”","cite":"- Micah Edwards"},{"t":"button","href":"https://too.fm/er3r14a?utm_source=ig&amp;amp;utm_medium=social&amp;amp;utm_content=link_in_bio&amp;amp;fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQMMjU2MjgxMDQwNTU4AAGn39COGDf2S0tdY4QVU-HMYBoIWDu8zlcNbe4BwTgYJp6Xgu8_VvJmbWvJ4rA_aem_lyVopUhDPbkdJ43A9Ywquw","label":"Listen on All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Texas Soul</em> is as fluid and diverse as the state it calls home. It’s butter and twang, pine and stone - a sound as vast and textured as Texas itself. “It’s falling in love under neon lights in a honky-tonk - equal parts sultry and steel, leather and lace,” Edwards explains. Across the album, Edwards balances sweeping themes with deeply personal storytelling. <strong>“Partner in Crime”&nbsp;</strong>captures a road-worn kind of romance rooted in loyalty and escape, while <strong>“River Man”&nbsp;</strong>leans into summer memories in the Texas Hill Country - where river days stretch long and dance floors come alive at night. At the center of it all, the title track <strong>“Texas Soul”</strong> serves as a defining statement - blending country, soul, and borderland influences into a sound that reflects both identity and place. “It’s meant to feel familiar, like coming home.”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817597/large-64b09c1d2f57f78274fe03603c1f328f.png","alt":"Cover art for 'Texas Soul'"},{"t":"p","html":"Edwards is not a newcomer. He has accumulated <strong>over 150 million streams</strong> on Spotify and Apple Music, earned spots on Spotify editorial playlists including All New Country, Retro Soul, and Soul 'n' the City, and made two guest appearances at the <strong>Grand Ole Opry</strong> in 2025. Earlier this year, he sold out headline shows in Houston, Austin, and Dallas before the album even officially dropped. He's shared stages with <strong>JOHNNYSWIM, The War &amp; Treaty, Saint Motel, and Mac Ayres</strong>, and is a Salt Lick Incubator grant winner and <strong>Tiny Desk Contest Top Shelf artist</strong>. The album itself was crowdfunded in under 30 days, raising over $30,000 from fans - a rare signal of grassroots demand in an era of algorithmic discovery. <em>Texas Soul</em> arrived after a multi-year creative journey that included two earlier EP installments, <em><strong>Pasadena</strong></em> (2024) and <em><strong>Concan</strong></em> (2025), both of which built anticipation track by track."},{"t":"p","html":"Still, Edwards sees the record less as a career milestone and more as a reflection of where he’s been. “This record lives in the spaces between things,” he says. “Between cultures. Between genres. Between who you were and who you’re becoming.” In Texas, those spaces have always been where the most interesting music is made, and with <em>Texas Soul</em>, Micah Edwards is claiming his place right in the middle of them."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817602/large-74d1bf6ecaf61c44ac13179d112bcd33.jpg","alt":"000001490021 (2).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817602/preview-c268977ca45d5706beb6dc1bb9ff1d2a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817604/large-ade45002a18761d86d30e29a0a9039db.jpg","alt":"000001490034 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817604/preview-661bedda04b9a07a9869fa18116d9648.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817603/large-cdc436fd5ed265c81c76f205e5be4aa7.jpg","alt":"000001490024.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817603/preview-2550bd378ecd11ac1d376288dc989eeb.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817605/large-dae57aa6f7e818c4c680f82bfa06d5b2.jpg","alt":"177A3265 (2).JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817605/preview-4905570d8cb84f8ed63ff0a37b387b1e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817606/large-dd1891cb84d356a5fa1d0485b31d4230.jpg","alt":"177A3254.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817606/preview-167eff64ca16b9be4d21abb0d628363e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817600/large-dd87a2df90153ebf024a86bd018f4d8c.jpg","alt":"0F6A7524 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817600/preview-8088f32b75c390fe5339f4fa3968cda6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817601/large-6b6af0fc66f17e352e37c1b967d7bd53.jpg","alt":"0F6A7683.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817601/preview-768c4d5e2730dd1dc748fa4dbc9b08f5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817599/large-a93875527bde19f03b2fd37fe4feb932.jpg","alt":"0F6A7551 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817599/preview-699f43dddefefec3cb39fbb29c84632f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817598/large-33a6c703536b58fde48ef1937d2f5bb3.jpg","alt":"0F6A7647.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817598/preview-6ff522e255f91420d8c2873363aab102.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images 1-5 by Alice Loyaza, Images 6-9 by Kirby Betancourt"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Micah Edwards:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.mrtexassoul.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/mrtexassoul\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/mrtexassoul\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCkXy_wAxVUanG6EjfExW0Eg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/75OSuJw6r1LCdYgmTt0gHs?si=dBiPJQNCRqqivlZX-cnjHQ&amp;dl_branch=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/micah-edwards/1469748388\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/AjZymJEXYz0","height":""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/75OSuJw6r1LCdYgmTt0gHs?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"450025","title":"Between Country and Soul, Micah Edwards Finds Home in the Contradictions of Texas on 'Texas Soul'","date":"2026-05-01","lead":"With Texas Soul, Houston songwriter Micah Edwards fuses country storytelling, vintage R&B, and Americana with boleros, rockabilly, and honky-tonk traditions - reflecting the cultural crossroads that have long shaped Texas music.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/450025/7eab00a4a24af17b1e64154e8913174e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"With <em>Texas Soul</em>, Houston songwriter Micah Edwards fuses country storytelling, vintage R&amp;B, and Americana with boleros, rockabilly, and honky-tonk traditions - reflecting the cultural crossroads that have long shaped Texas music."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>HOUSTON, TX (May 1, 2026) </strong>- Texas has never belonged to just one sound. Across the state, honky-tonks share space with soul clubs, borderland boleros drift through small towns, and pedal steel guitars echo across late-night dance halls. It’s a musical landscape built on contradiction - where country, R&amp;B, blues, and rock traditions have collided for generations."},{"t":"p","html":"On<strong>&nbsp;May 1st</strong>, Houston-based singer-songwriter <strong>Micah Edwards</strong> leans directly into that collision with his new album <em><strong>Texas Soul</strong></em>, blending country storytelling and vintage soul into a record shaped by identity, place, and the cultural crossroads of the Lone Star State. This sophomore full-length album is a love letter to the unsung communities of Texas - the small towns, the neon-lit dance halls, the quiet backroads where stories unfold. Each track is steeped in the essence of Texas, capturing the spirit of a place that thrives on its contrasts."},{"t":"button","href":"https://too.fm/er3r14a?utm_source=ig&amp;amp;utm_medium=social&amp;amp;utm_content=link_in_bio&amp;amp;fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQMMjU2MjgxMDQwNTU4AAGn39COGDf2S0tdY4QVU-HMYBoIWDu8zlcNbe4BwTgYJp6Xgu8_VvJmbWvJ4rA_aem_lyVopUhDPbkdJ43A9Ywquw","label":"Listen on All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817597/large-64b09c1d2f57f78274fe03603c1f328f.png","alt":"Cover art for 'Texas Soul'"},{"t":"p","html":"Edwards’ album arrives at a moment when Texas has quietly become one of the most influential centers of the modern soul revival. Artists like <strong>Leon Bridges</strong> and <strong>Charley Crockett</strong> have helped bring vintage soul textures back into the Americana and country conversation, reconnecting modern audiences with sounds rooted in place and tradition. With <em>Texas Soul</em>, Edwards adds his own voice to that movement - blending country storytelling, vintage R&amp;B, and borderland influences into a record shaped by the cultural crossroads of the Lone Star State. For Edwards, the album isn’t about inventing a new genre; it’s about naming one that has been living in Texas for generations. His distinct fusion of buttery textures in a country landscape leans into nostalgia, crafting music that feels like a homecoming.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/prerelease/5mpcUWtIA2DbXaOj2HL0UV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“When I say 'Texas Soul' is a spectrum, I mean it. This record moves from boleros to rockabilly, from ’60s R&amp;B to ’80s country, and somehow it all still feels like the same story. Texas has always been a crossroads, and I wanted the album to sound like that - wide, textured, and big enough to hold all of it.”","cite":"- Micah Edwards"},{"t":"p","html":"The project arrives after a multi-year creative journey that began in 2023 and unfolded through two earlier EP installments - <strong><em>Pasadena</em></strong> (2024) and <strong><em>Concan</em></strong> (2025) - before culminating in the full album release this spring. But for Edwards, <em>Texas Soul</em> is as much about identity as it is about music. “I’ve spent my life between worlds,” he says. “I’m half Black and half white. I grew up in California, but Houston is where I learned who I was. Texas taught me you don’t have to choose one side. You can be soft and strong. You can love boleros and honky-tonks. That tension - that ‘both and neither’ feeling - is what <em>Texas Soul</em> sounds like to me.”"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/AjZymJEXYz0","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"That duality runs through every corner of the record through subtle musical juxtapositions. Pedal steel drifts across jazz-inspired chord progressions. Horn sections swell beneath country melodies. Soul grooves settle into storytelling rooted in Americana tradition. &nbsp;<em>Texas Soul</em> is as fluid and diverse as the state it calls home. It’s butter and twang, pine and stone - a sound as vast and textured as Texas itself. “It’s falling in love under neon lights in a honky-tonk - equal parts sultry and steel, leather and lace,” Edwards explains. Across the album, Edwards balances sweeping themes with deeply personal storytelling. <strong>“Partner in Crime”&nbsp;</strong>captures a road-worn kind of romance rooted in loyalty and escape, while <strong>“River Man”&nbsp;</strong>leans into summer memories in the Texas Hill Country - where river days stretch long and dance floors come alive at night. At the center of it all, the title track <strong>“Texas Soul”</strong> serves as a defining statement - blending country, soul, and borderland influences into a sound that reflects both identity and place. “It’s meant to feel familiar, like coming home.”"},{"t":"quote","html":"“In a lot of ways, soul music and country music have always been neighbors...They’re both about truth. They’re both about feeling. Texas just happens to be a place where those traditions meet naturally.”","cite":"- Micah Edwards"},{"t":"p","html":"That sense of place carries into the album’s structure. Each side of the vinyl is named after a Texas community that helped shape Edwards’ life - not the postcard versions of the state, but the quieter pockets that define everyday Texas culture. “These aren’t the flashy places...They’re pockets - the real Texas.” <strong>Concan</strong> sits along the Frio River, where days are spent floating cold water and nights unfold beneath string lights and dance floors. <strong>Mission</strong>, deep in the Rio Grande Valley, welcomed Edwards into a culture rooted in family, long meals, and music that blends boleros with classic country. “I didn’t grow up there, but the Valley adopted me before I knew I needed it.” On the Gulf Coast, <strong>Galveston</strong> carries a slower rhythm. Edwards married his wife there, spent his first wedding night there, and filmed his first music video there - milestones that turned the island into a personal landmark. And then there’s <strong>Pasadena</strong>, the working-class Houston suburb once home to Gilley’s, the largest honky-tonk in the world. “Pasadena still feels like what Houston once was,” Edwards says. “It’s not flashy. It just is.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817598/large-33a6c703536b58fde48ef1937d2f5bb3.jpg","alt":"0F6A7647.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817598/preview-6ff522e255f91420d8c2873363aab102.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817599/large-a93875527bde19f03b2fd37fe4feb932.jpg","alt":"0F6A7551 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817599/preview-699f43dddefefec3cb39fbb29c84632f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817600/large-dd87a2df90153ebf024a86bd018f4d8c.jpg","alt":"0F6A7524 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817600/preview-8088f32b75c390fe5339f4fa3968cda6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817601/large-6b6af0fc66f17e352e37c1b967d7bd53.jpg","alt":"0F6A7683.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817601/preview-768c4d5e2730dd1dc748fa4dbc9b08f5.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Kirby Betancourt"},{"t":"quote","html":"“These songs are gratitude. They’re my way of saying thank you to the places that raised me, changed me, and reminded me who I am.”","cite":"- Micah Edwards"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by Micah Edwards alongside <strong>Kendrick Ballard</strong>, <strong>Anthony Farrell</strong>, <strong>Jack Gulielmetti</strong>, <strong>Cameron Jaymes</strong>, and <strong>Andrew Trube</strong>, <em>Texas Soul&nbsp;</em>arrives during a period of growing momentum for the Houston-based songwriter. Edwards has amassed <strong>more than 150 million streams across Spotify and Apple Music</strong>, earned placements on Spotify editorial playlists including <strong>All New Country</strong>, <strong>Retro Soul</strong>, and <strong>Soul ’n’ the City</strong>, and been recognized as both a<strong>&nbsp;Salt Lick Incubator grant winner&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Tiny Desk Contest Top Shelf artist</strong>. His ability to balance nostalgia with modern soul influences has also led to performances alongside <strong>JOHNNYSWIM, Saint Motel, Mac Ayres, and The War &amp; Treaty</strong>. In 2025, Edwards made two guest appearances at the <strong>Grand Ole Opry</strong>, and earlier this year sold out headline shows in Houston, Austin, and Dallas, further building anticipation for <em>Texas Soul</em>. After successfully crowdfunding over $30,000 in less than 30 days on Kickstarter, Edwards is set to bring the album to the stage this fall with the<em><strong>&nbsp;Texas Soul Tour </strong>-</em> including stops in Houston, Austin, Fort Worth, Dallas, and San Antonio."},{"t":"p","html":"Still, Edwards sees the record less as a career milestone and more as a reflection of where he’s been. “This record lives in the spaces between things,” he says. “Between cultures. Between genres. Between who you were and who you’re becoming.” In Texas, those spaces have always been where the most interesting music is made, and with <em>Texas Soul</em>, Micah Edwards is claiming his place right in the middle of them."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817602/large-74d1bf6ecaf61c44ac13179d112bcd33.jpg","alt":"000001490021 (2).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817602/preview-c268977ca45d5706beb6dc1bb9ff1d2a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817603/large-cdc436fd5ed265c81c76f205e5be4aa7.jpg","alt":"000001490024.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817603/preview-2550bd378ecd11ac1d376288dc989eeb.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817604/large-ade45002a18761d86d30e29a0a9039db.jpg","alt":"000001490034 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817604/preview-661bedda04b9a07a9869fa18116d9648.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817605/large-dae57aa6f7e818c4c680f82bfa06d5b2.jpg","alt":"177A3265 (2).JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817605/preview-4905570d8cb84f8ed63ff0a37b387b1e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817606/large-dd1891cb84d356a5fa1d0485b31d4230.jpg","alt":"177A3254.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817606/preview-167eff64ca16b9be4d21abb0d628363e.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Alice Loyaza"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Micah Edwards:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.mrtexassoul.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/mrtexassoul\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/mrtexassoul\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCkXy_wAxVUanG6EjfExW0Eg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/75OSuJw6r1LCdYgmTt0gHs?si=dBiPJQNCRqqivlZX-cnjHQ&amp;dl_branch=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/micah-edwards/1469748388\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/75OSuJw6r1LCdYgmTt0gHs?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"453398","title":"Reese Weil Ignites Late-Night Energy with New Single “Chaos” Featuring Nef The Pharaoh and Derek King","date":"2026-05-01","lead":"The Northern California artist blends melodic pop and West Coast hip-hop on a groove-driven new release recorded at Chico’s Nova Production Studio.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/453398/5d00b889699ccf45716445cd9c0f56b6.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Northern California artist blends melodic pop and West Coast hip-hop on a groove-driven new release recorded at Chico’s Nova Production Studio."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>CHICO, CA (May 1, 2026)</strong> - Rising West Coast artist <strong>Reese Weil</strong> returns with his latest single, “<strong>Chaos</strong>,” arriving Friday, May 1, 2026. Featuring Bay Area standout Nef The Pharaoh and multi-talented artist Derek King, the track delivers a hypnotic blend of hip hop, rap, and alternative sounds rooted in a distinctly West Coast aesthetic."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/3sIOv2FGIHc9HUzCC5hPtb?si=4ca04481ed0f4cb0","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Built around a melodic, atmospheric hook and smooth yet hard-hitting production, “Chaos” captures the rush of living fully in the moment; where late nights, attraction, and city energy collide into something unpredictable. The track balances emotional depth with confident swagger, moving seamlessly between vibe-driven vocals and charismatic verses."},{"t":"p","html":"“Chaos” explores themes of modern dating culture, escapism, and the allure of nightlife, embracing the intensity of real-life moments which are messy, exciting, and impossible to control. It reflects a generation drawn to connection over perfection, where chemistry and spontaneity take center stage."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/823187/large-dec78414c04a694fd5206ee07567b395.jpg","alt":"Cover Art"},{"t":"quote","html":"“There’s a line between control and letting go, and ‘Chaos’ lives right in that space. It’s about choosing the moment instead of overthinking it.”","cite":"Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, “Chaos” delivers a modern West Coast sound that feels equally at home in the club, on the radio, or cruising through the city after dark. With layered textures and Bay Area-inspired rhythms, the single embodies a polished yet unpredictable energy that defines Reese Weil’s evolving artistry."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/823188/large-1a7f46087b44a623aaa0e0b6ea4390ea.jpg","alt":"Photo Credit: Dana Hocking"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I think people are tired of everything being perfect all the time. ‘Chaos’ is about embracing the imperfect parts; the late nights, the feelings you can’t explain, the moments you just ride out.”","cite":"Reese Weil"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Main Artist: <strong>Reese Weil&nbsp;</strong><br id=\"isPasted\">Main Artist: <strong>Nef The Pharaoh</strong><br>Featured Artist: <strong>Derek King</strong><br>Producer: <strong>Dana Hocking&nbsp;</strong><br>Mastering Engineer: <strong>Carter Boy</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photo Credit: <strong>Dana Hocking, Reese Weil</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/823189/large-f318375ff50bd2059fbe83019496c240.jpg","alt":"Photo Credit: Dana Hocking"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"Reese Weil is a Northern California born artist, songwriter, and producer whose genre-blending sound bridges West Coast hip-hop, melodic pop, and alternative rock. Known for smooth, breathy vocals and groove-driven production, Weil crafts music that feels both laid-back and polished which captures the spirit of California while reaching a global audience."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil’s musical journey began early. At just four years old, he picked up a guitar in his hometown of Chico, California, laying the foundation for a lifelong dedication to songwriting and performance. His talent and work ethic eventually earned him a scholarship to the prestigious Berklee College of Music, where he refined his skills in music production, composition, and modern songwriting. The experience helped shape the versatile creative voice that defines his work today."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil has built an impressive list of accomplishments. He has opened for The Wailers, the legendary band associated with Bob Marley, and contributed songwriting for international pop icon Enrique Iglesias. His music has also found a home on television, with placements on series such as Bones and Twisted. In addition, his work has been published through the music company Pulse Music Group, further expanding his reach as a songwriter and producer."},{"t":"p","html":"With a growing catalog, high-profile collaborations, and a steadily expanding fan base, Reese Weil continues to carve out his place as a dynamic modern artist. His music brings an energy designed for stages, screens, and playlists around the world."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reeseweilmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Zi3EV89aof6OMz8SHTxDN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>​"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"453228","title":"Futuristic Jazz Meets Modern Composition on McArdle's Debut Album 'Halcyon Week'","date":"2026-04-17","lead":"A Sonic World Built on Contrast and Collaboration","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/453228/19f48ab39e598424f7e699b3a6b25035.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A Sonic World Built on Contrast and Collaboration"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>OAKLAND, CA (April 17,2026)&nbsp;</strong>- &nbsp;Composer, multi-instrumentalist, and longtime Bay Area collaborator <strong>Ian McArdle</strong> steps into the spotlight with the release of his debut album as a bandleader, <strong><em>Halcyon Week</em></strong>. A richly layered and deeply personal project, the album showcases McArdle’s expansive musical vision, blending acoustic instrumentation with forward-thinking production and experimental sound design."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/23aI4Xx4WKywx24XegDfqb?si=homHk2uwR9K8XNIatOezOg","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Halcyon Week is a striking introduction to McArdle’s creative identity; a “tug of war between many different influences and textures.” Drawing from over a decade immersed in the San Francisco Bay Area’s diverse music scene, the album bridges genres including jazz, blues, R&amp;B, and experimental electronic music."},{"t":"p","html":"With Halcyon Week, Ian McArdle emerges as a compelling new voice in contemporary music. One unafraid to blur boundaries, embrace complexity, and build a deeply immersive world of sound."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/823803/large-8a2b697fd7cafcae3c210bd8206dc9c2.png","alt":"Album Cover Art"},{"t":"p","html":"Listeners can expect a dynamic interplay between organic and synthetic elements: slide guitar and bass clarinet weave through glitchy polyrhythmic drums and expansive, transcendent synths. The result is a cinematic, ever-shifting soundscape that rewards deep listening while moving fluidly between introspective ambient passages and explosive, rhythmically complex improvisations."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This music is my world of sound, where I got to stretch my imagination and play into all my influences throughout the years.”","cite":"Ian McArdle"},{"t":"p","html":"Positioned at the intersection of futuristic jazz and modern composition, <em>Halcyon Week</em> will resonate with fans of boundary-pushing artists who blend improvisation with sonic experimentation. The album channels a wide spectrum of influences, from intricate jazz virtuosity to atmospheric, genre-defying production."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Featured Tracks"},{"t":"list","items":["“<strong>Saka</strong>” | A stream-of-consciousness exploration balancing vulnerability and abstraction, with lyrical fragments that mirror the album’s layered sonic approach.","“<strong>New Habitat</strong>” | A surreal, poetic journey through shifting emotional landscapes and dreamlike imagery.","“<strong>Fearless Love of Caution</strong>” | A dynamic piece that captures tension and release, pairing melodic sensitivity with rhythmic unpredictability."]},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817457/large-da6ac9a67d0120913f4d085f5c35aacc.jpg","alt":"Ginger Fierstein"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"list","items":["Composition, Production &amp; Lyrics: Ian McArdle","Mixed by: Cole Williams","Mastered by: Simon Lancelot","Artwork: Zander Raymond","Photography: Ginger Fierstein"]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Ian McArdle"},{"t":"p","html":"Ian McArdle is an Oakland, California–based composer, producer, and multi-instrumentalist whose work blends contemporary jazz with modern composition and experimental production. Drawing from the improvisational spirit of jazz and the sonic curiosity of indie and electronic music, McArdle creates detailed, layered recordings that reward close listening. His music often weaves together piano, synthesizers, textured vocals, and rhythm-forward arrangements, balancing structured composition with moments of spontaneous interplay."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/mc.arthurgiuseppe?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%253D%253D&amp;utm_source=qr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://ianmcardlemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a>​"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"449255","title":"Angels in Electric Chairs Blur the Lines Between Metal and Electronic on “Everything”","date":"2026-04-10","lead":"A contrast-driven release shaped by emotional upheaval, experimentation, and creative clarity.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/449255/1a57921d059ef309a1791a9c014fcc53.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A contrast-driven release shaped by emotional upheaval, experimentation, and creative clarity."},{"t":"p","html":"DENVER, CO - The metal band Angels in Electric Chairs is set to release their new single \"Everything\" on April, 10th. This song represents a significant progression in the band's musical style, blending melodic metalcore with industrial elements, synthesizer-driven ambiance, and deeply emotional lyrics."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/71aHSF3PyRBBAaqXeidlE9?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/818642/large-3ffbb814dd31a7c64200bdd138fe8045.jpg","alt":"Cover Art"},{"t":"p","html":"Emerging from Denver’s South Broadway music scene in 2024, Angels in Electric Chairs quickly developed a reputation for immersive performances that blend aggressive musicianship with striking visual elements. The band performs as a tight three-piece featuring vocalist <strong>Alissa Ann</strong>, guitarist<strong>&nbsp;Mike Miller</strong>, and percussionist <strong>Ayrton Sanguino </strong>creating a sound that fills venues with a powerful, cinematic intensity."},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Everything’ was our first attempt at a lot of things - combining synths and heavy guitars in a way that felt directive, and creating a vocal chop that could stand on its own in a metal track. It’s really an assimilation of the emotions we were experiencing at the time,”","cite":"The Band"},{"t":"p","html":"In 2025, the band expanded their presence across Colorado, performing at the regional music festival FoCoMX and appearing at well-known independent venues including Moe's Original BBQ &amp; Music Venue, Lost Lake Lounge, and The Coast (Soundbar)."},{"t":"p","html":"Their latest single, “Everything,” was one of the first songs written as part of the band’s new creative chapter. Developed after multiple lineup changes and creative shifts, the track became a moment of clarity for the group, capturing both the loss and resilience that defined that period."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/818643/large-bb76fada86121301b96d3275372feced.jpg","alt":"Angels in Electric Chairs"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Mike and I were trying to push forward after a lot of setbacks. Ironically, it ended up being one of the most seamless writing processes we’ve had together. It was experimental for us, but it felt like all the pieces clicked into place.”","cite":"Vocalist Alissa Ann"},{"t":"p","html":"Melancholic yet resolute, the song weaves heavy guitars with electronic textures and layered vocals, creating a sonic push-and-pull between vulnerability and strength. Structurally, “Everything” thrives on contrast: shifting guitar tones, dynamic vocal delivery, and a progression that defies expectations from its opening moments to its final crescendo."},{"t":"p","html":"The group takes inspiration from a variety of artists such as <strong>Underoath</strong>, <strong>Halsey</strong>, and <strong>Spiritbox</strong>, combining elements of metal, EDM, industrial, and pop to create their unique and boundary-pushing style."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"list","items":["Mike Miller: Guitars, bass, arrangement, programming","Noah Hansen: Drums","Ayrton Sanguino: Drums","Alissa Ann: Vocals, lyrics, arrangement, programming","Bobby Ferguson: Mixing, mastering"]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/818644/large-06100fdb17c3e5289345320e6dc62405.jpg","alt":"Angels in Electric Chairs "},{"t":"h3","html":"About Angels in Electric Chairs"},{"t":"p","html":"Angels in Electric Chairs is a revolution of genre, fusing decades of metal, EDM, industrial, and legacy pop influences. Having made their debut as a trio on Denver's S Broadway scene in '24, the Angels expanded upon their discography and local presence the next year - playing festivals like FoCoMx, as well as legacy venues like Moe's, Lost Lake, and Fort Collins' The Coast (Soundbar).&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"While the Angels may lack bodies on stage in comparison to their peers, they fill the open space with seething aggression. Featuring Alissa Ann on vocals, Mike Miller on guitar, and Ayrton Sanguino on percussion, the Angels bring a meticulously crafted sonic landscape and visual performance to their audience. This band never fails to subvert expectation."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Angels in Electric Chairs</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/AngelsinElectricChairs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://linktr.ee/angelsinelectricchairs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Linktr</a> &nbsp;"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"449853","title":"Mira Lazuli’s “Good News” Turns a Long-Distance Situationship Into Folk-Noir Gold","date":"2026-04-10","lead":"A Bittersweet Song About Distance, Desire, and Moving On","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/449853/c05020b7ae4f01cd164ee0b1b17f0db1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A Bittersweet Song About Distance, Desire, and Moving On"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>NEW ORLEANS, LA &nbsp;(APRIL 10,2026)</strong> - Singer-songwriter <strong>Mira Lazuli</strong> returns with a stirring new folk single, “<strong>Good News</strong>,” released April 10, 2026. Rooted in intimate storytelling and shimmering folk textures, the track captures the emotional turbulence of a fleeting romance and the quiet resolve that comes with moving forward."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/1fReT54T06aiJLpBW8NIe8?si=db02a6b20ce74d60","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Built around banjo, double bass, and haunting accordion lines, “Good News” pulses with the rhythmic drive of Appalachian and Old-Time traditions while drawing subtle inspiration from Eastern European harmonies, Sicilian folk, and a hint of Zydeco. The song unfolds in brisk 4/4 time, its anxious energy mirroring the uncertainty of distance and silence in a relationship that refuses to settle."},{"t":"p","html":"At its heart, “Good News” is a story of modern love told through timeless imagery. The song was inspired by a romantic connection sparked at the <strong>Barefoot Farmer’s Solstice Festiva</strong><strong>l</strong> in Tennessee. What began as a sweet festival romance turned into a complicated long-distance situationship, where shared phone locations and infrequent calls created more questions than comfort."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/Pb7Mm06inyM","height":""},{"t":"quote","html":"“Do you know what it’s like to share your location with a lover in a long-distance situation-ship? This song came out of that feeling. Trying to make sense of distance, silence, and the stories we tell ourselves when we’re waiting for someone to reach out.”","cite":"Mira"},{"t":"p","html":"Lyrically, the track blends poetic language with everyday modern references, weaving together images of palaces, fairies, messengers, and moonlit beds alongside street names, telephones, and snacks. This juxtaposition creates a sound world that feels both ancient and contemporary, folk storytelling filtered through the lens of modern romance."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817059/large-e58f2214de80afc43c0ccb5f8950212e.jpg","alt":"Cover Art by Nick Leonard"},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, “Good News” leans into a rich, layered vocal arrangement, with close three-part harmonies elevating the song’s emotional weight. The melancholic accordion refrain between verses creates a lonely atmosphere, echoing the restless thoughts that come with waiting for someone who may never call.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Even the song’s herbal imagery carries deeper meaning. The lyric “I got no thyme, no rosemary” references historical symbolism: thyme representing courage and protection from melancholy, and rosemary symbolizing love, loyalty, and remembrance. Absence becomes a metaphor for a relationship missing its essential components."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Mixing &amp; Mastering: <strong>Bob Gaiser</strong><br id=\"isPasted\">Double Bass &amp; Vocals: <strong>Lily McKay</strong><br>Vocals: <strong>Rosie Adams</strong><br>Guitar/Banjo &amp; Vocals: <strong>Ezra Meyer&nbsp;</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photo Credit: <strong>Nick Leonard</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Mira Lazuli"},{"t":"p","html":"Mira Lazuli is an Algerian-Québécois sapphic folk artist based in New Orleans. &nbsp;A classically and jazz-trained multi-instrumentalist, Mira blends French, folk, Mexican, and jazz influences into intimate, emotionally rich songs about queer relationships, healing, and self-discovery.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a sound that sits somewhere between the whimsical Americana of <strong>Sierra Ferrell</strong>, the narrative depth of <strong>Gillian Welch</strong>, and the roots revival spirit of <strong>Rhiannon Giddens</strong>, Mira brings a unique mix to contemporary folk music."},{"t":"p","html":"As a queer artist of color, they bring a fresh perspective to the folk landscape, creating songs that explore identity, emotional healing, and the complexity of queer relationships with vulnerability and warmth. Their music invites listeners to feel deeply, move freely, and feel more at home in themselves."},{"t":"p","html":"Whether performing solo or alongside collaborators, Mira’s music invites listeners to laugh, cry, dance, and reflect. Their work exists at the intersection of storytelling and catharsis which begs not just to be heard, but deeply felt."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://miralazuli.godaddysites.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/miralazuli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@MiraLazuli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Youtube</a> | <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/miralazuli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SoundCloud</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"451852","title":"Erin Lunsford says to “Call Me If You Need Me” in New Single","date":"2026-04-10","lead":"A Folk and Americana ode to friendship paired with an interactive affirmation hotline connecting fans through care and community","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/451852/1410cc35545a76f38d69aea484e99749.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A Folk and Americana ode to friendship paired with an interactive affirmation hotline connecting fans through care and community"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>RICHMOND, VA (APRIL 10, 2026)</strong> — Erin Lunsford releases her new single, “<strong>Call Me If You Need Me</strong>” on <strong>Friday April 10, 2026</strong>. Featuring a blend of folk, country, and Americana, the track explores the profound reliability of friendship and the unwavering commitment of showing up for people one sincerely cares about."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3B6yc3nedhEZUZ3IVj7OKK?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The new release was written when Lunsford was worried about a close friend who was suffering a mental health crisis. Evolving from a moment of fear into reflections and testament of their friendship, the single ultimately serves as a love letter – one that persists across time and distance. At its core, the song highlights the power of female friendships and the ability for women to be there for each other when needed, which is one of the foundational relationships in life. Through themes of mental health, loyalty, and chosen family, Lunsford frames these connections as deeply emotional and essential forms of love.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"I wrote this tune about the power of friendship and the fierceness with which I love my friends.","cite":"Lunsford expresses  when describing the core message of her song."},{"t":"p","html":"Extending her support beyond her immediate circle, Lunsford has launched an interactive, custom-built affirmation hotline. Listeners can navigate guided prompts designed to offer encouragement, provide emotional support, and most importantly, foster a sense of genuine connection. The main concept reflects the role friendships play in her life, while also showcasing the meaning of love in female friendships, where reassurance and support when it’s needed, friends are only one call away. Fans can dial <strong>804-322-9317</strong> to access the affirmation hotline."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/821143/large-0235818832efb10fd80e7f85061cc01c.jpg","alt":"Erin flower umbrella_websize.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, the song blends sweet country folk and spooky Americana with a six-piece band, while featuring influences reminiscent of Noah Kahan and Kacey Musgraves. Lunsford also commits to collaboration with female musicians. Her current band features more women than ever before, fostering a creative environment rooted in support and shared experience."},{"t":"p","html":"As the second single of 2026, 'Call Me If You Need Me' offers a poignant glimpse into an upcoming album centered on the enduring power of showing up for one another. With this release, she continues to establish herself as a compelling voice in the Americana and Folk space, one that merges emotional storytelling with innovative ways of building community through music."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Producer: Jacob Ungerleider<br>Mixing: Alex DeJong<br>Mastering: Danny Kalb<br>Synth: Ryan Lipps"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Erin Lunsford"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Erin Lunsford</strong> is an award-winning singer-songwriter from Fincastle, Virginia, now based in Richmond, whose work blends Appalachian roots with Americana, folk, and country influences. She has earned praise from <strong>NPR Music:</strong>"},{"t":"quote","html":"mesmerizing voice and fantastic vocal technique","cite":"NPR Music"},{"t":"p","html":"and"},{"t":"quote","html":"impressive, expressive voice and some serious guitar chops","cite":"NPR Music"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>A semi-finalist in the Songwriters Guild of America Country Song Contest</strong> for her song “Rhinestones,” Lunsford has built a reputation as a compelling storyteller. Her 2025 run of singles further defined her nostalgic, emotionally rich Americana sound, with Country Music News International calling “Last I Heard” a “meticulously crafted emotional time capsule… a gut-punch of a breakup song,” while The Auricular praised her ability to turn personal misfortune into “universal reflection” with “emotionally brilliant” vocals."},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond songwriting, Lunsford uses her platform to foster community impact. Her single “Strawberries” inspired a regional tour that <strong>raised over $16,000</strong> for local food pantries, with Richmond Grid noting her work as “a model of artist-led community organizing… turning release celebrations into opportunities for collective support.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Formerly the frontwoman of Erin &amp; The Wildfire featured by <strong>Rolling Stone Country as one of the “10 Best Things We Saw at FloydFest”</strong>, Lunsford has performed at major festivals and alongside artists such as <strong>Maggie Rose, Bruce Hornsby, and The Infamous Stringdusters</strong>. With her forthcoming full-length album set for Summer 2026, she continues to emerge as a rising voice in country and Americana, crafting songs that bridge personal storytelling with a deep sense of place and purpose."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Erin Lunsford</strong>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/erinlunsfordmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@erinlunsfordmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://www.erinlunsford.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/erinlunsfordmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@erinlunsfordmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/erinlunsfordmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6VQmzs195HRiyaBhz9JMlv?si=Uy1oWYtGQhODypXZc5kE0Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"447239","title":"Hallie Marie Finds Peace in the Fleeting with New Indie-Pop Single \"A Space of Clarity\"","date":"2026-03-27","lead":"Moving beyond heartbreak, the DC-based artist celebrates the art of letting go","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/447239/d30c93b1d48cb56213a32e458716e20d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Moving beyond heartbreak, the DC-based artist celebrates the art of letting go"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>WASHINGTON, DC (MARCH 27, 2026)</strong> –– Emerging pop artist <strong>Hallie Marie</strong> returns with her latest single \"<strong>A Space of Clarity</strong>,\" a bright and expansive track that captures the bittersweet beauty and the profound impact of a chance encounter. The song explores the trajectory of a fleeting romance, from initial spark to eventually returning to solitude; rather than dwelling on heartbreak, Marie shares gratitude for the opportunity to have experienced it at all. \"A Space of Clarity\" focuses on the peace found through letting go and returning a cherished memory back to the \"noumena.\" The song will be released on <strong>March 27, 2026</strong>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1ueMo2E9t2Tgmdywz9IzAW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"\"It's easy to be broken by the pain of loss, but it's also the natural consequence of anything beautiful; everything we have today we'll eventually lose. There's no negotiation. You'll have to let go because you can't hang onto it anyway.\"","cite":"Marie channels these reflections into her songwriting."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/812275/large-32cdfee903e2df51d11cb1c89863bb32.jpg","alt":"\"A Space of Clarity\" Album Cover"},{"t":"p","html":"The track's intentional sonic palette evokes the space of Paramore's \"The Only Exception,\" using atmospheric production to mimic the feeling of a clear day with blue skies. Through vibrant and burgeoning sounds, listeners are reminded of the moments when flowers bloom in spring before they inevitably fade."},{"t":"quote","html":"\"It's important to me that love remains pure in my memories so they don't become distorted by heartbreak or cynicism.\"","cite":"Marie shares, reflecting on the emotional intention behind the track."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/812274/large-582e1185a6b4db007bc7f82d7ba2b64b.jpg","alt":"Hallie Marie Photo 2.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"After her recent relocation to Washington, DC, this new release is the first in a series of songs Marie plans to record with guitarist <strong>Buddy Speir</strong>, drummer <strong>Andy Hamburger</strong>, bassist <strong>Eric Scott</strong>, and sound engineer <strong>Ken Schubert</strong>, resulting in a polished and professional sound that marks a significant milestone in Marie's journey as an artist."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"​​​​​Singer: <strong>Hallie Marie</strong><br>Songwriter:&nbsp;<strong>Hallie Marie</strong><br>Piano: <strong>Hallie Marie</strong><br>Guitar: <strong>Buddy Speir</strong><br>Drums: <strong>Andy Hamburger</strong><br>Bass:&nbsp;<strong>Eric Scott</strong><br>Sound Engineer: <strong>Ken Schubert</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hallie Marie"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Hallie Marie</strong> is an intellectually curious spirit who explores the complexities of human emotions by creating music that moves fluidly between the highs of love and joy to the depths of melancholy. Inspired by the likes of <strong>Sufjan Stevens, Billy Joel, and Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, Hallie Marie merges pop, rock, and folk elements to write musical anecdotes that foster genuine connections through heartfelt lyrics, which has caught the attention of major indie tastemakers and listeners alike."},{"t":"quote","html":"\"An artist who knows how to bring brevity to difficult concepts.\"","cite":"– Earmilk"},{"t":"quote","html":"\"Hallie builds a body of work grounded in truth and emotional resonance.”","cite":"– Neon Music"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Hallie Marie</strong> is a multifaceted Washington DC-based artist whose music critics have described as both “sad and hopeful” with an emotional weight that lingers long after the final note."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hallie Marie"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/halliemariemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@halliemariemusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/halliemariemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/people/Hallie-Marie/100068917929503/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qv9RFavvRmeHdVLljnpMBQ&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=be130915b0c44916\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"449863","title":"Reese Weil Delivers West Coast Vibes With Nef The Pharaoh and Cotati 7z on “The One”","date":"2026-03-27","lead":"The Northern California artist blends melodic pop and West Coast hip-hop on a groove-driven new release recorded at Chico’s Nova Production Studio.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/449863/287e8c483f19ec5a80b17b334f4615c0.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Northern California artist blends melodic pop and West Coast hip-hop on a groove-driven new release recorded at Chico’s Nova Production Studio."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>CHICO, CA (March 27, 2026)</strong> - Northern California artist, songwriter, and producer <strong>Reese Weil</strong> is set to release his new single “<strong>The On</strong><strong>e</strong>” on March 27, 2026, bringing together smooth West Coast hip-hop, melodic pop influences, and authentic Bay Area energy. The track features acclaimed rapper <strong>Nef the Pharaoh</strong> alongside rising collaborator <strong>Cotati 7z</strong>, delivering a groove-driven anthem centered around attraction, loyalty, and the thrill of discovering someone who stands out from the crowd."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/7Ap0Ko2r7iiT8AAn6fiymj?si=89a60276cb254fc0","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Born in Northern California and raised in the creative hub of Chico, Reese Weil has built a reputation as a versatile artist with a deep musical foundation. After picking up a guitar at just four years old, his path led him to <strong>Berklee College of Music</strong> on scholarship, where he refined his songwriting and production skills before launching a career marked by genre fluidity and high-level collaborations."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil’s sound blends smooth, breathy vocals with rhythm-forward grooves, drawing inspiration from icons like <strong>The Beatles</strong>, the psychedelic textures of <strong>Tame Impala</strong>, and the coastal grit of <strong>Sublim</strong><strong>e</strong>. The result is a distinctive style that bridges hip-hop, rock, and pop while maintaining a laid-back Northern California sensibility."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817075/large-f15ce9ebb9c7ac85374115b18b06be2f.png","alt":"Dana Hocking"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Getting Nef The Pharaoh and Cotati 7z on ‘The One’ brought that real Bay Area flavor to it. It’s one of those songs that feels classic but still fresh.”","cite":"Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"“The One” captures that vibe perfectly. The track blends modern West Coast hip-hop with melodic hooks and confident production, creating a romantic yet street-influenced sound designed for late-night drives, parties, and playlists alike. Recorded at Weil’s brand-new Nova Production Studio facility in Chico, the song began as a local production before expanding through Bay Area collaborations. The final vocal sessions came together when Nef the Pharaoh visited the studio, helping infuse the record with unmistakable regional flavor."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil’s growing catalog already includes notable accomplishments across music and entertainment. He has opened for <strong>The Wailers</strong>, the legendary group that carried the legacy of <strong>Bob Marley</strong>, and contributed songwriting for global superstar <strong>Enrique Iglesias</strong>. His music has also been licensed for television placements including<strong>&nbsp;Bones and Twisted</strong>, helping introduce his sound to audiences worldwide."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817074/large-e498838ff9aee3ccedfb3c33b655cb05.jpg","alt":"Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"Working out of his full-scale production studio Nova Production Studio, Weil writes, records, and produces music that blends the soul of Northern California with the polish of a global artist. With the release of “The One,” he continues to build momentum heading into a new era of releases that highlight his range as both a performer and producer."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Main Artist: <strong>Reese Weil&nbsp;</strong><br id=\"isPasted\">Main Artist: <strong>Nef The Pharaoh</strong><br>Main Artist:&nbsp;<strong>Cotati 7z</strong><br>Producer: <strong>Dana Hocking&nbsp;</strong><br>Mastering Engineer: <strong>Carter Boy</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Photo Credit: <strong>Dana Hocking, Reese Weil</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817076/large-785f0e81f79e4844fc3cb496b333090b.png","alt":"Dana Hocking"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"Reese Weil is a Northern California born artist, songwriter, and producer whose genre-blending sound bridges West Coast hip-hop, melodic pop, and alternative rock. Known for smooth, breathy vocals and groove-driven production, Weil crafts music that feels both laid-back and polished which captures the spirit of California while reaching a global audience."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil’s musical journey began early. At just four years old, he picked up a guitar in his hometown of Chico, California, laying the foundation for a lifelong dedication to songwriting and performance. His talent and work ethic eventually earned him a scholarship to the prestigious Berklee College of Music, where he refined his skills in music production, composition, and modern songwriting. The experience helped shape the versatile creative voice that defines his work today."},{"t":"p","html":"Weil has built an impressive list of accomplishments. He has opened for The Wailers, the legendary band associated with Bob Marley, and contributed songwriting for international pop icon Enrique Iglesias. His music has also found a home on television, with placements on series such as Bones and Twisted. In addition, his work has been published through the music company Pulse Music Group, further expanding his reach as a songwriter and producer."},{"t":"p","html":"With a growing catalog, high-profile collaborations, and a steadily expanding fan base, Reese Weil continues to carve out his place as a dynamic modern artist. His music brings an energy designed for stages, screens, and playlists around the world."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reeseweilmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Zi3EV89aof6OMz8SHTxDN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>​"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"449423","title":"Rahul Mukerji Announces New Global Fusion Album MRIDHANGIT","date":"2026-03-23","lead":"Rahul Mukerji unites global musicians including Praveen Sparsh and Pain of Salvation’s Leo Margarit.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/449423/2aa22ee6e856817a34312264ec56e43b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Rahul Mukerji unites global musicians including Praveen Sparsh and Pain of Salvation’s Leo Margarit."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>GERMANTOWN, MD (MARCH 23, 2026)</strong> – While the world was under quarantine, artist Rahul Mukerji found a creative North Star. Moving away from a solo “shred” approach to an international collaborative framework, the artist decided to unite musicians globally to serve as a vessel for diverse cultural narratives, marking the inception of his new project. Following his award-winning debut, <em>Ma De Re Sha</em>, Rahul Mukerji returns with <em><strong>MRIDHANGIT</strong></em>, a highly anticipated 11-track collection set for release on <strong>March 23, 2026</strong>. Acting as a sonic manifesto that translates across cultures, the album takes listeners on a journey through contrasting worlds. It moves from the dark dissonance of “<strong>Mr. Sinister</strong>” to the spirited camaraderie found in titles like “<strong>Kalli Penn</strong>” and the recently released song, “<strong>Dushtan</strong>.”"},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/2dCQoPQt1eIakOh12OTrnW?si=ujaEiSEZQBiN9Xxt-_pmCg","label":"Listen on Spotify","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2dCQoPQt1eIakOh12OTrnW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The title, <em><strong>MRIDHANGIT</strong></em>, is a linguistic fusion of Mridangam (a double-headed percussion instrument core to Carnatic music), Handpan (a melodic steel drum), and Guitar, reflecting the core purpose of the project: collaboration. These three instruments embody the blend of style and influences. During the cross-continental synergy, Mukerji also discovered that the collection of minds is stronger than one, transcending the forced isolation of the pandemic era. <em>MRIDHANGIT</em> stands as a testament of collaboration created in an uncertain environment and provides listeners with a rich and engaging musical journey."},{"t":"quote","html":"Each of [the musicians] has been able to provide their own voice and their own emotional interpretation of the song, based on the time we were all living through","cite":"Mukerji expressed as he reflected on the creative process of the album."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/816222/large-52eb89afb7bc774a41de68c32f064476.jpg","alt":"Mridhangit Album Cover by Proviscocity Studios"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>MRIDHANGIT</em> explores a unique composition style engineered to spark non-traditional creativity and improvisation, allowing each musician to express unfettered creative autonomy and let their personal heritage dictate the track's emotional arc. Some reputable musicians include <strong>Praveen Sparsh</strong>, prominent South Indian mridangam artist, <strong>Leo Margarit</strong>, Sweden-based drummer for Pain of Salvation, <strong>Ruben Rubio</strong>, versatile Spanish bassist, and&nbsp;<strong>Chaplin</strong>, South African pianist known for evocative tonal moods. Other musicians featured on this project include a Duduk player from Turkey, a clarinetist from France, and a violinist from Sri Lanka alongside talented local instrumentalists."},{"t":"p","html":"The project serves as the evolution of the award-winning <em>Ma De Re Sha</em>, Mukerji’s debut album, featuring more intricate arrangements and a layered musical palette. Former Iritis bandmate <strong>Bruce Ng</strong> also returned to this project as the co-producer to help shape <em>MRIDHANGIT’s</em> creative direction. Together, they honor the album’s global influences while showcasing the collaborative and improvisational spirit. Brett Caldas-Lima took part as a mixing and mastering engineer to ensure a high-fidelity sound."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"​​​​<u>General</u>​<br>Produced by: Bruce Ng &amp; Rahul Mukerji<br>Mixed &amp; Mastered by: Brett Caldas-Lima at Tower Studio<br>Album Artwork, Concept &amp; Layout: Proviscocity Studios<br>All Guitars: Rahul Mukerji<br>All Drums: Leo Margarit<br><br><u>Credits per track<br></u><strong>Mr. Sinister</strong><br>Fretless Bass: Ruben Rubio<br>Keyboards &amp; Tabla Programming: Rahul Mukerji<br><strong>Bheja Fry</strong><br>Bass: Rafael Freitas<br>Tabla Programming: Rahul Mukerji<br><strong>Twelve Ganeshas</strong><br>Bass: Ruben Rubio<br>Mridangam: Praveen Sparsh<br><strong>Enjoymaddi</strong><br>Upright Bass: Maciej S<br>Piano: Chaplin<br><strong>Mridhangit</strong><br>Bass: Ruben Rubio<br>Konnakol (Carnatic spoken rhythms): Praveen Sparsh<br>Mridangam: Praveen Sparsh<br>Flute: Rahul Krishnan<br>Tablas: Rahul Krishnan<br><strong>Kalli Penn</strong><br>Bass: Ruben Rubio<br>Keys: Chaplin<br>Percussion: Alejo Perezcuba<br><strong>Funky Pakora</strong><br>Clarinet: Dylan<br>Bass: Rafael Freitas<br>Keys: Emi Romero<br><strong>Dushtan</strong><br>Bass: Ruben Rubio<br>Keys: Chaplin<br>Percussion Programming: Rahul Mukerji<br>Violin: Thisara Bandara<br><strong>Rahu Ketu</strong><br>Bass: Ruben Rubio<br>Percussion Programming: Rahul Mukerji<br><strong>Four Seas</strong><br>Bass: Ruben Rubio<br>Piano: Chaplin<br>Mridangam: Praveen Sparsh<br><strong>Mutabor</strong><br>Duduk: Erkan Erginci<br>Tabla programming: Rahul Mukerji"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Rahul Mukerji"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Rahul Mukerji</strong> is a multi-disciplinary musician, composer, and visual artist whose creations bridge fusion, rock, jazz, and cinematic sound design into a signature style that is technically rigorous while still being emotionally immersive. Born in India and active for more than two decades, Mukerji has developed a variety of work that moves between high-energy performance and narrative-driven composition. Since his debut album in 2017, Mukerji has gained recognition through notable performances, including The John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts in 2020, spotlighted in Vintage Guitar Magazine in 2021, and been nominated for his work at the Washington Area Music Awards in 2022. Whether delivering dynamic guitar-forward performances, composing cinematic music, or shaping audio-visual narratives, Rahul Mukerji continues to explore the expansive possibilities of modern world fusion."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3roSwoPUD0LO6Gd89KgylG?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Rahul Mukerji"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.mukerji.us/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/rahul__mukerji/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Rahul.Mukerji.Artist/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/RahulMukerji\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Youtube</strong></a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"450615","title":"Brooke Ashton’s 'The Love of Song' Is a Love Letter to the Craft of Songwriting","date":"2026-03-18","lead":"With songs that unfold like front-porch confessions, Brooke Ashton’s new album channels the storytelling warmth of artists like Kacey Musgraves and Dolly Parton, blending heartfelt narratives and acoustic arrangements with reflections on motherhood, self-discovery, and t...","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/450615/0148a98f52d5f70faabc7dc4d4c9df89.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"With songs that unfold like front-porch confessions, Brooke Ashton’s new album channels the storytelling warmth of artists like Kacey Musgraves and Dolly Parton, blending heartfelt narratives and acoustic arrangements with reflections on motherhood, self-discovery, and the enduring power of music."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>GREENVILLE, SC (February 13, 2026)</strong> - Americana singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://brookeashtonmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brooke Ashton</a> invites listeners into a deeply personal world of reflection, resilience, and connection on her new album, <em><strong>The Love of Song</strong></em>. Rooted in honest storytelling and warm acoustic textures, the record is a tribute to the craft of songwriting and the enduring role music plays in helping people navigate life’s most meaningful moments."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/7m6tgJrZ4ovaftMA5jv4yw?si=PDWqBUQ8SleVnRT2BpUv4Q","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Raised in Pennsylvania and now rooted in the Southern landscape of South Carolina, Ashton draws from a life shaped by motherhood, nature, and a profound connection to music. Her songs unfold like front-porch confessions - earthy, intimate, and emotionally resonant. With a voice that carries both vulnerability and strength, Ashton blends Americana and singer-songwriter traditions into a sound that feels both timeless and deeply personal."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/818309/compressed_original-108dee4381e12ed153f9adfef84031cd.jpg","alt":"Photo Credit: isabellaosborn.photo\n"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The 'Love of Song' is a heartfelt album full of songs carefully selected to take the listener on a journey. It was born out of a lifelong relationship with music as both a refuge and companion. Each track was written in honest moments where melodies helped me make sense of real life.”","cite":"Brooke Ashton"},{"t":"p","html":"Through reflective lyricism and rich acoustic arrangements, the album celebrates the belief that songs have the power to heal, reveal truth, and bring people together."},{"t":"p","html":"The project represents more than just a collection of songs - it marks a creative milestone shaped by perseverance. The album took three years to complete, a journey that included the unexpected loss of Ashton’s original producer and close friend during the recording process. While raising three children and managing the responsibilities of daily life, Ashton continued carving out weekly studio sessions to finish the record. The result is a body of work that carries both emotional depth and quiet triumph."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/818314/large-af74df61eb2b1651c35a00328a17c4e5.jpg","alt":"Photo Credit: isabellaosborn.photo"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Music and songwriting have been a lifeline through every season of my life, I couldn’t keep these songs from the world - not with the chance that someone might benefit from hearing them. I didn’t set out to make a statement with this album. I just followed the songs where they led, and in the end it became a reflection of how deeply I love the craft of songwriting.”","cite":"Brooke Ashton"},{"t":"p","html":"With its warm acoustic spirit and reflective storytelling, <em>The Love of Song</em> evokes the soulful honesty of artists like<strong>&nbsp;Kacey Musgraves</strong> and <strong>Dolly Parton</strong>, while carving out its own path rooted in personal truth and introspection. Themes of womanhood, motherhood, nature, and self-discovery run throughout the record, inviting listeners to slow down and reconnect with what matters most."},{"t":"p","html":"Some of Ashton’s songs have already begun finding audiences beyond the album itself. Her track “<strong>Circles</strong>” was recently featured on the ESPN network’s television series TrueSouth, while <strong>“Ramblin’ Man</strong>” earned her a showcase opportunity at the Durango Songwriters Expo in October 2025."},{"t":"p","html":"At its core, <em>The Love of Song</em> is exactly what its title suggests: a heartfelt reflection on the mysterious bond between songwriter and melody. “Some of these songs felt like they were already waiting for me,” Ashton reflects. “This album is about that connection between a songwriter and the music that keeps showing up.”"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>The Love of Song </em>is available now on all major streaming platforms."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brooke Ashton"},{"t":"p","html":"Combining her love for lyrics and catchy melodies, Brooke Ashton enjoys writing songs about real life experiences. Honest, authentic, and inspiring are just a few words that have been used to describe her music. On any given day, Ashton can be found humming a new tune, belting out an existing song, or piecing together lyrics. She loves spending time with her family, hiking, adventure eating, traveling, and of course; songwriting!"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/818316/compressed_original-2c53abbeae48d623010c38ac28633c30.jpg","alt":"Photo Credit: isabellaosborn.photo"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Brooke"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://brookeashtonmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/brookeashtonmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/brookeashtonmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"447583","title":"Orange County Pop Artist Leake Drops Flirtatious New Single “Sweet”","date":"2026-03-13","lead":"Leake isn’t just bringing back big pop vocals, she’s reclaiming them.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/447583/af697d15e207aebb69b408f5aa6b37cc.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Leake isn’t just bringing back big pop vocals, she’s reclaiming them."},{"t":"p","html":"ORANGE COUNTY, CA - Rising pop artist Leake, the moniker of Taylor Leake, is set to release her bold and irresistibly catchy new single, “<strong>Sweet</strong>” on Friday, March 13, 2026. Packed with sky-high vocals, unapologetic attitude, and glossy 2010s-inspired production, “Sweet” marks a confident new chapter for the Orange County native."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/1lLoyB2usEWW0wZ2E6jKFS?si=ee24e7b215d74a23","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Blending the powerhouse vocal stylings reminiscent of <strong>Ariana Grande</strong> with the commanding presence of <strong>Christina Aguilera</strong>, Leake delivers a track that feels both nostalgic and refreshingly modern. “Sweet” revives the era of big pop hooks and challenging, belt-it-out choruses, the kind that demand to be sung at full volume with the windows down."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I think bringing back the loud, annoyingly high pop songs was needed now more than ever. This song is for my girls who use emotional detachment as protection.”","cite":"Leake shares."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/813751/large-ffe7ed41b06827f785c38bc8c356e5a9.jpg","alt":"\"Sweet\" Cover Art"},{"t":"p","html":"Built on punchy production from <strong>Nick Stone</strong>, “Sweet” leans into playful tension and late-night energy. The track’s shimmering pop layers and dynamic vocal runs showcase Leake’s technical range while maintaining a carefree, flirt-forward spirit."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I miss struggling to sing along in the car as a kid. Making music like this is what comes the most naturally and brings me the most satisfaction when it comes to creating.”","cite":"Leake"},{"t":"p","html":"More than just a pop release, “Sweet” taps into a cultural moment where autonomy, pleasure, and privacy intersect. It’s about knowing exactly what you want and refusing to over-explain it."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/813752/large-5c20582787e9a0ea3fc8aff13a2a34ad.jpg","alt":"Taylor Leake"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Production: Nick Stone<br id=\"isPasted\">Photo: <strong>Chloe Subia</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Taylor Leake"},{"t":"p","html":"Taylor Leake, known artistically as Leake, is a pop vocalist and songwriter hailing from Orange County, California. With a voice full of control and range, Leake is part of a new wave of pop artists reviving the unapologetic, high-gloss energy of 2010s radio, where powerhouse vocals and undeniable melodies take center stage. Drawing sonic inspiration from the vocal precision of Ariana Grande and the fearless intensity of Christina Aguilera, Leake blends technical vocal ability with playful confidence and emotional self-awareness. Her music centers on autonomy, desire, and the complexity of modern relationships.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Leake’s artistry is defined by contrast: sweet but sharp, polished yet raw, nostalgic yet forward-thinking. Whether delivering flirt-forward anthems or vocally demanding pop ballads, she brings a theatricality and commitment that feels both classic and current. With new music and visuals on the horizon, Leake is carving out a space where big vocals, bold femininity, and pop spectacle reign again."}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"449276","title":"Jean Noir Reimagines Southern California Nostalgia in New Single “Brad’s Cabana”","date":"2026-03-13","lead":"Blending Idyllic Melodies with Ambient Textures, the New Single Captures the Reckless Abandon of California Youth.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/449276/79bf3240c596fd8fa6432c45d19c76b9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Blending Idyllic Melodies with Ambient Textures, the New Single Captures the Reckless Abandon of California Youth."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>SANTA BARBARA, CA (March 13, 2026)</strong>&nbsp; — Singer-songwriter and multi-instrumentalist Jean Noir releases his new single, “Brad’s Cabana,” a track that transports listeners through a sonic portal into the reckless abandon and myth-making of his California youth. With roots in indie and punk bands, the artist’s latest project marks a return to music that features real-life vérité soundscapes. The new single \"Brad's Cabana\" is out on <strong>March 13, 2026.</strong>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/1O8edwYWS8Jstp9GM143tK?si=5wFHUidGQYuscJ1zHFwp0Q","label":"Listen Now","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Brad’s Cabana\" takes its name from a real place: a sun-bleached beach haunt in Santa Barbara that existed just outside the periphery of adult life. However, the song is less a portrait of a single location than a distillation of many—the hangouts, hideouts, and crumbling estates where California adolescence played out against a backdrop of faded glamour. Noir mines that particular alchemy to craft a song centered less on nostalgia for a specific place and more on a universal feeling that listeners will recognize as their own."},{"t":"quote","html":"The thing about Brad's Cabana is everyone has their version of it. Yours just had a different name... and probably wasn't a cabana.","cite":"Noir explains when describing the purpose of the song."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/816223/large-10df7ab605e7f873ba999ee4f87891c8.jpg","alt":"Photo credits to Veronica Black"},{"t":"p","html":"“Brad’s Cabana” is primarily anchored by finger-picked Baroque-style acoustic guitar arpeggios, resembling Mozart, while embellished with layers of orchestral arrangement inspired by the Beach Boys. Noir contrasts idyllic melodies with unsettling harmonic shifts and organic textures. The track is introduced by \"Brad's Cabana Intro,\" an ambient piece built from resampled field recordings captured at the artist's home studio. Key sonic elements, including a passing Amtrak horn and local coyote calls, act as a nocturnal counterweight to the atmosphere of the main single. Influenced by Sufjan Stevens, Vampire Weekend, Lana Del Rey, “Brad’s Cabana” sets the tone for Jean Noir’s forthcoming EP, Canyon Prince, and introduces the Jean Noir world."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Written, produced, and performed by&nbsp;<strong>Jean Noir</strong><br style=\"color: rgb(19, 20, 22); font-family: ProximaNova, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px;  white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\" id=\"isPasted\">Bass performed by&nbsp;<strong>Shiben Bhattacharya</strong><br style=\"color: rgb(19, 20, 22); font-family: ProximaNova, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px;  white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\">Additional engineering by&nbsp;<strong>Shiben Bhattacharya</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Scott Dittrich</strong><br style=\"color: rgb(19, 20, 22); font-family: ProximaNova, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px;  white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\">Mixed by <strong>Cole M.G.N.</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Jean Noir"},{"t":"p","html":"Based between Los Angeles and Santa Barbara, Jean Noir’s journey back to the spotlight has been anything but linear. After spending his twenties in the high-velocity indie punk bands Them Terribles and Dead Country, Noir stepped away from music to rehab old buildings into creative spaces for artists, and performers. The years spent working alongside other artists in those spaces proved formative in unexpected ways, and he returned to music with a new purpose: constructing a world of his own."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Jean Noir</strong>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1O8edwYWS8Jstp9GM143tK?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://instagram.com/jean_noir\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@JeanNoirOfficial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Youtube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.jeannoir.world\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1MFq4BDQXmo6DXNdbuiOzH?si=zOn7Sj2oTy2AgS98VbcAgw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"450060","title":"Ian McArdle Blends Synth Textures and Modern Jazz on New Single “Fearless Love of Caution”","date":"2026-03-13","lead":"A layered, forward-thinking jazz composition that rewards deep listening.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/450060/1d5c4266db241a64b39a25de46ba38a4.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A layered, forward-thinking jazz composition that rewards deep listening."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>OAKLAND, CA (March 13,2026)&nbsp;</strong>- &nbsp;Contemporary jazz composer, producer, and multi-instrumentalist <strong>Ian McArdle</strong> returns with his latest single, “<strong>Fearless Love of Caution</strong>”. The track is the newest preview of his forthcoming album <em><strong>Halcyon Week</strong></em>, showcasing McArdle’s distinctive blend of futuristic jazz composition, textured production, and emotionally resonant songwriting."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/2F3zLHV5jO0RnyOCbTFYBX?si=d362796a446543a7","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Built on a jagged, recurring synth loop that gradually intensifies, “Fearless Love of Caution” unfolds as a dynamic, shape-shifting composition. Layered, densely arranged vocals weave through melodic fretless bass and hybrid drums that drop in and out of the arrangement, creating tension and motion. The piece steadily crescendos into a high-energy piano solo before settling into a reflective groove, revealing the compositional depth and improvisational spirit at the core of McArdle’s sound."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817456/large-6f5ef723a2da561a9b8776a015c4a2d4.jpg","alt":"Ian McArdle"},{"t":"p","html":"Blending modern jazz sensibilities with experimental pop and forward-thinking production, McArdle crafts music that rewards careful listening. Fans of artists such as <strong>Pedro Martins</strong>, <strong>Jeff Parker</strong>, <strong>Blake Mills</strong> &amp; <strong>Pino Palladino</strong>, <strong>Bon Iver</strong>, <strong>Radiohead</strong>, and <strong>Jason Moran</strong> will find familiar inspiration within his exploratory sonic palette."},{"t":"quote","html":"“The chord progression stumbles and creates a tension, finally finding its footing at the piano solo.”","cite":"Ian McArdle"},{"t":"p","html":"Written, produced, and composed by McArdle, the track highlights his multifaceted musicianship as he performs piano, synthesizers, and vocals while leading a trio of trusted collaborators. The result is a composition that moves fluidly between structured songwriting and open-ended improvisation."},{"t":"p","html":"“Fearless Love of Caution” serves as the latest glimpse into <em>Halcyon Week</em>, an upcoming album that promises a rich blend of contemporary jazz, modern composition, and atmospheric production."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/817457/large-da6ac9a67d0120913f4d085f5c35aacc.jpg","alt":"Ginger Fierstein"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"list","items":["Composition, Production &amp; Lyrics: Ian McArdle","Piano, Synth &amp; Vocals: Ian McArdle","Drums: Shawn Myers","Fretless Bass: Keith Waters","Mixing &amp; Engineering: Cole Williams","Mastering: Simon Lancelot","View Mirror Photo: Ian McArdle","All Other Photos: Ginger Fierstein"]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Ian McArdle"},{"t":"p","html":"Ian McArdle is an Oakland, California–based composer, producer, and multi-instrumentalist whose work blends contemporary jazz with modern composition and experimental production. Drawing from the improvisational spirit of jazz and the sonic curiosity of indie and electronic music, McArdle creates detailed, layered recordings that reward close listening. His music often weaves together piano, synthesizers, textured vocals, and rhythm-forward arrangements, balancing structured composition with moments of spontaneous interplay."},{"t":"p","html":"His forthcoming album <em>Halcyon Week</em> continues this exploration, expanding his palette of futuristic jazz textures and intricate songwriting while maintaining an intimate, human core."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/mc.arthurgiuseppe?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%253D%253D&amp;utm_source=qr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://ianmcardlemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a>​"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"448577","title":"Veteran Songwriter Garry Manuel Returns with Defiant Protest Anthem “Stand For Good”","date":"2026-03-06","lead":"With “Stand For Good,” longtime independent artist Garry Manuel delivers one of the most uncompromising protest songs of his career, confronting injustice head-on through driving guitars and unflinching lyricism.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/448577/694fda933462059e07fb9816eef2937d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"With “Stand For Good,” longtime independent artist Garry Manuel delivers one of the most uncompromising protest songs of his career, confronting injustice head-on through driving guitars and unflinching lyricism."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>FAIRPORT, NY (March 6, 2026)</strong> - After more than four decades as a songwriter, producer, educator, and independent label founder, <strong>Garry Manuel</strong> delivers one of the most urgent recordings of his career. His new single, <strong>“Stand For Good,”</strong> out March 6, 2026, stands firmly in the lineage of American protest music - channeling grief, outrage, and moral conviction into a powerful rock statement that transforms tragedy into a call for unity, accountability, and moral courage."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2bl0l9tD26N6B1lMYkw9zY?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Built on industrial-leaning percussion, driving electric guitars, and emotionally charged vocals, “Stand For Good” directly addresses the fatal shootings of <strong>Renée Nicole Good</strong> and <strong>Alex Jeffrey Pretti </strong>during a protest against ICE in Minneapolis, grounding the song in real events and human experience. The track fuses rock with folk and folk-rock undertones, pairing a cinematic production with documentary-style lyricism that feels immediate and purposeful. Rather than speaking in broad abstractions, Manuel names the victims directly - a deliberate choice that amplifies their stories and honors their memory. The refrain, “<em>It’s understood - Let’s stand for Good,” </em>turns remembrance into resolve and gives the song its unifying, rallying core."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Watching the videos of the shots being fired at point-blank range into the bodies of Renee Good and Alex Pretti were sickening and appalling....There has been no accountability for their deaths. That should be troubling to every American.”","cite":"Garry Manuel, on what inspired his song \"Stand For Good\""},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/814677/large-5f1a8974a99be4d0fc0624f1824eaa6b.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Stand For Good\""},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, “Stand For Good” balances analog grit with modern clarity. Manuel oversees the composition and production, delivering vocals, electric guitars, and fretless bass, while <strong>Marshall Manuel</strong> brings precision through recording engineering, co-production, acoustic guitar, digital editing, and mastering. The arrangement weaves atmospheric textures with driving, conventional instrumentation, creating what Manuel describes as <em>“a news story as it’s happening, with the lyrics laying out the facts and the music holding the grief, anger, and weight that words alone can’t carry.” </em>The result is a track that feels both grassroots and expansive - intimate in its detail, yet powerful in its emotional and sonic impact."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/815102/large-32bac3b6ce7eaaac91dacd0d7cf0ba55.jpg","alt":"Marshall Manuel"},{"t":"p","html":"At a time when protest music is once again surging into the cultural conversation, Garry Manuel’s “Stand For Good” reinforces a truth that has echoed through American songwriting history: music remains one of the most potent vehicles for conscience."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Typically I don’t boast about my songs, however, after hearing this tune hundreds of times, I still feel my blood pressure rise. The music’s driving force, the production and lyrics combine into a powerful emotional experience. It speaks volumes and packs a punch.”","cite":"Garry Manuel on his song \"Stand For Good\""},{"t":"p","html":"Manuel is no stranger to politically conscious songwriting. In the early 1970s, with the band Sunup, he recorded “Attica,” reflecting on the Attica prison uprising, and “Old Wooden Barns,” an environmental warning issued before the band ever performed live. He later wrote and performed “Open Up,” continuing his engagement with civic themes. “Stand For Good” represents a continuation - not a departure - from a lifetime of socially reflective work."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/815099/large-8059717bdb6114f2ebf86b3a760df18d.jpg","alt":"Garry Manuel"},{"t":"p","html":"Unlike many artists entering political discourse for the first time, Manuel brings decades of independent industry experience to the table. As founder of <strong>Sunflare Records</strong>, he has maintained creative control over his catalog. He spent over 40 years mentoring musicians through Manuel’s Music Studio and the Rochester Area Music Project (RAMP), while also leading Project URGE, Inc., a nonprofit organization focused on collaborative solutions to poverty and racism in Rochester, New York."},{"t":"p","html":"The single arrives ahead of Manuel’s forthcoming album, <strong><em>Acoustically Speaking</em></strong>, a largely acoustic project slated for spring release. If that album explores reflection and restraint, “Stand For Good” is its counterpoint - immediate, forceful, and unwilling to let listeners look away."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"CONNECT WITH GARRY MANUEL"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.sunflaresongs.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/SunflareSongs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/sunflaresongs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCGZedbFE0crdFoGWeuu9Zog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/76NH1n3DCiInjGk6nXcDDa?utm_source=generator","height":"352"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"445956","title":"Emma Cook Expresses The Art of Unlearning with New Album “Of the Morning”","date":"2026-02-24","lead":"The Artist Finds Ease and Evolution in Shared Creative Spaces","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/445956/c165933d63dc65492f5a812e647c329e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Artist Finds Ease and Evolution in Shared Creative Spaces"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>BURLINGTON, VT (February 24, 2026)</strong> – Indie-folk artist Emma Cook is set to release her new album “Of the Morning” on Tuesday, February 24, 2026, which explores personal transformation and finding ease along the way. Blending Brooklyn-recorded base layers and Nashville session polishes, the 8-song album is her first solo project since becoming a full-time musician in 2018, marking a major career milestone. Her album release journey began in October 2025 with her first single “Thirteen Moons.”"},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/emmacook/of-the-morning","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"I've always had a lot of ideas, and I'm trying not to minimize the fact that as a self-employed indie musician it's a really big deal that I was able to see this Big Idea through.","cite":"Emma Cook on inspiration behind \"Of the Morning.\""},{"t":"p","html":"In Cook's experience, her 30s have been a season of unlearning and returning to herself – a transformative decade during which every song on this record was penned. The project's inception, an arrangement session with producer Katie Martucci, coincided with the her daughter's first birthday and mirrored a significant shift in Cook's own personal bandwidth. Moving away from her previously self-produced methods, she discovered a newfound necessity for collaboration with a producer to unlock further possibilities, defining her new direction."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/810332/large-5a97a95bfd7656a519fe8eaf38202d8a.jpg","alt":"Cover art for “Of the Morning” by Emma Cook"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The best part of this whole process has been getting to work with such talented and inspiring musicians and artists and creative folks along the way”","cite":"Cook expresses when discussing the process of bringing her vision to life."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/810333/large-104014d2d05c68f58647751bd6ef5324.jpg","alt":"Photo Credits to Macaulay Lerman"},{"t":"quote","html":"In late 2022, after the birth of my daughter, my priorities and intentions came more sharply into focus, and I knew I needed to make this album - for me, and for her.","cite":"Cook remarks."},{"t":"p","html":"“Of the Morning” features a cohesive 8-song story, distilled from an original 14 tracks, reflecting the collaborative energy between the artist and producer Katie Martucci. The release was made possible after a successful Kickstarter campaign that raised over $15,000, featuring unique merchandise, including protein pancake mix, jammy t-shirts, and custom mugs."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Vocals, Piano, Harmony Vocals - <strong>Emma Cook</strong><br>Acoustic Guitar, Harmony Vocals - <strong>Katie Martucci</strong><br>Percussion, Zither, Harmony Vocals - <strong>Dylan Mckinstry</strong><br>Harmony Vocals (You Are Not Alone, 21st Century) - <strong>Allie Chipkin</strong><br>Auxiliary Piano, Organ, Bass - <strong>Ben Sanders</strong><br>Drums - <strong>Mark Raudabaugh</strong><br>Bass - <strong>Michael Rinne</strong><br>Harmony Vocals (Forbidden Fruit) - <strong>Lizzy Ross</strong><br>Electric Guitar - <strong>Sam Talmadge</strong><br>Trumpet - <strong>Tree Palmedo</strong><br>Trombone -<strong>&nbsp;John Cushing</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Production and Technical Credits</strong><br>Producer - <strong>Katie Martucci</strong><br id=\"isPasted\">Recording Engineer (Brooklyn, NY) -<strong>&nbsp;Dylan Mckinstry at Greenpoint Recording Collective</strong><br>Recording Engineer (Nashville, TN) - <strong>Ben Sanders at Barnfire Creative</strong><br>Mixing - <strong>Scott Hudley</strong><br>Mastering - <strong>Philip Shaw Bova</strong><br>Cover Photo - <strong>Macaulay Lerman</strong><br>Album Design - <strong>Beenanza</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Emma Cook"},{"t":"p","html":"Living by the idea that \"finding ease doesn't mean a lack of effort,\" singer-songwriter Emma Cook turns inward, offering some of her most vulnerable and finely crafted work to date. Written during a transformational stretch of life - turning thirty in the early days of the global pandemic, becoming a mother, and reckoning with a rapidly changing world - these songs reflect what she calls her “delightfully melancholic experience of being human.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Weaving themes of moon cycles, forbidden fruit, motherhood, climate anxiety, and the everyday beauty in between, <em>Of the Morning</em> is, in Cook’s words, “a tender chronicle about growing the f** up.” With humor, honesty, and a soothing voice that has been called “incomparably smooth” (The Deli Magazine), Emma writes about Big Things - and the small, quiet moments that make a big life. Her expressive vocal range, jazz-inflected chord choices, and folk-rooted storytelling create a sound that’s both expansive and intimate. Think Maggie Rogers meets Carole King by way of the forest floor."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6wT4rgU77magWbJprjGXoI?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"A formidable songwriter and instrumentalist","cite":"Jordan Adams, Seven Days."},{"t":"p","html":"Emma grew up in the Michigan folk and traditional music scene, learning guitar and piano before she was a teenager. Her sound blends the folk, roots, pop, and jazz that raised her into something unmistakably her own. From 2013–2019, she toured throughout New England and the Midwest with her folk-funk band <strong>Questionable Company</strong>, playing festivals, dive bars, and barns. The group earned a loyal following and critical praise for their energy and musicianship. Moving away from her self-produced roots, Emma has entered a season of creative expansion, partnering with producer Katie Martucci to transform her intimate sketches into the lush, collaborative arrangements found throughout Of the Morning."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Emma’s music is warm, cozy and captivating all at once. She gave a house concert at our home, and everyone was rapt. Her beautiful voice, musicianship and storytelling provided a wonderfully intimate and memorable event for all.","cite":"Anne, House Concert Host."},{"t":"p","html":"Since then, Emma has continued to grow her artistry and will continue to perform at the following locations:"},{"t":"list","items":["<strong>Saturday, March 14th</strong> at <em>Higher Ground in S. Burlington, VT</em> with Reid Parsons and Danny LeFrancois -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://highergroundmusic.com/events/emma-cook/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Buy your tickets now</a>","<strong>Thursday, April 9th</strong> at <em>Club Passim in Cambridge, MA</em> with Kara McGee and Louie Lou Louis - <a href=\"https://www.passim.org/live-music/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Buy your tickets now</a>","<strong>Sunday, April 12th</strong> at&nbsp;<em>House Concert in Brooklyn, NY</em> with &nbsp;Louie Lou Louis - <a href=\"http://www.instagram.com/em_ma_cook\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Send a DM to get the address</a>"]},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/781356/large-eeabc6930e22123144aaebbfd56c563f.jpg","alt":"Image by Macaulay Lerman"},{"t":"p","html":"Now based in Vermont, Emma is not only a songwriter and performer, but also a beloved music educator and children’s musician in her local community. Deeply rooted in both her Michigan upbringing and Vermont home, she finds creative fuel in nature, family, and the simple joy of everyday life. “More than anything,” Emma says, “I believe in the power of music - to connect, to heal, to transform. These songs were offered to me from somewhere beyond myself, and now I offer them to you.”"},{"t":"p","html":"When she’s not making music, you’ll likely find Emma in the garden, riding her bike, doing yoga, making soup, swimming in wild water, or reading with her kiddo by her side."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Emma Cook:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.ecookmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"http://instagram.com/em_ma_cook\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"http://facebook.com/ecookmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6wT4rgU77magWbJprjGXoI\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/emma-cook/1542224776\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"445925","title":"An Enduring Voice from the Rock Underground","date":"2026-02-20","lead":"An Underground Story Still Unfolding","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/445925/698a2b34e228e314d3425001a3a761c4.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An Underground Story Still Unfolding"},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, CALIFORNIA - At an age when many artists are content to reflect on past achievements, Dave Lebental is still moving forward. His latest album, <em>Stylus</em>, follows 2024’s <em>The Long Player</em>, which earned positive attention across the music blogosphere and accumulated more than one million combined streams on Spotify and YouTube."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/3845N0PJaYwz6T57lJPo0Q?si=TXhoruvRQmuliNM7kawP0g","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Rather than remain in the Americana lane of his previous work, Lebental leans into his long-standing love of melodic, piano-driven rock on Stylus. Drawing inspiration from writers such as <strong>The Beatles</strong>, <strong>Elton John</strong>, <strong>Supertramp</strong>, and<strong>&nbsp;Elvis Costello</strong>, the album reflects a tradition of piano-based songwriting built on melody, emotional clarity, and songs designed to last."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/810941/large-caf9273cb31ddb2f46822a8dcdc89cc6.png","alt":"Stylus Cover Art"},{"t":"p","html":"Like the records that inspired it, <em>Stylus</em> is forward-looking rather than nostalgic. The album offers new songs for listeners who grew up with classic piano rock and are still searching for music that delivers the same sense of discovery and connection."},{"t":"p","html":"Lebental is joined by his live band, Karma Train, and together they are based in Los Angeles, touring West Coast venues while maintaining a global presence through a series of monthly live concert streams broadcast from an underground studio. These performances bring <em>Stylus</em> to life in full, offering audiences an unfiltered, performance-driven introduction to the record and the band behind it."},{"t":"quote","html":"“The title Stylus reflects who I am as a songwriter, a lifelong vinyl listener, and a recording artist who’s always balancing new ideas with classic form. I wanted a title that nodded quietly to my love of albums and the ritual of listening. I knew a stylus as the needle on a turntable, what I didn’t realize at first is that the word also means a writing instrument. Once I made that connection, it felt exactly right. The album lives at that intersection: songs written by hand, then brought to life on record.”","cite":"Dave Lebental"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/811192/compressed_original-ca83ec5360140101103ce517a78221c0.png","alt":"Tour Poster"},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, <em>Stylus</em> draws inspiration from the great album-makers of rock’s most enduring eras. Fans of <strong>The Beatles</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;Elton John</strong>, <strong>Supertramp</strong>, and <strong>Elvis Costello</strong> will recognize the emphasis on melody, structure, and emotional clarity, filtered through Lebental’s seasoned perspective."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I’m an older, fully independent artist operating mostly underground, touring the West Coast with my band Karma Train and supported by a passionate, word-of-mouth fanbase, I’m not chasing fads or seeking stardom. I create out of my love of great rock songs. My catalog resonates with all ages, but especially with older audiences who feel disengaged with the current sound of rock, rap, hip-hop, and kiddy pop music.”","cite":"Dave Lebental"},{"t":"p","html":"Dave is deeply committed to preserving the classic and timeless sound of vintage rock music. Creating and performing this genre is a joyful form of art that should be cherished in today's evolving world. The enthusiasm and happiness for this genre, often considered the foundation of music, is something Dave exudes in conversation and most definitely in his music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"In his upcoming album, Lebental offers new songs for listeners who grew up with classic piano rock and are still searching for music that delivers the same sense of discovery and connection."},{"t":"p","html":"This year, 2026, the group plans to go on tour to promote the new album, <em>Stylus</em>. The songs of this LP come to life on stage, with a focus on spontaneity, emotion, and connection, which result in performances that are best enjoyed by attentive fans who come back for more."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/810947/large-0c72639d5b1cdcc777231eb3e553c7ca.jpg","alt":"Dave Lebental Featured Photo"},{"t":"h2","html":"About Dave Lebental"},{"t":"p","html":"Dave Lebental is a rock singer-songwriter whose music blends piano-driven rock with Americana and blues, grounded in strong melodies and personal storytelling. Writing, producing, and releasing his own material, Lebental leads a seasoned live band, Karma Train, made up of accomplished players with deep roots in rock, soul, and blues."},{"t":"p","html":"Lebental first emerged in the 1990s as the singer-songwriter behind guitar-driven rock bands Sunflower and Placebo Royale. Placebo Royale’s independent release, Crème de Mentia, charted on CMJ and developed a dedicated underground following. Both bands were fixtures on the California rock club circuit, where Lebental built a loyal live audience and shared bills with artists including Mick Taylor, Jane’s Addiction, Midnight Oil, X, The Blasters, The Plimsouls, The Tubes, Edgar Winter, and Leon Russell, among others."},{"t":"p","html":"Today, <em>Stylus</em> marks Lebental’s second solo LP. Advance singles have gained traction across Spotify, U.S. radio playlists, and YouTube, while press coverage has highlighted his resilience and long-running commitment to artistic independence."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Dave"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@dlmusic.us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://dlmusic.us/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/dlmusic.us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/DLMusic.US/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCC5gMEB0_DV0ziMiu29WFQg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Youtube</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"446346","title":"INDVGO Reclaims Her Narrative in Atmospheric New R&B Single “Not About You”","date":"2026-02-20","lead":"A cinematic R&B journey that provides a sanctuary for listeners to sit with the thoughts they won’t say out loud.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/446346/44bee4f36ce3ce7aefe6aa2903815419.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A cinematic R&amp;B journey that provides a sanctuary for listeners to sit with the thoughts they won’t say out loud."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>BROOKLYN, NY (February 20, 2026)</strong> — Brooklyn, NY artist INDVGO dives into emotional restraints and dark-feminine storytelling with new song “Not About You,” which will be released on February 20, 2026, on all major streaming platforms. Perfect for a late-night drive environment, this alternative R&amp;B track fills up space during nocturnal hours when the city becomes quiet and thoughts intensify. The new release marks a definitive shift toward a moodier, more immersive sonic direction that listeners can expect to see more of in INDVGO's upcoming projects."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/5xTVtwxwuzD1MdeaS8jfAT?si=TXf0pyUWSnmPLxwicuPOig","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"It’s really the internal monologue fighting your pride. Like… you say you’ve moved on. You’re ‘over it.’ But you still catch yourself thinking about it... acting like the song isn’t about them. And technically? It’s not. It’s about you.","cite":"INDVGO expresses."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Not About You\" explores the tension one pretends to have moved on from a relationship, while playing past events in their heads on repeat. Concealing unresolved feelings, the track captures irritation, vulnerability, and self-awareness to express the feeling of living in one’s own thoughts. It’s a song for solitude, where listeners are invited to sit with what has not been vocalized."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/810958/large-55d83c5993a6d53c541179adb4e440b8.png","alt":"Photo Credits to INDVGO"},{"t":"p","html":"Engineered by Jorelle Montes and written by INDVGO, “Not About You” contains minimal and nocturnal production to create a cinematic space, allowing emotions to simmer instead of exploding. The artist drew inspiration from The Weeknd, Billie Eilish, and Jhené Aiko, immersing listeners through the atmospheric depth during after-dark listening environments."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Written by: INDVGO<br>Engineered, Mixed &amp; Mastered by: Jorelle Montes"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About INDVGO"},{"t":"p","html":"INDVGO is an alternative R&amp;B artist from Brooklyn, NY known for balancing soulful and cinematic noir influences. Her music centers around themes of emotional restraint, narcissistic relationships, and self-awareness, resonating with listeners by creating a sanctuary for thoughts to unfold."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/61Se7XU0y8Gi4T64t1nfMA?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with INDVGO </strong><a href=\"https://beacons.ai/indvgo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>here</strong></a>."}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"447236","title":"Oakland's Ian McArdle Redefines Jazz and Alternative with \"Saka\"","date":"2026-02-20","lead":"Bay Area's Favorite \"Side Musician\" Steps into Spotlight with an Experimental Instrumental Journey","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/447236/4b62483067fca1e4ddc6a7d86406e2ed.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Bay Area's Favorite \"Side Musician\" Steps into Spotlight with an Experimental Instrumental Journey"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>OAKLAND, CA (February 20th, 2026)</strong> — Composer, producer, and pianist <strong>Ian McArdle</strong>, from the Bay Area, releases his latest single, <strong>\"Saka\" on February 20, 2026</strong>. Preceding the debut of his album \"Halcyon Week\", the new release represents a bold step forward in McArdle’s vision as a solo artist."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/2ACnZTJkMRFCEDgyKGgQTE?si=551a5231ba2b4c5d","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Originated from an accidental loop on a Montreal Assembly Count To Five pedal, \"Saka\" blends the cerebral complexity of jazz with the raw energy of alternative, blossoming into a \"hazy futuristic jam\" that rewards close listening."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/812272/large-bae62b7969b6a6847aff01cdcfbecb13.jpg","alt":"Credits to Ginger Fierstein"},{"t":"quote","html":"For over ten years most people have known me as a capable side musician playing in many different genres in the vibrant Bay Area music scene, but this is my first time stepping out and bringing my musical vision to fruition.","cite":"McArdle  describes."},{"t":"p","html":"The single is anchored by a powerhouse percussion duo. While drummer Shawn Myers played a Haitian inspired 9/8 groove on the first half of the song, musician D'Mauriae Harris played heavy chop drums on the second half. In addition to the interesting drum arrangement, McArdle describes the lyrics as stream-of-consciousness, portraying abstract poetry rather than traditional storytelling."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/812273/large-a745e0ccc78d7065bb895310f0659237.jpg","alt":"Credits to Ginger Fierstein"},{"t":"quote","html":"This album features the talents of Bay Area musicians who I’m happy to have as friends and collaborators over the 10+ years I’ve been involved in this music scene","cite":"the artist mentions."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Production/Composition: Ian McArdle<br>Mixing/Engineering: Cole Williams<br>Mastering: Simon Lancelot<br>Artwork: Ginger Fierstein"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Ian McArdle"},{"t":"p","html":"Ian McArdle is a composer, session musician, producer, and pianist based in Oakland, CA. McArdle’s solo work explores the intersection of experimental jazz and modern composition establishing him as a rising force in the California jazz scene."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Ian McArdle</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/mc.arthurgiuseppe?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%253D%253D&amp;utm_source=qr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://ianmcardlemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"444296","title":"Rahul Mukerji Unites Musicians During the Pandemic Through Progressive Metal, Rock, and Jazz Fusion on New Single “Dushtan”","date":"2026-02-13","lead":"An Indo-Fusion Instrumental Exploring Restlessness, Resistance, and Unity Through Global Collaboration","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/444296/67555ff1760c228fa4243496953760af.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An Indo-Fusion Instrumental Exploring Restlessness, Resistance, and Unity Through Global Collaboration"},{"t":"p","html":"GERMANTOWN, MARYLAND (February 13th, 2026) — Rahul Mukerji, an innovative musician from Germantown, Maryland, now based in Boquete, Panama, releases his new single, “Dushtan,” out February 13, 2026, on all major streaming platforms. The track serves as the first introduction to his forthcoming album, slated for release later this year."},{"t":"p","html":"A project born from the pandemic, “Dushtan,” meaning “the rogue,” channels restlessness and resistance forged through isolation. During quarantine, Mukerji found the world locked inside a cage, where the feeling of separation haunted the artist. To translate that emotion, the musician blends indo-fusion instrumental music with progressive metal, rock, and jazz, collaborating with performers from around the world. The result is a heavy yet expansive composition that signifies unity amidst isolation."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3RtijFGgHuzfgeYXZDVR8r?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"Music is the universal language. This kind of asynchronous collaboration was a great way to pull people together during a time of separation.","cite":"Rahul Mukerji"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/810190/large-b4f0dccdf45ade3ff472927b0cce5536.jpeg","alt":"Image captured by Shawna Adora"},{"t":"p","html":"A longtime admirer of artists like Pain of Salvation, Symphony X, and more, Mukerji worked with instrumentalists trained across both Western and non-Western musical traditions. Rather than prescribing fixed parts, Mukerji allowed musicians to interpret their roles and inspirations freely, encouraging a sense of release and movement through structural frameworks, instead of sheet music."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/807775/large-dfd55d19b1057bbfe0010a6fceed5c03.jpg","alt":"Proviscocity Studios"},{"t":"p","html":"Written around a Phrygian tonality to emphasize a dark shade, the song carries a sense of urgency through bold percussion, a driving bass line, and an explosive drum performance by Leo Margarit, the accomplished drummer for the acclaimed progressive metal band Pain of Salvation. To subvert expectation, Mukerji incorporates a violin solo, adding a playful edge to the track’s intensity."},{"t":"p","html":"This is single will tease Mukerji’s innovative new album, Mridingit, which will be available on March 23, 2026."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by: Bruce Ng &amp; Rahul Mukerji<br id=\"isPasted\">Mixed &amp; Mastered by: Brett Caldas-Lima at Tower Studio<br>Album Artwork, Concept &amp; Layout: Proviscocity Studios<br><strong>Performers</strong><br>Rahul Mukerji: Guitars, Programming<br>Leo Margarit: Drums<br>Ruben Rubio: Bass<br>Chaplin: Piano, Keyboards<br>Thisara Bandara: Violin"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h2","html":"About Rahul Mukerji"},{"t":"p","html":"Rahul Mukerji is a multi-disciplinary musician, composer, and visual artist whose creations bridge fusion, rock, jazz, and cinematic sound design into a signature style that is technically rigorous while still being emotionally immersive. Born in India and active for more than two decades, Mukerji has developed a variety of work that moves between high-energy performance and narrative-driven composition. Since his debut album in 2017, Mukerji has gained recognition through notable performances, including The John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts in 2020, spotlighted in Vintage Guitar Magazine in 2021, and been nominated for his work at the Washington Area Music Awards in 2022. Whether delivering dynamic guitar-forward performances, composing cinematic music, or shaping audio-visual narratives, Rahul Mukerji continues to explore the expansive possibilities of modern world fusion."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Rahul Mukerji"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.mukerji.us/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/rahul__mukerji/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Rahul.Mukerji.Artist/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/RahulMukerji\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Youtube</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"444485","title":"Denver Alt-Pop Artist Shares “Hurry” to Explore Desire and Control","date":"2026-02-11","lead":"A hypnotic exploration of desire, control, and feminine autonomy","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/444485/c3dd2433afbc803303993e2b4c3a71e2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A hypnotic exploration of desire, control, and feminine autonomy"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>DENVER, CO (February 10, 2026)</strong> — Riah, a Denver-based artist, is premiering the official music video of her single “Hurry” on YouTube on February 10th, 2026. This track is originally from on her late-2024 album “Trauma Bond.\" Written from a place of emotional tension, “Hurry” explores the intersection between desire and action: The moment where wanting someone feels urgent but choosing costs power."},{"t":"p","html":"The music video will have a publically at Love Bites show at the Creepatorium on February 14th, where Riah will be performing her song live alongside other Aerial, Burlesque, Dance, and Live Music acts from the DejaView crew. All ticket sale payouts from this show will be donated to worthy current causes. Get your tickets <a href=\"https://creepatorium.holdmyticket.com/tickets/457257?tc=hmt&amp;fbclid=IwY2xjawPiMJtleHRuA2FlbQIxMABicmlkETFHT285MXhOc0xucjdNYVVrc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHtUgo0oF8xDYvBBGN7n5Kit_8ejpzY2bzTNveebWo75jIE88jyUmQT5i22dQ_aem_4V6ix4C3OGk6hPeLkFwEYA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>."},{"t":"p","html":"The track emphasizes anticipation rather than the feeling of release through leaning into the psychological push-and-pull, which is a concept that defines modern dating and intimacy. Riah’s signature balance of softness and menace is once again showcased in \"Hurry\" by blending atmospheric, rhythm-driven alt-pop with moody bass lines, intimate vocals, and restrained production."},{"t":"button","href":"https://youtu.be/6JoRwIrNYDA","label":"Preview Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"Hurry started picking up unexpected momentum months after the album came out, and that response made me realize the song still had more to say visually,","cite":"Riah expresses."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/808624/large-50981d3dcadb7e07e8c2150acf44c159.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13383.jpg"},{"t":"quote","html":"Even though it’s unconventional to release a video over a year later, the energy around it felt alive again, so I followed it.","cite":"Riah"},{"t":"p","html":"Directed with bold visual intention, the music video contains bright, intentional spaces, tightly choreographed movement, and multiple vibrant worlds, while introducing an alter ego, who embodies the internal conflict between instinct and restraint.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"Every setting is bold on purpose, mirroring the urgency and tension in the song.","cite":"Riah"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/808626/large-0712e2d05c366973e8157b4cf2f3085b.jpeg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13502.jpeg"},{"t":"quote","html":"She represents the part of me that pushes, challenges, and refuses to wait. Neither side is right or wrong.","cite":"Riah"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by Pacific and mixed and mastered by Quoc Truong, “Hurry” stands as a defining visual chapter for the song, reinforcing Riah’s confidence-driven approach to intimacy, autonomy, and self-duality. Rather than offering resolution, both the song and video sit comfortably in anticipation, who moves first, who waits, and who ultimately decides. The video was shot by Johnny Singels and choreographed by Lindsey Judd."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Artist &amp; Lyrics: Riah<br id=\"isPasted\">Produced by: Pacific<br>Mixed &amp; Mastered by: Quoc Truong<br>Videographer: Johnny Singels<br>Choreographer: Lindsey Judd"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Riah"},{"t":"p","html":"Riah is a rising force in the Bedroom Pop scene, known for her introspective, emotionally charged music that explores love, sex, loss, and a signature “villain energy.” Having entered the Los Angeles entertainment industry at just 17, she endured the harsh realities of the pre-Me Too era, which ultimately drove her to reclaim autonomy over her art. Now a successful entrepreneur, Riah returns to music on her own terms—infusing each lyric with raw honesty drawn from personal experience. A seasoned performer at festivals, clubs, and acoustic venues, she also channels her expressive power through competitive pole dance. With her unique blend of vulnerability and strength, Riah is redefining Bedroom Pop with authenticity and edge."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Riah"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://tr.ee/c0CFpxk2Pp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/riah/1687913738\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/riahmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"443092","title":"Kenny Hotopp Taps Nashville Musicians for New Americana Album “The South Looks Good on You”","date":"2026-01-30","lead":"An Introspective Americana Album Exploring Family, Memory, and Growth","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/443092/e239f783af878b6922d329598c3c57ea.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An Introspective Americana Album Exploring Family, Memory, and Growth"},{"t":"p","html":"WATERFORD, WI (January 30, 2026) — Kenny Hotopp, a Midwest-based Americana singer-songwriter, draws from authentic, lived experience on his new album “<em>The South Looks Good on You,</em>” out January 30, 2026, on all major streaming platforms. This introspective release marks a significant step forward in his career with elevated production."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/3Nrvf0xON0e2XpQtzhOQlQ?si=eocgKKgYTzSBaCaz3KuQ3w","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Hotopp’s creative journey began with a country band named Kenny and the Night Owls. Following the sudden passing of a band member, a shift in the band's dynamic prompted him to pursue a solo path as a singer-songwriter. On this new path, his sound evolved from country to Americana through collaborations with professional musicians from Nashville."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/805625/large-2a37ec48fdfc0290a121b2b395bb1d0d.jpg","alt":"Photo Credit: Kevin Viol"},{"t":"p","html":"The album's title track “<em>The South Looks Good on You</em>” documents the special moment when Hotopp’s daughter moved away to college in Mississippi. This song initially began as a poem and later transitioned into a song, recalling tears of goodbye and the realization that his daughter was thriving in her new chapter."},{"t":"quote","html":"She came home… looking healthy, having fun… and I just said, ‘The South looks good on you.'","cite":"– Kenny Hotopp"},{"t":"p","html":"From a wider lens, the album explores themes of family, love, reflection, and loss. The songs are drawn from small yet meaningful moments of his life, transforming Hotopp’s journal entries into music. The musician also shares memory-based stories to reflect his gratitude towards his father, starting with a previously released song, “American Legion Days,” written in remembrance of his time in the Air Force."},{"t":"p","html":"This album further reflects Hotopp’s artistic growth through collaborations with Nashville musicians who built full arrangements around his original songs. As the project came together, it evolved into a thematic calling card shaped by Hotopp’s time in Nashville, documenting both his musical and personal journey. What began as a creative process ultimately took on deeper personal meaning, capturing a pivotal chapter in both his artistic and personal evolution. The artist felt empowered and fully focused on songwriting and singing, almost as if he were performing karaoke to his original songs."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/805626/large-f73542cbd3898739e9be65cd43b7b25f.jpg","alt":"Photo Credit: Kevin Viol"},{"t":"h2","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"All songs written by: Kenny Hotopp<br>Vocals: Kenny Hotopp<br>Electric Guitar: Chris Leuzinger &amp; Austin Crum<br>Acoustic guitar: Austin Crum &amp; Adam Knight<br>Bass Guitar: Duncan Mullins &amp; Aaron Dingus<br>Steel Guitar: Tony Dingus<br>Fiddle: David Yates<br>Keys: Adam Knight&nbsp;<br>Drums: Johnathan Presnell<br>Sax: Tim Kinchen&nbsp;<br>Harmonica: Randy Miller<br>Background Vocals: Victoria Bowlin<br>Recorded at: Hilltop Studios / Nashville, TN<br>Mixed &amp; Mastered: Adam Knight<br>Album Photos: Kevin Viol"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h2","html":"About Kenny Hotopp"},{"t":"p","html":"Based in Waterford, Wisconsin, Kenny Hotopp writes and sings soul-felt songs about family, love, memory, and the lifelong search for peace. His music blends genres from Americana and folk to blues and country but always centers on authenticity, heart, and lived experience. Every track is a story, every lyric an invitation to connect."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Kenny Hotopp</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://kennyhotopp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/kenny_hotopp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=10234333295046619&amp;set=a.10201021262586627\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"442892","title":"Luke Dame Rides Through the Stages of Grief on New Single \"Wyoming\"","date":"2026-01-23","lead":"A Folk Original that Explores Isolation and Self-Reckoning, while Carrying the Emotional Weight of Hardcore and Metal","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/442892/b77eb6de09b070eea246913dbeb4efa0.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A Folk Original that Explores Isolation and Self-Reckoning, while Carrying the Emotional Weight of Hardcore and Metal"},{"t":"p","html":"Saint Albans, Vermont (January 23, 2026) — Based in Northern Vermont, singer-songwriter Luke Dame releases his introspective single, “Wyoming,” blending emotionally restrained songwriting shaped by his years living in Seattle with acoustic folk foundations. The track reflects on isolation and emotional withdrawal following a step back from public life, and will be released on January 23, 2026. Through this release, Dame hopes to share the kind of music he enjoys through authentic songwriting to capture his honesty and struggles."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/track/2cGz6e0UfYe0F4Zhngo0TP?si=5b5cdda6e3944783","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Dame wrote “Wyoming” during a period when he stopped posting on social media actively, withdrawing from the public’s eye. In that silence, he realized that many people he believed were friends never reached out once he disappeared. Hence, the track captures the grieving process, particularly the anger stage, of accepting the absence of a community he thought he had."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/805280/large-f6f56a516d8cdf4b40502787777f32bd.jpg","alt":"Montana Nolan (@moptana on Instagram)"},{"t":"quote","html":"It's funny how writing something so sad can be the best way to bring you joy. It is almost like catharsis.","cite":"Luke Dame"},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded at Serif Sound, mixed and produced by Koby Nelson, and mastered by Raelynn Janicke at Infrasonic Sound, the new single marks a focused and emotionally-grounded step forward as an emerging artist."},{"t":"quote","html":"“You can produce sounds on a song endlessly; you can't produce honesty. I hope this song sounds as honest to others as it feels to me.”","cite":"Luke Dame"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/805270/large-e61f382850af72d8d082c4fe9431a234.jpg","alt":"Montana Nolan (@moptana on Instagram)"},{"t":"h2","html":"About Luke Dame"},{"t":"p","html":"Luke Dame is a singer-songwriter based in Northern Vermont. He learned guitar as a child while playing in a church band, an experience that led him to join bands by the age of fourteen and ultimately introduced him to songwriting. Though Dame was involved in multiple music projects throughout his teens and early twenties, he eventually stepped away from music after facing a prolonged period of writer’s block."},{"t":"p","html":"In 2024, Dame and his girlfriend relocated from Seattle to a small apartment in Vermont, a transition that brought challenges as he adjusted from city life to a rural environment. During this period, Dame experienced a persistent sense of darkness that pushed him back toward songwriting. He went on to write over 30 new songs exploring themes of religious guilt and loss of faith, wanderlust, and the process of unlearning generational habits. At the core of Dame’s work is honesty. Where he once measured the value of his art by monetary success or status, he now writes simply to share his stories with anyone willing to listen."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Luke Dame:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/xpookiexbearx/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"http://lukedame.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"439445","title":"Columbus, OH Artists Matthew Morgan & Jamie Ravine Confront Resilience and Stereotypes in New Single “In The Blood”","date":"2026-01-16","lead":"A powerful collaboration exploring the isolating experience of being boxed into stereotypes as professional musicians and songwriters","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/439445/0bbb810c588ad5fafaf672d58fb088f8.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A powerful collaboration exploring the isolating experience of being boxed into stereotypes as professional musicians and songwriters"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>COLUMBUS, OH (January 16, 2026)</strong> — Matthew Morgan, an indie, alternative, and folk troubadour from Columbus, Ohio, collaborates with award-winning singer-songwriter and community leader Jamie Ravine on a new single, “<strong>In The Blood</strong>”, out January 16, 2026 on all major streaming platforms. Shaped by the challenges independent artists face in today’s music industry, “In The Blood” explores themes of resilience and the isolating experience of being boxed into stereotypes as a professional musician and songwriter."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/3DiTJUkoGkhDmtfjzvkjFX?si=cWKrLYeQTLGJgF6h1CR7TQ","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"The collaborative track highlights both artists’ strengths as indie rock and folk songwriters, while drawing subtle inspiration from the retro synth textures of the ‘80s and ‘90s that shaped their musical upbringing. With these instrumental choices, Morgan and Ravine aim to utilize bold sonic elements to make a confident declaration that this is who they are and they’re proud of what they do as singer-songwriters."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/802632/large-84166c90a48f20eb31c4ed5f459944b9.jpg","alt":"Robert Colgan"},{"t":"quote","html":"No one else has the right to define you. You owe it to yourself and the world to be comfortable in your own skin and to draw power and motivation from the blood that runs through your veins.","cite":"Morgan explains. Ravine also adds that one should"},{"t":"quote","html":"be authentically, unapologetically, and wildly you! People are going to try and pull you down, but that just means you're doing something worth noting.","cite":""},{"t":"p","html":"Morgan and Ravine feel that musicians are often misunderstood due to the perceived instability of pursuing a music career. Fortunately, Morgan discovered a sanctuary called \"Green Room\" in Columbus, Ohio, founded by Ravine. Created as a supportive space for musicians to be seen, heard, and valued, <em>Green Room</em> has grown into a vital community hub, offering connection and encouragement amid an increasingly challenging music industry landscape. As venues close, streaming payouts shrink, public arts funding disappears, and AI threatens creative labor, <em>Green Room</em> has become a stronghold for independent artists banding together. Today, the community includes over 400 members online, with more than 50 musicians gathering in person each month."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Songwriter: Matthew Morgan and Jamie Ravine<br>Producer: Brian Skeel<br>Press Photos: Robert Colgan"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/802629/large-2bf8dd3c90f44c9f2b5a2c8b8606b984.jpg","alt":"Robert Colgan"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Matthew Morgan"},{"t":"p","html":"Matthew Morgan is an indie, alternative, and folk artist inspired by the timeless songwriting of Nick Drake and Neil Young. Morgan’s music allows his baritone voice to float above delicate arrangements, while emphasizing a warm and soulful character. A natural storyteller whose songs feel less like narratives and more like impressionistic paintings, Morgan is also a multi-instrumentalist, crafting his music with guitar, piano, organ, harmonica, and a range of other instruments. His previous full-length album, Timepiece, released independently in October 2023, received positive reviews and charted at #24 on the FAI Folk Radio charts. Written in the wake of the COVID-19 pandemic, it reflects the emotional highs and lows of a deeply challenging period, while also highlighting Morgan’s commitment to creating songs that allow everyone to be seen, especially giving a voice to the outliers and members of marginalized communities."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Jamie Ravine"},{"t":"p","html":"Jamie Ravine is an award-winning singer-songwriter, performer, and music community leader who loves sharing her passion for music in Columbus, Ohio. Through emotionally rich and memorable melodies, Ravine’s musicality allows her to bring her originals into the recording studio and into acoustic performances. The artist is currently collaborating with producer Brian Skeel and numerous talented local musicians on a solo progressive concept album. Drawing inspiration from artists like Florence and the Machine, the new project will carry a ‘60s, Beatles-influenced psychedelic rock energy, which Ravine hopes to release in 2027. In addition to writing, Ravine supports the Columbus music community by hosting a monthly gathering for musicians, called Green Room, a space for like-minded musicians to network and strengthen relationships in the local scene. The community now has 400 members, growing from eight when it was first established in 2022. This project quickly became a support hub for artists in Central Ohio."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Matthew Morgan and Jamie Ravine"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/mattmorganmus/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Matthew Morgan</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/jamie.ravinemusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Jamie Ravine</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Kelly Wong","role":"","email":"kelly@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"440135","title":"Q*Bensis/Andrew Rathbone/The Guanz Unleash Funk Single “Devious”","date":"2026-01-09","lead":"A groove-heavy Pop/R&B debut that turns funk, flirtation, and manipulation into an irresistible late night anthem.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/440135/9ff32b1fad124f6daaeb4f80a1b58c18.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A groove-heavy Pop/R&amp;B debut that turns funk, flirtation, and manipulation into an irresistible late night anthem."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>RIVERSIDE, CALIFORNIA (January 9, 2026)</strong> – A slow burn jam that evolved into a full blown groove monster, “<strong>Devious</strong>” marks the debut collaboration between <strong>Q*Bensis, The Guanz, and Andrew Rathbone</strong>. This single is a meeting of modern funk, pop, and R&amp;B sensibilities that feels as seductive as it is unsettling."},{"t":"button","href":"https://ffm.to/sodamndevious","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Built on a hypnotic bass line and irresistible pocket, “Devious” pulls listeners straight into the tension of nightlife attraction and modern power dynamics. The track began as a casual jam between QBensis and The Guanz, who laid down bass, drums, and guitar until the instrumental nearly stood on its own. It wasn’t until Andrew Rathbone heard the track months later that the missing piece snapped into place. His instantly memorable hook “she’s so damn devious” gave the song its voice, attitude, and narrative bite."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/801740/large-96c28d8a57362005d995dd2ad1b6e768.png","alt":"Jorge Otero"},{"t":"quote","html":"“It’ll get your head boppin’ and your booty shakin’ like poolside palm trees.”","cite":"The Guanz on “Devious”"},{"t":"p","html":"Lyrically, “Devious” explores temptation, manipulation, and the blurred lines of desire in contemporary dating culture. Inspired by a real-life confession, the song balances flirtation with discomfort, exposing how charm and beauty can become tools of control. As the artists put it plainly; she’s not playing the game - she is the game."},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, the single delivers feel good, groove forward modern funk, blending pop accessibility with R&amp;B swagger. Fans of <strong>Bruno Mars</strong>, <strong>Grammatik</strong>, <strong>Tommy Richman</strong>, and <strong>Parliament</strong> will feel right at home as the bass stays thick, the rhythm stays playful, and the hook refuses to let go."},{"t":"p","html":"“Devious” is the first official release from this collaborative lineup, with a music video to follow shortly after release."},{"t":"h3","html":"Credits"},{"t":"p","html":"Producer / Composer / Performer: Q*Bensis<br>Co-Producer / Composer / Performer: The Guanz<br>Lyricist / Vocalist: Andrew Rathbone<br>Mastering: <strong>Bruce Templeton</strong><br>Artwork: <strong>Jorge Otero</strong><br>Press Photos: <strong>bbunnyx</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/801707/large-23435622357f7e56b0a62d82fd06ac76.jpg","alt":"Q*Bensis:The Guanz:Andrew Rathbone 1.jpg"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Q*Bensis/The Guanz/Andrew Rathbone"},{"t":"p","html":"Q*Bensis, The Guanz, and Andrew Rathbone unite in a groove-driven collaboration shaped by chance encounters and natural musical chemistry. Longtime collaborators and former bandmates in the Minneapolis-based project <strong>Exotic Matter</strong>, Q*Bensis and The Guanz relocated to California, where they continued refining a sound rooted in funk, rhythm, and electronic songwriting. Andrew Rathbone entered the fold after meeting Q*Bensis at an open mic, where his voice and lyrical perspective immediately stood out. Q soon began producing several of Andrew’s songs, with The Guanz contributing both in the studio and on stage. What began as a big move west and a chance encounter evolved into a bass-driven collaboration, with the door open for future releases."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Q*Bensis/The Guanz/Andrew Rathbone:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/qbensismusicca/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Q*Bensis</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/theguanz/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Guanz</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/rathbonemusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Andrew Rathbone</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"436240","title":"Mt. Gribley’s 'Moss on the Stone' Finds Beauty in the Breakdown","date":"2025-12-12","lead":"Singer-songwriter Mt. Gribley returns this winter with Moss on the Stone, a deeply personal, 10-track meditation on distance, memory, and messy middle-ground emotions.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/436240/b956277ac46be035dde00116bdf0c856.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Singer-songwriter Mt. Gribley returns this winter with<em>&nbsp;Moss on the Stone</em>, a deeply personal, 10-track meditation on distance, memory, and messy middle-ground emotions."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>MILFORD, CT (December 12, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>- &nbsp;Indie-folk troubadour <strong>Mt. Gribley</strong> (the musical moniker of <strong>Matt Jarrett</strong>) is set to release his deeply intimate new album <strong><em>Moss on the Stone</em></strong> on Friday, December 12th, 2025. A stirring folk chronicle of love, loss, and letting go, the 10-song collection offers a raw, emotionally layered journey through themes of familial sacrifice, anxiety, and quiet resilience - what Jarrett calls “a break-up album, minus the break-up.” Written during a time of personal upheaval and recorded over just five days, the album feels both immediate and weathered - like it’s been sitting in the woods waiting to be found.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://on.soundcloud.com/OhbF7W0WfyGXwjTXdn","label":"Preview Album Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"While <em>Moss on the Ston</em>e touches on themes of heartbreak and emotional distance, its roots are more nuanced. When his wife moved to the UK to pursue a PhD, Jarrett remained in Connecticut -suddenly navigating long-distance partnership, full-time work, and the unexpected role of solo caregiving for his teenage stepchild. “In a way, I became a single parent overnight - working, paying bills, holding down the fort, and dealing with the emptiness that comes from not having your person around. That’s where this record comes from.” What emerged is a full-length album shaped by three years of quiet transformation marked by separation, responsibility, and the quiet, often unnoticed resilience it takes to keep moving forward. <em>Moss on the Stone</em> is a weathered collection of songs carved from sleepless nights, distant love, and the stubborn ache of continuing on when your heart would rather not."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/798402/large-46ffb758b26ab01605c4f925c9540f47.jpg","alt":"Album art for 'Moss On the Stone', artwork by Jakub Woziwodzki"},{"t":"p","html":"Anchored by Mt. Gribley's signature garage-folk aesthetic - unpolished, evocative, and lyrically rich - the album arrives as the follow-up to this year’s stirring single <a href=\"https://ffm.to/orxjr5y\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">“Mourning Light”</a>, which introduced listeners to his gift for stark confessionals and minimalist storytelling. His latest work expands that sonic palette, echoing the moody textures of <strong>Frightened Rabbit</strong> and the folk sensibility of <strong>Gordon Lightfoot</strong>, all with the honesty of someone recording straight from the gut. While his understated acoustic textures and introspective, sharp-edged lyricism has been described as “soft-shoed folk” or “uptempo sad songs,” Jarrett insists there’s light at the end of each track... even if the mood starts dark, the songs always land in a place of resolve."},{"t":"p","html":"The most recent single <a href=\"https://ffm.to/9omyejx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">“Between the Walls”</a> (out November 28th) sets a tone that diverges slightly from the main theme of the album, an introspective folk-rock reckoning on memory, emotional inertia, and fractured identity. Over sparse acoustics and a poetic sense of decay, the track touches on family division, and to some extent, losing a family member due to today's political divisiveness in the US - a perfect meditation for Black Friday, after the \"joy\" of a Thanksgiving gathering. Other standouts include the title track “Moss on the Stone,” a metaphor-laced ballad on slipping stability, and “Saturn Returns,” a jaded but strangely hopeful anthem for anyone stumbling through personal reinvention. Across the record, Jarrett unpacks themes of long-distance love, spiritual disillusionment, and the weight of familial expectation - all with a diaristic warmth and raw vocal delivery."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795588/large-ff39d2ea792b323585f6838d21881e32.jpg","alt":"Single art for \"Between the Walls\", artwork by Jakub Woziwodzki"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Moss on the Stone is about stepping aside to support your family....It’s about temporarily rearranging your life, embracing the messy middle ground where mistakes and successes live side-by-side.”","cite":"- Mt. Gribley"},{"t":"p","html":"The album was tracked at Dirt Floor Recording &amp; Production with producer<strong>&nbsp;Eric Michael Lichter&nbsp;</strong>and mixed by <strong>Guido Falivene</strong>. Jarrett later added finishing touches at home, layering in subtle background vocals and percussive textures until each song felt “organically complete.” In its quiet catharsis, <em>Moss on the Stone</em> offers no easy answers - just a heartfelt invitation to sit with the uncertainty and maybe, if you’re lucky, find a way forward. Finding beauty in the breakdown, this album is a poetic, unvarnished exploration of what we give up - and who we become - when we try to hold it all together."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795906/large-9b9fb2dee5a2df4e21c297a51ca8aae0.jpg","alt":"Grib Shot B.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795906/preview-4884f17e5e2932ebb88862085d46ac65.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795905/large-87df65b08a17f1d2d765eae8d898c499.jpg","alt":"Grib Shot C.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795905/preview-e03e6a734de4c2b5e15bab8c2045b54c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795907/large-5e46f2cc68f0e2b8d82e5f9813327f8b.jpg","alt":"Grib Shot D.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795907/preview-cd2924eada64cc97a9c13811438b0930.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795596/large-58d0ea5d4e0d9be4434496d666365b75.jpg","alt":"Grib_brown_nogtr.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795596/preview-13e366051a09edd8a97186db107d1e37.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795592/large-c889c855d22680359cbba7c13e34e4f5.jpg","alt":"Grib_guitar_BW.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/795592/preview-28a46a81d193d19942edf4f11e48d725.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Mt. Gribley:"},{"t":"p","html":"Mt. Gribley is the minimalist folk project of Milford, Connecticut-based singer-songwriter Matt Jarrett. With finger-picked rhythms, stripped-back arrangements, and lyrics that wrestle with self-doubt and quiet resilience, his songs blend the warmth of folk’s roots with a subtle left turn - introspective, off-kilter, and emotionally raw."},{"t":"p","html":"The name Mt. Gribley is a nod to <em><strong>My Side of the Mountain</strong></em>, a favorite childhood book. Jarrett grew up in a divided musical household - his mother raised him on a steady dose of John Denver and Neil Diamond, while his father, a Methodist minister, brought home Wagner operas and hymns. His parents split by the time he was four.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Like many a pastor’s kid, Jarrett started his musical life behind a drum kit in metal bands, then rode the wave of ‘90s grunge. After graduating film school, he moved to New York City, where he spent 18 years editing television shows and chasing dreams of directing movies, all while quietly writing songs on a battered acoustic guitar. His turning point came in the late 2000s, when discovering artists like <strong>The Tallest Man on Earth</strong> and <strong>Iron &amp; Wine</strong> sparked a deeper dive into the 1960s folk canon - <strong>Bob Dylan</strong>, <strong>Neil Young</strong>, <strong>Nick Drake -&nbsp;</strong>and ignited a musical reawakening.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/780480/large-4dbae327841b9dde5f2e357f3e8b3fdd.jpg","alt":"Grib_Live_BW.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"Later, a divorce and the death of his father caused him to reassess everything, including his career in reality TV. “After my dad died, there was a piece of his history that I’d never understand,” Jarrett said, “in that he went to college pursuing music, and at some point changed his major to religion and never looked back. I never got a reason why from him. Now, of course, I never will. But I’ve always felt baffled by that decision.”"},{"t":"p","html":"The encouragement of his wife - now pursuing a PhD overseas - was a crucial push to pursue music more seriously. Her move abroad meant Jarrett took on a new role at home, stepping into full-time parenthood for his teenage stepchild, and finding songwriting material in the silence, responsibility, and longing that followed."},{"t":"p","html":"Mt. Gribley’s debut album, <strong><em>Semblance</em></strong>, arrived in 2019 via indie label <strong>Resonating Wood Recordings</strong>. Originally written, recorded, and mixed entirely by Jarrett, he later had it remixed and re-released as <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0oQZbZyf3Fy3hBWHJ2Rjg6?si=gujaQsNlSOmPTvvAzjVh4g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>reSemblance</em></strong></a><strong><em> -&nbsp;</em></strong>a hard-earned lesson in DIY production. In 2022, he followed up with <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0Krj5mYFmYouwC9hoBA7Ga?si=F8zYEdvnTJuFsENwOGipRw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>The Milksop EP</em></strong></a>, a three-song collection tackling confidence, depression, and learning to get out of your own way. Once again, Jarrett recorded all the parts himself, this time handing off mixing duties to Tony Calabro at Astoria Park Recording. Now he is anticipating his third release - a full length album <strong><em>Moss on The Stone</em></strong> that chronicles the last three years navigating sudden life changes, depression, loneliness, and the art of “keep on keepin' on” even when your heart would rather not."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0vOvSCbwHRSNyv4RsHkyJD?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Mt. Gribley:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.mtgribley.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0vOvSCbwHRSNyv4RsHkyJD\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/mtgribley/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"435604","title":"Kathryn Ryan Delivers a Hauntingly Honest Debut with Genre-Bending Self-Titled LP","date":"2025-12-09","lead":"On her first full-length release, singer-songwriter Kathryn Ryan invites listeners into a soundscape that’s as sweeping as it is intimate - where pedal steel meets cello, and forgiveness walks hand-in-hand with fury.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/435604/d9f894aca32a21ec205717808864885b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"On her first full-length release, singer-songwriter Kathryn Ryan invites listeners into a soundscape that’s as sweeping as it is intimate - where pedal steel meets cello, and forgiveness walks hand-in-hand with fury."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>EAU CLAIRE, WI / BOULDER, COLORADO (November 22, 2025)</strong> - With a voice as unshakable as it is vulnerable, Wisconsin-born, Colorado-based singer-songwriter <strong>Kathryn Ryan</strong> is set to release her self-titled debut LP on <strong>Philville Records&nbsp;</strong>this Saturday, November 22, with an accompanying <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/share/1Pqztftmdr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>album release show</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>at<strong>&nbsp;The Lakely</strong> in<strong>&nbsp;Eau Claire, WI</strong> from 6–10 p.m.. Equal parts vulnerable and bold, Kathryn Ryan’s self-titled debut is both timeless and refreshingly original - an Americana-laced exploration of love, loss, and letting go. Blending folk, country, and classical textures with a voice that disarms and lyrics that cut deep, she delivers a masterclass in emotional honesty, tracing the contours of heartbreak, healing, and the many shades of forgiveness."},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.philvillerecords.com/kathrynryan","label":"Information Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/02JQSDOdwfHbhaAXAsRnjl?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"On her self-titled debut album, Kathryn Ryan crafts a genre-defying journey through heartbreak, vengeance, and grace - delivered with deep empathy and a sly wink, especially when it comes to forgiveness. Rooted in Americana, alt-country, and indie-folk, her sound is enriched by classical flourishes and a subtle pop sensibility that never feels overdone. With a voice that disarms and lyrics that reveal sharp emotional insight, Ryan offers listeners moments of catharsis, clarity, and even wry humor. She doesn’t just sing about heartbreak - she scores it with cello, channels it through pedal steel, and softens it with grace."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/794702/large-6c65c0d7b81d369584507426101dc7fb.jpg","alt":"Cover art for Kathryn Ryan's self-titled debut album"},{"t":"p","html":"With echoes of <strong>Brandi Carlile</strong>, <strong>Emmylou Harris</strong>, and <strong>Fiona Apple</strong>, Kathryn’s sound is grounded in storytelling and soul. Her roots in rural western Wisconsin, combined with her classical training as a cellist, create a rich musical backdrop that’s all her own - both familiar and refreshingly new. The cello, which Ryan performs herself, features prominently throughout the album, providing a haunting undercurrent to many of the songs.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/7PXES9a1f_8","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"The 10-track album was recorded at Sueño Royale Studios in Eau Claire, WI, and produced by Kathryn Ryan and Matthew R. Sayles (Philville Records). Sayles also engineered, mixed, and mastered the project. The record features contributions from an impressive cast of Midwest musicians, including members of The Driftless Revelers, Lee “Big Country” Martin (of Feeding Leroy and collaborator of Trampled By Turtles) on pedal steel, Jerod Kaszynski on piano and upright bass, John Utphal on fiddle, and vocal support from Emily VanOpdorp and Irelyn Ulrich on the standout single, “Jesus Forgives.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/794703/large-053bd625e66dc0090949eeb8ee72e47b.jpg","alt":"Back cover and track list for Kathryn Ryan's debut self-title album"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/794701/large-e2386c7b8b64c984b48c48a5e6f57d3f.jpg","alt":"Album Release Show Info"},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.facebook.com/share/1Pqztftmdr/","label":"Album Release Show Info","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Kathryn Ryan:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.philvillerecords.com/kathrynryan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/kathryn.ryan.creates/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/kathryn.anderson.144734\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> |<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@KathrynRyanCreates\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> YouTube</a>| <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5BAa5BqH5YCNhI7fATs5Fi?si=CIGooBA5SauG4iEmTrJwQA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5BAa5BqH5YCNhI7fATs5Fi?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"436939","title":"Ernesto Lune Emerges from Heartbreak and Haze with Gritty, Lofi EP 'DAWN DEMONSTRATIONS'","date":"2025-11-27","lead":"Channeling shades of Mac DeMarco, King Krule, and Cindy Lee, Ernesto Lune delivers DAWN DEMONSTRATIONS - a gritty lo‑fi indie EP packed with crunchy guitars, tape‑warped textures, and diary‑like reflections pulled straight from late‑night overthinking.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/436939/99fa7c2981a82a40308f69c029873e1e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Channeling shades of Mac DeMarco, King Krule, and Cindy Lee, Ernesto Lune delivers <em>DAWN DEMONSTRATIONS</em> - a gritty lo‑fi indie EP packed with crunchy guitars, tape‑warped textures, and diary‑like reflections pulled straight from late‑night overthinking."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>BARCELONA, SPAIN (November 27, 2025)</strong> – Canadian artist <strong>Ernesto Lune</strong> returns with <strong><em>DAWN DEMONSTRATIONS</em></strong>, a raw, emotionally charged new EP that channels post-breakup melancholy into fuzzy, indie-pop reflections on love, purpose, and uncertainty. Written and recorded entirely in his Barcelona apartment, the project offers four tracks of lo-fi introspection with a wounded heart and wandering mind."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/62w3jHLyfLVA2VLJqdbJbo?si=Y_XRKZ6MTE6DzlkbS3FlqQ","label":"Stream Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/796667/large-682838465a75ab51b829aa6decf90f25.jpg","alt":"Cover art for 'DAWN DEMONSTRATIONS' EP"},{"t":"p","html":"Following his 2021 debut EP <em>some good air (in search of,)</em>, Lune - aka Tristan Plumb - continues to carve out a singular space in the indie landscape, where bedroom pop meets existential poetry. On <em>DAWN DEMONSTRATIONS</em>, he pulls listeners into a moment of personal reckoning, capturing the blur of heartbreak and the longing for clarity. The EP was written in just one month, serving as what Lune calls “a way of debriefing myself” after the end of a short-lived relationship."},{"t":"quote","html":"\"It's just one big question because nothing makes sense sometimes....I was thinking about love and freedom and who is really in control. How does one really find the right circumstances, the right people, the right path, the right time?\"","cite":"Ernesto Lune on the inspiration behind creating 'DAWN DEMONSTRATIONS'"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/796668/large-0f876ba4143a322107d3ebe27151d19e.jpg","alt":"Ernesto Lune, courtesy of artist"},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, <em>DAWN DEMONSTRATIONS</em> sits somewhere between <strong>Mac DeMarco</strong>’s slacker sensibility and <strong>King Krule</strong>’s moodier tendencies, with a dash of <strong>Cindy Lee</strong>’s distorted intimacy. Produced by Ernesto Lune and mastered by <strong>Max Igra [Museum Guard]</strong>, the EP is equal parts crunchy and confessional - lo-fi without losing emotional depth. Unpolished but unmistakably intentional. The songs tumble out like diary entries set to tape hiss and dreamy guitars. Tracks like <strong>“Out of Sight”</strong> and <strong>“Cracked Time”</strong> dive into disillusionment and inner unrest, while <strong>“Not For Now”</strong> and <strong>“Some Way Out”&nbsp;</strong>offer glimpses of acceptance and resolve.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Paired with self-made lyric visualizers for each track, <em>DAWN DEMONSTRATIONS</em> plays like a fully realized emotional document - scrappy, stirring, and steeped in late-night solitude. “It’s like someone who's rough around the edges, but has a good heart,” Lune says with a wry smile. With crunchy guitar loops, tape-warped textures, and diary-like lyrics, the EP is a bedroom pop soundtrack for those quiet, spiraling hours - gritty, unpolished, and deeply human. <em>DAWN DEMONSTRATIONS</em> positions Ernesto Lune as a compelling new voice in lo-fi indie, offering a raw and resonant listen for fans of introspective alt-pop with soul."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/OyYmcPf_rE8","height":""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Ernesto Lune:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/bigcatspajamaz/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2tEEqP2otKZEgOj0BXFXqh?si=uzQMVR3EQwqbbjbCK3dZvQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ernestolune\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2tEEqP2otKZEgOj0BXFXqh?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"429749","title":"Hallie Marie Blends New Orleans Funk with Harsh Reality in New Single “Mary”","date":"2025-11-19","lead":"A gut-punch narrative about domestic violence, denial, and survival","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/429749/ff7e87da5426e4760a9aa82c98649881.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A gut-punch narrative about domestic violence, denial, and survival"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>WASHINGTON</strong> (November 19, 2025) - Singer-songwriter <strong>Hallie Marie</strong> delivers a soul-shaking new single, “<strong>Mary</strong>.” The distinct mix of rock, blues, and funk not only combines genres but also conveys a powerful story about domestic abuse, refusal, and resilience."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/7r2wQvOORM3jf80WvJ2EBF?si=rRErnfN9Ry-xenHGKP6sNA","label":"“Mary”","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"The song conveys the story of a woman trapped in an abusive marriage, “Mary” follows the painful descent of someone who can’t or won’t see the danger she’s in. The song’s refrain - “Give thanks to the rain, otherwise how you gonna know before it’s too late?” - serves as both warning and wake-up call, urging listeners to recognize the signs of abuse before tragedy strikes."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wrote this song about a woman being physically abused by her partner, she is clearly in danger, but she refuses to admit it to herself. She doesn’t consider that he might kill her.”","cite":"- Hallie Marie"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/787842/large-eda447d36d70990814818ab188565bee.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Mary\""},{"t":"p","html":"Set against a backdrop of New Orleans swing, funky percussion, and sultry guitar lines, “Mary” creates a stark, chilling contrast: an upbeat groove paired with a message that is anything but light. With bold storytelling, emotional grit, and a groove you can’t shake, “Mary” is more than a song - it’s a warning, a mirror, and a possible lifeline."},{"t":"p","html":"“Mary” was written and co-produced by Hallie Marie, with longtime collaborator <strong>Andreas Landeck</strong>, and features the talents of <strong>Justin Bradford</strong> (guitar) and <strong>Adam Walsh</strong> (drums), Hallie’s former bandmates from her previous project, <strong>Direville</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"In the song’s unforgettable bridge, Hallie uses addiction metaphors to emphasize the trap of abuse:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lyrics Preview:</strong> One hit, two hits, Mary when you gonna quit? / Five, six, seven and if you get to heaven / Monday, Friday, how long’s it gonna take? / You don’t learn nothing for free."},{"t":"p","html":"“It’s a double meaning,” Hallie explains. “It’s about how she’s hooked, like an addict, unable to break free - and how close she is to dying from this abuse.”"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/-b10e31cd63b2c0317696d54d044a4e07.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-32 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/preview-c33bb4c8c0fb8d62a46ea644fb5ad2e1.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/-1302eb881563358853da571d1fb91c45.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-36 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/preview-e17e8b3fa61065cd5c4017c5cabd0e2d.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/large-3fd73d88583417c22d63d14ef4d100aa.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-14 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/preview-4811aaab4e4c9d4f52c8820f4714b20b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/large-29c12eef5ba54b62cc04f5bc34eee872.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-29 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/preview-24ede99c287103be1e22c17641577c77.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/-da81f45fe86805db981f72d86eff8965.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-46 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/preview-8f88dcb7cb4728eef25338442eb31f22.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/large-3740cb07a0046ee2a3bf82c6c328555f.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-44 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/preview-a44d9f029894f554f894eed711194762.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/large-69157f55a4afc3f0f8b64d0c7951e6c8.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-1 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/preview-88af250d089625bac98f9cf6e7350728.jpeg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hallie Marie:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a> is a multifaceted artist who beautifully balances light and shadow in her work. With an intellectually curious spirit, she dives deep into the complexities of human emotions, crafting music that resonates with listeners on many levels - from the highs of love and joy to the depths of melancholy. Drawing inspiration from artists like <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>, <strong>Billy Joel</strong>, and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, Hallie’s sound blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling."},{"t":"p","html":"Collaborating with the Denver-based band <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1UP2Zk7NI1U6KBhpPfPKBt?si=y0EiRbwmTCSlwg_-3sd3vg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Direville</a>, Hallie Marie has already begun to make her mark on the music industry with popular releases “<strong>Sympathy</strong>” and “<strong>Free Spirit</strong>”, among others. Now branching out on her own, her solo music endeavors combine poetic mystical imagery with direct and casual insight derived from raw life experience.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Embracing the beauty of authenticity and connecting with each of us at our core, Hallie invites her audience into her world, sharing not just her music but also her creative process - writing, arranging, and recording - along with the benefit of what she has learned through struggle and resilience. She aims to connect deeply with her listeners, sharing meaningful ideas that resonate long after the music ends."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hallie Marie!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/halliemariemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@halliemariemusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a> |&nbsp;<a href=\"http://instagram.com/halliemariemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qv9RFavvRmeHdVLljnpMBQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | &nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100068917929503\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"432656","title":"'The Voice' Alum Durell Anthony Returns with 'Lovenotes', A Soulful Testament to Lasting Love","date":"2025-11-14","lead":"Soul-Pop singer-songwriter Durell Anthony delivers a heartfelt celebration of love in all its forms and lifelong connection through ten soul-stirring tracks.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/432656/d8b86a46402c6c278368f8ee4ecf64fb.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Soul-Pop singer-songwriter Durell Anthony delivers a heartfelt celebration of love in all its forms and lifelong connection through ten soul-stirring tracks."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>SAN DIEGO, CA</strong> (November 14, 2025) - Soul-pop artist <strong>Durell Anthony</strong> returns this fall with <em><strong>Lovenotes</strong></em>, a deeply personal and universally resonant album that explores love in all its forms - romantic, familial, and human. Set for release on <strong>November 14,</strong> the ten-track project showcases Anthony’s smooth vocals, timeless melodies, and emotional storytelling, affirming his place as one of today’s most sincere voices in modern soul."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3TfsueXZP9oj6QTyBfwxVl?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Anchored by the 2024 San Diego Music Award–nominated single (Best Pop Song) <strong>“One More Night,”</strong> <em>Lovenotes</em> blends the warmth of classic R&amp;B with contemporary pop polish. Think John Legend meets Leon Bridges, with a touch of Brian McKnight - &nbsp;Anthony’s sound is rich with expressive piano, layered harmonies, and a falsetto that glides between joy and heartbreak. <em>Lovenotes</em> feels like a quiet conversation and a grand gesture all at once, creating a sound that feels both classic and contemporary that is perfect for listeners who crave sincerity and substance in modern pop-soul music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/793122/large-f793500a1ea646d50d0f59e4dc10af8a.jpg","alt":"Cover art for 'LoveNotes'"},{"t":"quote","html":"“'Lovenotes' isn’t an album about finding love - it’s about honoring it through commitment, faith, and intention...These songs come from my life and from the people who make it worth living.”","cite":"Durell Anthony on the inspiration behind 'Lovenotes'"},{"t":"p","html":"Perfect for listeners who love the richness of soul music and the timeless catchiness of pop, this album was produced by longtime collaborators <strong>Jordan Childs</strong> and <strong>Keegan Ferrell&nbsp;</strong>and speaks to the beauty and intentionality of commitment and lasting love in today's culture. Weaving through themes of devotion (“Be With U,” “Satisfied”), vulnerability (“Labyrinth,” “Dive”), unity (“Meet Me in the Middle”), and legacy (“Speechless,” “While You're Here”) with honesty and grace, <em>Lovenotes</em> is both a personal love letter and a universal reminder to cherish those closest to us - exploring what it means to love with purpose and presence while we still can."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/fK64y8C-f8k","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"First gaining national recognition on Season 20 of <strong>NBC’s&nbsp;</strong><em><strong>The Voice</strong></em>, where he joined John Legend's team with a powerful rendition of Marvin Gaye’s “What’s Going On,” - Durell Anthony has since built a reputation as a soulful and grounded storyteller. His vocals have appeared in projects for Disney, NBC, Fox, and Peacock, and he has performed for clients including Coca-Cola, BMW, and the California Secretary of State.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Whether you're driving with the windows down or reflecting on the people you cherish the most, Lovenotes invites listeners to pause, feel and love with intention. “My hope for <em>Lovenotes</em> is that it reminds people that real love is possible - the kind you grow with, laugh with, cry with, and hold on to.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/793123/large-c9e2e0d8099db122aa8e773d7d508687.jpg","alt":"Durell Anthony on 'The Voice'"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Durell Anthony:"},{"t":"p","html":"Durell Anthony is an American singer-songwriter whose smooth, soulful sound blends timeless influences with modern pop appeal. Inspired by icons such as Stevie Wonder, Marvin Gaye, Lionel Richie, Leon Bridges, &amp; John Legend, Durell has cultivated a distinctive style marked by his signature falsetto and heartfelt lyricism."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5YJVE9eXlpxpn3hNBTmqBo?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Originally from Atchison, Kansas, Durell gained national attention on <strong>Season 20 of NBC’s <em>The Voice</em></strong>, where his moving rendition of Marvin Gaye’s “What’s Going On” earned him a spot on John Legend’s team. The performance has since resonated widely, amassing nearly two million views across Instagram and TikTok. Throughout his career, Durell has collaborated with celebrated artists including Yolanda Adams and Carrie Underwood, contributed vocals to television projects for Disney, Fox, NBC, and Peacock, and performed for clients such as Bank of America, BMW, Chick-fil-A, Coca-Cola, the Marcus Allen Foundation, and California Secretary of State Shirley Weber."},{"t":"p","html":"A gifted songwriter with a growing catalog, Durell earned a 2024 San Diego Music Award nomination for \"Best Pop Song\" with his piano ballad “One More Night.” In 2025, he signed a deal to write and record music for television and film -marking the next chapter in a career defined by soul, authenticity, and purpose."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Durell Anthony:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.durellanthony.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/durellanthonysings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/durellanthonysings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@durellanthonysings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/durellanthonysings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"433491","title":"Lora Kelley Releases \"Where I Am Now\" — A Five-Year Journey Through Healing, Heartache and Homecoming","date":"2025-11-07","lead":"The Spiritual Americana record traces the quiet courage of rebuilding a life from the inside out","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/433491/702ba5028e792bc25d8fd2e42b3853e5.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Spiritual Americana record traces the quiet courage of rebuilding a life from the inside out"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Charlottesville, VA (November 7, 2025)</strong> — Americana artist and trauma-informed story work coach <strong>Lora Kelley</strong> releases her new full-length album, \"Where I Am Now,\" a deeply honest exploration of healing, loss and the work of reclaiming one’s life.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6HZ6YTQZSmYZNhxoz3k6wC?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Spanning five years of songwriting, the record blends Kelley’s warm, clear vocals with understated folk arrangements and spiritual undertones, echoing the melodic sensibilities of <strong>Natalie Merchant, Sandra McCracken and Nanci Griffith</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Where I Am Now\" began unknowingly in 2019, when Kelley wrote the song “Dust,” without realizing it would become the foundation of a larger body of work. The album began to take shape in 2023 when she shared a new song with longtime collaborator Jeremy Casella, who recognized the emerging arc. What followed is Kelley’s most expansive, vulnerable project yet: a collection tracing the choice to heal, the grief that choice demands, and the life that slowly unfurls on the other side."},{"t":"p","html":"“This record... is really my ‘book’ about navigating the complexities of what it means to heal and hold onto yourself, to cultivate a new and flourishing life while you do it,” Kelley shared. “I've worked with hundreds of people who decided to heal and then move through the uncertainty and hope of finding life on the other side. This album is for people who are on that path... I see you and I made it through. It was hard. But it was worth it.”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/792579/large-c99f275e03997a8df6ed2f506a3f49fa.jpg","alt":"Album art for \"Where I Am Now.\" Photo by Amy Cherry."},{"t":"p","html":"The album opens with “The Man Behind the Curtain,” a piercing reckoning with illusion, awakening, and self-reclamation. From there, Kelley moves into “If I Were Walking Down the Street With You,” a tender imagining of connection across estrangement; “Maybe,” a haunting portrait of leaving an unhealthy family system; and “Dust,” the song that first signaled the emotional center of the project."},{"t":"p","html":"Midway through the record, spiritual grounding takes shape in “Wisdom,” a song rooted in Proverbs 3, “Will You Hold My Arms Up,” a plea for presence in exhaustion and doubt, and “Gather Us Together,” a communal prayer for belonging, rest and repair."},{"t":"p","html":"The title track, “Where I Am Now,” marks a turning point—a steady-footed declaration of survival as Kelley names the quiet triumph of simply standing in a new place. The final two songs, “If You Let Me” and “I Remember You,” carry the emotional weight of relational repair with an honest look at the lingering grief of complicated love"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763792/large-040f26b07bc098f11a7be56c6ece467b.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-184.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763792/preview-bab801da600ba3701e09b5694e332bda.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763793/large-c253415328dd45d2f573e8555a00a593.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-48-2 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763793/preview-522091d282fcea1e14ae15584aa1bb21.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763791/large-44c5d725f595bf2ee8055e95fc686744.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-174.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763791/preview-892a437483001f7ba30f224eaaf03cbb.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by Amy Cherry"},{"t":"p","html":"Throughout the album, Kelley writes with the clarity and emotional depth that have come to define her work. She doesn't flatten the nuance of trauma and recovery; instead, she illuminates the heartbreak of losing the life one had before choosing to heal—a subject rarely named in music or spiritual culture. “Why would you feel sad to lose something that was so hurtful and ache-inducing? Only someone who has chosen to leave a relationship like that knows the complexity,” Kelley says. “It's taken some courage and vulnerability to write from my own heartache, and I hope that it helps people who feel alone in that experience to feel seen.”"},{"t":"p","html":"For Kelley, the album is both a personal milestone and a communal offering. “All healing asks you to touch the depths of your own heartache and loss,” she said. “You have what it takes. Just keep going. There are people waiting to welcome you as your body settles into safety, security, love, and wellbeing. I am one of them.”"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Production Credits:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Jeremy Casella (Producer), Matt Stanfield (piano), Josh Hunt (drums), Jacob Lowery (bass), Nate Duggar (guitar) and Mike Payne (guitar), with Evan Redwine (Engineer)"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lora Kelley"},{"t":"p","html":"Rooted in the themes of resilience and gentle honesty, Lora's work is deeply informed by her background in narrative-based trauma care, including her studies with the Allender Center. Her music stands as a testament to the beauty of brokenness, offering not platitudes, but presence — a hand to hold in the dark. Raised amid the liminality of faith and living today on a conserved farm in Virginia with her partner, children, and a lively menagerie of pets, Lora crafts songs that feel lived-in, earthy, and unflinchingly honest. Her new album, \"Where I Am Now,\" continues to explore the emotional terrains where suffering and hope coexist — a body of work poised to resonate with those yearning for deeper connection and sacred honesty."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6WXETjjadXjtTGA0k5IfM4?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lora Kelley:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.lorakelley.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lora_kelley/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/thelorakelley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/lorakelley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Patreon</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"432010","title":"Improvised And Sperimental Music | Reykjavík | Balder gernot Music","date":"2025-11-05","lead":"A rock odyssey inspired by The Grapes of Wrath, that speaks to the human condition with authenticity and power.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/432010/980153cb25e8f31bdf4f91d754f10a9b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A rock odyssey inspired by <em>The Grapes of Wrath</em>, that speaks to the human condition with authenticity and power."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Atripalda, Italy&nbsp;</strong>(November 15, 2025) - Artist <strong>Balder Gernot</strong> releases his new rock album, <strong><em>Great Spirit</em></strong>. The record draws inspiration from the character Jim Casy in John Steinbeck’s <em>The Grapes of Wrath</em>. By using poignant lyrics and impactful music, Gernot seeks to portray his observations of Americans today as a discerning outsider."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/19tXQtS2zgsPMn3vpEExVL?si=iRSlRELvRuuSnNY5kkUnNw","label":"'Great Spirit'","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Featuring vocals from acclaimed singer<a href=\"https://www.jamiewiltshire.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>&nbsp;Jamie Wiltshire</strong></a>, and mixed by <a href=\"http://www.marcoruggiero.it/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Marco Ruggiero</strong></a> - Gernot has assembled an all-star cast to bring his musical and lyrical creations to life. The album’s textures range from driving guitar riffs to introspective melodic passages, creating an atmosphere that mirrors the album’s themes of observation and reflection.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/789338/large-a47d9c97f1f7d1431c1ba082fd80dd92.jpg","alt":"Balder Gernot Album Art"},{"t":"p","html":"Lyrically, <em>Great Spirit</em> is a meditation on a fractured American identity, seen through the lens of a modern-day pilgrim. Channeling the soul of Jim Casy - the defrocked preacher from <em>The Grapes of Wrath</em> - Gernot takes on the role of the observer, the wanderer, and sometimes the prophet. Across the album’s sprawling narrative, he chronicles the erosion of faith, the persistence of suffering, and the quiet dignity of ordinary people navigating an uncertain land. Lines such as <em>\"No one believes in anything / That's why I’ve got to lead them\"</em> suggest a yearning for leadership, for purpose, and for unity in the face of spiritual and societal decay. Meanwhile, refrains like <em>\"We are all dirty beggars / and we are proud to be / at least we let the others sleep free\"</em> evoke the grit and grace of those who endure, even when unseen.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/789681/large-9580293f3af5537f1dab0d35a81f036c.png","alt":"“This Is The Road 66” Art"},{"t":"p","html":"Writing from the perspective of someone both within and outside the American experience, capturing a country in motion and in conflict, Gernot's America is both haunted and hopeful - a land where \"the hunger of a million souls cross our lands,\" but where resilience, and the possibility of renewal, still remain. Woven throughout the album is a sense of urgency - a whisper that something is shifting beneath the surface of everyday life.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.baldergernot.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Balder Gernot</strong></a> began playing music at a young age like many others, starting with an old acoustic guitar. His desire to express his inner feelings led him to create his own songs. Spending countless hours, days, and months listening to rock legends like <strong>Black</strong> <strong>Sabbath</strong>, <strong>Led</strong> <strong>Zeppelin</strong>, and <strong>Deep</strong> <strong>Purple</strong>, he also kept an eye on new musical developments."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0ONllzF9IKbHiF9SW1gkvg?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"After a hiatus of 25 years to focus on work, Gernot's long-dormant passion for music reignited. Establishing a modest home studio, he now dedicates time to composing music and writing lyrics. Additionally, Gernot has cultivated a network of fellow artists with whom he collaborates to produce and finalize albums."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Balder Gernot!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/JpG9axBy6Is?si=wYj2zosZ4NI4jz04","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.baldergernot.com/","img":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/e453da_16196fdc03b440aa9153288ea2858bc8%7Emv2.jpg/v1/fit/w_2500,h_1330,al_c/e453da_16196fdc03b440aa9153288ea2858bc8%7Emv2.jpg","title":"Improvised And Sperimental Music | Reykjavík | Balder gernot Music","desc":"balder gernot music instrumental sperimental soul viking story quorthon concept album rock electronic Edgar Allan Poe tales Album"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/balder.gernot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@baldergernot8957\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.baldergernot.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0ONllzF9IKbHiF9SW1gkvg?si=EbzH0rt6Rv-mK5vd3itzUQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"432436","title":"INDVGO Invites Fans Into an Intimate Confessional With Single “Remember”","date":"2025-11-04","lead":"An Unreleased Demo Inspired by Vintage Soul Classics, exclusively for fans.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/432436/910739d9df19c9846ebe5f05250ac9f8.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An Unreleased Demo Inspired by Vintage Soul Classics, exclusively for fans."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Brooklyn, NY (November 4, 2025)</strong> – Brooklyn-born singer, songwriter, and storyteller <strong>INDVGO</strong> returns with \"<strong>Remember</strong>\", an atmospheric, soul-soaked reflection on memory, betrayal, and renewal. The record blends the warmth of nostalgic soul with the intimacy of modern R&amp;B, creating something both vintage and new."},{"t":"button","href":"https://indvgo.bandcamp.com/track/remember","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Out November 4, 2025, the track will be released exclusively on <strong>Bandcamp&nbsp;</strong>as a \"secret drop for fans\" marking a rare and intimate offering. This release rewards day-one fans with a glimpse into INDVGO’s most vulnerable work, a confessional piece that feels personal, rare, and intentionally off the grid.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Rather than chasing algorithms, INDVGO is offering listeners an art moment, something intimate, cinematic, and rooted in raw emotion. The goal is to deepen connection, strengthen community, and remind listeners that some songs are meant to be experienced."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/790400/large-b3a638e0fbcb00c68e813f695332e574.png","alt":"Photo Credits: INDVGO"},{"t":"p","html":"“Remember” begins with nostalgia, a reflection on tenderness and what could have been. The kind of love that once felt pure, and gradually unfolds into confrontation and release. The lyrics weave between tenderness and tension, exploring how memory can both comfort and haunt us. The song captures the messy duality of heartbreak: the ache of what was lost and the empowerment that follows. “Remember” lives in that in-between space where pain becomes art, and reflection becomes liberation. It’s intimate, cinematic, and deeply human. The song is a modern ode to vulnerability turned power."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wrote it thinking about someone I once loved, realizing I didn’t need their sorry to move on.”","cite":"- INDVGO"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/790399/large-8a1395592e3efbd9f5ffa4d6b1722362.png","alt":"Photo Credits: INDVGO"},{"t":"p","html":"Think late-night smoky jazz club meets Brooklyn heartbreak, where soul, hip-hop, and noir melt into one moody R&amp;B confession. The kind of track that feels like a midnight journal entry read over candlelight. The production leans minimalist and atmospheric, letting her voice take center stage. Think <strong>Erykah Badu’s</strong> soulfulness, <strong>SZA’s</strong> emotional honesty, and the spoken-word intimacy of early <strong>Jill Scott</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"With themes of mental health, emotional healing, and self-worth, “Remember” stands as both a confessional and a reclamation. A song that reminds us that closure doesn’t always come from someone else; sometimes, it comes from within."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/790401/large-7cab9fe3acc1178e1e9b9ca10a24ae43.png","alt":"Photo Credits: INDVGO"},{"t":"h3","html":"About INDVGO:"},{"t":"p","html":"Born and raised in Brooklyn, she carries the city’s pulse in every note, a blend of elegance and edge, of silk and grit. Before she ever sang, she wrote. First stories, then poems, until her words began to ache for melody. What began as a quiet outlet became her confessional, a place where heartbreak and healing could coexist. Today, INDVGO stands as one of the most magnetic new voices in alternative R&amp;B. Her sound is a fusion of modern noir soul and late-night intimacy. Her vocals are velvet-soft yet heavy with feeling, wrapping around atmospheric beats, brushed drums, and mellow keys that echo the glow of midnight streets.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Her lyrics read like diary entries: unguarded, vulnerable, and unafraid to explore the messiness of love, desire, and transformation. Every performance feels like stepping into a secret - dimly lit, intoxicating, and alive. She doesn’t perform for the crowd; she pulls them into her world. A world where melancholy becomes art, and softness becomes power. INDVGO isn’t just an artist; she’s an experience, a dark-feminine muse for those who feel too deeply and love too hard. Soul wrapped in silk and shadow.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/61Se7XU0y8Gi4T64t1nfMA?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://beacons.ai/indvgo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/indvgo/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@indvgomusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"432695","title":"Acclaimed Artist Stephen Thomas Launches “LEVEL UP” - A Sneaker & Streetwear Brand Rooted in Creative Culture","date":"2025-11-04","lead":"From viral hits to high-heat kicks, music industry innovator Stephen Thomas launches LEVEL UP, a streetwear brand focused on empowering youth and elevating everyday style.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/432695/d324a73e2b9d0d04b340a86f6bbe0fd9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"From viral hits to high-heat kicks, music industry innovator Stephen Thomas launches LEVEL UP, a streetwear brand focused on empowering youth and elevating everyday style."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Charleston, WV</strong> (November 3, 2025) - Known for breaking boundaries in music, <a href=\"https://www.stephentmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a> is now doing the same in fashion with the official launch of his new brand <a href=\"https://thelevelupspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>LEVEL UP</strong></a> - a sleek new sneaker and streetwear brand built for tastemakers, trendsetters, and culture shifters. Offering curated footwear and apparel designed to empower the next generation through fashion that speaks to confidence, creativity, and individuality, LEVEL UP's mission is to elevate your style and step up your game. Merging edgy streetwear design with trusted brand partnerships - including top names like <strong>Nike</strong>, <strong>Adidas</strong>, <strong>Puma</strong>, and more - LEVEL UP delivers the gear to match your ambition."},{"t":"p","html":"Positioned as a bold new voice in sneaker and streetwear culture, “LEVEL UP isn’t just a store - it’s a mindset,” says the brand’s founder (Stephen Thomas). “We’re here to help people express who they are and where they’re going, from the ground up.” At its core, LEVEL UP is about more than just sneakers - it's about culture, confidence, and self-expression. Each product is selected for both style and purpose, offering customers a high-quality, fashion-forward experience that fuses urban edge with everyday wearability."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/791097/large-2f6fa81a81c22bcd4c97a9aac002c161.png","alt":"level up pr.png"},{"t":"p","html":"LEVEL UP is committed to empowerment through fashion, blending bold aesthetics with quality craftsmanship to deliver an unparalleled urban experience. The brand’s curated collections include Men’s, Women’s, and Kids’ Sneakers from top global brands, limited-edition streetwear that fuses modern design with cultural relevance, and apparel drops built for those who lead, create, and inspire. &nbsp;From school halls to creative studios to city streets, LEVEL UP is for those who are always evolving - and want their style to evolve with them.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Launched by creative entrepreneur and recording artist Stephen Thomas, LEVEL UP reflects the same values of authenticity, elevation, and bold self-expression that have defined his career. Known for his boundary‑pushing music, Stephen now translates that same spirit of evolution into fashion. Stephen first made waves by redefining genre boundaries and pioneering the \"universal genre\" - a blend of rock, alternative, hip‑hop and soul that earned him recognition from outlets such as  <em>The Source</em> and features on <em>MTV</em>, <em>Vibe</em> and more. With LEVEL UP, Stephen leverages the same authenticity and momentum he brings to music - and channels it into lifestyle culture. “In music I learned how to evolve, how to reach people, how to build community. Now I’m using that in fashion - because the way you dress is part of how you show up in life,” Stephen adds. The idea for LEVEL UP came to Stephen after talking with friend and now business partner - the owner of Cultures Shoes &amp; Apparel,&nbsp;<strong>Shawn Clark&nbsp;</strong>who is also an artist and creative. Cultures Shoes &amp; Apparel has been making waves in the sneaker scene located in Logan, WV for almost 5 years, and now - as the sister company to LEVEL UP - is working to continue building that culture and community around creative expression through style."},{"t":"p","html":"While the artist's name carries weight, the brand stands on its own as a new hub for fashion-forward individuals who want to own their look and level up their lives. With LEVEL UP he’s not just releasing a collection - he’s creating a look, a statement and a movement. As a brand built for people who move creatively and value identity, “LEVEL UP is about elevation - whether that’s in your music, your mindset, or your style,” says Stephen Thomas. “I wanted something that speaks to the journey of growing, reinventing and owning your lane - and fashion is how we show the world who we are. LEVEL UP is here to make sure you show up strong - wherever you're headed.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Shop the Collection Now"},{"t":"button","href":"https://thelevelupspot.com/","label":"SHOP","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/791499/large-4f791418700326c11cf3fd633e782050.png","alt":"Level Up Grand Opening Flyer_20251031_102856_0000.png"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"430026","title":"“Ten Feet Under” The Single That Began at The Start of Folk Duo, Woven Hollow","date":"2025-10-29","lead":"Woven Hollow, a duo of artistic and passionate collaborators, have unveiled their latest single \"Ten Feet Under,\" a project that originated in the early stages of their relationship.","hero":"","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Woven Hollow, a duo of artistic and passionate collaborators, have unveiled their latest single \"Ten Feet Under,\" a project that originated in the early stages of their relationship."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>GLENWOOD SPRINGS, CO</strong> (October 29, 2025) - The folk duo <strong>Woven Hollow</strong> from Colorado is back with their latest single “<strong>Ten Feet Under</strong>,” which is both moving and captivating. This song reflects on the passage of time, mortality, and being stuck in an emotional state of uncertainty. With its rich acoustic sounds, deep lyrics, and atmospheric production, it creates a cinematic experience for the listeners."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/album=3258123319/size=large/bgcol=ffffff/linkcol=0687f5/tracklist=false/artwork=small/transparent=true/","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Founded on <strong>Anna Murphy</strong>'s initial songwriting and later perfected with <strong>Van Wampler</strong>'s musical vision, “Ten Feet Under” originated during the early stages of their romantic and artistic collaboration. The song explores those moments where you're reflecting on life, but trapped in limbo between wondering if you're feeling regret or contentedness.... finding that, ultimately, we all have the same end. &nbsp;The result is an intricate exploration of the fleeting nature of existence, marked by regret, reflection, and acceptance."},{"t":"quote","html":"It felt like I was writing two different songs, until I showed Van what I was working on. He got excited and helped me bring it to life. I was thinking it might ultimately end up in the trash can, but he and I worked together to make it into something really special and unique.","cite":"- Anna Murphy on the creation of \"Ten Feet Under\""},{"t":"p","html":"Drawing influence from artists like <strong>Neko Case</strong>, <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, <strong>Aimee Mann</strong>, and the darker corners of <strong>Pink Floyd</strong>, “Ten Feet Under” lands in a space where folk pop meets ambient melancholy. Listeners will be pulled in by haunting fiddle lines from <strong>Camille Backman</strong>, warm trumpet flourishes by <strong>Kelly Thompson</strong>, and the song’s carefully layered arrangements, engineered and produced by Van Wampler at CinemaRaven Studios."},{"t":"p","html":"Mixed by <strong>Jason Richmond</strong> and mastered by <strong>Idania Valencia</strong> at Sterling Sound, “Ten Feet Under” delivers a sonically rich experience that complements its lyrical depth. The song's themes touch on mental health, feminism, and philosophical reflection, inviting listeners to sit with the discomfort, and beauty of life’s impermanence."},{"t":"h3","html":"Production Credits:"},{"t":"list","items":["Woven Hollow - Anna Murphy &amp; Van Wampler","Fiddle played by Camille Backman","Trumpet played by Kelly Thompson","Mixed by Jason Richmond","Mastered by Idania Valencia at Sterling Sound","Engineered by Van Wampler at CinemaRaven Studios&nbsp;"]},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/774460/large-622454f118623c534ac9acd3f7d1a07f.jpg","alt":"Van Wampler and Anna Murphy of Woven Hollow"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Woven Hollow:"},{"t":"p","html":"The sound of music and the beauty of the Rocky Mountains led the winding paths of Anna Murphy and Van Wampler to cross in 2017. A few recording sessions together quickly blossomed into an ongoing collaboration which quickly solidified itself as Woven Hollow. After recording a few songs and playing a short tour in 2019, the duet set out to record its first full-length album during the Covid lock down of 2020. Years of work on the album would see a number of incredible musicians adding their talent to Woven Hollow's compositions, and what started as a simple folk record grew into an adventurous project that can hardly be described by a single genre.&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"CONNECT WITH WOVEN HOLLOW:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.WovenHollow.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/wovenhollowmusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3EC1U6eXrn2Yj3SEQLPvnA?si=UTZVOfzqSL6Dhtl9cUhJxA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@wovenhollow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3EC1U6eXrn2Yj3SEQLPvnA?utm_source=generator","height":"352"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"428764","title":"New Single \"Revolving Doors\" Marks a Transformative Moment for Lia Pappas-Kemps","date":"2025-10-24","lead":"Dubbed “Toronto’s next breakout songwriter,” Lia Pappas-Kemps’ “Revolving Doors” captures the quiet turning point of letting go of old patterns and stepping into new love with raw honesty and delicate instrumentation.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/428764/534cbfedbc59d75033b35d4480724f33.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Dubbed “Toronto’s next breakout songwriter,” Lia Pappas-Kemps’ “Revolving Doors” captures the quiet turning point of letting go of old patterns and stepping into new love with raw honesty and delicate instrumentation."},{"t":"button","href":"https://lnk.to/revolvingdoors","label":"Listen to \"Revolving Door\" on All Major Platforms","color":"#554003"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>TORONTO</strong> (October 24, 2025) – Following the warm reception of her poignant 2025 release <a href=\"https://lpk.lnk.to/reservations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Reservations,”</strong></a> Toronto-based singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://linktr.ee/liapappaskemps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lia Pappas-Kemps</strong></a> returns with <a href=\"https://coalitionmusic.disco.ac/track-new/170756485/play?stream_only=1&amp;user_id=126463&amp;signature=yVT4dAMDF2RoPuBNYcbfx_6pfdE%253AQzh5iaEg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Revolving Doors”</strong></a> - an introspective and emotionally rich new single arriving on streaming platforms<strong>&nbsp;October 24</strong> via <strong>Coalition Music Records</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Rooted in Lia’s signature blend of vulnerable lyricism and cinematic folk-pop, “Revolving Doors” expands on the emotional terrain explored in her earlier work. Driven by hypnotic acoustic guitar and the atmospheric swell of Ray Goudy’s pedal steel, the song captures the quiet, often disorienting process of falling in love - and the subtle shifts that happen when we begin to change for someone new. Reflecting on the ever-turning cycle of people, feelings, and uncertainty, “Revolving Doors” ultimately finds its center in the quiet courage it takes to grow."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/5sJlQil4r3k","height":""},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Revolving Doors’ is a song I wrote about feeling your patterns change while falling in love with someone new. &nbsp;I wrote it by myself with just an acoustic guitar, and then decided to get my friend Ray Goudy to add pedal steel during the recording process, which became such a pivotal part of the song.","cite":"- Lia Pappas-Kemps"},{"t":"p","html":"Fans of boygenius, Fleetwood Mac, and Phoebe Bridgers will feel at home in Lia’s sonic world - one that effortlessly weaves timeless folk textures with contemporary alt sensibilities. The second offering from a forthcoming album due in late spring 2026, “Revolving Doors” is produced by longtime collaborator Elia Pappas at Taurus Studios (Toronto), mixed by Howie Beck and mastered by Kristian Montano, with performances from Lia (vocals/guitar), Ray Goudy (pedal steel), and Elia Pappas (guitar/bass)."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/784496/large-c239fc5078f68ab95e4bf5413d549da0.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Revolving Doors\""},{"t":"p","html":"The single continues Pappas-Kemps’ trajectory as one of Toronto’s most promising young songwriters with a growing reputation for atmospheric soundscapes and inventive guitar tunings. Her debut EP, <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/291dl72MoYUpT6uH9OCtB3?si=B_17SaejTLuOqmrL2Becbw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Gleam</strong></a><strong>,\"</strong> received praise from outlets including <a href=\"https://atwoodmagazine.com/lpkg-lia-pappas-kemps-gleam-ep-interview-music-feature/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Atwood Magazine</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://exclaim.ca/music/article/7-influences-that-help-give-lia-pappas-kemps-s-debut-ep-gleam-its-shine\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Exclaim</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://northerntransmissions.com/lia-pappas-kemps-debuts-catch-release/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Northern Transmissions</strong></a> and <a href=\"https://www.thestar.com/entertainment/music/shes-torontos-next-breakout-songwriter-lia-pappas-kemps-shining-debut-proves-why/article_71c1fab0-a049-11ef-a53e-ef213190bb63.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Toronto Star</strong></a>, which called her “Toronto’s next breakout songwriter.” Atwood described it as “a bold and brash introduction that aches with the weight of life lessons learned the hard way,” while <a href=\"https://completemusicupdate.com/approved-lia-pappas-kemps/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Complete Music Update</strong></a> noted she “blends alt-pop and alt-rock [on single 'Switchblade'], crafting a sound that could perfectly soundtrack a coming-of-age film.”"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/xHMktArdHgc","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Early singles such as \"Sad in Toronto\" and \"Object at Best\" showcased Lia's versatility, while her 2021 track <strong>\"Jinx\"</strong> has since surpassed <strong>4.4 million streams on Spotify</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/lOsml98szMY","height":""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lia Pappas-Kemps:"},{"t":"p","html":"For Lia Pappas-Kemps, expressing herself through art has always been second-nature. This is evident in the confident, natural presence the Toronto-born singer brings every time she steps on stage, stemming all the way back to the beginning of her career in music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"In 2021 and 2022, she launched her music career through a series of singles, including the grunge-inflected “Jinx” and the gorgeous, swooning ballads “Sad in Toronto” and “Object at Best\". In her emotionally unsparing, sensuous and critically acclaimed debut EP, \"Gleam,\" her intricate sound comes across, demonstrating influences from throwback alt-rock to ’70s troubadours to modern indie rock, but never truly resembling anyone but herself.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7N15xabCPo5XjsUSTnGVes?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"As <a href=\"https://www.cbc.ca/arts/q/lia-pappas-kemps-perfectly-captures-teen-angst-on-her-debut-ep-1.7452349\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tom Power</a> said of the project, \"Lia Pappas-Kemps perfectly captures teen angst on her debut EP\". Back again with her latest release, \"Reservations,\" Pappas-Kemps continues to trace her progress while finding her songwriting voice. But nothing about her music is underdeveloped. Instead, every new track plots a crystalline moment in an engaging coming-of-age story—one that will feel compelling for anyone whose desire has felt as heavy as the weight of the world."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lia Pappas-Kemps:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/liapappaskemps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@lia.pappas.kemps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/liapappaskemps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://x.com/lia_pappaskemps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a> | <a href=\"https://www.liapappaskemps.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/ca/artist/lia-pappas-kemps/1539183503\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7N15xabCPo5XjsUSTnGVes?si=oNPHA7Z6S-uNiKQKhvSazw&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=65c93ff6d32c45fb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"429498","title":"Waterplanet’s 'Spell It Out' EP Delivers Lush, Layered Indie Rock with a Purpose","date":"2025-10-24","lead":"The Baltimore duo’s new EP is a melodic call for clarity, connection, and quiet defiance in uncertain times.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/429498/58f27d5c4ede61821669be2e259d18fb.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Baltimore duo’s new EP is a melodic call for clarity, connection, and quiet defiance in uncertain times."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>BALTIMORE, MD</strong> (October 24, 2025) – Indie art rock duo <strong>Waterplanet</strong> returns with <em><strong>Spell It Out</strong></em>, their most expansive and cinematic recording to date. Releasing today, October 24, 2025, the 4-song EP blends psych-folk textures, pop sensibilities, and lyrical introspection into a sonic journey that is as stirring as it is hopeful."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/album=780784899/size=large/bgcol=ffffff/linkcol=0687f5/tracklist=false/artwork=small/transparent=true/","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Named after a lyric from the track <strong>“Get Out of Bed,”</strong> <em>Spell It Out</em> is a rallying cry for clarity, presence, and perseverance. “There is an optimism in the writing and production of these songs that attempts to counter the negativity of this period to carve a path forward.... not to lie down and feel steamrolled by the world,\" says the band.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Lyrically, <em>Spell It Out</em> navigates themes of awkwardness, overthinking, self-empowerment, and quiet resilience. Whether through cosmic metaphors or confessional lines, Waterplanet explores the unseen forces - natural, emotional, and spiritual - that connect us all. “All the songs have to do with things out of view… the elemental forces that drive life and connect us to each other, even when we aren’t necessarily conscious of those connections.” Although at times the lyrics might seem despondent, the tracks still feel weirdly positive and empowering due to the sense of melodic warmth and fullness that builds progressively throughout the EP."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/785306/large-f21af400f89a7ef4b0dc7b804452e266.jpg","alt":"Cover art for 'Spell It Out'"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Ryan Gallagher</strong> at <strong>Plaid Dog Recording</strong> in Waltham, MA, the EP marks a leap forward in both sound and scale for Waterplanet. Known for their melodic and experimental DIY approach, on <em>Spell it Out</em>, the band fully embraces lush arrangements and layered production.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The result is a richly textured collection that evokes sonic comparisons, from <strong>The Breeders’</strong> indie alt-rock to \"<strong>California Dreamin</strong>’\" era folk-pop. &nbsp;According to Waterplanet, “This time, we didn’t worry about making recordings we could easily reproduce live. &nbsp;We took a more layered approach - lots of vocals, classic drum kit, guitars, synths, even wind-up toys.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Channeling their adventurous sound palette into something more melodic and poppy, the tracks of <em>Spell It Out</em> are definitely about big finishes. On the bold garage-rock opener “<strong>Supersonic,</strong>” a horn section of Boston-area players helps propel the track to its exuberant conclusion. From the punk-tinged urgency of “<strong>Get Out of Bed</strong>” to the shimmering psychedelia of “<strong>Under, Over</strong>” and “<strong>Force of Nature,</strong>” each track steadily gains momentum before blooming into cathartic, full-bodied finales. “The songs swirl and build until they burst forth, as if they can’t contain themselves. It feels like setting off on a road trip first thing in the morning.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Formed by <strong>Millie Landrum</strong> and <strong>James Hesser</strong>, Waterplanet has become known for its genre-blurring blend of pop, rock and psych-folk. Veterans of the Baltimore music scene, the duo has toured the Mid-Atlantic, Midwest and Southeast, sharing stages with a variety of artists while steadily building a reputation for songs that are haunting yet strangely familiar."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771275/large-5b4c8f4750db6b0f350dc3819c138beb.jpg","alt":"Waterplanet_2024-118.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771275/preview-f3faf806805dee8088b2b5fe41016a31.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771276/large-8e0216c4ff36592d3c5ebeca525bce3a.jpg","alt":"Waterplanet_2024-85.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771276/preview-95315e33d85c644f16964464e77dc07b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771277/large-4c22f01b4d1ee6a48fc0084f3b19ca1f.jpg","alt":"Waterplanet_2024-125.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771277/preview-be3d2e189184589f89687391f38b91b7.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Greg Dohler."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Waterplanet:"},{"t":"p","html":"Waterplanet is the project of Baltimore-based songwriters and multi-instrumentalists Millie Landrum and James Hesser. With driving melodies and intertwining harmonies, the pair alternate vocals, acoustic guitar, percussion, and other instruments to create music that blurs the lines between pop, rock and psych-folk. Known for their playful yet introspective style, Waterplanet has toured throughout the Mid-Atlantic, Midwest and Southeast. Their new EP is set for release in October 2025."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/waterplanetband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/waterplanetband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@WATERPLANETband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://waterplanet.bandcamp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bandcamp</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"430344","title":"No More Secrets: Rebekah Gilbert’s Newest EP Exposes the Quiet Wars We Carry","date":"2025-10-22","lead":"Gritty and honest, this collection is about breaking cycles and finding the courage to leave what no longer serves you.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/430344/57946128d8d98b26ca260ad4b9c6fb0c.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Gritty and honest, this collection is about breaking cycles and finding the courage to leave what no longer serves you."},{"t":"p","html":"NASHVILLE, TN (November 6, 2025) – After releasing her single, “<strong>Secret Keeper</strong>” back in April, Nashville-based artist <strong>Rebekah Gilbert</strong> releases her EP, entitled the same - <em>Secret Keeper</em>. This new EP is a haunting, soul-baring collection of seven tracks that dig deep into the undercurrents of generational trauma, addiction, domestic violence, and the search for healing."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/5aOeL61y4bgdbtq8Tjy0XW?si=mAFZgiY2QjS-upyHs20cjQ","label":"“Secret Keeper”","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"The sound of <em>Secret Keeper</em> feels like home - earthy, honest, and just a little haunting. Blending the rootsy warmth of Americana with the raw intimacy of late-night confessions, this EP is both personal and universally resonant."},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by acclaimed songwriter-producer <strong>Nicole Witt</strong> and recorded at <strong>Sun Drop Sound Studio</strong> in Florence, Alabama, <em>Secret Keeper</em> captures emotional truth with lyrical precision. At the heart of the project is Gilbert’s gift for vulnerability, her words steeped in grit and grace. The sound evokes echoes of <strong>Gillian Welch</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;Brandi Carlile</strong>, and <strong>Jason Isbell</strong> - where heartache, heritage, and hope collide."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/9YHCR-uDsnU","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Secret Keeper&nbsp;</em>combines traditional instruments with melancholic tunes and personal songwriting, featuring talented artists like<strong>&nbsp;Jimbo Hart</strong> (on bass), <strong>Sol Philcox-Littlefield</strong> (playing guitars and banjo), <strong>Jon Davis</strong> and <strong>Justin Holder</strong> (drums), and <strong>Grayson Wright</strong> (on keys). From the aching vulnerability of “<strong>Sober</strong>” to the chilling family secrets of “<strong>Somebody Else’s House,</strong>” each track tells a cinematic, lived-in story that navigates the tightrope between silence and truth."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This EP is a reflection of the places I've been, both physically and emotionally, and the lessons I've learned along the way. I wanted to capture what it feels like to face your ghosts and still believe in grace and the possibility of healing.”","cite":"Rebekah Gilbert"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/786591/large-cf13f894a12e8498750bada737c03189.jpg","alt":"Emma Gilbert - Secret Keeper Art"},{"t":"p","html":"This EP is a raw, unflinching journey through family secrets, addiction, and personal reckoning. From the moonshine-soaked betrayal in “<strong>Somebody Else’s House</strong>” to the painful tug-of-war with toxic love in “<strong>Sober,</strong>” each song exposes what hides behind closed doors. “<strong>Secret Keeper</strong>” and “<strong>Ghosts</strong>” confront generational trauma and the burden of silence, while “<strong>Coosa River</strong>” tells a chilling story of escape from abuse. The closer, “<strong>Stay,</strong>” is a quiet but powerful anthem of liberation. Gritty and honest, this collection is about breaking cycles - and finding the courage to leave what no longer serves you."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Production Credits"},{"t":"list","items":["Producer: Nicole Witt","Engineering &amp; Mixing: Austin Motlow","Vocals: Rebekah Gilbert","Background Vocals: Nicole Witt","Guitars / Banjo: Sol Philcox-Littlefield","Bass: Jimbo Hart","Keys: Grayson Wright","Drums: Jon Davis and Justin Holder","Violin: Nicole Witt","Mastered by: Parachute Mastering","Recorded at Sun Drop Sound Studio, Florence, AL"]},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/786592/large-9f7598bd144876b8430bc00a9998ce4c.jpg","alt":"Photo by John Elrod"},{"t":"h3","html":"Writing Credits"},{"t":"list","items":["“Somebody Else's House” - Amanda Williams &amp; Rebekah Gilbert","“Sober” - Rebekah Gilbert","“Secret Keeper” - Keri Wooster &amp; Rebekah Gilbert","“Coosa River” - Michael Parris &amp; Rebekah Gilbert","“Ghosts” - Rebekah Gilbert","“Show Me Some Shame” - Jenny Littleton &amp; Rebekah Gilbert","“Stay” - Luis Rey &amp; Rebekah Gilbert"]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Rebekah Gilbert:"},{"t":"p","html":"With a voice that lingers long after the last note and folk-style storytelling, Americana singer-songwriter Rebekah Gilbert’s music is steeped in raw honesty and emotional depth. Originally from Maylene, Alabama, she is quickly making her musical presence known in her new Nashville home. Her recent songs explore addiction, family struggles, and the weight of generational cycles with unflinching vulnerability. Best described as “hauntingly honest Americana,” her sound blends folk roots with pop country that resonates deeply with listeners."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/786567/large-7b395859b9f6c8b434fffaea14e95824.jpg","alt":"Photo by John Elrod"},{"t":"p","html":"In February 2025, Rebekah released her first cover, a haunting rendition of Gnarls Barkley’s “<strong>Crazy</strong>”. Just a month later, she unveiled “<strong>Somebody Else’s House,</strong>” and now here she is following through with the EP!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.rebekahgilbert.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/RebekahGilbertWritingandMusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/rebekahlgilbert/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@gilbertrebekah\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@rebekahgilbertmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3HNZCei9Vhafw0UVcbBcZV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"426333","title":"LOBE Finds Joy in the Unexpected on Debut Album, “was that on purpose?”","date":"2025-10-21","lead":"Bay Area ensemble merges jazz, alt-folk and playful, nostalgic influences drawn from pop culture and childhood memory","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/426333/d9a4ab2cfca1cbe869abd454496d526f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Bay Area ensemble merges jazz, alt-folk and playful, nostalgic influences drawn from pop culture and childhood memory"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>OAKLAND, Calif.</strong> (October 21, 2025) — Bay Area collective LOBE releases its debut album, <strong>“was that on purpose?”</strong> today, a nine-song collection celebrating the joy and unpredictability of improvisation, the beauty of the mundane and the friendships that have sustained the group since their time together in Stanford's jazz program."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6G5qSPP9f6SHYzT5MChA3l?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Playful but rigorous, the record distills three years of collaboration into one project, merging contemporary jazz with folk-pop delicacy, disco exuberance, video game textures, and the wide-eyed wonder of childhood nostalgia."},{"t":"p","html":"The group is comprised of Daiki Nakajima (flute, bass, tenor/soprano sax), Sam Silverstein (violin), Ethan Buck (alto sax), Nolan Miranda (piano, synths), Mark Rau (bass, guitar), and Michael Hayes (drums)."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773393/large-ddec7987bf5c9dcd6c318de19952f007.png","alt":"Album art for \"was that on purpose?\" by Whitley Wilburn"},{"t":"p","html":"What began as casual sessions quickly evolved into a collaborative practice where members discovered a shared love for rhythm-forward improvisation and experimental sound. Songs written with each member’s voice in mind, like Michael's intricate polyrhythmic phrasing, Daiki’s soaring flute, or Ethan’s agile horn textures, took on new life in practice, evolving into music that challenged the band and deepened its bonds."},{"t":"p","html":"The album's nine chimeric works span a kaleidoscope of moods and influences, opening with “Sucker Punch,” a song that catches the listener off-guard by weaving between polyrhythmic, odd-time grooves and expansive, free-time improvisations, before moving into “Rain Pause (Rain Again),” showcasing Sam Silverstein's violin prowess. Next, \"imperfect misdemeanor\" takes listeners on a distorted, almost confrontational journey evoking a drum and bass-fueled video game fight scene that resolves into an ecstatic victory dance."},{"t":"p","html":"From there, the tone shifts as “Hummingbird Dances,” a 2024 ASCAP Herb Alpert Young Jazz Composer Award winner, sparkles with a joyful folk-to-electric shimmer. The Studio Ghibli-esque ballad “Moon Jelly” delicately floats until “parhelion” pulses with gaming energy, drawing from traditional free jazz in its composition, while “Set Time” showcases the group’s breadth in a more traditional swing context."},{"t":"p","html":"LOBE then reimagines the Beatles’ “Ob-La-Di, Ob-La-Da,” specifically inspired by a children’s bossa-nova version Nakajima enjoyed as a kid—weaving the classic melody through multiple ways of feeling the underlying time in 11. The record closes by looping back to “Sucker Punch (Intro),” a nod to circular form and the improvisational questions at the heart of the album."},{"t":"p","html":"Despite their eclectic ingredients, each piece shares a structural DNA of delicately composed passages that expand with interactive improvisations, balancing precision with spontaneity. Unlike many ensembles driven by a single bandleader, LOBE composes with one another in mind and resists hierarchy, preferring to workshop pieces collectively until they blur the line between rehearsal and hangout."},{"t":"p","html":"The album's title nods to the unique, collaborative discovery of improvisation, where each musical coincidence is an unplanned yet inevitable result from years of deep practice, as animated by coincidence, chemistry, and the kind of surprises that happen only among close friends."},{"t":"p","html":"It asks the question at the heart of improvisation: how much is intentional, and how much is spontaneous? For LOBE, there is beauty in the tension between the crafted studio LP and the inherent surprise of live performance. That spirit runs through the album, delivering a lasting record that highlights the fleeting, unpredictable magic of live performance."},{"t":"caption","html":"The mixing and mastering of the album is supported by <strong>YoungArts</strong>."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Whenever I sit down to play with LOBE, I’m never concerned with the outcome,\" said Nolan Miranda. \"We’re there to communicate, discover, and meld our minds... I’m incredibly lucky to have found such a beautiful group of people to explore and grow with over so many years.\""},{"t":"p","html":"\"'was that on purpose?' Maybe, maybe not, but there was intent behind it,\" said Mark Rau. \"There is a certain trust, respect, and friendship in the group that allows us to try ideas without the fear of failure, pushing our musical boundaries... It has been a huge privilege to work on this project with LOBE, and I can’t wait to have it out in the world.\""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Production credits:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Recording Engineer – Mark Rau"},{"t":"p","html":"Assistant Recording Engineers – Daiki Nakajima, Nolan Miranda, Taylor Goss"},{"t":"p","html":"Mixing – Jack Kelly"},{"t":"p","html":"Mastering – James Clemens-Seely"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About LOBE:"},{"t":"p","html":"Emerging from the San Francisco Bay Area, LOBE is a collective of award-winning composers, arrangers, and musicians that lives at the confluence of intricate writing, dynamic improvisation and imaginative textures. Originally united through a common penchant for rhythm-forward contemporary jazz, LOBE quickly developed an interest in building on this aesthetic with dance, folk, electronic, and pop influences. Over many years of practice, friendship, and chemistry, the group came into its distinctive voice: whimsical and unhurried, challenging but inviting, time-bending yet always attuned to the here and now."},{"t":"p","html":"LOBE is excited to showcase the culmination of the past three years of collaboration in their full-length debut album, \"was that on purpose?.\" Comprised of 8 chimeric original works and arrangements, \"was that on purpose?\" celebrates the beauty that arises from chance encounters, mundane experiences with friends, and musical relationships transcending the professional. With this release, LOBE hopes to spread the communal joy they feel every time they sit down together on stage, in rehearsal, and at the dinner table."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lobestagram/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://lobe.band/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> ​"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773394/large-77a0ff4ebe8bd4913a54582e30789cc4.png","alt":"ContactPage.png"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"423352","title":"Steve Erickson Confronts Modern Isolation and Inner Turmoil on 'Wonderland' EP","date":"2025-10-17","lead":"With electric urgency and lyrical depth, Erickson’s latest project explores the emotional fallout of addiction, disconnection, and loss.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/423352/235ce425a4ff7b07082e1a471c79dca6.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"With electric urgency and lyrical depth, Erickson’s latest project explores the emotional fallout of addiction, disconnection, and loss."},{"t":"p","html":"ASHEVILLE, NC / VERO BEACH, FL (October 15, 2025) – Americana artist <strong>Steve Erickson</strong> returns this fall with <strong><em>Wonderland</em></strong>, a raw and emotionally charged new EP set for release on October 15, 2025. <em>Wonderland</em> represents a sonic and thematic shift from his previous album Crooked Road, trading acoustic warmth for more electric, forceful instrumentation - and tackling darker emotional terrain."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6ymT7RdnbMuq6Y8gxqn6OX?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Built around four deeply personal and socially resonant songs, <em>Wonderland</em> captures the various ways distance can manifest in our lives: the growing void between people, the sense of a world unraveling, the private struggles of addiction, and the bottomless grief of loss. The EP opens with the title track, “Wonderland”- a stark and haunting piece inspired by Erickson’s experience supporting a close friend through substance abuse. From there, the journey deepens with “Fade Away”, a poignant reflection on emotional erosion in a relationship, and “One More Day”, a politically tinged portrait of societal collapse. The final track, “A Blacker Shade of Blue”, is a devastating meditation on grief, delivering one of Erickson’s most vulnerable vocal performances to date.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I started the EP with “Wonderland” - a song recorded during the Crooked Road sessions - but it didn’t fit that album’s feel. So I built the EP around it, trying to capture other examples of the overwhelming anxiety that many are feeling.”","cite":"Steve Erickson on the making of Wonderland EP"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/777697/large-fe48084a9411d37c969823e9166543d1.jpg","alt":"Cover art for the 'Wonderland' EP by Kostas Dimopoulos"},{"t":"p","html":"With echoes of classic protest anthems like “The Eve of Destruction”, <em>Wonderland</em> leans into a darker, stormier sound while retaining the lyrical honesty and melodic backbone that have become Erickson’s signature. The production, helmed by Erickson and longtime collaborator <strong>Jim Robeson</strong>, is sharp and intentional, matching the emotional weight of each track. Overall,&nbsp;<em>Wonderland</em> offers no easy answers. But through its honesty, it might provide something just as powerful: solidarity, catharsis, and the space to feel."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Praises for Steve Erickson"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"Introspective storytelling and acknowledgement of the past and present mark Erickson’s individuality as he brings tradition to the forefront.\" </em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; - </strong><a href=\"https://musicmecca.org/steve-erickson-pays-homage-to-appalachian-tradition-on-latest-album-crooked-road/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mae Farris, Music Mecca</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"He has that dark rich voice which works so well in traditionally based music.\"</em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;- </strong><a href=\"https://americana-uk.com/bluegrass-briefs-kyle-obrien-band-mission-hill-milltown-philosophers-steve-erickson-last-hour-bluegrass-blackwater-railroad-company\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tim Martin, Americana UK</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"An artist as dedicated to the true Americana sound as anyone... and the result is an album which can best be described as refreshingly pure!\"</em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;- </strong><a href=\"https://www.americanamusicappreciation.com/post/fine-contemporary-tribute-to-old-time-music\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Paul Cutler, Americana Music Appreciation</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"'Retrospective' cements his place as a key voice in the contemporary Americana and folk scene.\"</em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;- </strong><a href=\"https://www.mnprmagazine.com/news/steve-erickson-retrospective-compilation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Richard Bowell, MNPR</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"Steve Erickson reminds us that good storytelling never goes out of style.\"</em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<a href=\"https://www.allcountrynews.com/post/steve-erickson-s-retrospective-album-a-journey-through-a-decade-of-songwriting-and-storytelling\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">- All Country News</a>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Steve Erickson:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3cejBgcRgP4gWuMxWVaR7i?si=IqtNzdoVQ_6zzCeClksNmQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Steve Erickson</strong></a> is a seasoned musician whose journey into music began alongside a successful career in public relations across Atlanta, New York City, and Washington DC. &nbsp;Influenced by a wide range of musical styles, Erickson spent years letting melodies and lyrics percolate before finally taking the plunge into songwriting. “I was thinkingabout writing songs long before I actually wrote them down,” he recalls. “I didn’t know if they would be good enough. Well, I got over that - and the songs just started to flow.” His diverse songwriting style blends elements of country, blues, and folk with his songs having been praised as “well crafted,” and his live shows are known for their “high energy” and for “connecting directly with the audience.”"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687091/-0352cd56d98cac022a906cb902288003.webp","alt":"steve 3.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687091/preview-01cdc6516b0594c11977f66689af4149.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687090/large-67b4a206bcc4faf704a8cd565ad689d0.webp","alt":"steve 4.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687090/preview-c78b2c14c7479b963d632687ea7bb32f.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687089/large-af84399dd1c6870bfc9dc8695157e54f.webp","alt":"steve 5.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687089/preview-001122d9e3748d9f5aa1a83219917642.webp"}]},{"t":"p","html":"In Atlanta, Erickson wrote and performed with local bands including <strong>Truth in Advertising</strong>, <strong>DarkHorse</strong>, and <strong>The Remnants</strong>. After relocating to Washington, D.C., he joined forces with fellow singer-songwriter <strong>Nick Peters</strong> to form the acoustic duo <strong>Medium Gauge</strong>. Over an eight-year run,they combined original material with an eclectic mix of covers, building a loyal following in the region."},{"t":"p","html":"Now splitting his time between Asheville, North Carolina, and Vero Beach, Florida, Erickson continues to write, record, and perform with the same passion that sparked his musical journey. In 2012, he released his debut album <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/47yg8AH3fOvBUvcls5BYrH?si=He3bIgdLRiWwTH8FXAdieA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>It’s About Time</em></strong></a>, produced by <strong>John Krause</strong> and recorded at Cue Studios in Falls Church, Virginia. The album showcases Erickson’s storytelling abilities, blending pop sensibilities with country, blues, and folk influences. From the rollicking title track to the Caribbean-tinged “One Port Ahead of the Storm” and the soulful ballad “River”, the album defies strict genre classification."},{"t":"p","html":"His 2016 follow-up, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2SfnXMSMYkwpv5Xbfbp6y3?si=M6a_Z7RdT1ydjTRXnDu9lQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Music Tonight</em></strong>,</a> produced by <strong>Jim Robeson</strong> at Bias Studios in Springfield,Virginia, continued this Americana exploration with a diverse range of sounds and vivid lyricalimagery. The album features country-leaning tracks like “Friends” and “No Expectations”, upbeat numbers such as “Music Tonight” and “Midnight Potomac Ride”, and poignant ballads like “Sing That Old Song” and “Wind Across the Jetty”."},{"t":"p","html":"Erickson’s third release, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0RTW7pEFKjOey3RFePkahl?si=VZRt4AZfQriywSeotGvHrw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Moving On</em></strong></a><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong>(2019), again produced by Jim Robeson, reflects a maturing artistry and lyrical depth. Songs like the pop-driven title track and “Long Day Tonight” explore themes of change and resilience, while “Low Country Girl” and “Sweet and Fine” reveal Erickson’s Southern roots and playful embrace of swing and boogie-woogie. The album closes with a haunting rendition of the traditional “Wayfaring Stranger”."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7cMpYuyxi8LSUH4eIYdlTc?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"In 2024, Erickson released <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7cMpYuyxi8LSUH4eIYdlTc?si=st2hoM6_RRS1SLwMrwIYxA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Crooked Road</em></strong></a>, a project deeply influenced by his exploration of Appalachian music traditions. Reuniting with producer Jim Robeson at The Bar in Gaithersburg, Maryland, this fourth album pays tribute to the region’s musical heritage. The title track honors the 300-mile music heritage trail in Southwest Virginia, while originals like “Lay Me Down Beside My Love” and folk standards such as “Fair and Tender Ladies” and “In the Sweet By and By” weave together a rich Americana tapestry. From the uplifting “Perfect Day” and “Find a Light” to the introspective “Flipside” and “We Don’t Love Us Anymore”, <em>Crooked Road</em> is a compelling journey through sound, story, and place, featuring top-tier musicianship and a wide array of acoustic instrumentation."},{"t":"p","html":"Also released in 2024, the compilation album <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0Dyp97YlFsPxsA7csCM8VV?si=4Y25q_9gTxW2-QNZBVk_yg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Retrospective</em></strong></a> is a look back at a decade of storytelling, inviting listeners on a journey through Erickson’s evolution as a songwriter and recording artist. Featuring 15 original tracks, the album spans parts of his career from 2012 to 2024, offering listeners a deep dive into his distinctive blend of folk, Americana, blues, and country. Each track showcases Erickson’s signature storytelling, weaving together themes of love, loss, resilience, and the passage of time.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With each release, Steve Erickson continues to carve a distinct space in the Americana landscape - one rooted in tradition, yet unafraid to explore new musical terrain."},{"t":"p","html":"For more about Steve Erickson and his music, visit his <a href=\"https://ericksongs.net/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">official website</a>."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Steve Erickson!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3cejBgcRgP4gWuMxWVaR7i?si=0bQkIu7ET_i1vwD0D543qg&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=0da0ed3495db4227\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/steve-erickson/73492990\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://ericksongs.net/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"424549","title":"LifeSize is the project of Los Angeles-based artist Scott, blending heartfelt songwriting with roots-rock energy. His music has earned praised by The Mercury News as “poignant” and “vastly appealing,” drawing comparisons to legends like Tom Petty, Mark Knopfler, and Bruce Springsteen. With a sound that’s both timeless and deeply personal, LifeSize continues to build momentum—new music is set to arrive in 2025.","date":"2025-10-17","lead":"Produced by Grammy-Winner Dave Darling, the Genre-Bending Collection Taps Into Love, Loss, Survival & the Spirit of California","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/424549/bedaa65116810ff7befb18e259234283.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Produced by Grammy-Winner Dave Darling, the Genre-Bending Collection Taps Into Love, Loss, Survival &amp; the Spirit of California"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>LOS ANGELES</strong> (October 17, 2025) — <strong>LifeSize</strong>, the musical project of Los Angeles-based singer-songwriter <strong>Scott Marshall</strong>, will release its most expansive and emotionally resonant work to date with the self-titled double album<strong><em>&nbsp;LifeSize</em></strong>, arriving October 17, 2025 on vinyl and digital platforms. Building on three critically praised albums, each marked by Scott’s genre-blending sound and vivid storytelling, this release offers a \"best of\" statement that distills his most powerful musical moments into one collection."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2UW3sFPM9UQbqSng2PWK7r?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Following the critical acclaim of 2020’s <em><strong>Woolsey -&nbsp;</strong></em>a poignant tribute to California wildfires and personal rebirth - Marshall returns with a 24-track odyssey that traverses the full range of the human experience: from searing heartbreak and political unrest to spiritual awakening, redemption, and enduring love. “<em>LifeSize</em> is a deeply personal collection,” says Marshall. “I’m lucky I was able to get both joy and healing in the creation of this album. Everyone has experienced some form of love, great loss, redemption - and many of the other human experiences I delve into. I truly hope that listeners will find compassion and solace in my music.”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/779751/large-c82646b1563546f31aa4ebcfd76b3926.png","alt":"Tracklist for 'Lifesize' album"},{"t":"p","html":"The album was produced by Grammy Award-winning producer <strong>Dave Darling</strong> (Def Leppard, Janiva Magness, Brian Setzer), with additional production and mixing by Scott Marshall and Ryan Lipman. The project features an all-star lineup of collaborators, including <strong>Janiva Magness</strong> on lead vocals for the soul-stirring track “Always,” as well as acclaimed musicians <strong>Arlan Schierbaum</strong>, <strong>Carl Sealove</strong>, <strong>Elizabeth Wight</strong>, <strong>Jeff Turmes</strong>, and <strong>Roger Carter</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Written largely on Marshall’s 1966 Gibson 330, the only guitar he salvaged from the devastating Woolsey fire, <em>LifeSize</em> is as much about rebuilding as it is about remembering. “Every time I looked at it, touched it and played it, it was visceral,” he shares. “As if the guitar embodied the whole of my experiences and I had to somehow make it speak to get its stories out.” Blending alternative, roots-rock, pop, and cinematic storytelling, <em>LifeSize</em> nods to legends like <strong>Mark Lanegan</strong>, <strong>Nick Cave</strong>, <strong>The National</strong>, and <strong>Daniel Lanois</strong>, while carving out a singular sound that’s unmistakably Marshall’s. His voice - intimate yet widescreen - narrates tales of survival (“Buried Alive”), lust and longing (“Black Car”), spiritual reflection (“Man of Tao”), and fatherhood (“Where Does the Light Go?”) with poetic depth and raw vulnerability."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773190/large-a08b4b245a065b40c7de4ebe4e061d0b.jpg","alt":"LIFESIZE 4-26-26 V10.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773190/preview-8fee78bbcebfdf094e96d56ae605c460.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773188/large-c37a09cc5ab64bac1728dd50694a1763.png","alt":"LIFESIZE 3.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773188/preview-8eccd085ed306211595007f3637e8913.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773189/large-10759f9afe0a1e93d57c72ba3b6e9910.png","alt":"LIFESIZE 2.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773189/preview-987009aa8bd7056ec904ed21c9343cbc.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773191/large-255d0946b5b76f6b5c4622ad2d26d220.png","alt":"LIFESIZE 1.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773191/preview-111d8bc68a6fe73ddea524b7bb327624.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773192/large-8054f545c07a300b5e728534f8864c0d.jpg","alt":"Dreamwalking Poster.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773192/preview-23e5ac484112a889d8eb56c7add98da4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773187/large-b66cf297d40bc6e00f1feeb9b30dbccd.jpg","alt":"LifeSize Logo Cover.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773187/preview-8ee92f25c273ec5529eb19563e044fa3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773186/large-230c0dd7ac8f69844c369291fb828141.jpg","alt":"LIFESIZE LOGO.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773186/preview-f83e992528b9704c04f5ad8beb15232c.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images and artwork by Joe Tamel and George Kander."},{"t":"p","html":"Highlights from the record include the aching single “California Home,” a love letter to the Golden State; the brooding groove of “Cobra &amp; Mongoose”; and the sweeping closer “Constellations,” which distills the album’s cosmic themes of connection and transcendence.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"LifeSize’s previous releases have earned praise from The SoCal Sound’s Mimi Chen, KRSH’s Bill Bowker, and Jim Harrington of MediaNews Group, who wrote: “The music is impressive on so many different levels… a collection of vastly appealing roots-rock tunes that should appeal to fans of Mark Knopfler, Tom Petty, and Bruce Springsteen.” Airplay includes KCSN, KEXP, and The Krush. With this new release, LifeSize is not just revisiting the past but redefining it - offering listeners an album that’s both eternal and timely."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About LifeSize:"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.lifesizemusic.net/","img":"","title":"LifeSize is the project of Los Angeles-based artist Scott, blending heartfelt songwriting with roots-rock energy. His music has earned praised by The Mercury News as “poignant” and “vastly appealing,” drawing comparisons to legends like Tom Petty, Mark Knopfler, and Bruce Springsteen. With a sound that’s both timeless and deeply personal, LifeSize continues to build momentum—new music is set to arrive in 2025.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"Scott Marshall, the artist behind LifeSize, came of age in Seattle during a cultural boom that shaped his creative foundation. Growing up between households after his parents’ divorce, he absorbed a wide spectrum of sounds, from The Beatles and Hendrix to Sonic Youth and Screaming Trees, influences that continue to inform his expansive pop-rock sound."},{"t":"p","html":"After relocating to California following years of travel, Marshall began releasing music under the name LifeSize with Grammy-winning producer Dave Darling. The three critically acclaimed albums he's released so far have earned national airplay on KCSN, KEXP, and The Krush, and won praise from critics for his blend of roots-rock storytelling and genre-crossing ambition. His breakout album, \"<a href=\"https://lifesizemusic.bandcamp.com/album/woolsey\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Woolsey</a>,\" doubled as a tribute to California and a fundraiser for wildfire recovery, with proceeds benefiting Direct Relief."},{"t":"p","html":"With a voice both intimate yet expansive, Marshall continues to craft music that's timeless and resonant.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5fvymPLVzoCqOjewMOKFiD?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.lifesizemusic.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://lifesizemusic.bandcamp.com/album/lifesize\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bandcamp</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5fvymPLVzoCqOjewMOKFiD?si=ywIoPTS3Su-q77ptEm2yMg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/lifesize/385659171\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple&nbsp;</a>| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@lifesizearts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lifesizemusic4u/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/lifesizemusic4U\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"426376","title":"Stephen Thomas Debuts Powerful Country Single “Come Home to Me” - A Heartfelt Homecoming Anthem for Love, Loss, and Longing","date":"2025-10-17","lead":"With a genre-blurring sound and a heartbreakingly honest story at its core, Stephen Thomas’s debut country single “Come Home to Me” introduces a powerful new voice in modern country - where emotional truth meets undeniable commercial potential.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/426376/4f330b76153c54e1ce6d5220d448d4c3.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"With a genre-blurring sound and a heartbreakingly honest story at its core, Stephen Thomas’s debut country single “Come Home to Me” introduces a powerful new voice in modern country - where emotional truth meets undeniable commercial potential."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Nashville, TN</strong> (October 17, 2025) – Five-time Grammy-considered artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=j3WK1-UqRkuc7zz86MdrOw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>unveils his debut country release, <strong>“Come Home to Me,”</strong> a raw, soul-stirring ballad that captures the emotional gravity of separation, memory, and the longing to return to what feels like home. Known for pioneering the \"universal\" genre - &nbsp;a sonic blending across Pop, R&amp;B, Rock, and Hip-Hop, Thomas now steps into the Country/Americana space with unshakable authenticity."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/139yKb5bEDdKwbN95RYZIM?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/7DGp4lZAIIw","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"“Come Home to Me” is a genre-bending track that fuses modern country storytelling with pop-R&amp;B sensibilities - echoing the emotional depth of <strong>Nate Smith</strong>, the sonic warmth of <strong>Jordan Davis</strong>, and the crossover soul of artists like <strong>Kane Brown</strong> and <strong>Jimmie Allen</strong>. Laced with vivid lyrics and cinematic production, the song taps into universal themes of love, distance, and resilience. “This is one of the most personal songs I’ve ever written,” says Thomas. “It was inspired by my cousin Krystle Smallwood, who suffered a brain aneurysm - an experience that reminded me how fragile life is and how quickly it can change. However, I am truly grateful that God took care of her and she's doing well and we are able to share more great moments together. Because there's nothing like having family around. But it made me reflect on the people who feel like ‘home,’ and how we sometimes don’t realize what we had until it’s gone.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The accompanying music video brings these themes to life, highlighting the emotional arc of a relationship torn apart by time and circumstance. Through scenes of past joy and present heartache, Thomas invites listeners to relive their own memories of love lost - and found. Lyrically, “Come Home to Me” paints a vivid picture of love in its prime - long drives, moonlit nights, shared dreams - only to contrast it with the emptiness that follows when that love slips away. As Thomas sings in the hook, “Baby life goes on / You got to go another round / Just get back up when you get knocked down,” the song becomes a universal call for strength and reunion - whether romantic, familial, or spiritual."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/784022/large-d12284207b49da37f8a5a769af672129.jpg","alt":"e90d8b0a-e885-4de8-baf6-2ecc0fb0242e.jpg"},{"t":"quote","html":"\"The song is about remembering what it was like to live life in the fast lane, spending time with someone you love, sharing the laughs, the good news, and the true excitement together - only to realize how fast those moments can disappear. It’s about missing that person who made those memories so meaningful and wishing you had more time with them. \"","cite":"Stephen Thomas on the inspiration behind “Come Home to Me”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/781353/large-3b3d8e367b1ad47afaf9e139f3527293.jpeg","alt":"Single artwork for “Come Home to Me” by Stephen Thomas"},{"t":"p","html":"As a result, “Come Home to Me” opens the door to a range of human and cultural narratives beyond music, offering natural tie-ins to the broader need for “home” in all its forms. “In a world that often feels unsteady, this song is about that one place, or person, that reminds you who you are,” says Thomas. “Sometimes reality turns into a memory, which then becomes a dream,” Thomas shares. “And when those dreams fade, we’re left holding on to the moments that felt like home - hoping somehow, some way, that person finds their way back. We recall what it felt like to have that one person there - to love us for who we were and who we became. Then we wish we could have it again, chasing what was, only to realize it will never return. The only thing we can hold onto is the memory of when we did get our wish.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With this release, Stephen Thomas continues to push the boundaries of genre and storytelling, planting firm roots in country music while carrying the emotional weight and lyrical truth his fans have come to expect."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/781397/compressed_original-1c6d887601eaf5037afd68c2b8b54e96.jpeg","alt":"Image by Babs Photography"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Stephen Thomas:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=oHBViFwQQaaIjt97y8p4Og\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a> is an artist redefining genre boundaries and commanding attention across the music industry. Hailing from Charleston, West Virginia, and recently named an <strong>“Artist to Watch in 2025”</strong> by <strong><em>The Source</em></strong>, Stephen is a pioneering voice in what he calls the Universal genre - a blend of sonic influences that continues to evolve with his latest foray into rock and alternative music."},{"t":"p","html":"His transition into the rock space is already making waves. Stephen’s debut alternative record and music video for<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3cqqiH32fFqe2fHfBCXWWP?si=75a692df14ee45a6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>&nbsp;“Back Home”</strong></a>&nbsp; was featured on <strong>MTV</strong>, and the song continued to climb the <strong>Active Rock Radio charts into the Top 60</strong>. The single went viral on TikTok with <strong>over 500,000 views in just 24 hours</strong>, while both “Back Home” and his breakout anthem <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=783255a44a914f36\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Stay Strong”</strong></a>—a heartfelt tribute to military personnel, autoimmune warriors, and those facing mental health challenges—have been featured on <strong>major editorial playlists across Spotify, Amazon Music, Tidal, and more</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6MiuL2cjgcSGasS6ol0DT7?si=768e41a678e24270\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Breaking Hearts,”</strong></a> and now <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0ejRjauL0fasaqqjEmwha5?si=YcbK7C4hRwitVwvpI5_mMg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>The Universal Me</em></strong></a><strong>,</strong> build on this momentum, showcasing a raw, emotive sound that reflects his bold artistic reinvention. Hitting over 100K streams in its first 12 hours of release as a New Independent Artist, the EP showcases Thomas’s gift for crossing emotional and musical borders and has drawn comparisons to artists like <strong>MGK</strong>, <strong>Jelly Roll</strong>, <strong>Carrie Underwood</strong>, and <strong>Shaboozey&nbsp;</strong>speaking to his wide-ranging appeal and boundary-pushing creativity."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/op_ZEYZegos","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"As a national touring artist, Stephen’s resume includes <strong>five Grammy Award considerations</strong> as an independent act, a <strong>#2 spot on the iTunes Charts</strong> with <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5PGeydtICzokuReD9TOiHW?si=4278bc4bba8f4826\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Best Days,”</strong></a> and global exposure through Revolt TV with his video for <strong>“Search Me.”</strong> &nbsp;From his early beginnings to signing with <strong>SkeeloMusik/Sony RED</strong> in 2013 and later finding his artistic home with <strong>Creative Hearts Entertainment</strong>, Stephen’s journey has been one of constant growth and reinvention."},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond the music, Stephen’s story and sound have been spotlighted in MTV, Vibe Magazine, Swagger, Hype Magazine, Earmilk, V13, and The Source, among others. He’s performed alongside iconic names and walked red carpets at major events including the BET Live Experience."},{"t":"p","html":"Ten years into his career, Stephen continues to follow the advice that shaped his path: stay true to yourself. It’s a message that drives his music and fuels his mission to inspire the next generation of artists."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"All of Stephen’s latest releases are available on Spotify, Apple Music, Amazon Music, Tidal, and all major platforms. For updates, videos, and exclusive content, visit the links below."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephen!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.stephentmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/StephenTMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/404?fromUrl=/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/StephenThomas1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://x.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>X</strong></a>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/Cv0cZdtuXQn/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"429771","title":"Read More","date":"2025-10-15","lead":"Through every stylistic shift, there is a connective thread; a storyteller's voice rooted in lived experience, authenticity, and heart.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/429771/6ec84c970638881dbf648ef6f76b1895.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Through every stylistic shift, there is a connective thread; a storyteller's voice rooted in lived experience, authenticity, and heart."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>WATERFORD, WI&nbsp;</strong>(November 6, 2025) - Singer-songwriter Kenny Hotopp is proud to announce the release of his evocative new EP, <em><strong>Early Times</strong></em>. A rich blend of Bluegrass, R&amp;B, and Blues, <em>Early Times</em> offers a deeply personal yet universally relatable soundtrack to the human experience."},{"t":"button","href":"https://open.spotify.com/album/39VCYqhafGv1F65miRhzuU?si=PoEl632gSzmyubTTdexViA","label":"Early Times","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Written from a place of heartfelt reflection and seasoned perspective, <em>Early Times</em> is a 5-track journey through memory, love, and the quiet moments that shape a life. From soul-soothing ballads to playful rhythms, the EP touches on themes of marriage, fatherhood, and the endurance of love. All with Hotopp’s signature warmth and lyrical honesty."},{"t":"quote","html":"“These are stories I’ve lived or witnessed, but I leave space in the lyrics for you to find your own meaning, your own moments. Some are fun, a few are serious. But every song came from a real place and I think people will feel that”","cite":"- Kenny Hotopp"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/785765/large-9bcfaeb5f4666c29a32a4e711e6bc65c.jpg","alt":"Photo Credit: Kevin Viol\n"},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, <em>Early Times</em> draws from a wide palette. Collaborating once again alongside <strong>Philville Records</strong> studio out of Eau Claire, WI, the EP touches on bluegrass, R&amp;B, and even hints of psychedelic country, all the while remaining grounded in folk and Americana roots. Those who like <strong>Jason Isbell</strong>, <strong>Ray LaMontagne</strong>, or <strong>Gregory Alan Isakov</strong> will find something to love in Hotopp’s melodic storytelling and soulful delivery."},{"t":"p","html":"From the uplifting camaraderie of “<strong>We'll Go On</strong>” to the emotional resilience in “<strong>Pull Me Through</strong>,” Kenny Hotopp captures life’s quiet truths. “<strong>Forever This Time</strong>” questions love’s durability, while the title track, “<strong>Early Times,</strong>” looks back on Midwestern roots with tender detail. The EP closes with “<strong>Lost Track of Time,</strong>” a warm, romantic escape into the beauty of being fully present. Each song stands alone, yet together they form a deeply human narrative."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/785764/large-0acc2dcd160c2ef17ad7b32f36b51046.jpg","alt":"Photo Credit: Kevin Viol\n"},{"t":"h3","html":"Track Highlights"},{"t":"list","items":["“<strong>We'll Go On</strong>”: A playful, uplifting tune co-written with a friend from <strong>Eau Claire</strong>, filled with hope and camaraderie.","“<strong>Pull Me Through</strong>”: A heartfelt ode to the kind of love that helps carry us through life’s hardest days.","“<strong>Forever This Time</strong>”: A contemplative look at the fragility of love, and whether some endings might still hold the promise of forever.","“<strong>Early Times</strong>”: The title track, inspired by lyrics found in an old journal, paints a nostalgic portrait of growing up in the Midwest.","“<strong>Lost Track of Time</strong>”: A tender, timeless love song about getting beautifully lost in the moment."]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kenny Hotopp:"},{"t":"p","html":"Based in Waterford, Wisconsin, Kenny Hotopp writes and sings soul-felt songs about family, love, memory, and the lifelong search for peace. His music blends genres from Americana and folk to blues and country but always centers on authenticity, heart, and lived experience. Every track is a story, every lyric an invitation to connect."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/785766/large-ff792c133c9ab196109a8aaacf6ca177.jpg","alt":"Pullmethrough_Front.jpg"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Kenny Hotopp!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://kennyhotopp.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/kenny_hotopp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1sNEXAMPLELINK\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | &nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/kenny.hotopp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Mackenzie Baldwin","role":"","email":"mackenziebaldwin@pressedfreshcollective.com","phone":""}},{"id":"426555","title":"Emma Cook Debuts Folk-Pop Ode to Personal Transformation with New Single “Thirteen Moons”","date":"2025-10-14","lead":"The first single from her upcoming album Of the Morning, “Thirteen Moons” is a lush blend of seasonal reflection, healing, and dreamy folk-pop textures","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/426555/ab263d0bb6f5e3e74c9526942e1b86bd.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The first single from her upcoming album <em>Of the Morning</em>, “Thirteen Moons” is a lush blend of seasonal reflection, healing, and dreamy folk-pop textures"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>BURLINGTON, VT (October 14, 2025)</strong> – Indie-folk artist <strong>Emma Cook</strong> is set to release <strong>“Thirteen Moons”</strong> on Tuesday, October 14, 2025, marking the first single from her forthcoming album <strong><em>Of the Morning</em></strong>. With velvet-smooth vocals and warm, organic production, the track offers a stirring meditation on the power of returning to oneself - guided by the rhythms of nature. It's a modern folk song about moving through difficulty, and using the natural cycles and the seasons as guide points and check-ins as we expand and transform, beyond what we thought we were capable of.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3tT5eH9WDKJCl0lkCleUiT?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Thirteen Moons is about moving through difficulty and letting nature remind us that we’re allowed to rest, change, and come back to ourselves. We’re not always meant to be blooming.”","cite":"Emma Cook on inspiration behind “Thirteen Moons”"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Katie Martucci</strong> and featuring a vibrant ensemble of Nashville and Brooklyn-based musicians, “Thirteen Moons” is a shimmering folk-pop journey reminiscent of powerhouse artists like <strong>Maggie Rogers</strong> and<strong>&nbsp;Phoebe Bridgers</strong>. The instrumentation is lush and expressive: acoustic guitar, layered harmonies, trumpet and trombone swell behind Cook’s evocative lyricism. The result is both grounded and ethereal - what Cook playfully calls <strong>“Carole King and Dua Lipa co-writing a song about the moons.”</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/781355/large-5777cc7328169f1958ebc9dc5fb845b0.jpg","alt":"Cover art for “Thirteen Moons” by Emma Cook"},{"t":"p","html":"“Recording ‘Thirteen Moons’ was a cathartic experience,” says Cook. “As a song that I'd held so closely and spent a lot of time getting just right lyrically, landing where we did with the production was like being set free.” Lyrically, the song is inspired by the indigenous names for the full moons, and a year in which thirteen appeared on the calendar - an ancient and spiritual marker of time and change. Written after a year of personal challenges - and ultimately personal growth - Cook’s lyrics unfold like journal entries, blooming and receding with the seasons: <em>“I watched thirteen moons, wax and wane / To return, through it all…”</em> The single resonates with themes of mental health, seasonal transformation, and healing - inviting listeners to honor their own cycles of growth and pause."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Emma Cook:"},{"t":"p","html":"With her upcoming indie-folk album<strong><em>&nbsp;Of the Morning</em></strong>, singer-songwriter Emma Cook turns inward, offering some of her most vulnerable and finely crafted work to date. Written during a transformational stretch of life - turning thirty in the early days of the global pandemic, becoming a mother, and reckoning with a rapidly changing world - these songs reflect what she calls her “delightfully melancholic experience of being human.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Weaving themes of moon cycles, forbidden fruit, motherhood, climate anxiety, and the everyday beauty in between, <em>Of the Morning</em> is, in Cook’s words, “a tender chronicle about growing the f** up.” With humor, honesty, and a soothing voice that has been called “incomparably smooth” (The Deli Magazine), Emma writes about Big Things - and the small, quiet moments that make a big life. Her expressive vocal range, jazz-inflected chord choices, and folk-rooted storytelling create a sound that’s both expansive and intimate. Think Maggie Rogers meets Carole King by way of the forest floor."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6wT4rgU77magWbJprjGXoI?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"A “formidable songwriter and instrumentalist” (Seven Days VT), Emma grew up in the Michigan folk and traditional music scene, learning guitar and piano before she was a teenager. Her sound blends the folk, roots, pop, and jazz that raised her into something unmistakably her own. From 2013–2019, she toured throughout New England and the Midwest with her folk-funk band <strong>Questionable Company</strong>, playing festivals, dive bars, and barns. The group earned a loyal following and critical praise for their energy and musicianship - “leveraging Emma’s incomparably smooth vocals to create something that sounds close to magic” (The Deli Magazine)."},{"t":"p","html":"Since then, Emma has continued to grow as a solo artist, most recently opening for <strong>Katie Pruitt</strong> and performing at the legendary folk venue Club Passim in Cambridge, MA. In late 2024, she completed her first crowdfunding campaign, raising over $15K to fund <em>Of the Morning</em>, her first solo project in over a decade.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/781356/large-eeabc6930e22123144aaebbfd56c563f.jpg","alt":"Image by Macaulay Lerman"},{"t":"p","html":"Now based in Vermont, Emma is not only a songwriter and performer, but also a beloved music educator and children’s musician in her local community. Deeply rooted in both her Michigan upbringing and Vermont home, she finds creative fuel in nature, family, and the simple joy of everyday life. “More than anything,” Emma says, “I believe in the power of music - to connect, to heal, to transform. These songs were offered to me from somewhere beyond myself, and now I offer them to you.”"},{"t":"p","html":"When she’s not making music, you’ll likely find Emma in the garden, riding her bike, doing yoga, making soup, swimming in wild water, or reading with her kiddo by her side."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Emma Cook:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.ecookmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"http://instagram.com/em_ma_cook\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"http://facebook.com/ecookmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6wT4rgU77magWbJprjGXoI\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/emma-cook/1542224776\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"425553","title":"Lora Kelley Offers a Vulnerable Invitation to Love and Healing on New Single “If You Let Me”","date":"2025-10-03","lead":"Americana artist Lora Kelley returns with “If You Let Me” - a tender, emotionally resonant single that explores the courage it takes to offer and receive love in the face of fear, wounds, and the longing to be truly seen.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/425553/d67e7d2298e16445d45e78662cec2468.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Americana artist Lora Kelley returns with “If You Let Me” - a tender, emotionally resonant single that explores the courage it takes to offer and receive love in the face of fear, wounds, and the longing to be truly seen."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Charlottesville, VA (October 3, 2025)</strong> — Americana singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lora_kelley/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lora Kelley</strong></a> returns with <strong>“If You Let Me”</strong>, a soul-baring new single releasing October 3, as part of her upcoming record<strong><em>&nbsp;Where I Am Now</em></strong>. Known for her warm vocals and introspective storytelling, Kelley once again invites listeners into a deeply emotional and honest conversation - this time, about love, forgiveness, and the courage it takes to receive both."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/IfYouLetMe","label":"Listen Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Rooted in the rich textures of folk and Americana, “If You Let Me” echoes the intimate, earthy style of artists like <strong>Natalie Merchant</strong>, blending acoustic instrumentation with lyrical tenderness and a quiet but powerful strength. The track explores the vulnerability and resilience needed to love and be loved in return, especially in the wake of relational pain, fear, or generational patterns. “This song is a little bit about negotiating with our wounds - our capacity to love and receive love,” Kelley shares. &nbsp;“Shared love is love that is felt by both parties. Where both people can impact each other to the degree that they experience being love - at the same time,” says Kelley. “If that's not happening - then the question becomes - what's coming between my feelings of love for you and your ability to feel that. And can we be with whatever that is so that you actually get to experience and feel what it feels like to be loved.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Penned with raw lyrical intimacy, the song opens with a direct offer: <em>“If you let me, I will forgive you... If you let me, I will love you.”</em> As it unfolds, the message becomes a meditation on relational repair - between partners, within families, and with the parts of ourselves that fear we are too broken to be loved fully. “To be seen and felt. That’s what this song is about.”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/780014/compressed_original-46255573c9a1bd7ce8d779b986e8deb6.png","alt":"Cover art for “If You Let Me\" - Image by Amy Cherry."},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by the same trusted team behind her previous release <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6ztJWHEWHbpSFtD5fgpR8v?si=26487014517f41db\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Man Behind the Curtain”</strong></a><strong> -</strong> Jeremy Casella (Producer), Matt Stanfield (piano), Josh Hunt (drums), Jacob Lowery (bass), Nate Duggar (guitar) and Mike Payne (guitar), with Evan Redwine (Engineer) - , “If You Let Me” continues Kelley’s evolution as a writer of emotional depth and clarity. This single is the next offering from <strong><em>Where I Am Now</em></strong>, a record that charts the internal landscape of marriage, personal growth, and the hard-won beauty of honest connection."},{"t":"p","html":"Whether navigating the quiet spaces of long-term commitment or the reckoning that comes with inherited emotional wounds, “If You Let Me” offers a balm: the chance to choose softness over fear, repair over retreat, and love that is actively felt - if we’re willing to let it in."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763792/large-040f26b07bc098f11a7be56c6ece467b.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-184.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763792/preview-bab801da600ba3701e09b5694e332bda.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763793/large-c253415328dd45d2f573e8555a00a593.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-48-2 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763793/preview-522091d282fcea1e14ae15584aa1bb21.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763791/large-44c5d725f595bf2ee8055e95fc686744.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-174.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763791/preview-892a437483001f7ba30f224eaaf03cbb.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by Amy Cherry"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lora Kelley"},{"t":"p","html":"Rooted in the themes of resilience and gentle honesty, Lora's work is deeply informed by her background in narrative-based trauma care, including her studies with the Allender Center. Her music stands as a testament to the beauty of brokenness, offering not platitudes, but presence — a hand to hold in the dark. Raised amid the liminality of faith and living today on a conserved farm in Virginia with her partner, children, and a lively menagerie of pets, Lora crafts songs that feel lived-in, earthy, and unflinchingly honest. Her upcoming album, releasing November 7, will continue to explore the emotional terrains where suffering and hope coexist — a body of work poised to resonate with those yearning for deeper connection and sacred honesty."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6WXETjjadXjtTGA0k5IfM4?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lora Kelley:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.lorakelley.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lora_kelley/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/thelorakelley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/lorakelley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Patreon</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"425835","title":"Mt. Gribley Unveils “Mourning Light,” a Raw Reflection on Solitude and Staying Afloat","date":"2025-10-03","lead":"Mt. Gribley turns everyday ache into understated beauty on “Mourning Light” - a raw, resilient folk meditation that lingers long after the last chord.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/425835/47ac921809d0131c6762242913b8af0f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Mt. Gribley turns everyday ache into understated beauty on “Mourning Light” - a raw, resilient folk meditation that lingers long after the last chord."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>MILFORD, CT (October 3, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>- &nbsp;Alternative folk artist <strong>Mt. Gribley</strong> (the musical moniker of singer-songwriter <strong>Matt Jarrett</strong>) returns with “<strong>Mourning Light”</strong>, the poignant opening track from his forthcoming album <strong><em>Moss on the Stone </em></strong>via indie label <strong>Resonating Wood Recordings</strong>. With stark, slow-burning honesty and a voice that cuts through the noise, Mt. Gribley’s “Mourning Light” sets the tone for a breakup album without the breakup - marking the return of an artist whose quiet resilience speaks volumes.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://ffm.to/orxjr5y","label":"Listen Here","color":"#1c1c1c"},{"t":"p","html":"Written in a moment of early-morning haze, “Mourning Light” sets the emotional landscape for the album to come - capturing the disoriented, quietly heroic mindset of a man carrying the weight of solo parenthood, grief, and the deep ache of separation. “This song came quick and fast one early morning, and yes, I wrote it from bed, staring out the window,” says Jarrett. “It’s about getting up and doing what needs to be done, even when you feel like disappearing.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, Mt. Gribley weaves understated acoustic textures with introspective, sharp-edged lyricism, drawing influence from artists like Frightened Rabbit, The Tallest Man on Earth, and The Cave Singers. His sound has been described as “soft-shoed folk” and “uptempo sad songs,” but Jarrett insists there’s light at the end of each track... even if the mood starts dark, the songs always land in a place of resolve."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/781352/large-fe9acc47ab72508c9a24d7c60c55e12e.jpg","alt":"Single Artwork - \"Mourning Light\" by Mt. Gribley"},{"t":"p","html":"“Mourning Light” was produced and engineered by <strong>Eric Michael Lichter</strong>, mixed by <strong>Guido Falivene</strong>, and mastered by <strong>Steve Wytas</strong>. The track showcases Jarrett’s evolved songwriting voice, steeped in vulnerability and resilience. Lyrically, “Mourning Light” finds Jarrett reckoning with emotional inertia, grief, and familial tension, all while forging ahead. The chorus rings like a mantra: “<em>Hey, you mourning light / Leave me in the dark, I’ll be quite all right.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"This sentiment lays the groundwork for what Jarrett describes as “a breakup album without the breakup.” While <em>Moss on the Stone</em> touches on themes of heartbreak and emotional distance, its roots are more nuanced. When his wife moved to the UK to pursue a PhD, Jarrett remained in Connecticut -suddenly navigating long-distance partnership, full-time work, and the unexpected role of solo caregiving for his teenage stepchild. “In a way, I became a single parent overnight - working, paying bills, holding down the fort, and dealing with the emptiness that comes from not having your person around. That’s where this record comes from.” What emerged is a full-length album shaped by three years of quiet transformation marked by separation, responsibility, and the quiet, often unnoticed resilience it takes to keep moving forward. <em>Moss on the Stone</em> is a weathered collection of songs carved from sleepless nights, distant love, and the stubborn ache of continuing on when your heart would rather not."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/780479/large-a752d20c0767ef5c491f879d4be69543.jpg","alt":"Mt. Gribley, courtesy of artist"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Mt. Gribley:"},{"t":"p","html":"Mt. Gribley is the minimalist folk project of Milford, Connecticut-based singer-songwriter Matt Jarrett. With finger-picked rhythms, stripped-back arrangements, and lyrics that wrestle with self-doubt and quiet resilience, his songs blend the warmth of folk’s roots with a subtle left turn - introspective, off-kilter, and emotionally raw."},{"t":"p","html":"The name Mt. Gribley is a nod to <em><strong>My Side of the Mountain</strong></em>, a favorite childhood book. Jarrett grew up in a divided musical household - his mother raised him on a steady dose of John Denver and Neil Diamond, while his father, a Methodist minister, brought home Wagner operas and hymns. His parents split by the time he was four.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Like many a pastor’s kid, Jarrett started his musical life behind a drum kit in metal bands, then rode the wave of ‘90s grunge. After graduating film school, he moved to New York City, where he spent 18 years editing television shows and chasing dreams of directing movies, all while quietly writing songs on a battered acoustic guitar. His turning point came in the late 2000s, when discovering artists like <strong>The Tallest Man on Earth</strong> and <strong>Iron &amp; Wine</strong> sparked a deeper dive into the 1960s folk canon - <strong>Bob Dylan</strong>, <strong>Neil Young</strong>, <strong>Nick Drake -&nbsp;</strong>and ignited a musical reawakening.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/780480/large-4dbae327841b9dde5f2e357f3e8b3fdd.jpg","alt":"Grib_Live_BW.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"Later, a divorce and the death of his father caused him to reassess everything, including his career in reality TV. “After my dad died, there was a piece of his history that I’d never understand,” Jarrett said, “in that he went to college pursuing music, and at some point changed his major to religion and never looked back. I never got a reason why from him. Now, of course, I never will. But I’ve always felt baffled by that decision.”"},{"t":"p","html":"The encouragement of his wife - now pursuing a PhD overseas - was a crucial push to pursue music more seriously. Her move abroad meant Jarrett took on a new role at home, stepping into full-time parenthood for his teenage stepchild, and finding songwriting material in the silence, responsibility, and longing that followed."},{"t":"p","html":"Mt. Gribley’s debut album, <strong><em>Semblance</em></strong>, arrived in 2019 via indie label <strong>Resonating Wood Recordings</strong>. Originally written, recorded, and mixed entirely by Jarrett, he later had it remixed and re-released as <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0oQZbZyf3Fy3hBWHJ2Rjg6?si=gujaQsNlSOmPTvvAzjVh4g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>reSemblance</em></strong></a><strong><em> -&nbsp;</em></strong>a hard-earned lesson in DIY production. In 2022, he followed up with <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0Krj5mYFmYouwC9hoBA7Ga?si=F8zYEdvnTJuFsENwOGipRw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>The Milksop EP</em></strong></a>, a three-song collection tackling confidence, depression, and learning to get out of your own way. Once again, Jarrett recorded all the parts himself, this time handing off mixing duties to Tony Calabro at Astoria Park Recording. Now he is anticipating his third release - a full length album <strong><em>Moss on The Stone</em></strong> that chronicles the last three years navigating sudden life changes, depression, loneliness, and the art of “keep on keepin' on” even when your heart would rather not."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0vOvSCbwHRSNyv4RsHkyJD?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Mt. Gribley:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.mtgribley.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0vOvSCbwHRSNyv4RsHkyJD\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/mtgribley/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"418474","title":"Warren Teagarden Releases \"Haiku Islands Volume Two,\" an Indie Rock Collection","date":"2025-09-26","lead":"The second in a three-part EP series blends sharp wit and indie-rock reflection into self-contained 'islands' of sound.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/418474/444552b8d5fa1d80558c4df755217bcf.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The second in a three-part EP series blends sharp wit and indie-rock reflection into self-contained 'islands' of sound."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>SAN FRANCISCO (September 26, 2025)</strong> – Today, Singer-songwriter <strong>Warren Teagarden</strong> releases <strong>\"Haiku Islands Volume Two,\"</strong> the second installment in his three-part EP series exploring self-contained songs as independent “islands” of sound and style. The project pairs his lo-fi and garage-punk roots with more refined, nuanced arrangements, while keeping its core indie rock spirit."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4Ia4KYdTPY8Bzg5L6f4Rf7?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The series title nods to two ideas: 'islands' for the way each track stands on its own, and 'haiku' for the overall 5–7–5 concept across the trilogy — three EPs released with five, seven and five songs, respectively. <strong>\"<a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/warren-teagarden/sets/haiku-islands-volume-one?utm_source=clipboard&amp;utm_medium=text&amp;utm_campaign=social_sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Haiku Islands Volume One</a>,\"</strong> includes 5 tracks, \"Haiku Islands Volume Two,\" includes 7, and \"Haiku Islands Volume Three,\" will include 5. Teagarden says he was also drawn to prime numbers; each EP’s track count is prime, and the total number of songs across the series (17) is prime as well."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I'm willing to explore my ideas in the songs, almost thinking aloud rather than stating a conclusive viewpoint. The songs aren't so much trying to provide answers, but to ask interesting questions.\"","cite":"- Warren Teagarden"},{"t":"p","html":"The lead single, “Hella Kismet Shit,” released on Sept. 12, delivering a sly, anti-authoritarian bite. It's a fictionalized jab at a controlling figure, loosely inspired by a former day-job manager with a restless groove and sharp turns of phrase."},{"t":"p","html":"Other highlights include “The Accent,” which leans into night-driving imagery and the 'laws of attraction'; “Fun Times,” a bittersweet cut with wry, skewed humor; “Learning Love,” a reflection on relationships that didn’t go as planned (featuring lead vocals by Eliza Hunt); and “Birthday,” which recalls two very different nights with two New York bands set against shifting relationship tides."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/769999/large-240fa5140ae43d84caf6570d4d7bf9a9.jpg","alt":"Cover art by Lana Ip"},{"t":"p","html":"Teagarden recorded the EP with Mark Pistel at Room 5, mixed by Grace Coleman at Different Fur and mastered by Lien Do at Different Fur."},{"t":"p","html":"“I think a lot about what the future might look like,” Teagarden said. “You can’t really think about the future without thinking about the past, and how your past shapes the choices you make. Most of these songs deal in some way with navigating the possibilities of personal growth, tempered by the limitations of our own experience.”"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Tracklist:</strong>"},{"t":"list","items":[]},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/772453/large-c7b1facc6979961b221c79395cb63707.jpg","alt":"\"Hella Kismet Shit\" Cover Art by Warren Teagarden"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>About Warren Teagarden</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Warren Teagarden is a San Francisco-based indie rock songwriter known for distilling decades of influence, from Pixies and The Smiths to Violent Femmes and R.E.M., into sharp, self-assured songs that balance lyrical curiosity with rock ’n’ roll fundamentals."},{"t":"p","html":"Teagarden first gained traction with his band <strong>Warren Teagarden and the Good Grief</strong>, releasing multiple albums and earning steady college radio support, including spins on WFMU. In recent years, he has shifted to a solo approach, handling bass and lead guitar duties himself while inviting select collaborators into the studio. His songwriting blends the immediacy of lo-fi and garage-punk roots with more nuanced arrangements, allowing each track to stand apart in tone and theme."},{"t":"p","html":"His current project, <strong>\"Haiku Islands,\" </strong>is a trilogy of EPs united not by a narrative concept but by form: three releases with five, seven and five songs, each one a “self-contained island” of sound. The title nods both to the haiku’s syllable structure and to Teagarden’s fascination with prime numbers, which guide the track counts across his catalog."},{"t":"p","html":"Lyrically, Teagarden often writes from a place of reflection rather than resolution. Whether channeling wry humor, anti-authoritarian bite, or unguarded introspection, his songs invite listeners into a space where meaning is as much about the feeling as the words themselves."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.warrenteagarden.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/warrenteagarden/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/people/Warren-Teagarden-and-The-Good-Grief/100063884236520/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://x.com/WarrenTeagarden\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a> | <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/warren-teagarden\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Soundcloud</a>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770020/large-ee88a386e96522d9aa6b1465d0f499f5.jpg","alt":"Warren Teagarden performing at Hotel Utah. Photo by Mr. Dodgy."}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"421071","title":"LOBE Releases Playful New Single, “Hummingbird Dances”","date":"2025-09-22","lead":"Award-winning Bay Area collective blends jazz, folk and disco in a lighthearted new release supported by YoungArts","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/421071/adc399d0ef7332f7a8ebce7930a1c385.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Award-winning Bay Area collective blends jazz, folk and disco in a lighthearted new release supported by YoungArts"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>OAKLAND, Calif.</strong> (September 22, 2025) — Bay Area collective <strong>LOBE</strong> has released its new single <strong>“Hummingbird Dances,”</strong> a kaleidoscopic track that flits between folk delicacy and disco exuberance. Written by flutist and composer Daiki Nakajima, “Hummingbird Dances” earned Nakajima the prestigious <strong>ASCAP Herb Alpert Young Jazz Composer Award in 2024</strong>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4C0w2nnNmscBf3ztSS70kR?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by 1970s singer-songwriter folk, including Yumi Arai’s “Yasashisa Ni Tsutsumatreta Nara” and Joni Mitchell’s “Big Yellow Taxi,” the piece is transformed through LOBE’s distinctive lens: shifting time signatures, polyrhythmic layers, and an ethos rooted in shared joy and spontaneity."},{"t":"p","html":"LOBE is comprised of Daiki Nakajima (flute, bass, tenor/soprano sax), Sam Silverstein (violin), Ethan Buck (alto sax), Nolan Miranda (piano, synths), Mark Rau (bass, guitar), and Michael Hayes (drums). Emerging from the San Francisco Bay Area, the collective is known for bridging intricate writing and dynamic improvisation."},{"t":"p","html":"“I wanted to write a song with a fun listening experience,” said Nakajima. “For us, it’s about making music that feels alive in the moment. Music that's joyful, communal and a little surprising,\" he continued. \"It starts kind of folksy and gradually morphs into a digital disco sound.\""},{"t":"p","html":"The track evolves from a folk-inspired guitar solo from bassist/guitarist Mark Rau into a playful flute solo from Nakajima threading through the central 11/8 theme, and concludes with a climactic drum solo from Michael Hayes soaring over a disco vamp."},{"t":"p","html":"Unlike many ensembles driven by a single bandleader, LOBE composes with one another in mind, such as melodies written for Sam Silverstein’s shimmering violin tone or ostinatos tailored to Nolan Miranda’s percussive piano playing, creating music that feels inseparable from their friendships. The group resists hierarchy, preferring to workshop pieces collectively until they blur the line between rehearsal and simply spending time together. The result is music that’s as much a reflection of friendship as it is of compositional rigor."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773393/large-ddec7987bf5c9dcd6c318de19952f007.png","alt":"Album art for \"was that on purpose?\" by Whitley Wilburn"},{"t":"p","html":"LOBE's sound draws on an unusually wide palette: Studio Ghibli scores, breakbeat rhythms, folk memories, and the improvisational language of contemporary jazz, all filtered through a playful, nostalgic lens."},{"t":"p","html":"Formed while studying at Stanford, LOBE grew out of the jazz program, where members discovered a shared love for rhythm-forward improvisation and experimental sound. What began as casual sessions quickly evolved into a collaborative practice."},{"t":"p","html":"“Hummingbird Dances” is the first glimpse into LOBE’s forthcoming debut album, <strong>\"was that on purpose?,\"</strong> releasing this fall. The title itself nods to a question the group often asks: how much of improvisation is intentional, and how much is discovery? For LOBE, there is beauty in the tension between the crafted studio record and the spontaneity of live performance."},{"t":"caption","html":"The mixing and mastering of the single and album are supported by <strong>YoungArts</strong>."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Production credits:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Recording Engineer – Mark Rau"},{"t":"p","html":"Assistant Recording Engineers – Daiki Nakajima, Nolan Miranda, Taylor Goss"},{"t":"p","html":"Mixing – Jack Kelly"},{"t":"p","html":"Mastering – James Clemens-Seely"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>About LOBE</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Emerging from the San Francisco Bay Area, LOBE is a collective of award-winning composers, arrangers, and musicians that lives at the confluence of intricate writing, dynamic improvisation and imaginative textures. Originally united through a common penchant for rhythm-forward contemporary jazz, LOBE quickly developed an interest in building on this aesthetic with dance, folk, electronic, and pop influences. Over many years of practice, friendship, and chemistry, the group came into its distinctive voice: whimsical and unhurried, challenging but inviting, time-bending yet always attuned to the here and now."},{"t":"p","html":"In Autumn 2025, LOBE is excited to showcase the culmination of the past three years of collaboration in their full-length debut album, \"was that on purpose?.\" Comprised of 8 chimeric original works and arrangements, \"was that on purpose?\" celebrates the beauty that arises from chance encounters, mundane experiences with friends, and musical relationships transcending the professional. With this release, LOBE hopes to spread the communal joy they feel every time they sit down together on stage, in rehearsal, and at the dinner table."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lobestagram/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://lobe.band/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> ​"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773394/large-77a0ff4ebe8bd4913a54582e30789cc4.png","alt":"ContactPage.png"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"417365","title":"Bay Area Experimentalist Band, Pateka, Releases Self-Titled Debut LP","date":"2025-09-19","lead":"A kaleidoscopic blend of jazz, rock-psychedelia and neo-soul makes for an off-kilter yet heartfelt debut","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/417365/901fd2e63c6ac943cea84247ab75dd11.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A kaleidoscopic blend of jazz, rock-psychedelia and neo-soul makes for an off-kilter yet heartfelt debut"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/album=3288317834/size=large/bgcol=ffffff/linkcol=0687f5/tracklist=false/artwork=small/transparent=true/","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>RICHMOND, CA</strong> (September 19, 2025) – Today, experimental rock quartet, Pateka, releases their self-titled debut album, <strong>\"Pateka,\"&nbsp;</strong>a nine-track LP that blends jazz, rock-psychedelia and neo-soul experimentation with themes of friendship, grief and the esoteric."},{"t":"p","html":"Featuring a unique blend of synthesized sounds, samples, off-kilter grooves, and expansive jazz harmonies, the album represents a culmination of years of collaboration between <strong>Elihu Knowles</strong> (keys/vocals), <strong>Dylan Ransley</strong> (guitar), <strong>Quinn Girard</strong> (bass), <strong>Ryan Higley</strong> (drums), and <strong>Hayden Dekker</strong> (saxophone, flute, synthesizer*) lifelong friends who grew up making music, films and skate videos together in the East Bay."},{"t":"p","html":"Listening to \"Pateka\" feels like wandering through a dreamscape of the Bay Area’s avant-garde spirit. Neo-soul warmth and experimental rock collide in tracks that nod to <strong>Palm</strong>, <strong>Sweet Trip</strong>, <strong>Hiatus Kaiyote</strong>, and <strong>Standing on the Corner</strong>, while remaining wholly its own."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/769042/large-499cb6394cfc5d1a4f1c4a50f326e93c.jpg","alt":"Front Cover art by Pateka"},{"t":"p","html":"Living and working side by side in Richmond, CA, the band meticulously shaped the LP over months of revisions, balancing technical precision with their authentic, personal experiences. Throughout the album, snippets of real dialogue, layered samples, and shifting rhythms capture the humor, chaos, and intimacy of shared creative life, while also referencing important places and traditions from the band’s shared adolescence."},{"t":"quote","html":"'Teni' came from when we were all working at this Burmese restaurant together. The song plays with the duality of the fast-paced jazz we'd play in the dining room when it was super busy, juxtaposed with whatever was on the radio in the kitchen. Walking between those two zones on a busy day always feels super disorienting, and we wanted to write something that captured that. Most of the dialogue is real stuff we heard from coworkers and customers.”","cite":"- Elihu Knowles"},{"t":"p","html":"The album also represents a dedication to a close friend the band lost in 2021. <strong>\"Cafe Chroma\"</strong> explores the personal journey of grief and acceptance, reflecting on the process of losing someone and how to move forward. <strong>\"Big Red\"</strong> is a sentimental interlude and tribute, with the title being his nickname. <strong>“Loss,”</strong> a jazz standard-style track written shortly after his passing, captures the immediate emotions of that time. The band reworked it into a playful, almost drunken rendition, evoking the feeling of lamenting a lost friend."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4rUKotyAEn7kD6k0vHNlEc?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Though the album isn’t centered on grief, it’s impossible to ignore the impact of their friend's passing on the band. For Knowles and bassist Quinn Girard, it was the turning point that brought them home after living abroad, and, in many ways, the catalyst for the band’s reformation."},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to the album, Pateka is releasing a series of increasingly bizarre music videos, centered around a mysterious chrome theme. The video for “Cafe Chroma” (out now) takes viewers on a surreal journey with a strange character wandering through the world, stealing objects and spray painting them chrome in his lair.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/KHuMnziNGjE","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"The video for <strong>“Night Stairs”</strong> dives deeper, following the protagonist as he’s visited by godlike chrome beings and spirals into a hallucinatory nightmare. It’s the kind of mind-bending, otherworldly experience that only Pateka could create."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/I8J4F0oCsKw","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"The <strong>\"Odwalla\"</strong> video (coming soon) completes the narrative. The band has yet to reveal all the details, but expect more chrome, more fire, and the continuation of the unsettling desert journey that has come to define the visual world of the album."},{"t":"p","html":"Adding another layer of intrigue, the band’s <a href=\"https://www.pateka.world/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">website</a> released as a fully interactive video game where users can explore Pateka's surreal desert world in first-person. The game invites players to uncover hidden Easter eggs in an unsettling, dreamlike landscape, inviting fans further into their immersive world."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/769045/large-665601775351bd09a84e16d5d8d3c630.jpg","alt":"Back Cover art by Pateka"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Album Credits</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Elihu Knowles (keyboards/vocals)<br>Dylan Ransley (guitar/vocals)<br>Quinn Girard (bass)<br>Ryan Higley (drums)<br>Hayden Dekker (saxophone, flute, synthesizer*)"},{"t":"p","html":"All songs written, performed, produced &amp; mixed by Pateka, with contributions from: Jas Stade, Sara Vidal, Adam Pavel, Byron Hogan, Yuri Kye, Cameron Daly, Emmalee Johnson Kao, and Highland Residents."},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded &amp; Mastered by Neil Godbole at Airship Laboratories."},{"t":"caption","html":"*Hayden Dekker was a large contributor to the album, but no longer performs with Pateka regularly"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>About Pateka</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"A four-piece experimental rock group from the San Francisco Bay Area, Pateka’s genre-bending songwriting style draws on the close-knit bond of childhood friends Elihu Knowles (keyboards/vocals), Dylan Ransley (guitar), Quinn Girard (bass) and Ryan Higley (drums). The band, which is based in Richmond, CA, creates a unique blend of synthesized sounds, samples, off-kilter grooves, and expansive, jazz-influenced harmonies. Pateka’s sound has been compared to a variety of artists, including Palm, Badbadnotgood, Sweet Trip, Mid Air Thief, Jon Bap, Sun Ra, Pulgas, Os Mutantes and Standing on the Corner."},{"t":"p","html":"Prior to forming Pateka, frontman Elihu Knowles released music under the name <strong>Aaron Space &amp; his Terrestrial Underlings</strong>, including the full-length album, \"<a href=\"https://aaronspace.bandcamp.com/album/fishland\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fishland</a>,\" and EP, \"<a href=\"https://aaronspace.bandcamp.com/album/grid\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grid</a>,\" with the respected independent label <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/moonglyphrecords/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Moon Glyph</strong></a> in 2020. That project helped shape the eclectic, expansive sound he brings into this new chapter, where improvisation, storytelling and sonic experimentation coexist."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/suschords/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://pateka.bandcamp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bandcamp</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@Patekaband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.pateka.world/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/769047/large-eb9135ea60615fcb71bd9b51f1ab486a.jpg","alt":"Image by Mei Mei Mccomb"}],"contact":null},{"id":"417744","title":"Kim Edwards Unveils \"Vignettes,\" a Tender Collection of Story-Based Songs Exploring Life’s Seasons","date":"2025-09-19","lead":"With rich orchestration, the intimate album shares deeply empathetic, heartfelt and human stories exploring love, loss, and resilience.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/417744/6b0c4309be73a9e99700695059dda96e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"With rich orchestration, the intimate album shares deeply empathetic, heartfelt and human stories exploring love, loss, and resilience."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lehigh Valley</strong><strong>, PA (September 19, 2025)</strong> – Today, singer-songwriter Kim Edwards releases her latest full-length album, \"Vignettes,\" a deeply personal collection of story-driven songs that capture life in all its fragile, fleeting beauty."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0EkQqqcVATjUL7Ovd18sJg?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Spanning a decade of writing, \"Vignettes\" gathers ten intimate 'story songs,' each a standalone moment, like a breakup steeped in smoke and memory (<strong>“Ashes to Ashes”</strong>), a restless voyage across stormy seas (<strong>“The Seafarer’s Song”</strong>), the bittersweet ache of loving someone who can’t stay (<strong>“Raised by Wolves”</strong>) and a Dust Bowl-inspired journey across generations (<strong>“Steinbeck”</strong>).&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by books, podcasts, and the lives of friends and imagined characters, these songs form a gallery of emotion, including snapshots of love, loss, and the quiet resilience of the human heart."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Some friends have pointed out that the album seems to have a sad, or at least melancholy, theme to it,\" said Edwards. \"It wasn't my intention to create a bummer album, but it is sometimes easier for me to dig deep into the 'achier' feels and try to give words to these nuanced emotions. I think I'm just more naturally drawn to these types of songs; there's something really comforting and validating in hearing a song that makes you think, 'Ah, that person gets it.' Empathy is powerful. So maybe the common thread is less about sadness and more about empathy.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, \"Vignettes\" is the album Edwards always dreamed of making: a hushed, cinematic journey of piano, real strings and organic textures, produced in collaboration with longtime creative partner <strong>Jared Salte (Salt Shaker Studios)</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"True to Edwards’ vision, the record leans into dynamic, and at times rubato-style storytelling. From stripped-down piano ballads to orchestral swells, each track expertly bends with emotional nuance, warmth and honesty, rather than strict perfection. Real, lush strings throughout by <strong>Rob Szabo&nbsp;</strong>and a real horn section on <strong>\"Steinbeck\"</strong> (featuring <strong>Fletch Wiley</strong> on flugelhorn and trumpet and <strong>Phil Miller&nbsp;</strong>on trombone) bring warmth, texture and lift to the arrangements."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/769248/large-5f445610a5824f97404e6df30d513272.jpg","alt":"\"Vignettes\" Cover. Photo by Bruce Kite, design by Victoria Strout."},{"t":"p","html":"\"My favorite tracks on any album are the stripped-down, piano-and-strings, acoustic songs that usually are the last track of an album,\" Kim said. \"In the past, I was concerned that it would be too much to have an entire album of low-key, emotional ballad songs. But over time, I’ve come to focus more on creating music that I love and am proud of, rather than trying to anticipate what others might want.\""},{"t":"p","html":"The title, \"Vignettes,\" speaks to the nature of the album: a series of unconnected yet emotionally resonant sketches, drawn from lived experiences as well as imagined lives. Some songs were written over a decade ago; others are more recent. Together, they form a timeless, reflective body of work, one that feels like paging through a weathered journal or lingering in a quiet corner of memory."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748285/large-0b6197a6f051d62c8146b0bba7cbf73b.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0289.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748285/preview-bcd098cac55d2a0eb6f774e77a787a71.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748286/large-d7e1d9dc0fd77a1a60c2c144303c6c37.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0328.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748286/preview-3696cb8baf68ee148f0bfb241a64e885.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748284/large-b0ad8163393c6c2cbf500be49e658174.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0039.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748284/preview-70ba0c00623cb7165aa7d51893e21f33.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748288/large-a2e3c15bbc6e0af1049c6ab7a9aa63e0.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0052.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748288/preview-fc8ceb005772fc5462b875ad5550c920.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748287/large-934438af0366adc974540cf1dc309eca.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0398.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748287/preview-bf975564845cca27474a595e1bf8868b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748283/large-44156cfbc2050f9407a34bd86f00a033.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0135.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748283/preview-467a9947650ae95dcbcec1d19c1a40e7.jpeg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Bruce Kite"},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, \"Vignettes\" blends the lyrical intimacy of <strong>Ingrid Michaelson</strong> and <strong>Regina Spektor</strong> with the sweeping, cinematic textures of <strong>Sleeping At Last</strong> and <strong>Taylor Swift</strong>’s <strong>\"folklore.\"</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"The album’s visual identity leans further into nostalgia, evoking the 1930s and ’40s with analog-inspired photography by <strong>Bruce Kite</strong> and bookish, handwritten design by <strong>Victoria Strout</strong>. Edwards seeks to press the collection to vinyl, further emphasizing its timeless, tactile nature."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>\"Vignettes\" Track List:</strong>"},{"t":"list","items":[]},{"t":"p","html":"All songs written by Kim Edwards (c) 2012–2025 White Shore Music (ASCAP)"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4PCJGcs6ZoUsKBG1OSbyh6?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kim Edwards:"},{"t":"p","html":"With a voice as intimate as a journal entry and melodies that echo like memory, <strong>Kim Edwards</strong> crafts cinematic, emotionally rich songs that feel both timeless and deeply personal. A Lehigh Valley, PA-based singer-songwriter with roots in classical piano and a love for storytelling-driven pop, Edwards writes vignettes—poetic snapshots of longing, love, and quiet resilience."},{"t":"p","html":"Over the years, Edwards has developed a signature sound: moody, melancholic, and lush with introspective nuance. Inspired by the likes of <strong>Ingrid Michaelson</strong>, <strong>Regina Spektor</strong>, and <strong>Sleeping At Last</strong>, she blends lyrical vulnerability with orchestral textures often drawing comparisons to her influences while carving out a sonic world uniquely her own. Her songs have found homes in branded content for <strong>Chaco Shoes</strong>, <strong>Paraxel</strong>, and <strong>Disney Weddings</strong>, and her cover of “Auld Lang Syne” garnered over 150K Spotify streams after landing a spot on the platform’s Folksy Christmas playlist. In 2013, she was selected from hundreds of applicants for ASCAP’s prestigious <strong>Jerry Ragovoy Songwriters Workshop </strong>in NYC, has performed twice at <strong>Musikfest</strong> in Bethlehem, PA, and in storied venues like <strong>The Bitter End, Eddie’s Attic, </strong>and <strong>Bluebird Cafe</strong>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/dJeQnuBRcw8","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Among her most meaningful career moments, Kim had the rare honor of <strong>opening for</strong> <strong>The Beach Boys</strong>—a lifelong dream realized for the devoted fan—and also shared a stage with <strong>Jars of Clay</strong> at a local festival. These highlights underscore her steady dedication to her craft and the quiet authenticity that resonates through her music."},{"t":"p","html":"Edwards is embracing music on her own terms. Her forthcoming album, <strong><em>Vignettes</em></strong>, is the most personal and fully realized project of her career. Co-produced by <strong>Jared Salte</strong>, the album serves as a dream fulfilled: “Each song has its own special place in my heart,” she says. “There’s not a single filler.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Now a mother and entering into a reflective new chapter, Kim Edwards stands as a reminder that in a world obsessed with virality and speed, artistry rooted in depth, patience, and honesty endures. Her music offers a quiet refuge for the reflective listener—those seeking comfort, catharsis, or simply the feeling of being seen."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.kimedwardsmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://instagram.com/kimedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://facebook.com/kedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://x.com/kimedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a> | <a href=\"https://youtube.com/kimedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"419053","title":"17-year-old pop sensation Maria Deirisarri is set to release her debut album, \"In The Beginning,\" on September 29th. Hailing from Atlanta, her musical talent transcends her age, exploring genres from dark alternative to bossa nova. With over 77k Spotify streams and recognition from top publications like Earmilk and Conversations About Her, Maria's star is on the rise. Her music, influenced by her Hispanic heritage, surprises and captivates with its multilingual lyrics.","date":"2025-09-19","lead":"The multi-genre journey blends vengeance, romance, solitude, forgiveness, and spirituality","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/419053/6052d8edd54c0b21e7f337b9e6043e01.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The multi-genre journey blends vengeance, romance, solitude, forgiveness, and spirituality"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Roswell, GA (September 19, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>- Today, alt-pop singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?si=bpNuIeehSrqSbXVybDzELQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Maria Deirisarri</a> releases her debut EP, <strong>\"Si Vis Pacem,\"</strong> a five-song collection tracing the pursuit of peace in its many forms.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4Lx0ObhhcoGVpOcNnqHHq1?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Out now on all platforms, the record takes its name from the Latin phrase “si vis pacem, para bellum” — “if you want peace, prepare for war,\" and finds the 19-year-old artist navigating personal battles with striking lyrical honesty. Its wide-ranging sonic palette spans stripped-back alt-folk, bossa nova, cinematic folk, and intimate pop."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Si Vis Pacem\" unfolds like a map with five distinct routes: the smoldering “Parabellum” (feat. Corey Kilgannon) readies for battle with restrained power; “bluejay” revels in love’s lighthearted escape; “And I’ll Fly” seeks strength in nature’s stillness; “Letting It Go” honors the hard work of forgiveness; and “Prayer” offers peace through spiritual connection. Together, they form what Deirisarri calls her “five paths of peace.”"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Every lyric was a challenge to myself to be as honest and direct as I could. After around a year and a half, I’m pleased that 'Si Vis Pacem' is finally being released. I’m very proud of every song on the EP, the theme of peace that I wanted the EP to chase, and the cover art as well. It turned out so badass.”","cite":"- Singer-songwriter Maria Deirisarri"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770671/large-0c9de14aee59a033747ee4f7096cdbf8.png","alt":"\"Si Vis Pacem\" cover art. Image by Beatriz Deirisarri."},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded with co-producers <strong>Corey Kilgannon</strong> and <strong>Jacob Hudson</strong> at Beaches Vineyard and Pine Studios in Jacksonville, Florida, each track carries a distinct production identity. “Parabellum,” written the night before recording, was captured live in a single take with just four instruments, its sparseness amplifying the quiet confidence of its whispered warning. Inspired in part by the <strong>John Wick film series</strong>, which also partly inspired the EP's title, it frames vengeance as a necessary step toward peace."},{"t":"p","html":"The next track, “bluejay,” draws from bossa nova to tell the story of a fleeting summer romance. Recorded entirely to tape without a click track, the song relied on guitars to set its warm, unfiltered rhythm, giving it the feel of a private performance. “And I’ll Fly” finds empowerment in nature’s stillness, with expansive guitar textures and graceful piano that build into a soaring affirmation of self-reliance. The song’s visual imagery mirrors its lyrical landscapes, including nods to the trembling timber, shivering sea and mighty mountains she sings about. An accompanying music video further amplifies these themes, alongside real footage of Maria skydiving."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/Kc44XFLF5Mc","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"On “Letting It Go,” melancholic melodies meet hopeful undertones in a meditation on forgiveness. Kilgannon and Hudson’s understated production leaves space for Deirisarri’s soft but commanding vocal delivery, underscoring the song’s emotional weight. The closing track, “Prayer,” is sung in a self-created language and dedicated to God. Designed to be felt more than understood, it opens with a nod to Ludwig Göransson and Baaba Maal’s “Wakanda” from Black Panther, and closes the EP on a note of spiritual connection and belonging."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Si Vis Pacem\" marks a series of firsts for Deirisarri: her first EP, her first featured artist collaboration and her first music video release. From the analog warmth of “bluejay” to the live, one-take recording of “Parabellum,” the project captures an artist fully stepping into her vision — a body of work that stands as both a personal milestone and complete artistic statement."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770672/large-649503250b6f7a1c519380ea95ad74c4.jpg","alt":"IMG_7996.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770672/preview-f33ceb6f6867f958b18ba072b3317940.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770673/large-2abcfa5a1acda73899b955c017b63398.png","alt":"Untitled design - 1.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770673/preview-61d8416d0de123a58a61bbb6f8ee124e.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770675/-03e0a9d2eb4d3e0ccf76ed63542d8d16.png","alt":"Add a subheading - 1.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770675/-03e0a9d2eb4d3e0ccf76ed63542d8d16.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770676/large-354d786db361bcf33db68ec1c7d11973.jpg","alt":"B00517AA-9587-4724-9A6B-08CFDF43A00E.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770676/preview-0b5c081f009f4fffdc070020fcb7cad6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770677/large-3b5b62b41aaad718d602f28f5eeafb98.jpg","alt":"62205B81-D034-4834-861C-8A2ADBDF717B.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770677/preview-d8b311b33b8238171a0e2aa6bcc7332e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770674/large-f1dacecd080ecde0fecde3c4f60aca09.jpg","alt":"9CA484D9-ABAF-44DD-B902-D62F6F7DDE91.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770674/preview-9bff886fe4b1c378be97a9822ed9928e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770678/large-2d442eb8b7f6c398249f3d1c78bf1627.png","alt":"Si Vis Pacem Coverart.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/770678/preview-9270fa017f517d07d76944cf0d5b0d69.png"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Beatriz Deirisarri."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Maria Deirisarri:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Rising pop artist <a href=\"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maria Deirisarri</strong></a> is only 19, but her musicianship and lyricism suggest wisdom beyond her years. The Atlanta-based singer-songwriter experiments with many genres, from dark alternative to bossa nova, generating an eclectic mix of music notably showcased in her debut album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ?si=w6TbXsN-SJOMPd4mN151ZA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>In The Beginning</strong></em></a><em>.</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Already amassing over 110k streams on Spotify, and garnering attention from top publications such as <strong>EARMILK</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Conversations About Her</strong>, Maria Deirisarri’s success continues to increase with every release. The range of her sound entices listeners to discover every song’s personality, surprising them with lyrics connected to her Hispanic culture and multilingual heritage (such as in “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5am4tRMhZJObB1vjpzNTbG?si=6c8d80dc16304bd4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Same</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2HOQOaIyRpXxD6JzPwhEdY?si=31b49e0b35bf401a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Te Necesito</strong></a>”)."},{"t":"p","html":"The young artist has triumphed in various competitions, ranging from her Trailblazing Performer accolade from the International Singer-Songwriters Association, her second-place finish in <strong>Omega’s Got Talent</strong>, to her Talent Preliminary Award in the <strong>Miss Georgia Teen Volunteer Competition</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Maria Deirisarri’s vibrant artiste meets the listener with a grace and uniqueness that is a breath of fresh air. Fans are eager to see what this up-and-coming superstar has up her sleeve.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Follow Maria below for all music updates and upcoming announcements!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Maria Deirisarri!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/mariadeirisarri/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@mariadeirisarri","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com/","img":"","title":"17-year-old pop sensation Maria Deirisarri is set to release her debut album, \"In The Beginning,\" on September 29th. Hailing from Atlanta, her musical talent transcends her age, exploring genres from dark alternative to bossa nova. With over 77k Spotify streams and recognition from top publications like Earmilk and Conversations About Her, Maria's star is on the rise. Her music, influenced by her Hispanic heritage, surprises and captivates with its multilingual lyrics.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@mariadeirisarri?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCtx5jhQ5a3Fx8_EJxh54WsA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100063574507610\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"421786","title":"CO Folk Duo Woven Hollow Premieres “Reruns” - A Music Video 5 Years in the Making","date":"2025-09-17","lead":"Combining timeless folk harmonies with archival TV footage, the duo explores how nostalgia masks the uncomfortable truths of today’s world.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/421786/fb969118954690fc79ece6760eaa8c88.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Combining timeless folk harmonies with archival TV footage, the duo explores how nostalgia masks the uncomfortable truths of today’s world."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>GLENWOOD SPRINGS, CO (September 17, 2025)</strong> - Colorado-based folk duo W<strong>oven Hollow</strong> returns with their hauntingly beautiful new music video <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1aziGrWu5UgY3EV71BwfWV?si=05c06bf81bd842ac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Reruns,”</strong></a> arriving September 17, 2025. A tender yet piercing reflection on society’s cyclical patterns, cultural nostalgia, and the illusions of progress, the track pairs cinematic storytelling with raw folk lyricism delivered through the intimate harmonies of husband-and-wife duo <strong>Anna Murphy</strong> and <strong>Van Wampler</strong>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/9vQFu2BhENM","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Originally written and recorded during the early days of the 2020 lockdown, “Reruns” became the first completed track from the duo’s upcoming debut full-length album - an ambitious, genre-blurring project five years in the making. Set to the backdrop of a folk arrangement that blends vintage textures with modern poignancy, the song unpacks the ways we escape into media and memory to avoid confronting uncomfortable truths about the present. <em>“The internet would have us believe we’re living in a time of major progress,”</em> the band shares,<em>&nbsp;“but even the most ‘progressive’ among us still uphold habits and systems that are doing harm. ‘Reruns’ captures the nostalgia of a world where modern problems feel less present—even if that illusion isn’t real.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"The video, directed by <strong>Sam Blakesberg&nbsp;</strong>and Van Wampler, is a visual love letter to classic television and the complicated comfort it offers. The performance unfolds through the warped glass of a retro TV screen, playing back a meticulously edited montage of TV clips and scripted lines each synced to the song’s lyrics. <em>“It took years of searching old transcripts, scrubbing through episodes to find exact moments, and stitching it all together,”&nbsp;</em>says Van. <em>“There were times I wasn’t sure I’d ever finish it, but watching it now - it's certainly a piece that I'm proud of.”</em> For Anna, who is both a performer and a practicing mental health therapist, the process of filming the final shots brought its own challenges: <em>“As a woman and therapist, it was hard at first to be filmed with my body distorted by an old TV screen,”</em> she shares. <em>“But Van and I both believe in body positivity and health at every size, and his respect as both a friend and husband made me feel safe. This video really strums on those nostalgia strings. It reminds us how deeply media becomes part of our shared consciousness.”&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/774459/large-d2f7268c010c9e0a7ffd808416271a6a.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Reruns\""},{"t":"p","html":"This deeply layered visual project exploring escapism, television, and modern dissonance doesn’t just nod to the past - it invites us to question what we choose to relive, and what we need to rewrite. Framed by evocative lyrics like <em>“We can only dream that we're in those beautiful scenes / past the frame, beyond the set or the stage,</em>” “Reruns” offers a compelling glimpse into the emotional depth and cinematic scope of Woven Hollow’s forthcoming debut album."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Woven Hollow:"},{"t":"p","html":"The sound of music and the beauty of the Rocky Mountains led the winding paths of Anna Murphy and Van Wampler to cross in 2017. A few recording sessions together quickly blossomed into an ongoing collaboration which quickly solidified itself as Woven Hollow. After recording a few songs and playing a short tour in 2019, the duet set out to record its first full-length album during the Covid lock down of 2020. Years of work on the album would see a number of incredible musicians adding their talent to Woven Hollow's compositions, and what started as a simple folk record grew into an adventurous project that can hardly be described by a single genre.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/774460/large-622454f118623c534ac9acd3f7d1a07f.jpg","alt":"Woven Hollow.jpg"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"CONNECT WITH WOVEN HOLLOW:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.WovenHollow.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/wovenhollowmusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3EC1U6eXrn2Yj3SEQLPvnA?si=UTZVOfzqSL6Dhtl9cUhJxA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@wovenhollow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3EC1U6eXrn2Yj3SEQLPvnA?utm_source=generator","height":"352"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"421300","title":"Riah Breaks Down Barriers with \"The Fourth Wall\" Album and \"Reclamation\" Visual EP","date":"2025-09-13","lead":"An empowered exploration of trauma, power and liberation","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/421300/a6bbc96d12544592ad2741e21f171c1d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An empowered exploration of trauma, power and liberation"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>DENVER, CO</strong> (September 13, 2025) – Dark-pop artist <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/riahmusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Riah</strong></a> unveils her boldest work yet with the release of \"The Fourth Wall\" today, a full-length album paired with the \"Reclamation\" visual EP.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7FpduZyXjoVyseCcr9SMBM?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Together, these projects shatter the boundary between performer and audience, weaving confessionals, anthems and story-driven visuals into an immersive body of work that is as vulnerable as it is defiant."},{"t":"p","html":"Across its tracks, \"The Fourth Wall\" dives headfirst into themes of mental health, taboo pleasure, grief, and self-discovery. Songs like \"Talk to Someone\" wrestle with anxiety and the search for connection, while \"Skin on Chrome\" and \"Misb3hav3\" embrace sensuality and unapologetic desire."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Dear Unborn\" grieves a life that never came to be, and \"Home\" anchors the project with a rare moment of tenderness and stability. The record spans intimate alt-pop ballads and sultry, beat-driven dark R&amp;B, with sonic nods to <strong>Rihanna, Spelles, Two Feet, </strong>and<strong> RÜFÜS DU SOL</strong>."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773603/large-a9423818a63349c1895b85079c12ff66.jpg","alt":"COVERJPG.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773603/preview-1e10b7b3734096ca9f1073c75c10ae69.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773604/large-dc45c2db9a56d49aa6dba8d6e498466d.png","alt":"The Fourth Wall Tracklist (1).png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773604/preview-178f1e7fa191ceefb02fadd183c7eb40.png"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"\"The Fourth Wall\" cover art and track list."},{"t":"quote","html":"'The Fourth Wall' isn’t just an album to me—it’s me confronting my own truths and inviting people to see the raw, unfiltered parts of my story. I didn’t make this as background music. I made it as art that demands to be seen, heard, and felt.","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Riah"},{"t":"p","html":"Accompanying the album is \"Reclamation,\" a three-part visual EP that brings the record’s core themes to life through striking cinematic storytelling. Co-directed by Riah and Cinema King (Ed Kelly), the visuals transform \"Talk to Someone,\" \"Misandrist Interlude,\" and \"Sacrilege\" into visceral performances of vulnerability, rage and reclamation of self."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/LCXp86S9cag","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"The project follows the official music videos for \"Stand By You\" and \"Skin on Chrome,\" which introduced audiences to the world of \"The Fourth Wall\" and offered a first glimpse of the album’s fearless honesty and sensual edge."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/w5OIQbe5WL0","height":""},{"t":"quote","html":"'Reclamation' was my chance to turn pain into power. Each visual—whether vulnerable, furious, or taboo—is me reclaiming my narrative on my own terms.","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Riah"},{"t":"p","html":"The release follows the singles \"Stand By You\" and \"Skin on Chrome,\" both of which signaled Riah’s evolution into a deeper, darker sound that blends sultry R&amp;B textures with piercing honesty. With production credits spanning Riah herself alongside collaborators including Alissa Ann, DNA Picasso, El Javi, Dominick Williams, and 88 Noiz, the record is a true community effort anchored by Riah’s vision, celebrating resilience and radical self-expression."},{"t":"p","html":"An official album release event will be hosted on September 13 by <a href=\"https://www.multipass.com/album-release\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Callywood Music</strong></a>, where both the album and \"Reclamation\" will premiere in full."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746836/large-e77d8204f3ebbc7f5475bf372618966a.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13517.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746836/preview-489222ae1b9a2979761050ee9542b053.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746838/large-d005a4bebcff998d871013dcbd46f192.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13626.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746838/preview-d60c26362d10cbeed6ac1ac9b2c96e68.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746839/large-818b693b5f528c1567b7ff8456df0e23.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13650.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746839/preview-ef8caef77bebafb022593cf688b86097.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746840/large-cc99a6346f11e2c492558b973a346076.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13583.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746840/preview-445d73ecd8393f973aaffd9ffee1d23c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746837/large-560fe1b59f9fc41150ff00ca8f6ab8bb.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13742.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746837/preview-2b9c6cb084c4ce7dec5bad6a46f81e10.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773597/large-c4bece8f122040dfa9a046efefef3dc9.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13357.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773597/preview-be3821449ea7c1cf7112a917fc449cc3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773600/large-7f2e5663e91904b1f45cbb314417797f.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13761.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773600/preview-e28bc8ce21577b54f3329a24742d4617.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773601/large-3fe21f148beaf2eed5660395070a2b02.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13695.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773601/preview-3954111d26832b8b430cb949732d590a.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Martha Wirth"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Production Credits:</strong> Riah, Alissa Ann, DNA Picasso, El Javi, Dominick Williams, 88 Noiz, Sillage. Crcl, ProdbyCece, Austin Weller, NetUh."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/dNRx30t1Gp0","height":""},{"t":"h3","html":"About Riah:"},{"t":"p","html":"Riah, a rising force in the Bedroom Pop scene, is crafting introspective and evocative music that resonates with the complexities of love, sex, loss, and a distinctive \"villain energy.\" Drawing from personal life experiences, Riah channels deep emotion into every lyric and melody, creating an intimate connection with listeners.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Starting in the Los Angeles entertainment industry at the tender age of 17, Riah faced the harsh realities of the pre-Me Too era, which fueled her desire for autonomy and control over her artistic vision. After years of enduring the industry's darker side, she stepped back, determined to return to music only on her own terms. Now, as an accomplished entrepreneur, Riah has reclaimed her voice and is ready to make waves with a fresh and authentic sound."},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to her musical journey, Riah has captivated audiences at numerous festivals, clubs, and acoustic venues. Her passion for performance extends beyond music, as she is also a competitive pole dancer, having won in her division and heels categories in the prestigious PSO Mountain competition in 2023.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a unique blend of vulnerability and power, Riah is poised to leave a lasting impact on the music world, bringing a new level of depth and intensity to the Bedroom Pop genre."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Riah:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4W98Etru2ErpE95smqDdfh?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/riahmusic1991\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/riahmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@Riah-Music-1991\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"420860","title":"LifeSize is the project of Los Angeles-based artist Scott, blending heartfelt songwriting with roots-rock energy. His music has earned praised by The Mercury News as “poignant” and “vastly appealing,” drawing comparisons to legends like Tom Petty, Mark Knopfler, and Bruce Springsteen. With a sound that’s both timeless and deeply personal, LifeSize continues to build momentum—new music is set to arrive in 2025.","date":"2025-09-12","lead":"A love letter to the Golden State written in the aftermath of a Southern California wildfire","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/420860/28b5cab6cb0e64645e3b35e652194500.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"&nbsp;A love letter to the Golden State written in the aftermath of a Southern California wildfire"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>LOS ANGELES</strong> (September 12, 2025) — Singer-songwriter Scott Marshall, performing under the name <strong>LifeSize</strong>, releases his new single \"California Home\" today. The upbeat pop-rock track is both <strong>a love letter to and a reckoning with</strong> his home state, written in the aftermath of surviving a Southern California wildfire."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0T3DZe9GaGDK2gUGM5g2Rq?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Marshall, who came of age in Seattle’s vibrant music scene, grew up on a mix of <strong>The Beatles, Hendrix, Sonic Youth </strong>and local legends&nbsp;<strong>Screaming Trees</strong>, influences that shaped the eclectic sound he now carries into his Los Angeles–based work."},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by Grammy-winning producer Dave Darling and Marshall himself, \"California Home\" draws inspiration from California icons like the <strong>Beach Boys</strong> while also nodding to the modern pop-rock stylings of <strong>Maroon 5</strong> and <strong>The Neighbourhood</strong>. The single is the fourth release leading up to LifeSize’s eponymous album, \"LifeSize,\" set for Oct. 17."},{"t":"p","html":"\"'California Home' is a song I wrote in the wake of surviving a Southern California wildfire,\" said Marshall. \"I was struggling with my love affair for California and wanted to write a personal, reflective and observational song about what it means to me to be a Californian.\""},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773190/large-a08b4b245a065b40c7de4ebe4e061d0b.jpg","alt":"LIFESIZE 4-26-26 V10.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773190/preview-8fee78bbcebfdf094e96d56ae605c460.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773188/large-c37a09cc5ab64bac1728dd50694a1763.png","alt":"LIFESIZE 3.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773188/preview-8eccd085ed306211595007f3637e8913.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773189/large-10759f9afe0a1e93d57c72ba3b6e9910.png","alt":"LIFESIZE 2.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773189/preview-987009aa8bd7056ec904ed21c9343cbc.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773191/large-255d0946b5b76f6b5c4622ad2d26d220.png","alt":"LIFESIZE 1.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773191/preview-111d8bc68a6fe73ddea524b7bb327624.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773192/large-8054f545c07a300b5e728534f8864c0d.jpg","alt":"Dreamwalking Poster.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773192/preview-23e5ac484112a889d8eb56c7add98da4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773187/large-b66cf297d40bc6e00f1feeb9b30dbccd.jpg","alt":"LifeSize Logo Cover.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773187/preview-8ee92f25c273ec5529eb19563e044fa3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773186/large-230c0dd7ac8f69844c369291fb828141.jpg","alt":"LIFESIZE LOGO.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/773186/preview-f83e992528b9704c04f5ad8beb15232c.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"The lyrics highlight both the beauty and contradictions of life in the Golden State, moving from coastal imagery to traffic-weary musings, while carrying a distinctly uplifting tone.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Marshall reflects, “Bus tires drone on a flat Midwest lane / Makes you ache for the crack of a breaking wave,” underscoring the tension between leaving California and the longing to return."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I tried to write unvarnished, yet uplifting lyrics to music that gives homage to great California bands\"","cite":"- Scott Marshall"},{"t":"p","html":"The track doubles as a sweeping portrait of California. With nods to the state’s vast landscapes, Marshall sings, “Sing: Sierra, Joshua … No matter where I roam, it’s my home, California home,” anchoring the song’s chorus in both pride and yearning."},{"t":"caption","html":"Images and artwork by Joe Tamel and George Kander."},{"t":"p","html":"\"California Home\" is out now on all streaming platforms."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>About LifeSize</strong>"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.lifesizemusic.net/","img":"","title":"LifeSize is the project of Los Angeles-based artist Scott, blending heartfelt songwriting with roots-rock energy. His music has earned praised by The Mercury News as “poignant” and “vastly appealing,” drawing comparisons to legends like Tom Petty, Mark Knopfler, and Bruce Springsteen. With a sound that’s both timeless and deeply personal, LifeSize continues to build momentum—new music is set to arrive in 2025.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"Scott Marshall, the artist behind LifeSize, came of age in Seattle during a cultural boom that shaped his creative foundation. Growing up between households after his parents’ divorce, he absorbed a wide spectrum of sounds, from The Beatles and Hendrix to Sonic Youth and Screaming Trees, influences that continue to inform his expansive pop-rock sound."},{"t":"p","html":"After relocating to California following years of travel, Marshall began releasing music under the name LifeSize with Grammy-winning producer Dave Darling. The three critically acclaimed albums he's released so far have earned national airplay on KCSN, KEXP, and The Krush, and won praise from critics for his blend of roots-rock storytelling and genre-crossing ambition. His breakout album, \"<a href=\"https://lifesizemusic.bandcamp.com/album/woolsey\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Woolsey</a>,\" doubled as a tribute to California and a fundraiser for wildfire recovery, with proceeds benefiting Direct Relief."},{"t":"p","html":"With a voice both intimate yet expansive, Marshall continues to craft music that's timeless and resonant. \"California Home,\" out now, is the fourth single leading up to his forthcoming album, \"LifeSize,\" due Oct. 17, 2025."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5fvymPLVzoCqOjewMOKFiD?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.lifesizemusic.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://lifesizemusic.bandcamp.com/track/black-car-2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bandcamp</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5fvymPLVzoCqOjewMOKFiD?si=ywIoPTS3Su-q77ptEm2yMg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/lifesize/385659171\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple&nbsp;</a>| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@lifesizearts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lifesizemusic4u/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/lifesizemusic4U\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"417767","title":"Hallie Marie Music ✸☽ A Denver-Based musician who blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling. She has a series of releases arriving in 2025, with her first titled \"Indebted\" arriving January 21.","date":"2025-09-09","lead":"A soul-searching rock journey through dissociation, depression and the quiet miracle of coming back to yourself","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/417767/991b2752e640b6c88a2cb177f86b8e69.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A soul-searching rock journey through dissociation, depression and the quiet miracle of coming back to yourself"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>WASHINGTON</strong>&nbsp;<strong>(September 9, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>- Today, singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qjqY0W9hRpqy_g6Ky9uPyw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a> releases <strong>“Blue In Her Head,\"</strong> a sweeping and introspective single that journeys through isolation, healing and the slow spiritual awakening that comes from learning to see the beauty in life again."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5ENbeOGmvJTmlokjxY94gX?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Written by Hallie and recorded in collaboration with regular creative partner&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/andreaslandeckmusic/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Andreas Landeck</strong></a> (<strong>The Keep Recording</strong>), \"Blue In Her Head\" opens in a quiet, contemplative space before evolving into a dynamic, multi-phase rock arrangement. As strings, layered vocals and dueling guitar solos build across the track’s arc, so does Hallie’s narrative, moving from emotional detachment and longing to a reclamation of self, hope and presence."},{"t":"quote","html":"“There is a spiritual aspect to it; first, I feel alone and depressed, then I start wondering what’s beyond, understanding there is beauty out there, even if my mind blocks me from enjoying it, and then I begin to close that gap. This is much like the spiritual path of 'waking up' to reality instead of staying stuck in one’s thoughts and delusions that take them away from the light.\"","cite":"- Hallie Marie"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771524/large-5fa574fc407eb6bce3dc16860bb907d9.jpg","alt":"\"Blue In Her Head\" Cover Art by Hallie Marie."},{"t":"p","html":"Built around poetic lyrics that read like a dialogue between self and soul, \"Blue In Her Head\" personifies both the world and the self as elusive strangers — mysterious figures we long to understand. Hallie describes herself and others as hungry ghosts (a Buddhist theme), wandering in search of connection, meaning, and a way back home."},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, the track evokes the expansive psychedelia of <strong>Pink Floyd</strong>, with instrumental builds that reflect the emotional journey itself. Backing vocals bloom in the second chorus, strings swell in the bridge, and the final section brings a cathartic guitar duet that feels like a release, a reckoning and a return."},{"t":"p","html":"\"It starts out a bit spacious and the lyrics are describing an empty feeling,\" said Hallie. \"Then as the story goes on, more instrumental parts are added to convey the movement of depression and dissociation into exasperation and passion, love and recognizing beauty.\""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lyrics Preview:</strong> Tell me what’s a girl to do with all this blue in her head? / Cause there’s beauty all around and it doesn’t make sense / But sometimes for a moment she sees it / Feeling sand beneath her feet / A secret never meant to keep, she knows."},{"t":"p","html":"Throughout the song, the lyrics trace a journey from fear of love and vulnerability toward a growing awareness of beauty, both in the world and within the self. They reflect a deep emotional shift, marking a spiritual turning point and an awakening to humans' innate interconnectivity."},{"t":"p","html":"Following the warm nostalgia of her most recent single release, <strong>\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4IfwEmntaVlwdMx4zhHAti?si=pb9rKWaTTNineZ1yJ429qQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">3:59</a>,\"</strong> <strong>\"Blue In Her Head\"</strong> finds Hallie diving ever deeper into emotional terrain, reflecting on depression, identity and the courage it takes to stay open to life’s beauty, even when the mind resists."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/-b10e31cd63b2c0317696d54d044a4e07.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-32 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/preview-c33bb4c8c0fb8d62a46ea644fb5ad2e1.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/-1302eb881563358853da571d1fb91c45.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-36 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/preview-e17e8b3fa61065cd5c4017c5cabd0e2d.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/large-3fd73d88583417c22d63d14ef4d100aa.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-14 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/preview-4811aaab4e4c9d4f52c8820f4714b20b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/large-29c12eef5ba54b62cc04f5bc34eee872.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-29 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/preview-24ede99c287103be1e22c17641577c77.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/-da81f45fe86805db981f72d86eff8965.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-46 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/preview-8f88dcb7cb4728eef25338442eb31f22.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/large-3740cb07a0046ee2a3bf82c6c328555f.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-44 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/preview-a44d9f029894f554f894eed711194762.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/large-69157f55a4afc3f0f8b64d0c7951e6c8.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-1 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/preview-88af250d089625bac98f9cf6e7350728.jpeg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hallie Marie:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a> is a multifaceted artist who beautifully balances light and shadow in her work. With an intellectually curious spirit, she dives deep into the complexities of human emotions, crafting music that resonates with listeners on many levels — from the highs of love and joy to the depths of melancholy. Drawing inspiration from artists like <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>, <strong>Billy Joel</strong>, and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, Hallie’s sound blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling."},{"t":"p","html":"Collaborating with the Denver-based band <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1UP2Zk7NI1U6KBhpPfPKBt?si=y0EiRbwmTCSlwg_-3sd3vg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Direville</a>, Hallie Marie has already begun to make her mark on the music industry with popular releases “<strong>Sympathy</strong>” and “<strong>Free Spirit</strong>”, among others. Now branching out on her own, her solo music endeavors combine poetic mystical imagery with direct and casual insight derived from raw life experience.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Embracing the beauty of authenticity and connecting with each of us at our core, Hallie invites her audience into her world, sharing not just her music but also her creative process — writing, arranging, and recording — along with the benefit of what she has learned through struggle and resilience. She aims to connect deeply with her listeners, sharing meaningful ideas that resonate long after the music ends."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hallie Marie!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/halliemariemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@halliemariemusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/","img":"","title":"Hallie Marie Music ✸☽ A Denver-Based musician who blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling. She has a series of releases arriving in 2025, with her first titled \"Indebted\" arriving January 21.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://instagram.com/halliemariemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qv9RFavvRmeHdVLljnpMBQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | &nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100068917929503\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"419660","title":"Lia Pappas-Kemps Shares New Single, “Reservations”","date":"2025-08-29","lead":"Dubbed “Toronto’s next breakout songwriter,” Lia captures the ache of ignoring warning signs in love","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/419660/b667c2d56111f419ee0026d37fb7aa89.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Dubbed “Toronto’s next breakout songwriter,” Lia captures the ache of ignoring warning signs in love"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/lOsml98szMY","height":""},{"t":"button","href":"https://lpk.lnk.to/reservations","label":"Listen to \"Reservations\" on all major platforms","color":"#554003"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>TORONTO</strong> (August 29, 2025) – Today, <strong>Lia Pappas-Kemps</strong> releases her new single, <strong>\"Reservations,\"</strong> a wistful rumination on relationships, longing and the willful blindness that comes with desire. Out now on all streaming platforms via <strong>Coalition Music Records</strong>, the track finds Pappas-Kemps vulnerably bridging the grit of ’90s alt-rock with the intimacy of contemporary indie folk."},{"t":"quote","html":"'Reservations' is about misconstruing warning signs and choosing to be blissfully ignorant in a relationship, rather than confronting it. I wrote it by myself in my apartment in Montreal and recorded most of it live off the floor with a group of some of my favourite musicians in Toronto.\"","cite":"- Lia Pappas-Kemps"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771283/large-8854e864a920b07cf73e45bcb33d56be.jpeg","alt":"\"Reservations\" Cover Art."},{"t":"p","html":"The recording of \"Reservations\" captures a live immediacy that keeps Lia’s voice and songwriting at its core. The track is anchored by her distinct vocal phrasing, creating a tremble that’s both intimate and arresting."},{"t":"p","html":"Lush yet restrained instrumentation from <strong>Dylan Burchell</strong> (guitar),<strong>&nbsp;Julian Psihogios</strong> (drums), <strong>Melissa Paju</strong> (bass), and Lia herself (guitar) underpins Pappas-Kemps’ spectral vocal delivery, where she stretches words into shimmering, aching turns of phrase. Her performance lends the song an otherworldly beauty, evoking influences ranging from <strong>Mitski</strong> and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong> to <strong>Alanis Morissette</strong> and <strong>Luna Li</strong>, while remaining distinctly her own."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/108yZd1xm9BwvtZBYP0v91?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The single continues Pappas-Kemps’ trajectory as one of Toronto’s most promising young songwriters with a growing reputation for atmospheric soundscapes and inventive guitar tunings. Her debut EP, <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/291dl72MoYUpT6uH9OCtB3?si=B_17SaejTLuOqmrL2Becbw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Gleam</strong></a><strong>,\"</strong> received praise from outlets including <a href=\"https://atwoodmagazine.com/lpkg-lia-pappas-kemps-gleam-ep-interview-music-feature/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Atwood Magazine</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://exclaim.ca/music/article/7-influences-that-help-give-lia-pappas-kemps-s-debut-ep-gleam-its-shine\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Exclaim</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://northerntransmissions.com/lia-pappas-kemps-debuts-catch-release/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Northern Transmissions</strong></a> and <a href=\"https://www.thestar.com/entertainment/music/shes-torontos-next-breakout-songwriter-lia-pappas-kemps-shining-debut-proves-why/article_71c1fab0-a049-11ef-a53e-ef213190bb63.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Toronto Star</strong></a>, which called her “Toronto’s next breakout songwriter.” Atwood described it as “a bold and brash introduction that aches with the weight of life lessons learned the hard way,” while <a href=\"https://completemusicupdate.com/approved-lia-pappas-kemps/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Complete Music Update</strong></a> noted she “blends alt-pop and alt-rock [on single 'Switchblade'], crafting a sound that could perfectly soundtrack a coming-of-age film.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Early singles such as \"Sad in Toronto\" and \"Object at Best\" showcased Lia's versatility, while her 2021 track <strong>\"Jinx\"</strong> has since surpassed <strong>4.4 million streams on Spotify</strong>. Also an actor, Lia made her professional debut in the 2014 short film \"The Deceased,\" and is best known for her role as Jane in <strong>Netflix’s \"Anne with an E.\"</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded in Taurus Studios and produced by Elia Pappas, engineered by Thomas D’Arcy, mixed by Howie Beck, and mastered by Kristian Montano, \"Reservations\" further solidifies Pappas-Kemps’ evolution as an artist tracing a compelling coming-of-age journey through song."},{"t":"caption","html":"(p) &amp; (c) 2025 Lia Pappas-Kemps, under exclusive license to Coalition Music Records&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7N15xabCPo5XjsUSTnGVes?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>About Lia Pappas-Kemps</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"For Lia Pappas-Kemps, expressing herself through art has always been second-nature. This is evident in the confident, natural presence the Toronto-born singer brings every time she steps on stage, stemming all the way back to the beginning of her career in music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"In 2021 and 2022, she launched her music career through a series of singles, including the grunge-inflected “Jinx” and the gorgeous, swooning ballads “Sad in Toronto” and “Object at Best\". In her emotionally unsparing, sensuous and critically acclaimed debut EP, \"Gleam,\" her intricate sound comes across, demonstrating influences from throwback alt-rock to ’70s troubadours to modern indie rock, but never truly resembling anyone but herself.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"As <a href=\"https://www.cbc.ca/arts/q/lia-pappas-kemps-perfectly-captures-teen-angst-on-her-debut-ep-1.7452349\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tom Power</a> said of the project, \"Lia Pappas-Kemps perfectly captures teen angst on her debut EP\". Back again with her latest release, \"Reservations,\" Pappas-Kemps continues to trace her progress while finding her songwriting voice. But nothing about her music is underdeveloped. Instead, every new track plots a crystalline moment in an engaging coming-of-age story—one that will feel compelling for anyone whose desire has felt as heavy as the weight of the world."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/DNbXScjO7B4/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/xHMktArdHgc","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/liapappaskemps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@lia.pappas.kemps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/liapappaskemps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://x.com/lia_pappaskemps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a> | <a href=\"https://www.liapappaskemps.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/ca/artist/lia-pappas-kemps/1539183503\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7N15xabCPo5XjsUSTnGVes?si=oNPHA7Z6S-uNiKQKhvSazw&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=65c93ff6d32c45fb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"415208","title":"Stephen Thomas Unveils The Universal Me: A Bold EP Spanning Love, Identity and Resilience","date":"2025-08-22","lead":"A fearless genre-bending journey that celebrates complexity and reinvention.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/415208/780c70dd031b92aca8c53bf191442794.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A fearless genre-bending journey that celebrates complexity and reinvention."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Nashville, TN</strong> (August 22, 2025) – Five-time Grammy-considered artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=j3WK1-UqRkuc7zz86MdrOw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>returns with his most ambitious project yet, <strong>The Universal Me</strong>, a 5-track EP that refuses to be confined to a single sound or story. Out now, the project blends R&amp;B, country, pop, hip-hop and alt-rock in a seamless exploration of love, heartbreak, resilience and self-discovery."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0ejRjauL0fasaqqjEmwha5?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This project is me saying out loud, ‘I’m not just one thing.’ I’m made of hip-hop, country, rock/punk, pop, R&amp;B, and real-life experience—and The Universal Me is the sound of all those layers finally being heard.\"","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Stephen Thomas"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"A Multifaceted Story in Five Tracks"},{"t":"p","html":"Hitting over 100K streams in its first 12 hours of release as a New Independent Artist, the EP showcases Thomas’s gift for crossing emotional and musical borders:"},{"t":"list","items":["<strong>“Breaking Hearts”</strong> — the breakout single — is a raw anthem for letting go of toxic ties, paired with a cinematic <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=op_ZEYZegos\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">music video</a> directed by <strong>Will Thomas.</strong>","<strong>“Strange Love”</strong> explores modern relationships, emotional walls, and the push-pull of connection, alongside a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O47jhGfNefE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">music video</a> directed by <strong>Will Thomas</strong>.&nbsp;","<strong>“Outstanding”</strong> (featuring <strong>DJ Unk</strong>) is an upbeat, R&amp;B-driven tribute to confidence and love, blending nostalgic energy of the classic R&amp;B soul record by <strong>The Gap Band</strong> with modern swagger.","<strong>“Feening For Love”</strong> captures the longing and frustration of navigating half-hearted relationships.","<strong>“Come Home to Me”</strong> marks Thomas’s foray into country, weaving Nashville storytelling with soulful R&amp;B undertones to deliver an emotional ode to resilience and love."]},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/764443/large-030ac8cc73961a1ef269a2673779f3cf.png","alt":"\"The Universal Me\" EP Cover Art by <xx>"},{"t":"p","html":"The Universal Me was born from Thomas’s determination to express every facet of who he is: as a creator, a person, and a survivor. “Every song on this EP is a reflection of something I’ve felt, survived, or dreamed of,” he said. “Whether it's pain, passion, or power, I let it out through hip-hop, R&amp;B, country, or even alt-rock energy. Music isn’t about fitting in — it’s about being free enough to tell your story, your way.”"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/O47jhGfNefE","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Fans of <strong>Chris Brown, Ed Sheeran, Jelly Roll, MGK, Morgan Wallen, and Blink-182</strong> will find something to love in this project’s blend of soulful melodies, raw lyrics, and genre-spanning production."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I didn’t create The Universal Me just to be heard—I created it to connect. Whether you’re drawn to the soul of R&amp;B, the grit of punk, or the storytelling of country, there’s something in this project that speaks to the real you.\"","cite":"- Stephen Thomas"},{"t":"p","html":"Fresh off the successful release of <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6MiuL2cjgcSGasS6ol0DT7?si=09d2f95059f3427c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Breaking Hearts</strong></a><strong>”</strong> and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=1fe51c64b3f9473e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stay Strong</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> Thomas continues to build on a career marked by viral moments, national media coverage and Top 60 placements on Active Rock Radio. His journey from Charleston, WV to a national audience has seen major collaborations, red carpet appearances at events like BET Live, and global recognition on MTV, Revolt TV, Vibe, Earmilk, and The Source (which named him an “Artist to Watch in 2025”)."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/op_ZEYZegos","height":""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Stephen Thomas:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=oHBViFwQQaaIjt97y8p4Og\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a> is an artist redefining genre boundaries and commanding attention across the music industry. Hailing from Charleston, West Virginia, and recently named an <strong>“Artist to Watch in 2025”</strong> by <strong><em>The Source</em></strong>, Stephen is a pioneering voice in what he calls the Universal genre—a blend of sonic influences that continues to evolve with his latest foray into rock and alternative music."},{"t":"p","html":"His transition into the rock space is already making waves. Stephen’s debut alternative record and music video for<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3cqqiH32fFqe2fHfBCXWWP?si=75a692df14ee45a6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>&nbsp;“Back Home”</strong></a>&nbsp; was featured on <strong>MTV</strong>, and the song continued to climb the <strong>Active Rock Radio charts into the Top 60</strong>. The single went viral on TikTok with <strong>over 500,000 views in just 24 hours</strong>, while both “Back Home” and his breakout anthem <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=783255a44a914f36\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Stay Strong”</strong></a>—a heartfelt tribute to military personnel, autoimmune warriors, and those facing mental health challenges—have been featured on <strong>major editorial playlists across Spotify, Amazon Music, Tidal, and more</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6MiuL2cjgcSGasS6ol0DT7?si=768e41a678e24270\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Breaking Hearts,”</strong></a> and now <strong>\"The Universal Me,\"</strong> build on this momentum, showcasing a raw, emotive sound that reflects his bold artistic reinvention. Comparisons to artists like <strong>MGK</strong>, <strong>Jelly Roll</strong>, <strong>Carrie Underwood</strong>, and <strong>Shaboozey&nbsp;</strong>speak to his wide-ranging appeal and boundary-pushing creativity."},{"t":"p","html":"As a national touring artist, Stephen’s resume includes <strong>five Grammy Award considerations</strong> as an independent act, a <strong>#2 spot on the iTunes Charts</strong> with <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5PGeydtICzokuReD9TOiHW?si=4278bc4bba8f4826\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Best Days,”</strong></a> and global exposure through Revolt TV with his video for <strong>“Search Me.”</strong> &nbsp;From his early beginnings to signing with <strong>SkeeloMusik/Sony RED</strong> in 2013 and later finding his artistic home with <strong>Creative Hearts Entertainment</strong>, Stephen’s journey has been one of constant growth and reinvention."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond the music, Stephen’s story and sound have been spotlighted in MTV, Vibe Magazine, Swagger, Hype Magazine, Earmilk, V13, and The Source, among others. He’s performed alongside iconic names and walked red carpets at major events including the BET Live Experience."},{"t":"p","html":"Ten years into his career, Stephen continues to follow the advice that shaped his path: stay true to yourself. It’s a message that drives his music and fuels his mission to inspire the next generation of artists."},{"t":"p","html":"All of Stephen’s latest releases—including “The Universal Me\"—are available on Spotify, Apple Music, Amazon Music, Tidal, and all major platforms. For updates, videos, and exclusive content, visit the links below."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephen!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.stephentmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/StephenTMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/404?fromUrl=/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/StephenThomas1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://x.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>X</strong></a>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/Cv0cZdtuXQn/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"419646","title":"Waterplanet Finds Strength in Unity on New Single “Under, Over”","date":"2025-08-19","lead":"A spirited indie-rock anthem inspired by nature, resilience and collective purpose","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/419646/5e2b3ddb79bcb62800979ca4e51454b1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A spirited indie-rock anthem inspired by nature, resilience and collective purpose"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>BALTIMORE, MD</strong> (September 5, 2025) – Today, Baltimore poppy art-rock and psych-folk duo <strong>Waterplanet</strong> releases <strong>\"Under, Over,\"</strong> a soaring new single about perseverance and belonging. The track blends the band’s playfully introspective songwriting with driving melodies, harmonies, and a touch of psych-folk mysticism."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/track=3171921811/size=large/bgcol=ffffff/linkcol=0687f5/tracklist=false/artwork=small/transparent=true/","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Written by vocalist and multi-instrumentalist <strong>Millie Landrum</strong>, \"Under, Over\" explores how reconnecting with nature and one another can help transform despair into collective hope. “I hope 'Under, Over' inspires people,” said Landrum. “We’re living through pretty dark and divisive times, so I’d love to make someone feel better or help them change the channel to feel a bit happier. It’s a song about reconnecting to nature, to others, whatever helps re-center you.”"},{"t":"p","html":"The track’s lyrics grew from an experience Landrum had lying on the grass at <strong>Glastonbury Abbey</strong>, a place many believe to be an energetic center of the earth. That mystical sense of grounding runs throughout \"Under, Over,\" including in the lyrics, like “A million strong, a million high, a million voices fill the sky.”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771274/large-470f6e18d64235aa5b13a6c9663796af.png","alt":"\"Under, Over\" cover art by James Hesser."},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Ryan Gallagher</strong> and <strong>Waterplanet</strong> at <strong>Plaid Dog Recording</strong>, the single sits comfortably between the sunny harmonics of \"California Dreamin’\" and the raw edge of <strong>The Breeders</strong>. It marks the first release from Waterplanet’s forthcoming EP, due out October 2025."},{"t":"p","html":"Formed by <strong>Millie Landrum</strong> and <strong>James Hesser</strong>, Waterplanet has become known for its genre-blurring blend of pop, rock and psych-folk. Veterans of the Baltimore music scene, the duo has toured the Mid-Atlantic, Midwest and Southeast, sharing stages with a variety of artists while steadily building a reputation for songs that are haunting yet strangely familiar."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771275/large-5b4c8f4750db6b0f350dc3819c138beb.jpg","alt":"Waterplanet_2024-118.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771275/preview-f3faf806805dee8088b2b5fe41016a31.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771276/large-8e0216c4ff36592d3c5ebeca525bce3a.jpg","alt":"Waterplanet_2024-85.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771276/preview-95315e33d85c644f16964464e77dc07b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771277/large-4c22f01b4d1ee6a48fc0084f3b19ca1f.jpg","alt":"Waterplanet_2024-125.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/771277/preview-be3d2e189184589f89687391f38b91b7.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Greg Dohler."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>About Waterplanet</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Waterplanet is the project of Baltimore-based songwriters and multi-instrumentalists Millie Landrum and James Hesser. With driving melodies and intertwining harmonies, the pair alternate vocals, acoustic guitar, percussion, and other instruments to create music that blurs the lines between pop, rock and psych-folk. Known for their playful yet introspective style, Waterplanet has toured throughout the Mid-Atlantic, Midwest and Southeast. Their new EP is set for release in October 2025."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/waterplanetband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/waterplanetband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@WATERPLANETband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://waterplanet.bandcamp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bandcamp</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"414649","title":"Lora Kelley Releases New Single, “Man Behind the Curtain”","date":"2025-08-15","lead":"A Folk-Laden Reckoning with Illusion, Loss and Finding Home","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/414649/652507155efe3d7c88c95bb0138c352a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A Folk-Laden Reckoning with Illusion, Loss and Finding Home"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>North Garden, VA (August 15, 2025)</strong> — Blending unflinching vulnerability with Americana warmth, multidisciplinary artist and trauma-informed story work coach <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lora_kelley/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lora Kelley</strong></a> releases <strong>“Man Behind the Curtain”&nbsp;</strong>today, a song that peels back the myths we create about others and ourselves, to find truth and belonging."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6AjuEHWcmNg4D2jwTQ6Ojc?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"With “Man Behind the Curtain,” &nbsp;Lora invites listeners to walk a yellow-bricked path of grief, awakening and self-reclamation. The second single from her forthcoming album, the track distills her signature narrative voice, both tender and incisive, into a reflection on what happens when the stories we believe about someone unravel."},{"t":"p","html":"“There is a moment that comes for many of us,” she shares, “when you realize that who you thought a person was—and who they actually are—are not the same. It’s a disorienting grief. Who were you? Who was I? What do I do with what I thought I knew? What is left when I'm forced to face this reality?”"},{"t":"p","html":"Written in a single evening in the dead of winter, while a fire burned in the hearth, the song emerged as Kelley and her husband wrangled their three children at bedtime."},{"t":"p","html":"\"I called out to my husband: I have a song. I need to write it! He went about helping everyone get to their beds, teeth-brush, pajamas on, and all the things, and when they were done, I played it for him, and he said: This feels like you,\" said Lora."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763845/large-415d03aaad92646c53a48992327bda0b.png","alt":"Cover art for “Man Behind the Curtain.\" Image by Amy Cherry."},{"t":"p","html":"“Man Behind the Curtain” draws imagery from <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong>, evoking Dorothy’s realization that the powerful figure she sought for help was only smoke and shadow."},{"t":"p","html":"\"As I imagined Dorothy at the end of the Wizard of Oz,\" Lora shared, \"I thought - what does it feel like to wake up to having been sold (by the wizard and then from everyone else) that The Wizard was powerful, only to realize he wasn't who he said he was, and he wasn't who anyone said he was. His posture was one of exploitation, a structure of power, an idea and a fabrication. In fact, nothing that was offered by him to Oz or to her about him was true, real or helpful. Now what?\""},{"t":"p","html":"At its core, “Man Behind the Curtain” is a meditation on the fragility of trust and the courage it takes to reclaim one’s voice and homecoming. The lyrics weave a narrative of awakening:&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>What do I do with the friends that I’ve gained / This courage that I found, along with my heart and my brain / At the end of this yellow road will I have to leave them all behind? / Just to keep the man behind the curtain satisfied&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763792/large-040f26b07bc098f11a7be56c6ece467b.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-184.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763792/preview-bab801da600ba3701e09b5694e332bda.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763793/large-c253415328dd45d2f573e8555a00a593.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-48-2 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763793/preview-522091d282fcea1e14ae15584aa1bb21.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763791/large-44c5d725f595bf2ee8055e95fc686744.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-174.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/763791/preview-892a437483001f7ba30f224eaaf03cbb.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by Amy Cherry"},{"t":"p","html":"The single leans into earthy acoustic textures and understated yet stirring instrumentation, echoing the melodic sensibilities of artists like <strong>Nanci Griffith&nbsp;</strong>and<strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Natalie Merchant</strong>. Produced by Jeremy Casella, the track features a stellar lineup: Matt Stanfield (piano), Josh Hunt (drums), Jacob Lowery (bass), Nate Duggar (guitar) and Mike Payne (guitar), with Evan Redwine engineering."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Much of my work involves walking with survivors of trauma—people untangling harm that was caused by those who were meant to protect them. That’s the core grief this song sits with: what happens when your source of safety, or love, is also your greatest source of pain? How do you grieve what you never fully had? How do you find home again, within yourself?\"","cite":"Lora Kelley"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lora Kelley"},{"t":"p","html":"Rooted in the themes of resilience and gentle honesty, Lora's work is deeply informed by her background in narrative-based trauma care, including her studies with the Allender Center. Her music stands as a testament to the beauty of brokenness, offering not platitudes, but presence — a hand to hold in the dark. Raised amid the liminality of faith and living today on a conserved farm in Virginia with her partner, children, and a lively menagerie of pets, Lora crafts songs that feel lived-in, earthy, and unflinchingly honest. Her upcoming album, releasing November 7, will continue to explore the emotional terrains where suffering and hope coexist — a body of work poised to resonate with those yearning for deeper connection and sacred honesty."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6WXETjjadXjtTGA0k5IfM4?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lora Kelley:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.lorakelley.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lora_kelley/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/thelorakelley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/lorakelley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Patreon</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"412763","title":"Kim Edwards Channels Dust Bowl Grit and Longing in Sweeping New Story Song, “Steinbeck”","date":"2025-08-08","lead":"A vivid folk vignette full of heartbreak, grit and quiet hope, “Steinbeck” captures a fictional life shaped by hard choices and changing seasons.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/412763/2c77627b379bedb45c31f971cc6ece68.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A vivid folk vignette full of heartbreak, grit and quiet hope, “Steinbeck” captures a fictional life shaped by hard choices and changing seasons."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lehigh Valley</strong><strong>​</strong><strong>, PA (August 8, 2025)</strong> – With flugelhorns, sweeping strings and imagery straight out of a lost diary from the 1930s, singer-songwriter Kim Edwards releases “Steinbeck” today."},{"t":"p","html":"The new single paints a fictional portrait of one man’s journey through grief, love and the aching pursuit of a place to call home. The track leans into Edwards’ orchestral-folk sensibilities and narrative instincts, unfolding like a weathered novel passed down through generations."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/05Rx45FVbkIt5ISg7G85hG?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Loosely inspired by John Steinbeck’s \"The Grapes of Wrath,\" the track began with a seed of literary influence but quickly evolved into its own emotionally distinct narrative. It became a vignette of its own, representing a fictional character navigating the seasons of his life with grief, grit and growth."},{"t":"p","html":"\"There's nothing autobiographical in it, other than the common experiences we all share of transitioning from one life season to the next,\" Kim said. \"Sometimes they are transitions that have been thrust upon us, sometimes they are transitions birthed through growth, sometimes they are joyous, sometimes they are bittersweet,\" she continued."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/761381/large-4d4aa16e23950ac91fce30df50dc5a4c.jpg","alt":"\"Steinbeck\" cover art. Photography by Bruce Kite. Design by Victoria Strout."},{"t":"p","html":"Lyrically, the song is one of Edwards’ longest to date, chronicling a young man forced off his family land by the Dust Bowl who rides trains west, falls in love, and eventually returns to his roots, older and weathered but not without hope. The character’s voice carries each verse through grieving, leaving, loving, as the refrain echoes through the years."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lyrics preview: </strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"And he said, \"O my home, I'm leavin', leavin', leavin'\" / And he said, \"O my heart is grievin', grievin', grievin'\" / He gathered up all he owned / Headed west to the unknown"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748285/large-0b6197a6f051d62c8146b0bba7cbf73b.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0289.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748285/preview-bcd098cac55d2a0eb6f774e77a787a71.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748286/large-d7e1d9dc0fd77a1a60c2c144303c6c37.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0328.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748286/preview-3696cb8baf68ee148f0bfb241a64e885.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748284/large-b0ad8163393c6c2cbf500be49e658174.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0039.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748284/preview-70ba0c00623cb7165aa7d51893e21f33.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748288/large-a2e3c15bbc6e0af1049c6ab7a9aa63e0.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0052.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748288/preview-fc8ceb005772fc5462b875ad5550c920.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748287/large-934438af0366adc974540cf1dc309eca.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0398.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748287/preview-bf975564845cca27474a595e1bf8868b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748283/large-44156cfbc2050f9407a34bd86f00a033.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0135.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748283/preview-467a9947650ae95dcbcec1d19c1a40e7.jpeg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, “Steinbeck” blends the grounded storytelling of <strong>The Lumineers</strong> with the cinematic scope of <strong>Mumford &amp; Sons</strong>. Co-produced with longtime collaborator <strong>Jared Salte</strong> (Salt Shaker Studios), the arrangement features strings by <strong>Rob Szabo</strong> and a stunning horn section (flugelhorn and trumpet by<strong>&nbsp;Fletch Wiley</strong> and trombone by <strong>Phil Miller</strong>) that gives the instrumental bridge its emotional lift."},{"t":"p","html":"\"What I love about Jared is his knack for understanding the vision from my demo or notes and his incredible ability to deliver above and beyond,\" said Kim. \"He added the horn arrangement in the instrumental bridge, which gave the track an epic lift and helped to progress the story in a way that I had never imagined, but really love!\""},{"t":"p","html":"“Steinbeck” marks a striking moment in the reveal of Edwards’ upcoming full-length album, <strong>Vignettes</strong>, a collection of reflective, cinematic songs that blend memory and imagination. While many of Edwards’ tracks are drawn from personal experience, “Steinbeck” shows another side of her artistry, that of a storyteller capable of inhabiting other lives and sketching whole worlds in song."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4PCJGcs6ZoUsKBG1OSbyh6?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kim Edwards:"},{"t":"p","html":"With a voice as intimate as a journal entry and melodies that echo like memory, <strong>Kim Edwards</strong> crafts cinematic, emotionally rich songs that feel both timeless and deeply personal. A Lehigh Valley, PA-based singer-songwriter with roots in classical piano and a love for storytelling-driven pop, Edwards writes vignettes—poetic snapshots of longing, love, and quiet resilience."},{"t":"p","html":"Over the years, Edwards has developed a signature sound: moody, melancholic, and lush with introspective nuance. Inspired by the likes of <strong>Ingrid Michaelson</strong>, <strong>Regina Spektor</strong>, and <strong>Sleeping At Last</strong>, she blends lyrical vulnerability with orchestral textures often drawing comparisons to her influences while carving out a sonic world uniquely her own. Her songs have found homes in branded content for <strong>Chaco Shoes</strong>, <strong>Paraxel</strong>, and <strong>Disney Weddings</strong>, and her cover of “Auld Lang Syne” garnered over 150K Spotify streams after landing a spot on the platform’s Folksy Christmas playlist. In 2013, she was selected from hundreds of applicants for ASCAP’s prestigious <strong>Jerry Ragovoy Songwriters Workshop </strong>in NYC, has performed twice at <strong>Musikfest</strong> in Bethlehem, PA, and in storied venues like <strong>The Bitter End, Eddie’s Attic, </strong>and <strong>Bluebird Cafe</strong>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/dJeQnuBRcw8","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Among her most meaningful career moments, Kim had the rare honor of <strong>opening for</strong> <strong>The Beach Boys</strong>—a lifelong dream realized for the devoted fan—and also shared a stage with <strong>Jars of Clay</strong> at a local festival. These highlights underscore her steady dedication to her craft and the quiet authenticity that resonates through her music."},{"t":"p","html":"Edwards is embracing music on her own terms. Her forthcoming album, <strong><em>Vignettes</em></strong>, is the most personal and fully realized project of her career. Co-produced by <strong>Jared Salte</strong>, the album serves as a dream fulfilled: “Each song has its own special place in my heart,” she says. “There’s not a single filler.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Now a mother and entering into a reflective new chapter, Kim Edwards stands as a reminder that in a world obsessed with virality and speed, artistry rooted in depth, patience, and honesty endures. Her music offers a quiet refuge for the reflective listener—those seeking comfort, catharsis, or simply the feeling of being seen."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.kimedwardsmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://instagram.com/kimedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://facebook.com/kedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://x.com/kimedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a> | <a href=\"https://youtube.com/kimedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"415619","title":"Riah Premieres Sultry, Neon-Lit Music Video for “Skin on Chrome”","date":"2025-08-08","lead":"A Dark-Pop Celebration of Desire, Power, and Sensuality, Featuring Alissa Ann","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/415619/fc193beafae922366a19c2ff2c696cb4.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A Dark-Pop Celebration of Desire, Power, and Sensuality, Featuring Alissa Ann"},{"t":"p","html":"DENVER, CO (August 8, 2025) – Dark-pop artist <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/riahmusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Riah</strong></a> turns up the heat with the official music video for “Skin on Chrome,” the latest single from her forthcoming album, <strong>The Fourth Wall</strong>. Featuring fellow pole dancer and Singer-Songwriter<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/thealissaann/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Alissa Ann</strong></a>, the video is an unapologetic celebration of feminine power, sensuality and the thrill of being seen."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/w5OIQbe5WL0","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"A synth-laced fusion of dark pop and sultry R&amp;B, the track captures a late-night moment of temptation, where neon lights blur the lines between desire and identity. With lyrics that flirt with danger and vulnerability, the track captures the tension between who we are and who we want to be under the lights."},{"t":"p","html":"Directed by <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/cineking04/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ed Kelly (Cinema King)</strong></a>, the video takes viewers into a shadowy, intimate space, with smooth sequences of floor and chair work and deliberate, controlled yet playful pole dancing. The chemistry between Riah and Alissa Ann pulses through the screen, embodying the track’s seductive hook: <em>Just a little wrong, feel a little wrong—skin on chrome.</em>"},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Skin on Chrome’ is about that delicious tension between desire and danger—the moment you lean into being watched, and maybe even like it.","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Riah"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/764990/large-12ab1844442503262e2ab39efd146b63.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Skin on Chrome.\" Image by Martha Wirth, design by Alissa Ann. "},{"t":"p","html":"“We wanted this song to feel like slipping into a version of yourself that only exists under neon lights—bold, unapologetic, a little wrong in the best way,” Riah said. “There’s something powerful in reclaiming the gaze. We’ve often danced for others—but this track is about dancing for us.”"},{"t":"p","html":"“Skin on Chrome” is composed by <strong>Austin Weller</strong>, with mixing and mastering by <strong>Quoc Truong</strong>. It continues Riah’s evolution into a dark-pop soundscape reminiscent of <strong>The Weeknd</strong>, <strong>Two Feet</strong>, <strong>FKA Twigs</strong> and <strong>Rihanna</strong>, while remaining deeply personal and rooted in her own experiences. Drawing on her background as a sex worker and performer, Riah infuses the track with vulnerability, reckless abandon, and a defiant, self-owned sensuality."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746837/large-560fe1b59f9fc41150ff00ca8f6ab8bb.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13742.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746837/preview-2b9c6cb084c4ce7dec5bad6a46f81e10.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746836/large-e77d8204f3ebbc7f5475bf372618966a.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13517.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746836/preview-489222ae1b9a2979761050ee9542b053.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746838/large-d005a4bebcff998d871013dcbd46f192.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13626.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746838/preview-d60c26362d10cbeed6ac1ac9b2c96e68.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746839/large-818b693b5f528c1567b7ff8456df0e23.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13650.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746839/preview-ef8caef77bebafb022593cf688b86097.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746840/large-cc99a6346f11e2c492558b973a346076.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13583.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746840/preview-445d73ecd8393f973aaffd9ffee1d23c.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Martha Wirth"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Production Credits:</strong> Riah (Artist and Songwriter), Alissa Ann (Artist and Songwriter), Austin Weller (Composer), Quoc Truong (Mixing, Mastering); Ed Kelly AKA Cinema King (Videographer/Photographer)."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Working with Alissa Ann on this track brought an extra layer of raw feminine energy—she embodies exactly what this song is about: power, presence, and play.”","cite":"- Riah"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1TG0lfH8zKy8HOkPaxFLtb?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Riah:"},{"t":"p","html":"Riah, a rising force in the Bedroom Pop scene, is crafting introspective and evocative music that resonates with the complexities of love, sex, loss, and a distinctive \"villain energy.\" Drawing from personal life experiences, Riah channels deep emotion into every lyric and melody, creating an intimate connection with listeners.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Starting in the Los Angeles entertainment industry at the tender age of 17, Riah faced the harsh realities of the pre-Me Too era, which fueled her desire for autonomy and control over her artistic vision. After years of enduring the industry's darker side, she stepped back, determined to return to music only on her own terms. Now, as an accomplished entrepreneur, Riah has reclaimed her voice and is ready to make waves with a fresh and authentic sound."},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to her musical journey, Riah has captivated audiences at numerous festivals, clubs, and acoustic venues. Her passion for performance extends beyond music, as she is also a competitive pole dancer, having won the prestigious PSO Mountain competition in 2023.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a unique blend of vulnerability and power, Riah is poised to leave a lasting impact on the music world, bringing a new level of depth and intensity to the Bedroom Pop genre."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/xz1El91BAmg?si=dopvTyoauzWBBuM_","height":"315"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Riah:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4W98Etru2ErpE95smqDdfh?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/riahmusic1991\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/riahmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@Riah-Music-1991\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"408395","title":"INDVGO Unveils Lush, Haunting Music Video for “How Is It Love”","date":"2025-08-06","lead":"A Soulful Reflection on Healing, Inner-Strength and the Contradictions of Modern Love","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/408395/113b59f007a79a0a390d04bc30728024.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A Soulful Reflection on Healing, Inner-Strength and the Contradictions of Modern Love"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Brooklyn, NY (August 5, 2025)</strong> – Following the success of her introspective single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2qAY1Ju7Wer3mWaETcZwjY?go=1&amp;sp_cid=cf2574d8c3c2ab88c5653d52eabc4308&amp;utm_source=embed_player_p&amp;utm_medium=desktop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>How Is It Love</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> emerging R&amp;B artist <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/indvgo/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INDVGO</strong></a> returns with a powerful visual counterpart that deepens the emotional world of the track. Directed by <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/kojifilms/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Koji</strong></a>, the music video is a glamorous, slow-burning meditation on vulnerability, emotional resilience, inner peace, and the disorienting contradictions that define modern love."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/JiJFKnX1LJo","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Filmed across a series of intimate vignettes, the video opens with INDVGO alone, draped in shadow and soft spotlight. She’s grounded, luminous and holding heavy emotions -- not shown through grand gestures, but through glances, postures and presence."},{"t":"p","html":"As she moves through sun-drenched rooms filled with florals, books, and candlelight, the visuals lean into warmth, but never abandon their melancholy. Reflections in glass, silhouetted shadows, and recurring water imagery, including moments of body submersion, anchor the video in its core themes of emotional contradiction, self-reflection, and the slow work of healing. There’s softness here, but it’s hard-won."},{"t":"p","html":"From long shots in solitude to intimate close-ups that feel almost confrontational, INDVGO doesn’t perform pain so much as sit with it, letting it wash over and through her."},{"t":"quote","html":"‘How Is It Love’ is really about emotional chaos and finding peace within yourself. Healing starts when you fall deeply in love with your own soul.”","cite":"- INDVGO"},{"t":"p","html":"With dreamy lighting, soft shadows and blurred motion, the video moves with a poetic stillness, allowing space for grief, beauty and quiet contemplation. As INDVGO drifts between scenes of solitude and self-reflection, she tells a story of someone reclaiming power after emotional chaos."},{"t":"p","html":"At the 2-minute mark, the mood shifts and the softness gives way to something deeper with a beat drop. The scene transitions to the city streets at night, signaling her emergence into fully embodied self-acceptance. INDVGO is seen walking through a rain-slicked cityscape, the lighting fractured, her reflection blurred in car windows and wet pavement. It’s a pivotal turn: she’s no longer just reflecting, she’s moving forward. Still aching, but in motion."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/754252/large-26dd4d741bf0cce0cd447b03b8b8b3ea.png","alt":"Music Video Cover Photo.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/754252/preview-091ecf1d1eb3d214508e662597445c21.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/754249/large-da0b4b173d2a7ac85ea0cf27edc39897.jpg","alt":"Artwork 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/754249/preview-f8729fdad8136b64bd258b7047755be6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/754251/large-963b3410011b61098b22f5ee675397aa.jpg","alt":"Artwork 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/754251/preview-761c14631c0fedece337b04cde3dba6e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/754250/large-53420ae69e7fc83aa8d9fef6924dba38.png","alt":"Lyric Video Cover Photo.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/754250/preview-c7cd7be7400addcef1ff2a59f2e2a1b4.png"}]},{"t":"p","html":"The video deepens the emotional resonance of the song, which has drawn comparisons to <strong>Jhené Aiko</strong>, <strong>Summer Walker</strong>, and <strong>Kehlani</strong>, with a hint of <strong>Masego</strong>’s flair. The song’s moody, atmospheric instrumentation invites reflection, while INDVGO’s vocals are rich with longing, her lyrics brutally honest:"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“You the one, couldn’t fight that / So in love, it’s a mind trap / I’m gone, then I’m right back\"</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"The visual narrative captures this tension: beauty and melancholy, light and shadow, and showcases INDVGO's skills as a fully formed visual storyteller."},{"t":"p","html":"Overall, the song acknowledges love as both a source of strength and vulnerability, addressing its contradictions from emotional hurt to healing, self-discovery, and ultimately, peace. It's a celebration of inner strength and self-acceptance, offering a reflection on what it means to love and heal."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/61Se7XU0y8Gi4T64t1nfMA?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About INDVGO:"},{"t":"p","html":"INDVGO blends soulful melodies with elements of hip-hop, R&amp;B, and alternative influences to create a sound all her own. Her smooth, sensual vocals and nostalgic melodies are a reflection of life’s full spectrum – from love and luck to heartbreak and hardship. INDVGO’s artistry is deeply rooted in the pulse of New York City, capturing both its raw energy and intimate vibes. Her music explores themes of emotional depth, self-discovery, and empowerment, inviting listeners to connect through their own stories of resilience and growth.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://beacons.ai/indvgo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/indvgo/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@indvgomusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"411077","title":"Fulton Calvery Drops “Kissable,” a Hook-Heavy Pop Track You’ll Want on Repeat","date":"2025-07-25","lead":"New single “Kissable” showcases Fulton Calvery’s playful edge and pop sensibility blending playful swagger with modern rock edge","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/411077/3966d515e207fd78698a26e27b6f6995.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"New single “Kissable” showcases Fulton Calvery’s playful edge and pop sensibility blending playful swagger with modern rock edge"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Wichita, KS (July 25, 2025)</strong> - Rising genre-bending artist <strong>Fulton Calvery</strong>&nbsp;released his infectious new single, <strong>“Kissable,”</strong> on Friday, July 25, 2025. A hook-driven anthem that dances between flirtation and rock ‘n’ roll swagger, “Kissable” is a playful, magnetic ode to that one person who’s simply impossible to resist.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7oqxNqfRXur5gKt4EqjGml?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Driven by sultry vocals, gritty guitar lines, and tongue-in-cheek charm, the track captures the electric energy of falling hard and fast. With a sound that echoes the pop brilliance of Taylor Swift and Olivia Rodrigo, laced with a subtle Mick Jagger-style edge, Calvery brings a fresh, cinematic flair to the pop landscape. As the chorus rings out with the lyrics <em>“Why you got to be so kissable? Makes me lose all my principles”,&nbsp;</em>Calvery's strength as a singer-songwriter amidst his confident genre-blending musical style is on full display."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song initially started as an assignment for a lyric writing class at Berklee College of Music, and I actually got an A on it...I wanted to put together a track that was as fun to listen to as it is to dance to. The best feedback I’ve been getting? People keep asking me to play it again.”","cite":"Fulton Calvery on writing \"Kissable\""},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/758364/large-db135e891b1e92e4eaedd4d9ab6d673e.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Kissable\" by Fulton Calvery"},{"t":"p","html":"With its bold hooks and undeniable groove, “Kissable” makes the perfect soundtrack for late-night drives, dance floors, and anyone caught in the thrill of new attraction. \"Kissable\" was mixed and mastered by Carter Green, with drumming by Troy Schuster. &nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Fulton Calvery:"},{"t":"p","html":"Fulton Calvery is a rock artist from Wichita, Kansas, blending classic rock vibes with a modern twist. His music is raw, honest, and built around guitar-heavy hooks, powerful lyrics, and a style that’s all his own. With songs like “Premonition” and “Kissable,” he brings emotion and attitude together in a way that’s both relatable and unforgettable."},{"t":"p","html":"Music has always been part of Fulton’s DNA. He grew up just a block and a half from a nightclub where local bands played regularly—and he and his younger brother would eagerly help the musicians set up and tear down, often scoring impromptu lessons and advice from the pros. At 14, Fulton and his friends won their high school talent show in the group category, and by 16 he was playing professionally in bands. He’d bring his gig clothes to school, then hop on the band bus right out front—sometimes skipping the last class or two to hit the road."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/759388/compressed_original-6bdceca20ce78e6b5ddec579a72de6e2.jpeg","alt":"prod_track-files_1245225_extra_pictures_Fulton-Calvery_1.jpeg"},{"t":"p","html":"At 29, he won a guitar contest with a grand prize that sent him to meet Van Halen and receive a signed guitar. And in 2018, Fulton was inducted into the Kansas Music Hall of Fame as a member of the hard rock band Submytion, a group known for its energy, musicianship, and deep roots in the Midwest rock scene. More than just a musician, Fulton is a creative storyteller. Whether through lyrics, performance, or animated music videos, he pulls people into his world with emotion, humor, and grit. He’s not just making songs—he’s building experiences, one hook, one lyric, and one visual at a time."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Fulton Calvery:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://fultoncalvery.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/FultonCalveryMusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/fultoncalvery/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@fultoncalvery\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@FultonCalvery\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0C3RFIWke28QgAQOJJh1nw?utm_source=generator","height":"352"}],"contact":null},{"id":"401903","title":"New Pop Single “Strange Love” Explores the Emotional Fallout of Modern Romance","date":"2025-07-08","lead":"Stephen Thomas dives into the pop music scene with “Strange Love,” a genre-blending anthem for love without labels.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/401903/c076a7eb20cbcb76fd4e950bcd4dba4d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Stephen Thomas dives into the pop music scene with “Strange Love,” a genre-blending anthem for love without labels."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/O47jhGfNefE","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (June 8, 2025) - Pioneer of the \"Universal\" genre, artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=YTInGlyeR_Oow3q_1Wlt9g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen</strong> <strong>Thomas</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>unveils a bold and emotionally raw new single, <strong>“Strange Love,”&nbsp;</strong>a track that captures the bittersweet complexities of today’s relationship culture. Crossing over into the pop genre while blending elements of alternative R&amp;B, and dance, “Strange Love” - &nbsp;from his upcoming EP, <em>The Universal Me&nbsp;</em>- is as infectious as it is reflective—delving into the messy in-between spaces of hookups, blurred boundaries, and half-hearted commitments.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1pPyphk1nMc2IzmZr8bONC?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"With a sound that calls to mind the emotional resonance of <strong>Ed Sheeran</strong>, the rhythmic edge of <strong>Zedd</strong>, and the vocal stylings of J<strong>ustin Bieber</strong> and <strong>Chris Brown</strong>, the track weaves sharp lyricism and melodic vulnerability into a compelling sonic experience. <em>“This song carries a universal sound and a raw, emotional delivery,”</em> says Stephen. <em>“Lyrically, it explores the way we sometimes use others to move on from an ex to the next—even when we’re not truly ready. But in the process of making what feels like a mistake, we sometimes find something real. Because sometimes, the people we meet in our brokenness are the very ones who help us heal.”</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/744641/large-86b5cf49498c0a0bdda82513567c98a1.png","alt":"Cover art for \"Strange Love\" by Stephen Thomas"},{"t":"p","html":"The result is a song that cuts deep into the disillusionment of modern romance—where emotional availability is often optional, and connection is fleeting. Through lines like <em>“No risk, no sacrifice,”</em> the song challenges listeners to confront how they navigate intimacy, love, and the spaces in between. <em>“Love isn’t something you can construct with logic,”</em> Stephen adds. <em>“It’s strange, dangerous—an emotional rollercoaster where the unexpected can happen at any moment. But in its chaos, love isn’t just strange... it can be incredibly beautiful all at once.”</em>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“\"Strange Love\" is a song that many of my peers, including myself, have lived. It’s what exists in today's society. It’s the new love language—a lifestyle people call love, but it’s really just a strange kind of love. We live it daily.”","cite":"Stephen Thomas"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/745682/-9f4cf02301229ee0384e59715f42260c.jpg","alt":"Feb_13_2025_10_37_42_1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/745682/preview-1a1c835fafd2c5f4c6ef6e32ffc8066e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746000/-b35b08885c020f97743a916ce6367b09.jpg","alt":"IMG_20250213_113639_462.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746000/preview-84af4f234e7a285429347dece9beb0ec.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/745684/large-39f11e6a66b8433dd29194ff261b4cf0.jpg","alt":"Photo Feb 12 2025, 7 27 58 PM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/745684/preview-d1a8a4ac353d7c9aae727623b1c41cfb.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Behind the scenes of \"Strange Love\" music video"},{"t":"p","html":"Recently named as an \"<strong>Artist To Watch in 2025\"</strong> by <strong><em>The Source</em></strong>, Stephen's versatility is on full display as this five-time Grammy-considered artist continues to carve out his space in the industry with fearless creativity and personal storytelling."},{"t":"button","href":"https://symphony.to/stephen-thomas/strange-love","label":"PRE-SAVE \"Strange Love\"","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Stephen Thomas:"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676846/large-55a595b43551877ff75bb9984341f332.jpg","alt":"Photo by Josh Hanna"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=oHBViFwQQaaIjt97y8p4Og\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a> is an artist redefining genre boundaries and commanding attention across the music industry. Hailing from Charleston, West Virginia, and recently named an <strong>“Artist to Watch in 2025”</strong> by <strong><em>The Source</em></strong>, Stephen is a pioneering voice in what he calls the Universal genre—a blend of sonic influences that continues to evolve with his latest foray into rock and alternative music."},{"t":"p","html":"His transition into the rock space is already making waves. Stephen’s debut alternative record,<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3cqqiH32fFqe2fHfBCXWWP?si=75a692df14ee45a6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>&nbsp;“Back Home,”</strong></a>&nbsp; as the video was featured on <strong>MTV</strong>, and the song is continuing to climb the <strong>Active Rock Radio charts into the Top 60</strong>. The single went viral on TikTok with <strong>over 500,000 views in just 24 hours</strong>, while both “Back Home” and his breakout anthem <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=783255a44a914f36\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Stay Strong”</strong></a>—a heartfelt tribute to military personnel, autoimmune warriors, and those facing mental health challenges—have been featured on <strong>major editorial playlists across Spotify, Amazon Music, Tidal, and more</strong>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/op_ZEYZegos","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"His latest release, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6MiuL2cjgcSGasS6ol0DT7?si=768e41a678e24270\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Breaking Hearts,”</strong></a> builds on this momentum, showcasing a raw, emotive sound that reflects his bold artistic reinvention. Comparisons to artists like <strong>MGK</strong>, <strong>Jelly Roll</strong>, <strong>Carrie Underwood</strong>, and <strong>Shaboozey </strong>speak to his wide-ranging appeal and boundary-pushing creativity."},{"t":"p","html":"As a national touring artist, Stephen’s resume includes <strong>five Grammy Award considerations</strong> as an independent act, a <strong>#2 spot on the iTunes Charts</strong> with <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5PGeydtICzokuReD9TOiHW?si=4278bc4bba8f4826\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Best Days,”</strong></a> and global exposure through Revolt TV with his video for <strong>“Search Me.”</strong> &nbsp;From his early beginnings to signing with <strong>SkeeloMusik/Sony RED</strong> in 2013 and later finding his artistic home with <strong>Creative Hearts Entertainment</strong>, Stephen’s journey has been one of constant growth and reinvention."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond the music, Stephen’s story and sound have been spotlighted in MTV, Vibe Magazine, Swagger, Hype Magazine, Earmilk, V13, and The Source, among others. He’s performed alongside iconic names and walked red carpets at major events including the BET Live Experience."},{"t":"p","html":"Ten years into his career, Stephen continues to follow the advice that shaped his path: stay true to yourself. It’s a message that drives his music and fuels his mission to inspire the next generation of artists."},{"t":"p","html":"All of Stephen’s latest releases—including “Breaking Hearts,” “Back Home,” and “Stay Strong”—are available on Spotify, Apple Music, Amazon Music, Tidal, and all major platforms. For updates, videos, and exclusive content, visit the links below."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephen!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.stephentmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/StephenTMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/404?fromUrl=/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/StephenThomas1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://x.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>X</strong></a>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/Cv0cZdtuXQn/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"408152","title":"Hallie Marie Music ✸☽ A Denver-Based musician who blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling. She has a series of releases arriving in 2025, with her first titled \"Indebted\" arriving January 21.","date":"2025-07-02","lead":"Evoking the drifting beauty of a perfect summer gone too soon","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/408152/895eb06172b09a8a082d088245799596.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Evoking the drifting beauty of a perfect summer gone too soon"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Denver, CO</strong> <strong>(July 2, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>- Today, singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qjqY0W9hRpqy_g6Ky9uPyw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a> releases “3:59,” a love letter to summer travels, the people and places that change us, and the wonder of carrying those memories home. The sweeping new single captures the moment between joy and goodbye, where late nights, sun-soaked swims, and new connections collapse into the clarity of a flight home.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4IfwEmntaVlwdMx4zhHAti?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Written after Hallie’s transformative summers spent abroad, first in Spain, then in Berlin, “3:59” wraps oceanic guitar textures and synth-tide rhythms around her signature confessional lyrics. Produced in collaboration with <strong>Andreas Landeck</strong>, who also engineered the guitar work, the song mirrors the ebb and flow of memory itself: wistful, vivid, and impossibly tender."},{"t":"quote","html":"'Soaking wet on the shore' is me soaked in the beauty of all my travels while on the plane home, no longer in it but still dripping with it.\"","cite":"- Hallie Marie"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/754037/large-dd8d3fe093cc96c14059e49eddcc4b4a.jpg","alt":"Covert art for \"3:59\" by Hallie Marie"},{"t":"p","html":"From snapshots of swimming under moonlight in Spain to quiet moments with friends in Berlin’s parks and open mics, “3:59” unfolds like a photo album flicked through in real time. Hallie’s lyrics hold a space where deep gratitude and melancholy coexist, grounded in the kind of perspective that only comes from leaving something beautiful behind."},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, “3:59” is a shimmering blend of indie rock and alternative pop, with emotional guitar swells and ambient textures that evoke the meditative atmosphere of <strong>Depeche Mode</strong> or <strong>Daughter</strong>. The chorus crests and falls like the waves Hallie sings about, graceful, immersive and alive with memory."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lyrics Preview:</strong> And if I smile / It’s because I have everything, I have everything / Took a detour again / And so it began / But I feel it’s always alright in the end."},{"t":"p","html":"Fresh on the heels of previous singles, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7pJ7dINaRbJvhjAWXp3pHo?go=1&amp;sp_cid=cf2574d8c3c2ab88c5653d52eabc4308&amp;utm_source=embed_player_p&amp;utm_medium=desktop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">“Pure (Don’t You Still Remember?),”</a> <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1O4Q92TIuafovajnJyR557?si=549f851b577b4ab0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">“Indebted,”</a> and <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5MOvprcZTavKXYtApW4qKz?si=5f5e0783d94c47c4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">“Sanity,”</a> \"<strong>3:59</strong>\" continues to expand Hallie's unique voice in indie-pop, balancing poetic imagery with emotional immediacy. As always, she brings her full heart, and whole world, into the music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/-b10e31cd63b2c0317696d54d044a4e07.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-32 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/preview-c33bb4c8c0fb8d62a46ea644fb5ad2e1.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/-1302eb881563358853da571d1fb91c45.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-36 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/preview-e17e8b3fa61065cd5c4017c5cabd0e2d.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/large-3fd73d88583417c22d63d14ef4d100aa.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-14 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/preview-4811aaab4e4c9d4f52c8820f4714b20b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/large-29c12eef5ba54b62cc04f5bc34eee872.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-29 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/preview-24ede99c287103be1e22c17641577c77.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/-da81f45fe86805db981f72d86eff8965.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-46 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/preview-8f88dcb7cb4728eef25338442eb31f22.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/large-3740cb07a0046ee2a3bf82c6c328555f.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-44 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/preview-a44d9f029894f554f894eed711194762.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/large-69157f55a4afc3f0f8b64d0c7951e6c8.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-1 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/preview-88af250d089625bac98f9cf6e7350728.jpeg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hallie Marie:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a> is a multifaceted artist who beautifully balances light and shadow in her work. With an intellectually curious spirit, she dives deep into the complexities of human emotions, crafting music that resonates with listeners on many levels — from the highs of love and joy to the depths of melancholy. Drawing inspiration from artists like <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>, <strong>Billy Joel</strong>, and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, Hallie’s sound blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling."},{"t":"p","html":"Collaborating with the Denver-based band <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1UP2Zk7NI1U6KBhpPfPKBt?si=y0EiRbwmTCSlwg_-3sd3vg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Direville</a>, Hallie Marie has already begun to make her mark on the music industry with popular releases “<strong>Sympathy</strong>” and “<strong>Free Spirit</strong>”, among others. Now branching out on her own, her solo music endeavors combine poetic mystical imagery with direct and casual insight derived from raw life experience.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Embracing the beauty of authenticity and connecting with each of us at our core, Hallie invites her audience into her world, sharing not just her music but also her creative process — writing, arranging, and recording — along with the benefit of what she has learned through struggle and resilience. She aims to connect deeply with her listeners, sharing meaningful ideas that resonate long after the music ends."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hallie Marie!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/halliemariemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@halliemariemusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/","img":"","title":"Hallie Marie Music ✸☽ A Denver-Based musician who blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling. She has a series of releases arriving in 2025, with her first titled \"Indebted\" arriving January 21.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://instagram.com/halliemariemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qv9RFavvRmeHdVLljnpMBQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | &nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100068917929503\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"398636","title":"Aidan Leclaire Band Unleashes Raw Emotion with Debut Album, \"Hail to the Dogs\"","date":"2025-06-27","lead":"Hail to the Dogs explores disillusionment, self-discovery, and the fragile search for connection.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/398636/9b73b415fbb16dde91ee065825919592.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"<em>Hail to the Dogs</em> explores disillusionment, self-discovery, and the fragile search for connection."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4hcY2Q66SPsyTGWssmTgMN?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Vienna, VA (June 27, 2025) - Following the success of their cosmic sophomore EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3jVnrl0wSEsvdfsfyBxjZ8?si=8xUZwPESQaqwCfQNJOs4xg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>The Spaceman</em></strong></a>, the <a href=\"https://aidanleclaire.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aidan Leclaire Band</strong></a> returns with <em><strong>Hail to the Dogs</strong></em>, a gripping and emotionally charged new album, released today. Diving deep into the raw undercurrents of human experience, this new record explores loneliness, longing, and the unrelenting need for authenticity in a world obsessed with validation.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by the dark totalitarian allegories of <strong>George Orwell</strong>’s <em>Animal Farm</em>, <em>Hail to the Dogs</em> paints a portrait of a generation grappling with unseen powers and personal disillusionment. &nbsp;The album title and cover art get their inspiration from the book's concept, where no matter the species, there will always be a group looking to impose power and dominance."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/739340/large-c8ef94e39232bbe525cde6b6c1064477.jpg","alt":"Cover art by Ezequiel Crower"},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded across Washington D.C. and Northern Virginia with producers <strong>Ben Green (Ivakota Studios)</strong> and <strong>Nico Laget (Sweet Spot Studios)</strong>, the project captures a raw and soulful sound, pulling from the spirit of 1990s alt-rock while carving something wholly its own."},{"t":"quote","html":"“The album is meant to feel raw and dirty, but also beautiful,\" says frontman Aidan Leclaire. \"I wanted it to reflect how messy and fragile our lives can be, and how even in that chaos, there's something worth holding onto.\"","cite":""},{"t":"p","html":"The lead single, <strong>“Good Boy,”</strong> which released May 15, sets the tone with its punk-tinged high energy sound, centering on a yearning to escape materialism and rediscover purpose. Other highlights include <strong>“Is This All There Is?,” </strong>a searing portrayal of communication breakdown in a fractured relationship, and <strong>“Break,”</strong> reimagined from their earlier <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3jVnrl0wSEsvdfsfyBxjZ8?si=8xUZwPESQaqwCfQNJOs4xg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Spaceman</em> EP</a> to capture the fire of their live performances."},{"t":"p","html":"With standout tracks like the urgent, biting, <strong>“Find Me,”</strong> and the brooding anthem, <strong>“Dark Days, Long Nights,”</strong> <em>Hail to the Dogs</em> cements Aidan Leclaire Band’s reputation for creating music that is visceral, relatable, and timeless."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Aidan Leclaire Band:"},{"t":"p","html":"The <strong>Aidan Leclaire Band</strong> is a Washington, D.C.-Northern VA based group known for their eclectic blend of indie rock, alternative and pop music. Formed in 2024, the band has quickly risen in popularity, captivating audiences with their raw, emotional sound and impressive stage presence, cementing their place as one of the most exciting new acts on the scene."},{"t":"p","html":"Their earlier work, including 2024's <em>The Spaceman</em>, earned critical acclaim and a devoted following. Now, with <em>Hail to the Dogs</em>, the band pushes further, offering an unfiltered look at the struggles, contradictions, and hopes of a generation seeking its voice."},{"t":"p","html":"For more information about the Aidan Leclaire Band’s other upcoming shows and music, visit their website and follow them on Instagram, YouTube, and Spotify."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Aidan Leclaire!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/aidanleclairemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@aidanleclairemusic","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/PM6nTaMnIus","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/aidanleclairemusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR?si=AOgLXdj8T3W6EEMWrWxV-w&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=824640e65a9c4045\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|</strong> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCf-C9Au5-RM3bdQNqmW7WHA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://aidanleclaire.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@aidanleclairemusic?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"403845","title":"Kim Edwards Returns with Intimate New Take on Fan-Favorite Track “Far”","date":"2025-06-27","lead":"Piano and strings meet emotional weight in this cinematic reimagining of the 2020 synth-pop ballad.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/403845/0661ba900b1172a78b2967eda4597f3c.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Piano and strings meet emotional weight in this cinematic reimagining of the 2020 synth-pop ballad."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lehigh Valley, PA (June 27, 2025)</strong> – Singer-songwriter <strong>Kim Edwards</strong> invites listeners into a more vulnerable, stripped-back sonic world with the release of <strong>“Far (Strings Version),”</strong> a reimagined take on her 2020 synth-pop track that takes the heartache to a new level. Set for release on Friday, June 27, the song trades shimmering 80s textures for sweeping strings and intimate piano, spotlighting the lyrical ache and emotional core of the original."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1Pya4EAU9Ro5n70sNwmgyO?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Written in a single day—an anomaly for the typically meticulous songwriter—“Far” captures the emotional tug-of-war between longing for love and self-protection born of past wounds. That tension of wanting to be emotionally available but recognizing your own walls —that hope and hesitation—is the heart of this song. Its lyrics explore the push and pull of vulnerability, echoing the universal fear of letting someone in after you’ve been hurt. &nbsp;Edwards explains. <em>“The line that still hits me the most is from the final chorus: ‘Could the walls come down / And for how long? / Enough for you to prove me wrong?’,\"</em> explains Edwards.<em> \"I've felt that deeply in the past -- that idea of seeing something good come into your life, but it's hard for me to bring these walls down. I want to so badly; could I even do it long enough to let you get into my heart? So \"Far\" is really a song that is meant to put its arm around you and sit quietly next to you and meet you where you're at.\"</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746830/large-fa769295874122c6b9a21e8754bafdf4.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Far (Strings Version)\""},{"t":"p","html":"Originally released in 2020, the synth-pop version of “Far” marked a creative breakthrough for Edwards as a producer. But this new version, with its organic instrumentation and emotional spaciousness, feels especially personal. <em>“If the first version was a beautiful painting, this one is like cleaning away the varnish and seeing the deeper, richer colors underneath,</em>” Edwards adds. Produced by longtime collaborator <strong>Jared Salte</strong> (Salt Shaker Studios), the new version of “Far” leans into Edwards’ classical piano roots and cinematic influences—calling to mind the delicate orchestration of <strong>Sleeping At Last</strong> and the lyrical poignancy of <strong>Regina Spektor</strong>. Strings were performed by <strong>Rob Szabo</strong>, with additional mixing and mastering by <strong>Spencer Cheyne&nbsp;</strong>(The Mixing Station)."},{"t":"quote","html":"“The original ‘Far’ was a vibe—synthy and nostalgic....But this version feels like how the song was always meant to be. The string arrangement that Jared wrote is just stunning. It adds a depth that cuts to the heart of what I was trying to say.”","cite":"Kim Edwards"},{"t":"p","html":"This release is part of the slow reveal of Edwards’ upcoming full-length album, <strong><em>Vignettes</em></strong>—her most introspective and fully realized work to date. Known for her lush, melancholic soundscapes and journal-like lyrics, Kim Edwards continues to offer solace to the reflective listener: those searching for beauty in brokenness and strength in softness."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748284/large-b0ad8163393c6c2cbf500be49e658174.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0039.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748284/preview-70ba0c00623cb7165aa7d51893e21f33.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748288/large-a2e3c15bbc6e0af1049c6ab7a9aa63e0.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0052.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748288/preview-fc8ceb005772fc5462b875ad5550c920.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748285/large-0b6197a6f051d62c8146b0bba7cbf73b.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0289.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748285/preview-bcd098cac55d2a0eb6f774e77a787a71.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748286/large-d7e1d9dc0fd77a1a60c2c144303c6c37.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0328.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748286/preview-3696cb8baf68ee148f0bfb241a64e885.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748287/large-934438af0366adc974540cf1dc309eca.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0398.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748287/preview-bf975564845cca27474a595e1bf8868b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748283/large-44156cfbc2050f9407a34bd86f00a033.jpeg","alt":"Kim Edwards_0135.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748283/preview-467a9947650ae95dcbcec1d19c1a40e7.jpeg"}]},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4PCJGcs6ZoUsKBG1OSbyh6?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kim Edwards:"},{"t":"p","html":"With a voice as intimate as a journal entry and melodies that echo like memory, <strong>Kim Edwards</strong> crafts cinematic, emotionally rich songs that feel both timeless and deeply personal. A Lehigh Valley, PA-based singer-songwriter with roots in classical piano and a love for storytelling-driven pop Edwards writes vignettes—poetic snapshots of longing, love, and quiet resilience."},{"t":"p","html":"Over the years, Edwards has developed a signature sound: moody, melancholic, and lush with introspective nuance. Inspired by the likes of <strong>Ingrid Michaelson</strong>, <strong>Regina Spektor</strong>, and <strong>Sleeping At Last</strong>, she blends lyrical vulnerability with orchestral textures often drawing comparisons to her influences while carving out a sonic world uniquely her own. Her songs have found homes in branded content for <strong>Chaco Shoes</strong>, <strong>Paraxel</strong>, and <strong>Disney Weddings</strong>, and her cover of “Auld Lang Syne” garnered over 150K Spotify streams after landing a spot on the platform’s Folksy Christmas playlist. In 2013, she was selected from hundreds of applicants for ASCAP’s prestigious <strong>Jerry Ragovoy Songwriters Workshop </strong>in NYC, has performed twice at <strong>Musikfest</strong> in Bethlehem, PA, and in storied venues like <strong>The Bitter End, Eddie’s Attic, </strong>and <strong>Bluebird Cafe</strong>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/dJeQnuBRcw8","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Among her most meaningful career moments, Kim had the rare honor of <strong>opening for</strong> <strong>The Beach Boys</strong>—a lifelong dream realized for the devoted fan—and also shared a stage with <strong>Jars of Clay</strong> at a local festival. These highlights underscore her steady dedication to her craft and the quiet authenticity that resonates through her music."},{"t":"p","html":"Edwards is embracing music on her own terms. Her forthcoming album, <strong><em>Vignettes</em></strong>, is the most personal and fully realized project of her career. Co-produced by <strong>Jared Salte</strong>, the album serves as a dream fulfilled: “Each song has its own special place in my heart,” she says. “There’s not a single filler.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Now a mother and entering into a reflective new chapter, Kim Edwards stands as a reminder that in a world obsessed with virality and speed, artistry rooted in depth, patience, and honesty endures. Her music offers a quiet refuge for the reflective listener—those seeking comfort, catharsis, or simply the feeling of being seen."},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.kimedwardsmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://instagram.com/kimedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://facebook.com/kedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://x.com/kimedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a> | <a href=\"https://youtube.com/kimedwardsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"407695","title":"Blake Smeltz Releases Debut Album, Heartbreak Highway","date":"2025-06-27","lead":"Capturing the messy realities of growing up, breaking down, and finding your way","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/407695/f8d0c34b6588cf2ed9b5fa5e306f840f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Capturing the messy realities of growing up, breaking down, and finding your way"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>LYNCHBURG, VA</strong> (June 27, 2025) - Today, country artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6VtPWvA4PQlpSmWA85Ugni?si=Osp37CrKRd6fd9Ij9XNBPQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Blake Smeltz</strong></a> released his debut album, <strong>Heartbreak Highway</strong>, a striking collection of songs that trace personal heartbreak, youthful recklessness, deep loss, and hard-won healing."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7GbaHczkUv6298ojSctt88?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"A project as lived-in as it is lyrical, Smeltz distills the emotional highs and lows of relationships, resilience, and growing up across its 9 tracks, cementing him as a bold, gritty and heartfelt new voice in country music."},{"t":"p","html":"From the nostalgic rush of “Nicotine Daydream” to the ragged honesty of “Good Faith” and the gut-punch ache of “You Ain’t Whiskey,” the album captures what Smeltz does best: making personal stories feel universal. It's messy, real, and filled with heart."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This album is authentic and true, every last word. Each song is a personal experience, as well as being inspired by those around me who struggle to put emotions into words.\"","cite":"- Singer-songwriter Blake Smeltz"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753149/large-1ca9eb4cec2133b9e7eff93e8e2c588c.png","alt":"Heartbreak Highway Cover Art. Image Credit: Colby Smeltz"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>William Gawley, Michelle Robertson and Dave Flint</strong>, Heartbreak Highway pairs Smeltz’s gravel-edged vocals with unflinching, modern country storytelling. With one foot in the emotional territory of <strong>Zach Bryan</strong> and the other in the anthemic sway of <strong>Luke Combs</strong>, the album unspools like a map of the moments that make a man, weaving Blake's vivid lyricism with the emotional depth and introspection of lived experience."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753674/large-9d2d3f06a3acdc2295b03832c257b787.jpg","alt":"Photo May 26 2025, 2 08 35 AM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753674/preview-a46a4473709d13de3ac9c2c0e5c54d1c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753145/large-962a0c174360055175eeea0fd5e4bacd.jpg","alt":"Photo May 26 2025, 2 07 46 AM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753145/preview-13bacc8a27b260819f88f26219c7bf6e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753144/large-57677bdfc8f2996d760858c2b5cf26e7.jpg","alt":"church.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753144/preview-338779c1ce481010be91bd38e0be642d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741676/large-3ac8259bfb332a8dbd2cddf143077fcc.jpg","alt":"IMG_1098.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741676/preview-301d36105ee1e54d33a1128884c2ced5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741675/large-7bd2cd7780b1377ed5036340ea5c0f1d.jpg","alt":"BTS.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741675/preview-2f77adcfd926072da099e86848504c04.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753143/large-8b204b2c6ead1ba9d1979fed68be5453.png","alt":"IMG_0184.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753143/preview-7019b011b7d9f2d0244a8b3885f75249.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753147/large-3971dea001e39bbd810d367949f7b6b6.jpg","alt":"DSC00247.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753147/preview-877c1378e750b7b399be924289d6db90.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753675/large-1d1e2864e1b7fee7a6491a156a2884b5.jpg","alt":"Photo May 26 2025, 2 10 37 AM (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753675/preview-84b2407b8e25321d2ecdb96a9ec63984.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753146/large-69e22e3e5d11ebb19d5a06f43bf364d9.jpg","alt":"Photo May 26 2025, 2 05 58 AM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753146/preview-37fce06468ee646ed180061a1e0e9ed6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753679/large-844079727dbb1a6f0d02ab2749ca2148.jpeg","alt":"Black Grunge Music Festival Flyer.png (1).jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753679/preview-404bbf4fc6cb15ce724b41bb4981e83d.jpeg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Riley Lutz and Colby Smeltz."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Standout Tracks Include:</strong>"},{"t":"list","items":["<strong>“Nicotine Daydream,”</strong> a nostalgic, high-energy anthem about first love, Springsteen, and the memories that never quite fade.","<strong>“Good Faith,”</strong> a heartfelt track about grief, growth, and holding on to the people who help keep you steady when life hits hard.","<strong>“You Ain’t Whiskey,”</strong> a raw breakup ballad comparing lost love to the burn of whiskey's fleeting comfort.","<strong>“Dear Old Me,”</strong> a reflective letter to the future self, wondering if the sacrifices made along the way were worth it.","<strong>“Drive,”</strong> a moody, introspective look at escape and self-reckoning, written for anyone who’s ever needed to <em>just keep going</em>.","<strong>“The Road,”</strong> a slow-burning song about walking away from bitterness and choosing peace, even when it hurts."]},{"t":"p","html":"\"This album represents all that has made me who I am today,\" said Smeltz. \"All of these songs are inspired by my life, as well as those close to me. I feel the album as a whole helps put into words what many struggle to open up about. It's for everyone, from the alone and heartbroken, to the happy and enthusiastic. Every word is authentic.\""},{"t":"p","html":"The album will be accompanied by a release party in <strong>Nashville</strong> at 6 pm on July 1 at<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://localnash.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Local</strong></a>."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/753680/large-9c565bc9594f144b7e9174a9a3ad67f4.jpeg","alt":"Black Grunge Music Festival Flyer.png (1).jpeg"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/sBHlLKtjHBQ","height":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DKpugjZxlAL/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"h3","html":"About Blake Smeltz:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/blakesmeltz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Blake Smeltz</strong></a>, a native of Evington, Virginia, has always felt a deep connection to nature, a bond that resonates throughout his music. A self-taught artist who wears his heart on his sleeve, Blake merges sharp songwriting with captivating storytelling to craft songs that are both authentic and engaging. His raspy voice and tenderhearted approach allow him to forge meaningful connections with listeners, drawing them into his world. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by country legends like <strong>Luke Combs</strong>, <strong>Zach Bryan</strong>, and <strong>Jason Aldean</strong>, Blake seamlessly navigates genres, blending elements of country-rock, singer-songwriter, and everything in between. In 2023, he emerged with <em><strong>Demos From the 434</strong></em>, a project that ignited his passion for music and led him to ultimately release his debut album, <em><strong>Heartbreak Highway</strong></em>. Blake’s artistry is a unique blend of Zach Bryan’s introspective lyrics and Luke Combs’ soulful style, enriched by his own powerful voice and heartfelt storytelling.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Outside of music, his passions for motorcycle rides, racecars, and life on the open road fuel his adventurous spirit and inspire his creative process. &nbsp;<br id=\"isPasted\">Rooted in the stillness of nature and the beauty of God’s creation, Blake channels these experiences into lyrics that resonate deeply with his audience. With his passion for music and a life lived boldly, Blake Smeltz is poised to take country music to exciting new horizons. &nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6VtPWvA4PQlpSmWA85Ugni?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/blakesmeltz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Listening Links</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/blakesmeltz_music/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@blakesmeltzmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"408161","title":"17-year-old pop sensation Maria Deirisarri is set to release her debut album, \"In The Beginning,\" on September 29th. Hailing from Atlanta, her musical talent transcends her age, exploring genres from dark alternative to bossa nova. With over 77k Spotify streams and recognition from top publications like Earmilk and Conversations About Her, Maria's star is on the rise. Her music, influenced by her Hispanic heritage, surprises and captivates with its multilingual lyrics.","date":"2025-06-27","lead":"A stripped-back alt-folk reckoning steeped in restraint, rage, and release","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/408161/1403584905ab1b458a2717b888b419e6.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A stripped-back alt-folk reckoning steeped in restraint, rage, and release"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Roswell, GA (June 27, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>- Alt-folk singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?si=bpNuIeehSrqSbXVybDzELQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Maria Deirisarri</a> releases <strong>“Parabellum”</strong> today, the brooding and defiant final single from her upcoming EP, <strong>Si Vis Pacem</strong>. Featuring acclaimed indie artist and regular collaborator <strong>Corey Kilgannon</strong>, the track is out now on all platforms and marks one of the most emotionally direct, sonically refined moments of her career so far."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/44MlAiXV6OQvFIX0QWkynu?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Written the night before recording and <strong>tracked live</strong> in a single take, “Parabellum” is quiet in tone but bold in message. Inspired by a sudden rupture with someone she once loved, it’s a reckoning in disguise, a whispered, uncompromising warning: take what you want from me, but be ready for the fallout."},{"t":"p","html":"The track’s minimalist arrangement with just four instruments puts Maria’s voice front and center, full of quiet, restrained fury and lyrical clarity. Its commanding confidence draws from the idea behind its title, the Latin phrase “si vis pacem, <strong>para bellum</strong>,” meaning, “if you want peace, prepare for war.” The phrase is also a central motif in the <strong>John Wick film series</strong>, which helped inspire the song’s visual and emotional scope, also inspiring the EP's name."},{"t":"quote","html":"“There are some songs that come to you out of nowhere, when in reality, you've been working towards writing them your entire life. Parabellum is one of those songs for me.\"","cite":"- Singer-songwriter Maria Deirisarri"},{"t":"p","html":"Maria’s voice carries the weight of the wound and the warning. The song opens with candid studio dialogue that reveals its unfiltered origin. The result is minimal yet visceral, cinematic yet grounded."},{"t":"p","html":"\"It's so badass,\" said Maria."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/755913/large-e0075e3abfe3d900c524d8b7393d74a4.png","alt":"\"Parabellum\" cover art by Maria Deirisarri"},{"t":"p","html":"Lyrically, “Parabellum” traverses landscapes both literal and emotional: oceans, mountains, forests, deserts, and frozen lands appear not just as metaphors but as stages for a reckoning with identity, grief, and release. As Maria sings, “take whatever you want, whatever you see / just let me go and leave me be,” it becomes clear this is not a plea, but a boundary carved in sound."},{"t":"p","html":"These lines carry layered meaning, many also inspired by <strong>John Wick</strong>, with multiple allusions in the lyrics to specific moments from the movie series."},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Corey Kilgannon</strong><strong>&nbsp;at Beaches Vineyard</strong> and <strong>Jacob Hudson at Pine Studios</strong>, “Parabellum” straddles the line between alternative folk and cinematic minimalism: equal parts personal monologue and visual score. It’s the sound of letting go with precision, not apology. Using Kilgannon’s understated presence to add depth without distraction, the track hits with clarity few songs dare to reach."},{"t":"p","html":"The cover art, created by Deirisarri herself, further embodies the song’s themes of transformation and emotional release. Its design takes inspiration from the <strong>Great Wave off Kanagawa</strong>, an iconic Japanese woodblock print often interpreted to be a grand symbol of nature's power."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Maria Deirisarri:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Rising pop artist <a href=\"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maria Deirisarri</strong></a> is only 19, but her musicianship and lyricism suggest wisdom beyond her years. The Atlanta-based singer-songwriter experiments with many genres, from dark alternative to bossa nova, generating an eclectic mix of music notably showcased in her debut album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ?si=w6TbXsN-SJOMPd4mN151ZA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>In The Beginning</strong></em></a><em>.</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Already amassing over 110k streams on Spotify, and garnering attention from top publications such as <strong>EARMILK</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Conversations About Her</strong>, Maria Deirisarri’s success continues to increase with every release. The range of her sound entices listeners to discover every song’s personality, surprising them with lyrics connected to her Hispanic culture and multilingual heritage (such as in “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5am4tRMhZJObB1vjpzNTbG?si=6c8d80dc16304bd4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Same</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2HOQOaIyRpXxD6JzPwhEdY?si=31b49e0b35bf401a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Te Necesito</strong></a>”)."},{"t":"p","html":"The young artist has triumphed in various competitions, ranging from her Trailblazing Performer accolade from the International Singer-Songwriters Association, her second-place finish in <strong>Omega’s Got Talent</strong>, to her Talent Preliminary Award in the <strong>Miss Georgia Teen Volunteer Competition</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Maria Deirisarri’s vibrant artiste meets the listener with a grace and uniqueness that is a breath of fresh air. Fans are eager to see what this up-and-coming superstar has up her sleeve.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Follow Maria below for all music updates and upcoming announcements!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Maria Deirisarri!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/Kc44XFLF5Mc","height":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/mariadeirisarri/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@mariadeirisarri","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com/","img":"","title":"17-year-old pop sensation Maria Deirisarri is set to release her debut album, \"In The Beginning,\" on September 29th. Hailing from Atlanta, her musical talent transcends her age, exploring genres from dark alternative to bossa nova. With over 77k Spotify streams and recognition from top publications like Earmilk and Conversations About Her, Maria's star is on the rise. Her music, influenced by her Hispanic heritage, surprises and captivates with its multilingual lyrics.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@mariadeirisarri?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCtx5jhQ5a3Fx8_EJxh54WsA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100063574507610\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"403843","title":"Riah Releases New Single, “Stand By You,” From Upcoming Album","date":"2025-06-10","lead":"A Soulful, Slow-Burning Anthem of Support Without Sacrifice","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/403843/f87046a38848c9e364db6a89be8ab2e1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A Soulful, Slow-Burning Anthem of Support Without Sacrifice"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0F4nAgG18mpUhLhSzUK0hv?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"DENVER, CO (June 3, 2025) – Dark-pop artist <strong>Riah</strong> returns with a striking new single for “Stand By You,” with the music video following on June 10, the first release from her upcoming album, <em>The Fourth Wall,&nbsp;</em>out this fall. Seeking the single to stand out from the rest of her catalog, “Stand By You” has a heavily blues-influenced sound, offering a vulnerable meditation on love, boundaries, and emotional self-respect."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/sDnNU8IEcEA","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded at <strong>Conway Sound</strong> in Wheat Ridge, CO, and featuring celebrated guitarist <strong>El Javi</strong> and pianist <strong>Dominick Williams</strong>, “Stand By You” marks a sonic shift for Riah. The track leans into classic blues and R&amp;B textures, slowing things down, stripping them back, and letting the weight of every lyric breathe."},{"t":"p","html":"The single was captured live in-studio during an intimate recording session that also served as the backdrop for the official music video and BTS content, directed by longtime collaborator <strong>Chris Rasmussen</strong>."},{"t":"button","href":"https://youtu.be/dNRx30t1Gp0","label":"Preview the \"Stand By You\" BTS Video & Interview HERE","color":"#3693da"},{"t":"p","html":"With lyrics like <em>“If I could mend for you, I’d lick all your wounds / But I can’t, so I’ve gotta let you heal,”</em> Riah delivers a message many will recognize but few have put into words. “Stand By You” explores the quiet strength it takes to let go of control while remaining fully present, for a love that doesn’t rescue, but doesn’t walk away either."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song is my way of saying, ‘I’m here for you, but I won’t carry your healing for you.’ It’s about honoring someone’s strength, even when they don’t see it yet.\"","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Riah"},{"t":"p","html":"For an artist known for her fierce emotional honesty, this track feels both intimate and expansive. This time, the power comes not from confrontation, but from presence and choosing to stay."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Production Credits:</strong> Riah (Main artist and Songwriter), El Javi (Guitar, Bass, Arrangement), Dominick Williams (Piano, Arrangement); Chris Rasmussen (Videographer/Photographer)"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746837/large-560fe1b59f9fc41150ff00ca8f6ab8bb.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13742.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746837/preview-2b9c6cb084c4ce7dec5bad6a46f81e10.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746836/large-e77d8204f3ebbc7f5475bf372618966a.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13517.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746836/preview-489222ae1b9a2979761050ee9542b053.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746838/large-d005a4bebcff998d871013dcbd46f192.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13626.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746838/preview-d60c26362d10cbeed6ac1ac9b2c96e68.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746839/large-818b693b5f528c1567b7ff8456df0e23.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13650.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746839/preview-ef8caef77bebafb022593cf688b86097.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746840/large-cc99a6346f11e2c492558b973a346076.jpg","alt":"MariahAlbumShoot13583.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/746840/preview-445d73ecd8393f973aaffd9ffee1d23c.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Martha Wirth"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Riah:"},{"t":"p","html":"Riah is a rising force in the Bedroom Pop scene, crafting introspective and evocative music that resonates with the complexities of love, sex, loss, and a distinctive \"villain energy.\" Drawing deeply from personal life experiences, Riah channels raw emotion into every lyric and melody, creating an intimate connection with listeners.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Starting in the Los Angeles entertainment industry at the tender age of 17, Riah faced the harsh realities of the pre-Me Too era, which fueled her desire for autonomy and control over her artistic vision. After years of enduring the industry's darker side, she stepped back, determined to return to music only on her own terms. Now, as an accomplished entrepreneur, Riah has reclaimed her voice and is ready to make waves with a fresh and authentic sound."},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to her musical journey, Riah has captivated audiences at numerous festivals, clubs, and acoustic venues. Her passion for performance extends beyond music, as she is also a competitive pole dancer, having won the prestigious PSO Mountain competition in 2023.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a unique blend of vulnerability and power, Riah is poised to leave a lasting impact on the music world, bringing a new level of depth and intensity to the Bedroom Pop genre."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/xz1El91BAmg?si=dopvTyoauzWBBuM_","height":"315"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Riah:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4W98Etru2ErpE95smqDdfh?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/riahmusic1991\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/riahmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@Riah-Music-1991\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"400065","title":"Blake Smeltz Unveils Upbeat New Single, “Nicotine Daydream”","date":"2025-06-06","lead":"A nostalgic anthem about first love, letting go, and the moments that leave a mark","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/400065/e4a36c1c77f529d03b2138f4bdf95adc.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A nostalgic anthem about first love, letting go, and the moments that leave a mark"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5lGFnEBw0A86hU83eUXbIs?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"NASHVILLE, TN (May 23, 2025) - Country artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6VtPWvA4PQlpSmWA85Ugni?si=Osp37CrKRd6fd9Ij9XNBPQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Blake Smeltz</strong></a> releases his bittersweet, energetic new single, <strong>“Nicotine Daydream,”</strong> capturing the rush of young love and the memories that linger long after it fades."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/K8aGZ_RohXA","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Tracing the story of a first love tied tightly to youth and rebellion, “Nicotine Daydream,” is a song about associating your first love with the feeling of Nicotine. It captures imagery of blaring Springsteen on the radio, windows down, with nowhere to be but everywhere to go. As the years pass, a chance encounter stirs up old emotions, offering a sharp, relatable look at how certain moments stay with us forever."},{"t":"p","html":"Anchored by lines like,&nbsp;<em>\"Nicotine daydream at 18 here we go again / It’s been a couple years now since I last seen her face / ran into her the other day / and it gave my heart a race,\"</em> the track leans into the sweetness and sting of growing up, growing apart, and remembering who we once were."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741676/large-3ac8259bfb332a8dbd2cddf143077fcc.jpg","alt":"IMG_1098.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741676/preview-301d36105ee1e54d33a1128884c2ced5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741677/large-ebfdeeffede1039786418fc2d8ce2447.jpg","alt":"IMG_1102.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741677/preview-188aad6e3b4627e1037465feb69348bf.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741678/large-09d0fca60bace714d3296e8e69487f48.jpg","alt":"IMG_1099.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741678/preview-d081ed74a1e40fa7bf73ca25fb30c49b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741679/large-dd57f43df73e99e2e1461db7ef88e085.jpg","alt":"IMG_1103.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741679/preview-53244310bead171cdf4342512fdc09a0.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741680/large-40b5c54c436b2a01c212cebed94a5210.jpg","alt":"IMG_1101.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741680/preview-da3c661cf64fbe5dff1853ac136c30f6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741675/large-7bd2cd7780b1377ed5036340ea5c0f1d.jpg","alt":"BTS.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741675/preview-2f77adcfd926072da099e86848504c04.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"BTS Shots from filming the \"Nicotine Daydream\" music video. Credit to Charlotte Avenue Entertainment and Giovanne Gotay."},{"t":"p","html":"With a sound that echoes influences like <strong>Luke Combs</strong>, <strong>Zach Bryan</strong>, and <strong>Gavin Adcock</strong>, Smeltz pairs vivid storytelling with his signature raspy vocals, once again proving his knack for crafting songs that feel both personal and universal."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Nicotine Daydream is a song about associating your first love with the feeling of nicotine. It’s an upbeat song about growing up and growing apart, another perspective on a failed relationship. Everyone has one thing that reminds them of something they had in the past.”","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Blake Smeltz"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Charlotte Avenue Entertainment, David Flint</strong> and <strong>William Gawley</strong>, “Nicotine Daydream” is the latest preview from Smeltz’s forthcoming album, <em>Heartbreak Highway</em>, set for release this July. With this track, Smeltz continues to build on the emotional honesty and sonic grit that are quickly becoming his trademarks in today’s country scene."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6VtPWvA4PQlpSmWA85Ugni?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DIyhSJ7uQWi/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"h3","html":"About Blake Smeltz:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/blakesmeltz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Blake Smeltz</strong></a>, a native of Evington, Virginia, has always felt a deep connection to nature, a bond that resonates throughout his music. A self-taught artist who wears his heart on his sleeve, Blake merges sharp songwriting with captivating storytelling to craft songs that are both authentic and engaging. His raspy voice and tenderhearted approach allow him to forge meaningful connections with listeners, drawing them into his world. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by country legends like <strong>Luke Combs</strong>, <strong>Zach Bryan</strong>, and <strong>Jason Aldean</strong>, Blake seamlessly navigates genres, blending elements of country-rock, singer-songwriter, and everything in between. In 2023, he debuted with <em><strong>Demos From the 434</strong></em>, a project that ignited his passion for music and set him on a promising path in country music. Blake’s artistry is a unique blend of Zach Bryan’s introspective lyrics and Luke Combs’ soulful style, enriched by his own powerful voice and heartfelt storytelling.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Outside of music, his passions for motorcycle rides, racecars, and life on the open road fuel his adventurous spirit and inspire his creative process. &nbsp;<br id=\"isPasted\">Rooted in the stillness of nature and the beauty of God’s creation, Blake channels these experiences into lyrics that resonate deeply with his audience. With his passion for music and a life lived boldly, Blake Smeltz is poised to take country music to exciting new horizons. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/blakesmeltz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Listening Links</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/blakesmeltz_music/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@blakesmeltzmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"402092","title":"Kristen Budde Finds Freedom Behind the Wheel on Uplifting New Single “Drive”","date":"2025-06-06","lead":"Country artist Kristen Budde returns with “Drive,” a heartfelt anthem about freedom, healing, and chasing new beginnings, out June 6.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/402092/661fd2d75c96751e882d03cc68456880.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Country artist Kristen Budde returns with “Drive,” a heartfelt anthem about freedom, healing, and chasing new beginnings, out June 6."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Murfreesboro, TN (June 6, 2025)</strong> – Tennessee-based singer/songwriter Kristen Budde invites listeners to roll the windows down and turn the volume up on her liberating new country single, “Drive,” set for release on Friday, June 6, 2025. Her unique blend of Americana and Country music has captured hearts with this sonic snapshot of movement, healing, and chasing wide-open skies. “Drive” is a heartfelt anthem for anyone who’s ever needed to hit the road and leave the past behind."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/02dIDTwhOe7oGneAv5n4pQ?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Fresh off the release of her latest single “Regret”, &nbsp;“Drive” boasts a different side of Budde with shimmering acoustic textures, soaring harmonies. Echoing the styles of Fleetwood Mac, Little Big Town, and Sheryl Crow, “Drive” delivers that golden-hour feeling of motion and release. From backroad singalongs to long interstate escapes, “Drive” captures the power of movement — physical, emotional, and spiritual. <em>“Music, like driving, can be a great means of escape when life starts to feel a little too heavy,”</em> Budde explains. <em>“This song is about unapologetically moving toward a better future free from fear and regret.”</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/744642/large-96fc34eedeacc66de00b1997aae2fe7e.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Drive\" by Kristen Budde, artwork by Meagan Morris"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I love to drive and roll the windows down while singing at the top of my lungs because it makes me feel alive. That’s my wish for listeners when they hear this song. I hope ‘Drive’ becomes a soundtrack to road trips, life adventures — and even offers a little music therapy for whoever needs it.”","cite":"Kristen Budde"},{"t":"p","html":"Written in collaboration with <strong>Debbie Olson</strong>, the song is rooted in connection and resilience. Its original idea emerged during a writing retreat with <strong>Greg McFaden</strong>, <strong>Grace Hunt</strong>, and<strong>&nbsp;Jennifer Bast</strong>, and was later reimagined and completed by Budde and Olson, with blessings from the original co-writers. <em>“Being part of a song created with so many friends makes it extra special,”</em> Budde shares. Produced by <strong>Nicole Witt</strong>, the track features a top-tier lineup of musicians including <strong>Sol Philcox-Littlefield</strong> (guitar), <strong>Jimbo Hart</strong> (bass), and <strong>Grayson Wright</strong> (piano), with Budde’s expressive vocals at the wheel.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://vibe.to/drivebykristenbudde","label":"PRE-SAVE","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1acunSmvzDImLiyfa7Qdad?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kristen Budde:"},{"t":"p","html":"Kristen Budde, Tennessee based singer/songwriter and multi-instrumentalist, crafts songs that are honest and thoughtful with lyrics that are woven together like a conversation with a close friend. With vocals and melodies that can be both powerful and gentle, Kristen’s music is a blend of Americana and Country and her voice has been described as bringing life and light into a room. Kristen has a passion for creating joy-filled connection through the power of music and wholeheartedly believes that music has the ability to heal us. Budde made her musical debut in 2022 when she released her first single<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7j2mwnTaZaIuu9cUkJhxpI?si=9e64a5ef66164353\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\"Come Sit Down at My Table\"</strong></a> which delves into our need to belong and be seen and heard. Her debut 6-song EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3vWwjVeHureyaBFZMZLIOz?si=LjIcc-IiQQipmvPq_Bxc7w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Begin Again</strong></em></a> was released throughout 2023 and was a fulfillment a life long dream. The songs on <em>Begin Again</em> will take listeners on a journey through wrestling with fear, letting go and finding the courage to truly live. Kristen hopes these songs will inspire courage for listeners to take brave steps to build lives they love and will give hope that it's never too late to begin again."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/AoRVTjuz7ms","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Kristen is currently releasing singles and preparing to record her second album set to release in 2026. When Kristen’s not busy working on music, you can probably find her sipping coffee on her back porch or singing silly songs she made up for her family and pets!&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.kristenbuddemusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">WEBSITE</a> | <a href=\"https://instagram.com/kristenbuddemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/kristenbuddemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"400071","title":"Lora Kelley Announces New Single \"Will You Hold My Arms Up?\" — A Raw Invitation to Faith, Doubt, and Healing","date":"2025-05-30","lead":"Blurring the lines between folk confession and somatic storytelling, Lora Kelley offers \"Will You Hold My Arms Up?\" - an aching, Americana-infused meditation on faith, grief, and human resilience.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/400071/a2d2640569f8c5630452019407b9ba2f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Blurring the lines between folk confession and somatic storytelling, Lora Kelley offers \"Will You Hold My Arms Up?\" - an aching, Americana-infused meditation on faith, grief, and human resilience."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>North Garden, VA (May 30, 2025)</strong> — Multidisciplinary artist and trauma-informed story work coach <strong>Lora Kelley</strong> invites listeners into a stirring landscape of vulnerability and hope with her new single, \"<strong>Will You Hold My Arms Up?\"</strong>, ahead of her forthcoming album due this fall. Known for her compassionate work guiding individuals through healing, Lora's music is a profound extension of her life’s calling — a tender space where storytelling, spirituality, somatic healing, and song meet."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2mw4BHPMqFZ2Un0n6fVnFB?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/WillYouHoldMyArmsUp","label":"Listen on all Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Steeped in years of walking alongside others through their deepest wounds, Lora Kelley’s songwriting reflects a hard-won tenderness — an understanding that some forms of suffering cannot be undone, only witnessed. \"Will You Hold My Arms Up?\" rises from this sacred tension, shaped by a lifetime spent navigating the liminal spaces of faith and doubt. Growing up attuned to the emotional landscapes of the Psalms, Kelley found early resonance in the vulnerable confession, <em>\"I believe; help my unbelief.\"</em> Over time, she observed the ways religious culture often imposed shame around expressions of sadness, anger, or spiritual fatigue — a rigidity she found at odds with the profoundly human grief embodied by Jesus himself. <em>\"This song is a declaration of what it means to be human,\"</em> Kelley shares. <em>\"To have faith, yet lean on the faith of others. To find strength, and still grow tired. To know that God's presence holds steady even when our belief feels frayed. Sometimes, it’s enough simply to ask for someone to hold our arms up.\"</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/745216/large-b7580942b133435ffed6e97a87b79471.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Where I Am Now\""},{"t":"p","html":"A moving anthem for anyone who has wrestled with that exhaustion, doubt, and the longing to be held in the midst of hardship - the song weaves plaintive lyrics with an intimate Americana sound, reminiscent of artists like Porter's Gate, Madison Cunningham, and Natalie Merchant. Produced by Jeremy Casella, \"Will You Hold My Arms Up?\" features stirring performances from an all-star lineup of musicians, including Nate Duggar (guitar), Matt Stan (piano), John Hunt (drums), Jacob Blowery (bass), and Mike Payne (guitar). Engineered by Evan Redwine, the track captures the emotional intensity and quiet strength at the heart of Kelley's writing."},{"t":"quote","html":"\"If you ever feel shame about faith and doubt... or if you ever feel shame about feeling tired or around spirituality and God, this song is one of resonance. It's a cry for help when we just feel on the edges of our ability to stay present with ourselves and our hope.\"","cite":"Lora Kelley"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/745217/large-43c0fcfaef5356d57fbd975ef58a069e.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-48-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/745217/preview-df91bc72ed8acf143a9b27a410540bdf.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/745218/large-7fc534f192298e862c316f7b45672909.jpg","alt":"LoraKelley_FILM_March2025_AmyNicolePhotography-24.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/745218/preview-353b501920133496285dd070e3c5ec52.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by Amy Nicole Photography"},{"t":"p","html":"Rooted in the themes of resilience and gentle honesty, Lora's work is deeply informed by her background in narrative-based trauma care, including her studies with the Allender Center. Her music stands as a testament to the beauty of brokenness, offering not platitudes, but presence — a hand to hold in the dark. Raised amid the liminality of faith and living today on a conserved farm in Virginia with her partner, children, and a lively menagerie of pets, Lora crafts songs that feel lived-in, earthy, and unflinchingly honest. Her upcoming album will continue to explore the emotional terrains where suffering and hope coexist — a body of work poised to resonate with those yearning for deeper connection and sacred honesty."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6WXETjjadXjtTGA0k5IfM4?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lora Kelley:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.lorakelley.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lorakelleymusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/thelorakelley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/lorakelley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Patreon</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"405020","title":"Rachel Whitcomb’s ‘Wildest Dreams’ Is a Love Letter to ’90s Country","date":"2025-05-27","lead":"Out now, the Pittsburgh-based singer-songwriter delivers a fearless blend of heartache, humor and hard-won hope.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/405020/dc6cfc6c3bd3ebc436aeb394396eefaa.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Out now, the Pittsburgh-based singer-songwriter delivers a fearless blend of heartache, humor and hard-won hope."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>PITTSBURGH, PA</strong> (March 28, 2025) — Singer-songwriter <strong>Rachel Whitcomb</strong> returns with <em><strong>Wildest Dreams</strong></em>, a genre-spanning collection of original songs that channels the raw storytelling and vibrant instrumentation of '90s country with a personal edge.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Featuring some of Nashville’s most revered instrumentalists, the album showcases Whitcomb’s ability to write from experience while tapping into something universal: love, loss, desire, and the strength to keep going."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3j4HHchsCFiUT8EV9cf0os?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The 10-track album ranges from the electric twang of the Brent Mason-backed “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7abLKIBxLEFWfOG6L1hJdH?si=ce617d5af3b34fe1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Walk of Shame</a>” to the gut-punch ballad “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5mwuxVNVICNMgN5oTi9pdL?si=80522e1311694361\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">You’ll Want Me,</a>” and the unflinchingly honest anthem “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/13n1NrXAXMfBCBnyKzAArX?si=1941ede732f34615\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Live in the Lonely</a>,” which has moved live audiences to tears. Across the record, Whitcomb expertly blends traditional country textures including fiddle, steel guitar and stacked harmonies, with genre turns into adult contemporary, western swing and even ’80s-inspired rock."},{"t":"quote","html":"“The songs on Wildest Dreams are based on my own personal experiences that I think many people have. When audience members talk to me about these songs, they often tell me stories that relate to the emotions expressed, and then it's like we've known each other for years! As humans, we have a lot in common, and music can reveal those shared experiences.\"","cite":"- Singer-songwriter Rachel Whitcomb"},{"t":"h3","html":"Highlights include:"},{"t":"list","items":["<strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7abLKIBxLEFWfOG6L1hJdH?si=208c8ab08d924940\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Walk of Shame</a>,”&nbsp;</strong>a neon-lit, fiddle-fueled romp that nods to <strong>Pam Tillis</strong> while capturing the messy, funny aftermath of a night gone sideways.","<strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5mwuxVNVICNMgN5oTi9pdL?si=a762104b3432429d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">You’ll Want Me,</a>”</strong> a haunting ballad reminiscent of <strong>Faith Hill</strong> or <strong>Patty Loveless</strong> that imagines a woman forever lingering in a former lover’s mind.","<strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/13n1NrXAXMfBCBnyKzAArX?si=f1fa7dacfe3444d2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Live in the Lonely,</a>”</strong> which confronts the modern loneliness epidemic with tenderness and grace.","<strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1iykJeyxlDcSPNL5zSiQd4?si=6415b9d08f664e84\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Flirt With Me,</a>”</strong> a bold appeal for intimacy inside a marriage, written as a lyrical response to the Bruce Robison-penned <strong>Tim McGraw&nbsp;</strong>hit,<strong>&nbsp;“Angry All the Time.”</strong>","<strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7ITL5Pi8RHFzHByBmUtFeF?si=324469ca26254a24\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Control,</a>”</strong> a guitar-driven power track that brings in echoes of Heart and 80s rock attitude."]},{"t":"p","html":"Whitcomb, a breast cancer survivor as well as Associate Dean and Associate Professor of Music Education at <strong>Duquesne</strong><strong>&nbsp;University</strong>, is no stranger to resilience. But Wildest Dreams doesn’t lean on biography to earn its emotional weight. Shaped by a clear, confident voice, these songs are clever, sexy, vulnerable, and tough."},{"t":"p","html":"With production by Jacob Zang and John Nicholson across multiple studios in Nashville, Pittsburgh and beyond, the album features contributions from revered players including <strong>Brent Mason, Pat McGrath, Ryan Joseph, Scotty Sanders, Johnny Brown</strong> and more."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748893/large-263046365b5dd257d2a7a6fd1207ec4b.jpg","alt":"nashville music headshot photographer - Rachel Whitcomb promo -July 24, 2024 - 015.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748893/preview-264b1ff7914e98853d10da678fad98e5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748890/large-1c55b2590555723d3e35d8ff1c4524ad.jpg","alt":"nashville music headshot photographer - Rachel Whitcomb promo -July 24, 2024 - 014.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748890/preview-13eff8128b90ac1e84cdee8257f19d17.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748891/large-2a950be0f74e26cc676810046b35b79f.jpg","alt":"nashville music headshot photographer - Rachel Whitcomb promo -July 24, 2024 - 012.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748891/preview-87c397f67959f8022d082b113d17278f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748894/large-d1c99bdf2ed1cf040fb66060bc8f12d3.jpg","alt":"nashville music headshot photographer - Rachel Whitcomb promo -July 24, 2024 - 003.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748894/preview-a46a9a7665aaa2313c4f1911928dbd7f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748895/large-0257520c4dbfd66e1e06611e02dcc5f2.jpg","alt":"nashville music headshot photographer - Rachel Whitcomb promo -July 24, 2024 - 001.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748895/preview-fc659dfc4c19cd2cefcb838c298ef22c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748896/large-a5683f11425128d8cec8ff669687665e.jpg","alt":"nashville music headshot photographer - Rachel Whitcomb promo -July 24, 2024 - 011.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748896/preview-eda0f44e38db6b46e201bf75fc3fc747.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748897/large-8ee3b9c612d503397199b05c01b0295e.jpg","alt":"nashville music headshot photographer - Rachel Whitcomb promo -July 24, 2024 - 005.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748897/preview-8a9262c6ac38e6f67c39b34cff60d30c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748892/large-80c9c468ef595093a7ec971b6dc51047.jpg","alt":"nashville music headshot photographer - Rachel Whitcomb promo -July 24, 2024 - 006.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/748892/preview-3a58c00d2eba0a4f1a0071da9ee72801.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Music City Content Kings"},{"t":"p","html":"Whitcomb’s experience as a higher education leader and country artist adds depth to her writing and performances. Her academic work in music education and songwriting complements the personal storytelling that defines her music. “My songwriting informs my teaching, and my work with students fuels the stories I tell in song,” she says. “Everything informs everything else.”"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Wildest Dreams</em> is available now on all major streaming platforms."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/xSvZK0uVqRk","height":""},{"t":"h3","html":"About Rachel Whitcomb"},{"t":"p","html":"Rachel Whitcomb is a Pittsburgh-based singer-songwriter whose music blends the emotional clarity of '90s country with the melodic force of Americana. A seasoned performer and storyteller, she’s known for songs that carry grit and grace. Whether she’s delivering a fiddle-fueled barnburner or a piano ballad about loneliness, her work is as emotionally grounded as it is musically polished."},{"t":"p","html":"A breast cancer survivor and <strong>“One to Watch” (Nashville Songwriters Association International)</strong>, Whitcomb has performed for <strong>Tennessee Songwriters Week</strong> and advanced to its showcase at the Franklin Theatre. She's worked with top Nashville players including Brent Mason, Ryan Joseph, and Pat McGrath. Her latest album, Wildest Dreams, is a bold, emotionally rich collection of original songs exploring heartbreak, intimacy, survival, and strength."},{"t":"p","html":"Whitcomb serves as <strong>Associate Dean and Associate Professor of Music Education at Duquesne University’s Mary Pappert School of Music</strong>, specializing in early childhood music education, music teacher education, fostering creativity and incorporating popular music styles in music classrooms, and bringing songwriting into music instruction. Her work in education and songwriting are inextricably linked and rooted in the belief that music, when shared honestly, has the power to heal, connect and reveal what we have in common."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Rachel!</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/rachelwhitcombmusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/RachelWhitcombSingerSongwriter\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCtC2QjPx8wbQKvvnSKla4bQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.rachelwhitcomb.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a>​"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"384283","title":"HORSESHOES Announces 'suite ossuary', A Melancholic Indie Rock Journey Through Love And Loss","date":"2025-05-23","lead":"Indie rock artist Horseshoes unveils suite ossuary, a hauntingly intimate album that drifts between love and loss, wrapping listeners in a rainy-day haze of whispered melodies and ghostly echoes.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/384283/8eed33c85a42df2cdef2134b3b132a6a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Indie rock artist Horseshoes unveils <em>suite ossuary</em>, a hauntingly intimate album that drifts between love and loss, wrapping listeners in a rainy-day haze of whispered melodies and ghostly echoes."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7uVK8xyeNcJbM9o2EUeYwl?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"SALT LAKE CITY, UT (May 23, 2025) - Indie rock artist <strong>Horseshoes</strong> returns with<em><strong>&nbsp;suite ossuary</strong></em>, an album that lingers in the space between love and grief. It’s about transformation—the way falling in love can feel like shedding an old self, like saying goodbye to a version of you that no longer fits.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"\"This album is ideally suited for people interested in having a melancholic rainy day sort of afternoon....It seeks to celebrate the ghosts that haunt us as we fall in love.\"","cite":"HORSESHOES"},{"t":"p","html":"Fresh off the successful release of two singles - the title track \"suite ossuary\" and \"drive\" - the album is a beautiful journey through that disorienting space, where deep connection and quiet mourning feel like two sides of the same coin. The tracks lean into a rainy-day aesthetic, drawing from the hushed intimacy of Elliott Smith and the hazy textures of Duster, The Microphones, and The Postal Service. The influence of Miles Davis and Bill Evans hums beneath the surface, shaping the record’s slow-burning atmosphere. It’s not jazz, but it carries the same late-night solitude—the kind that turns small moments into something vast."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/719190/large-fb228f923457f3f5d911b953c3947bcc.jpeg","alt":"Cover art for 'suite ossuary' by Horseshoes"},{"t":"p","html":"From stripped-down acoustic moments to reverb-drenched waves of sound, <em>suite ossuary</em> builds a world that feels both intimate and expansive. It’s an album for anyone who’s ever felt love and loss tangled together, unsure where one ends and the other begins."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/725234/-bdf1d5741357edc9b631e25b35256dc3.jpeg","alt":"AustinSelectedHolga001HiRes.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/725234/-bdf1d5741357edc9b631e25b35256dc3.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560401/original-5552a690295dfef74777b49f4ad791f4.jpeg","alt":"photo-output.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560401/original-5552a690295dfef74777b49f4ad791f4.jpeg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Horseshoes:"},{"t":"p","html":"Austin Greaves is a Salt Lake City-based musician who performs under the name Horseshoes. He released his debut album, <em>Desert</em>, in June of 2022, which was followed up with a single “Come With Me,” released that October. His most recent album <em>Black Snow</em> gained considerable notoriety from industry tastemakers such as The Source, Plastic Mag and Earmilk who described him as <em>\"the genius behind this indie-rock creation, has masterfully captured the essence of the human experience, drawing audiences into a world where vulnerability is transformed into strength.\"&nbsp;</em>Stand out tracks “Hide and Seek,” “Say What You Mean,” &nbsp;and “L.A.” took center stage as Greaves<em>&nbsp;\"mastered the art of crafting music that tugs at the heartstrings while maintaining an upbeat and catchy sound.\" (Plastic Mag)</em>. To stay updated on all announcements and updates, follow Horseshoes on his social media channels linked below!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.horseshoestheband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/horseshoesguy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0cIVB4MH1nJhx5soIMZeKt?si=hLJSc-kqRLyy3txxAaKy2g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"399070","title":"Hallie Marie Music ✸☽ A Denver-Based musician who blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling. She has a series of releases arriving in 2025, with her first titled \"Indebted\" arriving January 21.","date":"2025-05-21","lead":"New single channels Sufjan Stevens-esque vulnerability with ethereal harmonies and raw emotional clarity","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/399070/5d4de69304283f9b13706d2d1b023fad.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"New single channels Sufjan Stevens-esque vulnerability with ethereal harmonies and raw emotional clarity"},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (May 21, 2025) - Emerging folk singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qjqY0W9hRpqy_g6Ky9uPyw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a> unveils her soul-stirring new single <strong>“Pure (Don’t You Still Remember?)”</strong> - a poignant meditation on the emotional fallout after a deep romantic connection unravels into silence. With intimate storytelling and a vocal performance that builds from fragile to transcendent, the track captures the ache of being forgotten by someone who once knew you most intimately."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7pJ7dINaRbJvhjAWXp3pHo?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Rooted in a minimalist acoustic guitar foundation, “Pure (Don’t You Still Remember?)” gradually blossoms into a layered, atmospheric soundscape where Hallie's voice becomes its own choir. The song evokes the sonic intimacy of artists like <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>—airy, introspective, and rich with harmonic depth—creating a space where the listener feels both the heartbreak and the lingering hope for gentleness after love fades."},{"t":"quote","html":"“It can be a jarring experience going from being super intimate and vulnerable with someone, to not interacting with them at all. It’s a different kind of heartbreak, wanting to keep doors open to kindness or friendship, while the other person just isn’t up for it.”","cite":"Hallie Marie on the inspiration behind “Pure (Don't You Still Remember?)”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/739870/large-b866a6c6ac608d17cb2a6e81ad6c46ce.jpg","alt":"Cover art for “Pure (Don't You Still Remember?)” by Hallie Marie"},{"t":"p","html":"Lyrically, Hallie navigates the spiraling thoughts that follow this kind of quiet ending:<em>&nbsp;“Now you won’t even look at me, am I nothing to you?”</em> she sings, searching for clarity in the void. Lines like “<em>If you only see a woman as Mary the virgin or Mary the other… you should take a look at your hands”</em> confront the emotional residue of being idealized, desired, and then dismissed—without closure. “This song was so much fun to record because I got to create a whole choir with just my voice,” she adds. “The way it opens up from a simple guitar and voice melody into a whole atmosphere of different vocal parts is very exciting for me.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Fresh off the release of her previous singles <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1O4Q92TIuafovajnJyR557?si=549f851b577b4ab0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">“Indebted”</a> and <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5MOvprcZTavKXYtApW4qKz?si=5f5e0783d94c47c4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">“Sanity”</a> - “Pure (Don’t You Still Remember?)” marks a resonant moment in Hallie Marie's evolving artistry—showcasing not only her lyrical honesty, but her ability to turn silence into song."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/-b10e31cd63b2c0317696d54d044a4e07.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-32 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/preview-c33bb4c8c0fb8d62a46ea644fb5ad2e1.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/-1302eb881563358853da571d1fb91c45.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-36 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/preview-e17e8b3fa61065cd5c4017c5cabd0e2d.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/large-3fd73d88583417c22d63d14ef4d100aa.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-14 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/preview-4811aaab4e4c9d4f52c8820f4714b20b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/large-29c12eef5ba54b62cc04f5bc34eee872.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-29 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/preview-24ede99c287103be1e22c17641577c77.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/-da81f45fe86805db981f72d86eff8965.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-46 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/preview-8f88dcb7cb4728eef25338442eb31f22.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/large-3740cb07a0046ee2a3bf82c6c328555f.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-44 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/preview-a44d9f029894f554f894eed711194762.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/large-69157f55a4afc3f0f8b64d0c7951e6c8.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-1 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/preview-88af250d089625bac98f9cf6e7350728.jpeg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hallie Marie:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a> is a multifaceted artist who beautifully balances light and shadow in her work. With an intellectually curious spirit, she dives deep into the complexities of human emotions, crafting music that resonates with listeners on many levels — from the highs of love and joy to the depths of melancholy. Drawing inspiration from artists like <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>, <strong>Billy Joel</strong>, and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, Hallie’s sound blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling."},{"t":"p","html":"Collaborating with the Denver-based band <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1UP2Zk7NI1U6KBhpPfPKBt?si=y0EiRbwmTCSlwg_-3sd3vg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Direville</a>, Hallie Marie has already begun to make her mark on the music industry with popular releases “<strong>Sympathy</strong>” and “<strong>Free Spirit</strong>”, among others. Now branching out on her own, her solo music endeavors combine poetic mystical imagery with direct and casual insight derived from raw life experience.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Embracing the beauty of authenticity and connecting with each of us at our core, Hallie invites her audience into her world, sharing not just her music but also her creative process — writing, arranging, and recording — along with the benefit of what she has learned through struggle and resilience. She aims to connect deeply with her listeners, sharing meaningful ideas that resonate long after the music ends."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hallie Marie!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/halliemariemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@halliemariemusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/","img":"","title":"Hallie Marie Music ✸☽ A Denver-Based musician who blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling. She has a series of releases arriving in 2025, with her first titled \"Indebted\" arriving January 21.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://instagram.com/halliemariemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qv9RFavvRmeHdVLljnpMBQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | &nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100068917929503\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"398539","title":"Melissa D Tackles the Afterlife with Humor and Heart in New Single “Will I Be Bored in Heaven?”","date":"2025-05-16","lead":"Blending folk-pop charm with Americana wit, Melissa D returns with \"Will I Be Bored in Heaven?\", finding laughter and light in life’s biggest unknown.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/398539/0d012cddea4c485a10ff1744eefad558.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Blending folk-pop charm with Americana wit, Melissa D returns with \"Will I Be Bored in Heaven?\", finding laughter and light in life’s biggest unknown."},{"t":"p","html":"MIDDLEBURY, VT (May 16, 2025) — What do dogs, dirty jokes, cheese, and celestial chores have in common? They all show up in <strong>\"Will I Be Bored in Heaven?\"</strong>—the witty, whimsical new single from Vermont-based folk-pop artist <strong>Melissa D</strong>, out Friday, May 16."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4RMdpFfNDSF9pTO077eB85?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Blending playful storytelling with spiritual curiosity, “Will I Be Bored in Heaven?” invites listeners to rethink the afterlife with laughter instead of fear. With a sound that’s been described as “John Prine meets Karen Carpenter,” Melissa D wraps honest questions about death in a warm, melodic hug—acoustic-driven, heartfelt, and just cheeky enough to make you smirk between verses."},{"t":"quote","html":"“One listener told me this song helped her not fear dying, which was incredibly moving...While I had so much fun crafting the lyrics, I was also processing my own thoughts about life and the afterlife.”","cite":"Melissa D on writing the song \"Will I Be Bored In Heaven?\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0ecqt82S1qiJVfSGKqZenW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The idea for the song came to her mid-chaos while packing for a road trip with her husband, Alan—who co-wrote several of the song’s standout lines, including the crowd-favorite: <em>“Will I have to try out for the choir?”</em> The couple wrote and laughed as they cruised Vermont’s backroads, capturing the spirit of a song that would soon become one of her most requested at live shows. <em>“People kept asking, ‘Play the heaven song!’”</em> Melissa shares. <em>“That’s when I knew it was time to get it properly recorded so folks could enjoy it anytime.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by Vermont’s own <strong>Colin McCaffrey</strong>, “Will I Be Bored in Heaven?” pairs folk sensibility with alternative country charm, topped off with Melissa’s signature earthy vocals—a blend of smoky sweetness and soul. “Music is my love language,” she adds. “When people connect with my songs, I feel fulfilled as a songwriter. I see songwriting as a form of energy work.”Whether you're searching for spiritual peace, a musical smile, or just wondering if there's wine in the great beyond, “Will I Be Bored in Heaven?” offers a fresh perspective on the hereafter—one clever chorus at a time."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/739248/large-63fdfa1e8bfe25fdf506caa6af877816.jpg","alt":"Cover Art by Jurgita Vaicekauskaite"},{"t":"p","html":"Folks who join Melissa D’s VIP community on Bandcamp will receive a download of \"Will I Be Bored in Heaven?\" along with her full back catalog, including exclusive tracks not available on major streaming platforms. Plus, 10% of all proceeds go to organizations that support homeless animals, from dogs and cats to bunnies and guinea pigs."},{"t":"button","href":"https://melissadsings.bandcamp.com/vip-songbird","label":"Join VIP Community","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Melissa D:"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Your hiatus from the hustle and bustle… with a side of silliness.</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Melissa Durkee Moorhouse, known artistically as Melissa D, hails from the rolling hills of rustic Vermont, USA. Her music is earthy, chill, and holistic—perfect for those seeking calm, connection, and a touch of lighthearted fun. A classically trained vocalist, Melissa’s journey spans from fronting the rock band The Alley Katz, where she shared the stage with musicians like Joe Moore (Pork Tornado—Jon Fishman of Phish) and Benjamin Orr (The Cars), to co-creating the folk-rock collaboration CHILL with Michael Cressey."},{"t":"p","html":"Since 2016, Melissa has quietly forged her own musical path, recording and releasing her solo work from her small rural home in New England. Partnering with producers Clint Bierman (The Grift), Kristina Stykos, and Phil Henry, she has chosen to bypass the traditional industry grind—big tours, record deals, and relocation—in favor of an independent, soul-driven approach. Despite no label, corporate sponsorship, or major promotion, Melissa D's soothing, heartfelt songs have reached thousands of listeners worldwide. Her music has been featured on Vermont Public, Women of Substance Radio, and Sip-N-Stream, among others. Her song <strong>\"Little Girl\"</strong> (the title track from her solo EP) was nominated for Best Song of America (American Roots genre) in the 2021 InterContinental Music Awards."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/feixpG4Ou1s","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond music, Melissa is deeply committed to animal rescue and humanitarian causes. She dedicated 20 years to public service as a counselor and advocate, making a lasting impact on countless lives."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Melissa D:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.melissadmusic.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCTQFmQ0ciUKT5qoN1ChUFrg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/melissadsings/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/melissadsings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> ​"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7tAhTOKKCZa50guCRWunwn?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"400096","title":"The Trouble Notes Announce U.S. Summer Festival Debut and Tease Ambitious New Fantasy-Inspired Project","date":"2025-04-28","lead":"The world folk fusion trio returns to the States with electrifying performances, new music, and a fantasy storytelling vision.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/400096/ab95e6468728142e93925f27f3025d66.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The world folk fusion trio returns to the States with electrifying performances, new music, and a fantasy storytelling vision."},{"t":"p","html":"(April 28, 2025) — Internationally acclaimed trio <a href=\"http://www.thetroublenotes.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Trouble Notes</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>will return to the United States this summer for debut performances at festivals from coast to coast.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"A <strong>world folk fusion powerhouse</strong> known for their <strong>electrifying performances</strong> and <strong>emotive musical storytelling</strong>, they've become a <strong>must-see act</strong> at major international festivals and concert stages alike. The group has thrilled audiences in over <strong>35 countries</strong> and performed live on <strong>national television in the USA, Japan, Brazil, and across Europe</strong>."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/741694/large-f6c2f5ffd23427f5c4fd5bd873eb51d9.png","alt":"The Trouble Notes USA Tour Dates"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Highlights and Achievements:</strong>"},{"t":"list","items":["Opened for music legends <strong>Jethro Tull</strong>, <strong>Rodrigo y Gabriela</strong>, and <strong>America&nbsp;</strong>on their European tours.&nbsp;","Performed at prominent festivals including <strong>Glastonbury (UK), Boomtown (UK), &nbsp;Castlefest (NL), </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?t=62&amp;v=T0WtSrRqi2o\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Echos et Merveilles (FR)</strong></a><strong> and Fusion Festival (DE)</strong>","Featured live on major TV networks including <a href=\"https://wgntv.com/midday-news/midday-fix-live-music-from-the-trouble-notes-2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>WGN-TV Chicago</strong></a><strong>, NHK Japan</strong>, and <strong>Globo Brazil</strong>.&nbsp;","Their second studio album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5luk6F956IAyTWoh35llWW\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Liberty Awaits</strong></em></a>, was hailed by <a href=\"https://earmilk.com/2023/05/22/the-trouble-notes-release-highly-anticipated-album-liberty-awaits/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Earmilk Magazine</strong></a> as <em>“a transcendent fusion of global folk traditions, rich with emotional depth and cultural resonance.”</em>&nbsp;","BBC Radio’s <strong>Faye Hatcher</strong> called their performance <em>“an absolute must-see! Their music takes you on a breathtaking journey around the world.”</em>"]},{"t":"p","html":"Now, standing on the brink of their third major release, the band is preparing to unveil their most ambitious project yet — <strong>a fantasy epic of their own creation</strong>. This time, they are not merely narrating real-world experiences but inventing an entire fictitious world, with their music serving as the <strong>soundtrack to a grand narrative adventure</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Their single, <strong>\"<a href=\"https://americana-uk.com/video-premiere-the-trouble-notes-storm-searching\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Storm Searching</strong></a>,\"</strong> is the first glimpse into this imaginative world, already thrilling fans across their European tour."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4jdhZj0UCo4Q8GnCXs2X9G?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"\"Our music has always been described as a journey. We’ve never allowed ourselves to be confined by a single genre, and that creative freedom has enabled us to bring our sound in a direction that best suits our storytelling. We wanted to deepen our craft by writing our own story, a tale born from both our experiences and the vibrant fantasy and cosplay communities we’ve become a part of in Europe. This new body of work is a soundtrack to our very own world.\"","cite":"- Bennet Cerven"},{"t":"p","html":"While the full story album is slated for release in <strong>2026</strong>, this summer’s U.S. tour will offer audiences a <strong>first taste </strong>of the new material, interwoven with the band’s already vast and emotionally powerful repertoire."},{"t":"p","html":"Audiences across America can expect a fusion of <strong>new adventures and timeless energy</strong> as The Trouble Notes return to share the next chapter of their ever-evolving journey"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/djRgJhEOEUU","height":""},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Trouble Notes:"},{"t":"p","html":"Formed in 2013 and hailing from <strong>three different continents</strong>, The Trouble Notes bring an unmatched global spirit to their music. The group is composed of <strong>American violinist and vocalist Bennet Cerven</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;German guitarist Florian Eisenschmidt</strong>, and <strong>Australian drummer Julian Lardis</strong>. Known for their electrifying live performances, they have captivated festival audiences worldwide, delivering high-energy shows that transcend borders and genres."},{"t":"p","html":"Blending emotive storytelling with dynamic, high-energy instrumentals, <strong>The Trouble Notes</strong> craft musical journeys that transport listeners to other worlds. Their debut album,<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.musicmusingsandsuch.com/musicmusingsandsuch/2018/2/17/interview-the-trouble-notes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Lose Your Ties</strong></em></a>, chronicled Cerven’s transformation from a Wall Street analyst to a globe-trotting musician chasing a dream. Their sophomore album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5luk6F956IAyTWoh35llWW\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Liberty Awaits</em></a>, wove together real-life stories of immigration and the characters they encountered on the road."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7i1WiSQVIHt4bZz8DhuylF?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with The Trouble Notes</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/...\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://instagram.com/thetroublenotes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://facebook.com/thetroublenotes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@TheTroubleNotes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/T0WtSrRqi2o","height":""}],"contact":null},{"id":"383245","title":"\"Breaking Hearts\": Stephen Thomas Delivers a Bold Anthem for Letting Go","date":"2025-04-25","lead":"\"Breaking Hearts\" is a bold track about breaking free from toxic ties and reclaiming your life.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/383245/0bd395586d62ad8b47ad5749ff14a4bf.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Breaking Hearts\" is a bold track about breaking free from toxic ties and reclaiming your life."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/op_ZEYZegos","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (March 7, 2025) - Pioneer of the \"Universal\" genre, artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=YTInGlyeR_Oow3q_1Wlt9g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen</strong> <strong>Thomas</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>is back with a striking new single, <strong>\"Breaking Hearts\",</strong> a raw, genre-blending anthem from his upcoming EP, <em>The Universal Me</em>. The track dives into the hard truths of walking away from toxic relationships, dead-end jobs, and anything else that holds you back."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6MiuL2cjgcSGasS6ol0DT7?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Recently named as an <em>\"Artist To Watch in 2025\"</em> by <strong><em>The Source</em></strong>, \"Breaking Hearts\" showcases Stephen's versatility as he mixes alternative pop, rock, and hip-hop, channeling the energy of Post Malone, Tech N9ne, MGK, and Fall Out Boy. Thomas’s signature \"universal\" sound, paired with emotionally charged lyrics, creates an anthem for anyone ready to reclaim their life. \"Stay away from those who drain you of the energy you need to function—for yourself and those who love you,\" says Stephen. \"People who don’t care never want you to win, while those who do will always push you past your limits to make you better in the end.\""},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723476/large-2230bdc50c6eb88b295d4b60ac7c620f.png","alt":"Breaking Hearts Album Cover_20241202_121315_0000.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723476/preview-81b1ef2fb5b9a49e87953f8df94c7b59.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723472/large-0047044f17d10334e68a353108b4f6e2.jpg","alt":"Photo Feb 11 2025, 9 31 22 PM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723472/preview-618f4874209dc5ef0c65788ec0b430fb.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723473/large-0bc57f3fad0733f299f1cb0a5d9bdfb2.jpg","alt":"Photo Feb 11 2025, 8 25 00 PM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723473/preview-b06ea861fb0aac7eeaf3be9f9635d4c7.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723474/large-18df11a01ce0862e3a9518b57be70fb1.jpg","alt":"Photo Feb 11 2025, 9 24 07 PM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723474/preview-4876da5b47a177ecde033be5e2730904.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723475/large-65835b014f29ad5f4cbba3906adcf2a9.jpg","alt":"20250211_215721.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723475/preview-29e8df9510fa1a31a382dcb8c24535c7.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723477/large-3d16980f4651d24e8c85c7b820d6773a.jpg","alt":"Photo Feb 11 2025, 9 31 34 PM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723477/preview-ebffd4d4c5a2cf5a3b53057d12933fa1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723478/large-12ed0be3e2ace0d120734eeed4d5b88f.jpg","alt":"20250211_214817.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723478/preview-fad7eb2ada138ab812bba332394e4ce3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723479/large-e7a710f84fc6167583686d8867ad1c2b.jpg","alt":"Photo Feb 11 2025, 9 44 49 PM (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723479/preview-df04e4e9d0b64ea35d731f43a45fbee2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723480/large-ee13d1f80fa930e20e4068222ff5eb3e.jpg","alt":"20250211_212309.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723480/preview-0f4a13000f41b04b6ef6505a0df35bdd.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Fans can look forward to the upcoming April 25 release of the music video, directed by Will Thomas, that brings that message to life. Scenes shift between quiet moments of self-reflection and powerful shots of breaking free—from relationships, expectations, and everything in between. It’s not just a breakup song; it’s a declaration of independence."},{"t":"p","html":"The release follows his well-received single <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=06882f0f28c442d1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Stay Strong\"</a>, which resonated with fans for its honest take on resilience. A five-time Grammy-considered artist, Stephen continues to carve out his space in the industry with fearless creativity and personal storytelling."},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>Cover art and images from behind the scenes of the \"Breaking Hearts\" music video</em>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://symphony.to/stephen-thomas/breaking-hearts","label":"STREAM ON ALL MAJOR PLATFORMS","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Stephen Thomas:"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676846/large-55a595b43551877ff75bb9984341f332.jpg","alt":"Photo by Josh Hanna"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=oHBViFwQQaaIjt97y8p4Og\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a> is an artist redefining genre boundaries and commanding attention across the music industry. Hailing from Charleston, West Virginia, and recently named an <strong>“Artist to Watch in 2025”</strong> by <strong><em>The Source</em></strong>, Stephen is a pioneering voice in what he calls the Universal genre—a blend of sonic influences that continues to evolve with his latest foray into rock and alternative music."},{"t":"p","html":"His transition into the rock space is already making waves. Stephen’s debut alternative record,<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3cqqiH32fFqe2fHfBCXWWP?si=75a692df14ee45a6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>&nbsp;“Back Home,”</strong></a>&nbsp; as the video was featured on <strong>MTV</strong>, and the song is continuing to climb the <strong>Active Rock Radio charts into the Top 60</strong>. The single went viral on TikTok with <strong>over 500,000 views in just 24 hours</strong>, while both “Back Home” and his breakout anthem <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=783255a44a914f36\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Stay Strong”</strong></a>—a heartfelt tribute to military personnel, autoimmune warriors, and those facing mental health challenges—have been featured on <strong>major editorial playlists across Spotify, Amazon Music, Tidal, and more</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"His latest release, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6MiuL2cjgcSGasS6ol0DT7?si=768e41a678e24270\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Breaking Hearts,”</strong></a> builds on this momentum, showcasing a raw, emotive sound that reflects his bold artistic reinvention. Comparisons to artists like <strong>MGK</strong>, <strong>Jelly Roll</strong>, <strong>Carrie Underwood</strong>, and <strong>Shaboozey </strong>speak to his wide-ranging appeal and boundary-pushing creativity."},{"t":"p","html":"As a national touring artist, Stephen’s resume includes <strong>five Grammy Award considerations</strong> as an independent act, a <strong>#2 spot on the iTunes Charts</strong> with <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5PGeydtICzokuReD9TOiHW?si=4278bc4bba8f4826\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Best Days,”</strong></a> and global exposure through Revolt TV with his video for <strong>“Search Me.”</strong> &nbsp;From his early beginnings to signing with <strong>SkeeloMusik/Sony RED</strong> in 2013 and later finding his artistic home with <strong>Creative Hearts Entertainment</strong>, Stephen’s journey has been one of constant growth and reinvention."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond the music, Stephen’s story and sound have been spotlighted in MTV, Vibe Magazine, Swagger, Hype Magazine, Earmilk, V13, and The Source, among others. He’s performed alongside iconic names and walked red carpets at major events including the BET Live Experience."},{"t":"p","html":"Ten years into his career, Stephen continues to follow the advice that shaped his path: stay true to yourself. It’s a message that drives his music and fuels his mission to inspire the next generation of artists."},{"t":"p","html":"All of Stephen’s latest releases—including “Breaking Hearts,” “Back Home,” and “Stay Strong”—are available on Spotify, Apple Music, Amazon Music, Tidal, and all major platforms. For updates, videos, and exclusive content, visit the links below."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephen!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.stephentmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/StephenTMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/404?fromUrl=/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/StephenThomas1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://x.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>X</strong></a>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/Cv0cZdtuXQn/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"398538","title":"Rebekah Gilbert Breaks the Silence with “Secret Keeper” — A Haunting Anthem of Healing and Liberation","date":"2025-04-25","lead":"Nashville artist Rebekah Gilbert’s “Secret Keeper” is a gripping anthem of truth, healing, and reclaiming your voice.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/398538/eaaa00e8af32b8f04eb26d38de2f8ac2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Nashville artist Rebekah Gilbert’s “Secret Keeper” is a gripping anthem of truth, healing, and reclaiming your voice."},{"t":"p","html":"NASHVILLE, TN (April 25, 2025) – Nashville-based Americana artist <strong>Rebekah Gilbert</strong> is set to release her compelling new single <strong>“Secret Keeper”</strong> on Friday, April 25, 2025—a raw, intimate exploration of the secrets we carry and the courage it takes to finally set them down. The song is the title track of her forthcoming EP, a deeply personal body of work tracing the journey from silence to self-liberation.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2DDj38HD9cWuIZH82aLKPu?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Blending haunting lyricism with a gently building pop-country sensibility, “Secret Keeper” lands sonically between the emotive landscapes of Patty Griffin, Allison Russell, and Brandi Carlile. Produced by Nicole Witt and featuring contributions from a stellar studio band, the track is as musically lush as it is lyrically vulnerable. “'<em>Secret Keeper' is an incredibly personal song and the title track of my EP—a collection of seven songs that explore the weight of secrets, the grip of addiction, the pull of generational cycles, the fragility of relationships, and the persistence of dreams,”&nbsp;</em>Gilbert shares. <em>“I co-wrote it with Keri Wooster after a powerful conversation about what it means to carry childhood secrets into adulthood. This song is about that turning point—realizing we no longer have to bear the silence or the shame.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Earlier this year, Gilbert set the stage for her forthcoming EP with the release of <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0BKPaho9FyQzf1nDw0wYDQ?si=e1cd1c016a0b43ba\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Somebody Else’s House,”</strong></a> a haunting Southern Gothic tale co-written with <strong>Amanda Williams</strong>. Inspired by a family revelation about an ancestor's secret double life, the song explores themes of generational secrecy and inherited truths. With its raw, bluesy country sound and vivid lyricism—<em>“190 proof, bottled up under the same roof”</em>—the track introduces the emotional terrain that “Secret Keeper” now expands upon."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/PM50fOlyBhY","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Where “Somebody Else’s House” peers into the past, “Secret Keeper” turns inward. More than a confessional, it’s a reclamation. Anchored by Gilbert’s evocative vocals and stirring storytelling, the song confronts the emotional toll of hidden trauma and the liberating power of truth. With lines like <em>“If I tell the truth, will I be free? / Or do I lock it up and hide the key?”</em> it deepens the EP’s throughline of mental health, breaking generational cycles, and stepping into the light after years in silence."},{"t":"p","html":"The song’s release marks a pivotal moment for Gilbert as she steps more boldly into her voice as a writer and truth-teller. Backed by a team of respected musicians including<strong>&nbsp;Jimbo Hart&nbsp;</strong>on bass, <strong>Sol Philcox-Littlefield</strong> on guitar, Grayson Wright on keys, Jon Davis on drums, Nicole Witt on violin and background vocals, and <strong>Austin Motlow</strong> on recording and mixing, “Secret Keeper” sets the stage for what promises to be a soul-stirring EP rollout."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/739339/large-1e082fedd52607ba521a7f09a34fe247.png","alt":"Cover art for \"Secret Keeper\" by Rebekah Gilbert"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Rebekah Gilbert:"},{"t":"p","html":"Rebekah Gilbert has been captivating audiences with her powerful songs, poetry, and prose since 2009. Her writing invites readers to reflect on their own journeys, while her soulful vocals pull listeners into a deep, personal experience. Drawing from the Americana genre, Rebekah’s music has been compared to the confessional lyrics of Patty Griffin; the soothing, moody vocals of Norah Jones; and the emotional, soulful delivery of Brandi Carlile. In February 2025, Rebekah released her first cover—a haunting rendition of Gnarls Barkley’s “Crazy”. Just a month later, she unveiled “Somebody Else’s House,” the lead single from her upcoming EP Secret Keeper, which offers a bold new glimpse into her evolving artistry.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Based in Nashville, Rebekah performs both locally and throughout the region, with plans to expand to national stages. Beyond performing, she’s passionate about creating spaces where others can share their stories and be heard."},{"t":"p","html":"A champion for late bloomers, Rebekah is passionate about encouraging others to pursue their dreams, no matter when they start. She often shares her own story of achieving goals and finding fulfillment later in life. Her first poetry book, <a href=\"https://a.co/d/gmjwUko\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Poems from the Back Pew: A Journey from Faith to Doubt and Beyond</strong></em></a>, is available in her shop and on Amazon. The companion EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/35DMxUNcmjKg3LStgoKuwg?si=BeHH8NgiTESYeEMmCFjdPQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Year of Jubilee</strong></em></a>, recorded in Nashville, is available on all streaming platforms. Both the poetry collection and the EP explore her journey of breaking free from evangelical beliefs, and the personal revolution that led her to a new sense of freedom."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.rebekahgilbert.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/RebekahGilbertWritingandMusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/rebekahlgilbert/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@gilbertrebekah\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@rebekahgilbertmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3HNZCei9Vhafw0UVcbBcZV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"396758","title":"Leanne Wilkins & the Weathered Release Full-Length Album, The Art of Letting Go","date":"2025-04-21","lead":"An intimate and soul-stirring journey through grief, healing, and rebirth.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/396758/b8d5ff1423384bd8ed3a8bf0dc221334.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An intimate and soul-stirring journey through grief, healing, and rebirth."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2MMOJFOmn8yMYytyycdBAm?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"SEATTLE (April 18, 2025) – Seattle-based roots rock &amp; soul band <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lwtheweathered/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Leanne Wilkins &amp; the Weathered</strong></a> unveil their long-anticipated full-length album, <em>The Art of Letting Go</em>, exploring the intertwined themes of shadow and light, grief and healing, and death and rebirth."},{"t":"p","html":"Written primarily on piano, lead singer-songwriter Leanne’s first musical love, the album marks a powerful return to songwriting after struggling with creative blocks for several years. Across eight poignant tracks, Leanne opens a window into her internal world, grieving the death of her younger sister, processing the complexities around her family of origin, and facing confusion while becoming a mother during a time of great societal upheaval. Leanne also touches on esoteric experiences and connections that guided her to pursue her calling.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Drawing from the golden age of ‘70s rock and modern soul sensibilities, <em>The Art of Letting Go</em> blends intimate storytelling with lush arrangements. Tracks like <strong>“Push &amp; Pull,”</strong> <strong>“Daughter,”</strong> and <strong>“Alt-Reality”</strong> delve into emotional surrender, generational trauma, and the fractured state of American culture. Others, like <strong>“Free Spirit”</strong> and <strong>“Light in the Darkness,”</strong> offer hopeful anthems for transformation and resilience."},{"t":"quote","html":"“The Art of Letting Go is a personal philosophy woven throughout the songs and stories in this album. It’s a practice that has become my lifesaver through periods of grief, uncertainty and change. Letting go requires releasing our desire to control, surrendering to the unknown, and cultivating absolute trust in the unfolding of life.”","cite":"- Leanne Wilkins"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/736326/large-35a1bd844c87487c7f9225959ace7994.png","alt":"Cover art by Kate Birch"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by icons including <strong>Carole King</strong>, <strong>Elton John</strong>, and <strong>Bill Withers</strong>, the album’s warm vintage tones and piano-forward sound mark a natural evolution from the band’s previous guitar-driven EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5leBsi4D5pL81KMwhzy84w?si=jamv8nyeT0-FuInh8Bc4Xw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Ordinary Grey</em></a>. Also drawing from modern artists like <strong>Grace Potter</strong> and <strong>Neal Frances,</strong> the result is a grounded, genre-defying soundscape that feels equally classic and contemporary."},{"t":"p","html":"Produced in Seattle at <strong>Avast and Nels Motel Studios</strong>, <em>The Art of Letting Go</em> was co-produced by <strong>Leanne Wilkins</strong> and <strong>Ben Loshin</strong>, recorded and mixed by <strong>Robb Davidson</strong>, and mastered by <strong>Rachel Field at Resonant Mastering</strong>. All songs were written by <strong>Leanne Wilkins</strong>."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Writing and recording this album opened my eyes to our limitless capacity to evolve as musicians...my songwriting, vocal ability, and confidence in my authentic expression have only sweetened with age. I think I’ve proven, at least to myself, it’s never the ‘wrong time,’ or ‘too late’ to make incredible music.”","cite":"- Leanne Wilkins"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5YaZ0wImCHMU87MefZlaKn?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Leanne Wilkins &amp; the Weathered:"},{"t":"p","html":"Since 1998, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4beFDwHsBf5lUo35DdX5ab?si=D1qoHO2dQa6LGDiE0zn0Uw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Leanne Wilkins</strong></a> has captivated audiences with her haunting melodies and lyrical depth. The Seattle-based artist’s latest project, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5YaZ0wImCHMU87MefZlaKn?si=LNyYZFqFSjq4jQhPhBzuLA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Leanne Wilkins &amp; the Weathered</strong></a>, blends roots rock with blues and soul influences, channeling a style that’s deeply personal and universally resonant. Her lyrics explore relationships, personal growth, and the search for truth, bringing warmth and authenticity to a sound that defies easy classification."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>The Weathered</em> recently completed their full-length album, <em><strong>The Art of Letting Go</strong></em>, a collection of songs exploring themes of death and rebirth, pain and redemption, shadow and light. Written during the pandemic, <em>The Art of Letting Go</em> took Leanne on a journey back to her roots, reconnecting with her love of piano and reflecting on the complexities of becoming a mother amid a time of widespread division."},{"t":"p","html":"Through <em>The Art of Letting Go</em>, Leanne channels her grief over her family of origin, including the death of her younger sister, and the questions she faced as a mother in an uncertain world. This album builds on <strong>The Weathered</strong>’s previous EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5leBsi4D5pL81KMwhzy84w?si=jamv8nyeT0-FuInh8Bc4Xw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Ordinary Grey</strong></em></a>, while delving into more experimental territory, with keys taking center stage alongside contributions from talented local musicians, including <strong>Derek Pulvino</strong> (guitar), <strong>Clint Hoyler</strong> (bass), and <strong>Ben Loshin</strong> (drums/co-producer). The record also features some incredible guest musicians: <strong>Tim Kennedy</strong> (Hammond B3), <strong>Josh Tvrdy</strong> (guitar), <strong>Charlie Smith</strong> (keys), and <strong>Abby Gundersen</strong> (strings)."},{"t":"p","html":"With <em>The Art of Letting Go</em>, Leanne and her band explore the many faces of love and self-acceptance, blending classic rock influences with modern soul for a listening experience that is as emotionally complex as it is musically rich. The album brings a message of healing and hope to the world after a particularly dark time in recent human history, promising to deepen the band’s connection with audiences in Seattle and beyond."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DHufGoeR5bV/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Leanne Wilkins &amp; the Weathered!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://theweatheredband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lwtheweathered/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/theweatheredband/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-MNuhJRnITz1wRye5E4VKg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5YaZ0wImCHMU87MefZlaKn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/leanne-wilkins-the-weathered/1098272476\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://leannewilkins.bandcamp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Bandcamp</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"397005","title":"Blake Smeltz Releases Stirring New Single, “Good Faith”","date":"2025-04-18","lead":"“Good Faith” explores love, loss, and staying grounded through life’s toughest trials","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/397005/d760afa2a6ae0632805fa6a59686e08f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"“Good Faith” explores love, loss, and staying grounded through life’s toughest trials"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3IgvkUPIbkIDh3yilHIi9T?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"NASHVILLE, TN (April 18, 2025) - Country artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6VtPWvA4PQlpSmWA85Ugni?si=Osp37CrKRd6fd9Ij9XNBPQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Blake Smeltz</strong></a>, continues to establish his place in the genre with the release of his latest single, <strong>“Good Faith.”</strong> ​"},{"t":"p","html":"Sweet, powerful and relatable, the track blends tender storytelling with Smeltz’s signature raspy vocals, echoing influences like <strong>Luke Combs</strong>, <strong>Zach Bryan</strong> and <strong>Gavin Adcock,</strong> while continuing to define a voice all his own."},{"t":"p","html":"The single tells the story of a man looking back on a lost love, a woman named Faith, who served as a partner and a guiding light. Through vivid imagery and heartfelt lyrics, Smeltz traces the emotional terrain of their relationship, her passing, and how her memory keeps him grounded."},{"t":"p","html":"With lines like <em>“I’ll stay sober, I’ll get older, I’ll keep that devil up off my shoulder / Just trying to keep this faith—good faith,”</em> the song captures the weight of grief, the resolve of growth, and the struggle to stay true to oneself. Set against a stripped-down, soulful arrangement, Smeltz leans into real vulnerability and resilience with equal force."},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Good Faith’ is for those who are lost but have someone, or had someone, who helped keep their head on straight,” says Smeltz. “This is not only a song that’s relatable, it tells a story that’s real.”","cite":"- Blake Smeltz"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/736608/large-11e1573e0d69ff31b8b7a7182e4c5b79.jpeg","alt":"Cover Art for \"Good Faith.\""},{"t":"p","html":"“Good Faith” was produced by <strong>Charlotte Avenue Entertainment and David Flint</strong>. It's the second single from Smeltz’s upcoming album, <em><strong>Heartbreak Highway</strong></em>, slated for release in July. With this track, Smeltz continues to establish himself as an exceptionally honest and sonically grounded new voice in country music."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/707052/large-d929b5d61a620096d21059cf5ad41f4f.jpg","alt":"Blake Smeltz. Image by Colby Smeltz."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6VtPWvA4PQlpSmWA85Ugni?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/FX2XsLv4gPk","height":""},{"t":"h3","html":"About Blake Smeltz:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/blakesmeltz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Blake Smeltz</strong></a>, a native of Evington, Virginia, has always felt a deep connection to nature, a bond that resonates throughout his music. A self-taught artist who wears his heart on his sleeve, Blake merges sharp songwriting with captivating storytelling to craft songs that are both authentic and engaging. His raspy voice and tenderhearted approach allow him to forge meaningful connections with listeners, drawing them into his world. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by country legends like <strong>Luke Combs</strong>, <strong>Zach Bryan</strong>, and <strong>Jason Aldean</strong>, Blake seamlessly navigates genres, blending elements of country-rock, singer-songwriter, and everything in between. In 2023, he debuted with <em><strong>Demos From the 434</strong></em>, a project that ignited his passion for music and set him on a promising path in country music. Blake’s artistry is a unique blend of Zach Bryan’s introspective lyrics and Luke Combs’ soulful style, enriched by his own powerful voice and heartfelt storytelling.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Outside of music, his passions for motorcycle rides, racecars, and life on the open road fuel his adventurous spirit and inspire his creative process. &nbsp;<br id=\"isPasted\">Rooted in the stillness of nature and the beauty of God’s creation, Blake channels these experiences into lyrics that resonate deeply with his audience. With his passion for music and a life lived boldly, Blake Smeltz is poised to take country music to exciting new horizons. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/blakesmeltz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Listening Links</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/blakesmeltz_music/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@blakesmeltzmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"389493","title":"Kristen Budde Unveils \"Regret,\" A Powerful Anthem About Letting Go and Moving Forward","date":"2025-04-11","lead":"Kristen Budde releases her introspective new single \"Regret\" reflecting on letting go of the past and embracing the present.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/389493/eefa912553c6f4546939d34cdfb3c95a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Kristen Budde releases her introspective new single \"Regret\" reflecting on letting go of the past and embracing the present."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Murfreesboro, TN (April 11, 2025)</strong> – Kristen Budde, the Tennessee-based singer/songwriter whose unique blend of Americana and Country music has captured hearts across the nation, is gearing up to release her latest single <strong>“Regret”</strong> on April 11, 2025. This reflective track, which explores the weight of past choices and the freedom of embracing the present, showcases Kristen’s unmistakable style—raw, honest, and deeply personal."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0WdkZOHdPx8L5HMgaalcYu?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The inspiration for “Regret” came after a trip back to the town where Kristen began her adult life. Revisiting familiar places stirred up a lot of “what ifs,” leading her to write a song that speaks to those who wrestle with the road not taken. As Kristen puts it, <em>“We can focus on what might have been, but it’s a dead-end road because we’ll never truly know. All we can do is let go of what’s behind us and move forward.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Kristen’s vocals have always been described as powerful yet vulnerable, and in “Regret,” she once again uses her voice to weave a story of introspection and hope. Reminiscent of Alison Krauss, Budde brings a delicate yet powerful quality to \"Regret,\" adding depth to its emotional reflection on the past. The track’s lush Americana instrumentation complements the personal theme—drawing listeners in with a sound that feels both intimate and expansive. <em>“I wanted to express the idea that all we really have is this moment, right now,”</em> Kristen shares. <em>“We can choose to live in the past and stay stuck, or we can use the present to start creating a life we want to live.”</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/730749/large-58e20b6fb82a97839b7dbe359adb3c81.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Regret\" by Kristen Budde. Imagery by Larry Budde."},{"t":"button","href":"https://vibe.to/regretbykristenbudde","label":"PRE-SAVE","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by Nicole Witt and engineered by Austin Motlow, “Regret” features a talented group of musicians, including Sol Philcox-Littlefield on guitars, Jimbo Hart on bass, Grayson Wright on piano, and Justin Holder on drums. Nicole Witt also lends her vocals on the track, adding depth to its emotional resonance. Mastered by Parachute Mastering, the single was recorded at Sundrop Sound Studio in Muscle Shoals, Alabama."},{"t":"quote","html":"“It’s easy to romanticize what we might have done differently in the past, but we have to trust that we did the best we could with what we knew. This song reminds us that no matter where we’ve been, we can always begin again.\"","cite":"Kristen Budde"},{"t":"p","html":"The single comes after Kristen’s highly praised debut EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3vWwjVeHureyaBFZMZLIOz?si=LjIcc-IiQQipmvPq_Bxc7w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Begin Again</strong></em></a>, which marked the start of her musical journey. As she looks ahead to her second album, due in 2026, “Regret” offers a glimpse of what’s to come. Kristen’s music continues to explore themes of personal growth, healing, and the courage to start anew.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1acunSmvzDImLiyfa7Qdad?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kristen Budde:"},{"t":"p","html":"Kristen Budde, Tennessee based singer/songwriter and multi-instrumentalist, crafts songs that are honest and thoughtful with lyrics that are woven together like a conversation with a close friend. With vocals and melodies that can be both powerful and gentle, Kristen’s music is a blend of Americana and Country and her voice has been described as bringing life and light into a room. Kristen has a passion for creating joy-filled connection through the power of music and wholeheartedly believes that music has the ability to heal us. Budde made her musical debut in 2022 when she released her first single<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7j2mwnTaZaIuu9cUkJhxpI?si=9e64a5ef66164353\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\"Come Sit Down at My Table\"</strong></a> which delves into our need to belong and be seen and heard. Her debut 6-song EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3vWwjVeHureyaBFZMZLIOz?si=LjIcc-IiQQipmvPq_Bxc7w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Begin Again</strong></em></a> was released throughout 2023 and was a fulfillment a life long dream. The songs on <em>Begin Again</em> will take listeners on a journey through wrestling with fear, letting go and finding the courage to truly live. Kristen hopes these songs will inspire courage for listeners to take brave steps to build lives they love and will give hope that it's never too late to begin again."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/AoRVTjuz7ms","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Kristen is currently releasing singles and preparing to record her second album set to release in 2026. When Kristen’s not busy working on music, you can probably find her sipping coffee on her back porch or singing silly songs she made up for her family and pets!&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.kristenbuddemusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">WEBSITE</a> | <a href=\"https://instagram.com/kristenbuddemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/kristenbuddemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"394279","title":"Read More","date":"2025-04-11","lead":"\"Can't Hide Beautiful\" is an energetic genre-blending track that showcases the dynamic sound of Michael Gilas","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/394279/67e2e921ebbcc3fb8d221227b1eab98f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Can't Hide Beautiful\" is an energetic genre-blending track that showcases the dynamic sound of Michael Gilas"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1IBkkOqVaYZfFCfcjwmh8b?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"San Diego, CA (April 11, 2025) – <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/412oFoFK213H1r4PBmz9Bn?si=TtZIIBFYSAifsPFG0E5Rew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Michael Gilas</strong></a> announces the release of his latest single, <strong>\"Can't Hide Beautiful\"</strong> from his upcoming debut album, <strong><em>231 Kensington Road</em></strong>. The track is a glimpse into Michael's musical journey post-recovery from a life-threatening neck injury, showcasing his ability to transform personal adversity into uplifting art."},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded in Nashville the song brings an upbeat, energetic sound that blends elements of rock and pop for a distinctive sound. Lyrically, the song's message brings to light inner beauty - that you can't hide what's inside of you. &nbsp;<em>\"you can't hide beautiful, what you are inside is all over you no matter what you do\"</em> is the hook of the chorus as Gilas seemingly writes about his muse, singing <em>\"tonight you will be mine\"</em>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/732810/large-e6b231162e65a631f813703996e412fa.png","alt":"Cover art for \"Can't Hide Beautiful\" by Michael Gilas"},{"t":"p","html":"Michael's life took a dramatic turn in December 2021 when he sustained a severe neck injury. The harrowing experience, filled with physical and mental anguish, became a turning point for him. <em>\"Music saved my life because I had nothing else,\"</em> he shares. Michael's journey of recovery, marked by resilience and hope, is woven into the fabric of his music, offering inspiration to others facing similar struggles."},{"t":"p","html":"Influenced by iconic artists such as <strong>The Eagles</strong>, <strong>Marvin Gaye</strong>, <strong>Carole King</strong>, <strong>Steely Dan</strong>, and <strong>Fleetwood Mac</strong>, Michael's sound is a testament to his diverse musical upbringing on Long Island. His early exposure to a wide array of genres is reflected in the eclectic mix of styles present in this single and his upcoming album, '<strong>231 Kensington Road</strong>.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Michael's creative process is meticulous, starting with guitar noodling and evolving through collaboration with his producer and collaborator <strong>Allan Phillips</strong>. <em>\"It’s a long process but it’s a lot of fun,\" </em>Michael notes.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With plans to continue writing, recording, and exploring new sounds, Michael's ambition is to leave a lasting impact through his dedication to quality music."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/412oFoFK213H1r4PBmz9Bn?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Michael Gilas:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/412oFoFK213H1r4PBmz9Bn?si=TtZIIBFYSAifsPFG0E5Rew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Michael Gilas</strong></a> is pleased to announce his debut album, '<strong>231 Kensington Road'&nbsp;</strong>— a sonic testament to his versatility as an artist. It was at this address that he discovered the musicians who would inspire him. Born and raised amidst the creative energy of this iconic location, each song embodies a unique musical exploration, inviting listeners on a vibrant journey through his musical universe, where rhythm, melody, and emotion converge in celebration."},{"t":"p","html":"Drawing inspiration from iconic figures such as <strong>The Beatles</strong>, <strong>Eagles</strong>, <strong>Steely Dan</strong>, <strong>The Doobie Brothers</strong>, <strong>Joni Mitchell</strong>, <strong>Fleetwood Mac</strong>, and <strong>Elton John</strong>, Michael pays tribute to their influence through his compositions."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>'</strong><strong>231 Kensington Road</strong><strong>'</strong> transcends mere album status; it encapsulates a profound journey—an ode to the transformative power of music to inspire, uplift, and unite."},{"t":"p","html":"The first song of the album, <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5hcbemBJX7Lqhcd8lXrFGz?si=9a0d66abe4fc4cfc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Let's Get Back To Us</strong></a><strong>\"</strong>, is just a taste of Michael's sonic vision. Follow his profile to join him on this exciting journey!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Michael Gilas!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/412oFoFK213H1r4PBmz9Bn?go=1&amp;sp_cid=fb0b24b82f029a635427e4c09d0b2224&amp;utm_source=embed_player_p&amp;utm_medium=desktop&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=554e7e4f19d744d8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/michael-gilas/1756545844\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://michaelgilas.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://michaelgilas.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"397027","title":"Nanná Millano Releases \"Wild Fire\": A Cinematic, Art-Pop Protest for a Planet on Fire","date":"2025-04-10","lead":"“Wild Fire” portrays a chilling visual of climate grief, ancestral wisdom, and a world on the brink.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/397027/3fad08a8644f44492692ca24f425850b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"“Wild Fire” portrays a chilling visual of climate grief, ancestral wisdom, and a world on the brink."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>PARIS, FRANCE (April 11, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>- Multidisciplinary artist and singer-songwriter Nanná Millano delivers a searing wake-up call with her new single <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4h4uw6UmZC20jgPGSSAeqc?si=40129bc04e834557\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Wild Fire”</strong></a>, out now via Believe. Blending evocative lyricism with atmospheric, art-pop production, \"Wild Fire\" is a raw, cinematic meditation on environmental collapse, climate anxiety, and the spiritual crisis of our time."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/d1nNPdzLEB4","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Echoing the urgency of <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2019/09/23/763452863/transcript-greta-thunbergs-speech-at-the-u-n-climate-action-summit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Greta Thunberg’s 2019 address</a> to world leaders, “Wild Fire” channels the same emotional intensity: <em>“Our house is on fire… I don’t want you to be hopeful. I want you to panic… and act as if our house is on fire. Because it is.”</em> Through haunting melodies and visceral lyrics, Nanná Millano transforms that call to action into an emotional experience — not just a warning, but a reckoning. The song doesn’t soothe; it stirs. It doesn’t ask for hope — it demands awakening."},{"t":"p","html":"Rooted in personal experience and cultural memory, \"Wild Fire\" draws on the devastation Millano witnessed in both Los Angeles and the Amazon. The lyrics read like an ancestral warning — stark, poetic, and urgent. <em>“We've been told... We've been told/And we didn't believe/Now we are seeing with our own eyes\"&nbsp;</em>she sings, <em>“Wild fire / It will catch you in your bed.”</em> A visceral blend of protest song, prayer, and nightmare. “As a Brazilian, I've experienced the despair of seeing the Amazon burning for years,” says Millano. “When we see the forest burn, we often don’t realize it’s also the home of many humans and living beings. We forgot that nature is our primal home. We are nature.”"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4h4uw6UmZC20jgPGSSAeqc?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The accompanying music video pays homage to American director <strong>David Lynch</strong>, whose passing in January from wildfire-related complications became a symbolic focal point for the project. Shot in a French castle and forest, the video is rich in surrealist imagery — a trapped butterfly, a blindfolded figure, a burning empire — and includes real footage of fires in Los Angeles and the Amazon. “There is deep symbolism in everything happening in Hollywood and the United States right now,” says Millano. \"I saw the american writer <strong>Jean Hegland</strong> say in a recent interview here in France that <em>“Hollywood on fire is a fairly powerful symbol of capitalism which devours itself”</em> and I completely agree with her. This is a moment to rethink our ways of living, learn from the fire, and rebuild differently.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Committed to action as well as art, Millano is using the video to support <strong>IPAM (Amazon Environmental Research Institute)</strong> — a Brazilian NGO working toward sustainable development in the Amazon.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/736615/large-211814f5f1eb4a8091a7de0e36214286.jpg","alt":"Photo by Maria Ribeiro"},{"t":"p","html":"With echoes of<strong>&nbsp;Björk</strong>, <strong>Fiona Apple</strong>, and <strong>Milton Nascimento</strong>, “Wild Fire” deepens Nanná Millano’s commitment to lyrical storytelling, emotional resonance, and socially conscious artistry. Produced by <strong>Andrew Gowie</strong> (<em>The 25th Hour</em>, Grammy-nominated for his work with Drake), the single marks the first release from her forthcoming sophomore album and signals a bold evolution in her sound. It follows the success of her 2024 debut,<strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/19NF6GxGQRrkDvlSlQ2FR7?si=oHnU99_gRYGe7DP0rgsjLQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Can’t Translate Saudade&nbsp;</em></strong></a>— a genre-blending exploration of Brazilian identity through themes of longing, love, and life away from home. Hailed for its poetic depth and sonic richness, the album featured renowned musicians <strong>Carlos Malta</strong> and <strong>Rafael Barata</strong>, solidifying Millano’s emergence as a singular voice on the global stage."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Nanná Millano:"},{"t":"p","html":"Nanná Millano is a Brazilian-born artist, singer, and songwriter currently based in Paris. With a career that bridges Brazil, the United States, and France, she weaves a distinctive musical identity—rooted in her Brazilian heritage and shaped by a global perspective. Her background in film and performing arts brings a strong narrative thread to her work, enriching both her songwriting and live performances with emotional depth and visual storytelling."},{"t":"p","html":"Her sound draws inspiration from a wide spectrum of artists, including Norah Jones, Björk, Tom Jobim, and Caetano Veloso. The result is a sonic palette that feels both nostalgic and forward-looking—ancestral yet contemporary—moving fluidly between sunny romantic melodies and lunar, shamanic soundscapes."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/736616/large-0a8660ec56500a9b5eebeda2e44eeb7c.jpg","alt":"Foto do Perfil Outubro 2024 (1).jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"In 2024, Nanná released her debut album, <em><strong>Can’t Translate Saudade</strong></em>, a deeply personal and cinematic body of work that explores the emotional complexities of a transatlantic love story shaped by longing. Distributed globally by Believe and available on vinyl, the album features 12 original tracks that blend elements of Bossa Nova, Tropicália, Funk, Jazz, and Pop. It showcases collaborations with acclaimed Brazilian musicians such as <strong>Carlos Malta</strong> (Hermeto Pascoal, Gilberto Gil, Lenine), <strong>Rafael Barata</strong> (Herbie Hancock, Esperanza Spalding, Roberta Sá), <strong>Simone Sou</strong> (Chico César, Bixiga 70), and singer<strong>&nbsp;Giuliano Eriston</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/19NF6GxGQRrkDvlSlQ2FR7?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The album’s release at the iconic Sunset-Sunside jazz club in Paris marked Nanná’s entry into the international scene, followed by a tour through Brazil. Her music captures the duality of saudade—that quintessentially Brazilian emotion of longing and nostalgia—evoking memory and melancholy for Brazilian audiences, while introducing international listeners to its poetic mystique."},{"t":"p","html":"A passionate advocate for female representation in the arts, Nanná actively collaborates with women musicians and creators. In 2018, she conceived and hosted <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@OALBUMDASMULHERESINCRIVEIS\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>O Álbum das Mulheres Incríveis (“The Album of Incredible Women”)</strong></a>, a docuseries celebrating the stories of extraordinary women. It aired on Lifetime Brazil and is freely available on YouTube."},{"t":"p","html":"Her creative philosophy is grounded in empathy, non-violence, and emotional connection. She believes in the transformative power of affection and authentic communication—a belief that resonates through every note and lyric of her work."},{"t":"h3","html":"CONNECT WITH NANNÁ MILLANO:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://nannamillano.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/nannamillano\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5qKF89pXb54Z4d3TZLMmJa?si=Bv1kVwcSQMSEPvghEDmNvA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/nannamillano\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"394282","title":"Maggie Baugh Kicks Off Headlining World Tour with Electrifying New Music and Unforgettable Performances","date":"2025-03-31","lead":"With the release of her sophomore album on the horizon, country artist Maggie Baugh announces her headlining \"Entertainers Heart\" World Tour and debuts new music along the way","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/394282/7e98cbbd111d99f30f48da939d7ac8b3.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"With the release of her sophomore album on the horizon, country artist Maggie Baugh announces her headlining \"Entertainers Heart\" World Tour and debuts new music along the way"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>NASHVILLE, TN (April 1, 2025)</strong> - <a href=\"https://maggiebaugh.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maggie Baugh</strong></a>, the dynamic Nashville-based singer-songwriter, is thrilled to announce her headlining international \"Entertainers Heart\" tour, set to captivate audiences across the globe. As a rising star with a reputation for captivating audiences from dive bars to iconic venues, Baugh's tour promises to be an unforgettable experience. Her previous performances have included memorable appearances at the Grand Ole Opry and the Country Music Hall of Fame, as well as high-profile TV spots on <em>The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon</em> and <em>The Kelly Clarkson Show</em>. With her debut album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/06tODvTM3ow58i4pVy71M7?si=8NyDbQMRTxeQNIho76B1tA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Dear Me</strong></em></a>, already earning massive success, Maggie is now preparing to take fans on a new adventure with her forthcoming self-produced sophomore album, <strong><em>Entertainers Heart</em></strong>, blending raw rock elements with her signature style. The \"Entertainers Heart\" World Tour will showcase not just her impressive vocal range and songwriting ability but her undeniable charisma as a live performer. This tour marks a defining moment in Maggie’s career, as she’s ready to prove she’s more than just an artist—she’s a true entertainer."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/733773/large-715ecb05ac2ceba5be9367a3853041a4.png","alt":"Tour Poster Summer Add.png"},{"t":"button","href":"https://maggiebaugh.com/tour","label":"More Info + Tickets Here","color":"#d9651d"},{"t":"p","html":"In tandem with her tour and in anticipation of the upcoming album, Baugh released her latest single,<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0USoR8s1Tpt0fyuu66GSoW?si=dfda37f48c724333\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>&nbsp;\"Headstone,\"</strong></a> on March 21, 2025. This release marks a notable evolution from her previous music offering a raw, rock-infused sound that quickly propelled the track to the top, reaching the #1 spot on Amazon's Movers and Shakers chart. \"Headstone\" delves into the profound contemplation of one's legacy, inspired by Baugh's reflection on encapsulating a lifetime's worth of experiences into a few words on a headstone.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0USoR8s1Tpt0fyuu66GSoW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"\"At the end of someone’s life, I never understood how you could wrap up all their years and memories into a few words on a headstone. I decided to write my perspective, if it all ended tomorrow, what would I want someone to write on mine.\"","cite":"Maggie Baugh on what inspired her latest release \"Headstone\""},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/733774/large-477d68d80985b1983099e09c055bd6ba.jpeg","alt":"9976CD03-B562-4194-B88F-A4E6F718972D.jpeg"},{"t":"p","html":"Maggie Baugh’s recent singles, \"Headstone\" and <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/29FY0glXiMMIGCjKKp3jJa?si=5f352697bf304830\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\"Other Side of the World,\"</strong></a> both from her upcoming album, exemplify a raw, live-band sound, with tracks recorded in real-time using authentic instruments. This approach creates an immersive, dynamic listening experience that fans will have the opportunity to enjoy during her \"Entertainers Heart\" World Tour. As Maggie continues to explore new sounds and styles, her live performances promise to deliver the same energy and fresh perspective that define her latest work."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/9Vm1ecbvplM","height":""},{"t":"h3","html":"About Maggie Baugh:"},{"t":"p","html":"Maggie Baugh, a versatile talent spanning genres from Classical to Country, has captured the music industry's attention with her independent success. Hailing from Boca Raton, FL, Maggie's journey began at just 13 years old when she performed alongside Charlie Daniels, an experience that launched her into touring across South Florida. Her mastery of multiple instruments and social media prowess, particularly through her viral TikTok series “Finish the Lick,” has earned her over 40 million views across all platforms."},{"t":"p","html":"In 2023, Maggie released her debut album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/06tODvTM3ow58i4pVy71M7?si=T1oAXDerQ2iLjkR65uTEWw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Dear Me</em></strong></a>, which quickly gained traction, landing on major editorial playlists like Spotify's \"Next From Nashville,\" \"New Music Friday Country,\" Apple Music's \"New In Country,\" \"Fresh From Nashville,\" and Amazon Music's “Breakthrough Pop” and \"Breakthrough Country.\" The album achieved <strong>over 500K streams on its first day</strong> and hit <strong>#19 on the iTunes US Country Album Chart</strong> and <strong>#9 on the iTunes Australian Country Album Chart</strong>. Her success also led to her joining <strong>Home Free</strong> on three national tours, performing at iconic venues including the Ryman Auditorium."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4E82Kdena6yf0reUDRzbvW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Maggie’s live performances have solidified her presence in the country music scene, gracing prestigious stages such as the<strong>&nbsp;Grand Ole Opry</strong> and the <strong>Country Music Hall of Fame</strong>. In the past year alone, she's appeared on major platforms including the <strong>CMT Awards, The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon, Jimmy Kimmel Live!, the Today Show, Nissan Stadium, and The Kelly Clarkson Show</strong>. Recently, she caught the attention of Keith Urban, who invited her to join his tour as a utility player."},{"t":"p","html":"Looking ahead to 2025, Maggie is preparing to release her sophomore album, self-produced, and embark on her headlining “Entertainers Heart” World Tour. From dive bars to festivals and everything in between, Maggie is ready to show the world what it means to be a true entertainer.&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h2","html":"Connect with Maggie Baugh:"},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://maggiebaugh.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/maggie_baugh/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/likemaggie\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@maggiebaugh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@MaggieBaugh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>​"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"380808","title":"RIAH UNLEASHES POWERFUL NEW MUSIC VIDEO FOR “DADDY ISSUES”","date":"2025-03-28","lead":"Riah Unveils \"Daddy Issues\" - A Raw, Visceral Dive into Betrayal, Healing, and Power","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/380808/86969d3af40d672d9edd073d15271f2b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Riah Unveils \"Daddy Issues\" - A Raw, Visceral Dive into Betrayal, Healing, and Power"},{"t":"p","html":"DENVER, CO (March 28, 2025) – Rising dark-pop artist <strong>Riah</strong> unveils the gripping new music video for <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7itpC3vNdHE5vVxhS6JfJN?si=1bb848cd45564b94\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Daddy Issues”</strong></a> diving deeper into the raw, emotional themes of her 2024 album Trauma Bond—an unflinching exploration of toxic relationships, abandonment, and personal reckoning. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Following the success of her video <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PJM9lJP1u7g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">“Sertraline,”</a> “Daddy Issues” is a seductive yet haunting track, weaving together elements of dark pop and R&amp;B with sultry melodies and biting lyricism. The song is a cathartic release, confronting the pain of broken promises, cycles of betrayal, and the ultimate decision to let go. Gritty, intimate, and unapologetic - Riah unravels the painful realization that some people—no matter how much you love them—will never change. Sharp and unfiltered, the lyrics walk the line between resentment and reluctant nostalgia, navigating the turmoil of anger, grief, and empowerment. There’s exhaustion in cleaning up someone else’s mess, a lingering ache for what could have been, and, ultimately, the clarity that comes with letting go."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/xz1El91BAmg?si=dopvTyoauzWBBuM_","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"Both a confrontation and a farewell, it only made sense to direct this video with a moody, evocative aesthetic, that pushes boundaries and brings the song’s tension to life. RIAH utilizes chair and pole work to symbolize the delicate dance between power and vulnerability, visually mirroring the song’s tension between love and destruction, freedom and entrapment. Using movement as a form of storytelling—balancing strength and fragility, control and chaos - it’s a deliberate choice to challenge outdated narratives around sensuality and reclaim it as an act of agency. “The movement in this video isn’t just for aesthetics—it’s an expression of survival and self-ownership,” RIAH explains. “Pole work has been stigmatized, and is often misunderstood, but it’s an art form—one that embodies control, resilience, and storytelling. I wanted to challenge outdated narratives and reclaim the narrative of sensuality as power, rather than objectification.”"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Pole work is often misunderstood... It’s not just about performance—it’s about reclaiming power, turning pain into something beautiful. In this video, it represents breaking free from someone else’s chaos and stepping fully into my own.”","cite":"Riah"},{"t":"p","html":"At its core, “Daddy Issues” is about realizing that some people will never change—no matter how many chances they’re given. It’s a song for anyone who’s had to let go of someone they once loved, whether it be a parent, a partner, or a friend. It’s for anyone who’s watched someone self-destruct and finally stopped waiting for them to get it right.“This song is deeply personal, but I know I’m not alone in feeling the weight of broken promises,” RIAH shares. “There’s a unique kind of grief that comes with knowing someone will never be who you needed them to be. But there’s also power in walking away.... 'Daddy Issues' is the moment you stop making excuses for them. The moment you stop cleaning up their mess.”"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Production Credits:</strong> Riah (Main artist and Songwriter), Nergeim Evgeni (Composer), Quoc Truong (Mixing/Mastering); Chris Rasmussen (Videographer/Photographer)"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720712/large-ac66983c3759694a8571dc9cbb3c78f6.jpg","alt":"DSC04562.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720712/preview-80db0c73da51896762009335347de63f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720713/large-5d9e5f2c537d2db66d1e1d3a549f4071.jpg","alt":"DSC02827.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720713/preview-451f75acf31b1fb4566d5373f1e4e161.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720714/large-739474b60d3429243a4356960a10277c.jpg","alt":"DSC02796.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720714/preview-2b5d0cf4d9040e2e3f6248fdfa837d14.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720715/large-3e11329b837c11cf75d2a8056dcf59a2.jpg","alt":"DSC02792.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720715/preview-e6df0ea954cadff04512b5e949a26420.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720716/large-f5493490910743824655c853a7858abf.jpg","alt":"DSC04605.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720716/preview-238ccdc33741ff0ea0c07ff596b34738.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720717/large-4bddabb33cb5af65a732bf692495e227.jpg","alt":"DSC04591.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/720717/preview-d265f142ed504b9e45cb96dcf376d0b7.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Pixil Studios"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Riah:"},{"t":"p","html":"Riah is a rising force in the Bedroom Pop scene, crafting introspective and evocative music that resonates with the complexities of love, sex, loss, and a distinctive \"villain energy.\" Drawing deeply from personal life experiences, Riah channels raw emotion into every lyric and melody, creating an intimate connection with listeners.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Starting in the Los Angeles entertainment industry at the tender age of 17, Riah faced the harsh realities of the pre-Me Too era, which fueled her desire for autonomy and control over her artistic vision. After years of enduring the industry's darker side, she stepped back, determined to return to music only on her own terms. Now, as an accomplished entrepreneur, Riah has reclaimed her voice and is ready to make waves with a fresh and authentic sound."},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to her musical journey, Riah has captivated audiences at numerous festivals, clubs, and acoustic venues. Her passion for performance extends beyond music, as she is also a competitive pole dancer, having won the prestigious PSO Mountain competition in 2023.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a unique blend of vulnerability and power, Riah is poised to leave a lasting impact on the music world, bringing a new level of depth and intensity to the Bedroom Pop genre."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Riah:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4W98Etru2ErpE95smqDdfh?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/riahmusic1991\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/riahmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@Riah-Music-1991\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"385689","title":"17-year-old pop sensation Maria Deirisarri is set to release her debut album, \"In The Beginning,\" on September 29th. Hailing from Atlanta, her musical talent transcends her age, exploring genres from dark alternative to bossa nova. With over 77k Spotify streams and recognition from top publications like Earmilk and Conversations About Her, Maria's star is on the rise. Her music, influenced by her Hispanic heritage, surprises and captivates with its multilingual lyrics.","date":"2025-03-28","lead":"A heartfelt anthem about finding peace through forgiveness","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/385689/aff1253ef31704171e9404527834a4de.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A heartfelt anthem about finding peace through forgiveness"},{"t":"p","html":"Roswell, GA (March 28, 2025) - Emerging alt-pop artist<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?si=bpNuIeehSrqSbXVybDzELQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maria Deirisarri</strong></a> returns with a deeply personal new single, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/48KeBS7KXk3jsiWThBXY6h?si=5521139a59664d93\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\"Letting It Go.\"</strong></a> Released today, the track explores themes of resilience, self-reflection, and moving on."},{"t":"p","html":"Written during a difficult time in her senior year of high school, \"Letting It Go\" marks a shift in Deirisarri’s songwriting, one where pain and betrayal transform into a message of acceptance and healing."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/48KeBS7KXk3jsiWThBXY6h?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I was tired of being walked over and carried so much resentment,\" Deirisarri shared. \"But I needed to let it go before it buried me. Instead of making this a song about anger and hate, I wanted to write about forgiveness and healing.\"","cite":""},{"t":"p","html":"The single’s bittersweet lyrics reflect this emotional journey:"},{"t":"p","html":"I’m getting back my soul / And though I’m losing control / I’m still going / And we both know that you ain’t coming with me."},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Corey Kilgannon</strong> and <strong>Jacob Hudson</strong>, \"Letting It Go\" delivers a melancholic yet hopeful sound, reminiscent of a positive spin on <strong>Billie Eilish’s</strong> \"The Greatest.\" Deirisarri’s soft yet commanding vocals guide the listener through an introspective experience, balancing sadness with an undeniable sense of growth, renewal and forgiveness."},{"t":"p","html":"\"This song is an honest reflection of who I was and what I felt in that moment,\" Deirisarri continued. \"It’s about finding peace through forgiveness, even when it hurts.\""},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/727354/large-1750324ea938694774bfbc0b8107e508.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Letting It Go\" by Maria Deirisarri"},{"t":"p","html":"The cover art, illustrated by Deirisarri herself, further embodies the song’s themes of transformation and emotional release. As the second-to-last single from her upcoming EP, <em><strong>Si Vis Pacem</strong></em>, \"Letting It Go\" further sets the stage for what promises to be a highly compelling project."},{"t":"p","html":"With her unique blend of alternative pop and introspective storytelling, Maria Deirisarri continues to carve out a space for herself in music, bringing raw authenticity and emotional depth to each release."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Maria Deirisarri:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Rising pop artist <a href=\"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maria Deirisarri</strong></a> is only 19, but her musicianship and lyricism suggest wisdom beyond her years. The Atlanta-based singer-songwriter experiments with many genres, from dark alternative to bossa nova, generating an eclectic mix of music notably showcased in her debut album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ?si=w6TbXsN-SJOMPd4mN151ZA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>In The Beginning</strong></em></a><em>.</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Already amassing over 110k streams on Spotify, and garnering attention from top publications such as <strong>EARMILK</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Conversations About Her</strong>, Maria Deirisarri’s success continues to increase with every release. The range of her sound entices listeners to discover every song’s personality, surprising them with lyrics connected to her Hispanic culture and multilingual heritage (such as in “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5am4tRMhZJObB1vjpzNTbG?si=6c8d80dc16304bd4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Same</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2HOQOaIyRpXxD6JzPwhEdY?si=31b49e0b35bf401a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Te Necesito</strong></a>”)."},{"t":"p","html":"The young artist has triumphed in various competitions, ranging from her Trailblazing Performer accolade from the International Singer-Songwriters Association, her second-place finish in <strong>Omega’s Got Talent</strong>, to her Talent Preliminary Award in the <strong>Miss Georgia Teen Volunteer Competition</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Maria Deirisarri’s vibrant artiste meets the listener with a grace and uniqueness that is a breath of fresh air. Fans are eager to see what this up-and-coming superstar has up her sleeve.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Follow Maria below for all music updates and upcoming announcements!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Maria Deirisarri!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/-1decT_f9k0","height":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/mariadeirisarri/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@mariadeirisarri","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com/","img":"","title":"17-year-old pop sensation Maria Deirisarri is set to release her debut album, \"In The Beginning,\" on September 29th. Hailing from Atlanta, her musical talent transcends her age, exploring genres from dark alternative to bossa nova. With over 77k Spotify streams and recognition from top publications like Earmilk and Conversations About Her, Maria's star is on the rise. Her music, influenced by her Hispanic heritage, surprises and captivates with its multilingual lyrics.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@mariadeirisarri?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCtx5jhQ5a3Fx8_EJxh54WsA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100063574507610\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"385713","title":"Rebekah Gilbert Unveils Gritty New Americana Single “Somebody Else’s House”","date":"2025-03-28","lead":"Americana singer-songwriter Rebekah Gilbert dives deep into family secrets and generational truths with her haunting new single \"Somebody Else’s House\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/385713/a59fcb868a54a4126e565d825fccd206.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Americana singer-songwriter Rebekah Gilbert dives deep into family secrets and generational truths with her haunting new single \"Somebody Else’s House\""},{"t":"p","html":"BIRMINGHAM, AL (March 28, 2025) – Americana singer-songwriter <strong>Rebekah Gilbert</strong> is gearing up to release her latest single, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0BKPaho9FyQzf1nDw0wYDQ?si=04d1325513ca44eb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\"Somebody Else’s House\"</strong></a>, on March 28, 2025. Co-written with country songwriting sensation <strong>Amanda Williams</strong>, the song tells a haunting Southern Gothic story of generational secrets, deception, and inherited truths. This marks the first release from Gilbert’s upcoming <em><strong>Secret Keeper</strong></em> EP, offering a raw, bluesy country sound that digs deep into family history and buried pasts."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/PM50fOlyBhY","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"The inspiration for \"Somebody Else's House\" comes from Gilbert’s own family. As a teenager, she discovered that an ancestor had led a double life—running moonshine while secretly supporting a second family just miles away. That revelation lingered, reinforcing the idea that what happens behind closed doors often stays there, unless someone decides to break the cycle."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>You never know what's going on</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>In somebody else's house</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>It's 190 proof/Bottled up under the same roof</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>In somebody else's house</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0BKPaho9FyQzf1nDw0wYDQ?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"caption","html":"Lyrics from \"Somebody Else's House\""},{"t":"p","html":"With a sound in the vein of Margo Price or Miranda Lambert, the track blends traditional country grit with deep, brooding Americana. Lyrically, it has the weight of an old folk ballad, the kind of story passed down through generations, where shame and legacy are intertwined. The phrase “190 proof, bottled up under the same roof” is a powerful metaphor, suggesting both the literal presence of moonshine and the emotional intensity of secrets brewing within a family. Sonically, the track creates a rich, layered sound with Gilbert's americana-country style shining through. A raw, bluesy edge is brought forth by the driving banjo riffs, and Gilbert's soulful vocals emphasize the song's dark undercurrents.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"\"This song is a reminder that our pasts may influence who we are, but they don't have to define us or our futures. It's also a reminder to be kind to people because you don't truly know what someone else is going through.\"","cite":"Rebekah Gilbert (Songwriter)"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/727369/large-afc151e269976b70482b2a0069528aae.png","alt":"Cover art for \"Somebody Else's House\" by Rebekah Gilbert"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by Nicole Witt, the song features Sol Philcox-Littlefield’s (banjo), Jimbo Hart (bass), Jon Davis (drums), and Grayson Wright (keyboards). A music video for \"Somebody Else’s House\" will drop alongside the single on March 28, 2025.&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Rebekah Gilbert:"},{"t":"p","html":"Rebekah Gilbert has been captivating audiences with her powerful songs, poetry, and prose since 2009. Her writing invites readers to reflect on their own journeys, while her soulful vocals pull listeners into a deep, personal experience. Drawing from the Americana genre, Rebekah’s music has been compared to the confessional lyrics of Patty Griffin; the soothing, moody vocals of Norah Jones; and the emotional, soulful delivery of Brandi Carlile."},{"t":"p","html":"Based in Birmingham, AL, Rebekah regularly travels to Nashville to write and perform. She recently released a cover song,<strong>&nbsp;“Crazy,”</strong> originally by Gnarls Barkley. This year she is also releasing a new EP, <strong><em>Secret Keeper</em></strong>, that showcases a different side of her artistry. She performs locally and regionally and is expanding to national venues. Rebekah enjoys hosting music events, creating spaces for others to share their voices."},{"t":"p","html":"A champion for late bloomers, Rebekah is passionate about encouraging others to pursue their dreams, no matter when they start. She often shares her own story of achieving goals and finding fulfillment later in life. Her first poetry book, <a href=\"https://a.co/d/gmjwUko\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Poems from the Back Pew: A Journey from Faith to Doubt and Beyond</strong></em></a>, is available in her shop and on Amazon. The companion EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/35DMxUNcmjKg3LStgoKuwg?si=BeHH8NgiTESYeEMmCFjdPQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Year of Jubilee</strong></em></a>, recorded in Nashville, is available on all streaming platforms. Both the poetry collection and the EP explore her journey of breaking free from evangelical beliefs, and the personal revolution that led her to a new sense of freedom."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.rebekahgilbert.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/RebekahGilbertWritingandMusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/rebekahlgilbert/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@gilbertrebekah\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@rebekahgilbertmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3HNZCei9Vhafw0UVcbBcZV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"386902","title":"Singer/Songwriter Kyle Davis released his sixth record, \"Make It Count\". Originally discorvered by Don Dixon and Phil Ramone, his music has been hailed in Billboard and Rolling Stone magazines.","date":"2025-03-28","lead":"A poignant reflection on loss, resilience, and the fragments of ourselves we fight to reclaim.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/386902/7f58c11f361bb01286b69301164c2b05.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A poignant reflection on loss, resilience, and the fragments of ourselves we fight to reclaim."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7t0JWjnNLIpTjUvzK9Dno9?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Prince George, VA (March 28, 2025)</strong> – Acclaimed singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://www.kylewdavismusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Kyle Davis</strong></a> debuts <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7t0JWjnNLIpTjUvzK9Dno9?si=Dypn5N2eRveLbANypTmKIw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Jericho</strong></em></a>, his first full-length album since 2020’s <em>Make It Count</em>. Released today, <em>Jericho</em> is an introspective exploration of loss, recovery, and rebuilding, contemplating the ways we compartmentalize our experiences, the struggle to move forward, and the unexpected paths toward redemption. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Blending the evocative storytelling of <strong>Jackson Browne</strong> with the soulful introspection of <strong>Peter Gabrie</strong>l and the timeless groove of <strong>Bill Withers</strong>, <em>Jericho</em> is a striking testament to Davis’s ever-evolving artistry. ​"},{"t":"p","html":"The album traverses a rich sonic landscape, from the contemplative depth of its title track, which explores the search for meaning beyond material wealth, to the poignant revelations of \"On a Ledge,\" examining the contrast between public scrutiny and private, often buried, struggles. \"Sail Away\" offers a powerful meditation on impermanence and acceptance, likening this emotional journey to water slipping through one’s fingers; intangible yet capable of carrying ships across the sea."},{"t":"p","html":"Another standout track, \"The Last Line,\" offers an emotional reflection on life’s struggles and the search for meaning. The song contrasts the mundane and extraordinary to convey a longing for redemption and a desire to leave a lasting impact, despite life’s challenges.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Jericho, both the song and the record, examines what it means to get another chance and put together the pieces of ourselves scattered across the floor... Not all of them fit together the same way anymore, but enough do.\"","cite":"Kyle Davis"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/xXg1Rv6dTXA","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Expanding on this theme, \"Passengers\" reflects on the idea that none of us are truly alone and that sometimes it takes working together to navigate life's challenges. Meanwhile, \"Now and Again\" wrestles with the guilt of moving forward after losing someone, suggesting that the people we love never truly leave us, remaining woven into the spaces between our lives and our memories."},{"t":"p","html":"Jericho marks Davis's seventh studio record and reunites the celebrated team behind his 1999 Sony debut, <em>Raising Heroes</em>. Produced by longtime collaborator <strong>Don Dixon </strong><strong>(R.E.M., The Smithereens)</strong>, <em>Jericho</em> was recorded at <strong>Mitch Easter’s iconic studio&nbsp;</strong>in Winston-Salem, with additional sessions at Davis’s home studio in Prince George, VA, and <strong>Elephant Ear Studio</strong> in Richmond, VA."},{"t":"p","html":"The album features an impressive lineup of musicians, including <strong>Don Dixon</strong> (bass, keys, trombone, snare), <strong>Mike Durham</strong> (electric guitar), <strong>Peter Holsapple</strong> (piano, mandolin, B3), <strong>Rob Ladd</strong> (drums), <strong>Corey Wells&nbsp;</strong>(electric guitar), and <strong>Hayes Elverston</strong> (harp). Davis himself contributes on guitar and piano."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/728585/large-a1ec2283b3aa136b4b72c67f96e1e2f2.jpg","alt":"Cover art by Santa Anna"},{"t":"p","html":"Renowned for his emotive voice and introspective songwriting, Davis’s career spans decades, with accolades including a 4-star review in <strong>Rolling Stone</strong>, a <strong>Billboard Magazine</strong> cover feature, multiple songs on the <strong>Triple AAA charts</strong> and collaborations with legendary artists like <strong>Bruce Hornsby</strong> and <strong>49 Winchester</strong>. He has shared the stage with icons such as <strong>Bob Dylan</strong>, <strong>John Mayer</strong>, and <strong>Hall &amp; Oates</strong>. After taking time away from music to raise his family, he re-emerged in 2020 with <em>Make It Count</em>, and now, with <em>Jericho</em>, he offers his most profound and heartfelt work to date."},{"t":"p","html":"“As I look back on making Jericho, I realize that creating records is a form of therapy for me,” Davis reflects. “Not every song is entirely first-person, but the themes of grief, resilience and reflection are universal. I hope these songs help listeners feel a connection to their own journeys.”"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5lq6g7ALA2XGi4f4e7YR9h?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kyle Davis:"},{"t":"p","html":"Kyle Davis, a Richmond, Virginia-based singer-songwriter, makes a triumphant return this winter with his latest record,<em>&nbsp;Jericho</em>. This marks Davis's seventh studio album and reunites the stellar lineup from his acclaimed 1999 Sony release,&nbsp;<em>Raising Heroes</em>. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Throughout his career, Davis has earned critical acclaim, including a 4-star review in <em>Rolling Stone</em>, a cover feature in&nbsp;<em>Billboard Magazine</em>, and multiple songs landing on the Triple AAA charts. His distinctive voice has graced major TV commercials and shows, as well as records by legendary artists like Bruce Hornsby and rising stars such as 49 Winchester. Davis has also shared the stage with icons ranging from Bob Dylan to John Mayer. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"After taking a hiatus to focus on raising his family, Davis returned to recording with <em>Make It Count</em> in 2020, an album praised by critics but released amidst the challenges of the COVID-19 pandemic. With&nbsp;<em>Jericho</em>, he raises the bar even higher. Produced by Don Dixon, much of the record was created at Mitch Easter’s studio in Winston-Salem, with final touches recorded at Davis’s home in Prince George, Virginia, and Elephant Ear Studio in Richmond. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a refined perspective on life, love, and loss, Davis’s songwriting has only deepened with time. His music continues to draw comparisons to the evocative storytelling of Jackson Browne, the soulful introspection of Peter Gabriel, and the timeless groove of Bill Withers—a testament to his ability to connect with audiences on a profound level."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/6s000ljQ-E4","height":""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Kyle!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DGowAWfOHNa/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.kylewdavismusic.com/","img":"","title":"Singer/Songwriter Kyle Davis released his sixth record, \"Make It Count\". Originally discorvered by Don Dixon and Phil Ramone, his music has been hailed in Billboard and Rolling Stone magazines.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/kylewdavismusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/kylewdavismusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCAd1M5QdT1GsfgFqngAEuUQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1fQuYKsLfkTcqpj1pIwTYz?si=qgjmSdbhTV6zJqr6wNkvWg&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=f3742451339946a5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"386936","title":"Hev's Journey Subscriber and Fan page. Subscribe for behind-the-scenes access for events, new songs, and much more.","date":"2025-03-28","lead":"\"Sinking\" is a powerful Pop/RnB anthem about reclaiming self-worth and navigating the complexities of toxic relationships.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/386936/6865fa656e2f82dcf6136c137981c80a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Sinking\" is a powerful Pop/RnB anthem about reclaiming self-worth and navigating the complexities of toxic relationships."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>SPOTSYLVANIA, VA (March 28, 2025)</strong> — <strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5RP7h9xg0Q5Th5qGbo6cek?si=WOUpuBZ1SLqjePE1mSIv-A&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=d8d1fe9140794257\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hev’s Journey</strong></a> is back with another powerful single,<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7ferD02Eum6QST9D0ky66W?si=c76ed24dac5c457f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\"Sinking,\"</strong></a> on March 28th. Blending Pop and RnB, the track dives deep into themes of self-worth and emotional resilience, offering listeners an honest glimpse into the struggles of navigating toxic relationships and finding the strength to reclaim your own identity."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7ferD02Eum6QST9D0ky66W?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Sinking\" captures the painful realization of pouring everything into a relationship where the love wasn’t returned. It’s a journey of loss, growth, and ultimately, empowerment. For Hev, this song became a way to process her own experience and recognize her value. The emotional weight behind the track speaks to anyone who's ever felt like they were losing themselves for someone else."},{"t":"p","html":"“I wrote ‘Sinking’ when I felt like I was losing someone I had poured everything into,\" says Hev. \"I loved when they didn’t love back or appreciate what I gave. Throughout this journey, I realized that I am worth more, and I am unwilling to give up who I am.\""},{"t":"quote","html":"\"This song resonates because it’s something everyone goes through—the push and pull of emotions. Each of us has to decide whether to stay true to ourselves or become what others want us to be.\"","cite":"Hev's Journey"},{"t":"p","html":"The sound of \"Sinking\" has a raw, soulful edge that recalls the intensity of Adele, but with a smoother, more introspective delivery. Hev’s voice, rich and emotive, takes center stage, guiding the listener through every beat and lyric with sincerity and strength. “I really enjoyed the emotional moments when making this song,” Hev reflects. “It felt real. I hope others can hear it and feel the same connection.”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/728596/large-7a303d191abbe181c6db123cdbbb9993.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Sinking\" by Hev's Journey"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by Grammy-winning, multi-platinum recording and mix engineer <strong>Serge “Surgical” Tsai</strong>, \"Sinking\" showcases a refined yet emotional sound that enhances Hev's storytelling. Tsai’s expert touch brings the track’s deep emotion to life, layering powerful instrumentation that complements Hev’s voice perfectly."},{"t":"p","html":"A versatile artist who seamlessly combines personal storytelling with universal themes, Hev’s Journey has been praised for her previous releases, including “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3zVKl8KTkye7RLt9b1JdMl?si=b21a6e3152a14545\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dance</strong></a>,” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7o8xjzUMtnzAOyndT0llwt?si=df7de73c68af405a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Broken Promises</strong></a>”, and has garnered attention from outlets such as <strong>Music By Humans&nbsp;</strong>and<strong>&nbsp;Rosa Distrito</strong>, among others. With her standout performance at <strong>Sweet Auburn Spring Fest&nbsp;</strong>in front of over 100,000 attendees, Hev’s Journey has solidified herself as a rising star.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond her music, Hev’s Journey is a passionate advocate for women’s empowerment, using her platform to inspire young people to embrace their voices. Her commitment to authenticity and cultural pride makes her a unique force in the music industry, resonating with listeners navigating their own journeys of love and self-discovery."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Sinking\" drops on March 28th, and you can catch it on all major streaming platforms. Stay tuned for updates and follow Hev’s Journey on social media for more news on upcoming releases."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/722694/large-61453a1d4cdf1c08203a63a53b0dfbbd.jpg","alt":"Why I Cry Cover Jpg to offically use.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/722694/preview-bb8a34c43424d73cc578d4292380963b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715294/large-2a6967d418a740870abf29e253db7b64.jpg","alt":"IMG_0640.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715294/preview-3fba38a33cd9eee4cff4a81c9c0b9a2c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715295/large-8daea2bb637fabff21f5d2613aec61a6.jpg","alt":"IMG_0539.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715295/preview-5263340c8742e77b3aab0c488cefdcbe.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715297/large-82a9eea91f3bd83b01867d743ca24ebd.jpg","alt":"IMG_0784.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715297/preview-5f132e99dec06344f3c79d701e20a152.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Mats Jerndal (Oddbox Studios)"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hev&#39;s Journey:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.hevsjourney.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Heavenleigh Villar</strong></a>, better known by her stage name<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5RP7h9xg0Q5Th5qGbo6cek?si=WOUpuBZ1SLqjePE1mSIv-A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hev’s Journey</strong></a>, is a rising Pop/R&amp;B artist whose heartfelt lyrics and captivating melodies have quickly earned her a dedicated fanbase. Based in <strong>Spotsylvania, VA</strong>, Hev’s music blends personal experiences with universally relatable themes, creating a sound that is both intimate and inspiring. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a style influenced by <strong>Adele</strong>, <strong>SZA</strong>, <strong>Laufey</strong>, and <strong>Liana Flores</strong>, Hev’s Journey crafts haunting, passionate, optimistic, and undeniably personal songs. Her artistry has evolved from early inspirations to a more self-reflective and raw sound, embracing her unique voice as a Dominican and African-American artist."},{"t":"p","html":"Hev’s Journey debuted with the single “<strong>Just Crush</strong>” and has since released a steady stream of music that showcases her growth as a songwriter and vocalist. Her discography includes several fan favorites including the most recently released “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3zVKl8KTkye7RLt9b1JdMl?si=910543ccfd7c48e4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dance</strong></a>”, which has been praised for its vibrant energy and cultural authenticity (<em><strong>The Concert Chronicles</strong></em>).&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/436x8jbcJgI","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Along the way, Hev’s Journey has been spotlighted by prominent publications and has graced the stage at major events like the <strong>Sweet Auburn Spring Fest</strong>, performing for over 100,000 attendees. She was also featured on the <em><strong>Women of Substance Podcast</strong></em>, highlighting her as a representative of empowerment, authenticity, and connection in the music industry.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Her music is for everyone—teens and adults alike—offering a soundtrack to life’s highs and lows. With a mission to inspire young people to use their voices, Hev’s lyrics often delve into personal challenges, such as overcoming self-doubt and proving critics wrong."},{"t":"p","html":"When she’s not writing or performing, Hev enjoys spending time with her beloved dog, <strong>Coco</strong>, and engaging with fans on social media. She also participates in philanthropic efforts, such as the <strong>Anne Beers Back to School Community </strong>and <strong>Empowerment Day</strong>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hev&#39;s Journey!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.hevsjourney.com/","img":"","title":"Hev's Journey Subscriber and Fan page. Subscribe for behind-the-scenes access for events, new songs, and much more.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://instagram.com/hevs.journey\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://tr.ee/WXwR3WOIlo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCqHGpnDx8VY3sONz-m75org?app=desktop&amp;sub_confirmation=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"382163","title":"Hallie Marie Music ✸☽ A Denver-Based musician who blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling. She has a series of releases arriving in 2025, with her first titled \"Indebted\" arriving January 21.","date":"2025-03-19","lead":"A raw and electrifying track that explores the thrill of impulsiveness, the weight of consequence, and the emotional highs and lows that follow","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/382163/31e554dbe2334d90b609dba899b948c9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A raw and electrifying track that explores the thrill of impulsiveness, the weight of consequence, and the emotional highs and lows that follow"},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (March 18, 2025) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qjqY0W9hRpqy_g6Ky9uPyw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a> has never been one to play it safe, and her new single <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5MOvprcZTavKXYtApW4qKz?si=0aec7d14538a45de\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\"Sanity\"</strong></a> dives headfirst into the chaos of impulsiveness and the thrill of not knowing where the night—or life—might take you. \"Sanity\" follows the release of the emerging alternative artist's successful rock ballad “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1O4Q92TIuafovajnJyR557?si=5e67e704d03440ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Indebted</strong></a>” - and showcases the evocative songwriting and powerful vocal delivery that fans are coming to love her for."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5MOvprcZTavKXYtApW4qKz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Blending alternative rock energy with an underlying punk attitude, \"Sanity\" mirrors the emotional whiplash of chasing freedom but waking up to the consequences. A song about losing yourself in the moment, getting swept away by new loves and new places - It starts with an easy, infectious rhythm, the kind that makes you want to dance in dimly lit rooms with strangers. Then, the song swerves into something weightier, unraveling into a moment of raw reflection. The shift mirrors the story it tells—excitement giving way to the cold slap of reality.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/723418/large-6d2b3b70251faed0ec8e3726f8940974.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Sanity\" by Hallie Marie"},{"t":"p","html":"Lyrically, \"Sanity\" is soaked in restless energy. The verses feel like speeding down a highway with no clear destination, while the chorus is an explosion of self-awareness—equal parts reckless and self-destructive. Lines like \"Well, I left my keys in another city / where the nights are long and the girls are pretty\" capture that sense of escapism, while \"If I wake in the morning with a heart attack / if I fall from heaven and it all goes black\" hint at the inevitable crash. This vivid portrayal of the rollercoaster of emotions that one can experience beautifully captures the highs and lows of life, painting a picture of the fragility of happiness and the harshness of reality."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song is about me losing myself in all the excitement of new loves and places, but then getting carried away by the exhilaration, which starts out fun but sometimes gets me into trouble. Having fun can be intoxicating but when taken too far can have negative consequences.\"","cite":"Hallie Marie on the inspiration behind \"Sanity\""},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/-b10e31cd63b2c0317696d54d044a4e07.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-32 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/preview-c33bb4c8c0fb8d62a46ea644fb5ad2e1.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/-1302eb881563358853da571d1fb91c45.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-36 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/preview-e17e8b3fa61065cd5c4017c5cabd0e2d.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/large-3fd73d88583417c22d63d14ef4d100aa.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-14 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/preview-4811aaab4e4c9d4f52c8820f4714b20b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/large-29c12eef5ba54b62cc04f5bc34eee872.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-29 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/preview-24ede99c287103be1e22c17641577c77.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/-da81f45fe86805db981f72d86eff8965.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-46 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/preview-8f88dcb7cb4728eef25338442eb31f22.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/large-3740cb07a0046ee2a3bf82c6c328555f.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-44 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/preview-a44d9f029894f554f894eed711194762.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/large-69157f55a4afc3f0f8b64d0c7951e6c8.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-1 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/preview-88af250d089625bac98f9cf6e7350728.jpeg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hallie Marie:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a> is a multifaceted artist who beautifully balances light and shadow in her work. With an intellectually curious spirit, she dives deep into the complexities of human emotions, crafting music that resonates with listeners on many levels — from the highs of love and joy to the depths of melancholy. Drawing inspiration from artists like <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>, <strong>Billy Joel</strong>, and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, Hallie’s sound blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling."},{"t":"p","html":"Collaborating with the Denver-based band <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1UP2Zk7NI1U6KBhpPfPKBt?si=y0EiRbwmTCSlwg_-3sd3vg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Direville</a>, Hallie Marie has already begun to make her mark on the music industry with popular releases “<strong>Sympathy</strong>” and “<strong>Free Spirit</strong>”, among others. Now branching out on her own, her solo music endeavors combine poetic mystical imagery with direct and casual insight derived from raw life experience.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Embracing the beauty of authenticity and connecting with each of us at our core, Hallie invites her audience into her world, sharing not just her music but also her creative process — writing, arranging, and recording — along with the benefit of what she has learned through struggle and resilience. She aims to connect deeply with her listeners, sharing meaningful ideas that resonate long after the music ends."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hallie Marie!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/halliemariemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@halliemariemusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/","img":"","title":"Hallie Marie Music ✸☽ A Denver-Based musician who blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling. She has a series of releases arriving in 2025, with her first titled \"Indebted\" arriving January 21.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://instagram.com/halliemariemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qv9RFavvRmeHdVLljnpMBQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | &nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100068917929503\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"363977","title":"17-year-old pop sensation Maria Deirisarri is set to release her debut album, \"In The Beginning,\" on September 29th. Hailing from Atlanta, her musical talent transcends her age, exploring genres from dark alternative to bossa nova. With over 77k Spotify streams and recognition from top publications like Earmilk and Conversations About Her, Maria's star is on the rise. Her music, influenced by her Hispanic heritage, surprises and captivates with its multilingual lyrics.","date":"2025-03-07","lead":"\"Brutally honest, infinite, raw, naturesque... As if the forest was singing a song about itself\" describes the new single from Maria Deirisarri.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/363977/8ed3be6b0e8bbf2757741dcfd259e4ce.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Brutally honest, infinite, raw, naturesque... As if the forest was singing a song about itself\" describes the new single from Maria Deirisarri."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/Kc44XFLF5Mc","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Roswell, GA (March 7, 2025) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?si=bpNuIeehSrqSbXVybDzELQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maria Deirisarri</strong></a>, an emerging artist in the folk music scene, is releasing a poignant new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5iAGvbD1dgZoCTbpjOA2gl?si=3bed13eaeabf4851\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>And I’ll Fly</strong></a>”, on <strong>Native American Heritage Day</strong>. Honoring the purity of the land and its people before the conquest, “And I’ll Fly” showcases Deirisarri’s unique sound and heartfelt storytelling, marking a significant milestone in her artistic journey as she invites listeners to experience the raw emotion and authenticity that defines her music."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5iAGvbD1dgZoCTbpjOA2gl?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The inspiration behind “And I’ll Fly” stems from a deeply personal period in Deirisarri’s life during her junior year of high school. Faced with academic pressures, a challenging relationship, and the burden of toxic friendships, she turned to songwriting as a means of self-reflection and healing. <em>“I needed to know that at the very least, I would be there for myself,”</em> Deirisarri shares, emphasizing the song’s themes of self-empowerment and honesty."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I didn’t think I would ever play the song live — let alone release it in such a pivotal moment of my life. I’m in my first semester of college, I’m discovering just what kind of musician I really am, and I’m building the foundation of where my artistic career is going to go. ‘And I’ll Fly’ is coming at such a perfect moment. It is such a November song, and if I ever needed to hear anything, it’s my own lyrics telling me to push forward.”","cite":"- Maria Deirisarri"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702041/large-6d1836934ece047cc24317c7df65323a.png","alt":"Cover art for \"And I'll Fly\""},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Corey Kilgannon</strong> at Beaches Vineyard and <strong>Jacob Hudson</strong> at Pine Studio in Jacksonville, Florida, “And I’ll Fly” captures the essence of the folk genre with its infinite, raw, and naturesque sound. The guitars evoke a sense of boundlessness, while the piano adds a light and graceful touch, creating an elegant and emotional listening experience. This production approach reflects Deirisarri’s artistic vision, showcasing her ability to connect deeply with her audience."},{"t":"p","html":"The lyrical content of “And I’ll Fly” addresses key themes such as mental health, spirituality in nature, and the pursuit of freedom. The song serves as a reminder of the importance of self-acceptance and resilience, resonating with listeners who may be facing their own challenges. Deirisarri’s heartfelt lyrics invite a moment of reflection and connection, fostering a sense of community among her audience."},{"t":"p","html":"The cover art for the single, which Deirisarri illustrated herself, features symbolic elements that reference the song’s themes and lyrics. Listeners can see two little bluejays on the cover, a little callback to the first single she released from the EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5760gKxngKv6eFoMKDU2Yw?si=c20d591b6d534666\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>bluejay</strong>.</a> The cover art also features a blackened river at the bottom, the trembling timber and faithful forest, a shivering sea, and the mighty mountains she sings about in the song.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5760gKxngKv6eFoMKDU2Yw?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702042/large-29cab9e252fcd75b7165571f69797e17.jpeg","alt":"Deirisarri creating the cover art for \"And I'll Fly\""},{"t":"p","html":"This newfound confidence in her music coincides with her exploration of her identity as a musician. Looking ahead, Deirisarri has exciting plans for the future, including the release of a music video for “And I’ll Fly,” which will be part of her upcoming EP, <em><strong>Si Vis Pacem</strong></em>. <em>“There may or may not be a little skydiving involved,”</em> she hints, adding an element of intrigue for fans eager to see how her artistic vision translates visually."},{"t":"p","html":"In describing her music, Deirisarri states, <em>“It sounds infinite, raw, naturesque. As if the forest was singing a song about itself.”</em> This description encapsulates the essence of “And I’ll Fly,” inviting listeners to embark on a journey that is both personal and universal. With this debut single, Maria Deirisarri is poised to make a lasting impact in the folk music landscape."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702043/large-227679eeb07216014d5db878b351a385.jpeg","alt":"Image of Maria Deirisarri"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Maria Deirisarri:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Rising pop artist <a href=\"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maria Deirisarri</strong></a> is only 18 years of age, but her musicianship and lyricism suggest wisdom beyond her years. The Atlanta-based singer-songwriter experiments with a multitude of genres, from dark alternative to bossa nova, generating an eclectic mix of music notably showcased in her debut album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ?si=w6TbXsN-SJOMPd4mN151ZA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>In The Beginning</strong></em></a><em>.</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Already amassing over 77k streams on Spotify, and garnering attention from top publications such as <strong>EARMILK</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Conversations About Her</strong>, Maria Deirisarri’s success continues to increase with every release. The range of her sound entices listeners to discover every song’s personality, and even surprises them with lyrics connected to her Hispanic culture and multilingual heritage (such as in “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5am4tRMhZJObB1vjpzNTbG?si=6c8d80dc16304bd4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Same</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2HOQOaIyRpXxD6JzPwhEdY?si=31b49e0b35bf401a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Te Necesito</strong></a>”)."},{"t":"p","html":"In recent months, this young artist has triumphed in various competitions, ranging from her Trailblazing Performer accolade from the International Singer-Songwriters Association, her second-place finish in <strong>Omega’s Got Talent</strong>, to her Talent Preliminary Award in the <strong>Miss Georgia Teen Volunteer Competition</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Maria Deirisarri’s vibrant artiste meets the listener with a grace and uniqueness that is a breath of fresh air. Fans are eager to see what this up-and-coming superstar has up her sleeve.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Follow Maria below for all music updates and upcoming announcements!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Maria Deirisarri!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/-1decT_f9k0","height":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/mariadeirisarri/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@mariadeirisarri","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com/","img":"","title":"17-year-old pop sensation Maria Deirisarri is set to release her debut album, \"In The Beginning,\" on September 29th. Hailing from Atlanta, her musical talent transcends her age, exploring genres from dark alternative to bossa nova. With over 77k Spotify streams and recognition from top publications like Earmilk and Conversations About Her, Maria's star is on the rise. Her music, influenced by her Hispanic heritage, surprises and captivates with its multilingual lyrics.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@mariadeirisarri?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCtx5jhQ5a3Fx8_EJxh54WsA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100063574507610\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"374639","title":"Maxwell Macey Releases Introspective Debut Single, “Need to Leave”","date":"2025-03-07","lead":"From stagnation to self-discovery, the new track blends indie folk intimacy with Americana warmth.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/374639/6961f1976874b677d2ca0475606533d4.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"From stagnation to self-discovery, the new track blends indie folk intimacy with Americana warmth."},{"t":"p","html":"SEATTLE, WA (March 7, 2025) — <strong>Maxwell Macey</strong>, an emerging voice in the indie-folk and alternative Americana scene, marks his debut with the release of <strong>“Need to Leave.”&nbsp;</strong>Exploring the connection between physical and emotional distance, the track captures the universal tension between comfort and growth."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0I7BzV0hqftSmRCxBjdd99?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Emerging from a pivotal moment of transformation, the song was written in stages between the confines of a Los Angeles studio apartment and the aftermath of a significant relationship's end. With its warm acoustic arrangements and confessional songwriting, “Need to Leave” blends the emotional vulnerability of artists like<strong>&nbsp;Phoebe Bridgers</strong> with the Americana warmth of <strong>The Lumineers</strong> and <strong>Jason Isbell</strong>."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715611/large-f5a3c55a68f169c1d7b41afe14759f42.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Need to Leave\""},{"t":"p","html":"As Maxwell later relocated to the Pacific Northwest, the track also represents a poignant meditation on breaking free from toxic cycles, embracing change and finding clarity in the vastness of natural spaces. The chorus serves as both a literal and metaphorical expression—leaving behind a physical space as well as the emotional weight of an unfulfilling life chapter.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>\"Need to Leave\" Chorus Preview:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"'Cause I've been all alone and all torn up, I'm ripping at the seams"},{"t":"p","html":"And they say time heals everything but I'm still waiting patiently"},{"t":"p","html":"And every day I try to keep my mind on what's in front of me"},{"t":"p","html":"But I just keep rewinding back to times when you were here with me"},{"t":"p","html":"And I think I need to leave"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Sometimes healing isn't just about time passing, but finding where you need to be. Writing this song helped me understand that feeling restless isn't just uncertainty, it's your inner compass pointing you toward necessary change.","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Maxwell Macey"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715612/large-4f107b595b7db1d6beafc4425f28b1a6.jpeg","alt":"DSC_4916_bw.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715612/preview-6874a0abfe014b074c41bd1818b6afff.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715613/large-061749d034f6945b31f237b2dc133059.jpeg","alt":"DSC_5147_bw.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715613/preview-f1bc99d1e2933b96ea5e534218622958.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715614/large-d7f4238787bd752404901d1bb5795276.jpeg","alt":"DSC_4980_bw.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715614/preview-100ca6e766384896919470d06285222e.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/713784/large-085c0e76e92f55d35631c11e1e35af59.jpg","alt":"DSC_5034.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/713784/preview-90899150cc0783e192b0d8adfa61f818.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/713786/large-5628fe8adefb26afedc34bce96fcd606.jpg","alt":"DSC_4966.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/713786/preview-a5aeb6f20295db2612263210ad3f44e1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/713787/large-aaf40dcb62035f4add04e0b5c18dcf2c.jpg","alt":"DSC_5079.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/713787/preview-062e7d271db263a39dd37bc1fe59c87b.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by <a href=\"https://rachelbennett.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rachel Bennett Photography</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"“Need to Leave” was written, performed, produced, engineered and co-mixed by Maxwell Macey, with mastering and co-mixing by <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/softglas/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Soft Glas</a> (Joao Gonzalez)."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Maxwell Macey:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Maxwell Macey</strong> is an indie-folk and Americana singer-songwriter whose music navigates the landscapes of personal growth, healing, and transformation. Drawing inspiration from the storytelling traditions of artists like <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, <strong>Zach Bryan</strong>, and <strong>Jason Isbell</strong>, Maxwell’s sound intertwines poetic lyricism with dynamic, genre-blending arrangements."},{"t":"p","html":"Raised in Southern California, Maxwell discovered his creative voice through a deep love of storytelling, sparked early on by influences such as <strong>Dave Matthews Band,</strong> <strong>John Mayer</strong> and <strong>Jack Johnson</strong>. After years spent honing his craft behind the scenes, he debuted with the deeply introspective single, <strong>\"Need to Leave\"</strong> in 2025."},{"t":"p","html":"Now calling Seattle home, Maxwell’s work reflects the tension between rootedness and the urge for change—a push and pull echoed in the Pacific Northwest’s vast natural landscapes. His songs weave intimate narratives of emotional resilience and self-discovery, offering listeners a heartfelt soundtrack for their own journeys through life’s uncertainties."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://maxwellmacey.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/maxwellmaceymusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@MaxwellMaceyMusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@maxwellmaceymusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>​"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"377350","title":"Racyne Parker Releases Debut Full-Length Album, \"Will You Go With Me?\"","date":"2025-02-25","lead":"Inviting self-discovery, dream-chasing, and connection with authentic, heartfelt storytelling and small-town twang.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/377350/dc2c8514074c918c906d4f683e5efda7.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Inviting self-discovery, dream-chasing, and connection with authentic, heartfelt storytelling and small-town twang."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>SEATTLE, WA</strong> (February 25, 2025)– Singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://racyneparker.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Racyne Parker</strong></a> unveils her dynamic debut album, <em><strong>Will You Go With Me</strong></em><em><strong>?&nbsp;</strong></em>A heartfelt blend of country, folk-rock, and Americana, the album weaves stories of self-discovery, dream-chasing, and connection with poignant, sweet lyrics and unforgettable melodies."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/365lCpY9RuBouGrfH8jKx7?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by her small-town upbringing in Southern Oregon, <strong><em>Will You Go With Me?&nbsp;</em></strong>acts as a score for Racyne's transition to urban life in Denver, and now Seattle. Showcasing lush instrumentation, vibrant hooks, and authentic lyrics, it reflects her evolution as an artist and individual.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This album represents a formative chapter of my life. It’s filled with reflection, self-discovery, dream-chasing, love and moments from all the life that happened while I was busy making plans. I found myself in these songs, and I hope you can find something in them, too.”","cite":"- Singer-songwriter Racyne Parker"},{"t":"p","html":"Drawing comparisons to <strong>Lainey Wilson</strong>, \"if she was from the PNW,\" <strong>Kacey Musgraves</strong>, <strong>Lord Huron</strong>, and <strong>Keith Urban</strong>, Racyne's sound is a fresh take on country and Americana, featuring standout tracks like the critically and fan acclaimed \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3nHKvKpYOpurnagFu0BXEO?si=dab59d3cc2894bb7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Make It Out Alive</a>,\" \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/63LmcLUCuzLXvMEiRyImpm?si=d6afa254f07346bd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Willow Tree</a>,\" \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6hLHCOYhyLgnREDhLPBU56?si=f811805929d04b49\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Already Late</a>,\" \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/06DFVnjywTvA38H7ftT66s?si=3507f0dc532545fc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Most Likely To Be</a>,\" and \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1oeES1dXH0kiBY39s5gNGJ?si=02974c4783744295\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Summertime Sweet</a>.\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/zzD5Bgr2rWg?si=61LElVxpXxCgHt5f","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"Capturing the spirit of small-town grit and the bittersweet pursuit of new beginnings, the album is brought to life with varied guitar, swelling pedal steel, dynamic bass, drums and ear-catching vocals with hooks to boot. The result is a dynamic, lyrically driven and full sound rooted in country, but growing into folk and Americana."},{"t":"p","html":"Like a personal photo album of the past five years, <strong><em>Will You Go With Me?</em></strong> captures the heartache of loss, the joy of love and the excitement of hitting the road, with Racyne’s lyrics inviting listeners to embark on a journey of connection and reflection with her."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>\"Will You Go With Me?\" LYRICS SNIPPET</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Somewhere between strong roots and light wings"},{"t":"p","html":"I want to soar ‘til I can’t get any older"},{"t":"p","html":"It’s bound to be a hell of a journey"},{"t":"p","html":"Will you go with me?"},{"t":"p","html":"“I’ve discovered so much joy in the music and the community built around it,” said Racyne. “[It] seems like we’ve come so far already... and yet, we’re just getting started on what is sure to continue to be a wild ride. And I certainly don’t want to keep at it all alone. So, of course, I have to ask—Will you go with me?”"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716470/large-8ef085113e200e8cb5f06d2e10a1355d.jpg","alt":"will-you-go-with-me-album-cover-3000.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716470/preview-92afbf2ccf0a6b59a0967b02072d9907.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716468/large-77ea45a4c49e840f47a76fb3e88f03ba.jpg","alt":"stephanie-mikuls-8 (2).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716468/preview-8ef6cce77dd5839c975efeb262d396d4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716473/large-062d726217263c521196362ce1e2a529.jpg","alt":"racyne-album-polaroids08.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716473/preview-8f43e34a7818c60e488c4774182ed4fa.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716472/large-c2d175fcb3cff81c5fe65a4402e4f15c.jpg","alt":"racyne-album-polaroids01.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716472/preview-edc1f234b66d2b8d899312bcd1e2f89e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716469/large-865a45a680566420c5b20c1e1837c625.jpg","alt":"stephanie-mikuls-14.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716469/preview-4759cc433cef6ade47e1c706adf2b2a1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716471/large-9e9b708b754dd36c326b2ff866cae147.jpg","alt":"stephanie-mikuls-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716471/preview-67ad9dbbee6269f4d4db07e0417675bc.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716465/large-489f35ae2346919aa2c68a3ca6ba0f9c.jpg","alt":"racyne-album-polaroids04.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716465/preview-23c53743878434594e5879de6c10c40a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716466/large-75480b0a7e7ed854e53e3c83e60c2b96.jpg","alt":"racyne-album-polaroids00.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716466/preview-3a5186f2b62abb3ad5d511dcd10a57fe.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716467/large-72a25be5962d19f7018c0a6450cc6413.jpg","alt":"stephanie-mikuls-13 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716467/preview-88eb87b0cb1f07c3290ed24acd14e5c3.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by Stephanie Mikuls"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"All songs on <em>Will You Go With Me?</em> are written by Racyne Parker, except <strong>“See How Far It Takes Me”</strong> (co-written with <strong>Claire Kelly</strong>) and <strong>“Get Close”</strong> (co-written with <strong>Andy Sydow</strong>). The album was primarily recorded, produced, and mixed by <strong>Randall Kent</strong> at <strong>Deaf Dog Studios&nbsp;</strong>in Nashville, with <strong>“Get Close”</strong> produced by <strong>Andy Sydow</strong> and engineered by <strong>Loren Dorland</strong> at <strong>Mighty Fine Studios</strong> in Denver.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Mastering was handled by <strong>Sam Moses</strong> at <strong>Moses Mastering</strong> (Nashville). The project features performances by <strong>Regan Akers</strong> (bass), <strong>Brian Cox</strong> (drums), <strong>Blake Mohler </strong>(banjo, lap steel, pedal steel), and <strong>Racyne Parker</strong> herself on vocals, guitar, and backing vocals, among others."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/racyneparker/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@racyneparker","post":false},{"t":"h3","html":"About Racyne Parker:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://racyneparker.com/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Racyne Parker</strong></a> is a Seattle-based singer-songwriter whose music blends country, folk, Americana, and singer-songwriter styles with heartfelt storytelling and emotional authenticity. Growing up in small-town Oregon, she found early inspiration from performing with her dad’s country-rock band."},{"t":"p","html":"Since launching her career in 2018, Racyne has released the critically acclaimed singles <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3nHKvKpYOpurnagFu0BXEO?si=dab59d3cc2894bb7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Make It Out Alive</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/63LmcLUCuzLXvMEiRyImpm?si=bcb594de4a984459\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Willow Tree</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/06DFVnjywTvA38H7ftT66s?si=9dcbcec23e464261\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Most Likely To Be</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> earning finalist spots in prestigious contests like <strong>Denver's&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://ktcl.iheart.com/alternate/amp/2023-11-01-hometown-for-the-holidays/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hometown for the Holidays</strong></a>, the <strong>Planet Bluegrass'&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://bluegrass.com/telluride/lineup/telluride-troubadour\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Telluride Troubadour Contest</strong></a> and <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/story.php/?story_fbid=1220818119256866&amp;id=100039860691949&amp;_rdr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Folk Festival's Songwriter Contest</strong></a>, and the <a href=\"https://unsignedonly.com/winners\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Unsigned Only organization's Song Contest</strong></a>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With influences like <strong>Kacey Musgraves</strong> and <strong>Lord Huron</strong>, her music explores themes of small-town life, chasing dreams, celebrating family and love, and finding joy in the little moments."},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@racyneparker/video/7460642220564122926","handle":"@racyneparker"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://racyneparker.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/racyneparker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/RacyneParkerMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC21kdV8q3gC23m_DOhQreoA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@racyneparker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"382371","title":"Hev's Journey Subscriber and Fan page. Subscribe for behind-the-scenes access for events, new songs, and much more.","date":"2025-02-21","lead":"Rising Pop/R&B Artist Explores Love, Loss, and Self-Doubt in Emotional New Release","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/382371/f85e9d29f2910f405e3d7029e35925b2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Rising Pop/R&amp;B Artist Explores Love, Loss, and Self-Doubt in Emotional New Release"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7wHvbRV0v2M26L8pnnIFIf?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Spotsylvania, VA (February 21, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>–<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5RP7h9xg0Q5Th5qGbo6cek?si=WOUpuBZ1SLqjePE1mSIv-A&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=d8d1fe9140794257\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hev’s Journey</strong></a>, the rising Pop/R&amp;B sensation recognized as an artist to watch in 2025, returns with her latest single, <strong>\"Why I Cry.\"</strong> Releasing on February 21, 2025, the track dives deep into the complexities of love, self-sabotage, and the emotional turbulence of losing both a relationship and oneself along the way."},{"t":"p","html":"Blending heartfelt storytelling with the lush, melodic sound of young <strong>Ariana Grande</strong>, \"Why I Cry\" encapsulates the bittersweet experience of planning a future with someone, only to watch it unravel. The song navigates shifting emotions, the power of doubt sown by friends, and the internal battle between hope and heartbreak."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song is one of my favorites,” shares Hev’s Journey. “I was able to sing about two artists that I admire in the song. It’s a fun and playful spin on losing love.”","cite":""},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by Grammy-winning, multi-platinum recording and mix engineer <strong>Serge “Surgical” Tsai</strong>, \"Why I Cry\" offers a seamless blend of smooth R&amp;B grooves and pop sensibilities, solidifying Hev’s Journey’s reputation as an artist who delivers both depth and relatability in her music."},{"t":"p","html":"A versatile artist who seamlessly combines personal storytelling with universal themes, Hev’s Journey has been praised for her previous releases, including “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3zVKl8KTkye7RLt9b1JdMl?si=b21a6e3152a14545\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dance</strong></a>,” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7o8xjzUMtnzAOyndT0llwt?si=df7de73c68af405a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Broken Promises</strong></a>”, and has garnered attention from outlets such as <strong>Music By Humans&nbsp;</strong>and<strong>&nbsp;Rosa Distrito</strong>, among others. With her standout performance at <strong>Sweet Auburn Spring Fest&nbsp;</strong>in front of over 100,000 attendees, Hev’s Journey has solidified herself as a rising star.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond her music, Hev’s Journey is a passionate advocate for women’s empowerment, using her platform to inspire young people to embrace their voices. Her commitment to authenticity and cultural pride makes her a unique force in the music industry, resonating with listeners navigating their own journeys of love and self-discovery."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/722694/large-61453a1d4cdf1c08203a63a53b0dfbbd.jpg","alt":"Why I Cry Cover Jpg to offically use.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/722694/preview-bb8a34c43424d73cc578d4292380963b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715294/large-2a6967d418a740870abf29e253db7b64.jpg","alt":"IMG_0640.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715294/preview-3fba38a33cd9eee4cff4a81c9c0b9a2c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715295/large-8daea2bb637fabff21f5d2613aec61a6.jpg","alt":"IMG_0539.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715295/preview-5263340c8742e77b3aab0c488cefdcbe.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715297/large-82a9eea91f3bd83b01867d743ca24ebd.jpg","alt":"IMG_0784.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715297/preview-5f132e99dec06344f3c79d701e20a152.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Mats Jerndal (Oddbox Studios)"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hev&#39;s Journey:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.hevsjourney.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Heavenleigh Villar</strong></a>, better known by her stage name<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5RP7h9xg0Q5Th5qGbo6cek?si=WOUpuBZ1SLqjePE1mSIv-A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hev’s Journey</strong></a>, is a rising Pop/R&amp;B artist whose heartfelt lyrics and captivating melodies have quickly earned her a dedicated fanbase. Based in <strong>Spotsylvania, VA</strong>, Hev’s music blends personal experiences with universally relatable themes, creating a sound that is both intimate and inspiring. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a style influenced by <strong>Adele</strong>, <strong>SZA</strong>, <strong>Laufey</strong>, and <strong>Liana Flores</strong>, Hev’s Journey crafts haunting, passionate, optimistic, and undeniably personal songs. Her artistry has evolved from early inspirations to a more self-reflective and raw sound, embracing her unique voice as a Dominican and African-American artist."},{"t":"p","html":"Hev’s Journey debuted with the single “<strong>Just Crush</strong>” and has since released a steady stream of music that showcases her growth as a songwriter and vocalist. Her discography includes several fan favorites including the most recently released “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3zVKl8KTkye7RLt9b1JdMl?si=910543ccfd7c48e4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dance</strong></a>”, which has been praised for its vibrant energy and cultural authenticity (<em><strong>The Concert Chronicles</strong></em>).&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Along the way, Hev’s Journey has been spotlighted by prominent publications and has graced the stage at major events like the <strong>Sweet Auburn Spring Fest</strong>, performing for over 100,000 attendees. She was also featured on the <em><strong>Women of Substance Podcast</strong></em>, highlighting her as a representative of empowerment, authenticity, and connection in the music industry.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Her music is for everyone—teens and adults alike—offering a soundtrack to life’s highs and lows. With a mission to inspire young people to use their voices, Hev’s lyrics often delve into personal challenges, such as overcoming self-doubt and proving critics wrong."},{"t":"p","html":"When she’s not writing or performing, Hev enjoys spending time with her beloved dog, <strong>Coco</strong>, and engaging with fans on social media. She also participates in philanthropic efforts, such as the <strong>Anne Beers Back to School Community </strong>and <strong>Empowerment Day</strong>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hev&#39;s Journey!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/436x8jbcJgI","height":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.hevsjourney.com/","img":"","title":"Hev's Journey Subscriber and Fan page. Subscribe for behind-the-scenes access for events, new songs, and much more.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://instagram.com/hevs.journey\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://tr.ee/WXwR3WOIlo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCqHGpnDx8VY3sONz-m75org?app=desktop&amp;sub_confirmation=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"382154","title":"Stone Cottage Studios Opens New Location and Announces Upcoming Events","date":"2025-02-18","lead":"Stone Cottage Studios makes its mark in the Boulder music scene with new Pearl Street Location","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/382154/da241d6a57c9fcd8b670649c3c342bd9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Stone Cottage Studios makes its mark in the Boulder music scene with new Pearl Street Location"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>BOULDER, CO (February 25, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>– <a href=\"https://www.stonecottagestudios.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stone Cottage Studios</strong></a>, a premier recording and live performance venue, is thrilled to announce the opening of its new location at 1928 Pearl Street in downtown Boulder. This beautifully restored historic brick building now serves as a vibrant hub for artists and music enthusiasts, offering a unique blend of high-quality audio experiences and intimate live events."},{"t":"p","html":"In partnership with <a href=\"https://crescendoaudio.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Crescendo Fine Audio</strong></a>, Stone Cottage Studios provides an unparalleled environment for both musicians and audiophiles. The facility features four dedicated listening rooms equipped with premium sound systems, allowing visitors to immerse themselves in exceptional audio experiences. Additionally, the venue offers a curated selection of vintage guitars, turntables, vinyl, amplifiers, and more, catering to the diverse needs of the music community."},{"t":"quote","html":"\"Our mission at Stone Cottage Studios is to support artists locally, nationally, and internationally through high-quality recordings, video production, livestream events, and collaborations....We are excited to bring this vision to life in our new Pearl Street location, creating a space where art and high-fidelity audio converge.\"","cite":"Jamie Maynard, founder of Stone Cottage Studios"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724246/large-037a1a339f2c48affe57dc4886ac3107.jpg","alt":"Viewing Rooms.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724246/preview-0ed3f6b1be760e135b50473253192c68.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724247/large-6960f4fc72da640232b66dc85ff81287.jpg","alt":"Untitled-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724247/preview-cd50bddd87d40fa35ed3dd348b3e52cc.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724248/large-12d215e8091fe672aace94a097c23749.jpg","alt":"DSC_1538.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724248/preview-17d195be3a4874b21706702d469545c9.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724249/large-222310c9110e18e6b4e3346f6873a5ce.jpg","alt":"Front .jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724249/preview-ba7b65a1dce793d0af06c3c348a57212.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724250/large-0083c8a7c0051ddc05af1f793fe33e9f.jpg","alt":"DSC_1570.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724250/preview-a39aece1bd0a04edc18d7f18d25c51f5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724251/large-7af40f698592774aa6d681384a847424.jpg","alt":"Live Room.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724251/preview-7f9d3e71992bbc9817655f54928901a4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724252/large-f967f25b69fd532a623b125300d46a5a.jpg","alt":"DSC_1527.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724252/preview-a529f0d5c3205b2a8d12b0bb52d22d04.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724253/large-3a9ea1f7e1f8445ff6aa351aa1f36dac.jpg","alt":"Untitled-1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724253/preview-26225bf70ac3785c69524c5361c3434a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724254/large-267a65e0be5c542cfc7dc70100d53b73.jpg","alt":"Viewing Room.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/724254/preview-5b78e7ab9a189124516c252a307604e7.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>Images of the new Stone Cottage Studios location on Pearl Street in Boulder, CO.</em>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Upcoming Events:"},{"t":"p","html":"To celebrate the opening, Stone Cottage Studios is inviting music fans to come and experience the new space, engage with their vibrant local music scene, and experience the fusion of artistic expression and high-fidelity audio. A series of a series of intimate live recording events featuring a diverse lineup of artists is scheduled including the following acts:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Liz Longley:</strong> Saturday, March 1st - Liz Longley is a Nashville-based singer-songwriter known for her captivating voice and deeply emotional music. A Berklee College of Music graduate, she has earned accolades from prestigious songwriting competitions, including the BMI John Lennon Songwriting Scholarship. Her critically acclaimed albums, from her self-titled debut to <em>Funeral For My Past</em>, showcase a blend of Americana, gospel-infused soul, and shimmering pop. Her devoted fanbase made headlines when they raised over $150,000 to help her reclaim and independently release her sixth album, making her the #4 most funded solo female musician in Kickstarter history. Praised by<em>&nbsp;Billboard</em>, <em>Forbes</em>, and <em>Newsweek</em>, Longley continues to forge a deeply personal connection with her listeners, creating music on her own terms."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Morgan Myles:&nbsp;</strong>Wednesday, March 5th - Morgan Myles is a Nashville powerhouse known for her five-octave range, genre-blending sound, and heartfelt storytelling. Rising to prominence with a third-place finish on <em>The Voice</em> and a standing ovation at her Grand Ole Opry debut, she has amassed 30+ million YouTube views and opened for artists like Luke Bryan, Jake Owen, and Kane Brown, performing over 100 shows a year. Featured in <em>Billboard</em>, <em>Rolling Stone</em>, and <em>CMT</em>, Myles defies country norms, fusing rock, soul, and Americana influences. Now signed with KZZ Music/Blue Élan, she embraces a more authentic artistic vision, continuing to build a career that deeply connects with audiences."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/726322/large-f7a78009842d230c7b000257c8caa534.png","alt":"Copy of Sat March 1 (1080 x 1080 px) (5).png"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connor Garvey &amp; Alexa Wildish:</strong> Thursday, March 6th - Connor Garvey and Alexa Wildish are two acclaimed singer-songwriters bringing depth and authenticity to the modern folk and Americana landscape. Garvey, an award-winning artist from Portland, Maine, captivates audiences with his engaging presence, poetic lyricism, and uplifting storytelling. His latest album, <em>Another End of the Year</em>, showcases his growth as a songwriter, tackling personal and universal themes with sincerity and optimism. Wildish, a Colorado-based artist with a background in classical voice and musical theatre, shifted to Americana after being inspired by The Wailin’ Jennys and Nickel Creek. Her self-titled debut EP, featuring contributions from industry greats, established her as a compelling new voice, earning her first place at Planet Bluegrass’s emerging songwriter competition. Following her standout run on <em>The Voice</em> in 2023, she released <em>After Love</em>, a cover EP expanding on the rich, ethereal folk sound of her debut. Together, Garvey and Wildish bring a heartfelt, evocative energy to every performance, blending masterful musicianship with deeply resonant storytelling."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Covenhoven:&nbsp;</strong>Saturday, March 8th - Covenhoven is the indie-folk project of multi-instrumentalist and singer-songwriter Joel Van Horne, known for his rich harmonies, evocative lyrics, and orchestral folk arrangements. Since 2013, he has released four full-length albums—with a fifth, <em>The Color of the Dark</em>, set for early spring 2025—featuring collaborations with artists from Bon Iver, Gregory Alan Isakov, and The Fray. His 2021 album <em>IV</em> expanded his sound into chamber pop, praised by <em>Bandwagon Magazine</em> for its lush instrumentation. Covenhoven has toured extensively, sharing the stage with Jose Gonzalez, Gregory Alan Isakov, and Lord Huron, while his music has reached millions through placements on TV shows like <em>13 Reasons Why</em>, <em>Nashville</em>, and <em>Teen Wolf</em>. Whether performing solo with looping textures or backed by a full band, Covenhoven’s sound captivates both intimate venues and grand outdoor spaces."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Junaco:</strong> Friday, March 21st - Los Angeles/Portland based indie folk/rock band Junaco is on tour promoting their winter single \"Serene\" and upcoming LP. Informed to inspire, collaborate, and create - Junaco is a project founded by Shahana and Joey La Rosa and the bands name means rolling with the pace of life, enjoying the present and living with intention."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Abby Posner:</strong> Saturday, March 22nd &nbsp;- Abby Posner is a Los Angeles-based multi-instrumentalist, composer, and performer known for her \"Genre Fluid\" approach, blending folk, roots, electronic, and pop. A CalArts graduate, she has composed music for major TV shows, films, and commercials, including Hulu’s <em>Maggie</em>, <em>The Fosters</em>, <em>This American Life</em>, and CW’s <em>Kung Fu</em>, with placements worldwide. She has appeared on <em>GLEE</em> and <em>Famous In Love</em>, performed live on <em>Good Day LA</em> and <em>KCAL 9 News</em>, and scored award-winning films like <em>Lady Buds</em> and <em>Elizabeth Sees</em>. Whether shredding a blues guitar solo, playing banjo, or looping multiple instruments, Posner brings passion and versatility to every performance."},{"t":"caption","html":"All shows - &nbsp;Doors open at 6 PM, with the live show starting at 7 PM. Each event includes an appetizer spread, complimentary non-alcoholic beverages (BYO allowed), and a meet-and-greet with the artists. With only 35 tickets available per show, attendees are encouraged to secure their spots promptly."},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.stonecottagestudios.com/events","label":"Tickets + Additional Info","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stone Cottage Studios:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.stonecottagestudios.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stone_cottage_studios/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Stone-Cottage-Sessions-431877924271245/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCC3_uNv54fAYixLW7tS9jnA?view_as=subscriber\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"379384","title":"JAntho CHO Unveils Psychedelic Journey with New Single \"Sheath\"","date":"2025-02-03","lead":"JAntho CHO Fuses Conscious Rap, Psychedelic Soundscapes, and Hypnotic Melodies to Explore Self-Actualization and Enlightenment","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/379384/a56fa88af134a452abfc488d9d9e6981.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"JAntho CHO Fuses Conscious Rap, Psychedelic Soundscapes, and Hypnotic Melodies to Explore Self-Actualization and Enlightenment"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7v6brwKWvYec0SYhuQI20g?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Kansas City, MO (February 3, 2025)</strong> – Rising genre-blending artist <strong>JAntho CHO</strong> is back with his latest sonic odyssey,&nbsp;<strong>\"Sheath\"</strong>—a mind-expanding track that fuses conscious rap, psychedelic soundscapes, and hypnotic melodies. From album <em>Cloud 180 2</em>, \"Sheath\" continues JAntho CHO’s exploration of self-actualization, enlightenment, and the transformative power of music."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/719423/large-417bfb8b9a42968d18c747eb90a8031b.png","alt":"Cover art for 'Cloud 180 2' album"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Sheath\" immerses listeners in an otherworldly experience, weaving together ethereal production and introspective lyricism. With themes of transcendence, spiritual awakening, and cosmic connectivity, the track paints a vivid picture of JAntho CHO’s journey through psychedelics and self-discovery. Trippy, melodic, and vibrantly psychedelic, \"Sheath\" pushes the boundaries of hip-hop and alternative music. The song’s hypnotic rhythm and atmospheric beats transport listeners to a lucid dream-like state, reminiscent of artists like Kid Cudi, Flying Lotus, and OutKast.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Sheath is existential....A trip to travel to.”","cite":"-JAntho CHO"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/t08X6cEdtfs","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"JAntho CHO, known for his genre-defying sound and thought-provoking artistry, has built a dedicated following since his early days in Kansas City, Missouri. His signature style—dubbed <em>CHO Music—</em>blends hip-hop, soul, jazz, blues, and alternative rock, creating a sound that resonates with listeners seeking both depth and innovation. With past projects like&nbsp;<em>Cloud 180</em>, JAntho CHO has consistently used music as a vessel for consciousness expansion. Now, with \"Sheath\", he invites fans to embark on yet another journey—a psychedelic voyage through the mind and spirit.&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with JAntho CHO:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/janthocho\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM</a> | <a href=\"https://x.com/janthocho\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter/X</a> |<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/JAnthoCHO816\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> FACEBOOK</a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"377161","title":"Singer/Songwriter Kyle Davis released his sixth record, \"Make It Count\". Originally discorvered by Don Dixon and Phil Ramone, his music has been hailed in Billboard and Rolling Stone magazines.","date":"2025-01-22","lead":"Kyle Davis anticipates the release of a new album with the title track \"Jericho\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/377161/5a1b3c46ce6c8acea0a0764d0486aa3b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Kyle Davis anticipates the release of a new album with the title track \"Jericho\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3rhJD4VibhTWaBMGEhdyvt?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Prince George, VA (February 28, 2025)</strong> – Acclaimed singer-songwriter Kyle Davis is set to make a powerful return this February with the release of his highly anticipated new single, <strong>\"Jericho\"</strong>. A tease to his upcoming album, the track offers a soulful journey through themes of love, loss, and self-discovery, and it stands as a testament to Davis's enduring ability to craft songs that resonate deeply with listeners. &nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/xXg1Rv6dTXA?si=M4ZQvCP-gYWpLXAZ","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Jericho\" marks Davis's seventh studio record and reunites the celebrated team behind his 1999 Sony debut, <em>Raising Heroes</em>. Produced and mixed by Don Dixon (R.E.M., The Smithereens), the track was recorded in the legendary Mitch Easter’s studio in Winston-Salem, with additional vocals captured at Davis’s home studio in Prince George, VA, and Elephant Ear Studio in Richmond, VA. A striking follow-up to his 2020 release, <em>Make It Count</em>, Davis reaffirms his place as one of Virginia’s most compelling voices, offering a song that is both deeply personal and universally relatable. &nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716259/large-e03a1e9b2f7307902f9b727e52db400d.jpg","alt":"\"Jericho\" cover art by Ande Davis"},{"t":"quote","html":"\"What draws me to Jericho is that he hasn’t given up and is still trying to slay the dragons in his life... He’s still seeking redemption this far down the line.”","cite":"Kyle Davis on new song \"Jericho\""},{"t":"p","html":"With its lush instrumentation—featuring contributions from musical luminaries like Rob Ladd (drums), Peter Holsapple (mandolin), and Davis himself on piano—\"Jericho\" is a heartfelt exploration of life’s complexities. Lyrically, the song delves into the search for meaning beyond material wealth, offering listeners a poignant reminder that fulfillment often lies in human connection and personal redemption. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Renowned for his emotive voice and introspective songwriting, Davis’s career spans decades and includes accolades such as a 4-star review in <em>Rolling Stone</em>, a cover feature in&nbsp;<em>Billboard Magazine</em>, and multiple songs on the Triple AAA charts. Having shared stages with icons like Bob Dylan and John Mayer, Davis continues to carve a unique path, blending influences that recall Jackson Browne, Peter Gabriel, and Bill Withers. &nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5lq6g7ALA2XGi4f4e7YR9h?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kyle Davis:"},{"t":"p","html":"Kyle Davis, a Richmond, Virginia-based singer-songwriter, makes a triumphant return this winter with his latest record,<em>&nbsp;Jericho</em>. This marks Davis's seventh studio album and reunites the stellar lineup from his acclaimed 1999 Sony release,&nbsp;<em>Raising Heroes</em>. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Throughout his career, Davis has earned critical acclaim, including a 4-star review in <em>Rolling Stone</em>, a cover feature in&nbsp;<em>Billboard Magazine</em>, and multiple songs landing on the Triple AAA charts. His distinctive voice has graced major TV commercials and shows, as well as records by legendary artists like Bruce Hornsby and rising stars such as 49 Winchester. Davis has also shared the stage with icons ranging from Bob Dylan to John Mayer. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"After taking a hiatus to focus on raising his family, Davis returned to recording with <em>Make It Count</em> in 2020, an album praised by critics but released amidst the challenges of the COVID-19 pandemic. With&nbsp;<em>Jericho</em>, he raises the bar even higher. Produced by Don Dixon, much of the record was created at Mitch Easter’s studio in Winston-Salem, with final touches recorded at Davis’s home in Prince George, Virginia, and Elephant Ear Studio in Richmond. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a refined perspective on life, love, and loss, Davis’s songwriting has only deepened with time. His music continues to draw comparisons to the evocative storytelling of Jackson Browne, the soulful introspection of Peter Gabriel, and the timeless groove of Bill Withers—a testament to his ability to connect with audiences on a profound level."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/6s000ljQ-E4","height":""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Kyle!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C_9NM9SSSsj/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.kylewdavismusic.com/","img":"","title":"Singer/Songwriter Kyle Davis released his sixth record, \"Make It Count\". Originally discorvered by Don Dixon and Phil Ramone, his music has been hailed in Billboard and Rolling Stone magazines.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/kylewdavismusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/kylewdavismusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCAd1M5QdT1GsfgFqngAEuUQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1fQuYKsLfkTcqpj1pIwTYz?si=qgjmSdbhTV6zJqr6wNkvWg&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=f3742451339946a5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"377165","title":"INDVGO Announces New Single, \"How Is It Love\" Just in Time for Valentines Day","date":"2025-01-22","lead":"R&B artist INDVGO explores the emotional depths of love and self-discovery with poignant new single, \"How Is It Love\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/377165/c3ac472ae6f4dfc6c4a3dbceb9b9885c.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"R&amp;B artist INDVGO explores the emotional depths of love and self-discovery with poignant new single, \"How Is It Love\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2qAY1Ju7Wer3mWaETcZwjY?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Brooklyn, NY (February 4, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>– Emerging R&amp;B sensation <strong>INDVGO</strong> is poised to captivate audiences with her deeply introspective new single, <strong>\"How Is It Love\"</strong>. Known for her evocative lyrics and genre-blending sound, INDVGO takes listeners on a journey through the raw, complex emotions of love—the highs, the lows, and everything in between."},{"t":"p","html":"\"How Is It Love\" is a soulful exploration of the contradictions of love and the resilience that comes from healing. Haunting melodies and smooth, sensual vocals amplify the emotional depth, making it a cathartic experience for listeners. The song’s lyrics, written by the artist herself, delve into the internal battle of being deeply in love yet feeling trapped by its complexities. Lines like <em>\"Now loving you just feels home\"</em> and \"<em>I'm healed, no need to cause you pain\"</em> suggests that while love has been a source of pain, it also empowers one to move forward into new relationships. The track’s chorus, repeating <em>\"How is it love?\"</em> challenges the romanticized ideals of love and instead embraces its messy, often painful reality. While INDVGO candidly explores heartbreak and healing, she speaks to the universal journey of self-discovery and empowerment and addresses the emotional labor often carried by women in relationships, making it an anthem of strength and self-love."},{"t":"quote","html":"“‘How Is It Love’ is really about emotional chaos and finding peace within yourself. Healing starts when you fall deeply in love with your own soul...This song is my way of processing the contradictions of love—the pain, the comfort, the resilience.”","cite":"- INDVGO"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/716261/large-6bde22187a8b3146d1a1a935226407a5.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"How Is It Love\""},{"t":"p","html":"INDVGO's introspective lyricism is expanded upon with an ethereal production style featuring a sound reminiscent of Jhené Aiko, Summer Walker, and Kehlani. The song’s moody, atmospheric instrumentation creates a reflective vibe, while INDVGO’s raw vocal delivery mirrors the emotional weight of the lyrics - balancing both vulnerability and empowerment. The song’s nostalgic undertones, captured in lines like <em>\"Loving on each other like it’s ‘93 / 3am chilling, you know where I be,\"</em> evoke a timeless quality that when set against its layered production builds a compelling soundscape to make the experience both intimate and universal for the audience. &nbsp;Overall, the song acknowledges love as both a source of strength and vulnerability, capturing the emotional push-and-pull of relationships in a way that resonates with anyone who has faced heartbreak or betrayal."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About INDVGO:"},{"t":"p","html":"INDVGO blends soulful melodies with elements of hip-hop, R&amp;B, and alternative influences to create a sound all her own. Her smooth, sensual vocals and nostalgic melodies are a reflection of life’s full spectrum – from love and luck to heartbreak and hardship. INDVGO’s artistry is deeply rooted in the pulse of New York City, capturing both its raw energy and intimate vibes. Her music explores themes of emotional depth, self-discovery, and empowerment, inviting listeners to connect through their own stories of resilience and growth.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://beacons.ai/indvgo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/indvgo/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@indvgomusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/61Se7XU0y8Gi4T64t1nfMA?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"363971","title":"Hallie Marie Music ✸☽ A Denver-Based musician who blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling. She has a series of releases arriving in 2025, with her first titled \"Indebted\" arriving January 21.","date":"2025-01-21","lead":"Denver singer-songwriter Hallie Marie breaks onto the scene with new single \"Indebted\".","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/363971/aaaf22728c362d604364693501b45de8.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Denver singer-songwriter Hallie Marie breaks onto the scene with new single \"Indebted\"."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1O4Q92TIuafovajnJyR557?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (January 21, 2024) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qjqY0W9hRpqy_g6Ky9uPyw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a>, an emerging artist known for her evocative songwriting and powerful vocal delivery, released her new rock ballad titled “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1O4Q92TIuafovajnJyR557?si=5e67e704d03440ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Indebted</strong></a>”. The song, launched on January 21, delves deep into the challenges of mental health and self-destruction, exploring the intricate emotional landscape and the vices that accompany these struggles. With a unique sound that blends elements of rock with soulful balladry, “Indebted” promises to resonate with listeners on multiple levels."},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/halliemarie/indebted","label":"Listen on All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"“Indebted” is not just a song but a poignant reflection on the cyclical nature of desire and suffering. Hallie draws inspiration from Buddhist philosophy, particularly the idea that desire can create both the universe and profound suffering. In her lyrics, she articulates her own personal journey, emphasizing the internal battle that often manifests as a directionless, painful longing. Hallie states, <em>“There is a tendency for artists and creatives of all kinds to self-sabotage. When I am low, it is my own thoughts, my own mind that creates the hell I am using a fix to try and escape from.... the moment I acknowledge that I am creating my own suffering is the moment I have the power to change it.”<strong></strong></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Never have I slipped so far away<br>Do I have to pay the devil off<br>For just one little tiny drop of heaven?<br>If anyone could bring me to this godforsaken place<br>It’s plain to see, it’s me, it’s only me<br>I’m indebted.</em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>&nbsp;- Lyrics from \"Indebted\" -</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711572/large-31ca4c70fa3427a91c9cc56003c01149.jpg","alt":"Cover Art for \"Indebted\""},{"t":"p","html":"The rock-ballad captures the emotional whiplash associated with the compulsive drive toward fleeting pleasures in an attempt to fill a void. Hallie aims to convey the message that while temporary escapes may provide momentary relief, they ultimately come at a significant cost. The lyricism in “Indebted” speaks to the price one pays for such fleeting moments of happiness, highlighting the inevitable come down that follows."},{"t":"p","html":"The soundscape for “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1O4Q92TIuafovajnJyR557?si=dc9ec75a51ef4a2f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Indebted</a>” is evocative - showcasing Hallie’s powerfully dramatic vocals against a soft and steady piano rhythm that morphs into a rock-infused power anthem by the end. A fusion of <strong>Fiona Apple</strong>’s raw emotionality intertwined with the grandeur of a gospel choir, the song is cinematic in nature - drawing parallels to a theme song for a <strong>James Bond</strong> movie with its dramatic flair and profound thematic content. As Hallie continues to carve out her space in the music industry, her ability to tackle such complex themes with authenticity will be what sets her apart."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/-b10e31cd63b2c0317696d54d044a4e07.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-32 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711574/preview-c33bb4c8c0fb8d62a46ea644fb5ad2e1.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/-1302eb881563358853da571d1fb91c45.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-36 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711576/preview-e17e8b3fa61065cd5c4017c5cabd0e2d.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/large-3fd73d88583417c22d63d14ef4d100aa.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-14 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711575/preview-4811aaab4e4c9d4f52c8820f4714b20b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/large-29c12eef5ba54b62cc04f5bc34eee872.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-29 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711573/preview-24ede99c287103be1e22c17641577c77.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/-da81f45fe86805db981f72d86eff8965.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-46 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711578/preview-8f88dcb7cb4728eef25338442eb31f22.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/large-3740cb07a0046ee2a3bf82c6c328555f.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-44 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711577/preview-a44d9f029894f554f894eed711194762.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/large-69157f55a4afc3f0f8b64d0c7951e6c8.jpeg","alt":"Hallie Marie - The Keep-1 Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/711579/preview-88af250d089625bac98f9cf6e7350728.jpeg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hallie Marie:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hallie Marie</strong></a> is a multifaceted artist who beautifully balances light and shadow in her work. With an intellectually curious spirit, she dives deep into the complexities of human emotions, crafting music that resonates with listeners on many levels — from the highs of love and joy to the depths of melancholy. Drawing inspiration from artists like <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>, <strong>Billy Joel</strong>, and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, Hallie’s sound blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling."},{"t":"p","html":"Collaborating with the Denver-based band <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1UP2Zk7NI1U6KBhpPfPKBt?si=y0EiRbwmTCSlwg_-3sd3vg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Direville</a>, Hallie Marie has already begun to make her mark on the music industry with popular releases “<strong>Sympathy</strong>” and “<strong>Free Spirit</strong>”, among others. Now branching out on her own, her solo music endeavors combine poetic mystical imagery with direct and casual insight derived from raw life experience.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Embracing the beauty of authenticity and connecting with each of us at our core, Hallie invites her audience into her world, sharing not just her music but also her creative process — writing, arranging, and recording — along with the benefit of what she has learned through struggle and resilience. She aims to connect deeply with her listeners, sharing meaningful ideas that resonate long after the music ends."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hallie Marie!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/halliemariemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@halliemariemusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.halliemariemusic.com/","img":"","title":"Hallie Marie Music ✸☽ A Denver-Based musician who blends pop, rock, and folk influences, creating a genuine connection through heartfelt lyrics and relatable storytelling. She has a series of releases arriving in 2025, with her first titled \"Indebted\" arriving January 21.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://instagram.com/halliemariemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/33JLx5OttrwiRHAUo8ClvP?si=qv9RFavvRmeHdVLljnpMBQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | &nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100068917929503\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"376056","title":"Nick Duane Releases Fifth Album, \"Credibility,\" a Deep Dive into the Human Condition","date":"2025-01-16","lead":"Providence-based indie artist blends raw emotion with decades of musical mastery.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/376056/2c0eef9f9ac71e0a76bf255baebd75c8.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Providence-based indie artist blends raw emotion with decades of musical mastery."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2Rm3iSWzo0mg43XTndHXFW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"PROVIDENCE, RI (January 28, 2025) – Today, acclaimed indie singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://nickduanemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Nick Duane</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>unveils his fifth album,<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://nickduane.bandcamp.com/album/credibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Credibility</strong></em></a>, a 12-track collection exploring the nuances of the human condition through vivid storytelling and genre-blending soundscapes.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Written, recorded, and produced between May and November 2024, <em>Credibility</em> captures the essence of an artist who has spent decades honing his craft while embracing creativity on his own terms."},{"t":"p","html":"Known for blending classic influences with a futuristic edge, Nick Duane’s work on <em>Credibility</em> is both deeply personal and universally relatable. The album features the emotionally charged <strong>“Oceans,”</strong> which Nick describes as \"in some ways, the most honest song I've ever written.\" Recorded in just three vocal takes, the track captures an unfiltered, raw vulnerability while he was overcome with emotion during recording."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“It Wasn't Me”</strong> starts the album with a cinematic, story-driven approach, masterfully setting the tone for the journey ahead. <strong>“Miles Away,”</strong> is a poignant narrative inspired by a whimsical songwriting exercise that transformed into a heartfelt exploration of longing and connection. Other highlights including <strong>“Lost My Cell Phone”</strong> showcase Nick’s knack for weaving humor and introspection into his lyrics."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Every song on Credibility reflects a unique moment of inspiration. Sometimes it’s imagining a relationship that never existed, other times it’s role-playing to tap into emotions I haven't experienced firsthand. Each track represents a piece of the human condition—our hopes, our losses, and those fleeting moments of clarity.”","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Nick Duane"},{"t":"p","html":"With influences ranging from <strong>The Beatles</strong> and <strong>David Bowie</strong> to <strong>Garbage</strong> and <strong>Tom Petty</strong>, Nick's songwriting reflects a deep appreciation for music’s transformative power. Whether crafting narrative-driven lyrics or experimenting with rock and synth-pop textures, <em>Credibility</em> marks the culmination of a career defined by individuality, emotional authenticity, and a lifelong dedication to music."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715131/large-ceb50234dc8f32fbaf16e130accf73ad.jpg","alt":"promo-Confessions-001.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715131/preview-cd4dd11bc3ea5a6a94acb6c38cb23987.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715132/-67e3fb90b045f6ae88723c00c3fe6c14.png","alt":"ckjj07co-768x678.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715132/-67e3fb90b045f6ae88723c00c3fe6c14.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715133/-77620da1110699e28e070f61a48ae9c6.jpg","alt":"nd-006-1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715133/preview-d729a902b2675ccde45939533a3bfdc0.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715134/-3bb7304bf9dc108578a26131a162434d.jpg","alt":"20246399_1514006322000025_3237526339963871767_n.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715134/-3bb7304bf9dc108578a26131a162434d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715135/-d992f21d57485daed1c96c994e2b3db1.jpg","alt":"Copy-of-DSCN2118-3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715135/-d992f21d57485daed1c96c994e2b3db1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715136/-d652180ad98a682fd7c0c31cb03d19c2.jpg","alt":"449730779_442748521919718_1144962524370806285_n.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715136/-d652180ad98a682fd7c0c31cb03d19c2.jpg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Nick Duane:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Nick Duane</strong> is an indie singer-songwriter and producer from Providence, RI, known for his innovative blend of indie rock that fuses classic and futuristic elements. Over decades of creating and recording original music, Nick has carved a distinct path, embracing creativity and individuality over mainstream trends."},{"t":"p","html":"A veteran of the music scene, Nick's journey began as a founding member of the <strong>Backslap Blues Band</strong>—the first group to perform at the iconic <strong>Lupo’s Heartbreak Hotel</strong>. He later joined <strong>DC Tenz</strong>, a rock band that won the <strong>WBRU Battle of the Bands</strong>. Transitioning into solo work, Nick released five albums (<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1eXNHsZgCdOIq2wnKnyvgi?si=TetxfT37QGG3ATGali-o2g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Confessions</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0yvyBEfAEi8YsJLLmj8rdk?si=5gPlJXVaSJex4x2jfljoBw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>When We Said Goodbye</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4Trm6rXYdhKLjwc3RdoSRR?si=1cU2-7ZKSQKKQ2kLuIhM6A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Before The Storm</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3uotLjEJ6sacEeUvsNHJXh?si=bCkSwOYwR56nKU-aHBlKAg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Broken Promises</strong></a>, and <a href=\"https://nickduane.bandcamp.com/album/credibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Credibility</strong></a>) and an EP (<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1fBjVJVKrNhalFG2968xPz?si=qtXmU04lQ1Wv4_8afnPe7Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Remake Remix</strong></a>), showcasing his signature style that blends rock, synth-pop, and introspection. His work has earned recognition, including a runner-up nomination for <strong>Singer-Songwriter of the Year</strong> at the <strong>Limelight Magazine Music Awards</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Nick has also collaborated on the <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4Fdb54Yk141jx4ff6aGGHm?si=UoQOYAz3SM-i-6S4-PACXA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cold Shivers</strong></a> project with fellow musician <strong>Jim Hall</strong>, releasing the EP,<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://coldshivers.bandcamp.com/album/this-that-and-no-other\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>This that and no other</strong></em></a>. Beyond accolades, Nick’s music is deeply personal, reflecting a lifetime of storytelling, inspiration from rock and pop history, and a commitment to preserving the art of original music."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://nickduanemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/nickduane/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NickDuaneMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://youtube.com/@nickduanemusic?feature=shared\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5dmATLKJjRpKEYYaGYJlw5?si=nssxja4SR7-4Ziny56zujA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://nickduane.bandcamp.com/album/credibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bandcamp</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"371497","title":"Stephen Thomas Drops New Music Video, \"Stay Strong\"","date":"2025-01-10","lead":"The powerful tribute to perseverance and resilience is brought to life with this captivating visual narrative.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/371497/0d3386f6bc01e1264d66f573615a8452.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The powerful tribute to perseverance and resilience is brought to life with this captivating visual narrative."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/DrmOmDf7twY","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Charleston, WV (January 10, 2025) - Universal artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=YTInGlyeR_Oow3q_1Wlt9g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen</strong> <strong>Thomas</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>amplifies the message of his<strong>&nbsp;</strong>latest alt-pop/rock single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=a142a46fef1f42b2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stay Strong</strong></a>”, with the release of its highly anticipated music video.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Delivering a powerful message of hope and resilience, the video blends heartfelt storytelling with striking visuals, serving as a beacon for anyone navigating difficult circumstances—whether stationed on the frontlines, enduring a challenging hospital stay, or simply facing another demanding day."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=aa85fa2cda124133\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Stay Strong</a>” is a heartfelt tribute to the unwavering courage of our troops, individuals battling autoimmune diseases, those facing mental health struggles, and anyone confronting life’s toughest obstacles. With every chord and lyric, Stephen reminds listeners that they are not alone in their battles, urging them to keep fighting and to stay strong."},{"t":"p","html":"Directed by Will Thomas, the \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=aa85fa2cda124133\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Stay Strong</a>\" music video is an emotional journey that follows a family facing adversity, further highlighting the song's themes. At its core, the story highlights a young child battling an autoimmune disease, and his father, a soldier, navigating the dual challenges of military service and family hardship.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“To survive and succeed in life, you have to fight. And your fight isn’t over yet, it’s just beginning. Stay strong, my friends.”","cite":"- Stephen Thomas, Singer/Songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"Interwoven scenes feature Stephen performing and fighting in combat uniform, symbolizing the struggles and victories of life’s battles. The video culminates in a triumphant moment of reunion and healing for the family, set against the backdrop of celebratory fireworks—a poignant visual of hope and renewal."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>\"Stay Strong\" Lyrics (SNIPPET)</strong><br><u><br></u><em>Hold on tight</em><br><em><br>It's the fight of your life</em><br><em><br>So live or die&nbsp;<br></em><br><em>You gotta take flight </em>"},{"t":"p","html":"A powerful anthem for anyone facing life’s trials, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=aa85fa2cda124133\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Stay Strong</a>\" draws inspiration from those on the frontlines—whether in military service, hospital beds, or everyday struggles. Through its universal message of endurance, the track has become a beacon of hope, encouraging all listeners to keep pushing forward."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/686538/large-8bd6ea6b24b81e805a6d59263429310c.png","alt":"Cover art for \"Stay Strong\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Stephen Thomas:"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676846/large-55a595b43551877ff75bb9984341f332.jpg","alt":"Photo by Josh Hanna"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=oHBViFwQQaaIjt97y8p4Og\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a>, a versatile Universal Artist whose musical odyssey has taken him from Charleston, West Virginia to the forefront of the industry. With a dynamic career marked by exploration and evolution, Stephen has recently embarked on a thrilling journey into the realms of rock and alternative music, infusing his sound with raw, authentic vibes that resonate deeply with audiences."},{"t":"p","html":"As a national touring recording artist, Stephen's talent has garnered widespread acclaim, earning him five <strong>Grammy Award</strong> considerations as an independent artist. From his early beginnings to signing with <strong>SkeeloMusik</strong> / <strong>Sony RED</strong> in 2013 and eventually finding his artistic home with <strong>Creative Hearts Entertainment</strong>, Stephen's journey has been one of constant growth and discovery."},{"t":"p","html":"Stephen's impact transcends mere accolades, with his interviews featured in prestigious publications such as <strong>MTV</strong>, <strong>Vibe</strong> <strong>Magazine</strong>, <strong>Hype</strong> <strong>Magazine</strong>, and <strong>TCT</strong> <strong>Network</strong>. He has graced renowned stages alongside industry icons and walked the red carpet at events like the <strong>2014</strong> <strong>BET</strong> <strong>Live</strong> <strong>Experience</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Amidst his diverse musical endeavors, Stephen's recent immersion into rock and alternative music has been particularly transformative. Embracing the genre's edgy, rebellious spirit, Stephen has honed his craft, crafting songs that pulsate with raw emotion and electrifying energy. His single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4IJY700TPZXKlrkO0mR4zM?si=Q_xjis9iTtyfjYRfshMH5g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Best Days</strong></a>,\" soared to #2 on the iTunes Charts, standing as a testament to his artistic versatility and widespread appeal. Meanwhile, his music video for \"<a href=\"https://youtu.be/wj8FAEyFpRA?feature=shared\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Search</strong> <strong>Me</strong></a>\" received global recognition, earning placement on <strong>RevoltTV</strong> and reaching millions worldwide. Stephen's music is now readily available on all streaming platforms, inviting listeners to embark on a sonic journey filled with rock and alternative vibes."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephen!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/Cv0cZdtuXQn/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.stephentmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/StephenTMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/404?fromUrl=/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/StephenThomas1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://x.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>X</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"374606","title":"Hev's Journey Subscriber and Fan page. Subscribe for behind-the-scenes access for events, new songs, and much more.","date":"2025-01-09","lead":"Rising Pop/R&B artist Hev's Journey cements her status as an \"Artist to Watch in 2025\" with her empowering, heritage-inspired single \"Dance\", a vibrant anthem celebrating joy, individuality, and cultural pride.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/374606/7d94697052031a790a00df227d5e6846.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Rising Pop/R&amp;B artist Hev's Journey cements her status as an \"Artist to Watch in 2025\" with her empowering, heritage-inspired single \"Dance\", a vibrant anthem celebrating joy, individuality, and cultural pride."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3zVKl8KTkye7RLt9b1JdMl?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Spotsylvania, VA (January 17, 2025)&nbsp;</strong>– Rising Pop/R&amp;B sensation <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5RP7h9xg0Q5Th5qGbo6cek?si=WOUpuBZ1SLqjePE1mSIv-A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hev’s Journey</strong></a> is making waves with her latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3zVKl8KTkye7RLt9b1JdMl?si=55c9531ca91c423e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dance</strong></a>”, positioning herself as an <strong>Artist to Watch</strong> in 2025. “Dance” captures the essence of carefree joy and empowerment, blending vibrant rhythms with heartfelt lyrics that resonate deeply with listeners.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Rooted in her Dominican heritage, “Dance” showcases Hev’s Journey’s ability to merge cultural authenticity with mainstream appeal. <em>“This song is about just enjoying the moment,”</em> says Hev’s Journey. <em>“It’s about having fun times with the girls, not needing anyone to complete your happiness. I wanted to create something true to me—something I could dance to that celebrates my roots.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"The track’s sound is an eclectic mix of <strong>Ariana Grande</strong>’s energy, <strong>SZA</strong>’s soulful depth, and <strong>Taylor Swift</strong>’s storytelling, delivering an irresistible blend of English and Spanish lyrics that celebrates Hev’s Journey’s dual heritage. <em>“When I first played ‘Dance’, my mom and dad immediately got up and started dancing. Once they heard the Spanish lyrics, they were so proud to see me embracing all parts of my heritage,”</em> she adds."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/436x8jbcJgI","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"As a versatile artist who seamlessly combines personal storytelling with universal themes, Hev’s Journey has been praised for her previous releases, including “Enough” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7o8xjzUMtnzAOyndT0llwt?si=df7de73c68af405a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Broken Promises</strong></a>”, and has garnered attention from outlets such as <strong>Music By Humans </strong>and<strong>&nbsp;Rosa Distrito</strong>, among others. With her standout performance at <strong>Sweet Auburn Spring Fest </strong>in front of over 100,000 attendees, Hev’s Journey has solidified herself as a rising star. Beyond her music, Hev’s Journey is a passionate advocate for women’s empowerment, using her platform to inspire young people to embrace their voices. Her commitment to authenticity and cultural pride makes her a unique force in the music industry."},{"t":"p","html":"With “Dance”, Hev’s Journey invites listeners to let go of life’s pressures, celebrate individuality, and, most importantly, dance. The single is now streaming on all major platforms."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715294/large-2a6967d418a740870abf29e253db7b64.jpg","alt":"IMG_0640.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715294/preview-3fba38a33cd9eee4cff4a81c9c0b9a2c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715295/large-8daea2bb637fabff21f5d2613aec61a6.jpg","alt":"IMG_0539.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715295/preview-5263340c8742e77b3aab0c488cefdcbe.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715297/large-82a9eea91f3bd83b01867d743ca24ebd.jpg","alt":"IMG_0784.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715297/preview-5f132e99dec06344f3c79d701e20a152.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715298/large-252fd38d3709dd84de0fef584fafac30.jpg","alt":"IMG_0640.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/715298/preview-ae57b2582d799aaa77dc6939dce0ab0f.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Mats Jerndal (Oddbox Studios)"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Hev&#39;s Journey:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.hevsjourney.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Heavenleigh Villar</strong></a>, better known by her stage name <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5RP7h9xg0Q5Th5qGbo6cek?si=WOUpuBZ1SLqjePE1mSIv-A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hev’s Journey</a>, is a rising Pop/R&amp;B artist whose heartfelt lyrics and captivating melodies have quickly earned her a dedicated fanbase. Based in Spotsylvania, VA, Hev’s music seamlessly blends personal experiences with universally relatable themes, creating a sound that is both intimate and inspiring. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a style influenced by the likes of <strong>Adele</strong>, SZA, <strong>Laufey</strong>, and <strong>Liana Flores</strong>, Hev’s Journey crafts songs that are haunting, passionate, optimistic, and undeniably personal. Her artistry has evolved from early inspirations like Ariana Grande to a more self-reflective and raw sound, embracing her unique voice as a Dominican and African-American artist."},{"t":"p","html":"Hev’<strong></strong>s Journey debuted with the single “<strong>Just Crush</strong>” and has since released a steady stream of music that showcases her growth as a songwriter and vocalist. Her discography includes several fan favorites including the most recently released “Dance”, which has been praised for its vibrant energy and cultural authenticity (<em><strong>The Concert Chronicles</strong></em>).&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Along the way, Hev’s Journey has been spotlighted by prominent publications and has graced the stage at major events like the Sweet Auburn Spring Fest, performing for over 100,000 attendees. She was also featured on the <em><strong>Women of Substance Podcast</strong></em>, highlighting her as a representative of empowerment, authenticity, and connection in the music industry.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Her music is for everyone—teens and adults alike—offering a soundtrack to life’s highs and lows. With a mission to inspire young people to use their voices, Hev’s lyrics often delve into personal challenges, such as overcoming self-doubt and proving critics wrong."},{"t":"p","html":"When she’s not writing or performing, Hev enjoys spending time with her beloved dog, <strong>Coco</strong>, and engaging with fans on social media. She also participates in philanthropic efforts, such as the <strong>Anne Beers Back to School Community </strong>and <strong>Empowerment Day</strong>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Hev&#39;s Journey!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.hevsjourney.com/","img":"","title":"Hev's Journey Subscriber and Fan page. Subscribe for behind-the-scenes access for events, new songs, and much more.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://instagram.com/hevs.journey\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://tr.ee/WXwR3WOIlo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCqHGpnDx8VY3sONz-m75org?app=desktop&amp;sub_confirmation=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"368944","title":"Blake Smeltz Unveils Country Music Video \"You Ain't Whiskey\"","date":"2024-12-06","lead":"Blake Smeltz solidifies his status as a rising country artist with the new single \"You Ain't Whiskey\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/368944/2045a89cd38a695a3583062b0f604a35.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Blake Smeltz solidifies his status as a rising country artist with the new single \"You Ain't Whiskey\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/sBHlLKtjHBQ","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"NASHVILLE, TN (December 6, 2024) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6VtPWvA4PQlpSmWA85Ugni?si=Osp37CrKRd6fd9Ij9XNBPQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Blake Smeltz</strong></a>, a rising star in the country music scene, has officially unveiled his latest music video, “<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sBHlLKtjHBQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>You Ain’t Whiskey</strong></a>”. Showcasing Smeltz’s unique style and emotional storytelling, the single is reminiscent of early <strong>Luke Combs</strong>, blended with <strong>Gavin Adcock</strong>’s unique vocal growl - further solidifying his place as an artist to watch.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2goSyLhUZT9dj5zv5i3Sgr?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2goSyLhUZT9dj5zv5i3Sgr?si=ee8629cd52194dfb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>You Ain’t Whiskey</strong></a>” explores the heartbreak experienced in the aftermath of a breakup. Stemming from personal experiences of love and loss, Smeltz portrays a reliance on whiskey as a temporary escape from the pain of losing someone - conveying the realization that while whiskey may bring a fleeting sense of relief, it cannot replace the love he once had. Lyrics like <em>“And now it’s empty and the bottle’s on the dresser/But it ain’t whiskey that I’m looking for/It’s the one that used to be beside me everywhere I’d go/Yeah you ain’t whiskey, But you damn sure hit me”</em> highlight the complexities of coping with heartbreak."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/707051/large-da15ca948a83d01604a63dfe9e68d407.png","alt":"Cover Art for \"You Ain't Whiskey\""},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song reflects a journey through love and loss that many can relate to. I wanted to create something that resonates with people and captures the raw emotions that come with heartbreak. ‘You Ain’t Whiskey’ is a reminder that while some things may offer temporary comfort, they can never replace what was truly special.”","cite":"- Blake Smeltz"},{"t":"p","html":"With “You Ain’t Whiskey”, Blake Smeltz continues to carve out his niche in the competitive country music landscape. Working alongside <strong>Charlotte Avenue Entertainment</strong>, the release of this music video marks an important milestone in his career, setting the stage for a new album slated for release in 2025."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/707052/large-d929b5d61a620096d21059cf5ad41f4f.jpg","alt":"Image of Blake Smeltz"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Blake Smeltz:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/blakesmeltz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Blake Smeltz</strong></a>, a native of Evington, Virginia, has always felt a deep connection to nature, a bond that resonates throughout his music. A self-taught artist who wears his heart on his sleeve, Blake merges sharp songwriting with captivating storytelling to craft songs that are both authentic and engaging. His raspy voice and tenderhearted approach allow him to forge meaningful connections with listeners, drawing them into his world. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by country legends like <strong>Luke Combs</strong>, <strong>Zach Bryan</strong>, and <strong>Jason Aldean</strong>, Blake seamlessly navigates genres, blending elements of country-rock, singer-songwriter, and everything in between. In 2023, he debuted with <em><strong>Demos From the 434</strong></em>, a project that ignited his passion for music and set him on a promising path in country music. Blake’s artistry is a unique blend of Zach Bryan’s introspective lyrics and Luke Combs’ soulful style, enriched by his own powerful voice and heartfelt storytelling.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Outside of music, his passions for motorcycle rides, racecars, and life on the open road fuel his adventurous spirit and inspire his creative process. &nbsp;<br id=\"isPasted\">Rooted in the stillness of nature and the beauty of God’s creation, Blake channels these experiences into lyrics that resonate deeply with his audience. With his passion for music and a life lived boldly, Blake Smeltz is poised to take country music to exciting new horizons. &nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6VtPWvA4PQlpSmWA85Ugni?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/blakesmeltz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Listening Links</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/blakesmeltz_music/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@blakesmeltzmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"312550","title":"Read More","date":"2024-11-15","lead":"\"Shapes In The Clouds\" portrays Erin & The Wildfire's unapologetic candor in a Dream-Pop soundscape.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/312550/fd97c2470ea1ba7cd4aa2fdb4427fdf0.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Shapes In The Clouds\" portrays Erin &amp; The Wildfire's unapologetic candor in a Dream-Pop soundscape."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2V33FE1dz0ENzcUksNa2J3?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Richmond, VA (November 15, 2024) - <a href=\"https://www.erinandthewildfire.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Erin &amp; The Wildfire</strong></a>, the dynamic indie-pop sensation from Richmond, Virginia, are back with a new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2V33FE1dz0ENzcUksNa2J3?si=407ca58e3e6b4a4a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Shapes In The Clouds</strong></a><strong>”</strong>, and tackling the nuances of uncomfortable conversations in their signature unapologetic lyrical style."},{"t":"p","html":"Grappling with the emotions that come with family politics and differing opinions in relationships, “Shapes In The Clouds” is about not seeing eye to eye on sensitive issues. <em>“Sometimes your family wants you to live your life in a way that you never pictured for yourself and that can cause some friction,”</em> states lead-vocalist Lunsford, who penned the song.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song came up for me in Spring of 2022 when I was having a tough conversation with a family member. I know I’m not alone in the complex feelings of frustration, love, impatience, patience, anger, and understanding that can all occur in a singular conversation with a family member that you don’t see eye to eye with. Relationships are hard and I wanted to lament about that feeling by turning it into something dance-y, pleading, and light.”","cite":"- Erin Lunsford, Lead Singer of Erin & The Wildfire"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644105/large-eb99fb092f988a41f809040c0bd3dfbe.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Shapes In The Clouds\" by Harry Slater"},{"t":"p","html":"Lacking harmony in our close relationships can leave us feeling misunderstood and distant, which Lunsford explores lyrically in her signature “blunt” writing style. With lyrics like <em>“I guess you’ll always hear what you want to hear”</em> and <em>“you hate me when I voice my doubts”,&nbsp;</em>Lunsford showcases what many experiences as “generational differences” coming to light... something relatable to many of the band's listeners."},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, “Shapes In The Clouds” is a dream-pop masterpiece, drawing comparison to the styles of artists like <strong>Maggie Rogers</strong> and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong> with its upbeat rhythm and bouncy melody. The indie guitar riffs and punchy drums lend to a sparkly soundscape that perfectly juxtaposes the message in the lyrics."},{"t":"p","html":"“Shapes In The Clouds” is the fourth single from Erin &amp; The Wildfire’s upcoming album and follows the tantalizing release of <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/65IqAJNpiJKnn1DGlT3ui1?si=14cb93f02f274c9d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\"Lightning So Blue”</strong></a> about female pleasure. The group has been working with <strong>Producer Rob Dunnenberger</strong>, and recording at <strong>Spacebomb Studio</strong> (Richmond, Virginia) to craft music that is both danceable and thought-provoking. Partnering with <strong>Ellis Tucker</strong> for the mix and master, “Shapes In The Clouds” promises to be a sonic journey unlike any other."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644102/large-b0413135f5a4f9d8aa4b1fa82edc6d52.jpg","alt":"ErinAndTheWildfire-2024Promo-HighRes-23.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644102/preview-d3c5027f0d2e2bb0e4edda0832ba4df4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644103/large-31e42365a10d882b56f6595c70a894e7.jpg","alt":"ErinAndTheWildfire-2024Promo-HighRes-25.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644103/preview-da2c22d818abe7a097c83ca79906865e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644104/large-31472fa032a595b9919617aa366397ef.jpg","alt":"ErinAndTheWildfire-2024Promo-HighRes-28.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644104/preview-6a1aec1c8780b5a5d6c2f21cc8714c94.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Joey Wharton"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Erin &amp; The Wildfire will be celebrating the single release with a show at </strong><a href=\"https://www.erinandthewildfire.com/shows\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Camel</strong></a><strong> on November 16th.</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/693632/large-3c1c5c0b15e72858df404a63fefe9043.jpeg","alt":"Click on the image for your tickets!"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Erin &amp; The Wildfire:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/03NHhY1mdWC3Hf9uJEnomj?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/03NHhY1mdWC3Hf9uJEnomj?si=EbLbl2Z7TOaoEy3QOnezrA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Erin &amp; The Wildfire</strong></a><strong>,</strong> originally formed by college friends in Charlottesville, Virginia, have blossomed into a tight-knit musical unit over the past decade. Now based in Richmond, Virginia, they fuse soul and indie-pop, drawing inspiration from a diverse range of artists like <strong>Emily King</strong> and <strong>D’Angelo</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Led by powerhouse vocalist <strong>Erin Lunsford</strong>, the band infuses their music with pop, funk, and indie vibes, complemented by the talents of <strong>Ryan Lipps</strong>, <strong>Nick Quillen</strong>, and <strong>Matt Wood</strong> - often accompanied by <strong>Stephen Roach</strong>. Lunsford’s lyrics delve into personal struggles, advocating for body acceptance and self-love while addressing broader issues like climate change and gender equality in the music industry."},{"t":"p","html":"Their second album,<em>&nbsp;</em><strong><em>Touchy Feely</em></strong>, released in 2022 and produced by <strong>Matthew E. White</strong>, received acclaim for its meticulous production and compelling songwriting, building on the success of their hit single “<strong>Shape</strong>.” More recently, the band has grown in their notoriety by supporting Sammy Rae &amp; the Friends on a national tour, among being a supporting band for other acts as well."},{"t":"p","html":"Erin &amp; The Wildfire have captivated audiences at sold-out shows and prestigious events like <strong>NPR’s Mountain Stage</strong>. They've supported national tours and shared stages with notable acts such as <strong>Chaka Khan</strong> and<strong>&nbsp;Jill Scott</strong>, leaving lasting impressions at major festivals across the East Coast. In 2019, Erin’s vocals were praised by <strong>Rolling Stone</strong> during her performance at <strong>FloydFest</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"The rising indie-pop band has released two other songs thus far in 2024, “<strong>Love Songs To Georgia</strong>” and “<strong>Lightning So Blue</strong>”, both met with critical acclaim from fans and industry tastemakers alike."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Erin &amp; The Wildfire!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.erinandthewildfire.com/links","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/erinandthewildfire/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@erinandthewildfire","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@erinandthewildfire\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ErinandtheWildfire/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QkCOA-8PfOg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.erinandthewildfire.com/links\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"361500","title":"Leanne Wilkins & the Weathered Drops “Alt-Reality”","date":"2024-11-15","lead":"A call for unity and compassion in a divided America.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/361500/68becf076983e80368a20a8899e740ae.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A call for unity and compassion in a divided America."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6r01e1qPQhaJ0wBDtooo6s?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"SEATTLE (November 15, 2024) – <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lwtheweathered/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Leanne Wilkins &amp; the Weathered</strong></a> unveil their compelling new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6r01e1qPQhaJ0wBDtooo6s?si=114b8a4568ad4b00\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Alt-Reality</strong></a>,” a raw, reflective anthem born from America’s growing ideological divide as the 2024 election looms."},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by experiences of strained relationships amid intense polarization, lead singer Leanne Wilkins wrote “Alt-Reality” as a meditation on compassion, empathy, and the power of choosing unity over division.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://soundcloud.com/leannewilkins/alt-reality/s-I4l48a9T1GM?si=8e9688e67fc042a6808576ffc0ade5f3&amp;amp;utm_source=clipboard&amp;amp;utm_medium=text&amp;amp;utm_campaign=social_sharing","label":"Listen to \"Alt-Reality\"","color":"#4d98ff"},{"t":"button","href":"https://soundcloud.com/leannewilkins/alt-reality-radio-edit/s-QxEjUab3yf9?si=439136d347314386aa6e6ad33bbfe106&amp;amp;utm_source=clipboard&amp;amp;utm_medium=text&amp;amp;utm_campaign=social_sharing","label":"Listen to \"Alt Reality\" Radio Edit","color":"#1052f4"},{"t":"p","html":"Anchored by Leanne’s rich vocals and introspective lyrics, “Alt-Reality” calls on the golden era of 1970s rock, layering soulful Wurlitzer keys and synth arrangements for an upbeat groove."},{"t":"p","html":"In an emotive outro, Leanne repeats the mantra – <em>“All we have is love” </em>– echoed in lush three-part harmonies, supported by guest musician <strong>Charlie Smith</strong>’s dynamic synth lines. The effect is both haunting and hopeful, invoking classic rock’s ability to channel larger societal issues while remaining intensely personal."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I hope this song will serve as a reminder through the upcoming election and going forward that ‘all we have is love.’ We all have the opportunity to choose love over fear.”","cite":"- Leanne Wilkins"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/698268/large-36b67038a0bc84941d4ead44f845849f.jpg","alt":"Album Art by Kate Birch"},{"t":"p","html":"“Alt-Reality” challenges listeners to recognize their shared humanity amid differences, and to strive for understanding over division. Drawing inspiration from her personal journey as a mother, and the nation’s shared struggles, Leanne and The Weathered look to encourage listeners to foster empathy and bridge divides in their own communities."},{"t":"p","html":"The band is excited to share “Alt-Reality” with audiences throughout Seattle and beyond, hoping it serves as a soundtrack to conversations on unity during one of the most polarized periods in recent history. The fourth single from the band’s upcoming album, it follows the summer releases of, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1byRinWPLL3aiVq3X5xmFI?si=481390081be7423d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Light in the Darkness</strong></a>,” “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2zniKfcYBF44o5VySeMmOe?si=597d02e3cb7d46bc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Another Life</strong></a>,” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0Hkxj8CZLxSU86wOtbVUIQ?si=64af01f377e54f16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Free Spirit</strong></a>.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced in Seattle at the legendary <strong>Avast and Nels Motel studios</strong>, “Alt-Reality” was recorded and mixed by <strong>Robb Davidson</strong> and mastered by <strong>Rachel Field</strong> at <strong>Resonant Mastering</strong>. The song is the latest single from Leanne Wilkins &amp; the Weathered’s upcoming 2025 album, <em>The Art of Letting Go</em>, which reflects Leanne’s journey through grief, motherhood, and personal rebirth."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5YaZ0wImCHMU87MefZlaKn?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Leanne Wilkins &amp; the Weathered:"},{"t":"p","html":"Since 1998, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4beFDwHsBf5lUo35DdX5ab?si=D1qoHO2dQa6LGDiE0zn0Uw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Leanne Wilkins</strong></a> has captivated audiences with her haunting melodies and lyrical depth. The Seattle-based artist’s latest project, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5YaZ0wImCHMU87MefZlaKn?si=LNyYZFqFSjq4jQhPhBzuLA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Leanne Wilkins &amp; the Weathered</strong></a>, blends roots rock with blues and soul influences, channeling a style that’s deeply personal and universally resonant. Her lyrics explore relationships, personal growth, and the search for truth, bringing warmth and authenticity to a sound that defies easy classification."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>The Weathered</em> recently completed their full-length album, <em><strong>The Art of Letting Go</strong></em>, a collection of songs exploring themes of death and rebirth, pain and redemption, shadow and light. Written during the pandemic, <em>The Art of Letting Go</em> took Leanne on a journey back to her roots, reconnecting with her love of piano and reflecting on the complexities of becoming a mother amid a time of widespread division."},{"t":"p","html":"Through <em>The Art of Letting Go</em>, Leanne channels her grief over her family of origin, including the death of her younger sister, and the questions she faced as a mother in an uncertain world. This album builds on <strong>The Weathered</strong>’s previous EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5leBsi4D5pL81KMwhzy84w?si=jamv8nyeT0-FuInh8Bc4Xw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Ordinary Grey</strong></em></a>, while delving into more experimental territory, with keys taking center stage alongside contributions from talented local musicians, including <strong>Derek Pulvino</strong> (guitar), <strong>Clint Hoyler</strong> (bass), and <strong>Ben Loshin</strong> (drums/co-producer). The record also features some incredible guest musicians: <strong>Tim Kennedy</strong> (Hammond B3), <strong>Josh Tvrdy</strong> (guitar), <strong>Charlie Smith</strong> (keys), and <strong>Abby Gundersen</strong> (strings)."},{"t":"p","html":"With <em>The Art of Letting Go</em>, Leanne and her band explore the many faces of love and self-acceptance, blending classic rock influences with modern soul for a listening experience that is as emotionally complex as it is musically rich. The album, set for release in 2025, brings a message of healing and hope to the world after a particularly dark time in recent human history, promising to deepen the band’s connection with audiences in Seattle and beyond."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DBsOyLWvD6w/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Leanne Wilkins &amp; the Weathered!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://theweatheredband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lwtheweathered/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/theweatheredband/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-MNuhJRnITz1wRye5E4VKg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5YaZ0wImCHMU87MefZlaKn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/leanne-wilkins-the-weathered/1098272476\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://leannewilkins.bandcamp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Bandcamp</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"362518","title":"Elder Grown Reflects on Life’s Rhythms in Nostalgic New Single, “Red Light”","date":"2024-11-15","lead":"The new single takes listeners on a journey through the universal experience of growing up.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/362518/3a385a2a5410bddd25a27ea9294331fd.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new single takes listeners on a journey through the universal experience of growing up."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7slovIz5NL2bfQShCZOllG?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (November 15, 2024) - Today, Colorado band <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?si=oTBzULe7SuydZlwGFQ-YxA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Elder Grown</strong></a> unveils its newest single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7slovIz5NL2bfQShCZOllG?si=8d947e6ce48442c1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Red Light</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> drawing listeners into a reflective journey through the band’s early days, childhood memories, and the impactful moments that shape who we become."},{"t":"p","html":"“Red Light” started with a keyboard melody by band member <strong>Brandon Clark.&nbsp;</strong>Evoking a powerful sense of nostalgia in fellow band member and lyricist <strong>Paul Hoffman,&nbsp;</strong>the melody<strong>&nbsp;</strong>inspired him to write about the memories that shaped Elder Grown and his early life."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/701202/large-5d78d184e8165fa6c9691bcdf2ce62ab.png","alt":"Cover art for \"Red Light\" by Alexis Malin\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t"},{"t":"p","html":"The song’s first verse explores early relationships, the unforgettable college days spent in party houses, and the band’s foundational years. The chorus serves as a symbolic pause — a “red light” — inviting reflection on life’s path and the value of each step along the way. In the second verse, Hoffman shifts to his childhood experiences, making “Red Light” a journey across different life stages, each one shaping identity and perspective."},{"t":"p","html":"<u><strong>\"Red Light\" Lyrics Snippet</strong></u>"},{"t":"p","html":"Backyard baseball and tracks on repeat"},{"t":"p","html":"Downloading tunes on the family PC"},{"t":"p","html":"Running in my bare feet oh you gotta see me"},{"t":"p","html":"Calling up my brothers like damn you gotta hear me"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The second verse teleports me right back to our backyard baseball field in Pagosa Springs\"","cite":"- Paul Hoffman, Elder Grown"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Jay Greens&nbsp;</strong>and<strong>&nbsp;Sam Kelly</strong>, the single is a showcase of the band’s musical roots and evolution, drawing inspiration from the nostalgic melodies and rhythmic flows of <strong>Mac Miller,</strong> <strong>Anderson .Paak&nbsp;</strong>and<strong>&nbsp;Atmosphere</strong>. With roots in hip-hop, funk, and soul, the band delivers this new release with its signature genre-blending sound that calls back old favorites while remaining strikingly fresh."},{"t":"p","html":"“Red Light” is the second single from Elder Grown’s upcoming album <em>Parachutes</em>, set for release on New Year’s Eve, December 31, 2024."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Elder Grown:"},{"t":"p","html":"Family and community are the roots of <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?si=oTBzULe7SuydZlwGFQ-YxA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Elder Grown</strong></a>, a band of brothers from Durango, Colorado. They consider every audience member to be their 6th collective member, the heartbeat that fuels their music. Elder Grown is a powerful rock band featuring hip-hop forward funk &amp; soul inspired, original songs. Their improvisational jams serve as the foundation for their captivating and genre-bending music. With groovy bass lines, screaming guitar, and bold saxophone, they invite listeners on a rollercoaster ride of musical exploration."},{"t":"p","html":"Switching instruments mid-song, Elder Grown defies conventions and takes you on a journey into the unrecognizably familiar. The band has released three albums and one single so far. Their debut album, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/75sf4VsRBdfvW8EuEBqyv3?si=IHiBlRvrTsuK3_O1n5hvDQ&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=166c25b42e8b4b88\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Fire On The Way</strong></a>”, released in 2011, an EP called “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/22Xy0KU3rMB0FH7mHhxj4c?si=9lJrbkHnQxu173yPTk9Clw&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=6c844eb1dea9480a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Motorhome Mixes</strong></a>”, released in 2014, a self-titled full-length album in 2018, and a new album to be released in the fall of 2024."},{"t":"p","html":"The band’s origin story dates back to the early 90s when the <strong>Hoffman</strong> brothers —&nbsp;<strong>Joshua</strong>, <strong>John</strong>, and <strong>Paul&nbsp;</strong>— grew up in Albuquerque, New Mexico, surrounded by their father's performances as a singer-songwriter. Their passion for music grew, and after moving to Southwest Colorado, they formed Elder Grown, embracing their multifaceted musical talents."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Sam</strong> <strong>Kelly</strong>, (saxophone), joined the band during their time at Fort Lewis College. His love for saxophone and unique sound contributed to Elder Grown's evolution."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Brandon</strong> <strong>Clark</strong>, primarily a guitarist, expanded his skills to bass and keyboards to keep up with the band's instrument swapping. His love for classic rock and soulful tunes adds a creative touch to their sound."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Guillaume</strong> <strong>Metz</strong>, a professional guitarist from Paris, France, joined Elder Grown in 2019. His expertise as a lead guitarist, backup vocalist, and auxiliary bassist brought depth and richness to their performances."},{"t":"p","html":"Together, Elder Grown continues to captivate audiences with their soul-inspired sound and a commitment to pushing musical boundaries. With a new album on the horizon, they look forward to sharing their journey with their extended family of listeners.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Elder Grown!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/DAjIzVDuWIm/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ElderGrown/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"></a>​​​<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/eldergrown?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&amp;igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ElderGrown/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.bandsintown.com/a/1142918?came_from=257\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>bandsintown</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"355366","title":"Old Tom & the Lookouts Drops New Album, 'Northeastern'","date":"2024-11-14","lead":"Boston Indie-Americana band explores mental health and Northeastern culture through gritty soundscapes.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/355366/2ae93f28b18f28deff2d8649849d2c3e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Boston Indie-Americana band explores mental health and Northeastern culture through gritty soundscapes."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5kKy5lT1q1sMISGt72rkIA?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"BOSTON, MA (November 14, 2024) – Today, indie-Americana band <a href=\"https://www.oldtommusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Old Tom &amp; The Lookouts</strong></a> released their new album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5kKy5lT1q1sMISGt72rkIA?si=ubxB0wzmSCGm2VKFPqimeA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Northeastern</strong></em></a>, a poignant and unflinching exploration of life in the Northeast. Addressing themes of mental health, substance abuse, and complicated relationships shaped by the region’s rugged culture, the album blends the heartfelt storytelling of <strong>Zach Bryan</strong> with the raw, melancholic energy of <strong>Counting Crows</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<em><strong>Northeastern</strong></em> offers a stirring reflection on life's challenges in this region. <em>“The Northeast is like playing a video game on hard mode,”</em> frontman <strong>Alex Calabrese</strong> explains. “There’s this culture of struggling silently — people drown their emotions in alcohol or drugs because we’re not talkers. But it’s a cycle that needs to be broken.”"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Northeastern","label":"Listen to 'Northeastern' on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Capturing the essence of the region’s emotional landscape, <em>Northeastern</em> focuses on battles with depression, anxiety, and failed relationships. <em>“It’s a tribute to my partner through our struggles with mental illness and also a begrudging love letter to the Northeast,”</em> says Calabrese. <em>“It’s baffling, and horrifying and awesome all at the same time. It’s just what it is.”</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3DUITrxYkgF5EOiSAwWWy7?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"The lead single, “Your Town,” released on October 18, 2024, and serves as a focal point of the album, encapsulating its themes of emotional survival and resilience in a region known for its toughness."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/690841/large-a062aa8385aa163c7f83fb79973cdb9a.jpg","alt":"DSCF3819.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/690841/preview-d5dddd476e67d78b7eb1f8dae6ac65a0.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/690842/large-b6f5d0fe63a57c4f5bb7e8f215cf5610.jpg","alt":"IMG_8448.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/690842/preview-b680068a2664da342ca078e7bec26170.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/690843/large-4477e809dd7115ebef53405f0104bd92.jpg","alt":"IMG_8456.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/690843/preview-ab4ac3405d7b8ec3593bd8553ebe715d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/690844/large-ba8960c82f16e7955aadb4769d5957a9.png","alt":"OT Logo Thicker Line.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/690844/preview-9997f6fd0b1fc9ab9939def16e9e5e5c.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/690845/large-4873ff930a05019b835d414c6ccf927e.jpg","alt":"DSCF3684-3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/690845/preview-e7a90b3a8727418e17e534a83e5c5609.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Northeastern</em> marks a stylistic evolution for the band, blending emo-country’s evocative storytelling with Americana’s grounded roots. The group builds on its folk foundations and ability to weave raw emotion into its music to introduce a more rock-oriented, cathartic energy, offering listeners a deeply emotional and authentic experience. <em>Northeastern</em> was recorded with and produced by <strong>Joe Dunn</strong>, whose work adds to the album’s gritty, Americana-infused sound."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4eVxPcjBhNSezlZi06MAhm?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Old Tom &amp; The Lookouts:"},{"t":"p","html":"Led by <strong>Alex Calabrese</strong>, Boston-based indie-folk band <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4eVxPcjBhNSezlZi06MAhm?si=mnTehYKsS9iQrxCCu_Lyyw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Old Tom &amp; The Lookouts</strong></a> blend the introspective grit of Americana with the emotional rawness of indie rock. Known for their brooding lyrics and powerful storytelling, the band explores themes of mental health, love, and resilience. Drawing influences from artists like <strong>Tom Waits</strong>, <strong>Frightened Rabbit</strong>, and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, Calabrese’s evocative vocals and poignant songwriting strike a chord with listeners searching for authenticity and emotional depth."},{"t":"p","html":"Old Tom &amp; The Lookouts have performed at notable venues such as Club Passim (Cambridge, MA), City Winery (Boston, MA), and Skylark Lounge (Denver, CO). Their previous release, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4cTDNN6zTrougPUDlvK0bh?si=bafqhzOpQmWpIC1R0QzAwA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Just For Beasts</em></a>&nbsp;(2021), co-created with violinist and vocalist <strong>Cecilia Vacanti</strong>, was praised by critics as “hauntingly beautiful” by&nbsp;<strong>Lunar Sonar</strong> and “essential listening” by&nbsp;<strong>Music Mecca</strong>. With <em>Northeastern </em>(2024), the band takes a bold step forward, embracing a more rock-driven sound while staying true to their emotionally charged roots."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Old Tom &amp; The Lookouts"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DCUgz5VOD46/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/VbnC98pq5XU?si=wYMTXWMt6vvDo7Kl","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.oldtommusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/oldtommusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/oldtommusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC19lK7-dYVIZQafikC3NAzQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://x.com/_oldtom_\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>X</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"363100","title":"Pablo Starr Releases New Single, \"Story of Life (Sorrow of Love, Joy of Music)\"","date":"2024-11-06","lead":"Exploring the bittersweet intersections of love, loss, and the timeless joy found in memory.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/363100/a4a53f8ae0edc7430beb3eaaa37d4b9b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Exploring the bittersweet intersections of love, loss, and the timeless joy found in memory."},{"t":"p","html":"PARIS (October 28, 2024) – Electronic music producer and indie artist <strong>Pablo Starr</strong> invites listeners into a vibrant, emotive journey with <strong>“Story of Life (Sorrow of Love, Joy of Music),”</strong> a heartfelt single that marks the beginning of a new chapter in Starr’s multi-dimensional career.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2iEZUfYrj5Nzp0So5O5vh5?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Known as the creator of <a href=\"https://fashionweekonline.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fashion Week Online®</a> and a former indie scene regular from Silver Lake to New York City, Starr’s latest work marries the contemplative essence of bossa nova and jazz standards with a modern, electronic twist. Rooted in love's delicate duality of joy and sorrow, “Story of Life” vividly portrays memories and how they come to life in the present moment."},{"t":"p","html":"Starr’s intricate lyrics dive into the aftermath of a breakup, capturing the nostalgic sweetness of love remembered and the peace music can bring even amid sadness. Inspired by electronic artists like Daft Punk, as well as bossa nova songwriters like Jobim, the track highlights Starr’s versatility as a musician and storyteller."},{"t":"p","html":"“In many ways, this song is a meditation on how memories of love stay with us, like flickers of light we can revisit anytime,” says Starr. “I wanted ‘Story of Life’ to encapsulate that duality of warmth and ache—which are such natural parts of life. It's a celebration of the imagination, and I hope this track resonates with people who have their own stories of love and loss.”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/700875/large-a9ff18dd754e230aed50aba19d6d7c28.png","alt":"Cover Art by Pablo Starr"},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded in his Paris studio and completely self-produced, “Story of Life” stands out for its textural depth and careful production, following the release of \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6BpdXGEPAm9VkoJ3grde09?si=AUmtj-wkTi-FdQdXyqM_Tg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Regular Losers</a>,\" \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3YNAzOsKsyxuHwRk2VUXrj?si=z2-7GwOaS_eYoS2Pac_6Gw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Glitching on My Coffee Break</a>,\" and \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0HGKUnaMsO3DhJB9Q0u6PR?si=Hr1KzznxTuq-xU3TIftICw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Heart Under Glass</a>\" from his upcoming self-titled project, <em>Pablo Starr</em><strong>.</strong>​"},{"t":"p","html":"\"I did the mixing, mastering, production, vocals, performances ....everything on my laptop. But I’m looking to expand my skills as a producer, and I have a masterclass coming up with the legendary <strong>Chris Gehringer</strong> (Drake, Dua Lipa, etc.) with <a href=\"https://mixwiththemasters.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Mix With the Masters</em></a>. I’m also a big fan of producers <strong>Ian Kirkpatrick</strong> and <strong>Finneas</strong>.\" - Pablo Starr"},{"t":"p","html":"As a celebrated editor in international fashion, Starr’s move to Paris marked a natural evolution for his creative pursuits. This latest track ties into a broader journey: Story of Life is part of an ongoing exploration in Starr’s music that complements his literary ventures, including the upcoming graphic novel <a href=\"https://cyberpink.co/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cyberpink®</a>. Each project reflects Starr’s unique perspective on fashion, music, and storytelling."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702248/large-a3ad6812e9600dc82ad839f82697afbd.jpg","alt":"Cyberpink®-Project-image.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702248/preview-ac9bb41a3bfc8f5cf212db0155558639.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702249/-c3a9c21f234e22277439c9c6dd6cc759.jpg","alt":"Cyberpink-excerpt-P30A.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702249/-c3a9c21f234e22277439c9c6dd6cc759.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702250/-92f6dbb43270b6c3a948d1ce962c6ffe.jpg","alt":"Cyberpink-excerpt-P40.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702250/-92f6dbb43270b6c3a948d1ce962c6ffe.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702251/large-1495172b00422fb4f0778c8d39f6da69.jpg","alt":"Cyberpink-excerpt-10.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702251/preview-fa9bacfc3f7a53eac57053875b12d820.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702254/large-e3f3e715307f42eb8d3a722baa7c54df.jpg","alt":"Cyberpink-excerpt-P21.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702254/preview-fab87c1011d861e4893e3dcb4cb7ae20.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702252/large-5516d7003ecd03745fba08e4ee30ea79.jpg","alt":"Cyberpink-excerpt-P19.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702252/preview-fd4ef8e96c37e5944d74ea54f24d2e09.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702253/large-a01ae7903904e49ed9a1c7c08fac7974.jpg","alt":"Cyberpink-excerpt-P30B.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702253/preview-5ef738960afcaa073b90507cbb75552a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702255/large-eba7b3aef056b45b8f1817763ae73be4.jpg","alt":"Cyberpink-excerpt-P3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702255/preview-480e8023d17c23ca937926a484f244c6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702256/large-9037643862269b24be3531d50b9920e8.jpg","alt":"Cyberpink-excerpt-P16.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/702256/preview-20000b3606f1312dee605f3a919348e0.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"The Cyberpink graphic novel / musical project, currently building a community for a <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/cyberpink/cyberpink-graphic-novel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kickstarter Pre-Launch</a>, is a futuristic, all-girl band tale of resilience and identity (listen to Cyberpink the band on streaming <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/09TQEaOaR0xhBzqgq4cnIm?si=Z2-Lw2EBQNqVrPnlMQDHkA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>).&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"People interested in supporting the Cyberpink graphic novel or finding out about the project can join the newly launched <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/cyberpinkmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cyberpink® Facebook group</a>, sign up to the <a href=\"https://cyberpink1.substack.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cyberpink® Substack</a>, or follow the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/cyberpink/cyberpink-graphic-novel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kickstarter Pre-Launch</a>! Early birds can save 50% off the Cyberpink® graphic novel bundle <a href=\"https://cyberpink.co/kickstarter\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/78j4zggFppLiXcjljgsEpo?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Pablo Starr:"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from New Orleans and having cut his teeth in the much-vaunted Silver Lake, LA music scene, Pablo Starr has had write-ups in SPIN and brushed shoulders with some of LA’s most successful acts."},{"t":"p","html":"Now based in Paris as the owner and founder of <a href=\"https://fashionweekonline.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fashion Week Online</a>, he's returning to his musical roots with a new project in development, slated for full release in 2025. The first tracks channel influences as diverse as <strong>Elvis Costello, Antonio Carlos Jobim, The Beatles</strong>, and <strong>‘80s music</strong> to create something honest, funny, and musically adventurous."},{"t":"p","html":"When not recording and playing music, Pablo can be seen hanging out with his 5lb dog Ava, going to fashion shows, or working on his forthcoming graphic novel <a href=\"https://cyberpink.co/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cyberpink</a>. You can follow him on IG <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/pablo.starr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">@pablo.starr</a>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/CpYAKo-Ns24/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Pablo Starr</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/pablo.starr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/78j4zggFppLiXcjljgsEpo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://api.ffm.to/bl/e/c/pablostarr?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://api.ffm.to/bl/e/c/pablostarr?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://cyberpink.co/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cyberpink</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"352174","title":"Adventure Lost – Get Lost","date":"2024-10-25","lead":"The 12-track LP displays the band's authentic creative talent, weaving the central theme into an immersive musical experience.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/352174/26a7ff8517ffb853b830cc0f60992d1f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The 12-track LP displays the band's authentic creative talent, weaving the central theme into an immersive musical experience."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3nvgkwUKxZIkca8lvrZsgi?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Philadelphia, PA (October 25, 2024) - Hailing from Philadelphia, the dynamic music group <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4TW6WmmJpnHsM2kk0r2HQR?si=ISs5hYrWS5acrqgMbKyM7A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Adventure Lost</strong></a> unveils their much-anticipated second album, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3nvgkwUKxZIkca8lvrZsgi?si=keh-To2lTZeosrv69z_eEA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Before the Memory Fades</strong></a>’, on October 25, 2024. This release promises to take listeners on a journey, featuring rich narratives and evocative soundscapes that showcase the band’s signature style. With melodies that easily resonate with fans of iconic groups like <strong>The</strong> <strong>Beatles</strong>, <strong>Coldplay</strong>, and <strong>Queen</strong>, the album’s innovative flavor draws audiences from all generations."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687555/large-37fc5824c972e64060ce69ece9b385ad.png","alt":"Cover Art for \"Before the Memory Fades\" by Swartz Brothers Arts"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Jack</strong> <strong>Faracchio</strong>, the band’s lead vocalist, began working on the second album ‘Before the Memory Fades’ in March 2023, following a transformative five-month solo backpacking trip across Europe, the Middle East, North Africa, and the USA. This concept album weaves together songs written over seven years into a dramatic narrative about pursuing one's heart despite risks, structured around three phases:"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687914/large-7f0bd5a91493ef438c31d50320595e7e.jpg","alt":"AdventureLost - PressPhoto - Band1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687914/preview-f9ce78625cce69a1118ed18976daf798.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687915/large-bef73ea2216cac8555c9b662a9d38662.png","alt":"Single Art - Lucy&#39;s Shoes.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687915/preview-f446c82d8d1b4f9f1171ebd73b692700.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687916/large-ccb23c99dd4deb46233dd99b112e1e27.png","alt":"Single Art - The End of Forever.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687916/preview-b2625696400b0366fc28aef3abd2615e.png"}]},{"t":"p","html":"• Pre-Journey (Yearning): Songs that evoke anticipation and longing.<br id=\"isPasted\">• During-Journey (Action &amp; Experience): Tracks that immerse listeners in the adventure itself.<br>• Post-Journey (Acceptance, Memory &amp; Reflection): Music that reflects on the aftermath and lessons learned."},{"t":"p","html":"This collection explores themes of existentialism and the quest for meaning, purpose, and belonging. Tracks “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1WZ20Xr3jORKyjYJuCXMA3?si=624f0579b8fc4a87\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ships</strong><strong>!</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/08oQk8rGKxLlLNJ9h4tlTY?si=2f6119da5a3f4a06\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>It’ll All Be Over Soon</strong></a>” focus on psychedelic exploration, while the narrative confronts fears like failure, aging, and risk. It addresses moving on from lost romance and overcoming heartbreak in tracks such as “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1PRzhY79xVD66d6NLtG8u5?si=0fd53149015d4899\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>What Might Be</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7neAg969AkDnfJmTwjTISk?si=3fe09d17f1d64ccc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Love and Violence</strong></a>”, alongside issues of poverty highlighted in “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5eJW5XQPzuzLLNjimx9nzl?si=b77b5c621ff449e4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lucy’s&nbsp;</strong><strong>Shoes</strong></a>.” Loneliness, depression, and insomnia are present, yet there’s a message of triumph through persistence in track, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7j2bss8K3CfvycI6lSt4m9?si=21a50583c02049ed\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>On</strong> <strong>T</strong><strong>he</strong> <strong>Edge</strong></a>.” The tension between staying and leaving appears throughout, culminating in the titular track, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/12qLS5wbNNPlRm08aaYOqQ?si=98e1896e1f304f89\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Before</strong> <strong>The&nbsp;</strong><strong>Memory</strong> <strong>Fades</strong></a>”, ultimately reflecting on the relentless passage of time and finding eternity in the present."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/12qLS5wbNNPlRm08aaYOqQ?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"quote","html":"“What really excites me is how each listener has their own interpretation of the story. I love that.”","cite":"- Jack Faracchio, Lead of Adventure Lost"},{"t":"p","html":"While much of the album features precise orchestration and professional recording, several tracks serve as an “audio journal”, giving off its own vibe of authenticity. These include iPhone voice memos that Jack has collected during the journey. Some examples like “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1me0jxz3tiHXJrBgGEs7PD?si=98c55eea18d548e1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mezzogiorno</strong></a>”, is an improvised phone recording from a lazy afternoon in Southern Italy. “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6Pvj9bMuxocoqmMA1DPW2y?si=dfcd11fdef5449be\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The End of Forever</strong></a>” includes an iPhone clip of a very enthusiastic announcer bending the band’s name at a show. “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7Gg9Z4paB4yLFlca23oOJs?si=f3b3e1b455474fd1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Another Day in Bed</strong></a>” concludes with a verse from the original voice memo demo, creatively bridging the first and final recordings in full circle."},{"t":"p","html":"The album’s mix of hi-fi production and lo-fi source materials mirrors the balance of rough and polished moments in real life. Striving for equilibrium, rather than abstract perfection, becomes the overarching theme of the LP."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>The album release show will take place on Saturday, November 2, 2024, at 118 North in Wayne, PA, with support from Chirp (MI). </strong>This will be the debut performance of the revamped five-piece live band, showcasing the entire LP from beginning to end."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Adventure Lost:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4TW6WmmJpnHsM2kk0r2HQR?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4TW6WmmJpnHsM2kk0r2HQR?si=LkVy5BdoQxqpekJ8-o0H_A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Adventure&nbsp;</strong><strong>Lost</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>is a musical project conceived in 2016 by <strong>Jack Faracchio</strong> and <strong>Larry I</strong><strong>accio</strong> in Philadelphia, focused on transforming dreams into music. Known for their dramatic, passionate, inspiring, and occasionally whimsical style, they released their debut concept album “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/235a2sKEIoXR9F8b4a9HvQ?si=XXpJeoVRQCGClNzEYQJEpw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Going Back to Sleep</strong></a>” in 2017 and performed hundreds of energetic shows as a trio until the pandemic prompted a return to their roots."},{"t":"p","html":"After years of travel and songwriting while living the stories that would culminate into a new era of music, Adventure Lost was reborn in 2024 as a five-piece band with their second album, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3nvgkwUKxZIkca8lvrZsgi?si=WVAsB4NJRG-UurVEs7oT9g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Before&nbsp;</strong><strong>The&nbsp;</strong><strong>Memory&nbsp;</strong><strong>Fades</strong></a>.” This 12-track concept album takes listeners on an emotional journey, blending genres to create a dynamic and uplifting experience. Each song contributes to a larger narrative about pursuing dreams and confronting fate."},{"t":"p","html":"Adventure Lost exists to transport the listener into their own musical universe - to immerse them in the stories, emotions, &amp; lore of the characters living within their songs. With influences ranging from <strong>The Beatles</strong> and <strong>Queen&nbsp;</strong>to <strong>Motown&nbsp;</strong>and jazz, Adventure Lost is often categorized as Progressive-Pop, Alt-Rock, or Art Pop/Rock, showcasing their diverse musical complexity and storytelling prowess."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Adventure Lost!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/EI3gEn-Nv0U","height":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://adventurelostmusic.com/","img":"https://adventurelostmusic.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/cropped-gbts-cutout-2.png?w=200","title":"Adventure Lost – Get Lost","desc":"Get Lost"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/adventure.lost/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/theadventurelost/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook&nbsp;</a>| <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4TW6WmmJpnHsM2kk0r2HQR?si=KNeA9XEERr-cqEXWg8zq1Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify&nbsp;</a>| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@adventurelost2772\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube&nbsp;</a>| </strong><a href=\"https://adventurelost.bandcamp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Bandcamp</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"348610","title":"FELL by Dave Tamkin with Brad Huffman and Chadzilla at Roots Music Project in Boulder, CO. Filmed by @pinksofahour July 2023#chadzilla #denver #boulder #boul...","date":"2024-10-11","lead":"A prodigious evening brings forth an enthralling blend of acoustics at Hey Nonny and Harmony Bar & Grill.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/348610/f390d5875f8dc2068470717e759780b9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A prodigious evening brings forth an enthralling blend of acoustics at Hey Nonny and Harmony Bar &amp; Grill."},{"t":"p","html":"<sup>​</sup><strong>Arlington Heights, IL</strong><strong>&nbsp;(October 11, 2024)</strong> – Get ready for an extraordinary evening as <a href=\"https://www.davetamkin.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dave Tamkin &amp; Co.</strong></a> brings their captivating blend of rhythmic acoustic sounds to <a href=\"https://www.heynonny.com/shows/dave-tamkin-co-2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hey Nonny</strong></a> on Friday, October 11, 2024, and another at <a href=\"https://products.spothopperapp.com/checkout?spotId=90945&amp;externalProductId=1066882&amp;_gl=1*1hw89q2*_ga*MTU0ODM2NDcyMi4xNzI1NDc5ODUz*_ga_VG24VK2VKT*MTcyNTY0MzE4NS4yLjEuMTcyNTY0MzMxMy4wLjAuMA..*_ga_PRY5LQJZBL*MTcyNTY0MzE4Ni4yLjEuMTcyNTY0MzMxMy4wLjAuMA..&amp;_ga=2.42293665.581464216.1725643186-1548364722.1725479853&amp;fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAAR0HsQa71qLKn69txouWRIunbmKzfcpJKGgKLMAEeG0_Iez14hIvcRuCtUY_aem_rwzCzBo-osTi1KBW0Ti1Jw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Harmony Bar &amp; Grill</strong></a> on Saturday, October 12, 2024. With unique performances scheduled at 7:00 PM and 9:00 PM, this is a night that fans of heartfelt, engaging music won’t want to miss."},{"t":"p","html":"Featuring the talents of <strong>Dave Tamkin</strong> (guitar/vocals), <strong>Brad Huffman</strong>, and <strong>Bryan Sansom</strong> (drums) — Dave Tamkin &amp; Co. is renowned for their dynamic live shows that seamlessly weave together elements of Americana, jazz, and indie rock. Their performances are not just concerts — they’re a journey through personal lyrics, skilled songwriting, and high-energy percussion, all delivered with an emotional punch that leaves audiences mesmerized."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/74uVL3i4i8ZKp5vYlEWmtI?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Tamkin, who has toured extensively across the United States and internationally, has shared the stage with artists like <strong>Will Hoge</strong>, <strong>Guster</strong>, and <strong>Donavon Frankenreiter</strong>. His commitment to connecting with fans through both intimate solo performances and full-band experiences continues with this special event at Hey Nonny."},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to his musical endeavors, Dave is also the co-host of the popular podcast “<a href=\"https://www.musicianstipjar.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Musicians Tip Jar</strong></a>,” where he and <strong>Chris Webb</strong> discuss the financial aspects of the music industry — a crucial resource for musicians worldwide. With over 100 episodes, the podcast has become a must-listen for those looking to navigate the business side of music."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683139/large-93863967986b560bdb005b06e36c618b.png","alt":"Click the image to get your tickets!"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>EVENT DETAILS:<br></strong>Date: <strong>Friday, October 11, 2024</strong><br>Location: <a href=\"https://www.heynonny.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hey Nonny, 10 S. Vail Ave, Arlington Heights, IL</a><br>Showtimes: <a href=\"https://www.heynonny.com/shows/dave-tamkin-co-2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">7:00 PM &amp; 9:00 PM</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><sup>Dave Tamkin &amp; CO. will donate a percentage of their merch sales to <a href=\"https://www.thebuddyfoundation.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Buddy Foundation</strong></a> of Arlington Heights to help support a <em>non-kill animal shelter</em>.</sup></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>EVENT DETAILS:</strong><br id=\"isPasted\">Date: <strong>Saturday, October 12, 2024</strong><br>Location:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://harmonybarandgrill.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Harmony Bar &amp; Grill, 2201 Atwood Avenue, Madison, WI 53704</a><br>Showtime: 09:00 PM ‐ 12:00 AM"},{"t":"p","html":"<sup><strong>Dave Tamkin &amp; CO. will donate a percentage of their merch sales to&nbsp;</strong></sup><a href=\"https://www.czarspromise.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><sup><strong>Czar’s Promise</strong></sup></a><sup><strong>&nbsp;to help animals dealing with cancer through hope, support, and funding for both the animal and their owners.&nbsp;</strong></sup>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Band Members:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Drums: <strong>Bryan Sansom</strong>, a local favorite from Arlington Heights, who frequently performs around the Chicagoland area with <strong>Gina Gonzalez</strong> and <strong>Kevin Mileski</strong>.<strong><br></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Guitar/Vocals: <strong>Brad Huffman</strong>, originally from Cleveland, OH, now based in Denver, CO."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683149/large-a6c4d7720300b58edef6021785601753.jpg","alt":"Dave_Tamkin_SPACE_WEB-56.jpg"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Dave Tamkin &amp; Successes:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.davetamkin.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dave Tamkin</strong></a> is a Singer/Songwriter who currently resides in Madison, CO via Boulder, CO and Chicago, IL. He has created his own unique style of rhythmic acoustic sounds that are based on a fresh musical vision. His shows vary from intimate solo acoustic performances to a full band experience (<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0b9qqzUoIIiRpArTWyG4KC?si=uKJvNtqZQauxxXX6UzwiPg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>DT&amp;CO.</strong></a>), encapsulating a mixture of personal lyrics and skilled songwriting set against a high-energy percussive backbone."},{"t":"p","html":"Dave has shared the stage with <strong>Guster</strong>, <strong>Will Hoge</strong>, <strong>The Samples</strong>, <strong>Brendan James</strong>, <strong>Rusted Root</strong>, <strong>Donavon Frankenreiter</strong>, <strong>Butch Walker</strong>, <strong>Freddy Jones Band</strong>, <strong>Eric Hutchinson</strong>, <strong>Willy Porter</strong>, <strong>The Violent Femmes</strong>, and <strong>Peter Mulvey</strong> to name a few. Tamkin has a style that’s hard to resist. His lyrics are unabashedly honest, and his passion for playing is undying."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Touring: </strong>Dave Tamkin has extensively toured across the United States and internationally, sharing his dynamic performances with audiences around the globe. His live shows, known for their blend of rhythmic acoustic sounds and high-energy percussion, have consistently captivated fans."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Podcast Host:&nbsp;</strong>Tamkin co-hosts the “Musicians Tip Jar” podcast with Chris Webb. The podcast has gained significant traction with over 100 episodes, focusing on the financial aspects of the music industry, making it a valuable resource for musicians looking to navigate the business side of their careers."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Educational Contributions:&nbsp;</strong>He co-wrote a course titled “<strong>The Financial Scale</strong>,” which is currently being taught at the University of Colorado Denver. This course highlights his dedication to educating upcoming musicians on the importance of financial literacy within the industry."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Collaborations and Shared Stages: </strong>Throughout his career, Tamkin has shared the stage with well-known artists such as Will Hoge, Guster, and Donavon Frankenreiter, further cementing his reputation in the music community."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Release of Live at eTown EP:&nbsp;</strong>Captured during a live performance at Boulder’s historic eTown, showcasing his growth and connection with audiences. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Tickets:</strong> Don’t miss out! Tickets are available now&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.davetamkin.com/tour\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HERE</a>.<br><strong>Social Media:&nbsp;</strong>Stay updated by following Dave Tamkin on Instagram&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/davetamkin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">@davetamkin</a>!<br><strong>Website:&nbsp;</strong>For more information, visit <a href=\"https://www.davetamkin.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.davetamkin.com</a>."},{"t":"p","html":"Stay tuned for what’s up and coming for Dave!"},{"t":"p","html":"<sub><strong>For press inquiries, please contact:<br></strong>Dawn Jones<br>Pressed Fresh PR<br>dawn@pressedfreshpr.com</sub>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Dave!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.davetamkin.com/","img":"","title":"Singer Songwriter, Dave Tamkin has created his own unique style of rhythmic - acoustic sounds based around a fresh musical vision","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ueOcp_kDzuI","img":"","title":"FELL by Dave Tamkin with Brad Huffman and Chadzilla at Roots Music Project in Boulder, CO. Filmed by @pinksofahour July 2023#chadzilla #denver #boulder #boul...","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/DaveTamkinMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/davetamkin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/davetamkin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/davetamkin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.bandsintown.com/a/11797\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">bandsintown</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://music.apple.com/ph/artist/dave-tamkin/200287485\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Apple Music</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"349995","title":"Read More","date":"2024-10-11","lead":"Inspired by childhood favorites, Houston alt-pop artist digs deeper into his sound with the stripped version of Feel.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/349995/d6d3ff2b804b41c40db2eba18c65e1fc.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Inspired by childhood favorites, Houston alt-pop artist digs deeper into his sound with the stripped version of <em>Feel</em>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1nurfy9bQX0AVLbEcz1Ym4?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Houston, TX (October 11, 2024)</strong> - A year after Houston-based alt-pop artist <a href=\"https://www.timqualls.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tim Qualls</strong></a> made waves with the release of his album <strong><em>‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3bQSWj2L69FZmAGzZIHmHg?si=zeJHkQUZSL2Hd4-EW-qkng\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Feel</strong></a>,’&nbsp;</em></strong>named the <a href=\"https://www.houstonchronicle.com/entertainment/music/article/houston-music-2023-best-albums-concerts-18590316.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">best album of 2023</a> by the <strong>Houston Chronicle</strong>,<strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong>Qualls is back with the reimagined,<em>&nbsp;‘</em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1nurfy9bQX0AVLbEcz1Ym4?si=sJwK3xBIQyyu6oikJmk3WQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Feel - Stripped</strong></em></a><em>,’&nbsp;</em>and accompanying single, <em>“</em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2L96RN7oMEF09ihHRrhgYW?si=8dbb88f5c7b64d40\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Mine - Stripped</strong></em></a><em>.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Drawing inspiration from his childhood favorite, <strong>Gavin DeGraw’s</strong> <em>‘Chariot - Stripped,’ </em>Qualls digs deeper into these ten songs, offering fans a more intimate, raw version of the record to showcase his artistry in a new light."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2L96RN7oMEF09ihHRrhgYW?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wanted to pause for a moment, revisit the music, and find more meaning between the lyrics, the melodies, and the rhythm. It was about trying to find the notes in between the piano keys, those that are often overlooked. One part stripped, one part LIVE, one part reimagined.”","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Tim Qualls"},{"t":"p","html":"<em><strong>Feel - Stripped</strong>&nbsp;</em>features live instrumentation, including contributions from long-time collaborator <strong>Ben Rothberg</strong>, and reimagined versions of tracks like “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7JlwPF8STz9vtpMpfCKFX3?si=e3429f8d7fed45e7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mine</strong></a>”, which was never released as a single on the original album, but shines in a new way on <strong><em>Stripped</em></strong>. Recorded through spontaneous late-night sessions with a group of musicians who previously worked on the album and had played it live together, the new version embodies a creative spirit emphasizing raw, live energy."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0yCalDjdZNVjsKSdIxK0HU?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“It was fun not to overthink anything happening and just create,”</em> Tim continued, <em>“Letting the music take us, wherever it wanted to take us. That was our motto, let’s not overthink anything going on.”</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/685169/large-eaca850725852221fbee2b3e1fad9db6.jpg","alt":"Cover Art for album single, 'Mine - Stripped'"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Ty, myself, Ben, and Colby, would show up late at night to record, with no preconceived ideas of how the tracks would go. We would talk for a bit, then eventually find our way over to an instrument or two and start to noodle around until we found a sound, tone, or vibe. From there, for all 10 songs, we would follow that random night's inspiration, letting the music guide us to where it wanted to go,”</em> Tim concluded."},{"t":"p","html":"Qualls is renowned for his rootsy, soulful, and ornate music style, characterized by its emotional and embellished elements. ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3bQSWj2L69FZmAGzZIHmHg?si=zFz1BmvmQce355Dmk1QHlg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Feel</strong></a>’ signified the culmination of a 15-year journey, with the songs eloquently recounting Tim's life experiences and emotions.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3bQSWj2L69FZmAGzZIHmHg?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"His ability to rework his material with such attention to detail is a testament to his dedication as an artist. <strong><em>Feel - Stripped</em></strong> offers a deeper emotional exploration while maintaining the soulfulness and vulnerability that made Feel originally resonate with listeners."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/685171/large-caddc8404dcc274b51c422a4caaa52be.jpg","alt":"QuallsAlbumArt_16_strippednew.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/685171/preview-a159ad123b4fa499dc76a878976116c1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584199/large-c8d2759e6e754385b924249350dbf53a.jpg","alt":"IMG_8117.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584199/preview-7abe55022dfe2bff893f5ef871a00b1e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584200/large-4e313ef0412a6bfa8b07e91e0efb47c0.jpg","alt":"IMG_8113.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584200/preview-5ef1f688ed5aae107033aa8d4831cb66.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590085/-aa85318b4efe2f99d31493cb488c0143.jpg","alt":"TIM2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590085/preview-0c5561a0d7bde7f458d1460acdef7be9.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590086/-2dbdff536fea382a6dffef4250c89c6e.jpg","alt":"TIM3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590086/preview-3726786253152efe265eaebd95e898e7.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/685169/large-eaca850725852221fbee2b3e1fad9db6.jpg","alt":"minestripped-web.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/685169/preview-c50095aae220132b5f9c8ab7115b6e09.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos and Artwork by Kirby Betancourt"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Tim Qualls:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/L6RnU-xJxz8","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Houston-based songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/12J7rAVoeFIUNkRelq5zw8?si=mYEMSXUbTVaATAl-tQ1ZYw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tim Qualls</strong></a> delivers rootsy soul music that is grounded in family, heartache, and a positive outlook on life very few write about. Influenced by legends like <strong>Ray Charles</strong>, <strong>Jamie Cullum</strong>, and <strong>John Mayer</strong>, musicians compare him to a <em>“soul artist that croons on the piano.”</em> His productions have been compared to <strong>Adele</strong>, <strong>Sam Smith</strong>, and <strong>Ryan Tedder</strong>. Once awarded <strong>Houston Press</strong>’ “Best New Act” award, Qualls continues to deliver new music every year. Tim has been featured on Spotify playlists such as <strong>LIFE SUCKS</strong>, <strong>DINNER MUSIC</strong>, <strong>SOULFUL BLEND</strong>, and <strong>COZY BLEND</strong>. Qualls’ recently-released singles <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2oheHd1XwCuN3cFzZV7Tid?si=4da46a8a26214bd1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Forever</strong></a><strong>,”&nbsp;</strong><strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0MA3vYM4gsD64hQXDZWUD8?si=5cebb944d65d42e3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Grave</strong></a>,<strong>”</strong> and “<strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/29f4uKrB8LFCT29EvNcidJ?si=aa25a248837e4969\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>History</strong></a>”</strong> are featured on his new album ‘Feel’<strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong>- now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Tim!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/timquallsmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@timquallsmusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.timqualls.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/timquallsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><strong><a href=\"https://www.twitter.com/timothyqualls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/timquallsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"351602","title":"Steve Dennis | Singer-Songwriter | Boston, MA - Lighthouse Inn Out July 9!","date":"2024-10-11","lead":"Inviting listeners into an intimate narrative of love, missed connections, and second chances.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/351602/eac7249824b7d21f7c5724e4784f960b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Inviting listeners into an intimate narrative of love, missed connections, and second chances."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0QDKFhBaGpMSOrn6vZfQFU?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ESSEX, MA (October 11, 2024)</strong> — Today, Indie-folk singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stevedennismusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Steve Dennis</strong></a> returns with his latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0QDKFhBaGpMSOrn6vZfQFU?si=768fd890127c4eb1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Annie</strong></a>,” inviting listeners into an intimate narrative of love, missed connections, and second chances. Produced by the acclaimed <strong>Jamie Mefford</strong>, the track blends Steve’s signature folk sound with the warmth of <strong>Gregory Alan Isakov</strong> and the laid-back charm of <strong>Jack Johnson</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by a real-life encounter, “Annie” is a deeply personal song that was almost left on the cutting room floor. As Steve recalls, <em>“I almost threw this song out, but after playing it out a couple of times, it shortly became my most requested song. Happy, I stuck with it.”</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687095/large-584a6a2dae272b9a7c3cabfcf6943b88.png","alt":"Cover Art for \"Annie,\" photo by Dani Odonnell"},{"t":"p","html":"The story behind “Annie” began when Steve found himself captivated by a checkout girl during a routine stop at a market. Though initially too nervous to act, he turned his car around after leaving and decided to take a chance. The song captures the vulnerability of love at first sight, the fear of rejection, and the courage to seize the moment."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Annie is for those people who are afraid of rejection. Just give it a shot.”","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Steve Dennis"},{"t":"p","html":"With evocative lyrics and a heartfelt melody, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0QDKFhBaGpMSOrn6vZfQFU?si=5f29ec3e65ab4705\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Annie</strong></a>” will resonate with anyone who's ever taken a risk in the name of love. Fans of artists like <strong>John Mayer</strong> will feel right at home in the blend of acoustic warmth and storytelling charm that Steve brings to the song."},{"t":"p","html":"“<u>Annie”</u><u>&nbsp;Lyrics Snippet</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"Annie B. I’m on my way down 95"},{"t":"p","html":"Repeating just what I want to say"},{"t":"p","html":"Don’t do this much, but I might as well take a try"},{"t":"p","html":"I can’t risk letting you get away"},{"t":"p","html":"As Steve jokes, <em>“You might cry. Sorry.”</em>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687096/large-e09d9859d5a80bde95a7329a60f8aa71.jpg","alt":"IMG_1662.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687096/preview-a3459f4f24d7d362aca6dad47b222fae.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687098/large-6a43a3734151d7dbd9524f0f5781bc5f.jpg","alt":"IMG_2590.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687098/preview-3ff986d189d54088711bf3d46ba3b3d5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687097/large-a98205f094219958c1def9bc5b84c942.png","alt":"Annie Cover Art.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687097/preview-155868997b6eedfba3726699cda8c6f2.png"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by Dani Odonnell"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Steve Dennis:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5Q7D3eliTavuZuXMrKHPrw?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from Cape Ann, Massachusetts, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5Q7D3eliTavuZuXMrKHPrw?si=ui1QK8mYRjGS8PSny1ooRw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Steve Dennis</strong></a> has spent the past decade performing at hundreds of venues across Massachusetts, Rhode Island, Maine, and New Hampshire, solidifying his place as a veteran of the New England music scene. In 2019, Steve expanded his reach by accepting an offer to perform with Royal Caribbean, entertaining audiences across the Virgin Islands and the Bahamas."},{"t":"p","html":"Steve’s music is characterized by his deep attention to the stories behind his songs, complemented by tasteful guitar work and soothing vocal melodies. Drawing inspiration from artists like <strong>Gregory Alan Isakov, Jackson Browne, and Jack Johnson</strong>, his sound blends easy listening with emotional depth."},{"t":"p","html":"Steve's recent work has seen him collaborate with industry heavyweights, including producer <strong>Jamie Mefford</strong> (Marionette Management) and mastering engineer <strong>David Glasser</strong> (Airshow Mastering). Both have worked with renowned acts such as <strong>Gregory Alan Isakov, Dave Matthews Band</strong>, the <strong>Grateful Dead</strong>, and <strong>Nathaniel Rateliff</strong>. With exciting new releases on the horizon, 2024 promises to be a standout year for Steve and his growing fanbase."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Steve!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/DAJ8JXHSq56/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.stevedennismusic.com/","img":"","title":"Steve Dennis | Singer-Songwriter | Boston, MA - Lighthouse Inn Out July 9!","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stevedennismusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5Q7D3eliTavuZuXMrKHPrw?si=0Fc247FHQtSFDkGtMutM-A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/steve-dennis/375028837\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> | <a href=\"https://www.stevedennismusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a></strong>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"348985","title":"Elder Grown Debuts Latest Single \"Parachutes\" at Animas City Theatre","date":"2024-09-28","lead":"Inviting audiences to a single release party with Eli Emmit Band, live at Animas City Theatre.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/348985/c0e466294576475c286e5a8a6bfecfb9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Inviting audiences to a single release party with Eli Emmit Band, live at Animas City Theatre."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3aTkJLu86xKiXj3E4tkoEL?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (September 28, 2024) - Rule-breaking musical band <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?si=oTBzULe7SuydZlwGFQ-YxA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Elder Grown</strong></a> takes music to new heights with their latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3aTkJLu86xKiXj3E4tkoEL?si=742ea80f587140b4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Parachutes</strong></a>”, celebrating its release on Saturday, <strong>September 28th</strong> at <strong>Animas City Theatre</strong> in Durango, CO. Featuring Durango's own <strong>Eli Emmit Band</strong>, this collaborative mix guarantees a night filled with vibrant rhythms and a distinctive experience."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/685987/large-46dd2385d15f931bbf36fd16e1733f3c.jpg","alt":"etix-Elder_23941724147450.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Elder Grown w/ Eli Emmit Band</strong><br><a href=\"https://www.animascitytheatre.com/?_gl=1*96ipr9*_ga*MTUxNTAwNDA2MC4xNzI2MTQ1Njc1*_ga_9BT49GESTJ*MTcyNjE0NTY3NC4xLjEuMTcyNjE0NTcyNi44LjAuMA..\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Animas City Theatre</a><br>Durango, CO<br>Doors at 7:00pm, Show at 8:00pm<br>Tickets on sale now online at <a href=\"https://animascitytheatre.com/event/elder-grown-with-eli-emmit-band/animas-city-theatre/durango-colorado/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.animascitytheatre.com</a><br>21+ / $20 / $25"},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.etix.com/ticket/p/96493464/elder-grown-with-eli-emmit-band-durango-animas-city-theatre?partner_id=100&amp;amp;_gl=1*16nk3rd*_ga*MTUxNTAwNDA2MC4xNzI2MTQ1Njc1*_ga_9BT49GESTJ*MTcyNjE0NTY3NC4xLjEuMTcyNjE0NTcyNi44LjAuMA..*_ga_PQ87YM5PX5*MTcyNjE0NTY3NS4xLjAuMTcyNjE0NTY3NS4wLjAuMA..&amp;amp;_ga=2.141061810.1609248756.1726145675-1515004060.1726145675","label":"Get Your Tickets HERE!","color":"#ff5f5f"},{"t":"p","html":"Written by <strong>Paul Hoffman</strong>, “Parachutes” talks about facing your fears, but also coming to terms with the idea that fear will always exist within us and around us in some form. Whether it is fear of the unknown, fear of making a mistake, or fear of being your authentic self, this song explores all the facets of fear and the growth that occurs when one faces them.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gseR-CKIchnxYHyG9G8MAEWDfYg11FRu/preview","height":"480"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I was always terrified of heights, until my girlfriend at the time surprised me with a skydiving date. I was 18 years old, and when I found myself strapped to a man I hardly knew sitting with my feet dangling off the side of a plane I had a choice to continue to be terrified, or to choose to live with that fear and embrace it. I embraced it, and I have never felt so free.”","cite":"- Paul Hoffman, Elder Grown"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/685978/large-9b8cfc5acba37fa742d065424c57de82.png","alt":"Cover art for \"Parachutes\""},{"t":"p","html":"Along with this theme, the topic of exploring who we are on the inside, and finding out a way to communicate and celebrate who we are to others, is addressed as well. Often people feel “less” or ashamed of certain aspects of who they are, and we hope “Parachutes” can serve as a reminder that every part of who you are is beautiful, and makes you, you."},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Jae Greens</strong> and <strong>Sam Kelly</strong>, the track masterfully combines jazz, funk, and hip-hop, evoking the sound of a fusion between the <strong>Red Hot Chili Peppers</strong>, <strong>Anderson .Paak</strong>, and <strong>Mac</strong> <strong>Miller</strong>, resulting in a snappy song with irresistible guitar riffs."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Elder Grown:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Family and community are the roots of <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?si=oTBzULe7SuydZlwGFQ-YxA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Elder Grown</strong></a>, a band of brothers from Durango, Colorado. They consider every audience member to be their 6th collective member, the heartbeat that fuels their music. Elder Grown is a powerful rock band featuring hip-hop forward funk &amp; soul inspired, original songs. Their improvisational jams serve as the foundation for their captivating and genre-bending music. With groovy bass lines, screaming guitar, and bold saxophone, they invite listeners on a rollercoaster ride of musical exploration."},{"t":"p","html":"Switching instruments mid-song, Elder Grown defies conventions and takes you on a journey into the unrecognizably familiar. The band has released three albums and one single so far. Their debut album, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/75sf4VsRBdfvW8EuEBqyv3?si=IHiBlRvrTsuK3_O1n5hvDQ&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=166c25b42e8b4b88\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Fire On The Way</strong></a>”, released in 2011, an EP called “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/22Xy0KU3rMB0FH7mHhxj4c?si=9lJrbkHnQxu173yPTk9Clw&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=6c844eb1dea9480a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Motorhome Mixes</strong></a>”, released in 2014, a self-titled full-length album in 2018, and a new album to be released in the fall of 2024."},{"t":"p","html":"The band’s origin story dates back to the early 90s when the <strong>Hoffman</strong> brothers —&nbsp;<strong>Joshua</strong>, <strong>John</strong>, and <strong>Paul&nbsp;</strong>— grew up in Albuquerque, New Mexico, surrounded by their father's performances as a singer-songwriter. Their passion for music grew, and after moving to Southwest Colorado, they formed Elder Grown, embracing their multifaceted musical talents."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Sam</strong> <strong>Kelly</strong>, (saxophone), joined the band during their time at Fort Lewis College. His love for saxophone and unique sound contributed to Elder Grown's evolution."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Brandon</strong> <strong>Clark</strong>, primarily a guitarist, expanded his skills to bass and keyboards to keep up with the band's instrument swapping. His love for classic rock and soulful tunes adds a creative touch to their sound."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Guillaume</strong> <strong>Metz</strong>, a professional guitarist from Paris, France, joined Elder Grown in 2019. His expertise as a lead guitarist, backup vocalist, and auxiliary bassist brought depth and richness to their performances."},{"t":"p","html":"Together, Elder Grown continues to captivate audiences with their soul-inspired sound and a commitment to pushing musical boundaries. With a new album on the horizon, they look forward to sharing their journey with their extended family of listeners.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Elder Grown!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/C-5bwLqOXmu/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ElderGrown/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"></a>​​​<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/eldergrown?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&amp;igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ElderGrown/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.bandsintown.com/a/1142918?came_from=257\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>bandsintown</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"351098","title":"Singer/Songwriter Kyle Davis released his sixth record, \"Make It Count\". Originally discorvered by Don Dixon and Phil Ramone, his music has been hailed in Billboard and Rolling Stone magazines.","date":"2024-09-27","lead":"A fresh taste from the highly-anticipated album, released with a cinematic music video.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/351098/88afe83efc548791dc9f85566fbf844b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A fresh taste from the highly-anticipated album, released with a cinematic music video."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2Af4jFhKnGQ4hnplFRYYgb?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Prince George, VA (September 27, 2024) - Virginia native and seasoned musician <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5lq6g7ALA2XGi4f4e7YR9h?si=YxaeVzj9RJO0vKWxmIp-lw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Kyle</strong> <strong>Davis</strong></a> takes listeners on an emotional ride with his new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2Af4jFhKnGQ4hnplFRYYgb?si=cf5c811cd4a34921\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Last Line</strong></a>,” released on September 27, 2024. This track is part of his highly anticipated upcoming album, <strong>‘</strong><strong>Jericho</strong>.’ Produced by <strong>Don</strong> <strong>Dixon</strong>, the single comes with a music video that captures some of the recording processes from the very studio it was made."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/6s000ljQ-E4","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"The song reflects on life’s struggles and the search for meaning, highlighting the narrator’s difficult journeys and personal transformations. There’s a longing for redemption and a desire for significance, despite the challenges faced. The imagery of superheroes and high altitudes contrasts the mundane with the extraordinary, emphasizing the aspiration for escape and a broader perspective."},{"t":"p","html":"Ultimately, “The Last Line” conveys a message of perseverance, with the hope that the final words or actions will hold profound meaning. The recurring theme of unexpected difficulties, symbolized by the rainy season, underscores the resilience needed to navigate life’s hardships."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687948/compressed_original-25247d70a4a2134ca62f93bfcc9844aa.jpg","alt":"Covert Art of \"The Last Line\" by Liz Davis"},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/kyledavis/the-last-line?utm_campaign=website&amp;amp;utm_medium=Email+&amp;amp;utm_source=SendGrid","label":"Listen to \"The Last Line\" on Streaming Platforms!","color":"#ff7070"},{"t":"p","html":"Blended with tasty guitar riffs and soulful melodies, “The Last Line” showcases Kyle’s powerhouse vocals in a way that captivates listeners from start to finish. As the debut single from the upcoming album ‘Jericho’, this song is sure to leave audiences eagerly anticipating more."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5lq6g7ALA2XGi4f4e7YR9h?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kyle Davis:"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/689800/compressed_original-4da8346b575452f7fba82672bfdc5659.jpg","alt":"kyle_davis1.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.kylewdavismusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Kyle</strong></a><strong>’s</strong> musical journey began in a home filled with music, where his grandmother and aunts played piano and sang gospel, and his father and brother played guitar. As a toddler, he would pretend to sing into makeshift microphones."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Ever since I can remember, I’ve felt a deep connection to music,” </em>Kyle recalls. <em>“I’d listen to my parents’ records and feel deeply moved by the emotions those artists expressed. I still feel that way even today.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"This passion led to a successful career from the start. In his early 20s, Kyle began recording albums like ‘<strong>Kyle Davis</strong>’, ‘<strong>Waiting For You</strong>’, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7AXVCPbp9Pnu1zfUMFdX1o?si=g-B5zlCeSLOXry9WudtAVA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Raising</strong> <strong>Heroes</strong></a>’, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2pzGtUoNpwj0ggfBTNyS6F?si=m6pIEJ2zTWWlhcTZqXdP_g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Don’t</strong> <strong>Tell the World</strong></a>’, and ‘<strong>River City Gang</strong>.’ His single “<strong>God Love Me</strong>,” released by <strong>Universal</strong> <strong>Records</strong>, became a fan favorite and critical hit. <strong>Billboard</strong> called him <em>“One of the best unsigned artists,”&nbsp;</em>and <strong>Rolling Stone</strong> gave his debut four stars, and he also shared the stage with <strong>Bob Dylan</strong>, <strong>John</strong> <strong>Mayer</strong>, and many others. Though compared to artists like <strong>Jackson</strong> <strong>Browne</strong> and <strong>David</strong> <strong>Gray</strong>, he remains his own man, a singular talent with an extraordinary gift for conveying stirring sentiment with richly rewarding results."},{"t":"p","html":"While Kyle’s path has taken different turns over the years, his devotion and determination are as steadfast as ever. <em>“My desire to share meaning through my music remains my personal priority,”</em> he insists. <em>“These days, more than ever, it’s important to find that common bond that connects us all. In my opinion, music provides that means.”</em>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Kyle!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C_9NM9SSSsj/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.kylewdavismusic.com/","img":"","title":"Singer/Songwriter Kyle Davis released his sixth record, \"Make It Count\". Originally discorvered by Don Dixon and Phil Ramone, his music has been hailed in Billboard and Rolling Stone magazines.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/kylewdavismusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/kylewdavismusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCAd1M5QdT1GsfgFqngAEuUQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1fQuYKsLfkTcqpj1pIwTYz?si=qgjmSdbhTV6zJqr6wNkvWg&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=f3742451339946a5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"351161","title":"Visionaries have a divine obligation in life. A child never chooses their family, circumstances, or fortune at birth. Stephen Thomas a Multi-Genre Artist that's forced to be reckon with. He's the future of the music and entertainment industry. He's outstanding for 2022 and the future to come.","date":"2024-09-27","lead":"A musical tribute to power through life's challenges, showcasing Stephen's powerhouse vocals.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/351161/ee37e075f9d5cdb946be68380ec08772.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A musical tribute to power through life's challenges, showcasing Stephen's powerhouse vocals."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Charleston, WV (September 27, 2024) - Universal artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=YTInGlyeR_Oow3q_1Wlt9g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen</strong> <strong>Thomas</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>returns with a fresh track focused on encouraging listeners to fight internal struggles with the title “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=a142a46fef1f42b2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stay Strong</strong></a>”, unleashed on September 27, 2024. The track further showcases Stephen’s talent as a singer, solidifying his position within the alternative/pop rock genre."},{"t":"p","html":"Building on the themes explored in his previous release,<strong>&nbsp;“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3cqqiH32fFqe2fHfBCXWWP?si=2cd8267abd884fd6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Back Home</strong></a>”, this new track vividly captures a spirit of inspiration and determination. It encourages listeners to embrace life with unwavering commitment, urging them to channel every ounce of their energy into moving forward and overcoming obstacles. Through its powerful message, the track inspires a relentless pursuit of success, motivating individuals to strive for victory no matter the challenges they face."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/686538/large-8bd6ea6b24b81e805a6d59263429310c.png","alt":"Cover art for \"Stay Strong\""},{"t":"p","html":"Stephen’s “Stay Strong” is a heartfelt tribute that draws inspiration from overcoming formidable challenges. It honors the unwavering courage of our troops, individuals battling autoimmune diseases, those facing mental health struggles, and anyone confronting life’s toughest obstacles."},{"t":"quote","html":"“In order to win in life, you have to fight. And your fight isn’t over yet; it’s just beginning. Stay strong, my friends.”","cite":"- Stephen Thomas, Singer/Songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>\"Stay Strong\" Lyrics (SNIPPET)</strong><br><strong>​</strong><u><br></u><em>You got an uphill battle</em><br><em><br>Stay strong&nbsp;</em><br><em><br>You gotta climb the valley&nbsp;<br></em><br><em>So long</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/Rc63gZweqAo","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Pouring his soul into every note of his music, Stephen’s “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eCaBda7pQk8ecAhq7GvJT?si=227e4730b4304a47\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stay Strong</strong></a>” sends a clear message of hope and resilience, to become a beacon for all those navigating difficult circumstances, whether you’re stationed on the frontlines, enduring a challenging hospital stay, or simply struggling through another demanding day. With every chord and lyric, Stephen reminds listeners that they are not alone in their battles—urging them to keep fighting and to stay strong through the trials they face."},{"t":"p","html":"The highly anticipated release will be accompanied by a visually stunning music video, adding even more excitement and anticipation for its debut."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Stephen Thomas:"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676846/large-55a595b43551877ff75bb9984341f332.jpg","alt":"Photo by Josh Hanna"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=oHBViFwQQaaIjt97y8p4Og\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a>, a versatile Universal Artist whose musical odyssey has taken him from Charleston, West Virginia to the forefront of the industry. With a dynamic career marked by exploration and evolution, Stephen has recently embarked on a thrilling journey into the realms of rock and alternative music, infusing his sound with raw, authentic vibes that resonate deeply with audiences."},{"t":"p","html":"As a national touring recording artist, Stephen's talent has garnered widespread acclaim, earning him five <strong>Grammy Award</strong> considerations as an independent artist. From his early beginnings to signing with <strong>SkeeloMusik</strong> / <strong>Sony RED</strong> in 2013 and eventually finding his artistic home with <strong>Creative Hearts Entertainment</strong>, Stephen's journey has been one of constant growth and discovery."},{"t":"p","html":"Stephen's impact transcends mere accolades, with his interviews featured in prestigious publications such as <strong>MTV</strong>, <strong>Vibe</strong> <strong>Magazine</strong>, <strong>Hype</strong> <strong>Magazine</strong>, and <strong>TCT</strong> <strong>Network</strong>. He has graced renowned stages alongside industry icons and walked the red carpet at events like the <strong>2014</strong> <strong>BET</strong> <strong>Live</strong> <strong>Experience</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Amidst his diverse musical endeavors, Stephen's recent immersion into rock and alternative music has been particularly transformative. Embracing the genre's edgy, rebellious spirit, Stephen has honed his craft, crafting songs that pulsate with raw emotion and electrifying energy. His single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4IJY700TPZXKlrkO0mR4zM?si=Q_xjis9iTtyfjYRfshMH5g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Best Days</strong></a>,\" soared to #2 on the iTunes Charts, standing as a testament to his artistic versatility and widespread appeal. Meanwhile, his music video for \"<a href=\"https://youtu.be/wj8FAEyFpRA?feature=shared\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Search</strong> <strong>Me</strong></a>\" received global recognition, earning placement on <strong>RevoltTV</strong> and reaching millions worldwide. Stephen's music is now readily available on all streaming platforms, inviting listeners to embark on a sonic journey filled with rock and alternative vibes."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephen!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C_wHTESP-DL/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.stephentmusic.com/","img":"","title":"Visionaries have a divine obligation in life. A child never chooses their family, circumstances, or fortune at birth. Stephen Thomas a Multi-Genre Artist that's forced to be reckon with. He's the future of the music and entertainment industry. He's outstanding for 2022 and the future to come.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.stephentmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/StephenTMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/404?fromUrl=/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/StephenThomas1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://x.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>X</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"351590","title":"Steve Erickson","date":"2024-09-27","lead":"Showcasing a decade of heartfelt storytelling, 'Retrospective' invites listeners on a journey through Steve Erickson’s evolution as a songwriter and recording artist.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/351590/af4f8118b130f4213229584ae511b8bb.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Showcasing a decade of heartfelt storytelling, '<em>Retrospective'</em> invites listeners on a journey through Steve Erickson’s evolution as a songwriter and recording artist."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0Dyp97YlFsPxsA7csCM8VV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"ASHEVILLE, NC / VERO BEACH, FL (September 27, 2024) – Today, acclaimed singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://ericksongs.net/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Steve Erickson</strong></a> unveils <strong>‘</strong><strong></strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0Dyp97YlFsPxsA7csCM8VV?si=J9eKPFzjSyuvtL_vIMX3rw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Retrospective’</strong></em></a>, a carefully curated collection of songs that capture over a decade of his musical journey.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Featuring 15 original tracks, the album spans parts of his career from 2012 to 2024, offering listeners a deep dive into his distinctive blend of folk, Americana, blues, and country."},{"t":"p","html":"<em><strong>‘Retrospective’</strong></em> gathers original standout songs from Erickson’s earlier albums, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/47yg8AH3fOvBUvcls5BYrH?si=kLHPMRyrSWGfRosFTl9VsA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>It’s About Time’</strong></a>, <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2SfnXMSMYkwpv5Xbfbp6y3?si=rAJMGLehSiiVP9XILNvbXw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Music Tonight’</strong></a>,&nbsp;<strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0RTW7pEFKjOey3RFePkahl?si=GUWr8FjDR6Cq2MRwAZ7r5g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Moving On’</strong></a>, and his latest release <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7cMpYuyxi8LSUH4eIYdlTc?go=1&amp;sp_cid=cf2574d8c3c2ab88c5653d52eabc4308&amp;utm_source=embed_player_p&amp;utm_medium=desktop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Crooked Road’</strong></a>, which shares a contemporary perspective on traditional Appalachian music. Each track showcases Erickson’s signature storytelling, weaving together themes of love, loss, resilience, and the passage of time."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7cMpYuyxi8LSUH4eIYdlTc?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"quote","html":"“It's been great to take stock after producing four albums to present a larger collection of these songs. After a decade of recording, it seemed like the right time to review some of my favorites.”","cite":"- Singer-Songwriter Steve Erickson"},{"t":"p","html":"Tracks like “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7kZj6iN1cEZYXH7OMi0GCy?si=fb08f57ef52f4bf4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>All or Nothing</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0vGmyRFx7Drr4noT1c5tOp?si=f6e599ac51e240a9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Living in Tune</strong></a>” bring to mind a timeless sound, reminiscent of classic Americana artists, while songs such as “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5MZygu5HTJqpRGoZyJnCdq?si=c2d031f9afc74a58\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>One Port Ahead of the Storm</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/71ypqNNCzKb1uElwU9ZaKH?si=b7b975077ac241f7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wind Across the Jetty</strong></a>” paint vivid landscapes through Erickson’s rich, evocative lyrics. The rowdy roadhouse song, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1k95wSBBkmTI7gfag78yPu?si=06eee220846e4283\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Music Tonight</strong></a>,” is fun and uplifting while the thought-provoking protest song, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/47535XX3GiVU5QKKINILh0?si=ffad8e0a2cf246f8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Higher Ground</strong></a>,” explores current conflicts. His meticulous approach to production is evident throughout the retrospective, with a rich array of acoustic instruments and contributions from talented musicians."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687105/compressed_original-e985646f1b1bd8ca235b14ede8a92a5d.jpeg","alt":"Cover art for \"Retrospective\""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Tracklist:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/47yg8AH3fOvBUvcls5BYrH?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<em><u>It’s About Time (2012)</u></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"1. One Port Ahead of the Storm"},{"t":"p","html":"2. All or Nothing"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Between the Lines"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2SfnXMSMYkwpv5Xbfbp6y3?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<em><u>Music Tonight (2016)</u></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Music Tonight"},{"t":"p","html":"5. Sing that Old Song"},{"t":"p","html":"6. Wind Across the Jetty"},{"t":"p","html":"7. Living in Tune"},{"t":"p","html":"8. Higher Ground"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0RTW7pEFKjOey3RFePkahl?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<em><u>Moving On (2019)</u></em>​"},{"t":"p","html":"9. Long Day Tonight"},{"t":"p","html":"10. River"},{"t":"p","html":"11. My Love Will Be With You"},{"t":"p","html":"12. Moving On"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7cMpYuyxi8LSUH4eIYdlTc?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<em><u>Crooked Road (2024)</u></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"13. Crooked Road"},{"t":"p","html":"14. Find a Light"},{"t":"p","html":"15. Blue Horizon"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Steve Erickson</strong>, who splits his time between Asheville, NC, and Vero Beach, FL, has spent the past decade perfecting his craft, producing four albums and building a dedicated fanbase. His latest project, <em><strong>Retrospective</strong></em>, cements his place as a key voice in the contemporary Americana and folk scene."},{"t":"p","html":"Retrospective is now available on all streaming platforms. For more information, visit <a href=\"https://ericksongs.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ericksongs.net</a>."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Praises for Steve Erickson"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"Introspective storytelling and acknowledgement of the past and present mark Erickson’s individuality as he brings tradition to the forefront.\" </em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; - </strong><a href=\"https://musicmecca.org/steve-erickson-pays-homage-to-appalachian-tradition-on-latest-album-crooked-road/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mae Farris, Music Mecca</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"He has that dark rich voice which works so well in traditionally based music.\"</em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;- </strong><a href=\"https://americana-uk.com/bluegrass-briefs-kyle-obrien-band-mission-hill-milltown-philosophers-steve-erickson-last-hour-bluegrass-blackwater-railroad-company\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tim Martin, Americana UK</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"An artist as dedicated to the true Americana sound as anyone... and the result is an album which can best be described as refreshingly pure!\"</em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;- </strong><a href=\"https://www.americanamusicappreciation.com/post/fine-contemporary-tribute-to-old-time-music\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Paul Cutler, Americana Music Appreciation</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"His music is both diverse and distinctive, a sound flush with elements that encompass bluegrass, country, blues, folk, and other elements that are part and parcel of an authentic traditional tapestry...It would be hard to imagine a more thoroughly satisfying set of songs.\"</em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;- </strong><a href=\"https://bluegrasstoday.com/crooked-road-steve-erickson/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lee Zimmerman, Bluegrass Today</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687091/-0352cd56d98cac022a906cb902288003.webp","alt":"steve 3.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687091/preview-01cdc6516b0594c11977f66689af4149.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687090/large-67b4a206bcc4faf704a8cd565ad689d0.webp","alt":"steve 4.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687090/preview-c78b2c14c7479b963d632687ea7bb32f.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687089/large-af84399dd1c6870bfc9dc8695157e54f.webp","alt":"steve 5.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687089/preview-001122d9e3748d9f5aa1a83219917642.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687088/large-2edb0341ba7ada08e43f2883acb73076.jpg","alt":"Crooked Road_Cover for CDB.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687088/preview-6fa0047148adf86a9f6334282859d35d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687093/large-1330b8c9d2f02e54d62ad801510b0990.webp","alt":"Steve.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687093/preview-cea11c6d13dba69fcfb0a1a21e6f1868.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687092/-eeaaccb8025e9f29b3f367d9ef0931b9.webp","alt":"steve 2.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/687092/-eeaaccb8025e9f29b3f367d9ef0931b9.webp"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Steve Erickson:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3cejBgcRgP4gWuMxWVaR7i?si=IqtNzdoVQ_6zzCeClksNmQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Steve Erickson</strong></a> is a seasoned musician whose journey into music began alongside a successful career in public relations across Atlanta, New York City, and Washington DC. Drawing from a diverse range of musical influences, Erickson's songwriting style blends elements of country, blues, and folk."},{"t":"p","html":"Originally involved with local bands like <strong>Truth in Advertising</strong> in Atlanta and later collaborating with <strong>Nick Peters</strong> in the duo <strong>Medium Gauge</strong> in Washington DC, Erickson has since established himself as a solo artist. Currently based between Asheville, North Carolina, and Vero Beach, Florida, Erickson’s musical repertoire is characterized by thoughtful storytelling and a rich sound."},{"t":"p","html":"His discography includes notable releases such as ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/47yg8AH3fOvBUvcls5BYrH?si=He3bIgdLRiWwTH8FXAdieA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">It's About Time’</a> (2012), ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2SfnXMSMYkwpv5Xbfbp6y3?si=M6a_Z7RdT1ydjTRXnDu9lQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Music Tonight’</a> (2016), ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0RTW7pEFKjOey3RFePkahl?si=VZRt4AZfQriywSeotGvHrw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Moving On’</a> (2019), and ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7cMpYuyxi8LSUH4eIYdlTc?si=st2hoM6_RRS1SLwMrwIYxA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Crooked Road’</a> (2024) which explores Appalachian music traditions with tracks like “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/50SS1BxbSUnn20zF9Vj0Hy?si=550bf30b2d4948ea\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Crooked Road</a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5W0nZqEIAcUY7su68yrlrp?si=5d5d9e3f24214b71\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lay Me Down Beside My Love</a>.” His latest release, Retrospective (2024), combines these albums in a refreshing new way, reflecting on an accomplished career in the space. Known for his ability to craft powerful narratives and connect deeply with his audience, Steve Erickson continues to evolve as a notable figure in contemporary Americana music."},{"t":"p","html":"For more about Steve Erickson and his music, visit his <a href=\"https://ericksongs.net/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">official website</a>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Steve Erickson!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3cejBgcRgP4gWuMxWVaR7i?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://ericksongs.net/home","img":"https://d10j3mvrs1suex.cloudfront.net/s:bzglfiles/u/398251/08ce1b7daced729db5c882f44487d4218600a3cd/original/moving-on-large-image.jpg/!!/meta%3AeyJzcmNCdWNrZXQiOiJiemdsZmlsZXMifQ%3D%3D.jpg","title":"Steve Erickson","desc":"Home page of Steve Erickson, a blues artist from Vero Beach. Florida. Singer-Songwriter Steve Erickson takes an eclectic approach to acoustic-based music. His moving Americana tunes provide a foundati"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3cejBgcRgP4gWuMxWVaR7i?si=0bQkIu7ET_i1vwD0D543qg&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=0da0ed3495db4227\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/steve-erickson/73492990\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://ericksongs.net/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"352621","title":"Aaron Stewart","date":"2024-09-27","lead":"The 12-track album delves into resilience, love, and personal growth, reflecting Aaron's 15-year journey.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/352621/0a3e86b33d5990630968f374e1902b9a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The 12-track album delves into resilience, love, and personal growth, reflecting Aaron's 15-year journey."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6uZvyZhyVP0aVAK4UODscp?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Vista, CA (September 27, 2024) — Singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0iVdetJG5c9fnmQlQJ3RMD?si=VyNZ22QtRPOv97wlRsjMCQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aaron Stewart</strong></a> revisits his passion for music with a vibrant new 12-track album, <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6uZvyZhyVP0aVAK4UODscp?si=X4V0e9nFTq6sB8ShRuAqwA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Traveling Light’</strong></a>, released on September 27, 2024. Hot on the heels of the latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6vxdV9K62aoXWml2sE2N6Y?si=GbNqUEJdRHyr8oKAaXHAyg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>A Little Bit Obsessed</strong></a><strong>,</strong>” the album showcases Aaron’s impressive vocals and catchy tunes, encapsulating the last 15 years of Aaron’s life, crafted with friends and co-writers who shared parts of that journey."},{"t":"p","html":"It culminated in reconnecting with an old friend, his producer <strong>Jeff</strong> <strong>Hoeppner</strong>, who made the creation of this project&nbsp;a significant and valuable experience in his career."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/688418/large-da07f022909dc9cdf819308da21de197.jpg","alt":"Cover art for 'Traveling Light', Designed by Shane Armitage"},{"t":"quote","html":"“After my 2009 album, I became a bit disillusioned with how much time I could pour into a creative endeavor that was ultimately fleeting. Those ups and downs ultimately led to ‘Rises and Falls’ where I came to the realization that artistry is an ongoing ebb and flow, and I can define success as the joy of creation itself.”","cite":"- Aaron Stewart, Singer-songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"‘<strong>Traveling Light</strong>’ is an album rooted in themes of resilience, love, and personal growth. The lyrics explore the highs and lows of life’s journey, from overcoming challenges in “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1bjRSBCm4paEoiBgDqcL9w?si=e7f837cf5952421b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Rises and Falls</strong></a>” to savoring the present moment in “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5WW32UEAgB0bHjDMiriCY0?si=203a12bcd0554088\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Savor</strong></a>.” Songs like “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/66x6xWghmvcGdzpck5rrYC?si=09aae521658f4409\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>A Little Bit Obsessed</strong></a>” playfully dive into the intensity of love, while “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3E1JQdN2LlhPFwWJgJV3XH?si=7b27bd33b1f144bb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Shining</strong> <strong>Armor</strong></a>” speaks to devotion and protection."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/66x6xWghmvcGdzpck5rrYC?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>\"Shining Armor\" Lyrics (SNEAK PEAK)<br></u></strong><br>Cuz you fought your best&nbsp;<br><br>And you need some rest<br><br>But you just cannot escape<br><br>If you call my name<br><br>I’ll be on my way<br><br>I will be your barricade&nbsp;<br><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Themes of reflection and healing are woven throughout tracks like “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/13TTVs0PHzrWHCuPkys5kM?si=6c1faf40777c4fd3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Silver</strong> <strong>Lining</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2OrVaSY3XqTjDByeYtGUDI?si=cde8fa2421d24b09\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Better</strong> <strong>Off</strong> <strong>Now</strong></a>,” urging listeners to find hope and peace despite life’s difficulties. Overall, the album conveys a message of perseverance, self-discovery, and joy."},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, 'Traveling Light' captures Aaron’s pop influences, with soaring melodies, lush harmonies, and dynamic production that continually builds throughout each track. His vocal style, reminiscent of <strong>Justin Timberlake</strong>, <strong>Bruno</strong> <strong>Mars</strong>, and <strong>Michael</strong> <strong>Jackson</strong>, shines through energetic, uplifting songs packed with catchy hooks and evolving layers of sound. With every song, the album radiates an undeniable sense of lightness and joy, leaving listeners feeling uplifted and inspired, as if the music itself is traveling with them, carrying a spark of hope."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/689185/-81cf29ca8437bdfdc1523eb3a63169b8.jpeg","alt":"L1_L2110ok Large.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/689185/preview-26ceeab544851c2a6973f4de19768013.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/689184/large-dc062a4d269e67a9c50652bf45f3abb4.jpg","alt":"L1_L2004ok.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/689184/preview-5137ebf32a9729860737a680f7002604.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/689182/large-34ce9326af362e84f5bcefdddd0ecf9d.jpg","alt":"L1_L2162ok.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/689182/preview-45310d0311e55759475ab6adc93a14e9.jpg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Aaron Stewart:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0iVdetJG5c9fnmQlQJ3RMD?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0iVdetJG5c9fnmQlQJ3RMD?si=N47ToFNzSEGJPcAq0eApYg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aaron Stewart</strong></a>’s musical journey took an unexpected turn after he earned his music degree, as life led him into software development. For a decade, his piano keys remained neglected, and his voice fell mostly silent, save for the occasional song he couldn’t resist writing. But the music never truly left him. The melodies of Christmas eventually pulled him back, leading to a Christmas album that marked his return."},{"t":"p","html":"Now, after 14 years, Aaron steps back into the spotlight with <strong>Traveling Light</strong>, a 12-track album blending new compositions with those written over the last decade. The project captures the essence of his journey, showcasing his over 5-octave vocal range, masterful piano skills, and a love for lush harmonies. Traveling Light is not just a return — it’s a revival, filled with the energy and soul of a man rediscovering his passion."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Aaron!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/OvaEWbbYBdE?si=U1PXt8860e6SSSiS","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://aaronstewart.com/","img":"https://d10j3mvrs1suex.cloudfront.net/s:bzglfiles/u/599860/959e27d0a1423df5324ba4060c5d7d904038a8ed/original/artistprofile.jpeg/!!/meta%3AeyJzcmNCdWNrZXQiOiJiemdsZmlsZXMifQ%3D%3D.jpg","title":"Aaron Stewart","desc":"Home page of Aaron Stewart, a songwriter artist from San Diego. Aaron steps back into the spotlight with Traveling Light, a 12-track album blending new compositions with those written over the last de"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/astewartmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/apstew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/apstew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@apstew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"338885","title":"Audra Watt","date":"2024-09-23","lead":"Reminiscent of boundless love that transcends time through a mother's eyes, now comes with an official music video.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/338885/4962c9592ba47095c71cd342d9544777.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Reminiscent of boundless love that transcends time through a mother's eyes, now comes with an official music video."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/doMAgCXtO_k","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Nashville, TN (September 23, 2024) - Singer/songwriter Audra Watt debuted her title track \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/64gZitIWmd3trVVQIiKWim?si=5becb42a61a2421b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Bullet Trains</strong></a>\" on August 9, 2024, along with a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=doMAgCXtO_k\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">music video</a> on September 23, 2024, that evokes a feeling of warmth and affection in viewers. This heartfelt song resonates with listeners who capture the timeless journey of parenthood through its vivid storytelling and relatable experiences, from the anticipation of childbirth to the bittersweet moments of watching a child grow up and move away through the swift passage of time."},{"t":"p","html":"Directed by <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/director_producer?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&amp;igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>William Gawley</strong></a> and produced by <a href=\"https://charlotteavenueentertainment.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Charlotte Avenue&nbsp;</strong><strong>Entertainment</strong></a>,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>the music video for \"Bullet Trains\" is a heartfelt visual journey that perfectly complements the song's emotional depth. Featuring cameo appearances from Audra Watt's sons, <strong>Nolan</strong> and <strong>Isaac</strong>, the video captures the tender moments of motherhood and the passage of time. The narrative follows Audra and her sons through various stages of life, with an actor portraying her \"grown-up\" son in the final scenes. The video's nostalgic and evocative imagery beautifully mirrors the song's themes, creating a touching tribute to the joys and challenges of raising a child."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/64gZitIWmd3trVVQIiKWim?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/audrawatt/bullet-trains-2","label":"Listen to \"Bullet Trains\" on Streaming Platforms!","color":"#ff5c5c"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Writing ‘Bullet Trains’ was an intimate experience, with both the melody and lyrics crafted to capture a deeply personal feeling. I was surprised and touched by how many people resonated with the song's themes. I'm so glad to finally release it and help others articulate the ups and downs of motherhood through music.”","cite":"- Audra Watt, Singer/songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"In \"Bullet Trains,\" Audra puts a new spin on the classic theme of \"<strong>Cat's in the Cradle</strong>\" from a mother's viewpoint. Her airy folk voice, similar to <strong>Kacey Musgraves</strong>, adds a unique element to the mid-tempo Americana melody reminiscent of<strong>&nbsp;Brandi Carlile's</strong> heartfelt storytelling. The reflective lyrics are reminiscent of <strong>Lori McKenna</strong>, while the warm acoustic production brings to mind <strong>Jason Isbell</strong>, creating a deeply resonant listening experience."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/673097/large-c95d8e407c6d4762daada6435cbc3a0a.jpeg","alt":"Audra4.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/673097/preview-1bc89c682c6f461c35740c609bf6cb30.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/673098/large-87fae7f60ad8e2b060a6b4ce98037b7e.jpeg","alt":"Audra2.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/673098/preview-41d05846645422d9dbcb7cf665f89266.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/673096/large-5693761655366f675973a23dad88c5f0.jpeg","alt":"Audra.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/673096/preview-ada9e904e8dff886b4269a4e68183929.jpeg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"The Americana-inspired sound, characterized by acoustic guitars and warm harmonies, complements the reflective lyrics, making \"Bullet Trains\" a moving anthem for anyone who has experienced the joys and challenges of raising a child. Perfect for fans of narrative songwriting and rich, melodic arrangements, this track is sure to leave a lasting impression."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Audra Watt:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6FssIhtpES3HRaKqgVxsYR?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3VjPlo3yb9K8Agv9kCQrvy?si=yc_oBXtSSQWn-c9F5U57fQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Audra Watt</strong></a>, a singer/songwriter from Nashville, started her musical journey at just four years old with the fiddle and began playing the piano at six. During her high school years in Memphis, her passion for music grew as she played woodwinds in various bands, orchestras, ensembles, and jazz on keys. Audra started writing songs then and continued at <strong>Vanderbilt University</strong>, where she also picked up the guitar.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"She took a 17-year hiatus from music to build a successful healthcare marketing career and start a family. Married to <strong>Ryan</strong> with two children, Audra reconnected with songwriting at 40. Since then, she has emerged in Nashville's music scene, performing in songwriter rounds and collaborating with artists. Audra has honed her skills through workshops, courses and master classes, earning recognition from <strong>Songtown</strong> and the <strong>Nashville Songwriters Association</strong>. Working towards her artist EP, her first single, \"<strong>Bullet Trains</strong>,\" about motherhood and time, is set to release in 2024. Audra's talent and charisma make her a sought-after collaborator in the industry. &nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Audra!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/C-dOVViOit4/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.audrawatt.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/65de24803891890816df3218/t/65e63604eee15b48e2bc0cc7/1709585924891/Audra+Watt_logo-fullcolor-rgb.png?format=1500w","title":"Audra Watt","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/audrawatt/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/AudraWattMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@AudraWattMusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"348127","title":"Dream Dream Dream My Friend. Out July 12. Wildlife Control blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: it doesnʼt matter if sheʼs analog or digital.","date":"2024-09-20","lead":"Wildlife Control bridges the fast-paced, tech-driven, and culturally divided present with a timeless blend of music.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/348127/8225996f9c14392a499567455f8b0e35.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Wildlife Control bridges the fast-paced, tech-driven, and culturally divided present with a timeless blend of music."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3phlXu5LEQdj6n74IL6ntr?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"NEW YORK, NY (September 20, 2024) - A decade since their self-titled debut trended across the indie music blog scene and onto the college radio charts, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2f2Bf7TxY9xWWbTETxtPnP?si=Q82Lx29NRUmK-r9C5ILytQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wildlife Control</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>returns with ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3phlXu5LEQdj6n74IL6ntr?si=glYmGlwQTAWk57FVUyeR8g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Love. Champion. Mountain. King.’</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"An album of paradoxes, it’s simultaneously deeply personal and human, embracing technology and AI, as evidenced by the artwork accompanying the album and singles. The music maintains the aesthetic, with the opening track, “<em><strong>Your Name Is Love</strong></em>,” immediately placing the listener in the story of the main character, an AI recalling their birth."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1CDe2pHha9LGLJSl2FeYXV?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"The tracks grow in lyrical and musical maturity as the album unfolds. Starting with youthful, simple, and energetic lyrics, it evolves into stories of mixed emotions, tragedies, heartbreak, longing, and finally an embrace of life and the differences between us all.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683519/large-7717feb0e8df179a0c623a0ec7641c0b.jpg","alt":"Cover Art for Love. Champion. Mountain. King."},{"t":"p","html":"In an age of fast-paced content, rapidly evolving technology, and divisions between cultures and beliefs, Wildlife Control has humanized the topics of today, wrapped them in many of the best elements from the last five decades of popular music, and delivered an album best summarized by the closing lyric, <em>“it’s alright, be different.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Their third LP, <strong>‘</strong><strong><em>Love. Champion. Mountain. King.’</em></strong> began as a self-portrait-style project by songwriter <strong>Neil Love</strong> during the pandemic. Unlike previous collaborative projects, Wildlife Control recorded every instrument themselves including guitars, bass, drums, synths, and brass, inspired by the process behind classic records like <strong>Stevie Wonder’s Innervisions</strong> and <strong>Paul McCartney</strong><strong>’s</strong> <strong>eponymous</strong> <strong>solo album</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The title ‘Love. Champion. Mountain. King.’ is a word-by-word translation of the names given to me when I was born. I hadn’t realized how deeply those names have influenced who I am until I started creating this album. Through this process, I’ve found strength and comfort in the multiple dimensions of who I am. If anything, I hope this album helps listeners feel that every proverbial box they’ve ever been put in is way too small.”","cite":"- Wildlife Control"},{"t":"p","html":"The record features Wildlife Control’s unique production and mixing aesthetic and was mastered by <strong>Joe LaPorta</strong> (<strong>The Shins, Sleigh Bells, Beach House, The National</strong>)."},{"t":"p","html":"The full-length album comes on the heels of four singles,<strong>&nbsp;“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3jV1UVysfz3HEIJT1Gs0Fe?si=5zywaW7kRna-HB2vPJB_Nw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Make Me Feel</a>,” “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5p6SX6n8g1jrREu8atGvDu?si=863468e8970945fd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Team You</a>,” “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7e1gM03sr3AhFi0DoXx7uD?si=HzjgCqRCRDuxKrC7EgMp7g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Dream Dream Dream My Friend</a>,”&nbsp;</strong>and<strong>&nbsp;“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1oG0EDktgqw4mgDpPK2jfw?si=jo5_T1jjTmm50J5BECq4dQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Your Blood on My Lips</a>,”</strong> which received positive reviews this summer across major music blogs. Tour dates for North and South America, as well as Europe and Asia will be announced later this fall. <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3phlXu5LEQdj6n74IL6ntr?si=WFqWPdhxSrWOJ_hy4R0LDg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Love. Champion. Mountain. King.</strong></a><strong>’</strong> is now available on all streaming platforms, vinyl, and CD via <a href=\"https://wildlifectrl.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lexsme Recording Co/AWAL</strong></a>. For more information, visit <a href=\"https://wildlifectrl.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>wildlifectrl.com</strong></a>."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663594/large-b5f3631336ee2c3ba2e3b8d3e691c44b.jpg","alt":"wildlife-control-dream-dream-dream-my-friend-cover-2400.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663594/preview-55dcd48cb549319ee72c20f117f8c397.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/670217/large-a5a38eb29ee6f382daeed171a5559944.jpg","alt":"Your-Blood-on-my-lips-cover-1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/670217/preview-858468ada9e4d195ec668c4d9bd9d520.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/650577/large-5027e40733d1058c1c69c7d82766a099.jpg","alt":"Make-Me-Feel-Cover-2.1-6000x6000_vivid.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/650577/preview-ec039b7ba20ba1d400edf6f298c2f7d1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/657077/large-81e86d0acd29325ac28d0d293397f623.jpg","alt":"Team-You-Cover-3-6000-Vivid-Warm.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/657077/preview-6df00e07bed60f6942272c08a0505676.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683524/large-746373024bbf01c17c993ca9171447c6.jpg","alt":"wildlife_control_lcmk_be_different_promo.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683524/preview-65eb7be733e3c7eaf2d2167d439d76ef.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683528/-e84ab91f6748ab828d8da87f87f4277e.jpg","alt":"wildlife_control_live_eric_hwang_vertical.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683528/preview-bf07a046168c515cca75fc00572ca7df.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683527/large-3958fb28df7f811b36025f12941ba3f6.jpg","alt":"wildlife_control_live_eric_hwang_square.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683527/preview-205e230179f1101a0f976f3c0550a11a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683525/large-50d4606ab3e144bd8db4fd95f0ce30d3.jpg","alt":"wildlife_control_live_crowd_eric_hwang_horizontal.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683525/preview-abe7235d88bd7fbe2c98cece8ec1f0e0.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683526/large-1b263eb592c48c428ac43c16426a9958.jpg","alt":"wildlife_control_live_eric_hwang_horizontal.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/683526/preview-630f5eab5f53be088dcbf01e8ee472f5.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Wildlife Control:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2f2Bf7TxY9xWWbTETxtPnP?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Grammy-nominated musician and producer, <a href=\"https://wildlifectrl.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wildlife Control</strong></a> (they/them), records and tours solo, duo, and with collaborators globally. They helped establish the New York shimmer pop sound in the early 2010s with their critically acclaimed eponymous debut album, which was the #1 self-released album on the <strong>NACC/CMJ</strong> <strong>Radio 200</strong> chart. The artist has sold out headlining shows at <strong>Mercury Lounge</strong> in New York City and <strong>Bottom of the Hill</strong> in San Francisco and played featured slots at <strong>SXSW</strong>, <strong>Bottlerock</strong>, and the <strong>CMJ</strong> <strong>Music</strong> <strong>Marathon</strong>. Wildlife Control’s innovative videos have garnered praise from <strong>WIRED</strong> and comparisons to groups like <strong>OK Go</strong> and <strong>Arcade</strong> <strong>Fire</strong>. Combining their indie rock sound with time-lapse and stop motion photography, the music video for the artist’s debut single “<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=boGyFAYomBo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Analog or Digital</strong></a>” went viral with over 500k views."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/boGyFAYomBo","height":""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Press Quotes:"},{"t":"p","html":"“Beauty and poetry in harmony and chords.” <strong>– WIRED</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"“Wildlife Control is back with a vengeance, steering listeners to a supersonic drive with the newest single, Make Me Feel.” <strong>– V13</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"“Wildlife Control masterfully blends pop, rock, and electronic music” <strong>– EARMILK</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"“Wildlife Control is youthful yet insightful. It feels like lying by a pool you broke into, young and drunk, next to someone you loved while looking at the stars knowing in your heart the world has a f*** ton more in store for you.” <strong>– VICE</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Wildlife Control!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/WcjUrJg9t4s?si=isxt7w5abjqGIW5J","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://wildlifectrl.com/","img":"","title":"Dream Dream Dream My Friend. Out July 12. Wildlife Control blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: it doesnʼt matter if sheʼs analog or digital.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCL3hF3eJdMBBvEnLLquputA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/wildlifecontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/wildlifecontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"340660","title":"Nikki Hayes Unveils Soulful New Single \"Above Trees\"","date":"2024-09-18","lead":"Nikki Hayes returns with an evocative R&B track, blending ethereal sounds with deep, soulful vocals.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/340660/5c9979d5c3a3289e19651c3f3c0798be.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Nikki Hayes returns with an evocative R&amp;B track, blending ethereal sounds with deep, soulful vocals."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3K4WGLDhgiStEJTd5jLefN?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"GILBERT, AZ (September 18, 2024) – Rising R&amp;B star <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5dKJEPrnjpRDw8mbH74rtS?si=0KodE414Qkq7aED2KOHX1A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Nikki Hayes</strong></a>&nbsp;just released her highly anticipated single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5amFYUN4OCiPyd4jpwxF1b?si=WqhOLJNHTUiJLT5CFU65jg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Above Trees</strong></a>,” an introspective love song she wrote from a place of self-love and acceptance."},{"t":"p","html":"Showcasing Nikki’s signature blend of heartfelt lyrics and enchanting vocals, the captivating new track draws inspiration from R&amp;B greats like <strong>Beyoncé</strong>, <strong>Stevie Wonder</strong>, and <strong>Toni Braxton</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Functioning as a love song to herself, Nikki shared that, “Above Trees” is <em>“about remembering what my love feels like — from giving my love to myself to receiving it unconditionally and openly.”</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681125/large-fd8ba4ab5f749be9442326a149a0343f.jpg","alt":"Photo credit: Deshaun Matthews"},{"t":"quote","html":"“It’s a song where I could say everything I’ve wanted to say, and hear everything I’ve wanted to hear. When we give ourselves our love, we learn that every bit of love comes from within — whether for ourselves, another person, or anything else.”","cite":"- Nikki Hayes on “Above Trees”"},{"t":"p","html":"Offering a soothing and introspective journey for listeners, the track invites exploration into themes of comfort, healing, and personal growth. With ethereal production from <strong>Joe Capo Kent</strong> and influences from artists like <strong>Daniel Caesar</strong> and <strong>D4VD</strong>, the song encapsulates Nikki’s journey of self-discovery and resilience through its powerful narrative and vocals."},{"t":"h3","html":"“ABOVE TREES” LYRICS (SNEAK PEAK)"},{"t":"p","html":"Let me take care of you"},{"t":"p","html":"Till I fill all the air of you"},{"t":"p","html":"I know that it’s law to love you"},{"t":"p","html":"And no one can take it from you"},{"t":"p","html":"&nbsp;&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"I could write you a love song every day"},{"t":"p","html":"I could rest in your face"},{"t":"p","html":"I could drown in your ways"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>About Nikki Hayes:</strong>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5dKJEPrnjpRDw8mbH74rtS?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Chicago-born <a href=\"https://itsnikkihayes.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Nikki Hayes</strong></a> has made a significant mark in the modern R&amp;B scene with her enchanting voice and fearless dedication. Her journey started at <strong>Studio One Dance Chicago</strong> at six years old and evolved through her acceptance into the iconic <strong>Walt Whitman</strong><strong>&nbsp;&amp; t</strong><strong>he Soul Children of Chicago</strong>. Over the years, Nikki has worked with Grammy-winning artists and producers, and her covers and singles have earned critical acclaim and industry recognition."},{"t":"p","html":"Nikki’s debut solo single in 2016, “<strong>Chance of Rain</strong>,” led to collaborations with prominent figures such as <strong>Vic Mensa</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Malik Yusef</strong> and <strong>Ye Ali</strong>. Her eclectic repertoire, including tracks like the award-nominated “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4fy1dwT3qobTsGKCo1Hp95?si=mOrANxOIT3O03LazBAxFew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Move</strong></a>,” has garnered praise from various media outlets and secured placements in popular TV shows like <strong>CW-TV’s “</strong>​​​​<strong>All American”</strong> and <strong>ABC-TV’s “For Life.”</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Currently based in Arizona, Nikki continues to captivate audiences with her soulful and dynamic sound. Her latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5amFYUN4OCiPyd4jpwxF1b?si=jUgwEWfhTE-udqDPwEHgzQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Above Trees</strong></a>,” is a testament to her artistic growth and unwavering commitment to authenticity."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Nikki!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/yyUZRqWK1xA","height":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/C8pJz8fpI-O/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/itsnikkihayes/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@ItsNikkiHayes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@NikkiHayes1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ItsNikkiHayes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://itsnikkihayes.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"346890","title":"Read More","date":"2024-09-13","lead":"Recent release, \"Jungle,\" now comes with an accompanying music video.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/346890/8a08003784cf05c87e937ee4b54d2687.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Recent release, \"Jungle,\" now comes with an accompanying music video."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3ct9nbH47N3YXwcuM1xTOJ?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"WEST PALM BEACH, FL (September 13, 2024) – Singer-songwriter and beat-maker <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/samarinsilence/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Samar in Silence</strong></a> unleashes her most personal and emotionally charged single yet, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3QAZMFMHXxgH1bjCRibQpK?si=zaN2z6TaQYKgB2LbSWNIKw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Burden</strong></a>.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Pulling listeners into the raw emotions of betrayal and heartbreak, this track explores the profound pain of discovering that a person you deeply cared for felt burdened by you all along. \"Burden\" is a haunting reflection on the deep pain of misplaced trust, and the heartache of discovering the truth too late."},{"t":"button","href":"https://on.soundcloud.com/VRGyg8xeMZyVh3gy8","label":"Listen to \"Burden\"","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\" 'Burden' is the most personal song I've written so far, and it's the foundation of my upcoming album,\"</em> Samar shares, <em>\"I created it two years ago when I was going through an incredibly tough situation with a friend. This person portrayed themselves as a safe space — someone I could confide in who made me feel truly cared for. Out of nowhere, they told me that I was a burden to them. That moment shook me to my core. It was as if everything I thought I knew about our relationship was turned upside down, leaving me reeling.\"</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Writing \"Burden\" was difficult for Samar, grappling with the emotional storm that followed this betrayal, delving into the weight of unspoken truths and the emotional scars carried. Alone in her room, she crafted a raw and visceral beat that matched the intensity of her feelings, the lyrics flowing from a place of deep hurt and confusion, but also from a desperate need to express the pain she was experiencing.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681881/large-15d6ae2c03ef8500e335dfe578e37de9.jpg","alt":"Samar In Silence - BURDEN_2523 Ron Darwish.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681881/preview-30be7f90ea12c0342c4b73f434e75b87.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681882/large-99eef66224eb31ff8519cf467f9af881.jpeg","alt":"Samar In Silence - BURDEN_2316 lighter Ron Darwish.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681882/preview-05f6f5e55021fbbd04855d76b54e56ce.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681890/large-a73b2de34b873bcc93cd7844698b5c4e.png","alt":"Samar In Silence - BURDEN_Cover_Art Ron Darwish.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681890/preview-7ca8f513b4fa3ac5c0cc24bd86281336.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681885/large-22f381d7ea16123ec1d314c2f7f6c8f8.jpg","alt":"Samar In Silence - BURDEN_2700 Ron Darwish.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681885/preview-95a99023089b5a6d7986143fab86c9fa.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681886/large-328d7e4939e2eca9f3c440a931b2fcd3.jpg","alt":"Samar In Silence-Jungle1 Ron Darwish.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681886/preview-f98603eb9c7d7116b71296ff5f497ad4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681884/large-f02539e443425b55d259c240890176e6.jpeg","alt":"Samar In Silence - AA-01 Ron Darwish.JPEG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681884/preview-433c1ec67892a9a46caa0372163d1691.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681888/large-570d58540e15811312087645bee5980d.jpeg","alt":"Samar In Silence - AA-03 Ron Darwish.JPEG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681888/preview-17289507337c63715dc10e15b33bc3d7.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681883/large-14e3d9082f95c4c845c9ff591908132f.jpeg","alt":"Samar In Silence - AA-34 Ron Darwish.JPEG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681883/preview-dc636502c56b2342c04df29f8870f7a6.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681887/large-da70c445643732987a59504525fa8e8d.jpeg","alt":"Samar In Silence - AA-40 Ron Darwish.JPEG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681887/preview-56b2a12f1d8808a3a53637f84a969dc5.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681889/large-96991a788895437be087f98c0dd964d0.jpg","alt":"Samar In Silence - 7764 Ron Darwish.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/681889/preview-ab39b651a50879791e8ba3f4eaf541a7.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"This song is the cornerstone of Samar's upcoming album because it represents this initial betrayal — the event that set everything in motion."},{"t":"p","html":"Accompanying \"<strong>Burden</strong>\" is Samar's recent release, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1XRi1Lh4iyUtGI4bLFlVX0?si=K3ztBJ01S-Cph53lsu4SYw&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=e351ae7d4e564e09\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Jungle</strong></a>,\" a gripping exploration of the mind's labyrinth, where overthinking and endless loops of thought create a sense of being lost in a mental wilderness. Its visuals immerse viewers in a haunting but beautiful world, perfectly capturing the song's essence and Samar's fight to escape her mind's cyclical nature."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/5nrSaED3Jtc?si=JkK3537UCZzY4_SW","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"The track’s beat, originally conceived by Samar in 2021, reflects a tropical vibe that guided her to its fitting title. What began as an unfinished project evolved into a powerful piece, spurred by a challenge from a close friend and the relentless drive to bring this inner \"jungle\" to life. \"Jungle\" pulls listeners into the very heart of Samar’s chaotic thoughts, offering both a sonic and visual experience that lingers long after the last note fades."},{"t":"p","html":"Both tracks stand as a testament to the resilience found in vulnerability, continuing Samar’s journey through the shadowy landscapes of human emotion. With her signature introspective lyricism and hauntingly evocative beats, Samar channels the raw power of her experiences into tracks that are as heavy as they are healing."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Samar in Silence:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5ClgSkTo0lSYBnojObZ7Ua?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://samarinsilence.com/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Samar in Silence</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>is a dynamic force in the music world, a singer-songwriter, and beat-maker who transforms the stillness of solitude into a powerful sonic experience. Her music emerges from the depths of isolation, creating a sound that breaks through the quiet, revealing raw, unfiltered emotion and truth."},{"t":"p","html":"With a voice that captivates and lyrics that resonate, <strong>Samar in Silence</strong> crafts songs that are deeply felt. Her artistry is a fusion of evocative beats and profound lyrical storytelling, striking chords that echo long after the music fades. Her songwriting process is a deeply introspective journey. Disconnecting from the noise of the world, Samar retreats into silence, where she unravels her thoughts and emotions. Starting with a beat, lyrics, or just a concept, her creative process is fluid and adaptive. Sometimes, the beat comes first, guiding her lyrical expression, and other times, lyrics form the foundation upon which she builds her sonic landscape. At times, she’s driven by a melody that captures the essence of her message, even before the lyrics materialize. This deeply introspective process allows her music to resonate with authenticity and depth."},{"t":"p","html":"Since releasing her debut singles \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6XRaNKq86Gf5NhOMbTsIBg?si=ITjUhVbvTpicJtH5CjkEVQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Energy</strong></a>\" and \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0EiH8PeWkIREk8VRPmnTsd?si=rdlIRK-GQlOZyv3nexdPpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>All I Know</strong></a>\" in 2021, Samar in Silence has continued to evolve her distinctive sound. Her upcoming second album, <strong>'</strong><strong>This Is Not Normal'</strong>, delves into the raw, unfiltered emotions of pain and resilience, navigating the shadows of deep hurt and the fragile flickers of triumph. This album is a haunting exploration of the darkness that lingers within and the relentless struggle to find light in the most shattered places."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Samar in Silence!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C_BLUxkxfuB/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://samarinsilence.com/index.html","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/samarinsilence/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://samarinsilence.com/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://youtube.com/@samarinsilence\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5ClgSkTo0lSYBnojObZ7Ua?si=9sX33fvmQyyDRoZL0FeNvg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/samar-in-silence/1573573849\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Apple Music</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"344954","title":"Aaron Bleiweiss Releases Debut Solo Album 'Twists and Turns'","date":"2024-09-06","lead":"An eclectic fusion of genres inspired by life in New York City.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/344954/c2d3d5fce7d669cad288610a1a0824ea.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An eclectic fusion of genres inspired by life in New York City."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3Z7AfZWh7LYnTauIp1xPOE?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"San Diego, CA (September 6, 2024) - Singer-songwriter<strong>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4wCUNgnbe2VSv6m8Nr51VS?si=6J0cVQKiR5e-3Sdz-5i5iw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Aaron Bleiweiss</a>&nbsp;</strong>just released his highly anticipated debut album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3Z7AfZWh7LYnTauIp1xPOE?si=IpRAljXMS4y5qiJTogtNng\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Twists and Turns</em></strong></a>. This collection of 11 tracks takes listeners on a sonic journey through New York via an eclectic array of genres, from funky grooves and catchy pop to intimate singer-songwriter moments and even a little bluegrass."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Twists and Turns</em> is the result of a five-year labor of love that began with a spark of inspiration in the Catskills and evolved into a deeply personal and diverse album. Aaron, a seasoned guitarist and performer, is no stranger to the music world. After years of touring with various bands, he embarked on a solo journey, driven by a desire to explore his creative potential."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656076/large-5c39fe2fff1e9d0705ba41b8227003f1.jpg","alt":"Cover Art for 'Twists and Turns'"},{"t":"quote","html":"“If you sit down and listen to the entire album from start to finish, you'll have been on a journey through so many different styles and genres. I think that’s one of the things I love most about it.\"","cite":"- Aaron Bleiweiss"},{"t":"p","html":"The album captures the essence of Bleiweiss' experiences during his years in New York City, where he found inspiration in the city's vibrant energy and diverse culture. Each track on <em>Twists and Turns</em> represents a different facet of his journey, reflecting personal experiences, emotional highs and lows, and moments of self-discovery."},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, the album showcases Bleiweiss' versatility, featuring guitar-driven melodies, warm layered background vocals, a full horn section, standout keys and synths, and contributions from a host of talented musicians. Tracks like \"<strong>Breathe</strong>,\" a deeply personal song written in memory of a close friend, highlight the emotional depth and authenticity that Bleiweiss brings to his music."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/50xgOjVAwzbs6WsanQSa2B?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"I lost my dear friend Brian to cancer while working on the album. We were inseparable growing up but drifted apart after college. We reconnected during his battle, and I flew to Washington to be with him before he passed. One day, I brought my guitar and played for him. Though he couldn’t speak, he listened, and that’s when 'Breathe' began to take shape. It’s the most personal, emotional track on the album, and every time I hear it, I think of the memories we shared.\"</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>\"Breathe\" [LYRICS SNIPPET]</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"How we got here it’s hard"},{"t":"p","html":"It’s so hard to explain"},{"t":"p","html":"Why this happened to you"},{"t":"p","html":"And why this happened today"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by<strong>&nbsp;Anthony Smith</strong> and Aaron Bleiweiss, <em>Twists and Turns</em> offers a rich, textured listening experience. The album's tracks are deeply personal, yet universally relatable, offering a narrative of self-discovery and resilience. Bleiweiss’ music, influenced by artists such as <strong>Stevie Wonder, Jamiroquai, Talking Heads, Chili Peppers, and Led Zeppelin</strong>, transcends traditional genre boundaries, creating a tapestry of sound that is as complex as the experiences that inspired it."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4wCUNgnbe2VSv6m8Nr51VS?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Aaron Bleiweiss:"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654631/large-e625422aeff46742061399a574e72edb.jpeg","alt":"HVUvAKiY.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654631/preview-fc3eafcb7eec7356999966d77b5de14a.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654628/large-1e260b927f85ee021a8ae8f0de282884.jpeg","alt":"8gUKCCfB.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654628/preview-b9513cbf17e58026d7c6af3915075e2b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654627/large-65b6bf53a9882bc02d76cf05fc8a52c7.jpeg","alt":"Mjf4Kcsm.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654627/preview-c1367f762e79024ed896dffa54b934fc.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654632/large-414f3cfb15248915905c45663dd59d20.jpeg","alt":"P81ofwOn.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654632/preview-9a21e8b7fa98cbed19e3720ccc8e4013.jpeg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4wCUNgnbe2VSv6m8Nr51VS?si=CV-GaCrrQOiA7kHdpsyTLQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aaron Bleiweiss</strong></a> is a guitarist, producer, and singer/songwriter currently based in San Diego, CA. By fusing guitar-heavy funk rock with soulful pop and blues, he creates a classic sound that pays homage to the past while still sounding vital and edgy in the modern world.<br><br>A native of Seattle, WA, Aaron was naturally drawn to the grunge and alternative rock that the Pacific Northwest is famous for. When he moved to Los Angeles to attend the&nbsp;<strong>Musician’s Institute</strong>, he developed an ear for the vintage soul and blues music that would define his style as a guitarist. After graduating, he toured the US, spending several years on the road before settling down in Brooklyn to pursue a solo career. The diversity and electric energy of New York can be clearly heard in Aaron’s solo work.&nbsp;<br><br>Working as a solo artist for the first time, he is confident yet introspective, as he expresses his thoughts about the journey life has taken him on. Entitled <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3Z7AfZWh7LYnTauIp1xPOE?si=IpRAljXMS4y5qiJTogtNng\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Twists and Turns</em></strong></a>, Aaron’s new album invites listeners on a journey through the winding paths and unexpected detours of life."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Aaron!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/XfMG6cZniVw?si=awB1Q0HZqVJejEjw","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C9qJdmXy5os/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/AaronBleiweissMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/aaronbleiweiss/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCPRg9gQgI0pSE5Qw2LuAzpw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"342991","title":"Keep for Cheap Drops Sophomore Album, 'Big Grass'","date":"2024-08-29","lead":"Celebrating its creative independence, the band releases its final album single, \"Life is Like This.\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/342991/fa98bdc2d016a030e725c76a4493764a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Celebrating its creative independence, the band releases its final album single, \"Life is Like This.\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6yrHgckJqvHouOR6QJBoc0?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Minneapolis, MN (August 29, 2024) - Step into <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6YKwoZUW4g50TuiyvVz7JR?si=cijLLPvETaWSNEMJx08XJA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Keep for Cheap</strong></a>’s cinematic universe with <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6yrHgckJqvHouOR6QJBoc0?si=jEALXY0bQXupZiZyGXc71Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Big Grass</em></strong></a> – the Midwest band’s highly anticipated sophomore album, released today. The jumping nine-track \"prairie-rock\" record is a beautiful gift born from the band's newfound independence, taking the reins of their craft to completely own this sonic space."},{"t":"button","href":"https://recordu.lnk.to/Life_Is_Like_This","label":"Listen to \"Life is Like This\"","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"We took control of our sound in Big Grass and it's some of our favorite music we’ve ever made.","cite":"- Keep For Cheap"},{"t":"p","html":"As the third and final single off <em>Big Grass</em>, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/14q45apErIXytTtwrSRcBc?si=517ce713c4bb4104\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Life Is Like This</strong></a>\" strolls along at a steady pace, flashing vignettes of life as someone who's passed early youth but not yet entered late adulthood. The song eventually reaches the destination of a fervent and cyclical chorus that cries the question, <em>“Are we doing our best at reaching to one another?” </em>\"Life Is Like This\" is the final track from the record, serving as the big release, ending in heartthrobs and a yearning for deep connection."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/14q45apErIXytTtwrSRcBc?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>\"Life Is Like this\" Lyrics (SNEAK PEAK)</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Feeling lost in the commotion<br><br>Oh, when you finally feel things changing<br><br>Crawl out of the hole that you’ve aged in<br><br>Everything is new&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676707/large-76fcd8d801018a495430d11301379f8e.jpg","alt":"Cover art for 'Big Grass' by Kate Malanaphy"},{"t":"p","html":"The band's ‘new’ sound is born from its commitment to building its world over the past 5+ years. <em>‘</em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6yrHgckJqvHouOR6QJBoc0?si=jEALXY0bQXupZiZyGXc71Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Big Grass’</em></a> is all the more sensitive, apparent, and jagged. <strong>Keep for Cheap</strong> has arrived home to its classic prairie rock taste – indie rock with country licks and heartfelt melodies teasing evolving youth, queer love and wanting more for humanity.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<u><strong>Big Grass Tracklist:</strong></u>"},{"t":"p","html":"1. <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3R8wiWafUIRMVbsb2daOfd?si=0c9fe8ee5fa842a0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FedEx</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"2. Yours/Mine"},{"t":"p","html":"3. Lakehouse"},{"t":"p","html":"4. Dark"},{"t":"p","html":"5. <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2JW5nHeU5EF3o1U0zF33mf?si=M6soCNRiQ8Wjj_tY4mgHOg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cyberspace</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"6. Talking Mushrooms"},{"t":"p","html":"7. Ski-Doo"},{"t":"p","html":"8. Begging"},{"t":"p","html":"9. Life Is Like This"},{"t":"p","html":"Exploring the complex journey of self-discovery and acceptance through its diverse tracks, the album begins with a yearning for a brighter future with \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3R8wiWafUIRMVbsb2daOfd?si=0c9fe8ee5fa842a0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FedEx</strong></a>,\" and the struggle to balance sharing oneself with others while maintaining individuality on \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1rNU7DuBT0c0e2T4d28DwG?si=63a1c78bc96b441d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Yours/Mine</strong></a>.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Continuing, it delves into the challenges of personal growth with \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5EMwG9OrLamSetmTP9nmDw?si=afbc417554084ea2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lakehouse</strong></a>,\" the dread of an uncertain future in \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0rJWHaHcMbPElcJ7sg4H7e?si=33b2fd3b31ca45c4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dark</strong></a>,\" and existential questioning in \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2JW5nHeU5EF3o1U0zF33mf?si=M6soCNRiQ8Wjj_tY4mgHOg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cyberspace</strong></a>.\" The narrative gradually shifts towards embracing the unknown, finding meaning together, and ultimately, accepting life's complexities and releasing the burden of past pain with \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3nzd68MTYmHWbHJ5V2kHn8?si=89a7e966813f4040\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Talking Mushrooms</strong></a>,\" \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3sf7WnQ47oRzjKqSa4tLQq?si=087e875ec2754e4f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ski-Doo</strong></a>\" and \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3rtA2Av6LksO9Z6t6FEfLd?si=becbfa3203bf4471\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Begging</strong></a>.\" Each track adds a new layer to this emotional journey, blending high-energy moments with introspective ones to reach the culminating track, \"Life Is Like This.\""},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676709/large-d62ab1b58e12453e918c0dfb73d0d5d8.jpg","alt":"LILT final.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676709/preview-f9e940424d33bd61d224be6e2ef98621.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676710/large-b3f7ce4c8ac31c6ee1cd316ee5b83dfc.jpg","alt":"DSC_0332.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676710/preview-1cad680eeaf6f2fccc0e98b138c10952.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676711/large-61c5f32355f7f8aa125681036bd485c6.jpg","alt":"DSC_0372.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676711/preview-95e57f6abd9a5fb52fd909bc304a8435.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676712/large-2620216e8a06079d9b358e198c686b96.jpg","alt":"DSC_0245-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676712/preview-329080f8d5d8139b5a8a437d890f6da5.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Cover art by Kate Malanaphy. Photos by Bethunni Schreiner"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Abe Anderson,</strong> ‘Big Grass’ can be described as a fusion of <strong>Wednesday's</strong> dark, atmospheric vibe with <strong>Sheryl Crow</strong>'s energetic and soulful edge, blended into a sound that features soaring indie rock infused with an alternative twang. This combination is complemented by powerful harmonies that create a rich, dynamic musical experience."},{"t":"p","html":"Many of the themes of the final song are echoed throughout the rest of the record. Written during Keep for Cheap's quarter-life crisis, like a view-master, the album flashes images of childhood passing you by, youthful love and happiness, fleeting nostalgia and feeling stuck in the current."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6YKwoZUW4g50TuiyvVz7JR?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Keep for Cheap:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Keep for Cheap</strong></a>’s special blend of indie, country, rock, and pop has a little something for everyone. Playing what they call “<strong>prairie rock</strong>,” the Minnesota five-piece’s playful sound will make you feel like a kid, then break your heart with its next turn of phrase. The band strives to make music that moves, with driving instrumentals and poignant lyrics. Drawing at times from their own love story, fronting members <strong>Kate Malanaphy</strong> and <strong>Autumn Vagle</strong> write music to make you pine over queer love and passing youth, seek inspiration in the natural world and connection wherever it can be made.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The emotion in their music mainly reflects the lives of songwriters and fronting members of the band, Autumn and Kate who formed a musical connection when they met in the alto section of college choir in 2017. They soon started “<strong>KfC</strong>”, became best friends and are now nearly five years in love, writing alternative country songs reflecting on their lives in Minnesota and the world as they see it. Their special connection brings a vivacious perspective to their music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Keep for Cheap!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/fk5YWkkqnko?si=nb9uwQBfsdhTGEHU","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/C-dQ6lTJcMs/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/keepforcheap?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&amp;igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC75Ms2W7_Q_bfn2cVLhTJ-Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://linktr.ee/keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Linktree</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"339909","title":"Mae Graf is an Indie-Pop musician who is making her debut in 2024. Her music is characterized by passionate melodies and introspective lyrics, which sets her apart- drawing from personal experiences and a wide array of influences.","date":"2024-08-23","lead":"The much-anticipated EP is a full-throttle display of heartfelt music, written and chanted by Mae Graf.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/339909/c7c6f0351e138d9ccc77837171b62ab9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The much-anticipated EP is a full-throttle display of heartfelt music, written and chanted by Mae Graf."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0NiHaSI2tRIT29Fxih2cr0?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Shreveport, LA (August 23, 2024) - Singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7AXxTBw47UcsiM0NzHZSFz?si=q5dcRFSkQ06S-5FuKkk4xg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mae</strong> <strong>Graf</strong></a> unleashes a fresh new EP titled '<a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Living\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Living</strong></a><strong>'</strong> on August 23, 2024. The 9-track EP blends Graf's heartfelt lyrics with her dynamic vocal style, creating a collection that aims to touch listeners' emotions. Every track is distinctive in its fusion of narrative and musicality, highlighting Graf's talent for instantly connecting with listeners."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Living","label":"Listen to \"Living\" on Streaming Platforms!","color":"#ff5656"},{"t":"p","html":"Known for her deep passion for music, Graf has drawn the lyrics from her own thoughts and personal experience and poured her heart into 'Living', taking listeners on a deep dive into the experiences of a free-spirited individual whose intense passion creates a rollercoaster of emotions. It captures the highs and lows of being accepted and betrayal from friendships, the challenges of self-reflection and social anxiety, and the joys of love alongside the heartache that often comes with it."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676399/large-d5cc125dd7d31b7a19a47925ccd6af28.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Living\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5PgtxtxztaRpMhTJOOydsr?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"'Living' EP features Graf's latest release \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0cTO3TX1MQKcYVYTpw3hx4?si=2db20e50d41d4cb2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>What</strong> <strong>abt</strong> <strong>me</strong><strong>?</strong></a>\", and a new take on \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/32PrUWu8mV6xud2WMplIJT?si=6082d1434e194e19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Like Me Better This Way</strong></a>,\" along with 6 new tracks offering a fresh perspective on alternative pop/rock.<br><br>Produced by <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/steelrecordsstudios/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Steel Records Studios</strong></a> and in collaboration with <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/thekyleroop/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Kyle Roop</strong></a> and <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/leifshivelyband/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Leif Shively</strong></a>,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>the catchy beats and storytelling approach is reminiscent of <strong>Taylor Swift</strong>'s narrative style, while Graf's vocal delivery evokes the energy of <strong>Avril Lavigne</strong>'s punk-pop sound. In the 'Living' EP, the songs come together to create an emotional journey that mixes excitement and struggle, showing a vibrant blend of youthful energy, introspection, and the effects of personal growth and connection."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7AXxTBw47UcsiM0NzHZSFz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Mae Graf:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.maegrafmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mae</strong> <strong>Graf</strong></a>’s musical journey is deeply rooted in her upbringing, where writing became her vessel for releasing emotions. From journaling to songwriting, her music reflects raw vulnerability, serving as a microscope into her soul and experiences. With a foundation built on real-life narratives, her emotionally driven melodies resonate with listeners, capturing the essence of human emotions."},{"t":"p","html":"From a young age, Mae was immersed in music, thanks to a nanny who sang and wrote songs with her. As she delved into voice lessons and school performances, her passion for music grew exponentially. Now at 15 and inspired by icons like <strong>Gracie</strong> <strong>Abrams</strong> and <strong>Taylor</strong> <strong>Swift</strong>, Mae’s raspy vocals and storytelling prowess evoke shades of <strong>Avril</strong> <strong>Lavigne</strong> and <strong>Phoebe</strong> <strong>Bridgers</strong>. Her indie-pop sound, characterized by passionate melodies and introspective lyrics, sets her apart, drawing from personal experiences and a wide array of influences. As she continues to evolve creatively, Mae Graf remains dedicated to her craft, aspiring to leave a lasting impact on the music industry.&nbsp;<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Mae!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/lX9FTEczHZs?si=_Vs6NPVMPLLUfK_w","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.maegrafmusic.com/","img":"","title":"Mae Graf is an Indie-Pop musician who is making her debut in 2024. Her music is characterized by passionate melodies and introspective lyrics, which sets her apart- drawing from personal experiences and a wide array of influences.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/maegrafmusic?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&amp;igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@maegrafmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@maegrafmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/people/Mae-Graf/61552522345848/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"343279","title":"Visionaries have a divine obligation in life. A child never chooses their family, circumstances, or fortune at birth. Stephen Thomas a Multi-Genre Artist that's forced to be reckon with. He's the future of the music and entertainment industry. He's outstanding for 2022 and the future to come.","date":"2024-08-23","lead":"The lively track centered on re-discovering happiness is now accompanied by a new music video.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/343279/5447151abc7f86dfb4f31b5a41c25dc8.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The lively track centered on re-discovering happiness is now accompanied by a new music video."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Rc63gZweqAo?si=YwNJWm1oZ4HWnje5","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, (August 23, 2024) - Building on the success of his latest single \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3cqqiH32fFqe2fHfBCXWWP?si=9c217bad7893421a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Back Home</strong></a>,\" released on May 17, genre-defying artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?si=3eTLwFoXTHmGfDSQyx7WjA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a> just released a captivating accompanying music video, exploring the journey of returning to who or what gives you peace, love, and happiness in life."},{"t":"button","href":"https://symphony.to/stephen-thomas/back-home","label":"Listen to \"Back Home\" on Streaming Platforms!","color":"#ff6666"},{"t":"p","html":"Directed by <strong>Will Thomas</strong>, starring Stephen Thomas and introducing <strong>Ava Breeze</strong>, the music video follows the story of a young woman battling serious challenges in life, including losing her job and facing eviction. Finding solace in those closest to her, in this case, her family, the young woman finds her way back home to her place of comfort and strength."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676844/large-3f294e2c231b1a43f3b4255bb87a13a4.webp","alt":"StephenT.webp"},{"t":"quote","html":"We only have one life to live. Fight, WIN, and do it again. You can always run in life but you'll never be able to hide from it. So even when things make you feel different embrace it. Because you'll always find your way back home.","cite":"- Stephen Thomas"},{"t":"p","html":"\"<strong>Back Home</strong>\" reminds listeners that the key to life is being free and that finding your path back home is the way to finding your true self. It's about overcoming life's challenges and knowing that fighting through obstacles always means you've truly won in the end."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3cqqiH32fFqe2fHfBCXWWP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Capturing the attention of both fans and critics alike, the song has earned significant media coverage. Its compelling alt-rock blend led to over 300,000 views on TikTok in under 24 hours, as covered in <a href=\"https://apnews.com/press-release/ein-presswire-newsmatics/social-media-5a223277592aa33e2f768dacd1074e76\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>AP News</strong></a>. <a href=\"https://earmilk.com/2024/06/10/stephen-thomas-soars-to-stardom-with-hit-anthem-back-home/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>EARMILK</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>highlighted Stephen’s 'soaring rise to stardom,' praising the anthem’s infectious energy and emotional depth. His growing influence in the music scene was further emphasized by <a href=\"https://wchsnetwork.com/2024/06/30/charleston-recording-artist-stephen-thomas-gains-popularity-with-new-rock-alternative-record/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>MetroNews</strong></a>, which noted his expanding popularity in the rock-alternative genre among giants like <strong>Metallica</strong>, <strong>Ghost</strong>, <strong>Linkin Park</strong> and <strong>Green Day</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Legendary producer <strong>Billie Lennox (</strong><strong>Beyoncé, Michael Jackson, The Notorious B.I.G., Lil' Kim)</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>praised Stephen for the song's quality and ability to switch genres, <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/story.php?story_fbid=10229958891249788&amp;id=1035146481&amp;mibextid=xfxF2i&amp;rdid=Lgv9JWzTt2OIrlay\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">sharing it on social media</a>. The<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.timeswv.com/news/life/mountain-state-artist-builds-following-with-new-single-back-home/article_676dcd8c-33ed-11ef-9068-2f28418b1d06.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Times West Virginian</strong></a> recognized Stephen’s ability to build a dedicated following with <em>Back Home</em>, noting his success and attributing the song's reception to its simple, yet deeply relatable message. <a href=\"https://voyagela.com/interview/check-out-stephen-thomass-story\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>VoyageLA</strong></a> delved deeper into his personal and artistic journey. Stephen’s appearance on <a href=\"https://www.wvmetronewstv.com/videos/charleston-musician-stephen-thomas-joins-the-show\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hoppy Kercheval’s Talkline</strong></a> provided further insight into his burgeoning career, solidifying his place as a rising star in the industry."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>\"Back Home\" Lyrics (SNIPPET)</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"We got one life to live&nbsp;<br><br>Its time to settle the score&nbsp;<br><br>Life can make you break&nbsp;<br><br>You gotta love it some more<br>&nbsp;<br>You gotta find your way back home"},{"t":"p","html":"Stephen, a multi-genre artist spanning hip-hop to R&amp;B, pop, rock and more, leans fully into alt-rock on this track, featuring edgy sounds reminiscent of <strong>MGK</strong>, <strong>YungBlud</strong>, and <strong>Travis</strong> <strong>Scott&nbsp;</strong>while delivering a powerful message similar to <strong>JellyRoll</strong>'s style. Resonating with a wide audience, but still carving its own unique path, the song stands out as authentic and perfectly unexpected."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4uJ7lJXHmrGMuyIzHcjXbY?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Stephen Thomas:"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/676846/large-55a595b43551877ff75bb9984341f332.jpg","alt":"Photo by Josh Hanna"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.stephentmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephen Thomas</strong></a>, a versatile Universal Artist whose musical odyssey has taken him from Charleston, West Virginia to the forefront of the industry. With a dynamic career marked by exploration and evolution, Stephen has recently embarked on a thrilling journey into the realms of rock and alternative music, infusing his sound with raw, authentic vibes that resonate deeply with audiences.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"As a national touring recording artist, Stephen's talent has garnered widespread acclaim, earning him five <strong>Grammy Award</strong> considerations as an independent artist. From his early beginnings to signing with <strong>SkeeloMusik</strong> / <strong>Sony RED</strong> in 2013 and eventually finding his artistic home with <strong>Creative Hearts Entertainment</strong>, Stephen's journey has been one of constant growth and discovery."},{"t":"p","html":"Stephen's impact transcends mere accolades, with his interviews featured in prestigious publications such as <strong>MTV</strong>, <strong>Vibe Magazine</strong>, <strong>Hype Magazine</strong>, and <strong>TCT</strong> <strong>Network</strong>. He has graced renowned stages alongside industry icons and walked the red carpet at events like the <strong>2014 BET Live Experience</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Amidst his diverse musical endeavors, Stephen's recent immersion into rock and alternative music has been particularly transformative. Embracing the genre's edgy, rebellious spirit, Stephen has honed his craft, crafting songs that pulsate with raw emotion and electrifying energy. His single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4IJY700TPZXKlrkO0mR4zM?si=Q_xjis9iTtyfjYRfshMH5g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Best Days</strong></a>,\" soared to #2 on the iTunes Charts, standing as a testament to his artistic versatility and widespread appeal. Meanwhile, his music video for \"<a href=\"https://youtu.be/wj8FAEyFpRA?feature=shared\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Search Me</strong></a>\" received global recognition, earning placement on <strong>RevoltTV</strong> and reaching millions worldwide. Stephen's music is now readily available on all streaming platforms, inviting listeners to embark on a sonic journey filled with rock and alternative vibes."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephen!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Lp3O6H8EBSM?si=qOQ9Ppm4CM8C9X86","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.stephentmusic.com/","img":"","title":"Visionaries have a divine obligation in life. A child never chooses their family, circumstances, or fortune at birth. Stephen Thomas a Multi-Genre Artist that's forced to be reckon with. He's the future of the music and entertainment industry. He's outstanding for 2022 and the future to come.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.stephentmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a> <strong>|</strong> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/StephenTMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/StephenThomas1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://x.com/stephentmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>X</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"335691","title":"Read More","date":"2024-08-20","lead":"The first album in the ambitious quest to record original songs for each national park features music by legendary artists Ry Cooder, Animal Collective, and Rising Appalachia — rallying around the one thing we can all agree on, Our National Parks: places of wonder.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/335691/9290cb5dca286c71dcf82df06d505e2c.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The first album in the ambitious quest to record original songs for each national park features music by legendary artists Ry Cooder, Animal Collective, and Rising Appalachia — rallying around the one thing we can all agree on, Our National Parks: places of wonder."},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.thenationalparkalbum.com/songs","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>National Parks, United States (August 20, 2024)</strong> - \"<a href=\"https://www.thenationalparkalbum.com/songs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The National Park Album</strong></a>\" is a unique collection of 15 original songs from a diverse set of talented and accomplished artists, with each track retelling histories and stories of parks that have captivated us throughout our lives. A hymn to an America of no division, this album not only showcases the stunning landscapes that define our nation, but also highlights the shared experiences and emotions that these natural wonders inspire in all of us."},{"t":"p","html":"Spearheaded by <strong>Fredrik Colting</strong>, a writer in awe of the unique concept of our National Parks, sets out on a cultural mission to capture the original meaning of all the U.S. national parks — wild, beautiful places that connect us with nature and our true selves."},{"t":"button","href":"https://music.apple.com/au/album/the-national-park-album/1763842095","label":"Listen to \"The National Park\" on Apple Music","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Two things that unite us as humans are our love for music and nature. I wanted to be part of creating an album that celebrated this connection in a time when we should be reminded of what unites us, rather than what divides us.”","cite":"- Fredrik Colting"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668879/large-e115e91a9df35acb012b5d787cea06d1.png","alt":"TheNationalParkAlbum_TitleArt.png"},{"t":"p","html":"<em><strong>Volume I</strong></em> is a collection of 15 original songs with each telling of fascinating park histories, from the visual spectacle of the <strong>Yosemite Firefall</strong>, the humble source of the <strong>Grand Canyon</strong>, to the harrowing 37 days of survival of <strong>Truman Everts</strong> in Yellowstone."},{"t":"p","html":"The \"National Park Album\" is available for streaming on all platforms on August 20, 2024. <strong>100% of profits go to support the parks.</strong> Limited edition vinyl sets can be purchased at <strong>Urban Outfitters</strong>, <strong>Huckberry</strong>, <strong>The Parks Project</strong> and <a href=\"https://www.thenationalparkalbum.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>thenationalparkalbum.com</strong></a>."},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.thenationalparkalbum.com/","label":"SUPPORT THE PARKS","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668015/-3a4d5984cb21867782986aae224683ea.gif","alt":"TNPA_Giftbox_AllProducts.gif"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Artists &amp; National Parks:"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668878/large-0c115030bbcc5d2f859dbe548fc5d0ac.jpg","alt":"Lead by Fredrick Colting"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong>In support of/ Supported by:</strong><strong><br></strong><br>- The National Park Service<br>- National Park Stores across the U.S.<br>- The Parks Project<br>- Huckberry<strong><em><br></em></strong>- REI<br>- Trader Joes"},{"t":"list","items":[]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"The Stories:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>America’s Best Idea&nbsp;</strong>(The National Parks)<br>Artist: <strong>David Karsten Daniels</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"The<strong>&nbsp;US National Parks</strong> have often been referred to as <em>“America’s Best Idea”</em> and they came about in a time when people increasingly were living in big cities, with hectic lives and busy minds. Heading into nature to heal from this daily bombardment of stresses carries an even greater weight today."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/40GxtoOMHs0ux7Wfs3C8Ob?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>The Edge of the Sea&nbsp;</strong>(Acadia)<br>Artist: <strong>Jessica Allossery</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Cadillac Mountain</strong> in <strong>Acadia National Park</strong> sits on the edge of the wild sea. This most Eastern point on the US mainland is where the day begins, quite literally, claiming the first official daylight."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6wTp3r9LUKOQctseIoIq1W?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>A Drop of Water&nbsp;</strong>(Grand Canyon)<br>Artist: <strong>Joseph DeNatale</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"It’s crazy to think that what begins as a drop of water in<strong>&nbsp;La Poudre Pass</strong> has, over thousands of years, carved the gigantic <strong>Grand Canyon</strong>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2RUc697ynBhe0NGow1eDda?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lady</strong><strong>&nbsp;Bird&nbsp;</strong>(Rocky Mountain)<br>Artist: <strong>Stefanie Joyce</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lady Isabella Bird</strong> was a trailblazing female explorer who traveled the world in search of adventure. In Colorado National Park, she hired local guide “<strong>Mountain Jim</strong>” to help her climb <strong>Long’s Peak</strong>. He was a ruffian and a killer, his face pockmarked from a fight with a bear, but he quoted poetry and Lady Bird fell in love."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3CJqcROIuvaZDEyxPN6woq?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Desert Eyes&nbsp;</strong>(Arches)<br>Artist: <strong>Jacob Montague &amp; John Brazell</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Sandstone</strong> arches dot the landscape as if creations in a Dali painting. These desert eyes are created from degrading rock over thousands of years and will eventually be destroyed by the same natural forces. This song is about this eternal yin/yang we see in nature, and within ourselves."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6qksqLoiirWNruxK1Xs3Xr?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Roadrunner&nbsp;</strong>(Joshua Tree)<br>Artist: <strong>Lynz&nbsp;</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"A <strong>Joshua Tree</strong> experiences from the view of a Roadrunner."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Congaree</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Artist: <strong>Animal Collective</strong>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4kwxTgCKMipBKhSnEstNKj?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Hyperion&nbsp;</strong>(Redwood)<br>Artist: <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/user/1176594662?si=9f4ce2460a9446b3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>James Worton</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"This is the tale about the actual tallest tree in the world. These giant redwood trees are an astonishing several thousands of years old and have literally seen the birth of America, standing tall and silent like wise, noble giants."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3I6e2ZqqoxQhXc9z7Tp5ci?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>The Wisdom of the Smoke&nbsp;</strong>(Great Smoky Mountain)<br>Artist: <strong>Rising Appalachia</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by the Appalachian culture this song begins with an old tale about the native Americans in the region and how they foresaw the coming persecution. According to legend a mountain opened up and offered to keep them safe inside. While half of the tribe hesitated and remained outside, the other half accepted the shelter. Ever since you can hear their laughter through the mountain.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6oNjc1vDfIcujBvJ0Bv3a1?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Stone Face&nbsp;</strong>(Bryce Canyon)<br>Artist: <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/user/t0qq54l59g1hyts7o7xlrnnsq?si=02bfaf38380f4091\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Josh Gold</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;ft. Crushboys</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"The <strong>Paiute</strong> people who occupied <strong>Bryce Canyon</strong> as early as 1200 A.D., considered the hoodoo rock towers to be the petrified remains of ancient beings that were turned into rocks by the Coyote, as a way to pay for their sins."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>37 Days in Wonderland&nbsp;</strong>(Yellowstone)<strong><br></strong>Artist: <strong>Jeff Kightly</strong>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5AbWowYbvVPmxHSeZmk5wP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Based on the true story of <strong>Truman Everts</strong> who was part of the first Presidential expedition sent to explore “Wonderland” as Yellowstone was called back then. He strayed from the pack and was suddenly lost and survived 37 days before being found, starving, burnt by geysers, and barely alive. Today, a plant that kept him alive bears his name."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>The Promised Land&nbsp;</strong>(Zion)<br>Artist: <strong>Jerry Popei&nbsp;</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Zion</strong> is like a <strong>Garden of Eden</strong> situated amid a harsh, desert landscape. The first Westerners that arrived there had to travel through this hot desert and when they entered the valley, nearly dead from dehydration, with streams and lush grass and trees, they named it Zion after the promised land in the Bible."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5H7KSTTsoonNLiC2oDLHqM?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Gods’ Land&nbsp;</strong>(Olympic)<br>Artist: <strong>Allison Preisinger</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"One thing about our National Parks, besides their grandeur and beauty, is the peril of visiting. Every year people venture into the wilderness of the parks, never to return. <strong>Olympic National Park</strong> history is filled with these mysterious disappearances, perhaps, as this song explores, due to the fickleness of the Gods."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>As Long as It Is Wild&nbsp;</strong>(Yosemite)<br>Artist: <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/user/matalgrif?si=461184a65b814617\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Matt Griffith</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"Based on the writings of <strong>John Muir</strong>, AKA \"<strong>The Father of Our National Parks</strong>,\" it begins with a description of the Firefall, which is what the waterfall looks like a day once every couple of years when the sun hits it just right and makes it radiate like glowing embers. Back in the 60s, the resort hotel in the park wanted a way to recreate this every night and dumped a barrel of glowing coals over the ledge of the mountain, creating a similar visual spectacle –<em>&nbsp;“Let the fire fall!”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lava Beds&nbsp;</strong>(Lava Beds)<br>Artist: <strong>Ry Cooder</strong>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1CPwHx5lgVxv0rfcp7UXLx?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Entering another world is as easy as getting out of your <strong>Tesla</strong> and stepping into one of the many extraordinary lava tubes. Over the last half-million years, volcanic eruptions on the <strong>Medicine Lake</strong> shield volcano have created a rugged landscape dotted with more than 800 caves that burrow towards the center of the earth."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.thenationalparkalbum.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.thenationalparkalbum.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"mailto:hello@thenationalparkalbum.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Contact The National Parks</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"336222","title":"Jesse Pringle Returns to the Ring At BFKC Fight Night in Kansas City","date":"2024-08-16","lead":"The Kill Em All actor makes a fierce comeback as a debut fighter at BFKC.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/336222/822a5ec537ab16640c84fbfdbedc7c9d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The <strong>Kill Em All</strong> actor makes a fierce comeback as a debut fighter at BFKC."},{"t":"p","html":"Kansas City, KS (August 16, 2024) - Singer-actor <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7MoXGvcoHJn9bnaWSVHSo1?si=BERvQbZaRn6ps7ESKmytEg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Jesse</strong> <strong>Pringle</strong></a> is poised to prove his athletic prowess in a showdown against <strong>Devon Schwan</strong> at the <a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/bkfc-fight-night-kansas-city-tickets-944187469137?aff=PRINGLE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>BFKC Fight Night</strong></a>, held in <strong>Memorial</strong> <strong>Hall</strong>, Kansas City on <strong>August 16, 2024, Friday,&nbsp;</strong>at<strong>&nbsp;8:00 PM EDT</strong>. Pringle will be debuting in the main event of Bare Knuckle Fighting Championship's Cruiserweight division, along with welterweight contenders <strong>Jake</strong> \"<strong>The Gypsy\" Lindsey</strong> and <strong>Elvin \"El Bandido\" Brito</strong>."},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/bkfc-fight-night-kansas-city-tickets-944187469137?aff=PRINGLE","label":"Get your tickets HERE!","color":"#ff4d4d"},{"t":"p","html":"After achieving success in the film industry as a screenwriter, producer, and actor, Pringle now enters the BFKC with gloves off (literally!), having previously showcased his talents as a singer on the same stage."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668894/compressed_original-6f9bcd1c487dfba2603f363fdc7cc954.jpg","alt":"Poster of Pringle VS Schwan at BKFC Fight Night"},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/bkfc-fight-night-kansas-city-tickets-944187469137?aff=PRINGLE","label":"Get your tickets HERE!","color":"#ff4d4d"},{"t":"h3","html":"Event Details:"},{"t":"p","html":"Pringle VS Schwan at BFKC Fight Night: Kansas City<br>Friday, August 16, 8:00 EDT<br>Memorial Hall<br>600 North 7th Street Trafficway Kansas City, KS 66101"},{"t":"p","html":"Tickets Available:<br>VIP Table Seating (Must buy 10) - $200.00 + Taxes &amp; Fees<br>Premium Lower Bowl - $75.00 + Taxes &amp; Fees<br>General Lower Bowl - $45.00 + Taxes &amp; Fees"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668898/large-2e8af68380bec1884d437555dafec1b3.jpg","alt":"IMG_2232 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668898/preview-8826202c20deaa5921289a020f4e6a7b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668899/large-b05409ecbc2c11d3ae04355264eba6b4.jpg","alt":"IMG_2231 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668899/preview-6e2701176016abcf859591bdb3b7b336.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668896/large-6925b3694a9cc7169e9e347d7c2404de.jpg","alt":"IMG_4840 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668896/preview-46dfcf02387721983cc049d13ef5a5e4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668897/large-58db97ddd97a682bd737448ce7953425.jpg","alt":"IMG_4753 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668897/preview-fe62a2472a5cd2af7e010fb23617659d.jpg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Jesse Pringle:"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668900/large-37b7d2730f0da4fc5f2a65b060616616.jpg","alt":"Jesse Pringle.jpg"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Jesse!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7MoXGvcoHJn9bnaWSVHSo1?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/jessepringlellc/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/thejessepringle\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UChT_KkvoC9c5tFM259GV2_g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"335535","title":"Ray Hou Debuts 'I Wake And Remember' EP","date":"2024-08-09","lead":"'I Wake And Remember' tells a cinematic story of resilience in the face of losing memories to the passage of time.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/335535/d2e5bfc8b9d29dba81fa4a90409eb639.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"'I Wake And Remember' tells a cinematic story of resilience in the face of losing memories to the passage of time."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/-IJU-jXHJG8?si=8incgKJCg1KWr7hh","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"The music video follows a charming figurine in its past life as it tries to piece together fragmented memories."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3kQBCMom66qPl5EUt33WlH?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Chicago, IL (August 9, 2024) - Originating from Taiwan, international singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/19A8GRUBh001nRwAaOuoe2?si=4q80gqenQi2qfmfU5iZGTA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ray</strong> <strong>Hou</strong></a>&nbsp;drops his debut EP, '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3kQBCMom66qPl5EUt33WlH?si=7aCNzR-BTwat6ZBnozmmQw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Wake And Remember</strong></a>,' on August 9, 2024. Masterfully written and produced by Ray, 'I Wake And Remember' seeks to capture an unyielding determination to resist losing precious memories of someone important, regardless of distance, circumstances, or the passage of time."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This EP is written as if I'm scoring a film. I hope it helps listeners visualize, or bring back memories that they think have been lost forever.”","cite":"- Ray Hou, Singer-songwriter"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667733/large-6f7fae0ab524e0f895e847698ed21d5c.webp","alt":"Cover art for \"I Wake And Remember\" EP"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>'I Wake And Remember'</strong> EP has 4 tracks, showcasing Ray's innate profession as a film composer, blending delicate vocals with cinematic elements. Through these sounds, Ray attempts to create a visualization of physical and emotional distance."},{"t":"p","html":"The first track, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0HKecTDGfsrFfY9rLg6HPU?si=500433ce02664efd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Two Birds</strong></a>,\" portrays the despairing journey of titular characters facing an inevitable separation. Ray incorporates delicately crafted piano and blends vocals ranging from intimate solos to desperate harmonies, illustrating internal desperation against vast external distances."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667887/large-274d49e26f7ff4b31d8bf32697da72c7.jpg","alt":"still_2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667887/preview-90fcce156573f25442674ab2d4950325.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667885/-b96374c85279d4e106e612bbb453436f.jpg","alt":"IMG_7350 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667885/-b96374c85279d4e106e612bbb453436f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667883/large-87ad03cc911f0d919007d2301d763826.jpg","alt":"07072024.Still005.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667883/preview-eb3c341adce6e5c42c7691ee67a14658.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667884/large-06289a5fd7b6ddd0932c534a0a71dd34.jpg","alt":"07072024.Still002.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667884/preview-bb54106fbc6882a73606423f76385b09.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667886/large-49b636a6d0ad22ae0c43c89bd2edc7ea.jpg","alt":"07072024.Still008.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667886/preview-b04b33d3d6b0971ea5f18fa5a3a20f73.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Followed by \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5nNoppLJ8OeIGE0Ltl9ZCy?si=42be479db53044db\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>It's Been So Long</strong></a>\", the song contrasts its preceding half by building a minimalistic sense of rhythm to the similarly harmonically vocalized and warm-toned arrangement. The narrator seeks to return to a forgotten home, having lost touch with himself over years of searching, only to realize that what he whole-heartedly seeks may be right in front of him."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667889/large-5bcf8732b61ab322e97470a65f12363e.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"A Long Distance Song\""},{"t":"p","html":"\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4SRlWBeEXqPIMc19re1Izl?si=2bf6a8c572b14e3c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>A</strong> <strong>Long</strong> <strong>Distance</strong> <strong>Song</strong></a>\" follows Ray's personal experience in a long-distance relationship. The song resonates an unmatched sense of longing and excitement as he travels to see his long-distance girlfriend after a grueling six months, but the wait ultimately proves worthwhile."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4SRlWBeEXqPIMc19re1Izl?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"The final and title track, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eb6O43OUOEKREswzsLViX?si=14603c70b66f48e0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Wake And Remember</strong></a>,\" draws from Ray's personal experience witnessing his grandmother's battle with dementia. It portrays how memories can unexpectedly resurface, evoking either intense euphoria or profound sadness. It is sung with a robotic hue, yet gets emotionally intense as memory crawls back - like an inanimate object coming back to life. The song serves as a testament to the unmatched power and will for the ones we love."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0eb6O43OUOEKREswzsLViX?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Ray's EP showcases dynamics that can be compared to well-known artists like <strong>Wave</strong> <strong>to</strong> <strong>Earth</strong>, <strong>Jacob</strong> <strong>Collier</strong>, <strong>grentperez</strong>, and <strong>Mitski</strong>, whose influences can be felt throughout the project. Although Ray has been involved in the music industry for a while, this is his highly anticipated debut EP as a solo artist and composer—definitely something to watch for!"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I hope this EP calms its listeners, whichever whirlwind they might be going through.”","cite":"- Ray Hou, Singer-songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Ray Hou:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/19A8GRUBh001nRwAaOuoe2?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"As a professional film composer, producer, and singer-songwriter, <a href=\"https://www.rayhoumusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ray</strong> <strong>Hou</strong></a> intends to create music that offers immunity in a fast-paced world. Growing up in Taipei, Taiwan, he spent hours in his family's film composing studio, immersing himself in the relationship between visuals and sound. This environment exposed him to a diverse array of musicians, greatly enhancing his musical versatility. In 2018, Ray began writing songs while building his career composing for advertisements, indie films, and eventually movies and TV shows."},{"t":"p","html":"Now a full-time film composer, producer, and singer-songwriter based in both Taipei and Chicago, Ray has a diverse portfolio that spans indie and commercial projects across Asia, Europe, and the US. In 2023 alone he has made custom music for brands such as <strong>Sony</strong>, <strong>McDonald's,</strong> and <strong>TGI</strong> <strong>Fridays.</strong> His original score for the indie film <strong>A</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Black</strong> <strong>Dog</strong> <strong>by the&nbsp;</strong><strong>Reef</strong> was showcased at the <strong>Berlin</strong> <strong>Film</strong> <strong>Festival.</strong> Ray is also featured in multiple large-scale Movies and TV Shows, including one that broke the national presale box office record in Asia."},{"t":"p","html":"Ray is currently in the process of composing for three undisclosed <strong>Netflix</strong> shows whilst releasing his first EP, '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3kQBCMom66qPl5EUt33WlH?si=6N4NYzs3TsGD8DpcrJyLRQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Wake And Remember</strong></a>,' which attempts to create an auditory sanctuary and portray different angles of visual distance through sound - as the pieces contrast between intimate and grand, warm and cold, the forming and the formless."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668858/large-85cbc781949ed7fba8413f176a921d77.jpg","alt":"SunMorn_20240229＿Ray專輯形象-4824P.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668858/preview-1fc72968458e394326363bb194a8045e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668859/large-39f65839eb83014eada6659b9b468cc1.jpg","alt":"SunMorn_20240229＿Ray專輯形象-4996P.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668859/preview-991fe777a55c8a135db5dad25a815a28.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668860/large-bb5cec40a7099f08c37bc95d8ac98f1b.jpg","alt":"SunMorn_20240229＿Ray專輯形象-5086P.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668860/preview-0fabf3b9d0a9f9a73704dea0a159a7e5.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photo credit Ruby Lai"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Ray Hou!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/rIftxG6an7Q?si=kUlgJcRyBHFI3PYl","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/C4-ZnBwPask/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><a href=\"https://www.rayhoumusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ray.houuuuu?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&amp;igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/19A8GRUBh001nRwAaOuoe2?si=zCGHeYhORXa8NJywkJl3FA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/ray-hou/1498712238\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a></strong>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"338299","title":"Dream Dream Dream My Friend. Out July 12. Wildlife Control blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: it doesnʼt matter if sheʼs analog or digital.","date":"2024-08-09","lead":"The track conveys a message of hope, all with Wildlife Control's unique flair.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/338299/b718beda8d992af6aa138b64daf91803.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The track conveys a message of hope, all with Wildlife Control's unique flair."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3r7B42XASvV248JDxx6hhu?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"New York City, NY (August 9, 2024) - Indie-rock musician <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2f2Bf7TxY9xWWbTETxtPnP?si=Q82Lx29NRUmK-r9C5ILytQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wildlife Control</strong></a> creates an ambient, electronic vibe with his latest beat titled \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3r7B42XASvV248JDxx6hhu?si=290c6b7d4064400e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Your Blood on My Lips</strong></a>,\" released on August 9, 2024.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"\"<strong>Your Blood on My Lips</strong>\" lyrics emerge as a compassionate response to a friend going through depression and trauma, conveying a genuine effort to provide solace and support through kind words, embodying a message of empathy and encouragement with the hope of healing as time goes."},{"t":"p","html":"<u><strong>Lyrics from \"Your Blood on My Lips\" by Wildlife Control</strong></u><strong><br></strong><br><em>But there’s no right or wrong&nbsp;<br>No matter what you do&nbsp;<br>Oh, you’re gonna bring yourself back to you, yeah&nbsp;<br>You’ll bring you back to you</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/670217/large-a5a38eb29ee6f382daeed171a5559944.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Your Blood on My Lips\""},{"t":"p","html":"\"Your Blood on My Lips\" is a mesmerizing blend of synth guitars and an upbeat rhythm that perfectly captures a classic cyberpunk vibe. It brings to mind <strong>a-ha</strong>'s iconic 80s hit \"<strong>Take on Me</strong>,\" but with a modern twist that incorporates Wildlife Control's groovy elements. The result is a truly unique indie-rock experience that transports listeners to nostalgic, airy soundscapes. The combination of these influences creates a sonic journey that is both familiar and fresh, making<strong>&nbsp;\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3r7B42XASvV248JDxx6hhu?si=49ba8a38e665445a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Your Blood on My Lips</strong></a><strong>\"</strong> a must-listen for fans of electronic and alternative music alike."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2f2Bf7TxY9xWWbTETxtPnP?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Wildlife Control:"},{"t":"p","html":"Grammy-nominated musician and producer, <a href=\"https://wildlifectrl.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wildlife Control</strong></a> (they/them), records and tours solo, duo, and with collaborators globally. They helped establish the New York shimmer pop sound in the early 2010s with their critically acclaimed eponymous debut album, which was the #1 self-released album on the <strong>NACC/CMJ</strong> <strong>Radio 200</strong> chart. The artist has sold out headlining shows at <strong>Mercury Lounge</strong> in New York City and <strong>Bottom of the Hill</strong> in San Francisco, and played featured slots at <strong>SXSW</strong>, <strong>Bottlerock</strong>, and the <strong>CMJ</strong> <strong>Music</strong> <strong>Marathon</strong>. Wildlife Control’s innovative videos have garnered praise from <strong>WIRED</strong> and comparisons to groups like <strong>OK Go</strong> and <strong>Arcade</strong> <strong>Fire</strong>. Combining their indie rock sound with time-lapse and stop motion photography, the music video for the artist’s debut single “<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=boGyFAYomBo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Analog or Digital</strong></a>” went viral with over 450k views."},{"t":"p","html":"Wildlife Control’s new album “<strong>Love. Champion. Mountain. King</strong>.” will be released on September 20, 2024. Pre-orders on vinyl, CD, and digital are available at <a href=\"https://wildlifectrl.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">wildlifectrl.com</a>!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Wildlife Control!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/WcjUrJg9t4s?si=isxt7w5abjqGIW5J","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://wildlifectrl.com/","img":"","title":"Dream Dream Dream My Friend. Out July 12. Wildlife Control blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: it doesnʼt matter if sheʼs analog or digital.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCL3hF3eJdMBBvEnLLquputA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/wildlifecontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/wildlifecontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"327988","title":"Home page of Dave Lebental, an americana, blues, country, jam, jazz, rock, songwriter artist from Los Angeles. Dave Lebental creates original music blending Soft Rock, Blues, and Country. He is a Multi-Instrumentalist and songwriter who performs live solo","date":"2024-08-02","lead":"Obscure Rock/Americana Singer-Songwriter is making an appearance at Ashkenaz Music & Dance Community Center.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/327988/9cf2f597c69163aa37bed9ed6d8cd09a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Obscure Rock/Americana Singer-Songwriter is making an appearance at Ashkenaz Music &amp; Dance Community Center."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/659802/large-25615b4da999a6d0b61421c6e31c6f60.png","alt":"Click the flyer to purchase tickets!"},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (August 02, 2024) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7lf4oQdww9xJEW4WF4UD43?si=TV4QoNMoSVmz9zNjHquj_g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dave Lebental</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;&amp; The Driftwood Souls&nbsp;</strong>announced a tour stop in Berkeley, CA for Friday, August 2nd, 2024, at the <a href=\"https://www.ashkenaz.com/#/events/109139\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ashkenaz Music &amp; Dance Community Center</a>. The band will perform the songs from Dave’s new album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5jTjCeNvYAlTC0Xr6Nhf9Y?si=KsvUZqPBQLGmWUKo9rDosQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>The Long Player</em></strong></a><strong>,</strong> and provide some previews of the upcoming singles. <em>The Long Player</em> has been receiving enthusiastic praise from underground music blogs and the independent music press. Writers have been noting the quality of the songwriting which has Classic Rock &amp; Americana influences. Released independently, the songs and videos have quietly generated over a million streams/views in the digital world and have spawned an underground fan base."},{"t":"p","html":"Tickets for the Ashkenaz show are available at <a href=\"https://www.venuepilot.co/events/109139/orders/new#/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.venuepilot.co/events/109139/orders/new#/</a>!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/m1pPv2pLdFk?si=ABp4Y5tnqhHRC694","height":"315"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5jTjCeNvYAlTC0Xr6Nhf9Y?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“I’m excited to get up to the Bay Area and play for a Northern California audience!”,</em> says Lebental.<em>“Over the years I’ve visited &amp; checked out many shows in the Bay Area and I just love the vibe. It’s got a feeling that sets it apart from other places. Right now, I’m in a cool period in my life where I get to release the music I want and play shows in the places that inspire me.”&nbsp;</em>Lebental’s backing band, <strong>The Driftwood Souls</strong>, is a talented crew comprised of drummer <strong>Bryon Holley</strong> (Isaac Hayes, Perry Farrell, Ruben Blades), saxophonist <strong>Dan Boissy</strong> (Macy Gray, John Legend, Fitz &amp; The Tantrums), bassist <strong>Mick Linden</strong> (John Goodsall, Paula Cole, Wilton Felder), and Guitarist/Keyboardist <strong>John “JT” Thomas&nbsp;</strong>(Billy Sherwood, Toni Childs, Graham Bonet). You can count on a zenful set with jammed-out versions of Dave’s well-written songs.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7lf4oQdww9xJEW4WF4UD43?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Dave Lebental:"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/659798/large-92749f19f6e57237805bcfd92050e6ab.png","alt":"meta_eyJzcmNCdWNrZXQiOiJiemdsZmlsZXMifQ==.png"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Dave Lebental</strong>, a veteran rocker, made waves in the ‘90s LA Club scene, opening for ex-Rolling Stones guitarist <strong>Mick Taylor</strong>. Despite promising prospects and gigs alongside notable artists, his big break eluded him. A few months after a Mick Taylor gig, family priorities led him to trade rock n’ roll for a day job."},{"t":"p","html":"Fast forward 27 years, Lebental, now 62, found renewed creative spark as an empty nester. Exploring the modern music landscape, he embraced digital recording and social media, crafting his debut solo LP, ‘The Long Player.’ The 11-track album, influenced by <strong>James Taylor</strong>, <strong>Ryan Adams</strong>, <strong>The Eagles</strong>, <strong>Tom Petty</strong>, and <strong>The Beatles</strong>, showcases old-school analog performances with multi-track recordings."},{"t":"p","html":"Happy as an independent artist, Lebental seeks to connect with his audience. After releasing <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7BoG1lgtFnxtrATjJoGpX2?si=3OF4hGaiR4yNc2aYRdg7BA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Granite Meadow</strong></a><strong>”</strong> in 2021, he unveiled his first full-length LP to a substantial online following of 38,000 on Facebook and 1,000,000 digital music fans. Performing with his band, The Driftwood Souls, and solo, Lebental’s upcoming tour dates and performances can be found at <a href=\"https://dlmusic.us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">dlmusic.us</a>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Dave!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C4L_I9fSPrj/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://dlmusic.us/","img":"","title":"Home page of Dave Lebental, an americana, blues, country, jam, jazz, rock, songwriter artist from Los Angeles. Dave Lebental creates original music blending Soft Rock, Blues, and Country. He is a Multi-Instrumentalist and songwriter who performs live solo","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@dlmusic.us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://dlmusic.us/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/dlmusic.us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCC5gMEB0_DV0ziMiu29WFQg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/DLMusic.US/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"332352","title":"17-year-old pop sensation Maria Deirisarri is set to release her debut album, \"In The Beginning,\" on September 29th. Hailing from Atlanta, her musical talent transcends her age, exploring genres from dark alternative to bossa nova. With over 77k Spotify streams and recognition from top publications like Earmilk and Conversations About Her, Maria's star is on the rise. Her music, influenced by her Hispanic heritage, surprises and captivates with its multilingual lyrics.","date":"2024-08-02","lead":"Reminiscing the unforgettable summer romance, with an elegant bossa nova flair.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/332352/60a1940be83bcb3c14e5a7e0f4b25e89.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Reminiscing the unforgettable summer romance, with an elegant bossa nova flair."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5760gKxngKv6eFoMKDU2Yw?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Roswell, GA (August 2, 2024) - Singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maria Deirisarri</strong></a> debuts \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5IBgd2csyozd3S3QXSBmf3?si=j3Yz8LrBR_i6vh0afLeOhw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>bluejay</strong></a>,\" her highly anticipated first single of 2024, following the success of her 2023 album \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ?si=1Q83HeTiQOWfrnrAHIajcw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>In the Beginning</strong></a>.\" \"<strong>bluejay</strong>\" captures the essence of summer with its simplistic, sweet, and airy feel that is sure to resonate with lovers among listeners.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The heartfelt lyrics of \"bluejay\" were drawn from Maria's personal journey of saying goodbye, intended as an unread love letter and a memento from one of the sweetest, most cherished summers she experienced. Drawing inspiration from bossa nova, the song commemorates every moment she shared with a person she could have loved, but for whom time ran short."},{"t":"quote","html":"“The title of the song is actually an allusion to its muse's name; but I wasn't about to name it after him, so I chose the next best bird.”","cite":"- Maria Deirisarri, Singer-songwriter"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664141/compressed_original-71d162c559edc6f61df350e86c0df0be.webp","alt":"Cover art for 'bluejay', drawn by Maria Deirisarri herself and edited by Beatriz Deirisarri"},{"t":"p","html":"For the first time, <strong>Maria</strong> collaborated with <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0XuYkyliNor6szd1B6oBKk?si=Ih0Lg5RySqG84GrpZxP1ew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Corey Kilgannon</strong></a>, a cherished folk artist known for \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0hJKOgE9t7j1WVOpBMpeY9?si=Q3nnCctKTw2nURVEy20ytw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Slim Margins</strong></a>\" and \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4CrSb6QANO8NX2rdLa9Hg7?si=9b18ab41e0904873\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>God Is Just The Universe</strong></a>.\" His studio, situated on the second floor of Jacksonville's Beaches Vineyard Church, offered a distinctive ambiance that Maria had never experienced in any of her previous recording projects.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The song was recorded through analog technology emphasized the importance of nailing each take perfectly since it would be difficult to redo specific lines or verses. This approach resulted in a 100% pure, unfiltered sound etched directly onto tape, distinct from the typical digital reproduction."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664615/large-ff62c7a33e44d01f09e4e07f66fa3b37.png","alt":"IMG_3255.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664615/preview-5418dfdd607bc9c6e7aaa93865ef8074.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664584/large-5de29d72d9d5106e9fa0e99c8857f580.png","alt":"IMG_3250.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664584/preview-15addbaa67982a536bc3326512422eee.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664609/large-4bb809e2d38fa17b28501ff969f834cc.png","alt":"IMG_3400.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664609/preview-50b165c08421ebbee15939192156da3d.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664612/large-1f321c5309048ce3b5feddba62d64da2.png","alt":"IMG_3412.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664612/preview-c783ea6c6f4b19b685edb8635da9bf02.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664613/large-223e0fe008a94ab6ae00e401409dfc54.png","alt":"IMG_3435.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664613/preview-5854fd4da5a8cab8fe08a18d298930b6.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664611/large-ae27b96c22829c79f2299df6aa014efb.png","alt":"IMG_3344.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664611/preview-948378493546c8d27c32e567481dcb58.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664608/large-f8dd57efe1f8909a88d0f7145f188aba.png","alt":"IMG_3271.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664608/preview-671929598bae3fa5954df1d7ee9316ab.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664610/large-f88d26f08c559c3e335a68c1bcd4fb95.png","alt":"IMG_3268.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664610/preview-59b8863d61b9b968c6b4b9310c64f1dc.png"}]},{"t":"quote","html":"“Recording \"bluejay\" was hardddd since we didn't have a click track, and \"bluejay\" is naturally a very rhythmic song. We had to rely on the guitars to guide the rhythm instead of a bass or drums, which I think ended up making it that much more romantic.”","cite":"- Maria Deirisarri, Singer-songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5IBgd2csyozd3S3QXSBmf3?si=dXTmIaE8Q--USrb5M99g8w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>bluejay</strong></a>\" stands as one of Maria's favorite love songs she's written that continues to remind her of summer. Eager listeners would also love to know that \"bluejay\" is the first of the 5 new songs from her upcoming, unreleased EP, \"<strong>Si Vis Pacem</strong>.\""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Maria Deirisarri:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Rising pop artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?si=Xds4ArOJR-2cK4gvpDa3fw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maria</strong> <strong>Deirisarri</strong></a> is only 17 years of age, but her musicianship and lyricism suggest wisdom beyond her years. The Atlanta-based singer-songwriter experiments with a multitude of genres, from dark alternative to bossa nova, generating an eclectic mix of music notably showcased in her debut album,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ?si=5PxCg_ffS4W3yOBVCzM4lw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>In The Beginning</strong></a>.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Already amassing over 77k streams on Spotify, and garnering attention from top publications such as <strong>EARMILK</strong> and <strong>Conversations About Her</strong>, Maria Deirisarri’s success continues to increase with every release. The range of her sound entices listeners to discover every song’s personality, and even surprises them with lyrics connected to her Hispanic culture and multilingual heritage (such as in “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7Bum6Hbsbd3hTyrWdiFaZB?si=66799e5fb9774bd0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Same</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/10HrEur1hApraufv2ih2ZY?si=5ce3cc3dcdc8443c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Te</strong> <strong>Necesito</strong></a>”)."},{"t":"p","html":"In recent months, this young artist has triumphed in various competitions, ranging from her Trailblazing Performer accolade from the International Singer-Songwriters Association, her second-place finish in <strong>Omega’s</strong> <strong>Got</strong> <strong>Talent</strong>, to her Talent Preliminary Award in the <strong>Miss Georgia Teen Volunteer Competition</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Maria Deirisarri’s vibrant artiste meets the listener with a grace and uniqueness that is a breath of fresh air. Fans are eager to see what this up-and-coming superstar has up her sleeve. Follow Maria below for all music updates and upcoming announcements!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Maria!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/oBYTFlobyBY?si=ywUuqBq0Tec2Jnjz","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/mariadeirisarri/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@mariadeirisarri","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com/","img":"","title":"17-year-old pop sensation Maria Deirisarri is set to release her debut album, \"In The Beginning,\" on September 29th. Hailing from Atlanta, her musical talent transcends her age, exploring genres from dark alternative to bossa nova. With over 77k Spotify streams and recognition from top publications like Earmilk and Conversations About Her, Maria's star is on the rise. Her music, influenced by her Hispanic heritage, surprises and captivates with its multilingual lyrics.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@mariadeirisarri?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCtx5jhQ5a3Fx8_EJxh54WsA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/media/set/?set=a.2656672987691809&amp;type=3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>​"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"334050","title":"Xan DuBose","date":"2024-08-02","lead":"The reflection of DuBose's artistic evolution, experiences, emotions, and growth throughout her career — captured in her debut EP.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/334050/d8f3dd0679aac6cc7346dc5b2a5ac945.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The reflection of DuBose's artistic evolution, experiences, emotions, and growth throughout her career — captured in her debut EP."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2evhaebgHYxernEdBdT8QB?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Charleston, SC (August 2, 2024) - Dynamic songstress <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1FtaimfBPkxh0WRi2kAg9l?si=ob2eVRdhQzi3UsZU7wcp0w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Xan DuBose</strong></a><strong></strong> launched her highly-anticipated EP, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2evhaebgHYxernEdBdT8QB?si=Ji_Me5Z5TBu-FUgBM_TDQA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Black</strong> <strong>&amp;</strong> <strong>White</strong></a>\" on August 2, 2024. Featuring a variety of genres, this six-track EP demonstrates DuBose's versatility as a singer/songwriter.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Black &amp; White\" is a powerful testament to the idea that we are all a series of contradictions. Spanning 2 years of hard work, this collection showcases versatility, power, independence, heartbreak, anger, and hope. Each track reflects the different facets of DuBose's music style and vocal ability, culminating in a work that is both deeply personal and universally relatable. \"Black &amp; White\" marks the beginning of what she hopes will be a long and impactful journey in music."},{"t":"button","href":"https://vyd.co/XanDuboseBlackWhite","label":"Stream 'Black & White' EP","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Creating 'Black &amp; White' was such a journey of expression. It allowed me to explore and embrace the contradictions within myself and my music. Each track has a piece of my soul and represents some portion of my artistry and it's just the beginning.\"","cite":"- Xan DuBose, Singer/songwriter"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666389/compressed_original-adf3dfceabebd9067b66444dbbec09ae.webp","alt":"Cover art for \"Black & White\" EP"},{"t":"p","html":"Featuring DuBose's successful titles like \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2MwLc56lkclkp5qVgKjhgD?si=873d602416234635\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Serious</strong> <strong>Craving</strong></a>\", \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2niEzh3Ogd7A1GYSVsBmSx?si=d3ea98c3e4b34cb7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Vice</strong></a>\", and her latest release \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1xkIQkvJoGb2HinzTzS3fj?si=568ca4e63d104278\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Unbreak</strong></a>\" comes the fresh, titular track \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2fg3mYBx9eJ48ZgWKKH0eI?si=e3decf49766c4e95\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Black</strong> <strong>&amp;</strong> <strong>White</strong></a>\" - a heartbreaking song spoken from emotional turbulence and longing in a complicated relationship, trapped in a cycle of hope and disappointment from a love that feels both conditional and insincere."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2fg3mYBx9eJ48ZgWKKH0eI?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"With resonating lyrics and DuBose's enchanting voice, her music leaves fans enthralled and would be listeners seriously craving for more."},{"t":"quote","html":"“With 'Black &amp; White,' I wanted to deliver a powerful and authentic representation of my artistry. It's a testament to the highs and lows, the strength and vulnerability that define who I am as a musician.\"","cite":"- Xan DuBose, Singer/songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Xan Dubose:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1FtaimfBPkxh0WRi2kAg9l?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Xan</strong> <strong>DuBose</strong> (she/her) is an exceptionally talented singer-songwriter hailing from the vibrant musical scenes of Columbia and Charleston, South Carolina. With a captivating voice that effortlessly blends elements of jazz, soulful vocals, contemporary sounds, and a touch of country flavor, Xan’s music resonates with listeners on a profound level."},{"t":"p","html":"Since making her debut in the SC music scene back in 2013, Xan has become a recognizable and highly sought-after artist. She gained considerable acclaim as a member of <strong>Patrick</strong> <strong>Davis</strong>’ <strong>Midnight</strong> <strong>Choir</strong>, a testament to her remarkable vocal prowess and stage presence. Her performances alongside acclaimed artists such as <strong>Darius</strong> <strong>Rucker</strong>, <strong>Thomas</strong> <strong>McClary</strong>, <strong>Charles</strong> <strong>Kelley</strong>, and others have further solidified her reputation as a standout talent."},{"t":"p","html":"Xan finds creative influence in iconic artists such as <strong>Bill</strong> <strong>Withers</strong>, <strong>Allen</strong> <strong>Stone</strong>, <strong>Madison</strong> <strong>Cunningham</strong>, and <strong>Brandi</strong> <strong>Carlile</strong>. These diverse influences infuse her music with a unique blend of heartfelt lyrics, soulful melodies, and a timeless quality that transcends genres."},{"t":"p","html":"With her versatile musical style, Xan DuBose takes her listeners on a captivating journey through the intricacies of jazz, the emotional depths of soul, the infectious beats of contemporary sounds, and the storytelling essence of country music. Her performances are characterized by an irresistible blend of vulnerability, passion, and authentic artistry that leaves a lasting impact on all who have the privilege of experiencing her music."},{"t":"p","html":"As Xan continues to mesmerize audiences and carve her own path in the music industry, her infectious energy and undeniable talent have firmly established her as a rising star. With each captivating performance and heartfelt composition, Xan DuBose is making an indelible mark on the music scene, captivating the hearts of listeners far and wide."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Xan!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/xan_dubose/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@xan_dubose","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.xandubosemusic.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/65274f91e2c93806f99f56ac/t/652c10fb748f3d00f34fbb60/1697386747072/xan-06.png?format=1500w","title":"Xan DuBose","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.xandubosemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1FtaimfBPkxh0WRi2kAg9l\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/alexandra.dubose.7?mibextid=LQQJ4d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"335718","title":"Improvised And Sperimental Music | Reykjavík | Balder gernot Music","date":"2024-08-01","lead":"The 10-track album encapsulates the dark reality of human society, from time immemorial to the living world.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/335718/349c9580b68f315cb2c87b4386c73f6e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The 10-track album encapsulates the dark reality of human society, from time immemorial to the living world."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3BRruJZAUoUZ4aY79oP6xq?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Reykjavík, Iceland (August 1, 2024) - Prolific artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0ONllzF9IKbHiF9SW1gkvg?si=9C6Scve5RhmIO_bcIVeSyg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Balder</strong> <strong>Gernot</strong></a> unleashed his latest album, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3BRruJZAUoUZ4aY79oP6xq?si=gv1ZbvIdRZm0LlIrFoj9Ew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I'm Just a Man</strong></a>\", on August 1, 2024, following the admirable success of \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5rgIt4NQYeV02YtyVrrLOa?si=57g5ARvaTE-vHLAIT2OAyQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Towards</strong> <strong>The</strong> <strong>End</strong></a>\" last November 2023. The album fuses rock and pop styles with Gernot's innovative touch, leaving profound messages subtly woven throughout its tracks."},{"t":"p","html":"\"I'm Just a Man\" is a deep exploration of human nature and society, spanning themes of existential angst, societal critique, and personal introspection. It begins with reflections on humanity's lost state in a turbulent universe and progresses through tracks that ponder the consequences of human actions and aspirations.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://artists.landr.com/055855115867","label":"Listen to \"I'm Just A Man\" on Streaming Platforms","color":"#ff6969"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667974/large-79d2bcb106807dde10384589ebebb1d0.jpg","alt":"Cover Art for \"I'm Just a Man\""},{"t":"p","html":"Musically diverse, it shifts from melodic rock to harder, more introspective tones, culminating in a poignant reflection on human flaws and societal entanglements. The album's narrative and evocative guitar solos weave together to convey a profound message about the complexities of being human, from the beginning of his existence on earth to the present day where the human tide moves and resides."},{"t":"p","html":"Gernot intricately linked each track, seamlessly connecting them with a subtle thread that unified the entire concept."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668320/-506e2ad56f31996dc59381a66e860ad1.jpg","alt":"01_Lost_Within_The_Universe_Canvas_.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668320/preview-094c3277569a5b3ad30f64aa1cad0e2f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668322/-9b13ca9d2c44397c7eb365208fb48e66.jpg","alt":"09_I_m_Just_A_Man_Canvas_.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668322/preview-9a6303d568789e4f775c7da63d1d3884.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668321/-5db6673d377e93c641e19b6c8c888ef1.jpg","alt":"10_The_Human_Tide_Canvas_.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/668321/preview-10e7f3f66439bc77994037f0e04ad49c.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Through the use of electric guitar and synthesizers, Gernot tailored the musical arrangement to complement the voice and style of the singer he collaborated with, producing songs that strike a balance between rock elements and melodious tones, conveying both harmony and tension."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Balder Gernot:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0ONllzF9IKbHiF9SW1gkvg?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.baldergernot.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Balder Gernot</strong></a> began playing music at a young age like many others, starting with an old acoustic guitar. His desire to express his inner feelings led him to create his own songs. Spending countless hours, days, and months listening to rock legends like <strong>Black</strong> <strong>Sabbath</strong>, <strong>Led</strong> <strong>Zeppelin</strong>, and <strong>Deep</strong> <strong>Purple</strong>, he also kept an eye on new musical developments."},{"t":"p","html":"After a hiatus of 25 years to focus on work, Gernot's long-dormant passion for music reignited. Establishing a modest home studio, he now dedicates time to composing music and writing lyrics. Additionally, Gernot has cultivated a network of fellow artists with whom he collaborates to produce and finalize albums."},{"t":"p","html":"Having reunited with old Italian friends, Gernot is currently collaborating on their debut album under the band name \"<strong>Zona</strong> <strong>Rimozione</strong>.\" This promises something exciting for listeners to anticipate!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Balder Gernot!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/JpG9axBy6Is?si=wYj2zosZ4NI4jz04","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.baldergernot.com/","img":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/e453da_16196fdc03b440aa9153288ea2858bc8%7Emv2.jpg/v1/fit/w_2500,h_1330,al_c/e453da_16196fdc03b440aa9153288ea2858bc8%7Emv2.jpg","title":"Improvised And Sperimental Music | Reykjavík | Balder gernot Music","desc":"balder gernot music instrumental sperimental soul viking story quorthon concept album rock electronic Edgar Allan Poe tales Album"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/balder.gernot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@baldergernot8957\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.baldergernot.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0ONllzF9IKbHiF9SW1gkvg?si=EbzH0rt6Rv-mK5vd3itzUQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"332743","title":"Artist on the Rise Karisa Brings in \"Endless Summer\"","date":"2024-07-26","lead":"Flavored with dancing, beach vibes, and the warmth of summer sun — a nostalgia trip encapsulated in one.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/332743/0acffac428eaed4c4498a8a5939e6dc7.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Flavored with dancing, beach vibes, and the warmth of summer sun — a nostalgia trip encapsulated in one."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1GphL7ntFjjsHIOzxyZdec?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Toronto, ON (July 26, 2024) - Canadian songstress <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0xiPUnPct1UgzYCIgLVYMV?si=87Db9uFbQnWZ9Zud16_GsA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karisa</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>enthralls listeners once more with her latest EP \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1GphL7ntFjjsHIOzxyZdec?si=bnPECToYRDyI04zSK0t6OA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Endless</strong> <strong>Summer</strong></a>\", released on July 26, 2024. With synths, drums, and guitar riffs that evoke the spirit of the 1980s and early 2000s, the EP vividly captures the essence of summer, setting a perfect backdrop for nostalgic reflections on sun-drenched memories."},{"t":"quote","html":"\"Endless Summer\" EP is a musical tribute to summertime, filled with memories.","cite":"- Karisa, Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666352/large-551ecf83450c12a99103983de20e5ef1.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Endless Summer\" EP"},{"t":"p","html":"The lyrics describe coastal settings in all three songs, painting an image in the listener's mind of the perfect \"California dream.\" The lyrical transitions from day to night or sunset to darkness are brought in to symbolize the end of this imagery, creating the feeling of these memories and days coming to an end."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Night Waves</strong> pays homage to the Vaporwave sound movement, while also using house synths and a catchy pop chorus. The song explores the feelings of trust and betrayal."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3mLwlWxXBywQVv6RfyoHif?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Coastal Dreams</strong> is inspired by the new wave electronic music (New Order, The Cure, Psychedelic Furs) from the 1980s mixed with modern Euro dance melodies. The song brings a nostalgic feel with a modern and unique twist. It captures the feeling of being young and free, driving along the Pacific Coast and following your heart."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1q6nG4Gd1W9sHoy5PK50C5?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Mirage</strong> is mixed with 1980s guitar riffs and mid-western pop-punk sounds to create an energetic alternative vibe. It takes inspiration from <strong>Don Henley</strong>’s \"<strong>Boys of Summer</strong>\" and <strong>Avril Lavigne</strong>'s debut album \"<strong>Let Go</strong>.\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5jvvJgJYyg2WItmF7ambAo?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Whether you find yourself dancing barefoot on the beach at sunset or cruising along coastal highways with the windows down, \"Endless Summer\" is an essential addition to your summer playlist, seamlessly blending into every moment of your sun-soaked adventures."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666287/large-56e3bd11c47df7034e9399b495035621.jpg","alt":"IMG_3810.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666287/preview-da1836b3faf9e52490cf1e02b781115d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666289/large-f0ab567097eaf0d4c0faaa5207830e02.jpg","alt":"IMG_3808.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666289/preview-71025573688c9b5e34158735f7750421.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666292/large-4aa5bd05a74d20b2331766f7b215f09e.jpg","alt":"IMG_3813.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666292/preview-bf248de730d7f4951a6da33689c9806c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666293/large-0b995f2b6e96912fbbb33b60f5434624.jpg","alt":"IMG_3781.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666293/preview-d987c06e8f3dc8a16c5ae637c73934ba.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666294/large-95c9b0306a65ff35365b18b3297cf82d.jpg","alt":"IMG_3815.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666294/preview-4f78f514edae4fc4517f5c2c46b223a8.jpg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Karisa:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0xiPUnPct1UgzYCIgLVYMV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Toronto-based Alternative Pop Singer <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0xiPUnPct1UgzYCIgLVYMV\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karisa</strong></a> has heavily relied on music and art throughout various stages of life. Karisa comes from an artistic family filled with creation and individuality. She recalls her love of music starting to bloom when she was a child sitting at the piano, recording herself singing."},{"t":"p","html":"Karisa’s first live performance was at a dive bar in Toronto’s <strong>Kensington Market</strong>. This experience sparked Karisa’s urge to become an established singer-songwriter and share her music with the world. She prides herself on creating music that expresses the emotion behind various experiences in life - the good, the bad, the ugly, and all that falls in between. Karisa hopes to create songs that provide listeners with a slice of happiness or comfort when they need it the most."},{"t":"p","html":"Stay tuned for more announcements and updates from Karisa via her social media channels below!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Karisa!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/N7Q6qzVXo0s?si=6P4g3FTjeZe8Ja-J","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/karisamusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@karisamusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@Karisamusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.karisamusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0xiPUnPct1UgzYCIgLVYMV?si=QyOFNv_XQP6xPo5wFgeczw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"335212","title":"Decoding \"Cryptograms\" - Mayday 13's Latest Album Unveiled","date":"2024-07-26","lead":"Mayday 13 showcases dynamic artistry in music with his sophomore album.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/335212/3c616b39e573466a5143398588e7e41b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Mayday 13 showcases dynamic artistry in music with his sophomore album."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0waLoBfAdqbGu9OE7OjDxo?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Mount Ephraim, NJ (Jul 26, 2024) - Solo indie-rock artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1F7CcCZFI0bYMrHYQnqMU3?si=b91k6t3wSgGsNUjz9GTPsA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mayday</strong> <strong>13</strong></a> makes a mark with his second album, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0waLoBfAdqbGu9OE7OjDxo?si=AXYe0qauQIODs_pnpFLx8w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cryptograms</strong></a>\", released on July 26, 2024. The album includes his most recent single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3YclGANzLDlceWG4q9FWZk?si=f4a52cc1fd8e4b49\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Radio</strong> <strong>Song</strong></a>\", and features 10 new tracks that explore all aspects of life, reflecting a range of emotions — joy, sadness, frustration, anger, and fear."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667718/large-a6550887368b3d625777dc99ee4f6019.jpg","alt":"Cover art for Cryptograms"},{"t":"quote","html":"I didn't set out to write about any specific topic or emotion; I simply let each song evolve naturally, inspired by what I was feeling or thinking at the time.","cite":"- Mayday 13, Indie-rock artist"},{"t":"p","html":"Written with raw spontaneity, each track showcases Mayday 13's lyricism and musicality, crafting a mysterious artistic expression within the realm of music."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667729/large-773bce8340a96c100a635514dd20cd99.jpg","alt":"Back cover of Cryptograms"},{"t":"p","html":"\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0waLoBfAdqbGu9OE7OjDxo?si=SRDElPfZTwKUMROEk5YWEQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cryptograms</strong></a>\" delves into messages hidden in plain sight, with the track listing itself serving as a cryptogram. The song titles cleverly spell out the album name on the back cover — the only spot you'll find it in the concept art or packaging. This intriguing detail is exclusive to those who own the CD, vinyl, or related merch, as the digital version keeps this hidden."},{"t":"p","html":"This album is deeply influenced by the Mayday 13's life experiences, showcasing tracks that echo the sounds of <strong>Arcade</strong> <strong>Fire</strong>, <strong>Bloc</strong> <strong>Party</strong>, <strong>Collective</strong> <strong>Soul</strong>, and <strong>Live</strong>. Additionally, Mayday 13 found inspiration from a variety of other musicians who have left a profound mark on their journey, such as <strong>Radiohead</strong>, The <strong>Killers</strong>, and <strong>Bruce</strong> <strong>Springsteen</strong>, shaping the overall sound and emotional depth of the project."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Mayday 13:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1F7CcCZFI0bYMrHYQnqMU3?utm_source=generator&theme=0","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from New Jersey, <strong>Mayday 13</strong>, the solo project of <strong>Brian</strong> <strong>Hadley</strong>, emerged in late 2022. Having spent the last ten plus years in the thriving Philadelphia cover scene, Brian always kept one toe dipped in the vast pool of original music. Pulling inspiration from the likes of <strong>David</strong> <strong>Bowie</strong>, <strong>Band</strong> <strong>of</strong> <strong>Horses</strong>, <strong>Radiohead</strong>, <strong>Live</strong>, <strong>Arcade</strong> <strong>Fire</strong>, <strong>M83</strong>, <strong>Manchester</strong> <strong>Orchestra</strong> and many others, Mayday 13 released his first full length album \"<strong>Dreaming</strong> <strong>is</strong> <strong>easy</strong>\" in the spring of 2023. ​"},{"t":"p","html":"Having achieved some admirable success, he released a follow-up single \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3YclGANzLDlceWG4q9FWZk?si=238d92ea14e546f5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Radio</strong> <strong>Song</strong></a>\" in May of 2024, part of Mayday 13's much anticipated sophomore album \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0waLoBfAdqbGu9OE7OjDxo?si=soRAiPzERU2Gq4q4eM2b6A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cryptograms</strong></a>\" which is now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Mayday 13!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/A3lB-2XF-oE?si=B4UpQ1VZWTwhDM02","height":"580"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/_mayday13/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/themayday13/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://mayday13.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"335094","title":"Keep for Cheap Drops Second Single, \"Cyberspace\", from Upcoming Album, 'Big Grass'","date":"2024-07-25","lead":"Exploring the complexities and contradictions of online existence with introspection and melody.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/335094/9ac30035007864fa2d36f31bddc6c36e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/79DPYgaQOgcBcO8Cr8fv4P?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"lead","html":"Exploring the complexities and contradictions of online existence with introspection and melody."},{"t":"p","html":"MINNEAPOLIS (July 25, 2024) - The Midwest's own “prairie-rock” pioneers,<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.keepforcheap.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Keep for Cheap</strong></a>, released their latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/79DPYgaQOgcBcO8Cr8fv4P?si=031dbfb399f24d8b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cyberspace</strong></a>,” and is now available on all streaming platforms. This track offers a sneak peek into their eagerly awaited sophomore album, '<strong>Big Grass</strong>', to debut in August 2024.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"“<strong>Cyberspace</strong>” is a meandering indie-rock tune that opens and closes with questions about why humans are so pervasively online. Inspired by the tangled relationship between social media and personal identity, Keep for Cheap reflects on the cyclical nature of harmful digital behaviors, including over-consumption and over-sharing."},{"t":"p","html":"The song addresses how social media feels necessary for connecting with others. However, as often a toxic and cyclical tool, its support of vapid and detached consumption habits leaves the band insecure in its growth as it struggles to produce viral content."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Cyberspace is a song about feeling drained by your biggest resource.”","cite":"- Autumn and Kate, the band’s fronting duo"},{"t":"p","html":"The song questions the need for external validation and a wider audience to witness individuals' lives feel actualized — themes of human indulgence and “shouting to the ether” echo throughout.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"As <strong>Autumn </strong>and <strong>Kate</strong>, the band’s fronting duo, lament, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/79DPYgaQOgcBcO8Cr8fv4P?si=b0bec1dc90e8408d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cyberspace</strong></a>\" is, <em>“a song about feeling drained by your biggest resource.” </em>It challenges listeners to ponder the true cost of the performance of our online lives, the hollow nature of virtual connections, the unseen consequences of our digital selves, and the implications of feeling more alive with our faces turned toward screens."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/667332/large-86ac688d128f0731f46944bedada4d9a.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Cyberspace\" by Kate Malanaphy"},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, “Cyberspace” blends shoegaze indie-rock with twangy punk influences, reminiscent of <strong>Wednesday</strong> and <strong>Bully</strong>, or <strong>Pinegrove</strong> meets <strong>Soccer Mommy</strong>. The track features spacey guitars, melodic yet driving bass, steady drums, and stirring vocals, creating a sound that is both immersive and thought-provoking. Produced by <strong>Abe Anderson</strong>, the band notes, <em>“It's one of our more in-depth arrangements on 'Big Grass,' capable of holding multiple meanings and resonating on various levels.”</em>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660206/large-e205fc7f615c1f5155a5139dfadc9cff.jpg","alt":"DSC_4473.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660206/preview-986f76b1b2546184f168efa2201333e8.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660207/large-69b6542ed531f03edc98b15cf0d2f35f.jpg","alt":"DSC_4493.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660207/preview-8558f747b9723b05efb347814a057df4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660205/large-ed575f51adf876a0c33425216e9ba2b2.jpg","alt":"DSC_4389.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660205/preview-49fea7a52618fe5511e46ac0e96de0b6.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by Bethunni Schreiner"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6YKwoZUW4g50TuiyvVz7JR?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Keep for Cheap:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Keep for Cheap</strong>’s special blend of indie, country, rock, and pop has a little something for everyone. Playing what they call “prairie rock,” the Minnesota five-piece’s playful sound will make you feel like a kid, then break your heart with its next turn of phrase. The band strives to make music that moves, with driving instrumentals and poignant lyrics. Drawing at times from their own love story, fronting members <strong>Kate Malanaphy</strong> and <strong>Autumn Vagle</strong> write music to make you pine over queer love and passing youth, seek inspiration in the natural world and connection wherever it can be made.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The emotion in their music mainly reflects the lives of songwriters and fronting members of the band, Autumn and Kate who formed a musical connection when they met in the alto section of college choir in 2017. They soon started “<strong>KfC</strong>”, became best friends and are now nearly five years in love, writing alternative country songs reflecting on their lives in Minnesota and the world as they see it. Their special connection brings a vivacious perspective to their music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Keep for Cheap!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/fk5YWkkqnko?si=ARUtD53zwNug3q6x","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C8uWN6hMHDp/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/keepforcheap/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC75Ms2W7_Q_bfn2cVLhTJ-Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://linktr.ee/keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Linktree</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"332096","title":"Zain Stephen Smith, also known by his stage name Zain Stephen or Zain, is a Caribbean-American singer, songwriter, musician, and record producer based in Atlanta, GA. Born in Long Island, New York, to Jamaican parents, Zain, often describing himself as a “citizenofdaworld”, spent his childhood growing up in Belize and Antigua before settling in Atlanta.","date":"2024-07-24","lead":"\"The Perfect Man\" showcases Zain's lyrical prowess to promote social awareness and foster equality.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/332096/1d7f7723afbb6f58d83bee220da681e0.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"The Perfect Man\" showcases Zain's lyrical prowess to promote social awareness and foster equality. &nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1Y2YqkDpm5fEJKMgsNaVkv?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Atlanta, GA (July 24, 2024) - Musical talent <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/15EGwhmd7yUmmBM56k6Ho3?si=G3PeO_MWTeeNFn-CfLEi3A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Zain Stephen</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>dropped his debut single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6dNdcqhSD3V03OeQQmM2J5?si=ae10240e779445e9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Perfect Man</strong></a>”, on July 19, 2024, now with its music video out. Driven by his experience after moving to the US, \"The Perfect Man” unleashed an extensive view of inequity that’s haunted minorities for a very long time."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Q_frTD6Ogqw?si=aQS-FT0nZm2m8lQn","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"Initially inspired by Zain’s personal quest for belonging, “The Perfect Man” also serves as a reflection of broader struggles within the African-American community, aiming to resonate with anyone facing similar challenges who continues to suffer in silence. The intro also points up Zain’s stance against pointless violence, relying solely on music for solace and finding hope in his faith."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664005/compressed_original-d4d26da0b518808dda990c2cdf181612.webp","alt":"Cover art for 'The Perfect Man'"},{"t":"quote","html":"Our cultures, backgrounds, and difference should be celebrated. It is who we are!","cite":"- Zain Stephen (Singer/Songwriter)"},{"t":"p","html":"Amid its powerful messages, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6dNdcqhSD3V03OeQQmM2J5?si=96521c3fc227471d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Perfect Man</strong></a>” presents a fresh, soulful R&amp;B sound that exudes chill vibes, appealing to listeners of all generations. Featuring a tasteful mix of musical instruments, \"The Perfect Man” evokes a blend reminiscent of <strong>Eryn</strong> <strong>Allen</strong> <strong>Kane</strong>, <strong>Aja</strong> <strong>Monet</strong>, and <strong>PJ</strong> <strong>Morton</strong>, sure to provoke thought among listeners."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Zain Stephen:"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664050/-a5f9043f5f00c905955dcd364da30895.webp","alt":"66745d_389fd1e817004af19b742fc03ebf042b~mv2.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664050/-a5f9043f5f00c905955dcd364da30895.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664049/-a924f8ef25620f57d3131113965bab1b.webp","alt":"66745d_81aa498be86a4b958c19e0ddd34d1378~mv2.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664049/-a924f8ef25620f57d3131113965bab1b.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664052/-ce2b6f124da0f100a79d58e84c6a85e6.webp","alt":"66745d_4e6e4be601384feb995175194b98f0e8~mv2.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664052/-ce2b6f124da0f100a79d58e84c6a85e6.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664048/-75d1dbfa21811ba97ed9d008e9d8a59f.webp","alt":"66745d_ef9ba8b1d42141c5aad782948d78a716~mv2 (1).webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664048/-75d1dbfa21811ba97ed9d008e9d8a59f.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664051/-9ef9e0b7c96e754335d9cecec134df54.webp","alt":"66745d_6e897e66309f4886b35276c733fcf9c5~mv2.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664051/-9ef9e0b7c96e754335d9cecec134df54.webp"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Zain Stephen Smith</strong>, also known by his stage name <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/15EGwhmd7yUmmBM56k6Ho3?si=G3PeO_MWTeeNFn-CfLEi3A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Zain Stephen</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>or <strong>Zain</strong>, is a Caribbean-American singer, songwriter, musician, and record producer based in Atlanta, GA. Born in Long Island, New York, to Jamaican parents, Zain, often describing himself as a “<strong>citizenofdaworld</strong>”, spent his childhood growing up in Belize and Antigua before settling in Atlanta."},{"t":"p","html":"At four or five years old, Zain would often be heard playing random notes and singing gibberish on an old upright piano in his house. A few months later, his mother signed him up for music lessons. It was then his passion for music started as he would go on to play in recitals and concerts for music schools in Belize and Antigua. Having a strong upbringing in the church, he became a prominent church pianist in Antigua. After moving to Atlanta to pursue his educational goals, Zain continued to be an active musician on the church scene as well as playing in the North Atlanta High School bands. Though a talented vocalist, Zain was shy to share his vocal talent and would not be heard singing in public other than a few times at church. In 2021 at the age of sixteen, Zain began writing songs as a form of therapy to cope with feelings of anxiety and being overwhelmed with moving to a new country again and not being able to “find himself.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"It was in February of 2022, inspired by recent events, that Zain would share his original music and vocal talent for the first time, singing an acoustic version of his unfinished song, “The Perfect Man,” and posting it on social media. In an emotion-filled gospel/soul piece, he sang about the oppressed experience of being a black man in America and received some attention after his friends shared the post and the video reached several thousand views."},{"t":"p","html":"Fast forward a few years and Zain released a studio version of&nbsp;<br>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1Y2YqkDpm5fEJKMgsNaVkv?si=2e7Ca7S4ReGkyyXuAHN6Xw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Perfect Man</strong></a>” song in July of 2024. Known for his vintage, soulful voice and instrumental style, he has cited <strong>Jon Batiste</strong>, <strong>Jonathan McReynolds</strong>, <strong>Samm Henshaw</strong>, and <strong>PJ</strong> <strong>Morton</strong> as his biggest musical influences. Zain also has a passion for melodica and can be seen covering many popular songs in videos on his social media. He has stated that he sees himself in the melodica,<em>&nbsp;“I think the melodica really summarizes me. It’s a frequently slept-on instrument with a fun and vintage personality that is seemingly simple, but is intricate and can easily light up a room.”</em>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Zain Stephen!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/hZeZLwAnszw?si=P1jMCEDttrLVJNNY","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.zainstephenmusic.com/","img":"","title":"Zain Stephen Smith, also known by his stage name Zain Stephen or Zain, is a Caribbean-American singer, songwriter, musician, and record producer based in Atlanta, GA. Born in Long Island, New York, to Jamaican parents, Zain, often describing himself as a “citizenofdaworld”, spent his childhood growing up in Belize and Antigua before settling in Atlanta.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/zain05stephen/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@zainstephen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@zainstephen?_t=8ebCVeBKmde&amp;_r=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://x.com/zain05stephen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a>&nbsp;</strong>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"338842","title":"Read More","date":"2024-07-23","lead":"An inspiring anthem encouraging simplicity and reconnection in our daily lives.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/338842/fea73481796b6027ece2e14d55c8ac42.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An inspiring anthem encouraging simplicity and reconnection in our daily lives."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5hcbemBJX7Lqhcd8lXrFGz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"San Diego, CA (July 23, 2024) – <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/412oFoFK213H1r4PBmz9Bn?si=TtZIIBFYSAifsPFG0E5Rew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Michael Gilas</strong></a> announces the release of his latest single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5hcbemBJX7Lqhcd8lXrFGz?si=4db8b95057c841cb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Let's Get Back To Us</strong></a>,\" from his upcoming debut album, '<strong>231 Kensington Road</strong>.' The song is the first glimpse into Michael's musical journey post-recovery from a life-threatening neck injury, showcasing his ability to transform personal adversity into uplifting art."},{"t":"p","html":"The single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5hcbemBJX7Lqhcd8lXrFGz?si=28d4a0a0d302415b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Let's Get Back To Us</a>,\" emphasizes the importance of simplicity and reconnection. <em>\"It’s really about not falling into a rut or routines,\"</em> Michael explains. \"The song is about simplicity and enjoyment in doing simple things, and not overthinking everything. The album is about the connection, or reconnection, with yourself and others.\" His music aims to bring an upbeat, positive message amidst the negativity of the world."},{"t":"p","html":"Michael's life took a dramatic turn in December 2021 when he sustained a severe neck injury. The harrowing experience, filled with physical and mental anguish, became a turning point for him. <em>\"Music saved my life because I had nothing else,\"</em> he shares. Michael's journey of recovery, marked by resilience and hope, is woven into the fabric of his music, offering inspiration to others facing similar struggles."},{"t":"p","html":"Influenced by iconic artists such as <strong>The Eagles</strong>, <strong>Marvin Gaye</strong>, <strong>Carole King</strong>, <strong>Steely Dan</strong>, and <strong>Fleetwood Mac</strong>, Michael's sound is a testament to his diverse musical upbringing on Long Island. His early exposure to a wide array of genres is reflected in the eclectic mix of styles present in this single and his upcoming album, '<strong>231 Kensington Road</strong>.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Michael's creative process is meticulous, starting with guitar noodling and evolving through collaboration with his producer and collaborator <strong>Allan Phillips</strong>. <em>\"It’s a long process but it’s a lot of fun,\" </em>Michael notes.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With plans to continue writing, recording, and exploring new sounds, he is preparing for live performances and collaborations with renowned artists like <strong>John Pena</strong> and <strong>Alex Acuna</strong>. Michael's ambition is to leave a lasting impact through his dedication to quality music."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/412oFoFK213H1r4PBmz9Bn?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Michael Gilas:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/412oFoFK213H1r4PBmz9Bn?si=TtZIIBFYSAifsPFG0E5Rew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Michael Gilas</strong></a> is pleased to announce his debut album, '<strong>231 Kensington Road'&nbsp;</strong>— a sonic testament to his versatility as an artist. It was at this address that he discovered the musicians who would inspire him. Born and raised amidst the creative energy of this iconic location, each song embodies a unique musical exploration, inviting listeners on a vibrant journey through his musical universe, where rhythm, melody, and emotion converge in celebration."},{"t":"p","html":"Drawing inspiration from iconic figures such as <strong>The Beatles</strong>, <strong>Eagles</strong>, <strong>Steely Dan</strong>, <strong>The Doobie Brothers</strong>, <strong>Joni Mitchell</strong>, <strong>Fleetwood Mac</strong>, and <strong>Elton John</strong>, Michael pays tribute to their influence through his compositions."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>'</strong><strong>231 Kensington Road</strong><strong>'</strong> transcends mere album status; it encapsulates a profound journey—an ode to the transformative power of music to inspire, uplift, and unite."},{"t":"p","html":"The first song of the album, <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5hcbemBJX7Lqhcd8lXrFGz?si=9a0d66abe4fc4cfc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Let's Get Back To Us</strong></a><strong>\"</strong>, is just a taste of Michael's sonic vision. Follow his profile to join him on this exciting journey!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Michael Gilas!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/412oFoFK213H1r4PBmz9Bn?go=1&amp;sp_cid=fb0b24b82f029a635427e4c09d0b2224&amp;utm_source=embed_player_p&amp;utm_medium=desktop&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=554e7e4f19d744d8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/michael-gilas/1756545844\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://michaelgilas.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://michaelgilas.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"298879","title":"Read More","date":"2024-07-19","lead":"MEMPHIS, TN (July 19, 2024) – Big Radio Records, a label of Memphis music mainstay Select-O-Hits, has inked Christopher Wyze & The Tellers for their debut album, ‘Stuck in the Mud.’ The 13-track studio release is scheduled to drop on June 21, 2024.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/298879/7998258cad413b9bf2dc94db8e0081d0.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5LoVKXP7M0aOTY2nSgpUmP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"MEMPHIS, TN (July 19, 2024) –<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.bigradiorecords.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Big Radio Records</strong></a>, a label of Memphis music mainstay <strong>Select-O-Hits</strong>, has inked <strong>Christopher Wyze &amp; The Tellers</strong> for their debut album, <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://cwyze.lnk.to/StuckInTheMudAlbum\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stuck in the Mud</strong></a><strong>.’&nbsp;</strong>The 13-track studio release is scheduled to drop on June 21, 2024."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“I learned about Wyze &amp; the Tellers from a producer-friend. Their blues, it grabbed him,”</em> says <strong>Johnny Phillips</strong>, who heads the label. Phillips listened and quickly decided he wanted Wyze’s Stuck in the Mud sound for his new and growing Big Radio Records label. <em>“These guys lay down a fresh sound, but with an ‘old as mud’ feel to it,”</em> he adds with a smile.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://cwyze.lnk.to/StuckInTheMudAlbum","label":"Listen to \"Stuck In The Mud\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/3nbzfu7BXk4","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"And Johnny Phillips should know. The label he runs operates within industry trailblazer Select-O-Hits, established in 1960 by his father, <strong>Tom Phillips</strong> and his uncle <strong>Sam Phillips </strong>of <strong>Sun Records</strong> fame. The company has been a part of more than 300 gold, platinum and Grammy-winning albums, including many blues hits over the past six decades, the latest being a Grammy for Best Contemporary Blues Album for <strong>Brother Johnny</strong> by<strong>&nbsp;Edgar Winter</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3AYuvdI7E0ln959gBk7wTP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"And while the band name Chistopher Wyze &amp; The Tellers may be new to the blues scene, frontman, harp player and singer-songwriter Wyze is anything but."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“I spent two decades doing blues standards,”&nbsp;</em>says the Indianapolis-based Wyze. <em>“It gets inside you and the stories just bubble up.”&nbsp;</em>He penned lyrics for the album in Clarksdale, ‘<strong>Miss</strong>.’ Recently, <strong>Nashville Songwriters Association International&nbsp;</strong>named Wyze a <strong><em>“One to Watch”</em></strong> songwriter (December 2023). A co-writer joins Wyze on each ‘Stuck in the Mud’ track."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/649584/large-a795f4578d8def6cd66f5fd61d8c8d22.jpg","alt":"Cover art for 'Stuck In The Mud'"},{"t":"p","html":"Recording in Muscle Shoals, AL and Clarksdale, MS, producer <strong>Ralph Carter&nbsp;</strong>directed the sessions. Classic rock lovers may know Carter from the prominence he reached early in his career as a tour musical director, bass player and song co-writer with <strong>Eddie Money</strong>. His works include the smash hit, “<strong>Shakin</strong>.” In the blues world, Carter has written, toured, recorded and produced with <strong>Sugar Ray Rayford </strong>and <strong>Franck L. Goldwasser</strong> <strong>(Paris Slim)</strong>, among others. Christopher Wyze handles lead vocals on all thirteen tracks, adding blues harp to seven of them. Other featured artists include <strong>Eric Deaton</strong> on acoustic, electric and slide guitar for <strong>Muscle Shoals </strong>tracks and <strong>Cary Hudson</strong> on electric, acoustic and slide guitars for Clarksdale tracks."},{"t":"quote","html":"“It’s truly an honor to join forces with Big Radio Records and have the chance to share our music with the world. We pour our hearts and souls into every note, and we're thrilled to have found a home where our vision can flourish.”","cite":"- Christopher Wyze of Christopher Wyze & the Tellers"},{"t":"p","html":"Deaton has been a key contributor to the Grammy-winning sound of the <strong>Black Keys</strong>, on tour and in studio, notably on their hit blues album <strong><em>Delta Kreme</em></strong>. Singer-songwriter/guitarist <strong>Cary Hudson</strong>, called <em>“a national treasure”</em> by <strong>Jason Isbell</strong>, formerly fronted the beloved rock band <strong>B</strong><strong>lue Mountain</strong>. In 2023, he was named Artist of the Year by <strong>Southland Music Line</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"‘Stuck in the Mud’ is one of three blues albums to be unveiled by Big Radio Records this summer. Wyze &amp; The Tellers also premiered the video single of ‘Stuck in the Mud’ on June 19th to coincide with the album pre-order kickoff. The full album debuts on June 21, 2024, with distribution via digital platforms, online retail outlets, and brick-and-mortar record stores by Select-O-Hits.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Music fans can sign up for release updates at: <a href=\"http://www.ChristopherWyze.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.ChristopherWyze.com</a> or visit the label <a href=\"https://www.BigRadioRecords.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.BigRadioRecords.com</a>&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Christopher Wyze &amp; The Tellers:"},{"t":"p","html":"After dreaming up songs for 15 years, <strong>Christopher Wyze </strong>is emerging as a powerful lyricist, having been named a “One to Watch” up-and-coming songwriter by Nashville Songwriters Association International in December 2023. His original outlook blends with the sounds and experiences that have shaped him: blues, rock-n-roll, Americana, and country, all melded together with Wyze’s distinctive voice and storytelling style. Born and raised in the southern hills of Indiana, Wyze has been deeply influenced by his time spent in the Mississippi Delta honing his narrative voice and musical sound. His head-turning, low bass vocals capture the essence of the South that has inspired him, lending a flint-edged honesty to the tales that unfold in his songs. &nbsp;Wyze's vignette's ebb and flow across time-frozen tales of humanity and hope, while not shying from the dark corners. Indeed, after one time through, listeners may find themselves returning in the days to come for frequent re-listens that add deeper meaning with every repeat."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Christopher Wyze &amp; The Tellers!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C8alIPSNOpK/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.bigradiorecords.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://christopherwyzeandthetellers.com/bio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/christopherwyze/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61559528035633\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.bigradiorecords.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Big Radio Records</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"331579","title":"Mae Graf is an Indie-Pop musician who is making her debut in 2024. Her music is characterized by passionate melodies and introspective lyrics, which sets her apart- drawing from personal experiences and a wide array of influences.","date":"2024-07-19","lead":"With emotional lyrics of broken promises, the single showcases Mae's heartfelt musical style.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/331579/0edce268122fa0d38351c31863387a08.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"With emotional lyrics of broken promises, the single showcases Mae's heartfelt musical style."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0cTO3TX1MQKcYVYTpw3hx4?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Shreveport, LA (July 19, 2024) - Singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7AXxTBw47UcsiM0NzHZSFz?si=Rlh-DITvTWCIWpJPcCta3A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mae Graf</strong></a> breaks new ground with her latest single, \"<a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Whatabtme\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>What abt me?</strong></a>\", which dropped on July 19, 2024, Friday. Following the success of her two singles <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Barbie\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Barbie</strong></a><strong>\"&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/32PrUWu8mV6xud2WMplIJT?si=8d04d490195a4f53\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Like Me Better This Way</strong></a><strong>\"</strong>, Graf delves into new depths of emotions of rage from a lover's betrayal that resonates easily with listeners."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Whatabtme","label":"Listen to \"What abt me?\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/665786/large-92bfbfa025073b4780831d3d4dad5fe5.png","alt":"Cover Art for \"What abt me?\""},{"t":"quote","html":"“What abt me?” Just scream it out.","cite":"- Mae Graf, Singer/songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"Graf's powerful voice in the song echoes the stylistic influences of <strong>Lacey</strong> <strong>Sturm</strong> from <strong>Flyleaf</strong> and <strong>Hayley</strong> <strong>Williams</strong> from <strong>Paramore</strong>, perfect for evoking a potent mix of unhinged emotions."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627771/large-1feefc82e080d00b0006f6f37f7716f4.jpg","alt":"DSC02763-2-_ZF-2973-88740-1-001_.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627771/preview-ac31bc9c361b243a886930017e38551a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627770/large-2db97d6637bc2925d3b4d09196d8d483.jpg","alt":"DSC02675-2-_ZF-2973-88740-1-002_.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627770/preview-efd3aef38e0da455c8647e9fb2c306d1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627773/large-5f210d04e3a392fc114ae8eec6535f9c.jpg","alt":"M10M3710.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627773/preview-9c843b7383d0e7f1f86cf4cb20e1857c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627774/large-d81cad93af586acbebe6998f9165209b.jpg","alt":"M10R3681.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627774/preview-e9eb2cf97bfa2e1bdfb736f7c09c2469.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627772/large-169874372357df560372c490a33dbb78.jpg","alt":"M10R3669.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627772/preview-902526797543383538cb346c6e36b950.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"\"<a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Whatabtme\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>What abt me?</strong></a>\" conveys a message to a lover who once filled the singer's heart with romantic fantasies of undying love, only to find another and treat them in the same manner. It stirs feelings of fury and an unrestrained desire to scream, while also weaving in the poignant ache of heartbreak, creating a deeply resonant musical experience."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7AXxTBw47UcsiM0NzHZSFz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Mae Graf:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Mae Graf</strong>’s musical journey is deeply rooted in her upbringing, where writing became her vessel for releasing emotions. From journaling to songwriting, her music reflects raw vulnerability, serving as a microscope into her soul and experiences. With a foundation built on real-life narratives, her emotionally driven melodies resonate with listeners, capturing the essence of human emotions."},{"t":"p","html":"From a young age, Mae was immersed in music, thanks to a nanny who sang and wrote songs with her. As she delved into voice lessons and school performances, her passion for music grew exponentially. Now at 15 and inspired by icons like <strong>Gracie</strong> <strong>Abrams</strong> and <strong>Taylor</strong> <strong>Swift</strong>, Mae’s raspy vocals and storytelling prowess evoke shades of <strong>Avril Lavigne</strong> and <strong>Phoebe</strong> <strong>Bridgers</strong>. Her indie-pop sound, characterized by passionate melodies and introspective lyrics, sets her apart, drawing from personal experiences and a wide array of influences. As she continues to evolve creatively, Mae Graf remains dedicated to her craft, aspiring to leave a lasting impact on the music industry.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Mae!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/lX9FTEczHZs?si=hZfGcINWngpPbQLX","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.maegrafmusic.com/","img":"","title":"Mae Graf is an Indie-Pop musician who is making her debut in 2024. Her music is characterized by passionate melodies and introspective lyrics, which sets her apart- drawing from personal experiences and a wide array of influences.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/maegrafmusic?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&amp;igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@maegrafmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@maegrafmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/people/Mae-Graf/61552522345848/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"330506","title":"Elder Grown- Funkalicious Rock'n Roots Music","date":"2024-07-13","lead":"Elder Grown's long-anticipated return is celebrated by a flurry of spectacular musical performances.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/330506/888388c8dbcc1f662f65aad575f78112.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Elder Grown's long-anticipated return is celebrated by a flurry of spectacular musical performances."},{"t":"p","html":"Aztec, NM (July 13, 2024) - <a href=\"https://eldergrownmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Elder Grown</strong></a>, the dynamic musical group, celebrated for blending genres and delivering captivating performances, joyfully unveils their eagerly awaited event: <a href=\"https://eldergrownmusic.com/summercamp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Elder Grown Summer Camp 2024</strong></a><strong>.</strong> This 2nd annual extraordinary single-night music festival will be held on Saturday, <strong>July 13th</strong>, kicking off at <strong>5:00 PM (MDT)</strong> at the scenic <a href=\"https://ticotimeresort.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tico Time River Resort</strong></a> in Aztec, New Mexico."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663044/compressed_original-65a617ad0420cc4c0029507b5f0b0d8b.png","alt":"Summer+Camp+Poster.png"},{"t":"button","href":"https://eldergrownmusic.com/summercamp","label":"Get Your Tickets NOW!","color":"#ff8888"},{"t":"p","html":"Alongside Elder Grown, get ready to be enthralled by the talents of other amazing bands such as <a href=\"https://www.desertchildmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Desert Child</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ora.band/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ora</strong></a>,<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/jcalvinmusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>J-Calvin</strong></a>, and <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/forest.thump/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Forest Thump</strong></a>! Spanning funk to folk, rock to reggae, the event offers a fresh musical flavor to suit every palate at the Elder Grown Summer Camp Music Festival."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663062/large-ccd90b92c2da8109f2d8dc3603e8c55d.jpg","alt":"EH3A2545.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663062/preview-d12884bca142299b5b6b4011869e2d3f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663063/-50aaad84a845287cd7b5497facd3c0d0.jpg","alt":"Desert+Child+2023+Promo+Photo.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663063/-50aaad84a845287cd7b5497facd3c0d0.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663059/-75482af75f5d92424e97cf665706ef46.jpg","alt":"untitled-9541.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663059/-75482af75f5d92424e97cf665706ef46.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663060/-dc8a7efc152ef3be5fb96d9c67e93643.jpg","alt":"Ora.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663060/-dc8a7efc152ef3be5fb96d9c67e93643.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663061/-8cae7392fe6a7100e1c42f48bf3c08ab.jpg","alt":"Forest+Thump.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663061/-8cae7392fe6a7100e1c42f48bf3c08ab.jpg"}]},{"t":"button","href":"https://eldergrownmusic.com/summercamp","label":"Get Your Tickets NOW!","color":"#ff8888"},{"t":"h3","html":"Single Entry Ticket + Car/Tent Camping Pass: $35.00"},{"t":"p","html":"Experience the full festival vibe by enjoying live music performances while camping in the beauty of <strong>Animas River Valley</strong>!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Single Entry Ticket (Camping not included): $30.00"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Elder Grown:"},{"t":"p","html":"Family and community are the roots of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?si=UGwB8bhlQciZIQtTL9xG3A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Elder Grown</strong></a>, a band of brothers from Durango, Colorado. They consider every audience member to be their 6th collective member, the heartbeat that fuels their music. Elder Grown is a powerful rock band featuring hip-hop forward funk &amp; soul inspired, original songs. Their improvisational jams serve as the foundation for their captivating and genre-bending music. With groovy bass lines, screaming guitar, and bold saxophone, they invite listeners on a rollercoaster ride of musical exploration."},{"t":"p","html":"Switching instruments mid-song, Elder Grown defies conventions and takes you on a journey into the unrecognizably familiar. The band has released three albums and one single so far. Their debut album, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/75sf4VsRBdfvW8EuEBqyv3?si=IHiBlRvrTsuK3_O1n5hvDQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Fire</strong> <strong>On</strong> <strong>The</strong> <strong>Way</strong></a>,\" released in 2011, an EP called \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/22Xy0KU3rMB0FH7mHhxj4c?si=9lJrbkHnQxu173yPTk9Clw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The</strong> <strong>Motorhome</strong> <strong>Mixes</strong></a>,\" released in 2014, a self-titled full-length album in 2018, and a new album to be released in the fall of 2024.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The band's origin story dates back to the early 90s when the Hoffman brothers—<strong>Joshua</strong>, <strong>John</strong>, and&nbsp;<strong>Paul</strong>—grew up in Albuquerque, New Mexico, surrounded by their father's performances as a singer-songwriter. Their passion for music grew, and after moving to Southwest Colorado, they formed Elder Grown, embracing their multifaceted musical talents.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Sam</strong> <strong>Kelly</strong>, (saxophone), joined the band during their time at Fort Lewis College. His love for saxophone and unique sound contributed to Elder Grown's evolution.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Brandon</strong> <strong>Clark</strong>, primarily a guitarist, expanded his skills to bass and keyboards to keep up with the band's instrument swapping. His love for classic rock and soulful tunes adds a creative touch to their sound."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Guillaume</strong> <strong>Metz</strong>, a professional guitarist from Paris, France, joined Elder Grown in 2019. His expertise as a lead guitarist, backup vocalist, and auxiliary bassist brought depth and richness to their performances."},{"t":"p","html":"Together, Elder Grown continues to captivate audiences with their soul-inspired sound and a commitment to pushing musical boundaries. With a new album on the horizon, they look forward to sharing their journey with their extended family of listeners."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Elder Grown!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C35rPm4ug1d/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://eldergrownmusic.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/56b56c938259b57383073e49/t/586435aabebafbe2173742ca/1482962346931/EG+Green+CircleTiny.png?format=1500w","title":"Elder Grown- Funkalicious Rock'n Roots Music","desc":"Colorado based professional funk, rock, roots, and soul band. Check Elder Grown's tour schedule and see where they're touring next."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/eldergrown\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ElderGrown/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.bandsintown.com/a/1142918?came_from=257\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>bandsintown</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"330830","title":"Neil Michael Anderson Releases Soulful Country-Rock Single, \"Say You Would\"","date":"2024-07-12","lead":"Inspired by a chance encounter with a group of travelers, Anderson’s new single captures the spirit of camaraderie and adventure.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/330830/c0aec90b69b17e349dc066029c6f6631.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Inspired by a chance encounter with a group of travelers, Anderson’s new single captures the spirit of camaraderie and adventure."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/08Timzd7huVC7j3V11yNH9?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"TRUTH OR CONSEQUENCES, NM and KANSAS CITY, MO (July 12, 2024) - Acclaimed Singer-Songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6o1vBPh6domkNIWE7b2L9A?si=kM3d3xopS6SaTsFfSCPhLA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Neil Michael Anderson</strong></a> is back with his latest single, <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/08Timzd7huVC7j3V11yNH9?si=5fc3bdd332554f99\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Say You Would</strong></a><strong>.\"</strong> This anthemic country-rock track invites listeners to embrace the joy of new friendship and the freedom of life on the road."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Say You Would\" channels <strong>The Black Crowes</strong> and <strong>Oasis</strong>, with a distinctive country twang. Following the success of <strong>\"<a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/WhatsYourTruth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">What’s Your Truth?</a>\"&nbsp;</strong>— which recently won a <strong>\"</strong><strong>Best Music Production</strong><strong>\"</strong> award at the <strong>2024 New Mexico Music Awards&nbsp;</strong>—Anderson’s new single continues to showcase his knack for blending genres and storytelling through music."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1ypdAgebhcUIGK6IdkaguV?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“I was hanging out with fellow co-producer <strong>Rob Stroup </strong>at the local brewery after a long day in the studio when we found ourselves surrounded by a group of friends who were reconnecting after being on the road. We all ate together, told stories, and made new friends. Feeling inspired, I went straight home and wrote 'Say You Would' in about 20 minutes. It’s one of those songs that comes all at once, in a flash,” </em>said Anderson."},{"t":"p","html":"With its soulful and edgy vocal delivery,<strong>&nbsp;\"Say You Would\"</strong> explores themes of love, friendship, and the allure of the open road. The track features Anderson's signature \"big sky\" sound, blending layers of electric and acoustic 12-string guitars, along with a church organ that evokes <strong>Procol Harum</strong>’s \"<strong>A Whiter Shade of Pale</strong>.\" The result is a richly textured soundscape that’s both uplifting and introspective."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/SayYouWould","label":"Listen to \"Say You Would\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/666934/large-2bbb6b0300b1b4b7175441bc4f6bd9da.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Say You Would\" by Neil Michael Anderson"},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded with a sense of immediacy, Anderson captured the song’s early emotion in just a few vocal takes. <em>“Having just written the song, I went into the living room and began recording. I could not wait to set up a vocal mike, so I just kneeled down and sang into the mic that I had set up for the guitar. I did two takes, and that was it.” </em>Anderson reflects."},{"t":"p","html":"The single features lead guitarist <strong>Chris Gennari</strong>, who adds a dynamic edge to the track, while Anderson added the large wall of rhythm guitars."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"When we finished the guitars, I told Chris it sounds like, 'If Skynyrd went to Nashville, and then Nashville went to England while flying 8 miles high,\"</em> Anderson said."},{"t":"p","html":"The track was produced and written by <strong>Neil Michael Anderson</strong> with co-production by <strong>Rob Stroup</strong>. The master was provided by <strong>Ed Brooks (Pearl Jam, Death Cab for Cutie, Fleet Foxes)</strong>."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Praise for Neil Michael Anderson:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>The previous single… \"What’s Your Truth?\" not only captivates with its catchy melodies but also challenges listeners to engage in introspection, making it a compelling piece that encourages a deeper understanding of self and the world around us.\"</em><br id=\"isPasted\"><strong>– Natalie Patrick, EARMILK</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"The addictive hooks and layered instrumentation offer something new with each play, while the introspective lyrics invite reflection.\"</em><br id=\"isPasted\"><strong>– Darryl Sterdan, TINNITIST</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"With a vibe that channels the easy-going spirit of The Eagles’ “Take It Easy” and the camaraderie of the Traveling Wilburys’ “End of the Line,” Anderson delivers an optimistic message that cuts straight to the heart.\"</em><br id=\"isPasted\"><strong>– KINDLINE MAGAZINE</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"Neil’s lead vocals soar over a rich tapestry of 12-string guitars and Hammond organs, punctuated by poignant lead guitar riffs.\"</em><br id=\"isPasted\"><strong>– Zohaib Chishti, VENTS MAGAZINE</strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Neil Michael Anderson:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://neilmichaelanderson.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Neil Michael Anderson</strong></a> is a singer-songwriter, with a 12-string guitar and a suitcase in hand. From country-rock anthems to big sky power ballads, Neil covers a lot of ground."},{"t":"p","html":"A poet by nature, Neil’s music is known for its deep and enigmatic lyrics, set to verse-chorus anthems, epic power ballads, and poetic art songs that tell a story. Sonically, Neil’s music is a melting pot of genres, blending folk-rock, country-rock, power ballads, psychedelic rock, ambient, and shoegaze, with the occasional accent of medieval troubadours, and Indian ragas."},{"t":"p","html":"Neil has collaborated with various artists, including <strong>The Sunwrecks</strong>, and occasional sit-ins with <strong>The Consequences</strong>. He won a “<strong>Best Music Production Award</strong>” at the 2024 New Mexico Music Awards, and will soon release a debut album. Stay tuned!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Neil Anderson!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/neilmichaelanderson/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@neilmichaelanderson","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://neilmichaelanderson.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/neilmichaelanderson\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/people/Neil-Michael-Anderson/pfbid0sXvdrKjBNr36TpEhde2f7yx6rqzvAVuz4vxDv57iuWsZwcD4cXVHipWvAYg7jWa7l/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"331530","title":"Team You. Out June 21. Wildlife Control blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: it doesnʼt matter if sheʼs analog or digital.","date":"2024-07-12","lead":"Wildlife Control’s latest single resembles Tom Petty meets Coldplay.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/331530/1170c5716af810e96d5a339bca22bc5d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Wildlife Control’s latest single resembles Tom Petty meets Coldplay."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/16DFdSffOQzKc5OD5OvPep?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>New York, NY</strong> (July 12, 2024) - NYC-based <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2f2Bf7TxY9xWWbTETxtPnP?si=ouuqM-tQRASjjg4Rcf65CQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wildlife Control</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>drops their third single in as many months with “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/16DFdSffOQzKc5OD5OvPep?si=fb7a0cd3da51439a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dream Dream Dream My Friend</strong></a>” - an uplifting track that looks back stylistically to timeless rock songwriting while looking forward with sonic textures that impart hope and optimism. Featuring a chorus of rich harmonies, the song grows from a simple guitar riff into an alt-pop stomp, with a brass ensemble and melodic bass lines in the bridge. It’s a song about dreaming big and never losing hope."},{"t":"p","html":"Also announced today via Wildlife Control’s mailing list are details of their rumored new album, <em><strong>Love</strong></em>.<em><strong>&nbsp;Champion. Mountain. King.</strong></em>, to be released on September 20, 2024."},{"t":"button","href":"https://wildlifectrl.com/dreamdreamdreammyfriend","label":"Listen to \"Dream Dream Dream My Friend\"","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Pre-orders on vinyl, CD, and digital are available at <a href=\"https://wildlifectrl.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>wildlifectrl.com</strong></a>."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/663594/large-b5f3631336ee2c3ba2e3b8d3e691c44b.jpg","alt":"wildlife-control-dream-dream-dream-my-friend-cover-2400.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Beauty and poetry in harmony and chords.”<br></em>– <strong>Curtis Silver</strong>, <strong>WIRED</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Wildlife Control is youthful yet insightful. It feels like lying by a pool you broke into, young and drunk, next to someone you loved while looking at the stars knowing in your heart the world has a f*** ton more in store for you.”<br></em>– <strong>Sophie Saint Thomas</strong>, <strong>VICE</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Lace up your sneakers and get ready to hit the ground running with ‘Team You.’ Wildlife Control has crafted a track that’s an experience.” &nbsp; &nbsp;</em><br><em>​</em>– <strong>Natalie Patrick</strong>, <strong>EARMILK</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Wildlife Control are writing classics. “Analog or Digital” is vaguely Ramones, vaguely Phoenix, wholly a triumph in rock that might be considered indie, and entirely awesome. It's a must listen.”</em><br>– <strong>Rachel Skotarczyk</strong>, <strong>INDIE SHUFFLE</strong>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2f2Bf7TxY9xWWbTETxtPnP?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Wildlife Control:"},{"t":"p","html":"Grammy-nominated musician and producer, <a href=\"https://wildlifectrl.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wildlife Control</strong></a> (they/them), records and tours solo, duo, and with collaborators globally. They helped establish the New York shimmer pop sound in the early 2010s with their critically acclaimed eponymous debut album, which was the #1 self-released album on the <strong>NACC/CMJ Radio 200&nbsp;</strong>chart. The artist has sold out headlining shows at <strong>Mercury Lounge</strong> in New York City and <strong>Bottom of the Hill</strong> in San Francisco, and played featured slots at <strong>SXSW</strong>, <strong>Bottlerock</strong>, and the <strong>CMJ Music Marathon</strong>. Wildlife Control’s innovative videos have garnered praise from <strong>WIRED&nbsp;</strong>and comparisons to groups like <strong>OK Go</strong> and <strong>Arcade Fire</strong>. Combining their indie rock sound with time-lapse and stop motion photography, the music video for the artist’s debut single “<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=boGyFAYomBo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Analog or Digital</strong></a>” went viral with over 450k views."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Wildlife Control!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/WcjUrJg9t4s?si=isxt7w5abjqGIW5J","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://wildlifectrl.com/","img":"","title":"Team You. Out June 21. Wildlife Control blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: it doesnʼt matter if sheʼs analog or digital.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCL3hF3eJdMBBvEnLLquputA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/wildlifecontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/wildlifecontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"336163","title":"Loki Moon","date":"2024-07-05","lead":"Exploring themes of self-discovery and cosmic love with its blend of electro-acoustic alt-pop.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/336163/05d7655a3dd33c12dfa868b3d9445432.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Exploring themes of self-discovery and cosmic love with its blend of electro-acoustic alt-pop."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7kqHJy932pRqinWA7y2xlc?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"DENVER, CO (September 26, 2024) - <strong>Loki Moon</strong>, the electro-acoustic, alt-pop duo, invites listeners on a journey through consciousness, self-reflection, and inter-dimensional love with their debut self-titled EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7kqHJy932pRqinWA7y2xlc?si=C8zTdsamTNms9XOU9xXMcw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Loki Moon</em></strong></a>."},{"t":"p","html":"The EP delves into themes of conscious awareness, growth and acceptance across its four tracks, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1IQZFTU3KmWNWHAiaYHP7f?si=c069ba2fa21141ac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Alone</strong></a>,\" \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/17wWJc5EjVVB1wYXWq64t2?si=1a56d69a4e3646b1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sleepwalker</strong></a>,\" \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2THQI2jyGlvqp6dkdw7rRM?si=6b0d7f70c3ff461e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>UFO</strong></a>,\" and \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/72kgPXx9zSzaUU586V1IL8?si=f597e4c4a54d473c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Chameleon</strong></a>.\" Offering a small glimpse into the etheric worlds that Loki Moon inhabits, and a springboard for what's to come, the EP demonstrates their seamless genre transitions and ability to retain their fundamental, authentic sound. Exploring what it means to truly reflect on oneself, as well as how that individual chooses to move within the collective, it asks,<em>&nbsp;\"What path will you choose?\"</em>."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/LokiMoon","label":"Listen to \"Loki Moon\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/649338/large-6dd527c444a26f3a5719e7d4dd82e458.png","alt":"Cover art for 'Loki Moon' by J Lambert Film"},{"t":"h3","html":"Track Highlights:"},{"t":"p","html":"\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1IQZFTU3KmWNWHAiaYHP7f?si=c069ba2fa21141ac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Alone</a>\" – With its haunting lyrics and evocative instrumentation, this track explores the nuances of conflict and resolution. The ethereal guitar solo and layered vocals create a sense of burning intensity and introspective dialogue."},{"t":"p","html":"\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/17wWJc5EjVVB1wYXWq64t2?si=1a56d69a4e3646b1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sleepwalker</a>\" – &nbsp;A captivating journey through metaphysical realms, \"Sleepwalker\" reflects on the overstimulation of the mind and the quest for clarity, exploring themes of social constructs, relationships, and internal struggles. The repetitive, mantra-like chorus, combined with a hypnotic melody, makes this track a standout.<br id=\"isPasted\"><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">"},{"t":"p","html":"\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2THQI2jyGlvqp6dkdw7rRM?si=6b0d7f70c3ff461e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">UFO</a>\" – Blending cosmic imagery with ethereal sounds, \"UFO\" transports listeners to another galaxy, reflecting on love, consciousness, and the mysteries beyond our everyday reality. The song's dreamy lyrics and intricate instrumental layers offer a mesmerizing exploration of spirituality and the human experience."},{"t":"p","html":"\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/72kgPXx9zSzaUU586V1IL8?si=f597e4c4a54d473c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Chameleon</a>\" – With its playful and introspective lyrics, \"Chameleon\" addresses the fluid nature of identity and love. The track’s minimalist arrangement and poignant vocals underscore the duo’s philosophical musings."},{"t":"p","html":"The EP features notable collaborators including <strong>Nathan Schramm</strong> (Björk, Sting, James Blake, Joshua Bell, David Crosby, Attica Quartet) on violin and viola for \"Alone,\" <strong>Ryan Christopher Imboden</strong> on Moog for both \"Sleepwalker\" and \"UFO\", and <strong>Damian Diaz</strong> (Trees Speak) on Moog and Mellotron for \"UFO\". Loki Moon is also mixed and mastered by a collective of engineers including <strong>Davis Ryan Jones</strong>, <strong>Pete Maher</strong> (The Pixies, Lana Del Rey, Jack White, Goldfrapp), <strong>Shawn Joseph</strong> (Johnny Greenwood, PJ Harvey, J Dilla, Black Coffee, Charles Mingus, Portishead, Trees Speak), and&nbsp;<strong>Dave Rowland</strong> (Ms Lauryn Hill, Travi$ Scott, Desiigner, Post Malone, Ellie Goulding, The-Dream, J Balvin)."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Loki Moon:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0860Nym6xJwvClvnx1bsVv?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Loki Moon</strong> is the trickster who dances in light and bathes in the dark - a polarity dressed in lullabies. An alt-R&amp;B electro-acoustic duo that brings forth an ethereal, percussive soundscape that explores that which is mystical and existential.... while still keeping an air of anonymity. Their music is ageless - speaking to the road less-traveled types - the wanderers, the outcasts."},{"t":"p","html":"Influenced by world music - a la Ethiopian jazz, music from the Sahara, and Japanese minimalist music - Loki Moon creates an immersive auditory experience that subjects listeners to explore their own subconscious. Born out of their connection over esoterism, and ideological and philosophical chemistry and perspective, the ever-evolving dialogue of their lyrics has been described as “<em>...strange, beautiful, and in its own right, a novel</em>” (<strong>-PopMatters</strong>)."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Loki Moon!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C8cUgIkuFU5/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.lokimoon.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/5a8482c912abd910ddfc8877/t/65bd3c8fed40f3361b93f80e/1706900623337/J.jpg?format=1500w","title":"Loki Moon","desc":"Mood & Color. Loki Moon is the trickster who dances in light and bathes in the dark \"...Strange, beautiful and in its own right, novel\" - Pop Matters, Chicago."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lokimoonmusic/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://facebook.com/lokimoonmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://tiktok.com/@lokimoonmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCpHZLZY5NwM-99px-3b8_Fw/xregexp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"327035","title":"Aidan Leclaire Band to Headline Pearl Street Warehouse on July 3rd","date":"2024-07-03","lead":"Showcasing two new singles, \"Control\" and \"The Kids Are Talking\" from their upcoming sophomore album, \"Spaceman.\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/327035/c166b76c9e7338a421ab882290166935.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Showcasing two new singles, \"Control\" and \"The Kids Are Talking\" from their upcoming sophomore album, \"Spaceman.\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7uELn8jkSItyKqdqblAV0W?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"WASHINGTON (July 3, 2024) - The <a href=\"https://aidanleclaire.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aidan Leclaire Band</strong></a> will be spotlighted at <a href=\"https://www.pearlstreetwarehouse.com/tm-event/aidan-leclaire-band/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Pearl Street Warehouse</strong></a> on July 3rd, 2024. This highly anticipated show is to be a major highlight of the summer, celebrating the release of their sophomore album, “<strong>Spaceman</strong>,” which released on July 1, 2024. The show will also debut their new singles, “<strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1B7al9xt18P7XCbjabgPCv?si=d431164eff3f4d30\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Control</a></strong>”<strong>&nbsp;</strong>and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7uELn8jkSItyKqdqblAV0W?si=19f3bd014ac44750\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Kids Are Talking</strong></a>,” the latter released on June 17th."},{"t":"p","html":"<u><strong>Event Details</strong></u><strong>:</strong>"},{"t":"list","items":["<strong>Date:</strong> July 3, 2024","<strong>Venue:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.pearlstreetwarehouse.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pearl Street Warehouse</a>, 33 Pearl Street, SW, Washington D.C. 20024","<strong>Doors Open:</strong> 8 PM","<strong>Tickets: </strong>$18. Available at <a href=\"https://www.ticketweb.com/event/aidan-leclaire-band-w-argo-pearl-street-warehouse-tickets/13394964?REFID=clientsitewp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TicketWeb</a>"]},{"t":"p","html":"Fans can expect to hear these new singles live for the first time, along with other tracks from the highly anticipated “Spaceman” album. The show will also feature performances by local favorites Argo and the Violet Queen, setting the stage for an unforgettable night of music."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>New Releases</u>:</strong>"},{"t":"list","items":["“Control” - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1B7al9xt18P7XCbjabgPCv?si=9a1d08732b9141ef\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Listen on Spotify</a>","“The Kids Are Talking” - OUT NOW - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5XIAMgrXD7A6z6iwH7LxCQ?si=aACHwA2rQu6h0Ya_7rMjZQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Listen on Spotify</a>"]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Aidan Leclaire Band:"},{"t":"p","html":"Formed by a group of passionate musicians from the Virginia and Washington D.C. areas, and led by the charismatic <strong>Aidan Leclaire</strong>, the <strong>Aidan Leclaire Band</strong> has quickly become a standout act in the local music scene. Known for its unique blend of indie-rock, folk, and pop, their music, characterized by playful yet heartfelt lyrics and captivating melodies, has resonated deeply with audiences across the East Coast and beyond."},{"t":"p","html":"Their debut album was a critical success, leading to a series of performances at prestigious venues in NYC, Boston, and Washington D.C., and a growing fanbase. With new music on the horizon, the band is poised to reach even greater heights."},{"t":"p","html":"For more information about the <a href=\"https://aidanleclaire.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Aidan Leclaire Band</a>’s other upcoming shows and music, visit their website and follow them on <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/aidanleclairemusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a>, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCf-C9Au5-RM3bdQNqmW7WHA/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>, and <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/aidanleclairemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@aidanleclairemusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCf-C9Au5-RM3bdQNqmW7WHA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://aidanleclaire.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"332263","title":"Aidan Leclaire Band Launches into Orbit with \"The Spaceman\"","date":"2024-07-01","lead":"The band's eagerly awaited second album, performed live, is now accessible to enthusiastic fans and listeners to experience.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/332263/578ae5da4e739627bf89326dcd51d2c7.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The band's eagerly awaited second album, performed live, is now accessible to enthusiastic fans and listeners to experience."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3jVnrl0wSEsvdfsfyBxjZ8?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Vienna, VA (July 1, 2024) - Genre-bending <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR?si=AOgLXdj8T3W6EEMWrWxV-w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aidan Leclaire Band</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>invites listeners to experience a cosmic journey with their latest album, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3jVnrl0wSEsvdfsfyBxjZ8?si=u6rZ9NWRS7Kvvuy7ElsSYg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Spaceman</strong></a>\", released on July 1, 2024. The 6-track album includes recent singles from the band like \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7uELn8jkSItyKqdqblAV0W?si=c826b424919f4815\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The</strong> <strong>Kids</strong> <strong>are Talking</strong></a>\" and \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1B7al9xt18P7XCbjabgPCv?si=e6a3e0e5e11c491f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Control</strong></a>,\" both of which have individually achieved significant success with thousands of streams within a short period."},{"t":"p","html":"The music is filled with angst, conveying a profound sense of confusion and uncertainty akin to feeling \"lost in space.\" It seamlessly blends elements from <strong>Nirvana</strong>, <strong>Weezer</strong>, <strong>Vampire</strong> <strong>Weekend</strong>, and <strong>Arcade</strong> <strong>Fire</strong>, resulting in a harmonious intergenerational fusion of musical styles."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/664117/compressed_original-c9d08678bba09f18fb3fe0bbb5bedeca.webp","alt":"Cover art for \"The Spaceman\""},{"t":"quote","html":"\"The Spaceman\" is an album that poignantly captures a generation's uncertainty, ambiguity, and angst, as well as the weight of the previous generation's actions. It delves deep into the collective consciousness, exploring the complex emotions of those striving to find their place in a world marked by inherited burdens.","cite":"- Aiden Leclaire Band"},{"t":"p","html":"Among its standout pieces is \"<strong>Blue</strong>,\" a bossa nova-sounding lounge-inspired melody that delves into the melancholic beauty of unfulfilled love, evoking a sense of longing and introspection.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Another highlight, \"<strong>Control</strong>,\" captures the uncertainty of not having a clear direction in life, its ethereal soundscapes painting a picture of drifting aimlessly through the vast expanse of existence. The album's titular track, \"<strong>Orbiting</strong>,\" completes the journey with its cosmic themes, inviting listeners to traverse through the boundless reaches of space, finding solace in its mysteries."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Aidan Leclaire Band:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1nuTrJzXtkxgTAWe4kutGR?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Formed by a group of passionate musicians from the Virginia and Washington D.C. areas, and led by the charismatic <strong>Aidan</strong> <strong>Leclaire</strong>, the <strong>Aidan</strong> <strong>Leclaire</strong> <strong>Band</strong> has quickly become a standout act in the local music scene. Known for its unique blend of indie-rock, folk, and pop, their music, characterized by playful yet heartfelt lyrics and captivating melodies, has resonated deeply with audiences across the East Coast and beyond."},{"t":"p","html":"Their debut album was a critical success, leading to a series of performances at prestigious venues in NYC, Boston, and Washington D.C., and a growing fanbase. With new music on the horizon, the band is poised to reach even greater heights."},{"t":"p","html":"For more information about the Aidan Leclaire Band’s other upcoming shows and music, visit their website and follow them on Instagram, YouTube, and Spotify."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Aidan Leclaire!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/uMwtWiNUvKU?si=IZVlcgh-CZMMvIT5","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/aidanleclairemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@aidanleclairemusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCf-C9Au5-RM3bdQNqmW7WHA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://aidanleclaire.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@aidanleclairemusic?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"323961","title":"Jacob McCurdy's \"Trouble\" Chronicles a Journey of Resilience and Hope","date":"2024-06-29","lead":"With raw emotion and unwavering honesty, Jacob McCurdy's latest single offers listeners a glimpse into his transformative journey.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/323961/0b0a917478014e00afd09a5f1d424b5a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"With raw emotion and unwavering honesty, Jacob McCurdy's latest single offers listeners a glimpse into his transformative journey."},{"t":"p","html":"<sub>Content Warning: Details about stroke are incorporated herein. Reader's discretion is advised.</sub>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6koo7na0MNFaiS2NRan6YW?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Portland, ME (June 29, 2024) — Indie-Americana artist, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0yA6Qdw3Ntzr0zhAo7T5Yx?si=6LemW6PIQ2u-EjRBqaKg5w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Jacob McCurdy</strong></a>, returned with a soul-stirring release, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Trouble\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Trouble</strong></a><strong>”&nbsp;</strong>on June 21st, released with a music video on June 29th, following a year of personal challenges and triumphs. Blending elements of indie pop and folk rock, McCurdy’s newest single digs into themes of resilience and hope in the face of adversity."},{"t":"p","html":"With heartfelt, poignant lyricism and infectious melodies, “Trouble” encapsulates McCurdy’s signature sound while offering a raw and introspective exploration of personal struggle.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Trouble","label":"Listen to \"Trouble\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/WkEHHagQpBU?si=194G1bbImy54vBJ7","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"A year ago, while shooting the cover art for “Trouble,” the artist suffered an ischemic stroke caused by <strong>Fibromuscular Dysplasia</strong>. Thanks to his girlfriend, <strong>Hannah Jenkins'</strong> quick action, his life was saved. Despite initially insisting he was fine, he realized he had significant weakness on his left side. After a few days in the hospital, he was discharged with activity restrictions. Gradually, he regained strength and started playing guitar and singing again, although his left hand was still <em>troubled</em> a year later."},{"t":"p","html":"McCurdy’s latest release is a testament to his perseverance and artistic growth. The song invites listeners to join him on his journey of self-discovery and healing.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"\"Co-writing these songs has been like therapy for me. I think writing them helped me get through a break-up, a pandemic, and my own anxiety.\"","cite":"- Indie-Americana artist, Jacob McCurdy"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>\"Trouble\" LYRICS (SNEAK PEAK)</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"Just like a kick in my throat"},{"t":"p","html":"I might be out for a long time"},{"t":"p","html":"I’m dropping down like gravity"},{"t":"p","html":"Until there’s nothing left inside of me"},{"t":"p","html":"​-"},{"t":"p","html":"I’m at the end of the road"},{"t":"p","html":"We’ve been standing here a long time"},{"t":"p","html":"Motionless in the left lane"},{"t":"p","html":"While the dotted lines run back"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"Co-written with a talented group of musicians, including <strong>Mike Maurice</strong>, <strong>Jordan Brooks</strong> and <strong>Alex Calabrese</strong>, “Trouble” emerged from late-night jam sessions and collaborative songwriting sessions. The result is a captivating musical journey that resonates with authenticity, vulnerability and hope for the future as Jacob McCurdy continues to solidify his place in the indie music scene. Additionally, McCurdy will be cycling 100 miles throughout June in support of the <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/donate/1197647681613715\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>American Heart Association</strong></a>."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656608/large-fb975d14de4dc6bbca099a794074374f.jpg","alt":"big-15.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656608/preview-7ad86c85cb414e274d9d211ebe51361d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656609/large-36fa1f7b91c5cc41d91aab87cd6db28a.jpg","alt":"big-16.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656609/preview-85ea42454f9ec0c644b2d900a47de654.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656610/large-2c5507512aba90bdd278b1bc41fdf588.jpg","alt":"big-17.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656610/preview-c45989acb6c0617a39b6145a0ee8813f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656611/large-4d6446968a615dbd743dd70f826d913d.jpg","alt":"big-14.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656611/preview-6ba96420a8eb320812cac98f34966078.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656612/large-703f90ed49bacc5bd2ff8accbcf575ab.jpg","alt":"big-12.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656612/preview-d12be88164d1e19d87345a49f1f78ebe.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656613/large-b1bd9df6acf3f2948bf031bc5c8a5027.jpg","alt":"big-13.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656613/preview-c4a5ef62f45037f2607eec8c33087d48.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656614/large-144839c950cd8436cfb8fa38cdb8f39f.jpg","alt":"big-03.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656614/preview-47d086787fae5973ad46130e42a8db11.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photo Credit Hannah Jenkins"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0yA6Qdw3Ntzr0zhAo7T5Yx?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Jacob McCurdy:"},{"t":"p","html":"Mustachioed Mainer,<strong>&nbsp;Jacob McCurdy</strong>, blends folk, rock, and roots into his very own brand of indie-americana. McCurdy wears his heart on his sleeve, captivating audiences with honest lyricism and soulful melodies. Through collaborative songwriting and a commitment to authenticity, he shares his songs with the hope that others can heal from his experiences and enjoy a glimpse of what the future might bring."},{"t":"p","html":"McCurdy’s musical journey began with the debut of his first album in 2011. What started as a senior project recording an album for an artist, turned into an opportunity for McCurdy himself to step into the spotlight. Collaborating with his best friend and roommate, <strong>Adam Hanson</strong>, McCurdy spent Christmas break crafting a record that would kickstart his artistic exploration."},{"t":"p","html":"Fast-forwarding through nine years of fronting his wedding band, <strong>The Dapper Gents</strong>, McCurdy released <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/23kKmC9fcJbIz0PNEaxEO8?si=D5B9-PfdQ82jLY6qmbLanA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">For the Weekend (FTW)</a>”</strong> on July 24, 2020. This EP significantly shifted McCurdy’s musical journey, drawing from deeper life experiences and heartaches. Subsequent releases, such as “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7y4JDY7Yy0ZiPQWEarIzRQ?si=ydiBIJkgReGzsj6ATV2q-A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ready to Fall</strong></a>,” “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7ETqIpeHBPUXk21TpO4yOH?si=mPssdbmCTqmUPultrQhzRQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Make a Fuss</strong></a>,” “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1MR3OYvgorVgSfJfdgiiN4?si=OgFBVB20TZaMNKeX5Ho4Ig\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Feels Like Home</strong></a>,” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4yNGaYfvRtIDFzkBU7mbS5?si=0T_dqDzWTsGy9fKlbjPXLg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Out On The Run</strong></a>,” have showcased McCurdy’s growth as an artist, delving into themes of resilience, gratitude, and inner turmoil.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"McCurdy continues solidifying his place in the indie music scene, inviting listeners into his journey of love, heartbreak, and self-discovery, hoping to create music that resonates on a profound level."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Jacob McCurdy!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/mjfgTjzxsTA?si=HaUOnn97jpjPDizF","height":"315"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@jacobmccurdymusic/video/7375643239938002222","handle":"@jacobmccurdymusic"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/C6HtAzxrrH2/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://jacobmccurdymusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://linktr.ee/jacobmccurdy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Linktree</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/jacobmccurdymusicpage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a></strong><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCckZjnRuCPUMK-T2dqyN6-A/featured\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"329757","title":"Quan Pablo Conquers Adversity with \"No Turning Back\"","date":"2024-06-29","lead":"The album reflects Quan's personal experiences, showcasing the strength of resilience and faith through lyrical artistry.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/329757/e83b3b9e6cbf8f74bfab8e36b146144a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The album reflects Quan's personal experiences, showcasing the strength of resilience and faith through lyrical artistry."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0kEXXpBSTjMUOQlV4zHmPL?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Savannah, GA (June 29, 2024) - Hip Hop artist, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7BVCrDEyhLX3KrTXJSmvyn?si=-QKoLZxkTieifTdGA_iV3Q&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=7e97640db3b547e2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Quan Pablo</strong></a> makes waves with his latest album “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0kEXXpBSTjMUOQlV4zHmPL?si=rLCsOpcEQdKh2wAdwdqjfg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>No Turning Back</strong></a>.” The album is shaped by Quan Pablo’s personal pain, lessons learned, and growth challenges."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Never give up on you. Always keep faith in God. Go hard until your last breath.”","cite":"- Quan Pablo"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/661862/compressed_original-c85942f40be51bc79439444ae3d383dc.webp","alt":"Cover Art for \"No Turning Back\""},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/662761/large-436bdcaee2b4bd7caba2b5f9a5dbc4b9.jpg","alt":"IMG_20210615_164126809.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/662761/preview-fde2d82d33786ad3bba3966d9a131f97.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/662762/large-f8c2dce3f5fa55a4fd73f9778c090f1b.jpg","alt":"IMG_20210619_080155823_HDR.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/662762/preview-7f7ca2a214ad080d4ab0b6a0c8cf84b5.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Quan’s lyrics highlight the value of maintaining patience and faith in God, even when success appears out of reach. “No Turning Back” revolves around the theme of personal development, never thinking you’re too old to improve by setting goals to change your life, and appreciating people who loved and believed in you."},{"t":"p","html":"Quan tells a story of determination and belief through his album, but also embracing failures and taking advice to be a stronger, better version of oneself."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7BVCrDEyhLX3KrTXJSmvyn?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Quan Pablo:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7BVCrDEyhLX3KrTXJSmvyn?si=L3e4CF35TpWaVmnJ_oa7Nw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Quan Pablo</strong></a> grew up in Savannah, Georgia, starting to rap at the age of 12. Even as a child, he harbored a deep love for music, nurtured by the songs he heard in church and his mother’s melodies while she cooked. However, he found himself drawn to the streets, where trouble awaited him, leading to repeated encounters with jail and causing anguish for those who cared about him.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Eventually, the streets became his harsh reality, shaping him through pain into a person of strength and wisdom. Overcoming adversity became his hallmark, strengthened by his unwavering faith in God, believing that with faith, one can always find a way out.<br><br>Through his music, Quan Pablo is determined to inspire people, emphasizing that regardless of circumstances or challenges, anyone can rise as an underdog and achieve victory. His message encourages belief in oneself and perseverance, urging listeners to never lose hope and always strive for success."},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"322122","title":"Aaron Bleiweiss Slows Down with \"Speed of Light\"","date":"2024-06-28","lead":"The latest single from the upcoming album, 'Twists and Turns' sees Bleiweiss embracing the present.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/322122/ea5e5531fbc7b02ad74b56566fa7707d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The latest single from the upcoming album, 'Twists and Turns' sees Bleiweiss embracing the present."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0YkfjEL12dlGB30PJHvLpi?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"San Diego, CA (June 28, 2024) - Singer/songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4wCUNgnbe2VSv6m8Nr51VS?si=6J0cVQKiR5e-3Sdz-5i5iw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aaron Bleiweiss</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>entices listeners to make every second count with <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0YkfjEL12dlGB30PJHvLpi?si=d1ae0787def7491b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Speed of Light</strong></a>”, the first from his 11-track album<em>&nbsp;</em><strong><em>Twists and Turns</em></strong>. Inspired by the vibrant energy of the city’s bustling streets during his stint in The Big Apple, Aaron channels his reflections and adventures into a dynamic fusion of funk, pop, and rock melodies."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/656076/large-5c39fe2fff1e9d0705ba41b8227003f1.jpg","alt":"Cover art for upcoming album 'Twists and Turns'"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Remember it’s OK to slow down, catch your breath, and take it all in. It’s easy to get blinded by the pace of life and miss some of the best moments that are happening right before your eyes.”","cite":"- Aaron Bleiweiss"},{"t":"p","html":"Purposely fused with an eclectic blend of vintage 70’s funk grooves and modern electronic exploration, “Speed of Light” takes on how things in life go by so fast. It serves as a much-needed reminder to embrace the present moment with a gentle pace, allowing yourself to breathe deeply and immerse in the richness of experiences, noticing the beauty in the seemingly mundane and finding joy in the simplest of things."},{"t":"p","html":"With its guitar-driven, jazz-infused harmonies and breezy rhythms, “Speed of Light” effortlessly lifts spirits. Featuring a range of talented collaborators, this delightful track promises broad appeal, making it a superb addition to any relaxed, feel-good playlist."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4wCUNgnbe2VSv6m8Nr51VS?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Aaron Bleiweiss:"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654631/large-e625422aeff46742061399a574e72edb.jpeg","alt":"HVUvAKiY.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654631/preview-fc3eafcb7eec7356999966d77b5de14a.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654628/large-1e260b927f85ee021a8ae8f0de282884.jpeg","alt":"8gUKCCfB.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654628/preview-b9513cbf17e58026d7c6af3915075e2b.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654627/large-65b6bf53a9882bc02d76cf05fc8a52c7.jpeg","alt":"Mjf4Kcsm.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654627/preview-c1367f762e79024ed896dffa54b934fc.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654632/large-414f3cfb15248915905c45663dd59d20.jpeg","alt":"P81ofwOn.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/654632/preview-9a21e8b7fa98cbed19e3720ccc8e4013.jpeg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4wCUNgnbe2VSv6m8Nr51VS?si=CV-GaCrrQOiA7kHdpsyTLQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aaron Bleiweiss</strong></a> is a guitarist, producer, and singer/songwriter currently based in San Diego, CA. By fusing guitar heavy funk rock with soulful pop and blues, he creates a classic sound that pays homage to the past while still sounding vital and edgy in the modern world.<br><br>A native of Seattle, WA, Aaron was naturally drawn to the grunge and alternative rock that the Pacific Northwest is famous for. When he moved to Los Angeles to attend the&nbsp;<strong>Musician’s Institute</strong>, he developed an ear for the vintage soul and blues music that would define his style as a guitarist. After graduating, he toured the US, spending several years on the road before settling down in Brooklyn to pursue a solo career. The diversity and electric energy of New York can be clearly heard in Aaron’s solo work.&nbsp;<br><br>Working as a solo artist for the first time, he is confident yet introspective, as he expresses his thoughts about the journey life has taken him on. Entitled <strong><em>Twists and Turns</em></strong>, Aaron’s new album is slated for release this September. With each track, Aaron invites listeners on a journey through the winding paths and unexpected detours of life. In the meantime, Aaron is self-releasing a series of singles, providing a glimpse into the sonic tapestry that awaits within <em>Twists and Turns</em>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Aaron!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/7zkXzI2KuJ0?si=pDbOeLl-Htgl2GRX","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C8flNTpStKG/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/AaronBleiweissMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/aaronbleiweiss/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCPRg9gQgI0pSE5Qw2LuAzpw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"328243","title":"Keep For Cheap Unveils New Single, \"FedEx,\" from Upcoming Album, \"Big Grass\"","date":"2024-06-27","lead":"Inspired by a tour misfortune-turned-lesson, \"FedEx\" navigates life’s complexities with authenticity and resilience.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/328243/beeee5954cf8030b86b670238256d8c3.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Inspired by a tour misfortune-turned-lesson, \"FedEx\" navigates life’s complexities with authenticity and resilience."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3R8wiWafUIRMVbsb2daOfd?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"MINNEAPOLIS (June 27, 2024) - Emerging from the heart of the Midwest with their unique “prairie-rock” sound, <a href=\"https://www.keepforcheap.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Keep For Cheap</strong></a> announces the release of their latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3R8wiWafUIRMVbsb2daOfd?si=79ab429e92e64322\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FedEx</strong></a>,” now available on all streaming platforms. This release is a taste of their highly anticipated sophomore album, “<strong>Big Grass</strong>,” set to debut in August 2024."},{"t":"p","html":"“FedEx” tells the personal story of a girl navigating life in today’s hypocritical America, still searching for the wonder in everything. Inspired by a real-life tour incident involving a FedEx truck mishap in North Dakota, the song serves as a poignant commentary on the challenges of life, particularly as openly queer artists in today’s complex sociopolitical climate."},{"t":"p","html":"“FedEx” offers a stream-of-consciousness look into touring rural America as a visibly queer artist, capturing the need to endure both covert and overt judgment. The song addresses recent discriminatory legislation and the lack of safety for queer, particularly trans, people in the US. Its intense, driving energy reflects the anxiety surrounding the rise of fascism and xenophobia in recent years. Amid this fear, however, lies a determination to stay open to experience and keep searching for humanity's beauty and wonder."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660204/large-549730d2429cbf322b4ff8a57e897ad4.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"FexEx\" by Keep For Cheap"},{"t":"p","html":"Fronting members <strong>Autumn </strong>and <strong>Kate</strong>, whose musical synergy began in the alto section of their college choir in 2017, infuse “FedEx” with their trademark mix of playful and heart-wrenching elements. The track’s lyrics delve into themes of systemic discrimination, the search for wonder amidst chaos, and the resilient spirit of those who dare to live authentically."},{"t":"button","href":"https://recordu.lnk.to/FedEx","label":"Listen to \"FedEx\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Keep For Cheap’s upcoming 9-track album “Big Grass” promises to be an emotional rollercoaster, with “FedEx” setting the tone. Their previous single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4f34m2WKY7CAiwGWTcNdG8?si=0c509765eadb49d1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lakehouse</strong></a>,” released in September 2023, also features in the album, showcasing the group’s growth and the depth of their musical and lyrical exploration."},{"t":"p","html":"The band, known for their energetic live performances and authentic storytelling, has shared the stage with notable artists such as <strong>Beach Bunny</strong>, <strong>Remo Drive</strong>, <strong>Boyish</strong>, <strong>Bad Bad Hats</strong>, <strong>The Greeting Committee</strong>, <strong>Gully Boys</strong>, and <strong>Miloe</strong>. Midwesterners can look forward to a local album release show this September, with additional Midwest tour dates to be announced soon."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660205/large-ed575f51adf876a0c33425216e9ba2b2.jpg","alt":"DSC_4389.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660205/preview-49fea7a52618fe5511e46ac0e96de0b6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660206/large-e205fc7f615c1f5155a5139dfadc9cff.jpg","alt":"DSC_4473.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660206/preview-986f76b1b2546184f168efa2201333e8.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660207/large-69b6542ed531f03edc98b15cf0d2f35f.jpg","alt":"DSC_4493.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/660207/preview-8558f747b9723b05efb347814a057df4.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by Bethunni Schreiner"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6YKwoZUW4g50TuiyvVz7JR?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Keep For Cheap:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Keep For Cheap</strong></a>’s special blend of indie, country, rock, and pop has a little something for everyone. Playing what they call “prairie rock,” the Minnesota five-piece’s playful sound will make you feel like a kid, then break your heart with its next turn of phrase. The band strives to make music that moves, with driving instrumentals and poignant lyrics. Drawing at times from their own love story, fronting members <strong>Kate</strong> and <strong>Autumn</strong> write music to make you pine over queer love and passing youth, seek inspiration in the natural world and connection wherever it can be made.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The emotion in their music mainly reflects the lives of songwriters and fronting members of the band, Autumn and Kate who formed a musical connection when they met in the alto section in college choir in 2017. They soon started “KfC”, became best friends and are now nearly five years in love, writing alternative-country songs reflecting on their lives in Minnesota and the world as they see it. Their special connection brings a vivacious perspective to their music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Keep For Cheap!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/TcOuhbFsKsg?si=-Y3Mdh6yP1R2dx1X","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C8mZ2rAslEU/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/keepforcheap/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC75Ms2W7_Q_bfn2cVLhTJ-Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://linktr.ee/keepforcheap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Linktree</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"324889","title":"Wildlife Control blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: it doesnʼt matter if sheʼs analog or digital.","date":"2024-06-21","lead":"Wildlife Control’s got your back with \"Team You\" just in time for Summer playlists.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/324889/8b30164caa55d9c573a365538f019870.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Wildlife Control’s got your back with \"Team You\" just in time for Summer playlists."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5p6SX6n8g1jrREu8atGvDu?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (June 21, 2024) - NYC-based<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2f2Bf7TxY9xWWbTETxtPnP?si=jKb2uj66TguuDoaT_XwjUA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wildlife Control</strong></a> follows their recent <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/18c0mxhpR23bj96k5Iqkaq?si=53423d03640e43df\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">“Make Me Feel”</a> release with the new single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5p6SX6n8g1jrREu8atGvDu?si=e708909d20be404f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Team You</strong></a><strong>”</strong> - an uplifting pop-driven track imbibed with sports metaphors. Featuring the melodic pop vocals set over rhythmic synths and electric guitars that Wildlife Control has become known for, “Team You” blurs the lines between genres while delivering a track that is simultaneously fresh and familiar."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/657077/large-81e86d0acd29325ac28d0d293397f623.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Team You\" by Wildlife Control"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Beauty and poetry in harmony and chords.”</em><br>– Curtis Silver,<strong> WIRED</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Wildlife Control is youthful yet insightful. It feels like lying by a pool you broke into, young and drunk, next to someone you loved while looking at the stars knowing in your heart the world has a f*** ton more in store for you.”</em><br>– Sophie Saint Thomas, <strong>VICE</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Wildlife Control are writing classics. “Analog or Digital” is vaguely Ramones, vaguely Phoenix, wholly a triumph in rock that might be considered indie, and entirely awesome. It's a must listen.”</em><br>– Rachel Skotarczyk, <strong>Indie Shuffle</strong>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2f2Bf7TxY9xWWbTETxtPnP?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Wildlife Control:"},{"t":"p","html":"Grammy-nominated musician and producer, <strong>Wildlife Control</strong> (they/them), records and tours solo, duo, and with collaborators globally. They helped establish the New York shimmer pop sound in the early 2010’s with their critically-acclaimed eponymous debut album, which was the #1 self-released album on the <strong>NACC/CMJ Radio 200 Chart</strong>. The artist has sold out headlining shows at <strong>Mercury Lounge</strong> in New York City and <strong>Bottom of the Hill&nbsp;</strong>in San Francisco, and played featured slots at <strong>SXSW</strong>, <strong>Bottlerock</strong>, and the <strong>CMJ Music Marathon</strong>. Wildlife Control’s innovative videos have garnered praise from WIRED and comparisons to groups like <strong>OK Go</strong> and <strong>Arcade Fire</strong>. Combining their indie rock sound with time-lapse and stop motion photography, the music video for the artist’s debut single<strong>&nbsp;“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1muCDX7rYQRv1q4ocLcnVZ?si=1810223e48754b72\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Analog or Digital</strong></a><strong>”</strong> went viral with over 450k views."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/boGyFAYomBo?si=lj8yyCjYefg2-tGp","height":"315"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Wildlife Control!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://wildlifectrl.com/","img":"","title":"Wildlife Control blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: it doesnʼt matter if sheʼs analog or digital.","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/wildlifecontrol/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@wildlifecontrol","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/wildlifecontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@WildlifeControl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"325864","title":"Xan DuBose","date":"2024-06-21","lead":"\"Unbreak\" discovers the unspoken emotions of parting ways, with the hope of finding the right love one day.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/325864/df606bfd484be10f0e9a679107d6f042.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Unbreak\" discovers the unspoken emotions of parting ways, with the hope of finding the right love one day."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1xkIQkvJoGb2HinzTzS3fj?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Charleston, SC (June 21, 2024) - Rising artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1FtaimfBPkxh0WRi2kAg9l?si=tuG8LqqWRqS8vWiPuv1YSQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Xan DuBose</strong></a> takes on a lovely somber note on her newest single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1xkIQkvJoGb2HinzTzS3fj?si=ff4fd102b83d488b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Unbreak</strong></a>.” The song highlights her ability to traverse various genres, offering a glimpse into what awaits listeners on her much-anticipated EP, slated for release in August 2024."},{"t":"p","html":"A fusion of contemporary flair and timeless jazz elegance, “Unbreak” brings the jazz club to listeners, set to enchant the audience’s emotions with Xan’s smooth, velvety vocals."},{"t":"button","href":"https://vyd.co/Unbreak","label":"Listen to \"Unbreak\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#ff9f8b"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/658120/large-29b57986bea10a238ab00218c94fc320.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"Unbreak\""},{"t":"quote","html":"“Recording “Unbreak” was an incredibly emotional experience- It was so honest and raw and I tried to convey that with the vocals without letting the emotion get the best of me.”","cite":"- Xan Dubose (Singer/Songwriter)"},{"t":"p","html":"The track delves into the anguish of departing from a relationship that no longer fits, despite lingering feelings of love. Featuring beautiful jazz piano parts and heartfelt lyrics, every note and word is filled with deep emotion and soul. Ultimately, the song conveys a message of hope for a future love that will heal all the hurt."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1FtaimfBPkxh0WRi2kAg9l?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Xan DuBose:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1FtaimfBPkxh0WRi2kAg9l?si=T1B-GkhjRg2azKjcSq877Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Xan DuBose</strong></a> (she/her) is an exceptionally talented singer-songwriter hailing from the vibrant musical scenes of Columbia and Charleston, South Carolina. With a captivating voice that effortlessly blends elements of jazz, soulful vocals, contemporary sounds, and a touch of country flavor, Xan’s music resonates with listeners on a profound level."},{"t":"p","html":"Since making her debut in the SC music scene back in 2013, Xan has become a recognizable and highly sought-after artist. She gained considerable acclaim as a member of <strong>Patrick Davis’ Midnight Choir</strong>, a testament to her remarkable vocal prowess and stage presence. Her performances alongside acclaimed artists such as <strong>Darius Rucker</strong>, <strong>Thomas</strong> <strong>McClary</strong>, <strong>Charles</strong> <strong>Kelley</strong>, and others have further solidified her reputation as a standout talent."},{"t":"p","html":"Xan finds creative influence in iconic artists such as <strong>Bill</strong> <strong>Withers</strong>, <strong>Allen</strong> <strong>Stone</strong>, <strong>Madison</strong> <strong>Cunningham</strong>, and <strong>Brandi</strong> <strong>Carlile</strong>. These diverse influences infuse her music with a unique blend of heartfelt lyrics, soulful melodies, and a timeless quality that transcends genres."},{"t":"p","html":"With her versatile musical style, Xan DuBose takes her listeners on a captivating journey through the intricacies of jazz, the emotional depths of soul, the infectious beats of contemporary sounds, and the storytelling essence of country music. Her performances are characterized by an irresistible blend of vulnerability, passion, and authentic artistry that leaves a lasting impact on all who have the privilege of experiencing her music."},{"t":"p","html":"As Xan continues to mesmerize audiences and carve her own path in the music industry, her infectious energy and undeniable talent have firmly established her as a rising star. With each captivating performance and heartfelt composition, Xan DuBose is making an indelible mark on the music scene, captivating the hearts of listeners far and wide."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Xan!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/xan_dubose/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@xan_dubose","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.xandubosemusic.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/65274f91e2c93806f99f56ac/t/652c10fb748f3d00f34fbb60/1697386747072/xan-06.png?format=1500w","title":"Xan DuBose","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.xandubosemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/user/1250467657?si=21afa3c610744cee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/alexandra.dubose.7?mibextid=LQQJ4d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"328170","title":"Loki Moon's \"UFO\" Takes Listeners on a Cosmic Journey","date":"2024-06-20","lead":"\"UFO\" reflects on love, consciousness, and the mysteries beyond our everyday reality.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/328170/3990f2edd0835eb7b184a653a69468ee.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"UFO\" reflects on love, consciousness, and the mysteries beyond our everyday reality."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3bhRQvRnYiu2WsKVZs2FPb?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"DENVER, CO (June 20, 2024) - &nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.lokimoon.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Loki Moon</strong></a>, the electro-acoustic alt-pop duo known for their ethereal and immersive sound, just released their latest single, “<a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/UFO\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>UFO</strong></a>,” offering a mesmerizing exploration of spirituality and the human experience.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"In a time of uncertainty, “UFO” is a beacon of light, guiding listeners through the dark with its hypnotic sound and profound lyrics. The song encapsulates themes of duality, questioning, “Was it delicate or twisted?” and suggests that love can be both. This duality underscores the extremes of human experience, and “UFO” serves as a calming presence amid the chaos.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/UFO","label":"Listen to \"UFO\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Born from deep introspection following a personal conflict, the first verse acts as a plea for spiritual guidance, illuminating a dark path. The second verse highlights the individual's responsibility to maintain their light and avoid being drawn into the depths of consciousness.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The track’s soothing yet enigmatic sound is reminiscent of <strong>James Blake</strong>, <strong>Bon Iver&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>, creating an ethereal atmosphere that resonates deeply with its audience."},{"t":"quote","html":"“'UFO' is an offering to the great mystery, the sound and space between the material and etheric world.”","cite":"- Vocalist Ashley Edwards"},{"t":"p","html":"As anticipation builds for Loki Moon’s upcoming album, “UFO” sets the stage for what promises to be an extraordinary journey, continuing the duo’s exploration of profound themes through their distinctive, immersive sound."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0860Nym6xJwvClvnx1bsVv?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Loki Moon:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Loki Moon</strong> is the trickster who dances in light and bathes in the dark - a polarity dressed in lullabies. Comprised of <strong>Ashley Edwards</strong> and <strong>Davis Jones</strong>, Loki Moon is an alt-R&amp;B electro-acoustic duo who bring forth an ethereal, percussive soundscape that explores that which is mystical and existential. While keeping an air of anonymity, their music is ageless - speaking to the road less-traveled types - the wanderers, the outcasts."},{"t":"p","html":"Influenced by world music - a la Ethiopian jazz, music from the Sahara, and Japanese minimalist music - Loki Moon creates an immersive auditory experience that subjects listeners to explore their own subconscious. Born out of their connection over esoterism, and ideological and philosophical chemistry and perspective, the ever-evolving dialogue of their lyrics has been described as “<em>...strange, beautiful, and in its own right, a novel</em>” (-<strong>PopMatters</strong>)."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Loki Moon"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@lokimoonmusic/video/7382483244161240362","handle":"@lokimoonmusic"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/C8U5Oreu560/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lokimoonmusic/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://facebook.com/lokimoonmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://tiktok.com/@lokimoonmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCpHZLZY5NwM-99px-3b8_Fw/xregexp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"276241","title":"Read More","date":"2024-06-19","lead":"Experience the impact of \"Resurrection,\" which explores themes of redemption, renewal, hope, and more.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/276241/18153082b5bc4e480cbdc0a01acee124.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Experience the impact of \"Resurrection,\" which explores themes of redemption, renewal, hope, and more."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3Te8FSX6dHbO5Ch9hvhMi0?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Gordonsville, VA</strong> (June 19, 2024) - Indie sensation Andrew Neil, hailing from Gordonsville, VA, just dropped the highly anticipated single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5IB6Qn5XWe4DDT9EXTvCIn?si=0aa67a265d764242\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Resurrection</strong></a>” on June 19, 2024, under the moniker: <strong><em>Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple</em></strong>. Classified as alternative rock and post-grunge, the song promises a unique blend of punchy dynamics, raw authenticity, and profound lyrics that resonate with the universal theme of overcoming life's challenges."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>Themes of Redemption, Renewal, and Hope</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"“Resurrection” goes beyond musical boundaries, delving into the profound themes of redemption, renewal, and a second chance at life and love. <strong>Andrew Neil</strong>, the creative force behind the band, reflects on the song, stating, <em>“It conveys themes of rising from the ashes, emerging from depression, and falling in love with life again.”</em> The band’s journey, marked by struggles with mental illness, addiction, and homelessness, is channeled into their music, creating a relatable experience for listeners. It seamlessly weaves between energetic, driving rhythms and more introspective, melodic sections creating a rich tapestry of sound."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Resurrection","label":"Listen To \"Resurrection\" On All Streaming Platform","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"“There’s a saying ‘Wherever you go, go with all your heart.’ When Code Purple recorded our first album everyone showed up prepared but, equally as important, with their heart in the right place… the place of love.”","cite":"- Andrew Neil, Lead Singer, Andrew Neil & Code Purple"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6QUGMOwpGGRqhFW7ZD4eJB?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>A Sonic Journey with Depth and Authenticity</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Describing the sound of “Resurrection,” Neil explains,&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“It is very punchy, yet there are moments of dynamics. The song, like the whole album is like a diamond in the rough; polished just enough to maintain raw, true authenticity, with subtle, yet relatable nuggets of truth.”","cite":"- Andrew Neil, Lead Singer, Andrew Neil & Code Purple"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Daniel Houser, lead guitarist/banjo player, adds, </em><br>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Sonically, the song has the balance of a lit candle, flowing like the pouring of candle wax, with heavy chorus tones for clarity.”","cite":""},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614209/large-540ed7096c888c71f5586a6c9c64b298.png","alt":"Resurrection_Back_Cover_3000x3000.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614209/preview-7fb533ca65589b823ebbd30daff41a2f.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614210/large-6d0434a294c4e045815cea9f8bceb6c6.png","alt":"Resurrection_Front_Cover_3000x3000.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614210/preview-f9453e6cfa1dba7b5cd012761ff3de11.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614211/large-db3f058813583caa660f8f439607aaba.png","alt":"_Transparency.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614211/preview-c7e4cfb2a45cc090c8c5885d9ac7e7c2.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614212/large-ed7d307ac3ed4267870affd7a918b74c.png","alt":"IMG_1325.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614212/preview-71b72a014f76ddfd52e6a270877d16a9.png"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>A Song Beyond Music: Resilience, Love, and Redemption</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"“Resurrection” invites listeners on an evocative journey of personal transformation, exploring the depths of adversity and the uplifting power of finding solace and hope in a special person. <strong>Ray Maternick</strong>, band manager and the founder of <strong>Tree Heart Records LLC</strong>, offers an insightful analysis of the track:"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Almost everyone can relate to the song ‘Resurrection.’ It emphasizes the theme of resurrection and the opportunity for second chances. It is a testament to the transformative impact of love and support, steering life towards a positive trajectory. Our family, like many other families, experienced this first-hand.”","cite":""},{"t":"p","html":"Maternick’s interpretation sheds light on the deeper layers of the song, capturing its essence as an anthem for renewal, emotional revival, and hope - even in the darkest times.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The song hits harder than Jesus Christ Superstar as it packs a significant emotional punch, powerful lyrics, dynamic composition, and a passionate performance. I believe it has potential to resonate deeply with audiences and leave a lasting impression.”","cite":"- Daniel Houser, Lead Guitarist/Banjo, Andrew Neil and The Code Purple"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>Live Shows and Album Details</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to the single release, Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple will kick off live shows starting in early 2024. The upcoming album, also titled <em><strong>Resurrection</strong></em><strong>&nbsp;</strong>will feature a total of nine original songs, eight of which were written by Andrew Neil and one track written by the band’s drummer, <strong>Logan Wayne</strong>. Cover art for the album, which will be unveiled shortly, is being rendered by <strong>Daniel Benayun</strong>, a rusing Bostonian artist who has been compared to <strong>Andy Warhol</strong> and other Pop Art legends."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614212/large-ed7d307ac3ed4267870affd7a918b74c.png","alt":"IMG_1325.png"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Andrew Neil</strong>, born on August 9, 1988, in Colorado Springs, is the creative force behind the indie sensation “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6QUGMOwpGGRqhFW7ZD4eJB?si=booFs-qRQJiYxOmUrxXZLg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple</strong></a>.” Overcoming challenges, Andrew’s journey is a testament to the transformative power of music. A former High School Athlete and US Military Academy recruit, his life took an unexpected turn in 2009 after a traumatic head injury, sparking the creation of over 450 original compositions. Often compared to “Outsider music artist” <strong>Daniel Johnston</strong>, Andrew’s musical narrative unfolded in 2017 with “Code Purple,” a lofi masterpiece recorded within the walls of a psychiatric hospital. Partnering with producer Andy Waldeck, subsequent studio albums like “<strong>M</strong><strong>erry Go Round (2018)</strong>,” “<strong>Freak (2019)</strong>,” “<strong>Sunny Side (2021)</strong>” and “<strong>Alien (2022)</strong>,” showcased resilience and creative depth, even amid a battle with Non-Hodgkin’s Lymphoma in 2019."},{"t":"p","html":"Sparked by an opportunity to perform as the opening act for the <strong>Raelyn Nelson Band</strong> in Nashville, Andrew Neil formed a new band to back him up. &nbsp;The band’s initial lineup featured Andrew Neil on rhythm guitar and lead vocals, accompanied by <strong>Daniel Houser</strong> on lead guitar and banjo, <strong>Alan Warren</strong> on bass, <strong>Rick Shaw</strong> on mandolin, and <strong>Zach Bullock</strong> on drums."},{"t":"p","html":"Following their performance, the band experimented with their sound by recording and releasing a lo-fi track titled “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2UV0x98VGgwP4zF22WXGqS?si=dc662b2274654f2d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Like</strong></a>” as a single. However, shortly after its release, Zach Bullock and Alan Warren stepped down from the band due to long-term commitment issues. This led to a month-long search for a new drummer, culminating in the addition of Logan Wayne, while Rick Shaw transitioned to playing bass."},{"t":"p","html":"In August 2023, with their refreshed lineup, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6QUGMOwpGGRqhFW7ZD4eJB?si=kukSeOESRCCl4bAooy-PyQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple</strong></a>” spent four productive days at <strong>White Star Sound Studios</strong> in Louisa, Virginia. During this time, they recorded twelve original tracks. Out of these, nine tracks were selected to be part of their debut album ‘Resurrection,’ marking a significant milestone in the band’s evolving musical narrative."},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond the studio, a forthcoming book chronicles Andrew Neil’s battle with mental illness and cancer. With the built anticipation for the release of the album’s Title track “<strong>Resurrection</strong>” on 19 January 2024, Andrew Neil’s mantra, <em>“Music makes a difference in this jello world,”</em> resonates as a guiding principle in their remarkable journey of resilience and self-discovery."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/YOzofIbs6-A?si=B_LuD1UFJE350d0S","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@codepurpleband/photo/7375253387811540266","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/CodePurpleBand/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/andrewneilmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@codepurpleband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"315872","title":"Loki Moon","date":"2024-06-06","lead":"\"Sleepwalker\" is a journey through the law of opposites in Loki Moon's quintessential \"electro-sensory alt-R&B\" sound.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/315872/3b4873b0d068edeeba91371f51b9ed53.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Sleepwalker\" is a journey through the law of opposites in Loki Moon's quintessential \"electro-sensory alt-R&amp;B\" sound."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/309rvGCOnXjATswic1b6Sg?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"DENVER, CO (June 6, 2o24) - <strong>Loki Moon</strong>, an alt-R&amp;B electro-acoustic duo, released their latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/309rvGCOnXjATswic1b6Sg?si=3643c8fb1c3f4f12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sleepwalker</strong></a>”, providing a captivating preview of their upcoming self-titled album. With thought-provoking lyrics and an enchanting melody, “Sleepwalker” takes listeners on a mesmerizing journey through the <strong>Law of Opposites</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"In a world filled with chaos and uncertainty, “Sleepwalker” offers a much-needed escape. Loki Moon’s unique blend of retro-futurism and dystopian elements creates an immersive sonic experience that delves deep into the human psyche, exploring themes of apocalypse, relationships, internal struggle, and the crumbling of society. It invites listeners to reflect on their own consciousness and the challenges faced in a rapidly changing world. The track is a testament to the band’s ability to navigate the complexities of the human condition and deliver a message that is both thought-provoking and relatable."},{"t":"p","html":"Vocalist of Loki Moon, <strong>Ashley Edwards</strong>, shares the inspiration for “Sleepwalker”: <em>“The track was born out of a period of self-reflection and a desire to understand the direction society is heading. It explores the metaphysical feeling of shift and change, as well as the overstimulation of the mind in the face of technocracy. “Sleepwalker” urges individuals to hold on to their individuality and reclaim their creativity and sovereignty.” </em>The track is a call to awaken from the default mode of living and embrace the voice within."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/649338/large-6dd527c444a26f3a5719e7d4dd82e458.png","alt":"Cover art for \"Sleepwalker\" by J Lambert Film"},{"t":"p","html":"With “Sleepwalker,” Loki Moon demonstrates their mastery of storytelling through music. Sonically, the track weaves a complex web of moods with a mantra-esque electro-sensory alternative R&amp;B sound born on an old-school casio... an ode to early beatmakers with a tinge of <strong>Kali Uchis&nbsp;</strong>vs <strong>J Dilla</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"As anticipation builds for Loki Moon’s upcoming album, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/309rvGCOnXjATswic1b6Sg?si=689b71e270f84604\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sleepwalker</strong></a>” sets the stage for what promises to be a remarkable musical journey. The band's ability to explore profound themes while delivering captivating melodies and etheric soundscapes is a testament to their artistry and creativity."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0860Nym6xJwvClvnx1bsVv?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Loki Moon:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Loki Moon</strong> is the trickster who dances in light and bathes in the dark - a polarity dressed in lullabies. Comprised of <strong>Ashley Edwards</strong> and&nbsp;<strong>Davis Jones</strong>, Loki Moon is an alt-R&amp;B electro-acoustic duo who brings forth an ethereal, percussive soundscape that explores that which is mystical and existential. While keeping an air of anonymity, their music is ageless - speaking to the road less-traveled types - the wanderers, the outcasts."},{"t":"p","html":"Influenced by world music - a la Ethiopian jazz, music from the Sahara, and Japanese minimalist music - Loki Moon creates an immersive auditory experience that subjects listeners to explore their own subconscious. Born out of their connection over esoterism, and ideological and philosophical chemistry and perspective, the ever-evolving dialogue of their lyrics has been described as <em>“...strange, beautiful, and in its own right, a novel”</em><em>&nbsp;</em>(-<strong>PopMatters</strong>)<em>.</em>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Loki Moon!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/C7zke2pPcjo/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.lokimoon.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/5a8482c912abd910ddfc8877/t/65bd3c8fed40f3361b93f80e/1706900623337/J.jpg?format=1500w","title":"Loki Moon","desc":"Mood & Color. Loki Moon is the trickster who dances in light and bathes in the dark \"...Strange, beautiful and in its own right, novel\" - Pop Matters, Chicago."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lokimoonmusic/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://facebook.com/lokimoonmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://tiktok.com/@lokimoonmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCpHZLZY5NwM-99px-3b8_Fw/xregexp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"330064","title":"Steve Erickson's New Album, \"Crooked Road,\" Offers a Modern Exploration of Appalachian Music","date":"2024-06-01","lead":"Drawing listeners into the history of the Blue Ridge Mountains, “Crooked Road” gets its inspiration from Virginia’s Heritage Music Trail.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/330064/da613b242c558f444ca8024b9bd5ada0.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Drawing listeners into the history of the Blue Ridge Mountains, “Crooked Road” gets its inspiration from Virginia’s Heritage Music Trail."},{"t":"p","html":"SOUTHWEST VIRGINIA (June 2024) – Steve Erickson unveils his fourth studio album, \"Crooked Road,\" sharing a contemporary perspective on traditional Appalachian music. Drawing inspiration from <a href=\"https://thecrookedroadva.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Virginia’s Heritage Music Trail</a>, a 333-mile journey through Southwest Virginia's rich musical landmarks, the album pays homage to the region's old-time and bluegrass traditions."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7cMpYuyxi8LSUH4eIYdlTc?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The album's title track, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/50SS1BxbSUnn20zF9Vj0Hy?si=dd7b1e06c6174db4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Crooked Road</a>,” narrates the journey along this historic trail with its evocative lyrics and melodic structure, celebrating the cultural milestones and timeless sounds of the storied region.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Blending authentic folk melodies with innovative interpretations, the album paints vivid pictures of life's joys and sorrows in the landscapes of the Appalachian Mountains. Produced in collaboration with acclaimed producer Jim Robeson, the tracks immerse listeners in the region's vibrant heritage."},{"t":"p","html":"Erickson’s original compositions, such as “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5W0nZqEIAcUY7su68yrlrp?si=c6c7d943f0354a96\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lay Me Down Beside My Love</a>,” are interwoven with traditional tunes like “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/22DPOIa6CmVmU1R6TPJD3E?si=e158ea10079a4be8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fair and Tender Ladies</a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3WXKShNbZRH3Cf08VUZBcc?si=928709b97b53425e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">In The Sweet By and By</a>,” creating a tapestry of Americana soundscapes. The album also features the upbeat “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2s6HiOiXNxkpyMoEiUlmNv?si=9520db2c236a4412\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Perfect Day</a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1QFAmkieNq8LYOzwxUXRLx?si=47a24ba5f86c431d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Find a Light</a>,” juxtaposed with the more somber “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3GB8IKOuUtKyxOWQSJo7zu?si=0e69c47c805d475a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Flip Side</a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4fJT8cky9FlJidJ7MvWBmD?si=06e9863b0d2a4327\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">We Don’t Love Us Anymore</a>.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Erickson seamlessly blends traditional sounds with contemporary flair, creating a unique auditory experience showcasing his passion for Appalachian traditions and music. His meticulous approach to production is evident throughout the album, with a rich array of acoustic instruments and contributions from talented musicians in the genre."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Crooked Road\" is <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7cMpYuyxi8LSUH4eIYdlTc?si=JOA70caYSkq2aJ496T-r9w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">available now</a> on all major streaming platforms."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/662403/large-39f0b015d7e4b9494277a057ade29c79.jpg","alt":"Cover Art for \"Crooked Road\" by Brett Sayles"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Steve Erickson:"},{"t":"p","html":"Steve Erickson is a seasoned musician whose journey into music began alongside a successful career in public relations across Atlanta, New York City, and Washington DC. Drawing from a diverse range of musical influences, Erickson's songwriting style blends elements of country, blues, and folk."},{"t":"p","html":"Originally involved with local bands like Truth in Advertising in Atlanta and later collaborating with Nick Peters in the duo Medium Gauge in Washington DC, Erickson has since established himself as a solo artist. Currently based between Asheville, North Carolina, and Vero Beach, Florida, Erickson's musical repertoire is characterized by introspective storytelling and a rich sound."},{"t":"p","html":"His discography includes notable releases such as <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/47yg8AH3fOvBUvcls5BYrH?si=He3bIgdLRiWwTH8FXAdieA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">It's About Time</a> (2012), <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2SfnXMSMYkwpv5Xbfbp6y3?si=M6a_Z7RdT1ydjTRXnDu9lQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Music Tonight</a> (2016), and <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0RTW7pEFKjOey3RFePkahl?si=VZRt4AZfQriywSeotGvHrw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Moving On</a> (2019). His latest release, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7cMpYuyxi8LSUH4eIYdlTc?si=st2hoM6_RRS1SLwMrwIYxA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Crooked Road</a> (2024), explores Appalachian music traditions with tracks like \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/50SS1BxbSUnn20zF9Vj0Hy?si=92c2d52c090d482a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Crooked Road</a>\" and \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5W0nZqEIAcUY7su68yrlrp?si=3e2fc549983f4d2d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lay Me Down Beside My Love</a>.\" Known for his ability to craft evocative narratives and connect deeply with his audience, Steve Erickson continues to evolve as a notable figure in contemporary Americana music."},{"t":"p","html":"For more about Steve Erickson and his music, visit his <a href=\"https://ericksongs.net/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">official website</a>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Steve Erickson!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3cejBgcRgP4gWuMxWVaR7i?si=0bQkIu7ET_i1vwD0D543qg&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=0da0ed3495db4227\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/steve-erickson/73492990\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> | <a href=\"https://ericksongs.net/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Emma Mackintosh","role":"","email":"emma@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"314317","title":"Peanut Butter Mosquito (PBM) | Welcome to PBM Online Hub","date":"2024-05-31","lead":"Grosse Pointe Shores, MI (May 31, 2024) - Alt-rock band Peanut Butter Mosquito has returned to the music scene with their highly anticipated new single, \"When I Die\". After a nearly 20-year break from the public eye, the band showcases their unique sound and explores the...","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/314317/9ab4f9567b29609877af1355a9245c70.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2mnV2NxEW0hDALHNRweW24?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Grosse Pointe Shores, MI (May 31, 2024) - Alt-rock band <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/06PhuoYsjw1N6sXNfvkyx4?si=UO1-24LfSze9xhrnP4H-Tw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Peanut Butter Mosquito</strong></a> has returned to the music scene with their highly anticipated new single, <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0d4lWSYtwoVGYVKEDyoyjH?si=IQ3c1oVWQiaCmsiobwjQfw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>When I Die</strong></a><strong>\"</strong>. After a nearly 20-year break from the public eye, the band showcases their unique sound and explores the impact of technology on society. With their melodic, power-pop, alt-rock style, the band offers a refreshing sound that appeals to a wide range of listeners.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With \"When I Die\", Peanut Butter Mosquito delves into the pervasive presence of technology in our lives. The song serves as a commentary on the state of communication in today's world, questioning whether the advancements in technology have truly been beneficial. The band tackles this issue head-on, reminding listeners of <strong>Dr. Ian Malcolm</strong>'s famous quote from <strong>Jurassic Park</strong>: <em>\"They were so preoccupied with whether or not they could, they didn't stop to think if they should.\"</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/645941/large-39bd40c63eaf273f9530b0fd03d1df9b.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"When I Die\" by Peanut Butter Mosquito"},{"t":"p","html":"Throughout their 20-year hiatus, the music industry has undergone significant changes, largely due to the propulsion of technology. Peanut Butter Mosquito has witnessed this evolution and recognizes the need to adapt to the new landscape. Their decision to return to the music scene was driven by their unwavering passion for creating music and the belief that dreams and creativity have no age limit. The band's members, now in their 40s, are excited to embark on this new chapter independently, without the constraints of labels or management. They hope to inspire others from all walks of life to continue pursuing their passions."},{"t":"p","html":"Over the past two decades, Peanut Butter Mosquito's music has evolved while maintaining its unique identity. Their songs have been likened to the energetic style of <strong>Green Day</strong>, as well as the New Wave sound of <strong>Oingo Boingo</strong>. Each track tells a specific story, with the sound adjusted accordingly. The band's music is known for its ability to captivate audiences of all ages, particularly those who appreciate alternative rock and pop music. With a focus on college-age crowds and individuals who can relate to their experiences, Peanut Butter Mosquito continues to create music that speaks to their listeners' hearts."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/645942/large-bb7b13bea635bd1d2b4fa4c8e58e3b4f.png","alt":"Image of Peanut Butter Mosquito by Erik Krefeld "},{"t":"h3","html":"About Peanut Butter Mosquito:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>PBM </strong>was established at <strong>Cousino High School</strong> in Warren, MI, by <strong>Nate Castle</strong> and <strong>Tom Torrento</strong>. The band welcomed new members with diverse musical backgrounds, introducing fresh ideas and creativity. Transitioning from a ska style to a blend of rock, pop, jazz, blues, and swing, PBM has evolved its sonic identity, creating a unique mix of genres known as the \"fuzzy feel-good collection.\" The band gained local recognition for their horn-infused rock, clever lyrics, and harmonious vocals, coupled with their strong work ethic and on-stage camaraderie.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Emphasizing audience engagement, PBM values building connections, fostering camaraderie, and providing memorable experiences. Their music has reached a global audience through compilations from indie labels like <strong>RawFish Records</strong>, <strong>LittleGiants Records</strong>, <strong>Baby Boom Records</strong>, and <strong>Honey Records</strong>, spanning countries such as Germany, England, Japan, Scotland, and France. Their second album, <em><strong>One Sip At A Time</strong></em>, achieved national distribution in 2006. PBM's musical journey included a notable appearance on NBC's <strong><em>America's Got Talent</em></strong>, where their performance of the original song \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5W8aISfX1KSUFNzkYOuou0?si=X2mk-Ic0TVaKdqARkIlGLA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Password</strong></a>\" propelled them to the semi-finals. They toured extensively, performing in over 40 states and internationally, sharing stages with renowned acts like<strong>&nbsp;Tommy James </strong>and the <strong>Shondells</strong>, <strong>Blessed Union of Souls</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;Gavin Degraw</strong>, <strong>Cherry Poppin' Daddies</strong>, and The Presidents of The United States of America.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/06PhuoYsjw1N6sXNfvkyx4?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Currently, PBM is revisiting past hits and crafting new music, embarking on live performances and studio recordings at <strong>Tempermill Studios</strong> and <strong>Third Man Records</strong>. With a focus on expanding their fan base, PBM eagerly anticipates the next phase of their musical journey. From their humble beginnings to their significant presence in the local music scene, PBM remains true to their originality while embracing growth and change. They prioritize their fans, creating lasting connections and cherished memories through their music, resonating globally with tours and compilations. With a history of sharing the stage with renowned artists and making an impact on <em>America's Got Talent</em>, PBM is set for a new era of recording and performing, dedicated to growing their fan base and producing captivating music for existing and new listeners. Entering this next musical chapter, the band's dedication, passion, and creativity shine through, signifying an exciting phase in their artistic journey filled with enthusiasm."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Peanut Butter Mosquito!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2FPBM.PeanutButterMosquito%2Fposts%2Fpfbid0DDB6EqSoJnzjnrRe4U97tTjSnQfDmi6kzdWC6qN8eXYQJ5AC1o5Yf8BBY7X8f1Nel&show_text=true&width=500","height":"762"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.pbmband.com/","img":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/99ebe6_34cd356595244149ba58d7293f6f296d%7Emv2.png/v1/fit/w_2500,h_1330,al_c/99ebe6_34cd356595244149ba58d7293f6f296d%7Emv2.png","title":"Peanut Butter Mosquito (PBM) | Welcome to PBM Online Hub","desc":"Peanut Butter Mosquito (PBM) is a seven-member horn-driven pop-rock band inspired by artists like Dave Matthews Band, BNL, Chicago, Green Day, and Reel Big Fish. Known for their vibrant performances, "},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://music.youtube.com/channel/UC632nGAicXM3F5kbtxJgGIQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube Music</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/pbm.peanutbuttermosquito/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/PBM.PeanutButterMosquito\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"315484","title":"Official website of Lola Kristine: singer, pianist, and composer based in Southern California.","date":"2024-05-24","lead":"'CHAPTERS' showcases Lola Kristine's singer-songwriter style, weaving in elements of Americana, Retro-Soul, and Indie-Pop.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/315484/131eb3c67d5553d63b4fcda50b8c563d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"'CHAPTERS' showcases Lola Kristine's singer-songwriter style, weaving in elements of Americana, Retro-Soul, and Indie-Pop."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6mmdsoYEgyp6GjHHAo6VNg?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"LAGUNA BEACH, CA (May 24, 2024) - Soulful songstress, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?si=9_XafeBmRw2Oo_ligDe3WQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lola Kristine</strong></a>, captivates listeners with her highly anticipated new album, <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6mmdsoYEgyp6GjHHAo6VNg?si=Y3-QzzucQOyIhBamM8Ljbw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>CHAPTERS</strong></a><strong>’&nbsp;</strong>out on May 24, 2024. This heartfelt collection of songs takes listeners on a personal journey of redemption, showcasing Lola’s raw and vulnerable storytelling through five beautifully crafted chapters."},{"t":"p","html":"From the opening chapter, Lola’s search for love and stability is laid bare, as she navigates the complexities of romantic relationships. As the album progresses, ‘CHAPTERS’ delves deeper into Lola’s emotional journey, exploring themes of grief, lost love, and facing your inner demons. Lola ultimately comes out on the other side full of self-empowerment, and having found true healing within."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I was unconsciously addicted to love and totally codependent until enough painful breakups caused me to wake up. The album is a look inside my heart and head - getting swept off my feet, losing love, learning how to forgive and grow, loving again but with a new sense of independence and ultimately crossing the shore to freedom. Going from a starved child to a woman who feels whole and complete.”","cite":"-Lola Kristine"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong><em>An inside look at each of the Chapters:</em></strong>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/12lQLBgFlI6FdVt5kVoXA6?si=S2eYsM1vS76HoZ8pA2BICA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Chapter 1: <em>Rose-Colored Glasses</em></strong></a><strong>:</strong> This heroine’s journey begins with Lola looking for her holy grail in the form of a romantic partner. &nbsp;Dependent on the magical feeling of falling in love, “California Cowboy” sings about trying to find home and stability in a partnership. “You and Me” paints Lola’s desire to have the simplicity of a fairytale-like romance to fulfill her. &nbsp;&nbsp;"},{"t":"caption","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1erhxIjaxePFBGEVjTSOnA?si=UB9wSvW_Qcel8BZIQ1vIZw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Chapter 2: <em>When Things Fall Apart</em></strong></a><strong>:&nbsp;</strong>The dream of happily-ever-after starts to fall apart in Chapter Two. Beginning with denial in “Just Friends”, then turning to grasping and grieving in “Sheets” as the comfort slips away. &nbsp;This chapter closes out with the epic “Wish You Love,” a reflection on forgiveness. Lola sings of allowing the fire of pain refine us in order to truly heal and love again.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/q8H01u6RyWc","height":""},{"t":"caption","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1zEFcukoOFwDG4ATM8tk8j?si=goLxxdVCSSScDi5Q2YdsPw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Chapter 3: <em>Into the Woods</em></strong></a><strong>:</strong> Left alone, Lola is forced to face her inner demons: guilt, shame, and other hidden shadows she was able to distract herself away from with romance. “Find Me in the Wilderness” dives deep into her wild feminine soul, where she reclaims the lost child within as she embodies the fierce mother wolf. &nbsp; The lioness is unleashed in “Living for Myself,” a bluesy rock anthem about finding your inner power, standing up for yourself, female empowerment and embracing your uniqueness."},{"t":"caption","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3JaBGTFengk8S1Y9qK6KRb?si=VDgYIYIzRWezxOerfK65Mw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Chapter 4: <em>A New Dance</em></strong></a><strong>:</strong>&nbsp; As a woman who knows her worth and her desires, Lola now enters into the dating world with a different perspective. She’s no longer looking for a prince charming to save her, but a partner who respects and cherishes every aspect of her. &nbsp;This chapter bursts with the joy of Lola finding that love. &nbsp;Beginning with “Brighter,” Lola reflects on this new kind of relationship in lyrics such a:<em>\"</em><em>You’re not like the others. You’re kind like my father. You treat me like a queen. You’ll be my reminder that life can be brighter...\"</em> The groovy Motown feel of “So Easy” perfectly depicts the ecstatic lightness of an uncomplicated romance. Feeling the bliss of her wild feminine nature being safely held by a steady masculine force, Lola sings of the beauty of this yin-yang match and dreams for the future in “Gypsy Soul.” &nbsp;"},{"t":"caption","html":"<strong>Chapter 5: <em>Parasamgate</em>:</strong> We all learn lessons throughout our lives in different ways. For Lola, romantic relationships have been the biggest catalyst for her spiritual growth. &nbsp;Her journey through romance and heartbreak &nbsp;has led her to an inner freedom she never knew existed. &nbsp;The final chapter of the album begins with “Never Knew,” a ballad about overcoming fear and feeling the unconditional love of Christ that pours from life when we let go and surrender. &nbsp;The transcendent finale to the album came to Lola in the form of a dream. &nbsp;The song was brought to life in a writing session with her friend and co-producer for the album, Justin Busch. &nbsp;“The Other Side” captures the essence of heaven on earth. &nbsp;Instead of believing in the myth of separation, this song invites listeners to see the interconnectedness of all life. To no longer be a victim of the past, but to co-create your own story of bliss with the Divine. <em>\"Heaven isn’t simply a place you go, It’s a winding canyon inside your soul.\"</em>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/649349/large-57e8abc2a00e78e6b01018183e8f8287.png","alt":"Cover art for 'CHAPTERS' by Lola Kristine"},{"t":"p","html":"With a unique blend of influences spanning from country-pop and Americana, to retro soul and R&amp;B, ‘CHAPTERS’ offers a rich and diverse musical experience that will resonate with a wide range of listeners. A testament to the power of music as a means of storytelling and personal transformation, this captivating album invites listeners to embark on an emotional journey of redemption and self-discovery, leaving them inspired and uplifted."},{"t":"p","html":"The release of ‘CHAPTERS’ has already generated significant buzz within the industry and among the general public. <strong>EARMILK</strong>, <strong>Playground UK</strong>, <strong>Buzz Music</strong>, <strong>Canadian Beats Passport</strong>, and <strong>Music Mecca&nbsp;</strong>are just a few of the publications that have praised Lola’s talent and the emotional depth of her music. In addition to critical acclaim, Lola has also secured radio play and interviews on local radio shows along the West Coast. Her song “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/50SMAqxLnZmHDlbX17aoO1?si=b2af98a6229e4d92\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Just Friends</strong></a>” from the album even made its way onto an episode of <em><strong>Children Ruin Everything</strong></em><strong>&nbsp;</strong>on the <strong>CW network</strong>."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Her evocative storytelling and soulful vocals create an intimate connection with listeners, inviting them to join her on a personal journey of love’s complexities.”","cite":"- EARMILK Music Magazine"},{"t":"p","html":"To further celebrate the release of ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6mmdsoYEgyp6GjHHAo6VNg?si=4dNayb9HRd2xpsZmcPE7-Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>CHAPTERS</strong></a>,’ Lola Kristine will be unveiling the music video for <strong>‘Other Side’</strong> in early June, directed by the talented <strong>Paul James Houghton</strong>. Fans can also look forward to the release of the album on vinyl in early Fall."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584167/large-f821f30371443470d22b2cd2f82c1f6f.jpg","alt":"IMG_8664.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584167/preview-14d4629bd8ece50ea51ab9f288f32f64.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584166/large-c99003dc237595c08e7b1a280afa32ec.jpg","alt":"IMG_8774.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584166/preview-de212dced0ef265484d13f8530d40c21.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584165/large-681c1ace08691f5d1d98c9e132b15daf.jpg","alt":"IMG_8854.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584165/preview-30ab94b10c3b1d7f7c4252f76eebb21e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584164/large-e5808947d3d37bc884029569bbcaa654.jpg","alt":"IMG_8673.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584164/preview-711fc68b8607ef1026eab77eaf78b923.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by MJ Photography"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lola Kristine:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?si=byr3Z1fAQF6MUeZOWC4tdQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lola Kristine</strong></a> is a singer, pianist and songwriter based in Laguna Beach, California. Known as “the little girl with the big voice,” Lola has been staggering audiences her whole life with the depth of soul she possesses in both her timeless songwriting and penetrating singing. Hearing her sing feeds your soul and reconnects you with what is right in the world."},{"t":"p","html":"From humble beginnings in St. Louis, Missouri, Lola has taken her music across the country, touring with noted musicians such as <strong>Premik Russell Tubbs (Santana, Sting, James Taylor)</strong>, <strong>Jeff Haynes (Joni Mitchell, Herbie Hancock)</strong> and bass virtuoso <strong>Michael Manring</strong>. She has collaborated with artists from all over the world, including <strong>Kinobe</strong> (Uganda) in a series sponsored by American Voices. In 2022, a live video of Lola performing went viral on TikTok, hitting 4.5M views which boosted her online presence. She is gaining notoriety amidst legendary rockstars such as <strong>Mick Fleetwood</strong> and <strong>Don Cromwell of Air Supply</strong>. She is currently living in Southern California, where she can be found performing at venues and clubs all up and down the coast."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lola Kristine!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.musicoflola.com/","img":"","title":"Official website of Lola Kristine: singer, pianist, and composer based in Southern California.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/musicoflola/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC7LAxI_AIC0YgeP0CcLYNOw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?si=IwYrZHbmSH6HjpNiFyEtDw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"317616","title":"Stephanie Babirak Battles Betrayal In \"Hey Cain\"","date":"2024-05-24","lead":"\"Hey Cain\" sees Babirak battle grief and betrayal on her journey to acceptance in new folk-rock track.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/317616/a6cfa2e6d7e04558b660949bd0042ef2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Hey Cain\" sees Babirak battle grief and betrayal on her journey to acceptance in new folk-rock track.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2b2OWjmn4ySdHCBpkdkDbw?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (May 24, 2024) - In a string of dynamic single releases leading up to a highly anticipated album, <a href=\"https://www.stephaniebabirak.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephanie Babirak</strong></a> debuts a heartfelt and vulnerable indie-rock track with her newest offering, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2b2OWjmn4ySdHCBpkdkDbw?si=333534cb89224a62\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hey Cain</strong></a>.”"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/650547/compressed_original-54f7f72ec0e3e38e17d4e6710011c46e.jpeg","alt":"Cover art for \"Hey Cain\"; Image by Johnel Clemente"},{"t":"p","html":"“Hey Cain” sees Babirak using the allegory of <strong>Cain&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Abel&nbsp;</strong>(from the <strong>Old Testament</strong> in the Bible) to explore the emotions that come with betrayal and the many forms of grief that ensue as a result. Referencing the famous bible verse <em>“Love is patient, love is kind”</em> from <strong>Corinthians&nbsp;</strong>in the <strong>New Testament</strong>, Babirak showcases exquisite wordplay in her lyrics by accusing someone of being<em>“So impatient, so unkind....your love don’t look like mine</em>.” The song then moves into the chorus where Babirak grapples with the strange grieving process that occurs when letting go of people who are okay with losing you. Lyrically, the song is one that hopes to bring the listener to the final stage of grief - acceptance - while simultaneously acknowledging how difficult it can be to actually get there. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, the track is reminiscent of a<strong>&nbsp;Phoebe Bridgers&nbsp;</strong>style with its dreamy folk-rock sound infused with harp... a quintessential element to Babirak’s discography. Friends and collaborators <strong>Peter Scoma</strong> and <strong>Cody Geil</strong> are also featured on this track to bring to life what has been described as a “boy genius meets the Beach Boys” soundscape."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641244/large-779d0ec8dd865f2c8a12e614063bf763.jpg","alt":"IMG_6585.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641244/preview-2dded95fa1481145e9f4669fd4b910f2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641245/large-5e62e4957bec2dd93117a27affc3ee80.jpg","alt":"IMG_6586_copy.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641245/preview-e4abe43b3459316385524f09adfa509c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641246/large-e2b323b485d62d6deea773a5f966e222.jpg","alt":"IMG_0343_copy.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641246/preview-b33dc441bb25ff4406e1908c499bf5a1.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>Images by David Zayas Jr.</em>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1RTP3uUSd5w7QVQuslDnm4?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Stephanie Babirak:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1RTP3uUSd5w7QVQuslDnm4?si=2gQcdqO1RcaYRiO32YJcPw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephanie Babirak</strong></a> is a renowned harpist based in New York City. Lauded as “seraphic” and “a lovely harpist” by the <strong>Huffington Post</strong>, she is best known for her contemporary approach to the harp. She has performed with pop acts like <strong>Adele</strong>, <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, and <strong>Sandra Day</strong>, and her performances have been featured in the <strong>2018 Super Bowl&nbsp;</strong>commercial for <strong>Hyundai Genesis</strong> and on <strong>NBC’s “Mr. Robot.”</strong> She has toured nationally and internationally, playing venues ranging in size and prestige from debuting works at <strong>Carnegie Hal</strong>l and <strong>Lincoln Center</strong>, the <strong>Edinburgh Fringe Festival</strong>, to a sound bath in a Brooklyn salt cave. Her mission is to create music that makes the harp relevant and accessible to all audiences.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephanie!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/stephaniebabirak/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@stephaniebabirak","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.stephaniebabirak.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/stephbabirak/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"319054","title":"Neil Michael Anderson Debuts Award-Winning Country-Rock Anthem, “What’s Your Truth?”","date":"2024-05-24","lead":"A fun highway song, akin to The Eagles, Traveling Wilburys, and John Lennon — inspired by the town of Truth or Consequences, NM.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/319054/d0e2c409c5ce87e806cb376abf295142.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A fun highway song, akin to The Eagles, Traveling Wilburys, and John Lennon — inspired by the town of Truth or Consequences, NM."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1ypdAgebhcUIGK6IdkaguV?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"TRUTH OR CONSEQUENCES, NM (May 24, 2024) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6o1vBPh6domkNIWE7b2L9A?si=2O2bn8GYRe-TtRJ5a0Dw7g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Neil Michael Anderson</strong></a>, a singer-songwriter based in Truth or Consequences, NM has released the country-rock track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1ypdAgebhcUIGK6IdkaguV?si=7452846cc676487c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>What’s Your Truth?</strong></a><strong>”</strong>, inspired by the town’s own name. The song showcases a unique blend of genres and invites listeners to “go deep on truth” through a catchy and inspiring musical experience."},{"t":"p","html":"Favored by listeners at live shows, and around the campfire, the song has just received a<strong>&nbsp;“Best Music Production Award” </strong>at the <strong>2024 New Mexico Music Awards</strong>."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Never have I been welcomed like I have by the people of Truth or Consequences. Every time I come back here, it feels like I am returning home. I’ve loved singing this song to them around the campfire, and on the stage. And now, it’s for the world.”","cite":"- Neil Michael Anderson"},{"t":"p","html":"With “What’s Your Truth?”, Neil asks the world a penetrating question about the nature of truth, consequences, and love. The song combines the fun and catchy vibe of songs like <strong>The Eagles’ “Take It Easy”</strong> and <strong>Traveling Wilburys’ “End of the Line”</strong>, alongside an aggressively optimistic message, reminiscent of<strong>&nbsp;John Lennon</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/WhatsYourTruth","label":"Listen to \"What's Your Truth\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#fa3b68"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/651239/large-c72f536ac56f5a698f055f8196a17ad0.jpg","alt":"Cover art for \"What's Your Truth\" by Neil Michael Anderson"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/WhatsYourTruth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>What’s Your Truth?</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is a stand-out single, with its unique blend of hook-laden vocals, rich orchestration, and a wall of harmonies. The lead vocal rises assertively from a backdrop of 12-string guitars, Hammond organs, chimey lead guitar riffs, and a banjo, building to a transcendental finish."},{"t":"p","html":"Neil refers to the single as “Classic Americana, crossed with an impressionistic painting”, incorporating touches of orchestral and shoegaze styles. The addictive hooks and layered instrumentation ensure that repeat listeners will discover something new with each play, while the introspective lyrics invite reflection on one’s self and the state of the world."},{"t":"p","html":"Written and produced by Neil Michael Anderson, the track was mastered by <strong>Ed Brooks </strong>(<strong>Pearl Jam, Death Cab for Cutie, Fleet Foxes</strong>). Production primarily occurred in New Mexico, at <strong>Taproot Studios</strong> in Truth or Consequences, NM, with <strong>Rob Stroup </strong>(<strong>Tony Furtado, Anna Graceman, Kick Stand Up</strong>), and some tracking at <strong>Shadowscape Records</strong> in Kansas City, with <strong>Sean Lea</strong> and <strong>Corey Martin </strong>(<strong>Folk Alliance International, The Sweet Remains, Sawyer Fredericks, Glad Ghosts</strong>)."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Neil Anderson:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Neil Michael Anderson</strong> is a singer-songwriter, with a 12-string guitar and a suitcase in hand. From country-rock anthems to big sky power ballads, Neil covers a lot of ground."},{"t":"p","html":"A poet by nature, Neil’s music is known for its deep and enigmatic lyrics, set to verse-chorus anthems, epic power ballads, and poetic art songs that tell a story.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, Neil’s music is a melting pot of genres, blending folk-rock, country-rock, power ballads, psychedelic rock, ambient, and shoegaze, with the occasional accent of medieval troubadours, and Indian ragas."},{"t":"p","html":"Neil has collaborated with various artists, including <strong>The Sunwrecks</strong>, and occasional sit-ins with <strong>The Consequences</strong>. He won a <strong>“Best Music Production Award”</strong> at the 2024 New Mexico Music Awards, and will be releasing a debut album later this year."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Neil Anderson!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/neilmichaelanderson/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@neilmichaelanderson","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://neilmichaelanderson.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/neilmichaelanderson\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram&nbsp;</strong></a>|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/events/1376961402931663?active_tab=about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"316407","title":"View martysongs’s Linktree. Listen to their music on Spotify here.","date":"2024-05-17","lead":"The latest album elebrates the transformative power of love and the human spirit.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/316407/4dcbc61cd4311470d13e0f88defd7b03.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The latest album elebrates the transformative power of love and the human spirit."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6QcaNSHinNXzfE8JawTvVk?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Austin, TX</strong> (May 17, 2024) - Seasoned artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3e2PdcbAflyA9g25SVcQiS\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Marty Thompson</strong></a> is set to bring the beat with his latest album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6QcaNSHinNXzfE8JawTvVk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Love Makes Better People</em></strong></a>, dropping on May 17, 2024. The album's lead single, \"<strong>Love Makes Better People</strong>,\" showcases Marty's unique ability to craft songs that are both deeply personal and universally relatable, fused with its uplifting message and catchy hooks."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/648949/-359fae44e982a6a958edc9b1c7af0813.webp","alt":"martyt.com_2024_Marty_Thompson_Records_Logo__se8evt.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/648949/-359fae44e982a6a958edc9b1c7af0813.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/648948/-86e519a2ebe9b872960b23044a878b39.webp","alt":"IMG_5931_royl8w.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/648948/-86e519a2ebe9b872960b23044a878b39.webp"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/648950/-d65ed95d0f1e422b368651e4c2e3cd57.webp","alt":"purplebass_xtsxlp.webp","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/648950/preview-d6dd66094e843c69d920dc00f986808d.webp"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Amid the rising popularity of psychedelic soundscapes, <em>Love Makes Better People&nbsp;</em>showcases Thompson's soulful storytelling that sets him apart. Drawing inspiration from the timeless music like the <strong>Grateful Dead</strong>, <strong>Widespread Panic</strong>, and <strong>U2</strong>, Thompson weaves together intricate melodies, thought-provoking lyrics, and infectious grooves that will transport listeners to a realm of cosmic rebellion and self-discovery."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3e2PdcbAflyA9g25SVcQiS?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"From poet Chris Zimmerly's scattered beauty on \"<strong>Joy Wins the Great Marble Race</strong>\" to the jazzy lead guitars from <strong>Mikey 'Black' Baker</strong> and the introspective musings of \"<strong>Should We Take the High Road</strong>?\", <em>Love Makes Better People</em> is a testament to Marty's growth as an artist and his unwavering commitment to creating music that resonates with the heart and soul."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Marty Thompson:"},{"t":"p","html":"Marty Thompson is an accomplished Songwriter, Musician, Producer, and Audio Engineer taking cues from a wide palette of jazz, rock and roll, psych-country and electronica, cleverly forging his own unique signature.&nbsp;<br><br>The independent artist was raised in West Texas in the 1980’s and was influenced heavily by classic Texas Rock and Psych-Country cross-vibes. Electrified under the Friday Night Lights, he had worn out and replaced his cassette of <strong>Van Halen</strong>’s debut album by age 6, saw <strong>Ozzy</strong> w/ <strong>Randy Rhodes</strong> at age 8, had complete collections of all <strong>Beatles</strong>,&nbsp;<strong></strong><strong>Zeppelin</strong>, and <strong>Pink</strong> <strong>Floyd</strong> albums by age 11, and saw <strong>ZZ Top</strong> in concert twice before age 15. It’s safe to say roots were grown!&nbsp;<br><br>Electrified under the Friday Night Lights, he now has written over over 300 original pieces of music. Marty performs with a modified steel string acoustic Martin 000-MMV, Gibson ES-335, or Gibson Thunderbird bass, as well as mandolin, banjo, piano, synth, Moog, latin percussion, and other instruments. He performs live with different arrangements but also multiple instruments at once utilizing looper technology on the fly. He also prides himself in studio audio engineering, and has built two extensive studios to record in. &nbsp;He uses these talents to multi-track and mix original compositions for release to the public.&nbsp;<br><br>In the mid-90's, Marty worked as Stage Tech at The Aardvark in Ft. Worth, Texas, also playing the regular acoustic drop-in show on Sundays (portrayed in his song Sunday / Sunshine). This Ft. Worth landmark was crucial in his development as a budding musician. He worked and played with <strong>Col. Bruce Hampton</strong>, <strong>Jimmy Herring</strong>, <strong>Patrice Pike</strong> (Sister 7), <strong>The</strong> <strong>Toadies</strong>, <strong>Tripping Daisy</strong>, <strong>Soulhat</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;The Grapes</strong>, <strong>Deep Blue Something</strong>, <strong>Matchbox 20</strong>, and many more. It was also at this time he met his wife, <strong>Kara</strong>, who introduced him to <strong>Paul Schnarz</strong>, manager for <strong>The Chicks</strong>. Marty moved to Tennessee in '97 he (along with <strong>Sam Holt</strong> and <strong>David</strong> <strong>Dean</strong>) formed a band called <strong>StormWatch</strong>. &nbsp;StormWatch had regional success traveling around the South, as well as a fabled tour through Texas in Summer ’98. Through his relationship with Schnarz, Marty obtained a job at ASCAP in membership. Working here allowed him to network and share music with other songwriters, including <strong>Waylon</strong> <strong>Jennings</strong>. &nbsp;This was also when he was introduced to experimental recording techniques and production philosophy.&nbsp;<br><br>Marty continues to compose and produce music, releasing new material often and keeping his loyal fanbase on its toes."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Marty!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://linktr.ee/martysongs","img":"","title":"View martysongs’s Linktree. Listen to their music on Spotify here.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/martythompsonmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/martysongs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"319128","title":"Wildlife Control blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: it doesnʼt matter if sheʼs analog or digital.","date":"2024-05-16","lead":"Indie rock artist drops new single just in time for anyone jonesing for a summer anthem.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/319128/ece6464fbcf825ea4955a584b5ba5274.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Indie rock artist drops new single just in time for anyone jonesing for a summer anthem."},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (May 23, 2024) - NYC-based<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2f2Bf7TxY9xWWbTETxtPnP?si=jKb2uj66TguuDoaT_XwjUA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wildlife Control</strong></a> steers listeners to a supersonic drive with latest single, \"<strong>Make Me Feel</strong>\". Equipped with an upbeat rhythm and powerful chords, Wildlife Control delivers a catchy tune that both rock and electropop lovers would easily tap their feet to."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/18c0mxhpR23bj96k5Iqkaq?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Make Me Feel\" brings forth vivid imagery of ecstatic emotions that listeners would feel with a loved one, and finds beauty in the simplest ways that love can be expressed."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/650577/large-5027e40733d1058c1c69c7d82766a099.jpg","alt":"\"Make me Feel\" Cover Art"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>\"And as I leave the earth&nbsp;<br>This swirling ball of blue&nbsp;<br>Picture the universe&nbsp;<br>Standing right before you\"</em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>Lyrics from \"Make Me Feel\"</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Make Me Feel\" marks a return to the melodic lyricism of Wildlife Control’s indie rock debut, which trended at the height of the music blog era and topped college radio."},{"t":"button","href":"https://wildlifectrl.com/makemefeel","label":"Listen to 'Make Me Feel' on Streaming Platforms","color":"#ff8d8d"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Wildlife Control:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2f2Bf7TxY9xWWbTETxtPnP?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Grammy-nominated musician and producer, <strong>Wildlife Control</strong> blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: \"it doesnʼt matter if she's&nbsp;<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1muCDX7rYQRv1q4ocLcnVZ?si=b30209c8b6b44266\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Analog or Digital</strong></a>\".<br><br>Wildlife Control's music covers the span of the depth of emotions in living a full life. From growing up as the only minority in a rural town, to going through the ups and downs of finding love, experiencing joy, pain, addiction, and always coming out on the other side better and stronger for it. That depth in the story is what keeps their fans interested and listening a decade on.&nbsp;<br><br>Inspired by <strong>The Beatles',</strong> often classed with <strong>Phoenix</strong>, and compared to <strong>Tom Petty&nbsp;</strong>by <strong>Dan Reynolds</strong> from <strong>Imagine Dragons</strong>, Wildlife Control's eclectic music and interesting experiments with video and sound tend to create discovery moments outside the industry that brings new audiences in."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Wildlife Control!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://wildlifectrl.com/","img":"","title":"Wildlife Control blurs the lines between visual art, music, and technology. Their aesthetic combines sampled and synthesized sounds and visuals in an alchemical mixture that is best summarized by the final words of their debut release: it doesnʼt matter if sheʼs analog or digital.","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/wildlifecontrol/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@wildlifecontrol","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/wildlifecontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@WildlifeControl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"318306","title":"Buy tickets online. Roswell Cultural Arts Center ticket reservation system. Book your tickets instantly.","date":"2024-05-13","lead":"The alt-pop artist brings her debut album to the Roswell Cultural Arts Center.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/318306/738ca658d59359464925ce0f494d3908.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"h3","html":"The alt-pop artist brings her debut album to the Roswell Cultural Arts Center."},{"t":"p","html":"ROSWELL, GA (May 13, 2024) - Rising pop artist <a href=\"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Maria Deirisarri</a> is performing in her hometown of Roswell, GA, this June 8 at the Roswell Cultural Arts Center, at 7 pm. Join the winner of the International Singer-Songwriter’s Association “Trailblazer Performer” Award as she presents songs from her debut album, In The Beginning."},{"t":"p","html":"The event, co-presented by the City of Roswell and the Roswell Youth City Council, promises to be an unforgettable night of music and community. Don't miss Maria's unique sound and infectious energy, tickets are available at the link below."},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://roswellcac.showare.com/orderticketsarea.asp?p=273&amp;a=8&amp;backurl=//roswellcac.showare.com/default.asp","img":"","title":"Buy tickets online. Roswell Cultural Arts Center ticket reservation system. Book your tickets instantly.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"Deirisarri's album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>In The Beginning</em></a>, represents a statement and introduction to her artistry and passion. Guiding listeners through a sonic journey of ethereal instrumentals and power-driven themes, her lyrical sentiments span love, fear, and resistance as she ultimately reaches a point of self-discovery within its resolution."},{"t":"p","html":"At just 18 years old, the Atlanta-based singer-songwriter experiments with a multitude of genres from Alt-Rock to Bossa Nova, suggesting wisdom beyond her years with her musicianship and lyricism."},{"t":"p","html":"Roswell Cultural Arts is committed to partnering with world-class artists who also call north Metro Atlanta home. This event is an opportunity for the community to come together, enjoy exceptional music, and celebrate the success of a talented local artist.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584560/large-ae88f6b79f8a11187ddde2897bf9aae6.jpg","alt":"IMG_3468.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584560/preview-aef2bfbdd600aa978d77e0d9da82a5a3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584561/large-eee8d219ca43d6969bb7c8fb76c23aa7.jpg","alt":"IMG_9140.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584561/preview-b6b91784e4715e10b6701b64ace813bb.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584559/large-5db114bbfa921ec30ac484cfd79ad0eb.jpg","alt":"2428ADA2-92CF-4AA5-9B23-29E254B7FF7D.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584559/preview-da45d7986405fb978b915b39c7fef178.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584562/large-057636ea55607a88af4114e4a0972543.jpg","alt":"82B2CA09-30C5-46F1-9D0F-D4D5E546C8C6.tif","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584562/preview-8acab54fcc89b44fcf9b0287116da0b2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584557/large-a959cb8c7efad763db8d037c8dd52523.jpg","alt":"5B6C8138-DBB7-4DE8-8938-CE13D96D0171.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584557/preview-46a73e97601b434e88a1d36a8ab0af4c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584556/large-473281368f60078b0a0af18e7d976530.jpg","alt":"044B2808-787C-48A8-891C-037BACC0988E.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584556/preview-ca23acc8e22ae25426baf072c990fefd.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Maria Deirisarri:"},{"t":"p","html":"Rising pop artist <strong>Maria Deirisarri</strong> is only 18 years old, but her musicianship and lyricism suggest wisdom beyond her years. The Atlanta-based singer-songwriter experiments with a multitude of genres, from dark alternative to bossa nova, generating an eclectic mix of music notably showcased in her debut album, In The Beginning."},{"t":"p","html":"Already amassing over 77k streams on Spotify, and garnering attention from top publications such as <strong>EARMILK</strong> and <strong>Conversations About Her</strong>, Maria Deirisarri’s success continues to increase with every release. The range of her sound entices listeners to discover every song’s personality, and even surprises them with lyrics connected to her Hispanic culture and multilingual heritage (such as in “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7Bum6Hbsbd3hTyrWdiFaZB?si=148f3290894c4340\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Same</a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/10HrEur1hApraufv2ih2ZY?si=44bd1e8b3e9f4184\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Te Necesito</a>”)."},{"t":"p","html":"In recent months, this young artist has triumphed in various competitions, ranging from her Trailblazing Performer accolade from the International Singer-Songwriters Association, her second-place finish in <strong>Omega’s Got Talent</strong>, to her Talent Preliminary Award in the <strong>Miss Georgia Teen Volunteer Competition</strong>. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Maria Deirisarri’s vibrant artiste meets the listener with a grace and uniqueness that is a breath of fresh air. Fans are eager to see what this up-and-coming superstar has up her sleeve. Her new album,<em>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ?si=NTLsWe2VRmmKfF15Mos3EA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">In The Beginning</a>&nbsp;</em>officially released on September 29th and is available on all streaming platforms!&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Follow Maria below for all music updates and upcoming announcements."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Connect with Maria!</strong>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/mariadeirisarri/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@mariadeirisarri","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@mariadeirisarri?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCtx5jhQ5a3Fx8_EJxh54WsA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/media/set/?set=a.2656672987691809&amp;type=3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"312601","title":"Emerging Artist Totten Bridge Evokes Strong Emotions with \"Seasons Change\"","date":"2024-05-10","lead":"Exploring the emotional journey behind the only timeless constant, change.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/312601/6b13169a6e5805062b9393ee99d9532e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Exploring the emotional journey behind the only timeless constant, change."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5cY7hgW8okLvbO7pfCZsYX?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (April 19, 2023) - <strong>Totten Bridge</strong>, a rising alternative pop rock artist known for stirring his listeners’ emotions released his latest single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5cY7hgW8okLvbO7pfCZsYX?si=13ac5531ac664c86\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Seasons Change</strong></a><strong>”</strong>. The track evokes strong emotions and serves as a ‘call to action’ to overcome fear and start living life. While life could be tough enough, “Seasons Change” fuses together both a dark feel and a positive message, leaving listeners feeling motivated to embrace change."},{"t":"quote","html":"“My mother passed away in March and the grief was profound and palpable. &nbsp;At her wake, I played the Fleetwood Mac song \"Songbird\" as a tribute to her life and it helped me to process what I was feeling.&nbsp; \"Seasons Change\" was a song that I had been working on but it was finished during this agonizing time. &nbsp;It has a contemplative yet powerful message to embrace change in order to live your best life and enjoy the journey. &nbsp;Don't worry about what was...focus on what is and what's to come!\"","cite":"- Alternative Rock Artist, Totten Bridge, on the song’s inspiration."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3GG5WYbs8fYoX6InnvMklW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The famous <strong>Thomas Fuller</strong> quote - “the night is darkest just before the dawn” - is an apropos metaphor that speaks to how someone feels when they are at a low point in life. &nbsp;“Seasons Change” sends a melancholic feeling for yearning and warmth, just as one would look to the dark skyline before the daybreak and the hope that the start of new day brings.<br><br>Overall, \"Seasons Change\" boasts a powerful rhythm and driving beat, while the lyrics deliver a strong message of desire to overcome fear, taking on life's biggest challenges, and embracing the future."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644120/compressed_original-5e1419e6f48bfbcd23c18b8799f10a12.webp","alt":"Seasons_Change_Cover_Art_dwukd5.webp"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wanted Seasons Change to feel powerful and cause someone to listen to the lyrics as a call to action about embracing change and overcoming their fears.\"","cite":"Alternative Rock Artist, Totten Bridge"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Totten Bridge:"},{"t":"p","html":"The Covid lockdowns of 2020 became the inspiration for New York City based songwriter/producer/creator<strong>&nbsp;James Palace&nbsp;</strong>to begin the journey of creating the songs and finding a co-producer to help him craft the music that would become TOTTEN BRIDGE. Unbound by genre and defined by an endless and experimental musical pursuit, the multi-faceted artist has garnered over 2.7 million streams and over 100,000 monthly listeners on Spotify alone as well as publication support from the likes of <em>Clash</em>, <em>Notion</em>, <em>Earmilk</em>, <em>Backseat Mafia</em>, <em>Medium</em>, and&nbsp;<em>Music Crowns</em> amongst others."},{"t":"p","html":"TOTTEN BRIDGE’s songs focus on the universally big themes of life and love with lyrics that are relatable in their concise, philosophical and emotive directness with the goal to speak to each listener personally. With lyrics that are more haiku than narrative, James Palace taps into the universal unconscious with a stoicism steeped in fate."},{"t":"p","html":"Relying on infectious melodies and tight musical arrangements that culminate in anthemic sing-along choruses, TOTTEN BRIDGE’s music is an eclectic blend of alternative pop rock with both British and American influences that are also infused with elements of EDM, folk, and American Heartland sounds."},{"t":"p","html":"What’s old is new...what’s new is old...this is TOTTEN BRIDGE!"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Totten Bridge:"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/tottenbridge/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@tottenbridge","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"313711","title":"Xan DuBose","date":"2024-05-10","lead":"\"Vice\" embodies a pop-country-western feel and powerful vocals, establishing Xan DuBose as an up-and-comer to watch","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/313711/a62ba745d155b0019250070b0bae2bc1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Vice\" embodies a pop-country-western feel and powerful vocals, establishing Xan DuBose as an up-and-comer to watch"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2niEzh3Ogd7A1GYSVsBmSx?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Charleston, SC (May 10, 2024) - Genre-bending artist <a href=\"https://www.xandubosemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Xan DuBose</strong></a> (she/her) presents the second single,<strong>&nbsp;\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2niEzh3Ogd7A1GYSVsBmSx?si=c4bbe7416a794b38\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Vice</strong></a><strong>\"</strong>, from her highly anticipated upcoming EP set to release in August 2024."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Vice\" showcases what makes DuBose an \"artist on the rise\" - her powerhouse vocals that leave audiences feeling confident and empowered. Effortlessly blending elements of jazz, soul, and contemporary country flavor, DuBose's voice is uniquely her own and sets the perfect sassy cadence for what the song is about... succumbing to one's own \"vice\". For some it's money, for some it's alcohol, but in this song the vice is a relationship... a person you can't live without."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/645551/large-f6559267f88a0ab77516dfff4d59c053.jpeg","alt":"Cover art for \"Vice\""},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>Don’t blame me, its not my fault</em>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>I'll react to how you make me wanna risk it all  </em>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>All bets off I'm going under, Pulling me under </em>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>Lines crossed under the covers, under the covers </em>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>It's the best kinda bad when ya make me scream your name </em>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>Lyrics from \"Vice\"</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Evoking a particularly pop-country-western feel in this track, \"Vice\" is brought to life by the musicians behind the track. Ripping guitars and golden-colored piano and organ bits give the song a unique flair that inspired DuBose to add in her own stylings of vocal stacks that \"blow it out\" in the best way possible. \"I sang those lyrics and the harmonies with all the strength I had left and I really think we hit it out of the park,\" says DuBose. \"I'm so thankful the musicians in the room were able to set the stage for this style of singing and that it all came together so beautifully.\""},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625410/large-acebf8828f6c8a695ba936635d712c37.jpg","alt":"6I5A5188.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625410/preview-0a0b074c14122b7c1ce566c667d1556c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625412/large-eb4a7af7ff840eec00346837e7ba0504.jpg","alt":"6I5A2827.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625412/preview-eed8b97430b3dfc111aa943838f0523a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625409/large-01fe7663da0213b824be6147366cbce0.jpg","alt":"6I5A5206.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625409/preview-17a53c6d2509c1c49097930f174d715c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625411/large-3a14033ac0c3d3eb57dd37d452a391c9.jpg","alt":"6I5A4917.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625411/preview-cd145594d4a563d250359bfda5365c48.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Images by Josh Norris"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Xan DuBose:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Xan DuBose</strong> (she/her) is an exceptionally talented singer-songwriter hailing from the vibrant musical scenes of Columbia and Charleston, South Carolina. With a captivating voice that effortlessly blends elements of jazz, soulful vocals, contemporary sounds, and a touch of country flavor, Xan's music resonates with listeners on a profound level."},{"t":"p","html":"Since making her debut in the SC music scene back in 2013, Xan has become a recognizable and highly sought-after artist. She gained considerable acclaim as a member of <strong>Patrick Davis' Midnight Choir</strong>, a testament to her remarkable vocal prowess and stage presence. Her performances alongside acclaimed artists such as <strong>Darius Rucker</strong>, <strong>Thomas McClary</strong>, <strong>Charles Kelley</strong>, and others have further solidified her reputation as a standout talent."},{"t":"p","html":"Xan finds creative influence in iconic artists such as <strong>Bill Withers</strong>, <strong>Allen</strong> <strong>Stone</strong>, <strong>Madison</strong> <strong>Cunningham</strong>, and <strong>Brandi</strong> <strong>Carlile</strong>. These diverse influences infuse her music with a unique blend of heartfelt lyrics, soulful melodies, and a timeless quality that transcends genres."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2MwLc56lkclkp5qVgKjhgD?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"With her versatile musical style, Xan DuBose takes her listeners on a captivating journey through the intricacies of jazz, the emotional depths of soul, the infectious beats of contemporary sounds, and the storytelling essence of country music. Her performances are characterized by an irresistible blend of vulnerability, passion, and authentic artistry that leaves a lasting impact on all who have the privilege of experiencing her music."},{"t":"p","html":"As Xan continues to mesmerize audiences and carve her own path in the music industry, her infectious energy and undeniable talent have firmly established her as a rising star. With each captivating performance and heartfelt composition, Xan DuBose is making an indelible mark on the music scene, captivating the hearts of listeners far and wide."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Xan!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.xandubosemusic.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/65274f91e2c93806f99f56ac/t/652c10fb748f3d00f34fbb60/1697386747072/xan-06.png?format=1500w","title":"Xan DuBose","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/xan_dubose/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@xan_dubose","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/user/1250467657?si=21afa3c610744cee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/alexandra.dubose.7?mibextid=LQQJ4d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"308731","title":"Rooted Unveils Captivating New Single \"Heart of This Place\"","date":"2024-05-03","lead":"Los Angeles, CA (May 3, 2024) - Rooted, a dynamic west coast pop-rock band, is released their latest single, “Heart of This Place”. The band, known for their infectious melodies and heartfelt lyrics, delivers yet another unforgettable track that is sure to resonate with ...","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/308731/16157cd3d10465888f305202dbd38731.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2l5J4V8IXLticZucXsZDou?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (May 3, 2024) - <a href=\"https://rooted.band\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Rooted</strong></a>, a dynamic west coast pop-rock band, is released their latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2l5J4V8IXLticZucXsZDou?si=5adaa977e4bb4c8e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Heart of This Place</strong></a>”. The band, known for their infectious melodies and heartfelt lyrics, delivers yet another unforgettable track that is sure to resonate with listeners worldwide."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/91oIXgcLUmQ","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"“Heart of This Place” invites listeners on a journey through the bustling streets of Los Angeles, capturing the essence of love, friendship, and the magic of the city. Working with <a href=\"https://www.bernardyagee.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Bernard Yagee</strong></a> (songwriter and producer of the track), the catchy hooks and uplifting energy serves as an anthem for anyone who has found solace and belonging in the vibrant heart of a bustling metropolis."},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/rooted2/heart-of-this-place-feat-maddox-lim","label":"Listen to \"Heart of This Place\" on Streaming Platforms","color":"#ff9797"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641209/large-88e11bfeb59ec74bb9f8b5075e991478.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-04-09 at 1.46.57 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641209/preview-1d2c8a1460e61da86fc55e845fe5c2fd.png"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>\"HEART OF THIS PLACE\" LYRICAL SNEAK PEAK</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I'm here to stay</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Don't go away</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Reunited, once again</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>In LA, long as you're with me</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Dreams awake in the heart of this place</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Set against a backdrop of shimmering lights and starlit skies, the song paints a picture of reunion and celebration. Maddox Lim and Genevieve Thai deliver emotive vocals backed by the band's signature blend of pop and rock, creating a sonic landscape that is both nostalgic and exhilarating."},{"t":"p","html":"With its infectious energy and heartfelt lyrics, “Heart of This Place” is poised to become a standout track in Rooted's impressive discography. The song's release coincides with AAPI Heritage Month, adding an extra layer of significance to its message of unity and belonging."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"quote","html":"The world is becoming more and more chaotic, not only by the wars we're witnessing, but also by the habits we're adapting where most of our core principles and values are being diluted to an extent where they're about to seize to exist. I wrote this song for Rooted to awaken the younger generation about those values and what actually truly matters, that is family, strong bonds, and togetherness.","cite":"Bernard Yagee - Songwriter & Producer"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Rooted"},{"t":"p","html":"Sparkling songcraft, impressive musicality, and captivating enthusiasm: Rooted is a five-member indie pop-rock band from the Los Angeles suburbs of the San Gabriel Valley whose shining artistry far surpasses the members’ chronological ages."},{"t":"p","html":"The Asian-American quintet of high school students has built a substantial following with performances at carnivals, street fairs, school events, battles of the bands, and onstage at the massive Los Angeles County Fair in Pomona, California to commemorate AAPI month."},{"t":"p","html":"Vocalist and guitarist <strong>Maddox Lim</strong> and <strong>Genevieve Thai</strong>, are Rooted co-founders. Joined by <strong>Eula Johnson</strong> on synth &amp; keyboards, bassist <strong>Alex</strong><strong>&nbsp;Calonzo</strong>, and <strong>Joshua Sang</strong> on drums. The five evolved as a band while performing covers by not only current artists like <strong>Harry Styles</strong>, <strong>Ed Sheeran</strong>, and <strong>Taylor Swift</strong> but play a multitude of 80s and 90s covers — what they classify as “older music with a lot of depth and meaning.”"},{"t":"p","html":"It might be observed that the rise of Rooted signifies the edge of an increasingly multicultural narrative, with inclusion and representation to inspire the new generations of creators. Charismatic, authentic, and exhilarating, Rooted presents fresh music with the power to open doors — a vibrant soundtrack for a welcome future."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Rooted!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/RootedBandMusic/about/?ref=page_internal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC0UP2dh_0bgZ49a4RVf2lfA?view_as=subscriber\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@rootedband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/rooted.band/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@rooted.band","post":false}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"312541","title":"Mae Graf is an Indie-Pop musician who is making her debut in 2024. Her music is characterized by passionate melodies and introspective lyrics, which sets her apart- drawing from personal experiences and a wide array of influences.","date":"2024-05-03","lead":"An acoustic-pop ballad about finding oneself amidst betrayal.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/312541/8209410e63dd5f02e56464a395f7759c.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"An acoustic-pop ballad about finding oneself amidst betrayal."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/32PrUWu8mV6xud2WMplIJT?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Shreveport, LA (May 3, 2024) - On the rise Pop artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7AXxTBw47UcsiM0NzHZSFz?si=KKYjv11hQwmrachOHhuNXA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mae Graf</strong></a> announces the release of her second single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/32PrUWu8mV6xud2WMplIJT?si=c27c40134b604c22\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Like Me Better This Way</strong></a>”. A vulnerable acoustic indie ballad, the track sees Graf grappling with rejection and betrayal, but coming out the other side a stronger person for it."},{"t":"p","html":"Known for drawing upon her own experiences to create her music, Graf presents an intimately raw portrayal of what it's like to lose friends and be betrayed by those who you care about most. Written after the loss of a friend, “I Like Me Better This Way” shares Graf's perspective of not knowing what she did wrong, but being ghosted anyways."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/ILikeMeBetterThisWay","label":"Listen to \"I Like Me Better This Way\" on Streaming Platforms","color":"#ff9797"},{"t":"quote","html":"I wrote this in a very dark place just trying to recover from what had just happened. I want this song to touch people and normalize the other side of being ghosted by people you thought cared about you.","cite":"Mae Graf, Songwriter"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/633022/large-e854b86d92871786b7076d7255b43527.png","alt":"Cover Art, \"I Like Me Better This Way\""},{"t":"p","html":"“I Like Me Better This Way” is the follow up to her wildly successful debut single <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eBExqKXxd1SHDVPGW4PUN?si=a5927f860a584a36\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Barbie”</strong></a> and showcases a different side of Graf's musical artistry. Graf's debut was met with astounding praise with publications like <strong><em>Elite Music News</em></strong> and <strong><em>PopOff</em></strong><em>&nbsp;</em>claiming, “Graf’s voice conjures up suggestions of <strong>Avril Lavigne</strong> and <strong>Liz Phair</strong>, with its delectable rasping quality. It’s a grand voice, powerful yet nuanced by a steady succession of flaring timbres.”"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627770/large-2db97d6637bc2925d3b4d09196d8d483.jpg","alt":"DSC02675-2-_ZF-2973-88740-1-002_.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627770/preview-efd3aef38e0da455c8647e9fb2c306d1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627771/large-1feefc82e080d00b0006f6f37f7716f4.jpg","alt":"DSC02763-2-_ZF-2973-88740-1-001_.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627771/preview-ac31bc9c361b243a886930017e38551a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627772/large-169874372357df560372c490a33dbb78.jpg","alt":"M10R3669.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627772/preview-902526797543383538cb346c6e36b950.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627773/large-5f210d04e3a392fc114ae8eec6535f9c.jpg","alt":"M10M3710.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627773/preview-9c843b7383d0e7f1f86cf4cb20e1857c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627774/large-d81cad93af586acbebe6998f9165209b.jpg","alt":"M10R3681.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627774/preview-e9eb2cf97bfa2e1bdfb736f7c09c2469.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Mae Graf:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7AXxTBw47UcsiM0NzHZSFz?si=wA6U7OalRsWImG1t2r_5IA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mae Graf</strong></a>’s musical journey is deeply rooted in her upbringing, where writing became her vessel for releasing emotions. From journaling to songwriting, her music reflects raw vulnerability, serving as a microscope into her soul and experiences. With a foundation built on real-life narratives, her emotionally driven melodies resonate with listeners, capturing the essence of human emotions."},{"t":"p","html":"From a young age, Mae was immersed in music, thanks to a nanny who sang and wrote songs with her. As she delved into voice lessons and school performances, her passion for music grew exponentially. Now at 15 and inspired by icons like<strong>&nbsp;Gracie Abrams</strong> and <strong>Taylor Swift</strong>, Mae’s raspy vocals and storytelling prowess evoke shades of <strong>Avril Lavigne&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>. Her indie-pop sound, characterized by passionate melodies and introspective lyrics, sets her apart, drawing from personal experiences and a wide array of influences. As she continues to evolve creatively, Mae Graf remains dedicated to her craft, aspiring to leave a lasting impact on the music industry.&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Mae!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.maegrafmusic.com/","img":"","title":"Mae Graf is an Indie-Pop musician who is making her debut in 2024. Her music is characterized by passionate melodies and introspective lyrics, which sets her apart- drawing from personal experiences and a wide array of influences.","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/maegrafmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@maegrafmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@maegrafmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@maegraf4599\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"310080","title":"Stephanie Babirak Enchants Listeners with New Single \"Berry Quartz\"","date":"2024-04-26","lead":"This haunting melody of love lost and longing unveiled on Friday, April 26.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/310080/3771058f97f6c35abb52273578c218e2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This haunting melody of love lost and longing unveiled on Friday, April 26."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1Zfs4Rgequ5dLpSJpy4yt9?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (April 26, 2024) - Prepare to be swept away by the haunting melodies of <a href=\"https://www.stephaniebabirak.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephanie Babirak</strong></a>'s latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1Zfs4Rgequ5dLpSJpy4yt9?si=44cd36123c644f94\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Berry Quartz</strong></a>,”.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"In “Berry Quartz,” Babirak's poignant lyrics paint a vivid picture of yearning and remembrance, evoking the bittersweet ache of longing for someone who is no longer there. The gentle strumming of the guitar and the ethereal tones of the harp create a mesmerizing backdrop, while the layered synths and atmospheric strings add depth and richness to the sound."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1RTP3uUSd5w7QVQuslDnm4?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Collaborating with friends <strong>Peter Scoma</strong> and <strong>Cody Geil</strong>, Babirak elevates “Berry Quartz” to new heights, infusing it with a rich, emotive energy that resonates deeply with listeners. From its heartfelt lyrics to its captivating melodies, “Berry Quartz” is a testament to Babirak's prowess as a storyteller and musician, offering a poignant reflection on love, loss, and the enduring power of memory."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641244/large-779d0ec8dd865f2c8a12e614063bf763.jpg","alt":"IMG_6585.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641244/preview-2dded95fa1481145e9f4669fd4b910f2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641243/-182d26adc0217c45e73c6ccfe8651ffe.jpg","alt":"IMG_6337.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641243/preview-cec426785bab3c2224b06b867144dfc2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641245/large-5e62e4957bec2dd93117a27affc3ee80.jpg","alt":"IMG_6586_copy.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641245/preview-e4abe43b3459316385524f09adfa509c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641246/large-e2b323b485d62d6deea773a5f966e222.jpg","alt":"IMG_0343_copy.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641246/preview-b33dc441bb25ff4406e1908c499bf5a1.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Stephanie Babirak:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Stephanie Babirak</strong> is a renowned harpist based in New York City. Lauded as “seraphic” and “a lovely harpist” by the <strong>Huffington Post</strong>, she is best known for her contemporary approach to the harp. She has performed with pop acts like <strong>Adele</strong>, <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, and <strong>Sandra Day</strong>, and her performances have been featured in the <strong>2018 Super Bowl </strong>commercial for <strong>Hyundai Genesis</strong> and on <strong>NBC’s “Mr. Robot.”</strong> She has toured nationally and internationally, playing venues ranging in size and prestige from debuting works at Carnegie Hall and Lincoln Center, the Edinburgh Fringe Festival, to a sound bath in a Brooklyn salt cave. Her mission is to create music that makes the harp relevant and accessible to all audiences.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephanie!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/stephaniebabirak/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@stephaniebabirak","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/stephbabirak/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"308102","title":"Matthew Morgan Breaks New Ground with \"Two-Sided Town\" - A Sonic Exploration of Modern ​Division","date":"2024-04-23","lead":"The new track was officially launched on Friday, April 23rd on all streaming platforms.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/308102/32c497b95a95362056d1b92a508f54a6.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new track was officially launched on Friday, April 23rd on all streaming platforms."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1YZu8wpULesTMO5pFgnTr0?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Columbus, OH (April 23, 2023) - &nbsp;After the resounding success of his indie-folk album, '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5Jgv2h2lPqq3YdlVxQC9KY?si=hQJHIdjRS-ahAHm7c0bnvA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Timepiece</strong></a>', singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://www.matthewmorganmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Matthew Morgan</strong></a> is back with a captivating new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4ygb5rCxJPLyiJ6jABM4Jm?si=5DinDa4lSuqzV-7kFHlFlQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Two-Sided Town</strong></a>”. This track marks a departure from Morgan's previous work as he ventures into alternative rock territory, delving into the intricate nuances of modern societal polarization."},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by the talented <strong>Brian Skeel</strong>, based in Columbus, Ohio, “Two-Sided Town” is a powerful sonic journey that showcases Morgan's vocal prowess and his ability to craft evocative narratives. Set against a backdrop of stirring melodies and sharp percussion, the song's waltz-like rhythm captures the listener's attention from the very first note."},{"t":"p","html":"The song's lyrics offer a stark commentary on the current state of affairs, exploring themes of political and social division, the erosion of trust, and the urgent need for unity.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I think that a lot of people are shocked by how separated we are as a society and culture right now and I think a lot of us are wondering how much of this divide is rooted in truth and how much of it is perpetuated by the constant stream of media. Regardless, there is clearly a big disconnect and inability to communicate effectively in the US and it starts with our leaders in congress and trickles down.\"","cite":"- Matthew Morgan, Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/639741/large-bdce761612bdae93efdb24c697474feb.png","alt":"Artwork & Imaged by Rob Colgan"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Accompanying the release of “Two-Sided Town” is an official lyric video, providing viewers with a visual interpretation of the song's compelling narrative.</em>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/gAhIa29tVyo","height":""},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>LYRICS FROM \"TWO-SIDED TOWN\"</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"We're falling down"},{"t":"p","html":"In this two-sided town<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\">_"},{"t":"p","html":"We are alive"},{"t":"p","html":"In this great divide"},{"t":"p","html":"In these city walls"},{"t":"p","html":"We should burn them all"},{"t":"p","html":"Or knock them down"},{"t":"p","html":"And I can't back down"},{"t":"p","html":"​_"},{"t":"p","html":"'Cause oh your mouth is frightening"},{"t":"p","html":"When the words come out"},{"t":"p","html":"Your lies and hate fall down like rain"},{"t":"p","html":"In this two-sided town"},{"t":"p","html":"​_"},{"t":"p","html":"We're falling down"},{"t":"p","html":"In this two-sided town"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Matthew Morgan:"},{"t":"p","html":"Matthew Morgan is on a mission to prove to the world that alternative folk can be embraced by the LBTQIA+ community, that a singer-songwriter from the heartland can compose words expressing anti-racist sentiment, and that a great-sounding country song can carry a deeper message without relying on overused and outdated tropes! Refusing to be labeled, or pigeonholed into genderized, racialized, or any other “-ized” stereotypes he joins the ranks of similar progressive singer-songwriters such as <strong>Orville Peck</strong>, <strong>Crys Matthews</strong>, and <strong>Willy Carlisle</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Matthew released his debut CD with Chicago’s acoustic indie label, CAUDog Records in 2012 immediately going on tour around the Midwest and Southern US states in cohort with his band, <strong>The Lost Brigade</strong>. The touring resulted in sold-out shows headlining at Chicago’s famous Double Door nightclub and House of Blues and opportunities to share the stage with more notorious acts at music festivals including opening for <strong>Dave Davies</strong> (The Kinks) and <strong>Company of Thieves</strong> at Taste of Lincoln Ave (Chicago) and <strong>SXSW </strong>(Austin) in 2013."},{"t":"p","html":"Seeking a more introspective sound to his song craft Morgan parted ways with The Lost Brigade in 2014 and recorded a new solo EP that was released independently the following year. While The Lost Brigade’s sound was indebted to contemporary indie rockers like <strong>Wilco&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>The Decemberists</strong>, the <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/44glNFQhBi6FiBJ6t1FjbQ?si=Yus5xNaiSgios8jGUOvzbw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Empathy for Inanimate Objects</strong></a><strong>’</strong> EP calls to mind the happier moments of <strong>Elliott Smith</strong> or the open-ended ponderings of <strong>Tom Brousseau</strong>. Empathy as a whole was very well received and Morgan garnered his first published reviews and the inclusion in the “Best of 2015” by the Nashville Music Guide. A new “Family” band was formed and the empathy tour resulted in venues of greater status including an opening slot or <strong>Ben Ottewell</strong> (of Gomez) and a chance to debut at Chicago’s premiere music club, The Metro.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5Jgv2h2lPqq3YdlVxQC9KY?si=M-2OvqfgSeyR_4sPxJ4Uww\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Timepiece</strong></a><strong>’</strong> marks Morgan’s first full release since 2015 - showcasing his maturity as a songwriter and storyteller, now available for streaming on all platforms! Morgan's new single \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1YZu8wpULesTMO5pFgnTr0?si=23e195e5d3ec47c6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Two-Sided Town</strong></a>,\" was launched on Friday, April 23rd."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Matthew!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/mattmorganmus/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@mattmorganmus","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://matthewmorganmusic.com/bio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/mattmorgansmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/matthewmorganmusic1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"307175","title":"Home page of Brooke Ashton. Brooke’s songwriting delves into universal themes of love, hope, resilience, and the human condition. Her lyrics are steeped in emotional honesty, addressing the challenges and triumphs of life with vulnerability and authentic","date":"2024-04-19","lead":"Ashton's inspiring new song reflects on the beauty and fragility of life.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/307175/ac8c5575bc1012bbc21ed190c964ba5a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Ashton's inspiring new song reflects on the beauty and fragility of life."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1RwSwZYCSm3Sm0hINHXzyT?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Greenville, SC (April 19, 2024) - <a href=\"https://brookeashtonmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Brooke Ashton</strong></a>, a talented singer-songwriter from Greenville, SC, released her poignant new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1RwSwZYCSm3Sm0hINHXzyT?si=607c4b63380c41c8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Someone</a>”. This thought-provoking song, inspired by the passing of a dear friend, delves into the depths of the human experience, urging listeners to cherish the present moment and love wholeheartedly."},{"t":"quote","html":"“If I've ever written a song that had the potential to 'change the world,' this would be it. I got goosebumps when writing this song, and I get chills every time I listen to it. This song was divinely inspired, and I am honored to have received it.\"","cite":"Brooke Ashton, SC-Based Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7D7Qq9H039uiuZ77vMlcVz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"With heartfelt lyrics and a powerful melody, “Someone” serves as a reminder of the importance of living in the present and showing compassion to others. The song captures the essence of the human condition, highlighting the universal need for connection and understanding."},{"t":"p","html":"Described as ethereal, grounded, and reflective, “Someone” falls within the genres of melancholic folk and Americana. The track's evocative sound invites listeners to embark on a journey of introspection."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/639200/large-9e3205cc543a043714a0f9f2352ff216.png","alt":"\"Someone\" Cover Art"},{"t":"quote","html":"“All of the musicians who collaborated on this song donated their time and expertise in loving memory of a mutual friend. Their collective efforts have resulted in a touching tribute to the beauty and fragility of life.\"","cite":"Brooke Ashton, SC-Based Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/639201/large-677a3e69dd00cb49fe7ca146ba0c5be1.jpg","alt":"_dsc2657_edit_jpeg.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/639201/preview-536ee3209c759b1485883d79db016931.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/639202/large-dedd00a5876a2309f70e1f17946ca28d.jpg","alt":"_dsc2729_edit_jpeg.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/639202/preview-19253a1e3c9505b4d05408b627e29a45.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644504/large-89e5d65d315a037ff7a74081d5c3fb0f.jpg","alt":"brooke_ashton_courtesy_artist.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644504/preview-006c50efb15e350f42547adbb491c3a6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644505/large-ba419cdf53b50723d7a43f4c1ea17597.jpg","alt":"brooke_ashton_2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/644505/preview-31da85189f761e84aa633929c142ddbd.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brooke Ashton:"},{"t":"p","html":"Combining her love for lyrics and catchy melodies, Brooke Ashton enjoys writing songs about real life experiences. Honest, authentic, and inspiring are just a few words that have been used to describe her music. On any given day, Ashton can be found humming a new tune, belting out an existing song, or piecing together lyrics. She loves spending time with her family, hiking, adventure eating, traveling, and of course; songwriting!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Brooke!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://brookeashtonmusic.com/","img":"","title":"Home page of Brooke Ashton. Brooke’s songwriting delves into universal themes of love, hope, resilience, and the human condition. Her lyrics are steeped in emotional honesty, addressing the challenges and triumphs of life with vulnerability and authentic","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/brookeashtonmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@brookeashtonmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<br><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/brookeashtonmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://brookeashtonmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"312536","title":"Magdalena Rose","date":"2024-04-18","lead":"Magdalena Rose Breathes New Life Into Her Remake of The Classic Jazz Standard","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/312536/b0081b124bfdd34acf3929991dd63f83.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Magdalena Rose Breathes New Life Into Her Remake of The Classic Jazz Standard"},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/magdalenarose/georgia-on-my-mind","label":"Stream Here","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"GEORGIA, USA (April 24, 2024) - Multi-genre artist Magdalena Rose has recently released a captivating jazz cover of the timeless song \"Georgia On My Mind\". Drawing inspiration from her childhood in Montana, where she first heard the song by the legendary Ray Charles, Magdalena's rendition pays homage to the rich history and significance of this American classic."},{"t":"p","html":"To re-create this song, Magdalena collaborated with a talented team of musicians and producers. Vocal arrangements by Magdalena Rose, saxophone by Kyle Schroeder, drums by Jonathan Thomas, piano by Joe Cosas, and string arrangements by Aaron Warwick come together to create a soulful and nostalgic sound."},{"t":"p","html":"What sets Magdalena Rose's jazz cover apart from other versions is its ability to transport listeners to a place of emotional resonance. With a focus on evoking a dream-like quality, Magdalena's rendition breathes new life into this beloved jazz standard, offering a fresh perspective on the genre."},{"t":"p","html":"The re-release of the song commemorates the date of its inauguration as the official state song of Georgia on April 24, 1979, bringing attention to the enduring impact of \"Georgia On My Mind\" and its place in American music history."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/643779/large-12da8f0dfc7a34a44d20cea0a2d63ee1.jpg","alt":"Cover Art for \"Georgia On My Mind\" by Magdalena Rose"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Magdalena Rose:"},{"t":"p","html":"Magdalena Rose is a multi-genre artist, vocalist, recording artist and songwriter originally from Butte, Montana. She began her music career performing in school and church plays, local sporting events and holiday parties. As a youth Magdalena became an active choir member, competing in Pacific Northwest Choir tours and Solo &amp; Ensemble competitions. She attended Concordia University Portland on both choir and cross-country scholarships. After settling in Florida, Magdalena began collaborating with local musicians and performing in fine dining establishments across Tampa Bay. Her smooth jazz influence is showcased through her previous works, her rendition of George Gershwin's \"Summertime\" was released in November 2022 followed by her first original single, \"Fooled Me,\" and debut album, <em>It's a Wonderful World</em>, in 2023.&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>CONNECT WITH MAGDALENA ROSE:</strong>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5TRBd7QpBvbGS4HlVUX0eI?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://magdalenarose.net/","img":"https://s0.wp.com/i/blank.jpg","title":"Magdalena Rose","desc":"Visit the post for more."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/magdalenarosep/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@magdalenarosep","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"310673","title":"Pop-Soul Singer Adelide to Release New Single \"Witness,\" A Modern Twist on Forbidden Love","date":"2024-04-11","lead":"A tantalizing reinterpretation of the age-old tale of temptation, reimagined as a modern, queer romance.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/310673/57b309d4c18e5069c28b29f12afc8a5a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A tantalizing reinterpretation of the age-old tale of temptation, reimagined as a modern, queer romance."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1re3TIqQjPyyfdedkXcC06?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Brooklyn, NY (May 10, 2024) - <a href=\"https://www.itsadelide.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Adelide</strong></a>, the emerging NYC soul-pop sensation, is poised to captivate audiences with her latest release, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1re3TIqQjPyyfdedkXcC06?si=e8aca032f7b3472e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Witness</strong></a>.\" This track, a fusion of soul-pop and disco, offers a modern interpretation of the age-old story of temptation and forbidden love, drawing parallels to the Garden of Eden narrative."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/qAzM9Z3F0UE?si=6NizCljPPupw2Qra","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"\"Witness\" unfolds as a tantalizing reinterpretation of the age-old tale of temptation, reimagined as a modern, queer romance fueled by synthesizers, disco balls, and desire. Adelide's distinct vocals intertwine with pulsating rhythms and shimmering melodies, guiding listeners through a narrative that explores the complexities of passion and surrender. With its synth-driven take on 80s funk and disco, \"Witness\" offers a fresh sonic experience that resonates with audiences across genres."},{"t":"p","html":"The accompanying music video, directed and produced by Margot Bennett, further delves into the song's themes while taking viewers on a visually stunning journey through a modern-day Garden of Eden. With striking cinematography and choreography, the video elevates \"Witness\" to a multisensory experience that lingers long after the music fades."},{"t":"quote","html":"I created an entire music video around the idea of a pear functioning as a sexy, feminine alternative to the Biblical apple, but I literally cannot bring myself to eat one. When the crew found out, they made me take a bite on camera, and I promptly spat it out - that footage exists somewhere.","cite":"Adelide, Soul-Pop Musician"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>\"WITNESS\" LYRICS (SNEAK PEAK)</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"Look what you’ve done dear"},{"t":"p","html":"Look at what you’ve done to me"},{"t":"p","html":"​Deep in your garden"},{"t":"p","html":"Hidden so the world can't see"},{"t":"p","html":"Reach out your hand and make me take a bite"},{"t":"p","html":"If we’re not supposed to"},{"t":"p","html":"Why's it have to feel so right"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"Crafted over the course of a year, “Witness” is a cohesive and compelling distillation of the eclectic influences of her debut EP. Director Margot Bennett's contributions color the track with depth and scale, inviting viewers into a world where temptation lurks around every corner."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Margot and I happened to meet at a show where we were both performing, just as I had begun exploring the idea of making a music video. This serendipity was the swift kick I needed to bring my imagination into action. Six months later, we had our team assembled and got to work.\"","cite":"Adelide, Soul-Pop Musician"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/642835/large-1a9c3e1f7e0592a32aa9a503c24ab424.jpeg","alt":"AD3.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/642835/preview-54f9dbb02c0d4d4b198dfff74c443cde.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/642836/large-7a4e9ab25c4b19c26d688b8f7348b731.jpeg","alt":"AD4.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/642836/preview-68bb8d96b6185d11fd3dafe8bac0926c.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/642837/large-691302e11c0b9750099e2e50fbd77f44.jpeg","alt":"AD1.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/642837/preview-3d5f29250e62690ce62c44d0510e9f2c.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/642838/large-65a8941876b8d4f5a9a6aa3b99aeeaf6.jpeg","alt":"AD2.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/642838/preview-831b108077a0574c1b7319a2f3633016.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/642995/large-833250afd146bf3a2e1bb26b5a7ea9c1.jpg","alt":"KAYLA_CARRY_ME_05.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/642995/preview-55d4bea09f701a3690b98870959570db.jpg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Adelide:"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from Brooklyn, NY, singer-songwriter <strong>Adelide </strong>intertwines coolly personal lyrics with twinkling synthesizers and lush guitars to create her signature brand of soul-pop. Her music lives in a world of implied intimacy, like the corner of an old photograph or an overheard conversation. It is a space to reimagine and confront the past in a haze of fog machines and strobe lights. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"As the first in a series of singles set to release in 2024, \"Witness\" is the opening statement of Adelide’s next sonic and visual chapter. Her self-titled debut EP, featuring her signature blend of soul-pop, is out now and available everywhere. With an extended version of \"Witness\" featuring Melvin Knight slated for release on May 30th, Adelide continues to push and redefine the boundaries of modern music. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0zXhxzXds0Ea3AUz5063hL?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Adelide!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/its.adelide\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@adelideknits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>​"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/its.adelide/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@its.adelide","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"310077","title":"Brandon Vee - YouTube","date":"2024-04-10","lead":"Orlando, FL (April 8, 2024) - Brandon Vee, a rising R&B artist known for his blend of Funk, Soul, and Pop, unveils his latest single, \"Yellow,\" on April 8, 2024. The song brings forth a message of resilience, joy, and acceptance, especially resonant during Autism Awa...","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/310077/baf938aaae1290d747b204dff5e95e8d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0hr7Le9uEGBooCtUwZDehK?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Orlando, FL (April 8, 2024) - <strong>Brandon Vee</strong>, a rising R&amp;B artist known for his blend of Funk, Soul, and Pop, unveils his latest single, \"Yellow,\" on April 8, 2024. The song brings forth a message of resilience, joy, and acceptance, especially resonant during Autism Awareness Month. \"Yellow\" is more than just a song; it's a beacon of light for those navigating challenges, particularly individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD)."},{"t":"quote","html":"“My daughter has ASD and the artist I have collaborated with has a son who has Autism. Since it is Autism awareness Month, we both have encountered the challenge of helping our children navigate through school and social interactions.\"","cite":"- R&B Artist, Brandon Vee"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"The song's lyrics encapsulate the theme of embracing one's true self amidst societal pressures and internal struggles. Brandon Vee's poignant verses convey empathy and support, reminding listeners that their uniqueness is their strength. Through the catchy chorus, Vee affirms, \"Can’t nobody ever / Steal my yellow never / All My joy and pleasure / It’s all mine forever.\""},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641240/-540cbabb4ec88d7be1570bc9ba77534e.jpeg","alt":"image1.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641240/-540cbabb4ec88d7be1570bc9ba77534e.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641241/large-08d7c24fa61a7378a9b349222292fafa.jpeg","alt":"image0.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641241/preview-7f54053981007d84c4438da734efd44a.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641247/-4c883f3a622b1865e9a7248a2b065c48.jpeg","alt":"image2.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/641247/-4c883f3a622b1865e9a7248a2b065c48.jpeg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Describing the sound of \"Yellow\" as Funk-infused, Happy, Cheerful, and Soulful, Brandon Vee emphasizes the importance of understanding and acceptance. He remarks,"},{"t":"quote","html":"&nbsp;\"We can’t assume that everyone is at the same emotional capacity we are at, for those on the Spectrum, socializing can be very tough.\"","cite":"- R&B Artist, Brandon Vee"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"Accompanying the release is the vibrant cover art and a photo featuring Brandon Vee alongside the featured artist Kristen Warren. The collaboration between these two talents not only delivers a memorable musical experience but also serves as a testament to the power of inclusivity and support."},{"t":"p","html":"As the world observes Autism Awareness Month, this release shines a light on the importance of mental health awareness and acceptance.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brandon Vee:"},{"t":"p","html":"Brooklyn, NY native Brandon Vee fuses the energy of hip-hop with the classic melodies of R&amp;B and Jazz to create a funk-inspired aura and sound. Brandon started his lyrical journey at the young age of 10 when he started writing poetry to express complex feelings of heaviness and discomfort. Brandon continues to use music as a medium of self-discovery and healing intertwining the boundaries of his own worldly perspectives with personal growth. Brandon Vee creates a unique and powerful sound with his music, carrying listeners through storylines of spirituality, introspection, and self-discovery. Vee draws inspiration from diverse yet legendary artists such as <strong>J. Cole</strong>, <strong>Childish Gambino</strong>, and <strong>Funkadelic</strong>. In 2022, Brandon Vee performed alongside famous artists such as <strong>Meg The Stallion</strong>, <strong>Denzel Curry</strong>, <strong>EarthGang</strong>, and more, inspiring him to showcase his new music on a live platform more often. Vee's new single \"<strong>Yellow</strong>\" released on Monday, April 8th and is dedicated to Autism Awareness Month."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Brandon Vee!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://Brandon%20Vee%20Shopify\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Brandon Vee Shopify</strong></a>"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.youtube.com/user/brandonveemusic?cbrd=1&amp;ucbcb=1","img":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/ytc/AGIKgqM6UblH3ImOAL4zsQwvmw6wgpalTJcvHXBv3B8NbA=s900-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj","title":"Brandon Vee - YouTube","desc":"Brandon Vee is an artist and performer from Brooklyn NY. His music combines Hip-Hop with Soul, R&B, Funk and even Jazz. As an artist, Brandon provides a pers..."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Cstlj_aLEHD/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://Instagram.com/thatmanvee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.thatmamvee.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>WEBSITE</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/officialbrandonvee/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/thatmanvee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>SOUNDCLOUD</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"297396","title":"Read More","date":"2024-04-05","lead":"Dynamic pop-indie ensemble from Richmond, VA have launched their new sonic gem.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/297396/78b351ba12d350772d9e4825655e32d2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"p","html":"Dynamic pop-indie ensemble from Richmond, VA have launched their new sonic gem."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/65IqAJNpiJKnn1DGlT3ui1?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Richmond, VA (April 5, 2024) - <a href=\"https://www.erinandthewildfire.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Erin &amp; The Wildfire</strong></a>, the dynamic pop and indie sensation hailing from Richmond, Virginia, are set to electrify the music scene once again with their latest single, “<strong>Lightning So Blue</strong>” released on Friday, April 5, 2024."},{"t":"p","html":"“Lightning So Blue” encapsulates raw honesty and trust within intimate moments, exploring themes of relationships, intimacy, and female pleasure. The track's lyrics vividly describe the sensation of orgasm, with lines like “the lightning was so blue behind my eyes” painting a picture of the transcendent experience."},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/erinandthewildfire/lightning-so-blue?utm_campaign=website&amp;utm_medium=Email%20&amp;utm_source=SendGrid","label":"Listen to \"Lightning So Blue\" on All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#f3866f"},{"t":"quote","html":"'Lightning So Blue' is my favorite song we've recorded in this last year. It's dance-y and fun, but it's also sensual and mysterious.\"","cite":"- Erin Lunsford, Lead Singer of Erin & The Wildfire"},{"t":"p","html":"Musically, “Lightning So Blue” is a fusion of pop and indie elements, with hints of R&amp;B adding depth to the melody and vocal interpretation. The track seamlessly transitions between dark, bass-heavy verses and shimmering, bright choruses, mirroring the changing states of the body during intimate moments."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/03NHhY1mdWC3Hf9uJEnomj?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"'Lightning So Blue' is about being honest and trusting in intimacy. When I sing 'lightning so blue behind my eyes,' it’s describing how your vision blurs during orgasm. It's weird that talking about orgasm can feel taboo for women, but understandable when there’s an ongoing and historical effort by lawmakers to limit women’s bodily autonomy. I wrote this song to encourage women to feel good in their sexuality and confident in their ability to talk openly about pleasure. This song serves as a reminder that we are in control of our own bodies and can feel confident standing in our own pleasure.”","cite":"- Erin Lunsford, Lead Singer of Erin & The Wildfire"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"Producer <strong>Rob Dunnenberger</strong>, along with recording at <strong>Spacebomb Studio</strong> in Richmond, Virginia, has helped Erin &amp; The Wildfire craft a song that is both danceable and thought-provoking. Mixed by <strong>Alex DeJong</strong> and mastered by <strong>Ed Brooks</strong> at <strong>Resonant Mastering</strong>, “Lightning So Blue” promises to be a sonic journey unlike any other.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/633019/large-70f254b890029c9c6d35d966bdd60bca.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-03-08 at 12.44.37 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/633019/preview-c6a23abb8dcd2acc31873e101eb81e01.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/633020/large-70440a5d6100fed9f6638d903d70897f.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-03-08 at 12.44.31 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/633020/preview-b5c4612596dfed337de612f5c57ff650.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/633021/large-691b4ab25b02a6ea1b6056e2725b16fd.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-03-08 at 12.44.51 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/633021/preview-958e97a8c7b8daebdc5b51a2d637555e.png"}]},{"t":"p","html":"***<em>Fans can catch the band live at their single release show at&nbsp;</em><a href=\"https://www.gettightrva.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Get Tight Lounge</strong></em></a><em>&nbsp;in Richmond, VA on <strong>Saturday, April 6, 2024</strong>, with special guest <strong>Shera Shi</strong>.***</em>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://dice.fm/event/ro3xw-erin-the-wildfire-single-release-show-6th-apr-get-tight-lounge-richmond-tickets?pid=530cb286&amp;_branch_match_id=946034778613073593&amp;_branch_referrer=H4sIAAAAAAAAA8soKSkottLXz8nMy9ZLyUxO1UvL1XdNSk5ONDA2srAwN7AvyEyxNTU2SE4ysjADAEYFGRcuAAAA","label":"GET YOUR TICKETS HERE","color":"#f3866f"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Erin &amp; The Wildfire:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Erin &amp; The Wildfire,</strong> originally formed by college friends in Charlottesville, Virginia, have blossomed into a tight-knit musical unit over the past decade. Now based in Richmond, Virginia, they fuse soul and indie-pop, drawing inspiration from a diverse range of artists like <strong>Emily King</strong> and <strong>D’Angelo</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Led by powerhouse vocalist <strong>Erin Lunsford</strong>, the band infuses their music with pop, funk, and indie vibes, complemented by the talents of <strong>Ryan Lipps</strong>, <strong>Nick Quillen</strong>, and <strong>Matt Wood</strong> - often accompanied by <strong>Stephen Roach</strong>. Lunsford’s lyrics delve into personal struggles, advocating for body acceptance and self-love while addressing broader issues like climate change and gender equality in the music industry."},{"t":"p","html":"Their second album, “<strong>Touchy Feely</strong>,” released in 2022 and produced by <strong>Matthew E. White</strong>, received acclaim for its meticulous production and compelling songwriting, building on the success of their hit single “<strong>Shape</strong>.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Erin &amp; The Wildfire have captivated audiences at sold-out shows and prestigious events like <strong>NPR’s Mountain Stage</strong>. They've supported national tours and shared stages with notable acts such as <strong>Chaka Khan</strong> and<strong>&nbsp;Jill Scott</strong>, leaving lasting impressions at major festivals across the East Coast. In 2019, Erin's vocals were praised by <strong>Rolling Stone</strong> during her performance at <strong>FloydFest</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"The rising indie-pop band released their song “<strong>Love Songs To Georgia</strong>” earlier this year and released their new single, “<strong>Lightning So Blue</strong>” on April 5th, 2024.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Erin &amp; The Wildfire!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.erinandthewildfire.com/links","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@erinandthewildfire/video/7353257052086586667","handle":"@erinandthewildfire"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/erinandthewildfire/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@erinandthewildfire","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@erinandthewildfire\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ErinandtheWildfire/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QkCOA-8PfOg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.erinandthewildfire.com/links\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"293182","title":"Rising Pop Sensation Mae Graf Drops Debut Single, \"Barbie\"","date":"2024-03-29","lead":"Prepare for a scream-in-the-car pop anthem about love, loss, and self-discovery.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/293182/7e0de0c88b8266e21ba25f4cee558294.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Prepare for a scream-in-the-car pop anthem about love, loss, and self-discovery."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0eBExqKXxd1SHDVPGW4PUN?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Shreveport, LA (March 29, 2024) - Up-and-coming Pop artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7AXxTBw47UcsiM0NzHZSFz?si=KKYjv11hQwmrachOHhuNXA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mae Graf</strong></a> launched the release of her debut single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0eBExqKXxd1SHDVPGW4PUN?si=9a687e35b9b943fa\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Barbie</strong></a>” on March 1st, Friday. “Barbie” is guaranteed to wow listeners with its infectious beat and heartfelt lyrics.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/lX9FTEczHZs?si=8aXZihvN7Cn1p71Y","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"“Barbie” delves into the tumultuous emotions of young love and self-discovery, as Mae Graf reflects on her teenage experiences with vulnerability and honesty. Written at the tender age of 13, “Barbie” channels Graf’s personal journey of navigating relationships, self-esteem, and the pressures of comparison."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Barbie","label":"Listen to \"Barbie\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/633022/large-e854b86d92871786b7076d7255b43527.png","alt":"MAE.png"},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Barbie’ was my first song, born from a tangled situation: I liked a guy who was also talking to my friend. It sparked emotions that I ended up pouring into the music. Although this song is upbeat and fun, it’s also very vulnerable and relatable in a way.”","cite":"- Mae Graf, Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"With its upbeat tempo and impassioned vocals, “Barbie” encapsulates the essence of Graf’s signature sound. Combining elements of pop with a raw emotional edge, the song serves as a powerful anthem for anyone who has grappled with feelings of insecurity and self-doubt."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627770/large-2db97d6637bc2925d3b4d09196d8d483.jpg","alt":"DSC02675-2-_ZF-2973-88740-1-002_.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627770/preview-efd3aef38e0da455c8647e9fb2c306d1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627771/large-1feefc82e080d00b0006f6f37f7716f4.jpg","alt":"DSC02763-2-_ZF-2973-88740-1-001_.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627771/preview-ac31bc9c361b243a886930017e38551a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627772/large-169874372357df560372c490a33dbb78.jpg","alt":"M10R3669.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627772/preview-902526797543383538cb346c6e36b950.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627773/large-5f210d04e3a392fc114ae8eec6535f9c.jpg","alt":"M10M3710.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627773/preview-9c843b7383d0e7f1f86cf4cb20e1857c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627774/large-d81cad93af586acbebe6998f9165209b.jpg","alt":"M10R3681.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627774/preview-e9eb2cf97bfa2e1bdfb736f7c09c2469.jpg"}]},{"t":"quote","html":"“This is a song for listeners to scream-sing in the shower, in the car, or wherever they are. It embodies female rage.”","cite":"- Mae Graf, Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Mae Graf:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7AXxTBw47UcsiM0NzHZSFz?si=wA6U7OalRsWImG1t2r_5IA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Mae Graf</strong></a>’s musical journey is deeply rooted in her upbringing, where writing became her vessel for releasing emotions. From journaling to songwriting, her music reflects raw vulnerability, serving as a microscope into her soul and experiences. With a foundation built on real-life narratives, her emotionally driven melodies resonate with listeners, capturing the essence of human emotions."},{"t":"p","html":"From a young age, Mae was immersed in music, thanks to a nanny who sang and wrote songs with her. As she delved into voice lessons and school performances, her passion for music grew exponentially. Now at 15 and inspired by icons like<strong>&nbsp;Gracie Abrams</strong> and <strong>Taylor Swift</strong>, Mae’s raspy vocals and storytelling prowess evoke shades of <strong>Avril Lavigne </strong>and <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>. Her indie-pop sound, characterized by passionate melodies and introspective lyrics, sets her apart, drawing from personal experiences and a wide array of influences."},{"t":"p","html":"As she continues to evolve creatively, Mae Graf remains dedicated to her craft, aspiring to leave a lasting impact on the music industry. With debut music on the horizon for 2024, it’s only a matter of time before Mae Graf becomes a rising sensation in the indie-pop scene."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Mae!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/maegrafmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@maegrafmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@maegrafmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@maegraf4599\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"295220","title":"Andrew Neil & Code Purple's \"Houston\" Takes Listeners On a Cosmic Ride Through Love and Loss","date":"2024-03-29","lead":"The new song explores space-related themes that artfully tie into the song's introspective lyrics.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/295220/c91d121044ca419a669d65ca2bb32f49.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new song explores space-related themes that artfully tie into the song's introspective lyrics."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0lfpvw0i1VSnLb2AnKzopg?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Gordonsville, VA</strong> (March 29, 2024) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6QUGMOwpGGRqhFW7ZD4eJB?si=KvF4mefwT7ylsP6tH61KoQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple</strong></a>, the acclaimed alternative rock band known for their innovative sound and thought-provoking lyrics, released their latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0lfpvw0i1VSnLb2AnKzopg?si=40986896e9624e94\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Houston</strong></a>,” on March 29, 2024. This eagerly anticipated track promises to captivate listeners with its psychedelic rock vibe and whimsical journey through themes of love, loss, and personal transformation."},{"t":"p","html":"“Houston” showcases Andrew Neil’s signature blend of imaginative storytelling and raw emotion, weaving together elements of science fiction, personal turmoil, and romantic entanglements into a captivating musical narrative. The song’s lyrics, penned by Andrew Neil himself, offer a quirky yet poignant exploration of the human condition, set against a backdrop of cosmic adventure and introspection."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/houston","label":"Listen to \"Houston\" on All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"LYRICAL PREVIEW"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Houston, we have a little problem</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Pretty girls their hearts I rob them</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Houston, we have a little problem, here here</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>No way in hell you’re going to solve em</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Houston, we have a little problem</em>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"With references to space exploration, existential crises, and the enduring allure of the American West, “Houston” invites listeners on a multi-dimensional voyage that transcends traditional genre boundaries. The song’s infectious melody and evocative lyrics promise to leave a lasting impression, inviting audiences to ponder the deeper meanings behind the music."},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Houston’ illustrates the sad ending of a relationship. This relationship at one time filled me with such happiness I was higher than outer space but what goes up must come down and it came down.”","cite":"- Andrew Neil, Lead Singer, Andrew Neil & Code Purple"},{"t":"p","html":"Featuring Andrew Neil’s distinctive vocals and Code Purple’s dynamic instrumentation, “<strong>Houston</strong>” offers a fresh perspective on the complexities of human emotion and the universal quest for belonging. From its catchy hooks to its introspective lyrics, this latest release is poised to resonate with listeners from all walks of life."},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to its musical merits, “Houston” provides fertile ground for exploration beyond the realm of music. Drawing on themes of science fiction, personal transformation, and cultural mythology, the song opens the door to a wide range of non-music topics, from the psychology of self-reflection to the cultural impact of space exploration."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6QUGMOwpGGRqhFW7ZD4eJB?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Andrew Neil</strong>, born on August 9, 1988, in Colorado Springs, is the creative force behind the indie sensation “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6QUGMOwpGGRqhFW7ZD4eJB?si=booFs-qRQJiYxOmUrxXZLg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple</strong></a>.” Overcoming challenges, Andrew’s journey is a testament to the transformative power of music. A former High School Athlete and US Military Academy recruit, his life took an unexpected turn in 2009 after a traumatic head injury, sparking the creation of over 450 original compositions. Often compared to “Outsider music artist” <strong>Daniel Johnston</strong>, Andrew’s musical narrative unfolded in 2017 with “<strong>Code Purple</strong>,” a Lofi masterpiece recorded within the walls of a psychiatric hospital. Partnering with producer Andy Waldeck, subsequent studio albums like “<strong>M</strong><strong>erry Go Round (2018)</strong>,” “<strong>Freak (2019)</strong>,” “<strong>Sunny Side (2021)</strong>” and “<strong>Alien (2022)</strong>,” showcased resilience and creative depth, even amid a battle with Non-Hodgkin’s Lymphoma in 2019."},{"t":"p","html":"Sparked by an opportunity to perform as the opening act for the <strong>Raelyn Nelson Band</strong> in Nashville, Andrew Neil formed a new band to back him up. &nbsp;The band’s initial lineup featured Andrew Neil on rhythm guitar and lead vocals, accompanied by <strong>Daniel Houser</strong> on lead guitar and banjo, <strong>Alan Warren</strong> on bass, <strong>Rick Shaw</strong> on mandolin, and <strong>Zach Bullock</strong> on drums."},{"t":"p","html":"Following their performance, the band experimented with their sound by recording and releasing a lo-fi track titled “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2UV0x98VGgwP4zF22WXGqS?si=dc662b2274654f2d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Like</strong></a>” as a single. However, shortly after its release, Zach Bullock and Alan Warren stepped down from the band due to long-term commitment issues. This led to a month-long search for a new drummer, culminating in the addition of Logan Wayne, while Rick Shaw transitioned to playing bass."},{"t":"p","html":"In August 2023, with their refreshed lineup, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6QUGMOwpGGRqhFW7ZD4eJB?si=kukSeOESRCCl4bAooy-PyQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple</strong></a>” spent four productive days at <strong>White Star Sound Studios</strong> in Louisa, Virginia. During this time, they recorded twelve original tracks. Out of these, nine tracks were selected to be part of their debut album ‘Resurrection,’ marking a significant milestone in the band’s evolving musical narrative."},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond the studio, a forthcoming book chronicles Andrew Neil’s battle with mental illness and cancer. The band’s new song “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0lfpvw0i1VSnLb2AnKzopg?si=2a83ebc2016c4c33\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Houston</strong></a>” launched on Friday, March 29th. Learn more about new music below!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple!"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@codepurpleband/video/7330389172899007790","handle":"@codepurpleband"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/R6lVWXtFgDM?si=Zch-ZXw9tsdnUY5c","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/CodePurpleBand/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/andrewneilmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@codepurpleband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"293174","title":"Dreamcat Weaves Sensory Haven with New Single \"Nostalgia\"","date":"2024-03-22","lead":"The Alaskan pop duo's new tune blasts through with nostalgic sonic beauty","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/293174/8151e59347f75b17e81afd973ff96646.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Alaskan pop duo's new tune blasts through with nostalgic sonic beauty"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3vdaYFfhaPdFAPA4bG7qcJ?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Anchorage, ALASKA (March 22, 2024) - Rising indie-pop duo <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3K9fTRuyA2UY0vs4ncFs3p?si=tB6jUwJURZGwM7VbBh6YkQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>dreamcat</strong></a>&nbsp; pulls audiences back to memory lane with their new single “<a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Nostalgia\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Nostalgia</strong></a>”, dropped on March 22,2024. <strong>Em Glaves</strong> and <strong>Colton Ciufo</strong> created their new song with producer <strong>James Glaves</strong> - rendering a sound that blends the essence of a summer anthem from the 80's with a modern pop song."},{"t":"p","html":"“Nostalgia” promises to be a captivating journey through memories and emotions, blending the familiarity of the past with the excitement of the present. The track transports listeners to a realm of cherished memories and wistful yearning."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Nostalgia","label":"Listen to \"Nostalgia\" on All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/627764/large-e238bbda611af0c36fe91a3083b34e86.jpg","alt":"\"Nostalgia\" Cover Art"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song is about how music can have a profound effect on one's emotions. It's a reflection on the beauty and complexity of nostalgia, and we're excited to share it with the world.\"","cite":"- dreamcat, Indie-Pop artist"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>\"NOSTALGIA\" LYRICS (sneak peak)</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>On the streets, summer days through the lens of a Sony Hi8</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Ridin’ our bikes to the video store</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Havin’ dreams about, the pink sky over the cellphone tower.</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I don’t wanna let go of nostalgia</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I don’t wanna let it go (ext.), no no no no no.</em>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"With each verse of “Nostalgia,” listeners are transported to a time of carefree summer days, riding bikes to the video store, and gazing up at the pink sky. The repetition of “I don't wanna let go of nostalgia” echoes the sentiment of holding onto cherished moments, even as time passes.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3K9fTRuyA2UY0vs4ncFs3p?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About dreamcat:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>dreamcat</strong> AKA <strong>Colton Ciufo</strong> has loved performing and creating music since childhood. As a result of taking piano lessons as a kid, dreamcat played synth in a metal band with his friends, performing and playing some of his first shows when he was only 17. dreamcat has carefully curated his niche within the music industry and has fine-tuned his songwriting over the years. Music has always been dreamcat's escape, using creativity as a means for coping with alcoholism, social anxiety, and depression. Since attending a rehab facility in Southern California, dreamcat has been going through positive psychological, lifestyle, and spiritual changes. dreamcat's purpose is to make positive yet heartfelt music that makes him feel good and inspires listeners from whatever place they find themselves in life. Tune in to dreamcat's latests track,<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Nostalgia\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Nostalgia</strong></a>!<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with dreamcat!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/dreamcat123456/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@dreamcat123456","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"295232","title":"Stephanie Babirak Unveils Emotionally Charged Song \"Waves and Whispers\"","date":"2024-03-22","lead":"The acclaimed classically trained harpist-turned-singer fuses folk-pop with harp-forward echoes of the heart.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/295232/785b3905b5fcd03f4193f16eda7941e9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The acclaimed classically trained harpist-turned-singer fuses folk-pop with harp-forward echoes of the heart."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/41RTAVvnuqZvO1vqyKmH1G?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (March 22, 2023) - <a href=\"https://www.stephaniebabirak.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stephanie Babirak</strong></a>, acclaimed folk-pop artist and classical harpist, drops the latest release of her latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3TWEFrkhUbkvP1TZxCTarZ?si=8kiwXXIZTOiFi46rkB4y4w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Waves and Whispers</strong></a>,” which debuts on Friday, March 22, 2024."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1RTP3uUSd5w7QVQuslDnm4?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"“Waves and Whispers” captures the essence of beachy folk-pop with its haunting melodies and heartfelt lyrics. Combining Babirak's signature harp melodies with evocative vocals, the song explores themes of love, loss, and the pain of separation. Written during a period of personal introspection, the song reflects Babirak's own experience of going no contact with a loved one, expressing the agony of not being able to communicate with someone deeply missed."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song started off as just a little melody on the harp. I hadn't written a song for over a decade (I was pursuing a career as a classical harpist) and this was the melody that brought me back to songwriting...and I've written many songs since!\"","cite":"- Stephanie Babirak, NYC-Based Singer-Songwriter/Harpist"},{"t":"p","html":"In “Waves and Whispers,” Stephanie Babirak channels the raw emotions of love and loss into haunting melodies and poignant lyrics. Babirak shares that the song emerged from a deeply personal experience of estrangement, reflecting the anguish of being unable to communicate with a beloved family member. Each note and lyric is infused with the ache of longing and the bittersweet nostalgia of memories past. Through her music, Babirak delicately weaves together the threads of heartbreak and hope, inviting listeners into a journey of emotional resonance and introspection."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/632342/large-e50196c856f34044ac4eb280527dbe9e.png","alt":"\"Waves and Whispers\" by Stephanie Babirak // Cover Art"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Whether you are going through a breakup or have lost someone or are choosing not to speak to someone, &nbsp;I think we all have the experience of the pain of not being able to talk to someone you love very much and having every little mundane thing remind you of them.\"","cite":"- Stephanie Babirak, NYC-Based Singer-Songwriter/Harpist"},{"t":"p","html":"With its poignant lyrics and captivating melodies, \"Waves and Whispers\" is a testament to Babirak's talent as both a musician and a storyteller. <em>The song was co-written with Babirak's longtime friend and collaborator, <strong>Peter Scoma</strong>, who adds depth to the track with his guitar and vocals.</em>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/632343/-b92050d4946dfd218bd0dc0cb7727584.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-03-06 at 3.26.26 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/632343/-b92050d4946dfd218bd0dc0cb7727584.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/632344/large-e67baebda322899f7d200516539d2e4a.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-03-06 at 3.26.48 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/632344/preview-24195fd6c5607126b659f0deb6adb008.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/632345/large-7ccf10e76a13103f66f0c1ca33f5d043.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-03-06 at 3.26.37 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/632345/preview-e90576edd3879cdc9da6b92758a16e38.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Stephanie Babirak:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Stephanie Babirak</strong> is a renowned harpist based in New York City. Lauded as “seraphic” and “a lovely harpist” by the <strong>Huffington Post</strong>, she is best known for her contemporary approach to the harp. She has performed with pop acts like <strong>Adele</strong>, <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, and <strong>Sandra Day</strong>, and her performances have been featured in the <strong>2018 Super Bowl </strong>commercial for <strong>Hyundai Genesis</strong> and on <strong>NBC’s “Mr. Robot.”</strong> She has toured nationally and internationally, playing venues ranging in size and prestige from debuting works at Carnegie Hall and Lincoln Center, the Edinburgh Fringe Festival, to a sound bath in a Brooklyn salt cave. Her mission is to create music that makes the harp relevant and accessible to all audiences.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Stephanie!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/stephaniebabirak/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@stephaniebabirak","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/stephbabirak/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"291624","title":"Xan DuBose Unleashed Sultry New Single: \"Serious Craving\"","date":"2024-03-15","lead":"Charleston, SC (March 15, 2024) - Rising artist Xan DuBose (she/her) captivates audiences with the release of their latest single, \"Serious Craving\". This enticing track delves into the depths of desire and longing, exploring the irresistible pull towards someone who may...","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/291624/5bceb659ce04a2a7eb9ddb2a2942c324.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6qzYHUpbe0e9lD0wNgROcj?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Charleston, SC (March 15, 2024) - Rising artist <a href=\"https://www.xandubosemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Xan DuBose</strong></a> (she/her) captivates audiences with the release of their latest single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6qzYHUpbe0e9lD0wNgROcj?si=7htJEoLsSqymdYFUt8tWvA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Serious Craving</strong></a>\". This enticing track delves into the depths of desire and longing, exploring the irresistible pull towards someone who may not be the best choice but remains impossible to resist."},{"t":"p","html":"\"Serious Craving\" paints a vivid picture of the passion and tension experienced when consumed by desire. Recorded in the aftermath of a tumultuous breakup, the song serves as a candid reflection of the raw emotions that come with yearning for someone who ignites a fire within, even amidst the pain of heartache."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wanted to step outside of my comfort zone, liberating myself from the confines of convention, and to wholeheartedly dive in to this journey without hesitation. My intention was for this song to embody the essence of the bold individual that I aspire to become. Embracing every part of yourself including your sensuality and confidence is imperative, I wasn’t going to let anything stand in the way of that.”","cite":"-Xan DuBose, Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626982/large-293247d79c6965418d5842f64199363b.jpeg","alt":"\"Serious Craving\" Cover Art"},{"t":"p","html":"Blending elements of pop, country, and alt-rock, <strong>Xan DuBose</strong> delivers a powerful performance that showcases their vocal prowess and diverse musical influences. Drawing inspiration from the likes of <strong>Allen Stone</strong>, <strong>Amy Winehouse</strong>, and <strong>Carrie Underwood</strong>, the track exudes a sultry and seductive vibe, weaving together intricate vocal jazz melodies with infectious country-western rhythms."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625410/large-acebf8828f6c8a695ba936635d712c37.jpg","alt":"6I5A5188.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625410/preview-0a0b074c14122b7c1ce566c667d1556c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625409/large-01fe7663da0213b824be6147366cbce0.jpg","alt":"6I5A5206.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625409/preview-17a53c6d2509c1c49097930f174d715c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625411/large-3a14033ac0c3d3eb57dd37d452a391c9.jpg","alt":"6I5A4917.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625411/preview-cd145594d4a563d250359bfda5365c48.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625412/large-eb4a7af7ff840eec00346837e7ba0504.jpg","alt":"6I5A2827.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625412/preview-eed8b97430b3dfc111aa943838f0523a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625413/large-b1d1d8f470d9048575cc56300de25e8c.jpg","alt":"6I5A2949.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625413/preview-b621935c6e63aa73b90528ed0c398595.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625414/large-a80cc9ada66bb72d1cc74493db6300ce.jpg","alt":"6I5A2230.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/625414/preview-bd2b510a4d9a5f6c2df81f97bb2a5e6e.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Accompanying the release of \"Serious Craving,\" fans can anticipate a mesmerizing music video starring Xan DuBose and featuring <strong>Trey Francis</strong>, a prominent figure in the South Carolina music scene. Scheduled for release two weeks after the single's debut, the music video promises to visually encapsulate the song's themes of desire, love, and tension."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Xan DuBose:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Xan DuBose</strong> (she/her) is an exceptionally talented singer-songwriter hailing from the vibrant musical scenes of Columbia and Charleston, South Carolina. With a captivating voice that effortlessly blends elements of jazz, soulful vocals, contemporary sounds, and a touch of country flavor, Xan's music resonates with listeners on a profound level."},{"t":"p","html":"Since making her debut in the SC music scene back in 2013, Xan has become a recognizable and highly sought-after artist. She gained considerable acclaim as a member of <strong>Patrick Davis' Midnight Choir</strong>, a testament to her remarkable vocal prowess and stage presence. Her performances alongside acclaimed artists such as <strong>Darius Rucker</strong>, <strong>Thomas McClary</strong>, <strong>Charles Kelley</strong>, and others have further solidified her reputation as a standout talent."},{"t":"p","html":"Xan finds creative influence in iconic artists such as <strong>Bill Withers</strong>, <strong>Allen</strong> <strong>Stone</strong>, <strong>Madison</strong> <strong>Cunningham</strong>, and <strong>Brandi</strong> <strong>Carlile</strong>. These diverse influences infuse her music with a unique blend of heartfelt lyrics, soulful melodies, and a timeless quality that transcends genres."},{"t":"p","html":"With her versatile musical style, Xan DuBose takes her listeners on a captivating journey through the intricacies of jazz, the emotional depths of soul, the infectious beats of contemporary sounds, and the storytelling essence of country music. Her performances are characterized by an irresistible blend of vulnerability, passion, and authentic artistry that leaves a lasting impact on all who have the privilege of experiencing her music."},{"t":"p","html":"As Xan continues to mesmerize audiences and carve her own path in the music industry, her infectious energy and undeniable talent have firmly established her as a rising star. With each captivating performance and heartfelt composition, Xan DuBose is making an indelible mark on the music scene, captivating the hearts of listeners far and wide."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Xan!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/iiVeYxh0eu4?si=AKVJL0QxTscgoI9b","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/xan_dubose/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@xan_dubose","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/user/1250467657?si=21afa3c610744cee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/alexandra.dubose.7?mibextid=LQQJ4d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"295226","title":"Experience the Vibrant Energy of Racyne Parker Through Her Latest  Release, \"Already Late\"","date":"2024-03-14","lead":"This pop-country anthem officially launched, just in time for sunny days and warm weather adventures.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/295226/dfc47f22979d26299af0cdfbf88f63eb.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This pop-country anthem officially launched, just in time for sunny days and warm weather adventures.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6hLHCOYhyLgnREDhLPBU56?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (March 14, 2024) - Rising indie-folk singer <a href=\"https://racyneparker.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Racyne Parker</strong></a> is set to captivate audiences once again with her latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6hLHCOYhyLgnREDhLPBU56?si=254a1926a9504727\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Already Late</strong></a>,” which dropped on March 14, 2024."},{"t":"p","html":"“Already Late” exudes vibrant energy with its driving guitars and heartfelt vocals, delivering a blend of country, pop-country, singer-songwriter, folk, and Americana influences. The song encapsulates the exhilarating pursuit of dreams while navigating the complexities of love and life’s uncertainties."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/AlreadyLate","label":"Listen to \"Already Late\" on Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song is for you if you’re working towards something bigger than what you’ve got while also building your life at home with the people you love.”","cite":"- Racyne Parker, Indie-Folk Singer"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/DHjBhRj5NRU?si=B6JOEgvff7nxrJnc","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"With bright and happy energy, “Already Late” serves up fun road trip vibes while capturing the angst of chasing dreams while being in love. The lyrics paint a vivid picture of feeling behind on one’s aspirations, even amidst a fulfilling relationship and a sense of home. Racyne Parker’s introspective storytelling delves into the internal conflict of striving for success while cherishing the connections that ground us."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I always feel like I’m running late - literally, figuratively, existentially - even if I have nowhere to be. I don’t think that feeling will ever go away, but at least now I have this feel-good jam to soundtrack those moments.”","cite":"- Racyne Parker, Indie-Folk Singer"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/630528/large-607e218fe633c81a69ed8c597908f7d7.jpg","alt":"racyne-already-late-9.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/630528/preview-03119a4f6c380ebebcb09fdafee3c678.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/630529/large-3ecb998be5deff38f024790767aa200e.jpg","alt":"racyne-already-late-6.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/630529/preview-dc4d81fb5d676d7ceab9e5ac899c8070.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/630530/large-ddb21fa032a96b2d12a1f1283dd43dec.jpg","alt":"racyne-already-late-1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/630530/preview-5d3dbb499e3e7fa9cb4ac965187a0fd4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/630535/large-438a00a4c80fd5da7a8ac0d95925e69d.jpg","alt":"2Already Late - Lyric Video v2.00_02_02_28.Still001.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/630535/preview-9ea4f69d2bbd231ac2f573ab8a8a4b77.jpg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Randall Kent</strong> at<strong>&nbsp;Deaf Dog Studios </strong>in Nashville, TN, and featuring a talented ensemble including <strong>Brian Cox </strong>on drums, <strong>Regan Akers </strong>on bass, and <strong>Blake Mohler </strong>on guitar, “Already Late” promises to be a standout addition to playlists alongside artists like <strong>Maggie Rogers</strong>, <strong>Kacey Musgraves</strong>, <strong>Lainey Wilson</strong>, and <strong>Kelsea Ballerini</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Accompanying the release, Racyne Parker unveils an official Vevo lyric video, produced and directed by <strong>Seth Beamer Productions</strong>, on her </em><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@RacyneParker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>YouTube</em></a><em> channel. “</em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6hLHCOYhyLgnREDhLPBU56?si=d2d702c4bf99474b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Already Late</strong></em></a><em>” marks the third single from Racyne Parker’s upcoming project, promising an exciting journey for fans eagerly awaiting her next musical endeavor.</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/69uzZLXVJPGmB52ik2Rw0g?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Racyne Parker:"},{"t":"p","html":"Originally from Southern Oregon, Denver-based singer-songwriter <strong>Racyne Parker</strong> draws inspiration from country, modern folk, indie rock, and pop influences, to deliver catchy lyrics, warm vocals, and a contemporary style that fits in well on playlists next to <strong>Kacey Musgraves, Taylor Swift, </strong>and<strong> Caylee Hammack.</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"An engaging and low-stakes performer, Racyne is bound to play a song that you know while also introducing new songs to you that you’re sure to love."},{"t":"p","html":"Her honest and original tunes draw on her experiences with living in and leaving a small town, navigating uncertainty in love and life, and finding joy in the little moments.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"An up-and-comer in the Denver music scene, with lots of new music on the way, Racyne hopes to build community, create joy, and remain true to herself through the music that she makes.<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Racyne!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/4INHqTTYZ2Q?si=IHH4aMf0QCttDQzY","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/racyneparker/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@racyneparker","post":false},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@racyneparker/video/7289306760421051678","handle":"@racyneparker"},{"t":"p","html":"<br><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/RacyneParkerMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@racyneparker?is_from_webapp=1&amp;sender_device=pc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | ​<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/racyneparker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/racyneparker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>threads</strong></a><br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"296096","title":"Custom Vinyl Records Pressing Offers Revolutionary Discounts on Vinyl Record Pressing","date":"2024-03-02","lead":"TORONTO, CANADA (March 2, 2023) -  Custom Vinyl Records Pressing, a pioneering force in the vinyl pressing industry, announces an unprecedented 30% discount on all vinyl record pressing services, revolutionizing the landscape for music enthusiasts and independent artists...","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/296096/b04706d0a822ede2eaecc7603112833d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"p","html":"TORONTO, CANADA (March 2, 2023) - &nbsp;<a href=\"https://customvinylrecordspressing.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Custom Vinyl Records Pressing</a>, a pioneering force in the vinyl pressing industry, announces an unprecedented 30% discount on all vinyl record pressing services, revolutionizing the landscape for music enthusiasts and independent artists alike."},{"t":"p","html":"Founded by Paul Murton, Custom Vinyl Records Pressing traces its roots back to 1998 when Murton embarked on his journey as a sales representative at the esteemed Sony music plant. Following Sony's departure from Canada, Murton seized the opportunity, inheriting the legacy of the plant's equipment and employees. What started as a venture into CD duplication evolved into a full-fledged endeavor focusing on vinyl record production."},{"t":"quote","html":"“In 2017, the music industry witnessed a resurgence in vinyl records, yet challenges persisted in meeting the demand. With the inception of Custom Vinyl Records Pressing, we aimed not only to meet but to surpass industry standards.\"","cite":"- Paul Murton, Founder & Owner of Custom Vinyl Records Pressing"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"The company's commitment to innovation led to a groundbreaking partnership with a German manufacturer, resulting in the development of a state-of-the-art press capable of producing superior quality vinyl records in 4 weeks time. Unlike its predecessors, this cutting-edge press enables short runs of records at a remarkable 36% discount, making high-quality, retail-ready vinyl records more accessible than ever before."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Custom Vinyl Records Pressing is dedicated to empowering artists and labels by providing unparalleled quality and affordability. We believe that every artist deserves the opportunity to share their music in the timeless format of vinyl.\"","cite":"- Paul Murton, Founder & Owner of Custom Vinyl Records Pressing"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"In line with this vision, Custom Vinyl Records Pressing offers competitive pricing, with 100 retail-ready records available for as low as $1,199, ushering in a new era of accessibility and creativity in the music industry."},{"t":"p","html":"+++"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>For more information on Custom Vinyl Records Pressing and their services, visit <strong>customvinylrecordspressing.com</strong> or contact Paul Murton directly at <strong>(888) 679-1207</strong>.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\"></em>"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"288179","title":"Shawn Price Unveils Powerful Single \"Lay Our Burdens Down\"","date":"2024-02-29","lead":"This release marks Price's long-awaited return to the indie music scene.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/288179/d5693f9b39b06717a7dc3b7802d4ec93.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This release marks Price's long-awaited return to the indie music scene."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6LeS6IWMbrkiutWB7ckfOT?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Worthington, OH (February 29, 2024) - Rising Ohio-based musician <a href=\"https://shawnpricemusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Shawn Price</strong></a>&nbsp;makes a remarkable return to the music scene with the release of his latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3f6CazzMTecFEaXVLH8QIR?si=TZfppRnNQl26g9SaTbDGTg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lay Our Burdens Down</strong></a>.” This highly anticipated track dropped on Thursday, February 29, 2024."},{"t":"p","html":"“Lay Our Burdens Down” pays homage to the era of 70’s rock, with instrumentals and tonal elements infused with a soulful touch. The song takes listeners on a journey through the struggles of individuals holding on to life’s challenges, only to decide to release their burdens and pursue a more fulfilling existence."},{"t":"quote","html":"“It’s been far too long since I’ve released new music, and I’m excited to rediscover who I am as an older, more mature artist.”","cite":"-Shawn Price, Alt-Rock Musician"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>LYRICS PREVIEW</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Someone stoke my fire</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>We're gonna let it burn to black</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>We don’t need to hold it back</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Let the flames rise higher and higher</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>We’re gonna lay our burdens down</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5ihnQytfie7c9vPmG8rwuL?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The single, produced and recorded by <strong>Jay Alton</strong> and mastered by <strong>Brian Lucey</strong>, boasts a lineup of talented local Columbus musicians, including <strong>Jeff Straw</strong> on keys, <strong>Eric Clemens&nbsp;</strong>on electric guitar, <strong>Rob Mottice</strong> on drums, and <strong>Patrick Long</strong> on bass. Price’s wife, <strong>Sarah Price</strong>, is featured on harmonies, adding an extra layer of depth to the song."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/618627/compressed_original-28dc4da224de46fe89ec9849f6c8b211.png","alt":"Cover Art for “Lay Our Burdens Down”"},{"t":"p","html":"In “Lay Our Burdens Down,” Shawn Price delves into the complexities of life, offering a poignant reflection on the universal struggle to balance comfort with the yearning for something more profound. With introspective lyricism, Price challenges listeners to contemplate what it truly means to live authentically — to leave everything on the table while uncovering joy in the simplicity of everyday existence.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I ultimately aim to create music I’d enjoy listening to, and hope audiences old and new will enjoy this new single as much as I do.”","cite":"- Shawn Price, Alt-Rock Musician"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<em><strong>**To celebrate the release, Price will be performing live at&nbsp;</strong></em><strong><a href=\"https://www.theramblinghouse.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>The Rambling House&nbsp;</em></a></strong><em><strong>in Columbus, OH, on February 29th at 9 pm EST. Don’t miss the opportunity to witness this dynamic artist in action!**</strong></em>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Shawn Price:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Shawn Price</strong> is a folk rock singer-songwriter known for his soulful voice and heartfelt lyrics. Shawn got his start playing as the lead singer and songwriter of the band <strong>The Olde Souls </strong>and <strong>The Makeshift Band</strong>, entertaining countless bar patrons over the years."},{"t":"p","html":"After taking a hiatus to focus on his family, Shawn has recently returned to the music scene as a solo artist, showcasing his talents as a singer and songwriter. His music draws inspiration from the highs and lows of everyday life, finding truth in both the surreal and mundane."},{"t":"p","html":"With a sound that blends folk, rock, and pop influences, Shawn’s music harkens back to the soulful 70s and has been compared to the stylings of <strong>Joe Cocker</strong> and <strong>Ray Lamontagne</strong>. His lyrics are honest and relatable, while his performances are filled with energy and charm. Shawn Price is a must-see performer for music fans looking for an authentic and engaging live experience. Price’s new single released on February 29th, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6LeS6IWMbrkiutWB7ckfOT?si=be01a660097a4023\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lay Our Burdens Down</strong></a>” marking his return to the music scene after over a decade."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Shawn!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Gp7TyG-ZCHg?si=mkNl8xVyP5yZTDwJ","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/shawnpricemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@shawnpricemusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://shawnpricemusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/shawnpricemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a> <strong>|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@shawnpricemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"291878","title":"ellakate is an alternative pop singer-songwriter making her debut Fall 2022. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way. To keep up with ellakate, check out her Instagram and stay tuned for new music coming soon.","date":"2024-02-23","lead":"The 5-track musical milestone guides listeners through a range of emotional trials and tribulations.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/291878/994e8ff4a2fd3a2f91c1585de2e58f38.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The 5-track musical milestone guides listeners through a range of emotional trials and tribulations."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3gkCMBVjqKgNFYaaUZRdtD?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Atlanta, GA (February 23, 2024) - Emerging pop sensation <strong>ellakate </strong>unveils her highly anticipated 5-song EP: <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3gkCMBVjqKgNFYaaUZRdtD?si=2MDUK6AbRm6DsdIrD8BTSQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Illusion</em></strong></a>. Combining elements of Pop and Alternative Pop, ellakate invites listeners on a profound journey delving into themes of mental health, toxic relationships, coping mechanisms, addiction, loneliness, obsession, and burnout."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Illusion</em> is a compilation of songs that intricately narrate the journey of using unhealthy coping mechanisms to alleviate negative emotions. From grappling with burnout and boredom to seeking solace in intentionally volatile relationships, each track unveils a different facet of the human experience. Through poignant lyrics and emotive melodies, ellakate's EP serves as a testament to the illusory comfort provided by these mechanisms, ultimately leading back to the same feelings of emptiness and loneliness."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This EP is a group of songs that are all unique in style, yet cohesive in story. Each song conveys a different emotion, taking you on a sonic journey. From the upbeat, fun vibe of 'Dry' to the eerie theatricality of 'I’m Yours,' and the stripped-back vulnerability of 'Illusion,' there's something for every listener to connect with.\"","cite":"- ellakate, Rising Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626439/large-b10db69064f650047d4cd2cdc641d17f.png","alt":"Illusion Cover Art"},{"t":"p","html":"Reflecting on the creative process, ellakate expressed her deep attachment to <em>Illusion</em>, a culmination of over a year's work. Delighted with the final product, she explored various sounds to convey emotions while aiming to offer solace to listeners grappling with similar experiences. She believes the EP resonates with themes of burnout, obsession, and heartbreak, hoping to reassure her audience that they are not alone."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626440/large-76119f9bab1135c09b648f89d8c2cc8d.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-02-19 at 2.21.36 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626440/preview-f6e20b225b9a675ce6fa79d2411a1d73.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626441/large-e741dc8be6a4d1a559b24b3b71ca4c6f.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-02-19 at 2.21.49 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626441/preview-c9f1b65a01be069728121105769e1f85.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626443/large-2a9753eab9833031c9b2fe7e3c5f1f52.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-02-19 at 2.21.42 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626443/preview-85c1b56c0b4c0b7f38dc186495a91c86.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626442/large-937228875843fcda5bace144832f0d6a.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-02-19 at 2.21.26 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626442/preview-6d79b093968bcb7ebd307953d975a1a5.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626444/large-0a6f8e2ce4ca72ed39e05e03a2b11363.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2024-02-19 at 2.21.55 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626444/preview-74a0e4db2e12cbe8ff0f55382e50b7f9.png"}]},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0t5IrUFo0RQnOfVkhZplHd?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About ellakate:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Ella Greenbaum</strong>, artistically known as ellakate, is an alternative pop singer-songwriter born, raised, and based in Atlanta, Georgia. Growing up with musical parents and a knack for creating and performing, ellakate found a passion for music that went beyond forcing her brothers to listen to her melodies as a child.&nbsp;<em>“When my dad first explained what the song ‘<strong>Brandy</strong>’ by <strong>Looking Glass</strong> was about, I discovered the magic of storytelling in songwriting. I have been singing and making up songs for as long as I can remember,”</em> said ellakate about her innate talents. She has written hundreds of songs since her childhood exploring topics that coincide with the journey of growing up and finding love, filling piles of notebooks in her room with song lyrics. ellakate’s songs recount stories and experiences that may have not happened to her but are inspired by events that have impacted her."},{"t":"p","html":"Her voice has been compared to a<strong>&nbsp;</strong>“young <strong>Sara Bareilles</strong>,” showing her vocal prowess - honest and sensual, with a hint of innocence. Her sultry vocals mixed with her haunting, bold, and romantic sound are reminiscent of artists like <strong>Billie Eilish</strong>, <strong>Fiona Apple</strong>, and <strong>Lana Del Rey</strong>. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way. She just released her debut EP, <em>Illusion</em>, on <em>Friday, February 23rd</em>!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With ellakate!"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@ellakatemusic/video/7245424410902007083","handle":"@ellakatemusic"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/ellakatemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@ellakatemusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.ellakate.com/","img":"","title":"ellakate is an alternative pop singer-songwriter making her debut Fall 2022. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way. To keep up with ellakate, check out her Instagram and stay tuned for new music coming soon.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@ellakatemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ellakate9262\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.deezer.com/us/artist/185794237\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Deezer</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/ellakate/1648638724\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Apple Music</strong></a><br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"292648","title":"Reese Weil Unveils Electrifying EP 'Beatwave' - A Fusion of Hip-Hop, Rap, and Rock","date":"2024-02-21","lead":"This EP redefines musical boundaries with genre-fluid collaboration and innovation","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/292648/dfcf35c93ad3d5f3749f6c1988d73dd7.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This EP redefines musical boundaries with genre-fluid collaboration and innovation"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://on.soundcloud.com/1nQR3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LISTENING LINK</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"SAN FRANCISCO, CA (February 14, 2023) - San Francisco-based artist <strong>Reese Weil&nbsp;</strong>has announced the release of his highly anticipated EP: <strong><em>Beatwave&nbsp;</em></strong>- available now on all major streaming platforms. The EP, which dropped on February 14, 2024, showcases a dynamic fusion of hip-hop, rap, and rock, featuring collaborations with renowned artists Nef the Pharaoh and Scando the Darklord."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1sBccPKgFWTizZJEJkORO6?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Beatwave</em> is a testament to the transformative power of collaboration and the boundless creativity that emerges when diverse talents converge. With Nef the Pharaoh’s lyrical prowess, Scando the Darklord’s sharp wit, and Reese Weil’s soulful melodies, each track becomes a sonic journey through the heart of the Bay Area’s vibrant music scene.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Collaborating on ‘Beatwave’ was like a musical homecoming, blending the raw energy of Bay Area hip-hop with soulful melodies and electrifying guitar riffs. It’s a testament to the power of unity and creativity in music.\"","cite":"Reese Weil, CA-Based Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/626995/large-6852a3e6164a8a446b5ca5acf947614c.jpg","alt":"'Beatwave' Cover Art"},{"t":"p","html":"From infectious rhythms to thought-provoking lyrics, <em>Beatwave</em> captivates listeners with its raw energy and unapologetic authenticity. It’s more than just an EP; it's a celebration of individuality and a testament to the enduring spirit of innovation in music."},{"t":"p","html":"The EP features standout tracks such as \"Day Drinkin',\" \"Night Ain’t Over,\" \"Wild Side,\" \"Airplanes,\" \"Sweet to Sour,\" and \"Summer Love,\" each offering a unique sonic experience that transcends traditional genre boundaries."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Being part of this EP allowed me to explore new sonic territories and push the boundaries of my own musical style. It’s a fusion of genres that resonates with the soul, showcasing the beauty of artistic collaboration.\"","cite":"Reese Weil, CA-Based Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Reese Weil"},{"t":"p","html":"Reese Weil is a classically trained guitarist from Chico, CA who began playing guitar at the tender age of four. Heavily influenced by artists like the Beastie Boys, The Beatles, Steely Dan, Tame Impala, Sublime, and Jack Johnson, Weil’s signature tone incorporates a breathy melodic delivery that flows smoothly into tight rhythmic pockets, usually reserved for an emcee. After attending Berklee, Weil set out to make a career in music and played hundreds of shows across Northern California which led him to catch the eye of producer (and founder of Mighty Oak Records), Marty James. While creating Weil’s new EP, the two coined the term “lake-pop” to describe the new genre of feel-good acoustic guitar merged with beat-heavy, aggressive mixes that they have found themselves creating. This eclectic mashup of alternative-pop genres seamlessly blends Weil’s world-class guitar playing with James’ gritty breakbeat signature production style, making for a unique representation of the Northern California lifestyle - a cornerstone that both Weil and Mighty Oak Records have built their identity upon.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"All about small-town dreams with big city passion, Weil embodies the DIY spirit of NorCal with his songs having been dubbed as “the sound of the 530 area code”. Eclectic and gritty, yet soulful and uplifting at the same time, Weil’s music speaks to people with lifestyle hobbies that are characteristic of the NorCal area such as snowboarding, skating, surfing, x-games, and several others. “Music has been the way that I have expressed myself my entire life,” says Weil. “Its been the one constant and kept me sane when life felt too heavy. I will always pour all my soul into every song and performance I'm working on.” Weil is eager to hit the road touring the west coast with the release of his new music this summer as he feels that the songs from the EP are the first true reflection of him as an artist. “This is the best music I've ever made.”"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Reese!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/reeseweil530/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a>​"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reeseweil530/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@reeseweil530","post":false}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"289067","title":"Enchanting Melodies and Whimsical Narratives: Andrew Neil & Code Purple Unveil Their Latest Single \"Blue Moon\"","date":"2024-02-16","lead":"The new track officially drops on all streaming platforms, pushing the boundaries of musical creativity.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/289067/dd7fc7ad5409d0ca4cd5e1c5540b5c0e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new track officially drops on all streaming platforms, pushing the boundaries of musical creativity."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/195Ni2APzwIj8RiI3A0PDv?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Gordonsville, VA</strong> (February 16, 2024) - Renowned for their innovative blend of Alternative Rock, Rock, Garage Rock, and Progressive Rock, <strong><em>Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple</em></strong> have once again pushed the boundaries of musical creativity with their latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/195Ni2APzwIj8RiI3A0PDv?si=aPcDUklrTPOM4MJ9_T9ceQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Blue Moon</strong></a>.” Set to captivate audiences with its whimsical narrative and infectious melody, “Blue Moon” promises to be a standout addition to the band's repertoire."},{"t":"p","html":"The song, co-written by<strong>&nbsp;Andrew Neil</strong> and <strong>Logan Wayne</strong>, takes listeners on a journey through themes of friendship, adventure, and youthful rebellion. With lyrics that paint a vivid picture of playful companionship symbolized by an owl and a mysterious “Were Were Werewolf,” “Blue Moon” invites audiences to embrace the excitement of the night and seize the moment."},{"t":"p","html":"“Blue Moon” delves into the concept of change and unpredictability, using the titular celestial event as a metaphor for rare and transformative experiences. Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple expertly craft a narrative that resonates with listeners, evoking a sense of nostalgia while simultaneously igniting a spirit of adventure."},{"t":"quote","html":"“We wanted to create a song that captured the essence of friendship, adventure, and the magic of the unknown. ‘Blue Moon’ is a celebration of life’s rare and special moments, encouraging listeners to embrace the excitement of the night and live life to the fullest.”","cite":"- Andrew Neil, Lead Singer, Andrew Neil & Code Purple"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6QUGMOwpGGRqhFW7ZD4eJB?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"“Blue Moon” by Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple isn’t just a catchy tune; it’s an anthem of empowerment and resilience. Through its whimsical lyrics, Andrew Neil shares personal struggles and triumphs, using the metaphor of a “Blue Moon” to symbolize hope in the face of adversity. From overcoming mental illness to finding purpose and love, the song’s message resonates deeply with listeners, inspiring them to embrace courage and optimism in their own lives."},{"t":"p","html":"The track pays homage to the timeless allure of <strong>Warren Zevon</strong>’s 1978 hit, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6kotXaSQaGYxE62hVpdHWu?si=06178812b47c4a46\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Werewolves of London</a>.” Like Zevon’s classic, “Blue Moon” conjures whimsy and mystery, drawing listeners into a world of playful companionship and hidden depths. With its infectious melody and profound lyrics, “Blue Moon” invites audiences to embrace the magic of the night and seize every opportunity for adventure, echoing the spirit of resilience that defines rock music."},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to its enchanting lyrics and melody, “Blue Moon” also carries a deeper significance with its reference to the celestial phenomenon of a “Blue Moon.” Occurring approximately once every 2 to 3 years, a “Blue Moon” symbolizes rarity and unpredictability, mirroring the themes explored in the song."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614210/large-6d0434a294c4e045815cea9f8bceb6c6.png","alt":"Resurrection_Front_Cover_3000x3000.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614210/preview-f9453e6cfa1dba7b5cd012761ff3de11.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614212/large-ed7d307ac3ed4267870affd7a918b74c.png","alt":"IMG_1325.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614212/preview-71b72a014f76ddfd52e6a270877d16a9.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/620799/large-3a3417c4fc986c07663d10ae7f991c3e.jpg","alt":"thumbnail_IMG_2720.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/620799/preview-0265ed02ea2a991e444cf4fb281fa074.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/620800/large-e2351a4dce8f310ab6281d83f433db08.jpg","alt":"ANCP_Photos_for_FP_Concert-16.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/620800/preview-2ff869474be16f6059a1ffbaa925ba3c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/620801/large-ca4c905dc547fb5db4d3b6aeeec94332.jpg","alt":"ANCP_Photos_for_FP_Concert_1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/620801/preview-c0e0f2fd7d665decb77d63e9d0b1334f.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Andrew Neil</strong>, born on August 9, 1988, in Colorado Springs, is the creative force behind the indie sensation “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6QUGMOwpGGRqhFW7ZD4eJB?si=booFs-qRQJiYxOmUrxXZLg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple</strong></a>.” Overcoming challenges, Andrew’s journey is a testament to the transformative power of music. A former High School Athlete and US Military Academy recruit, his life took an unexpected turn in 2009 after a traumatic head injury, sparking the creation of over 450 original compositions. Often compared to “Outsider music artist” <strong>Daniel Johnston</strong>, Andrew’s musical narrative unfolded in 2017 with “Code Purple,” a lofi masterpiece recorded within the walls of a psychiatric hospital. Partnering with producer Andy Waldeck, subsequent studio albums like “<strong>M</strong><strong>erry Go Round (2018)</strong>,” “<strong>Freak (2019)</strong>,” “<strong>Sunny Side (2021)</strong>” and “<strong>Alien (2022)</strong>,” showcased resilience and creative depth, even amid a battle with Non-Hodgkin’s Lymphoma in 2019."},{"t":"p","html":"Sparked by an opportunity to perform as the opening act for the <strong>Raelyn Nelson Band</strong> in Nashville, Andrew Neil formed a new band to back him up. &nbsp;The band’s initial lineup featured Andrew Neil on rhythm guitar and lead vocals, accompanied by <strong>Daniel Houser</strong> on lead guitar and banjo, <strong>Alan Warren</strong> on bass, <strong>Rick Shaw</strong> on mandolin, and <strong>Zach Bullock</strong> on drums."},{"t":"p","html":"Following their performance, the band experimented with their sound by recording and releasing a lo-fi track titled “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2UV0x98VGgwP4zF22WXGqS?si=dc662b2274654f2d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Like</strong></a>” as a single. However, shortly after its release, Zach Bullock and Alan Warren stepped down from the band due to long-term commitment issues. This led to a month-long search for a new drummer, culminating in the addition of Logan Wayne, while Rick Shaw transitioned to playing bass."},{"t":"p","html":"In August 2023, with their refreshed lineup, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6QUGMOwpGGRqhFW7ZD4eJB?si=kukSeOESRCCl4bAooy-PyQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple</strong></a>” spent four productive days at <strong>White Star Sound Studios</strong> in Louisa, Virginia. During this time, they recorded twelve original tracks. Out of these, nine tracks were selected to be part of their debut album ‘Resurrection,’ marking a significant milestone in the band’s evolving musical narrative."},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond the studio, a forthcoming book chronicles Andrew Neil’s battle with mental illness and cancer. With the built anticipation for the release of the album’s Title track “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1rqXWC6mpb8aC0grjYkeok?si=oynlBwUeTzizgq1rxbJMKw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Resurrection</strong></a>” on 19 January 2024, Andrew Neil’s mantra, <em>“Music makes a difference in this jello world,”</em> resonates as a guiding principle in their remarkable journey of resilience and self-discovery."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Andrew Neil &amp; Code Purple!"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@codepurpleband/video/7330389172899007790","handle":"@codepurpleband"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/CznzQoO4o-8?si=v-6W2lDpnjAPK5ZW","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/CodePurpleBand/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/andrewneilmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@codepurpleband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"284558","title":"Gemïny Drops 6-Track Dream-Pop EP On Valentine's Day","date":"2024-02-14","lead":"The dark and captivating release, 'My Dark. Twisted Valentine' officially released, leaving listeners twisted.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/284558/a1e6ddef16841d99a4b768dfee9f7e3a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The dark and captivating release, 'My Dark. Twisted Valentine' officially released, leaving listeners twisted."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/66qUyf6j1jE7HfUrT8DChd?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Columbia, SC (February 14, 2024) - Independent pop-soul artist<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/minime.ge_/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Gemïny&nbsp;</strong></a>continues to captivate audiences with the release of his latest EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/66qUyf6j1jE7HfUrT8DChd?si=nIkenvjdT12hd6W1jsSxxw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>My Dark. Twisted Valentine</strong></em></a> on Valentine’s Day. Featuring six emotionally charged tracks, the EP delves into themes of mental health, depression, self-image, heartbreak, love, abuse, trauma, guilt, regret, and insomnia, offering a raw and honest exploration of the artist’s inner world."},{"t":"p","html":"The EP is more than just a collection of tracks; it is a manifestation of Gemïny’s introspection, drawing inspiration from recurring dreams that have left an indelible mark on his life. Gemïny’s creative process for <em>My Dark. Twisted Valentine</em> is rooted in a desire to communicate directly with his audience, sharing the intricacies of his being.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The artist’s unique perspective allows for a profound exploration of the effects of these dreams on the central love story, as well as the psychological reasoning behind the decisions made within that narrative."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>​TRACK LIST</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"01 - Alone (Sleepless)"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1jfYtMwUTUGxjfnw9c5FHN?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"02- <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6vMweclBTLSFMN0lSmU08J?si=a277ad0f793544d9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Run Me Down</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"03 - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2oDgzJLsigz4xMIvc3RpdP?si=995a31c2bb2c48a5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Vice</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"04 - Rock (Right Now)"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4cmvqCpuWLsCNXsHxGqTzw?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"05 - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6w4Bgns9zCPLzwnmKWhRxS?si=143c820252ac45bf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Used 2 Be</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"06 - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1PFMrUverJTUSOgGggmsK8?si=92cd1c1121ae4ef8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TKO (Cradle Song)</a>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"quote","html":"“In ‘Vice,’ I dive into the depths of my own struggles with depression and self-image. It’s not about a person but echoes the internal strife we all confront. The ‘relationship’ in the song mirrors the ongoing battle within.”","cite":"-Gemïny, Pop-Soul Singer/Artist"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614611/large-bf9ea877533a04e02eedd78a41be7b74.jpg","alt":"ALBUM ART"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>SOUNDSCAPE</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"The sound of the EP is a moody yet eclectic mix, rooted in the Pop genre but with a diverse range of influences. Gemïny takes listeners on a sonic journey, from the angsty and chaotic Alone, blending hip-hop, classical, and rock influences, to the yearning melodies of 00’s R&amp;B and Pop ballads in Run Me Down. The EP also features upbeat reggaeton-influenced guitars, synth-heavy riffs, and 808-heavy club-centric vibes, creating a unique and modern experience that seamlessly connects multiple Pop eras."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I’ve really grown to appreciate the struggle of putting together a narrative that flows seamlessly. Choosing from a bunch of songs and ensuring their stories harmonized while making sense in the overall sequence was no easy task.”","cite":"-Gemïny, Pop-Soul Singer/Artist"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3Wm0Khz27xWSexaDJ95RpW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Gemïny:"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from Raleigh, NC, pop-soul artist <strong>Sage “Gemïny” Wesley</strong> fuses raspy rock and smooth jazz to create a unique sound that keeps audiences grooving. Gemïny studied music composition at the University of South Carolina under Composition Professor <strong>John Fitz</strong>. After a brief hiatus in 2020, Gemïny began participating in freelance work such as recording hooks and background vocals for aspiring artists to raise money for the <strong>National Alliance on Mental Illness (NAMI)</strong>. This charity work grew into booking a few small gigs around Columbia where Gemïny performed backup and keys for various bands. Gemïny’s raw vocals and authentic sound make listeners feel like they’re in the audience at one of his live shows or alongside him in the recording studio. Connecting lyrical expression to heartbreak, guilt, lost love, and more, Gemïny displays a strong affinity for storytelling with songs reminiscent of a page ripped from a classic love story: a redefined iteration of the <strong>Heartbreak Hotel</strong>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Gemïny!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/KKly8gRGE-Q?si=9FufP6M6WxDiKKul","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/Cgm4NDjpGgA/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/minime.ge_/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/sage.wesley.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC0hlC08gTP-NnFY-N-9Zinw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YOUTUBE </a>| </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@code5idkthidman\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"277679","title":"Rob Carranza Unveils Remastered Song \"Lucky Ones\"","date":"2024-02-02","lead":"This timeless track explores themes of redemption and gratitude, intertwining music and passion.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/277679/4413a2101220e99071561c27d4a491f2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This timeless track explores themes of redemption and gratitude, intertwining music and passion."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5j9ZqtIq2WoALwRcC9Zx9Z?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston, TX (February 2, 2024) - Renowned singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://carranzaband.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Rob Carranza</strong></a> is captivating audiences once again with the remastered version of his emotive single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5j9ZqtIq2WoALwRcC9Zx9Z?si=d4473c0e2c1449fd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lucky Ones</strong></a>” - released on Friday, February 2, 2024.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Written during the poignant period surrounding the birth of Carranza’s son, “Lucky Ones” reflects the artist’s journey through recovery, gratitude, and newfound fatherhood. Freshly injected into <strong>Alcoholics Anonymous</strong> at the time, Carranza channels his emotions into a powerfully resonant piece that explores themes of redemption and the blessings of life."},{"t":"p","html":"Described as a compelling blend of Power Pop and Rock, this remastered track showcases Carranza’s signature sound and the evolution of his musical prowess. The remastered version promises an enhanced sonic experience, bringing new life to an already timeless composition."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614064/large-5248196da2eeec0337ddeed3e4db233d.png","alt":"Lucky Ones - Cover Art"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wrote this song at the coming of my son’s birth. Freshly injected into AA, I was grateful to be blessed with a child as well as to be alive. ‘Lucky Ones’ is a reflection of my journey through recovery, marriage, and the immense gratitude I feel for my family.”","cite":"- Rob Carranza, Houston-Based Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"Carranza’s single not only resonates with its powerful musical composition but also delves into significant non-music topics such as mental health, children, recovery, marriage, and gratitude. The artist’s genuine and relatable storytelling makes “Lucky Ones” a profound and heartfelt addition to his discography."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/613535/large-869de57af7fa010b360336659f64d44d.jpg","alt":"Photo Feb 23, 12 08 45 AM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/613535/preview-dd0163f99c35391418c10dcc5489b144.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/613536/large-9e8f016bd7e985175abbb80a9a68a949.jpg","alt":"Photo Feb 23, 12 08 51 AM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/613536/preview-caca9cfe17c746e228509f8f5d50171d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/613537/large-2450eaf05255d0888813ffd5d527f099.jpg","alt":"Photo Feb 22, 11 55 11 PM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/613537/preview-54759d1342738155e7c6d707469b5042.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/613538/large-decb356ff22beb0a39d4d383545277c3.jpg","alt":"Photo Feb 23, 12 15 56 AM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/613538/preview-77a608b034fa4bccabf96787121e44ec.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Rob Carranza:"},{"t":"p","html":"In the heart of the Lone Star State, amidst the vibrant music scene of Houston, Texas, lives a seasoned singer-songwriter named Rob Carranza. With a voice that echoes the soul of the city and lyrics that paint vivid portraits of life in the South, Rob is a true musical maestro.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Rob’s journey began in the humid summers of Houston, where the notes of blues/Rock of ZZTop and the crunch post-grunge of King’s X flowed through the air. Inspired by the rich musical tapestry of his surroundings, he picked up his first guitar and never looked back. From smoky dive bars to intimate coffeehouses, Rob honed his craft, his songs becoming anthems for the souls of Texas."},{"t":"p","html":"The son of a preacher-man, Rob grew up in Houston with the strong undertones of southern church in his lyrics. &nbsp;Rob’s mother, a talented drummer and bar owner from <strong>Corpus Christi TX</strong>, infused him with the necessary skills for the music biz."},{"t":"p","html":"Houston itself became Rob’s muse, its sprawling streets and diverse neighborhoods providing the backdrop for his tales of love, loss, and the relentless pursuit of dreams. From Spring Branch, the Heights, to Montrose, every corner held a story waiting to be sung, and Rob’s heartfelt Rock Anthems captured the essence of the city."},{"t":"p","html":"Alongside fellow musicians, Rob formed bonds that transcended mere camaraderie. Together, they crafted melodies that resonated with the collective heartbeat of Houston. Their harmonies echoed through the city's soul, leaving an indelible mark on its musical legacy.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"One fateful night, under the starlit Texas sky, Rob Carranza took the stage at the renowned <strong>Buzz Fest</strong>. The crowd, a sea of eager faces, hung on every note, every word. With each strum of his guitar and every lyric that left his lips, Rob poured his heart into the performance, leaving an indelible mark on the hearts of all who listened."},{"t":"p","html":"As most determined songwriters do, Rob eventually made his way to LA to record a demo with a famed producer. The demo was unanimously picked up by 6 labels; most notably <strong>Universal Records</strong>. Giving in to the vices of fame and fortune, Rob battled the demons of alcohol as most artists do, eventually leading to his dropping out of the touring “band on the road” life."},{"t":"p","html":"Rob Carranza’s songs continue to weave through the tapestry of Houston’s music scene, his legacy living on in the hearts of fans and aspiring musicians alike. His melodies are an enduring tribute to the spirit of the city and a testament to the power of music to connect us all."},{"t":"p","html":"In the annals of Houston’s musical history, the name <strong>Rob Carranza</strong> stands as a testament to the enduring power of a true singer-songwriter. Through his music, he painted a vivid portrait of the city he loved, leaving a legacy that will resonate for generations to come."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Rob!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/tNQirMcHix0?si=W5sGs6vdYbFXfBC3","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/robcarranzamusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@robcarranzamusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@robcarranzamusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.carranzaband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCiNLtkJ-WOmmVA5-ZyVMi3w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/carranzamusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"276236","title":"Indie Artist Pretoria Dropped Highly Anticipated Single \"Seven\"","date":"2024-01-19","lead":"The Michigan-based artist explores diverse emotional planes with this new track.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/276236/d73d0e0aad6695102702f8d1d00a9526.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Michigan-based artist explores diverse emotional planes with this new track."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0jLk4PJZ7AaibwphZN2i3O?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Grand Rapids, MI (January 19, 2024) - Grand Rapids-based indie/rock/pop sensation <a href=\"https://linktr.ee/pretoriamusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Pretoria</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>just released their new single, “<strong>Seven</strong>,” finally hitting the airwaves on January 19, 2024. The independently recorded and produced track launches as an echo to their previously released debut album. Pretoria's new music promises to captivate audiences with its catchy, upbeat, and atmospheric sound, showcasing the band's signature style."},{"t":"p","html":"“Seven” explores the theme of the end of a situationship, with the protagonist grappling with the challenge of mustering the courage to break things off. Penned by lead vocalist <strong>Rob Gullett</strong>, the lyrics are inspired by real-life events, depicting feelings of cluelessness, anxiety, and over-analysis, all while harboring a longing to be with the other person. The song gets its name from the estimated seventh occurrence of such situations in DeWitt’s life, adding a personal touch to the narrative."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612782/large-79d25c3019c11666f4b5b72689d1ca80.jpg","alt":"Cover Art for \"Seven\""},{"t":"p","html":"The distinctive sound of “Seven” is characterized by its upbeat and sunny instrumental backdrop, a hallmark of Pretoria’s unique musical identity. The trio of talented guitarists—<strong>Josh Bilisko</strong>, <strong>Matt Burdick</strong>, and <strong>Matt Pavlock</strong>—contribute to the song’s dynamic atmosphere, weaving hooky and calculated guitar lines throughout, culminating in an anthemic ending."},{"t":"p","html":"Pretoria, known for their ability to seamlessly blend melancholic lyricism with pleasant indie-rock melodies, has crafted a track that is both introspective and uplifting. The contrast between the lyrics’ emotional depth and the vibrant instrumentals showcases the band’s artistic prowess."},{"t":"p","html":"Lead vocalist Rob Gullett shared his excitement about the upcoming release, stating,&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Seven might be our best release yet. It’s a song that captures the essence of our experiences and emotions, and we can’t wait for our fans to hear it.”","cite":"- Ben DeWitt, Lead Vocalist (Pretoria)"},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to the song’s release, Pretoria has also hinted at an upcoming debut album tour, promising fans an immersive live experience that complements the energy of their music."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3dK49BK2fasxOmbCkUXhGc?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Pretoria:"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from Grand Rapids, MI, Pretoria is a dynamic five-piece indie rock band making waves in the DIY music scene. Celebrating the excitement of their debut album, the band is embarking on a journey to expand their reach from the Midwest and beyond. Renowned for their electrifying live performances, Pretoria is a must-see act, embodying the essence of a DIY music scene gem.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"As Pretoria released their latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5BLpBnhvojj1BZtoYPwV4F?si=volqn_qdQvC9sA9_SR1qcA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Seven</strong></a>,” a captivating exploration of the complexities of relationships. With plans for a Midwest tour in 2024 and aspirations for a national tour on the horizon, Pretoria is set to enchant audiences with their infectious sound."},{"t":"p","html":"Already making waves with their first album, the band has an arsenal of demos ready for at least two more albums, showcasing their prolific creative output."},{"t":"p","html":"Dreaming big,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3dK49BK2fasxOmbCkUXhGc?si=L_9GkiIGSmio36L3h-OcJw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Pretoria</strong></a> envisions their music becoming the soundtrack of a massive coming-of-age film, solidifying their place in the indie rock scene and beyond. Stay tuned for the exciting next chapter in Pretoria’s musical odyssey!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Pretoria!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C2IK5KwLTWP/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/md6HArosm4k?si=FwdjV45EPb-yE37F","height":"315"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@pretoriamusic/video/7324811262632774954","handle":"@pretoriamusic"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/pretoriamusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Linktree</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/pretoriamusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://twitter.com/pretoriamusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCZTQNoIgY_ovurknBTd0SBw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/PretoriaMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"277681","title":"Official website of Lola Kristine: singer, pianist, and composer based in Southern California.","date":"2024-01-19","lead":"The two-track release, \"chapter three: into the woods,” is an anthem from the depths of the wild soul.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/277681/beb42a45a5ba0ceea67ffea411d92de7.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The two-track release, \"chapter three: into the woods,” is an anthem from the depths of the wild soul."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1zEFcukoOFwDG4ATM8tk8j?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"LAGUNA BEACH, CA (January 19, 2024) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?si=s5G-8qLvTyiyg4ae44jLPQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lola Kristine</strong></a>, the boho songstress hailing from Southern California, just released the third installment of her musical journey with “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1zEFcukoOFwDG4ATM8tk8j?si=8nHnuGkFQGeyuSjF5kjlSQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>chapter three: into the woods</strong></a>” on Friday, January 19, 2024. The upcoming album is a powerful exploration of self-discovery and reclamation, featuring two captivating tracks, “<strong>Find Me in the Wilderness</strong>” and “<strong>Living for Myself</strong>.”"},{"t":"p","html":"“<strong>Find Me in the Wilderness</strong>” - A journey into Lola’s darkness, a returning home to her roots and inner child. This dark rock anthem is a commitment to facing hidden demons, breaking free from chains, and embracing the untamed spirit within. The chorus howls with the resilience of Lola’s spirit, <em>“I will not be afraid because I know the sun will rise again.”</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0hQ4fwuV5qgPA6d15JTAw5?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"quote","html":"“These are two of my favorite songs I’ve ever written. They push me to my edge vocally where I can hold nothing back. ‘Find Me in the Wilderness’ was the missing piece to tie the album together, inviting listeners to rediscover their wild souls.”","cite":"- Lola Kristine, LA-Based Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"“<strong>Living for Myself</strong>” - A liberation of Lola’s fierce power as she sings about embracing her unique multi-faceted self. Recorded live in the studio, this blues rock track captures the raw energy of Lola’s performance. The song is a powerful declaration of independence, female empowerment, a rejection of societal expectations, and a celebration of living authentically."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6xh9KRBISeaoXey1sQe4yd?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wrote ‘Living For Myself’ after a meeting with a powerful music manager who said I need to stick to one style if I wanted to be successful. That I should keep myself in a nice box. This song began as my response to him.”","cite":"- Lola Kristine, LA-Based Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/613240/large-f6c0ac5b50ef3dcadedbcea968567c3e.png","alt":"ALBUM ARTWORK: Diana Rosa Cordova and Lucas Halopoff"},{"t":"p","html":"The sound of this chapter stretches genres: from country rock and Americana to retro soul and blues. It is both fierce and catchy, with “Find Me in the Wilderness” drawing inspiration from artists like <strong>Brandi Carlile</strong> and <strong>The Lone Bellow</strong>, while “Living for Myself” features <strong>Motown </strong>flavors reminiscent of <strong>Aretha Franklin </strong>and <strong>Sister Sparrow</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Accompanying the release is a live music video for “Living for Myself,” recorded during the studio session, scheduled to drop a week after the album release.</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"The entire <em><strong>CHAPTERS</strong></em> album is a personal journey through Lola Kristine’s life, marked by love, heartbreak, self-discovery, and redemption. Each chapter unfolds like a page from her diary, inviting listeners to resonate with their own experiences. <em>CHAPTERS</em> is a testament to true love’s transformative power and the freedom that comes with embracing one’s authentic self. “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1zEFcukoOFwDG4ATM8tk8j?si=UXRVbnkaQgyM8xVax7ZNUA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>chapter three: into the woods</strong></a>” is Lola Kristine’s first release with <a href=\"https://www.worldpeachrecords.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">World Peach Records</a>, an all-female indie label."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>“Find Me in the Wilderness” Credits:</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Songwriter: <strong>Laura Kristine Hennicke</strong>; Producer: <strong>Lola Kristine</strong>; Co-producer: <strong>Justin Busch</strong>; Vocals, keyboard, buffalo drum, background vocals, synths: Lola Kristine; Bass:<strong>&nbsp;Jesse Stern</strong>; Drums and percussion: <strong>Kiel Feher</strong>; Guitars: <strong>Cameron Morgan</strong>; Banjo: <strong>Lucas Halopoff</strong>; Howls: <strong>Diana Rosa Cordova</strong> and <strong>Taria Buchanan</strong>; Mixing: <strong>Tyler Norris</strong> with ma6io; Mastering: <strong>Duncan Ferguson </strong>with <strong>The Voltage Exchange</strong>; Executive Producer: <strong>John Ward</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>“Living for Myself” Credits:</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Songwriter: Laura Kristine Hennicke; Producer: Lola Kristine; Co-producer: Justin Busch; Vocals, piano, background vocals: Lola Kristine; Electric guitars: <strong>Sarven Manguiat</strong>; Acoustic guitar: Justin Busch; Organ and Wurlitzer:<strong>&nbsp;Ryan Marquez</strong>; Drums and percussion: Kiel Feher; Background vocals: <strong>Marisa Rambaran</strong>, <strong>Sarven Manguiat</strong>, and Justin Busch; Mixing: Tyler Norris with ma6io; Mastering: Duncan Ferguson with The Voltage Exchange; Executive Producer: John Ward"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592107/large-3617932e5b0534aca34ee0ac26e0c547.jpg","alt":"Enlight331.JPG"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lola Kristine:"},{"t":"p","html":"Lola Kristine is a singer, pianist and songwriter based in Laguna Beach, California. Known as “the little girl with the big voice,” Lola has been staggering audiences her whole life with the depth of soul she possesses in both her timeless songwriting and penetrating singing. Hearing her sing feeds your soul and reconnects you with what is right in the world.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"From humble beginnings in St. Louis, Missouri, Lola has taken her music across the country, touring with noted musicians such as <strong>Premik Russell</strong> <strong>Tubbs</strong><strong>&nbsp;(Santana, Sting, James Taylor), Jeff Haynes (Joni Mitchell, Herbie Hancock)</strong> and bass virtuoso <strong>Michael Manring</strong>. She has collaborated with artists from all over the world, including <strong>Kinobe</strong> (Uganda) in a series sponsored by <strong>American Voices</strong>. In 2022, a live video of Lola performing went viral on <strong>TikTok</strong>, hitting 4.5M views which boosted her online presence. She is gaining notoriety amidst legendary rockstars such as <strong>Mick Fleetwood</strong> and <strong>Don Cromwell</strong> of <strong>Air Supply</strong>. She is currently living in Southern California, where she can be found performing at venues and clubs all up and down the coast."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lola Kristine!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/q8H01u6RyWc?si=sYaq4h_CG4PxI2Qr","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.musicoflola.com/","img":"","title":"Official website of Lola Kristine: singer, pianist, and composer based in Southern California.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://instagram.com/musicoflola\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC7LAxI_AIC0YgeP0CcLYNOw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube </a>| </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?si=hmR1xgocRoqKVRInC1oRqQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"284317","title":"Racyne Parker Dropped New Alt-Country Single \"Willow Tree\"","date":"2024-01-18","lead":"This sonic \"friends-to-lovers\" tale mesmerizes listeners with dreamy instrumentals and heartfelt lyrics.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/284317/44b3dc98a291f4739fd6578bfe68e8cd.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This sonic \"friends-to-lovers\" tale mesmerizes listeners with dreamy instrumentals and heartfelt lyrics."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/63LmcLUCuzLXvMEiRyImpm?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (January 18, 2024) - Indie-folk singer <a href=\"https://racyneparker.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Racyne Parker</strong></a> just released her latest<strong>&nbsp;</strong>sonic<strong>&nbsp;</strong>creation, “<a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/WillowTree\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Willow Tree</strong></a>,” a soulful journey through the enchanting stages of a friends-to-lovers romance. The track, rooted in Country, Alt-Country, Folk, Americana, and Singer-Songwriter genres, captures the essence of falling in love and the enduring power of relationships."},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by classic love stories in films such as “<strong>Love and Basketball</strong>,” “<strong>The Man in the Moon</strong>,” and “<strong>The Notebook</strong>,” Racyne Parker decided to craft her own narrative. “Willow Tree” tells the story of two childhood friends growing up together, facing the trials of life, and ultimately finding love that withstands the test of time, much like the movies that have always captured Racyne’s heart."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/WillowTree","label":"Listen To \"Willow Tree\" On All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614218/large-2d3673feb13818b69616da1b0ffa58d4.jpg","alt":"racyne-willow-tree-FINAL-3000x3000.jpg"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I love love and wanted to write a song where it all works out despite the usual hiccups. Turns out, even a happy love song turns out a bit melancholic.”","cite":"- Racyne Parker, Indie-Folk Singer"},{"t":"p","html":"While the song may seem lyrically simple at first, “Willow Tree” weaves a tapestry of complex emotions, blending elements of angst, longing, melancholy, and joy. The delicate vocals, ambient pedal steel, simmering mandolin, compelling rhythms, and enchanting guitar riffs create a musical experience that gracefully balances wistful nostalgia with a happily-ever-after vibe."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614213/large-848e7732d6bd0fd3d11be78e24bde528.jpg","alt":"racyne-willow-art-4_Small.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614213/preview-beb437593f36366ccd27cae356ed747e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614214/large-1eb504f95146c22187b94a0d9711b3a0.jpg","alt":"racyne-willow-art-2_Small.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614214/preview-c08fa2179f575e99ebb54687384f3b3a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614215/large-076697812b35fd1e3fbbb76473366d6a.jpg","alt":"RacyneParkerMusic_Logo.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614215/preview-6daacd256b2f6e3c0fec82ddcf1015d6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614217/large-404d0d420782a84061771a3ab8d721fb.jpg","alt":"racyne-willow-art-3_Small.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614217/preview-0ffcb56e359376f617794fa42033f660.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Produced by <strong>Randall Kent</strong> of <strong>Deaf Dog Studios</strong> in Nashville, Tennessee, the song features a talented ensemble, including Regan Akers on bass, <strong>Brian Cox </strong>on drums, and <strong>Blake Mohler</strong> on pedal steel. The result is a versatile sound that effortlessly crosses over into singer-songwriter, folk pop, and indie playlists."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>An official lyric video for <strong>“</strong></em><a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/WillowTree\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Willow Tree</strong></em></a><em><strong>”</strong>&nbsp;was also released on VEVO alongside the song. Furthermore, the song is part of a more extensive project by Racyne Parker, with details set to be unveiled later in the year.</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/69uzZLXVJPGmB52ik2Rw0g?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Racyne Parker:"},{"t":"p","html":"Originally from Southern Oregon, Denver-based singer-songwriter <strong>Racyne Parker</strong> draws inspiration from country, modern folk, indie rock, and pop influences, to deliver catchy lyrics, warm vocals, and a contemporary style that fits in well on playlists next to <strong>Kacey Musgraves, Taylor Swift, </strong>and<strong> Caylee Hammack.</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"An engaging and low-stakes performer, Racyne is bound to play a song that you know while also introducing new songs to you that you’re sure to love."},{"t":"p","html":"Her honest and original tunes draw on her experiences with living in and leaving a small town, navigating uncertainty in love and life, and finding joy in the little moments.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"An up-and-comer in the Denver music scene, with lots of new music on the way, Racyne hopes to build community, create joy, and remain true to herself through the music that she makes.<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Racyne!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/racyneparker/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@racyneparker","post":false},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@racyneparker/video/7289306760421051678","handle":"@racyneparker"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/N2F2KBlB0No?si=1yYXTyHr3IaC8DBA","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"<br><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/RacyneParkerMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@racyneparker?is_from_webapp=1&amp;sender_device=pc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | ​<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/racyneparker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/racyneparker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>threads</strong></a><br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"275337","title":"Songs Of Resilience: A.H. Pettus' Musical Journey Through Hardship, Grief, and Redemption","date":"2024-01-12","lead":"Charlotte, NC (January 12, 2024) - A.H. Pettus, the genre-blending artist originally from outside Charlotte, NC, unveiled his latest album, How The West Was Once this past June 2023. This raw and heartfelt album takes listeners on an emotional rollercoaster, navigating t...","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/275337/aa6d2156cc461d2a69912740a45701e1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/77fz5C344QZlm9Lw8cuTLD?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Charlotte, NC (January 12, 2024) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/77uCdMKyLCuOP5mvsQdn6j?si=zb1-90liSbWayATOmbmH6g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>A.H. Pettus</strong></a>, the genre-blending artist originally from outside Charlotte, NC, unveiled his latest album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/77fz5C344QZlm9Lw8cuTLD?si=0ccb0248e0da47c2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>How The West Was Once</strong></em></a> this past June 2023. This raw and heartfelt album takes listeners on an emotional rollercoaster, navigating the tumultuous landscapes of divorce, grief, and redemption through a fusion of Folk, Singer-Songwriter, Western-Country, Americana, Rock, and Punk influences."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>ALBUM TOPICS &amp; THEMES</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"In <strong><em>How The West Was Once,&nbsp;</em></strong>A.H. Pettus explores various aspects of human experience, from life’s big questions to post-divorce challenges. Through a gripping narrative set in the old West, he touches on themes like justice and survival. The album reflects Pettus’ personal journey through divorce, finding solace and happiness unexpectedly. Inspired by the war in Ukraine, one song reflects on the broader impact of war on humanity. The album closes on a positive note, with Pettus expressing gratitude for his new family, friends, and listeners on this musical journey."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612770/compressed_original-b1111bc3de21e1362cdc574d9cf04b00.jpg","alt":"ALBUM COVER ART"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>ABOUT “HOW THE WEST ONCE WAS”</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"In 2018, amidst the aftermath of a challenging divorce, A.H. Pettus sought refuge in the creation of <em><strong>How The West Was Once</strong></em>. This record serves as a musical memoir, capturing Pettus’ emotional journey through grief, love, and self-discovery over the course of two years. Recording, instrumentation, mixing, and mastering were all executed by Pettus in his basement studio, showcasing a hands-on approach to his craft. From melancholic beginnings to uplifting resolutions, the album encapsulates the artist’s resilience and growth."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Some people have therapists, and some people have a bottle of bourbon and a guitar.”","cite":"- A.H. Pettus, Alternative Folk Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6OpOnvfWoO7wa5DXeLnFkg?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About A.H Pettus:"},{"t":"p","html":"As the lead singer and head songwriter of Charlotte, NC area super-group ‘<strong>Remy St. Claire</strong>’ over a decade ago, Alexander is back with a more stripped-down western-folk sound with his new solo record <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/77fz5C344QZlm9Lw8cuTLD?si=0507d706384549fb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>How The West Was Once</strong></a>."},{"t":"p","html":"Comprised of songs written before, during, and after the divorce from his first wife. You get an intimate look inside the rise and fall of a love story. Mixing Appalachian-folk, indie-rock, country-western, and a little bit of punk, it is a truly special and intimate recording of its raw delivery and emotional attachment. Written over a period of 5 or so years, and recorded entirely by Alexander himself, it’s simple, but in a world so complicated, sometimes simple is just what you need. Among music, Alexander has been an actor since the age of 6 doing voice-over work for Lionsgate’s ‘<strong>Christmas in Cartoontown</strong>’, and starring with the late <strong>Mickey Rooney</strong> in ‘<strong>The Lost Stallions: The Journey Home</strong>.’"},{"t":"p","html":"He has written two novels, two kids television series, and two feature films one of which was nominated for the Nichols Prize and was a PAGE’s finalist. He also is a painter specializing in acrylics and has sold paintings to the Belk family and the Bates family among others over his artistic career. He also has been nominated and competed for the Southern Prize in art for the Southeast."},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"275895","title":"Ethereal Harmony Unveiled: STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION Released Captivating Single 'Drifters'","date":"2024-01-12","lead":"Embark on a musical odyssey with a fusion of Dance-Pop, Piano Rock, and Electro Pop.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/275895/8bbfeaac72a50cb0194fedb4600f739e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Embark on a musical odyssey with a fusion of Dance-Pop, Piano Rock, and Electro Pop.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\"><br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2bw4hLPKQIAQVENVlq3lE9?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Tokyo, JAPAN (January 12, 2023) - Rising Tokyo-based musician <a href=\"https://stereodivefoundation.jp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION</strong></a>&nbsp;just dropped his new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2bw4hLPKQIAQVENVlq3lE9?si=910edbcf136545c0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Drifters</strong></a>” on Friday, January 12th, 2024. This new anime-inspired track seamlessly blends Pop, Piano Rock, and electro-pop, transcending conventional boundaries of musical genres."},{"t":"p","html":"“Drifters” emerges as a captivating anime anthem meticulously crafted with a dance-pop foundation, seamlessly veering towards a pop-oriented style that sets it apart from the ordinary. STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION skillfully integrates a calming ambiance in select segments, intertwining samples and analog synths to create an immersive auditory experience with enchanting vocal processing."},{"t":"p","html":"The production of this new song reflects a conscious commitment to the artistry of modulations, deftly playing with passing chords to weave a rich musical tapestry. Crafted with precision, the melody is a testament to STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION’s dedication to creating a comforting and enjoyable listening experience."},{"t":"p","html":"STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION invites music enthusiasts and anime aficionados alike to immerse themselves in the enchanting world of “Drifters.” This single stands as a testament to the artist’s prowess in transcending musical boundaries and delivering a sonic masterpiece that resonates on a profound level."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612259/large-e9e9f649840c0e38820d6c64afea5116.jpg","alt":"ARTWORK BY: SHINYA YOSHINO (BAVIC) "},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song is perfect for times when you want to unwind, like during a leisurely drive! Maintaining a positive mindset is crucial in living each day to the fullest. It is important to always have a sense of purpose, think consciously, and act with intention as the key to living flexibly.”","cite":"- Stereo Dive Foundation, Tokyo-Based Singer/Artist"},{"t":"button","href":"https://lnk.to/LZC-2680","label":"Listen to \"Drifters\" HERE!","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"“Drifters” is also the official Ending theme of the TV anime series <strong><em>SYNDUALITY Noir.</em></strong>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>2024 SHOW INFORMATION</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>2/2 - ANIME EXPO SANTIAGO</strong> Santiago, CL: ​EVENT <a href=\"https://anime-expo.cl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LINK</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>3/8-3/10 - ANIME MILWAUKEE</strong> Milwaukee, WI: EVENT <a href=\"https://animemilwaukee.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LINK</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>3/29-3/31 - KAWAII KON HAWAII</strong> Honolulu, HI: EVENT <a href=\"https://kawaiikon.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LINK</a><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6yLTrq59HxfE6aTq8r4gVP?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://stereodivefoundation.jp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION</strong></a> is a sound-making project created by <strong>RON</strong>, who works on songwriting, composing, and arrangement of music. RON’s work has been featured as soundtracks for animation titles and other media content.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"In 2013, he launched his activities as STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION with the track “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2sChoyJsa5j3JLnTtVx0S8?si=42ffb223c5f84704\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Daisy</strong></a>” which was featured as the ending theme song of the anime series “<strong>Beyond the Boundary</strong>.” Since then, he has created and sung theme songs for many popular anime such as “<strong>Dimension W</strong>”, “<strong>Food Wars!</strong>”, “<strong>Moriarty the Patriot</strong>”, and “<strong>That Time I Got Reincarnated as a Slime</strong>.” Under the name “RON,” he has produced songs for voice actors and artists, and has also sung for “<strong>Hypnosis Mike</strong>,” “<strong>A3!</strong>” and “<strong>Love Live! Sunshine!!</strong>.”"},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to his talent as a multi-player of various musical instruments, he also is a Sound Artisan who produces a track with the futuristic synth work and a melody that will resonate with your heart. RON has been reputable for his distinct programming arrangements with it being able to adapt to various genres of music along with his catchy and artistic sounds."},{"t":"p","html":"RON has also created soundtracks, theme songs, and character songs for anime titles such as “<strong>Re:Zero: Starting Life in Another World</strong>” and “<strong>BNA</strong>.” He will do whatever it takes to express his desired sounds with his incredible sense, regardless of any method - this is STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/9-Bj9Z2J5ZM?si=Cu9NQtiNE6ltTfzO","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/ron_sdf/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@ron_sdf","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://stereodivefoundation.jp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a> |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/STEREODIVEFOUNDATIONOfficialChannel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RON_SDF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"275932","title":"Dave Lebental's New Album 'The Long Player' Takes a Harmonious Journey Through Life's Chapters","date":"2024-01-12","lead":"This 11-track LP is a tasty blend of rock, Americana, and blues that every listener will put on a loop.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/275932/78c9a18841b1661abf0d4e8f0afb6d4a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This 11-track LP is a tasty blend of rock, Americana, and blues that every listener will put on a loop."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5jTjCeNvYAlTC0Xr6Nhf9Y?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (January 12, 2024) - <a href=\"https://dlmusic.us/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dave Lebental</strong></a>, a seasoned LA musician, just released his much-anticipated album, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5jTjCeNvYAlTC0Xr6Nhf9Y?si=LYOPMTKXRj6doBuNzsrW1g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Long Player</strong></a>’ on Friday, January 12, 2024. This uniquely diverse 11-track LP promises a tasteful blend of Rock, Blues, Americana, and Singer-Songwriter influences."},{"t":"p","html":"‘<strong>The Long Player</strong>’ is not just a musical journey; it’s a testament to resilience, dedication, and a love for the art that transcends time. The artist, who put his promising music career on hold to raise a family, returns after 27 years to a transformed musical landscape, creating an album that reflects his experiences, observations, and emotions."},{"t":"p","html":"<u><strong>ALBUM HIGHLIGHTS</strong></u>"},{"t":"p","html":"“<strong>I'm Not Too Old</strong>” - An anthem for Lebental and his generation, capturing the spirit of endurance and passion."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5uX5queUmwX3jBm6pCDXvJ?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4nbkMYXiIZWgYiGL554Qk2?si=7e548f8bd6a9424b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Monique</strong></a>” - A song of unrequited love, echoing the sentiments of a friend enamored with the complexities of romance."},{"t":"p","html":"“<strong>Granite Meadow</strong>” - Reflects on the wonderment of nature, inspired by Lebental's personal experience in the mountains."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5LJz2xfCQTkNNJ1I6SXg1z?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3wFYwsXb9xiOmE1T5eteSL?si=3007e56b905b4926\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>What You Got</strong></a>” - A poignant conclusion to the LP, a song dedicated to the younger generation, affirming individual value and capability.<br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612305/large-04051941277cd1c8441901f6c85f151f.png","alt":"Album Cover Art"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>ABOUT THE ALBUM</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"All 11 songs on the album were crafted on an acoustic guitar, providing a cohesive thread throughout. However, the album showcases Lebental’s versatility with each track uniquely arranged, textured, and presenting a captivating blend of Rock, Blues, Americana, and Singer-Songwriter elements."},{"t":"p","html":"Beyond the material on the LP, this artist has some interesting storylines that include:<br>"},{"t":"list","items":["<em><strong>Modern Day Musical Rip Van Winkle</strong></em>: A story of pausing a music career, returning after 27 years, and navigating a changed musical terrain.","<em><strong>Busking Across America</strong></em>: Lebental fulfills a lifelong dream of touring the US, sharing the adventure of a 62-year-old man, his wife, one guitar, and a cell phone camera.","<em><strong>A Promise Fulfilled</strong></em>: Lebental, whose son was saved by Children's Hospital of Los Angeles, dedicates all proceeds from the Vinyl LP &amp; CD sales to the institution."]},{"t":"quote","html":"“I find being in the mountains inspirational. Getting away from all the sounds of the city and hearing the wind through the trees is incredible. ‘Granite Meadow’ describes my experience in a meadow where I felt connected to everything around me.”","cite":"- Dave Lebental, LA-based Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612304/-c57f6ab017553221a23841277de48054.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-12-20 at 4.27.56 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612304/preview-9af7dda6ab14b81a95fc56f558cd3f1b.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612302/large-31f1831a67d28ad68c813643a7195bd1.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-12-20 at 4.28.01 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612302/preview-938653d08f08e6a4b5bf893a739746c2.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612303/large-9a85669a740b48562347b4d8a1535946.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-12-20 at 4.27.49 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612303/preview-6e65ad5cdfcf4b52ed3ab80b7f3e309a.png"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>PHILANTHROPIC WORK</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"In a heartwarming gesture, Lebental fulfills a personal promise by donating all proceeds from his new album ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5jTjCeNvYAlTC0Xr6Nhf9Y?si=u1NWji6xRTSg4QXIs2qEAA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Long Player</strong></a>’ to the Children’s Hospital of Los Angeles, where his son was saved 20 years ago."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Dave Lebental:"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/612771/large-d1a8a46fa3ef2fd66c39ca40df068998.png","alt":"Mick Taylor & Dave Lebental"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Dave Lebental</strong>, a veteran rocker, made waves in the ‘90s LA Club scene, opening for ex-Rolling Stones guitarist <strong>Mick Taylor</strong>. Despite promising prospects and gigs alongside notable artists, his big break eluded him. A few months after a Mick Taylor gig, family priorities led him to trade rock n’ roll for a day job."},{"t":"p","html":"Fast forward 27 years, Lebental, now 62, found renewed creative spark as an empty nester. Exploring the modern music landscape, he embraced digital recording and social media, crafting his debut solo LP, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5jTjCeNvYAlTC0Xr6Nhf9Y?si=2c1B7u_-SqiFj4xqh-2DGw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Long Player</strong></a>.’ The 11-track album, influenced by <strong>James Taylor</strong>, <strong>Ryan Adams</strong>, <strong>The Eagles</strong>, <strong>Tom Petty</strong>, and <strong>The Beatles</strong>, showcases old-school analog performances with multi-track recordings."},{"t":"p","html":"Happy as an independent artist, Lebental seeks to connect with his audience. After releasing “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7BoG1lgtFnxtrATjJoGpX2?si=DpD3uvxZQm-baOEHbEtfpw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Granite Meadow</strong></a>” in 2021, he unveiled his first full-length LP to a substantial online following of 38,000 on Facebook and 1,000,000 digital music fans. Performing with his band, <strong><em>The Driftwood Souls,</em></strong> and solo, Lebental’s upcoming tour dates and performances can be found at <a href=\"https://dlmusic.us/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">dlmusic.us</a>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Dave!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/QDcYM2dBXfY?si=OD7pMeE_lLUR2hbs","height":"315"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2FDLMusic.US%2Fposts%2Fpfbid02WY8Qp7soFBQeeyVLuMgHA8bqbD4vJVZkHCC3DkbxecChbfG9W8wtTBgwPsrDHfcvl&show_text=true&width=500","height":"250"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/C0hVgJovwrl/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@dlmusic.us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://dlmusic.us/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/dlmusic.us/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a>&nbsp;<strong>| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCC5gMEB0_DV0ziMiu29WFQg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"284580","title":"The Narcissist Cookbook: A Unique Blend of Music, Storytelling, and Unapologetic Authenticity","date":"2024-01-05","lead":"Stirling, UK (January 5, 2023) - Born and raised on the picturesque island of Arran off the west coast of Scotland, The Narcissist Cookbook, led by the enigmatic Matt Johnston (they/them), has carved a distinctive path in the music scene. Surrounded by the eclectic sound...","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/284580/a2bcb56209627644699f53a22dee8f2e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"p","html":"Stirling, UK (January 5, 2023) - Born and raised on the picturesque island of Arran off the west coast of Scotland, <strong>The Narcissist Cookbook</strong>, led by the enigmatic Matt Johnston (they/them), has carved a distinctive path in the music scene. Surrounded by the eclectic sounds of American blues and country rock, Matt's musical journey took a pivotal turn at the age of 13 when a pirated tape of Green Day's \"Insomniac\" album ignited a passion for music that defied conventions."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/39XOEoh22kWNy5vsEZbAuX?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>From Punk to Unconventional Storytelling: The Evolution of The Narcissist Cookbook</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Fully self-taught and driven by the rebellious spirit of punk, Matt's musical journey unfolded through busking, playing in bars, and navigating the complexities of life. However, a dark period, including the loss of their voice for nine months and a deep dive into substance abuse, spurred a transformation. Experimenting with spoken monologues inspired by diverse influences, The Narcissist Cookbook emerged, using the guitar to amplify the power of their words.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>Defining Moments and Explosive Growth: This Is How We Get Better</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"The Narcissist Cookbook's third album, \"This Is How We Get Better,\" marked a turning point, propelling them into the spotlight. With a devoted global fanbase and a sold-out UK tour, Matt found themselves at the forefront of a movement resonating with those seeking honest, introspective, and fearless musical narratives.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>Beyond Borders: Future Plans and Unveiling MYTH</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Looking ahead to 2024, The Narcissist Cookbook aims for international tours and the release of the 40-minute compilation album, featuring the highly-requested \"Courtney (Director's Cut).\" Matt is also crafting a new album, \"MYTH,\" exploring codependency, fairytales, and a haunted children's book-on-tape.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>WORDS TO DESCRIBE THE ARTIST: Unveiling the Multifaceted Persona</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"In defining The Narcissist Cookbook, terms like neurodivergent, honest, confrontational, vibrant, and empowering come to the forefront. Matt Johnston embraces their queerness, delivering a unique blend of thrashy acoustic punk, folk storytelling, and one-person theatre performances.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>CAREER HIGHLIGHTS: From Intimate Shows to Global Recognition</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"The recent sold-out UK tour witnessed unforgettable moments, with venues filled to capacity and meet-and-greet lines stretching for hours. Matt's unapologetic approach to songwriting, tackling topics like mental health, non-monogamy, and abusive relationships, has resonated deeply with a diverse audience.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>MORE ABOUT MATT JOHNSON: A Musical Alchemist and DIY Pioneer</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Self-built and independent, Matt's journey from small-scale productions to sold-out venues without management or a record label is a testament to their resilience. Each album, from \"MOTH\" to \"HYMN,\" pushes the boundaries of the traditional format, reflecting a commitment to artistic exploration.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>ARTIST'S MESSAGE TO FANS: A Call to Embrace Vulnerability</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Matt Johnston's core message revolves around self-acceptance and the acknowledgment of the parts of oneself that may be deemed too scary or vulnerable. Through music and storytelling, they encourage fans to embrace their fears, believing that true healing comes from openness rather than hiding.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>PHILANTHROPY: Supporting TransLifeline</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>In support of the transgender community, The Narcissist Cookbook has contributed to compilations benefiting TransLifeline, a non-profit organization offering peer-to-peer support and crisis helplines.</em><br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614624/large-56b5c2d26b72476975732eb9e8d247bc.jpg","alt":"bw_4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614624/preview-275a0607420d2363075aa91aaf4dcda0.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614626/large-92c928a61e5a4f6619a5bc0ea7569d92.jpg","alt":"5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614626/preview-92a6cf057bc09f613a0d5c1153585538.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614625/large-97790fbcb180ee129a2255ae6189ab3e.jpg","alt":"bw_1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614625/preview-e34f3f032d47c9b152cf2bdacf36317d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614627/large-88dca4b4bca8044427863e9bec3c1135.jpg","alt":"2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/614627/preview-d5ed9994229c19e4ebcc0662624559cd.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photo credit: Regenweibchen Photography<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Narcissist Cookbook!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/thenarcissistcookbookofficial/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@thenarcissistcookbookofficial","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://youtube.com/@TheNarcissistCookbook?si=X9NhF6HnOPZAGmFr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YOUTUBE</strong></a>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://thenarcissistcookbook.bandcamp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>BANDCAMP</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"271551","title":"Diane Louvel, a singer-songwriter from New York City and Paris, is a master of melody-driven indie folk. With her pure and soulful voice, she effortlessly combines emotive lyrics with a captivating storytelling style. Diane draws inspiration from the complexities of life. Diane Louvel Music","date":"2023-12-08","lead":"New York, NY (December 8, 2023) - Indie-Folk artist Diane Louvel drops her latest single, “Better Than You,” on December 8, 2023. The song is a captivating blend of alt-country and folk-pop that explores the complexities of relationships.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/271551/5b63b3659aab5b93f80bb6908e6cd880.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3QCHeYnDE4bVaKgSR8uKUf?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (December 8, 2023) - Indie-Folk artist <a href=\"https://www.dianelouvelmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Diane Louvel</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>drops her latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3QCHeYnDE4bVaKgSR8uKUf?si=8728c07737cf4b7f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Better Than You</strong></a>,” on December 8, 2023. The song is a captivating blend of alt-country and folk-pop that explores the complexities of relationships.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"“Better Than You” lyrically dissects the dynamics of a challenging relationship, capturing the essence of staying in a connection despite its evident toxicity. The song takes listeners on a journey through the emotional highs and lows, delving into the paradoxical nature of being both victim and perpetrator in a tumultuous relationship."},{"t":"quote","html":"“The lyrics are somewhat rational and analytical with spikes of 'WTF am I thinking' woven in.”","cite":"- Diane Louvel, Indie-Folk Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"“Better Than You” is part of Diane Louvel’s upcoming album, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2U0KksqU8hjX36YfWX3yZI?si=8YRHDHN8TIyT07HXRR3B7w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Above and Beyond</strong></a>,” which follows the success of three previously released singles. The song features a controlled and thoughtful musical arrangement, creating an intimate one-on-one conversation between the artist and the audience. The soulful guitar solos and riffs throughout the song add a melancholic feel, complementing the introspective nature of the lyrics."},{"t":"p","html":"“Better Than You” promises to be a standout addition to Diane Louvel’s discography, showcasing her ability to craft emotionally resonant narratives within the alt-country and folk-pop genres. As the release date approaches, fans and music enthusiasts alike can anticipate a unique and compelling musical experience from this talented artist."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>A Glimpse of \"Better Than You\" Lyrics</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"You talk about the therapy of time<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"But you haven’t asked how I am since 2018<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"You’re just another foolish genius&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"But I’ll say yes to everything<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Cause I’ve got nothing better to do<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"And I make the same mistake I made before<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Keeping one hand frozen on the door<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"I may be a fool but I’d rather be a jester<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"'Cause man, no one bums me out better than you<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Man, no one bums me out, better than you<br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/609068/large-8c603d8e62f70ce82a045845dd54aaca.jpg","alt":"\"Better Than You\" Cover Art"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Diane Louvel:"},{"t":"p","html":"Never underestimate the power of proximity. Growing up in two epicenters of culture, fashion, and music (New York City and Paris), it isn’t exactly a surprise that Diane Louvel ended up a creative artist; what is staggering is the level of mastery she’s achieved in her craft as a singer-songwriter. Weathering the storm of losing her brother (and the loneliness that followed) provided more than some meaningful tunes: it armed her with purpose. The result is spritely, almost effervescent Americana, rooted with a strength only a working woman’s hands that tills the land could have. And with a voice like<strong>&nbsp;Joni Mitchell</strong> by way of<strong>&nbsp;Neko Case</strong>, it’s just a matter of time before fans of classic bards like <strong>Laura Nyro&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Willie Nelson&nbsp;</strong>(and contemporaries like <strong>Father John Misty&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Lana Del Rey</strong>) get wise to this rising star in the circuit."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Diane!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/dianelouvel/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@dianelouvel","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.dianelouvelmusic.com/","img":"","title":"Diane Louvel, a singer-songwriter from New York City and Paris, is a master of melody-driven indie folk. With her pure and soulful voice, she effortlessly combines emotive lyrics with a captivating storytelling style. Diane draws inspiration from the complexities of life. Diane Louvel Music","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.dianelouvelmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@waltz_withdiane?is_from_webapp=1&amp;sender_device=pc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/DianeLouvelMusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"270556","title":"Official website of Lola Kristine: singer, pianist, and composer based in Southern California.","date":"2023-11-28","lead":"\"Just Friends,\" one of Lola's recently released songs, comes to life with a new music video.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/270556/f6eb3edf26043a2c7c7d0f6af478bccc.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Just Friends,\" one of Lola's recently released songs, comes to life with a new music video."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/q8H01u6RyWc?si=7IdtgzMjWxWYBTJo","height":"385"},{"t":"p","html":"LAGUNA BEACH, CA (November 28, 2023) - Singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?si=s5G-8qLvTyiyg4ae44jLPQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lola Kristine</strong></a> just launched an official music video for her recently released song, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1T4eIT0u7D99Xmu1XUndEp?si=af2787a9d6dc4f2e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Just Friends</strong></a>” on Tuesday, November 28th."},{"t":"p","html":"“Just Friends” explores the troubling thoughts that can arise within, stemming from a complicated relationship gone wrong. The music video itself demonstrates how one’s confusion can lead to heartbreak. This delicate yet passionate video paints a reflection of rejection on the same canvas, encapsulating how it feels to harbor a deep sense of regret and unrequited affection for another."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1T4eIT0u7D99Xmu1XUndEp?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"h3","html":"SONG CREDITS:"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Producer: Lola Kristine</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Songwriters: Lola Kristine and Justin Busch</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Co-producer: Justin Busch</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Mixing: Tyler Norris with ma6io</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Mastering: Duncan Ferguson with The Voltage Exchange</em>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592105/large-276db6291af3da6d6d3443b8709f4442.jpg","alt":"just friends 5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592105/preview-07cede9cfd93c1239de1c9b1e3c22ecd.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592103/large-42cfe37d7f09c9bfd97f82bb7803d28b.jpg","alt":"just friends 4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592103/preview-785ef0c0d249d2dd7a6e1bfa024ef7c1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592102/large-5adb2a6bb195d923896e1e467bb7e55a.jpg","alt":"just friends still 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592102/preview-d700f489593011fd900e64fcb74a0444.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592104/large-8feebfef7842ecf923131def03a5438e.jpg","alt":"just friends 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592104/preview-4d60444e977716716f2213a484716e32.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592106/large-93ca27719b56b149ab7c8a6ed0e67236.jpg","alt":"just friends 6.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592106/preview-d51efa8a640bd652a10c6b0b232cff91.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592107/large-3617932e5b0534aca34ee0ac26e0c547.jpg","alt":"Enlight331.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592107/preview-7af37a75cb35da6df4b56bf66efa51f6.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>​Preview photos from \"Just Friends\" music video launching at end of ​November</em><br>"},{"t":"lead","html":"TOUR"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>*Kristine is excited to share her first full-length album with the world and plans to start by traveling back to her hometown to share her amazing work this holiday season. Find her December 21st, 2023, 7:30 p.m. at The Sheldon in St. Louis, Missouri.*</em>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong><u>LOLA KRISTINE TOUR DATES &amp; INFO:</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>December 6, 2023, Wednesday:</strong> Le Papagayo Carlsbad @ 6:30 pm, Carlsbad, CA, United States<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>December 21, 2023, Thursday:</strong> Lola Kristine at the Sheldon St. Louis @ 7:30 pm, St. Louis, MO, United States<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lola Kristine:"},{"t":"p","html":"Lola Kristine is a singer, pianist and songwriter based in Laguna Beach, California. Known as “the little girl with the big voice,” Lola has been staggering audiences her whole life with the depth of soul she possesses in both her timeless songwriting and penetrating singing. Hearing her sing feeds your soul and reconnects you with what is right in the world.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"From humble beginnings in St. Louis, Missouri, Lola has taken her music across the country, touring with noted musicians such as <strong>Premik Russell</strong> <strong>Tubbs</strong><strong>&nbsp;(Santana, Sting, James Taylor), Jeff Haynes (Joni Mitchell, Herbie Hancock)</strong> and bass virtuoso <strong>Michael Manring</strong>. She has collaborated with artists from all over the world, including <strong>Kinobe</strong> (Uganda) in a series sponsored by <strong>American Voices</strong>. In 2022, a live video of Lola performing went viral on <strong>TikTok</strong>, hitting 4.5M views which boosted her online presence. She is gaining notoriety amidst legendary rockstars such as <strong>Mick Fleetwood</strong> and <strong>Don Cromwell</strong> of <strong>Air Supply</strong>. She is currently living in Southern California, where she can be found performing at venues and clubs all up and down the coast."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lola Kristine!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.musicoflola.com/","img":"","title":"Official website of Lola Kristine: singer, pianist, and composer based in Southern California.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://instagram.com/musicoflola\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC7LAxI_AIC0YgeP0CcLYNOw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube&nbsp;</a>| </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?si=hmR1xgocRoqKVRInC1oRqQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"266152","title":"View BRII_music’s Linktree. Listen to their music on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music here.","date":"2023-11-17","lead":"The highly-anticipated 6-track EP officially launched, exploring themes of dating, relationships, and the euphoria of falling in love.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/266152/cc4a879a58efc597f2e3981bad3ad35e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The highly-anticipated 6-track EP officially launched, exploring themes of dating, relationships, and the euphoria of falling in love."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1MTaHLR5EPnvq1c2VZ2wTO?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, CA (November 17, 2023) - Rising pop R&amp;B sensation <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5OVMuAGwhVrQZ8xG7bgVOs?si=CT4p7qFEQiycfdpAJ9k99w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Brii Elliss</strong></a> is set to captivate hearts and ears with her much-anticipated 6-track EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1MTaHLR5EPnvq1c2VZ2wTO?si=Kj6k17SoTROJpkIRg-kv5A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>All-In</strong></em></a> which released on November 17, 2023. The EP explores themes of dating, relationships, and the euphoria of falling in love."},{"t":"p","html":"Brii Elliss, known for her soulful and melodious tunes, created <em>All-In</em> during the early stages of her long-term relationship, where she was basking in the warm glow of genuine love for the first time. The EP perfectly encapsulates that unique phase in a relationship when mutual love is a revelation, and the world appears brighter and more enchanting.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The honeymoon phase is such an exciting stage of a relationship, and it doesn’t last forever, so I really wanted to capture the essence of that.”","cite":"Brii Elliss - Pop Singer"},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically, the record offers a delightful blend of mid-tempo love songs with a Pop R&amp;B flare. Brii Elliss’ soulful voice and the EP’s catchy melodies are sure to leave a lasting impression on listeners. From the tender emotions of “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5Wm1cjkes50KHF4ZsftQsV?si=23afe4a94233466f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Perfect 4 Me</strong></a>” to the vibrant energy of “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7gKZCpNA7wc8WndZOjmfIt?si=b13c043348ed451a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Midas</strong></a>” and the enchanting harmonies of “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3Aftwl8HVPYfJW5C38traP?si=cd6ba6c4497a48ec\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Never Know</strong></a>” the EP is a journey into the heart of love and the allure of relationships."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7gKZCpNA7wc8WndZOjmfIt?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"The EP’s artwork reflects the optimism and vibrancy of the early stages of love with its bright and colorful aesthetic. <em>All-In</em> is an invitation to embrace love with open arms, just as Brii has, and to enjoy every moment of its magic."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/598787/large-672cf13178620b525da25f90319e24e2.jpg","alt":"\"All In\" Cover Art"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>'ALL-IN' TRACKS:</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"01 - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3wUuSsKJjmE5W6Phu0eDZi?si=cd9e57b508674191\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Now I Got U</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"02- <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1qBSFGClLwhW57Xf6v5EEz?si=02dc12cfeb184f64\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Follow</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"03- <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5Wm1cjkes50KHF4ZsftQsV?si=ba2c7078fb6e4b07\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Perfect 4 Me</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"04 - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7gKZCpNA7wc8WndZOjmfIt?si=9b8f258105724840\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Midas</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"05- <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1Km2dkFvOLMACOSSwjt97n?si=2db81d7beeb7423a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Get Enough</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"06- <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3Aftwl8HVPYfJW5C38traP?si=237c0497f27f4704\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Never Know</a>"},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to the EP release, Brii Elliss has a special treat for her fans. She will be releasing three mini music videos for the songs “Perfect 4 Me,” “Midas,” and “Never Know.” These videos will feature the first verse and chorus and, although not official music videos, will provide fans with an exciting visual representation of the EP’s essence. The more content, the better, as they say, and Brii Elliss is committed to delivering an immersive experience to her audience."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5OVMuAGwhVrQZ8xG7bgVOs?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brii Elliss:"},{"t":"p","html":"Up-and-coming pop artist <a href=\"https://www.briielliss.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Brii Elliss</strong></a> is a singer-songwriter who brings a certain closeness to her lyrics, giving testament to the power of storytelling in music. With an Irish father and Puerto Rican mother, her voice and life experiences create a unique blend that filters into her songs effortlessly, showcasing a sultry R&amp;B chill-pop soundscape that captivates and entrances listeners. Working with Grammy-winning producer <strong>Synematik&nbsp;</strong>to create her signature buttery sound, Brii pulls inspiration from artists like <strong>Amber Mark, H.E.R., Snoh Aalegra, Jhene Aiko</strong>, and <strong>Jazmine Sullivan</strong>, with a deeply rich tone that is quickly creating a buzz in the music community. A New Jersey native who has been singing since she can remember, Brii was on the path to stardom by the age of 12, having already auditioned for the famed X-Factor show and made it through several rounds.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Throughout high school, she continued pursuing this passion by writing new songs and recording them, honing her piano skills, and preparing to move to LA where she attended college at Loyola Marymount University and graduated with her Bachelor’s degree in music. As she began to record her own music she realized how much she needed music to be center stage in her life. <em>“I’m in my element when I am recording and surrounded by other creatives. It feels like home to me, and it’s still my happy place today.”&nbsp;</em>Needless to say, her happiness and passion in the studio shines through her work as her debut single garnered over 17K streams upon release while showcasing her authentic songwriting and silky low voice. Fans have already started rallying behind her and eagerly anticipate what’s to come next for this budding artist. Lucky for them, Brii has lots of new music up her sleeve for 2023 and plans to share her soulful vibe with the world... one song at a time."},{"t":"p","html":"Brii Elliss officially released her 6-track EP: <em><strong>All-In</strong></em> on Friday, November 17. This creation is a testament to the power of love and the magic it brings into our lives."},{"t":"p","html":"For all updates and announcements, make sure to keep up with Brii on her social media pages, linked below!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Brii Elliss!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/iGWGsuYX-EA?si=g2sJbcp3sQ_RoKTF","height":"315"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://linktr.ee/BRII_music","img":"","title":"View BRII_music’s Linktree. Listen to their music on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music here.","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/brii_elliss/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@brii_elliss","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.briielliss.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@brii_elliss\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@briielliss\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"266168","title":"Read More","date":"2023-11-17","lead":"The rising Boston-based singer officially released her new track, set to be an anthem for the overthinkers.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/266168/715d877ad3845c7e3362b26c7941ea30.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The rising Boston-based singer officially released her new track, set to be an anthem for the overthinkers."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1Atq6MOO1m1MSwQrVdtO4U?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Boston, MA (November 17, 2023) - <a href=\"https://www.alainamaymusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Alaina May</strong></a>, the emerging Indie-Pop singer-songwriter, is set to captivate hearts and minds with her latest release, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1Atq6MOO1m1MSwQrVdtO4U?si=1c0ca199b5dc40dd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Keeps Me Up</strong></a>.” The introspective track dropped on November 17, 2023, and promises to be an anthem for anyone who’s ever spent sleepless nights lost in the labyrinth of their own thoughts."},{"t":"p","html":"Alaina May’s music showcases her soulful vocals and evocative lyrics. Her music offers a distinctive glimpse into her individual struggles while also striking a chord with timeless themes like unfulfilled opportunities, unrequited feelings, and self-doubt."},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Keeps Me Up’ is the product of quite a few sleepless nights spent overthinking and wondering what could’ve been. If you can relate, this song is for you.”","cite":"- Alaina May, Indie-Pop Singer"},{"t":"p","html":"The song’s journey began in September 2022, during Alaina’s sophomore year at Boston University. “Keeps Me Up” isn’t just about a specific person, but also the myriad of worries and anxieties that disrupt our peace, making it relatable to a broad audience. Alaina May poured her emotions into this track, crafting it from a voice memo on her phone and a messy page in her writing notebook.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The song’s sound is best described as acoustic-centric, with clear and dreamy vocals. It’s a genuine singer-songwriter experience, with elements of “bedroom pop” perfect for late-night listening. The minimalist, ambient production allows the powerful lyrics to shine while adding ear candy through vocal drone synths, sparkly synth arpeggios, and harmonies layered over simple acoustic guitar and piano tracks."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2ajMOVSXSjHyFhSnzBKBTb?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Collaborating with longtime friend and producer&nbsp;<strong>Nate Blanck</strong> (known as “<strong>Philia</strong>”), Alaina May transformed her acoustic vision into a complete track. The result is a composition they both take pride in, a testament to their creative synergy and commitment to crafting meaningful music."},{"t":"p","html":"For fans of Alaina May and newcomers alike, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1Atq6MOO1m1MSwQrVdtO4U?si=1a847076394b46f9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Keeps Me Up</strong></a>” marks the start of an exciting chapter in her musical journey. Hailing from Lake Country, Wisconsin, and currently a junior studying Business at Boston University, Alaina May’s heartfelt lyrics and melodies promise to resonate deeply with those who appreciate authentic storytelling in music."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/596593/large-ca2ac9520b83c3d25b8ab8498b583f58.png","alt":"\"Keeps Me Up\" Cover Art by Stephanie Liu, Graphic Design Major, Boston University"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>\"KEEPS ME UP\" LYRICS</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"When I close my eyes<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"To fall asleep at night<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"I try my best to clear my mind<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"But it never works<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"-"},{"t":"p","html":"In this dark and quiet room<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"I try not to thinking about you<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"And how you smell like her perfume&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"But I can't help it&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"​-<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"And oh"},{"t":"p","html":"Why can't I let go<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Of these restless thoughts in my head&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"All those things I should've said<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"It keeps me up<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"It keeps me up<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"-"},{"t":"p","html":"Felt too good to be true<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"I miss when had nothing to lose<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"If I could run on back to you<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"I would every time<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"-"},{"t":"p","html":"But things don't always go<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"The way we want them to<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"So stay in the corner of my mind<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Some things are better left behind<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"-"},{"t":"p","html":"And oh<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Why can't I let go<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Of these restless thoughts in my head<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"All those things I should've said<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"It keeps me up<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"It keeps me up<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"-"},{"t":"p","html":"When I close my eyes<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"To fall asleep at night<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591457/large-4c6dc3616563361b13f021ff1455b225.jpg","alt":"Alaina Keeps Me Up Art.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591457/preview-b6a22b61b22775ae4f27ae4fe940d8b8.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591458/large-8712263b27694d45f8f3661f3617522d.jpg","alt":"Alaina and nate.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591458/preview-6841e0aa558f03b941a73bc60f4631d3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591459/large-c63f38c6aace9136142c124859376928.jpg","alt":"Alaina guitar film.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591459/preview-874ff8016cd7407655131f6c75e6510b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591460/large-71f962934804a24a7ed8cc5c17dcb68f.jpg","alt":"Alaina studio.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591460/preview-1f6e61b42938d7ef94a4b5aaa1bbd1b0.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photo Credit: Maddie Walczak (@madelinewalczak)"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Alaina May:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Alaina May</strong> is a twenty-year-old indie-pop singer-songwriter from just outside of Milwaukee, Wisconsin, but currently living in Boston, Massachusetts, studying at Boston University. She has been playing music since she was 6 years old, but really discovered a passion when she got her first guitar at 10 years old. In more recent years, Alaina has ventured into songwriting and playing gigs at local restaurants and events in her hometown of Oconomowoc. Her music is acoustic-centric, with relatable coming-of-age lyrics, and catchy melodies. &nbsp;She recorded and released a 4-track EP, entitled “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1B846xzFFOIrd0XVrHZY4a?si=Ml9WnQHNSHevTVRf-JxTew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>417</strong></a>,” in September of 2022 and is also featured on several other tracks. But it was until writing and recording her new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1Atq6MOO1m1MSwQrVdtO4U?si=1a847076394b46f9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Keeps Me Up</strong></a>,” that Alaina felt like she found her sound as an artist and a songwriter. With a collection of new music and lyrics in the works, her journey is just getting started."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Alaina!"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@alainamaymusic/video/7298767062627913002","handle":"@alainamaymusic"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.alainamaymusic.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/Cy4Qf_cOnKE/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.alainamaymusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/alainaamay\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"mailto:alainamaymusic@gmail.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">E-mail</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@alainamaymusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"267333","title":"Tokyo-Based Artist STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION Drops New Electronic Single","date":"2023-11-17","lead":"The track \"MONOGRAM\" officially released, delving into the profound connection between family and personal identity.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/267333/eb1cf7a47eb6ce8e24478f999eac2fe5.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The track \"MONOGRAM\" officially released, delving into the profound connection between family and personal identity."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/135nKXuCgD9wcByXRWjB4o?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Tokyo, JAPAN (November 17, 2023) - Emerging Tokyo-based musician <a href=\"https://stereodivefoundation.jp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION</strong></a> released his new song “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/135nKXuCgD9wcByXRWjB4o?si=617f899404404408\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>MONOGRAM</strong></a>” on Friday, November 17. This unique composition delves into the profound connection between family, interpersonal bonding, and personal identity - all set against a backdrop of electronic, pop, and rock influences, with a special focus on piano rock."},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by the idea that a name is the first gift one receives in life, STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION explores the concept that the name bestowed upon us becomes an enduring connection with our inner selves. By contemplating the emotions and significance behind our names, we can forge a deep bond, using our names as guiding stars throughout life’s journey."},{"t":"quote","html":"“It’s been a long time since I released a new sound for SDF! I want listeners to feel the passion and nostalgia packed into piano rock and be able to enjoy it.”","cite":"- RON from STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/596591/large-66ebe3388a518ef086ce659fa5a3ebe0.jpg","alt":"Cover Art Design by Shinya Yoshino (BAVIC)"},{"t":"p","html":"“MONOGRAM” is featured as the theme song for a popular Game App: “<a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.bandainamcoent.tensuramrkww&amp;pcampaignid=web_share\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>That Time I Got Reincarnated as a Slime: ISEKAI Memories</strong></a>.”"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/I4zvhx4g2rk?si=3M4JuhXCaz7kRlNE","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"For those eager to explore the depths of “MONOGRAM,” the song’s lyrics are available in both Japanese and English, enabling a broader audience to appreciate the artistry and message contained within the song. These lyrics convey a deep emotional connection to names, bonds, and the world’s beauty, inviting listeners to embark on a heartfelt musical journey."},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>TOUR INFORMATION</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>10.29 Anime Weekend</strong> Atlanta, GA: EVENT<a href=\"https://awa-con.com/guests/stereo-dive-foundation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">&nbsp;LINK</a><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>11.11 KYOANI MUSIC FESTIVAL</strong> Kyoto, JP: EVENT&nbsp;<a href=\"https://kyoani-event.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LINK</a><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>12.16 TENSURA 10th LIVE</strong>\u0003Chiba, JP: EVENT <a href=\"https://10th.ten-sura.com/live\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LINK</a><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>02.02 ANIME EXPO SANTIAGO</strong> Santiago, CL: ​EVENT <a href=\"https://anime-expo.cl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LINK</a><br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5FW8M5cMPA24iL0TNT2Ojg?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/596589/large-1690ce0e420b308ddf82f55bca5c4168.jpg","alt":"SDF_A.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/596589/preview-cd60b333eb79370881dda3e05a10496d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/596590/large-d84bcf473782a278c6fd876e33a3e5b5.jpg","alt":"SDF_H1_MONOGRAM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/596590/preview-22c032ab862303ab297efd2b2fd79535.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://stereodivefoundation.jp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION</strong></a> is a sound-making project created by <strong>RON</strong>, who works on songwriting, composing, and arrangement of music. RON’s work has been featured as soundtracks for animation titles and other media content.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"In 2013, he launched his activities as STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION with the track “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2sChoyJsa5j3JLnTtVx0S8?si=42ffb223c5f84704\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Daisy</strong></a>” which was featured as the ending theme song of the anime series “<strong>Beyond the Boundary</strong>.” Since then, he has created and sung theme songs for many popular anime such as “<strong>Dimension W</strong>”, “<strong>Food Wars!</strong>”, “<strong>Moriarty the Patriot</strong>”, and “<strong>That Time I Got Reincarnated as a Slime</strong>.” Under the name “RON,” he has produced songs for voice actors and artists, and has also sung for “<strong>Hypnosis Mike</strong>,” “<strong>A3!</strong>” and “<strong>Love Live! Sunshine!!</strong>.”"},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to his talent as a multi-player of various musical instruments, he also is a Sound Artisan who produces a track with the futuristic synth work and a melody that will resonate with your heart. RON has been reputable for his distinct programming arrangements with it being able to adapt to various genres of music along with his catchy and artistic sounds."},{"t":"p","html":"RON has also created soundtracks, theme songs, and character songs for anime titles such as “<strong>Re:Zero: Starting Life in Another World</strong>” and “<strong>BNA</strong>.” He will do whatever it takes to express his desired sounds with his incredible sense, regardless of any method - this is STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/9-Bj9Z2J5ZM?si=Cu9NQtiNE6ltTfzO","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/ron_sdf/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@ron_sdf","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://stereodivefoundation.jp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a> |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/STEREODIVEFOUNDATIONOfficialChannel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/RON_SDF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"268675","title":"Isabella Dussias Unveils Indie Pop Ballad 'Honest'","date":"2023-11-11","lead":"\"Honest\" offers a soul-baring musical journey through NYC's indie scene.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/268675/9df742a7510b7740fe8052b50364fc3b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Honest\" offers a soul-baring musical journey through NYC's indie scene."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3ad7VRNlegl8dcGpM9uqVT?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (November 11, 2023) - <a href=\"https://isabelladussias.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Isabella Dussias</a>, the rising star in the indie music scene, just released her emotive and soul-stirring single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3ad7VRNlegl8dcGpM9uqVT?si=8bcb17c4d4bb4acf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Honest</strong></a>,” on November 11, 2023. Isabella Dussias’ “Honest” is an indie pop ballad infused with folk influences that explores themes of heartbreak and vulnerability in the face of manipulation.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I really enjoy pulling from my background as a composer in writing for strings and some  more typical orchestral instruments, and I think I definitely tapped into that in the production of this track.”","cite":"- Isabella Dussias, NYC-based singer-songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"The song “Honest” delves deep into the complex emotions of falling victim to manipulation while grappling with heartbreak. It tells a compelling story of one person leading another on, even when unspoken mutual feelings exist. Isabella’s lyrics capture the emotional turmoil of dealing with someone who won’t fully commit, yet can’t help revealing their affection. The central lyrical theme of being “too honest” with oneself underscores the experience of being so self-aware of manipulation that it becomes challenging to act naturally, confirming the manipulator’s success."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/599090/large-a3b0a277faa67e0e76b0fc6cdcde14ef.jpeg","alt":"\"Honest\" Cover Art"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I hope this song can provide some kind of catharsis to whoever may be experiencing a similar, frustrating situation.”","cite":"- Isabella Dussias, NYC-based singer-songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"Isabella’s expert songwriting, combined with her unique blend of instrumentation, creates a gradually intensifying atmosphere in “Honest.” The track begins with delicate elements like the ukulele, violin, and harp in the first verse, reflecting vulnerability and hesitation. As the song progresses, the lyrics evolve from expressing helplessness to frustration, and the production mirrors this emotional intensity with the introduction of drums, electric guitar, and piano. “Honest” features a gradual build that eventually erupts into an emotional crescendo."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3UfoQWFZPSZ44fD5IANBX3?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Isabella Dussias is an artist to watch in the indie pop and folk music scene, and “Honest” showcases her versatility as a musician and her ability to connect with audiences on a deep, emotional level. With her powerful storytelling and musical prowess, Isabella has already made waves in New York City and is poised to captivate listeners worldwide with her latest release."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Isabella Dussias:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3UfoQWFZPSZ44fD5IANBX3?si=rofKV23pS1CbnEMUaFpzcw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Isabella Dussias</strong></a> is a 20-year-old singer-songwriter/composer, whose indie pop music is influenced by folk, rock, and orchestral elements. She enjoys the entire process of creating music: writing, producing, and performing. She is a multifaceted musician whose creative range spans from writing and performing her pop music to composing for film and musical theatre. Check out Isabella’s new song, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3ad7VRNlegl8dcGpM9uqVT?si=ad6ac443e1554754\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Honest</strong></a>,” now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Isabella!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ac6glaO8ox8?si=bHkOFcLGVpgrWQV6","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/isabelladussiasmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@isabelladussiasmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/isabella.dussias\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://twitter.com/IsabellaDussias\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCx0Q53J-0C0vbvNOQLZEAzw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"264782","title":"This is the homepage for A Permanent Shadow, an Electronic Rock and Synth Pop band based in Barcelona. New album HUMDRUM is out on March 4, 2022.","date":"2023-11-10","lead":"The Barcelona-based artist launched the music video for the new track that delves into emotionally charged themes.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/264782/056e99e456957837536828544c45f3ae.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Barcelona-based artist launched the music video for the new track that delves into emotionally charged themes."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5qATNxVXZ11LaMGFQZdv2p?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Barcelona, SPAIN (November 3, 2023) - <a href=\"https://www.apermanentshadow.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>A Permanent Shadow</strong></a>, the musical collective around <strong>CP Fletcher&nbsp;</strong>aims to captivate listeners with his electrifying new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1xJ8hMoehinP2SyuDCRN9s?si=_sG-VFZ4TaKFVda1Eol03A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Brother</strong></a>.” This bold and intimate track officially launched on Friday, November 3rd, and promises to deliver a captivating sonic experience that showcases the artist’s unique sound and boundless creativity."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/0C-43Q6APpA?si=Rd1KSwjcAR7BBwbp","height":"385"},{"t":"p","html":"“Brother” marks a compelling expansion of A Permanent Shadow’s evolving musical catalog, skillfully merging elements of Indie-Pop and Post-Punk. Crafted around the absence of singer CP Fletcher’s brother, this single delves into emotionally charged themes that strike a chord with the artist. “Brother” creates an introspective path for listeners to walk, contemplating life-altering scenarios, nostalgic moments, and the uncertain future."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589295/large-67b6f7b6743fbf09dc77ed09a60a3b50.jpg","alt":"\"Brother\" Cover Art and Photos by Daniel Díaz."},{"t":"p","html":"A Permanent Shadow has been making waves in the Barcelona music scene, refining a unique sound that explores an unparalleled sonic terrain. Channeling the spirit of early 80s New Wave music, “Brother” is a catchy track enriched with captivating percussive intricacies, guaranteed to get listeners moving to the beat. CP Fletcher and his team are thrilled to share “Brother” with fans across the world. This song is a vibrant and intense experience that reflects the artist’s dedication to exploring new musical horizons."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I feel a sense of sadness for not having a brother, but I'm fortunate to have a beloved sister. I celebrate my brother’s enduring spirit, which I believe is always with me.”","cite":"- A Permanent Shadow (CP Fletcher), Alternative Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"“Brother” is a sneak peek of A Permanent Shadow’s upcoming full-length LP, which was recorded by the usual team of CP Fletcher on vocals as well as multi-instrumentalists and producers <strong>Valentí Nieto</strong> and <strong>Albert Català</strong>. The LP will be the third record released by A Permanent Shadow and will tackle topics loosely related to dysfunctional topics on a personal and geopolitical level. Musically, the LP will feature a guitar-driven sound that strays from A Permanent Shadow’s previous releases.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589296/large-159762219a2bf8de3902e421318405cf.jpeg","alt":"APS PROMO (2).jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589296/preview-93382c8a6d085a3c0e6aadb1a932d08a.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589297/large-223a1826b16d3709ecf599bffef74c68.jpg","alt":"A Permanent Shadow - Brother.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589297/preview-3c5a52a7a7954b033e870a7c227c665a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589298/large-e369976aa7f0575cd140600f34e6a490.jpg","alt":"APS PROMO (4).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589298/preview-36dc913b318abe395edbc08807a292c7.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589299/large-232f080f97b031cda26eea7e48b5ecb1.jpg","alt":"APS PROMO (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589299/preview-74ffacecba40cff23793c12efbc819fd.jpg"}]},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6mrGJN7uKAelkBlqMqUn8d?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About A Permanent Shadow:"},{"t":"p","html":"A Permanent Shadow is a band for want of a better description. Its only fixture is CP Fletcher who for his recordings surrounds himself with a rotating cast of musicians and producers. Fletcher used to be a drummer in various bands that went nowhere, so at one point, inspired by David Bowie's death, he decided to form his own band as a singer. CP took his first steps as a frontman man forming a <strong>Lou Reed&nbsp;</strong>tribute project, <strong>The Magic</strong> and <strong>Loss Orchestra</strong>. Such is his admiration for the curmudgeon from New York that the tribute experience ended up bleeding into A Permanent Shadow via a cover of <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1MNWaaHKNJGQlqH3xUys5d?si=9e59ab1be4524036\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sword of Damocles</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> originally featured on Reed’s Magic and Loss album and included on the band's first album “Songs of Loss” in a reworked form.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The band involves various collaborators, although two musicians so far feature on all recordings: <strong>Albert Català</strong>, a classically trained piano player, helps CP whip the demos into shape, while the finishing touches in the studio are usually provided by renowned producer <strong>Valentí Nieto</strong>. Both albums <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0d7H2IzDxXwpNsW4NheDdY?si=JE_vOr5jS4ali2DmtX8Ubw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Songs of Loss</strong></a><strong>”</strong> (2019) and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/59GgNHgWEJzZrgGMriVpAj?si=_bq1MQj1Soq3coDIfTbxng\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Humdrum</strong></a><strong>”</strong> (2022) as well as the EP <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/45TQ4Z15JQObdtLpvGuPIU?si=IgMtPgWrTBW4b1UcnSZT9Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>UnderCover</strong></a><strong>’</strong> (2022) and the new single were recorded with contributions from these two musicians."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with A Permanent Shadow!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/R6TBGLfuup4","height":"450"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/apermanentshadow/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@apermanentshadow","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.apermanentshadow.com/","img":"","title":"This is the homepage for A Permanent Shadow, an Electronic Rock and Synth Pop band based in Barcelona. New album HUMDRUM is out on March 4, 2022.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/apermanentshadow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook </strong></a><strong>| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@APermanentShadow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube </strong></a><strong>| </strong><a href=\"https://twitter.com/apermanentshad1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"265000","title":"Charlie John Drops Highly Anticipated Eclectic Album: CHARLIE","date":"2023-11-10","lead":"The 12-track record promises a diverse and eclectic sound and explores important life lessons.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/265000/612d82fbe337f4da61f4c1e811434473.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The 12-track record promises a diverse and eclectic sound and explores important life lessons."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1DiS1IWKQuTUQmVnQBOpds?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Covington, KY (November 10, 2023) - Emerging singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://www.charliejohnmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Charlie John</strong></a>, captivates music lovers with the release of his new album “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1DiS1IWKQuTUQmVnQBOpds?si=qlNL3w8cTmC13dfQhHRf-Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>CHARLIE</strong></a>.” The new record promises a diverse and eclectic sound, drawing influences from Acoustic Pop, Singer-Songwriter, Pop/Rock, and even elements of Dance."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4ZA9n5a5pwCT27HjeNOMfs?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Charlie John has been on a musical journey for more than 12 years, during which he wrote hundreds of songs. “CHARLIE” consists of 12 tracks that are especially meaningful to the artist. This album not only demonstrates his growth as a songwriter and producer but also explores the important life lessons he has gained throughout his journey."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Out of the hundreds of songs I’ve written over the years, these are the 12 I feel closest to.”","cite":"-Charlie John (Singer-Songwriter)"},{"t":"p","html":"The album pays homage to a wide array of musical inspirations, featuring tracks that draw from artists such as <strong>Phil Collins</strong>, <strong>John Mayer</strong>, <strong>Ed Sheeran</strong>, and <strong>The Band Camino</strong>. In a heartfelt tribute, the album closes with a cover of Phil Collins’ iconic hit, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2ZVF7xhETPG9ulckfOWTzO?si=954badf2567a4b6a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Take Me Home</strong></a>.”"},{"t":"p","html":"“CHARLIE” is a musical exploration of diverse genres, revealing Charlie John’s artistic versatility. The album blends elements from Acoustic, Pop, Top40, and Singer-Songwriter styles to craft a captivating and immersive listening experience. The themes covered in this album delve into topics including mental health, unrequited love, romantic attraction, heartbreak, introspection, and the sense of belonging."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589673/large-62fa007e4cab50081f6a248594d66cff.jpg","alt":"CHARLIE Album Cover Art"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589670/large-470223d1cbb0ff07264e001efd0cd054.jpg","alt":"348856486_725845835982414_7939910428239050201_n.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589670/preview-fbafd3663076b6d1f470971caddb4d82.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589671/large-1b68eb29b842ad9dfe5331211a804a8f.jpg","alt":"Charlie_BACK.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589671/preview-bfee5f8949ad374f8a02e4ac6a8cf8e3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589672/large-75982e39a4c3e2b44c6e4929018dc3ef.jpg","alt":"Charlie_FRONT.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589672/preview-2c669fe4baed93c6566c313f84ce6bce.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589674/large-bb35b69ce2427ed1b23dff2596419fb4.jpg","alt":"Promo 1_30_23.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589674/preview-0c8a89faf3552c70adbec73eacb89bb9.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Charlie John:"},{"t":"p","html":"Born into a family of musicians, singers and songwriters, Charlie’s unquenchable passion for great music and melodies seemed only natural. In 2013, 2014 and 2016 Charlie was contacted by the producers of the TV show “<strong>The Voice</strong>” and invited to audition in Chicago, Dallas and Nashville. Charlie has been a full-time musician for over 12 plus years, performing locally in KY but also all over the US - from LA to Vegas to New York."},{"t":"p","html":"He also recently won <em>“Best Original Pop Song”</em><strong>&nbsp;</strong>and <em>“Best Original Singer/ Songwriter Song” </em>in the 2016 <strong>Ohio Music Awards</strong>&nbsp;and the overall Grand Prize in the <strong>Songdoor 2016 International Songwriting Competition</strong> with his song “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1HWefmmg2FwcaZ1n0IFTxy?si=c47f8f6c223e43f3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Change Me</strong></a>.”"},{"t":"p","html":"In 2023 and currently living in Covington, KY, Charlie was invited to perform a set of original music at <strong>SXSW&nbsp;</strong>in Austin, TX as well as <strong>Summerfest 55</strong> in Milwaukee, WI, the biggest music festival in the world. He continues to write, perform, and produce his own blend of Pop, Soul, and Indie music and tour the country as well as release one song per month culminating in his new record “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1DiS1IWKQuTUQmVnQBOpds?si=TlHjzZZ7RHujQRQtHM-4vA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>CHARLIE</strong></a>,” now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Charlie!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/charliejohnmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@charliejohnmusic","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/SJHLH-QInxE?si=qM8iAfM8DaxiuHYq","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://charliejohnmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/cjohnmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@charliejohnmusic_\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCdYeT14xLbhJlVtI3-DZHuw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"265531","title":"Official website of Lola Kristine: singer, pianist, and composer based in Southern California.","date":"2023-11-10","lead":"This release marks part 2 of Lola's 5-part chapter series, taking listeners on a journey of healing and self-discovery.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/265531/0f142224f56de532e42458fb2930a3fe.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This release marks part 2 of Lola's 5-part chapter series, taking listeners on a journey of healing and self-discovery."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1erhxIjaxePFBGEVjTSOnA?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"LAGUNA BEACH, CA (November 10, 2023) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?si=s5G-8qLvTyiyg4ae44jLPQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lola Kristine</strong></a>, the renowned artist known for her soulful and melodious compositions, is set to tug at the heartstrings of her audience with her latest work, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1erhxIjaxePFBGEVjTSOnA?si=GUIvclciRDGiUKImi3_bpQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘</strong><strong>chapter two: when things fall apart.’</strong></a> The chapter just released on November 10, 2023, and promises a musical exploration of themes of heartbreak, forgiveness, love, and more.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"ABOUT THE CHAPTERS:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lola Kristine</strong> is releasing 5 chapters of song pairings before launching her forthcoming album, <strong>‘CHAPTERS’</strong>. Taking the helm as the primary producer and songwriter, Lola invites her audience into a more profound exploration of her soul's expression through the formation of this record.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"‘CHAPTERS’ unfolds as a narrative composed of five distinct chapters, each narrating a poignant piece of her path to redemption. Commencing with her journey of passionate infatuation and the ensuing heartbreak, the album delves deeper beneath the surface to reveal the essence of a fierce, untamed spirit.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592105/large-276db6291af3da6d6d3443b8709f4442.jpg","alt":"just friends 5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592105/preview-07cede9cfd93c1239de1c9b1e3c22ecd.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592103/large-42cfe37d7f09c9bfd97f82bb7803d28b.jpg","alt":"just friends 4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592103/preview-785ef0c0d249d2dd7a6e1bfa024ef7c1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592102/large-5adb2a6bb195d923896e1e467bb7e55a.jpg","alt":"just friends still 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592102/preview-d700f489593011fd900e64fcb74a0444.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592104/large-8feebfef7842ecf923131def03a5438e.jpg","alt":"just friends 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592104/preview-4d60444e977716716f2213a484716e32.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592106/large-93ca27719b56b149ab7c8a6ed0e67236.jpg","alt":"just friends 6.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592106/preview-d51efa8a640bd652a10c6b0b232cff91.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592107/large-3617932e5b0534aca34ee0ac26e0c547.jpg","alt":"Enlight331.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592107/preview-7af37a75cb35da6df4b56bf66efa51f6.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>​Preview photos from \"Just Friends\" music video launching at end of ​November</em><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<em><strong>*CHAPTER TWO REACHES HOLLYWOOD*</strong></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>‘chapter two: when things fall apart’</strong> is making waves in the entertainment industry as her song <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1T4eIT0u7D99Xmu1XUndEp?si=1e679ebd3cf04158\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">‘<strong>Just Friends</strong>’</a> finds its way onto the soundtrack of the popular Canadian TV show, <a href=\"https://www.cwtv.com/shows/children-ruin-everything/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Children Ruin Everything</strong></em></a> Season 3, Episode 4, airing on <strong>CTV</strong>. The episode is scheduled for release on October 18th, 2023, providing Canadian audiences with a captivating sonic backdrop to the show's narrative.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"For fans across the border, the good news continues, as this Canadian broadcast will be followed by an anticipated airing in a few months on <strong>Roku</strong> and <strong>CW</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"This placement marks a significant milestone in Lola Kristine's music career, showcasing her growing presence in both the Canadian and American entertainment landscapes. Stay tuned for a mesmerizing fusion of visuals and music as ‘Just Friends’ enhances the viewing experience for fans on both sides of the border."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>‘chapter two: when things fall apart’</strong> features Lola Kristine's evocative lyrics and poignant melodies that work in tandem to paint a vivid picture of the human experience. Her music seamlessly crosses genres, offering a fusion of soul, folk, adult contemporary, Americana, R&amp;B, and more - creating a unforgettably unique sound. Lola Kristine's second chapter touches on a wide array of themes, from toxic relationships and denial, to the refining power of pain and loss. Her songs are a testament to the resilience of the human spirit and its capacity for love even in the face of heartbreak and despair."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591039/large-c8e66655153360fad5cecec66542dff2.jpg","alt":"COVER ART - chapter two: when things fall apart"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The powerful fire of pain and loss served as a reawakening, leaving me in a place where I can still feel love for those who have hurt me.\"","cite":"Lola Kristine, Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>ABOUT \"chapter two: when things fall apart\"</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"This release unfolds like a compelling narrative, with key tracks such as <strong>‘Just Friends,’ ‘Sheets,’</strong> and <strong>‘Wish You Love’</strong> guiding listeners through the highs and lows of love and loss. <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1T4eIT0u7D99Xmu1XUndEp?si=664a8d2624dd444d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘Just Friends’</strong></a> captures the desperate plea for a lover to rekindle the electric connection they once shared, while <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1ufO3gW9LDlGX8T7mEB7Y5?si=f1f5fcf5315b4445\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘Sheets’</strong></a> offers a haunting melody, a reflection on lost dreams and fading memories. This part of Lola's journey represents an emotional zenith that is reached with <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7kil7NneUpoyOmTIaluoP5?si=9c209188f2684d53\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘Wish You Love,’</strong></a> a song born from the depths of sorrow and anger. Lola Kristine's artistic journey in crafting these songs and her commitment to their authenticity is a testament to her talent and resilience."},{"t":"h3","html":"SONG CREDITS:"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Producer: Lola Kristine</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Co-producer: Justin Busch</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Mixing: Tyler Norris with ma6io</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Mastering: Duncan Ferguson with The Voltage Exchange</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Executive Producer: John Ward</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“Just Friends”</strong> - Songwriters: Laura Kristine Hennicke and Justin Busch; Vocals, keyboard, background vocals, synths: Lola Kristine; Bass: Jesse Stern ; Drums: Tom Kendall Hughes; Guitars: Jon Conley."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“Sheets”</strong> - Songwriter: Laura Kristine Hennicke; Vocals, piano, background vocals, synths, drums &amp; bass production: Lola Kristine; Acoustic and electric guitars: Sarven Manguiat; Background vocals: Sarven Manguiat."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“Wish You Love</strong>” - Songwriter: Laura Kristine Hennicke; Producer: Lola Kristine; Co-producer: Justin Froese and Justin Busch; Vocals, piano, synths: Lola Kristine; Acoustic guitar: &nbsp;Justin Froese; String arrangement and performer: Andrew Joslyn."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>*In addition to release of chapter two, Lola Kristine is set to take her music on tour, connecting with her audience on an intimate and personal level.*</em>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong><u>LOLA KRISTINE TOUR DATES &amp; INFO</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>November 17, 2023, Friday:</strong> The Beach House SB @ 7:00 pm, Seal Beach, CA, United States<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>December 6, 2023, Wednesday:</strong> Le Papagayo Carlsbad @ 6:30 pm, Carlsbad, CA, United States<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>December 14, 2023, Thursday:</strong> LOLA KRISTINE FULL BAND at SKYLOFT @ 8:00 pm, Laguna Beach, CA, United States<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>December 21, 2023, Thursday:</strong> Lola Kristine at the Sheldon St. Louis @ 7:30 pm, St. Louis, MO, United States<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lola Kristine:"},{"t":"p","html":"Lola Kristine is a singer, pianist and songwriter based in Laguna Beach, California. Known as “the little girl with the big voice,” Lola has been staggering audiences her whole life with the depth of soul she possesses in both her timeless songwriting and penetrating singing. Hearing her sing feeds your soul and reconnects you with what is right in the world.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"From humble beginnings in St. Louis, Missouri, Lola has taken her music across the country, touring with noted musicians such as <strong>Premik Russell</strong> <strong>Tubbs</strong><strong>&nbsp;(Santana, Sting, James Taylor), Jeff Haynes (Joni Mitchell, Herbie Hancock)</strong> and bass virtuoso <strong>Michael Manring</strong>. She has collaborated with artists from all over the world, including <strong>Kinobe</strong> (Uganda) in a series sponsored by <strong>American Voices</strong>. In 2022, a live video of Lola performing went viral on <strong>TikTok</strong>, hitting 4.5M views which boosted her online presence. She is gaining notoriety amidst legendary rockstars such as <strong>Mick Fleetwood</strong> and <strong>Don Cromwell</strong> of <strong>Air Supply</strong>. She is currently living in Southern California, where she can be found performing at venues and clubs all up and down the coast."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lola Kristine:"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.musicoflola.com/","img":"","title":"Official website of Lola Kristine: singer, pianist, and composer based in Southern California.","desc":""},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"http://instagram.com/musicoflola\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC7LAxI_AIC0YgeP0CcLYNOw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube&nbsp;</a>| <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?si=hmR1xgocRoqKVRInC1oRqQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"265662","title":"Kevin Goodwin Takes A Heartfelt Journey Through Time In New Single, \"Forevermore\"","date":"2023-11-10","lead":"A raw and emotional testament to love and longing, the track leaves listeners lingering for romance.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/265662/36cd7094a511d334a95cf29a3fbfd043.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A raw and emotional testament to love and longing, the track leaves listeners lingering for romance."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1xEs6kZJqOGvUglOqjmP7R?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Chapel Hill, NC (November 10, 2023) - Singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://www.kevingoodwinmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Kevin Goodwin</strong></a> just released his latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2thZLVSOQrabkQJWDzGf02?si=104fc890b6e24776\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Forevermore</strong></a>” on November 10, 2023. This heartfelt ballad is a raw and emotional testament to love and longing, as Goodwin bares his soul in an attempt to rekindle a romance that has lingered in his heart for years."},{"t":"p","html":"“Forevermore” explores the depths of love, dating, breakups, and the longing that often remains long after a connection has been severed. The song recounts a significant conversation between Goodwin and former love, the inspiration behind this poignant track. With this song, Kevin Goodwin hopes to bridge the gap that has separated them for years and rekindle the flame of their past love."},{"t":"p","html":"Goodwin’s music typically resonates with a broad audience, but “Forevermore” is a departure from his usual approach. He wrote this song with a very specific audience in mind - the woman he hopes will hear it and be moved to reconnect with him."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590577/large-6d3b953fc6ad88b1aae01d8e8345a882.jpg","alt":"\"Forevermore\" Cover Art by  Daniel Ruhland"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song is very different from anything I've written before. All of my songs are pulled from personal experiences I’ve had, but I usually write with a larger audience in mind and try to make songs as relatable as possible. With Forevermore, I wrote the song for an audience of one.”","cite":"- Kevin Goodwin, Indie Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"The track opens with a gentle piano and vocals that gradually build in intensity, climaxing in a powerful guitar-driven rock outro. The minimalistic production throughout the song emphasizes its raw and emotional essence. The song paints a vivid picture of love’s enduring presence, even after years of separation, and the hope of rekindling that flame."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590659/large-df3aa8cae5104e0f284ea88fec154be6.jpg","alt":"Press photo Kevin Goodwin 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590659/preview-1f9d72d1c885f3959685e7853b87cfc9.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590657/large-2cdf8f8f4f985aaac6f5f2e4ebddd640.png","alt":"Press photo Kevin Goodwin 1.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590657/preview-b9524003e018ee6b07a80ab6367e8053.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590658/large-c980afe536d9e815e5c75d0377e7af64.png","alt":"Press photo Kevin Goodwin 2.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590658/preview-4f0db2e83c0518192eec96d144f60b68.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592090/large-b058daadc189ae2322fe381030d89e97.jpeg","alt":"Press photo Kevin Goodwin 6.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592090/preview-048a42c0687ea241c4cb7090143f5be1.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592091/large-51ea07c8cff0dcaafa171bba0a7b731a.png","alt":"Press photo Kevin Goodwin 5.PNG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/592091/preview-b7ad0beb3360ff62d6885afbeaf286ff.png"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em><u>FOREVERMORE LYRICS:</u></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I know it's been years</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>But it's really good to hear your voice again</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Despite how things might appear</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I never wanted to forget</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>The things we said</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I replay them in my head</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Yeah, I've got regrets </em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>But you were never one of them</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"-"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Time couldn't stop</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>My memories of us</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"-"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I know you tried to forget the past</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>But now I'm asking you to bring it back</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I kept your secrets just like I promised</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>We weren't perfect but our love was honest</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"​-<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I hope you know</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>There's nothing I won't do</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>To show you that</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I never stopped loving you</em><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kevin Goodwin:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Kevin Goodwin</strong> is a hopeless romantic and singer-songwriter from Chapel Hill, North Carolina. He’s passionate about making songs that sound like they would have been popular twenty years ago. Kevin fell in love with writing and performing music at a young age, and spent most of his time throughout high school writing songs and playing shows around his hometown. He loves lots of different kinds of music, but his favorite genre has always been 2000's pop rock.<strong>&nbsp;The Fray</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;John Mayer</strong>, <strong>Counting Crows</strong>, and other artists in that vein are his biggest influences. Anything they’d be playing in a dentist's office or at <strong>Harris Teeter</strong>, that’s what he’s into."},{"t":"p","html":"On February 1st, 2019, Goodwin released his debut EP, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2ld2o4L4PnIQNJGkV7whQk?si=IOOuNEGHQ5q5MHnUEDvutw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>This Is How It Starts</strong></a>.’ That record would go on to gain traction, surpassing over 250,000 streams on Spotify. He then released his sophomore EP, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7MflVNLwiHdP3xJZoq3gtJ?si=4SdAo7zVTqqAyY48jBGL0A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Heart of the City</strong></a>,’ on March 5th, 2021. That record would also go on to garner over 250,000 streams on Spotify. His most recent EP, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3lYfQFgMI4IsNWjYYQLZj1?si=efkhPgMMR1y0X1HXSW3V0g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>One Hell of a Night</strong></a>,’ was released on August 25th, 2023. The lead single from this most recent record, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6OXc7l7t6EVqmVItIVlAki?si=69f017821cab4003\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Best Damn Time</strong></a>,’ recently surpassed 100,000 views on YouTube and has received radio play."},{"t":"p","html":"Kevin’s latest single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2thZLVSOQrabkQJWDzGf02?si=3d43c9a472c14e0b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Forevermore</strong></a>” is a vulnerable ballad that was written as an attempt to reconnect with a former love, and is now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Kevin!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4890mBPAQV8jDjH49BAGUC?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/kevingoodwinmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@kevingoodwinmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4890mBPAQV8jDjH49BAGUC?si=kzU039XCROyHpW-23byBFA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/kevin-goodwin/1414627017\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Music</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/kevingoodwinmusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC3r_YSfLKrov3ZzwFXCueyg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@kevingoodwinmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"266160","title":"Introducing Kim Brogli's New EP: The Fight","date":"2023-11-10","lead":"The debut EP features an array of soul-stirring songs that contain elements of country, Americana, and folk.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/266160/bd764a5c2018e12a1a051c4810d90731.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The debut EP features an array of soul-stirring songs that contain elements of country, Americana, and folk."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2xiZ2zjr5R2tlZf9HGSEze?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"College Grove, TN (November 10, 2023) - Rising artist <a href=\"https://www.kimbrogli.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Kim Brogli</strong></a> released her debut EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2xiZ2zjr5R2tlZf9HGSEze?si=63ykddsWRVGFEOtPhk7WYw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">‘<strong>The Fight’</strong></a>, on November 10, 2023. The new record will include an eclectic mix of musical styles and poignant themes. With influences from Americana, Folk Rock, and Alternative Country, Kim's EP takes listeners on a journey through life's trials and triumphs, including mental health awareness, love and relationships, parenting, self-doubt, and self-help, all while maintaining an element of fun.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT THE EP</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Kim Brogli delves into her personal experiences and the challenges that have shaped her life in this new EP. <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/31BuKwC772TseurCXOgux5?si=4fd56e9750fc41f0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘The Fight’</strong></a> explores the depths of self-doubt and condemnation in tracks like <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/31BuKwC772TseurCXOgux5?si=4fd56e9750fc41f0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘Let Her Go,’</strong></a> advocating for self-acceptance and hope. In the title track, ‘The Fight,’ Kim explores the complex world of parenting and the importance of teaching children valuable life lessons. Love and relationships take center stage in her cover song, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4Szl1jBr0srQZhjcaY8m80?si=d529f8dc3e7a4eb3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘Crazy For You,’</strong></a> while <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2In0eJpe9I0gTlVOAKIQbW?si=941e375088ca40ed\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘What A Waste’</strong></a> provides a heartfelt commentary on addiction and its impact on loved ones. To ensure a balanced mix of emotions, the EP also includes a lighthearted take on Kim's life journey in <strong>‘It's a Good Day.’</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"‘The Fight’ offers a unique soundscape of mid-tempo love songs with an R&amp;B pop flair. Kim Brogli's soul-stirring lyrics are reminiscent of artists like Patty Griffin, Lori McKenna, or Brandi Carlile, infused with hints of blues, akin to Grace Potter or Susan Tedeschi. The EP's vocal delivery combines elements of sweetness and grit, making for a truly engaging musical experience.&nbsp;"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>TRACK LIST</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Track 01: The Fight</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Track 02: Let Her Go</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Track 03: Crazy For You</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Track 04: What A Waste</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Track 05: It's A Good Day</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591448/large-a92d273d7a53a12929e2fed057b94121.png","alt":"The Fight: Cover Art"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/524zMfMtxBzJmyaXk4zfK5?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I'm super excited to release my debut EP. This body of work encompasses a good mix of tempo along with a variety in sound and messages. From the serious repercussions of addiction on loved ones, to perspective on parenting to just having a good time enjoying the blessings of life, this EP has it all.\"","cite":"Kim Brogli, Country Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>*Kim Brogli has released professional music videos for \"What A Waste\" and \"Crazy For You,\" which are on her <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCLUqHDysd6NxPjuqxZQW6AQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Youtube channel</a>*</em><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kim Brogli:"},{"t":"p","html":"An out-of-the-box creative coupled with a fierce drive, work ethic, and unique ability to pull at your heart, Nashville-based singer-songwriter&nbsp;<strong>Kim Brogli</strong> is making her mark among Nashville songwriters. The Middle Tennessee native was always a writer and storyteller at heart. She recalls with laughter being the ADHD kid who was constantly in trouble at school, making the other kids laugh with her outrageous humor and telling stories that kept kids laughing or in suspense til the end. In the fourth grade, Kim tried out for the school choir and didn’t make it. <em>“I was a sensitive kid and have always been harder on myself than anyone else could ever be. So when I didn’t make the choir, I never sang again publicly. I just thought...I must be a terrible singer. It never dawned on me I was nervous and shy.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"She went on to graduate from The University of Alabama with a degree in French and International Business. &nbsp;After a successful career selling real estate, she bought guitars for her twin boys and ended up playing them herself. &nbsp;After getting her own guitar for Christmas that year, she began taking voice lessons, and that led to putting her words on paper into song. After recording a few singles with her then-vocal coach <strong>Kristen Smith</strong>, acclaimed producer, <strong>Will Gawley</strong>, found Kim on Instagram and said her soulful voice was reflective of those ‘70s songwriters. She has often been compared to <strong>Emmylou Harris</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;Alison Krauss</strong>, <strong>Lori McKenna,</strong> and <strong>Sarah Jarosz</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"They decided to record her debut EP, which includes four original songs she wrote or co-wrote with hit songwriter, James Dean Hicks. &nbsp;In it, she touches on subjects like faith, love, life lessons, self-doubt, parenting, and many other feelings she has processed on paper. She is slowly finding an audience in the Americana market. Her songs have the ability to bring tears and make you reflect upon the deeper meaning of life in a sweet, understated way. She performs mostly around Nashville at this time."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Kim!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/8mm1_Eddp4k?si=lHRmmldoRz2yqVT6","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/kimbroglimusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@kimbroglimusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/kimbroglimusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/kimbroglartist\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TWITTER</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@kimbrogli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"266161","title":"New Song Alert: Ámaris Unveils \"Different\" – A Powerful Journey Through Change","date":"2023-11-10","lead":"London-based electronic artist drops her new track, exploring profound themes of mental health and personal transformation.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/266161/a2618e948e7aacbfd84155c0e47a551d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"London-based electronic artist drops her new track, exploring profound themes of mental health and personal transformation."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4sEbA3e80JSSZhT7n0wvcY?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"London, UK (November 10, 2023) - Electronic music artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6oqjlwI9NonKlLldVEObEf?si=l5nlplHCS1qxuMPd8wyzaw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ámaris</strong></a>, who is also known as <strong>Amaris Emersleben,</strong> is back with her latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2lFpPlyDOp5ky0zL0KZbvl?si=590379c9de844600\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Different</strong></a>,” which just dropped on November 10th, Friday. This hauntingly beautiful track, nestled within the electronic and electronica genres, explores profound themes of mental health and personal transformation. It is a testament to Ámaris’ unique ability to provide comfort and solace through her music."},{"t":"p","html":"“Different” expresses the struggle of breaking free from toxic circumstances. It soothes listeners during moments of sadness and ignites inspiration for fresh starts, serving as a powerful reminder to embrace new beginnings. The heart and soul of this track lie in the realization that new beginnings can be overwhelming, encapsulating the emotions that come with change and the feeling of drifting in uncharted waters."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I believe in the power of escapism for the sake of our sanity. As a creative, I see my role as providing an avenue for people to escape from the challenges and complexities of their lives, even if only for a while.”","cite":"- Ámaris - Electronic Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"The cover artwork for “Different” is a striking visual representation of the song’s essence, having been photographed during a shoot in an actual river. This intentional choice mirrors the feeling of <em>drifting </em>that often accompanies moments of introspection and rumination. Originally planned for inclusion in Ámaris’ synth-pop album <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6XR9kuZ40K6PKh2BW1qmDS?si=tpFN9Vh4Txu3jmY4fAY9lg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Love and Oceans</strong></em></a>, which was released earlier this year, “Different” has found its own unique space in the spotlight."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6oqjlwI9NonKlLldVEObEf?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591449/large-39b903cd1891ebfc357b720caca286ff.jpg","alt":"9_Amaris_Emersleben_Photo_by_Claudia_Reinert.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591449/preview-506e3935c2d1c09171fa774527d1bf60.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591450/large-891c4f2bdf979ca4d15a8dd1b323b601.jpg","alt":"3_amaris_photo_by_Claudia_Reinert.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591450/preview-eff5407359ba1a385537a5bed1f98a1e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591451/large-41062a010866ba3840a4fb7a54ebd3c4.jpg","alt":"5_Amaris_Emersleben_Photo_by_Claudia_Reinert.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591451/preview-9c5028265f045e772002dd2c6858b983.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591452/large-31179e5aeb80f87183356abbb2caacd4.jpg","alt":"2_Amaris_Emersleben_Photo_by_Claudia_Reinert.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591452/preview-ee011f4f2823713df6b41e5b52607956.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591454/large-55b8f17b7ba51c762d5343e23bfd376c.jpg","alt":"4_amaris_emersleben_Photo_by_Claudia_Reinert.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591454/preview-b1c1ae9bf5410a1c11a6b84c59c35007.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by Claudia Reinert"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Ámaris:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Amaris Emersleben</strong>, also known as “Ámaris”, is a music producer (“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6XR9kuZ40K6PKh2BW1qmDS?si=wUd0gsXzQPqgifSIubjh7Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Love and Oceans</strong></a>”, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1coJyOCJEVfZBt9woSXoPM?si=gt-TzaiKRtu3_p6BavxvBw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dream World</strong></a>”), a fantasy author (“<strong>Lagoona: A Journey through the Reef</strong>”), and an actor. Her most recent album “Love and Oceans” was released in 2023. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Amaris grew up in Switzerland as the daughter of a teacher and a Swiss musician and a professor of music. Her family is from the Netherlands, New Zealand, and Switzerland, which is why she grew up with English, German, and Dutch. After her parents’ divorce, she moved to Zurich where she attended school. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Amaris received her formal training at drama school in Zurich, and at the Stage &amp; Musical School in Frankfurt, Germany, where she started to listen to electronic music for her dance studies, which made her discover the genre. Being new to subjects such as Jazz Dance, and Modern Dance, Amaris needed to train in the evenings in her free time to achieve the levels of the other students, with which her new-found passion for electronic music helped. She then started the dance floor project <strong>“Geiko– female electronic dance music”</strong>, the first album of which was released in 2014. Although she had already released music earlier, this was her first official album. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"After returning to Zurich to complete a degree in Business Law and to work as a playlist manager for Sony Music, she later moved to London where she started working on her synth-pop-influenced album “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6oqL9pjcSxExcy4lTsd8EP?si=n8C8rWhASlKkopXrceXsBQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Neon Colours</strong></a>,” which was well-received by critics. In 2018, she released “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7MKZ7NwMoE2kAxrDCZfOka?si=-4M9O63mTsOqQ8Bw_gN3oA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aquamarine</strong></a>”, an album inspired by the oceans. In 2020, Amaris released “Dream World”, with the song “Dream World” receiving 100k streams on Spotify alone. In 2023, she co-produced the documentary <strong>“On Tape- Ask the Music Producers”</strong> together with L.A.-based director <strong>Maria Corso</strong>. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Amaris’ skills in combining genres such as electronica, R&amp;B, and pop have defined her music as being genre-defying.<em>&nbsp;“Creativity is my fuel,”</em> says Amaris, <em>“I can rely on it. I’d say that this is probably my actual skill.”</em>&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Amaris is very vocal about the protection of the oceans and is an ambassador for the non-profit organization <strong>Big Blue Ocean Clean-up</strong>, which works to reduce plastic waste in the oceans. Her fantasy story “Lagoona: A Journey through the Reef” raises awareness for the disappearing coral reefs and ocean pollution. &nbsp; &nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Ámaris!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/silvermaranth/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@silvermaranth","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/wFnz3eVhpVA?si=QqndzezCYEVddg8C","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@silvermaranth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/silvermaranth/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@silvermaranth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"268681","title":"Alt-Pop Artist Karisa Unveils New Song \"Hostage of Paradise\"","date":"2023-11-10","lead":"Exploring themes of mental health, Karisa's latest single balances melancholy and joy while delving into love and lust.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/268681/f29b7f752483429aa55107fa14d6cf7e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Exploring themes of mental health, Karisa's latest single balances melancholy and joy while delving into love and lust."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/52Rx3al646OlRbRM57Rri1?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Toronto, ON (November 10, 2023) - Chart-topping alternative artist <a href=\"https://www.karisamusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karisa</strong></a> just released her latest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/52Rx3al646OlRbRM57Rri1?si=50677171ed474db0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hostage of Paradise</strong></a>,” on November 10, 2023. A compelling blend of Pop, EDM, Alternative, Synth, and Dance-pop genres, the song promises to captivate audiences with its intricate narrative and unique sound.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"“Hostage of Paradise” delves into the complex theme of mental health, juxtaposing feelings of sadness and melancholy with moments of joy and beauty. With lyrics that explore the depths of love and lust, KARISA’s latest single plays with the contrast of words and descriptive visuals. It masterfully creates an image of beauty that is continually undermined by darkness.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The new track narrates the story of a tragic beauty, trapped in a place or state of mind that appears lavish yet harbors darkness. Despite the wonder in the physical world, the lyrics reveal an underlying sadness that challenges the exterior world's beauty and perfection. “Hostage of Paradise” serves as a musical depiction of being a hostage to one’s own mind, trapped in a place of darkness and sadness, even amidst the world's physical beauty."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/599900/large-e639b87053b03c5d2617097abd58bedb.jpeg","alt":"Cover Image for Hostage of Paradise"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Hostage of Paradise represents the internal struggle of melancholy; that despite beauty in the world, your state of mind is ultimately where your perception exists.”","cite":"- Karisa, Alternative Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"“Hostage of Paradise” draws its inspiration from the classic synth sounds of the 1980s and pairs them with percussion inspired by early 2000’s beats. This unique blend of soundscapes promises to transport listeners through a captivating musical journey."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/599902/large-9bd3bdab1ec40305d69fe58073050ccf.jpeg","alt":"image4.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/599902/preview-21bb42c2a0885d8e43c19f8e4fb5a36d.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/599901/large-ccb1126910ad3d62af182df39c6e266b.jpeg","alt":"image5.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/599901/preview-28ef5220c01a79b7ed1d2cd631f68e41.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/599903/large-ae68180ce19c10442baf19443ba14541.jpeg","alt":"image3.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/599903/preview-585b5286ebe7373d26820e201d7fe790.jpeg"}]},{"t":"quote","html":"My goal while writing this song was to capture the contradiction between depression and happiness, how both can exist and be at war in ​one's mind.”","cite":"- Karisa, Alternative Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"Co-produced by KARISA and sound engineer <strong>CL3VR</strong> (<strong>Lucas Vuco</strong>), “Hostage of Paradise” showcases the artists’ combined expertise, resulting in a track that promises to be a highlight in their respective careers."},{"t":"p","html":"<em><strong>As an added treat for fans, the official music video for “Hostage of Paradise” is set to debut in January 2024, providing a visual accompaniment that is sure to enhance the emotional depth of the song.</strong></em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0xiPUnPct1UgzYCIgLVYMV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Karisa:"},{"t":"p","html":"Toronto-based Alternative Pop Singer <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0xiPUnPct1UgzYCIgLVYMV?si=ExX_nic_RFGBjzF6Bwas-Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karisa&nbsp;</strong></a>has heavily relied on music and art throughout various stages of life. Karisa comes from an artistic family filled with creation and individuality. She recalls her love of music starting to bloom when she was a child sitting at the piano, recording herself singing. Karisa’s first live performance was at a dive bar in Toronto’s <strong>Kensington Market</strong>. This experience sparked Karisa’s urge to become an established singer-songwriter and share her music with the world. She prides herself on creating music that expresses the emotion behind various experiences in life - the good, the bad, the ugly, and all that falls in between. Karisa hopes to create songs that provide listeners with a slice of happiness or comfort when they need it the most. Her single <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5w5aH5ehURdjfup5oqHfro?si=edb12f7046d74792\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Next To You</a>”</strong> and latest release, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/52Rx3al646OlRbRM57Rri1?si=474cd90e01dd43f1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hostage of Paradise</strong></a>” just dropped on November 10, and is now available to stream on all platforms!"},{"t":"p","html":"Stay tuned for more announcements and updates from Karisa via her social media channels below!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Karisa!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/N7Q6qzVXo0s?si=ZmSpwF48Kqpw12WB","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/karisamusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@karisamusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://youtu.be/Naya3blJQ-E\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.karisamusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0xiPUnPct1UgzYCIgLVYMV?si=9Z6ixsxSR9ir5rJwL-eOWg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"270013","title":"ellakate is an alternative pop singer-songwriter making her debut Fall 2022. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way. To keep up with ellakate, check out her Instagram and stay tuned for new music coming soon.","date":"2023-11-10","lead":"The new single by ellakate and Whitney Bjerken delves into themes of friendship, overcoming bad exes, and embracing the spirit of badassery.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/270013/eaa873d19ac1a73ea12ac33b45cf1b30.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new single by ellakate and Whitney Bjerken delves into themes of friendship, overcoming bad exes, and embracing the spirit of badassery.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2UZ2QKAc8U0ipShyGllEPV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Atlanta, GA (November 10, 2023) - Today marks the release of “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/28nUJ0WKhOGlSjCdSucVuT?si=lWiCZm5eTgap3AwpXgLyJQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TAG TEAM</strong></a>,” a dynamic and sassy pop collaboration between rising pop sensation <a href=\"https://www.ellakate.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>ellakate</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>and the talented <strong>Whitney Bjerken</strong>. The song is a catchy, girl power anthem that delves into themes of friendship, overcoming bad exes, and embracing the spirit of badassery."},{"t":"p","html":"“TAG TEAM” is a testament to the power of female camaraderie and the strength that arises when two individuals come together against a common adversary. Written and sung by ellakate and Whitney Bjerken, the song narrates the story of two empowered women joining forces to confront an ex-lover who failed to treat them with the respect they deserve.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The chemistry between ellakate and Whitney shines through, creating a musical experience that is not only catchy but also emotionally charged.<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/vPkr-gnqzp4?si=gplqYQ8FbzhZTHYi","height":"315"},{"t":"quote","html":"“It was so fun writing and working together with Whitney on this song. We had actually never worked together before this and are now great friends because of it.”","cite":"- ellakate, Rising Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"The track boasts a catchy and sassy pop sound that is bound to resonate with audiences seeking a bold and empowering musical experience. “TAG TEAM” encapsulates the essence of friendship, resilience, and reclaiming one's power after a toxic relationship."},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong><u>\"TAG TEAM\" LYRICS TEASER</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"you really think ur the shit<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"You really think you got it"},{"t":"p","html":"but your a loser through and through<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"I bet that you didn’t expect this<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"both your exes would go make a fool outta you<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"betcha didn’t think we’d show up the tag team you never knew<br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/601260/compressed_original-a516a1e1a0d14eea0a84eb8964a93185.png","alt":"\"TAG TEAM\" Cover Art"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0t5IrUFo0RQnOfVkhZplHd?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About ellakate:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Ella Greenbaum</strong>, artistically known as ellakate, is an alternative pop singer-songwriter born, raised, and based in Atlanta, Georgia. Growing up with musical parents and a knack for creating and performing, ellakate found a passion for music that went beyond forcing her brothers to listen to her melodies as a child.&nbsp;<em>“When my dad first explained what the song ‘<strong>Brandy</strong>’ by <strong>Looking Glass</strong> was about, I discovered the magic of storytelling in songwriting. I have been singing and making up songs for as long as I can remember,”</em> said ellakate about her innate talents. She has written hundreds of songs since her childhood exploring topics that coincide with the journey of growing up and finding love, filling piles of notebooks in her room with song lyrics. ellakate’s songs recount stories and experiences that may have not happened to her but are inspired by events that have impacted her."},{"t":"p","html":"Her voice has been compared to a<strong>&nbsp;</strong>“young <strong>Amy Winehouse</strong>,” showing her vocal prowess - honest and sensual, with a hint of innocence. Her sultry vocals mixed with her haunting, bold, and romantic sound are reminiscent of artists like <strong>Billie Eilish</strong>, <strong>Tove Lo</strong> and <strong>Lana Del Rey</strong>. ellakate recently released her new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2UZ2QKAc8U0ipShyGllEPV?si=2f8221121e1f479b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TAG TEAM</strong></a>” and plans to release her debut EP in early 2024. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With ellakate!"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@ellakatemusic/video/7245424410902007083","handle":"@ellakatemusic"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/ellakatemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@ellakatemusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.ellakate.com/","img":"","title":"ellakate is an alternative pop singer-songwriter making her debut Fall 2022. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way. To keep up with ellakate, check out her Instagram and stay tuned for new music coming soon.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@ellakatemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ellakate9262\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.deezer.com/us/artist/185794237\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Deezer</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/ellakate/1648638724\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Apple Music</strong></a><br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"264322","title":"Antonio Lopez Drops Highly Anticipated Album: Here We Are","date":"2023-11-03","lead":"The Indie-Folk album officially launched,","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/264322/a5449c0ff3ac2574e3d3ac8d69fda492.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Indie-Folk album officially launched,&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7I8YZrbayJOoW09TsrlJX1?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Longmont, CO (November 3, 2023) - Esteemed Alternative-Folk artist <strong>Antonio Lopez</strong> released his new album <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7I8YZrbayJOoW09TsrlJX1?si=Ki8U2woITlOSeA22cih5Yg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Here We Are</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on Friday, November 3. This record offers listeners an outlet for emotional introspection through powerful messages related to mental health and human rights by a voice from the BIPOC community. Through the lens of his indigenous Chicano roots, Lopez speaks many truths with gentle precision. “Here We Are” is the long-awaited successor to his award-winning album <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/343IYPZ6Tq4yKsq18DrEvp?si=W6jKGaWFTsKSOyOWrsQMFw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Roots and Wings</strong></em></a>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3q1hLZjfSE9QS0u86fiD0l?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"“Here We Are” is an alluring collection of songs about the intimate connection between our hopes, dreams, and fears. The album is lyric-forward folk, with marimba swells and swooning Spanish guitar flourishes on top of a rock-solid rhythm section. Paired with Lopez’s emotive vocals, these vibrant instrumentals create a salt-of-the-earth soundscape for listeners to explore."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/HereWeAre","label":"Listen to \"Here We Are\" on ALL Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Just beyond our fears is where our dreams reside. They exist outside our comfort zone. I named this album “Here We Are” to remind myself that the best way to get there is by being present in the here and now.”","cite":"- Antonio Lopez, Indie-Folk Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"The album’s title, “Here We Are,” conveys a meaningful message. Lopez adeptly explores our human tendency to dwell in our thoughts, revisiting the past and envisioning the future. The album’s namesake serves as a gentle nudge to recognize that life unfolds in the present."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587941/large-e952e1c0a2cf672e29fa05c2cf49f8f5.png","alt":"Here We Are Album Cover Art by Lauren Wright"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Part of finding yourself is finding your people. Each of my bandmates brings something unique to the table. At our best, we transcend individual performance, building team confidence.”","cite":"- Antonio Lopez, Indie-Folk Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"“Here We Are” is a collaborative effort that showcases the creative contributions of Lopez’s bandmates: <strong>Chad E. Mathis</strong>, <strong>Jonathan Sadler</strong>, and <strong>Christopher Scott Wright</strong>. Together, this group of musicians have crafted an album that creates an outlet for self-discovery, engagement with the present, emotional expression, and more.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587942/-caa99d1b94961815c2f26ebfe0bd4566.jpeg","alt":"Antonio Lopez promo 6 credit Lauren Wright.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587942/preview-f6264e761e388516939743d5cfdae611.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587943/large-17406935545701909059e30274c8d53b.jpeg","alt":"Antonio Lopez live photo 2 credit Cassidy Wayant.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587943/preview-8fef5b27139bb113f48ac027fe0647a7.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587944/large-274491c1931dcc7bb8871ef882fe9326.jpg","alt":"Antonio Lopez headshot cropped credit Lauren Wright.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587944/preview-06b29ede204a9e7e436e929fbbcceead.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587945/large-a2e13f472496e4532d198d38a511ad67.jpg","alt":"Antonio Lopez Band 2023 2 credit Lauren Wright.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587945/preview-d932b9fee82ed24412fac7c211b3ca60.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587946/large-fbf2e251ec8ccd92181077e03587a3cf.jpg","alt":"Antonio Lopez Band promo photo 2023 credit Lauren Wright.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587946/preview-a61747a4d2fbeef3110e2b061d8ae18a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587947/large-15e0db09daee9fa9db59db22a9a047a5.png","alt":"Here We Are Album Cover.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587947/preview-0e48508c9651a4dfd9b36fa02da4e6f8.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Antonio Lopez:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Antonio Lopez</strong> is a quiet man with something to say. His music is like an onion, each layer revealing more. His adept guitar work and composition skills are never used in a showy way but rather like the spices in a home-cooked meal. The result is a feast of emotions that delight the listener.<br style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Birdseye, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\">“Here We Are,” the new album by Antonio Lopez, explores the intimate connection between our hopes, dreams, and fears. “Here We Are” is an alluring collection of songs written by an artist wrestling with his ego as he chases success and slow dances with failure. Through the lens of his indigenous Chicano roots, Lopez speaks many truths with gentle precision. Rather than tell the listener what to feel or think, Lopez invites you to see yourself reflected in the lyrical stories created by his music. <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7I8YZrbayJOoW09TsrlJX1?si=IhNaQ5B8QIuTdC8-nhPvKw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Here We Are</strong></a><strong>”</strong> officially released on November 3rd, and is now available for streaming on all major platforms and purchase on CD and vinyl through <a href=\"https://www.antoniolopezmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.antoniolopezmusic.com</a>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The album release show will also be hosted at <strong>Swallow Hill Music</strong> in Denver, CO on November 3rd (8 pm MST). Get your tickets <a href=\"https://swallowhillmusic.org/event/antonio-lopez-album-release-party/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Antonio!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/antonio_lopez_music/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@antonio_lopez_music","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/AntonioLopezMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/AntonioALopezMusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3q1hLZjfSE9QS0u86fiD0l?si=pTsy0rJdRUSaq7Ow3co8PQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.antoniolopezmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"264792","title":"The Erly Unveils Dynamic LP - Culture Fever - A Musical Journey Through Time and Emotion","date":"2023-11-03","lead":"The diverse 11-track record features tracks steeped in Jazz-Rock, Disco, Soul, and more.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/264792/498c16a224c96b8a4c4fdfd3d422ec79.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The diverse 11-track record features tracks steeped in Jazz-Rock, Disco, Soul, and more."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1acM3vo5SjE8CnOKhglgCf?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Niles, MI (November 3, 2023) - <a href=\"https://theerlyband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Erly</strong></a>, a four-piece ensemble hailing from Niles, Michigan, is proud to announce the release of their highly-anticipated LP titled: <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1acM3vo5SjE8CnOKhglgCf?si=YXRQL0MxRVSDynl75y1qBg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Culture Fever</strong></em></a>. This record is set to take listeners on a sonic rollercoaster through the realms of Jazz-Rock, Disco, Soul, Roots-Rock, and Adult/Contemporary genres. Female empowerment, mental health struggles, identity, and several other complex themes are woven into the lyrics and instrumentation on this record, creating an unparalleled depth to The Erly’s sonic profile.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"ABOUT THE LP: CULTURE FEVER"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Culture Fever</em> boasts a total of 11 captivating tracks featuring vocals from each member of the band - including <strong>Alyssa</strong> (keys), <strong>Collin</strong> (bass), <strong>Trevor</strong> (guitar), and <strong>Fran</strong> (drums). The LP was meticulously crafted in 2022 at Dr. Richard’s Audio in Valparaiso, Indiana. Under the guidance of producer <strong>Nick Rapley</strong> (known for his work with Bartees Strange and Lizzie No), The Erly expanded their sound beyond the confines of a typical four-piece band. The addition of horn and string arrangements, expertly arranged by <strong>Harris Karlin</strong> and&nbsp;<strong>Brian Moore,&nbsp;</strong>brought a rich and dynamic dimension to the LP. Notably, the band collaborated with horn and string players from eight different cities, ensuring that every instrument and sound on the album was produced by a human being."},{"t":"quote","html":"“We took our time to craft songs that will impact the listener sonically, as well as deliver an emotional punch lyrically.”","cite":"- The Erly, Michigan-Based Jazz Rock Group"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/W6E-VeiK1Y8?si=Q-BZHHVNT2KbfMlI","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"This LP is like a breath of fresh air, transporting listeners to the nostalgic aura of the 1970s. These songs represent the kind of music that makes you want to take the long way home on a warm summer night.<em>&nbsp;</em>Guitar-driven Jazz Rock tracks like <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3gzPTwdLU3HiP1HSWbMyJw?si=ccac370e86454037\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Flame the Main</strong></a><strong>”</strong> and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0yKYKEaulOAB1DFF6m3RQU?si=23e5085f30574ca6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Faces in the Attic</strong></a><strong>”</strong> were written to tackle unsettling feelings of resentment, addiction, and avoidance coping. <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4hXr94TEtokUsJ2ZbIbjHI?si=2e38c9bd4522488c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Take it As it Goes</strong></a><strong>”</strong> and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/00riPtflGG4LQiycmO8tjr?si=9c0459553d6b4d3c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tracing Circles</strong></a><strong>”</strong> reflect the sentiment of yearning for <em>something more</em> in everyday life. <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5DE395yF9XD0s1ys1UTzWb?si=72a42526c5f54b1f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Paralyzed</strong></a><strong>”</strong> and<strong>&nbsp;“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2fTsoqVLhFyOz7b6qRh2eK?si=e0a87c65d07740f4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Somewhere in My Mind</strong></a><strong>”</strong> bring culture and soul into this record, throwing it back to the iconic Disco era of the 1970s. Rounding out the LP with some down-to-earth melodies, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0TfNrrjHxpZi3tv4LiSQfJ?si=87764e08f5164b5d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Right Way</strong></a><strong>”&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6K9HUNXsv5G0CqvarFTJ2z?si=8354a0cb733447fb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Red Roof Inn</strong></a><strong>”</strong> tug at the heartstrings with smooth rhythms and harmonies.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"CULTURE FEVER - FUN FACTS"},{"t":"p","html":"1- The lead vocals for “Flame The Main” and “What To Do With You” were completed in one take each."},{"t":"p","html":"2- The Erly drew inspiration from at least 30 different artists across a wide range of genres."},{"t":"p","html":"3- “The Right Way” was spontaneously written in the recording studio during downtime."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0TfNrrjHxpZi3tv4LiSQfJ?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"4- Alcohol and other substances were consumed during the recording process to capture the desired character, both vocally and musically."},{"t":"p","html":"5- The original title for the song “Somewhere in My Mind” was “Culture Fever.” The band felt it was too good of a name for one song, so they made it the album title."},{"t":"p","html":"6- “Culture Fever” took the entire year of 2022 to record, with weekend recording sessions spread out over multiple months."},{"t":"p","html":"7- The album tracks were run through an analog tape machine before mastering, adding a warm and vintage touch to the sound."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3QPLdBDMCs5nyauZZMX7IW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591094/large-b732c11811bb6a74a8abb163a325e2b4.jpg","alt":"ERLY2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591094/preview-48f9a8df3ba0fba71b536956b08368f1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591096/-ea2453c793af5541e5f9baa65fb62a74.jpg","alt":"ERLY3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591096/preview-26882255e9911c05ba1f7e228a0335fd.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591095/large-701c911cedc0e85ff9a8781c856c799e.jpg","alt":"ERLY4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591095/preview-792147576cb32fd8abffc0240a69ebcb.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"PHOTO CREDIT: KELSIE HERZOG"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Erly:"},{"t":"p","html":"Michigan-based Indie-Soul group <strong>The Erly</strong> combines sonic elements from the ‘60s and ‘70s Rock, Pop, and Funk, creating a fresh<em>&nbsp;“Modern Disco”</em> sound and vibe of their own. Fueled by collaboration, friendship, and timeless good vibes, the quartet would fit right in at Woodstock ‘69 or at the indie nerve center that is <strong>SXSW</strong>. Most of <strong>The Erly</strong>’s music features clean guitar work, layered vocals, and groovy undertones that energize even their most solemn-sounding tracks. The band is composed of Drummer <strong>Fran Gleason</strong>, Bassist <strong>Collin Mattiford</strong>, Guitarist <strong>Trevor McDonald,</strong> and Keyboardist <strong>Alyssa Serviss</strong>, with all 4 members featured on vocals. <strong>The Erly</strong> was created in 2018 when Mattiford and Gleason decided to expand upon their pre-established musical duo. Since their formation in 2018, <strong>The Erly</strong> has released two full albums and four singles with more music on the way. <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0QzfIYmj30ksSmpWPrhxpm?si=80a4bb72f7aa48fc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Paralyzed</strong></a><strong>”</strong> dropped mid-August and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3aITimGk0InPUdYHaW49UZ?si=4d069fff904b4bea\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Flame The Main</strong></a><strong>”</strong> launched September 20th, both of which are now featured within The Erly’s newest record, <em><strong>Culture Fever -&nbsp;</strong></em>available on all streaming platforms on November 3rd, 2023.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"For all announcements and updates, stay connected with The Erly on social media!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Erly!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/theerlyband/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@theerlyband","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Ftheerlyband%2Fposts%2Fpfbid02SciuMhjycWBqZqAoLSFZ3nG9qKMnATQLzT7L5ngzJxSTyCZpwTsMRMGEjHub1zTml&show_text=true&width=500","height":"709"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/theerlyband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@TheErly\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"264999","title":"The Labra Brothers Drop Captivating LP: Home","date":"2023-11-03","lead":"Sibling band, The Labra Brothers, released their standout LP - a fusion of Latin and Americana sonic profiles.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/264999/87eebd7328eae2a3094765c5a2988b97.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Sibling band, The Labra Brothers, released their standout LP - a fusion of Latin and Americana sonic profiles."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/74TM8s9QLDWSGJI19fqogQ?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Youngstown, Ohio (November 3, 2023) - Latin sibling band, <a href=\"https://www.thelabrabrothers.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Labra Brothers</strong></a>, are thrilled to release their upcoming LP: <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/74TM8s9QLDWSGJI19fqogQ?si=i-Or7ivISkWPWkTGlLpb_Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Home</strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em>on Friday, November 3rd<em>.&nbsp;</em>This record promises a musical excursion that masterfully merges the two distinct genres of Latin and Americana, showcasing the brothers’ exceptional talents in creating soulful, heartfelt compositions."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>‘Home’</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>is a diverse compilation of musical styles, heavily influenced by Latin American genres like merengue, cumbia, and mariachi - all while retaining the Labra Brothers’ soulful Latin-Funk sound. The album features acoustic undertones and an upbeat percussion section, reinforcing the authenticity of the more traditional-leaning songs. The addition of accordion, trumpet, and violin adds a lively texture, complementing the honest and relatable songwriting and lyrics that solidify the album."},{"t":"quote","html":"“It was such a great experience putting this project together. We had an opportunity to work in multiple studios with great engineers, producers, and musicians. We're stoked for our listeners to hear these new songs, which we think are the most accurate representation of the Labra Brothers to date.”","cite":"- The Labra Brothers, Latin Sibling Band"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0WD7SIWiyR0lKrnPgVEdbk?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/74TM8s9QLDWSGJI19fqogQ?si=XiGoVGMzSYiKMdovm_pqRA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Home</strong></a><strong>’</strong> features a compelling mix of English and Spanish tracks, demonstrating the band’s connection to their Latin roots while appealing to a broader international audience. Tracks like <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0INvREltkXWMxbJHzRWij2?si=99b6decfde6e4986\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lonely</a>,”</strong> <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3OjoJhvXqUt304BEIQPo49?si=bb94e364364b4f3c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Los Días</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/14gPL282qUiLvYjzrrCtEg?si=8475ab42110147ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Not Far From Home</strong></a><strong>”</strong> explore themes of love, relationships, and the longing for home, resonating with listeners on a deeply emotional level. As a special addition to the album, the band has included two altered versions of previously released songs, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/323WnfkMkTyPtwtOglkasm?si=cde3f7c636a34832\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Not Far From Home</strong></a><strong>”</strong> (now offering a version en español), and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3ZMIVZJwSzUc7PM989zLgO?si=1488acae06a34ee7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Be Cool</strong></a><strong>”</strong> (live acoustic version). The mariachi-infused title track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0WD7SIWiyR0lKrnPgVEdbk?si=5ce38c7614f64f5d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Home</strong></a><strong>,”&nbsp;</strong>features powerful 4-part harmonies, now made possible by the band’s addition of the fifth Labra brother, <strong>Victor</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"With this LP, The Labra Brothers invite listeners to experience a musical work of art that spans the globe, stirs deep emotions, and immerses you in their distinctive musical world."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589669/compressed_original-b68673d24271d6b963f1acb7458f45a1.jpeg","alt":"Home (LP) Cover Art"},{"t":"h3","html":"LP Credits:"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Produced by: The Labra Brothers, Danny Svenson</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Recorded &amp; Mixed at: Bearcave Recording</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Additional recording with: Todd Maki&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Labra Brothers:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>The Labra Brothers</strong> are a Latin Funk sibling band from rustbelt Northeast Ohio. Influenced by the diverse music tastes of their parents, the brothers developed a distinguished sound that combines blues, funk, and Latin. After falling in love with playing their own renditions of their favorite music, the band decided to put their talents to work within their original creations. Consisting of <strong>Adrian Labra</strong> on vocals and guitar, <strong>Cristian Labra</strong> on vocals and bass, <strong>David Labra</strong> on vocals, guitar, and sax, <strong>Antonio Labra</strong> on percussion, <strong>Danny Svenson</strong> on keys, <strong>Victor Labra</strong> on vocals and percussion, and <strong>Matt Hayes</strong> on drums, the band quickly discovered their ability to effortlessly interlock in an instrumental groove with each other. The Labra Brothers continue to release music and have established themselves regionally as a dynamic and diverse powerhouse of musical presentation. With four-part sibling vocal harmonies at the forefront, their versatility has become more evident with each new original studio recording they release. The Brothers had an eventful 2022, during which they played a direct support role for <strong>Average White Band</strong>, and were voted “<strong>Best Latin</strong>” by the <strong>Cleveland Music Awards</strong>. This year (2023), The Labra Brothers opened for <strong>Los Lobos,&nbsp;</strong>and were awarded <strong>Editor’s Pick for “Best Latin Fusion Band” in</strong> <strong>Cleveland Magazine</strong>. Check out The Labra Brothers’ new LP, <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/74TM8s9QLDWSGJI19fqogQ?si=slsUv_uaTz2OftqYNc-Ydg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Home</strong></a><strong>.’&nbsp;</strong>Stay tuned for more from the brothers!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Labra Brothers!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2RxirsfpxfaajELy8K4z7B?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/labrabrosmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@labrabrosmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.thelabrabrothers.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheLabraBrothers/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"265005","title":"Alternative Hip-Hop Artist JIREH Drops 7-Track EP: B-SIDES","date":"2023-11-03","lead":"The Baton Rouge-based artist officially unveiled the new EP,","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/265005/69467c4be262226fabd465394bf6308d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Baton Rouge-based artist officially unveiled the new EP,&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3PB3VNX7NH5tmRzP7wuCHl?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Baton Rouge, LA (November 3, 2023) - Emerging artist <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/jirehpc/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>JIREH</strong></a> unveiled a brand new EP titled<strong>&nbsp;‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3PB3VNX7NH5tmRzP7wuCHl?si=KbAUVfqFQ2WFEQExu-9fHg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>B-SIDES</strong></a><strong>’</strong> on November 3, 2023. This release promises to deliver a unique blend of Southern charm and refreshing authenticity that showcases JIREH’s dedication to staying true to his own musical identity."},{"t":"p","html":"‘B-SIDES’ refuses to conform to expectations, promising an exciting and soulful experience that reflects JIREH’s individuality. With a commitment to crafting music that resonates with his personal style, Jireh aims to create an EP that captures his essence while providing an alternative to the algorithm-driven mainstream. In his own words, the artist expresses his vision for the upcoming EP:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7aEkh8osePkHEee0Xi947K?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I hope people have as much fun listening to B-SIDES as I did while I was creating it.”","cite":"- JIREH, Alternative HipHop Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"‘B-SIDES’ represents a fusion of Alternative Hip-Hop and Rap genres, embodying themes of self-assurance, self-reliance, and love boundaries. This EP serves as a testament to JIREH’s artistic evolution, as he continues to explore his unique sound and create music that speaks to his audience on a personal level. The artist’s dedication to his Southern roots shines throughout the tracks on this EP, infusing the music with a smooth, raw, and wise energy that makes it one-of-a-kind.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\"><br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589680/large-4c4a6661737694620ebd3742d5f97b42.jpg","alt":"IMG_7667 2.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589680/preview-6e08ba73b7d4f4a534b3fe0f617b026a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589681/large-f8e8a0020a58ecf06721a57c7941eca1.jpg","alt":"IMG_7668 2.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589681/preview-2ed554a6c11c9a85624777b86744593e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589682/large-fb1dcaccf9f70c95d807ebad25789881.jpg","alt":"IMG_7666 2.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589682/preview-0e9dea4d17903ad86c132364b719594b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589683/large-43ec03594d473bc746da249edf23efe5.jpg","alt":"IMG_0545.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589683/preview-227daef35a5a380ef439685b673fd82a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589684/large-3848a31cbcd236612b533751a80fa50a.jpg","alt":"IMG_0543.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589684/preview-9c01e1c9d1f38476b70dc49c32cc01ec.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589685/large-d425c400e474c0cb456bae5333b0f71e.jpg","alt":"IMG_0528.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/589685/preview-9ab6a3e26991cb14f2cb240b20bac6b6.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photo credit: Carlos Sanchez (forest photos); Dennis Ross (blue photos)"},{"t":"h3","html":"About JIREH:"},{"t":"p","html":"Combining his southern flare, mixed with unparalleled lyricism, Baton Rouge-bred <strong>JIREH</strong> is here to embed his name amongst those of the greats. His ability to captivate audiences and produce unique stories is bar none. He began rapping seriously in high school, where he would use equipment given to him by his father and brother, and since then, he has hit the ground running. Amassing a multitude of streams across all DSPs and consistently strengthening his pen, his dedication to his art is apparent and ever-growing. With the release of his EP<strong>&nbsp;‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0kuaFLF5BFVdgeCcPVdnJH?si=gQGectTJThi4wGTfzWCpFA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Quit Playing</strong></a><strong>’</strong> in the latter half of 2022, JIREH gained respect and attention from the Hip-Hop community, helping to further establish his image and career in the music industry. JIREH released his new EP,<strong>&nbsp;‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3PB3VNX7NH5tmRzP7wuCHl?si=_NpKVBOtTdO3ypcZSBvzyQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>B-SIDES</strong></a>,’&nbsp;</strong>on November 3rd, 2023, and is now available to stream on all major platforms."},{"t":"p","html":"For all updates and announcements, make sure to keep up with JIREH on his social media pages linked below!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Jireh!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/jirehpc/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@jirehpc","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/jirehpc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.threads.net/@jirehpc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">threads</a> |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/jireh.toussaint?mibextid=LQQJ4d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> </strong>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"264333","title":"Emily Nicole Green Drops Career-Defining Debut EP: 'Outrunning The Animal'","date":"2023-10-30","lead":"The 5-track EP provides listeners with a window into Green's soul, musical vision, and artist identity.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/264333/750c59cc36108ba64411c528dd137080.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The 5-track EP provides listeners with a window into Green's soul, musical vision, and artist identity."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/playlist/0s1SJC3ZJPQ1yv6u6zdEWv?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (October 30, 2023) - In the vibrant city of New York, <a href=\"https://www.emilynicolegreen.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Emily Nicole Green</strong></a>, an exceptional singer-songwriter, is boldly redefining herself at the age of 40, demonstrating that her boundless creativity knows no age limits. Emily released her debut 5-track EP, <strong><em>‘</em></strong><em><strong>Outrunning The Animal’</strong>&nbsp;</em>on her 40th birthday, October 30th. Emily stands as a beacon of light in the realm of independent artists. This record brims with raw emotion and boundless lyrical creativity, which Green has already begun to see resonate with listeners thanks to the powerful and positive reaction to the singles she has been releasing."},{"t":"p","html":"Emily Nicole Green introduces the world to her music through this highly-anticipated release, as she successfully weaves various captivating narratives through the soulful roots of her unique brand of storytelling. ‘Outrunning The Animal’ creates a musical labyrinth that melds the vibrant notes of pop, the rustic allure of country, the haunting cadence of blues, the sultry strains of jazz, and the timeless charm of folk."},{"t":"p","html":"Each track on this record is a testament to the multifaceted nature of Emily’s artistry, inviting listeners on a journey through the corridors of her heart and mind. Prepare to be swept away on a symphonic odyssey, where emotion flows like a river and melodies paint vivid landscapes of the human experience. Emily Nicole Green’s debut EP is not merely an album; it offers a window into her past, her present, and her aspirations for the future."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I hope these songs will offer the feeling that vulnerability is powerful and helps us connect with ourselves and each other. My goal for these songs is that they get to the hearts that need them.\"","cite":"- Emily Nicole Green, NYC-Based Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3Q95xairnETh0NeC4QK7Sp?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"In “<strong>Hole In My Heart</strong>,” the opening track of Emily Nicole Green’s EP, we’re transported to the core of country-influenced music. Green’s delivery transmits the emotions she is feeling to her listeners. Her vocals are effortlessly supported by distinctive guitar twang and emotive vocals that guide the listener through the sonic re-enactment of gut-wrenching heartbreak."},{"t":"p","html":"As the album unfolds, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3dSmlxpSvh7RKiq9vlIdZa?si=021c744e0cbb4c72\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wreckage</strong></a>” takes us on a different musical voyage, diving headfirst into the world of jazz. Dynamic vocals ebb and flow, from sultry and smoky to powerful and commanding, creating a sonic landscape that mirrors the chaos and emotional turmoil of love’s rejection. It’s a bluesy, jazz-infused exploration of anger and self-discovery, offering a safe harbor for those who have weathered the storm of heartbreak to express their pain and reclaim their self-worth."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1QdXz7KTAK8J65zORQLAig?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0uqAhnxsrCKRQN5btgVL8D?si=91992c463d534227\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Thief</strong></a>” is the third track on <em>‘Outrunning The Animal’</em> and it beckons us into the realm of Americana, where rich storytelling and timeless melodies intersect. Here, Green crafts a poignant narrative that intimately captures her ache, drawing on the roots of American folk music. This Americana ballad is the most raw and vulnerable song on the EP, reeling listeners into its deep emotional allure.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"“<strong>Courage</strong>” explores themes of self-discovery, transformation, and the impact of losing a significant person in one's life. The verses convey a sense of vulnerability and inner turmoil, suggesting a struggle with self-acceptance and change. The repeated chorus questions whether the narrator will find the courage to embrace the changes needed to become the person they lost had believed was inside of them. The bridges express gratitude for the support and love received, highlighting the importance of connections."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0ZDQSHmgfEciN3Qul6O5Wc?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Finally “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5QlHxADLZsI26wccH2egw2?si=d26bba3bd81f48b7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>It's Gonna Be Okay</strong></a>,” brings the album to a close with the warm embrace of soothing pop and Americana overtones, and Emily Nicole Green takes a bow to her three years of work in creating this record. It's a lullaby for all ages, a tender melody that reaches deep into the heart during moments of struggle, offering a glimmer of hope and resilience. The song's pop sensibilities provide a comforting familiarity, like a reassuring friend in times of distress. It's a reminder that even in the darkest of moments, there's a soothing melody to guide us through the storm. This track creates a fitting finale to a collection of songs that have explored various genres, each one a testament to the depth and breadth of human emotion.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587962/large-14830e29122879e49823ae114bd2f923.jpeg","alt":"'Outrunning The Animal' Cover Art (front)"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/588511/large-450d9c4c0f9b586db14215584b924cbe.png","alt":"'Outrunning The Animal' Cover Art (back)"},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Outrunning The Animal’ is an invitation to face ourselves. We are part animal and part human and the more we learn to be with the parts of ourselves that are unwieldy and untidy and very much alive, the more these parts can stop sabotaging us and fueling our addictions and anxieties in failed attempts to get our acknowledgment and validation. These emotional parts of us will eventually demand to be heard. We can’t outrun the animal because we are the animal. In spite of our best efforts, we can’t outrun ourselves. I hope these songs will be like close friends that you can call on when you want to feel some kind of catharsis or when you want to feel a little bit less alone.\"","cite":"- Emily Nicole Green, NYC-Based Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577852/large-13a9e03e27c35edcf2de0b83b664cd34.jpeg","alt":"EMILY2.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577852/preview-0556589028dfd82200d7053157acc3c7.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577853/large-510f403fcf2b3cd7646a155db114dde3.jpeg","alt":"EMILY5.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577853/preview-bf7f245b177afbacad805b7e0a1d1e33.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577854/large-7ac30d8fa16f2eea1c468c6dce3d5689.jpeg","alt":"EMILY4.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577854/preview-cdc0a478798d4b93e095bd6375812e83.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577855/large-dd3b6fbb0221174c89d8f61553b51015.jpeg","alt":"EMILY1.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577855/preview-c8d8161df898b2c18ee7888086105079.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577856/large-218db235c2b9275b4b396e7eaaa749c5.jpeg","alt":"EMILY3.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577856/preview-cbe29e298c74a55c0402f8d9b9cf2bf3.jpeg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>Photo Credit: Richard Corman</em>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Emily Nicole Green:"},{"t":"p","html":"NYC-based singer-songwriter, Emily Nicole Green shines a light into the depths of her own emotional interiority with her lyrics and her sound. Her vulnerable writing, powerful vocal, and skillful vibrato work together to offer listeners immediate emotional resonance and stirring storytelling that stays with them long after her songs end.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Green has been writing and performing her original songs since she was a freshman in high school. At 17, she began dealing with debilitating anxiety and panic that stopped her from pursuing a career in music for nearly two decades. In 2019, she decided it was now or never and began pouring herself into her music. She posted cover songs on Patreon and a year later landed her first TV spot with a cover of<strong>&nbsp;“Greasy Frybread”</strong> played over the credits of Season 1, Ep. 4 of FX’s<strong>&nbsp;Reservation Dogs</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Green’s songwriting is where she gives herself permission to tell herself her truth, processing her emotions and not judging what they have to say, letting the songs be told by the parts of her that still ache.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Emily Nicole Green’s debut 5-track EP, ‘Outrunning The Animal,’ fuses Americana with indie-folk, pop, jazz, blues, and country. The EP will officially launch on Green's 40th birthday, October 30th, and will be available for streaming on all platforms + will be available for purchase on vinyl.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"On what guides her writing, Emily says, <em>“At the altar of the ache, you’ll find the light below the wound.”</em>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Emily!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/oyF5Yo2q1O4?si=YB1U0mIgZxTGXQun","height":"435"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/emilynicolegreen/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@emilynicolegreen","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/EmilyColeGreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@emilycolegreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/EmilyNicoleGreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"264315","title":"View BRII_music’s Linktree. Listen to their music on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music here.","date":"2023-10-27","lead":"This new emotion-packed track officially launched ahead of Brii's second studio album.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/264315/584226900ecfd7c24cac7fe89515235e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This new emotion-packed track officially launched ahead of Brii's second studio album."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7L9owFsLpok0C5fOhGxXut?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, CA (October 27, 2023) - Rising R&amp;B Pop sensation <strong>Brii Elliss</strong> truly knows how to captivate listeners with her new single <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7L9owFsLpok0C5fOhGxXut?si=5ba3eb2f7f974a20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Perfect 4 Me</strong></a></strong><strong>,”&nbsp;</strong>which dropped on Friday, October 27.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>The artist’s second EP, <em><strong>All-In</strong></em> is set to release and will be available to stream on all major platforms on November 17th."},{"t":"p","html":"“Perfect 4 Me” beautifully captures the essence of the honeymoon stage in a relationship, where everything seems perfect and life appears brighter. Through emotion-packed lyrics, Brii explores the emotions behind her experience with all-consuming love."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Perfect 4 Me” captures the profound experience of falling deeply in love with someone for the first time. The lyrics behind this song represent my personal experience with young love, which I think listeners will resonate strongly with.”","cite":"- Brii Elliss, R&B Pop Artist"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>\"PERFECT 4 ME\" LYRICS</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>When the day is done</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Oh Baby</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>You're the one I want</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>So Crazy</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>There’s no if, and, buts or maybes</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>You’re my safety</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>You saved me yea </em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I know I’m done searching </em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Never been more certain </em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>You lift my every burden </em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Couldn’t be more perfect for me </em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"With an infectious melody and upbeat tempo, “Perfect 4 Me” makes listeners bop their heads to the beat. This track carefully fuses lighthearted instrumentals with genuine lyrics about newfound love. “Perfect 4 Me” is the perfect prelude to Brii’s upcoming EP - promising fans an unforgettable musical journey filled with love, passion, and authenticity."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/588788/large-e6c1805ba5d22e0ae61448aeacd67f99.jpg","alt":"\"Perfect 4 Me\" Cover Art by Devon Asher "},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5OVMuAGwhVrQZ8xG7bgVOs?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brii Elliss:"},{"t":"p","html":"Up-and-coming pop artist <a href=\"https://www.briielliss.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Brii Elliss</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>is a singer-songwriter who brings a certain closeness to her lyrics, giving testament to the power of storytelling in music. With an Irish father and Puerto Rican mother, her voice and life experiences create a unique blend that filters into her songs effortlessly, showcasing a sultry R&amp;B chill-pop soundscape that captivates and entrances listeners. Working with Grammy-winning producer <strong>Synematik&nbsp;</strong>to create her signature buttery sound, Brii pulls inspiration from artists like <strong>Amber Mark, H.E.R., Snoh Aalegra, Jhene Aiko</strong>, and <strong>Jazmine Sullivan</strong>, with a deeply rich tone that is quickly creating a buzz in the music community. A New Jersey native who has been singing since she can remember, Brii was on the path to stardom by the age of 12, having already auditioned for the famed X-Factor show and made it through several rounds. Throughout high school, she continued pursuing this passion by writing new songs and recording them, honing her piano skills, and preparing to move to LA where she attended college at <strong>Loyola Marymount University</strong> and graduated with her Bachelor's degree in music. As she began to record her own music she realized how much she needed music to be center stage in her life.&nbsp;<em>“I’m in my element when I am recording and surrounded by other creatives. It feels like home to me, and it’s still my happy place today.”&nbsp;</em>Needless to say, her happiness and passion in the studio shine through her work as her debut single garnered over 17K streams upon release while showcasing her authentic songwriting and silky low voice. Fans have already started rallying behind her and eagerly anticipate what's to come next for this budding artist. Lucky for them, Brii has lots of new music up her sleeve for 2023 and plans to share her soulful vibe with the world... one song at a time."},{"t":"p","html":"Brii Elliss will officially release her much-anticipated EP<strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong><strong>‘All In’</strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong>on Nov 17th , and just released a new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7L9owFsLpok0C5fOhGxXut?si=6d115a84a53d4d1f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Perfect 4 Me</strong></a>” on October 27th as a prelude to the EP. For all updates and announcements, make sure to keep up with Brii on her social media pages, linked below!"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Brii Elliss!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://linktr.ee/BRII_music","img":"","title":"View BRII_music’s Linktree. Listen to their music on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music here.","desc":""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/iGWGsuYX-EA?si=g2sJbcp3sQ_RoKTF","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/brii_elliss/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@brii_elliss","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.briielliss.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@brii_elliss\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@briielliss\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"263870","title":"Matthew Morgan Released A Powerful Alternative Folk Album: Timepiece","date":"2023-10-20","lead":"The Columbus-based Alternative artist officially launched his extraordinary 10-track record.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/263870/4c45a2e27f4024b30b2dfc27a48e3a90.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Columbus-based Alternative artist officially launched his extraordinary 10-track record."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5Jgv2h2lPqq3YdlVxQC9KY?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Columbus, OH (October 20, 2023) - Hailing from Columbus, Ohio, Folk artist <a href=\"https://www.matthewmorganmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Matthew Morgan</strong></a> is poised to make an indelible mark on the music scene with his highly anticipated follow-up album,<strong>&nbsp;<em>‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5Jgv2h2lPqq3YdlVxQC9KY?si=sHPzVDV0RWyoiAvWj5kQZg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Timepiece</a>.’</em>&nbsp;</strong>This extraordinary collection of songs showcases Morgan’s captivating storytelling prowess while addressing contemporary issues of social justice, LGBTQI+ diversity and acceptance, Black Lives Matter, equal rights, and the ongoing impact of the pandemic."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>‘Timepiece’</strong> defines Morgan’s modern indie-folk storytelling style. This ten-song album delves deep into the intricacies of the post-pandemic world, celebrating diversity and acceptance while shedding light on the struggles faced by marginalized communities. Through his easy-going and soulful style, Morgan weaves a narrative that resonates with listeners, offering both comfort and powerful messages of change."},{"t":"quote","html":"“We need other hearts to make us strong.”","cite":"- Matthew Morgan, Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"Musically ‘Timepiece’<em>&nbsp;</em>creates a collage of melancholy sentiments with an optimistic overtone. Morgan’s tenor voice is supported by acoustic richness and orchestral instrumentation - resulting in an intimate, captivating emotional journey."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/596624/large-912ac0d5919e8c83c102586be2cc265a.png","alt":"\"Timepiece\" abum cover art + photos by Rob Colgan (robcolganphotography.com)"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>‘Timepiece’</strong> is not just an album - it is a call to action, and an invitation to explore complex societal issues through the lens of heartfelt music. This record holds powerful messages and thought-provoking themes, leaving a unique impact on society as a whole.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Morgan ignites his passion for social justice through the music he creates. Each song is infused with earnest reflections on injustice and acceptance, resonating with listeners of all backgrounds. Morgan uses ‘Timepiece’ as a platform to voice a universal understanding of the struggle for equal rights and racial violence. Morgan shares his thoughts on the album's title track below:"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The song “Timepiece” is the true story of two boys who had their friendship cut short by parents who couldn’t accept their love for each other. Our world should celebrate love in all its many forms!”","cite":"- Matthew Morgan, Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587119/large-65f4d760255c9819317183234ca5446b.jpg","alt":"Timepice Promo 2 - Matthew Morgan - 2023.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587119/preview-d2045b3bf6e27c5e16e104d6aad9c2f4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587121/large-c9594b638f5fb9780dd410eaf78597da.jpg","alt":"mm6325-Matthew Morgan-Timepiece-publicity image 002.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587121/preview-5753dbe6f5d04c9f4e193ebafa5add73.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587123/large-4f1e476cf1706c7099e6c5db9c1f9686.jpg","alt":"mm6238-Matthew Morgan-Timepiece-pubilicity image 001.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587123/preview-0b5022c02a2d0c173d74f887376ffe57.jpg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>LYRICS FROM \"TIMEPIECE\"</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>But, oh the heart doesn't lie,</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>it just counts up the wishes in each person's mind.</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>It's a timepiece of spotless design,</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>but it's not always on time.</em><br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3L482PoQtRf3B6WHFesiIh?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Timepiece:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><em>‘</em></strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5Jgv2h2lPqq3YdlVxQC9KY?si=Yzfx6wscRDSdrUAp_Z3vyw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Timepiece</em></strong></a><strong><em>’</em></strong> was recorded over the span of three years with producer, <strong>Jay Alton</strong> (Columbus, OH) and features a host of top-tier instrumentalists including; <strong>Chris Shaw</strong> (violin, bass, and percussion), <strong>Chris Bosca</strong> (pedal steel and mandolin), along with <strong>Jill Crist</strong> (cello). The album was mixed by Alton and mastered by <strong>Brian Lucey </strong>at Magic Garden Mastering (<strong>Michael Buble</strong>, <strong>The Black Keys</strong>)."},{"t":"p","html":"‘Timepiece’ is a tour de force in heartfelt storytelling<br>that is unafraid to explore contemporary issues of social justice in a post-pandemic world, celebrating diversity and acceptance. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With the opening track <strong>​“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1GhS8ElsII4jJ1ayBuvVVO?si=38c4247a3b494115\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Isolation</strong></a><strong>”​</strong> Matthew reflects, <em>“I always thought I could face life's challenges alone, but then I discovered we need other hearts to make us strong” </em>expressing that being aware of vulnerability can make life richer. A signature of Matthew’s songwriting is being unafraid to explore social justice topics such as gender identity in the robust ballad,<strong>&nbsp;“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4u3Oy4T7XYCUwoz4AYW3cj?si=e253caa2a71a4e42\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sunny</strong></a><strong>”</strong> and a poignant statement that black lives still matter in <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6ZaZ4GjTqtBSqbYcxUZp1S?si=7e3b4901c7b84525\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Good Life</strong></a><strong>.”</strong>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1GhS8ElsII4jJ1ayBuvVVO?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"The album’s title track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3L482PoQtRf3B6WHFesiIh?si=4a9dc336e3a840ea\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Timepiece</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is a truthful narrative about same-sex love thwarted by parents’ rigid views. <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/58AsAnjFgSEc2hFfxwuVqZ?si=140ccf51a9e54656\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Victory Song</strong></a><strong>”</strong> gives listeners the courage to persevere and overcome life’s challenges. Overall, the tracks on ‘Timepiece’ stop the clock on a culture that has become unrecognizable and helps us to remember that we all have the opportunity to be the change we need in the world."},{"t":"p","html":"The music pulls you in from start to finish like having a conversation with an old friend and only after you’ve signed on do you realize the strength of the message."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Matthew Morgan:"},{"t":"p","html":"Matthew Morgan is on a mission to prove to the world that alternative folk can be embraced by the LBTQIA+ community, that a singer-songwriter from the heartland can compose words expressing anti-racist sentiment, and that a great-sounding country song can carry a deeper message without relying on overused and outdated tropes! Refusing to be labeled, or pigeonholed into genderized, racialized, or any other “-ized” stereotypes he joins the ranks of similar progressive singer-songwriters such as <strong>Orville Peck</strong>, <strong>Crys Matthews</strong>, and <strong>Willy Carlisle</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Matthew released his debut CD with Chicago’s acoustic indie label, CAUDog Records in 2012 immediately going on tour around the Midwest and Southern US states in cohort with his band, <strong>The Lost Brigade</strong>. The touring resulted in sold-out shows headlining at Chicago’s famous Double Door nightclub and House of Blues and opportunities to share the stage with more notorious acts at music festivals including opening for <strong>Dave Davies</strong> (The Kinks) and <strong>Company of Thieves</strong> at Taste of Lincoln Ave (Chicago) and <strong>SXSW </strong>(Austin) in 2013."},{"t":"p","html":"Seeking a more introspective sound to his song craft Morgan parted ways with The Lost Brigade in 2014 and recorded a new solo EP that was released independently the following year. While The Lost Brigade’s sound was indebted to contemporary indie rockers like <strong>Wilco&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>The Decemberists</strong>, the <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/44glNFQhBi6FiBJ6t1FjbQ?si=Yus5xNaiSgios8jGUOvzbw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Empathy for Inanimate Objects</strong></a><strong>’</strong> EP calls to mind the happier moments of <strong>Elliott Smith</strong> or the open-ended ponderings of <strong>Tom Brousseau</strong>. Empathy as a whole was very well received and Morgan garnered his first published reviews and the inclusion in the “Best of 2015” by the Nashville Music Guide. A new “Family” band was formed and the empathy tour resulted in venues of greater status including an opening slot or <strong>Ben Ottewell</strong> (of Gomez) and a chance to debut at Chicago’s premiere music club, The Metro.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5Jgv2h2lPqq3YdlVxQC9KY?si=M-2OvqfgSeyR_4sPxJ4Uww\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Timepiece</strong></a><strong>’</strong> marks Morgan’s first full release since 2015 - showcasing his maturity as a songwriter and storyteller, now available for streaming on all platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Matthew!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/yDcnbu18B6Y?si=jYuj1tYD8PlInbif","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/mattmorganmus/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@mattmorganmus","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://matthewmorganmusic.com/bio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>WEBSITE</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/mattmorgansmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong> </a>|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/matthewmorganmusic1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YOUTUBE</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"264308","title":"Horseshoes Unveiled Captivating New Album \"Black Snow\" - A Journey of Authenticity, Honesty, and Uncertainty","date":"2023-10-20","lead":"'Black Snow' officially dropped for streaming on all major platforms.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/264308/b66b52bf2282f33aadd8d763aede3194.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"'Black Snow' officially dropped for streaming on all major platforms."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6KcYGezN46DvPmgqG5GhQi?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Washington, DC (October 20, 2023) - Indie-Rock artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0cIVB4MH1nJhx5soIMZeKt?si=0RHAiQQVTNuyK96Ks7il5Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Horseshoes</strong></a> released his highly-anticipated album<strong> </strong><em><strong>‘</strong></em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6KcYGezN46DvPmgqG5GhQi?si=xEm5N9nwSY-ql_mKAT1vow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Black Snow</strong></em></a><em><strong>’</strong>&nbsp;</em>on Friday, October 20th. The 10-track record delves deep into the themes of authenticity, honesty, and the challenge of remaining true to oneself amidst life's uncertainties."},{"t":"p","html":"‘Black Snow’ is a compelling exploration of the internal struggle that many of us face - the battle between staying authentic to our true selves and succumbing to the pressure of conforming to societal expectations. Horseshoes take listeners on a thought-provoking journey, inviting them to question their own authenticity and self-awareness."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/591081/large-e4f74675f1740b2117c45c770b60a80e.jpg","alt":"1695749907.jpg"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This album explores my confusion and journey to try and see things more clearly.”","cite":"- Horseshoes, Indie-Rock Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"One significant influence on the creation of ‘Black Snow’ was the birth of Horseshoes’ daughter. This life-changing event inspired him to strive for a truer and more pure perspective, resulting in a more playful and open musical approach. The album encapsulates the artist’s willingness to step out of his comfort zone and experiment with new sounds and melodies. The instrumentation behind the tracks effortlessly blends various Indie-Rock and Americana influences, drawing inspiration from artists like <strong>Elliott Smith</strong>, <strong>Alex G</strong>, <strong>Sufjan Stevens</strong>, and <strong>Wilco</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0IbusYAp0hPJJRvBSSBGXU?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/BlackSnow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Black Snow</strong></a><strong>’</strong> is set to be a powerful addition to Horseshoes’ discography, promising to resonate with fans of Indie-Rock, Indie-Pop, and Americana music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/BlackSnow","label":"Listen to 'Black Snow' on ALL Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"lead","html":"BLACK SNOW - TRACK SEQUENCE"},{"t":"p","html":"Track 01 - LA"},{"t":"p","html":"Track 02 - Say What You Mean"},{"t":"p","html":"Track 03 - Too Scared"},{"t":"p","html":"Track 04 - Hide And Seek"},{"t":"p","html":"Track 05 - Dreaming"},{"t":"p","html":"Track 06 - Black Snow"},{"t":"p","html":"Track 07 - The Sacrifice"},{"t":"p","html":"Track 08 - Seagulls"},{"t":"p","html":"Track 09 - Dezso"},{"t":"p","html":"Track 10 - Santa Cruz"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Horseshoes:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Austin Greaves&nbsp;</strong>is a Washington DC-based musician who performs under the name <strong>Horseshoes</strong>. He released his debut album, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4X4f7fYdW98GedO8tKDh0T?si=Up5VrHYbT2GqWrpxmlxw2w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Desert</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> in June of 2022, which was followed up with a single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4x86xnafoYR0SDd6RvYQbz?si=wNflVB0YS2O8CfEQE-T8Pw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Come With Me</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> released in October 2022. You can stream Horseshoes’ recently released singles <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/29zUzEi2MIZA5NhbWUaREp?si=41ded00bd6434e5c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hide and Seek</strong></a>,”&nbsp;</strong><strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3NCMYYe6cYK4pVQzEbs9lV?si=TCj02gYjSYSQyTXNK3aaPw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Say What You Mean</strong></a><strong>,” &nbsp;</strong>and<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4NGxseYp3FrD82SULfj0jI?si=ce35d7b0b0aa468c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“L.A.”</strong></a> on all major platforms, as well as the standout album <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/BlackSnow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Black Snow</strong></a><strong>’&nbsp;</strong>which<strong>&nbsp;</strong>officially launched on Friday, October 20.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"To stay updated on all announcements and updates, follow Horseshoes on his social media channels linked below!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Horseshoes!"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@horseshoesguy/video/7258329364922649902","handle":"@horseshoesguy"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/CyoZq07ptb9/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@horseshoesguy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/horseshoesguy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"265268","title":"Read More","date":"2023-10-20","lead":"The new record released features 10 emotionally charged songs that touch upon themes of family, love, and self-discovery.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/265268/84c8f2ead2afb97dd242fef819c22d86.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new record released features 10 emotionally charged songs that touch upon themes of family, love, and self-discovery."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3bQSWj2L69FZmAGzZIHmHg?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston, TX (October 20, 2023) - Houston-based Alt-Pop artist <a href=\"https://www.timqualls.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tim Qualls</strong></a> is making waves in the music industry with his newly released album <strong><em>‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3bQSWj2L69FZmAGzZIHmHg?si=zeJHkQUZSL2Hd4-EW-qkng\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Feel</strong></a>.’</em></strong> This record, featuring ten compelling tracks, is a testament to Qualls’ distinctive musical approach and creative vision. Notable among these tracks are <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/76lzx2LKGitSG7ZbveV54T?si=7afec6abd51d404c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>History</strong></a><strong>”</strong> and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4FWCm2bCvqd6W9newzslQ7?si=9127b448bc4e4686\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Grave</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> each delivering a distinct emotional and sonic experience."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I hope this piece of art can reset the bar for me musically and really set a new tone for my listeners.”","cite":"- Tim Qualls, Alt-Pop Singer"},{"t":"p","html":"Qualls is renowned for his rootsy, soulful, and ornate music style, characterized by its emotional and embellished elements. The inception of his latest album was sparked by the creation of the song <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2jyUFjMhhYk9a0nOMTk9G6?si=297ed3c5cca342a3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stay</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> a pivotal moment in his musical journey."},{"t":"p","html":"Once the artist was able to gain full control over his music, he was able to dedicate himself to crafting a unified piece of art that demonstrated his range as a musician. ‘Feel’ signifies the culmination of a 15-year journey, with the songs eloquently recounting his life experiences and emotions. Tim Qualls takes immense pride in this collection of songs, aspiring to establish a new standard for himself as an artist and songwriter."},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>​ALBUM DISCOGRAPHY </strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>STAY</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"“STAY” is an uplifting and bittersweet love song that evokes deep emotions. The lyrics express a yearning for someone to remain by your side, and the song is driven by the gentle melody of the piano and resonant electric guitar, creating a moving musical landscape."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2jyUFjMhhYk9a0nOMTk9G6?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>FEEL</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"As the title track of the album, “FEEL” is a somber reflection on the uncertainties of one's emotions when faced with a profound connection. It serves as an ode to a loved one, with stripped-down vocals and instrumentals that lay bare the depth of feeling."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>FAMILY TIES</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"An epic piano arrangement defines “FAMILY TIES,” a heartfelt tribute to the importance of family and the longing felt when separated from loved ones. This song is a musical expression of gratitude and relaxation, highlighting the significance of familial bonds."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/78KYV6YsqUK808liAbcPM2?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>I SWEAR TO GOD I TRIED</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"“I SWEAR TO GOD I TRIED” is an emotional ballad infused with cello elements. It delves into the complexities of love, including the conflicts and moments of doubt. The song explores the desire to persevere in a relationship despite the challenges and concludes on a hopeful note, building up to a positive resolution with emotional string elements."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>HISTORY</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"“HISTORY” is a synth ballad that beautifully celebrates the enduring strength of long-term love. It reflects on how adversity can fortify love and relationships, showcasing the idea that love can conquer all. The song's unique blend of piano ballad tenderness and pop energy, complemented by evocative lyrics and layered instrumentals, inspires listeners to take on the world."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/76lzx2LKGitSG7ZbveV54T?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>THIS WORLD</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"“THIS WORLD” offers an upbeat and dynamic sound with prominent synth elements and percussion driving the rhythm. Dark overtones set the mood, and the track features layered vocals and echoing effects, creating a dynamically engaging musical experience."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>SAFE</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"A jazzy tune, “SAFE” exudes a sultry and romantic atmosphere, with smooth guitar melodies and a powerful bass line. The song is a love-filled composition that enchants the listener."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>MINE</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"In “MINE,” the listener embarks on a dystopian journey, on the verge of a new awakening within a relationship. The chorus adds depth to Tim’s strikingly powerful vocals, creating a captivating and thought-provoking soundscape."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>FOREVER</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"This heartfelt journey through life’s ups and downs is about finding something that guides you, whether it’s a person, passion, or purpose. Qualls’ soulful vocals capture the desire to hold onto moments of happiness and clarity, creating a nostalgic and introspective vibe."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584199/large-c8d2759e6e754385b924249350dbf53a.jpg","alt":"IMG_8117.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584199/preview-7abe55022dfe2bff893f5ef871a00b1e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584200/large-4e313ef0412a6bfa8b07e91e0efb47c0.jpg","alt":"IMG_8113.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584200/preview-5ef1f688ed5aae107033aa8d4831cb66.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590085/-aa85318b4efe2f99d31493cb488c0143.jpg","alt":"TIM2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590085/preview-0c5561a0d7bde7f458d1460acdef7be9.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590086/-2dbdff536fea382a6dffef4250c89c6e.jpg","alt":"TIM3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590086/preview-3726786253152efe265eaebd95e898e7.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photos by Houston-Based Photographer Kirby Betancourt<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Tim Qualls:"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston-based songwriter <strong>Tim Qualls</strong> delivers rootsy soul music that is grounded in family, heartache, and a positive outlook on life very few write about. Influenced by legends like <strong>Ray Charles</strong>, <strong>Jamie Cullum</strong>, and <strong>John Mayer</strong>, musicians compare him to a <em>“soul artist that croons on the piano.”</em> His productions have been compared to <strong>Adele</strong>, <strong>Sam Smith</strong>, and <strong>Ryan Tedder</strong>. Once awarded <strong>Houston Press</strong>’ “Best New Act” award, Qualls continues to deliver new music every year. Tim has been featured on Spotify playlists such as <strong>LIFE SUCKS</strong>, <strong>DINNER MUSIC</strong>, <strong>SOULFUL BLEND</strong>, and <strong>COZY BLEND</strong>. Qualls’ recently-released singles <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2oheHd1XwCuN3cFzZV7Tid?si=4da46a8a26214bd1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Forever</strong></a><strong>,”&nbsp;</strong><strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0MA3vYM4gsD64hQXDZWUD8?si=5cebb944d65d42e3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Grave</strong></a>,<strong>”</strong> and “<strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/29f4uKrB8LFCT29EvNcidJ?si=aa25a248837e4969\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>History</strong></a>”</strong> are featured on his new album ‘Feel’<strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong>- now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Tim!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/timquallsmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@timquallsmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.timqualls.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIM QUALLS OFFICIAL WEBSITE</strong></a>"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.timqualls.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/timquallsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><strong><a href=\"https://www.twitter.com/timothyqualls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TWITTER</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/timquallsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"266428","title":"Jazz- Rock Band The Erly Launches New Music Video for \"Flame The Main\"","date":"2023-10-19","lead":"The recently released music video gives listeners a taste of the gritty, sultry sound of their upcoming EP: Culture Fever","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/266428/f2828a26ac593b728f14fe203b0d8a2f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The recently released music video gives listeners a taste of the gritty, sultry sound of their upcoming EP: Culture Fever"},{"t":"p","html":"Niles, MI (October 13, 2023) - Michigan-based indie band,<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://theerlyband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Erly</strong></a>, unveiled their latest musical creation, \"<strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3aITimGk0InPUdYHaW49UZ?si=977a83a3142c4644\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Flame The Main</a>”</strong> on September 20th. This infectious track is the fourth single to be released from The Erly's highly anticipated upcoming album, \"Culture Fever,\" set to hit the shelves on November 3, 2023. As a tantalizing teaser for what's to come, fans can look forward to an accompanying music video for \"Flame The Main,\" slated for release in the upcoming months. With this exciting new release, The Erly is poised to set the stage on fire with their unique blend of disco-infused sounds and visually captivating storytelling."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/W6E-VeiK1Y8?si=Q-BZHHVNT2KbfMlI","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"The music reverberates like a vintage Cadillac rumbling through the deserted streets of Main Street at 4 a.m., capturing the essence of a bygone era. The sonic landscape mirrors the atmosphere of a riverboat casino, and the lyrics echo the voices of enigmatic characters entangled in their dubious ambitions and vices. \"Flame The Main\" is a vivid narrative crafted by the band, delving into the turbulent life of someone thrust into a world of chaos, leading to a cascade of self-destructive behaviors. Themes of evasion, substance abuse, the relentless pursuit of intangible dreams, and a pervasive sense of insecurity all find their place in this riveting new rock track.<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3QPLdBDMCs5nyauZZMX7IW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580111/large-1391af554d2814f05cf459bfdea1e33d.jpg","alt":"FLAM1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580111/preview-c6e2e995ba84440d6a89c3bfed11e0b6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580113/original-058c0adcd67897cc6c1a6290713c257f.jpg","alt":"FLAME2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580113/preview-cf6d31436c834a337913d04e33057385.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580114/large-34a5c54b2165cbe1c275ac368565ef24.jpg","alt":"FLAME4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580114/preview-d9795994509c0bd4012272fcfacd9c40.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580112/large-f07f1c63c3a96d78af130655759085a6.jpg","alt":"FLAME3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580112/preview-590f7669822045afa671103be5a5505a.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"PHOTO CREDIT: KELSIE HERZOG"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Erly:"},{"t":"p","html":"Michigan-based Indie-Soul group <strong>The Erly</strong> combines sonic elements from the ‘60s and ‘70s Rock, Pop, and Funk, creating a fresh<em>&nbsp;“Modern Disco”</em> sound and vibe of their own. Fueled by collaboration, friendship, and timeless good vibes, the quartet would fit right in at Woodstock ‘69 or at the indie nerve center that is <strong>SXSW</strong>. Most of <strong>The Erly</strong>’s music features clean guitar work, layered vocals, and groovy undertones that energize even their most solemn-sounding tracks. The band is composed of Drummer <strong>Fran Gleason</strong>, Bassist <strong>Collin Mattiford</strong>, Guitarist <strong>Trevor McDonald,</strong> and Keyboardist <strong>Alyssa Serviss</strong>, with all 4 members featured on vocals. <strong>The Erly</strong> was created in 2018 when Mattiford and Gleason decided to expand upon their pre-established musical duo. Since their formation in 2018, <strong>The Erly</strong> has released two full albums and four singles with more music on the way. <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0QzfIYmj30ksSmpWPrhxpm?si=80a4bb72f7aa48fc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Paralyzed</strong></a><strong>”</strong> dropped mid-August and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3aITimGk0InPUdYHaW49UZ?si=4d069fff904b4bea\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Flame The Main</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is slated to launch on September 20th, both of which will be featured within The Erly’s upcoming record, <em><strong>Culture Fever -&nbsp;</strong></em>available on November 3rd, 2023."},{"t":"p","html":"For all announcements and updates, stay connected with The Erly on social media!<br>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/theerlyband/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@theerlyband","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/theerlyband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@TheErly\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"262758","title":"Country Singer Kim Brogli Dropped Soul-Stirring Single \"What a Waste\"","date":"2023-10-13","lead":"The highly-anticipated track launched its official music video, sending a vital message.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/262758/36f3f7d69f583de7d80bfdaca6812e75.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The highly-anticipated track launched its official music video, sending a vital message."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4G2gqSoKF0HPBBbaOfLB7R?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"College Grove, TN (October 13, 2023) - Country Singer-Songwriter <a href=\"https://www.kimbrogli.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Kim Brogli</strong></a> released her new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4G2gqSoKF0HPBBbaOfLB7R?si=cc1286d9061842af\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>What A Waste</strong></a>” on Friday, October 13th. The new song communicates various sentiments about addiction and sends a powerful message about its’ all-consuming destructive force. Furthermore, the official music video for “What A Waste” just launched on Kim’s <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@kimbrogli7621\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube channel</strong></a>."},{"t":"p","html":"Co-written with award-winning songwriter&nbsp;<strong>James Dean Hicks</strong>, Brogli’s lyrics call for a re-evaluation of damaging patterns that ultimately end up hurting not only ourselves but also the ones that we love. With addiction and mental health-related issues on the rise since the Covid-19 pandemic, Brogli uses the song to prompt those who need support to seek out help."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/lnWmEFciYFc?si=tswELnZsNEzTEnxY","height":"439"},{"t":"button","href":"https://vyd.co/Whatawaste","label":"Listen to \"What A Waste\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/585221/large-40639f383f9edb1508e0f712babedbff.png","alt":"KIM.png"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>“What A Waste” Lyrics</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>You can’t feel love if you don’t love yourself</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Or keep blaming all your pain on someone else</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I pray that you’ll wake up</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>And see the choice is clear</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Cause if you wake up one day and no one’s here</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>What a waste</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>What a waste</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>The time that you’ve lost can’t be replaced</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>If you let all your tomorrows</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Turn into days of sorrow</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>And the tears of regret roll down your face</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>What a waste</em><br>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“When we wrote this song, both James (Dean Hicks) and I were discussing the hurt, scars, and pain associated with addiction. “What A Waste” is a reminder that it’s never too late to ask for help, no matter what circumstance you are in.”","cite":"- Kim Brogli, Country Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“What A Waste” is the second single from Brogli’s upcoming debut EP <strong>The Fight</strong>, set to launch later this season.&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/524zMfMtxBzJmyaXk4zfK5?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Kim Brogli:"},{"t":"p","html":"An out-of-the-box creative coupled with a fierce drive, work ethic, and unique ability to pull at your heart, Nashville-based singer-songwriter&nbsp;<strong>Kim Brogli</strong> is making her mark among Nashville songwriters. The Middle Tennessee native was always a writer and storyteller at heart. She recalls with laughter being the ADHD kid who was constantly in trouble at school, making the other kids laugh with her outrageous humor and telling stories that kept kids laughing or in suspense til the end. In the fourth grade, Kim tried out for the school choir and didn’t make it. <em>“I was a sensitive kid and have always been harder on myself than anyone else could ever be. So when I didn’t make the choir, I never sang again publicly. I just thought...I must be a terrible singer. It never dawned on me I was nervous and shy.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"She went on to graduate from The University of Alabama with a degree in French and International Business. &nbsp;After a successful career selling real estate, she bought guitars for her twin boys and ended up playing them herself. &nbsp;After getting her own guitar for Christmas that year, she began taking voice lessons, and that led to putting her words on paper into song. After recording a few singles with her then-vocal coach <strong>Kristen Smith</strong>, acclaimed producer, <strong>Will Gawley</strong>, found Kim on Instagram and said her soulful voice was reflective of those ‘70s songwriters. She has often been compared to <strong>Emmylou Harris</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;Alison Krauss</strong>, <strong>Lori McKenna,</strong> and <strong>Sarah Jarosz</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"They decided to record her debut EP, which includes four original songs she wrote or co-wrote with hit songwriter, James Dean Hicks. &nbsp;In it, she touches on subjects like faith, love, life lessons, self-doubt, parenting, and many other feelings she has processed on paper. &nbsp;She is slowly finding an audience in the Americana market. Her songs have the ability to bring tears and make you reflect upon the deeper meaning of life in a sweet, understated way. &nbsp;She performs mostly around Nashville at this time."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Kim!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/8mm1_Eddp4k?si=lHRmmldoRz2yqVT6","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/kimbroglimusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@kimbroglimusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/kimbroglimusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/kimbroglartist\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TWITTER</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@kimbrogli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"263937","title":"Read More","date":"2023-10-13","lead":"The Alt-Pop artist drops her 4-track EP, a bubbly wonderland exploring notions of various subjects.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/263937/52e38e16ce62910515a729cc851e3d89.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Alt-Pop artist drops her 4-track EP, a bubbly wonderland exploring notions of various subjects."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7MugEUIkFHUqt4q5FWNyUQ?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"New Orleans, LA (October 13, 2023) - Rising Alternative Pop artist, <a href=\"https://www.sarijordan.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sari Jordan</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>launches her highly-anticipated EP<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7MugEUIkFHUqt4q5FWNyUQ?si=kK__D60SQ722GyACHvIh7A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘Sing to the Moon’ </strong></a>on Friday, October 13th. The light and uplifting 4-track collection is a bubbly wonderland that explores notions of self-discovery, healing, unrequited love, introspection, and closure. Jordan gifts listeners with a well-crafted collection of songs and stories that reach the soul."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><em>*‘Sing to the Moon’</em></strong><strong><em>&nbsp;</em>Release Show: October 12 @&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://chickiewahwah.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Chickie Wah Wah</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;in New Orleans, LA*</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Compiled of songs that were written between 2021 and 2022,<em>&nbsp;‘Sing to the Moon’</em> is the byproduct of Sari Jordan’s journey - a delicate balancing act between schooling, working, and pursuing musical aspirations. This album plunges into the complexities of human emotions, signifying a significant chapter in Jordan’s growth and evolution as an artist."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Making this record showed me how important it is to get to know yourself. I hope these songs create an immersive haven for people to be comfortable with spending time alone.”","cite":"- Sari Jordan, Alt-Pop Singer"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>‘Sing to the Moon’</em> appeals to a musical palate that is vulnerable, light-hearted, honest, and soulful. Jordan’s Norah Jones-esque vocals are seamlessly complemented by a modern take on jazz-pop instrumentals that run throughout this record. Jordan’s “learning-through-doing” approach to artistry not only applies to her recording process for this album but also shines through in lyrical themes. Jordan sings about cycles of conflict, healing, and closure - all intertwined in a reflection of the past. The Alt-Pop singer hopes listeners can resonate with the feelings related to growing pains and being scared to flourish. Jordan shines through as a standout up-and-coming artist both artistically and spiritually with the picture she has painted in this release.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Each track on the album encapsulates a distinct emotion and storytelling style, making it a captivating journey from start to finish. Jordan’s experience as a live performer in New Orleans shines through with dynamic live band arrangements and the gentle yet commanding presence she forges.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/590665/large-6c33c0f9712f3dc0a901ead3bb170561.png","alt":"Sing to the Moon Album Cover: Photos by Noe Cugny"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>ABOUT THE ALBUM:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Track 01</em> - “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/438xgmYNCE9zJe4jEFfFjw?si=72b6f8579c0b4f55\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Daydreams</strong></a>” - A dreamy, wistful, defensive lament inspired by bedroom jazz and Broadway. Yearning, with an emotive melody. Inspired by a stubborn crush. Influenced by <strong>Eloise, Bruno Major, Billie Eilish</strong>, and <strong>Broadway</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Track 02</em> - “<strong>Ceasefire!</strong>” - Modern and eclectic. Comforting and expansive. A song that is, at its climax, dark and tense, but cathartic in its resolve and release. Ethereal background vocals bring the song back down to an earthier place once it lifts off. Sounds inspired by psychedelic rock, neo-soul, and Broadway. It has a distinct and dynamic live band sound and arrangement.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4Zb009ub8GBMreqyEGsf2A?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Track 03</em> - “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4dqEEfmt0DjKzFBKGDh00e?si=b788fd93887e4a56\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sing To The Moon</strong></a>” - A spirited, sentimental love letter is sent to New Orleans within the lyrics, arrangement, and instrumentation of this track. Inspired by traditional (“trad”) jazz styles.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Track 04</em> - “<strong>Deep End</strong>” - A vocal-heavy, sad-girl Americana take on a 2023 synth ballad. Sounds like a breakup cry. Even though electronic elements are at the forefront of this song, this is one of the earthier tracks on the record. Inspired by <strong>Maggie Rogers, Phoebe Bridgers, Becca Stevens, </strong>and <strong>Andrew Bird</strong>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1iCtQJJ0qzCnweWalJLtQW?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587154/-af41292ef49a6da805bf45c988d2920a.jpg","alt":"MOON5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587154/preview-558922c22dcb5cf7c13b1a4a4519f57a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587155/-e118000b06c2b84e5697476108e57dd1.jpg","alt":"MOON3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587155/preview-4b1430ba40110cc9f4e613412b4ab493.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587153/large-8d58fbbcbb4e999048e6445255c190de.jpg","alt":"MOON1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587153/preview-1a2df9c6925473e32ba8ee22a5b2cf62.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587156/large-d013550827db3380f02a6d5ba4e2a094.jpg","alt":"MOON2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587156/preview-2bb6e9383a1231c34af53d03f44aac74.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587157/large-2aeb02916948e623e0a99dd4d0c8ab75.png","alt":"MOON6.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587157/preview-3f236b120989300a55f6c8a8d3953063.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Sari Jordan:"},{"t":"p","html":"Known for a voice that oscillates from smoky-sweet soft to big-hearted belt and back again, New Jersey-born vocalist, songwriter, and musician Sari Jordan (they/she) spends their days and nights loving and learning down in New Orleans."},{"t":"p","html":"The sensitive, silly-goose songstress first decamped to the Crescent City for college in 2018, and soon set off on a whirlwind romance with the great American songbook. The local culture coalesced with a lifelong love for theater, soul, and alternative indie/psych rock, each deeply rooted in the city Sari now calls home."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/32POifvtGNBo1CGQo0wn5X?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Characterized by raw honesty and playful boldness, Sari’s voice commandeers ears with a confident, stated presence. Debut EP <em>‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7MugEUIkFHUqt4q5FWNyUQ?si=FyrYsFv4Rj-JZzik0K-G0A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sing To The Moon</strong></a>’ </em>(due Fall 2023) features a tasting menu of original music essentially ripped from diary entries over the past couple of years. The project is an amalgamation of Sari’s kaleidoscopic influences, embodying elements of <strong>Lianne La Havas</strong>, <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, <strong>Billie Holiday</strong>, <strong>Nai Palm of Hiatus Kaiyote</strong>, and <strong>Billie Eilish</strong>, in a succulent gumbo with Sari’s own gossamer, angelic style.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Sari!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/sarijjordan/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@sarijjordan","post":false},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@sarijjordan/video/7286551271148965162","handle":"@sarijjordan"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.sarijordan.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.sarijordan.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@sarijjordan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://twitter.com/sarijjordan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/SariJordan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://sarijordan.bandcamp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>bandcamp&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/sarijordanx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"263941","title":"Cliffs and Caves - YouTube","date":"2023-10-13","lead":"The Mother-daughter Americana duo leaned into Contemporary Christian music for their new single.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/263941/02c70bfb2c868f13c39712b87235766e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Mother-daughter Americana duo leaned into Contemporary Christian music for their new single."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1y2rPwT7ulaeEQ4tdbcfbj?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston, TX (October 13, 2023) - Mother-daughter Americana duo <a href=\"https://cliffsandcaves.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cliffs + Caves</strong></a> drops their new inspiring single, <a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/YouCantStop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“You Can’t Stop”</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>on Friday, October 13th. The new track leans heavily into Contemporary Christian music influences, nicely complementing themes of faith and worship Cliffs + Caves often tap into.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"“You Can’t Stop” includes several themes tied to biblical references, serving as an ode to God and his grace. The mother-daughter duo wanted to write a song for the body of Christ to sing together, rejoicing in God’s love and plan for his people. One of the key messages conveyed in this song is remaining steadfast in the midst of whatever tragedy is at hand. “You Can’t Stop” is a reminder that nothing can hinder God’s plan for His people."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/YouCantStop","label":"Listen to \"You Can't Stop\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587921/large-c94c097476b266553c6e77618b9b341c.jpg","alt":"\"You Can't Stop\" Cover Art by Kirby Trapolino"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Our eternity is secure in His grace and mercy - so we will never stop singing to the one who gave us life.”","cite":"- Cliffs + Caves, Mother-Daughter Americana Duo"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587922/large-8328903a5b237533ea0c1ae81febe815.jpg","alt":"CLIFF11.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587922/preview-1012d16033937ed13f9b256f571d50af.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587923/large-ca0ca1252580fcb07f6b08c475a8a96e.jpg","alt":"CLIFF0.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587923/preview-f436970362e002013896f5d1ffe44482.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587924/large-a1b3741c7ef6236d1214e7db3f5f0392.jpg","alt":"CLIFF22.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587924/preview-8b28c8fc10b6443a060388ae88efb7cc.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587925/large-ee10111fc9dd8d92e2259933964612b2.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-10-05 at 8.15.32 AM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587925/preview-67d0cdb97f4b064885e9b216a4856a26.png"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Lindsey Justice sheds some light on the inspiration for “You Can’t Stop” below: </strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“During the early months of Covid, churches were deemed “non-essential.” Even when public worship resumed, many people were instructed that singing wasn’t allowed. At the time, I found it so shocking that Target and Walmart could be found essential - yet our access to gather with our fellow believers to pray and study together was shut down. We wrote this song as a testament to God and his power. Nothing happening in our world can stop His word from going forth into the hearts and minds of people to the end of the earth.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Even though our music has always been focused within the Americana/folk genre, my daughter Claire and I both have a very strong Christian faith that has been a consistent theme in our songs. I have been a worship leader with Community Bible Study for years and Claire has spent the past couple summers between college at Texas A&amp;M serving as a worship leader at Camp OTX in Bandera. Our love for the Lord is so much a part of who we are that we wanted to release this worship song as an expression of our faith in Jesus and the great encouragement we have walking with fellow believers.”</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1J0Q7piRpWRQHW9IegFT4X?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Cliffs + Caves:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://cliffsandcaves.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cliffs + Caves</strong></a>, the mother-daughter duo of <strong>Lindsey</strong> and <strong>Claire Justice</strong>, unabashedly share their deeply personal and relatable stories through songs that resonate with listeners of all generations. Best known in their home state of Texas for their unique blend of Contemporary Americana music, the pair showcases the musical ingenuity that is created when artistry runs in the family with intimate lyrics lilting intrinsically over smooth musical progressions. Their previous discography includes their 2017 debut EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3SanUmvSOsrCrv1A4NlXZ2?si=nzqjn0iqSQOKnlxOcWf5yA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hold On</strong></a> (recorded with Grammy-nominated producer <strong>Jamie Candiloro (Ryan Adams, R.E.M., The Eagles)&nbsp;</strong>and featuring performances by legendary <strong>Willie Nelson</strong>’s harmonica player, <strong>Mickey Raphael</strong>, and sophomore EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4gEhBjWLd5a66JwQRENwNs?si=29JFfKxoSCqgPHKkQN5n0Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Capsize</strong></a> (produced by <strong>Chris Jacobie (Penny and Sparrow, Jarrod Dickenson, Duncan Fellows)</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"The original songs are a team effort with the duo individually contributing to the mastery of their lyrics and melodies. Moreover, twenty-year-old Claire being a multi-instrumentalist, not only composes the music for the tracks but also bestows a knack for songwriting. Their newer music further explores the duo’s ability to portray life through lyrics as they evolve into a more alternative Maggie-Rogers-esque sound while still maintaining their Americana roots and drawing inspiration from benchmark artists like <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, <strong>Lake Street Dive</strong>, and <strong>Patty Griffin</strong>. Stay tuned for what’s next from the duo!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Cliffs + Caves!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://cliffsandcaves.com/","img":"","title":"The official website for Texas-based mother/daughter duo Cliffs + Caves.","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.youtube.com/@cliffsandcaves2211?cbrd=1&amp;ucbcb=1","img":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/ytc/AGIKgqPPr5Gr4PP4mqpjJaBZqVj2m9DugGwqDXATUSgtYw=s900-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj","title":"Cliffs and Caves - YouTube","desc":"Cliffs + Caves, the mother-daughter duo of Lindsey and Claire Justice, unabashedly share their deeply personal and relatable stories through songs that reson..."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/CseY3SYuju0/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/cliffsandcaves\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a>​"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"263942","title":"Racyne Parker Unveils Haunting New Single \"Make It Out Alive\"","date":"2023-10-13","lead":"The Denver-based singer-songwriter releases her new song, transporting listeners through a raw narrative on facing demons.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/263942/fe5b1f82fad8969fbba2aee48e4b5c1a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Denver-based singer-songwriter releases her new song, transporting listeners through a raw narrative on facing demons."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3nHKvKpYOpurnagFu0BXEO?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (October 13, 2023) - Americana artist <strong>Racyne Parker&nbsp;</strong>drops her new single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/MakeItOutAlive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Make It Out Alive</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> on Friday, October 13th - just in time for the “spooky season.” Both chilling and melancholic, this song transports listeners through a rich and raw narrative about facing inner demons, finding closure, and leaving the past behind to make way for a brighter tomorrow."},{"t":"p","html":"A weeping and mournful pedal steel opens the song, introducing listeners to the dark and lonesome world that “Make It Out Alive” has sculpted. A hypnotic acoustic guitar embellished with a solitary whistle completes the rugged and desolate ambiance. There is an old-soul presence in Parker’s voice as she shares her compelling tale of resilience and transformation."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/MakeItOutAlive","label":"Listen to \"Make It Out Alive\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/69uzZLXVJPGmB52ik2Rw0g?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"After experiencing a sudden and inexplicable loss last year, I needed a place to contain the anger that I was feeling. I needed a place where the scales were balanced - that place didn’t exist in the real world, so that place became ‘Make It Out Alive.’","cite":"- Racyne Parker, Indie-Folk Singer"},{"t":"p","html":"“Make It Out Alive” taps into a Country-Western soundscape, blending ominous vocals with echoing banjo and cello accents. As the chorus unfolds like a flower, Parker reaches peak emotional depth and beauty."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587159/large-e15a724a0fa959b4080fb1cf80ed4f2d.png","alt":"\"Make It Out Alive\" Cover Art by Stephanie Mikuls"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wanted the song to feel more nuanced than anything I’ve done before. I didn’t want to hide what I felt at that time, but I also didn’t want this song to be weighed down by where it came from.”","cite":"- Racyne Parker, Indie-Folk Singer"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em><u>\"Make It Out Alive\" Lyrics </u></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"No surprises, last page first<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Upfront, no lies, truth until it hurts<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Another chapter, another verse<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Forked tongues, pretty words, unspoken bridges burned<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"I should’ve known, never could<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Dare I say, got me good<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"I think I won’t, you think I would<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Leave well enough alone<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"*The release of “Make It Out Alive” will be followed by a lyric video that releases on October 30th - further embellishing the song’s narrative."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Racyne Parker:"},{"t":"p","html":"Originally from Southern Oregon, Denver-based singer-songwriter <strong>Racyne Parker</strong> draws inspiration from country, modern folk, indie rock, and pop influences, to deliver catchy lyrics, warm vocals, and a contemporary style that fits in well on playlists next to <strong>Kacey Musgraves, Taylor Swift, </strong>and<strong> Caylee Hammack.</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"An engaging and low-stakes performer, Racyne is bound to play a song that you know while also introducing new songs to you that you’re sure to love."},{"t":"p","html":"Her honest and original tunes draw on her experiences with living in and leaving a small town, navigating uncertainty in love and life, and finding joy in the little moments.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"An up-and-comer in the Denver music scene, with lots of new music on the way, Racyne hopes to build community, create joy, and remain true to herself through the music that she makes.<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Racyne!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/racyneparker/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@racyneparker","post":false},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@racyneparker/video/7289306760421051678","handle":"@racyneparker"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/R6QPMcV2VsI?si=yV0VavpMxyQpyXTM","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"<br><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/RacyneParkerMusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@racyneparker?is_from_webapp=1&amp;sender_device=pc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | ​<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/racyneparker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/racyneparker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>threads</strong></a><br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"264075","title":"The Labra Brothers Drop New Single Ahead of November LP","date":"2023-10-13","lead":"Sibling band The Labra Brothers releases their new single \"Lonely,\" artfully crafted with intricate storytelling.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/264075/0407b9cb51755644c40d3ddefc71b67e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Sibling band The Labra Brothers releases their new single \"Lonely,\" artfully crafted with intricate storytelling."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6OXgSdy6mcWMnGm2U0kAjQ?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Youngstown, Ohio (October 13, 2023) - Latin sibling band <a href=\"https://www.thelabrabrothers.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Labra Brothers</strong></a> releases a new Cumbia-style single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6OXgSdy6mcWMnGm2U0kAjQ?si=f1e73dc045f44ed3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lonely</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on Friday, October 13. “Lonely” gives listeners a taste of the band's upcoming LP releasing on November 3rd: <em><strong>Home</strong>.&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"With intricate storytelling artfully crafted in both Spanish and English, “Lonely” pays homage to The Labra Brothers’ musical and cultural roots. Various sentiments like love and obsession are explored through interwoven harmonies and rich background instrumentals. Colorful bits of accordion are sprinkled throughout the track, accompanied by Latin percussion elements that will leave listeners tapping their feet to the beat.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“A heartfelt thank you goes out to our dedicated listeners who support and celebrate the rich Latin influences that run deep within our music. We appreciate you!”","cite":"- The Labra Brothers, Indie-Latin Band"},{"t":"p","html":"This song is a fresh take on the Latin-Funk genre our music usually fits into. For the creation of “Lonely,” The Labra Brothers put a modern twist on a classic Cumbia-style groove. The band infused traditional sonic elements of the genre such as acoustic guitar, but they personalized it by expanding their percussion section and blending both English and Spanish into their music."},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>\"LONELY\" LYRICS</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"Hey, I’m so done being lonely<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Hey, yes you’d better believe me<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"I’m so done being lonely<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Yes you’d better believe when I tell you<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"That this one is gonna be mine<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Tengo un amor que no puedo creer<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Todos los días la quiero ver&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"En mi canción la quiero poner<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"y me hace sentir feliz<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Song Credits:"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Produced by: <strong>The Labra Brothers, Danny Svenson</strong></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Recorded &amp; Mixed at: <strong>Bearcave Recording</strong></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Mastered by:<strong>&nbsp;Jamie Vitullo </strong></em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587382/large-973e62884d66d4700e4cfb4388fcaef0.jpg","alt":"\"Lonely\" Cover Art by Mollie Crowe"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587379/large-8539f060c111289835834f1ee40e7994.jpg","alt":"LONELY SINGLE COVER (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587379/preview-c259fec76d587368ad88cf4d2c8e040a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587380/large-16334de47d77fa2f4c718bd1f23e2645.jpg","alt":"labra-7582.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587380/preview-cc7c73181470eb64702db1ddfdd6e409.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587381/large-800870de3fa22c4fb2dbfd36baae0bf1.jpg","alt":"DSC_9207.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587381/preview-c80405438044335ee1a86b80df0d8c16.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Labra Brothers:"},{"t":"p","html":"The Labra Brothers are a Latin Funk sibling band from rustbelt Northeast Ohio. Influenced by the diverse music taste of their parents, the brothers developed a distinguished sound that combines blues, funk, and Latin. After falling in love with playing their own renditions of their favorite music, the band decided to put their talents to work within their original creations. Consisting of <strong>Adrian Labra</strong> on vocals and guitar, <strong>Cristian Labra</strong> on vocals and bass, <strong>David Labra</strong> on vocals, guitar, and sax, <strong>Antonio Labra</strong> on percussion, <strong>Danny Svenson</strong> on keys, <strong>Victor Labra</strong> on vocals and percussion, and <strong>Matt Hayes</strong> on drums, the band quickly discovered their ability to effortlessly interlock in an instrumental groove with each other. The Labra Brothers continue to release music and have established themselves regionally as a dynamic and diverse powerhouse of musical presentation. With four-part sibling vocal harmonies at the forefront, their versatility has become more evident with each new original studio recording they release. The Brothers had an eventful 2022, during which they played a direct support role for <strong>Average White Band</strong>, and were voted <strong>“Best Latin”</strong> by the <strong>Cleveland Music Awards</strong>. This year (2023), The Labra Brothers opened for <strong>Los Lobos,&nbsp;</strong>and were awarded <strong>Editor’s Pick for “Best Latin Fusion Band”&nbsp;</strong>in <strong>Cleveland Magazine</strong>. Check out The Labra Brothers’ new single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6OXgSdy6mcWMnGm2U0kAjQ?si=1c77a68b96844e63\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lonely</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> on all streaming platforms! Stay tuned for the band's LP: <em>Home</em> releasing on November 3, 2023.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Labra Brothers!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2RxirsfpxfaajELy8K4z7B?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@labrabrosmusic/video/7270493904271609119","handle":"@labrabrosmusic"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/Cqte1xrvGNM/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.thelabrabrothers.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheLabraBrothers/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>​"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"260937","title":"Keepers of Humanity","date":"2023-10-06","lead":"The San Francisco-based group is redefining the West Coast Alt-Rock music scene with a new 5-track EP.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/260937/8f9d5e9dd693c4ffc1e661df43b193f3.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The San Francisco-based group is redefining the West Coast Alt-Rock music scene with a new 5-track EP."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5myULM7VZUDLnnJL7LfmNH?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"San Francisco, CA (October 6, 2023) - Piano-forward Alternative Rock Band <a href=\"https://keepersofhumanity.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Keepers of Humanity</strong></a> releases their second studio EP, <em>‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5myULM7VZUDLnnJL7LfmNH?si=tecfYHwkTGG7mysVCIIYRg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Pansori</strong></em></a></em><em>.’&nbsp;</em>The 5-track EP was produced under <strong>Rockstone Records</strong>, and is already available for streaming on all platforms beginning Friday, October 6. ‘Pansori’ explores themes of paying homage to familial roots, finding peace from the love of a soulmate, suppressing passions to fulfill your parents' dreams, and more. The emotionally charged lyrics found within this EP urge listeners to connect with Keepers of Humanity on a more intimate level, getting to know the band's journey and overall ethos."},{"t":"p","html":"The title of the EP, ‘Pansori,’ is inspired by its namesake - the ancient Korean art of rhythmic storytelling. Following that element of tradition, ‘Pansori’ is a collection of five epic songs that explore the human experience. From the anguish of a misunderstood teenager and the gut-wrenching battles of adulthood to second chances in righting old wrongs in parenthood, Keepers of Humanity is proud to share this multi-dimensional EP with the world."},{"t":"quote","html":"“With an eclectic mix of genres, Pansori constantly surprises listeners with inviting yet immediate songs that hold your attention from start to finish. It was really fun working with producer Mat Gilbert to push ourselves and our sound in new directions.”","cite":"- Steven Bonaccorso, Guitarist - Keepers of Humanity"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>ABOUT THE EP</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Driven piano sounds intertwine with innocent-seeming vocals to create what is a theatrical, edgy, and modern EP: <em>Pansori</em>. This Alt-Rock release incorporates a wide range of genres including psych, blues, metal, punk, ambient and even classical music, reminding listeners of <strong>Kate Bush</strong>, <strong>Tori Amos</strong>, and <strong>Amanda Palmer</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5myULM7VZUDLnnJL7LfmNH?si=Red8mvwBRnC6LohL-jVMZA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘Pansori’</strong></a> is KOH’s first EP release under San Francisco indie record label <strong>Rockstone Records</strong>. The opening track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2PZ7esVDkCLO17dqAa8gsv?si=180efaee4ad64ec4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Intersection</strong></a><strong>,”&nbsp;</strong>is actually also a re-recording of the closing track of their previous album, <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5yNYspq26iHITIdwTcff3C?si=ddaa767c99af4f14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Freedom in the Chaos</a>,”</strong> self-released in 2019, giving listeners a rare opportunity to witness side-by-side the evolution of the band’s sound. Producer <strong>Mat Gilbert</strong> re-imagines the song with a punch, sizzle, and polish that can be heard throughout the EP and is characteristic of Gilbert’s highly distinct production style."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5myULM7VZUDLnnJL7LfmNH?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>ABOUT THE TRACKS</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Pansori</em>’s opening track, “<strong>Intersection</strong>,” is a cry for acceptance from a young person who has been forced to follow the crowd. This track is an ode to the people who ultimately reject the naysayers, follow their own path, and emerge confident in their authentic selves.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The lyrics reflect many times in life when I’ve experienced the need to break free, whether that was when leaving a bad relationship, fighting racial discrimination as a Korean-American woman, clashing with musicians over creative differences, and more. Like I say in the song, “let me be me.” \"Intersection\" is also a tribute to the musicians I look up to who have found success in remaining true to their own sound.”","cite":"- Jean Nanjo, Lead Singer - Keepers of Humanity"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2PZ7esVDkCLO17dqAa8gsv?si=ce0ba88664f341da\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Intersection</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is an upbeat song, introduced by <strong>Steven Bonaccorso</strong>’s killer guitar riffs, joined by <strong>Rudy Choy</strong>’s punchy bass lines. Organ and piano accents give this track texture and color while lead singer <strong>Jean Nanjo</strong> ties it all together with her sweet, girl-next-door vocals."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2PZ7esVDkCLO17dqAa8gsv?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This album reflects how varied musical tastes come together in harmony. Sometimes you need to rock out, and sometimes you need to just chill. Our music has a little bit of everything for listeners of all genres.”","cite":"- Rudy Choy, Bassist - Keepers of Humanity"},{"t":"p","html":"The EP’s second track, <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4zmT3B8rOY0JsVCAUEW1k5?si=0eb16696a29c471a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>No Greater</strong></a>,”</strong> describes the inner torment of living a lie with no way to escape. The lyrics are awe-striking and raw, containing sentiments such as, <em>“My inner shadow parasite, it laughs while eating me alive.”</em> “No Greater” breathes life and imagery into the suffering of a tortured soul. This song was written during one of the lowest points of (lead singer) Nanjo’s life, when the feeling of despair consumed her life and left her begging for some sense of relief. Nanjo’s vocals soar over Bonaccorso’s ethereal string tone, evoking anguish that ends with a tumultuous piano solo and powerful finale."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4nA5LnhYjmHZb7GqPhyHbG?si=3185c1f9027e4aeb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Pansori</strong></a><strong>,”&nbsp;</strong>is the third song and title track for this EP, serving as the standout storytelling component for this project. “Pansori” creates a fascinating juxtaposition of two main vocal parts across worlds and timelines - one an older male honoring his mother in the epic traditional style of Korean <em>pansori</em>, and the other, a young woman singing in English about the modern crisis of suppressing your own passions to fulfill the expectations of Asian immigrant parents. &nbsp;Life meets art within “Pansori” as the male vocals for this tune are composed and performed by Nanjo’s father, <strong>Ik Shin</strong>. Synth harp and flute accentuate the song’s ethnicity, but the backbone of this track lies within the bluesy-rock style of bass and guitar riffs from Choy and Bonaccorso."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Listeners get to rock out to this EP while losing their minds, honoring their respective cultures, and smiling at their true love, all in one sonic work of art.”","cite":"- Jean Nanjo, Lead Singer - Keepers of Humanity"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6wkj5CdLGTtLdgHhmdUvkk?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The fourth song featured on the EP is titled, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2NNtKATA47hdot3173z6XN?si=2aa7a0b24e914c80\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cosmic Mind</strong></a><strong>”&nbsp;</strong>which creates a mini vacation from the density of the three tracks preceding it. “Cosmic Mind” is a perfect storm of conflicting imagery, sometimes whimsical and magical, and at other times, disturbing. “Cosmic Mind” is a frantic, experimental foray into madness enhanced by Nanjo’s classically-inspired piano statements. The organ lines pound over epic bass and guitar riffs from Choy and Bonaccorso, driven by powerful and relentless percussive elements. Nanjo’s vocals become increasingly otherworldly and euphoric, closing “Cosmic Mind” out with a punk-inspired explosion.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The EP concludes with its final track, <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0MFIJmyk8I4Cfz7xcHFkh3?si=727f9fd39e874d4d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Fantasy at Daybreak</strong></a>,”</strong> a gentle, beautiful expression of love between soulmates. The song slightly blurs the line between a dream and reality, keeping listeners on their toes as the EP concludes. This track was co-written with Choy, featuring pulsating grooves and lush underlying beats backed by Nanjo’s pure and dreamy vocals."},{"t":"p","html":"IMAGE CREDIT: <a href=\"https://www.stevengregoryphotography.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Steven Gregory Photography</a>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581803/large-16245fde63504f679cd8538886f44c75.jpg","alt":"SGP_3232 EDIT C sq.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581803/preview-f2bfd2fce41c884ebf20afd6270edde5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581804/large-13179e6349d541682ab5b7279a60ebef.jpg","alt":"SGP_3232 EDIT A sq.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581804/preview-adf276988603a20db84fdb66a0a10a7a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581805/large-66087e94be29d04eef6b013ee50e1583.jpg","alt":"SGP_2093 EDIT .jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581805/preview-9b2ecbe657c41e383b3f73e1f804611b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581806/large-b771761d386d3274976ed87572751f85.jpg","alt":"SGP_1738 EDIT .jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581806/preview-557bd4a3841b840c16bbf50f03961645.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581807/large-9ef14e077cf64a33ba958858dee9f96f.jpg","alt":"SGP_3040 EDIT A BW.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581807/preview-f100419011e22230cebdce1010ad7675.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581808/large-e06993f4ec4cb7f16d737232c09728c7.jpg","alt":"SGP_2026 EDIT A sq.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581808/preview-8b07aa2559eefaa08f5af3614e337ad3.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Keepers of Humanity:"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from San Francisco, CA -<strong>&nbsp;Keepers of Humanity</strong> is a four-piece Alt-Rock band made up of four friends pursuing their love of creating raw, evocative music. Due to their feminine yet edgy piano-driven sound, Keepers of Humanity's music has often been compared to Kate Bush, Tori Amos, and Amanda Palmer. With <strong>Jean Nanjo</strong> on vocals, piano and keys; <strong>Rudy Choy</strong> on bass; <strong>Steven Bonaccorso</strong> on guitars; and <strong>Alexi Robins</strong> on drums, each member of the band brings a unique sonic element to the table. Keepers of Humanity's 2019 debut 8-track album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5yNYspq26iHITIdwTcff3C?si=n8ZbMYxzSKy6kLHPi954Eg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Freedom in the Chaos</strong></em></a>, transports listeners through fluctuating moods and intense emotions, all grounded in sincerity and light. Recorded and mixed on fully analog equipment, the album has a vibrant, spontaneous, and organic feel. Keepers of Humanity just released their follow-up EP, <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5myULM7VZUDLnnJL7LfmNH?si=5_RM1YByQFmUwuK2s0Wefg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Pansori</strong></a><strong>’</strong> in October 2023 under the San Francisco-based indie record label, <strong>Rockstone Records</strong>.<em>&nbsp;</em>Their EP teaser single, <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2PZ7esVDkCLO17dqAa8gsv?si=8148478640f640f4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Intersection</a>,”</strong> was released on September 8, 2023 and is now available for streaming on all platforms."},{"t":"p","html":"Follow Keepers of Humanity on their social media channels linked below for all updates and upcoming announcements!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Keepers of Humanity!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/qt1YCo8JKjQ?si=e91y1EQUcv8moXKX","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/keepersofhumanity/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@keepersofhumanity","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://keepersofhumanity.com/","img":"https://d10j3mvrs1suex.cloudfront.net/s:bzglfiles/u/719584/6bf5ec1640aaad48080f54ba4691403459449466/original/manatee-head-logo.png/!!/meta%3AeyJzcmNCdWNrZXQiOiJiemdsZmlsZXMifQ%3D%3D.png","title":"Keepers of Humanity","desc":"Home page of Keepers of Humanity, an alternative, indie, pop, rock, songwriter group from San Francisco. Keepers of Humanity is a piano-driven indie rock band from San Francisco, California. Reminisce"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://keepersofhumanity.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>WEBSITE</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/keepersofhumanitySF/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"262512","title":"Psychedelic Soul Artist Terri J. Releases Eclectic 10-Track Album","date":"2023-10-06","lead":"The album \"Groovy Moovy\" officially drops, exploring expansive sophisticated themes.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/262512/54233052a91987fb4fa9d24360151ab4.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The album \"Groovy Moovy\" officially drops, exploring expansive sophisticated themes."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7sr8SpdZjpBD8626wCKpua?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"San Francisco, CA (October 6, 2023) - <a href=\"https://lytlifecoach.wixsite.com/terri-j\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Terri J.</strong></a> releases her debut album<strong>&nbsp;“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7sr8SpdZjpBD8626wCKpua?si=3JcenmOASXiUKEhXgkub9w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groovy Moovy</a>”</strong> on Friday, October 6. The 10-track album intricately explores expansive themes like self-confidence, true love, owning one’s power, and joy.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I don’t really like to sing about breakups too much. I like to sing about love and promote it however I can. That being said, heartbreak is a real thing and we have to talk about it sometimes.”","cite":"- Terri J., Independent Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"p","html":"Terri J. blends her singular songwriting style and euphoric harmonies with rhythms inspired by Soul music from the ‘60s and ‘70s. The artist also incorporates various Neo-Soul influences into her music, resulting in a record that sounds classic yet fresh at the same time."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3ylqWrZLD2yqSqoMa97O8u?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Terri J. teamed up with Producer/Guitarist <strong>Mat Gilbert</strong> to create the cosmic adventure that is&nbsp;<em>“Groovy Moovy.”</em> The album’s instrumentation and lyrics intertwine to represent a beautifully captivating reflection of both Terri’s and Mat’s creative styles. This enchanting 10-track record represents how different styles can fuse together to form something new."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584563/large-a83af992b2466d91bef81a45c547f188.png","alt":"Cover art credit: Edward Axel; Photo credit: JRae  "},{"t":"quote","html":"“I saw Terri composing a lot of this stuff a capella, building chords by ear with only vocals. I think that approach is a big part of her unique style. She has a great ear that allows her to take harmony to unusual places based on what sounds good. We have created a larger-than-life sound with only drums, bass, guitar, and vocals.”","cite":"- Mat Gilbert, Producer"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1bdpxYfa2aK1ALYc2ec3If?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Terri J.:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Terri J.</strong> is an iconic, international recording artist originally from Memphis, TN. After 14 years and counting, she has continued to spread her musical footprint across the West Coast of the US via the San Francisco Bay Area where she recorded her first album. She can also be found doing live performances of her original music at well-known venues such as <strong>Brick &amp; Mortar Music Hall</strong> and <strong>Cornerstone Berkeley</strong>. Her new album <strong>“</strong><strong>Groovy Moovy”</strong><em>&nbsp;</em>houses eclectic gems such as her hit singles <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/459mx6JK6ZHsJcH8ftnL0e?si=e09cf49fbbfc435b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lie</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> a classic retake on<strong>&nbsp;“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/485DHJLgDqUqrkHutJTTKq?si=c7b35d9e94674058\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Let’s Stay Together</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> and the title track <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3ylqWrZLD2yqSqoMa97O8u?si=d3cdebe512da4f2f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Groovy Moovy</strong></a><strong>.”</strong> Her recent live performance of “Lie” in Oakland, CA secured her the 1st Place title at <strong>Oakland’s Got Talent 2023</strong>. With her multi-faceted outlook on songwriting, she is sure to have something in her discography for every listener."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Terri!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/terrijsings/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@terrijsings","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/qpKxt_t9GHU?si=sSaEKCcsCEr4fbbz","height":"315"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC_v3mAo-a3yTGN-JfEzUGqw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YOUTUBE</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@terrijsings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"></a></strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@thetroublenotesofficial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"264332","title":"Jazz-Rock Band,The Erly, Announces Midwest Tour Ahead of November Album Release","date":"2023-10-05","lead":"The fall tour will span across the Midwest from October 21 through November 18","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/264332/e3cc4773e740ecc3392428e825bb357c.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The fall tour will span across the Midwest from October 21 through November 18"},{"t":"p","html":"Niles, MI (October 5, 2023) - Michigan-based Jazz-Rock band,<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://theerlyband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Erly</strong></a>, is embarking on their debut tour in anticipation of upcoming album,&nbsp;<em>Culture Fever</em>. This tour promises an unforgettable live music experience, as The Erly get to showcase their individuality while connecting with fans, old and new. See below for all tour ​dates, locations, ticket links, event info, and more!<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\">"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3QPLdBDMCs5nyauZZMX7IW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>TOUR DATES + DETAILS</u>"},{"t":"h3","html":"1. Akron, Ohio - The Rialto Theatre"},{"t":"list","items":["Date: October 21, 2023","Event Name: MIC1PARK: MAGIC MIDWEST MINI FIELD TRIP","About: An exciting 9-band extravaganza featuring some of the best bands in the Midwest, put on by Mic1park! Featuring: The Erly, Four Times Louder, Faith In Failure, Girl Cologne, Half Past Late, Sherry Lane, Formerly Candice, Jonah Leatherman, and Urban Honey.","Doors: 3:00 PM EST","Show: 4:00 PM EST","Address: The Rialto Theatre, 1000 Kenmore Blvd, Akron, OH 44314","Tickets: Get Tickets <a href=\"https://www.therialtotheatre.com/tickets/midwest-magic-mini-field-trip-102123?fbclid=IwAR0Tci3fsafU5Bxy70I11PcJhiTLwTIj9-1IaM6_wj_q77h-cSKpy7VFIrk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Here</a>","Facebook Event Page: Event Details <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/events/284267567677222\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Here</a>"]},{"t":"h3","html":"2. Three Oaks, Michigan - The Acorn Theater"},{"t":"list","items":["Date: November 3, 2023 (<em><u>Culture Fever Album Release Show</u></em>)","Opener: Kelly Hoppenjans","Doors: 7:00 PM EST","Show: 8:00 PM EST","Address: The Acorn Theater, 107 Generations Dr, Three Oaks, MI 49128","<a href=\"https://www.acornlive.org/events/the-erly-album-release/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Event Page</a>&nbsp;","Facebook Event Page: <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/events/6044107599027337\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Event Details</a>","Tickets: Get Tickets <a href=\"https://ci.ovationtix.com/35261/production/1175144?performanceId=11341143&amp;fbclid=IwAR0REUj9znsu7yEYle1uAOOzW6cYni39y34CvEUDrth1GKnRCn0jA-YuCG0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Here</a>"]},{"t":"h3","html":"3. Cleveland, Ohio - TempleLive: Jester’s Lounge"},{"t":"list","items":["Date: November 10, 2023","With: Melted Strawberry &amp; Blue Hour","Doors: 7:00 PM EST","Show: 8:00 PM EST","Address: TempleLive, 3615 Euclid Ave, Cleveland, OH 44115","Tickets: Coming Soon / Door Charge","Event Link: Coming Soon"]},{"t":"h3","html":"4. Chicago, Illinois - Cubby Bear"},{"t":"list","items":["Date: November 16, 2023","With: Lost Pyramids &amp; SunnDog","Doors: 7:30 PM CST","Show: 8:00 PM CST","Address: The Cubby Bear, 1059 W Addison St, Chicago, IL 60613","Tickets: Get Tickets <a href=\"https://www.ticketweb.com/event/mic1park-pres-lost-pyramids-w-cubby-bear-tickets/13392308?pl=cubby00&amp;fbclid=IwAR1FKHl5YF1eDybx0MUNKjFzVoht53SXfJ-yvf-Z6K8Ro5P_DatoXWa-1Us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Here</a>","Event Page: <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/events/1276741049881848\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Event Details</a>"]},{"t":"h3","html":"5. Milwaukee, Wisconsin - Lilliput Records (In-Store Performance)"},{"t":"list","items":["Date: November 17, 2023","Show: 5:00 PM CST - 7:00 PM CST","Address: Lilliput Records, 1669 N Farwell Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53202","Tickets: Free Show","Event Link: Coming Soon"]},{"t":"h3","html":"6. TBA - November 18, 2023"},{"t":"list","items":["<em>*More details to come soon</em>"]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580111/large-1391af554d2814f05cf459bfdea1e33d.jpg","alt":"FLAM1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580111/preview-c6e2e995ba84440d6a89c3bfed11e0b6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580113/original-058c0adcd67897cc6c1a6290713c257f.jpg","alt":"FLAME2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580113/preview-cf6d31436c834a337913d04e33057385.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580114/large-34a5c54b2165cbe1c275ac368565ef24.jpg","alt":"FLAME4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580114/preview-d9795994509c0bd4012272fcfacd9c40.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580112/large-f07f1c63c3a96d78af130655759085a6.jpg","alt":"FLAME3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580112/preview-590f7669822045afa671103be5a5505a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587952/-ff31f079793754d3b8d67f65a37796b4.jpg","alt":"The Erly - October 21st Poster.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587952/-ff31f079793754d3b8d67f65a37796b4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587954/large-92d69c5ffd02bb680fd6c824adff44f9.png","alt":"The Erly - November 3rd Poster 2.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587954/preview-7fe2ba6cedce6f0bea7192dae0e87d3d.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587955/large-dd3b83f1ece9372bb46bd1a5189fc656.png","alt":"The Erly - November 3rd Poster 1.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/587955/preview-41a8d17922ad9e126a7c6a7ed58de78e.png"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"PHOTO CREDIT: KELSIE HERZOG"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Erly:"},{"t":"p","html":"Michigan-based Indie-Soul group <strong>The Erly</strong> combines sonic elements from the ‘60s and ‘70s Rock, Pop, and Funk, creating a fresh<em>&nbsp;“Modern Disco”</em> sound and vibe of their own. Fueled by collaboration, friendship, and timeless good vibes, the quartet would fit right in at Woodstock ‘69 or at the indie nerve center that is <strong>SXSW</strong>. Most of <strong>The Erly</strong>’s music features clean guitar work, layered vocals, and groovy undertones that energize even their most solemn-sounding tracks. The band is composed of Drummer <strong>Fran Gleason</strong>, Bassist <strong>Collin Mattiford</strong>, Guitarist <strong>Trevor McDonald,</strong> and Keyboardist <strong>Alyssa Serviss</strong>, with all 4 members featured on vocals. <strong>The Erly</strong> was created in 2018 when Mattiford and Gleason decided to expand upon their pre-established musical duo. Since their formation in 2018, <strong>The Erly</strong> has released two full albums and four singles with more music on the way. <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0QzfIYmj30ksSmpWPrhxpm?si=80a4bb72f7aa48fc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Paralyzed</strong></a><strong>”</strong> dropped mid-August and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3aITimGk0InPUdYHaW49UZ?si=4d069fff904b4bea\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Flame The Main</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is slated to launch on September 20th, both of which will be featured within The Erly’s upcoming record, <em><strong>Culture Fever -&nbsp;</strong></em>available on November 3rd, 2023."},{"t":"p","html":"For all announcements and updates, stay connected with The Erly on social media!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Erly!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/sp563zO9lTo?si=M0aMl3eq9Jc7wJl5","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/theerlyband/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@theerlyband","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/theerlyband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@TheErly\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"262018","title":"Read More","date":"2023-09-29","lead":"Synth ballad \"History\" officially drops as a testament to the strength and tenacity of long-term love.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/262018/3327ab7adaddc7687da6da32fdcf81ea.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Synth ballad \"History\" officially drops as a testament to the strength and tenacity of long-term love."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/73nSPYKTSVcE4UDqT1Ms56?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston, TX (September 29, 2023) - Houston-based Alt-Pop artist <a href=\"https://www.timqualls.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tim Qualls</strong></a> unveils his new uplifting synth ballad, <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/73nSPYKTSVcE4UDqT1Ms56?si=AMyP1aHOQKasFX9JYa3pPQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>History</strong></a>”</strong> on Friday, September 29. “History” is the third track released from Qualls’ upcoming debut album. This song serves as a testament to the strength and tenacity of long-term love."},{"t":"p","html":"Written for his wife, Tim Qualls views “History” as an exploration of love that grows stronger with time, demonstrating how moments of hardship can fortify love and relationships. This release celebrates the unwavering trust in a partnership, knowing that, regardless of life’s challenges, the love shared between two people can conquer anything."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/585740/large-42a4bf7ab0f661278372a109971060e7.jpeg","alt":"Cover Art Credit: Kirby Betancourt; In-Studio Photos: Paul Pelc."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584199/large-c8d2759e6e754385b924249350dbf53a.jpg","alt":"IMG_8117.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584199/preview-7abe55022dfe2bff893f5ef871a00b1e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584200/large-4e313ef0412a6bfa8b07e91e0efb47c0.jpg","alt":"IMG_8113.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584200/preview-5ef1f688ed5aae107033aa8d4831cb66.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584201/large-3f0db39597bf0b2d7d0495cf4428bd1a.jpg","alt":"historynewnew.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584201/preview-fd29a2c1b022f83cd5f86713aa130441.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"“History” skillfully marries piano balladry with the energy and appeal of pop music. Layered instrumentals, inquisitive lyrics, and Qualls’ crisp vocals create a sonic tapestry that will inspire listeners to take on the world. &nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“History” is a uniquely grounded homage to long-term relationships and the unwavering trust that exists within a partnership.”","cite":"- Tim Qualls, Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/12J7rAVoeFIUNkRelq5zw8?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>Photos by Houston-Based Photographer Kirby Betancourt</em><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Tim Qualls:"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston-based songwriter <strong>Tim Qualls</strong> delivers rootsy soul music that is grounded in family, heartache, and a positive outlook on life very few write about. Influenced by legends like <strong>Ray Charles</strong>, <strong>Jamie Cullum</strong>, and <strong>John Mayer</strong>, musicians compare him to a <em>“soul artist that croons on the piano.”</em> His productions have been compared to <strong>Adele</strong>, <strong>Sam Smith</strong>, and <strong>Ryan Tedder</strong>. Once awarded <strong>Houston Press</strong>’ “Best New Act” award, Qualls continues to deliver new music every year. Tim has been featured on Spotify playlists such as <strong>LIFE SUCKS</strong>, <strong>DINNER MUSIC</strong>, <strong>SOULFUL BLEND</strong>, and <strong>COZY BLEND</strong>. <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2oheHd1XwCuN3cFzZV7Tid?si=4da46a8a26214bd1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Forever</strong></a><strong>”,&nbsp;</strong><strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0MA3vYM4gsD64hQXDZWUD8?si=5cebb944d65d42e3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Grave</strong></a>,<strong>”</strong> and <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/29f4uKrB8LFCT29EvNcidJ?si=aa25a248837e4969\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>History</strong></a>”</strong> will be featured Qualls’ upcoming debut album. <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/73nSPYKTSVcE4UDqT1Ms56?si=F6A-_Ao5Qt-AdL4F_KR3cw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>History</strong></a><strong>”&nbsp;</strong>is now available for streaming on all major platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Tim!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/timquallsmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@timquallsmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.timqualls.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIM QUALLS OFFICIAL WEBSITE</strong></a>"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.timqualls.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/timquallsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><strong><a href=\"https://www.twitter.com/timothyqualls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TWITTER</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/timquallsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"262502","title":"Claire Reneé Launches Long-Awaited EP: Journal Entries 1-4","date":"2023-09-29","lead":"The LA-based musician releases her 4-emotionally charged tracks project that resonates with listeners of all genres.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/262502/3480b8ed956285fdabf2ca46b324aa15.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The LA-based musician releases her 4-emotionally charged tracks project that resonates with listeners of all genres."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3dC8evHpcdLz59tjtahwA7?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, CA (September 29, 2023) - Rising R&amp;B artist <a href=\"https://www.clairereneemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Claire Reneé</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>drops her new EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3dC8evHpcdLz59tjtahwA7?si=3k98EPcfT8qFFP7Oy_pg3Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Journal Entries 1-4</strong></em></a>, on Friday, September 29. The release is composed of four emotionally charged singles that inspire and resonate with listeners of all genres.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Journal Entries 1-4 Tracks:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1q4TnDPpaig60yqKPvExQV?si=1fae7b245adb4bf4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Stay Away</strong></a>​<br><em>- Produced by <strong>Jaye Locke</strong>; Co-produced by <strong>Sean Silverman</strong></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0QJdtymqRYGcEAcjUl7N7E?si=52717e77cb824e8d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sadder Days</strong></a>​<br><em>- Produced by Jaye Locke; Co-produced by <strong>Silas Wong</strong></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4Kd5hJKJ0gMhTg9yXPAwoX?si=9de4ad7a6de5400f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Waste My Time</strong></a><br><em>- Produced by Jaye Locke</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0zwMOZ6fG515fCDIkKjStR?si=766aa722eb1746ba\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Don't Wanna Wait</strong></a>​<br>- <em>Produced by <strong>Sam Hoffman</strong> and Claire Reneé</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Journal Entries 1-4</em> flows through various life scenarios and circumstances that lead us to express ourselves in some way. Thoughts, emotions, and experiences are backed by unique emotions, often helping us to navigate through love, relationships, and figuring out who we are.<br>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Journal entries can reveal so much about the past, whether that is looking back on a challenge you overcame or realizing how stuck you were in that moment of struggle Looking back on dated words is a bittersweet moment of pride that makes you realize your inner strength and determination to carry on.”","cite":"- Claire Reneé, R&B Singer"},{"t":"p","html":"Journaling has always been a nostalgic passion for Claire. Each entry represents one point in time, and if you look back on your words while in another chapter of your life, the things you can uncover are awe-striking. Claire Reneé created each song and melody, pouring her soul into each sentiment. Each track on the EP will have a corresponding lyric video, and eventually a music video - so stay tuned!<br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584555/large-e2e52555e6735e7cf068f4344296eedf.png","alt":"Journal Entries 1-4: Cover art by Rachel Summer assisted by Annie Denten."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I Don’t Wanna Wait” allowed me to question the notion that everything has to be a cosmic sign or message for a person or moment to be meant for you. External ideas, forced timelines, and projections don't need to be a part of your timeline.”","cite":"- Claire Reneé, R&B Singer"},{"t":"p","html":"<u><strong>“I DON’T WANNA WAIT” LYRICS</strong>&nbsp;</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I don’t need to wait for a spaceship to arrive</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Message in the clouds</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Light rays beaming from the sky</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I don’t wanna wait for</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>A perfect moment in time</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>My life is not a movie</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I’m just trynna get mine</em><br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584545/large-b3a979fc265d01a05bc4756e0f4d3651.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-09-25 at 10.30.08 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584545/preview-2799a6dc5a8eceaeeec9307b6d57bb1b.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584546/large-384bde227490c918dc21ee1736c50192.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-09-25 at 10.29.59 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584546/preview-fdd30359ad9b083b12335ccd978ed446.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584547/-068b38c2cede2f47c9972fbc3c20095b.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-09-25 at 10.30.39 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584547/preview-48dfb54e3a997eab525358c9358430db.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584549/large-edfa7ac896aa9f12dcdf8c17841a82ae.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-09-25 at 10.30.27 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584549/preview-363363d7bebd83fccd25c52bdd707c6d.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584551/large-6dae9d634768e56e9194cb94a097037c.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-09-25 at 10.28.30 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584551/preview-c7a962c01d368bbeb38e6b5becbb0624.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584550/large-b5657e07dc43ed284fd0da69cec1d91c.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-09-25 at 10.30.17 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584550/preview-e0291dd2724fc7cd3b4f231c5d20373c.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584548/large-bb4a265453c13f11696639f3639dd8bb.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-09-25 at 10.29.04 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584548/preview-5b6329a5bddc780c41cee543502b3378.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584552/large-8fded55420b164cdbdca530a1b9130a7.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-09-25 at 10.29.51 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584552/preview-ced413e08d32480ac93796c8204947a6.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584553/large-13edf2ed46ce7016db66fdbcd7124b9b.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-09-25 at 10.28.46 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584553/preview-6e3b177a5de38a81327673396c0398d6.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584554/large-b432eb563948b85765c316139c5c3077.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-09-25 at 10.29.37 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584554/preview-71922da59711873ec778e671aaebee39.png"}]},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1Wp8w74ZupCeCZfZwewX25?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Claire Reneé:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.clairereneemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Claire Reneé</strong></a> is more than a musician—she’s an immersive journey. With a foundation in classical dance, Claire’s musical expression transcends genres, effortlessly blending R&amp;B, soul, jazz, and pop, all while drawing inspiration from her hip-hop influences. Her voice is raspy yet graceful, creating a tapestry of sound that resonates with profound emotion, complemented by her distinctive harmonies that never fail to evoke a mesmerizing atmosphere.&nbsp;<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\">"},{"t":"p","html":"Dancing her way into the spotlight from a tender age of 4, Claire’s path was paved with dedication and nurtured by prestigious institutions like <strong>The Dance Theater of Harlem</strong> <strong>and </strong><strong>Alvin Ailey</strong>. Claire’s evolution has been nothing short of remarkable. This duality of dance and music found its zenith during her time in High School at the <strong>Professional Performing Arts School </strong>in Manhattan. Her talent later led her to prestigious music programs at both <strong>Berklee College of Music </strong>and <strong>The New School for Jazz and Contemporary Music</strong>, crowning her as a multifaceted gem in the music realm."},{"t":"p","html":"Claire’s new creative chapter is marked by her latest single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/43DEVwmJ2AGyHoeMLC0kMW?si=fafa421b6f31476e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sadder Days</strong></a>.<strong>”</strong> This evocative track serves as the first glimpse into her upcoming EP, titled “Journal Entries 1-4,”<strong>&nbsp;</strong>scheduled to grace our ears in September 2023. Through “Sadder Days,” Claire delves into the raw emotions that thread through the human experience, inviting listeners to connect with a narrative that resonates on a deeply personal level."},{"t":"p","html":"Claire's EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3dC8evHpcdLz59tjtahwA7?si=-ZNNhRlVQeG3rmXKZq-7_A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Journal Entries 1-4</strong></em></a>, launched on September 29 and is now available on all streaming platforms! Stay tuned for all updates and announcements via Claire's social media pages linked below.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Claire Reneé!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/artisterenee/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@artisterenee","post":false},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@artisterenee/video/7258331308743462186","handle":"@artisterenee"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.clairereneemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/clairereneemusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ArtisteRenee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter&nbsp;</strong></a>| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/ArtisteRenee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"262508","title":"Alt-Pop Artist Maria Deirisarri Unveils Debut Album 'In The Beginning'","date":"2023-09-29","lead":"The Atlanta-based musician officially releases her new album, driving listeners through a sonic journey.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/262508/fcc4fcc91cc52da2eddc342e5c115867.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Atlanta-based musician officially releases her new album, driving listeners through a sonic journey."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Atlanta, GA &nbsp;(September 29, 2023) - Alternative-Pop artist, <a href=\"https://www.mariadeirisarri.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maria Deirisarri</strong></a>&nbsp;drops her new 13-track record, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ?si=O_9PKjquRFe80EYi0yG_EQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>In The Beginning</strong></em></a>,<em>&nbsp;</em>on Friday, September 29th. This impressive album successfully showcases Deirisarri’s full range of skills and influences as she makes her mark on the music industry.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>‘In The Beginning’</em> is more than just an album - it is a statement and introduction to Maria Deirisarri's artistry and passion. This release will guide listeners through a sonic journey through ethereal instrumentals and power-driven themes. Deirisarri's lyrical sentiments span across love, fear, and resistance, as she ultimately reaches a point of self-discovery within the album's resolution."},{"t":"quote","html":"‘In The Beginning’ encompasses so many experiences and time periods in my life, acting as a collection of memories and progress. From “Te Necesito,” which I wrote when I was ten, to “Pieces,” a song I wrote a few months ago - this record represents all of who I have grown to be.”","cite":"- Maria Deirisarri, Alt-Pop Singer"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>‘In The Beginning’&nbsp;</em>seamlessly blends enticing Latin rhythms with pop sensibilities and melodies. Crisp yet calming vocals at the beginning of the album lead into the electrifying nature of <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3Ipu3JBvpAT1bkb0alZvvA?si=67b961c2c8a8405c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Itilu</strong></a><strong>”</strong> with little to no hesitation. Deirisarri's “all-or-nothing” songwriting shines within the juxtaposition of these similar yet dissonant tracks to create an eclectic offering of stories and mystic memories.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584559/large-5db114bbfa921ec30ac484cfd79ad0eb.jpg","alt":"In The Beginning Cover Art - by Beatriz Deirisarri"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Since I was a little girl, I knew I would release an album someday. Now that day is here, and I can't help but see my record as an offering. An offering to God, to my family, to myself, and to the world.”","cite":"- Maria Deirisarri, Alt-Pop Singer"},{"t":"p","html":"The album features twelve songs produced by <strong>Patrick Taylor </strong>and one track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/10HrEur1hApraufv2ih2ZY?si=3b57f15bb7de444b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Te Necesito</strong></a><strong>,”&nbsp;</strong>produced by <strong>Jason Andrews</strong> at Spotlight Sound Studio. Overall, <em>“In the Beginning”</em> is upbeat, sensual, tender, fun and carefree and marks extraordinary first steps into musical discovery."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584556/large-473281368f60078b0a0af18e7d976530.jpg","alt":"044B2808-787C-48A8-891C-037BACC0988E.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584556/preview-ca23acc8e22ae25426baf072c990fefd.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584557/large-a959cb8c7efad763db8d037c8dd52523.jpg","alt":"5B6C8138-DBB7-4DE8-8938-CE13D96D0171.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584557/preview-46a73e97601b434e88a1d36a8ab0af4c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584558/large-17af31fe155a27995caa5265426dbeff.jpg","alt":"2428ADA2-92CF-4AA5-9B23-29E254B7FF7D.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584558/preview-5cba8ac3a9d6d69e6769ac15b1cf24a4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584560/large-ae88f6b79f8a11187ddde2897bf9aae6.jpg","alt":"IMG_3468.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584560/preview-aef2bfbdd600aa978d77e0d9da82a5a3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584561/large-eee8d219ca43d6969bb7c8fb76c23aa7.jpg","alt":"IMG_9140.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584561/preview-b6b91784e4715e10b6701b64ace813bb.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584562/large-057636ea55607a88af4114e4a0972543.jpg","alt":"82B2CA09-30C5-46F1-9D0F-D4D5E546C8C6.tif","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584562/preview-8acab54fcc89b44fcf9b0287116da0b2.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Maria Deirisarri:"},{"t":"p","html":"Rising pop artist&nbsp;<strong>Maria Deirisarri</strong> is only 17 years old, but her musicianship and lyricism suggest wisdom beyond her years. The Atlanta-based singer-songwriter experiments with a multitude of genres, from dark alternative to bossa nova, generating an eclectic mix of music notably showcased in her debut album, <em><strong>In The Beginning. </strong></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Already amassing over 77k streams on Spotify, and garnering attention from top publications such as <strong>EARMILK&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Conversations About Her</strong>, Maria Deirisarri’s success continues to increase with every release. The range of her sound entices listeners to discover every song’s personality, and even surprises them with lyrics connected to her Hispanic culture and multilingual heritage (such as in <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7Bum6Hbsbd3hTyrWdiFaZB?si=148f3290894c4340\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Same</strong></a><strong>”</strong> and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/10HrEur1hApraufv2ih2ZY?si=44bd1e8b3e9f4184\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Te Necesito</strong></a><strong>”</strong>)."},{"t":"p","html":"In recent months, this young artist has triumphed in various competitions, ranging from her Trailblazing Performer accolade from the International Singer-Songwriters Association, her second-place finish in <strong>Omega’s Got Talent</strong>, to her Talent Preliminary Award in the <strong>Miss Georgia Teen Volunteer</strong> <strong>Competition</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Maria Deirisarri’s vibrant artiste meets the listener with a grace and uniqueness that is a breath of fresh air. Fans are eager to see what this up-and-coming superstar has up her sleeve. Her new album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2Wt1iciqQc7Uld2DNfPdvZ?si=NTLsWe2VRmmKfF15Mos3EA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>In The Beginning</strong></em></a><em><strong>&nbsp;</strong></em>officially released on September 29th and is now available for streaming on all platforms!&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Follow Maria below for all music updates and upcoming announcements.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vtuHVHOiQ7DqTk7B4Ycaz?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Maria!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/mariadeirisarri/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@mariadeirisarri","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@mariadeirisarri?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCtx5jhQ5a3Fx8_EJxh54WsA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/media/set/?set=a.2656672987691809&amp;type=3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"262713","title":"Rising Star Charlotte Sands Wins Grand Prize In 2023 Unsigned Only Music Competition","date":"2023-09-28","lead":"Judges include Robert Smith (The Cure), Aimee Mann, Rodney Atkins, Hillsong Worship, Walk The Moon, Morgan Wade, Sanctus Real, and more!","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/262713/c1466531144b43c3a5229a92c33bec31.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Judges include Robert Smith (The Cure), Aimee Mann, Rodney Atkins, Hillsong Worship, Walk The Moon, Morgan Wade, Sanctus Real, and more!<br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584848/large-7c8f993bfd9ecb5dc1cf374e1d8f2fa7.jpg","alt":"charlotte press 1 smaller.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"Nashville, TN (September 28, 2023) - The <a href=\"https://www.unsignedonly.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Unsigned Only Music Competition</strong></a>, renowned for celebrating the best of independent and unsigned artists, is pleased to announce the 2023 winners."},{"t":"p","html":"Established in 2012, this year’s competition garnered almost 6,000 entries from almost 100 countries, reflecting the immense pool of musical talent worldwide. Winners share in over $150,000 in cash and prizes are split among 38 winners, including a $20,000 (US) cash prize to the overall Grand Prize winner. In addition to cash and merchandise, winners receive invaluable exposure through press, social media, and more.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"It is with great pleasure that Unsigned Only bestows its highest honor, the overall Grand Prize, to <strong>Charlotte Sands</strong>, a Hopkinton, MA native who currently resides in Nashville, TN, for her upbeat, hit-worthy single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2ptbBxMTCbFBefVMXwrdSC?si=e906f83935054875\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dress</strong></a><strong>.”</strong><br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2ptbBxMTCbFBefVMXwrdSC?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"The winning song, written in response to the negativity surrounding <strong>Harry Styles</strong> wearing a dress on the cover of <strong>Vogue</strong>, went viral when it was released and became an anthem of self-expression for millions of listeners worldwide. The song has racked up more than 45 million plays on Spotify alone and has helped to launch Sands’ career. Since then, the electric blue-haired, tattooed singer/songwriter has put out a lot more singles, charted on <strong>Billboard</strong>, toured with <strong>Yungblud</strong>, amassed a legion of fans, and is embarking on a Fall tour in the US and Europe – all while remaining an indie artist. Raised on the pop-punk bands of the early 2000s and rooted in the storytelling of folk singer/songwriters, Sands combines upbeat melodies with unabashedly honest, self-reflective lyrics. Dubbed an<em>&nbsp;“unstoppable force”</em> by<strong>&nbsp;Alternative Press</strong>, Sands’ personal mission is to create a safe space for people to feel accepted and celebrated for their weirdness and diversity, and her fans take pride in championing her as they recognize how she champions them."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Charlotte Sands seems to be an unstoppable force of talent,”</em> said Co-Founders <strong>Candace Avery</strong> and <strong>Jim Morgan</strong>. <em>“Her music reflects the essence of what it means to be truly exceptional in the world of unsigned, indie artists. We are excited to see how she, as well as our other winners, will shape the future of the music industry.”</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to the Grand Prize winner, many other deserving artists garnered first and second-place wins in the competition. A winner was also selected in <strong>Fandemonium</strong>, Unsigned Only’s public, popular vote which is separate from the winners selected by the official judging panel. To see the winners and to listen to the winning songs, go to: <a href=\"https://www.unsignedonly.com/winners\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.unsignedonly.com/winners</a>.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"The complete panel of judges includes:<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Aimee Mann</strong>; <strong>Robert Smith</strong> <em>(The Cure)</em>; <strong>Rodney Atkins</strong>; <strong>Sanctus Real</strong>; <strong>I Am They</strong>; &nbsp;<strong>Darryl McDaniels</strong> <em>(Run DMC)</em>; <strong>O.A.R.</strong>; <strong>Nicholas Petricca&nbsp;</strong><em>(Walk The Moon)</em>; <strong>The Devil Makes Three</strong>; <strong>Janiva Magness</strong>; <strong>Morgan Wade</strong>; <strong>Gonzalo Rubalcaba</strong>; <strong>Paula Arenas</strong>; <strong>Ruthie Foster</strong>; <strong>Dame Evelyn Glennie</strong>; <strong>Kenny Barron</strong>; <strong>Derek Brown</strong> <em>(The Flaming Lips)</em>; <strong>Russ Landau</strong>; <strong>Zbigniew Preisner</strong>; <strong>Jay Allen</strong>; <strong>Francisca Valenzuela</strong>; <strong>David Benoit</strong>; <strong>Chaerin Kim</strong>; <strong>Vertical Worship</strong>; <strong>Tinariwen</strong>; <strong>Anthony DeCurtis</strong> (Contributing Editor, <strong>Rolling Stone</strong>); <strong>Lyndsey Parker</strong> (Managing Editor, <strong>Yahoo Music</strong>); <strong>Christopher Scapelliti</strong> (Editor-In-Chief, <strong>Guitar Player</strong>); <strong>Kevin McNeese</strong> (President, <strong>NewReleaseToday</strong>); <strong>Jeff Zuchowski&nbsp;</strong>(VP, Artist Marketing/Industry Relations, <strong>Pandora</strong>); <strong>John Dibiase</strong> (President, <strong>Jesus Freak Hideout</strong>); <strong>Angel Romero</strong> (Music Consultant); <strong>Hilary Saunders</strong> (Managing Editor, <strong>No Depession</strong>); <strong>Jason Lipshutz</strong> (Music Editor, <strong>Billboard</strong>); <strong>Cyrus Kyle Langhorne</strong> (Founder, <strong>AttackTheCulture.com</strong>); <strong>Art Tipaldi</strong> (Editor, <strong>Blues Music Magazine</strong>); <strong>Brandon Chitwood</strong> (Founder/Writer, <strong>The EDM Scholar</strong>); <strong>Michael West</strong> (Reviews Editor, <strong>DownBeat</strong>); <strong>David Silbaugh</strong> (Talent Buyer, <strong>Summerfest</strong>); <strong>Brinson Strickland</strong> (President, <strong>Collective Music Nashville</strong>); <strong>James Kempner</strong> (Owner, <strong>JMK Connections</strong>); <strong>Paul Riario</strong> (Tech Editor, <strong>Guitar World</strong>); <strong>Jennifer Taunton</strong> (Music Supervisor, <strong>Level Two Music</strong>); <strong>James Whitting</strong> (Partner, <strong>Paradigm Talent Agency</strong>); <strong>Paul De Barros&nbsp;</strong>(Pop Music Editor/Jazz Writer, <strong>Seattle Times</strong>); <strong>Alison Bonaguro</strong> (Freelance Country Music Journalist); <strong>Gaston Leone</strong> (Talent Buyer, <strong>Goldenvoice</strong>); <strong>Dylan Berry</strong> (Owner, <strong>SmashHaus</strong>); <strong>Mike Locke</strong> (VP, Creative Synchronization &amp; Marketing, <strong>Atlas Music</strong>); <strong>Mark Garfield</strong> (Co-Director, <strong>Pop-Up Music UK Ltd.</strong>); <strong>Debra Delshad </strong>(Sr. Director, Synchronization &amp; Licensing, <strong>Angry Mob Music</strong>); and <strong>Daryl Berg </strong>(VP, Music Strategies and Licensing Hallmark (<strong>Crown Media</strong>)."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584852/compressed_original-94c3fd9e615779a50ec309b719024e5d.png","alt":"logo.png"},{"t":"p","html":"Unsigned Only is sponsored by: <strong>ACE Products</strong> (Pig Hog Cables), <strong>Adam Audio</strong>, <strong>Alphabet Arm Design</strong>, <strong>Audix, Disc Makers</strong>, <strong>Eventric</strong>, <strong>Hiscox Cases</strong>, <strong>Image-Line Software</strong>, <strong>Joshua Tree Recording Studio</strong>, <strong>Ovation</strong>, <strong>Peavey Electronics</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;Play MPE</strong>, <strong>Protege</strong>, <strong>The Music Business Registry</strong>, <strong>WMR Music Group,</strong> and <strong>Süss Cookie Company</strong>.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>For more information and to enter, go to&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.unsignedonly.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.unsignedonly.com</a>.</em>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"262731","title":"Elder Grown Returns To Cervantes' Other Side As They Open For Illiterate Light","date":"2023-09-28","lead":"The audiences better be prepared for this highly-anticipated concert in celebration of Elder Grown's musical journey.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/262731/1a6635dba1392f0f261a752aec0f6cf6.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The audiences better be prepared for this highly-anticipated concert in celebration of Elder Grown's musical journey."},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (September 28, 2023) — Get ready for an electrifying evening of music as <a href=\"http://eldergrownmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Elder Grown</strong></a> makes their triumphant return to<strong>&nbsp;Cervantes’ Other Side</strong> in Denver, where they are set to open for <a href=\"https://cervantesmasterpiece.com/event/illiterate-light-w-elder-grown/cervantes-other-side/denver-colorado/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Illiterate Light</strong></a>, the small-town organic farmers turned major label rock stars. This highly-anticipated concert is a celebration of Elder Grown’s musical journey and an opportunity for music enthusiasts aged 16 and up to experience an unforgettable night of genre-defying music."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584855/large-24a905694de43287021c0076edfe9073.jpeg","alt":"Illiterate_525091692703220.jpeg"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Event Details:</strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Date</strong>: Saturday, November 04<br><strong>Venue</strong>: <a href=\"https://cervantesmasterpiece.com/venue/cervantes-other-side/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cervantes’ Other Side, 2635 Welton St., Denver, CO</a><br><strong>Doors Open</strong>: 7:00 PM<br><strong>Show Starts</strong>: 8:00 PM<br><strong>Ticket Price</strong>: $18 USD<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Elder Grown, known for their captivating live performances that seamlessly blend funk, rock, pop, and hip-hop, is back at Cervantes’ Other Side to take you on a musical journey that defies expectations. From the first note to the fourth hour, Elder Grown encourages you to break down your idea of genre and tempo with your hips and heartbeat. Their performances are like a personal <strong>Pandora </strong>station, rollercoastering listeners through seamless, rule-breaking sound."},{"t":"p","html":"Switching instruments mid-song, you never know who is going to sing or play what next at an Elder Grown performance. Their ability to captivate audiences and create an atmosphere of pure musical freedom is a testament to their unique talent.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"This performance at Cervantes’ Other Side holds special significance as Elder Grown returns to the venue where they’ve left a lasting impression on fans and fellow musicians alike. Their journey has been marked by relentless dedication to their craft, and their return to the Cervantes stage is a momentous occasion for both the band and their devoted followers."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584859/large-10288638cc74cc7802e6952c6110acf4.jpg","alt":"EH3A8909 (1).jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"As a perfect prelude to the night, Illiterate Light, known for their electrifying live performances and genre-blending sound, will be headlining the event. Mixing soaring indie rock, swirling psychedelia, and atmospheric folk into a captivating blend, Illiterate Light’s music is a fitting complement to Elder Grown’s boundary-pushing style."},{"t":"p","html":"This event is open to music lovers aged 16 and up, offering an opportunity for fans of all ages to come together and enjoy an evening of remarkable music. With a limited number of tickets available, it is advisable to purchase them in advance to secure your spot at this highly anticipated concert.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Tickets can be purchased online at <em><a href=\"https://cervantesmasterpiece.com/event/illiterate-light-w-elder-grown/cervantes-other-side/denver-colorado/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.cervantesmasterpiece.com/event/illiterate-light-w-elder-grown/cervantes-other-side/denver-colorado/</a> </em>or at the venue’s box office on the day of the event."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Elder Grown:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Elder Grown</strong> is a genre-defying band that combines funk, rock, pop, and hip-hop, offering a unique and improvisational musical experience. Their captivating live performances and seamless sound have made them a fan favorite, and their return to Cervantes’ Other Side is a testament to their enduring musical journey. To learn more, visit <a href=\"https://eldergrownmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.eldergrownmusic.com/</a>."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Cervantes’ Other Side:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Cervantes’ Other Side</strong> is a renowned live music venue located in the heart of Denver, Colorado. With a commitment to showcasing diverse musical acts and providing an intimate concert experience, Cervantes’ Other Side has become a beloved destination for music lovers in the area. To learn more, visit <a href=\"https://cervantesmasterpiece.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.cervantesmasterpiece.com/</a>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Elder Grown!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2FElderGrown%2Fposts%2Fpfbid02P8t6BR1S1Lx3hVSKFvvWGpis5QZLMF7NHCFY3HxCqVnMUJ7MEUjFCtuEC3Dvp2SUl&show_text=true&width=500","height":"629"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/ElderGrown\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ElderGrown/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>| <a href=\"https://www.bandsintown.com/a/1142918?came_from=257\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">bandsintown</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/album/elder-grown/1376637581\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Apple</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"260986","title":"Karmic Neighborhood Releases Preview Soundtrack Album for Upcoming Feature Film, \"Equinox the Musical\"","date":"2023-09-22","lead":"California-based musical duo are set to release the official preview soundtrack on Friday, September 22nd","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/260986/56e5b5110a92b90cca28c8b8a1261aa2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"California-based musical duo are set to release the official preview soundtrack on Friday, September 22nd"},{"t":"p","html":"Royal Oaks, CA (September 22, 2023) - <strong>Armand Ruby</strong> and <strong>Julian Colbeck</strong> of musical group <a href=\"https://karmicneighborhood.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karmic Neighborhood</strong></a> are officially releasing the <a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/EquinoxtheMusicalPreviewSoundtrack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">preview soundtrack album</a> for their upcoming feature film, <a href=\"https://equinoxmusical.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Equinox the Musical</strong></em></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>on the fall equinox: Friday, September 22nd. The 14-track album complements the feature film in conveying the story of two homeless young lovers who discover that forgiveness, gratitude and love can be the keys to navigating life’s most challenging circumstances. Some cosmic themes featured within the album include perseverance, forgiveness, gratitude, love, selflessness, and every emotion in between."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Equinox the Musical is music with a mission. On the one hand, it's jam-packed with catchy rock songs and stellar performances. And on the other, it lives in the serious context of the unhoused, with compassion and dignity.”","cite":"- Julian Colbeck, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"p","html":"Twice a year, on the spring and fall equinox, there is equal time split between day and night. This worldwide equilibrium of darkness and light paints a picture of balance. <a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/EquinoxtheMusicalPreviewSoundtrack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Equinox the Musical Preview Soundtrack</strong></em></a><em>&nbsp;</em>asks listeners defining questions like:<em>&nbsp;</em><em>“How do we cope with the stressors that threaten to push us off our stride?” </em>or, <em>“How does someone in less fortunate circumstances maintain any sense of balance in the daily struggle just to survive?”</em> Karmic Neighborhood seeks to emphasize that everyone has a story, no matter how apparent it may be on the surface. Equinox the Musical reveals the stories of four homeless individuals - two young lovers with troubled pasts, an elderly wise woman who has lost everything except her dignity, and an attorney recovering from the depths of addiction - and the people who support them on their way. The public face of homelessness is too often someone suffering from serious mental health issues or addiction, but many others endure the indignities of a life gone awry with a quiet dignity. At a time of great social upheaval, the world needs to see and hear this tale of compassion and perseverance in the face of conflict."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/583494/compressed_original-b983140d1c0235e39778c6692fdc6450.jpg","alt":"Equinox the Musical Preview Soundtrack Cover Art"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Spanning the range of human emotions - from deepest despair to tenderest romantic love to an ebullient celebration of life - Equinox the Musical is a roller coaster ride through the human condition in the current era.”","cite":"- Armand Ruby, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"p","html":"The 14 songs on the Equinox Preview Soundtrack album are sung by a diverse set of characters in a variety of settings, with a wide range of musical styles, all helping to tell the film’s story. The record begins with the exuberant, electrified dance tune, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7i1al6cU34Y5CNTDPuJV3d?si=0120a739aa644ce8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>It's a New Day</strong></a><strong>”</strong>, introducing listeners to the musical film's cast of characters. The groovy, Latin-inspired song <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/06p06hjFNIOHdttT1dBl8U?si=107535c0af3c4d49\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>How Do I Start Over?</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is sung by two middle-aged social service professionals who harbor a secret attraction. The rest of the preview soundtrack traverses a wide range of genres and is concluded with the closing ensemble number, <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6i0sjJFTqCkp9VbWsnpfaW?si=88ce4e8d500e487d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Equinox</strong></a>.”&nbsp;</strong>The frenetic Surf-rock tune <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5deV6AHfUs5sVTgudrBZLZ?si=d57f7135d84c464f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Living Loving</strong></a><strong>”</strong> acts a coda and will play during the film's credits."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/u4Nc6j1RSb4?si=ajOaaXXqFFvFtbpK","height":"400"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Karmic Neighborhood:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Armand Ruby&nbsp;</strong>and<strong>&nbsp;Julian Colbeck</strong>, the core duo behind <a href=\"https://karmicneighborhood.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karmic Neighborhood</strong></a>, have taken very different paths to the present moment. The West Coast-based team are two lifelong musicians who met by chance when they moved to the same neighborhood on the central California coast. Julian began his career as a London-based keyboardist and is an accomplished, lifelong music industry veteran, while Armand worked professionally as an environmental scientist in the U.S. and stayed involved in music as a part-time musician and songwriter. Armand and Julian formed a strong bond through their shared passion for music and their painful yet hopeful life experiences of surviving cancer. The two rhythmic alt-pop collaborators found inspiration within the harmony of their own respective life journeys and a mutual interest in musical innovation.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vnYPcPpvzO0hhjR6YMUkV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Armand Ruby:"},{"t":"p","html":"Like many creatives, Armand was a sensitive child. Growing up, this was of course a blessing and a curse, in the face of both the world’s beauty and its harshness. Throughout his childhood in the northeastern United States, Armand was aware that maintaining this sensitivity might be a challenge. So keeping this cherished inner life alive became a lifelong ambition – and it found expression through music and songwriting. Armand wrote his first little tune at the age of 11, and as a teenager began composing songs, something he’s continued to do throughout life. But his musical talent was matched by a proclivity for science, and a scholarship to an Ivy League university led to a career as an Environmental Scientist."},{"t":"p","html":"Still, Armand continued to be active musically: songwriting, recording demos, performing in rock bands no one’s ever heard of, leading small choral groups, and for several years even singing in a professional opera chorus. A breakthrough came in 2010-2011 with the writing of the book and songs for a musical stage play, <strong>“Equinox.”</strong> Directing the play in its brief but sold-out run in Santa Cruz California was, according to Armand, <em>“both the most difficult and most rewarding experience of my life.”&nbsp;</em>With Equinox, Armand finds himself working at the creative intersection of art and social activism – shining a new light on the often out-of-sight homeless population and the many ways people can become homeless, through story and music. Moving in 2019 to the rural Monterey Bay area community of Royal Oaks, Armand found that one of his neighbors, Julian Colbeck, was an experienced music arranger, producer and keyboardist. From that auspicious meeting arose the musical partnership known as&nbsp;<a href=\"https://karmicneighborhood.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Karmic Neighborhood</a>.<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Julian Colbeck:"},{"t":"p","html":"Julian Colbeck grew up in the south of England, where he learned how to play the piano and ultimately pursued his dreams of being in a London-based rock ‘n’ roll band in his late teens. Julian’s music career took off with the band <em><strong>Charlie</strong></em>, with whom he scored several US Top 40 singles including <strong>“Watching TV”</strong> and <strong>“LA Dreamer.”</strong> Over the span of a 40-year career, Julian worked and toured as a keyboard player/producer with <strong>YES&nbsp;</strong>alumni group <strong>Anderson Bruford Wakeman Howe</strong>, former Genesis guitarist <strong>Steve Hackett</strong>, <strong>Charlie</strong>, <strong>John Miles</strong>, and more. In 2008 Julian began work with his long-time friend, <strong>Alan Parsons</strong>, on the award-winning instructional video series: <a href=\"https://www.artandscienceofsound.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Alan Parsons’ The Art &amp; Science Of Sound Recording</strong></a>. Julian also has written for many esteemed music industry publications and has authored many music and music technology books. Beginning in late 2019, and interrupted by intensive treatment for stage 4 cancer, Julian saw something of value in his neighbor Armand Ruby’s songwriting and his <em>Equinox&nbsp;</em>film project and worked as an arranger, co-producer, and keyboardist on the Equinox preview soundtrack recordings."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Karmic Neighborhood!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2FtheKarmicNeighborhood%2Fposts%2Fpfbid035RCGoegwKBZCjVCwiN8S16hxphXEKjCbwx1YpMFZsRv6uRFvLmZnfNC9kaAotiDdl&show_text=true&width=500","height":"498"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/karmicneighborhood/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@karmicneighborhood","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/karmicneighborhood/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100082755791779\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | </strong><a href=\"mailto:armand@armandrubymusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>EMAIL</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"260989","title":"Indie Artist Horseshoes Drops New Single, \"L.A.\"","date":"2023-09-22","lead":"The Indie-Rock singer releases a new track exploring the dissonance between authenticity and superficiality.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/260989/016e0fbc0ac876138de999beb048383b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Indie-Rock singer releases a new track exploring the dissonance between authenticity and superficiality."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4NGxseYp3FrD82SULfj0jI?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Washington, DC (September 22, 2023) - Indie-Rock artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0cIVB4MH1nJhx5soIMZeKt?si=0RHAiQQVTNuyK96Ks7il5Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Horseshoes</strong></a>&nbsp;drops a new song, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/LA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>L.A</strong></a>.<strong>”&nbsp;</strong>on Friday, September 22. “L.A.” explores the dissonance between authenticity and superficiality, and how we are supposed to navigate those themes throughout our lives.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"“L.A.” acts as a deep five into the feelings one experiences when feeling the pressure to do what they're told. Over a tumultuous sonic journey with strong lead vocals, classy piano riffs, and soft instrumentals, this track concludes with the notion that it is better to just be who you are rather than try to conform to who others want you to be."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Authenticity and staying true to oneself is the silver lining within this song, which I hope listeners can resonate with.”","cite":"- Horseshoes, Indie-Rock Artist"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/LA","label":"Listen to \"L.A.\" on All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Picture a clear and sunny day in Los Angeles where no one seems to have a care in the world. Now picture a crowd of those people smiling and laughing, and imagine the one person who feels stuck in a pool of people who don't understand what it feels like to be depressed. Horseshoes highlights the reality of struggling to force yourself to be happy, just because being unhappy doesn't seem to fit the norm."},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong><u>\"LA\" LYRICS</u></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Depression in the sun</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>And it's raining down roses on everyone</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Watch them wither on the ground</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Detached at the stem, never knew when you became unbound</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>The angels are overcome</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>They've seen it all before but now you've come to settle the score</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>The oasis is in a drought</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>They said \"keep it moving, don't shout, get clever and figure it out\"</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Calm and steady when you're ready</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Please strike a pose</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Early morning sun's a warning</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>To do what your told</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>But I'd rather die</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Than spend a life time</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Trying to become</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Some other guy</em><br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581863/-425e83fafab696368495d60c56d61fcd.jpeg","alt":"original-24b2dd890e38da8d880275178a9a4dd1.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581863/-425e83fafab696368495d60c56d61fcd.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581864/-a44c6ad05a7ada4e81a9b3cf8f6dea95.jpeg","alt":"original-5552a690295dfef74777b49f4ad791f4.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581864/-a44c6ad05a7ada4e81a9b3cf8f6dea95.jpeg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Horseshoes:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Austin Greaves&nbsp;</strong>is a Washington DC-based musician who performs under the name <strong>Horseshoes</strong>. He released his debut album, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4X4f7fYdW98GedO8tKDh0T?si=Up5VrHYbT2GqWrpxmlxw2w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Desert</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> in June of 2022, which was followed up with a single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4x86xnafoYR0SDd6RvYQbz?si=wNflVB0YS2O8CfEQE-T8Pw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Come With Me</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> released in October 2022. You can stream Horseshoes’ recently released singles <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/29zUzEi2MIZA5NhbWUaREp?si=41ded00bd6434e5c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hide and Seek</strong></a>”</strong> and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3NCMYYe6cYK4pVQzEbs9lV?si=TCj02gYjSYSQyTXNK3aaPw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Say What You Mean</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on all platforms now. Horseshoes releases his new track <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4NGxseYp3FrD82SULfj0jI?si=ce35d7b0b0aa468c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“L.A.”</strong></a> on Friday, September 22.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"To stay updated on all announcements and updates, follow Horseshoes on his social media channels linked below!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Horseshoes!"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@horseshoesguy/video/7258329364922649902","handle":"@horseshoesguy"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/horseshoesguy/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@horseshoesguy","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@horseshoesguy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/horseshoesguy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"261812","title":"Alaskan Indie Artist Dreamcat Drops Electrifying EP \"Juicebox\"","date":"2023-09-22","lead":"The 3-track EP delivers a bright and uplifting soundscape brimming with hope to listeners.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/261812/2f1bc3e844fa56b0cb523ab1ee1ecce8.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The 3-track EP delivers a bright and uplifting soundscape brimming with hope to listeners."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1iSdXxKobqg4jieXSskiHn?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Anchorage, ALASKA (September 22, 2023) - Synth-Pop sensation, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3K9fTRuyA2UY0vs4ncFs3p?si=tB6jUwJURZGwM7VbBh6YkQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>dreamcat</strong></a>, is all set to enchant fans with his new EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1iSdXxKobqg4jieXSskiHn?si=5GHhfNqTTLmCcjkD7j07BQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Juicebox</strong></em></a>. Released on September 22, 2023, this fresh collection of songs promises to deliver a bright and uplifting soundscape brimming with hope."},{"t":"p","html":"Drawing inspiration from artists like<strong>&nbsp;Empire of the Sun, MGMT</strong>, and <strong>STRFKR</strong>, dreamcat's music offers a mesmerizing and invigorating take on electronic and pop genres. With grace and finesse, dreamcat examines notions of friendship, self-discovery, and sobriety, while daring to want something more. <em>Juicebox</em> captures the essence of finding new ways to experience the joy of life and emphasizes the importance of friendship and love."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/161169JuiceBox","label":"Listen to \"Juice Box\" on All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"“It's not always easy coming up with a positive, universal theme for a song or EP. Juicebox connects complex emotions in one sonic dosage of reality.\"","cite":"- dreamcat, Indie-Pop artist"},{"t":"p","html":"Such themes are brilliantly expressed on the EP’s opening song <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7u9rm65B7VXTGOPpTNjd3d?si=d4f50e011da44c33\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Best Friend</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> a heartfelt and number that conveys a depth of emotion simply and succinctly. Written for his girlfriend, “Best Friend” serves as a grateful acknowledgment of her unwavering love and support during turbulent times, including dreamcat’s own rollercoaster path to sobriety.&nbsp;"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>“Best Friend” Lyrics</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Sometimes I feel like something's missing maybe<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"It must be my best friend<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"And when you're feelin' like a low down junkie<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"You know I'm your best friend<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"And if you need a little plane ride money<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Just call your best friend<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"And if you think that something might be funny<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Tell me, I'm your best friend<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"And when you feel a little low down honey<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"You know I'm your best friend<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3K9fTRuyA2UY0vs4ncFs3p?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/583891/large-afe6567238f7f6e26bef648667af7d84.jpg","alt":"Rock1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/583891/preview-8a6c788210840a30966d0654fb93f3cf.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/583892/large-a17eb4520e280945334ae15e292f7674.jpg","alt":"treefront_edit1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/583892/preview-f025fba9cd946a070a44804637a837ee.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/583893/large-ddf0a54de695f9b307a6ffcaecb60a71.jpg","alt":"Rock2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/583893/preview-54098c933068108e599ea2bb3085e6b6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/583894/large-ce59a2d5757b10da89b907327b119e31.jpg","alt":"UnderTree_edit2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/583894/preview-0be16ba0802cf257dd75b78ceee8e525.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About dreamcat:"},{"t":"p","html":"dreamcat AKA <strong>Colton Ciufo</strong> has loved performing and creating music since childhood. As a result of taking piano lessons as a kid, dreamcat played synth in a metal band with his friends, performing and playing some of his first shows when he was only 17. dreamcat has carefully curated his niche within the music industry and has fine-tuned his songwriting over the years. Music has always been dreamcat's escape, using creativity as a means for coping with alcoholism, social anxiety, and depression. Since attending a rehab facility in Southern California, dreamcat has been going through positive psychological, lifestyle, and spiritual changes. dreamcat's purpose is to make positive yet heartfelt music that makes him feel good and inspires listeners from whatever place they find themselves in life. Tune in to dreamcat's new EP,<strong> <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1iSdXxKobqg4jieXSskiHn?si=dYawvdNMR56hjYKSdtZOBw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Juicebox</em></a></strong>!<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with dreamcat!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/dreamcat123456/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@dreamcat123456","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"261993","title":"View BRII_music’s Linktree. Listen to their music on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music here.","date":"2023-09-22","lead":"The new track captures the listeners' ears with the sensation of falling in love.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/261993/51df67f5cdb0cec46222a3ea6459e4fe.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new track captures the listeners' ears with the sensation of falling in love."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7g01ix2sbZZ7ou1YPVuJJf?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, CA (September 22, 2023) - Los Angeles-based R&amp;B artist, <strong>Brii Elliss</strong>, is certain to entice music lovers with her most recent single, &nbsp;<strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7g01ix2sbZZ7ou1YPVuJJf?si=df0db461bd3a4a42\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Follow</strong></a><strong>.”</strong> The song sets out to capture the magical sensation of falling madly in love."},{"t":"p","html":"Alluring and innocent, “Follow” is a musical delight that was written about the process of discovering that Elliss’ current boyfriend is in fact “the one” - despite outside skepticism.<br>"},{"t":"lead","html":"\"FOLLOW\" LYRICS<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I will follow you where you’re goin’</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>And I’m one step behind don’t you know it</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Cuz life without you can’t imagine</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I don’t think I could go back</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>And I’ll follow you where you’re goin</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>&nbsp;Some call it a honeymoon phase</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>But feels like I’ve been with you for ages</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>You’re the song that I can’t unwrite</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>It’s been keeping me up at night</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Can’t believe that you chose me</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Never mad babe you froze me</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>In the best type of way</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>You chilled all the hate and now I’m exploding<br></em><br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5OVMuAGwhVrQZ8xG7bgVOs?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I meant for this project to put a self-empowerment spin on the classic love song. I wanted the listener to feel like they should never settle for anything less than they deserve.”","cite":"- Brii Elliss, Indie-Pop Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"With masterfully crafted hooks, Elliss has created a track that is just as much R&amp;B as it is sugary sweet Pop. The chill and relaxed vibe feels as breezy as a summer Sunday afternoon. “Follow” constructs a sunny yet soothing aura that is sure to leave listeners smitten.<br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/583905/large-2d5d65d799faa45c56c8bafb7178e5ee.jpg","alt":"\"Follow\" Cover Art by ______"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493573/large-276587b288ad68337779672cb896ff43.png","alt":"Solitaire Album Cover (1) (1).png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493573/preview-52f2715aec70fb0df5553e1273b406cb.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493569/original-0fac4c5e609b66d6ad2650644ecee1f5.jpg","alt":"image1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493569/preview-d2a6069f439b98a6aca929683a013c00.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493572/large-d883208c47a7d4c95818624439f43678.jpg","alt":"image3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493572/preview-aa31b9efe598fce3f2f7035c4217aaa0.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494963/large-168106205206004a1a9515720f0a1e4a.jpg","alt":"_MG_1165.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494963/preview-e43dc142f9f8c92abe736bfa147849fc.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494964/large-b3639cf8865a92baffc41bb10995f905.jpg","alt":"_MG_1018.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494964/preview-4e89be11b59fb880e172f45f32ee99c3.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brii Elliss:"},{"t":"p","html":"Up-and-coming pop artist Brii Elliss is a singer-songwriter who brings a certain closeness to her lyrics, giving testament to the power of storytelling in music. With an Irish father and Puerto Rican mother, her voice and life experiences create a unique blend that filters into her songs effortlessly, showcasing a sultry R&amp;B chill-pop soundscape that captivates and entrances listeners. Working with Grammy-winning producer <strong>Synematik&nbsp;</strong>to create her signature buttery sound, Brii pulls inspiration from artists like <strong>Amber Mark, H.E.R., Snoh Aalegra, Jhene Aiko</strong>, and <strong>Jazmine Sullivan</strong>, with a deeply rich tone that is quickly creating a buzz in the music community. A New Jersey native who has been singing since she can remember, Brii was on the path to stardom by the age of 12, having already auditioned for the famed X-Factor show and made it through several rounds. Throughout high school, she continued pursuing this passion by writing new songs and recording them, honing her piano skills, and preparing to move to LA where she attended college at <strong>Loyola Marymount University</strong> and graduated with her Bachelor's degree in music. As she began to record her own music she realized how much she needed music to be center stage in her life.&nbsp;<em>“I'm in my element when I am recording and surrounded by other creatives. It feels like home to me, and it's still my happy place today.”&nbsp;</em>Needless to say, her happiness and passion in the studio shines through her work as her debut single garnered over 17K streams upon release while showcasing her authentic songwriting and silky low voice. Fans have already started rallying behind her and eagerly anticipate what's to come next for this budding artist. Lucky for them, Brii has lots of new music up her sleeve for 2023 and plans to share her soulful vibe with the world... one song at a time."},{"t":"p","html":"Brii Elliss officially releases her EP, <em><strong>Follow&nbsp;</strong></em>on Nov 17th. Her title track for the album, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7g01ix2sbZZ7ou1YPVuJJf?si=c0750a42e9e54cb2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Follow</strong></a><strong>”</strong> releases on Friday, September 22nd. For all updates and announcements, make sure to keep up with Brii on her social media pages, linked below!"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Brii Elliss!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://linktr.ee/BRII_music","img":"","title":"View BRII_music’s Linktree. Listen to their music on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music here.","desc":""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/iGWGsuYX-EA?si=g2sJbcp3sQ_RoKTF","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/brii_elliss/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@brii_elliss","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.briielliss.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@brii_elliss\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tik Tok</a>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@briielliss\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"262212","title":"Official website of Lola Kristine: singer, pianist, and composer based in Southern California.","date":"2023-09-22","lead":"The Laguna Beach songwriter showcases her unique indie folk, country-esque style with two captivating singles, \"California Cowboy\" and \"You and Me\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/template_background/262212/5aa62377f3bdd42f1a99dbf67035ea09.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Laguna Beach songwriter showcases her unique indie folk, country-esque style with two captivating singles, \"California Cowboy\" and \"You and Me\"<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"LAGUNA BEACH, CA (September 22, 2023) - <em>Chapter 1: Rose Colored Glasses</em> is a significant milestone for Lola Kristine as she takes listeners on a personal journey into her world. Offering a fresh sound that blends elements of pop, adult contemporary, Americana, R&amp;B, and country rock, this chapter sets the stage for a heartfelt story of redemption, exploring themes of falling in love, romance, and new beginnings. With her soulful voice and captivating lyrics, Lola Kristine invites the audience to experience the magic and vulnerability of love.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/12lQLBgFlI6FdVt5kVoXA6?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The first tease of her upcoming album <em>CHAPTERS</em>, <em>Chapter 1</em> consists of two standout singles, \"California Cowboy\" and \"You and Me\". \"California Cowboy\" introduces listeners to Lola's enchanting storytelling, as she shares her experience of falling in love too fast. The song, which started as a sweet love song on the piano, evolves into a country rock anthem, showcasing Lola's versatility as an artist. \"If you need any help with the imagery of what a California Cowboy looks like, think silk pajamas with a Bass Pro Shop trucker hat and a Bud Light on ice. Classy yet down-home country,\" says Lola Kristine. \"Being a Midwestern transplant to California myself, you can see why I fell head over heels.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"\"You and Me\" takes on a cozy and sweet R&amp;B groove, creating the perfect backdrop for a romantic morning with a lover. With its soulful, cute, and dreamy vibe, the song captures the essence of Lola Kristine's unique style. \"Falling in love can be a pretty addicting feeling. I know I have been blinded by it many times. I’d find myself getting swept up in the idea of someone, rather than the person that is actually in front of me,” says Lola , remarking on some of the inspiration behind the songs.<br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584163/large-3d380ccea3f18e4d268c6d1c97dfc3c0.jpg","alt":"Cover art for 'Chapter 1: Rose Colored Glasses' by Lola Kristine"},{"t":"p","html":"Scheduled for release on September 22, 2023,&nbsp;<em>Chapter 1: Rose Colored Glasses</em> will be available on Spotify, Apple Music, and all major platforms as fans and general listeners alike can look forward to immersing themselves in Lola Kristine's heartfelt storytelling and soulful melodies. With 'Chapter 1', Lola Kristine sets the stage for an album that promises to captivate and inspire. “The songs on Chapter One really capture the innocent, sweet, starry-eyed mood of a fresh romance,\" says Lola Kristine of the new release. \"I wrote them at a time when life sent me a very potent muse. Little did I know during those first precious moments with him that this man would unearth so much within me and be a major catalyst for transformation in my life.\"<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\">"},{"t":"h3","html":"About &#39;CHAPTERS&#39;"},{"t":"p","html":"Soulful songstress, Lola Kristine, is taking listeners on a personal journey into her world with the songs on her upcoming album, <em>CHAPTERS</em>. After two successful EP releases, Lola decided to take on the challenge of creating a full-length album. Stepping into the role of primary producer and songwriter for this project, Lola will be sharing a more intimate experience of her soul’s expression than ever before. &nbsp;The album is broken up into five chapters that tell a heartfelt story of redemption. &nbsp;Beginning with her experience of falling in love too fast and getting her heart broken yet again after a painful divorce, the album then dives deeper beneath the surface into the heart of the wild woman. Chapter 3 represents a major turnaround in Lola’s life as she began to reconnect with herself and reclaim her power. Finding true healing within opened the door for a new kind of relationship to emerge. &nbsp;The listener is then invited to feel the purity of a joy-filled romance, where it’s safe to be who you are. &nbsp;The final chapter brings us onto a new shore, beyond the illusion of painful stories of the past. &nbsp;Lola’s album rings out with a clear message: True love will set us free.<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584164/large-e5808947d3d37bc884029569bbcaa654.jpg","alt":"IMG_8673.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584164/preview-711fc68b8607ef1026eab77eaf78b923.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584165/large-681c1ace08691f5d1d98c9e132b15daf.jpg","alt":"IMG_8854.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584165/preview-30ab94b10c3b1d7f7c4252f76eebb21e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584166/large-c99003dc237595c08e7b1a280afa32ec.jpg","alt":"IMG_8774.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584166/preview-de212dced0ef265484d13f8530d40c21.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584167/large-f821f30371443470d22b2cd2f82c1f6f.jpg","alt":"IMG_8664.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/584167/preview-14d4629bd8ece50ea51ab9f288f32f64.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lola Kristine"},{"t":"p","html":"Lola Kristine is a singer, pianist and songwriter based in Laguna Beach, California. &nbsp;Known as “the little girl with the big voice,” Lola has been staggering audiences her whole life with the depth of soul she possesses in both her timeless songwriting and penetrating singing. &nbsp;Hearing her sing feeds your soul and reconnects you with what is right in the world. &nbsp;<br>From humble beginnings in St. Louis, Missouri, Lola has taken her music across the country, touring with noted musicians such as Premik Russell Tubbs (Santana, Sting, James Taylor), Jeff Haynes (Joni Mitchell, Herbie Hancock) and bass virtuoso Michael Manring. &nbsp; She has collaborated with artists from all over the world, including Kinobe (Uganda) in a series sponsored by American Voices. In 2022, a live video of Lola performing went viral on TikTok, hitting 4.5M views which boosted her online presence. She is gaining notoriety amidst legendary rockstars such as Mick Fleetwood and Don Cromwell of Air Supply. She is currently living in Southern California, where she can be found performing at venues and clubs all up and down the coast.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Lola has also gained notoriety as a songwriter and original artist. She was a Top Ten Finalist in the 2015 Wildflower! Songwriting Competition in Richardson, Texas. &nbsp;She was chosen as “Artist of the Week” in Coming Up Magazine in May 2017. Her debut EP has received recognition from Los Angeles music blogs, local radio play and placement on prominent Spotify playlists. Her song \"Bring My Baby Back to Me\" was a selected as a finalist in the International Songwriting Competition. &nbsp;Her 2020 album project From Darkness to Light gained international attention with top plays in UK and Indonesia. Each single was accompanied by a blog post. In 2022, Lola collaborated with long time friend Justin Froese on a project called \"Willow and the Wave.\" &nbsp;They released an album of meditative and inspiring pieces. &nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"When off the stage, Lola works as a studio musician: session singing, arranging, coaching and playing keyboard. &nbsp;She has worked with Grammy-award winning producers. &nbsp;You can hear her voice on Season 5 Episode 3 of DC’s Legends of Tomorrow as Ava Sharpe’s voice singing “Poison” on the CW network. &nbsp;She was featured on Todd Mosby’s Open Waters (winner of ZMR’s Best Contemporary Instrumental Album) produced by Will Ackerman. &nbsp;She also plays a unique new instrument called the handpan and is a sponsored Novapans artist.&nbsp;<br>Lola is a Summa Cum Laude graduate from Webster University with a degree in Jazz Performance and Composition. When she is not performing, Lola coaches, teaches private lessons and holds workshops. &nbsp;She also loves surfing and yoga.<br>Lola’s true passion lies in the healing art of music. &nbsp;She first fell in love with music in the church. Her music is the most pure form of her soul's expression. &nbsp; Her desire is to use music as a unifying and activating force. &nbsp; She is finding ways to bridge her passion for music with the causes she believes in. &nbsp;Lola wrote 'Power of the People' inspired by the Black Lives Matter movement in 2020, premiering it at a protest in Anaheim, CA. &nbsp;She created a music video with footage from the protest that was then featured in Voice of OC news. &nbsp; Lola's powerful song 'We Are One' was featured on lran TV Network as part of the Woman Life Freedom movement in 2022. &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Her next project, entitled <em>CHAPTERS</em>, will be released over the coming months. This is the first full-length album she has written and produced as a solo artist.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lola Kristine:"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.musicoflola.com/","img":"","title":"Official website of Lola Kristine: singer, pianist, and composer based in Southern California.","desc":""},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"http://instagram.com/musicoflola\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC7LAxI_AIC0YgeP0CcLYNOw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube&nbsp;</a>| <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2YGZ6KlNauWge3ZJXxQ0Ns?si=hmR1xgocRoqKVRInC1oRqQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spotify</a>"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"259919","title":"Jazz Rock Band The Erly Launches New Track, \"Flame The Main\"","date":"2023-09-20","lead":"The Erly releases their new jazzy single ahead of their upcoming LP, 'Culture Fever.'","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/259919/7394f4f5fdc137da0d379f6d1a778e96.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Erly releases their new jazzy single ahead of their upcoming LP, 'Culture Fever.'"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3aITimGk0InPUdYHaW49UZ?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Niles, MI (September 20, 2023) - Michigan-based Disco quartet,<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://theerlyband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Erly</strong></a>, drops their new song <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3aITimGk0InPUdYHaW49UZ?si=977a83a3142c4644\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Flame The Main</a>”</strong> on Wednesday, September 20. “Flame The Main” is the fourth single to be released from The Erly’s upcoming album, <em><strong>Culture Fever</strong>,&nbsp;</em>which will be available on November 3, 2023.<em>&nbsp;</em>The music video for “Flame The Main” will be released within the next few months following the song's release."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“Flame The Main”</strong> sounds like the dive bar in town that stays open until the sun comes up. It smells like an ashtray and tastes like a shot of bourbon followed by lager. It sounds like a vintage Cadillac echoing off the buildings of Main Street at 4 a.m. It has the sonic essence of a riverboat casino and echoes like the shouts of shady characters clutching to their questionable aspirations and vices. The band wrote “Flame The Main” about someone who is thrown into a scene of turmoil, which leads to a plethora of self-destructive activities. Avoiding important issues, drug/alcohol abuse, chasing intangible dreams, and insecurity are all themes explored within this new rock track."},{"t":"p","html":"In order to convey their message in the right light, The Erly made sure to include an abundance of attitude within this single. The drums have a slight swing, the guitar shimmers in the heat, and the organ roars. The vocals are crusty, yet humid. The horns are blasting and in your face."},{"t":"quote","html":"“From horns and intertwined keyboards to auxiliary percussion and strong lead vocals, this is the most layered track we have created to date. The heart of this single is a live band sound, strategically enhanced by nuanced bells and whistles of the recording process.”","cite":"- The Erly, Disco Band"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3QPLdBDMCs5nyauZZMX7IW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580111/large-1391af554d2814f05cf459bfdea1e33d.jpg","alt":"FLAM1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580111/preview-c6e2e995ba84440d6a89c3bfed11e0b6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580113/original-058c0adcd67897cc6c1a6290713c257f.jpg","alt":"FLAME2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580113/preview-cf6d31436c834a337913d04e33057385.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580114/large-34a5c54b2165cbe1c275ac368565ef24.jpg","alt":"FLAME4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580114/preview-d9795994509c0bd4012272fcfacd9c40.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580112/large-f07f1c63c3a96d78af130655759085a6.jpg","alt":"FLAME3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/580112/preview-590f7669822045afa671103be5a5505a.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"PHOTO CREDIT: KELSIE HERZOG"},{"t":"p","html":"The Erly’s drummer <strong>Fran Gleason</strong> is featured on vocals for this track, and even inspired the name, “Flame The Main.” The phrase “Flame The Main” was a common phrase from Gleason's family back in Bradford, PA in reference to cruising down Main Street in the 1970s. Produced by <strong>Nick Rapley</strong>, the song features a horn section and various key changes, as well as many unique percussion elements such as a bottle of <strong>Snoop Dogg</strong>’s wine.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Flame The Main” is a main character song, transporting listeners to Los Angeles in the 70s - the era of hot rods and radio classics. The chorus beckons a cruise down a main drag preferably at sunset or the dead of night.”","cite":"- The Erly, Disco Band"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Erly:"},{"t":"p","html":"Michigan-based Indie-Soul group <strong>The Erly</strong> combines sonic elements from the ‘60s and ‘70s Rock, Pop, and Funk, creating a fresh<em>&nbsp;“Modern Disco”</em> sound and vibe of their own. Fueled by collaboration, friendship, and timeless good vibes, the quartet would fit right in at Woodstock ‘69 or at the indie nerve center that is <strong>SXSW</strong>. Most of <strong>The Erly</strong>’s music features clean guitar work, layered vocals, and groovy undertones that energize even their most solemn-sounding tracks. The band is composed of Drummer <strong>Fran Gleason</strong>, Bassist <strong>Collin Mattiford</strong>, Guitarist <strong>Trevor McDonald,</strong> and Keyboardist <strong>Alyssa Serviss</strong>, with all 4 members featured on vocals. <strong>The Erly</strong> was created in 2018 when Mattiford and Gleason decided to expand upon their pre-established musical duo. Since their formation in 2018, <strong>The Erly</strong> has released two full albums and four singles with more music on the way. <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0QzfIYmj30ksSmpWPrhxpm?si=80a4bb72f7aa48fc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Paralyzed</strong></a><strong>”</strong> dropped mid-August and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3aITimGk0InPUdYHaW49UZ?si=4d069fff904b4bea\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Flame The Main</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is slated to launch on September 20th, both of which will be featured within The Erly’s upcoming record, <em><strong>Culture Fever -&nbsp;</strong></em>available on November 3rd, 2023."},{"t":"p","html":"For all announcements and updates, stay connected with The Erly on social media!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Erly!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/W6E-VeiK1Y8?si=Q-BZHHVNT2KbfMlI","height":"315"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/theerlyband/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@theerlyband","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/theerlyband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@TheErly\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"258173","title":"Read More","date":"2023-09-15","lead":"The New Orleans-based musician officially launched her new track exploring themes of conflict, closure, and healing.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/258173/5e14c0dbc123485e868eeea8cb37580a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The New Orleans-based musician officially launched her new track exploring themes of conflict, closure, and healing."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3VouCvjByCTpzd79K9HSMP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New Orleans, LA (September 15, 2023) - Alternative artist, <a href=\"https://www.sarijordan.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sari Jordan</strong></a><strong>,</strong> dropped her new 2023 track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3VouCvjByCTpzd79K9HSMP?si=958934af5e18468a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ceasefire!</strong></a><strong>”</strong><em>&nbsp;</em>on Friday, September 15th. The lyrics behind this song explore themes of conflict, closure, and healing. Ethereal vocals and a distinct live-band sound take listeners on an expansive journey through times of darkness and tension, ultimately moving towards a comforting and cathartic release. The melodies and rhythms for “Ceasefire!” were inspired by sounds from Psychedelic Rock, Neo-Soul, and Broadway."},{"t":"p","html":"“Ceasefire!” represents various instances of conflict and resilience. Sari Jordan conveys a message of clarity, reminding listeners that the walls we create for self-protection can block us from seeing the full picture, resulting in miscommunication and confusion. This dreamy track is a song to blast when you're in the car driving away from a heated argument.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song acts as a reminder that everyone has their own unique perspective and experience in life. This is one of those songs that teaches you something after you listen to it all the way through. I learned a lot about myself and gained clarity from writing and seeing this track through to completion.”","cite":"- Sari Jordan, Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/TSA-2JzbchE?si=6OnS1XOSPLDjFp8P","height":"392"},{"t":"p","html":"“Ceasefire!” was originally written on the ukulele and further arranged to fit the fuller sound of a complete band. Sari Jordan began the recording process on the fateful date of January 1st, 2023. Sari and her band perform this song live whenever they get the chance, igniting the audience with raw talent and fostering an emotional connection with fans old and new."},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>SONG CREDITS</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>PRODUCED, MIXED, AND MASTERED BY KEENAN MCRAE</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>VOCALS - SARI JORDAN</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>DRUMS - ALFRED JORDAN JR.</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>GUITAR - MAX BRONSTEIN</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>BASS - LEX WARSHAWSKY</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>KEYS - MERELL BURKETT</em><br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/578048/large-14b88e4a68e47430258658d64cb91f91.png","alt":"\"Ceasefire!\" Cover Art; All photo credit goes to Kate Luehrson and Noe Cugny"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576353/original-c5ed853aa55b62d91e3d5b07d400ef3c.jpg","alt":"S1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576353/preview-f613d58cfcd912f3c7ed48c27f13c6e4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576354/original-f666dca5ead2fa11ccba0b63ea3c3790.jpg","alt":"S2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576354/preview-f4f670daca2633451fe976ed94488745.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576357/large-221082202fe3734fe8ded13308310a3f.png","alt":"S4.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576357/preview-64f7f39e8818d756fa6fba20c494f290.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576355/large-8b48072d856a52f10ad12d3448b9442b.png","alt":"S5.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576355/preview-a246874b0608c22f934b787f8bbabf94.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Sari Jordan:"},{"t":"p","html":"Known for a voice that oscillates from smoky-sweet soft to big-hearted belt and back again, New Jersey-born vocalist, songwriter, and musician Sari Jordan (they/she) spends their days and nights loving and learning down in New Orleans. Sari will be releasing their debut EP <strong>“Sing to the Moon”</strong> in late 2023, a collection of original compositions that reflect nascent ruminations with subtle confidence and ample whimsy.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The sensitive, silly-goose songstress first decamped to the Crescent City for college in 2018, and soon set off on a whirlwind romance with the great American songbook. The local culture coalesced with a lifelong love for theater, soul, and alternative indie/psych rock, each deeply rooted in the city Sari now calls home.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/32POifvtGNBo1CGQo0wn5X?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Characterized by raw honesty and playful boldness, Sari’s voice commandeers ears with a confident, stated presence. Debut EP “Sing To The Moon” (due Fall 2023) features a tasting menu of original music essentially ripped from diary entries over the past couple of years. The project is an amalgamation of Sari’s kaleidoscopic influences, embodying elements of <strong>Lianne La Havas</strong>, <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, <strong>Billie Holiday</strong>, <strong>Nai Palm of Hiatus Kaiyote</strong>, and <strong>Billie Eilish</strong>, in a succulent gumbo with Sari’s own gossamer, angelic style.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The sum of these parts delivers a tender, folky neo-soul that aims an arrow directly at the heart. Her songs make listeners want to give themselves a giant hug, and whisper sweetly things will be okay. “Sing To The Moon” croons lullabies to a younger you. Reminds one of walking and talking with yourself; of tending to and rebounding from heartbreak. Each song is affectionate and intentional, a cocktail of warmth, depth, and unfettered brightness. At 23, Sari Jordan is just getting started."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Sari!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/sarijjordan/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@sarijjordan","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.sarijordan.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.sarijordan.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@sarijjordan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://twitter.com/sarijjordan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter </strong></a><strong>| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/SariJordan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://sarijordan.bandcamp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>bandcamp </strong></a><strong>| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/sarijordanx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"260526","title":"LA-Based Artist Eddie Boy Drops New Single \"Sweet & Sour Sugar Lemon\"","date":"2023-09-15","lead":"The new dance-worthy track transports listeners through a timeline of uncertainty amid the pandemic.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/260526/e4eb542c2c0eb4de50a6f88d2dc2cc35.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new dance-worthy track transports listeners through a timeline of uncertainty amid the pandemic."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6QxwodAX2kL3jX1NPSErXE?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (September 15, 2023) - Los Angeles-based Pop musician <strong>Eddie Boy</strong> just launched a new track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6QxwodAX2kL3jX1NPSErXE?si=208af737ae054b67\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sweet &amp; Sour Sugar Lemon</strong></a><strong>”</strong>&nbsp;on Friday, September 15. The dance-worthy new single is an ode to melancholic feelings associated with finding love in times of uncertainty."},{"t":"p","html":"“Sweet &amp; Sour Sugar Lemon” tells the story of finding love during the pandemic, when uncertainty about the future circled our minds and hearts. Love crept into the artist's life while the rest of the world seemed dark and hopeless - which caused an influx of conflicting emotions. Through a catchy chorus and upbeat instrumentals, Eddie Boy explores the various stages of experiencing a worldwide phenomenon that now feels like a distant dream. “Sweet &amp; Sour Sugar Lemon” transports listeners through a timeline of the pandemic, with a resolution of present-day thoughts and feelings around those unsettling years we all experienced together.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/SweetSourSugarLemon","label":"Listen on All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"lead","html":"\"SWEET &amp; SOUR SUGAR LEMON\" LYRICS"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>It was strange, don’t you remember</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>First exchange was in December</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Back then it was hard believing</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Quarantine would give it meaning</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>2019 was bitter</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Our future back then tasted like</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Sweet and sour sugar lemon</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Sweet and sour sugar lemon</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Day by day turning sweeter</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"“Sweet &amp; Sour Sugar Lemon” has been in the making for quite a while. It has gone through many revisions during the recording process, making the final result all-the-more special and full of meaning. Eddie Boy looks back at this song and similar to a time capsule, it takes him back to that time of bittersweet nostalgia of trying to navigate love through the pandemic.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Looking back to this period in my life makes me appreciate a unique love that sprouted during such a dire worldwide situation. There's also a sense of appreciation I feel in the timing of it, being as though we may never experience a reality like that ever again.”","cite":"- Eddie Boy, Alt-Pop Singer"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581045/large-08d8d6b1d51955ff09a7c33de3bf7af8.jpg","alt":"Cover Art by Eddie Boy"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581771/large-8c9621a4e433580fbcda16dd05c57b74.jpg","alt":"EB_LAR_09.07.23_1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581771/preview-acad1f0b7b4ea1b22e9f0ced672e8b2a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581772/large-316ff1f96d199d920d9fd3a90f9fd5f8.jpg","alt":"EB_LAR_09.07.23_2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/581772/preview-c72b76770b7f73e60e5d1bee328c9d97.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Eddie Boy:"},{"t":"p","html":"Born in Mexico City and based in Los Angeles, <strong>Eddie Boy</strong> is a multi-talented artist, producer and writer, who has been performing and creating songs since a very young age. His music is the byproduct of a multi-cultural upbringing, having spent his childhood years in Mexico and most of his adult years in the United States surrounded by a wide array of international friends and artists. His sound can be described as fresh, relatable and emotional, combining prominent elements of pop writing with R&amp;B, disco, and a strong Latin influence. He is currently based in Los Angeles and has collaborated with internationally appraised names such as <strong>Leonel Garcia</strong>, <strong>Sabino</strong>, <strong>Jesse Baez</strong>, <strong>Ariza</strong>, <strong>Kordelya&nbsp;</strong>and several others. Eddie Boy's new single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/SweetSourSugarLemon\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sweet &amp; Sour Sugar Lemon</strong></a><strong>”</strong> dropped on Friday, September 15th, and is now available for streaming on all major platforms. Stay tuned for a corresponding music video and lyric video soon after!&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Follow Eddie Boy on all socials (linked below) for all music announcements and updates!<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6w3y5rVRV6cnbVh5kkbCqQ?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Eddie Boy!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/eddieboy.mp3/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@eddieboy.mp3","post":false},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@eddieboy.mp3/video/7278532133939957035","handle":"@eddieboy.mp3"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@eddieboy.mp3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a> | ​<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/eddieboymp3/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"258721","title":"Keepers of Humanity","date":"2023-09-08","lead":"\"Intersection\" is a tease of the anticipated upcoming EP 'Pansori' from the 4-piece San Francisco-based band.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/258721/2853ab508d698d1d3e3ec8688a11aeeb.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Intersection\" is a tease of the anticipated upcoming EP 'Pansori' from the 4-piece San Francisco-based band."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0MF0mJo5qo3qB5jQAbDxoC?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"San Francisco, CA (September 8, 2023) - Emerging Alt-Rock Band, <a href=\"https://keepersofhumanity.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Keepers of Humanity</strong></a> just launched their new track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0MF0mJo5qo3qB5jQAbDxoC?si=fe8adad9bbd24ee1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Intersection</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on Friday, September 8. This track gives listeners a taste of the Alt-Rock group's upcoming EP, <em><strong>Pansori</strong>. Pansori&nbsp;</em>will officially launch on October 8 under <strong>Rockstone Records</strong>, and “Intersection” will be featured as the opening track. “Intersection” is a re-recording of the closing track of KOH's self-released album <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5yNYspq26iHITIdwTcff3C?si=LKLFGtPhRC6PpAb_L0varA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>‘</strong><strong>Freedom in the Chaos’</strong></a><em>&nbsp;(2019).&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"The lyrics behind this track represent a “cry for acceptance” from someone who has been relentlessly pushed by others to fit into a mold and be something they’re not. As the song progresses, the person experiencing this turmoil ultimately rejects the critical voices and emerges a strong and confident authentic self."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I love rocking out to this song. Every time we play it, it’s like you’re hanging with your best buddies and having a blast.”","cite":"Jean Nanjo, Lead Singer - Keepers of Humanity"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577566/large-9051263d37ca5e9622867a6bb16b543e.jpg","alt":"KO2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577566/preview-650a6f120dbfaad0f8f19dd0ab26bf4a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577568/large-8400f6c5f4900f7dcb145ae6c3ddebf4.jpg","alt":"KOOO.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577568/preview-ca3dd06c84ee3128558316126d887123.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577567/large-dc3473b31444663deafd67b06310300c.jpg","alt":"KO5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577567/preview-242003ea80196367009017b7cdf3ebae.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577569/large-59f0f7cae1cee34a4906bb5fc18ed3df.jpg","alt":"KO4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577569/preview-b2f512809511b054f8fc9a0429b77924.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577570/large-c2203445976a808894172e2acd856df7.jpg","alt":"KO3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577570/preview-4a1cdb1b13bf9ce64da8b8e10b487537.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577571/large-d719fc1257b7ef71692a030fefc8e283.jpg","alt":"KO7.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577571/preview-9683332eb63b6587c45be89973e62e4a.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"“Intersection” taps into the feelings associated with leaving a bad relationship, racial discrimination, creative struggle, and more. A powerful line in the song, <em>“let me be me,” </em>reflects a long-awaited sentiment of peace after experiencing the trials and tribulations of life. Each member of the band has a uniqueness in the way they think and interpret music, all coming together to create an authentic, down-to-earth sound. “Intersection” is a celebration of individuality and homage to musicians who have made their mark by staying true to their ambitions."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577537/large-1e4e8cd9252e213c3ea873eb31d1e409.png","alt":"Keepers of Humanity Cover Art, \"Intersection\""},{"t":"p","html":"“Intersection” is an upbeat, guitar-driven song reflecting sonic elements from famous bands such as <strong>Dire Straits</strong> and <strong>Black Keys</strong>. “Intersection” energizes listeners of all genres, opening with Steven Bonaccorso’s edgy hard-rock guitar riff, which is joined by Rudy Choy’s punchy finger-played bass lines, and a four-on-the-floor power drum beat backing it all. Jean Nanjo's sweet, girl-next-door vocals tie all elements of the song together in harmony."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“Intersection” will be performed as part of a set at KOH’s EP release preview show on September 20 at the legendary&nbsp;</em><a href=\"https://goldengatebandshell.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Golden Gate Park Bandshell&nbsp;</em></a><em>in San Francisco, presented by <strong>Illuminate Live</strong> and <strong>SF RPD</strong>. Free for all ages!</em>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Keepers of Humanity:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Keepers of Humanity</strong> is a piano-based Alt-Rock band from San Francisco, CA. They have an edgy, theatrical, and eclectic vibe, often reminding listeners of <strong>Kate Bush</strong>, <strong>Tori Amos</strong>, and <strong>Amanda Palmer</strong>. In 2019, Keepers of Humanity (KOH) self-released their first album, ‘Freedom in the Chaos,’ and were subsequently invited to join indie label: <strong>Rockstone Records</strong>. The band will be releasing their follow-up EP, <em><strong>Pansori</strong></em>, on October 6, 2023 under the same label. KOH's new single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7nFri9u4OUqOnIyPLggkuH?si=owKa2bSaSxq_FxcDBLylGA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Intersection</strong></a><strong>”</strong> dropped on September 8 and is featured on the upcoming EP as well.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The band members each hail from vastly different musical backgrounds, creating a unique, genre-blending sound. Lead singer <strong>Jean Nanjo</strong><em>&nbsp;</em>is an intensively-trained classical pianist; Bassist <strong>Rudy Choy </strong>was a DJ in the 90's hip-hop backpacker scene; Guitarist <strong>Steven Bonaccorso</strong> has a deep background in Folk music; and Drummer <strong>Alexi Robins</strong> is a chameleon, having experience with every music genre under the sun. Charming, upbeat, approachable, and always full of energy, each song KOH creates has a deeply personable and emotional essence, resonating with listeners who feel lost in any way. Introspection, uncertainty, chaos, hope, inner strength, and true love are all themes that KOH taps into when creating their songs and albums."},{"t":"p","html":"To keep up with KOH, follow them on their social media channels linked below, and stay tuned for more announcements!<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6wkj5CdLGTtLdgHhmdUvkk?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Keepers of Humanity!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/keepersofhumanity/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@keepersofhumanity","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://keepersofhumanity.com/","img":"https://d10j3mvrs1suex.cloudfront.net/s:bzglfiles/u/719584/6bf5ec1640aaad48080f54ba4691403459449466/original/manatee-head-logo.png/!!/meta%3AeyJzcmNCdWNrZXQiOiJiemdsZmlsZXMifQ%3D%3D.png","title":"Keepers of Humanity","desc":"Home page of Keepers of Humanity, an alternative, indie, pop, rock, songwriter group from San Francisco. Keepers of Humanity is a piano-driven indie rock band from San Francisco, California. Reminisce"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://keepersofhumanity.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>WEBSITE</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/keepersofhumanitySF/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"258986","title":"Americana Ballad \"Thief\" Gets Us Ready For Emily Nicole Green’s Debut EP","date":"2023-09-08","lead":"“Thief” just dropped in anticipation of Green’s forthcoming EP, ‘Outrunning the Animal, slated to release on October 30th on vinyl and streaming.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/258986/508979aeebfc737278bf3c1cb4f5a0cc.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"“Thief” just dropped in anticipation of Green’s forthcoming EP, ‘<em>Outrunning the Animal</em>, slated to release on October 30th on vinyl and streaming."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0uqAhnxsrCKRQN5btgVL8D?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (September 8, 2023) - NYC-based singer-songwriter <strong>Emily Nicole Green&nbsp;</strong>drops new single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0uqAhnxsrCKRQN5btgVL8D?si=e39dbded12134472\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Thief</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on Friday, September 8 and you might have to pull over if you’re listening to this one while driving. This track is, in many ways, the most raw and revealing of the 5-songs on Green’s upcoming debut EP,<strong>&nbsp;‘Outrunning The Animal,’</strong> both musically and in terms of letting listeners feel her ache. “Thief” is an Americana ballad that calls on elements of Jazz, Folk, and Pop, resulting in a track that feels timeless and emotionally stirring."},{"t":"p","html":"“Thief” is a song about being abandoned or rejected in some way by someone you love. It’s an invitation to stop abandoning ourselves in response. It’s also about realizing two opposing truths can co-exist in the same person. It’s about creating space for what actually happened alongside how you hoped things would have gone."},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Thief’ explores the process of acknowledging and validating the pain that we experience, while also looking at how our own responses to situations may have led us to doing additional damage to ourselves. It’s about understanding the impact that these people who have hurt us have had on us and not shying away from naming their impact on us. At the same time, it’s about no longer making a three-dimensional human into a one-dimensional villain, it’s about admitting the complexities and making room for them.”","cite":"- Emily Nicole Green, Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577852/large-13a9e03e27c35edcf2de0b83b664cd34.jpeg","alt":"EMILY2.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577852/preview-0556589028dfd82200d7053157acc3c7.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577853/large-510f403fcf2b3cd7646a155db114dde3.jpeg","alt":"EMILY5.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577853/preview-bf7f245b177afbacad805b7e0a1d1e33.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577854/large-7ac30d8fa16f2eea1c468c6dce3d5689.jpeg","alt":"EMILY4.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577854/preview-cdc0a478798d4b93e095bd6375812e83.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577855/large-dd3b6fbb0221174c89d8f61553b51015.jpeg","alt":"EMILY1.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577855/preview-c8d8161df898b2c18ee7888086105079.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577856/large-218db235c2b9275b4b396e7eaaa749c5.jpeg","alt":"EMILY3.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/577856/preview-cbe29e298c74a55c0402f8d9b9cf2bf3.jpeg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>Photo Credit: Matthew Alexander</em><br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/playlist/0s1SJC3ZJPQ1yv6u6zdEWv?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Emily Nicole Green:"},{"t":"p","html":"NYC-based singer-songwriter, Emily Nicole Green shines a light into the depths of her own emotional interiority with her lyrics and her sound. Her vulnerable writing, powerful vocal, and skillful vibrato work together to offer listeners immediate emotional resonance and stirring storytelling that stays with them long after her songs end.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Green has been writing and performing her original songs since she was a freshman in high school. At 17, she began dealing with debilitating anxiety and panic that stopped her from pursuing a career in music for nearly two decades. In 2019, she decided it was now or never and began pouring herself into her music. She posted cover songs on Patreon and a year later landed her first TV spot with a cover of<strong>&nbsp;“Greasy Frybread”</strong> played over the credits of Season 1, Ep. 4 of FX’s<strong>&nbsp;Reservation Dogs</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"Green’s songwriting is where she gives herself permission to tell herself her truth, processing her emotions and not judging what they have to say, letting the songs be told by the parts of her that still ache.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Emily Nicole Green’s debut EP, ‘Outrunning The Animal,’ which mixes Americana with indie-folk, pop, jazz, blues, and country, is anticipated to be released on October 30th of this year.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"On what guides her writing, Emily says, <em>“At the altar of the ache, you’ll find the light below the wound.”</em>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The EP:"},{"t":"p","html":"Emily Nicole Green’s forthcoming debut EP, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/playlist/0s1SJC3ZJPQ1yv6u6zdEWv?si=1ba25ff2f48c45cb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Outrunning The Animal</strong></a>,’ is set to be released in October 2023. The EP includes five songs that are grounded in Americana, but lean into other genres such as — pop (<strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5QlHxADLZsI26wccH2egw2?si=8ace0dc71f3f49d9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>It’s Gonna Be Okay</strong></a><strong>”</strong>), country (<strong>“Hole In My Heart”</strong>), blues and jazz (<strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3dSmlxpSvh7RKiq9vlIdZa?si=2217f78c8b484853\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wreckage</strong></a><strong>”</strong>), and folk (<strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0uqAhnxsrCKRQN5btgVL8D?si=145069a4325c4b4e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Thief</strong></a><strong>”</strong>)— depending on the track... In her songwriting for this EP, Green works through grief and rage, rejection and desperation, and the indignities of unrequited love, while testing out the waters of acceptance and hope."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Emily!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/oyF5Yo2q1O4?si=YB1U0mIgZxTGXQun","height":"435"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/emilynicolegreen/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@emilynicolegreen","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/EmilyColeGreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@emilycolegreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/EmilyNicoleGreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"259475","title":"Diane Louvel, a singer-songwriter from New York City and Paris, is a master of melody-driven indie folk. With her pure and soulful voice, she effortlessly combines emotive lyrics with a captivating storytelling style. Diane draws inspiration from the complexities of life. Diane Louvel Music","date":"2023-09-08","lead":"The NYC-based singer-songwriter releases her new song, exploring themes of societal expectations and work-life balance.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/259475/8ed44a75bdae9857155a81f69b0e2bbd.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The NYC-based singer-songwriter releases her new song, exploring themes of societal expectations and work-life balance."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1tNKo1S95DpLhcU1HT9TmU?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (September 8, 2023) - Alt-Country artist <a href=\"https://www.dianelouvelmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Diane Louvel</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>just released her new song, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1tNKo1S95DpLhcU1HT9TmU?si=c7bb6488f0cc42f3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Above and Beyond</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on Friday, September 8th. This single will eventually be a part of Louvel’s upcoming album, also titled <em>‘Above and Beyond.’ </em>This new track from Diane Louvel explores themes of societal expectations and work-life balance through melancholic folk instrumentals and raw, down-to-earth vocals."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>\"Above and Beyond\" Lyrics&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><em>I wake up the dawn and</em></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><em>Above and beyond is the altar that we're gonna pray to</em> </strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><em>To make ourselves loved</em></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><em>Make ourselves everything we ever promised</em></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><em>Everything we compromise</em></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><em>But I'll carry on, walking along</em></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><em>Invisible to everyone but you</em></strong><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"The lyrics behind “Above and Beyond” signify that we can easily lose ourselves in striving to please others. The title of this track is an overused expression in the corporate world, which fosters a clever irony between the meaning of the lyrics and the unraveling of their meaning. This juxtaposition can also be seen within the humorous aspect of Louvel’s words and the sincerity in her voice."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/579092/large-99a2a260e0ac46e7f44dfdcf08ec943f.jpg","alt":"\"Above and Beyond\" Cover Art by Thomas Pirel"},{"t":"p","html":"The song pokes fun at the idea that you only really get ahead in life by going “above and beyond” what’s technically required. Once this precedent is set, that overachiever mentality becomes the true expectation. There’s no such thing as meeting the standard anymore because we are seen as lesser than if we don’t push ourselves to overperform. In the corporate world, this idea isn’t anything new, but Louvel strives to acknowledge the personal sacrifice that is required to survive in that type of environment.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song was originally written as observational humor but it turned out to be kind of sincere. I wanted to include the idea of “being seen” and the power of friendship as a vital antidote to an otherwise cynical view of hustle culture.”","cite":"- Diane Louvel, Alternative Country Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1pO7633g4ZIxPeTPOcToAe?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Diane Louvel:"},{"t":"p","html":"Never underestimate the power of proximity. Growing up in two epicentres of culture, fashion, and music (New York City and Paris), it isn’t exactly a surprise that Diane Louvel ended up a creative artist; what is staggering is the level of mastery she’s achieved in her craft as a singer-songwriter. Weathering the storm of losing her brother (and the loneliness that followed) provided more than some meaningful tunes: it armed her with purpose. The result is spritely, almost effervescent Americana, rooted with a strength only a working woman’s hands that tills the land could have. And with a voice like<strong>&nbsp;Joni Mitchell</strong> by way of<strong>&nbsp;Neko Case</strong>, it’s just a matter of time before fans of classic bards like <strong>Laura Nyro </strong>and <strong>Willie Nelson </strong>(and contemporaries like <strong>Father John Misty </strong>and <strong>Lana Del Rey</strong>) get wise to this rising star in the circuit."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Diane!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/dianelouvel/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@dianelouvel","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.dianelouvelmusic.com/","img":"","title":"Diane Louvel, a singer-songwriter from New York City and Paris, is a master of melody-driven indie folk. With her pure and soulful voice, she effortlessly combines emotive lyrics with a captivating storytelling style. Diane draws inspiration from the complexities of life. Diane Louvel Music","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.dianelouvelmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>WEBSITE</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@waltz_withdiane?is_from_webapp=1&amp;sender_device=pc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/DianeLouvelMusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"258041","title":"Claire Reneé Releases New Track “Waste My Time”","date":"2023-08-30","lead":"California-based R&B artist Claire Reneé drops her new R&B single ahead of September EP.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/258041/9a6a96430a32606dc31b4226d943eafc.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"California-based R&amp;B artist Claire Reneé drops her new R&amp;B single ahead of September EP."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3jHbNAymaGuaff9XVX9R4n?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, CA (August 30, 2023) - Independent singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://www.clairereneemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Claire Reneé</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong> just released an upbeat R&amp;B dance track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3jHbNAymaGuaff9XVX9R4n?si=6d5aa7a428d64a12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Waste My Time</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> on Wednesday, August 30th. “Waste My Time” is an end-of-summer anthem you can listen to with your girlfriends before going out for a fun night."},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song embodies a 'glow-up after the break-up,' mentality, providing listeners with an uplifting message of positivity and light.”","cite":"Claire Reneé, R&B Artist"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"“Waste My Time” is an ode to learning from relationships and realizing the things you do/don't want along the way. Claire wants to share the idea of awareness in relation to how other people treat you. Through emotionally-charged lyrics and a driving melody, Claire emphasizes the importance of creating boundaries and knowing your worth."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576175/large-04de29a1c9824d934162563343fcd61c.png","alt":"\"Waste My Time\" Cover Art"},{"t":"lead","html":"<u>\"WASTE MY TIME\" LYRICS</u>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Time</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Revealed what was right in front of my face</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>It took me a while to see</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>But it’s okay</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Lowkey it’s a win</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Cause I am free of you</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>And all of the things you do</em><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"SONG CREDITS"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Song produced by Jaye Locke. Melody and Lyrics written by Claire Reneé.<br></em><br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576178/large-d9d2306f8d9d26b4ce966485358f1cef.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-24 at 2.35.04 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576178/preview-9d637be9268cd7eb672deef2486548df.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576176/large-e5ec2872899b5cb1a3e23cd67677e12d.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-24 at 2.34.32 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576176/preview-df66a94b8b18bbf293c2c8cc863c60a9.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576177/large-07c9a2e2abb354792b9bc01110751bf6.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-24 at 2.34.43 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576177/preview-b8a88966ba0c52ce7c8e760d7d422105.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576183/large-cb1edcac946c9aa959ddcd7e44d17578.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-24 at 2.34.53 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576183/preview-daf839f0c93957d4c62c44fc3eee479f.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576179/large-f17544cbc6c434311ac37ad9f7507158.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-24 at 2.35.13 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576179/preview-0d38a8eba29f0b78392883d469dad92d.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576184/large-cd2dfc65e9419ccc6aab90a12ab654c6.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-24 at 2.37.32 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576184/preview-48c8f29dd1f7d00f5f41c2cd5393bb47.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576182/large-ce9ed0d448a470fd716720924e50d291.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-24 at 2.35.31 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576182/preview-675cf5e8a1a4c456fb3eb552039ca451.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576180/large-0a70922a37d9e5a5361c644be9a3cb9b.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-24 at 2.36.10 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576180/preview-bda5999c6f36cb77aee5fd914aab041a.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576181/large-d250418c5912ad261f53debbeddd8e6e.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-24 at 2.34.03 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/576181/preview-55a710f59f3e691eff4a77751b0fbdd6.png"}]},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1Wp8w74ZupCeCZfZwewX25?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Claire Reneé:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.clairereneemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Claire Reneé</strong></a> is a classically trained dancer who sings from the soul. Singing a combination of R&amp;B, soul, jazz, and pop while being heavily influenced by hip-hop, this singer/songwriter’s raspy yet graceful vocals, along with her unique harmonies, always provide an incredible vibe and sound. This multi-talented artist has quite a unique background. Claire began dancing at the early age of 4 and trained at highly esteemed dance schools such as The Dance Theater of <strong>Harlem and Alvin Ailey</strong>. Her natural ear for music and performance led her to study at Berklee College of Music and The New School for Jazz and Contemporary Music."},{"t":"p","html":"Claire Reneé's recently released nine-track album “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5a1GX9zKYwN1pVhlgiYMGu?si=PMVf5djoSHqjnaE3pJzSsg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wings</strong></a>”<strong>&nbsp;</strong>is inspired by relationships and how we cope with both the beautiful and challenging sides of it, touching on certain experiences that help us navigate these situations. Claire confides, <em>“The human experience encompasses lots of different emotions. There may be some anger, sadness, clarity, visits from spirit guides, and even epiphanies. We lead out by honoring that we want to change or see a change in our lives. That includes doing work on ourselves while reminding ourselves we will always push through and even find our Wings. Getting to the other side brings light and even empathy to the very same ones who hurt you, couldn’t show up for you, or wronged you in the past.”</em> Claire's recently released single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/43DEVwmJ2AGyHoeMLC0kMW?si=fafa421b6f31476e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sadder Days</strong></a><strong>”&nbsp;</strong>as well as her newest song “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3jHbNAymaGuaff9XVX9R4n?si=c924f44be47a4ab8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Waste My Time</strong></a>” are now available for streaming on all platforms!"},{"t":"p","html":"Stay tuned for the release of Claire's EP, Journal Entries 1-4, launching on September 29!<br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Claire Reneé:"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/artisterenee/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@artisterenee","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/XwgjrgTJQ5U?si=LeMSSZVNJ--rBIjX","height":"315"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@artisterenee/video/7258331308743462186","handle":"@artisterenee"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.clairereneemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/clairereneemusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ArtisteRenee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter&nbsp;</strong></a>| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/ArtisteRenee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"256872","title":"Read More","date":"2023-08-25","lead":"California-based musical duo releases sixth and final single from their upcoming feature film soundtrack album.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/256872/941a1d33cb40c69a5e2e8fa1c65de88b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"California-based musical duo releases sixth and final single from their upcoming feature film soundtrack album."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4LooHVDJ5QGLT5ZKPv7TQj?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Royal Oaks, CA (August 25, 2023) - <strong>Armand Ruby</strong> and <strong>Julian Colbeck</strong> of musical group <a href=\"https://karmicneighborhood.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karmic Neighborhood</strong></a>&nbsp;releases the sixth and final single of the preview soundtrack for their upcoming feature film<em><strong>&nbsp;</strong></em><a href=\"https://equinoxmusical.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Equinox the Musical</em></strong></a>. Equinox is the story of two homeless young lovers who discover that forgiveness, gratitude and love can be the keys to navigating life’s most challenging circumstances. The full <a href=\"https://equinoxmusical.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Equinox the Musical&nbsp;</em></strong></a>preview soundtrack album will be released on the fall equinox, Sept 23, 2023."},{"t":"p","html":"The new Surf-Rock song, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4LooHVDJ5QGLT5ZKPv7TQj?si=a9eb25d0af594756\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Living Loving</strong></a><strong>”&nbsp;</strong>officially launches on Friday, August 25. This track heavily taps into surf punk culture, diving into themes of joy and ebullience in celebration of what it means to be alive. This light-hearted tune will play during the film credits, providing the audience with some relief after experiencing the emotionally-charged ending of the film."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/LivingLoving","label":"Listen to \"Living Loving\" on All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Living Loving’ is a no-holds-barred surf rocker featuring James Durbin at his snarling best.”","cite":"- Julian Colbeck, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"quote","html":"‘Living Loving’ is an ebullient celebration of life, wrapped up in a high-speed surf punk fireball.”","cite":"- Armand Ruby, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"p","html":"<br><strong>SONG CREDITS:</strong><br><em>Composed by Armand Ruby. Arranged by Julian Colbeck. Produced by Julian Colbeck and Armand Ruby. Vocals by James Durbin. Guitars by Andrew Synowiec. Keyboards/synths by Julian Colbeck. Bass guitar by Peter Wilde. Drums by Michael Strunk. Patrick Brede, recording engineer.<br>Recorded at Keith Greeninger's Wind River Studios in Santa Cruz (AKA \"Keith's Music Barn\") and at Casa Ruby in Royal Oaks, CA&nbsp;</em><br><br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573814/large-80e71a2532a94fc24377c7ad1fa3a727.jpg","alt":"\"Living Loving\" Cover Art"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Karmic Neighborhood:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Armand Ruby </strong>and<strong>&nbsp;Julian Colbeck</strong>, the core duo behind <a href=\"https://karmicneighborhood.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karmic Neighborhood</strong></a>, have taken very different paths to the present moment. The west coast-based team are two lifelong musicians who met by chance when they moved to the same neighborhood on the central California coast. Julian began his career as a London-based keyboardist and is an accomplished, lifelong music industry veteran, while Armand worked professionally as an environmental scientist in the U.S. and stayed involved in music as a part-time musician and songwriter. Armand and Julian formed a strong bond through their shared passion for music and their painful yet hopeful life experiences of surviving cancer. The two rhythmic alt-pop collaborators found inspiration within the harmony of their own respective life journeys and a mutual interest in musical innovation.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vnYPcPpvzO0hhjR6YMUkV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Armand Ruby:"},{"t":"p","html":"Like many creatives, Armand was a sensitive child. Growing up, this was of course a blessing and a curse, in the face of both the world’s beauty and its harshness. Throughout his childhood in the northeastern United States, Armand was aware that maintaining this sensitivity might be a challenge. So keeping this cherished inner life alive became a lifelong ambition – and it found expression through music and songwriting. Armand wrote his first little tune at the age of 11, and as a teenager began composing songs, something he’s continued to do throughout life. But his musical talent was matched by a proclivity for science, and a scholarship to an Ivy League university led to a career as an Environmental Scientist."},{"t":"p","html":"Still, Armand continued to be active musically: songwriting, recording demos, performing in rock bands no one’s ever heard of, leading small choral groups, and for several years even singing in a professional opera chorus. A breakthrough came in 2010-2011 with the writing of the book and songs for a musical stage play, <strong>“Equinox.”</strong> Directing the play in its brief but sold-out run in Santa Cruz California was, according to Armand, <em>“both the most difficult and most rewarding experience of my life.”&nbsp;</em>With Equinox, Armand finds himself working at the creative intersection of art and social activism – shining a new light on the often out-of-sight homeless population and the many ways people can become homeless, through story and music. Moving in 2019 to the rural Monterey Bay area community of Royal Oaks, Armand found that one of his neighbors, Julian Colbeck, was an experienced music arranger, producer and keyboardist. From that auspicious meeting arose the musical partnership known as&nbsp;<a href=\"https://karmicneighborhood.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Karmic Neighborhood</a>.<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Julian Colbeck:"},{"t":"p","html":"Julian Colbeck grew up in the south of England, where he learned how to play the piano and ultimately pursued his dreams of being in a London-based rock ‘n’ roll band in his late teens. Julian’s music career took off with the band <em><strong>Charlie</strong></em>, with whom he scored several US Top 40 singles including <strong>“Watching TV”</strong> and <strong>“LA Dreamer.”</strong> Over the span of a 40-year career, Julian worked and toured as a keyboard player/producer with <strong>YES&nbsp;</strong>alumni group <strong>Anderson Bruford Wakeman Howe</strong>, former Genesis guitarist <strong>Steve Hackett</strong>, <strong>Charlie</strong>, <strong>John Miles</strong>, and more. In 2008 Julian began work with his long-time friend, <strong>Alan Parsons</strong>, on the award-winning instructional video series: <a href=\"https://www.artandscienceofsound.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Alan Parsons’ The Art &amp; Science Of Sound Recording</strong></a>. Julian also has written for many esteemed music industry publications and has authored many music and music technology books. Beginning in late 2019, and interrupted by intensive treatment for stage 4 cancer, Julian saw something of value in his neighbor Armand Ruby’s songwriting and his <em>Equinox&nbsp;</em>film project and worked as an arranger, co-producer, and keyboardist on the Equinox preview soundtrack recordings."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Karmic Neighborhood!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2FtheKarmicNeighborhood%2Fposts%2Fpfbid035RCGoegwKBZCjVCwiN8S16hxphXEKjCbwx1YpMFZsRv6uRFvLmZnfNC9kaAotiDdl&show_text=true&width=500","height":"498"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Fp%2FCukG75AJFLL%2F%3Futm_source%3Dig_web_copy_link%26igshid%3DMzRlODBiNWFlZA%253D%253D","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/karmicneighborhood/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100082755791779\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | </strong><a href=\"mailto:armand@armandrubymusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>EMAIL</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"256891","title":"Read More","date":"2023-08-25","lead":"The new song talks about being afraid to share one's lesser side, yet leaves listeners on groove.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/256891/9c984e1bfd3c278d9a7421b2379b57ac.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new song talks about being afraid to share one's lesser side, yet leaves listeners on groove."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0MA3vYM4gsD64hQXDZWUD8?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston, TX (August 25, 2023) - Houston-based Alt-Pop artist <a href=\"https://www.timqualls.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tim Qualls</strong></a> just released a new track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0MA3vYM4gsD64hQXDZWUD8?si=133df071c1a0446c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Grave</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on Friday, August 25. “Grave” is the second single released from Qualls’ upcoming debut album. The lyrics behind this upbeat Pop song dive into the fear associated with forming new relationships and opening up to someone. Sharing the good, bad, and ugly parts of yourself with a new person can be scary and leave you feeling exposed."},{"t":"p","html":"The title of the song, “Grave” is ironically contrasted with the jovial nature of the track’s instrumentals, featuring an infectious bass line and ethereal synth elements. “Grave” serves as a reminder that everyone has some type of skeleton in the closet, and sometimes leaning into the fear of exposing those secrets will set you free. Without letting the lyrics sink in, one would think this track is about cheating or lying in a relationship. By letting the lyrics sink in, listeners will find that the song is more about insecurity and vulnerability than it is about toxicity. “Grave” was meant for listeners to enjoy and have some fun with while realizing that the track is also riddled with deeper meanings and metaphors."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/12J7rAVoeFIUNkRelq5zw8?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Some of the best songs come from the dissonance created when a song's lyrics and tone steer the listener in polarizing directions.”","cite":"- Tim Qualls, Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574322/original-8773d2cbc1bd437b2181e6a6b1005648.jpg","alt":"grave 6.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574322/preview-e2e1819f0496dbdf2f16e5b9826b012a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574323/large-c1afb163a87f9c9ce72bd85dd47ae0eb.jpg","alt":"grave4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574323/preview-ed7344fa8a18d6c89793b5fe0f50b081.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574319/large-3f337e09bb9a85cdedd94ef6f479fa1c.jpg","alt":"grave2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574319/preview-0a0154b3dc7b991b856988c080331df3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574320/large-ee7726a9a33aae2318be5434a229d705.jpg","alt":"grave 5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574320/preview-66a3d66576ea74a4d65763209453f1ec.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574321/large-381d280d06c18f45247faf27fe175d8e.jpg","alt":"grave3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574321/preview-9eb69647aa0f7449b9e4207e28d50b5c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574318/large-93edda0a0291250f36f7fd246f14728d.jpg","alt":"grave.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574318/preview-3355b90be54ec32727baf7603fba7b8c.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>Photos by Houston-Based Photographer Kirby Betancourt</em><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Tim Qualls:"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston-based songwriter <strong>Tim Qualls</strong>, delivers rootsy soul music that is grounded in family, heartache, and a positive outlook on life very few write about. Influenced by legends like <strong>Ray Charles</strong>, <strong>Jamie Cullum</strong>, and <strong>John Mayer</strong>, musicians compare him to a “soul artist that croons on the piano.” His productions have been compared to <strong>Adele</strong>, <strong>Sam Smith</strong>, and <strong>Ryan Tedder</strong>. Once awarded Houston Press’ “Best New Act” award, Qualls continues to deliver new music every year. Tim has been featured on Spotify playlists such as <strong>LIFE SUCKS</strong>, <strong>DINNER MUSIC</strong>, <strong>SOULFUL BLEND</strong>, and <strong>COZY BLEND</strong>. His recently released single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2oheHd1XwCuN3cFzZV7Tid?si=4da46a8a26214bd1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Forever</strong></a><strong>”</strong> and his newest song <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0MA3vYM4gsD64hQXDZWUD8?si=5cebb944d65d42e3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Grave</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is a part of Tim Qualls’ upcoming debut album. “<strong>Grave</strong>” officially launched on August 25 and is now available for streaming on all major platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Tim!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/timquallsmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@timquallsmusic","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/x086UZWj-ks","height":"395"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.timqualls.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIM QUALLS OFFICIAL WEBSITE</strong></a>"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.timqualls.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/timquallsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><strong><a href=\"https://www.twitter.com/timothyqualls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TWITTER</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/timquallsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"256893","title":"Britt Devens","date":"2023-08-25","lead":"Devens' 10-track Indie-Folk LP officially launches, exploring a variety of theme.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/256893/263c6960eb4ee6db38197c6c8fe6ea70.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Devens' 10-track Indie-Folk LP officially launches, exploring a variety of theme."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1pJQW8geTMNbmpzOVIOtD8?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (August 25, 2023) - Indie-Folk singer-songwriter <strong>Britt Devens&nbsp;</strong>officially releases her 10-track LP,<strong> “</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1pJQW8geTMNbmpzOVIOtD8?si=_usmRcUmSl2ZJbzpy912EA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><strong>Here I Go Again</strong></strong></a><strong><strong>”</strong> </strong>on Friday, August 25th. Each track on the album explores a new theme, ranging from mental health and the love of a woman, to sobriety and times of hardship.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"“Here I Go Again” encompasses a decade of emotion channeled through musical expression, producing an honest and raw work of art for listeners to resonate with. The dreamy, sometimes melancholy nature of the tracks on this release are juxtaposed with occasional Alt-Rock elements to ground the record in harmony. Many of the lyrical elements on this album were crafted throughout various parts of the western US and inspired by the diverse yet magical landscapes that Devens has experienced.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6lmnc7nwT9e6z36dDG4LXB?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“From deserts and oceans, to redwoods and mountains, this album holds a decade of music and memories. “Here I Go Again” holds stories of good and healthy times, bad and toxic times, and all of the life that happens in-between.”","cite":"- Britt Devens, Indie-Folk Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"“Here I Go Again” is a reminder that we can do anything we set our minds to. Devens hopes to connect with listeners through this album, helping them remember to be kind to themselves while experiencing any change or battle in life. Devens expresses her personal battles and journeys through songwriting with each release and point in time. “Here I Go Again” explores Devens' life through vulnerable yet relatable lyrics for listeners to relate to and resonate with. Devens' 2021 EP <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5nO2zKN0Tmn24E21wil3vu?si=MXzgfpgwTRS6J461dLz3mA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Back to Me</strong></a><strong>”&nbsp;</strong>primarily focused on prioritizing mental health at a different stage in her life.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The album is full circle. I'm back home in Colorado and after years of not being able to fully commit to my art due to choices that no longer align with my values and life happening as it does, \"here I am, here I stand, here I go again\" (lyrics of the title track) is a metaphor of so many things in life. I'm sure many people can relate...it's about gettin' after your dreams or whatever it is you're working towards, standing up and trying again. Just keep going and trust the process!”","cite":"- Britt Devens, Indie-Folk Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"Devens worked to produce this record alongside co-producer <strong>Ben Pisano</strong> (of Corsicana). Devens also would like to thank the extremely talented musicians who contributed to the album's creation: <strong>Emily Winter </strong>(violin), <strong>Teodor Vanovski </strong>(percussion), <strong>Max Hass</strong> (bass), <strong>William Falkner </strong>(electric guitar), and <strong>Ben Waligoske</strong> (pedal steel).&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573818/large-ffc2a2dabcfd501edf574a1d421845cf.jpg","alt":"BRITT5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573818/preview-bae2b9862f6c752e5e984d82370ce97b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573821/large-f8682627331bb0d5a69172d85f48968f.jpg","alt":"BRITT4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573821/preview-b7ced705a12d513ef5b3269e0ceeb25f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574977/large-9cd3eb54d3f4dd80dd0e8cc4c6f764d4.jpg","alt":"BRITT2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/574977/preview-b25ab10b23818677e09ee935ef50336a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/575604/large-8f5b44a76a2de207aad29497518e8cfe.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-22 at 3.00.05 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/575604/preview-cca1a52b297d229dec9b2fbd583fcc51.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/575605/large-ab91e7de459a2a99553baa0495531607.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-08-22 at 3.00.13 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/575605/preview-97189e2cce7ba3b672c69fca309c4c86.png"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"<em><u>PHOTOS BY: TREVOR HUSTER</u></em>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Britt Devens:"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from Denver, CO, <strong>Britt Devens</strong> has always had a deep connection with music. Her background as an avid writer eventually led to her pursuit of songwriting and singing, realizing that this method of musical expression added a therapeutic element to her life. Britt Devens is a sober, LGBTQ-friendly musician who writes songs about hope, heartbreak, and recovery. Devens strives to create music that helps listeners stay grounded and cope with whatever they are experiencing in life. Devens' journey with music is furthered and deepened with her most recent LP, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1pJQW8geTMNbmpzOVIOtD8?si=_usmRcUmSl2ZJbzpy912EA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Here I Go Again</strong></a><strong>,”&nbsp;</strong>now available for streaming on all platforms.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Stay tuned for all future updates and announcements via Britt Devens' social media channels linked below! With her newest release, Devens is working to support and raise profits for <strong>The Phoenix </strong>- a safe and active sober community for those seeking recovery from addiction. To become a member, all that is required is 48 hours of continued sobriety. Fans interested in supporting the cause can donate <a href=\"https://fundraise4phoenix.funraise.org/fundraiser/britt-devens-88d1064?x_firstName=Britt&amp;x_lastName=devens&amp;x_email=brittdevensmusic%40gmail.com&amp;fundraiserPrompt=3473891\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>HERE</strong></a>.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"***Devens and her band are throwing a release show on Saturday, September 9th at<em><strong>&nbsp;The Roxy on Broadway</strong></em> in Denver, CO. Britt and the band will take the stage at 9:30 PM alongside artists such as <strong>Lonely Choir</strong>, <strong>Jordin Dearinger</strong>, and <strong>Oli McCracken</strong>. Vinyl records and t-shirts will be available at the show!***&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Britt!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://linktr.ee/brittdevensmusic?fbclid=IwAR0gg5cT9W1QqMjYHfOLZ3H4aIMqFx5ylSj1zLnf7eNG9ZcguerdPNPIgJA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>LINKTREE</strong></a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fbrittdevensmusic%2Fposts%2Fpfbid032uj8uhP8j3TYRSurFsoY42nSvdCTgTBvV6wJcvtuRhfgsuTrTbBMczAFZPjJwHxpl&show_text=false&width=500","height":"498"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.brittdevens.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/6367cac828ea03445a988411/t/637bf47e72df82609c865212/1669067904643/FAE156F1-C9B6-4E9C-BE7C-B30AA92A8726.jpeg?format=1500w","title":"Britt Devens","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/brittdevensmusic/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/brittdevensmusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://brittdevens.bandcamp.com/album/here-i-go-again\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>BANDCAMP</strong></a>&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"256904","title":"Folk-Rock Artist Skittish Drops New Album, 'Midwest Handshake'","date":"2023-08-25","lead":"The 10-track record throws listeners back to retro while immersing present-day emotions.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/256904/6ca3a60991f156d4a323da4edc9a38a1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The 10-track record throws listeners back to retro while immersing present-day emotions."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2kzWsKXHIMKACvJ8ByFJHQ?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (August 25, 2023) - Rising Folk-Rock artist <a href=\"https://iamskittish.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Skittish</strong></a> officially releases his 10-track album<strong>&nbsp;‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2kzWsKXHIMKACvJ8ByFJHQ?si=-2GyAKu6R5iugY-W-51MCw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Midwest Handshake</strong></a><strong>’&nbsp;</strong>on Friday, August 25. Inspired by sounds from the 1960’s <strong>Muscle Shoals </strong>era of music, this record bathes present-day emotions in a retro aura of sound, creating an organic and grounded composition. The album includes nuances of orchestral instruments, which was an important element for the artist since he has been working in film sound production for the last few years.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Although the sound of popular music has changed over the course of time, overarching generational problems have remained the same and their sentiments continue to seep into modern-day music. The lyrics behind Midwest Handshake are a testament to timeless themes such as social division, dating, and love, and more.<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2ywD4Qa0z1r1KcjmZfV83X?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<em><u>SONG CREDITS (by track number)</u></em>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Jeff Noller - Vocals, Instruments, Writing; Gracie Huffman - Vocals on 2, 4, and 7; Chris Lahn - Orchestration; Brian Griffin - Drums on 4 and 7; Mark O’Day - Drums on 2, 3, 5, 9; Jeremy Krueth - Percussion on 1; Jacqueline Ultan - Cello; Stephen Murray - Stand Up Bass; Ben Etter - Mixing and Additional Production.</em><br>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The songs on this album are a mixture of lessons from the last few years of my life. I grew up in the midwest and after traveling all over the country, I recently landed in LA. Navigating new waters such as the LA social landscape, dating scene, and cultural climate are all challenges I've channeled into my new music.”","cite":"- Skittish, Folk-Rock Musician"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573830/large-c74cb51a3b6c44316cc468774d8aba57.jpg","alt":"Midwest Handshake Cover Art"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573828/large-ce34dc995dea7635b7264d8c064e0e22.jpg","alt":"SK2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573828/preview-039152ae17ed45424d02cfbc716b5567.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573829/large-481fcd200e9ea194f3e714da7a1093e1.jpg","alt":"SK1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573829/preview-9a651817c3cfbec5e92c8fe7966b9f70.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Skittish:"},{"t":"p","html":"Though currently based in Los Angeles, the roots of Skittish have always been Minnesotan. <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2kzWsKXHIMKACvJ8ByFJHQ?si=mEgDNZ6dQPux_eaFfEDa1A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Midwest Handshake</strong></a><strong>’</strong> was written by <strong>Jeff Noller</strong> (<strong>Skittish</strong>) over a two-month visit back home, temporarily trading the land of Teslas and tents for 10,000 lakes. The songs are framed in various Mid-20th Century musical styles that would likely be played at the Grand Ol’ Opry in 1960 (with a dash of '80s-inspired emo sounds and tones). Modern topics like entrenched politics, media obsession, and are given a retro-veneer, implying we still have the same concerns and desires as we once did, just a different ways of expressing them. Noller is supported by additional lead vocals from <strong>Gracie Huffman</strong> (Lighthearted) as well as string and brass orchestration provided by <strong>Chris Lahn</strong>. Drummer <strong>Brian Griffin</strong> (<strong>Lana Del Rey</strong>, <strong>Dolly Parton</strong>) lends his talents to 3 songs, as<strong>&nbsp;Jeremy Krueth</strong> and <strong>Mark O’ Day</strong> round out the rest of the percussion. Stand up bass and cello are prominently featured on the album, and are played masterfully by <strong>Stephen Murray</strong> and <strong>Jacqueline Ultan</strong>, respectively. Additional mixing and production help was provided by<strong>&nbsp;Ben Etter </strong>(Deerhunter, Kaiser Chiefs) whose analogue wonderland provided just the right amount of muscle-shoals-esque grit to the mix. This is the 7th full-length album released by Skittish. Existing somewhere in the friction caused by our idealized version of home rubbing against reality. The lush instrumentation evokes a fuzzy black and white sitcom, while vocal barbs remind the listener of the task at hand. <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2kzWsKXHIMKACvJ8ByFJHQ?si=mEgDNZ6dQPux_eaFfEDa1A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Midwest Handshake</strong></a><strong>’</strong> officially released on August 25th and is now available for streaming on all platforms.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Stay tuned for more Skittish updates and announcements to come!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Skittish!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/skittishmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@skittishmusic","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/BxvgTznDtyE?si=EDwfhirKwlfiofyw","height":"395"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"http://facebook.com/skittishmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/skittishmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"256076","title":"Toronto-based Alt-Pop Artist Karisa Launches New Single, \"Next To You\"","date":"2023-08-24","lead":"The new track provides listeners with a sense of euphoria, now with an astonishing music video.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/256076/681da1f96a3b748c73b9d55b123f9ed7.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new track provides listeners with a sense of euphoria, now with an astonishing music video."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5w5aH5ehURdjfup5oqHfro?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Toronto, ON (August 24, 2023) - Alternative Pop Artist <a href=\"https://www.karisamusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karisa</strong></a> drops her latest single, “<strong>Next To You”</strong> on Thursday, August 10th. “Next To You” is a light-hearted summer anthem about falling in love, happiness, and having a good time. The track merges iconic 1980s synth elements with EDM sounds of the early 2000s to create a unique sound that provides listeners with a sense of euphoria. Some lyrics from this new single read:"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>And we can follow the stars</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>And we can watch the moon</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>And as the tide goes down</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I'll be right next to you</em><br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/cxp5XPSnB1Q?si=bzLJ84ehxG5qwVbi","height":"395"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Water and the tide work as a metaphor for conflicting tropes of timelessness, renewal and eternity against the vagrancies of time and the demands it puts on us in life.”","cite":"-Karisa, Alt-Pop Singer"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0xiPUnPct1UgzYCIgLVYMV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"button","href":"https://music.amazon.com/albums/B0CFB2L9BT?marketplaceId=ART4WZ8MWBX2Y&amp;musicTerritory=CA&amp;ref=dm_sh_2Pu5M9ppmwy9SJ2tmUa9L0RrT","label":"Stream \"next to you\" on Amazon","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"The lyrics and melody within “Next To You” were inspired by the feeling of spending a blissful summer with the person you love. Karisa hopes that listeners associate this new track with a day at the beach when the sun hangs low in the sky and summer heat radiates around you. “Next To You” fuses the feelings and experiences related to the life we live and the love around us. The lyrics and background instrumentals work together in harmony, creating an invigorating and bright tune."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572621/large-cbe07ace18327648c18e9192ac090b9d.jpg","alt":"KARISA 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572621/preview-c5cabacddb7eb390d6a7bf66241fd221.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572624/large-5b74f938930ccbcb5df495642ea69b7f.jpg","alt":"KARISA 4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572624/preview-51de32ade13355627fb46122c67fb2a7.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572623/large-82fb2abc951ecd3c3a1f6b50c6e764c0.jpg","alt":"KARISA .jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572623/preview-6880ddf6aef25bbf25ce541b3802e7f1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572625/large-a71d62b2d405ef4eff0951c11696e6d6.jpg","alt":"KARISA 5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572625/preview-9d82c5c33626ecf12b328f7033e379cc.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572626/large-0aa8a0aa6c55f402f8cd2208fe099a13.jpg","alt":"KARISA 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572626/preview-a6ada94939e4d541bc8dc20e2bc1282b.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Karisa:"},{"t":"p","html":"Toronto-based Alternative Pop Singer <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0xiPUnPct1UgzYCIgLVYMV?si=ExX_nic_RFGBjzF6Bwas-Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karisa&nbsp;</strong></a>has heavily relied on music and art throughout various stages of life. Karisa comes from an artistic family filled with creation and individuality. She recalls her love of music starting to bloom when she was a child sitting at the piano, recording herself singing. Karisa's first live performance was at a dive bar in Toronto’s Kensington Market. This experience sparked Karisa's urge to become an established singer-songwriter and share her music with the world. She prides herself on creating music that expresses the emotion behind various experiences in life - the good, the bad, the ugly, and all that falls in between. Karisa hopes to create songs that provide listeners with a slice of happiness or comfort when they need it the most. Her single <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5w5aH5ehURdjfup5oqHfro?si=edb12f7046d74792\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Next To You</a>”</strong> is now available to stream on all platforms!&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Stay tuned for more announcements and updates from Karisa via her social media channels below!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Karisa!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/karisamusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@karisamusic","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Naya3blJQ-E","height":"380"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://youtu.be/Naya3blJQ-E\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.karisamusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0xiPUnPct1UgzYCIgLVYMV?si=9Z6ixsxSR9ir5rJwL-eOWg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spotify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"256898","title":"Indie-Folk Artist Lewis Turner Launch Debut Album \"Of Fibre and Fixes\"","date":"2023-08-21","lead":"The Colorado-based musician releases his 9-track Americana album, creating an endless wave of emotion.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/256898/cdc0911e56a54bcf748fa69f8ba66f2f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Colorado-based musician releases his 9-track Americana album, creating an endless wave of emotion."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/10dOCHgZzT0lE81Y6sYD3k?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Fort Collins, CO (August 21, 2023) - Indie-Folk artist <a href=\"https://www.lewisturnermusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lewis Turner</strong></a> officially drops his debut album<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/10dOCHgZzT0lE81Y6sYD3k?si=66F5jQeITUGlU8_7dIq-iA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“</strong><strong>Of Fibre and Fixes”</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>on August 21st. The record features 9 tracks, two of which Turner has already released as singles. “Of Fibre and Fixes” showcases Lewis’ vast and evolving range as both a musician and deeply-rooted storyteller. The tracks on this record are seamlessly intertwined, each tune possessing its own unique sonic fingerprint. The album as a whole creates an endless wave of emotion that carries listeners through a journey of growth and change.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“These songs are a timestamp of a very specific point in my life. My lyrics describe and reflect various themes, one in particular being ‘the unknown.’ I find myself falling back into cycles in life and relationships, and the album itself is a representation of this forever ebbing and flowing pattern.”","cite":"- Lewis Turner, Indie-Folk Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"From soul-stirring ballads to foot-tapping Americana-infused rhythms, the album invites listeners to explore the intricate layers of Lewis’ musical evolution. At times, a haunting eeriness lingers, casting a beguiling spell that draws listeners into introspective realms. In other moments, a lush fullness envelops the music, surrounding the listener in a warm embrace of harmonies and arrangements.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“It’s one thing to write a song but bringing a song to life is a whole different animal. The fascinating thing about making music is hearing what people connect to and resonate with. I’m excited to hear what comes through for the listeners, and how that feedback will help me grow as an artist. The collective experience we all share in being human is what makes music meaningful.”","cite":"- Lewis Turner, Indie-Folk Artist"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2iocxCZc0ygouSiLZGdPvu?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"lead","html":"CREDITS&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Production and mastering by Tyler Lindgren </em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Strings by Russick Smith</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Lead guitar by Steven Beck</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Mixing by Andrew Berlin (of Gregory Alan Isakov)</em><br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573823/large-8448785e2de9b404079dd6046abe6f49.jpg","alt":"L6.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573823/preview-110c4c1bccd0e14dc3ecf28b74313119.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573824/large-50f6b1dbf6a206c4fc5bd8f43c41f5b7.jpg","alt":"L3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573824/preview-2d61e59930d8c85b6068d6586e5e166a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573825/large-fcad3931ec74a0e89a18dae261df8614.jpg","alt":"L1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573825/preview-1e6205bf7accb7fcc945a7cdffeebae2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573826/large-cab6832766eb4d98fbfb97e22585d434.jpg","alt":"L5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573826/preview-2af031db2e7fe9ecfbfa245a6eba4492.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573827/large-5bc65f22c655f55217ed5c32e78b041d.jpg","alt":"L2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573827/preview-a61e99e32f3aadcc352367e39c2a2234.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About the album:"},{"t":"p","html":"Lewis Turner’s album, “Of Fibre and Fixes,” embodies a captivating fusion of diverse genres that colors his musical upbringing. Drawing inspiration from Turner’s eclectic musical palette, the album weaves a tapestry of soulful melodies, evoking a sense of nostalgia and depth within each track."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/10dOCHgZzT0lE81Y6sYD3k?si=7pY9kSbJRjSOP--2zOpJyw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Of Fibre and Fixes</strong></a>”</strong> took shape during the formative years of Turner’s adolescence amidst a life-changing sailing voyage across the Pacific Ocean. As a teenager on the cusp of adulthood, Turner found himself grappling with profound questions of the unknown and the role identity plays in what makes us unique."},{"t":"p","html":"Turner’s experiences of sailing against the backdrop of endless horizons naturally wove themselves into the fabric of the folk-like melodies that define this project. “Of Fibre and Fixes” became a vessel through which Turner channeled his innermost thoughts, emotions, and uncertainties."},{"t":"p","html":"Under the guidance of producer and multi-instrumentalist <em><strong>Tyler Lindgren</strong></em>, each track evolved into a canvas on which the raw emotions and contemplations of teenage years were expressed. The layers and melodies within the album depict the waves of Turner’s nautical odyssey."},{"t":"p","html":"This album stands as both a reflection of Turner’s personal path through the tumultuous waters of adolescence and a chronicle of his encounters with the enigmatic aspects of life. The record invites listeners to embark on their own “introspective sail,” guided by the rhythmic currents of identity, doubt, and the quest for understanding."},{"t":"p","html":"Mixer&nbsp;<em><strong>Andrew Berlin</strong></em><strong>&nbsp;</strong>enriched the album with his meticulous touch, unraveling and shaping the delicate nuances within each composition. Berlin’s craftsmanship created a sonic landscape that allowed the raw human themes to take center stage, providing listeners with an opportunity to immerse themselves fully in the album’s introspective atmosphere."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lewis Turner:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2iocxCZc0ygouSiLZGdPvu?si=6K8aeoYQSaujoqJehmPc4g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lewis Turner</strong></a>’s musical style is a fluid blend of Folk and Americana, steeped in story-telling lyrics and grounded with harmonic instrumentals that ease the soul. Born and raised in Fort Collins, Colorado, Turner grew up listening to artists like <strong>Bob Dylan</strong>, <strong>James Taylor</strong>, <strong>Brandi Carlile</strong>, and <strong>Joni Mitchell</strong>, all inspirations for Turner’s journey as a professional musician. Turner made his official debut as a singer-songwriter with the release of his first single<strong>&nbsp;‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2q3LxFSYMCjbQQztmK3RbO?si=u_7gq4GCQr29B48Yeis2Gg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Get Out Of My Head</strong></a><strong>’&nbsp;</strong>in November 2019. This release helped Turner gain local, national, and then global recognition, amassing over half a million streams by early-2020. Lewis is a passionate live performer, with a soulful voice that captivates audiences. He was a finalist in <strong>Sonic Spotlight 2021</strong>, where his infectious songs earned him airtime on <strong>105.5 The Colorado Sound </strong>and a live set at Washington’s, an iconic Fort Collins venue. And as of Summer 2023, Turner was selected out of over 420 applicants as a Finalist in the <a href=\"https://bluegrass.com/folks/lineup/songwriter-showcase\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Planet Bluegrass Songwriter Showcase</strong></a>, making him one of the youngest contestants in the 25-year history of the competition.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Turner has found his niche within the Indie-Folk genre and is about to release his debut 9-track studio album,<em>&nbsp;</em><strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/10dOCHgZzT0lE81Y6sYD3k?si=AXvRKsCNS7q0GsE_mSQAWA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Of Fibre and Fixes</strong></a><strong>.”</strong> The record just officially launched on August 21 and is now available to stream on all platforms. Stay tuned for all of Lewis Turner’s updates and announcements as he continues to rise within the Colorado music scene and beyond!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Lewis!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/lewiscashturner/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@lewiscashturner","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/PDWrpA0KdkA","height":"450"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100082968663060\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCrk6uqEstLgwf4P0T-1Tp4A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.lewisturnermusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"254529","title":"Disco Group The Erly Drops New Single Ahead of Fall Album","date":"2023-08-16","lead":"The Erly releases \"Paralyzed\" alongside an official music video, putting listeners in an uncontrollable groove.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/254529/4fdd3d1789bfaca30bd084e01c710d84.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Erly releases \"Paralyzed\" alongside an official music video, putting listeners in an uncontrollable groove."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0QzfIYmj30ksSmpWPrhxpm?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Niles, MI (August 16, 2023) - Michigan-based Disco quartet,<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://theerlyband.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Erly</strong></a>, just released their new single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0QzfIYmj30ksSmpWPrhxpm?si=61eda7c26dfa4206\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Paralyzed</strong></a>” on Wednesday, August 16th. “Paralyzed” is the first single to drop from <strong>The Erly</strong>’s upcoming album, <em><strong>Culture Fever</strong>,&nbsp;</em>which officially launches on November 3, 2023.<em>&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Touching upon concepts related to relationships, falling in love, and female empowerment, “Paralyzed” is a funky, upbeat tribute to those “warm and fuzzy” feelings we can't control. This single is an ode to the ‘70s Disco with groovy instrumentals and strong yet smoky lead vocals. The powerful rhythmic horn section and layered percussion are supported by cascading string melodies throughout the track, transporting listeners back to Disco music at its prime.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/sp563zO9lTo?si=x0lTMEclvXhXr3op","height":"410"},{"t":"p","html":"The intention for “Paralyzed” was to emulate the feeling of weightlessness one experiences while listening to ‘70s Disco bands like <strong>The Bee Gees</strong> or <strong>Earth, Wind &amp; Fire</strong>. <strong>The Erly</strong> strive to keep Disco alive by making music that is easily as danceable and energizing as it was back in the day.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3QPLdBDMCs5nyauZZMX7IW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“We started writing this song on floor 27 of the Hilton Hotel in Cleveland, OH. We wrote the majority of the chorus there with some additional brainstorming done in the studio. Alyssa’s notorious opening line of “God dammit” came about because she exasperatedly said it in the studio when she was stumped on writing the first verse. After that, it all fell together like magic.”","cite":"- The Erly, Disco  Quartet/Band"},{"t":"p","html":"The music video for “Paralyzed” was filmed on June 25th in Chicago with <strong>Max Williams</strong>. The video fixates on a hyper-‘80s scene while including ‘70s-inspired attire as portrayed in the album’s promotional photos. As an ironic nod to the famous late ‘70s “<strong>Disco Demolition Night</strong>,” the music video includes a scene of the band putting on a record-breaking performance while wearing “Disco Sucks” t-shirts."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/565990/large-5f06868fb1b96a842ac20722413633df.jpg","alt":"ERLY2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/565990/preview-6396787c20ecb593c389624d01724235.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/565991/original-8c1622aa3ae91e21766d6c39dc8bcc15.jpg","alt":"ERLY3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/565991/preview-0329bd9b495da918465d890b272a4918.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/565993/large-d65e02f7e4eba704f9fd99d210717bc3.jpg","alt":"ERLY4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/565993/preview-2f8dfcd53eafde557d561c64b6d3cbb5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/565992/large-e3097014ea867fb67ff99885b4f90710.jpg","alt":"ERLY1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/565992/preview-d5c7fe8b43bbe79cf6da80575dacf4c5.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Erly:"},{"t":"p","html":"Michigan-based Indie-Soul group <strong>The Erly</strong> combine sonic elements from the ‘60s and ‘70s Rock, Pop, and Funk, creating a fresh “Modern Disco” sound and vibe of their own. Fueled by collaboration, friendship, and timeless good vibes, the quartet would fit right in at Woodstock ‘69 or at the indie nerve center that is <strong>SXSW</strong>. Most of <strong>The Erly</strong>’s music features clean guitar work, layered vocals, and groovy undertones that energize even their most solemn-sounding tracks. The band is composed of Drummer <strong>Fran Gleason</strong>, Bassist <strong>Collin Mattiford</strong>, Guitarist <strong>Trevor McDonald,</strong> and Keyboardist <strong>Alyssa Serviss</strong>, with all 4 members featured on vocals. <strong>The Erly</strong> was created in 2018 when Mattiford and Gleason decided to expand upon their pre-established musical duo. Since their formation in 2018, <strong>The Erly</strong> has released two full albums and four singles with more music on the way. Their new single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0QzfIYmj30ksSmpWPrhxpm?si=80a4bb72f7aa48fc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Paralyzed</strong></a><strong>”</strong> just dropped alongside an official music video. “Paralyzed” will be featured on The Erly’s upcoming record, <em><strong>Culture Fever</strong></em>, to be available on November 3rd, 2023.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"For all announcements and updates, stay connected with The Erly on social media!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Erly!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/theerlyband\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@TheErly\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/theerlyband/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@theerlyband","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"256073","title":"Americana-Indie Rock Artist Horseshoes Launches New Track","date":"2023-08-11","lead":"Authenticity: The theme of Horseshoes' new release, \"Say What You Mean.\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/256073/c6232399cc6a48d0eaa4b1a80ea8038d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Authenticity: The theme of Horseshoes' new release, \"Say What You Mean.\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0G5fwyDDTskmynoY8w5zHn?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Washington, DC (August 11, 2023) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0cIVB4MH1nJhx5soIMZeKt?si=0RHAiQQVTNuyK96Ks7il5Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Horseshoes</strong></a> drops a new Indie-Rock single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://www.distro.direct/freshnoise/shareLink.php?release_id=QmNNcG5UelNjdmxHdE5aVlpteTNVUT09\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Say What You Mean</strong></a><strong>”&nbsp;</strong>on Friday, August 11. The recurring theme within this new track is authenticity. The soft acoustic instrumentals supported by a yearning yet empowered lead vocal create a song for all types of listeners to relate to and absorb.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"'Say What You Mean' is about the obstacles we all face when trying to connect with others and understand who they truly are.”","cite":"- Horseshoes, Indie-Rock Artist"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/SayWhatYouMean","label":"Stream \"Say What You Mean\" on All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"The person <em>narrating </em>this song is initially frustrated that somebody isn’t being upfront about who they really are. In an attempt to understand this person, the narrator puts himself at risk of getting hurt. The main character wonders if this person hasn’t developed a sense of self, and therefore doesn’t know what they want. The lyrics reflect an unexpected ending to the song when the confused narrator admits that he has difficulty understanding others because of his own narcissistic consumption with himself.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572870/large-ce2123ea5a3f8f7247a45f2fb5f1cb69.jpg","alt":"Say What You Mean, Cover Art"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Horseshoes:"},{"t":"p","html":"Austin Greaves is a Washington DC-based musician who performs under the name <strong>Horseshoes</strong>. He released his debut album, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4X4f7fYdW98GedO8tKDh0T?si=Up5VrHYbT2GqWrpxmlxw2w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Desert</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> in June of 2022, which was followed up with a single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4x86xnafoYR0SDd6RvYQbz?si=wNflVB0YS2O8CfEQE-T8Pw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Come With Me</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> released in October 2022. You can stream Horseshoes’ recently released single <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/29zUzEi2MIZA5NhbWUaREp?si=41ded00bd6434e5c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hide and Seek</strong></a>”</strong> on all platforms. Listen to Horseshoes’ newest single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3NCMYYe6cYK4pVQzEbs9lV?si=TCj02gYjSYSQyTXNK3aaPw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Say What You Mean</strong></a><strong>”</strong>&nbsp;which is now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0cIVB4MH1nJhx5soIMZeKt?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Horseshoes!"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@horseshoesguy/video/7258329364922649902","handle":"@horseshoesguy"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CuZR2EyOMlG/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@horseshoesguy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TikTok</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/horseshoesguy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"256475","title":"Read More","date":"2023-08-11","lead":"After a brief hiatus, the Oregon-based singer-songwriter returns with Americana-esque single that explores complexity.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/256475/3c03a3ee9d0bfff56630a1f3df714b20.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"After a brief hiatus, the Oregon-based singer-songwriter returns with Americana-esque single that explores complexity."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4SLtwOXAH1kMNjuz2v05Oo?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Bend, OR (August 11, 2023) - Indie-Folk artist <a href=\"https://www.jacobeverettwallace.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Jacob Everett Wallace</strong></a> is returning to the music scene with the release of his brand new single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4SLtwOXAH1kMNjuz2v05Oo?si=bfd184a94c014907\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wild Iron</strong></a><strong>”</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>available to stream on all platforms on Friday, August 11. “Wild Iron” explores complex ideas pertaining to freedom, community, purpose, and more. Wallace expresses emotions associated with breaking the mold of tradition and building a life for yourself away from the people you know and the place you once called home.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5osBGYANkGnzwbWqnQPKLK?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"WILD IRON LYRICS"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Too many irons in the fire</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>It's a long way to reach</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>There's no time for goodbyes</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Just a moment left to grieve</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>All the things I've acquired</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Turned into shackles choking me</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>I gotta be free, I gotta breathe</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>So I'm running wild, like wild iron</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"The Indie-Folk singer puts his storytelling skills to the test with this Americana tune, referencing freedom through motifs like being a “mustang,” a “maverick,” and a “wild iron.” Jacob Everett Wallace wants listeners to feel comforted in the notion that none of us know exactly where our paths may lead, but that fear of the unknown is part of what makes the journey exciting. The inspiration for this new track struck when Jacob suffered a hockey injury and was forced to stay home for a while to recover. It was the time spent re-connecting with family and community that made Jacob look at life from a new perspective while still staying true to his nonconformist ways. “Wild Iron” serves as a reminder that you can discover a true sense of home and stability by going back to your roots and slowing down once in a while to regain a stable foundation."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573162/large-e54881cf9185545f84bfc7aab3064b3e.png","alt":"\"Wild Iron\" Cover Art"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573154/large-9922fb6305742557be6df397e94e4d03.jpg","alt":"jacob4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573154/preview-558d611b4fae55c4ab941ce96072307f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573155/large-05c7c2e542232cea956085ee945ce557.jpg","alt":"jacob 6.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573155/preview-a99465abb940ff53f932f3b36802e4a2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573156/large-304e6454cb3991392b3196cb1523a0cf.jpg","alt":"jacob5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573156/preview-4546079e469c3d491d7cb23dd748bf0d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573157/large-7203f1f49bc51923db13ce9d511c02f0.png","alt":"JACOB3.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573157/preview-03fb24ad16c2e0bc0d3344b32bef3b11.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573161/large-5351adb29befdf6d37f85b4926c6fecf.png","alt":"jacob333.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573161/preview-adc2cc4e480deefc90d2202a5b1a31bb.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573158/large-ec77a8f9330440b369cf60441c19aad6.png","alt":"JACOB2.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573158/preview-6a4e7b39c469f2140cef8e7f12b3c6d7.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573159/large-02523b2856be38b0b1f7ee7b70a1f348.png","alt":"JACOB 6.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573159/preview-4aa23096568ee2dcb3be73edba450f98.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573160/large-6d4cc8882dd769be8bbaf3bcb27f97a6.png","alt":"JACOB1.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/573160/preview-7353d0e89cbc0ae7fa2e6044350a6ba8.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Jacob Everett Wallace:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.jacobeverettwallace.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Jacob Everett Wallace</strong></a> is an independent singer-songwriter with a folk-forward sound that is carried by descriptive lyrics that carry listeners through complex stories of life and meaning. Wallace seeks the truth in anything he sets his mind to, including his work as a self-made entrepreneur, graphic designer, writer, songwriter, producer, audio engineer, and pastor. Originally from Texas, Wallace currently resides in Bend, Oregon. He has performed at all types of venues all over the US, as well as a few shows overseas. Charged with dynamic instrumentals and strong vocal range, Wallace endeavors to connect to listeners on a personal level with the music he creates. Wallace currently has two EPs under his belt, and is adding to his discography with his latest release “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4SLtwOXAH1kMNjuz2v05Oo?si=33928f93fd90475e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wild Iron</strong></a>,” now available for streaming on all platforms!&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Stay tuned for tour announcements and release updates from Jacob Everett Wallace on his social channels!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Jacob!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/jacobeverettwallace/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@jacobeverettwallace","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://jacobeverettwallace.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.jacobeverettwallace.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ChrisBloommusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"></a></strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/jacobeverettwallacemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"254799","title":"Read More","date":"2023-08-04","lead":"This track is the fifth release of a six-single series leading up to the soundtrack album launch for the pair's original feature film, 'Equinox the Musical.'","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/254799/cd4549764b925e869d6deb781cb51492.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This track is the fifth release of a six-single series leading up to the soundtrack album launch for the pair's original feature film, 'Equinox the Musical.'"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/632CeP5rhgQHZmtvpFdYkb?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Royal Oaks, CA (August 4, 2023) - <strong>Armand Ruby</strong> and <strong>Julian Colbeck</strong> of musical group <a href=\"https://karmicneighborhood.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Karmic Neighborhood&nbsp;</strong></a>continue their pre-album releases with the new alternative rocker, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/632CeP5rhgQHZmtvpFdYkb?si=fb95ffdc5e14496b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>That’s Me</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> the fifth track in a series of singles from the <a href=\"https://equinoxmusical.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Equinox the Musical</strong></em></a> preview soundtrack. Equinox is the story of two homeless young lovers who discover - during the course of one tumultuous day - that forgiveness, gratitude, and love can be the keys to navigating life’s most challenging circumstances. This track touches upon themes of resilience, perseverance, and hopefulness while facing a major crossroads in life. “That’s Me” is an upbeat, rock-adjacent tune, reminiscent of the <strong>Blues Brothers’</strong> version of <strong>“Theme from Peter Gunn”</strong> or&nbsp;<strong>Weezer’s “Hash Pipe.”</strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Many of us may never have to face a moment in life where we literally don’t know where to turn. We have to make choices, sure, but we usually have options. Imagine facing a crossroads without any obvious path forward, and no option to go back from where you came – yet nevertheless forward you must go.<br>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/ThatsMe","label":"Listen to \"That's Me\" on All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"In the Equinox screenplay, the main character, <strong>Jason</strong>, leaves his beloved Katie behind and heads out into the unknown with his backpack, guitar, and an old suitcase. In “That’s Me,” he demonstrates his vulnerability and perseverance in that moment, as he puts the bravest face he can on his plight, singing,&nbsp;<em>“Every place that I arrive, that’s me on the other side.”</em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Having lost the comfort of a place to call home, he’ll now have to rely on himself to reorient on the other side of wherever he’s going. As he goes, he has to acknowledge his past mistakes, without wanting to be defined by them. And in the bigger picture of who he truly is, “the other side” also can refer to a transcendent reality and an identity that lives beyond the realm of the senses.<br>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“That’s Me” is a gritty, swaggering statement of intent a la early Doors, launched by the searing vocals of James Durbin.”","cite":"- Julian Colbeck, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This new track is a declaration of defiant resiliency in the face of a menacingly uncertain future.”","cite":"- Armand Ruby, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/566621/large-f9d8456d6595b4e8b362a5508d1b9704.jpg","alt":"KN3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/566621/preview-971333adb0c9f22d3e9d90c91e8140cc.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/566622/large-f684ba13c041d27984bff0807ad3ceb1.jpg","alt":"KN1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/566622/preview-5f37e57faf8810afe7d306b048a508ae.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/566623/large-b9ea99218ec55f6cc437f1da54d8a41f.png","alt":"KN2.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/566623/preview-8efd142f0f9115714b73cb67e01c0d83.png"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<em>“That’s Me” was composed by Armand Ruby, arranged by Julian Colbeck, and produced by Julian Colbeck and Armand Ruby. Vocals by <strong>James Durbin</strong>. Guitars by <strong>Baird Miller</strong>. Keyboards/synths by Julian Colbeck. Bass guitar by <strong>Peter Wilde</strong>. Drums by <strong>Michael Strunk</strong>. <strong>Patrick Brede</strong>, recording engineer.</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"The full&nbsp;<a href=\"https://equinoxmusical.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Equinox the Musical</strong></a> preview soundtrack album will be released on the fall equinox, Sept. 22, 2023.<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Karmic Neighborhood:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://karmicneighborhood.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Karmic Neighborhood</a>’s Armand Ruby and Julian Colbeck, the core duo behind Karmic Neighborhood, have taken very different paths to the present moment. The west coast-based team are two lifelong musicians who met by chance when they moved to the same neighborhood on the central California coast. Julian began his career as a London-based keyboardist and is an accomplished, lifelong music industry veteran, while Armand worked professionally as an environmental scientist in the U.S. and stayed involved in music as a part-time musician and songwriter. Armand and Julian formed a strong bond through their shared passion for music and their painful yet hopeful life experiences of surviving cancer. The two rhythmic alt-pop collaborators found inspiration within the harmony of their own respective life journeys and a mutual interest in musical innovation.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vnYPcPpvzO0hhjR6YMUkV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Armand Ruby:"},{"t":"p","html":"Like many creatives, Armand was a sensitive child. Growing up, this was of course a blessing and a curse, in the face of both the world’s beauty and its harshness. Throughout his childhood in the northeastern United States, Armand was aware that maintaining this sensitivity might be a challenge. So keeping this cherished inner life alive became a lifelong ambition – and it found expression through music and songwriting. Armand wrote his first little tune at the age of 11, and as a teenager began composing songs, something he’s continued to do throughout life. But his musical talent was matched by a proclivity for science, and a scholarship to an Ivy League university led to a career as an Environmental Scientist."},{"t":"p","html":"Still, Armand continued to be active musically: songwriting, recording demos, performing in rock bands no one’s ever heard of, leading small choral groups, and for several years even singing in a professional opera chorus. A breakthrough came in 2010-2011 with the writing of the book and songs for a musical stage play, <strong>“Equinox.”</strong> Directing the play in its brief but sold-out run in Santa Cruz California was, according to Armand, <em>“both the most difficult and most rewarding experience of my life.”&nbsp;</em>With Equinox, Armand finds himself working at the creative intersection of art and social activism – shining a new light on the often out-of-sight homeless population and the many ways people can become homeless, through story and music. Moving in 2019 to the rural Monterey Bay area community of Royal Oaks, Armand found that one of his neighbors, Julian Colbeck, was an experienced music arranger, producer and keyboardist. From that auspicious meeting arose the musical partnership known as&nbsp;<a href=\"https://karmicneighborhood.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Karmic Neighborhood</a>.<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Julian Colbeck:"},{"t":"p","html":"Julian Colbeck grew up in the south of England, where he learned how to play the piano and ultimately pursued his dreams of being in a London-based rock ‘n’ roll band in his late teens. Julian’s music career took off with the band <em><strong>Charlie</strong></em>, with whom he scored several US Top 40 singles including <strong>“Watching TV”</strong> and <strong>“LA Dreamer.”</strong> Over the span of a 40-year career, Julian worked and toured as a keyboard player/producer with <strong>YES&nbsp;</strong>alumni group <strong>Anderson Bruford Wakeman Howe</strong>, former Genesis guitarist <strong>Steve Hackett</strong>, <strong>Charlie</strong>, <strong>John Miles</strong>, and more. In 2008 Julian began work with his long-time friend, <strong>Alan Parsons</strong>, on the award-winning instructional video series: <a href=\"https://www.artandscienceofsound.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Alan Parsons’ The Art &amp; Science Of Sound Recording</strong></a>. Julian also has written for many esteemed music industry publications and has authored many music and music technology books. Beginning in late 2019, and interrupted by intensive treatment for stage 4 cancer, Julian saw something of value in his neighbor Armand Ruby’s songwriting and his <em>Equinox&nbsp;</em>film project and worked as an arranger, co-producer, and keyboardist on the Equinox preview soundtrack recordings."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Karmic Neighborhood!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fpermalink.php%3Fstory_fbid%3Dpfbid028B4DmeLchn3mad1CNvhtcbUzZwwHQMWbJz2j8zrRmV6wJKprMZeMSApBoFuSNdzCl%26id%3D100082755791779&show_text=true&width=500","height":"539"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Fp%2FCukG75AJFLL%2F%3Futm_source%3Dig_web_copy_link%26igshid%3DMzRlODBiNWFlZA%253D%253D","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/karmicneighborhood/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100082755791779\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | </strong><a href=\"mailto:armand@armandrubymusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>EMAIL</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"254982","title":"Brandon Vee - YouTube","date":"2023-08-04","lead":"New R&B single \"Java Love\" leaves listeners in a groove and launches an official music video!","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/254982/fff00ba7b3d15a5a6d5e4787f50c5126.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"New R&amp;B single \"Java Love\" leaves listeners in a groove and launches an official music video!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7FJwYtNDvm8GItn5MFZec2?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Orlando, FL (August 4, 2023) - R&amp;B Singer-Songwriter <strong>Brandon Vee&nbsp;</strong>drops a new single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7FJwYtNDvm8GItn5MFZec2?si=81682d7800a04363\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Java Love</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on Friday, August 4th. The song’s overarching theme connects the concept of coffee to men and women of color. Some of the chorus lyrics read:&nbsp;"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>Java love (oh yeah oh yeah)</em>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>I need your Java love </em><br>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>Melanin my medicine </em><br>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>Everything I love it when </em><br>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>I need that </em><br>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>I love that </em><br>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>Gimme your Java love</em><br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/gkM1TiALE_k","height":"475"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The lyrics, ‘Coffee you are my happiness straight black with no additives’ and ‘Caution that you’re hot, but I know you’re not, they just want to put the label on’ stand out to me. They point to the notion of media continuously trying to take women of color and make them ‘palatable’ for others by lightening their skin, hiding their curves, or altering how they speak.”","cite":"- R&B Artist, Brandon Vee, on the meaning behind lyrics of \"Java Love\""},{"t":"p","html":"Vee describes that as a Black and Latino man, <strong>“</strong><em><strong>Being accepted in certain situations such as intimacy, but just as easily being dismissed in other scenarios”</strong></em> is a vicious cycle that society has supported time and time again. The lyrical metaphor in “Java Love” highlights the societal issue of hyper-sexualization in the media, especially for women of color. Vee goes on to explain that often, <em>“<strong>...Women of color get labeled as ‘sassy’ or ‘angry black women’ when they try to express themselves or stand up for themselves. My goal for this new single was to empower women of color and remind them that they seen, heard, acknowledged, and celebrated from one person of color to another.</strong>”</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/567594/large-cb711714ebbac9e3bfc87e1ff5c10623.jpg","alt":"\"Java Love\" Cover Art"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/567591/large-b6436313409002bdf6716ce0958928b4.jpg","alt":"brandon2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/567591/preview-896e2313bf4be294b1f52cae6f6045e6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/567592/large-1ea9207ad27218cc54c69c62051983d3.jpg","alt":"brandon3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/567592/preview-2469944522849980b6d05a298f3d7d68.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/567593/large-175cb6ec34ebc78c6f0edf14824f8616.jpg","alt":"brandon 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/567593/preview-b7db34d6e06f54d03b86cd87d92e2ca1.jpg"}]},{"t":"quote","html":"“Java Love” shines light on women of color feeling a constant pressure to measure up to societal standards of who they ‘should be.’ This track acts as a celebration of differences and a reminder of love above all of the challenges in this world.”","cite":"- R&B Artist, Brandon Vee"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brandon Vee:"},{"t":"p","html":"Brooklyn, NY native Brandon Vee fuses the energy of hip-hop with the classic melodies of R&amp;B and Jazz to create a funk-inspired aura and sound. Brandon started his lyrical journey at the young age of 10 when he started writing poetry to express complex feelings of heaviness and discomfort. Brandon continues to use music as a medium of self-discovery and healing intertwining the boundaries of his own worldly perspectives with personal growth. Brandon Vee creates a unique and powerful sound with his music, carrying listeners through storylines of spirituality, introspection, and self-discovery. Vee draws inspiration from diverse yet legendary artists such as <strong>J. Cole</strong>, <strong>Childish Gambino</strong>, and <strong>Funkadelic</strong>. In 2022, Brandon Vee performed alongside famous artists such as <strong>Meg The Stallion</strong>, <strong>Denzel Curry</strong>, <strong>EarthGang</strong>, and more, inspiring him to showcase his new music on a live platform more often. Brandon is dedicated to themes of challenge and healing within his newest album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4SrmEBuPAHhQFKZi6cB7xF?si=-pmO6Se5RdyGyHcq0Vpyzw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Revolution Of The Soul”</strong></a> which released on April 28th, 2023. Stream Brandon’s new single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7FJwYtNDvm8GItn5MFZec2?si=8b8e15e9805345e6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Java Love</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on all streaming platforms now!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Brandon Vee!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://Brandon Vee Shopify\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Brandon Vee Shopify</strong></a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/zug3osYvEc4","height":"400"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.youtube.com/user/brandonveemusic?cbrd=1&amp;ucbcb=1","img":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/ytc/AGIKgqM6UblH3ImOAL4zsQwvmw6wgpalTJcvHXBv3B8NbA=s900-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj","title":"Brandon Vee - YouTube","desc":"Brandon Vee is an artist and performer from Brooklyn NY. His music combines Hip-Hop with Soul, R&B, Funk and even Jazz. As an artist, Brandon provides a pers..."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Cstlj_aLEHD/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://Instagram.com/thatmanvee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.thatmamvee.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>WEBSITE</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/officialbrandonvee/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/thatmanvee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>SOUNDCLOUD</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"256045","title":"Americana Artist Drew Angus Released Brand New Track, \"Broken Heart Last\"","date":"2023-08-03","lead":"The Pop-Rock single is now available to stream on all platforms!","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/256045/506636f4eb40b0b18b3819cef8b5ec3b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Pop-Rock single is now available to stream on all platforms!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/37XX6q8sxIWlOcJcUl60Iq?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Bridgeport, CT (August 3, 2023) - Americana artist, <strong>Drew Angus</strong><strong>,</strong> recently released his new Pop-Rock track, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/37XX6q8sxIWlOcJcUl60Iq?si=b1bfdc5a95b742db\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Broken Heart Last</strong></a>” The song explores themes of heartbreak, falling out of love, relationship turmoil, and more. When the dust settles from a breakup, some days become better than others, but it still hurts when the positive memories of your relationship come flooding back. “Broken Heart Last” provides validation and comfort to listeners who have experienced that crushing post-breakup headspace."},{"t":"p","html":"The lyrics behind “Broken Heart Last” are an upbeat interpretation of the fated question, “How long does a broken heart last?” This track was co-written with New York-based songwriter <strong>Matt Giella</strong> during the pandemic - an era of hardship in both Drew and Matt's lives. At the time, Matt was coping with his divorce while Drew was dealing with a breakup. The duo created “Broken Heart Last” from each of their experiences with failed relationships and the endless pain tied to those sentiments.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/572550/large-93217d350671796a58ddbb063114ab1b.jpg","alt":"Broken Heart Last: Cover Art"},{"t":"quote","html":"“There are countless songs about break-ups and exes, so Matt and I wanted to write something different for listeners to digest. 'Broken Heart Last' dives deeper into the pain associated with a broken heart and discusses the timeline of those unrequited feelings that are often ignored.”","cite":"- Drew Angus, Americana Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3JRBME1P6HDp6nAmcUaaHC?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Drew Angus:"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from Bridgeport, Connecticut, singer-songwriter Drew Angus is putting his own spin on New Americana music, creating catchy yet down-to-earth tunes to share with listeners old and new. With indelible hooks, savvy craftsmanship and relatable lyrics, Angus brings a certain verve to his work that resonates with audiences and fellow performers alike. Angus’ mantra, <em>“I sing for my supper,”</em> reflects his determination and passion for making his mark on the world as an independent artist.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Angus grew up with artists such as <strong>Tom Petty</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;The Beatles</strong>, and<strong>&nbsp;The Rolling Stones</strong>, which have all influenced the artist’s tone and songwriting style to this day. Angus also gains inspiration from modern artists such as <strong>Ben Rector</strong>, <strong>The Lone Bellow</strong>, and <strong>John Mayer</strong>. Angus places his music at the intersection of Americana and Rock ‘n Roll, with a sprinkle of Funk and Retro Soul. Angus has shared stages with <strong>Harry Styles</strong> and <strong>Nile Rogers</strong> (on <em>SNL</em>), <strong>Pat Benatar</strong>, <strong>Ann Willson of Heart</strong>, <strong>Andrea Bocelli</strong> (on <em>Live with Kelly &amp; Ryan</em>), and has toured with <strong>Marc Broussard</strong>. The up-and-coming artist is quickly gaining a following with his lively performances and soulful singing. &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Angus’ latest release, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/37XX6q8sxIWlOcJcUl60Iq?si=cf3cc00317bd4419\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Broken Heart Last</a>,” is an original single he wrote with his friend, Matt Giella and the ultimate <strong>Summer Jam</strong>. The fresh, exciting beat of the song instantly makes you forget you’re reminiscing on a love once lost. The song is available on all streaming platforms. Look out for some more new music from Drew later this year."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Drew!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/drewangusmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@drewangusmusic","post":false},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@drewangusmusic/video/7256814662602280235","handle":"@drewangusmusic"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/drewangusmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@drewangusmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tiktok</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/drewangusmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.threads.com/drewangusmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Threads</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"253562","title":"Orlando Mendez from NBC's \"The Voice\" Drops Country-Rock Single, \"Where I Am Right Now\"","date":"2023-07-28","lead":"The new track \"Where I Am Right Now\" will be the title song of Orlando Mendez's upcoming EP.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/253562/66ac5c6f815090be1dfa0ed923957435.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The new track \"Where I Am Right Now\" will be the title song of Orlando Mendez's upcoming EP."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5WjclqQmS1yyUQp7UAN4t0?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Nashville, TN (July 28, 2023) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1e6rjNsWdsCyUk4HyzgQ6w?si=Hcge_fYHQSOUzFwgr18Bww\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Orlando Mendez</strong></a>, aka the “Cuban Cowboy” from Season 22 of NBC's hit show <em><strong>T</strong></em><strong><em>he Voice</em></strong> is dropping a new Country-Rock ballad,<strong>&nbsp;“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5WjclqQmS1yyUQp7UAN4t0?si=1bf8baf25bf843a6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Where I Am Right Now</strong></a><strong>.”&nbsp;</strong>This track will be the title song for Mendez's upcoming EP, launch date to be determined. “Where I Am Right Now” will give listeners a taste of what's to come in the EP, with lyrical references to falling in love, heartbreak, being stuck in the past, and echoes of nostalgia that tie into this new EP's intention."},{"t":"p","html":"“Where I Am Right Now” was written by <strong>Jason Nix</strong>, <strong>Reid Isbell,</strong> and <strong>Jessie Alexander</strong>. The story told by lyrics and smooth melodies revolves around a man who struggles to let go of a failed relationship and get over the past. This main character finds himself constantly out of touch with his current reality because his mind lives in memories of his ex-lover. The song dives deep into the imagery that is constantly playing in this character's head: the sunset, high tide, dancing with his past lover and staring into her eyes. When the daydream ends, the man finds himself sitting at a bar trying to drown his heartbreak at the bottom of a “poor me round.”"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>YEAH, YOU OUGHTA HEAR HER LAUGHING</em><br>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>I’M &nbsp;DROWNING IN A FULL MOON FROM AN “I THINK I LOVE YOU” &nbsp;</em><br>"},{"t":"lead","html":"<em>WHILE I’M SITTING AT A BAR AT THE BOTTOM OF A POOR ME ROUND </em><br>"},{"t":"caption","html":"<em><u><strong>~ \"Where I Am Right Now\"&nbsp;</strong></u></em><strong><u>Lyrics ~</u></strong>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1e6rjNsWdsCyUk4HyzgQ6w?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"This track fuses melodic elements of Country music with Classic Rock instrumentals. A steady kick-drum beat and dreamy chorus carry the storytelling element of this track, conveying the all-consuming feeling of being stuck in a memory. “Where I Am Right Now” continues with a seemingly controlled flow until a gut-wrenchingly raw bridge breaks the pace: <em>“I've tried my best to move on, but your memory doesn't really care. It will find me right where I'm at and take me right back there.” </em>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I truly believe that anyone who listens to this song can relate or at least empathize with the feelings the lyricist is going through. Everyone can conjure up at least one haunting memory from their past that impacted them deeply. I find that connection beautiful and powerful.”","cite":"- Orlando Mendez, Country-Rock Singer"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563620/large-55f53c5273e74391497952d42147ae29.jpg","alt":"ORL6.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563620/preview-aefcaf9c54abcee62043ca717bbf2bd9.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563621/original-0aa7d49408519332f330a09cf6176226.jpg","alt":"ORL7.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563621/preview-8114e9bd68d6462a3f1cad3324ef2bb6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563622/large-370305f8e5bbf6576893ba375827e965.jpg","alt":"ORL4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563622/preview-af889800d3d0f2f4c43d00924fb8d37a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563623/large-e658db6ce7350f642fb92a805ffc445d.jpg","alt":"ORL5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563623/preview-46c9a7917a4d0874d2a84e0a86e6ebec.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563625/large-4319ae141f309ab4341ed022578705f8.jpg","alt":"ORL2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563625/preview-1a689c31d64ae44a178993249be4f602.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563624/large-f1b70cbc4da8603746b7061f118114a5.jpg","alt":"ORL3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563624/preview-b67c2b0c35562988896485f50bd5dbfe.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563626/large-d9075fc0be014a166e8f8d479b4de2aa.jpg","alt":"ORL1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563626/preview-69a5ced389de8645ee971af1a5b9c103.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563627/large-a9269110fdb9f51c94917340131b29be.jpg","alt":"ORL8.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563627/preview-10f739b34bae20e196b450078634f1c4.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Orlando Mendez:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1e6rjNsWdsCyUk4HyzgQ6w?si=Hcge_fYHQSOUzFwgr18Bww\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Orlando Mendez</strong></a>, aka “The Cuban Cowboy,” was born and raised in Miami, FL. He is a second-generation Cuban American who found a love for country music at an early age. After graduating from the University of Florida and pursuing a short acting career, Orlando began to write and sing his longtime passion: country music. For almost two years he performed all over Florida with his band, “<strong>The Orlando Mendez Band</strong>.” In 2022, Orlando auditioned for season 22 of “<em>The Voice</em>” and was awarded a unanimous, four-chair turn by the coaches on the panel: <strong>Blake Shelton, John Legend, Gwen Stefani&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Camila Cabello</strong>. He was heralded for his unique voice and powerful stage presence and featured in three performances on the show. Orlando now lives in Nashville, TN and is currently in the process of releasing his debut EP. His aim is to bring the vibrancy and energy of his background to the truth and simplicity of country music. Check out Mendez's new single “Where I Am Right Now” now available on all platforms! <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5WjclqQmS1yyUQp7UAN4t0?si=bf4ea57aab0f4f5f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Where I Am Right Now</strong></a><strong>”</strong><em>&nbsp;</em>is also the name of Mendez's upcoming EP,<em>&nbsp;</em>produced by <strong>Nick Worley</strong>. Stay connected with Orlando Mendez on socials for more announcements and EP launch updates!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Orlando!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/orlandojmendezmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@orlandojmendezmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@orlandomendezofficial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/orlando.mendez.54?mibextid=LQQJ4d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://twitter.com/OrlandoMendez54\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TWITTER</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"253570","title":"Claire Reneé Releases New Song “Sadder Days” Ahead of EP","date":"2023-07-28","lead":"California-based R&B artist Claire Reneé will release this new track on Friday, July 28th","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/253570/4c0dfbab6fed47900a699978f41f3c12.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"California-based R&amp;B artist Claire Reneé will release this new track on Friday, July 28th"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/43DEVwmJ2AGyHoeMLC0kMW?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, CA (July 28, 2023) - Rising R&amp;B artist<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.clairereneemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Claire Reneé</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>drops her new single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/43DEVwmJ2AGyHoeMLC0kMW?si=9070a663a6c3431b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sadder Days</strong></a>” on Friday, July 28th. This sultry, soulful track pulls in elements from the current R&amp;B and pop landscapes, moving away from the jazzy route Claire usually takes in her music. The lyrics behind this track relate to the confusing emotions associated with dating and complex relationships, romantic or platonic. Claire reflects on the writing process for “Sadder Days,”<em>&nbsp;</em>remembering a point in time when she trusted people to a fault - especially when it came to them having power over her emotions."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wrote this song about not understanding how someone could give up so abruptly and easily on a relationship. That feeling of the other person letting go hits so deeply, leaving you feeling, angry, and hurt. I hope listeners resonate with the sentiment of getting through the anger, giving up the need to understand what exactly changed in the relationship and healing enough to wish that person well without closure.”","cite":"- Claire Reneé, R&B/Soul Artist"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1Wp8w74ZupCeCZfZwewX25?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"“Sadder Days” will be part of Claire Reneé's upcoming EP, <em><strong>Journal Entries 1-4</strong></em>, which will touch upon some of the same themes. Claire hopes the EP will be relatable for people who journal or track how they are feeling or thinking. Each track on the diary-like EP will act as a journal entry from a significant point in time. The reminiscent nature of this EP is similar to looking back at the past and saying, <em>“What was I thinking,”</em> or <em>“Wow, I've really grown.”</em>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563630/original-a5c5588d2d1da2327683c640169d9537.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563630/preview-11e1eda6239db01899958c36dfb52f0b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563629/original-1220af4c8a321362c1e4b5665db90966.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563629/preview-5ecd9bfaa759fcd301bda2dad32f6112.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563631/original-1fe657373d8f301a377ed9d65e26d4f7.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE6.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563631/preview-54b686b9264fdb67600b02d0d43c8b8a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563628/large-57c5ddc604d4dc44d54d95440e08ef7b.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE 11.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563628/preview-820604a0b4c01362c8d894c1ca68e2be.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563632/large-2975a742bdb9d70157aa2f42ab459123.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE0.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563632/preview-3f09dadbee88f526dce9dbb17c48ce16.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563633/large-e7531776c0fc7a39d45e87b4e1b9ee5d.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE12.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563633/preview-b0b1902708e8814a51d102cca6fb4697.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563634/original-b2aba95d956ce3a6c24b01b2aefb4373.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563634/preview-99eeb11b54011790586522a175fb1423.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563635/original-dfb3a3efc5e86e7cbfecf0b75f5e6d28.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE7.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563635/preview-fb6f83c2918c24b67045c14469f71dc4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563636/large-698d23636fc1e90316a99ce5f5622ba6.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE8.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563636/preview-5a1b355615c05f51b44b2508bd33d067.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563637/large-dff518cd8da0fc7fad1386a542884109.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE9.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563637/preview-3fb9168f5971f4bd39a49c92b76d4495.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563638/original-ed6b2e5f09498438be8f8d6ae0593c7f.jpg","alt":"CLAIRE5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563638/preview-88b1dec82b42b275826f28c02eb6aff6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563639/large-df70cfc617e7837533157b721f03caa5.png","alt":"CLAIRE1.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/563639/preview-b9ec7a22eeeb3a632ffe46a1087e95a0.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Claire Reneé:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.clairereneemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Claire Reneé</strong></a> is a classically trained dancer who sings from the soul. Singing a combination of R&amp;B, soul, jazz, and pop while being heavily influenced by hip-hop, this singer/songwriter’s raspy yet graceful vocals, along with her unique harmonies, always provide an incredible vibe and sound. This multi-talented artist has quite a unique background. Claire began dancing at the early age of 4 and trained at highly esteemed dance schools such as The Dance Theater of <strong>Harlem and Alvin Ailey</strong>. Her natural ear for music and performance led her to study at Berklee College of Music and The New School for Jazz and Contemporary Music."},{"t":"p","html":"Claire Reneé's recently released nine-track album “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5a1GX9zKYwN1pVhlgiYMGu?si=PMVf5djoSHqjnaE3pJzSsg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wings</strong></a>”<strong>&nbsp;</strong>is inspired by relationships and how we cope with both the beautiful and challenging sides of it, touching on certain experiences that help us navigate these situations. Claire confides, <em>“The human experience encompasses lots of different emotions. There may be some anger, sadness, clarity, visits from spirit guides, and even epiphanies. We lead out by honoring that we want to change or see a change in our lives. That includes doing work on ourselves while reminding ourselves we will always push through and even find our Wings. Getting to the other side brings light and even empathy to the very same ones who hurt you, couldn’t show up for you, or wronged you in the past.”</em> You can stream Claire's most recent single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/43DEVwmJ2AGyHoeMLC0kMW?si=fafa421b6f31476e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sadder Days</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on all platforms now! Stay tuned for the release of Claire's EP, <em><strong>Journal Entries 1-4</strong></em>, launching on September 29.&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Claire Reneé:"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/artisterenee/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@artisterenee","post":false},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@artisterenee/video/7258331308743462186","handle":"@artisterenee"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.clairereneemusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Website</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/clairereneemusic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ArtisteRenee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter&nbsp;</strong></a>| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/ArtisteRenee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"253947","title":"Alt-Pop Artist Alec Rose Releases New Single, \"Nothing New\"","date":"2023-07-28","lead":"Alec Rose officially drops latest self-produced bedroom pop single","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/253947/1bab6005dd7a2c6ba67cf9fd0d381642.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Alec Rose officially drops latest self-produced bedroom pop single"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2nQOlJrIj4b4Z69qNcvcYC?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (July 28, 2023) - Alt-Pop artist, <strong>Alec Rose,</strong> just released his new track, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2nQOlJrIj4b4Z69qNcvcYC?si=4472f5d4291044e9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Nothing New</strong></a><em>”&nbsp;</em>on Friday July 28th. Written, recorded, and produced by Alec Rose, “Nothing New” has Lo-fi undertones that are enhanced by charming lead vocals. This track touched upon themes such as: mundanity, feeling stuck, boredom, and more. Rose's lyrics were inspired by the societal expectation of needing something new to report, and being made to feel “less than” when you don't have anything exciting going on in your life."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/21CQpG0IwpVT2SJmoYaeYX?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"“Nothing New” leans into a minimalistic style while managing to maintain a modern clarity and intentionality in the production. The track's wide range of frequencies creates a sonic blend that hits listeners with an intriguing immediacy. The intentional quality of the production elements sets the tone for the song in a way that compliments the lyrical content and vocal performance. The intensity of instrumentals fused with the attitude of the lead vocal immediately fosters an intimacy that invites the listener into a relatable conversation over acoustic chords, snaps, drums, synth and sub bass. Referring to the finalized track, Rose remarks,"},{"t":"quote","html":"“The result is a unique, charming and relatable snack of a song.”","cite":"-Alec Rose, Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/564492/large-7e18076fd00785bb64387d8f17e2ad0e.jpg","alt":"\"Nothing New\" Cover Art"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Alec Rose:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Alec Rose</strong> is a Los Angeles-based singer, songwriter, musician and producer originally from Chicago, IL. He is happiest when he is making melodies and effortlessly alchemizing incoherent thoughts into articulate and beautiful lyrics. Rose developed his signature sound around his falsetto croon, lower register ramblings, or top-of-his-range rasp. With heavy influence from <strong>Bon Iver</strong>, <strong>Frank Ocean</strong>, <strong>Alabama Shakes</strong>, and <strong>Phil Collins</strong>, Rose's music is a captivating fusion of alternative, pop, and folk. Rose's debut single <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3sEYezu4CcrExwNyF5Md4x?si=31c9df2e3fb641d6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Underwater</strong></em><strong>&nbsp;</strong></a>launched in early 2023 and his most recent single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2nQOlJrIj4b4Z69qNcvcYC?si=fe665c3b36db45b9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Nothing New</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is now available for streaming on all platforms! “Nothing New” was mixed by <strong>NICOLOSI </strong>and mastered by <strong>John Davis</strong>. Stay tuned for upcoming release announcements and updates via Alec's social media platforms linked below!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Alec Rose!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/CvPln9SLGHG/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@alecrosemusic/video/7260350174516546859","handle":"@alecrosemusic"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100090103134102\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/alecrosemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@alecrosemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@alecrosemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"252172","title":"ellakate Drops Music Video For Upbeat Alt-Pop Track \"Dry\"","date":"2023-07-21","lead":"\"Dry\" plays ahead of ellakate's debut EP launching in the Fall.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/252172/c893b9e71942ad128d7d6412327e0df6.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Dry\" plays ahead of ellakate's debut EP launching in the Fall."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7xwlFkejBrhkn4jEHEkjVD?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Atlanta, GA (July 21, 2023) - Rising Alt-Pop artist <a href=\"https://www.ellakate.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>ellakate</strong></a> just released her new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7xwlFkejBrhkn4jEHEkjVD?si=ef230ce4280e4c8d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dry</strong></a>,” on July 14th, and dropped a <a href=\"https://youtu.be/VDCdDiRkv0w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">music video</a> for the world to see on July 21st. The song will be followed by its music video release on July 21st. This new track was inspired by feeling burnt-out, numb, and indifferent. <strong>ellakate</strong> hopes to connect to listeners with her emotionally powerful lyrics and driving, catchy melodies that offer a sense of euphoria. Both “<strong>Dry</strong>” and “<strong>I'm Yours</strong>,” which ellakate released last month, will be part of an upcoming EP slated to launch in August.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/VDCdDiRkv0w","height":"350"},{"t":"p","html":"&nbsp; &nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ellakate</strong> explains that “Dry” is a song she wrote while experiencing an intense burn-out. The artist was inspired to write lyrics such as <em>“Trekking through the desert hoping for some angsty weather,”</em> while she was simultaneously juggling school, work, and athletics. “Dry” confronts ellakate’s lack of motivation and her craving for her ambition back."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561190/large-532263f3e5a400f72beb62dc72eead81.png","alt":"\"Dry\" Cover Art"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song is about the vicious cycle of exhaustion and feeling numb. “Dry” conveys the internal frustration I have from not being able to dig myself out of that hole. I love the fusion of lively instrumentals juxtaposed by lyrics that express my fatigue.”","cite":"ellakate, Rising Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560440/original-a986b1279efab5677e2b802ca3ba7666.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-07-11 at 6.57.57 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560440/preview-dea8e19461d137abf638cabbb01ab333.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560442/original-4548bff0f12c9b77c6e21c90753f7148.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-07-11 at 6.57.19 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560442/preview-76ac34f949b66a52a02f903d10c40df6.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560441/original-31f971457ea8aca419d5aaedfde3db8f.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-07-11 at 6.58.17 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560441/preview-b93be07fcd9876646a8accf5405f9066.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560446/original-6d2a39289c2f0d10e3ea062f5cccac71.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-07-11 at 6.57.08 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560446/preview-582649369a1f807ae87b134d75788c2e.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560445/original-8af07ff4e66f49b6733fb12cb2bfe1a8.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-07-11 at 6.58.33 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560445/preview-7a1fe00124f6f353c0c6fa5e540a2048.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560444/large-d0ffeb8c1eec8a828f7381aca8a1e72c.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-07-11 at 6.57.46 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560444/preview-9b416d7c1d9b265966fa16d345b3786d.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560443/large-87ce9a9272aa03eac35d04d6b424ba5c.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-07-11 at 6.58.08 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560443/preview-92638dc74a931581c2b0f370da90187e.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560447/large-42d946aa32a580c66520462f681c6fba.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-07-11 at 6.56.56 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560447/preview-ade8e43472dcc1d78cad08e5acb7aa81.png"}]},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0t5IrUFo0RQnOfVkhZplHd?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About ellakate:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Ella Greenbaum</strong>, artistically known as ellakate, is an alternative pop singer-songwriter born, raised, and based in Atlanta, Georgia. Growing up with musical parents and a knack for creating and performing, ellakate found a passion for music that went beyond forcing her brothers to listen to her melodies as a child.&nbsp;<em>“When my dad first explained what the song ‘<strong>Brandy</strong>’ by <strong>Looking Glass</strong> was about, I discovered the magic of storytelling in songwriting. I have been singing and making up songs for as long as I can remember,”</em> said ellakate about her innate talents. She has written hundreds of songs since her childhood exploring topics that coincide with the journey of growing up and finding love, filling piles of notebooks in her room with song lyrics. ellakate’s songs recount stories and experiences that may have not happened to her but are inspired by events that have impacted her."},{"t":"p","html":"Her voice has been compared to a<strong>&nbsp;</strong>“young <strong>Amy Winehouse</strong>,” showing her vocal prowess - honest and sensual, with a hint of innocence. Her sultry vocals mixed with her haunting, bold, and romantic sound are reminiscent of artists like <strong>Billie Eilish</strong>, <strong>Tove Lo</strong> and <strong>Lana Del Rey</strong>. She has plans to release music throughout 2022 and 2023 and perform live shows in addition to casual appearances. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way. Stay tuned for ellakate’s upcoming EP late this summer - which will include her two most recent releases, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6Xk9Zucz7S2PPXOFeeeH8q?si=2e699c834ccf4cf7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I'm Yours</strong></a>,” and “<strong>Dry</strong>.” Stay tuned for the “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7xwlFkejBrhkn4jEHEkjVD?si=7f21434c0d454e6d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dry</strong></a>” music video, officially dropping on July 21st. To keep up with ellakate's latest releases, performances, announcements, and more - check out her social profiles below!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With ellakate!"},{"t":"tiktok","href":"https://www.tiktok.com/@ellakatemusic/video/7245424410902007083","handle":"@ellakatemusic"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"252611","title":"Tim Qualls Launches New Pop Single \"Forever\"","date":"2023-07-21","lead":"Alt-Pop artist Tim Qualls releases his new single as the first track to be featured in his upcoming debut album.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/252611/b96d270597f9ed7228c4336e9e8f3faa.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Alt-Pop artist Tim Qualls releases his new single as the first track to be featured in his upcoming debut album."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2oheHd1XwCuN3cFzZV7Tid?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston, TX (July 21, 2023) - Houston-based Alt-Pop artist <a href=\"https://www.timqualls.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tim Qualls</strong></a> releases his newest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2oheHd1XwCuN3cFzZV7Tid?si=2e2a2bbd8bbf4fc2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Forever</strong></a>” on Friday, July 21. The new song will be featured in Qualls’ upcoming debut album. This new track is a feel-good tune that describes the intoxicating feeling of finding a “twin flame” and falling in love. The song is a lush, melodic balance of organic vocals, brought together by grounded yet upbeat instrumentals.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I hope this song translates to listeners as the sentiment of wanting to hold onto the special and euphoric moments in life.”","cite":"- Tim Qualls, Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561192/large-3ce4584fdb1b37922c05ec0e29a82d3d.jpg","alt":"\"Forever\" Cover Art - Tim Qualls"},{"t":"p","html":"This new release represents two versions of the artist, one young and naive and one grown-up and mature, fusing together in harmony. Qualls remarks that this track, “<em>T</em><em>his track represents the type of music I wish I was mature enough to write when I was younger,”&nbsp;</em>says Qualls<em>.&nbsp;</em>Qualls strives to share music with listeners that is emotionally honest, dynamic, and transformative. With the release of \"Forever<em>,\"&nbsp;</em>the artist is defining a new era of life and creation. This single and upcoming album define a new, more refined and mature version of Tim Qualls as a songwriter and overall artist. The production of the upcoming debut album took 10 years of studio time, life experience, and personal growth to bring to fruition.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/12J7rAVoeFIUNkRelq5zw8?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561194/large-84839ec026451871d369802d29b6d3d2.jpg","alt":"TIM5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561194/preview-8a704bc87bb83d8b59ec738975277c1b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561193/large-7a4c6700edda03448ea2871d40ad110c.jpg","alt":"TIM 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561193/preview-c17affba9b040fd31176880e9582ee01.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561196/original-5fe7ab72be12b623afc646f44aadcc7d.jpg","alt":"TIM3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561196/preview-5b8d7ceb191e49eb405d51e049b36dbe.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561195/original-56da010d578f837186e871b9cc7f0904.jpg","alt":"TIM2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561195/preview-bc123971464c9d5e4b7f36fbd5b0b4f1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561197/large-3493ec06b65e2eba17fabe28e7ae244c.jpg","alt":"TIM4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/561197/preview-438db03120bb4083eab4a4a21f895773.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Tim Qualls:"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston-based songwriter <strong>Tim Qualls</strong>, delivers rootsy soul music that is grounded in family, heartache, and a positive outlook on life very few write about. Influenced by legends like <strong>Ray Charles</strong>, <strong>Jamie Cullum</strong>, and <strong>John Mayer</strong>, musicians compare him to a “soul artist that croons on the piano.” His productions have been compared to <strong>Adele</strong>, <strong>Sam Smith</strong>, and <strong>Ryan Tedder</strong>. Once awarded Houston Press’ “Best New Act” award, Qualls continues to deliver new music every year. Tim has been featured on Spotify playlists such as <strong>LIFE SUCKS</strong>, <strong>DINNER MUSIC</strong>, <strong>SOULFUL BLEND</strong>, and <strong>COZY BLEND</strong>. His new single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2oheHd1XwCuN3cFzZV7Tid?si=4da46a8a26214bd1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Forever</em></strong></a><strong>”</strong> released on July 21st, will be part of Tim Qualls’ upcoming debut album."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Tim!"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"251699","title":"Emily Nicole Green Releases Catchy, Cathartic Americana Primal Scream with “Wreckage”","date":"2023-07-20","lead":"Green describes Wreckage as “The Letter You Wrote To Your Ex But Burned Before Sending” and digs in deep to a swampy, bluesy, Americana soundscape.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/251699/11cafd711d938605b8a4a2aa7a0777ac.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Green describes Wreckage as “The Letter You Wrote To Your Ex But Burned Before Sending” and digs in deep to a swampy, bluesy, Americana soundscape.<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3dSmlxpSvh7RKiq9vlIdZa?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (July 20, 2023) - NYC-based singer-songwriter, <strong>Emily Nicole Green</strong>, is releasing her second track, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3dSmlxpSvh7RKiq9vlIdZa?si=0b90e776383f487b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wreckage</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on July 20th, and this time her Americana sound is leaning heavily into jazz and blues. Green taps into the seething anger and biting shame that are the fallout from the rejection of unrequited love as her emotionally charged lyrics and gritty, raw vocals offer the fury of a woman scorned. We are taught to keep these kinds of feelings under wraps, but at least for the two minutes and thirty-two seconds that the song is playing, Green grants us permission to feel every one of those feelings and then some. “Wreckage” is a song for the people who have been brought to their knees by the very person they thought loved them back."},{"t":"p","html":"The musical composition Green has produced with “Wreckage,” is a genre-bending mix of jazz and blues alongside pop and Americana. Her vocal moves from sultry and smoky into powerful and brutal, making you feel like you’re lost at sea with no sign of land, sonically encapsulating the feeling of being completely blindsided by a new reality you were not at all prepared for. By saying the things we have all wanted to say at one time, but didn’t, “Wreckage,” rewrites that time in your life when you realized that the solid ground beneath your feet was actually quicksand and offers you a safe space where you can let it all hang out. “Wreckage” offers solidarity to those who have been gaslit and led on, only to fall from the heights that love or even the possibility of love, can take you. Green calls on clever, biting wit to help express her feral feelings in lines such as: <em>“It must have all been in my head, all those nights of candid conversations, boundaries breaking left and right ‘til 3am were never laced with romantic intonations, hey, that’s just how you talk to friends.” </em>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://lnk.to/wreckage","label":"Listen on All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Music is a safe space to go to when we need to let our anger run free. The intensity of emotions we are left to sift through in the wake of heartbreak—especially when we don’t see that kind of rejection coming—can shake us to the core and put us on our knees, completely shifting our sense of reality as we know it. We need to be able to scream and rage and cry. We need to reconnect to our sense of self and begin to rebuild from the wreckage. We need to do what we can to feel the pain so we can release it from our bodies. Singing this song at the top of your lungs in the car may not be what your therapist ordered, but I highly recommend it.”","cite":"- Emily Nicole Green on the inspiration for her new song, \"Wreckage\""},{"t":"p","html":"In the fever dream of emotion that suffuses this track, there is also a sense of reclaiming a self-worth that has been trampled on, with lyrics like <em>“thought you could treat me like a losing scratch-off ticket, the kind you’d shove in a junk drawer.”</em> Awakening an empowerment, a recollection of identity, and a sense of self that may have gone missing during the relationship itself or during the cat-and-mouse lead up that offered false hope for a relationship. Anger is active, it’s not passive. It shows there is still a fire in the belly and that once the pain has subsided, there will be a Phoenix rising from these ashes.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560381/large-13ee4b6e28f0b2d1f99aa7ae364dbf3d.jpg","alt":"Copy of 05_Richard Corman (Credit)_photo_for web.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560381/preview-a43cbf6d7f0ca0828c9d3fd3094f05fb.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560383/large-2d427268342b8ca7786330bc4cfe203c.jpg","alt":"Copy of 06_Richard Corman (Credit)_photo_forweb.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560383/preview-921dfc3091b02821e00518acd4cc408a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560392/large-5e7591110f2570e7d2f369886ec3d64b.jpeg","alt":"EMILY1.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560392/preview-0feb2e57f29b496848a6ece7774afc06.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560393/large-e3a4ae4cd8878ca65740ea883624d250.jpeg","alt":"EMILY2.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560393/preview-e089c53fe3f6b196eafb9e3b838889b5.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560394/large-62431571663127b494c71b1605827d15.jpeg","alt":"EMILY5.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560394/preview-f6afd982f8049762721a8ab16b6cc415.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560395/large-0af0198b0c5cbe626af2780bdebcb9fe.jpeg","alt":"EMILY4.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560395/preview-bc9db7e123b3ad86df0d42b42669755c.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560396/large-2d50c1e055f976b2bb2bdd3b5f80958f.jpeg","alt":"EMILY3.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560396/preview-f0c857bbceedfbc2d33acf2fa12f67ef.jpeg"}]},{"t":"quote","html":"Being treated like this and feeling this anger response awakened the part of me that remembers who the hell I am. This song is for the part of me that wants to have a chance to say everything I felt and validate the reality of what I experienced, but also for the part of me that wants to hold myself accountable for not letting this happen to me again.","cite":"- Emily Nicole Green"},{"t":"p","html":"Emily Nicole Green's vocals are supported by a jazz drum kit, electric bass, and piano all played by <strong>Greg Neel</strong>, a haunting cello by <strong>Erica Ransbottom</strong>, and a punchy upright bass played by <strong>Barry Bales</strong>. Produced by Emily Nicole Green. Arranged by <strong>Mike Williamson</strong>. Recorded and Mixed by <strong>Ryan Wilson</strong> at <strong>HeyHey Studios</strong> in Griffin, GA and mastered by <strong>Alex Sterling</strong> at <strong>Precision Sound Studios</strong> in NYC."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3dSmlxpSvh7RKiq9vlIdZa?si=2217f78c8b484853\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wreckage</a>”</strong> is the second release to be included within Emily Nicole Green’s forthcoming EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/playlist/0s1SJC3ZJPQ1yv6u6zdEWv?si=1ba25ff2f48c45cb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Outrunning The Animal</strong></em></a>, anticipated to be released in October of this year."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/playlist/0s1SJC3ZJPQ1yv6u6zdEWv?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Emily Nicole Green:"},{"t":"p","html":"NYC-based singer-songwriter, Emily Nicole Green shines a light into the depths of her own emotional interiority with her lyrics and her sound. Her vulnerable writing, powerful vocal, and skillful vibrato work together to offer listeners immediate emotional resonance and stirring storytelling that stay with them long after her songs end.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Green has been writing and performing her original songs since she was a freshman in high school. At 17, she began dealing with debilitating anxiety and panic that stopped her from pursuing her dreams for nearly two decades. In 2019, she decided it was now or never and began pouring herself into her music. She posted cover songs on Patreon and a year later landed her first TV spot with a cover of “<strong>Greasy Frybread</strong>” played over the credits of Season 1, Ep. 4 of FX’s <strong>Reservation Dogs</strong>.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Green’s songwriting is where she gives herself permission to tell herself the truth, processing her emotions and not judging what they have to say, letting the songs be told by the parts of her that still ache. On what guides her writing, Emily says, <em>“At the altar of the ache, you’ll find the light below the wound.” </em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Emily Nicole Green’s debut EP, <em>Outrunning The Animal</em>, which mixes Americana with indie-folk, pop, jazz, blues, and country, is anticipated to be released in October of this year."},{"t":"h3","html":"About The EP:"},{"t":"p","html":"Emily Nicole Green’s forthcoming debut EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/playlist/0s1SJC3ZJPQ1yv6u6zdEWv?si=1ba25ff2f48c45cb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Outrunning The Animal</strong></em></a>, is set to be released October 2023. The EP includes five songs that each live in the liminal space between Americana and indie folk, while leaning into other genres— pop (<strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5QlHxADLZsI26wccH2egw2?si=8ace0dc71f3f49d9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>It’s Gonna Be Okay</strong></a><strong>”</strong>), country (<strong>“Hole In My Heart”</strong>), blues and jazz (<strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3dSmlxpSvh7RKiq9vlIdZa?si=2217f78c8b484853\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wreckage</strong></a><strong>”</strong>)—depending on the track. In her songwriting for this EP, Green works through grief and rage, rejection and desperation, the indignities of unrequited love, while testing out the waters of acceptance and hope."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6QNbIluNpRc2ejEJmFQFUT?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Emily!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/emilynicolegreen/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@emilynicolegreen","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/EmilyColeGreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@emilycolegreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/EmilyNicoleGreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"251265","title":"Karmic Neighborhood Releases Alt-Pop Single \"I Learned to Forgive\" Ahead of Feature Film","date":"2023-07-14","lead":"This track is the fourth release of a six-single series leading up to the soundtrack album launch for 'Equinox the Musical.'","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/251265/d011f3dccc8604e8e80cff9a5bda4bf2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This track is the fourth release of a six-single series leading up to the soundtrack album launch for 'Equinox the Musical.'"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0ifmeAbWrjnKyzeKN8oJIr?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Royal Oaks, CA (July 14, 2023) - <strong>Armand Ruby&nbsp;</strong>and<strong>&nbsp;Julian Colbeck&nbsp;</strong>of musical group <strong>Karmic Neighborhood</strong>&nbsp;just released a new alt-pop single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0ifmeAbWrjnKyzeKN8oJIr?si=cb7ac270fc124e1c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Learned to Forgive</strong></a>,<strong>”</strong> the fourth track in a series of singles for their upcoming feature film“<a href=\"https://equinoxmusical.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Equinox the Musical</strong></a>.” Equinox is the story of two homeless young lovers who discover that forgiveness, gratitude, and love can be the keys to navigating life’s most challenging circumstances. This track touches upon themes of forgiveness, resiliency, peace of mind, hopelessness, and more.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"In the film, the message of forgiveness is delivered in a heartfelt way from Phoebe, the homeless wise-woman who counsels main character <strong>Katie </strong>in her time of distress. This mid-tempo power song contains mesmerizing lead vocals, intertwining vocal harmonies, and a scintillating instrumental backing track.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/ILearnedtoForgive","label":"Listen to \"I Learned To Forgive\" On All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Forgiveness is a mysterious thing. We might think that it benefits the person being forgiven, that it's something we do for someone else. But even more than that, we are the ones who benefit when we can forgive someone who has wronged us. Replacing our resentment and anger with compassion can have the magical effect of restoring our sanity - freeing us from the burden of obsessing over the wound. This message is powerfully delivered in “I Learned to Forgive” by the compelling vocals of well-known Santa Cruz (California) vocalist <strong>Tammi Brown</strong>, backed by Colbeck and Ruby’s dynamic instrumental arrangement.&nbsp;There are echoes of <strong>Nina Simone</strong> in the combination of Brown's moving vocals and the song’s social message.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“A triumph of light at the end of a tunnel of adversity, Tammi Brown brings soulful grit to the vocal of this powerful and relentless mid-tempo rocker.”","cite":"- Julian Colbeck, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I Learned to Forgive is a moving affirmation of the power of forgiveness – encouraging us to just get over it and get on with life.”","cite":"- Armand Ruby, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"p","html":"The full Equinox the Musical preview soundtrack album will be released on the fall equinox, Sept. 22, 2023.<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/557687/large-1c0ee00937d00b7391c11069aca92745.jpg","alt":"armand 99.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/557687/preview-d2cada7e913f87c05552054a8eee7cde.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/557688/large-4816e9e83ce7a26de96002a8e6dced4a.jpg","alt":"armand 98.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/557688/preview-b15341076a98aea57e0b5a02081a9908.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Karmic Neighborhood:"},{"t":"p","html":"The west coast-based team are strangers-turned-neighbors, turned rhythmic alt-pop collaborators. <strong>Armand Ruby</strong> and <strong>Julian Colbeck</strong> are two lifelong musicians in their 60's who met by chance when they moved to the same neighborhood on the central California coast. <strong>Julian </strong>was formerly a London-based rock star and lifelong music industry veteran, while <strong>Armand </strong>was professionally an environmental scientist who stayed involved in music as a part-time musician and songwriter. Armand and Julian formed a strong bond through their shared passion for music and the painful yet hopeful life experience of surviving cancer. The two found inspiration within the harmony of their own respective life journeys and a mutual interest in musical innovation.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vnYPcPpvzO0hhjR6YMUkV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Armand Ruby:"},{"t":"p","html":"Like many creatives, Armand was a sensitive child. Growing up, this was of course a blessing and a curse, in the face of both the world’s beauty and its harshness. Throughout his childhood in the northeastern United States, Armand was aware that maintaining this sensitivity might be a challenge. So keeping this cherished inner life alive became a lifelong ambition – and it found expression through music and songwriting. Armand wrote his first little tune at the age of 11, and as a teenager began composing songs, something he’s continued to do throughout life. But his musical talent was matched by a proclivity for science, and a scholarship to an Ivy League university led to a career as an Environmental Scientist."},{"t":"p","html":"Still, Armand continued to be active musically: songwriting, recording demos, performing in rock bands no one’s ever heard of, leading small choral groups, and for several years even singing in a professional opera chorus. A breakthrough came in 2010-2011 with the writing of the book and songs for a musical stage play, <strong>“Equinox.”</strong> Directing the play in its brief but sold-out run in Santa Cruz California was, according to Armand, <em>“both the most difficult and most rewarding experience of my life.”&nbsp;</em>With Equinox, Armand finds himself working at the creative intersection of art and social activism – shining a new light on the often out-of-sight homeless population and the many ways people can become homeless, through story and music. Moving in 2019 to the rural Monterey Bay area community of Royal Oaks, Armand found that one of his neighbors, Julian Colbeck, was an experienced music arranger, producer and keyboardist."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Julian Colbeck:"},{"t":"p","html":"Julian Colbeck grew up in the south of England, where he learned how to play the piano and ultimately pursued his dreams of being in a London-based rock ‘n’ roll band in his late teens. Julian’s music career took off with the band <em><strong>Charlie</strong></em>, with whom he scored several US Top 40 singles including <strong>“Watching TV”</strong> and <strong>“LA Dreamer.”</strong> Over the span of a 40-year career, Julian worked and toured as a keyboard player/producer with <strong>YES&nbsp;</strong>alumni group <strong>Anderson Bruford Wakeman Howe</strong>, former Genesis guitarist <strong>Steve Hackett</strong>, <strong>Charlie</strong>, <strong>John Miles</strong>, and more. In 2008 Julian began work with his long-time friend, <strong>Alan Parsons</strong>, on the award-winning instructional video series: <a href=\"https://www.artandscienceofsound.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Alan Parsons’ The Art &amp; Science Of Sound Recording</strong></a>. Julian also has written for many esteemed music industry publications and has authored many music and music technology books. Beginning in late 2019, and interrupted by intensive treatment for stage 4 cancer, Julian saw something of value in his neighbor Armand Ruby’s songwriting and his <em>Equinox&nbsp;</em>film project and worked as an arranger, co-producer, and keyboardist on the Equinox preview soundtrack recordings."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Karmic Neighborhood!"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"248844","title":"Hip Hop Artist Brandon Vee Drops New Single \"Introverted\"","date":"2023-07-07","lead":"Reiki Healer x R&B artist Brandon Vee releases his new upbeat track + music video.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/248844/acc5c42eb37b93c1b98013cf0e52482b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Reiki Healer x R&amp;B artist Brandon Vee releases his new upbeat track + music video."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5oMdQHEcMhC8SADFCmFE7S?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Orlando, FL (July 7, 2023) - Soulful R&amp;B artist <strong>Brandon Vee</strong> drops his new single, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5oMdQHEcMhC8SADFCmFE7S?si=e6d7ecc1bd2540ce\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Introverted”&nbsp;</strong></a>this Friday, July 7th. The song, “Introverted” explores feelings and experiences from an introvert's perspective. Brandon expresses that as an introvert, boundary-setting can be difficult, especially while trying to accept who you are as a person. The lyrics behind this track tap into the struggles of being an introvert in an upbeat and playful way."},{"t":"p","html":"“Introverted” was created as a comfort for introverted listeners, reminding them that they aren't alone. This lively party song recognizes that introverts aren't always the “life of the party,” but that doesn't mean they can't have fun in their own way. The music video for the single was inspired by the legendary film, <strong>“Castaway”</strong> the iconic volleyball <strong>“Wilson.”</strong> Brandon Vee wanted to tie this reference into the music video as an ironic nod to introverts wanting to be alone (especially on vacation). Catch the Castaway-inspired music video for <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5oMdQHEcMhC8SADFCmFE7S?si=e8ac206cc0d24046\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Introverted”</strong></a> on June 30th!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/wS1OW6PJZDY","height":"485"},{"t":"quote","html":"'Introverted' is the party song for people who don’t go to parties.”","cite":"Brandon Vee, R&B Artist"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/553513/original-ed600422df54dab54b4b00664c969f21.jpg","alt":"BRANDON1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/553513/preview-cec723dd30424a3fa62ea64a2825be7e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/553514/large-944375d2d39baf1e2118b0923d07db9d.jpg","alt":"BRANDON2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/553514/preview-6017209ea5986d78f57c7f4876fbea14.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brandon Vee:"},{"t":"p","html":"Brooklyn, NY native Brandon Vee fuses the energy of hip-hop with the classic melodies of R&amp;B and Jazz to create a funk-inspired aura and sound. Brandon started his lyrical journey at the young age of 10 when he started writing poetry to express complex feelings of heaviness and discomfort. Brandon continues to use music as a medium of self-discovery and healing intertwining the boundaries of his own worldly perspectives with personal growth. Brandon Vee creates a unique and powerful sound with his music, carrying listeners through storylines of spirituality, introspection, and self-discovery. Vee draws inspiration from diverse yet legendary artists such as <strong>J. Cole</strong>, <strong>Childish Gambino</strong>, and <strong>Funkadelic</strong>. In 2022, Brandon Vee performed alongside famous artists such as <strong>Meg The Stallion</strong>, <strong>Denzel Curry</strong>, <strong>EarthGang</strong>, and more, inspiring him to showcase his new music on a live platform more often. Brandon is dedicated to themes of challenge and healing within his newest album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4SrmEBuPAHhQFKZi6cB7xF?si=-pmO6Se5RdyGyHcq0Vpyzw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Revolution Of The Soul”</strong></a> which released on April 28th, 2023. Stream Brandon's new single <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5oMdQHEcMhC8SADFCmFE7S?si=e8ac206cc0d24046\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>“Introverted”</strong></a> on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Brandon Vee!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://Brandon Vee Shopify\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Brandon Vee Shopify</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"248849","title":"Americana-Indie Rock Artist Horseshoes Drops New Upbeat Single","date":"2023-07-07","lead":"Americana-indie rock artist Horseshoes launches the new single, \"Hide and Seek\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/248849/ce8c9b550d935ee71f03c3db4e0325d6.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Americana-indie rock artist Horseshoes launches the new single, \"Hide and Seek\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/29zUzEi2MIZA5NhbWUaREp?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Washington, DC (July 7, 2023) - Emerging indie-rock artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0cIVB4MH1nJhx5soIMZeKt?si=0RHAiQQVTNuyK96Ks7il5Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Horseshoes</strong>&nbsp;</a>launches his new song, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/29zUzEi2MIZA5NhbWUaREp?si=544e0b9d828746b1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hide and Seek</strong></a><strong>”&nbsp;</strong>on Friday, July 7. Although the song has a light overtone, the message relates to holding onto the past. The song starts off referencing somebody who is scared to be abandoned again - which relates to the overall theme of “Hide and Seek.” Horseshoes is inspired by the playful nature of the relationship he has with his daughter, and infuses that lightheartedness into his music."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/HideandSeek","label":"Listen to \"Hide and Seek\" on All Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song encourages listeners to realize the dissonant interplay between having fun and being scared, not unlike playing a game of Hide and Seek.”","cite":"Horseshoes, Indie-Rock Artist"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560403/large-a4f9a5c58f9c71c520b10f59ebe13a19.jpg","alt":"image_processing20230619-979470-1jqpox8 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560403/preview-6ecad797c9d06bb09421b3a585f37ce9.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560402/original-24b2dd890e38da8d880275178a9a4dd1.jpeg","alt":"AustinSelectedHolga001HiRes.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560402/original-24b2dd890e38da8d880275178a9a4dd1.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560401/original-5552a690295dfef74777b49f4ad791f4.jpeg","alt":"photo-output.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/560401/original-5552a690295dfef74777b49f4ad791f4.jpeg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<sup>Photo Credit: Nancy Breslin</sup><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Horseshoes:"},{"t":"p","html":"Austin Greaves is a Washington DC-based musician who performs under the name Horseshoes. He released his debut album, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4X4f7fYdW98GedO8tKDh0T?si=Up5VrHYbT2GqWrpxmlxw2w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Desert</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> in June of 2022, which was followed up with a single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4x86xnafoYR0SDd6RvYQbz?si=wNflVB0YS2O8CfEQE-T8Pw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Come With Me</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> released in October 2022. Check out Horseshoes' new single <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/29zUzEi2MIZA5NhbWUaREp?si=84aa70f5a6414946\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hide and Seek</strong></a><strong>”</strong> now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0cIVB4MH1nJhx5soIMZeKt?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Horseshoes!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@horseshoesguy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/horseshoesguy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"250659","title":"This is the homepage for A Permanent Shadow, an Electronic Rock and Synth Pop band based in Barcelona. New album HUMDRUM is out on March 4, 2022.","date":"2023-07-07","lead":"A Permanent Shadow officially releases his newest single, \"Number One Fan.\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/250659/766b456b87766d9faab58ec6fd8f1281.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"A Permanent Shadow officially releases his newest single, \"Number One Fan.\"<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5GnMsEgsx5d9z5yav4vJlz?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Barcelona, SPAIN (JULY 7, 2023) - <a href=\"https://www.apermanentshadow.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>A Permanent Shadow</strong></a>, the musical collective around <strong>CP Fletcher </strong>just released a new pop-inspired single, <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5GnMsEgsx5d9z5yav4vJlz?si=5289fba52406473e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Number One Fan</strong></a>.”</strong> This new track dives into themes related to toxic relationships such as loyalty, regret, remorse, and more."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>A Permanent Shadow</strong> wrote this single after ruminating around the question,<em>&nbsp;“Can you go back in time to fix things that lie firmly in the past?”.</em> “<em>Number One Fan</em>” is a catchy yet melancholic ode to loyalty and unconditional support. The song fuses modern pop with sonic elements from eighties electronic music."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6mrGJN7uKAelkBlqMqUn8d?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"CP Fletcher of&nbsp;<strong>A Permanent Shadow</strong> channeled<strong>&nbsp;Joni Mitchell</strong>’s <strong>“Big Yellow Taxi”</strong> while writing this new track, taking Joni's powerful songwriting skills and using them as inspiration for his own creativity.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I don’t tend to write lyrics about personal relationships. I’m much more comfortable writing about tsunamis, self-help gurus, religion or the corporate world.”","cite":"CP Fletcher of A Permanent Shadow, Alternative Pop Artist"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/556636/original-cdcf5ab95e619f2dad8d1bef6e863c99.jpg","alt":"FAN1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/556636/preview-022708374805a841e9547935e01771d7.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/556638/original-785b04798265b366c00ecc754a66fc8c.jpg","alt":"FAN4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/556638/preview-56afd8caddd1beef1882043c6510f062.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/556637/large-cd4131741b133145200b88cd2db90e22.jpg","alt":"FAN2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/556637/preview-ff92750506a7edb396e49639b0051de5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/556639/large-33cba84852d354d43d3695cad922f673.jpg","alt":"FAN3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/556639/preview-e46b1e3160061c350ba6c49638fb3ca2.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About A Permanent Shadow:"},{"t":"p","html":"A Permanent Shadow is a band for want of a better description. Its only fixture is CP Fletcher who for his recordings surrounds himself with a rotating cast of musicians and producers. Fletcher used to be a drummer in various bands that went nowhere, so at one point, inspired by David Bowie's death, he decided to form his own band as a singer. CP took his first steps as a front man forming a <strong>Lou Reed </strong>tribute project, <strong>The Magic</strong> and <strong>Loss Orchestra</strong>. Such is his admiration for the curmudgeon from New York that the tribute experience ended up bleeding into A Permanent Shadow via a cover of <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1MNWaaHKNJGQlqH3xUys5d?si=9e59ab1be4524036\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sword of Damocles</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> originally featured on Reed’s Magic and Loss album and included on the band's first album “Songs of Loss” in a reworked form.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The band involves various collaborators, although two musicians so far feature on all recordings: <strong>Albert Català</strong>, a classically trained piano player, helps CP whip the demos into shape, while the finishing touches in the studio are usually provided by renowned producer <strong>Valentí Nieto</strong>. Both albums <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0d7H2IzDxXwpNsW4NheDdY?si=JE_vOr5jS4ali2DmtX8Ubw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Songs of Loss</strong></a><strong>”</strong> (2019) and <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/59GgNHgWEJzZrgGMriVpAj?si=_bq1MQj1Soq3coDIfTbxng\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Humdrum</strong></a><strong>”</strong> (2022) as well as the EP <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/45TQ4Z15JQObdtLpvGuPIU?si=IgMtPgWrTBW4b1UcnSZT9Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>UnderCover</strong></a><strong>’</strong> (2022) and the new single were recorded with contributions from these two musicians."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with A Permanent Shadow!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/R6TBGLfuup4","height":"450"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/apermanentshadow/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@apermanentshadow","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.apermanentshadow.com/","img":"","title":"This is the homepage for A Permanent Shadow, an Electronic Rock and Synth Pop band based in Barcelona. New album HUMDRUM is out on March 4, 2022.","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/apermanentshadow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook </strong></a><strong>| </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@APermanentShadow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube </strong></a><strong>| </strong><a href=\"https://twitter.com/apermanentshad1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Twitter</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"248447","title":"Kēvens' \"Sweet Lady Liberty\" (Radio Remix) Celebrates Equality, Positivity, and Independence","date":"2023-06-30","lead":"The popular 2018 track is resurfacing just in time for this year's Fourth of July holiday.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/248447/11a62948044429cb1bfc503b1fceefb9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The popular 2018 track is resurfacing just in time for this year's Fourth of July holiday."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/735YiFOI8vxDfvuykb5lNB?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Miami, FLORIDA (June 30, 2023) - International recording artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5bLc9sWbEvo3I1DypRoOy5?si=qS-XQtlrQkaqDjgSxUIBtw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Kēvens&nbsp;</strong></a>released <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5pCRIBtdCG7qGh47Uvt9ki?si=11782476112a4cd7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sweet Lady Liberty</a>”</strong> back in 2018 as an ode to independence and freedom. The single focuses on the love we all feel for the “Idea” of a country designed around the oft-repeated concepts of liberty and equality. In a climate where many Americans find themselves suffering the effects of straying from those concepts, “Sweet Lady Liberty” reminds us that we all play a part in upholding those notions and dreams. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Every song I sing speaks to each person individually and differently, depending to what they’re going through in life. My music helps people connect with themselves on an elevated level.”","cite":"Kēvens,  Electronic  Reggae Artist"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"248270","title":"Kēvens Fuses Reggae and EDM in New Single “Legal Dreamers\"","date":"2023-06-23","lead":"Kēvens, the self-proclaimed “Keeper of Dub” takes listeners on a soul-healing journey with this captivating track.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/248270/932c2f0b220b7e672783276384413edf.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Kēvens, the self-proclaimed “Keeper of Dub” takes listeners on a soul-healing journey with this captivating track."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3Z6tTojYktYXDY7MQAzvCr?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Miami, FLORIDA (June 23, 2023) - Emerging electronic artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5bLc9sWbEvo3I1DypRoOy5?si=aJXiIkqGQX2WB3VzIsq2wA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Kēvens</strong></a> just released a new EDM-Reggae crossover single, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3Z6tTojYktYXDY7MQAzvCr?si=7fdee3efaca04b34\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Legal Dreamers</strong></a><strong>”&nbsp;</strong> this Friday, June 23rd. Kēvens believes that music is a powerful tool that can bring people from all walks of life together. “Legal Dreamers” &nbsp;is a testament to Kēvens' talent as a musician and his dedication to spreading love and positivity through creative expression. Kēvens' unique blend of dub and EDM creates a sound that is both fresh and familiar, and his lyrics speak to the heart of the human experience. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"'Legal Dreamers' is more of a mantra than a record -  one recited towards a world built on love and inclusion. Legal Dreamers is the soundtrack cultivating safe spaces where we can feel free to love openly again. Complementing one another as the marriage of the drum and the bass have done for generations in reggae. So as a follower of the keeper of dub, let us remember in dub we trust, in this life, love is a must.”","cite":"Kēvens Electronic-Reggae Musician"},{"t":"button","href":"https://kevens.lnk.to/LegalDreamers","label":"Stream \"Legal Dreamers\" On All Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Recognized as a live drum and bass pioneer, Kēvens was the first to bring these musical elements to the early rave scene back in the late 90s. Kēvens has performed live with his band at iconic EDM festivals such as <strong>The Florida Zen Music Festival</strong>, <strong>Cyberfest,</strong> and <strong>Ultra Music Festival</strong>."},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"248833","title":"Electronic R&B Artist Jesse Pringle Releases New Single","date":"2023-06-23","lead":"The fresh track, \"Other Side\" dives into themes of mental health, self-empowerment, astrology, and more.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/248833/b1437f9b288d72199f8a49b735474661.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The fresh track, \"Other Side\" dives into themes of mental health, self-empowerment, astrology, and more."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6t1thRUFhPvfT6BGZPs1LH?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<br>Kansas City, MO (June 23, 2023) - Emerging electronic artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7MoXGvcoHJn9bnaWSVHSo1?si=kVz26kKUT5Kd4bmzZDC5ug\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Jesse Pringle</strong></a> just released his new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6t1thRUFhPvfT6BGZPs1LH?si=6cc4205a76a443fa\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Other Side</strong></a>” this Friday, June 23rd. The song includes LoFi undertones backed by powerful lyrics inspired by Jesse's life experiences. Jesse aims to share his vulnerability with listeners, emphasizing notion of living life to the fullest potential rather than being unhappy and unmotivated. “Other Side” touches upon themes related to mental health struggles, self-empowerment, human design, and more.&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"248841","title":"Karmic Neighborhood Releases \"Everybody Needs to Love\" Ahead of Feature Film","date":"2023-06-23","lead":"This track is the third release of a six-single series leading up to the soundtrack album launch for 'Equinox the Musical.'","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/248841/a085efdedf4637a77210b57283571e31.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This track is the third release of a six-single series leading up to the soundtrack album launch for 'Equinox the Musical.'"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3k2JqrnLue58w4ZsyOzfI1?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Royal Oaks, CA (June 23, 2023) - <strong>Armand Ruby </strong>and<strong> Julian Colbeck&nbsp;</strong>of musical group&nbsp;<strong>Karmic Neighborhood</strong> are releasing a new ballad, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3k2JqrnLue58w4ZsyOzfI1?si=e837f26a56bd4aa8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Everybody Needs to Love</strong></a>,<strong>”</strong> the third track in a series of singles for their upcoming feature film“<strong>Equinox the Musical</strong>.” This heartfelt ballad is on the mellow side but packs a powerful message.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"In the film, the song “Everybody Needs to Love” is a duet between the curmudgeonly <strong><em>Professor</em></strong><em>&nbsp;</em>(vocals by Armand Ruby) and the compassionate café waitress, <strong><em>Amy </em></strong>(vocals by <strong>Ariel Thiermann</strong>). In the screenplay, the Professor complains about the homeless man sitting outside the café, and in reply, Amy shares her understanding that the man is a homeless veteran suffering from crippling PTSD. Amy's kindness opens the Professor’s heart to a more sympathetic view."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/EverybodyNeedstoLove","label":"Listen On All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song speaks to the reality of our shared humanity, and the possibility that love and compassion can arise within us when we confront the more difficult aspects of the human condition.\"","cite":"- Armand Ruby, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"p","html":"This song was inspired by real events. While working in an office in Davis, California, Armand would often see a scruffy guy sitting on the curb outside the Jack in the Box fast-food joint across the street. Just a quiet, somber-looking person, not the least bit frightening or offensive. One day Armand stopped on his way by and said hello, and impulsively asked the man if he’d like a sandwich, to which the man gratefully agreed. That first time, the man carefully cut the sandwich in half, poignantly saying he’d save the other half for later, showing Armand just how meaningful this small gesture of kindness had been. In that moment, Armand realized a fundamental truth - that being human means not just wanting to be loved, but also needing to love.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"quote","html":"'Everybody Needs to Love' is a raw, no-frills piano ballad about the need for human kindness.”","cite":"- Julian Colbeck, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/553511/large-e1df029691e9128a904e4f53fb8c13f9.jpg","alt":"KARMIC1.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"The full preview soundtrack album for “Equinox the Musical” will be released on the fall equinox, Sept. 22, 2023.<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Karmic Neighborhood:"},{"t":"p","html":"The west coast-based team are strangers-turned-neighbors, turned rhythmic alt-pop collaborators. Armand Ruby and Julian Colbeck are two life-long musicians in their 60's who met by chance when they moved to the same neighborhood on the central California coast. Julian was formerly a London-based rock star and lifelong music industry veteran, while Armand was professionally an environmental scientist who stayed involved in music as a part-time musician and songwriter. Armand and Julian formed a strong bond through their shared passion for music and the painful yet hopeful life experience of surviving cancer. The two found inspiration within the harmony of their own respective life journeys and a mutual interest in musical innovation."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vnYPcPpvzO0hhjR6YMUkV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Armand Ruby:"},{"t":"p","html":"Like many creatives, Armand was a sensitive child. Growing up, this was of course a blessing and a curse, in the face of both the world’s beauty and its harshness. Throughout his childhood in the northeastern United States, Armand was aware that maintaining this sensitivity might be a challenge. So keeping this cherished inner life alive became a lifelong ambition – and it found expression through music and songwriting. Armand wrote his first little tune at the age of 11, and as a teenager began composing songs, something he’s continued to do throughout life. But his musical talent was matched by a proclivity for science, and a scholarship to an Ivy League university led to a career as an Environmental Scientist."},{"t":"p","html":"Still, Armand continued to be active musically: songwriting, recording demos, performing in rock bands no one’s ever heard of, leading small choral groups, and for several years even singing in a professional opera chorus. A breakthrough came in 2010-2011 with the writing of the book and songs for a musical stage play, <strong>“Equinox.”</strong> Directing the play in its brief but sold-out run in Santa Cruz California was, according to Armand, <em>“both the most difficult and most rewarding experience of my life.”&nbsp;</em>With Equinox, Armand finds himself working at the creative intersection of art and social activism – shining a new light on the often out-of-sight homeless population and the many ways people can become homeless, through story and music. Another breakthrough came while working to convert the Equinox stage play into a feature-length musical film screenplay. Moving in 2019 to the rural Monterey Bay area community of Royal Oaks, Armand found that one of his neighbors, Julian Colbeck, was an experienced music arranger, producer and keyboardist.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Armand and Julian teamed up as Karmic Neighborhood to produce a ‘preview soundtrack’ album of the songs from “Equinox the Musical,” being released worldwide by <a href=\"https://freshnoisedistro.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Fresh Noise Distro</strong></a> in 2023. As a precursor to making the Equinox feature film, in 2021 Armand wrote and directed the short musical film, <strong>“I Said I Will,”</strong> featuring the song <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/09L2h21DyZ4ZRNnZSLIXx9?si=f279b950a43e4b16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Don’t Want to Walk Away</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> produced by Colbeck and Ruby. The film won several awards at film festivals, including for <strong>Best Soundtrack</strong>, <strong>Best Original Score</strong>, and <strong>Best Music Video</strong>."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Julian Colbeck:"},{"t":"p","html":"Julian Colbeck grew up in the south of England, where he learned how to play the piano and ultimately pursued his dreams of being in a London-based rock ‘n’ roll band in his late teens. Julian’s music career took off with the band <em><strong>Charlie</strong></em>, with whom he scored several US Top 40 singles including <strong>“Watching TV”</strong> and <strong>“LA Dreamer.”</strong> Over the span of a 40-year career, Julian worked and toured as a keyboard player/producer with <strong>Yes&nbsp;</strong>alumni group <strong>Anderson Bruford Wakeman Howe</strong>, former Genesis guitarist <strong>Steve Hackett</strong>, <strong>Charlie</strong>, <strong>John Miles</strong>, and more. In 2008 Julian began work with his long-time friend, <strong>Alan Parsons</strong>, on the award-winning instructional video series: <a href=\"https://www.artandscienceofsound.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Alan Parsons’ The Art &amp; Science Of Sound Recording</strong></a>. Julian also has written for many esteemed music industry publications and has authored many music and music technology books. Beginning in late 2019, and interrupted by intensive treatment for stage 4 cancer, Julian saw something of value in his neighbor Armand Ruby’s songwriting and his <em>Equinox&nbsp;</em>film project and worked as an arranger, co-producer, and keyboardist on the Equinox preview soundtrack recordings. Armand and Julian's collaboration on this work led to the production of their recent release, the radio remix of “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2GwLujewDO5BidnKDXmsNd?si=1ce7ed5a69f84b2b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Don’t Want to Walk Away</strong></a>,” followed by the current series of singles from <em>Equinox the Musical</em>. Karmic Neighborhood's new single from <em>Equinox the Musical,</em> <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3k2JqrnLue58w4ZsyOzfI1?si=09bcd8d2ca204c59\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Everybody Needs to Love</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Karmic Neighborhood!"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"243020","title":"ellakate Unties Music Video For Latest Track 'I'm Yours'","date":"2023-06-17","lead":"Rising pop artist ellakate recently dropped an emotionally eerie love song, now out with music video.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/243020/27b0c2c7cead2c35fbc6152f69e23150.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Rising pop artist ellakate recently dropped an emotionally eerie love song, now out with music video."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6Xk9Zucz7S2PPXOFeeeH8q?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Atlanta, GA (June 16, 2023) - Alt-pop artist <strong>ellakate&nbsp;</strong>just released her brand new track <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6Xk9Zucz7S2PPXOFeeeH8q?si=df940879adda4510\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I'm Yours</strong></a><strong>”</strong> on Friday, May 26th. The song explores themes of toxic love and giving your all to a partner, so much so that it becomes consuming. As the song progresses, it becomes clear that the artist has lost herself in pouring her entire identity and focus into her partner. “I'm Yours” has a sinister feel to it, with dynamic tones and contrasting harmonies. ellakate often incorporates some form of tonal dissonance into her music, creating a distinct sound for herself within the ever-so-broad pop genre."},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"247045","title":"Home - Jett Jenkins Music","date":"2023-06-16","lead":"Rising independent artist Jett Jenkins explores new musical avenues with fresh grunge-inspired sound.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/247045/53cbffe6b9d78c1d3683b0d1e91325bc.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Rising independent artist Jett Jenkins explores new musical avenues with fresh grunge-inspired sound."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2PVhF0CPzyggMDBzukjz52?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (June 16, 2023) - Rising singer-songwriter <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5eQTLH2RK7Et9can4bdmI7?si=rmimbbuLTGCJ-vUNgJr6AA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Jett Jenkins</strong></a>&nbsp;just released her newest single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2PVhF0CPzyggMDBzukjz52?si=d1b466643b8840a2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Bite the Bullet</strong></a>” on Friday, June 16th. The sound of the song is delicate and dreamy with the infusion of a gritty undertone. The track mixes the usual <em>“poppy” </em>sound of Jett's music with darker elements of new-wave synth. The lyrics behind this song reflect struggles with mental health, grief, perseverance, and more."},{"t":"quote","html":"“Bite the Bullet” is about pushing through difficult seasons of life. It's about being proud of yourself, for just being on this earth and surviving. Holding your head up in the hard times, which might not have completely passed, but standing and staying. Staying to find something, anything.”","cite":"Jett Jenkins, Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5eQTLH2RK7Et9can4bdmI7?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The chorus of the song reads, <em>“I hope you know how proud. I am you made it. Pushing past a bullet. Biting with your teeth. Ready to implode. When voices raising. You are so unsure. You’re so afraid of everything. Searching for a heart of gold.”</em> Jett was inspired by <strong>Neil Young's “Heart of Gold”</strong> for this play on words, bringing as though Neil is one of the artists that has helped her get through hard times.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I hope this song helps listeners get through whatever battle they are experiencing because that's what music does for me - music is and always has been what keeps me going.”","cite":"Jett Jenkins, Alt-Pop Artist"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550483/original-bb5d0df2d69e2e305cbfca09dd14c965.jpg","alt":"JETT 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550483/preview-d5fadf3c52aca4811e652a935a40b7b7.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550484/large-b18589ab44fce838f687a468801e89cb.jpg","alt":"JETT 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550484/preview-049600474e8b9ab8d6f29064f345aa5b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550485/large-3a628e8cd877b3a0f3b7eb0ad9038de1.jpg","alt":"JETT 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550485/preview-a2c60e1b8b43cf15a9a043fe86909f9c.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Jett Jenkins:"},{"t":"p","html":"Jett Jenkins is a Brooklyn-based indie pop artist who layers dreamy, colorful production behind heavy lyricism. With stylings residing somewhere between <strong>Billie Eilish</strong> and <strong>Blondie</strong>, this poignant singer-songwriter leaned into her passions after having an inspirational experience at a Clairo concert. Years of playing the guitar and performing in musical theater prepared this emerging artist to dive into her music career; her debut E.P. is described as relatable, emotional, and delivering “lyrics beyond her years.” Alongside her debut in music, Jenkins is preparing to make the transition into young adulthood as she anticipates the move from home to college. This promising powerhouse makes a show-stopping introduction in her first single, <strong>“<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1uZG2ygTi1bSDmqtZyCIfj?si=167ff340bb2c4d83\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">City in Anger</a>,”</strong> in which she captivates listeners with passionate vocals, invigorating instrumentation, and lyrics steeped in melancholy. Jett Jenkins, with her spellbinding charisma, is on track to finding a home on the playlist of indie-pop lovers for years to come. “Bite the Bullet” is now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Jett!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/therealjettjenkins/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@therealjettjenkins","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://jettjenkins.com/","img":"https://jettjenkins.com/wp-content/uploads/jett-logo1.gif","title":"Home - Jett Jenkins Music","desc":"Jett Jenkins is a indie pop artist based in Texas. As a singer and songwriter her music styling falls somewhere between Billie Eilish and Blondie."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/missjettpresley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>​YouTube</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/jettjenkinsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/jett-jenkins/1595458604\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Apple Music</strong></a><br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"247261","title":"Orlando Mendez from NBC's \"The Voice\" Releases New Country Rock Track","date":"2023-06-16","lead":"The \"Cuban Cowboy\" just dropped the new single \"Long Gone Lullaby\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/247261/7c7b167094f5ef0cc3310fe93f30228f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The \"Cuban Cowboy\" just dropped the new single \"Long Gone Lullaby\"&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3MhSlGRWdHgvp67bzbXOK4?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Nashville, TN (June 16, 2023) - <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1e6rjNsWdsCyUk4HyzgQ6w?si=Hcge_fYHQSOUzFwgr18Bww\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Orlando Mendez</strong></a>, aka the “Cuban Cowboy” from Season 22 of NBC's hit show <strong>“<em>The Voice</em>”</strong> is launching a brand new single. The track, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3MhSlGRWdHgvp67bzbXOK4?si=48488741e9724171\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Long Gone Lullaby</strong></a>” is a gritty, honest, country-rock revenge ballad. The single was produced by <strong>Lucio Rubino</strong>, featuring Orlando Mendez on lead vocals and <strong>Jack Sizemore</strong> on the guitar.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1e6rjNsWdsCyUk4HyzgQ6w?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"“Long Gone Lullaby” is an energetic breakup anthem that embraces the power of finally being over an ex. The lyrics are charged with brutal honesty and a bit of bitterness. The song captures a feeling of weathering the storm of heartbreak and finally starting to see the light on the other side. Soft and tender musical elements are featured at the beginning of the track, making the listener assume that this is a love song. The chorus comes in strong, with a punch of rock-and-roll and a tinge of harsh lyrics that change the dynamic of the tune completely. The song is centered around the final line of the chorus which says it all: <em>“Here's your long gone lullaby.” </em>The juxtaposition of sweet and bitter sentiments throughout “Long Gone Lullaby” keeps listeners on their toes, keeping the ear sharp and the heart sore.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Currently based in Nashville, TN, Orlando Mendez was born and raised in Miami, Florida. During his time on NBC's hit show “<em>The Voice</em>,” Mendez was dubbed “The Cuban Cowboy” by fans supporting his Miami-inflused country-rock flare. Mendez's grandparents were tobacco farmers back in Cuba for several generations. After <strong>Fidel Castro</strong> took over the island, his grandparents' land and everything they had built for themselves was confiscated. They made the hard decision to leave Cuba with just the clothes on their backs in pursuit of a better life for their kids and for their kids' kids (Orlando and his siblings). Orlando expresses gratitude for his family and all they have given up to provide him with a better life:"},{"t":"quote","html":"“They made sacrifices so I could be here today pursuing the American dream and trying to make a name for myself in the world of country music.”","cite":"Orlando Mendez, Country Rock Singer"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550908/original-775a60bf6dc1c14401d1348878ba9e86.jpg","alt":"ORLANDO 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550908/preview-8634c80e67260da3439be582754e84b8.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550907/large-0add863df594d930d10f031f97f4c0a6.jpg","alt":"ORLANDO 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550907/preview-5d482527514cd73554e76399bddf094f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550909/original-cf5982d059a7745af936585ff30b0bb2.jpg","alt":"ORLANDO 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550909/preview-f389ebac1800937964c5e6e498b48f77.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Orlando Mendez:"},{"t":"p","html":"Orlando Mendez, aka “The Cuban Cowboy,” was born and raised in Miami, FL. He is a second-generation Cuban American who found a love for country music at an early age. After graduating from the University of Florida and pursuing a short acting career, Orlando began to write and sing his longtime passion: country music. For almost two years he performed all over Florida with his band, “<strong>The Orlando Mendez Band</strong>.” In 2022, Orlando auditioned for season 22 of “<em>The Voice</em>” and was awarded a unanimous, four-chair turn by the coaches on the panel: <strong>Blake Shelton, John Legend, Gwen Stefani&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Camila Cabello</strong>. He was heralded for his unique voice and powerful stage presence and featured in three performances on the show. Orlando now lives in Nashville, TN and is currently in the process of releasing his debut EP. His aim is to bring the vibrancy and energy of his background to the truth and simplicity of country music. Check out “Long Gone Lullaby” which is now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Orlando!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/orlandojmendezmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@orlandojmendezmusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@orlandomendezofficial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/orlando.mendez.54?mibextid=LQQJ4d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>| </strong><a href=\"https://twitter.com/OrlandoMendez54\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TWITTER</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"247265","title":"Ámaris Wen Released New Whimsical Synth-Pop Album, \"Love and Oceans\"","date":"2023-06-16","lead":"London-based electronic artist Ámaris Wen just dropped a 10-track electronic-infused record.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/247265/569cd3e48dfc4c1b41eb5d61fa792ae3.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"London-based electronic artist Ámaris Wen just dropped a 10-track electronic-infused record."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6XR9kuZ40K6PKh2BW1qmDS?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"London, UK (June 16, 2023) - Synth-pop-inspired musical artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6oqjlwI9NonKlLldVEObEf?si=l5nlplHCS1qxuMPd8wyzaw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ámaris Wen</strong></a> is launching her new 10-track record, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6XR9kuZ40K6PKh2BW1qmDS?si=Sop0R94NShWjrsumjQRbCQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Love and Oceans</strong></a>” on Friday, June 16th. The electronic-inspired album explores themes related to women empowerment, toxic relationships, and mental health struggles. Ámaris strives to provide listeners with an escape route through her music. The tracks within the new album “Love and Oceans” soothe the mind after a breakup, inspiring an embrace of new beginnings.&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Although my music isn't always upbeat and light, it soothes listeners with lyrical messages related to embracing new beginnings and ​opportunities.\"","cite":"Ámaris Wen, Pop-Synth Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ALBUM DISCOGRAPHY:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Songs on the album such as <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6LEDSftgUf7gmwxRFBPBXx?si=b3da381f7f014332\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Subconscious</strong></a><strong>’</strong> and <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2ga0AFa5PPWDNNuzhhiGwW?si=e9466578f2584de4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Missing You</strong></a><strong>’</strong> translate into a whirl of dreamy moonlight overtones.<strong>&nbsp;‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7bXYQTDESzAGtTjYeANdjl?si=c822883eb481479d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Nostalgia</strong></a><strong>’</strong> immerses you in the feeling of not being able to let go of a relationship you know isn’t good for you.‘Nostalgia’ was inspired by synth-pop, and Ámaris wanted the song to sound slightly ‘retro’ to reflect the feeling of nostalgia throughout the song. <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0qxYAAelVOXVLjGbLT8kCD?si=e572900b35734ae2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Oyster Bed</strong></a><strong>’</strong> acts as a reminder to dream big and move on from what was holding you back. 'Subconscious’ was inspired by the feeling of drifting during a spell of insomnia, a condition Ámaris herself experiences from time to time due to a thyroid condition. <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0mjCud8KyR07lpG7cMOzg8?si=cb9fb86ae34d45fe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Visionary</strong></a><strong>’</strong> was inspired by the feeling of latching onto a relationship that isn’t good for you, and explores the process of letting go of toxicity.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://soundcloud.com/amariswen/sets/love-oceans/s-SUaDqtdMDaM","label":"Listen to \"Love and Oceans\" on SoundCloud","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6oqjlwI9NonKlLldVEObEf?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Ámaris created a set of dreamy AI-generated images to accompany the album and its message: </em><br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550912/original-a63e2d1ded5d39dcf05b3cc5dbfd9f52.jpg","alt":"AMARIS 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550912/original-a63e2d1ded5d39dcf05b3cc5dbfd9f52.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550913/large-5b9cb8530b2af482e8947fbd079f039b.jpg","alt":"AMARIS 7.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550913/preview-8e7fe73218c3349bf8f4f3b1b7aefde5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550915/original-b313c36412a699495f8b2196bcb0f95e.jpg","alt":"AMARIS 4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550915/preview-db878f13403ba733ef3cf4ffcbf14aec.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550914/large-3bc38cbae200522bdfb199db8649a900.jpg","alt":"AMARIS 5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550914/preview-1825ba60dfb326f1c82cd156199aa12f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550916/large-51d587ca83a7ee7693b832b2c6b5bc9a.jpg","alt":"AMARIS 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550916/preview-913b57cfef036bee3f11edddc145ef99.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550917/original-2844f625157caa315c8070fce61534a2.jpg","alt":"AMARIS 6.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550917/preview-36ccc99aab383418e27c6cd31d47b94a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550918/large-9b4efc780168851d84d28342c9c3970f.png","alt":"AMARIS 1.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550918/preview-5db59c8c5b8835841a98f26676166c9e.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/551872/large-1c826d31efda31a2cbae1768eac3a673.jpg","alt":"Love_and_oceans2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/551872/preview-c0865f41143be6b0cdcc23d7b0ba7f25.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/551873/large-7401e547a2d145a9f0517c0ad7a81e2f.jpg","alt":"Love_and_oceans5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/551873/preview-fb14d60416121a90a9345b33865029e8.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Ámaris Wen:"},{"t":"p","html":"Ámaris Wen is a recording artist, music producer, actor, and songwriter. Ámaris grew up in Central Switzerland as the daughter of a teacher and Swiss musician and professor for music, <strong>Kurt Baumann</strong>, which fostered her connection with music from an early age. Her family is from the Netherlands, New Zealand, Switzerland, and England, which is why Ámaris grew up with English, German, and Dutch. After her parents’ divorce, she moved to Zurich where she received her formal training at drama school in Zurich, and later at the Stage &amp; Musical School in Frankfurt, Germany, where she started to listen to electronic music for her dance studies. Ámaris' 2014 dance floor project <strong>“Geiko– female electronic dance music</strong>,<strong>”</strong> was her first-ever album released. After returning from Germany to Zurich to work as a playlist manager for major record labels, she later moved to London where she started working on her first more R&amp;B and synthpop-influenced album <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6oqL9pjcSxExcy4lTsd8EP?si=QqmgPhlbS_2s3ZgtRnqO9A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Neon Colours</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> which was well-received by critics. In 2018, she released <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7MKZ7NwMoE2kAxrDCZfOka?si=PWzrj9SrSL2kCUkGSoGuzA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Aquamarine</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> a full-length album inspired by the oceans. This was followed by <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2VGLMRJtmuWgCXkcmpA3BJ?si=cbUSMaP5RIqvNP_kzKChcQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>26</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> a brooding and thoughtful album, released in 2019. Listen to her new album, “Love and Oceans,” now available on all streaming platforms!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Ámaris Wen!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/silvermaranth/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@silvermaranth","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@silvermaranth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/silvermaranth/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@silvermaranth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"247375","title":"Electronic Artist dreamcat Just Dropped New Single, \"Fresh Air\"","date":"2023-06-16","lead":"This defining synth-pop track is dreamcat's first single to launch ahead of EP release.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/247375/a951059336fc27bfe930a4a2ffee0418.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This defining synth-pop track is dreamcat's first single to launch ahead of EP release."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6TbNWqs1MmLm9w3yrc6Qfe?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Anchorage, ALASKA (June 16, 2023) - Anchorage-based up-and-coming alternative artist <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3K9fTRuyA2UY0vs4ncFs3p?si=tB6jUwJURZGwM7VbBh6YkQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>dreamcat</strong>&nbsp;</a>just launched his new single on June 16th. The synth-pop tune will be the first of many tracks to be included on his upcoming EP (launch date TBD). The new track “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6TbNWqs1MmLm9w3yrc6Qfe?si=151e1cbc2c044f1b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Fresh Air</strong></a>” was produced and written by dreamcat in the middle of the Alaskan winter. The lyrics of “Fresh Air” are supposed to be a beacon of hope and light for warmer weather and better times ahead. The chords and instrumentals give the song a groovy overtone, supported by falsetto vocals and intricate layering of electronic vibrations. dreamcat strives to provide listeners with a positive energy, encouraging them to find joy and love within the simplicity of life. The inspiration for this EP is largely tied to dreamcat's journey with sobriety. After being out of rehab for a couple of months, the artist turned to music as a therapeutic outlet for the soul."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I want people to feel good about themselves, being alive, and in the moment.”","cite":"dreamcat, Alternative Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/FreshAir","label":"Listen On All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3K9fTRuyA2UY0vs4ncFs3p?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"“Fresh Air” is the first release of many upcoming singles to be included within dreamcat's long-awaited EP. The artist has been working with <strong>James Glaves</strong>, a local hero for the music community in Alaska, to mix and master some of the track's production elements. James Glaves has worked with key artists around the globe (i.e. “<strong>Medium Build</strong>”) and has landed some of his music within the hit TV show, <strong><em>“Gone Girl.”</em></strong>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552822/large-48c8d303a03901372cd2a8cb3e393c29.jpg","alt":"large-freshair_edit1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552822/preview-78e05aafe08a8170cfe0951e1bf632c6.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552819/large-633ec8f530a8f11ceeac6cbbf910eaca.jpg","alt":"large-DUGOUT2_VTG2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552819/preview-d320f66fb6c992d9a2eb3e9c4226d92b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552821/large-7fab1abe6efe93247a982d4a80bbb0d4.jpg","alt":"large-Homerun1_B_W.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552821/preview-ada1f462c79e1f6215386fc940c69968.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552823/large-7a075be3c0b9b1db74c6b996787de1e8.jpg","alt":"large-Dugoutfence_VTG.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552823/preview-b24a41f56982c80de90e11926efbbb45.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552820/large-f5eceb5e3fff27057f2d4dc460510322.jpg","alt":"large-gradientdugout.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552820/preview-59cd3133d01e5172b2bef1947b136bfe.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About dreamcat:"},{"t":"p","html":"dreamcat AKA Colton Ciufo has loved performing and creating music since childhood. As a result of taking piano lessons as a kid, dreamcat played synth in a metal band with his friends, performing and playing some of his first shows when he was only 17. dreamcat has carefully curated his niche within the music industry and has fine-tuned his songwriting over the years. Music has always been dreamcat's escape, using creativity as a means for coping with alcoholism, social anxiety, and depression. Since attending a rehab facility in Southern California, dreamcat has been going through positive psychological, lifestyle, and spiritual changes. dreamcat's purpose is to make positive yet heartfelt music that makes him feel good and inspires listeners from whatever place they find themselves in life. Check out dreamcat's Instagram for all announcements/updates!<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with dreamcat!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/dreamcat123456/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@dreamcat123456","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"248262","title":"Emerging Alternative Artist \"A Permanent Shadow\" Recently Launched New Single","date":"2023-06-14","lead":"The eclectic track, \"A Xmas Gift in May\" draws inspiration from Depeche Mode, David Bowie, Iggy Pop, and other 80s Indie-Pop icons.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/248262/88598a71723c3467cf04fa54e50da4b3.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The eclectic track, \"A Xmas Gift in May\" draws inspiration from Depeche Mode, David Bowie, Iggy Pop, and other 80s Indie-Pop icons."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4t9fooPiKJZT3XmzcJ0NOl?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Barcelona, SPAIN (May 19, 2023) - <a href=\"https://www.apermanentshadow.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>A Permanent Shadow</strong></a>, the musical collective around <strong>CP Fletcher</strong>, returns with a standalone single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4t9fooPiKJZT3XmzcJ0NOl?si=511d24236b6a46ee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>A Xmas Gift in May</strong></a>” Originally titled <strong>“Black Lolita,”</strong> the track was initially not intended for release, but CP changed his mind after listening back to the original version sung by a guest vocalist."},{"t":"p","html":"The original was recorded in 2021 as a birthday gift for a soon-to-be past flame of CP’s, inspired by the rather rocky beginning of a relationship that eventually proved short-lived and turbulent.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/R6TBGLfuup4","height":"475"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wrote this song in a state of absolute euphoria and an unbearable urge to be with a person who in hindsight was not for me. All the red flags were there but I refused to acknowledge them. It’s a heartfelt piece of romanticism, which is a rare subject matter for me to write about. I hope managed to pack feelings of desire, longing and uncertainty into the song.”","cite":"CP Fletcher, A Permanent Shadow"},{"t":"button","href":"https://hypeddit.com/69qkk3","label":"LISTEN ON ALL MAJOR PLATFORMS","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"“A Xmas Gift in May” was released in its original arrangement which features some interesting musical references to classic Sixties pop like “<strong>All You Need Is Love</strong>,” albeit in a modern guise using a metronomic backbeat and modern-day production values. CP is especially fond of a remix performed by longtime collaborator Valen Nieto which leans heavily on elements of Eighties Italo Disco. The EP release is completed with an intimate take consisting of piano and lead vocals only.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552188/large-cdbdf66d1421aa30fd1b8e8dedf45714.jpg","alt":"CP2 .jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552188/preview-8e47ca22547e55de2bada637ee47ca29.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552189/large-af9f4e088acb1867aac4124dcd5c1728.jpg","alt":"CP3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552189/preview-6f38f2c4da3daab0acc027e1e10ef68d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552190/large-7226db8468e67e1ae61b99fba3576606.jpg","alt":"CP4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552190/preview-91cca8c424a5462acf020f0d95d96e23.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552191/large-354e1fee74e5818d0abde5cc038207d2.jpg","alt":"CP 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/552191/preview-9335847ea2a0c2a39aad5108144708c2.jpg"}]},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song and another standalone single we are planning to release will not feature on the long play... The album has a different sound and narrative that neither of these two compositions would fit in with. A straight love song like this one would be at odds with the rather bleak lyrical themes that the album deals with.”","cite":"CP Fletcher, A Permanent Shadow"},{"t":"p","html":"The upcoming LP, “<strong>No Leaf Clover</strong>” will be A Permanent Shadow’s third released record after “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0d7H2IzDxXwpNsW4NheDdY?si=cjUv3siuQHOizvrRS7TDYA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Songs of Loss</strong></a>” (2019) and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/59GgNHgWEJzZrgGMriVpAj?si=svP4m8RuSP2E-YL2uBYptw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Humdrum</strong></a>” (2022). CP Fletcher is the group’s sole constant member, although multi-instrumentalist and producer <strong>Valentí Nieto</strong> as well as keyboarder <strong>Albert Català</strong> have featured on all APS releases."},{"t":"p","html":"A Permanent Shadow has another covers - only EP in the works and are working to demo the songs for a fourth album. But before those efforts bear any demonstrable results, there’s the small matter of the new single. Stay tuned for more to come from this up-and-coming alternative artist.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6mrGJN7uKAelkBlqMqUn8d?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About A Permanent Shadow:"},{"t":"p","html":"A Permanent Shadow is a band for want of a better description. Its only fixture is CP Fletcher who for his recordings surrounds himself with a rotating cast of musicians and producers. Fletcher used to be a drummer in various bands that went nowhere, so at one point, inspired by David Bowie's death, he decided to form his own band as a singer. CP took his first steps as a front man forming a <strong>Lou Reed </strong>tribute project, <strong>The Magic</strong> and <strong>Loss Orchestra</strong>. Such is his admiration for the curmudgeon from New York that the tribute experience ended up bleeding into A Permanent Shadow via a cover of <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1MNWaaHKNJGQlqH3xUys5d?si=9e59ab1be4524036\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Sword of Damocles</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> originally featured on Reed’s Magic and Loss album and included on the band's first album “Songs of Loss” in a reworked form.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The band involves various collaborators, although two musicians so far feature on all recordings: Albert Català, a classically trained piano player, helps CP whip the demos into shape, while the finishing touches in the studio are usually provided by renowned producer <strong>Valentí Nieto</strong>. Both albums “Songs of Loss” (2019) and “Humdrum” (2022) as well as the EP <strong>‘</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/45TQ4Z15JQObdtLpvGuPIU?si=IgMtPgWrTBW4b1UcnSZT9Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>UnderCover</strong></a><strong>’</strong> (2022) and the new single were recorded with contributions from these two musicians."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with A Permanent Shadow!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/apermanentshadow/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@apermanentshadow","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.apermanentshadow.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/apermanentshad1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://facebook.com/apermanentshadow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://youtube.com/@APermanentShadow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"242944","title":"Nicolas McCoppin Just Launched New Dance-Pop Single \"L.E.S. boy\"","date":"2023-06-09","lead":"Top 40 artist Nicolas McCoppin releases ethereal sucker-punch dance track \"L.E.S. boy\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/242944/0b08025e41f272c8792aa4f199ed64af.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Top 40 artist Nicolas McCoppin releases ethereal sucker-punch dance track \"L.E.S. boy\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0N1laWmN5VrGl68pJ3B8un?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (June 9, 2023) - Alt-pop artist <strong>Nicolas McCoppin</strong>&nbsp;just released a new NYC-inspired single \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0N1laWmN5VrGl68pJ3B8un?si=352e91ae73fd4dd2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>L.E.S. boy</strong></a>\" on Friday, June 9th. This dance-worthy track is an upbeat interpretation of topics related to relationships, heartbreak, the LGBTQ+ community, self-discovery, mental health, and more. \"L.E.S. boy\" is the definition of a catchy comeback anthem dedicated to McCoppin's time spent living in the Manhattan's East Village. In an aching reminiscence, \"L.E.S. boy\" reflects McCoppin's transcendence into a new self-power that he hopes to convey to listeners through a more exploratory sonic landscape. An auditory sucker-punch to the gut, bright melodies are contrasted with industrial textures and beats amidst an ethereal aura that flows in and out creating a cinematic listening experience."},{"t":"p","html":"McCoppin's lyrics explore the fear associated with codependency, specifically highlighting how empty one can feel once that attachment breaks. Nicolas has grown to be more confident in himself, and has worked to include himself on the list of people he holds close to his heart. Complete with introspective lyrics and optimistic instrumentals, L.E.S. boy represents a painful yet rewarding rebirth of the soul.<br>"},{"t":"quote","html":"“L.E.S. boy is the first chapter of my rediscovery. I had to find a version of myself that could survive betrayal by two of the closest people in my life. I was drowning in confusion and for a long time couldn’t put my feelings into words. Creating L.E.S. boy helped me to express and uncover the person I was becoming.\"","cite":"Nicolas McCoppin, Indie-Pop Artist"},{"t":"p","html":"\"L.E.S. boy\" launches just in time for Pride month and is the perfect soundtrack to any and all Pride celebrations in NYC and beyond! Nicolas McCoppin is a member of the LGBTQ+ community himself and makes a conscious effort to support efforts as much as he can. Pride is McCoppin's favorite time of year, and he is thrilled that this release will be available for listeners to stream and dance to all month long.<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542455/large-2be920015b594f0d9fa78516f2ee6cf3.jpg","alt":"2W5A3302.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542455/preview-40c19701f72864682963bd4950aebbcb.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542454/large-f8c7a5ef178e70a5fcbc0785ecc0efee.jpg","alt":"2W5A3278.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542454/preview-885f6abf7bd99d6ffc32663689abf42a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542458/large-302c6a4b3d80bf063fc3e16149fb80a0.jpg","alt":"LES-BOY-SQ-VERT.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542458/preview-fef93142cc7c7ccb25224b88a48a51d0.jpg"}]},{"t":"quote","html":"“This song is for everyone who has loved, lost, and felt every emotion in-between. I hope L.E.S. boy can provide listeners with the same sense of serenity and joy it brought me.\"","cite":"Nicolas McCoppin, Indie-Pop Artist"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong><em>\"L.E.S. boy\" Collaborators:</em></strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Visuals Shot + Edited by Devin Kasparian (Kim Petras - Slut Pop / Formally with Flaunt Mag, Vice and Paper Mag) Creative Direction by Guillermo Cardenas Fashion styling by Guillermo Cardenas Additional styling by Anderson Rose Executive produced by Nick Trapani Written by Zach Beebe, Earth To Emily (Elio’s writer - Charli XCX’s protégé), Nick Trapani and Nicolas McCoppin Mixed by Marvin Delgado (Grammy Nominated / 3x platinum engineer) Mastered by Demitrius Lewis II (Grammy Winning mastering engineer) Managed by Shelby Chargin, DECMD Entertainment Written and recorded between Los Angeles, CA and New York, NY Released via Loverboy Recordings, LLC exclusively licensed to Beatroot, LLC.</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7eeVgpwUPqZaaDUnRE0B6j?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Nicolas McCoppin:"},{"t":"p","html":"With a mission to create space for himself in pop music, McCoppin offers a fresh perspective on the timeless genre. McCoppin has been described as <em>“...a once-in-a-lifetime artist. He comes across as a storyteller, first and foremost, with an incredible gift for creating music unlike anything we’ve heard before,”</em> (<strong>Ascribe Magazine</strong>), <em>“a rising figure in the LGBTQ community as the next major pop artist to watch,” (<strong>Instinct Magazine</strong>) </em>and a <em>“smooth pop hottie”</em> (<strong>Queerty</strong>)."},{"t":"p","html":"2021 was a standout year for McCoppin, making his mark on the music industry with the official US radio debut of lead single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3qVZzx23JKXBwqsLkcjawH?si=1d9126b825124846\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Heaven</strong></a>”. “Heaven” entered <strong>Mediabase’s US Pop/Top 40 radio chart</strong> at #40 in June of 2021 continued to climb charts each week with rave reviews from station programmers across the US. McCoppin’s career quickly skyrocketed with a distribution deal with <strong>AWAL</strong> (a division of Sony Music Entertainment) that boosted his online fanbase and cultivated over 850,000 worldwide streams on his debut EP, ‘<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7MXoyrh5e7NtjeSETZ2lfB?si=pwVTTPOQTJCOMQMe88foQQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Loverboy</strong></a>’ the same year. ‘Loverboy’ was featured on a billboard in Times Square for its’ global release weekend and launched the LGBTQ artist to be named as an Instagram Official Pride Creator. This success led to a deluxe repackage of the EP, where McCoppin collaborated with <strong>Bonnie McKee</strong> (<strong>Katy Perry </strong>- “<strong>Teenage Dream</strong>”) to write the track “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5XwCLhTd5pumM9M2Xk3vMf?si=48d0302775c842c2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dancing on the Moon</strong></a>”. The rising artist also boasts support from the fashion industry, with fashion icon Moschino Couture collaborating to dress and style the “Heaven” music video."},{"t":"p","html":"McCoppin’s considerable appeal as a pop artist is further solidified through the plethora of praise he has received from top industry influencers. McCoppin’s 2021 releases were highlighted within several high-profile publications including <strong>VEVO</strong>, <strong>Spotify</strong>, <strong>Grindr</strong>, <strong>Queerty, Medium</strong>, <strong>Instinct Magazine</strong>, and others, with NYS Music stating that McCoppin’s music is “an East Coast ‘Teenage Dream”. The young pop artist translates his online industry success to packed shows at various venues in NYC including The <strong>Bowery Electric</strong>,<strong> Piano’s</strong>, <strong>Knitting Factory</strong>,<strong> Berlin Under A</strong>,<strong> and YouTube Space NYC</strong>. He has also performed on the west coast at <strong>The Hotel Cafe</strong> in LA. Nicolas recently signed an exclusive licensing distribution deal with <strong>Beatroot, LLC/Made In Memphis Entertainment </strong>in May 2023. His upcoming releases will be under <strong>Loverboy Recordings, LLC.</strong> exclusively licensed to Beatroot, LLC!&nbsp;<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"lead","html":"<strong>Connect With Nicolas!</strong>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/nicolasmccoppin/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@nicolasmccoppin","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"246579","title":"Musical Trio Lotion Princess Drops New Single \"Reassurance\"","date":"2023-06-09","lead":"This dreamy indie-pop track dives into themes of mental health awareness, relationships, self-worth, and more.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/246579/4c10176632dc7e73909fcda6f76b3ebe.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"p","html":"<em>This dreamy indie-pop track dives into themes of mental health awareness, relationships, self-worth, and more.</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2MK6gmVSF5Qmhc0kfTzcZ2?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Boston, MA (JUNE 9, 2023) - Indie-pop trio, <strong>Lotion Princess</strong>, just dropped their new single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2MK6gmVSF5Qmhc0kfTzcZ2?si=f266b1dfb80f4c95\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Reassurance</strong></a>,” on Friday, June 9th. The new euphoric track touches upon many complex themes, one being the yearning for reassurance. The lyrics describe a toxic sense of needing that reassurance so badly that it seems as if you can't survive without it. The single opens with the following related lines, <em>“Are you mad at me. I don’t know what I mean. I just wanna feel closer to you baby. All this insecurity. Grows so deep inside of me.”</em> The desperation for certainty drives the energy and power of the song. The backing vocals of the chorus<em>&nbsp;“Want you...to know...I'm sorry”</em> capture the sincerity of the apology, but are ultimately sentimental words delivered from an honest yet broken place."},{"t":"p","html":"The single is deeply rooted in the &nbsp;theme of OCD and the grip it can have on a person, and a relationship. Singer-Songwriter Sasha Snoad of Lotion Princess speaks on her own struggles with OCD:<br>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/Reassurance","label":"Listen On All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I've struggled with relational OCD for my whole life, along with other forms of OCD. When most people think of OCD they think of cleanliness, hand washing, and being a “neat freak,” for me, OCD shows up as dynamics in close relationships. The way OCD works is having a thought (the obsession) and subsequently doing something that neutralizes the thought (the compulsion). My compulsion is reassurance-seeking, and I've done it a lot in my relationship with my partner, soon to be my spouse. It's not always reassurance-seeking like “do you want to be with me” - it can be “did that thing I said hurt your feelings” or “are you mad at me?” This song is about the frustration and guilt I feel about bringing the OCD  into our relationship, and fissures and pain it has caused. This track gives voice to the panic I experience while in the throws of the OCD cycle, and the yearning for recovery. .. At the same time, this song is about caring for myself when I’m at my worst, especially when I’m mad at myself for not being able to heal quicker.”","cite":"Sasha Snoad, Lotion Princess"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549847/large-cf4484240f566337f631247085dc0e68.jpg","alt":"20220416_MM_LP-47.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549847/preview-77c92cf22b12aa0edafba60c62bee34f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549849/large-84869b1ff1a6802509eba1803926f7e0.jpg","alt":"20220416_MM_LP-61-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549849/preview-d3823093c5e579e44f8484e8b3e25fb5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549848/large-c2ff50d418807996a440654aa6dd97cf.jpeg","alt":"20220416_MM_LP-182.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549848/preview-56f3759f783e02e375d27a7341187824.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549850/large-9d384828abdb5bf27ba4a7c360b430f9.jpg","alt":"155905.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549850/preview-3146e80a052c916305d065ee95607759.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Lotion Princess:"},{"t":"p","html":"Indie-pop band Lotion Princess is <strong>Sasha Snoad</strong>, <strong>Tommy Sherrod</strong> and <strong>Andrew Grossman</strong>. The group emerged from the 2016 DIY music scene in Washington, D.C. with a hypotonic and expansive sound called “an aural form of a cathartic walk in the woods” by DCist. In their 2019 debut EP, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/2sJZDFxjmUzRZS7jwY1BoQ?si=vMXaWdP8RNiKIHKV9HfzKQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Take Care</strong></a>,” Sasha Snoad developed her identity as a songwriter, drawing on personal experiences of heartbreak in the deeply emotional record. Three back-to-back singles in 2020 process queer love, friendship and mental health. A standout of the collection is “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1WCX0PH3ifyHPqwtqTiVHL?si=149f43a148374a7a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>In the Summer</strong></a>,” a breakup anthem with driving beats and soaring harmonies that feel hopeful and confident, while tinged with anger and regret. This is music to make you feel seen, know your value, and be kinder to yourself."},{"t":"p","html":"Lotion Princess just launched their new single, “Reassurance” on June 9th - now available to stream on all platforms. The single is part of the band's second EP, which will launch at the end of this summer. Make sure to follow Lotion Princess on social media to keep up with all of their upcoming announcements, including shows and tickets!<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Lotion Princess!"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"246874","title":"Joel Sammut and Dakota Blue's Collaboration Will Leave You Asking \"What Happened To The Weekend\" With This Haunting Post-pandemic Ballard","date":"2023-06-09","lead":"This latest alt-rock release from Joel Sammut has listeners feeling as though they've just woken from a strange reality.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/246874/41574a3ab76458599b455513aefa04d9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This latest alt-rock release from Joel Sammut has listeners feeling as though they've just woken from a strange reality."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2rJ1mmL5cASMJrRJypROc9?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Byron Bay, AUSTRALIA (June 9, 2023) - Australian producer-singer-songwriter, <strong>Joel Sammut</strong>, just released yet another awakening track in collaboration with <strong>Dakota Blue</strong> on Friday,June 9th. Boasting a grunge-alt-rock soundscape, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1eXTm1Xz9eWZVBCh3eDPy2?si=hsYcnUIWTlqUaK6FRJlDrg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>What Happened To The Weekend</strong></a>\" was inspired by feeling foreign in a post-pandemic reality, exploring the strange feeling of being abruptly thrown back into the real world. <em>\"It is about being taken aback by how quickly time has passed whilst trying to make sense of it,\"</em> says Dakota. Written on New Year's Day, Dakota was hit with the realization of how fast the world revolves and felt foreign to it. <em>\"It all sort of feels like a strange dream you’re trying to wake from.\"&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Collaborating with Dakota Blue, the duo created a unique sound that's described as <em>\"If Rowland S. Howard and Joy Division had a love child.\"&nbsp;</em>Once Dakota laid down vocals, synths and guitars – Joel then took the beat and drops to another level. Layering percussion to link with the dark vibe and building the sections between. <em>\"We passed the track back and forth postal service style 3 times total – which we really enjoyed compared to producing solo. We've also never met in real life, only on Instagram and found each other cause we're both DIY bedroom producers.\"</em>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://streamlink.to/trouble_","label":"Listen On All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Working together entirely remotely, the two DIY bedroom producers bring an ethereal vibe to the otherwise rock-focused track. Infusing various elements borrowed from the electronic genre, experimental guitar sounds, and layers of synths, this is the first collaboration from the two producers who are already working on subsequent singles to follow.<br>"},{"t":"quote","html":"Can we beat the system and escape the matrix?","cite":""},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Running out of time<br>Every single day<br>I didn’t see the signs<br>I looked the other way…</em><br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550286/large-1bb972e92ba903e37bf81183e11e707f.jpg","alt":"What_Happened_to_the_weekend_Lo_Res01.jpg"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6ooE5iBoXAQiy1QHtV5ZKS?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Joel Sammut:"},{"t":"p","html":"Originally from Sydney, Joel is an Australian producer/singer-songwriter currently based in Byron Bay. Creating both nostalgic and spirited music, Joel has crafted his sound to be both fresh and timeless. A unique blend of pop, rock and electronic elements, Joel's music contains short yet emotionally-charged sentiments. Released in 2021, his track \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3stCs4KVlIBOjwOSe50RA7?si=56e23a21abc64d04\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Bleeding Man</strong></a>,\" follows a theme of heartache, while \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4VGvajv6c7rzoSs3nvxz9h?si=f9jSCXR0SpWaSJ9ZlZ-w-Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Home Ghost</strong></a>,\" released in the same year, reflects an expression of feeling lost and stuck at home during the pandemic. Joel is constantly growing and evolving his sound as a collaborative artist and producer, often tapping into varying sonic elements that define his sound and place within the music industry. Joel just released his single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3ABTJUl1wTDLxe6rd3rH3T?si=7a190c90e521491b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Trouble</strong></a>,\" this April 2023, which took inspiration from experimental artists such as <strong>Tame Impala</strong>, <strong>David Bowie</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Cocorosie</strong>, and more.<br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"246348","title":"Read More","date":"2023-06-08","lead":"Blending elements of Americana, folk, and jazz all within the parameters of a traditional pop structure, Emily Nicole Green debuts a powerfully poignant earworm to ease our individual and collective heartache.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/246348/07130bb07d1bae127ca0bd1466c0f2c0.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Blending elements of Americana, folk, and jazz all within the parameters of a traditional pop structure, Emily Nicole Green debuts a powerfully poignant earworm to ease our individual and collective heartache."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://app.prowly.com/app/56123/content/stories?allStories=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"IT'S GONNA BE OKAY\" LISTENING LINK</a>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5QlHxADLZsI26wccH2egw2?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (June 8, 2023) - <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5QlHxADLZsI26wccH2egw2?si=4492436009e8439d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>It’s Gonna Be Okay</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> the debut single from singer-songwriter <strong>Emily Nicole Green</strong>, just dropped on all music streaming platforms on June 8, 2023."},{"t":"p","html":"At a time when the world will have us believe that all hope is lost, “It’s Gonna Be Okay,” serves as a beacon of light for the ones who need it and, as Green sings, <em>“the ones still out there on the ledges.”</em> “It’s Gonna Be Okay,” provides listeners with accessible, relatable lyrics that offer understanding and empathy, <em>“No one's fine we're all fraying at the edges,”</em> and <em>“Sometimes, ya’ just need to hear ‘em say, it’s gonna be okay.”</em> These words are then filtered through Green’s soul-stirring vocals. Green explains that her own healing has been inextricably tied with her songwriting. Her words carry an emotional weight that you can hear and feel with your whole body. They echo the pain that accumulates as we attempt to keep up with society’s unwieldy requirements and meet its impossible expectations. Listeners receive her reassurances and her ability to translate emotion with so much nuance and care—through her vocal performance and her writing—proving that she has earned a spot at the table with her peers and in the conversation more broadly. &nbsp;It's also why people from all walks of life will feel like she is talking directly to them no matter what they are going through."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/-cMDiqRlN8o","height":"315"},{"t":"quote","html":"“I think about, \"It’s Gonna Be Okay,\" as a kind of lullaby that we can sing to ourselves and with people we love when things feel too hard, too scary, or too out of control. Adults need lullabies too. We need help managing our emotions. Life asks a lot of us. Sometimes we need to look for lifelines. Music can show up for us on demand, imbue us with resilience, and help us heal. I hope this song can be a salve to the hearts who need it.”","cite":"- Emily Nicole Green on her new song, \"It's Gonna Be Okay\""},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549568/large-b9beac1f46b31d1cc5bf9546852db2fe.jpg","alt":"Photo Credit: Richard Corman\n"},{"t":"p","html":"The musical composition Green has produced with “It’s Gonna Be Okay,” is sophisticated and warm. It serves to elevate and support the vocal as upright bass, pedal steel, cello, keys, and acoustic guitar buoy Green’s words as she pours herself into them. Exhibiting a mastery of technique, Green effortlessly transitions between chest and head voice with a skillful use of vibrato that enhances the emotional impact. Evoking a deep, lived-in earnestness, Green draws comparisons to <strong>Amy Winehouse</strong>, <strong>Brandi Carlile</strong>, <strong>Bonnie Raitt</strong>, and <strong>Ani DiFranco</strong> for her distinct vocal style that is both empowering and comforting all in the same breath. Collaborating with powerhouse musicians <strong>Matt McDaniel</strong> on pedal steel and <strong>Barry Bales</strong> on upright bass, the subtlety of the instrumentation lays the foundation for Green’s heart-string-pulling performance."},{"t":"p","html":"“It’s Gonna Be Okay” is the debut track for Emily Nicole Green’s forthcoming EP, <em>Outrunning The Animal</em>, anticipated to be released in October of this year."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Emily Nicole Green:"},{"t":"p","html":"NYC-based singer-songwriter, Emily Nicole Green shines a light into the depths of her own emotional interiority with her lyrics and her sound. Her vulnerable writing, powerful vocal, and skillful vibrato work together to offer listeners immediate emotional resonance and stirring storytelling that stay with them long after her songs end.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Green has been writing and performing her original songs since she was a freshman in high school. At 17, she began dealing with debilitating anxiety and panic that stopped her from pursuing her dreams for nearly two decades. In 2019, she decided it was now or never and began pouring herself into her music. She posted cover songs on Patreon and a year later landed her first TV spot with a cover of “<strong>Greasy Frybread</strong>” played over the credits of Season 1, Ep. 4 of FX’s <strong>Reservation Dogs</strong>.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Green’s songwriting is where she gives herself permission to tell herself the truth, processing her emotions and not judging what they have to say, letting the songs be told by the parts of her that still ache. On what guides her writing, Emily says, <em>“At the altar of the ache, you’ll find the light below the wound.” </em><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Emily Nicole Green’s debut EP, “Outrunning The Animal,” which mixes Americana with indie-folk, pop, jazz, blues, and country, is anticipated to be released in October of this year.<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550223/large-afde3df3bece825c79906714eb7d5e59.jpg","alt":"image_processing20230601-4171608-1dvzf8v.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550223/preview-cdfebcdaed77bb6f612209761fef66d5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550225/large-8bdf31b2ad041d489aca28abe34f98a5.jpg","alt":"Emily Green_RC_Edited For Web.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550225/preview-671067d574bfa689087bfc38b9f9e4d3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549775/large-fc951e02a412069f72d44459bc0845a3.jpeg","alt":"Photo Credit: Don Johnson","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549775/preview-2e8fe5d3674d0cce31612e1b81da1181.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550224/large-33a62e07e0e0bb474367bcaa3bdaa383.jpg","alt":"Emily Green_RC_Photo 5_Edited For Web.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550224/preview-58dc59421dc3b29bf0427946d400bb99.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550226/large-2b8dceba354bc371ff413a30f1eb9e59.jpg","alt":"Emily Green_RC_Photo 2_Edited For Web.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550226/preview-1ab37db5fbbdd515db23c01f016f2c35.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550278/large-4702a9d5d6fe7cb8253f8f6ea6467cb0.jpg","alt":"RC4531_web_edited.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/550278/preview-0888fd7b80f2ae86e0e31e3378980079.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About The EP:"},{"t":"p","html":"Emily Nicole Green’s forthcoming debut EP, <em>Outrunning The Animal</em>, is set to be released October 2023. The EP includes five songs that each live in the liminal space between Americana and indie folk, while leaning into other genres— pop (\"It’s Gonna Be Okay\"), country (\"Hole In My Heart\"), blues and jazz (\"Wreckage\")—depending on the track. In her songwriting for this EP, Green works through grief and rage, rejection and desperation, the indignities of unrequited love, while testing out the waters of acceptance and hope. <strong></strong>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Emily!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/emilynicolegreen/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@emilynicolegreen","post":false},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Femily.n.green%2Fposts%2Fpfbid0232EW3yZbfk4DvVquCt9FbWGzsZckK9wXxJGDhFJRpnh6YXsuTZT5MQFzoW7L9yEel&show_text=true&width=500","height":"250"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://open.spotify.com/user/31kbm4hi4kjxaky6i326vnkcomom?si=8e14ee45666c4a26","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/EmilyColeGreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@emilycolegreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/EmilyNicoleGreen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"237291","title":"This is the standard home page. You can see this text if you choose the default page template for your home page. To display the sections,...","date":"2023-06-02","lead":"Colorado-based \"campfire classical\" composer performs emotionally evocative cello piece with a cinematic new visual.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/237291/145f7a3b69029becfbac006f1f225356.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Colorado-based \"campfire classical\" composer performs emotionally evocative cello piece with a cinematic new visual."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/kFQWKN-H_MM","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"DENVER, CO (April 5, 2023) - Self-proclaimed \"campfire classical\" composer <strong>Russick Smith</strong> has released a video for <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7yETSSCVLrlV5g2jVjj0WZ?si=dcd9afb2188e4cf0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Architecture of Vapor</strong></a><strong>\"</strong> - a cinematic orchestral piece featuring Smith on a solo cello. The visual follows a young girl with a clear passion for both cello and sketching, as she grows up and becomes an Architect. Seemingly pushed towards her work more and more as she matures, she finds herself in a place of burn-out and lacking inspiration. It is at this moment she sees an aerialist (<strong>Jennifer Thies</strong>) dancing upon silks over an empty stage as a lone cellist plays an evocatively emotional melody backed by the ensemble's deep soundscape. Inspired once again, the young architect returns to her work with a feeling of enjoyment, like she once did as a child."},{"t":"p","html":"Aerialist and Architect Jennifer Thies (featured in the video) commissioned Smith to compose this piece during the pandemic, requesting <em>\"something that rips my heart open in a good way.\"</em> Taking 3 days to write, record, and score the piece entirely at home, Smith took the challenge and manifested it into a contemplative and passionate composition that brings to life thematic ideas of rekindling a lost passion, the pain of utter beauty, and the intangible and ever-changing nature of the emotions that affect us.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531066/large-1c9cb482da1a1b8864aac1d08dc9502b.jpg","alt":"The Architecture of Vapor - Still Frame 3.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"When commissioning the piece to Smith, Thies described the sound she was looking for by explaining, <em>\"As an Architect, I know sometimes the most heartbreakingly beautiful projects are small and concise, but speaking as a Writer, I also know that when the heart bleeds it can produce volumes.\"</em> Smith began to look for a word to describe this feeling - the pain of utter beauty - but ultimately, came up short instead of labeling the sections after ephemeral emotional words from other languages: '<strong>toska</strong>',<strong> </strong>'<strong>sehnsucht</strong>'<strong>, </strong>'<strong>nostimon</strong>'<strong>, </strong>'<strong>dor</strong>'<strong>, </strong>'<strong>saudade</strong>'<strong>,</strong> and '<strong>mono no aware</strong>.' In his research for those words, he also came across the archaic term '<strong>the vapors</strong>.' <em>\"That got me thinking about the intangible and ever-changing nature of the emotions that affect us; what creates them, how do we define them?\"</em> says Smith. <em>\"How do we form a tangible definition of intangible things in a constant state of change, especially when they're complex? What is the definable structure of complex emotions, if any?\"</em> The confluence of these thoughts is what led to the concept of 'the architecture of vapor' - questioning how an Architect would define a cloud of vapor in a blueprint. <em>\"The moment that it would be tangibly qualified, the drawing would be incorrect,\"</em> remarks Smith. <em>\"Perhaps a similar thing happens with our internal emotional structures?\"</em><br><br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531072/large-6a42c362a248b8c7af977a41f393c69e.jpg","alt":"Russick Smith - Seated BW.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531072/preview-8742543f8944e167ba07a22697b0dc39.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531067/large-c6f895efcd2883d31e9465569aecf794.jpg","alt":"The Architecture of Vapor - Still Frame 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531067/preview-d880c720e8bab7ded1172884ea80ae2e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531068/large-4f650a0f177577f6a5d1bc73d2b34c98.jpg","alt":"The Architecture of Vapor - Still Frame 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531068/preview-324c696ad1e6ce6a2dbf70a16adc26af.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531069/large-5a9b45393a88d8d3bef6c58767aab9d1.jpg","alt":"The Architecture of Vapor - Still Frame 4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531069/preview-ba1d0c82e1dec207f1325b9ad833885e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531070/large-ed9c3b6b4fab1d4d460bf968ad339c89.jpg","alt":"AoV-Video-Cover.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531070/preview-b58aa821e4f13db3ceb5df95ac4dd7de.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531073/large-69506ead6d096782b6696304d3b10f07.jpg","alt":"Russick Smith - Color Vertical.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531073/preview-b0247768b7cec71fc1eb5e846f921bf4.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531071/large-9767022c399503562f632c40bf168862.jpg","alt":"The Architecture of Vapor - Still Frame 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531071/preview-5a3e27950dc758d04491a6c201ae53e3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531074/large-00c70434980d7e232fa0e05f6577fd20.jpg","alt":"Russick Smith - Music For The Birds.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531074/preview-305cdac2dd44ea3d6d0c151deed5b431.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Russick Smith:"},{"t":"p","html":"At one point, in the middle of a rainy night, you could have found him up the mast of a 19th-century schooner wrestling a flogging sail off the coast of Nova Scotia. At another point, two miles above the sea, you could have found him in a blizzard behind the wheel of a road plow clearing mountain roads. And then, walking along a forest path, you could look up into a tree and see Russick Smith, lit by a ray of light, playing his cello. He is a man unbound by convention on a mission to fight cynicism with wonder.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"The only child of a wildland firefighter and a psychiatric nurse, Smith was raised rambling through natural environments of the western US in the bed of a pickup truck. After seeing a cello in his elementary school cafeteria, he began playing music at age nine. By high school, he wanted to step away from the cello in favor of the electric bass; the allure of high-energy heavy metal outweighing the nuanced refinement of the traditional cello repertoire. But four years after that, he found himself more enthralled with the technical prowess of the jazz greats.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7yETSSCVLrlV5g2jVjj0WZ?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"After attending school for audio engineering at the <strong>Conservatory of Recording Arts and Sciences</strong>, Smith went on to work as an Assistant Engineer in the Woodstock, NY area. There he worked on records with artists such as <strong>The Black Crowes</strong>, <strong>Peter Murphy</strong>, and <strong>Levon Helm</strong>. While at Helm’s home, he assisted on “<strong>Electric Dirt</strong>,” which won the first-ever <strong>Grammy award</strong> for&nbsp;<strong>Best Americana Album</strong>. However, despite achieving some professional aspirations in that environment, it left him emotionally isolated. His restlessness led him out of music to pursue a myriad of avenues in search of a tenable life balance, with his instruments an ever-present shadow. He worked aboard traditionally rigged sailing ships <strong>Mystic Whaler</strong> and the<strong> Pride of Baltimore II</strong>, cello jammed beneath a fo’c’sle bunk or mandolin swinging above his bed in stormy seas. He worked as a snowboard instructor, his upright bass tucked in the corner of his basement apartment. He was a night-shift plow diver, recording new compositions as a way to give variation to six months of winter routine. A baker, a photographer, a lawn mower, a bus driver, the man emptying a trash can on the corner of the street; at some point you may have seen him…&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"It was on that foundation that Smith’s musical voice was forged; an identity formed between rolling seas and rolling hills, heavy weather and heavy machines, between a relentless imagination and a doubtful heart. And today he is lauded by his community. Colorado governor Jared Polis called him “uniquely Colorado,”&nbsp;<strong>Yo-yo Ma</strong> called his playing at a 2018 performance “gorgeous,” and music fans took notice when a news story about his arboreal performances was syndicated across the country. Even so, you still might not have seen him…but maybe walking that sunny forest path, exploring a desert canyon, or sitting in a concert hall someday, at some point, you will."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Russick Smith!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6T0N7UAY6mU88929XDTeyx?utm_source=generator","height":"380"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"http://russicksmith.com/","img":"","title":"This is the standard home page. You can see this text if you choose the default page template for your home page. To display the sections,...","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/russicksmith/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;| </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/russicksmith\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>F</strong><strong>acebook</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/russicksmith\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YouTube</strong></a><br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"243001","title":"Independent Chilled-Pop Singer-Songwriter, FAYYE, Dropped Her Newest Track 'Different Today'","date":"2023-06-02","lead":"FAYYE drops 'Different Today' to mark her upcoming 4-track EP, 'Rise'","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/243001/39f61d8722fe8f0033055fac53611152.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"FAYYE drops 'Different Today' to mark her upcoming 4-track EP, 'Rise'<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2FpHVwB5i1m97bRgSWpzwY?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"London, ENGLAND (June 2, 2023) – Chilled-pop singer-songwriter, <strong>FAYYE</strong>, just released her latest single, '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2FpHVwB5i1m97bRgSWpzwY?si=65bbb59d68d54419\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Different Today</strong></a>.'"},{"t":"p","html":"Both peaceful and bewitching, smooth melodies and layered harmonies intertwine to create dreamy, majestic overtones that set the scene for a story about mental health, empowerment, and independence.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"FAYYE wrote the lyrics one summer morning at 5 am. The rain of the night before had ‘washed the ghosts away’ and the stillness of a new day filled the air. It felt like a new beginning."},{"t":"quote","html":"“I wanted to write something to mark that moment at dawn, when anything is possible - before the day has decided what it's going to be.\"","cite":"FAYYE, Chilled-Pop Singer-Songwriter"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/0ZiVxl0eYKmmFI4JlxP9Wu?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"'Different Today' is released as part of FAYYE's four-song EP, '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/0ZiVxl0eYKmmFI4JlxP9Wu?si=DW4HA9aUSwuKhSQ7M1aZSg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Rise</strong></a>' which also released on June 2nd. Each track on the EP explores themes of rediscovered self-worth and conviction following a period of change and growth FAYYE experienced in her early twenties. Telling stories about new horizons and turned pages, this is an EP for anyone making a fresh start."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/544920/large-6c5dfd7d446515bbfc25acf40ce3278e.jpg","alt":"Copy of _DSC9306.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/544920/preview-874b525b86c18cbfcb42fb6ca492c980.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/544921/large-b99642e5594a3e7dfc7bee3c5ebca4c8.jpg","alt":"COVER ART.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/544921/preview-35e63ed14f5139cd1d81f2f9d7b6ffa3.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About FAYYE:"},{"t":"p","html":"London-based Greek-Irish singer-songwriter, FAYYE, is paving her own path as an independent artist in the pop music scene. Drawing on her experience as a classical concert pianist, each song starts at the piano, showcasing bewitching vocals, distinctive soaring melodies and shimmering overtones. Fearlessly exploring themes of vulnerability, frailty and resilience, her music captures the flicker of a moment – whether it’s the ambience of a dimly lit city street, the quiet stillness of daybreak or the thrill of an athlete inches away from the finish line."},{"t":"p","html":"Having caught the attention of critics at <strong>Clash</strong>, <strong>BBC Radio</strong>, and audiences at <strong>Ronnie Scott</strong>'s alike, FAYYE is working towards the launch of her second EP, ‘Rise’. ‘Rise’ triumphantly signals a new beginning for FAYYE. In her own words, <em>“I wrote ‘Rise’ after a period of change and growth in my early twenties. The songs are about discovering new horizons and trusting your intuition. I wrote them for anyone making a fresh start.”&nbsp;</em> In celebration of her EP, FAYYE is performing London's <a href=\"https://starinshoreditch.co.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Star in Shoreditch</a> on June 13th! Listen to FAYYE's new single 'Different Today' on all platforms!"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"245231","title":"Karmic Neighborhood Release \"Where Do I Go Now?\" Ahead of Feature Film","date":"2023-06-02","lead":"This track is the second release of a six-single series leading up to the soundtrack album launch for 'Equinox the Musical.'","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/245231/aca734636ca185aac8bb35a45a7427df.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This track is the second release of a six-single series leading up to the soundtrack album launch for 'Equinox the Musical.'<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0YrIe61CIjQf2P8jIszwLg?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Royal Oaks, CA (June 2, 2023) - Armand Ruby and Julian Colbeck of Karmic Neighborhood are releasing their alt-pop single, \"Where Do I Go Now?\", the second in a series of singles from the preview soundtrack for “Equinox the Musical,\" a feature film currently in development. “Equinox the Musical\" is the story of two homeless young lovers who discover (in the course of one tumultuous day) that forgiveness, gratitude and love can be the keys to surviving even the most chaotic circumstances.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Imagine you’ve screwed up – badly – and your life is falling apart. You’ve managed to get kicked out of your place, or fired from your job, or both – and now you literally don’t know where to go. That’s what happens to Jason, the lead character in “Equinox the Musical”, in what is known in the film biz as the story’s “precipitating event”. \"Where Do I Go Now?\" explores themes of hopelessness, homelessness, angst, and despair, reflecting the intense feelings experienced by Jason as he suddenly finds himself out on the street. Carrying his backpack, guitar, and an old suitcase, Jason heads out into the unknown, feeling vulnerable and desperate, with nowhere to turn. The scene’s intensity is conveyed brilliantly in “Where Do I Go Now” by the searing, soaring vocals of rocker James Durbin.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"The full preview soundtrack album for “Equinox the Musical\" will be released on the fall equinox, Sept. 22, 2023.<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/WhereDoIGoNow","label":"Listen On All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"Where Do I Go Now? is a jangly, grungy 'cri de coeur' against love and life amongst the dispossessed.","cite":"Julien Colbeck, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Where Do I Go Now? is a raucous, angst-filled ride through the twisting streets of an uncertain future, with Despair at the wheel.”","cite":"Armand Ruby, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"button","href":"https://equinoxmusical.com/","label":"Learn more about 'Equinox The Musical'","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548758/large-fe5de623de3c89712a2edef045c23f66.jpg","alt":"ARMAND 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548758/preview-299736547f2fb00ef0038198bee927de.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548759/large-63c52ffa0bfe5ef6d618ec04114c942a.jpg","alt":"ARMAND 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548759/preview-82a99135df86fb1042c91accda9fae70.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548761/large-87ca0b4171427dc32f53ab37b05cf869.png","alt":"ARMAND 2.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548761/preview-84856a2ae40a27236a816c5439eb147a.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548760/large-5039c17926b51e2e8f60bf28405e0e2c.png","alt":"ARMAND 4.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548760/preview-dcb5e2ded2cba52c85a42d8b11d669ed.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Karmic Neighborhood:"},{"t":"p","html":"The west coast-based team are strangers-turned-neighbors, turned rhythmic alt-pop collaborators. Armand Ruby and Julian Colbeck are two life-long musicians in their 60's who met by chance when they moved to the same neighborhood on the central California coast. Julian was formerly a London-based rock star and lifelong music industry veteran, while Armand was professionally an environmental scientist who stayed involved in music as a part-time musician and songwriter. Armand and Julian formed a strong bond through their shared passion for music and the painful yet hopeful life experience of surviving cancer. The two found inspiration within the harmony of their own respective life journeys and a mutual interest in musical innovation."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vnYPcPpvzO0hhjR6YMUkV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Armand Ruby:"},{"t":"p","html":"Like many creatives, Armand was a sensitive child. Growing up, this was of course a blessing and a curse, in the face of both the world’s beauty and its harshness. Throughout his childhood in the northeastern United States, Armand was aware that maintaining this sensitivity might be a challenge. So keeping this cherished inner life alive became a lifelong ambition – and it found expression through music and songwriting. Armand wrote his first little tune at the age of 11, and as a teenager began composing songs, something he’s continued to do throughout life. But his musical talent was matched by a proclivity for science, and a scholarship to an Ivy League university led to a career as an Environmental Scientist."},{"t":"p","html":"Still, Armand continued to be active musically: songwriting, recording demos, performing in rock bands no one’s ever heard of, leading small choral groups, and for several years even singing in a professional opera chorus. A breakthrough came in 2010-2011 with the writing of the book and songs for a musical stage play, <strong>“Equinox.”</strong> Directing the play in its brief but sold-out run in Santa Cruz California was, according to Armand, <em>“both the most difficult and most rewarding experience of my life.”&nbsp;</em>With Equinox, Armand finds himself working at the creative intersection of art and social activism – shining a new light on the often out-of-sight homeless population and the many ways people can become homeless, through story and music. Another breakthrough came while working to convert the Equinox stage play into a feature-length musical film screenplay. Moving in 2019 to the rural Monterey Bay area community of Royal Oaks, Armand found that one of his neighbors, Julian Colbeck, was an experienced music arranger, producer and keyboardist.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Armand and Julian teamed up as Karmic Neighborhood to produce a ‘preview soundtrack’ album of the songs from “Equinox the Musical”, being released worldwide by <a href=\"https://freshnoisedistro.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Fresh Noise Distro</strong></a> in 2023. As a precursor to making the Equinox feature film, in 2021 Armand wrote and directed the short musical film, <strong>“I Said I Will,”</strong> featuring the song <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/09L2h21DyZ4ZRNnZSLIXx9?si=f279b950a43e4b16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Don’t Want to Walk Away</strong></a><strong>,”</strong> produced by Colbeck and Ruby. The film won several awards at film festivals, including for Best Soundtrack, Best Original Score, and Best Music Video.<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Julian Colbeck:"},{"t":"p","html":"Julian Colbeck grew up in the south of England, where he learned how to play the piano and ultimately pursued his dreams of being in a London-based rock ‘n’ roll band in his late teens. Julian’s music career took off with the band <em><strong>Charlie</strong></em>, with whom he scored several US Top 40 singles including <strong>“Watching TV”</strong> and <strong>“LA Dreamer.”</strong> Over the span of a 40-year career, Julian worked and toured as a keyboard player/producer with <strong>Yes&nbsp;</strong>alumni group <strong>Anderson Bruford Wakeman Howe</strong>, former Genesis guitarist <strong>Steve Hackett</strong>, <strong>Charlie</strong>, <strong>John Miles</strong>, and more. In 2008 Julian began work with his long-time friend, <strong>Alan Parsons</strong>, on the award-winning instructional video series: <a href=\"https://www.artandscienceofsound.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Alan Parsons’ The Art &amp; Science Of Sound Recording</strong></a>. Julian also has written for many esteemed music industry publications and has authored many music and music technology books. Beginning in late 2019, and interrupted by intensive treatment for stage 4 cancer, Julian saw something of value in his neighbor Armand Ruby’s songwriting and his <em>Equinox&nbsp;</em>film project and worked as an arranger, co-producer, and keyboardist on the Equinox preview soundtrack recordings. Armand and Julian's collaboration on this work led to the production of their recent release, the radio remix of “I Don’t Want to Walk Away.” Karmic Neighborhood's new single from <em>Equinox the Musical,</em> <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/02dCSya8eXq3gRfaEeHGK6?si=6e15e2ec4a794fa5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Song of Wonder</strong></a><strong>”</strong> is now available on all streaming platforms."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Karmic Neighborhood!"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"245888","title":"Music | Culture Power45","date":"2023-06-02","lead":"Electric dance trio drops this release in celebration of their return to the realm of electronic music.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/245888/3a1ed2db76d2775544161546b82efef6.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"p","html":"<em>Electric dance trio drops this release in celebration of their return to the realm of electronic music.</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1q3Hf52Y8v5Dip8JayVvBG?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Atlanta, GA (JUNE 2, 2023) - Afro-futuristic trio known as <strong>The Degabah System</strong> is hitting the electronic scene with their new studio album, '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1q3Hf52Y8v5Dip8JayVvBG?si=TYqvKrF3STKh1ezMpssCgQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Saqqara</strong></a>!<strong>'</strong> The group describes Saqqara as <em>\"A macrocosm of hard-hitting light, love and sound.\"</em> The 14-track instrumental album features distorted intricacies and soulful congruity that transports listeners through new-found dimensions and sonic profiles. Saqqara is a hard-hitting sonic conundrum into the abyss of EDM/House Music and it is guaranteed to jack your body."},{"t":"p","html":"Each track on this album has a unique aura, perfect for whatever mood you're in, whether that involves dancing, relaxation, cooking, etc. Each member of The Degabah System cultivates their own sounds, coming together in perfect balance and harmony to create a futuristic yet grounded sound. Various instrumental elements such as synth, bass, drums, and organ are curated by each member of the group, bouncing between the distinct stylings of <strong>Annie Mae Bonaparte</strong>, <strong>Malcolm Garvey Dubois</strong>, and <strong>Mr. Jack Body</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/549731/large-b8d2dbb9e6f164b690ad253ba5b582f1.jpg","alt":"large-Degabah System color final cover (1).jpg"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Degabah System:"},{"t":"p","html":"The intraterrestrial trio known as <strong>The Degabah System</strong> returns under the guidance of <a href=\"http://www.fatnice.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Fatnice</strong></a> with their debut full-length protribution, '<strong>SAQQARA</strong>!' Saqqara is a macrocosm of hard-hitting light, love and sound as can be heard on the introductory track '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/16isFOLsOfLcIjIPcoEEtC?si=f415fa9ba4474be5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Enter The Degabah</strong></a>', previously released as a 45 via the group's label \"<a href=\"https://culturepower45.bandcamp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Culture Power 45</strong></a>\". From the distorted intricacies of 'Enter The Degabah', the soulful congruity of tracks '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/07dTtZrIM9UHrOxrVg8KMG?si=460eb8cac8f44a94\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Up Sibley Blvd</strong></a>.' and '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/60x4xyfhW9NVEZDJRna0mx?si=68721255a15c4a83\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Ben is Here</strong></a>' to the time-traveling kicks of '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4CB5yiGxA5wm07RMu2URok?si=e8be7e4606f44cb2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>STOP</strong></a>' and '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5368fzjsoCswVLf3VoeANv?si=9ef423a2b3f248e5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>More Sofa Love</strong></a>', Saqqara is a hard-hitting sonic conundrum into the abyss of <strong>House </strong>- guaranteed to jack your body. <strong>Annie Mae Bonaparte</strong> also known as 'The Extrataless' is the lifeline of Degabah, she gave birth to the light and cultivates the sound. Annie Mae is a 7th-degree light source and conjures the harmonies of the organ and synth from the ultraviolet rays of the gavel of <strong>Imhotep</strong>. <strong>Malcolm Garvey Dubois</strong> is a historian of many spaces and many names. In this plane, he is the curator of the bass. Malcolm is a 5th-degree light source and keeper of the Books of Bass Theory and Manipulations Volumes 1-700. <strong>Mr. Jack Body</strong> is a 1000-generation member of The Hummers of the Drum Sect, a secret society believed to have established sound in and outside of itself. Mr. Body is 100 degree light source and keeper of The Scrolls of JACK! Together these three light sources have manifested and integrated their knowledge and experience with my guidance to fulfill your body's need to dance! <em>“There’s No Need To Fear The Degabah System is Hear!”</em>&nbsp;'Saqqara' is now available on all platforms on June 2, 2023."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Degabah System:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://culturepower45.bandcamp.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BUY VINYL HERE</a>"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://culturepower45.bandcamp.com/","img":"https://f4.bcbits.com/img/0016005517_23.jpg","title":"Music | Culture Power45","desc":"Culture Power45. Chicago, Illinois. Culture Power45 Brand Partners with Solar Babies Art Institute LLC grounded in providing culturally based sound to a worldwide audience via the limited vinyl, tapes"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"245906","title":"Elder Grown- Funkalicious Rock'n Roots Music","date":"2023-05-31","lead":"Indulge in an unforgettable evening of live music hosted by Elder Grown, augmented with more performances.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/245906/9a83ac3bafeb1fbfad15d7e66c7502e8.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"p","html":"Indulge in an unforgettable evening of live music hosted by Elder Grown, augmented with more performances."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548771/large-dcc7559208b0ab36587700e770886e3c.jpg","alt":"IMG_6690.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"Aztec, NM (July 8, 2023) — <strong>Elder Grown</strong>, the dynamic musical ensemble renowned for their fusion of genres and captivating performances, is proud to announce their highly anticipated event: <strong>Elder Grown's Summer Camp</strong>. This exceptional one-night music festival will take place on <strong>Saturday, July 8th</strong>, starting at 5 pm at the picturesque <a href=\"https://ticotimeresort.ticketspice.com/elder-grown-july-8th\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Tico Time River Resort</strong></a> in Aztec, New Mexico."},{"t":"p","html":"Elder Grown's Summer Camp guarantees an unforgettable evening of live music featuring a stellar lineup of talented artists. Audiences will be treated to performances by <strong>Ava Swan</strong>, <strong>Rachel Angel</strong>, <strong>Nelleke</strong>, and a late-night set by the <strong>Forest Thump</strong>."},{"t":"p","html":"To ensure a seamless ticketing process, Elder Grown offers various ticket tiers to accommodate different preferences. Online ticket options include:"},{"t":"p","html":"<b>Day Tickets: $15</b>"},{"t":"p","html":"Enjoy the musical journey of Elder Grown's Summer Camp for a single day from 5 pm."},{"t":"p","html":"<b>Tickets with Camping Passes: $20</b>"},{"t":"p","html":"Immerse yourself fully in the festival atmosphere by enjoying the musical performances and camping under the stars. This ticket option includes both festival entry and a camping pass."},{"t":"p","html":"<b>Weekend Camping Passes and Show Tickets: $35</b>"},{"t":"p","html":"Indulge in a weekend-long experience by accessing the entire festival, including camping facilities. Immerse yourself in the magic of Elder Grown's Summer Camp throughout the weekend."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548770/compressed_original-085960ed1da24038e8725f019eebcc95.jpg","alt":"ELDER GROWN.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"Elder Grown's Summer Camp aims to create an inclusive and vibrant community celebration. The festival provides a platform for artists to showcase their talents while offering attendees an opportunity to experience a wide range of musical styles. Tico Time River Resort serves as the perfect backdrop, combining natural beauty with the power of music."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"Funk meets Pop, Rock meets Hip Hop, Jazz meets Reggae,\"</em> explains <strong>Sam Kelly</strong>, a driving force behind Elder Grown's captivating sound. <em>\"We invite you to break down your preconceptions of genre and join us on a soul-stirring journey. From the first note to the last, Elder Grown will ignite your senses and challenge your perceptions of what music can be.\"</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Tickets for Elder Grown's Summer Camp are now available for purchase through the official festival <a href=\"https://ticotimeresort.ticketspice.com/elder-grown-july-8th\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">website</a>. Don't miss this extraordinary opportunity to be part of a transcendent musical experience and join the Elder Grown community for an unforgettable night under the stars."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548763/large-87dad5aa38b095c4159eeccfcd8b5953.jpg","alt":"IMG_1030.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548763/preview-864f2371365648fd96d411b0371142fb.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548766/large-fd520eabf94941822e8a3908cf0785c2.jpg","alt":"EH3A8810 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548766/preview-86de1fdbf2c5da2b5ef44e8192ecfa22.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548765/large-8e995a3912e6c8ecdebc7a5bcdd81901.jpg","alt":"EH3A8695.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548765/preview-46df9f88b8b87f91fe438644c16f9b86.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548764/large-b6967d136dc0b4b664e69011de0af888.jpg","alt":"EH3A8628 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548764/preview-895658b2342a532c054a684995bd7579.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548767/large-12daa1163009d0f8aa1ea9c93be8bc0c.jpg","alt":"EH3A8678 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/548767/preview-1c89a7ec7c90d124532c25b94fe4483f.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>About Elder Grown:</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Elder Grown is a dynamic musical ensemble that defies genre boundaries. With their fusion of funk, pop, rock, hip-hop, jazz, and reggae, they create a soul-inspired sound that captivates audiences. From improvisational jams to instrument-swapping performances, Elder Grown takes listeners on a captivating musical journey. Drawing inspiration from various artists, their unique sound blends elements of different genres to create an unforgettable experience."},{"t":"p","html":"Visit Elder Grown's <a href=\"https://eldergrownmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">website</a> and follow them on socials to keep updated!"},{"t":"button","href":"http://eldergrownmusic.com/press-kit","label":"Elder Grown Press Kit","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"For more information, media inquiries, or press passes, please contact:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Sam Kelly</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Elder Grown"},{"t":"p","html":"Samkelly09@gmail.com"},{"t":"p","html":"(970) 799-5498"},{"t":"p","html":"J-Calvin | Booking/Management ​| <a href=\"https://www.jcalvinmusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Website</a><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Snazzy Licks | Booking/Management | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/snazzylicks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Indigo Room | Talent Buyer |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/indigoroomdurango/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"http://eldergrownmusic.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/56b56c938259b57383073e49/t/586435aabebafbe2173742ca/1482962346931/EG+Green+CircleTiny.png?format=1500w","title":"Elder Grown- Funkalicious Rock'n Roots Music","desc":"Colorado based professional funk, rock, roots, and soul band. Check Elder Grown's tour schedule and see where they're touring next."},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"242031","title":"Hip Hop Artist Brandon Vee Just Released New Single \"Why\"","date":"2023-05-26","lead":"Reiki healer x recording artist Brandon Vee releases new exploratory single.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/242031/4d8c6edb81fe2ddbe6b3fa45d7e2ebb4.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Reiki healer x recording artist Brandon Vee releases new exploratory single."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/5lZNvqCUFHUYK6Q1nvEdzP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Orlando, FL (MAY 26, 2023) - R&amp;B artist <strong>Brandon Vee</strong> just released a new experiential single, <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5lZNvqCUFHUYK6Q1nvEdzP?si=eb7418b2994e4347\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Why</strong></a><strong>\"</strong> on May 26. This track is part of his album <strong>\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4SrmEBuPAHhQFKZi6cB7xF?si=KKvRah9OS7SBa2uJ19Hevw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Revolution of the Soul</a>.\" </strong>In Brandon's words, this new song is inspired by \"the act of avoiding your best self.\" In this work, the artist interprets life's struggles from various lenses, one relating to how we process our surroundings in childhood and how adults impact our sense of the world. Another topic explored through Vee's lyrics is the warped sense of freedom and equality we experience as Americans and how these entities have changed over time. Vee switches lenses yet again within the second verse of the song, referencing the societal pressure and impossible beauty standards women in America. Vee brings to light how these pressures result in negative talk around self-image and how this ultimately causes mental health struggles.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534740/large-dfcccc4e76a1d42b1fcaf0d7e635c8ac.jpg","alt":"IMG_1905.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534740/preview-41ffa0af96b4720a8526c869b603b06e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/540780/large-5699088928c8122f49fb5272a936a10e.jpg","alt":"unnamed2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/540780/preview-ef9183168f841d604e3ac5e561506915.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/540781/large-623c1ed716b24a23bc05487f0bbf0c2f.jpg","alt":"unnamed.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/540781/preview-0dfcc03921b3cf2b0c4cdf5506a3556a.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brandon Vee:"},{"t":"p","html":"Brooklyn, NY native Brandon Vee fuses the energy of hip-hop with the classic melodies of R&amp;B and Jazz to create a funk-inspired aura and sound. Brandon started his lyrical journey at the young age of 10 when he started writing poetry to express complex feelings of heaviness and discomfort. Brandon continues to use music as a medium of self-discovery and healing intertwining the boundaries of his own worldly perspectives with personal growth. Brandon Vee creates a unique and powerful sound with his music, carrying listeners through storylines of spirituality, introspection, and self-discovery. Vee draws inspiration from diverse yet legendary artists such as <strong>J. Cole</strong>, <strong>Childish Gambino</strong>, and <strong>Funkadelic</strong>. In 2022, Brandon Vee performed alongside famous artists such as <strong>Meg The Stallion</strong>, <strong>Denzel Curry</strong>, <strong>EarthGang</strong>, and more, inspiring him to showcase his new music on a live platform more often. Brandon is dedicated to themes of challenge and healing within his newest album, \"Revolution Of The Soul\" which released on April 28th, 2023."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Brandon Vee!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://Brandon Vee Shopify\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Brandon Vee Shopify</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://Instagram.com/thatmanvee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.thatmamvee.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>WEBSITE</strong></a>&nbsp;| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/officialbrandonvee/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/thatmanvee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>SOUNDCLOUD</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"242475","title":"Cliffs and Caves - YouTube","date":"2023-05-26","lead":"Mother-daughter americana duo release their 6-track EP including hit single \"Mint Gum\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/242475/ff13bc49926a4ecf620fcf2ebe0b8572.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Mother-daughter americana duo release their 6-track EP including hit single \"Mint Gum\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4yPCrmgRYC4coipOqrzOtN?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston, TX (MAY 26, 2023) - <a href=\"https://cliffsandcaves.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cliffs + Caves</strong></a>&nbsp;just released their long-awaited 6-track EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4yPCrmgRYC4coipOqrzOtN?si=M2QHAy_sRgSwSZzTJKzjEw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Lost The Trail</strong></em></a> on May 26th. The tracks include: <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3tvZi3hKI3NlT8jWVWuHX1?si=ba54a28410694864\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Sunrise</strong></em></a><em>, </em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6fuUeePkEi8Mx4kG1Qfa22?si=7d1ab1fa71f44445\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Mint Gum</strong></em></a><em><strong>&nbsp;</strong>(feat. David Ramirez), </em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2QcsyCzzBQy8JMIZJv42ac?si=aa94f4a4a5554e28\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Eso Si Que Es</strong></em></a><em>, </em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5OZxS06uvQUuXToXSDc6Om?si=9604588baf264bae\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Radiant</strong></em></a><em>, </em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4Dnb9swzjPlf5He0Ra38PV?si=d69ae3f381e1438b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>The Coop</strong></em></a>, and <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4dEjLFwnSrzQGxy0ba7BPL?si=b1cda3ac48fe4a7b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Knew My Name</strong></em></a>. Through folk-inspired rhythms and emotional lyrics, this EP highlights sentiments of love, heartbreak, struggle, perseverance, and more. <strong>Claire and Lindsey</strong> create a unified emotional masterpiece with their release of Lost The Trail, with each track containing lyrics that foster empathy and human connection. Lindsey and Claire strive to create tracks that hold great truth and console the minds of those who seek healing."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/138490LosttheTrail","label":"Listen On All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"The name \"Lost The Trail\" is an ode to the simultaneously beautiful and heartbreaking elements of life, which can be wild to experience both at the same time all at once. The EP is meant to reinforce that no one is alone in the complexities of life - and sometimes, all we can do is smile in acceptance until we find the way back to our trail/path. \"Lost the Trail\" is all about embracing the wilderness of life and all of its unexpected turns. It's about the realization that life itself is the \"not knowing\" where we are headed or what’s coming around the corner.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The EP also tells the tale of how mom, Lindsey Justice and daughter Claire Justice have evolved in their relationship as Claire enters young adulthood.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\">&nbsp;"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Lost The Trail is my defining phrase in this new phase of life in college. I have been taking paths that I never could have imagined, and exploring everything life has to offer. This new chapter is far off of the beaten path and no where near the trail I had imagined for myself going down.\"","cite":"Claire Justice, Cliffs + Caves"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Our music seems to reflect how the craft of joint songwriting has become such a rich bonding experience. We write about what we’ve been experiencing- some of it was the hardest we’ve lived through, some the brightest- but we were honest about all of it.\"","cite":"Lindsey Justice, Cliffs + Caves"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by modern alternative music icons such as <strong>Maggie Rogers</strong>, <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, <strong>Boy Genius</strong>, and <strong>Noah Gundersen</strong>, Cliffs + Caves define their sound as <em>\"Indie-Americana.\"</em> Whether you're floating down the river or hiking up the <strong>Grand Tetons</strong>, Cliffs + Caves provide the perfect balance of chill and uplifting music for your sweet summer adventures."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541204/large-c5140308d7e3b9c3ab89f595e1722448.jpeg","alt":"F0AC0EA2-6108-44E7-A043-7F99F2E6A151.jpeg"},{"t":"p","html":"The duo is releasing a music video for the EP track <strong>\"The Coop\"</strong> sometime in late June. Stay tuned for more music videos and announcements and key partnerships that Cliffs + Caves are working to bring to fruition."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1J0Q7piRpWRQHW9IegFT4X?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Cliffs + Caves:"},{"t":"p","html":"Cliffs + Caves, the mother-daughter duo of Lindsey and Claire Justice, unabashedly share their deeply personal and relatable stories through songs that resonate with listeners of all generations. Best known in their home state of Texas for their unique blend of Contemporary Americana music, the pair showcases the musical ingenuity that is created when artistry runs in the family with intimate lyrics lilting intrinsically over smooth musical progressions. Their previous discography includes their 2017 debut EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3SanUmvSOsrCrv1A4NlXZ2?si=nzqjn0iqSQOKnlxOcWf5yA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hold On</strong></a> (recorded with Grammy-nominated producer <strong>Jamie Candiloro (Ryan Adams, R.E.M., The Eagles)&nbsp;</strong>and featuring performances by legendary <strong>Willie Nelson</strong>’s harmonica player, <strong>Mickey Raphael</strong>) and sophomore EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4gEhBjWLd5a66JwQRENwNs?si=29JFfKxoSCqgPHKkQN5n0Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Capsize</strong></a> (produced by <strong>Chris Jacobie (Penny and Sparrow, Jarrod Dickenson, Duncan Fellows)</strong>. The original songs are a team effort with the duo individually contributing to the mastery of their lyrics and melodies. Moreover, twenty-year-old Claire being a multi-instrumentalist, not only composes the music for the tracks but also bestows a knack for songwriting. Their newer music further explores the duo's ability to portray life through lyrics as they evolve into a more alternative Maggie-Rogers-esque sound while still maintaining their Americana roots and drawing inspiration from benchmark artists like Phoebe Bridgers,<strong>&nbsp;Lake Street Dive,&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Patty Griffin</strong>. Stay tuned for what's next from the duo!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Cliffs + Caves!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://cliffsandcaves.com/","img":"","title":"The official website for Texas-based mother/daughter duo Cliffs + Caves.","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.youtube.com/@cliffsandcaves2211?cbrd=1&amp;ucbcb=1","img":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/ytc/AGIKgqPPr5Gr4PP4mqpjJaBZqVj2m9DugGwqDXATUSgtYw=s900-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj","title":"Cliffs and Caves - YouTube","desc":"Cliffs + Caves, the mother-daughter duo of Lindsey and Claire Justice, unabashedly share their deeply personal and relatable stories through songs that reson..."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/CseY3SYuju0/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/cliffs_and_caves/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM&nbsp;</a>| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/cliffsandcaves\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a>​"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"241812","title":"The Trouble Notes Announce Second Studio Album Ahead of Fall 2023 North American Tour","date":"2023-05-19","lead":"The Trouble Notes releases new folk-inspired album \"Liberty Awaits\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/241812/3817daa9f11160d5dabd1f4849849766.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Trouble Notes releases new folk-inspired album \"Liberty Awaits\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5luk6F956IAyTWoh35llWW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"BERLIN, GERMANY (May 19, 2023) - Ahead of their Fall 2023 tour, <a href=\"https://thetroublenotes.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Trouble Notes</strong></a> are releasing their second studio album <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5luk6F956IAyTWoh35llWW?si=FxCXWeHjSviZZZ5TxQJ-Kg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Liberty Awaits</strong></em></a><em><strong>&nbsp;</strong></em>on May 19th. The album is an exploration and fusion of various folk styles, delving deep into the complex nuances of the rich cultural fabric of our world. Hailing from 4 different continents, each member of The Trouble Notes brings a unique perspective to the music that proves that music is a universal language. As a central theme for the album, the band drew influence from different stories of cross-cultural integration due to the current and historical migration of people across land and sea."},{"t":"p","html":"Liberty Awaits is a vast expansion of the group's repertoire, an introduction of <em>new instruments</em> and <em>melodic voices</em> on top of a stable foundation for which the group has become internationally known over nearly a decade. Each track on the album is rich in emotion and spirit, containing a mature yet playful overtone. In addition to the core band members, the album features tracks with prodigious Ecuadorian singer <strong>Carola Zerega</strong>, French pianist <strong>Freddy Dubois</strong>, and Belgian bassist <strong>Olivier van Betsbrugge</strong>.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"242730","title":"Melodic Rock Artist Todd Michael Chapman Released New Single \"Hold On Tight\"","date":"2023-05-19","lead":"This expressive new track from Todd Michael Chapman dropped on May 19th.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/242730/acc5ec2a0778adc5a416cca1477bd912.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This expressive new track from Todd Michael Chapman dropped on May 19th."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0yY7qxCIRIsNGLGAzqjtfV?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Buffalo, NY (May 19, 2023) - Rust-belt rocker <strong>Todd Michael Chapman</strong> is releasing his new single,<strong> \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0yY7qxCIRIsNGLGAzqjtfV?si=03e6e4f946ad41e6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">​Hold On Tight​</a>\"</strong> on May 19th. The new track meets at a crossroads of classic and modern rock, producing an overtone reminiscent of <strong>Lynyrd Skynyrd's</strong> \"<strong>Simple Man</strong>\". Chapman dedicates this tune to each of his children and their uniquely inspiring life endeavors. He wrote the lyrics of \"Hold On Tight\" as encouragement for his kids and listeners to persevere through life's challenges and trials, reminding them that there is always someone cheering them on. \"Hold On Tight\" is a beacon of light for anyone who struggles to fit in, reassuring them that everything will work out in the end."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/1498281697%3Fsecret_token%3Ds-3NHAulGjKMS&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false&show_teaser=true","height":"166"},{"t":"p","html":"Todd Michael Chapman released his debut EP in December of 2022 and has been hard at work creating new music and reinventing his melodic rock sound. Todd has dedicated most of his adult life to family and raising children, but he never lost sight of his undying passion for music. The soothing tone that Chapman creates through various guitar melodies and harmonized vocals puts listeners at ease, allowing them to drift into a state of tranquility. Chapman's sound is inspired by country rock, 70's rock and 90's alt-rock, influenced by great artists such as <strong>Tonic</strong>, <strong>Jude Cole</strong>, <strong>REO Speedwagon</strong>, and <strong>Keith Urban</strong>."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5do7rTGXEBlKusrEMzwKOB?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Todd's music is a mix of various genres that combine to form a modern interpretation of melancholic rock. \"Hold On Tight\" was written, recorded, and produced by Todd Michael Chapman with guest <strong>Mike Schill</strong> on bass guitar. The single features strong tempo and lyrical attitude changes that bring a certain sonic edge to the table. Complex rhythms capture a range of emotions, starting from a place of desperation and climbing an optimistic mountain towards inspiration."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542025/large-be709a6cc247b0903a8433f2b40903cb.jpg","alt":"toddmichael-39.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542025/preview-5b4e7aed1926568b353f031d3b87511c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542026/large-983bfacf09d5bde93c26f8f7d2d2122e.jpg","alt":"toddmichael-59.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542026/preview-99f9667ffd061dd2893fc5d1cff24d39.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542027/large-985276a8c02c6029ca73dc44c1fadcd7.jpg","alt":"toddmichael-121.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542027/preview-ee120f19b809726dc15bc7d5c922224e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542028/large-1c028f4ba4b92b0e4e21128ff9c42fe7.png","alt":"Hold On Tight - TMC - Album Art.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542028/preview-085cdb6d4f63208cbcde58b8a406ac16.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Todd Michael Chapman:"},{"t":"p","html":"Born and raised in Western New York, Todd Michael Chapman is a rust-belt-inspired melodic rock singer, songwriter, and musician. He received his first guitar around age 7 as a gift from his aunt, learned his first chords from his bass-playing cousin, and began writing songs in his early teens. As a high school senior, Todd began playing clubs in and around Buffalo, NY. By age 19 he’d recorded some of his original songs with one receiving airplay on <strong>97 Rock</strong>, a local Buffalo radio station which sponsored a weekly local music hour. In his 20's, Todd moved to Phoenix, AZ to focus on raising a family and building a career in technology, putting his music career on the back burner."},{"t":"p","html":"While living in Phoenix, Todd connected with local musicians and continued writing and recording songs. In 2006, he moved back to Buffalo, NY and after playing a handful of gigs with local bands, he set up a studio in the basement of his home. In 2020, Todd began writing music again and revisiting some of his previously recorded songs. The results can be heard in his 2022 debut EP, <strong>“</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3iXFaH0RaaNRtktGEn76q4?si=6aXf3pJeT9GlIiCI9cwyew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Now &amp; Again</strong></a><strong>”</strong>, aptly named as it combines newly written songs with rewrites of a few of his older compositions. His latest single \"Hold On Tight\" releases on Friday, May 19, and will be available for streaming on all platforms."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Todd!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://instagram.com/toddmichaelchapman\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAG</strong><strong>RAM</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ToddMichaelChapman\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://twitter.com/ToddMichaelChap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>T</strong><strong>WITTER</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.toddmichaelchapman.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>WEBSITE</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"236243","title":"Musician|Band Nonē Sunshine is an independent rock artist based out of Denver, CO. For new, original music releases and event dates be sure to check here often","date":"2023-05-18","lead":"Tech-Veterans Turned Rock and Roll Stars Realize 20+ Years Dream of Pursuing Music.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/236243/6356ab82aedd6f8e299b32e26fc63c83.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Tech-Veterans Turned Rock and Roll Stars Realize 20+ Years Dream of Pursuing Music."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5SiPgNxGYskOuhikQtyNd0?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Denver, CO (May 18, 2023) – Life-long friends turned 90’s alternative rock-inspired musical duo, <strong>NONĒ SUNSHINE</strong>, are releasing their debut LP, '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5SiPgNxGYskOuhikQtyNd0?si=VDBAWuyaSZiLsYqmdViWIQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>I</em></strong><strong><em><strong>nsides Out</strong></em></strong></a>.' After 20+ years of focusing on family and being separated by distance, corporate America tech veterans, <strong>Derek Hyde</strong> (Songwriter, guitar, vocals) and <strong>Thomas Scott Laird</strong> (Songwriter, bass, vocals, guitar) are finally able to reunite and pursue their collective passion for rock and roll.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The 12-song Alternative-Rock LP will feature guitar-forward tracks and layered melodies, highlighting themes related to the meaning of life while simultaneously portraying the essence of nostalgia. With this release (mixed by multi-platinum producer <strong>Barrett Jones</strong>), NONĒ SUNSHINE strives to cultivate an upbeat sound while heavily focusing on the importance of meaningful and memorable lyrics. The pair's sound is inspired by iconic rock bands such as <strong>The Foo Fighters</strong>, <strong>Our Lady Peace</strong>, and <strong>Oasis</strong>."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/InsidesOut","label":"Listen On All Major Listening Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Derek and Thomas Scott (TS) made their official debut as NONĒ SUNSHINE last Spring (April 2022), when they performed alongside American rock band, <strong>Sponge</strong>. After their first live performance as NONĒ SUNSHINE, the pair launched their debut single \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6V9xxWZChh5Gn76WdE1inN?si=85bc9b02ed164498\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>S.O.S.</strong></a>\" Although Derek and TS are geographically split between Denver, CO and Tucson, AZ, the two have worked 20+ years to uphold their kinship and musical connection - ultimately fulfilling their goal of becoming a band. Derek and TS live by the notion, <em>“If you want it, go for it,” </em>and want to show fans that they are a testament to never losing sight of the things you love to do."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528596/large-a2ca675339a90471b418e7ea5e97e8ba.jpg","alt":"_10A2091.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528596/preview-385aefb7cbb5d9312f929a881ec80659.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528597/large-7adc20a0ff6c24f02bf5223a7fc13d75.jpg","alt":"_10A2221-1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528597/preview-e5a797fd10c095b6c089d54d6e60f2d1.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528598/large-81dcb1c54605b94a4e99c05aba9e95aa.jpg","alt":"_10A2249.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528598/preview-6dc45c1633a538f4280018cd811abb52.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528595/large-34f4bfb6aceaa1d239cc1da2e8455c60.jpg","alt":"NONE SUNSHINE NEW.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528595/preview-8514c81869fff33bbbdcaffd79bfe837.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528594/large-2708220f57d1d4ef7ac0c8bc823beb71.jpg","alt":"VINTAGE NONE SUNSHUNE.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528594/preview-6ac967c0d9f62867630444646c7f43aa.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About NONĒ SUNSHINE:"},{"t":"p","html":"NONĒ SUNSHINE is an Alternative Rock band based out of Denver, CO and Tucson, AZ comprised of it’s two primary members Derek Hyde and Thomas Scott (TS) Laird. The band’s music ranges from moody to full-on explosive, continuously providing listeners with a binding ‘hook’ that seamlessly guides upbeat melodies."},{"t":"p","html":"NONĒ SUNSHINE is just getting started, but has been decades in the making. After meeting through an online musician’s classified ad 20+ years ago, Derek and TS struck up an immediate friendship. Finding a kinship in songwriting, they soon learned they shared a similar lens in how they viewed the world. Although life ultimately got in the way the first time around, the duo stayed close and continued to write songs for the sheer love of the art and process. With cutting-edge technology that has allowed TS and Derek to collaborate remotely, the two are leveraging new musical technology available to bring the vision of NONE SUNSHINE to fruition. Through the use of <strong>Logic Pro X</strong>, the <strong>Universal Audio</strong> suite, <strong>Soundbetter</strong>, <strong>Fiverr</strong>, and a vast array of equipment they have amassed over the years, the dynamic duo is positioned to launch their first LP this May 2023."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With NONĒ SUNSHINE!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6VyDmoHb4kEFBizoBWz4fe?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/thenonesunshine/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@thenonesunshine","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100069209409705","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.nonesunshine.com/","img":"","title":"Musician|Band Nonē Sunshine is an independent rock artist based out of Denver, CO. For new, original music releases and event dates be sure to check here often","desc":""},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"241397","title":"Just Back from Mexico Tour, Indie Band 'Alex McCue & The Group Activity' Released Bilingual Single","date":"2023-05-18","lead":"The blissful indie-pop anthem \"Dialogues With God\" launched May 18th.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/241397/09031fee5e244c24db629cafb1fa2595.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The blissful indie-pop anthem \"Dialogues With God\" launched May 18th."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7IvemSLlXsgBIgP9TyWH90?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (May 18, 2023) - Fresh off of a 17-date tour through Mexico and the US, <strong>Alex McCue &amp; The Group Activity </strong>has just released their new bilingual single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7IvemSLlXsgBIgP9TyWH90?si=9db48a803c804e0d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Dialogues With God</strong></a>,\" on May 18th. The upbeat track and live studio video were recorded in Valencia, Spain, where Alex spent a year studying music production and soaking up the vibrant sounds of the city. The lyrics bounce back and forth between English and Spanish, and the melody contains a jazzy overtone, paying homage to the dynamic influence of Valencian culture and McCue's time in Mexico. The single features <strong>Alex McCue</strong> on vocals and guitar, <strong>Diego Gutierrez</strong> on Trumpet, <strong>Cristian Delabela</strong> on Bass, and <strong>Marcos Regidor</strong> on Drums."},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"241803","title":"Rising Pop-Soul Artist Gemïny Releases Sultry Single \"Nicotine\"","date":"2023-05-18","lead":"Gemïny incorporates elements of soul, pop, and R&B within a new lyrically complex single.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/241803/eb0186afcca5c7ecfa5d90ed3e75aa83.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Gemïny incorporates elements of soul, pop, and R&amp;B within a new lyrically complex single."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/16FSxSIcKncPOSVCXamvnt?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Columbia, SC (MAY 18, 2023) - R&amp;B-inspired pop artist <strong>Gemïny </strong>will release his new single \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/16FSxSIcKncPOSVCXamvnt?si=08c1a724a5c341c4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Nicotine</strong></a>\" on May 18th, 2023. The track transports listeners through the juvenile cycle of lust, catching feelings, confusion, and betrayal. \"Nicotine\" dives into the emotion elicited from toxic love and dating styles. The release of this new tune elicits a sentiment of <em>\"making peace with the past\"</em> for Gemïny. The upbeat yet eerie overtone of this single creates a stark sonic contrast, turning this release into a cerebral experience for the listener."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3Wm0Khz27xWSexaDJ95RpW?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"With over 1 million streams across all platforms, Gemïny is constantly working on new music including his <strong>\"Victoria's secret\" album</strong> (release date TBD). Nicotine will be featured on the Episodic track list for \"<strong>My Dark Twisted Valentine</strong>\" as well. Visit Gemïny's <a href=\"https://whygeminy.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">website&nbsp;</a>to learn more about the inspiration behind his music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://minimege.com/smokeshow","label":"Listen On All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541113/large-cec5a97811d1f25764c66a6e764d1958.jpg","alt":"Foto 5-6-23 (clean).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541113/preview-0d6307dd3c4edda66de5e5a72adc2e2b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541114/large-ecb2a10fe00dc483d8c3031736cfbad3.jpg","alt":"Foto 5-8-23, 1 41 41 PM.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541114/preview-9621e5ffd6d44ccce74d03356bd5e7ff.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541115/large-e2db772c857075f5508d61311216775b.jpg","alt":"Foto 5-7-23 (grain).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541115/preview-1a887a169fc5e520290ba467b759f1b3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541116/large-60ffbf881be9b41c8ba158ab4ec316ed.png","alt":"Screen Shot 2023-05-04 at 3.05.59 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541116/preview-dc264107acaea35c48babf01d3329da1.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Gemïny:"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from Raleigh, NC, pop-soul artist Sage “Gemïny” Wesley fuses raspy rock and smooth jazz to create a unique sound that keeps audiences grooving. Gemïny studied music composition at the University of South Carolina under Composition Professor <strong>John Fitz</strong>. After a brief hiatus in 2020, Gemïny began participating in freelance work such as recording hooks and background vocals for aspiring artists to raise money for the <strong>National Alliance on Mental Illness (NAMI)</strong>. This charity work grew into booking a few small gigs around Columbia where Gemïny performed backup and keys for various bands. Gemïny's raw vocals and authentic sound make listeners feel like they're in the audience at one of his live shows or alongside him in the recording studio. Connecting lyrical expression to heartbreak, guilt, lost love, and more, Gemïny displays a strong affinity for storytelling with songs reminiscent of a page ripped from a classic love story: a redefined iteration of the <strong>Heartbreak Hotel</strong>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Gemïny!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/minime.ge_/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/sage.wesley.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC0hlC08gTP-NnFY-N-9Zinw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YOUTUBE&nbsp;</a>| <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@code5idkthidman\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"243975","title":"Stone Cottage Studios Presents 2023 Summer Artist Series with Live Performances","date":"2023-05-18","lead":"Stone Cottage Studios kicks off their summer garden concert series in Boulder, CO with May 27th debut performance","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/243975/ac1430f37e3961bff2b0c8de00f8e08d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Stone Cottage Studios kicks off their summer garden concert series in Boulder, CO with May 27th debut performance"},{"t":"p","html":"Boulder, CO (MAY 27, 2023)- <a href=\"https://www.stonecottagestudios.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Stone Cottage Studios</a> presents their Summer 2023 <em>Outdoor Artist Series,</em> featuring live performances from esteemed singer-songwriters in an intimate garden setting. The series begins on Saturday, May 27th and will run until early September. Guests are encouraged to bring drinks, food, blankets and low back chairs for the show. Check out <a href=\"https://www.stonecottagestudios.com/events\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">show information</a> and performer bios below!"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>TIME</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Doors @ 5:30pm | Show begins @ 6:00pm<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<u><strong>LOCATION</strong></u>"},{"t":"p","html":"The Stone Cottage (3091 7th St, Boulder, CO)<br>"},{"t":"table","html":"<table><tbody><tr><td>ARTISTS</td><td>SHOW DATE</td><td>TICKETS</td></tr><tr><td>David Berkeley + Megan Burtt</td><td>Saturday, May 27</td><td><a href=\"https://stonecottagestudios.ticketspice.com/an-evening-with-david-berkeley-and-megan-burtt\" title=\"\" fr-original-style=\"\" style=\"background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none; color: rgb(97, 77, 255); user-select: auto; box-sizing: inherit; outline: none; transition: color 0.4s ease-in-out 0s; cursor: pointer;\">Linked</a></td></tr><tr><td>JoAnna James<br fr-original-style=\"\" style=\"box-sizing: inherit; outline: none;\"></td><td>Saturday, June 17</td><td><a href=\"https://stonecottagestudios.ticketspice.com/stone-cottage-studios-presents-joanna-james\" title=\"\" fr-original-style=\"\" style=\"background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none; color: rgb(97, 77, 255); user-select: auto; box-sizing: inherit; outline: none; transition: color 0.4s ease-in-out 0s; cursor: pointer;\">Linked</a></td></tr><tr><td>The Young Fables</td><td>Saturday, June 23</td><td><a href=\"https://stonecottagestudios.ticketspice.com/an-evening-with-the-young-fables\" title=\"\" fr-original-style=\"\" style=\"background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none; color: rgb(97, 77, 255); user-select: auto; box-sizing: inherit; outline: none; transition: color 0.4s ease-in-out 0s; cursor: pointer;\">Linked</a></td></tr><tr><td>Lauren Frihauf + Laura Cutler</td><td>Saturday, July 1</td><td><a href=\"https://stonecottagestudios.ticketspice.com/stone-cottage-studios-presents-lauren-frihauf\" title=\"\" fr-original-style=\"\" style=\"background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none; color: rgb(97, 77, 255); user-select: auto; box-sizing: inherit; outline: none; transition: color 0.4s ease-in-out 0s; cursor: pointer;\">Linked</a></td></tr><tr><td>Natalie Spears + Gabrielle Louise and Ryan Dilts</td><td>Saturday, July 15</td><td><a href=\"https://stonecottagestudios.ticketspice.com/stone-cottage-studios-presents-an-evening-with-natalie-spears-gabrielle-lo\" title=\"\" fr-original-style=\"\" style=\"background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none; color: rgb(97, 77, 255); user-select: auto; box-sizing: inherit; outline: none; transition: color 0.4s ease-in-out 0s; cursor: pointer;\">Linked</a></td></tr><tr><td>Forest Sun</td><td>Saturday, August 5</td><td><a href=\"https://stonecottagestudios.ticketspice.com/an-evening-with-forest-sun\" title=\"\" fr-original-style=\"\" style=\"background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none; color: rgb(97, 77, 255); user-select: auto; box-sizing: inherit; outline: none; transition: color 0.4s ease-in-out 0s; cursor: pointer;\">Linked</a></td></tr><tr><td>Dave Tamkin + Lucas Wolf</td><td>Saturday, August 25</td><td><a href=\"https://stonecottagestudios.ticketspice.com/an-evening-with-dave-tamkin-and-lucas-wolf\" title=\"\" fr-original-style=\"\" style=\"background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none; color: rgb(97, 77, 255); user-select: auto; box-sizing: inherit; outline: none; transition: color 0.4s ease-in-out 0s; cursor: pointer;\">Linked</a></td></tr><tr><td>Pamela Machala Band</td><td>Saturday, September 9</td><td><a href=\"https://www.stonecottagestudios.com/events\" title=\"\" fr-original-style=\"\" style=\"background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none; color: rgb(97, 77, 255); user-select: auto; box-sizing: inherit; outline: none; transition: color 0.4s ease-in-out 0s; cursor: pointer;\">Linked</a></td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://www.stonecottagestudios.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>STONE COTTAGE STUDIOS</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"Founded and launched in early 2018 in Boulder Colorado, the Stone Cottage Studios is a unique and inspiring Music Discovery space in support and promotion of local and visiting musicians. We are musicians, songwriters, audio engineers and filmmakers. We are passionate about music and the community and provide pro audio recording and cinematic video production in both our authentic, unique and inspirational studio and in our other curated live and live stream event locations. We help Artists bring Music to their Fans and the world and Music Lovers with the Discovery of new Artists.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"In addition to curating live events, we also bring Artists and Fans together Globally through High Definition Live Stream Concerts and also promote Artists through our Studio Artist Sessions. These Sessions are interview based and Artists are able to tell their stories and connect with fans through conversation and their music. We help musicians with marketing and visibility by distributing the Sessions and individual song performances across available media channels. It’s all about capturing musicians at their best and discovery across musical genres!<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"The original cottage was built in the early 1900’s by a local miner and stone mason. We rebuilt the studio in 2012 with Arts and Music in mind and the Stone Cottage Studios was born. The goal was to give rise to a unique, intimate and inspirational space that showcases musicians with high level audio recording and filming. Every aspect in the Studio from the gear and the expertise was assembled to create the very best experience for everyone. With the growth of our Stone Cottage Team and our expansion into the Hybrid Live and Live Stream space, we are more excited than ever to brig our unique experience and intimate stages to the Artists, Fans and the Music Community— all in the Celebration of the Beauty that Music adds to our lives.<br>"},{"t":"lead","html":"ARTIST INFORMATION<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.davidberkeley.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>DAVID BERKELEY</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"David Berkeley’s gift as a songwriter and storyteller is that he sees the tragedy and comedy in life, writing songs capable of both breaking and healing the heart. Berkeley has been called a “musical poet,” by the San Francisco Chronicle, and the New York Times praises his “lustrous, melancholy voice with shades of Tim Buckley and Nick Drake.” That voice and his gift with words is what first sets Berkeley apart from all other guitar-slinging songwriters. But it is his onstage charisma and unparalleled between-song repartee that truly puts him in a class by himself. Each show is completely unique, and David’s humanity shines through every note he sings and every word he speaks. Berkeley has released seven studio albums, one live album, and authored two books, each of which pairs with one of his albums. He was a guest on This American Life, telling an outrageous story of a private serenade he was once hired to perform, and he has won many songwriting awards and honors including ASCAPs Johnny Mercer Songwriting Award.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://www.meganburtt.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>MEGAN BURTT</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"Megan Burtt is an international touring singer/songwriter decorated with national recognition. &nbsp;She is the winner of the Kerrville NewFolk, Rocky Mountain Folk Festival and Westword Music Award and a finalist in MountainNewSong, Songwriter Serenade and Great American Song Contest. In 2010 she released “It Ain’t Love”, a 12-song collection she made with bandmates, among them, Louis Cato (of Jon Batiste and Stay Human, house band for Stephen Colbert, Marcus Miller, Snarky Puppy, and Bobby McFerrin). She worked with the same group for her 2015 release “The Bargain” which charts her recovery from a serious illness with songs that move from darkness to light. In 2013 she released “In Good Company: The Colorado Sessions” a collaborative album of co-writes with Colorado bands including SHEL and Covenhoven. December 2019 marked the 10th year Megan performed throughout the Pennsylvania state maximum security prison system with her band. Megan has toured as a headlining artist, and as support for acts including Gregory Alan Isakov, Marc Cohn, Brett Dennen, Glenn Phillips of Toad The Wet Sprocket, Lissie, Stephen Kellogg and Leanne Rimes. In 2015 she collaborated with the Colorado Symphony Orchestra as a featured artist. Megan is also a member of an Americana-Roots band called \"Gingerbomb\" made up of five redheads.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://joannajamesmusic.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>JOANNA JAMES</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"JoAnna James is a singer and multi-instrumentalist who has been writing, recording and performing for over 20 years. In addition to having released several of her own albums and singles, she has collaborated with Duane Lundy (Ringo Starr, The Lumineers), Jessy Greene (Foo Fighters, Wilco, Pink), Joshua Grange (k.d. lang, Sheryl Crow, Lucinda Williams), and Grammy Award winner Dan Wilson (Adele, Taylor Swift). She continues to produce songs with her long-time writing partner, Alain Whyte (Morrissey) for popular TV shows such as Riverdale and Gossip Girl and has received two consecutive “Female Vocalist of the Year” awards in her home state of Minnesota.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Shortly after relocating to Los Angeles in 2008 where she hit the ground running with musical luminaries, she woke up one morning experiencing a sudden onslaught of debilitating physical symptoms that would eventually be diagnosed as Multiple Sclerosis. After several years of being in and out of hospital rooms, doctors telling her she would never walk again, insurance battles and trying new medicines, she is thriving again and re-entering the music scene with her newest release, Walk With the Night. JoAnna currently resides in Colorado and composes for independent film projects and commercials in addition to working with various songwriters both domestically and internationally. JoAnna has a few more shows planned through the end of the year, including a Minnesota show in May, an October show in Kentucky, California (date TBD), and Arizona (date TBD). Check out JoAnna's website to stay updated on all announcements!"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://www.theyoungfables.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>THE YOUNG FABLES</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"The Young Fables create music with classic storytelling weaved into traditional country roots music with pop sensibilities. East Tennessee (Maryville) natives, Laurel Wright and Wes Lunsford are influenced by timeless treasures like Patsy Cline, Bonnie Raitt, Glen Campbell and Chet Atkins. The duo’s unique sound has resonated with audiences around the globe as live performances have transformed into stages from which The Young Fables (TYF) discuss themes and topics typically saved for the therapy couch. Band manager Patryk Larney admits, ”Witnessing The Young Fables is like watching a tennis match of talent; her voice, his guitar work. ” Larney is not the first to notice the pair’s skillset. The sultry toned vocalist’s first break came when she won the Texaco Country Showdown at 16 years of age - the grand prize awarded her $100K and a performance on the prestigious Ryman Auditorium stage. Wright used the experience as a springboard to expand booking throughout east Tennessee and it wasn’t long before she caught the eye of Gretsch endorsed guitarist Wes Lunsford. The two discovered an instant connection and The Young Fables were born.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Wright and Lunsford joined forces with Music City’s Hope Tree Entertainment and the couple dropped their debut album Two in 2017, followed by Old Songs (a collaboration with GRAMMY® Award-winning producer Mitch Dane) in 2019. Their sound - a whimsical, distinguishable classic country-meets-Americana blend - was praised by iconic artists and taste-makers alike, with Big Machine CEO Scott Borchetta calling Wright’s vocals “flawless,” and nine-time GRAMMY® Award winning artist Sheryl Crow tweeting, “Laurel’s as good as any country singer out there!” Their releases opened the door for a Rolling Stone “10 Best Country and Americana Songs of the Week” nod, direct support for artists like Vince Gill, Amy Grant, Lauren Alaina, Rascal Flatts and Josh Turner, and an invitation from multi-platinum songstress Shania Twain to take part in the CBS showcase celebration Real Country. “Wes is a perfect partner for Laurel’s voice. I fell in love with these guys as a genuine, authentic talent and sound,” mused Twain, and Travis Tritt added, “Our industry needs (TYF) right now!”<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Now, The Young Fables have released their third record Pages (September 2022) and are gearing up for the rental release of their feature documentary 'The Fable of a Song', chronicling a remarkable series of events that rocked TYF in 2018. The story of the tragedies that the band underwent have delivered a notable platform from which the duo speaks to a global audience about depression, loss and resilience. The film, produced by Patryk Larney, has already captured multiple awards, including the 2021 Nashville Film Festival Audience Choice Award. “We didn’t set out to write an album - we just starting writing as a means of release and it happened to resonate with people everywhere,” Wright reveals. “We feel fortunate to have a space to share our music and are so grateful that our story seems to be helping others with their healing. That’s a reward unlike any other.”<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://laurenfrihaufmusic.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>LAUREN FRIHAUF</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"You might recognize Lauren Frihauf from Season 19 of NBC's \"The Voice\", where she made it to the Knockout Rounds on Teams Gwen and Legend, or lately, from her feature in NPR Music's Tiny Desk 'Top Shelf'!Lauren's first original releases are part of a collaboration project, culminating in her debut album, 'The Latona EP'. Her songwriting is intricate, personal, and authentic, and her vocals have been compared to Joni Mitchell, Amy Winehouse, and Madison Cunningham. Lauren's music is indie singer-songwriter with folk and neo-soul elements. The urban vibe of her music is a surprising contrast to the rural farm where Lauren lives and creates. She is currently recording a solo project she can't wait to share with the world!&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://www.annacutlermusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>ANNA CUTLER</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"Anna Cutler is a singer/songwriter and keyboardist based out of Boulder, Colorado. She started playing the keyboard at the age of six, by 13 she had booked her first gig, and by 18 she had performed to a crowd of 3,000 people. Above anything else, Anna is an entertainer. Inspired by other singer-songwriters like Norah Jones and John Craigie, she loves to connect with fans through lyrics and storytelling. She often sings about the romance of life and the downfalls of love, and offers her audience a bit of comic relief in-between songs. She shines brightest when performing live, and captivates the crowd, whatever the size, with her witty charm and truthful portrayal of life. It is not easy to stick Anna into a single genre. Her voice is raspy yet sweet and she writes music as if she were the lovechild of Adele and Regina Spektor; call it Americana/Folk-Pop with ballad undertones if you must.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://nataliespears.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>NATALIE SPEARS</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"Based in the Colorado Rocky Mountains, Natalie Spears brings listeners in touch with the warmth of community, the quiet awe of wild places, and the intimate corners of humanity. Inspired by her father's English Folk heritage and talents as a Jazz pianist, Spears carries a deep love for both porch picking music and music that swings. Drawing on these roots and pulling from a quiver of instruments (banjo, bass, piano, and guitar), her sound is both nostalgic and contemporary, sassy and sweet, contemplative and playful.Born and raised in the heart of Washington DC, Spears took after her father, and began playing piano at age five. By fifth grade she was schlepping an upright bass on the school bus, playing saxophone in a band, and taking drum lessons. Music fell by the wayside after high school but in her early 20’s, Spears stumbled upon American Roots music. While playing bass in an Old-Time string band, she became enamored by the driving rhythm of the clawhammer banjo, and since then, has dedicated herself to learning the instrument and its history. Spears currently performs and tours with her duo project, Lizzy Plotkin &amp; Natalie Spears. In 2021, their debut EP, “Just Over the Ridge,” reached #10 album of the year on the Folk Alliance International Dj Folk Charts and her song, Seasons Change, reached #4 song of the year. She has toured throughout the United States performing at the John Hartford Memorial Festival (Bean Blossom, IN), Blackpot Festival (Lafayette, LA), and Palisade Bluegrass and Roots Festival (Palisade, CO), and has shared the stage with musical greats like Peter Yarrow, the Infamous Stringdusters, Drew Emmit (Left Over Salmon), and Jamestown Revival.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://gabriellelouise.com/gabrielle-with-ryan-dilts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>GABRIELLE LOUISE &amp; RYAN DILTS</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Gabrielle Louise &amp; Ryan Dilts are a pairing of sensitivity and force, performing songs that combine Americana and bluegrass traditions. Gabrielle’s emotive vocal delivery and honed songwriting is elevated by the nuance and precision of Ryan’s agile guitar work. His flatpicking has a crystalline quality that converses with her voice eloquently, subdividing the time to create layered rhythmic interest and weave hypnotic spells. While their material harnesses the authenticity of folk music, it is arranged with a sophistication that aims to honor both of their personal heroes: Joni Mitchell and Tony Rice. Gabrielle joins Ryan in this project on the heels of a long career as a recording artist and touring musician. Known for her authenticity and candor on stage, her performances delight and enchant. After graduating Berklee College of Music in 2007, she crossed the country many times over in a veggie oil powered tour van, released nine records of original work, and has been entrusted to open for greats from Joan Osborn to the late Guy Clark. Career highlights include giving an original TEDx talk on storytelling, taking first place in the Songwriter Serenade Competition, and watching her record \"If the Static Clears\" climb to #6 on the National Roots Music Report for Contemporary Folk Album.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://forestsun.com/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FOREST SUN</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"Forest Sun was born in upstate New York to folksinging back-to-the-land hippie parents. His dad used to chop wood with neighbor Garth Hudson of the Band and literally built the floor that Bob Dylan stood on at manager Albert Grossman’s Bearsville studios in Woodstock, NY. &nbsp;His mom heard Pete Seeger and Joan Baez play when they filmed a TV show in her uncles living room in Boston, and dated one of the Chambers Brothers before she met his dad. &nbsp;Weaned on a diet of Jackson Browne and Toots and the Maytals, some of Forest’s earliest memories are of his dad playing “Poncho and Lefty” by Townes Van Zandt and his mom singing Elizabeth Cotton’s “Freight Train”. Forest wrote songs with Rory Block when he was six years old, learned to juggle with WavyGravy when he was 9, and studied drumming with the late African master percussionist Babatunde Olatunji as a teenager. &nbsp;In college he played in a band with SNL star Maya Rudolph. They opened for No Doubt at the Catalyst in Santa Cruz before Forest left to study art in Spain.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"A pioneer of the DIY movement he recorded his first record in his bedroom in San Francisco with bassist Seth Ford Young (Tom Waits, Edward Sharpe) and toured Europe for the first time, including playing at the Rally on Dam Square in Amsterdam for the Tibetan Freedom Concert where he first met Ben Harper, Alanis Morrisette and Thom Yorke.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"With over 78 million plays on Pandora, troubadour and award-winning songwriter, Forest Sun, enlivens audiences around the globe with his wealth of songs and stories, all sung and told in a laid-back California style. Sun's soulful music draws on a deep well of Americana and is compared to everyone from Jack Johnson and The Avett Brothers to Van Morrison and Bob Dylan. &nbsp;He’s played festivals from California (Strawberry Music Festival, American River Music Festival) to Europe (Belladrum in Scottland, Fiesta City in Belgium),opened for such luminaries as Lyle Lovett, Bonnie Rait, Steve Earle, Keb Mo, and toured with folks like Brett Dennen, Mason Jennings and the Beach Boys (Forest met famed Beach Boys producer Van Dyke Parks at a festival porch jam and later swapped songs on his piano at his house in LA). Musical collaborations on his records include members of Bob Dylans band, members of Calexico/Iron and Wine, Heather Massse(The Wailin' Jennys, Prairie Home Companion) Jolie Holland (The Be Good Tanyas), &nbsp;JT Nero(of Birds of Chicago), Sean Hayes, jam band ALO, and bluegrass band Hot Buttered Rum. His latest album has been featured on Songpickr and Folk Alley playlists and delivers the introspective depth and playful, uplifting, soul-nourishing songwriting fans have come to expect.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://www.davetamkin.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>DAVE TAMKIN</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"Singer/Songwriter, Dave Tamkin, currently resides in Boulder, CO. He has created his own unique style of rhythmic-acoustic sounds that's based around a fresh musical vision. His shows vary from intimate solo acoustic performances to a full band experience (DT&amp;CO.) encapsulating a mixture of personal lyrics and skilled songwriting set against a high-energy percussive backbone.He's shared the stage with Guster, The Samples, Brendan James, Rusted Root, Donavon Frankenreiter, Butch Walker, Freddy Jones Band, Eric Hutchinson, Willy Porter, The Violent Femmes, and Peter Mulvey to name a few. Tamkin has a style that's hard to resist. His lyrics are unabashedly honest and his passion for playing is undying.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT </strong><a href=\"https://lucaswolfmusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>LUCAS WOLF</strong></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"Lucas Wolf is a South Dakota born, Arizona raised singer songwriter currently touring the western region of the United States. He has supported bands such as Robert Randolph and the Family Band, &nbsp;Leftover Salmon, Lion Vibes, Gipsy Moon, Mountain Standard Time and more. &nbsp;He writes heartfelt, thoughtful lyrics and his songs are delivered with passion and sincerity each and every time. Once upon a time he lived as a wandering, hitch-hiking busker playing his music from town to town, never knowing where he would end up next. &nbsp;As time went on, life on a never-ending road lost its allure and he decided to stay put a while and pour himself fully into his music. &nbsp;He is currently working on his second full length record out of Boulder Colorado.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>ABOUT THE </strong><a href=\"https://pamelamachala.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>PAMELA MACHALA</strong></a><strong> BAND</strong>"},{"t":"p","html":"Colorado-based singer, songwriter, and pianist Pamela Machala (“MOCK-uh-luh”) writes \"catchy, heartfelt, thought-provoking songs\" (Westword) with influences ranging from jazz and soul to musical theater and folk. She was awarded the Grand Prize in the 2019 SongDoor International Songwriting Competition, was a 2021 Finalist in the Rocky Mountain Folks Festival Songwriter Showcase, and has opened for icons including Lisa Loeb and Rachel Price. Her all-female band (featuring Adrienne Osborn on bass, JJ Jones on drums, Amanda Morin on guitar, and Kate Farmer on vocals) takes her sound to the next level, reminiscent of 70's favorites like Carole King and James Taylor.<br>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"241823","title":"Karmic Neighborhood to Launch \"Song of Wonder\" Ahead of Feature Film","date":"2023-05-12","lead":"This single is the first in a six-single series leading to the release of the preview soundtrack album for 'Equinox the Musical.'","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/241823/fc0c7a21a6297f26581e603f15d416f0.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This single is the first in a six-single series leading to the release of the preview soundtrack album for 'Equinox the Musical.'"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/02dCSya8eXq3gRfaEeHGK6?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Royal Oaks, CA (May 12, 2023) - <strong>Armand Ruby</strong> and <strong>Julian Colbeck</strong> of <strong>Karmic Neighborhood</strong>&nbsp;just dropped a new alt-pop single,<strong>&nbsp;\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/02dCSya8eXq3gRfaEeHGK6?si=96c57e42ac7545ae\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Song of Wonder</strong></a><strong>,\"</strong> on May 12th, as the initial track showcasing the music from the upcoming feature film, <em><strong>Equinox the Musical</strong></em>. In \"Song of Wonder”, the film’s principal female protagonist, <strong>Katie</strong>, rises up in defiance of her past and present troubles to declare her determination to live life on her own terms, as a force for good in the world.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/SongofWonder","label":"Listen On All Major Streaming Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Equinox the Musical</em> is the story of two young homeless lovers who discover - throughout a tumultuous day - that forgiveness, gratitude, and love can be the keys to surviving even the most chaotic life circumstances. Prior to \"Song of Wonder\" being performed in the musical, the audience has watched flashback scenes from the disturbing events that led to Katie becoming homeless and hospitalized with pneumonia, before being admitted to the relative safety of the homeless shelter. In an earlier scene, Katie learns that her beloved, the young Jason, later in the day will be kicked out of the shelter, throwing their lives into uncertainty and turmoil."},{"t":"p","html":"“Song of Wonder” features the vocals of newcomer <strong>Kristen Trayer</strong>, who channels her inner <strong>Bjork </strong>and <strong>Kate Bush</strong> in her inventive harmonies and vocal delivery. The track was produced by Julian Colbeck and Armand Ruby, composed by Armand Ruby, and arranged by Julian Colbeck, with guitars by <strong>Andrew Synowiec</strong> and keyboards/synths by Julian Colbeck. Colbeck describes the song as <em>\"A hauntingly beautiful kaleidoscope of natural sounds and harmonic vocals that immediately reels the listener in while lingering in the mind.\"</em>"},{"t":"quote","html":"\"This is a song about the resiliency of the human spirit, rising up to overcome adversity.\"","cite":"Armand Ruby, Karmic Neighborhood"},{"t":"button","href":"https://equinoxmusical.com/","label":"Learn more about 'Equinox The Musical'","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/540373/large-5f4099e3ae9a83bd95fd6f98a5b71559.jpg","alt":"AR headshot outdoors 4-13-23 DSC07250.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/540373/preview-83293cadbb6dc2eaab19dc86df1a5ba2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/540375/large-8bb69aae409876a63abcfc0bb6e4f23e.jpg","alt":"Song of Wonder cover art v2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/540375/preview-c44fb783b1446e0319793031ad19ccff.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/540374/large-2a97f0054872c18be826b0cf598a88c5.png","alt":"Kristen w-headphones - photo from Julian 2021.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/540374/preview-7a04733d9609965a4b70e11cafcb48d0.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Karmic Neighborhood:"},{"t":"p","html":"The west coast-based team are strangers-turned-neighbors, turned rhythmic alt-pop collaborators. Armand Ruby and Julian Colbeck are two life-long musicians in their 60's who met by chance when they moved to the same neighborhood on the central California coast. Julian was formerly a London-based rock star and lifelong music industry veteran, while Armand was professionally an environmental scientist who stayed involved in music as a part-time musician and songwriter. Armand and Julian formed a strong bond through their shared passion for music and the painful yet hopeful life experience of surviving cancer. The two found inspiration within the harmony of their own respective life journeys, and a mutual interest in musical innovation.<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vnYPcPpvzO0hhjR6YMUkV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Armand Ruby:"},{"t":"p","html":"Armand spent most of his childhood in the northeastern US, during which he discovered two of his main passions: science and music. Although he dreamed of pursuing a career in music, Armand accepted an Ivy-League scholarship out of high school and went on to become an environmental scientist. Over the course of his university studies, throughout marriage and children and his science career, Armand continued to tap into his musical talent by songwriting, performing in bands, recording demos, and in many other ways. Armand also channeled his songwriting abilities through the creation of a musical play, <strong><em>Equinox The Musical</em></strong>, which he presented to audience acclaim in 2011. After surviving a prostate cancer scare and difficult separation from his partner, Armand moved to the rural Monterey Bay area community of Royal Oaks in 2019. There he discovered that one of his neighbors, Julian Colbeck, was an experienced music arranger, producer and keyboardist. The pair recorded a preview soundtrack of the songs from <em>Equinox the Musical</em> and collaborated on production of a short musical film, “<strong>I Said I Will</strong>.\" The award-winning film featured the original version of “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/09L2h21DyZ4ZRNnZSLIXx9?si=20f5983a18554d67\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Don’t Want to Walk Away</strong></a>,” produced by Armand Ruby and Julian Colbeck, with final mix by <strong>Alan Parsons</strong>. Karmic Neighborhood's new single from <em>Equinox the Musical,</em> \"<strong>Song of Wonder</strong>\" will be available on all streaming platforms May 12."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Julian Colbeck:"},{"t":"p","html":"Julian Colbeck grew up in the south of England, where he learned how to play the piano and ultimately pursued his dreams of being in a London-based rock ‘n’ roll band in his late teens. Julian’s music career took off with the band <em><strong>Charlie</strong></em>, with whom he scored several US Top 40 singles including “<strong>Watching TV</strong>” and “<strong>LA Dreamer</strong>.\" Over the span of a 40-year career, Julian worked and toured as a keyboard player/producer with Yes alumni group <strong>Anderson Bruford Wakeman Howe</strong>, former Genesis guitarist <strong>Steve Hackett</strong>, <strong>Charlie</strong>, <strong>John Miles</strong>, and more. In 2008 Julian began work with his long-time friend, <strong>Alan Parsons</strong>, on the award-winning instructional video series: Alan Parsons’ The Art &amp; Science Of Sound Recording. Julian also has written for many esteemed music industry publications, and has authored many music and music technology books. Beginning in late 2019, and interrupted by intensive treatment for stage 4 cancer, Julian saw something of value in his neighbor Armand Ruby’s songwriting and his <em>Equinox&nbsp;</em>film project, and worked as arranger, co-producer and keyboardist on the Equinox preview soundtrack recordings. Armand and Julian's collaboration on this work led to the production of their recent release, the radio remix of “I Don’t Want to Walk Away.\" Karmic Neighborhood's new single from <em>Equinox the Musical,</em> \"<strong>Song of Wonder</strong>\" will be available on all streaming platforms May 12."},{"t":"h3","html":"CONNECT WITH KARMIC NEIGHBORHOOD!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100082755791779\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | <a href=\"mailto:armand@armandrubymusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EMAIL</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"242714","title":"Home page of Mayday 13","date":"2023-05-12","lead":"Alternative pop artist Mayday 13 is making his mark on the music industry with the release of his 9-track album.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/242714/5cfbef1116cf05009ea83ddcb0f4ea23.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Alternative pop artist Mayday 13 is making his mark on the music industry with the release of his 9-track album."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1AmtMODGpRwCLQumecyqpx?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Mount Ephraim, NJ (May 12, 2023) - Independent alt-pop artist <strong>Mayday 13</strong>&nbsp;dropped his debut record \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1AmtMODGpRwCLQumecyqpx?si=sa_pfmdiQVeHF3TZf2JstA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Dreaming Is Easy</strong></em></a>\" on Friday, May 12. This launch marks the official debut of Mayday 13's career in the music industry. The <strong>9-track album</strong> has a somber overtone that evokes deep introspection while it touches upon emotions associated with relationships. Although many of the songs on this record follow a gloomy tone, the messages within Mayday 13's lyrics point to the uplifting conclusion that there is hope for redemption in any situation.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Dreaming Is Easy\" is about never losing sight of the dreams you once held close to your heart. Whether these \"dreams\" are related to keeping a relationship together or feeling supported by people who surround you, Mayday 13 highlights the hardships we experience in life. The struggle of feeling seen and understood is explored within track 3 of the album \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2UfzSEGDNvpI5zdF5lmyPI?si=dae6c05e6aca4604\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Spirits</strong></a>,\" which includes the lines: <em>I want to find a place where I belong A place for me that I can call my own I hope to God that I am not alone I want to find a place where I belong.</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Mayday 13 pushed the boundaries of his artistry by creating this album entirely solo. He played and recorded the various instruments featured on each track, wrote his own lyrics, and produced the entire project once it was ready for completion. Mayday 13 created a cohesive sound to the album by integrating dreamy background instrumentals that flow in and out of each song. The storytelling element of this release was the most important to the artist, as his goal was to create something unique that reflected his style and mood.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541988/large-d1c1f83ff658e6e1e8db07f01c6fa69e.jpg","alt":"7J0A4161.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541988/preview-3c6c6e95a571c268632adfe56ebfcb3c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541989/large-60910077dbd11f9ab1ae94043461884c.jpg","alt":"7J0A4174.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541989/preview-e222e78635cf3e15d218565289d4a138.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541990/large-8ff907654ccabbd94f41cce2a6383d15.jpg","alt":"7J0A4100.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541990/preview-abce6e7b3fe61989db27037149f07937.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541991/large-5a53e02cca46305979e9b085be421278.jpg","alt":"7J0A4091.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541991/preview-fa8dc517af2365c364e1ac549fbfea11.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<em>The week of the release, $1 of every album sold will go to benefit Families with Children battling Osteosarcoma with <a href=\"https://www.mibagents.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MIBagents.org</a>.</em><em>&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/541986/compressed_original-f7f067ff098876277f51d3ee077599b4.png","alt":"\"Dreaming Is Easy\" Album Cover"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Mayday 13:"},{"t":"p","html":"New Jersey-based alternative musician Mayday 13, the solo project of <strong>Brian Hadley</strong>, emerged in late 2022. Having spent the last ten-plus years in the thriving Philadelphia cover gig scene, Brian has always stayed connected to the vast universe of original music. Pulling inspiration from the likes of <strong>David Bowie</strong>, <strong>Band of Horses</strong>, <strong>Radiohead</strong>, <strong>M83 </strong>and <strong>Manchester Orchestra</strong>, Mayday 13 will release its first 9-track album on May 12, 2023. For the latest announcements and release updates, make sure to check out <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/_mayday13/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>@_mayday13</em></strong></a> on Instagram."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Mayday 13!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://mayday13.com/","img":"","title":"Home page of Mayday 13","desc":""},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/_mayday13/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/themayday13/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"242993","title":"Indie Folk Artist Madison McCreary Releases Album 'Time + Tide'","date":"2023-05-11","lead":"The recently released album explores themes of growing pains, change, love, and more","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/242993/cac442af70a99dd1941163633354b61d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The recently released album explores themes of growing pains, change, love, and more"},{"t":"p","html":"Kona, HAWAI'I (April 30, 2023) - Alternative folk artist Madison McCreary recently launched her 9-track album \"Time and Tide\". The album was officially dropped on April 30th and is now available on all streaming platforms. The record touches upon themes of dating, friendships, restlessness, and the complicated emotions that arise while being home for the holidays. A misty, nostalgic tone fuses with story-driven lyrics and female-powered harmonies to create the dreamy release that is \"Time and Tide\"."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542461/large-c4ba97565d6575643f714797a4b17235.jpg","alt":"large-Madison in the grass_-25.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542461/preview-a06483b66be846e3b1f4ffa6d28035fa.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542460/large-d6feefc161e0301385115c4fa8ee15ce.jpg","alt":"large-Madison in the grass_-15.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542460/preview-51994626590bb26c20a0f525f353d458.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542459/large-2b05f999a94bc870de783b4c33f54852.jpg","alt":"large-Madison in the grass_-42.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/542459/preview-6f7c6ae8b99e9cdc20ab475323732678.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"Photo Credit: Lia-Lucine Cary&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Each track on the album is either named after a month or has a month hidden in its meaning or lyrics, reiterating the theme of time. McCreary's lyrics ebb and flow through phases of growth in her life and the lives of her loved ones. Crisp harmonies and smooth rhythms play into elements of beauty and nature, representing time and gravity affecting the tides of life. The opening track \"January\" considers the fear and risk associated with being vulnerable and diving into something new - whether it be a new year, a new relationship, or a new job. The record is concluded with track 9, \"December,\" which warmly embraces the listener in the sentiment: home is not a place, it is the people we love. The album's instrumentation floats from being homey and grounded to being fairy-like and light, embodying different stages of childhood and &nbsp;growing pains."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2ZhKMdRGJshwtuodkpA2jw?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Time + Tide is a window into my head and heart. It moves through the months of the year, capturing the tension between the desire to stay rooted and roam free. I hope my music creates the same nostalgic feeling as rediscovering an old folded-up note in your back pocket.\"","cite":"Madison McCreary, Indie-Folk Artist"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong><u>Album Collaborators</u></strong><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Emily Wills (backup vocals, fiddle, guitar, mandolin, piano); Chris Joslin (banjo, mandolin, dobro, guitar); Hadley Rouse (backup vocals); Matthew Wills (percussion, bass)</em><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Madison McCreary"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from Kona, Hawai'i, Madison McCreary has been writing songs for as long as she can remember. Madison grew up on a dairy farm in western Kentucky and has now lived in Hawai'i for the past 6 years. Both Kentucky and Hawai'i have largely influenced Madison's style of music (banjo and ukulele, mandolin and ocean sounds). She has performed in small folk /bluegrass shows across KY alongside her childhood best friends, Emily Wills and Hadley Rouse. Madison's music has been a highly personal endeavor for her up until now. The release of her debut album, \"Time + Tide\" is the first time she has shared her music with the world. Follow Madison McCreary on social media to stay updated on what she's got coming up next!&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Madison!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/madison.mccreary.stuart/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@madison.mccreary.stuart","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"240905","title":"Cliffs + Caves Release New Single, \"Eso Si Que Es\" Ahead of May EP Launch","date":"2023-05-05","lead":"Houston-based mother-daughter folk duo releases new soulfully inspiring single.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/240905/dcef9cf73ce13c12b92aebea558248c8.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Houston-based mother-daughter folk duo releases new soulfully inspiring single.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3iN0ly4z70yeF94lHzXPkG?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston, TX (MAY 5, 2023) - Mother-Daughter duo <strong>Cliffs + Caves</strong> create inspirational music with a balance of folky, acoustic sounds. In their new single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3cym3ovnWEHlov6VfmE9Xu?si=jX_dKTe3QiSHOimHHTlB1g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Eso Si Que Es</strong></em></a>,\" they explore notes of Ben Howard-inspired fingerstyle guitar and delicate layering of powerful harmonies, proving their flexibility as artists and exploratory spirit when it comes to creating new music. This track includes emotionally charged themes such as loss, love, grief, heartache, empathy for loved ones, and more.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The artists describe the aura of this song as soothing and calming. Continuing on about the meaning of this single, Lindsey Justice of Cliffs + Caves remarks,<em>“It’s about letting yourself experience the fullness of whatever life has - whether it’s wonderful or heartbreaking, or both simultaneously.”</em> The song's title is a play on the famous saying <em>“It is what it is,”</em> but with a more hopeful overtone to the sentiment. The lyrics and rhythms of this track convey all of the complex emotions we undergo, and how life itself \"is what it is,\" in a more optimistic light. The song takes inspiration from famous singer-songwriters like <strong>Damien Rice</strong>, <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, and <strong>Noah Gundersen</strong>."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/EsoSiQueEs","label":"Listen On All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1J0Q7piRpWRQHW9IegFT4X?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Both this new release and the upcoming EP were inspired by some time the duo spent in Jackson Hole and the Grand Tetons last year soaking up the snow, wildlife, and magic of the mountains. On the way back from the trip, Lindsey received a call relaying that her dear friend was back in the hospital for a difficult cancer treatment. This devastating news was the inspiration for the first few lines of the song, <em>“Life is full of magic things mixed between tragedies. Love is every hug hello and I told you so. I wish I’d known how fast it goes. If we don’t break we must bend at the weight of the world. Just breathe.”</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"Claire and Lindsey wrote the lyrics to this Eso Si Que Es a few weeks later, reflecting on the ambivalence of life's tragedies and magic moments that form the human experience. This new track acts as a reminder to appreciate moments shared with the people you love, because time itself is one of the most valuable things we have.<br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/539003/large-173f83c9f01d74b944bbd163dd99be13.jpeg","alt":"BA231082-93FA-4F44-B307-F4788DF9CCEE.jpeg"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Cliffs + Caves:"},{"t":"p","html":"Cliffs + Caves, the mother-daughter duo of Lindsey and Claire Justice, unabashedly share their deeply personal and relatable stories through songs that resonate with listeners of all generations. Best known in their home state of Texas for their unique blend of Contemporary Americana music, the pair showcases the musical ingenuity that is created when artistry runs in the family with intimate lyrics lilting intrinsically over smooth musical progressions. Their previous discography includes their 2017 debut EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3SanUmvSOsrCrv1A4NlXZ2?si=nzqjn0iqSQOKnlxOcWf5yA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Hold On</strong></a> (recorded with Grammy-nominated producer <strong>Jamie Candiloro</strong> (<strong>Ryan Adams</strong>, <strong>R.E.M.</strong>, <strong>The Eagles</strong>) and featuring performances by legendary <strong>Willie Nelson</strong>’s harmonica player, <strong>Mickey Raphael</strong>) and sophomore EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4gEhBjWLd5a66JwQRENwNs?si=29JFfKxoSCqgPHKkQN5n0Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Capsize</strong></a> (produced by <strong>Chris Jacobie</strong> (<strong>Penny</strong><strong>&nbsp;and Sparrow</strong>, <strong>Jarrod Dickenson</strong>, <strong>Duncan Fellows</strong>). The original songs are a team effort with the duo individually contributing to the mastery of their lyrics and melodies. Moreover, twenty-year-old Claire being a multi-instrumentalist, not only composes the music for the tracks but also bestows a knack for songwriting. Their newer music further explores the duo's ability to portray life through lyrics as they evolve into a more alternative Maggie-Rogers-esque sound while still maintaining their Americana roots and drawing inspiration from benchmark artists like Phoebe Bridgers, <strong>Lake Street Dive</strong>, and <strong>Patty Griffin</strong>. Cliffs + Caves is thrilled to be releasing a preview single \"Eso Si Que Es\" on May 5th, ahead of their album launch at the end of May!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Cliffs + Caves!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/cliffs_and_caves/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM&nbsp;</a>| <a href=\"https://cliffsandcaves.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">WEBSITE</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/cliffsandcaves\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCx_Hx-JPyBxN0j_nRro8vig\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YOUTUBE </a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"239521","title":"Loose Bolts Announces New Track \"Could I Stay Here?\" Releasing May 24","date":"2023-05-02","lead":"Loose Bolts drops dreamy alt-rock single ahead of Fall 2023 EP release","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/239521/35d2170d5aad9ef48e6d2dcc0c7bc85b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Loose Bolts drops dreamy alt-rock single ahead of Fall 2023 EP release"},{"t":"p","html":"Nashville, TN (May 24, 2023) - Rising Indie Pop artist Loose Bolts is releasing a new track, \"Could I Stay Here?\" on May 24th. The track was written from a place of nostalgia and reflection on the state of mind he would find himself in as an inexperienced young man, dipping his toes into the world of romance. This track is the first \"act\" in Loose Bolts' upcoming Fall 2023 EP, \"Temerity.\" Temerity will serve as a deep dive into his formative emotional struggles as he discovers how naive and flawed his perspective once was, ultimately leading to revelations in the areas of self-awareness, and the importance of taking risks in life.<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>\"Could I Stay Here?\" is meant to soundtrack a \"first love\" story, where every experience feels simultaneously indulgent and addicting. The artist explains that the 1st verse of this song references his tendencies to be overzealous and allow anxiety to get the best of him (in an endearing but unknowingly toxic way). This is emphasized by the 2nd verse and bridge, both referencing the grandiose nature of a first love/relationship and how it can be all-consuming yet electrifying. The tune is a bittersweet reminiscence of the past and is reinforced by an instrumental that echoes classic 2000's Indie/Emo sounds from iconic groups such as The Strokes &amp; Dashboard Confessional, combined with the faded splendor of bands like The 1975 or The Cure.<br id=\"isPasted\"><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">Loose Bolts layers sonic elements such as guitar, bass, drums, synthesizers, and vibraphone to create an airy, crunchy groove that carries the track. This evolves into a whirling, shoegaze-inspired staccato explosion. That is, until the very end, where it’s just him and his acoustic guitar, suggesting to the listener that this beautiful experience may have just been a farce after all. In the words of the singer, \"It's a perfect track for your daily run, a drive to the beach, or a skate to the dispensary.\"&nbsp;<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>This catchy and captivating opening track is an ode to his former misconceptions of life and love; All of the excitement, the insecurities, the misdirected passion, and most importantly, the earnestness of it all. If the wide-eyed, unbridled version of your younger self dealt with social anxiety and a lot of rejection, you might find the sentiments displayed pretty relatable."},{"t":"p","html":"Stay tuned for the cheeky, yet endearing music video for \"Could I Stay Here?\", releasing June 22nd (Directed by Gavin Hulburt of Nashville Indie band Drive! Drive!)<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/loosebolts4real/loose-bolts-could-i-stay-here-indie-pop-rock-single-2022/s-8epxV12eTt6?si=27018a0619454174b96a08adb1c15a98&amp;utm_source=clipboard&amp;utm_medium=text&amp;utm_campaign=social_sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PRIVATE LISTENING LINK</a><br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6bEGHauD5q2kivJyVYNIf3?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Loose Bolts:"},{"t":"p","html":"Resembling a similar creative situation such as Tame Impala or Prince, Loose Bolts is the solo outlet of songwriter, producer, and multi-instrumentalist Ian Brice. What started in 2015 as a Florida-based, heavily Folk Punk-influenced side project to a Blackened Death Metal outfit, has blossomed into a Nashville-based one-stop shop for all your Indie/Pop/Rock cravings (and those are just the main umbrellas). Whether we’re talking about artists such as Julian Casablancas, Patrick Stump, or Dashboard Confessional, Loose Bolts fits almost squarely into the vast and colorful lineage of solo (and sometimes not so much) musical visionaries that have made their impact over the last 2 decades. 2023 marks a new era for Loose Bolts with the newest single release “Could I Stay Here?\" available May 24th wherever you discover fresh, new music. Keep an eye out for updates regarding Loose Bolts' upcoming EP, \"Temerity,\" to be release this Fall!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Loose Bolts!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@looseboltsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;|</strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/looseboltsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>INSTAG</strong><strong>RAM</strong></a><strong> |<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/looseboltsmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> FACEBOOK</a> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/LooseBolts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YOUTUBE</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"238143","title":"Nelleke Releases New Track 'Send The Rain' Ahead of Full EP","date":"2023-04-28","lead":"'Send The Rain' gives listeners a taste of what's to come from Nelleke's upcoming EP release: bird /on concrete","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/238143/a93518273fd7903a60613fa2932d0c0c.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"'Send The Rain' gives listeners a taste of what's to come from Nelleke's upcoming EP release: bird /on concrete"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0N5x6Zgy5hKXbsKLOfpYY5?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Rotterdam, NETHERLANDS (April 28, 2023) - Netherlands Indie-Folk artist<strong>&nbsp;Nelleke</strong> is releasing her new single '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0N5x6Zgy5hKXbsKLOfpYY5?si=0c30454b500546e9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Send The Rain</strong></a>,' which is part of her full EP slated to launch in early September. The track was written as a fictional confrontation with a person. One of the questions Nelleke asked herself while writing the lyrics was, <em>\"What would I say to someone who has hurt me?\"</em> The song expresses a cry for clarity and starting over. Within the melancholy verses, the artist yearns to be able to see the world through rose-colored glasses once again. The track ends on an optimistic note, creating a perspective that embraces the romanticism within this life. Nelleke reflects on her work and states that, <em>\"The end of 'Send The Rain' is a celebration of messiness.\"</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0gMqIo1XytRF3KiK8O2NUu?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"The beginning of this single comes off as a folk-based acoustic guitar song, mainly focused on sentiment of the words, reflecting a poem-like structure. Nelleke summons conflicting feelings with a driven acoustic guitar and echoey voices in the distance. The singer expresses a feeling of weightlessness while her and the other character in the song dive into the water. To end the narrative created within the sing, Nelleke included synthesized rhythms to represent celebration and an upbeat tone.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"Send The Rain is the climax moment of my upcoming EP, and the song that represents duality in its purest form,\" </em>says Nelleke, <em>\"The vocal expression in the song is raw and gut-wrenching, emphasizing the emotions associated with frustration and struggle.\"</em> Nelleke wants her listeners to see this new single as the perfect introduction to her debut EP, '<strong>bird /on concrete</strong>,' which will release in September of this year. The EP features themes of duality: calmness versus anger, masculinity versus femininity, and more."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/1362916231%3Fsecret_token%3Ds-EttnnihXFBF&color=%23bcecbc&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false&show_teaser=true&visual=true","height":"300"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/532521/large-4c9c3c0dc4beb9bbc05f56d441ee82ad.png","alt":"SELECTED DESIGN (2).png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/532521/preview-f076f3be0d200eb8382b76e9be93a613.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/532522/large-1e31829979684af1077d5131f2315d01.jpg","alt":"25022023--8.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/532522/preview-9679d58ee81cd4f7a1b41de19ad15fcf.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/532523/large-10fcc6f804ce12d3219197a841660b56.jpg","alt":"25022023--11.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/532523/preview-6392cb23932603feb9995aec0cfb51f1.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Nelleke:"},{"t":"p","html":"Nelleke is a singer, songwriter and producer from a small town in The Netherlands. At an early age, Nelleke was inspired by well-known singers like <strong>Joni Mitchell</strong>, <strong>Sting</strong>, <strong>Bonnie Raitt </strong>and <strong>Bon Iver</strong>, ultimately propelling her to pursue a career in music. Nelleke studied musical theatre at Codarts University of the Arts in Rotterdam, Netherlands. After graduating from university, Nelleke landed a role at '<strong>Soldaat van Oranje</strong>' (one of the most renowned musicals in The Netherlands) and continued to pour her passion into musical theater. It wasn't until early 2020 when Nelleke decided to accept a residency at the Banff Centre for Arts and Creativity, leaving theatre behind to pursue her solo career as a singer-songwriter. Nelleke recently graduated from Berklee College of Music, where she worked alongside professional sound engineers and creatives to produce her debut EP ''bird /on concrete'' (releasing early September 2023). The project organically attracted a team of producers, engineers and creatives around her, who helped her create this body of work. Nelleke's music can best be described as contemporary romanticism, featuring themes related to nature, relationships and womanhood. Her music oscillates between Alternative Pop and Indie-Folk and she is always discovering new realms of musical expression."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Nelleke!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/nelleke_music/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM</strong></a> |<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/nelleke.music/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>FACEBOOK</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"239522","title":"R&B Artist x Reiki Healer Brandon Vee Releases Therapeutic Album \"Revolution Of The Soul\"","date":"2023-04-28","lead":"Soulful Hip-Hop Artist Brandon Vee shares inspirational new music that taps into human connection.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/239522/0cd70fd1a4fa3643db66745e9938e98a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Soulful Hip-Hop Artist Brandon Vee shares inspirational new music that taps into human connection."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4SrmEBuPAHhQFKZi6cB7xF?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Orlando, FL (April 28, 2023) - At the crossroads of Hip-Hop and Funk is where we find emerging singer-songwriter <strong>Brandon Vee</strong> and his new album, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4SrmEBuPAHhQFKZi6cB7xF?si=ra-ALi7FTXWtWB97ScixKA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Revolution Of The Soul</strong></em></a>.\" This 7-track project reinforces themes of self-love, internal conflict, mental health, and the challenges that comes along with facing these subjects. The word \"revolution\" refers to the never-ending change occurring all around us and inside our souls as human beings. Through this new music, Brandon aims to highlight that revolutions and love are similar, both at times seeming like an uphill battle filled with frustration and yearning for light."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/723ARnLLkvF9V7RRzHQrEM?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"quote","html":"“A revolution can be translated to feel like war occurring within our hearts and souls... Healing isn't linear and turmoil is inevitable on the path to light, but what matters most is embracing the walls one has to climb to escape from the darkness.\"","cite":"- Brandon Vee"},{"t":"p","html":"Brandon is a mental health advocate and a certified Reiki Healer, investing time and passion into his body, soul, music, and the environment. After battling depression for several years and eventually overcoming it, Brandon has shifted his focus to self-love and healthy habits that both energize and inspire him to create therapeutic music. Brandon's songs are intended to encourage listeners to believe in themselves through positive yet empathetic messaging. \"Revolution Of The Soul\" acts as a reminder that we all contain the internal power to create beauty from what life has given us, even in the darkest of times."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534737/original-6f7aae371992ac32f546c1a7f5720a7d.jpeg","alt":"E52F7A32-22A2-40EF-8BF0-CB5EA49F5964.JPEG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534737/original-6f7aae371992ac32f546c1a7f5720a7d.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534738/original-ab4fad86355217ae4ff7ec0c89f68e37.jpg","alt":"IMG_1961.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534738/original-ab4fad86355217ae4ff7ec0c89f68e37.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534740/large-dfcccc4e76a1d42b1fcaf0d7e635c8ac.jpg","alt":"IMG_1905.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534740/preview-41ffa0af96b4720a8526c869b603b06e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534739/large-0728b8d3e7dd6d6442b8dcbb8ba492e9.jpg","alt":"IMG_1163.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534739/preview-cb0c4dd6cbf9f6e3d75ba296123e6b34.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534741/large-6d8c6c80e0e96f7ab40ffc2e9bec6975.jpg","alt":"vee 5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534741/preview-a0d18ea79fb8f5ea233ca68734ea42ec.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Check out the official video for Brandon Vee's 2020 hit single<strong>&nbsp;\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/42jnMpME6NIchyCozX33Ai?si=5d60b7e7a61b4dc7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Java Love</strong></a>\" below:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/vDBM3QXUUlc","height":"315"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brandon Vee:"},{"t":"p","html":"Brooklyn, NY native Brandon Vee fuses the energy of hip-hop with the classic melodies of R&amp;B and Jazz to create a funk-inspired aura and sound. Brandon started his lyrical journey at the young age of 10 when he started writing poetry to express complex feelings of heaviness and discomfort. Brandon continues to use music as a medium of self-discovery and healing intertwining the boundaries of his own worldly perspectives with personal growth. Brandon Vee creates a unique and powerful sound with his music, carrying listeners through storylines of spirituality, introspection, and self-discovery. Vee draws inspiration from diverse yet legendary artists such as <strong>J. Cole</strong>, <strong>Childish Gambino</strong>, and <strong>Funkadelic</strong>. In 2022, Brandon Vee performed alongside famous artists such as <strong>Meg The Stallion</strong>, <strong>Denzel Curry</strong>, <strong>EarthGang</strong>, and more, inspiring him to showcase his new music on a live platform more often. Brandon is dedicated to themes of challenge and healing within his newest album, \"Revolution Of The Soul\" which released on April 28th, 2023."},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://Brandon Vee Shopify\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Brandon Vee Shopify</strong></a>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Brandon Vee!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://Youtube.com/user/brandonveemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>YOUTUBE</strong></a><strong> |&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://Instagram.com/thatmanvee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM</strong></a> | <a href=\"https://www.thatmamvee.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>WEBSITE</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"237499","title":"The Trouble Notes Release Psychedelic Rock-Infused Single \"Turkish Delight\"","date":"2023-04-21","lead":"The Trouble Notes Fuse 1970's Latin Cumbia, Indie-Rock, and Turkish Funk to Explore Unique Sound.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/237499/61d479b67bcdabf96464dde0961897d5.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Trouble Notes Fuse 1970's Latin Cumbia, Indie-Rock, and Turkish Funk to Explore Unique Sound."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/72iPz7LyR4Yhzg0YZgNnkP?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Berlin, GERMANY (April 21, 2023) - Inspired by the popular Turkish Psychedelic Rock and Latin Cumbia tunes from the 1970’s, <a href=\"https://thetroublenotes.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Trouble Notes</strong></a> announce the release of their new single, <em>\"</em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/72iPz7LyR4Yhzg0YZgNnkP?si=eceacd85f3b04bca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Turkish Delight</strong></em></a><em>.\"</em> This single departs from the group's usual string-dominant overtone and leans into new sonic elements such as electric guitar. The Trouble Notes support a funk-rock aura in this track with groovy bass lines and Turkish funk-inspired violin. This rhythmic song is a playful reminder of the group’s worldly musical influences, making a point to bind various transcontinental rhythms and melodies."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/vMMzFfsnWFw","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"<em>\"We spend a lot of time in the van while on tour, and that means we are frequently listening to music,\"</em> says Violinist <strong>Bennet Cerven</strong> from <em>The Trouble Notes</em>. During their most recent tour, TTN was inspired by newfound genres such as 1970's Latin Cumbia, Asian Psychedelic, and Middle Eastern Funk. The Trouble Notes have expressed that <em>Turkish Delight</em> was created as an ode to these under-appreciated sounds that deserve to be celebrated. Emphasizing the experimental nature of their new single, Cerven additionally notes, <em>\"... it was a fun excuse for me to play some bass!\"</em>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531578/large-1268510ef7a782e25cd98bd7ef876be4.jpg","alt":"Turkish Delight_Video Shoot_(c) Stefanie Tendler (42).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531578/preview-c900eb1b0b9f5c2f93ca720553231340.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531580/large-aa72f5f4bbc1040b00e13da04cdc762e.jpg","alt":"Turkish Delight_Video Shoot_(c) Stefanie Tendler (32).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531580/preview-efa62b1bfcce8547717dfcb56b0d8d9a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531582/large-9baf61fd4a3f59820fda891f68ccf070.png","alt":"The Trouble Notes - Turkish Delight Single Artwork.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531582/preview-b616816ea53c1b58940854f66b425903.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Trouble Notes:"},{"t":"p","html":"Sitting somewhere between traditional folk, modern classical, and tribal dance music, The Trouble Notes have traveled their way across continents in search of musical influences. The band has proudly built its multifarious audience independently – known colloquially as <strong>“The Troublemakers”</strong>- a testament to their self-made success story that has led to major festival appearances, multiple film scores and an extensive tour schedule spanning the globe. The core of the band consists of violinist Bennet Cerven, guitarist <strong>Florian Eisenschmidt</strong>, vocalist/percussionist <strong>Carola Zerega</strong> and percussionist <strong>Julian Lardis</strong>. In 2017 a series of videos of the band performing on the streets in France and Germany went certified viral, amassing more than 100 million views on social media and bringing them international notoriety. They recorded their debut album <strong>'</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7jcL8aABNKpyueaH9wHBzM?si=HT138IUYRoirX0jdtuVZ1A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Lose Your Ties</strong></a><strong>'</strong> at Riverside Studios in Berlin, Germany working with Lebanese producer <strong>Khalil Chahine</strong>. Worldly percussion rhythms transport the audience across genre with an uplifting spirit for which The Trouble Notes have become world renown. Their show \"<strong>More Violins, Less Violence</strong>\" is packed with songs from their 2nd Studio album '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1Cq3yTrY1ltI1XC1egbwMf?si=M2i_tO5LRF2jfMr0I6P4Ew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Liberty Awaits</strong></a>.' Their repertoire brings the traditions of Europe and the Americas together and carries a message of Unity in Diversity.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With The Trouble Notes!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7i1WiSQVIHt4bZz8DhuylF?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@thetroublenotesofficial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ChrisBloommusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"></a><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheTroubleNotes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/thetroublenotes/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"237871","title":"Yew Haiku Announces Launch of New Pop-Synth Album, \"Century Gothic\"","date":"2023-04-21","lead":"This dark and dreamy album explores technology-related modern dating downfalls, feeling disconnected from a social sphere, and more.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/237871/e41c5eafe225dfc21ad9135832684965.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"This dark and dreamy album explores technology-related modern dating downfalls, feeling disconnected from a social sphere, and more."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5xa3AWVhLeF9R65ZGox57o?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Nashville, TENNESSEE (April 21, 2023) - Gothic Pop-Synth musical artist, <strong>Yew Haiku</strong>, is releasing her new album <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5xa3AWVhLeF9R65ZGox57o?si=YqDrcDnfSnOhpjU7dkf9Ig\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>Century Gothic</em></strong></a> at the end of April 2023. This 5-song album contains themes of modern dating downfalls, how technology has changed emotional connection, fear of economic collapse, feeling largely disconnected from a peer group while trying to fit into one, and more. The lyrically dreamy album contains a tinge of darkness from time to time, with lyrics such as, <em>\"An endless dream became a nightmare...\"</em> from the track<em>&nbsp;</em><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/712odL4XfL1tzOhi2Vj5Ln?si=a67ff0e5c4ec4187\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Real Eyes Realize Real Lies</strong></em></a>. Yew Haiku expresses that this album was inspired by, <em>\"visions of unnecessary technological expanse encroaching upon human nature and psychological faculties,\"</em> and wanting to ​make time stand still by capturing this notion within the music.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\">"},{"t":"p","html":"This album consistently oscillates between sentiments of mourning and acceptance. One of the songs on the album, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3MNsYsjhNmHmpjcYVkjgil?si=a3630df5e310431f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Dream Sequence</strong></em></a>, was written in an attempt to harness the meditative potential of sound design. Another track, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1Vyr0BTrYMoKy5MlgtpZZK?si=312246988a1548e6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Peach Nietzsche</strong></em></a>, is about navigating the presence of despair creeping into what seems like an ideal life situation. The album's second track&nbsp;<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3atWrijFeRE5odIsTHfVwe?si=a9c0d611eb974b07\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Experience or Turing</strong></em></a><em>&nbsp;</em>is meant to portray the story of hypothetically receiving a sentimental letter from a \"perfectly curated\" AI love interest. The dialogue of the song consists of the AI lover warning the infatuated girl to stay away from him, although she thinks she loves him. The other tracks on the album transcend from fantasy and touch back to earth by tapping into more traditional themes such as unrequited love.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"To note:&nbsp;<em>Yew Haiku will be releasing a music video for <strong>Peach Nietzsche</strong> sometime this summer 2023!</em>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531748/large-3a3a3e5c13e0491a492d5838efa670dc.jpg","alt":"CenturyGothic_branded.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531748/preview-97d399fa2e9b0ba4aa472a00a9e51e65.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531750/large-7f6dd835ea77cf39d669e54a557899b3.jpg","alt":"2023YewHaikuPR_2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531750/preview-56cc83193db95d4fa7f14bb07fb3c73a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531752/large-89430245c1c9217ad6650c920ca5127f.png","alt":"Website_or_PR.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531752/preview-38babdda73aee72373c815495b20f161.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Yew Haiku:"},{"t":"p","html":"Yew Haiku is the songwriting project of <strong>Fuschia Smith</strong>. Equal parts Hot Topic Goth Shaman and Sonic Top Ramen, Smith blurs lines stylistically. Formed in isolation, the project spawned the 2021 single Psy and Cygnet with assistance from LANND's own Brian Squillace. In 2023’s release Smith acts as producer presenting a pastiche of synth, guitar solos, and stoic lyrical themes. What remains is a sense of something arcane yet experimental. As much an homage to <strong>Judy Garland</strong> as it is Kraftwerk, she reimagines lost kittens, star lore, and failed romance in a synthy Victorian mourning ritual. The first single, Peach Nietzsche, was inspired by the <strong>Heart Sutra</strong>, a Zen chant that is meant to take us back to beginner’s mind, a precious zero point that can allow us to accept the saccharine and the sour."},{"t":"h3","html":"Listen to Yew Haiku"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6VB41XSzs6I0SulHDRgMFj?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Yew Haiku!"},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/yewhaiku/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"238843","title":"Karmic Neighborhood to Launch \"I Don't Want to Walk Away\" Radio Remix","date":"2023-04-21","lead":"Scientist and songwriter Armand Ruby teams up with British Keyboardist and Producer Julian Colbeck to release alt-pop track.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/238843/f39de10ef7d6f26d70e97e39631391c1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Scientist and songwriter Armand Ruby teams up with British Keyboardist and Producer Julian Colbeck to release alt-pop track."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2GwLujewDO5BidnKDXmsNd?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Royal Oaks, CA (April 21, 2023) - This Friday, April 21st, <strong>Armand Ruby</strong> and <strong>Julian Colbeck</strong> are releasing their radio remix, <strong>\"</strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2GwLujewDO5BidnKDXmsNd?si=18f3141383804c17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Don't Want to Walk Away</strong></a><strong>\"</strong> under the <strong>Karmic Neighborhood</strong> artist title, with vocals by rocker <strong>James Durbin</strong>. This dreamy yet upbeat track reflects themes of mystery and pain associated with the sudden and unexpected ending of an intense romantic relationship. The lyrics <em>\"I don’t want to say goodbye, I said I will, and I will, but I don’t want to,\"</em> play into an overarching concept of \"lost love.\" Armand and Julian strive to connect to their listeners on an emotional level via the release of this single and on additional Karmic Neighborhood projects to come."},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/IDontWanttoWalkAwayradioremix","label":"Listen On All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"The west coast-based team are strangers-turned-neighbors, turned rhythmic alt-pop collaborators. Armand Ruby and Julian Colbeck are two life-long musicians in their 60's who met by chance when they moved to the same neighborhood on the central California coast. Julian was formerly a London-based rock star and lifelong music industry veteran, while Armand was professionally an environmental scientist who stayed involved in music as a part-time musician and songwriter. Armand and Julian formed a strong bond through their shared passion for music and the painful yet hopeful life experience of surviving cancer. The two found inspiration within the harmony of their own respective life journeys, and a mutual interest in musical innovation.<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1vnYPcPpvzO0hhjR6YMUkV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Armand Ruby:"},{"t":"p","html":"Armand spent most of his childhood in the northeastern US, during which he discovered two of his main passions: science and music. Although he dreamed of pursuing a career in music, Armand accepted an Ivy-League scholarship out of high school and went on to become an environmental scientist. Over the course of his university studies, throughout marriage and children and his science career, Armand continued to tap into his musical talent by songwriting, performing in bands, recording demos, and in many other ways. Armand also channeled his songwriting abilities through the creation of a musical play, “<strong>Equinox The Musical</strong>,” which he presented to audience acclaim in 2011. After surviving a prostate cancer scare and difficult separation from his partner, Armand moved to the rural Monterey Bay area community of Royal Oaks in 2019. There he discovered that one of his neighbors, Julian Colbeck, was an experienced music arranger, producer and keyboardist. The pair recorded a preview soundtrack of the songs from “Equinox the Musical” and collaborated on production of a short musical film, “<strong>I Said I Will</strong>.\" The award-winning film featured the original version of “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/09L2h21DyZ4ZRNnZSLIXx9?si=e0a9f1afa1684eba\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>I Don’t Want to Walk Away</strong></a>,” produced by Armand Ruby and Julian Colbeck, with final mix by Alan Parsons."},{"t":"h3","html":"About Julian Colbeck:"},{"t":"p","html":"Julian Colbeck grew up in the south of England, where he learned how to play the piano and ultimately pursued his dreams of being in a London-based rock ‘n’ roll band in his late teens. Julian’s music career took off with the band <em><strong>Charlie</strong></em>, with whom he scored several US Top 40 singles including “<strong>Watching TV</strong>” and “<strong>LA Dreamer</strong>.\" Over the span of a 40-year career, Julian worked and toured as a keyboard player/producer with Yes alumni group <strong>Anderson Bruford Wakeman Howe</strong>, former Genesis guitarist <strong>Steve Hackett</strong>, <strong>Charlie</strong>, <strong>John Miles</strong>, and more. In 2008 Julian began work with his long-time friend, <strong>Alan Parsons</strong>, on the award-winning instructional video series: Alan Parsons’ The Art &amp; Science Of Sound Recording. Julian also has written for many esteemed music industry publications, and has authored many music and music technology books. Beginning in late 2019, and interrupted by intensive treatment for stage 4 cancer, Julian saw something of value in his neighbor Armand Ruby’s songwriting and his Equinox film project, and worked as arranger, co-producer and keyboardist on the Equinox preview soundtrack recordings. Armand and Julian's collaboration on this work led to the production of their current release, the radio remix of “<strong>I Don’t Want to Walk Away</strong>.\"&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"CONNECT WITH KARMIC NEIGHBORHOOD!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100082755791779\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | <a href=\"mailto:armand@armandrubymusic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EMAIL</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"239490","title":"Australian Indie-Rock Artist Joel Sammut Releases New Track \"Trouble\"","date":"2023-04-21","lead":"Joel Sammut releases his new 90's grunge-inspired single on April 21st.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/239490/270e40055c39057cdd78775f8082b16f.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Joel Sammut releases his new 90's grunge-inspired single on April 21st."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3ABTJUl1wTDLxe6rd3rH3T?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Byron Bay, AUSTRALIA (April 21, 2023) - Primal Scream-inspired Australian singer and producer, <strong>Joel Sammut</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>is releasing a new groovy alt-rock track \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3ABTJUl1wTDLxe6rd3rH3T?si=ac4d0827639543de\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>T</strong></em><em><strong>rouble</strong></em></a>\" this Friday. The song dives into the theme of risky love and is supported by a cool, sultry rhythm that acts as the glue for each verse. The lyrics within this track constantly juxtapose each other with various tones and repetitive feelings. The first verse relates to love and passion, repeating <em>\"I’ll get a love like that, dancing and living heart attack\"</em> twice. The chorus switches sentiments immediately, conveying a mysterious conversation between two friends, <em>\"Oh yeah, hot damn, Do you think it's risky, Trouble man.\"</em> Joel wanted to create this stark contrast of emotions to emphasize how themes of love and trouble are often intertwined with one another while falling for someone."},{"t":"button","href":"https://soundcloud.com/joelsammut/trouble/s-nsDW4fFZrGa?si=699f2d4d719247a586806d61c168c80a&amp;utm_source=clipboard&amp;utm_medium=text&amp;utm_campaign=social_sharing","label":"Listen on Soundcloud","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Produced in just under two days, Joel added a beat to the song first, then the bass line, and lastly began adding in the verses and switch-ups. Layered experimental guitar sounds throughout the single are a reference to an early 90's grunge style, laced with interchanging early 80s/90s-inspired hip-hop beats. Additionally, the synth solo at the end of <em>Trouble</em> was inspired by American y2k Indie Rock band <strong>Cocorosie </strong>and was recorded on a Cat Keyboard Kids Toy that Joel sampled. Joel's old-school hip-hop influences include <strong>Beastie Boys </strong>and <strong>Slick Rick</strong>, while his general flare as an artist has been compared to surf-rock singer <strong>Mac Demarco</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6ooE5iBoXAQiy1QHtV5ZKS?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534660/large-0fa242b33a6a0c50a0bcc224aea97dfd.png","alt":"97100029.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534660/preview-f01cf1fdee91a8e33b8b136f746b8e52.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/535819/large-32537008f3a8f48add3d82b31da166fc.jpg","alt":"___IMG_8237_2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/535819/preview-320d451dc0b4f1b5ed772e0b00bd1ac3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/535820/large-2b3d2b0fb0fecf586cd23e61a928ef3a.jpg","alt":"___IMG_8254.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/535820/preview-1d010dd2bfe6d87a1380d253ec04b54e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534658/original-e7c30fb884cfcdc41582f555ad4af6d7.jpg","alt":"0.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/534658/preview-dd170f7dae838d658a00bc87ab3622b5.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Joel Sammut:"},{"t":"p","html":"Originally from Sydney, Joel is an Australian producer/singer-songwriter currently based in Byron Bay. Creating both nostalgic and spirited music, Joel has crafted his sound to be both fresh and timeless. A unique blend of pop, rock and electronic elements, Joel's music contains short yet emotionally-charged sentiments. Released in 2021, his track \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3stCs4KVlIBOjwOSe50RA7?si=f01f25a2098f4126\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Bleeding Man</strong></a>,\" follows a theme of heartache, while \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4VGvajv6c7rzoSs3nvxz9h?si=wToPJ7xkTjO58zSWsOTTJQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Home Ghost</strong></a>,\" released in the same year, reflects an expression of feeling lost and stuck at home during the pandemic. Joel is constantly growing and evolving his sound as a collaborative artist and producer, often tapping into varying sonic elements that define his sound and place within the music industry. Joel is releasing a fresh single, \"Trouble,\" this April 2023, which takes inspiration from experimental artists such as <strong>Tame Impala</strong>, <strong>David Bowie</strong>, <strong>​</strong><strong>Cocorosi​e</strong>, and more.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Joel!"},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@joelsammut_\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/joelsammut/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">INSTAGRAM</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ChrisBloommusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"></a><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/joelsammut/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"237292","title":"Jacob McCurdy Releases New Folky Single \"Out On The Run\"","date":"2023-04-14","lead":"Americana-esque Vocalist Jacob McCurdy Taps Into Themes of Fate & Love Within New Single","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/237292/c3452e26e1354c8073690f70a3666d81.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Americana-esque Vocalist Jacob McCurdy Taps Into Themes of Fate &amp; Love Within New Single"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6hq2YzBeQENII2L7aCecCG?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Portland, ME (April 14, 2023) - Rising small-town folk artist <strong>Jacob McCurdy</strong> is releasing his new sentimentally complex single today, April 14th. The track, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6hq2YzBeQENII2L7aCecCG?si=cdc7f2ec94774579\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Out On The Run</em></a><em>,&nbsp;</em>was inspired by falling in love and the uneasy feeling that comes along with it. Co-written with <strong>Alex Calabrese</strong>, the exploratory aura of <em>Out On The Run</em> has opened up new creative avenues for Jacob as an artist and songwriter.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/OutOnTheRun","label":"Listen on All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"The nostalgic single is driven by crisp vocals and acoustic guitar, which are later accompanied by a riveting trumpet solo. The track is glued together by harmonizing vocals, creating a warm undercurrent that carries listeners through the love story being told. Jacob traverses new stylistic terrain with this release, urging listeners to believe in their journey and find joy along the way. Jacob says that his father loves to tell people that,"},{"t":"quote","html":"“Each of Jacob's songs contain some element that resonates with everyone - from teenagers to grandparents.\"","cite":""},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531062/large-2b508e64b81545a1c8baf1e4a65a0f0b.jpg","alt":"j-023.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531062/preview-2245261bcbdae6b16212114d9b44d83a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531063/large-13bab6dba70000af384306c5cb03b420.jpg","alt":"JM&amp;amp;HLAS-108color.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531063/preview-06767e88b85a3f8e334cb9d411bf2065.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531064/large-b64587af2632784fcf40408807867864.jpg","alt":"JM&amp;amp;HLAS BandW.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531064/preview-f5b753e28870098235a09aef0c8ef3a9.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531065/large-bf33183da6ac5f646c3e40e901332e77.jpg","alt":"j-026.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531065/preview-01aa159af4461601db354798ee432b4a.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Jacob McCurdy:"},{"t":"p","html":"Mustachioed Mainer, Jacob McCurdy, blends Folk, Rock, and Roots into his very own brand of Indie-Americana. Love, heartbreak, joy, and the perfect moment all pitched against the lush backdrop of honest harmony. McCurdy wears his heart on his sleeve, sharing past traumas with the hope that they and anyone else experiencing them can begin to heal.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Jacob McCurdy!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0yA6Qdw3Ntzr0zhAo7T5Yx?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/jacobmccurdymusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@jacobmccurdymusic","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/_chrisbloom?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">​</a><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@jacobmccurdymusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ChrisBloommusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"></a><a href=\"https://facebook.com/jacobmccurdymusicpage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"237798","title":"Jett Jenkins Releases Vulnerable New Track - \"Someone Special\"","date":"2023-04-14","lead":"\"Someone Special\" creates an intimate listening experience with passion-filled vocals and down to earth lyrics","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/237798/c0fec34c7cad3e5655edff0e9abc0a22.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Someone Special\" creates an intimate listening experience with passion-filled vocals and down to earth lyrics"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6r9wmPmFXvxq0irAEP2DTM?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (April 14, 2023) - Up-and-coming indie-pop artist <strong>Jett Jenkins</strong> has announced the release of her new single, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6r9wmPmFXvxq0irAEP2DTM?si=a6c1cae2da77493c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Someone Special</a>.\" This track tells the story of losing the element of friendship with someone you strongly love. Referring to the aftermath and hurt of ending a friendship with someone, Jett says, <em>\"There is not hatred, but rather growing apart and the pain that comes with that.\"</em> Through raw tones and minimal background noise, Jett Jenkins creates a candid vocal that carries throughout the song, emphasizing the dichotomy between an energized sound and a tired singer. <em>\"Thought you were someone, someone special to me,\"</em> is one of the main sentiments repeated throughout the track, reiterating that losing a best friend never gets easier, but there is hope that it will with time.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/SomeoneSpecial","label":"Listen on All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5eQTLH2RK7Et9can4bdmI7?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Jett speaks on her thought process while writing this song - digging deeply into her emotions, <em>\"I wrote this song about a year ago, when I realized a friendship with someone I love had almost disappeared.\"</em> The artist also shared that despite Someone Special's somber overtone, she intended for a wave of optimism to exist within the intertwining lyrics and melodies. This single is the first release of two new musical projects Jett Jenkins has been working on."},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531586/compressed_original-00555f83f5e582080f0e917c0b3d94ba.png","alt":"\"Someone Special\" by Jett Jenkins - Cover Art"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Jett Jenkins:"},{"t":"p","html":"Jett Jenkins is a Brooklyn-based indie pop artist who layers dreamy, colorful production behind heavy lyricism. With stylings residing somewhere between <strong>Billie Eilish</strong> and <strong>Blondie</strong>, this poignant singer-songwriter leaned into her passions after having an inspirational experience at a Clairo concert. Years of playing the guitar and performing in musical theater prepared this emerging artist to dive into her music career; her debut E.P. is described as relatable, emotional, and delivering “lyrics beyond her years.” Alongside her debut in music, Jenkins is preparing to make the transition into young adulthood as she anticipates the move from home to college. This promising powerhouse makes a show-stopping introduction in her first single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1uZG2ygTi1bSDmqtZyCIfj?si=167ff340bb2c4d83\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">City in Anger</a>,” in which she captivates listeners with passionate vocals, invigorating instrumentation, and lyrics steeped in melancholy. Jett Jenkins, with her spellbinding charisma, is on track to finding a home on the playlist of indie-pop lovers for years to come. Stay posted for the upcoming release of her new single - the second song released alongside her most recent track, \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6r9wmPmFXvxq0irAEP2DTM?si=f1eed7f0f90b4ee8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Someone Special</a>.\""},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Jett!"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/therealjettjenkins/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@therealjettjenkins","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"232421","title":"The secret of the Labra Brothers entertainment appeal and confident energetic performances is rooted in their solid multi-instrumental musicianship strength. Their multi-genre mastery and cross-generational fans take this band from casinos to night spots, weddings and festivals.","date":"2023-04-07","lead":"The Labra Brothers EP 'Be Cool' Combines Latin, Funk, and Soul to Share Positive Upbeat Message","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/232421/f20483031870124969685cb5e41a14a9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Labra Brothers EP 'Be Cool' Combines Latin, Funk, and Soul to Share Positive Upbeat Message&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7GsUafBcKpqeZ3nJMyYrod?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Youngstown, Ohio (April 7, 2023) - Latin American brother band, The Labra Brothers, are establishing a distinct sound for themselves with their upcoming EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7GsUafBcKpqeZ3nJMyYrod?si=_imsx5qGSvKDUoyD6S4LtA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Be Cool</em></a>. After several releases experimenting with unique blends of their favorite genres while accentuating their versatile musicianship, the band successfully crafted a sound that could only be known as The Labra Brothers. <em>Be Cool</em> is the epitome of The Labra Brothers’ sound and is a mix of Latin rhythms, funk-inspired grooves, and soulful vocals. The EP establishes the tone for future releases as The Labra Brothers continue to perfect their sound."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/playlists/1564690507%3Fsecret_token%3Ds-lMPEQVovE5A&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false&show_teaser=true&visual=true","height":"300"},{"t":"p","html":"A three-song project, <em>Be Cool</em> is an uplifting and danceable EP that embodies kindness and compassion. The title track and single “Be Cool” was released on February 25, 2023, and is all about being kind to those around you. The Labra Brothers seek to continue to spread the positive message with the rest of their EP. They hope to encourage listeners to persevere with patience and kindness through the highs and lows of life. Accompanying the release of their single “Be Cool” was a music video filmed in San Luis Potosí, Mexico, which gives their listeners the opportunity to visually experience their music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521252/large-00eff667f09ca9ef3c0fdd04739ab5ae.jpg","alt":"The_Labra_Brothers_-_EP_Cover (2).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521252/preview-1f9fd93536fa389dcdab6d20c6109869.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521251/large-c5272144e268dbd28bbc1c0afabdca02.jpg","alt":"DSC_9508.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521251/preview-8f6f474650e40ee603ed819d5ad7eeab.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521253/large-ded719958d865173c4896b6d1b58f715.jpg","alt":"DSC_9339.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521253/preview-a1920227c43a505161acb9bfa7c31533.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521255/large-18ba078ebe97a1e702ecd6bc176914ac.jpg","alt":"DSC_9448.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521255/preview-4da2a58a84e6ff835456c7660f165e66.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521257/large-49b9452ac7ad67faed2cfe41683f56fe.jpg","alt":"DSC_9185.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521257/preview-73b171909eff181856d0c94f733d2c8f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521258/large-01a0895bcd90989e232af2cc825ead72.jpg","alt":"DSC_9451.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521258/preview-d699eca74cf87c544ea7b41680120662.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Labra Brothers:"},{"t":"p","html":"The Labra Brothers are a Latin Funk sibling band from Rustbelt, Northeast Ohio. Influenced by the diverse music taste of their parents, the brothers developed a distinguished sound that combines blues, funk, and Latin. After falling in love with playing their own renditions of their favorite music, the band decided to put their talents to work within their original creations. Consisting of <strong>Adrian Labra</strong> on vocals and guitar, <strong>Cristian Labra</strong> on vocals and bass, <strong>David Labra</strong> on vocals, guitar, and sax, <strong>Antonio Labra</strong> on percussion, <strong>Danny Svenson</strong> on keys, and <strong>Matt Hayes</strong> on drums, the band quickly discovered their ability to effortlessly interlock in an instrumental groove with each other. The Labra Brothers continue to release music and have established themselves regionally as a dynamic and diverse powerhouse of musical presentation. With three-part sibling vocal harmonies at the forefront, their versatility has become more evident with each new original studio recording they release. The Brothers had an eventful 2022, during which they played a direct support role for <strong>Average White Band</strong>, and were voted \"<strong>Best Latin Artist</strong>\" by the <strong>Cleveland Music Awards</strong>. Stay tuned for upcoming releases and live shows from The Labra Brothers in early 2023!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Labra Brothers:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2RxirsfpxfaajELy8K4z7B?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/labrabrosmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@labrabrosmusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.thelabrabrothers.com/","img":"","title":"The secret of the Labra Brothers entertainment appeal and confident energetic performances is rooted in their solid multi-instrumental musicianship strength. Their multi-genre mastery and cross-generational fans take this band from casinos to night spots, weddings and festivals.","desc":""},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"234227","title":"Chris Bloom's \"Frames\" Inspires Listeners to Embrace Their Unique Journey and Believe in Themselves","date":"2023-04-07","lead":"Chris Bloom Rejects Self-Doubt in R&B Pop Single \"Frames\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/234227/8e70a37ebe593efe3e3a09521253a557.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Chris Bloom Rejects Self-Doubt in R&amp;B Pop Single \"Frames\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/26Wu4IgW5PdhPgXdSjO0QW?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (April 7, 2023) - Rising R&amp;B and pop artist, <strong>Chris Bloom</strong>, is releasing his empowering new single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/26Wu4IgW5PdhPgXdSjO0QW?si=7a024a51500b489d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Frames</a>” which inspires listeners to believe in themselves. With its reflective and thoughtful lyrics, “Frames” confronts Bloom’s regret of doubting himself during his formative years. However, the track also serves as a revelation that it is never too late to believe in yourself. Self-assurance and confidence can be cultivated later in life and “Frames” is a testament to that. Too often individuals second guess their intuition, but it's that same instinct that is acting in their best interest. Drawing from personal experience, Bloom encourages listeners to ignore external influences and focus on making decisions that will lead to prosperity in their lives. With vivid metaphors and evocative imagery, Bloom portrays the individuality of everyone's unique journeys. Bloom sings, \"<em>Picture frames never fit the whole thing, do they?</em>\" - a powerful reminder that everybody’s path is different and cannot be entirely understood by anyone else.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"“Frames” features an immersive and alluring soundscape that makes it stand out against other comparable R&amp;B and pop songs. Chris Bloom’s soulful vocals sit seamlessly on top of spacious reverb-soaked electric guitars, passionately delivering his message. The song’s depth is accentuated by his hypnotic vocal harmonies and adlibs, which captivate the audience and keeps them listening from start to finish. The drums in “Frames” contribute to the song's engagement, as they provide a driving and compelling rhythm. The groove complements the rest of the instrumentation, creating a cohesive listening experience. Overall, the outstanding production quality of “Frames” highlights Bloom’s unparalleled songwriting and smooth vocals.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524694/large-81075835b2803d482306f2e2dac153a2.jpg","alt":"IMG_0981.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524694/preview-272736f0e4c57a80493a6699598064a2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524695/large-c5e85378d47f4cd24d77c8d73aafed3d.jpg","alt":"dsc06097.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524695/preview-6cc08ad261ba08e82a0e6ebb6d876f04.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524696/large-0f3611ea42b42d70d9785ca6538af52d.jpg","alt":"1.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524696/preview-71211d2b9fc6c1f61e1e70fc0313e699.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524698/large-0bd9d51f5c8a89eb45d9ed0c8fdfb745.jpg","alt":"dsc06178.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524698/preview-77ee65d8fcfdb74741914049fb3afbcf.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524697/large-27b4821d5df3a555dc876fca8ba65aee.jpg","alt":"dsc06129.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524697/preview-fd2032ca86fed6965853ca7fc4243a17.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Chris Bloom:"},{"t":"p","html":"Chris Bloom, born Christopher Burkich, holds a fluidity in genres and production. From his first two singles “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/28CAJhU60sk9pR4vjNEEBR?si=01425f38986c42be\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Learning Curve</strong></a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0tn0Pwa52ihju1GVAulWok?si=d5b5563aee8540a0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Petals</strong></a>”, to his latest 2020 EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6b0ueFQMQJZCJq8PJ0eMis?si=o2ggTn0ZQHi5siWlKTkBgw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>CAFÉ</em></strong></a>, his sound has ranged from R&amp;B and Hip-Hop, to pop and acoustic influences. Bloom grew up in Chattanooga TN, in a household where all types of music were celebrated. This, and being a self-taught singer, musician, and producer has allowed him to be a comfortable writer with a distinct voice. At the age of seventeen, he dropped out of high school and moved with his siblings to Los Angeles to pursue music. Since then, he has performed on two North American tours and one Australian tour with <strong>Scotty Sire</strong>, <strong>Sonreal</strong>, and <strong>Bruce Weigner</strong>.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Chris Bloom!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7CHhuFCa2PZXtPhXUY4wVy","height":"380"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/_chrisbloom/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@_chrisbloom","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/_chrisbloom?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TWITTER</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@chrisbloom_?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ChrisBloommusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YOUTUBE</a><br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"237261","title":"Emilia Suárez Releases New Single 'Where We Left Off' Straight The Heart","date":"2023-04-07","lead":"'Where We Left Off' Tells an Emotional Tale of Loneliness, Insecurity, and Heartache","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/237261/25caa53a1b881c6dc989b2c13e472a8a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"'Where We Left Off' Tells an Emotional Tale of Loneliness, Insecurity, and Heartache<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6JcATH6i4eOaRQ7UkJNe5A?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Brooklyn, NY (April 7, 2023) - Earthy folk artist<strong>&nbsp;Emilia Suárez</strong> released her new single '<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6JcATH6i4eOaRQ7UkJNe5A?si=64db9bc5b2c94e1a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Where We Left Off</a>,\" today (April 7th). In her own words, this new project was an exploration of feelings, and sorting out relentless emotions through musical expression. Within the music, Emilia has fostered a dialogue between her emotions and inner thoughts - ultimately unveiling aching themes of loneliness, uncertainty, restlessness, and unrequited love. The etherial nature of this song transports listeners through the ever-so painful process of replaying moments from an ended relationship in your head over and over again. Emilia describes the track's sentiment as \"<em>L</em><em>ament over a lost relationship that I left on the tip of my tongue for as long as I could</em>,\" candidly baring her deepest insecurities in and out of love. This single has allowed the artist to be vulnerable and honest about the difficult and confusing emotions one experiences after a breakup, which she hopes can resonate with her listeners while create a sentiment of support. \"Where We Left Off\" is an ode to all things left unsaid, feelings that felt invalidated and lack of self-confidence, interwoven with a voice of hope for healing and moving forward. Emilia shares this single was created with a different approach than some of her other music, in which she feels a struggle convey her emotions while simultaneously creating a cohesive sound. Referring to \"Where We Left Off\" and its singularity, Emilia shares that \"<em>The choices we made with the double vocal serve to represent an inner self-deprecating singing a duet with a more hopeful one.</em>”"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/63N2LyprPztDL4WwgiZ7L5?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Emilia turns an artistic corner with the release of \"Where We Left Off,\" which she produced with childhood best friend, <strong>Logan Smith</strong>. The two speak the same language in terms of stylistic choices and taste in music, which has translated into the fluid and delicate overtone this single possesses.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531022/large-8e312a945bf732b7bbf9e3a8b3d78f68.jpg","alt":"BD368B47-2267-44A9-9723-4E7186EB5F70.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531022/preview-228b5af8f984dc97e4979603407b3048.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531023/large-33c9124f124c08178ec77ad5ff539d6e.jpg","alt":"IMG_3280.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531023/preview-5757c0f80a671c2e412a64729cf8087f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531024/large-117b43b31da3d334743d4757f50090d2.jpg","alt":"IMG_3283.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531024/preview-e5a3035c607ecbd6c51ecc764156ea0d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531028/large-fe24cdd05f07d0e62e637d502bda62e1.jpg","alt":"COVER ART.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/531028/preview-1c023d09107d63c54265ac9864f3f184.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Emilia Suárez:"},{"t":"p","html":"Emilia Suárez is a Bolivian-American singer-songwriter and actor based in Brooklyn, NY. She launched her independent music career in 2021 with the release of her first single, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0HNFaobUlcZQIhVxrAiTit?si=9bfab61beaf64e65\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">lil ghost</a>”, followed by “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/6I1XbYeBsDJU2LDyryc4lD?si=f020512fb22f4bcf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Float</a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7llxVL0wbPT3eXa3xCGO6A?si=83d5954b8e9445ba\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Timing</a>” in 2022. Her music has gained over 100,000 streams on Spotify and has been placed on playlists around the world. Her music video \"Timing\" was just released a few weeks ago on Youtube (click <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@emsuarley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a> to view). She can be seen in the recently launched musical-comedy series on Hulu titled, \"<em><strong>Up Here</strong></em>.\" Emilia is also featured on the cast album from <em>Up Here</em>, featuring original music by <strong>Kristen Anderson-Lopez</strong> and <strong>Robert Lopez</strong>. Emilia has additionally been case alongside <strong>Florence Pugh</strong> and <strong>Morgan Freeman</strong> in MGM/Killer Films feature, \"<strong>A Good Person</strong>,\" which released in theaters a the end of March 2023. Throughout these next couple of exciting months of releases, Emilia can be found at <strong>The Old Globe</strong> performing in <strong>Destiny of Desire by Karen Zacharías</strong>."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Emilia!"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@emsuarley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>TIKTOK</strong></a><strong> | </strong><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/emsuarley/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>INSTAGRAM</strong></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"234032","title":"The official website for Texas-based mother/daughter duo Cliffs + Caves.","date":"2023-03-31","lead":"The Alt-Americana Track Delivers a Powerful Message to Find Solace in Tangible Relationships in a World of Misinformation and Doubt","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/234032/12a79c183fe7a87885aede9e54f5a8e8.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Alt-Americana Track Delivers a Powerful Message to Find Solace in Tangible Relationships in a World of Misinformation and Doubt"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/4S8krtlReAGRgPRk0OUgE0?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"College Station, Texas (March 31, 2023) - <strong>Cliffs + Caves</strong> transports listeners to a spacious soundscape in their newest single “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4S8krtlReAGRgPRk0OUgE0?si=5809c7368fd1488d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mint Gum</a>,” featuring David Ramirez. With an alt-Americana sound that is uniquely their own yet reminiscent of Lake Street Dive and Phoebe Bridgers, the duo’s new single is an emotional track with a powerful message. Amidst a vast expanse of misinformation and conspiracy theories, listeners can ground themselves in a tangible reality with “Mint Gum.”"},{"t":"p","html":"At the core of the song is a profound message that expresses deep concern about the oversaturation of misinformation in our time. In “Mint Gum,” Cliffs + Caves explores the impact of conspiracy theories in today's society and offers a heartfelt solution. It can be challenging to distinguish fabrication from fact. As doubt persists, it becomes even more difficult to discern what to build our personal beliefs around. However, the riveting track encourages listeners to find solace in the tangible relationships they have with their loved ones. The song serves as a powerful reminder that the love, care, heartbreak, sympathy, sadness, and joy we have for each other is what bond us together and creates concrete connections.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/MintGum","label":"Listen to \"Mint Gum\"","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"\"Mint Gum\" showcases the seamless vocal interplay of Cliffs + Caves and David Ramirez, whose distinct styles blend effortlessly to deliver the song's thought-provoking lyrics. A mesmerizing fusion of retro keyboards, punchy drums, atmospheric leads, and expressive guitars gives the song a cinematic quality that is both captivating and evocative. The production quality of \"Mint Gum\" is an indication of the band's commitment to creating an engaging listening experience, with every instrument and melody manufactured to enhance the overall sound of the track.<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528647/large-7834037a820ec7ea943b47aa77e12592.jpeg","alt":"MINT GUM.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528647/preview-49f923231b2d6fdd92a03c7547e667af.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528646/large-c8ef846533f02fb421b071b8be51f72d.jpg","alt":"Bandera-34.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528646/preview-baad0bd0d03ea038819c1ebe436cca02.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528641/large-a258ad0fe28118d36920c388c67d0acc.jpg","alt":"Bandera-362 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528641/preview-35439347da4941c860e76fc8e4ab3793.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528644/large-d4fa7108170bc3a9afb66fea7b0474cc.jpg","alt":"Bandera-40.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528644/preview-a43c6508ee9ad6a6de5042f91fbf3bc3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528643/large-ebff81e084b7710236592afa0344b9c5.jpg","alt":"Bandera-361.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/528643/preview-b77a94c8b91e96d2665cecf26f9859c6.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Cliffs + Caves:"},{"t":"p","html":"Cliffs + Caves, the mother-daughter duo of Lindsey and Claire Justice, unabashedly share their deeply personal and relatable stories through songs that resonate with listeners of all generations. Best known in their home state of Texas for their unique blend of Contemporary Americana music, the pair showcases the musical ingenuity that is created when artistry runs in the family with intimate lyrics lilting intrinsically over smooth musical progressions. Their previous discography includes their 2017 debut EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3SanUmvSOsrCrv1A4NlXZ2?si=nkS9N16CRmOeADyhhoTK6Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hold On</a> (recorded with Grammy-nominated producer <strong>Jamie Candiloro</strong> (<strong>Ryan Adams</strong>,<strong> R.E.M.</strong>, <strong>The Eagles</strong>) and featuring performances by legendary <strong>Willie Nelson</strong>’s harmonica player, <strong>Mickey Raphael</strong>) and sophomore EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4gEhBjWLd5a66JwQRENwNs?si=Aps5nYpyQVSHt4Rfs0SygA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Capsize</a> (produced by <strong>Chris Jacobie</strong> (<strong>Penny </strong><strong>and Sparrow</strong>, <strong>Jarrod Dickenson</strong>, <strong>Duncan Fellows</strong>). The original songs are a team effort with the duo individually contributing to the mastery of their lyrics and melodies. Moreover, twenty-year-old <strong>Claire </strong>being a multi-instrumentalist, not only composes the music for the tracks but also bestows a knack for songwriting. Their newer music further explores the duo's ability to portray life through lyrics as they evolve into a more alternative Maggie-Rogers-esque sound while still maintaining their Americana roots and drawing inspiration from benchmark artists like <strong>Phoebe Bridgers</strong>, <strong>Lake Street Dive</strong>, and <strong>Patty Griffin</strong>. With a love for writing songs and performing them live, Cliffs + Caves is thrilled to be releasing new music which they will be playing at a variety of upcoming shows in 2023!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Cliffs + Caves!"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://cliffsandcaves.com/","img":"","title":"The official website for Texas-based mother/daughter duo Cliffs + Caves.","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/cliffs_and_caves/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@cliffs_and_caves","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@cliffsandcaves2211\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YOUTUBE</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"235752","title":"Nilka","date":"2023-03-31","lead":"Nilka's First Self-Produced EP Contains Seven Soulful Pop Songs Inspired by Psalms","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/235752/5da74133ecaf8191728c77ae7b45fab1.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Nilka's First Self-Produced EP Contains Seven Soulful Pop Songs Inspired by Psalms"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/65ac0xEqI9SvUnENNpvopY?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Nashville, TN (March 31, 2023) - Rising bedroom pop artist, <strong>Nilka</strong>, is releasing her first self-produced EP <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/65ac0xEqI9SvUnENNpvopY?si=NTZhxD_VT0CLKeG2XUXJ-w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Sacred</em></a>, featuring seven spiritually charged songs inspired by her personal experiences with her faith. A collection of soulful prayer songs, <em>Sacred</em> showcases how Nilka’s faith has played a pivotal role in navigating through overcoming hardships. The EP serves as a reflection of her personal growth and resilience, with each track encapsulating the transformative journey that has shaped her into the artist she is today. Drawing inspiration from the Psalms, Nilka carefully crafted each song on the EP, using them as a personal reminder that she is never alone. <em>“My goal is to create a safe space for others to heal through their connection to the words and be reminded of God's love,”</em> says Nilka, hoping that&nbsp;<em>Sacred</em> will provide listeners the same comfort it provided her. The final song “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7uqqYK7t7BMHEOhX10pDeU?si=dbc2551555234bf8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sanctuary</a>” offers solace to listeners, reminding them of the importance of finding a safe space for healing and growth. Through her smooth and expressive vocals, Nilka offers her audience comfort in the face of adversity. The EP’s introspective lyrics and memorable melodies create a serene atmosphere, providing a sense of peace to those who listen."},{"t":"p","html":"<em>Sacred</em> features dreamy and soulful pop sounds, with lo-fi elements that curate an immersive and intimate ambiance. Through heartfelt lyrics, Nilka delves into important themes such as mental health, spirituality, self-growth, and family relationships, providing a relatable and engaging listening experience for her audience. The result of Nilka’s artistic vision is an authentic and reflective expedition that takes listeners on a captivating sonic and lyrical journey of life's challenges and achievements. As a Latin-American artist, Nilka is proud to showcase her Puerto Rican heritage through bilingual lyrics that add a multicultural perspective to her EP. Her thought-provoking lyrics explore the complexities of identity and culture, making her music accessible to a wide range of listeners. Additionally, each song will be accompanied by an official lyric video, further immersing listeners in the meaning behind Nilka’s earnest lyrics."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/527556/large-392d9069fd71b14c93eee1951826d124.jpg","alt":"SACREDalbumart.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/527556/preview-cfe2ac8a705929b56b52b177f2bda3a5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/527555/original-e90e9d344d1668d6ddbe2a2f52477e0f.jpg","alt":"PhotoByAnnaKaufmann_IMG_3824.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/527555/preview-2c2ad3450e2dffa7d72a5742906c60b2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/527554/large-cda529acd7e72f4834e82e24b597c0ba.jpg","alt":"PhotoByAnnaKaufmann_IMG_3825.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/527554/preview-ab88ec578dee2436be89792e44240b3e.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Nilka:"},{"t":"p","html":"Florida-native artist, Nilka, is transcending the soul-pop genre with her fluid vocals and dreamy bedroom production. Nilka fell in love with creating songs as a young girl fusing her thoughts to a string of notes with lyrics originating back to the early age of nine years old. Five years later she taught herself how to play guitar, cementing her melody-lyric combinations and her pensive songs became like entries in a journal. Songwriting was a way for Nilka to confront experiences in her life and music became her outlet. Throughout grade school, she participated in different bands and choirs where she became fascinated with the impression symphonic music could leave on an audience and she has been inspired by a broad spectrum of genres from Motown to Folk music. In 2014 Nilka graduated from Polk State College with an Associate of Arts degree emphasized in music where she studied Classical Voice. During the summer of 2014, Nilka relocated to Nashville, Tennessee to finish her Bachelor of Music degree at <strong>Belmont University</strong> in Commercial Voice and Songwriting."},{"t":"p","html":"Nilka has been releasing music since 2017 and during that time has gained song placements on HULU’s series “<strong>Light as a Feather</strong>” as well as the series “<strong>Love Island Australia</strong>”. Her songs have been released by EDM labels such as <strong>NoCopyrightSounds</strong> and <strong>Magic Records</strong> and now in the next 12 months, she is set to release her first self-produced album project consisting of seven songs that reflect on her spirituality and deepest relationships. Nilka’s lyrics undeniably share a message of how powerful and sacrificial true love is and her music captivates listeners with a soul-moving experience revealing a unique and authentic perspective of the human experience."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Nilka!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3JED4McgKAqYMqDrPStAxg?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/nilkamusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@nilkamusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.nilkamusic.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/58c372cf8419c2ae2beac186/t/5eacbe12625c2f2eff896969/1588379157920/RWEPartworkOG.JPG?format=1500w","title":"Nilka","desc":""},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"230498","title":"Jett Jenkins Releases Music Video for her Highly Praised 2021 Single “City in Anger”","date":"2023-03-24","lead":"“City in Anger” recounts Jenkin’s experience finding peace in a chaotic world through brooding lyricism backed by a cascading drum beat and gritty electric guitar.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/230498/91b9835f47658a8e571e781d1a394c4a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"“City in Anger” recounts Jenkin’s experience finding peace in a chaotic world through brooding lyricism backed by a cascading drum beat and gritty electric guitar.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"230960","title":"C H I S O M .","date":"2023-03-24","lead":"Afro-Pop Infused Hip-Hop Album 'Bracelets' Seeks to Appreciate Life’s Beauty While Embracing Anti-Materialism","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/230960/e7801eaccdc66e82487201b0e4ef75b9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Afro-Pop Infused Hip-Hop Album '<em>Bracelets'</em> Seeks to Appreciate Life’s Beauty While Embracing Anti-Materialism"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1LctEi9HdRjxpdb4WvIHah?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Washington, D.C. (March 24, 2023) - <strong>Chisom</strong>’s album <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1LctEi9HdRjxpdb4WvIHah?si=Jhqh9RIMS46o-hIfzdm-TQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Bracelets</em> </a>encompasses the captivity of materialism while still seeking to appreciate the finer things in life. The soulful twelve-song album showcases Chisom’s adept lyricism and unparalleled take on afro-pop-infused hip-hop. The word “bracelets” is a metaphor for handcuffs - a metaphor Chisom valiantly adopts to represent breaking free from societal constraints in his new album. Not only is Chisom breaking free of societal constraints, but he is also breaking free from genre constraints with the diverse album. Primarily a hip-hop artist, Chisom combines Hip-Hop, Alternative Hip-Hop, Soul, Afropop, and Afro-fusion to create a distinct and memorable sound in <em>Bracelets.&nbsp;</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"The initial idea for&nbsp;<em>Bracelets&nbsp;</em>came to fruition during a month-long trip to Houston, Texas. The Texas heat and nights out with old friends melded perfectly with Chisom's daily writing and recording sessions. Inspired by the change of environment, the lyrics began pouring out of him at an expeditious pace. He noticed that a common theme in the lyrics was breaking free from materialism. However, it wasn’t until he wrote the fifth track on the album, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3doVOYjHd6jhkwh8JIIFmc?si=5212587f8f52439f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Within</a>,” that he was confident he had a message he needed to share."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/playlists/1571276959%3Fsecret_token%3Ds-qcWTgwMd2jO&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false&show_teaser=true","height":"450"},{"t":"p","html":"The title track, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3LWvgrq1nibrJwfU36GHLv?si=ef16c4a58a7f4731\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bracelets</a>,” was written after an undesirable interaction with the police. Chisom was no stranger to police misconduct and mustered the utmost respect and patience while answering unmerited questions. Having been accused of driving too close to the car in front of him, Chisom felt disheartened by the police officer's response to cuff him and search his car. When they inevitably found nothing in his vehicle, they left without so much as uttering an apology. Chisom walked away furious, confused, and abashed. However, rather than sulking over the adverse feelings, he transformed the troublesome experience into a catchy and compelling body of art."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518653/original-b3ddcddd424562bc2dcc2080cdb31f01.jpg","alt":"Winter Chief 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518653/preview-245ea68ec0b22f48ed7ccf5bf11018fe.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518654/large-ffa8af6f901fdab8a87fa4dbdbf4b6fd.jpeg","alt":"Posted_DC.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518654/preview-32aa6af693bad82764de13c927595126.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518657/large-7244674591cc3fb6832b6fd0c24c88e3.jpeg","alt":"Waterfront.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518657/preview-9bddc3482f2826f2b3ee8e7d2266e521.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518655/large-3553d7b3939a612f991c0a781e6653a6.jpg","alt":"CHIEF (Portrait).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518655/preview-e422efa819b673f27de7948b2978a26e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518660/large-f94cbf42cf9bc37400a25c6053dde012.jpeg","alt":"Chisom - Bracelets (Artwork).jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518660/preview-60ff19792c9991c94237af613f4af45e.jpeg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Chisom:"},{"t":"p","html":"Chisom blends vintage east coast hip-hop with a deep affection for the complex beauty of traditional African music to create his signature sound. The Detroit-born, D.C.-based Nigerian-American artist has been studying his craft for years, giving his lyricism a potent blend of intellectualism and authenticity. While he wears his passion for the genre’s history on his sleeve, Chisom is devoted to paving his own path, and bringing hip-hop to a higher level of consciousness. His music celebrates his rich heritage while making meaningful observations on American society. With recent releases featured in OkayPlayer, DJBooth, and XXL in addition to a steady stream of new material expected this year, Chisom is poised to become a vital voice of his generation."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Chisom!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7KzAUl5cI7gDiIe1qzZdRb?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.africanchisom.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/58262b9be4fcb538dd7a0c4e/t/5828b53d46c3c4d32c9edc8a/1479062850348/Chisom+Head+2.png?format=1500w","title":"C H I S O M .","desc":"Official website of Chisom. - Nigerian-American Dream-Hop Artist"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/africanchisom/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@africanchisom","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/africanchisom/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/Chisom\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YOUTUBE</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"232740","title":"To reduce cultural barriers, The Trouble Notes have made it their mission to create their own cultural universe. Their self-described \"Acoustic Dance Music\" ...","date":"2023-03-21","lead":"The Trouble Notes are returning to stages across North America with a 13 date Tour slated for Fall of 2023","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/232740/8c79d919f67a2fa248a223cce06382e4.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Trouble Notes are returning to stages across North America with a 13 date Tour slated for Fall of 2023"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7i1WiSQVIHt4bZz8DhuylF?utm_source=generator","height":"380"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"BERLIN, GERMANY (March 8, 2023) - Sitting between traditional folk, modern classical, and tribal dance music, The Trouble Notes are announcing their return to North America with the <strong>‛More Violins, Less Violence’ tour</strong> slated for the fall of 2023. Showcasing songs from their second studio album<em><strong>&nbsp;Liberty Awaits&nbsp;</strong></em>and spanning&nbsp;<strong>13 dates&nbsp;</strong>from October through November, the band is eager to reunite with their Troublemakers in the US and Canada. Carrying a message of “unity in diversity,” their repertoire brings the traditions of Europe and the Americas together, featuring songs like “Grand Masquerade” and “Never Dream Alone” that have amassed millions of views and listens worldwide."},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>As art and music are a force for healing in this world, one dollar of every ticket and five dollars of every ‛More Violins, Less Violence’ T-Shirt sold will be donated to a charitable cause helping children affected by violence. </strong><br>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524651/large-953e9b0ab3f5183df9bd6a8b53ad1b0e.png","alt":"Photo by Stefanie Tendler."},{"t":"h3","html":"US/CANADA TOUR DATES"},{"t":"p","html":"October 26th Chicago, IL - Martyrs'&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"October 29th Toronto - Drom Taberna<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 1st Montréal - L'Escogriffe<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 2nd Saratoga Springs - Caffe Lena<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 3rd Cambridge, MA - The Underground<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 5th Brooklyn, NY - Sultan Room<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 8th Philly, PA - Milkboy Philly<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 11th Charlotte, NC - Evening Muse<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 12th Asheville, NC - The Grey Eagle<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 15th Atlanta, GA - Smith's Olde Bar<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 17th Columbus, MS - Muddy Waters Sports Bar<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 18th Knoxville, TN - Scruffy City Hall<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 19th Louisville, KY - Mag Bar<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 25th Munster, IN - Theatre at the Centre<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"November 26th Madison, WI - High Noon Saloon<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Trouble Notes:"},{"t":"p","html":"Sitting between traditional folk, modern classical, and tribal dance music, <a href=\"https://thetroublenotes.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Trouble Notes</strong></a> have traveled across continents in search of musical influences to give listeners the unrivaled music of the generation. The band has proudly built its diverse audience independently, known colloquially as <strong><em>The Troublemakers </em></strong><em>--</em> a testament to their self-made success story that has led to significant festival appearances, multiple film scores, and an extensive tour schedule spanning the globe.&nbsp;<br><br>In 2017, a series of videos of the band performing on the streets in France and Germany went certified viral, amassing more than 100 million views on social media and bringing them international notoriety. They recorded their debut album&nbsp;‛<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/05lK2OB6LAYFranTHTFxoV?si=fcj90-4pShK4szRGbftwtQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Lose Your Ties</em></a><em>’</em> at Riverside Studios in Berlin, Germany working with Lebanese producer, Khalil Chahine. The album was released in February 2018 and peaked in the top 10 of the iTunes charts for their genre in France, Germany, and the USA. Their music has been featured in award-winning films and documentaries, and their headline “<strong>Lose Your Ties</strong>” Tour featured sold-out concerts in Europe and North America. They have performed live on television in the USA, Japan, Brazil, Germany, and France. And in 2019, they toured supporting Rodrigo y Gabriela as a part of their Grammy Award-winning “<strong>Mettavolution</strong>” Tour.&nbsp;<br><br>Currently performing across Europe and gearing up for a North American tour in the fall of 2023, The Trouble Notes allow listeners to travel across oceans and time with the soulful melodies of Bennet’s violin and Carola’s voice as your body pulses with the explosive energy from Florian’s guitar. Worldly percussion rhythms transport the audience across genres with an uplifting spirit for which The Trouble Notes have become world renown.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/fEuksdJf2FE","height":""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Trouble Notes:"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/thetroublenotes/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@thetroublenotes","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.thetroublenotes.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.youtube.com/thetroublenotes?cbrd=1&amp;ucbcb=1","img":"","title":"To reduce cultural barriers, The Trouble Notes have made it their mission to create their own cultural universe. Their self-described \"Acoustic Dance Music\" ...","desc":""},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"233140","title":"View BRII_music’s Linktree. Listen to their music on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music here.","date":"2023-03-17","lead":"\"Solitaire\" explores the emotions that come with falling into and out of love","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/233140/ac88c02f0fae0a4822b6af848635ff5a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Solitaire\" explores the emotions that come with falling into and out of love"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/yLC7W7uJRJw","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, CA (March 17, 2023) - <strong>Brii Elliss</strong> just released her seven-song pop album “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6bBvLFkz6mLYNekaeHywiQ?si=BhaC-ciRSFOPWWha50iRUA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Solitaire</a>.” Inspired by Elliss’ experiences being single and dating, the name “Solitare” was fitting because solitaire is a game that is played alone. Elliss wants the album to spark empowerment, love, forgiveness and exploring the emotions that come with falling in and out of love. Each song is about a different experience Ellis had while dating.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6bBvLFkz6mLYNekaeHywiQ?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5jK7liISl9b3ganwos4GuJ?si=04b47f7719cf4a78\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">What You Do to Me</a>\" explores having feelings for the wrong person, who does not treat you right. Brii Elliss shares that <em>“It's about wishing you could push those feelings away and ignore them because you know it isn't right, but still coming back for some reason. I've learned that sometimes the chase is exciting and fun but if love is what you're looking for, it won't end well.”</em> Similarly, the final song “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/569Lm5z11ZZQDp0mzsJ4tp?si=a00d0bc832564b31\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spades</a>” is about a relationship that didn’t work out. Written about a person that was so different from Ellis, they couldn’t be a match. Despite this realization, the feelings were still there, so she was at an impasse and unsure of what to do. “<em>I didn't want to end things because I really enjoyed spending time with him, but as time went on it felt like a decision had to be made and I knew it wouldn't become anything serious,”</em> says Ellis. Writing this song was a way for Brii Ellis to contemplate how to move forward."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493573/large-276587b288ad68337779672cb896ff43.png","alt":"Solitaire Album Cover (1) (1).png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493573/preview-52f2715aec70fb0df5553e1273b406cb.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493569/original-0fac4c5e609b66d6ad2650644ecee1f5.jpg","alt":"image1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493569/preview-d2a6069f439b98a6aca929683a013c00.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493572/large-d883208c47a7d4c95818624439f43678.jpg","alt":"image3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493572/preview-aa31b9efe598fce3f2f7035c4217aaa0.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494963/large-168106205206004a1a9515720f0a1e4a.jpg","alt":"_MG_1165.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494963/preview-e43dc142f9f8c92abe736bfa147849fc.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494964/large-b3639cf8865a92baffc41bb10995f905.jpg","alt":"_MG_1018.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494964/preview-4e89be11b59fb880e172f45f32ee99c3.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brii Elliss:"},{"t":"p","html":"Up-and-coming pop artist Brii Elliss is a singer-songwriter who brings a certain closeness to her lyrics, giving testament to the power of storytelling in music. With an Irish father and Puerto Rican mother, her voice and life experiences create a unique blend that filters into her songs effortlessly, showcasing a sultry R&amp;B chill-pop soundscape that captivates and entrances listeners. Working with Grammy-winning producer <strong>Synematik </strong>to create her signature buttery sound, Brii pulls inspiration from artists like <strong>Amber Mark, H.E.R., Snoh Aalegra, Jhene Aiko</strong>, and <strong>Jazmine Sullivan</strong>, with a deeply rich tone that is quickly creating a buzz in the music community. A New Jersey native who has been singing since she can remember, Brii was on the path to stardom by the age of 12, having already auditioned for the famed X-Factor show and made it through several rounds. Throughout high school, she continued pursuing this passion by writing new songs and recording them, honing her piano skills, and preparing to move to LA where she attended college at Loyola Marymount University and graduated with her Bachelor's degree in music. As she began to record her own music she realized how much she needed music to be center stage in her life. <em>\"I'm in my element when I am recording and surrounded by other creatives. It feels like home to me, and it's still my happy place today.\" </em>Needless to say, her happiness and passion in the studio shines through her work as her debut single garnered over 17K streams upon release while showcasing her authentic songwriting and silky low voice. Fans have already started rallying behind her and eagerly anticipate what's to come next for this budding artist. Lucky for them, Brii has lots of new music up her sleeve for 2023 and plans to share her soulful vibe with the world... one song at a time.<br style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; box-sizing: border-box; border-width: 0px; border-style: solid;\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Brii Elliss:"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://linktr.ee/BRII_music","img":"","title":"View BRII_music’s Linktree. Listen to their music on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music here.","desc":""},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@brii_elliss\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tik Tok</a>&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/brii_elliss/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@brii_elliss","post":false}],"contact":null},{"id":"233808","title":"Emilia Suárez’ “Timing” is a Dynamic Retelling of Unabashed Presence","date":"2023-03-17","lead":"The Hulu and MGM Actress will Release “Timing” Music Video on March 17th","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/233808/fc271145fe13aca498977ecff3ef9088.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Hulu and MGM Actress will Release “Timing” Music Video on March 17th<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/gLZWIBMOYfk","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"BROOKLYN, NEW YORK (March 17, 2023) - Bolivian-American actress and singer-songwriter <strong>Emilia Suárez</strong> just released her music video “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7llxVL0wbPT3eXa3xCGO6A?si=96eee7c7752d412e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Timing</a>.” The indie-alternative single is a vulnerable, dreamy and evocative piano ballad with symphonic and atmospheric sounds."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7llxVL0wbPT3eXa3xCGO6A?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"This music video lives between a liminal space and memories; it is a dramatized version of what writing this song was actually like for Suárez. The video captures Suárez truly in the moment and with an unabashed presence, something she hadn’t experienced until she was with this person. Suárez reflects that “I think in this video, we captured that, which makes it all the more painful to know that those two crazy kids just can't make it! And there’s no real reason or lesson to cling to for why. Some people are just there to teach you that you deserve so much better, and for me, that was really hard to let go of”.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Writing the song was an atypical experience for Suárez, as she didn’t intend to write about this relationship, but it’s the only place her mind wanted to live. “This song is touching a lot on the nature of the relationship and grappling with the inability to move on. It was also designed to call myself out a bit. If I’m actively choosing to relive it, I’m the reason it stays with me. The ‘inability’ is more voluntary than the poets would like to admit,” Suárez expresses.<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524074/large-68a1baf193a677bb5e0eaa4e4ac56274.jpg","alt":"thumbnail.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524074/preview-aa221732a2bd6702e6ef6ff8f22d8697.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524075/large-70fd8e19b4497fe2201b9b123b0ce030.jpg","alt":"COVER ART FOR SONG TIMING.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524075/preview-a0bc4215f87471bf9eb12aec75f45928.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524076/large-416dcd9d7ee7fb5c305c9cd8438b433a.jpg","alt":"IMG_3282.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524076/preview-12d7935810c031440df2749b03619105.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524077/large-bf17f197563019be3e97f92b0e89e0a4.jpg","alt":"IMG_3280.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524077/preview-713909e0847fa8dfd46a809126a0d286.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524078/large-5c6d59e86ade2aaf48c1ee99a83e2190.jpg","alt":"Timing_Stills_1.44.2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524078/preview-87128cc7c45ada35ecdef5fe4659358a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524079/large-90e9864ae73026b3bc4b7ad2218d0197.jpg","alt":"Timing_Stills_1.40.1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524079/preview-40c209c77dee52fd783748dd8742c404.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524081/large-3e4234ab8b7e60d0b2decf13e70393f8.jpg","alt":"timing_1.9.1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524081/preview-3551d8564da0a78290c9d8bd8df158ee.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524082/large-54c56bd011cecbd470f488c7d87bd802.jpg","alt":"Timing_Stills_1.109.1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/524082/preview-5f4d6c9ab5f9130a28b93e2ed1019d4a.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Emilia Suárez:"},{"t":"p","html":"Emilia Suárez is a Bolivian-American singer-songwriter and actor based in Brooklyn, NY. She launched her independent music career in 2021 with the release of her first single, “lil ghost”, followed by “Float” and “Timing” in 2022. Her music has gained over 100,000 streams on Spotify and has been placed on playlists around the world. Her music video \"Timing\" will be the first of many releases in 2023. She can be seen in the upcoming musical-comedy series, Up Here, from the director of Hamilton, coming to Hulu on March 24th. She is also featured on the cast album of the same name, featuring original music by Kristen Anderson-Lopez and Robert Lopez. Emilia can also be found alongside Florence Pugh and Morgan Freeman in MGM/Killer Films feature A Good Person, coming to theaters the same day. Throughout these next couple of exciting months of releases, she can be found at The Old Globe performing in Destiny of Desire by Karen Zacharías.<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Emilia Suárez!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/63N2LyprPztDL4WwgiZ7L5?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/emsuarley/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@emsuarley","post":false}],"contact":null},{"id":"230108","title":"Contemporary Christian Artist Chris Liverman Encourages Listeners to Run Toward God in New Song “Destiny”","date":"2023-03-10","lead":"Chris Liverman Eagerly Pursues God Above All Else In New Worship Song","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/230108/9713fea64aec8ff8735094d55ba38187.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Chris Liverman Eagerly Pursues God Above All Else In New Worship Song"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0ndAuHMcim1gc8HrxofcJe?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"<br>Virginia Beach, VA (March 10, 2023) - <strong>Chris Liverman</strong>’s new song “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0ndAuHMcim1gc8HrxofcJe?si=2fe88c1f76c545b0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Destiny</a>” is about rejecting worldly desires and focusing one’s mind and spirit on God. “Destiny” follows the release of Liverman’s song “Purpose” which made the Top 20 list for Christian streams and downloads during its first week. With music featured on the<em>&nbsp;</em><a href=\"https://www1.cbn.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Christian Broadcasting Network</em></a> and several Christian radio stations, Chris Liverman is fervently working to spread God’s bountifulness and continues to do so in the new single “Destiny.”&nbsp;"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/officialchrisliverman/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@officialchrisliverman","post":false}],"contact":null},{"id":"233338","title":"Thomas Goforth Reveals His \"Intentions\" in New Country Single","date":"2023-03-10","lead":"\"Intentions\" Highlights Thomas Goforth's Smooth Vocals and Purposeful Storytelling","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/233338/3f7d37968cd1120e249a588fcd7cbe1a.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Intentions\" Highlights Thomas Goforth's Smooth Vocals and Purposeful Storytelling"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/7LK4LSSLe87nZkLGvqz0NR?utm_source=generator","height":"152"},{"t":"p","html":"Barnhart, MO (March 10, 2023) -\"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7LK4LSSLe87nZkLGvqz0NR?si=38aec6dd0cd244a0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Intentions</a>\" is the latest single from country artist <strong>Thomas Goforth</strong> and exemplifies his captivating and meaningful storytelling. The single follows the release of his highly acclaimed song \"<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7suMSqrEA6RrlfzVvWWQ78?si=fe6641aae4974a29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">I Wish I Liked Bourbon</a>\" which amassed nearly one hundred thousand views on TikTok alone. A country pop song with crisp vocals, memorable melodies, and driving acoustic guitars, “Intentions” shapes Goforth's sound as he continues to grow his discography.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Written in ten minutes, the lyrics for “Intentions” effortlessly flowed out of Thomas Goforth. He wrote “Intentions” about meeting a potential love interest for the first time. The song tells the story of the initial physical attraction between two strangers on a night out. They are both interested in the other but neither knows the true intentions behind the interaction. In the song, he questions if the woman is looking for a fling or a long-term relationship, and sings <em>“But still I don't know your next move. Don't know what you plan to do to me” </em>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/522824/large-74e4cc237296fc1dc9a8c9688cb97403.png","alt":"C238E236-4736-4785-AB33-6D117A078750.PNG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/522824/preview-0c6f046aa86c0c1eecbeded42384e844.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/522820/large-5107049a9049b1586e106be348b66bfa.jpg","alt":"IMG_4814.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/522820/preview-2be8773c2e9401fe53f3536689a84aa0.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/522821/large-c39b7d4acaa6945bec092a91641e8e66.jpg","alt":"IMG_4757.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/522821/preview-84aea699ffd04f743370176547e3854f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/522822/large-3ac4d7af4eef5bed82c2ce4c757fb9ef.jpg","alt":"IMG_4811.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/522822/preview-e4f544297918d6eff087794817cb797d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/522823/large-5debd6edcb8ef95a53ef1ccc975a703e.jpg","alt":"4B9D07C0-0336-4B1A-85E2-3B3128856E61 (1).JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/522823/preview-e120220ddc40e4a7424c792b67189252.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Thomas Goforth:"},{"t":"p","html":"Born and raised in Barnhart, MO, country artist Thomas Goforth found his passion for music at nine years old. It didn’t matter what the genre of music was, as long as Goforth was listening to and making music, he was happy. This boundless love for music reflects today in Goforth’s ability to carve out an authentic and unique space for himself in the country music scene. By fifteen years old, Goforth was writing and recording his original songs at a local studio, Shock City Studio. Continuing to grow his audience, he began to gain traction by posting covers of popular songs on YouTube. Today he’s found success through TikTok, with his recent single “I Wish I Liked Bourbon” garnering nearly one hundred thousand views on the popular social media platform. Influenced by <strong>Morgan Wallen </strong>and <strong>Luke Combs</strong>, Goforth continues innovating within the genre, implementing his distinct style into country music.&nbsp;"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Thomas Goforth!"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5BSIU5Om7q2oViApGhbiw1?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/thomasgoforthmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@thomasgoforthmusic","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@thomasgoforthmusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok </a>| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCDz5IaoMAO4n9QGjXcDqF-w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> ​"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"233163","title":"Micah Edwards","date":"2023-03-08","lead":"\"Mr. Texas Soul\", Micah Edwards, is set to take the stage at SXSW on March 15th showcasing his signature retro-pop-soul sound","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/233163/ba7b99374b2491f3e4f768bd426769a9.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Mr. Texas Soul\", Micah Edwards, is set to take the stage at SXSW on March 15th showcasing his signature retro-pop-soul sound"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/75OSuJw6r1LCdYgmTt0gHs?utm_source=generator","height":"380"},{"t":"p","html":"AUSTIN, TX (March 8, 2023) - Micah Edwards, ubiquitously known as \"Mr. Texas Soul\", is bringing his retro-pop-soul soundscape to<strong>&nbsp;SXSW</strong> with an artist <strong>showcase at Cooper's BBQ on March 15th from 9:20 PM - 10:10 PM.</strong> Having recently reached <strong>over 1 million monthly Spotify listeners</strong>, Edwards will be performing with his full band (including a rhythm and horn section) to showcase his golden-toned, fresh take on soul music that has been described as a \"Willie Nelson meets Leon Bridges\" style."},{"t":"button","href":"https://schedule.sxsw.com/2023/events/MS56399","label":"Event Info","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"quote","html":"This will actually be my first show in Austin, and I couldn't imagine a better introduction than at SXSW.","cite":"Micah Edwards"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/fP16uCTpfAI","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"Planning to perform tracks from his most recent debut full-length album, <em>Jean Leon</em>, Edwards exemplifies a unique 21st-century retro-pop eruption fit with buttery vocals, gut-wrenching melodies, and tender lyrics that follow the themes of faith and family. Bitter, yet uplifting, <em>Jean Leon</em> draws inspiration from retro soul and classic country - giving a nod to the artists before him, as a young virtuoso who understands not just the heart, but the musical precision of retro-soul and country music. Someone who pays homage to Curtis Mayfield’s brilliance of guitar in early Impressions records and Etta James’ almost conversational vocal expression, while embracing his classic country songwriting influence through calculated storytelling employing the fiddle and steel guitar. Someone who respects and honors Leon Bridges, Nathaniel Rateliff &amp; The Night Sweats, Marcus King, Durand Jones &amp; The Indications, Aaron Frazer, Michael Kiwanuka—but leans heavily into the sounds of this particular moment. This is a daring explorer who has created a unique fusion of retro and contemporary elements to defy what has been done before and craft a new genre: Texas soul."},{"t":"p","html":"Recently <strong>featured on Tiny Desk Contest’s 2022 Top Shelf</strong> and as an <strong>opener for duo The War and Treaty</strong>, the Houston, Texas artist has more to come in 2023 including upcoming performance dates as an opener for <strong>Madeline Edwards </strong>in both Dallas and Houston (April 2023) and as an opener for <strong>Kam Franklin</strong> and <strong>David Michael Wyatt</strong> (May 2023).&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Micah Edwards:"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.mrtexassoul.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/6098303ecd437570e8d75b78/t/60ed017bc1f2f619459e9833/1626145149802/Untitled+design+%2814%29.png?format=1500w","title":"Micah Edwards","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/p/CmEz1fCJgkv/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"","post":true}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"232476","title":"Read More","date":"2023-03-07","lead":"Singer-Songwriter Alexander Ruwe Releases Melancholic Pop Ballad","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/232476/a156e181942b4d686abcfefbca052459.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Singer-Songwriter Alexander Ruwe Releases Melancholic Pop Ballad"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2NogXxIDbBsziKXEegf3Kq?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"St Louis, MO (March 24, 2023) – “Wandering” is the latest single from singer-songwriter Alexander Ruwe and is a vulnerable representation of not only his writing style but the inner workings of his mind. The melancholic pop song is Ruwe’s personal reflection on tragedy and loss over time. Written when he felt lost and hopeless, Ruwe seeks to connect with his audience through authenticity and storytelling around personal and universal shared experiences.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by the moments of all consuming hopelessness, Alexander Ruwe stays true to the realities of hardship and offers community and comfort in “Wandering.” The goal of the track is not to give a false sense of hope or optimism, but rather remind his audience that, no matter what they are experiencing, they are not alone. The insightful track seeks to encourage listeners to accept troubling moments for what they are while emphasizing perseverance and human connection. An immersive song brimming with cinematic strings, warm pianos, passionate vocals, and descriptive lyrics, “Wandering” tugs at the heartstrings of listeners and evokes immense emotion. In addition to the release of his single, Ruwe will be releasing a music video on March 27, 2023."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521301/large-f9ff475286d58a5520e53b4076ac9a41.png","alt":"Screenshot 2022-12-14 at 1_23_49 PM.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521301/preview-99a37e1ea563d1e47c613aa631164d00.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521300/large-b1c141fd89ad3b31f2442db3b1d81d2e.jpg","alt":"ALEX MULTI_00_00_14_08_Still001.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521300/preview-4c76478cf24cf5a4bba09b7a69023fd8.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521299/large-f156034f763de66d168b574014602741.png","alt":"Wandering Album Art.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/521299/preview-89bfd3d3984d2606ab7e17428fd5e399.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Alexander Ruwe"},{"t":"p","html":"Writing songs since he was just a teen, Alexander Ruwe launched his professional career as a singer-songwriter and artist in his early 20s. In addition to writing music for his own artist project, Ruwe has found success in the industry writing for others. The St. Louis, MO, based artist regularly performs his original music throughout the Midwest, where he captivates audiences with his eclectic song book, and deep, emotive voice. A multi-faceted creative, Ruwe wrote a children’s lullaby which he later turned into a highly praised children’s book. Committed to doing some good with this undertaking, Ruwe donates to World Central Kitchen for every copy of the book, \"Good Night, Little Darlings,\" that is sold. With new music and an album on the way, Ruwe looks forward to sharing his message with the world.<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Alexander Ruwe"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2oUfIt8H527Cz5bheDaMTV?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.alexanderruwe.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/5a4baaa7d55b416671333142/t/5e0f56820eeb83355fdfe3b2/1578063495925/Alex%27s+Businesscard+2020.png?format=1500w","title":"Alexander Ruwe","desc":"Midwest Songwriter, Multi-Instrumentalist & Leader of The Alex Ruwe Band"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/alexanderruwe/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@alexanderruwe","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.facebook.com/AlexanderRuweMusic","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""}],"contact":null},{"id":"225013","title":"J. Matthews Conquers His Fears in Indie Pop EP 'Courage'","date":"2023-03-03","lead":"Debut EP From J. Matthews Gives Listeners a New Perspective on Fear and Perseverance","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/225013/8011aaed35b017eb7f13a6753603ae61.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Debut EP From J. Matthews Gives Listeners a New Perspective on Fear and Perseverance&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7kucgdtRTPHtyKhq8CVXoK?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"North Haven, CT (March 3, 2023) - J. Matthews’ debut indie pop EP, ‘<em><strong>Courage</strong></em>,’ chronicles a series of experiences that grew Matthews into a confident and grounded version of himself. <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7kucgdtRTPHtyKhq8CVXoK?si=lDkIF-9hSAi21QcAKD218w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><strong>Courage</strong></em></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong>is comprised of four indie pop songs, “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5bBCY6pDZmoGT5KErUv4DN?si=fcfd7278ff964a12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Courage for Fools</strong></a>,” “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0y7A8JdY9opmK6wvxOACNQ?si=d04cd1e6d55f4fc4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Wanderlust</strong></a>,” “<a href=\"https://pressedpr.prowly.com/225984-j-matthews-finds-love-when-he-least-expects-it-in-new-indie-pop-single-for-you\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>For You</strong></a>,” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2ujENImvR8c9MNjaMhY3JG?si=561b460239c54ccc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Nothing to Fear</strong></a>” which detail the fears and insecurities Matthews had as he went through college. J. Matthews wrote the EP to encourage people to persevere even when it feels challenging or hopeless. He says, <em>“If you have the Courage to start a journey and stay the course, you'll find that you have “Nothing to Fear” by the end of it. Begin a fool, stay strong, and you'll be unafraid after the lessons are learned.”</em>&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"<em><strong>Courage</strong></em><strong>&nbsp;</strong>opens with a song about the fear of making the first move. J. Matthews knew this fear all too well during his freshman year of college when he let the fear of rejection get in the way of being with the girl he liked. He admitted his feelings to her after several drinks of ‘liquid courage’, but he felt like a fool for never expressing these feelings sober. He follows the opening track with his songs “<strong>Wanderlust</strong>,” a song about the fear of missing out, and “<strong>For You</strong>,” a song dedicated to the girl he fell in love with when he was least expecting it. By the end of the EP, J. Matthews gains perspective on how minuscule his past fears now seem in “<strong>Nothing to Fear</strong>.” The closing track is about realizing that in the grand scheme of things, what once mattered to you years ago no longer matters. He was inspired to write “Nothing to Fear” after coming home from college and seeing the growth he made while he was away. It was a reflective time for him, and he was able to look back on the time that had passed and be proud of the lessons he learned and the progress he had made."},{"t":"p","html":"As a singer-songwriter first and foremost, J. Matthews felt it crucial to have cohesivity in the lyrics and overarching story of <em><strong>Courage</strong></em>. Additionally, Matthews uses the instrumentation of his tracks to elevate the lyrics and ignite emotion in his listeners. Matthews incorporates elements of dance-pop, pop-rock, and alternative, in the indie pop EP which contains moody guitars, ethereal pads, dynamic drums, and emotive vocals. &nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506975/large-9e9dee6ee1ada988894b53089451605a.jpg","alt":"EP Cover.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506975/preview-086de9f26607d9ade66c6e8ee4f051a3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506976/large-0ab6f15337e974c6c879ec6768ba9424.jpg","alt":"JMatt spotify profile pic .jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506976/preview-bd53ff0816bb787b458aa7e7dcea1039.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506977/large-7325f5447864c3e091efce3a94d72329.jpg","alt":"Wanderlust-Distro.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506977/preview-59759f3a58cd4d0985ba7e2769a08755.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506978/large-23d8a66271aca168b49b7ea01c5a4be7.jpg","alt":"Courage for Fools Cover Art .jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506978/preview-370a9c9ef428d72df5745196c0222532.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506979/large-a73320265dbd5cc42c9ec04f99112d4e.jpg","alt":"IMG_0115 (1).JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506979/preview-caf23f0c7a2387574d2d8e8b80bbfeb6.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About J. Matthews"},{"t":"p","html":"A songwriter first, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6LZHdh9JNBz74zevk2t1q6?si=cEXO3RkHRX-LV8JTvg7Gog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>J. Matthews</strong></a> prides himself on his intricate and illustrative lyrics. Matthews started his musical journey spending his days writing poems, songs, and stories to perfect his craft. Storytelling quickly became the centerpiece of his music. Not letting genre define the music he makes, Matthews experiments with an array of genres to create his own unique style. Matthews believes that any story worth telling has its phases, unique chapters, unexpected twists, and his music captures this ideology through an unexpected, yet cohesive, rhapsody. When listening to J. Matthews, you'll feel deep, personal expression in his voice, wrapped around a melody to match, connecting stories that transcend linear genre."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6LZHdh9JNBz74zevk2t1q6?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/officialjmatthews/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@officialjmatthews","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/officialjmatth3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TWITTER</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/officialj.matt97\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@official_jmatthews?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCsxKF-xWmtER7a83Ee4aTEQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YOUTUBE</a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"229028","title":"To reduce cultural barriers, The Trouble Notes have made it their mission to create their own cultural universe. Their self-described \"Acoustic Dance Music\" ...","date":"2023-03-03","lead":"The Trouble Notes Debut Music Video for \"Banjolorian\" and Announce North American Tour Dates","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/229028/e2c11055480d35d1e4973368722c01d5.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Trouble Notes Debut Music Video for \"Banjolorian\" and Announce North American Tour Dates"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3a8FcdGjTJ8JWeycJsppwR?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"BERLIN, GERMANY (March 3, 2023) - Sitting between traditional folk, modern classical, and tribal dance music, The Trouble Notes’ newest single “<strong>Banjolorian</strong>” showcases a playful mix of traditional folk instruments and hip-hop grooves, juxtaposing rural Americana folk and urban rhythms that have been a driver behind the group’s unique sound. The vision for the song came together while traveling extensively in the American west during their <em><strong>Lose Your Ties</strong></em> tour in 2019. In typical “Trouble” fashion, they met brilliant musicians from both the Hip-hop and Folk scenes that shaped the vision for the song, dreaming to create something that would fuse the two genres together."},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/fEuksdJf2FE","height":""},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fEuksdJf2FE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Banjolorian</a> is playful and light-hearted on the surface, but beneath the uplifting melodies is a deep appreciation for the traditions of the genres. <em>“Growing up in the Midwest of America, I was exposed to a wide range of musical influences. Yes, I studied classical music, but my music collection was highlighted by Americana, Rock, and Hiphop records,”</em> says violinist <strong>Bennet Cerven</strong>. <em>“It was these influences that led me to shape the repertoire of The Trouble Notes. '<strong>Banjolorian</strong>' is a nod to those formative years of my life.”</em>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513537/large-d5eb36fc1d2f8c4044342d6702b13079.jpeg","alt":"The Banjolorian_(c) Aurore Florsh.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513537/preview-f2e9368f28a998bb3e04ca2470224d86.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513535/large-f85fd36fe1b3af8af45acd408da315fb.jpg","alt":"The Trouble Notes_Bajolorian_(c) Stefanie Tendler (39).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513535/preview-0ff4edac936f02b295fdcee42636efd8.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513534/large-90c95f62b94df75123a04200213d94fe.jpg","alt":"The Trouble Notes_Bajolorian_(c) Stefanie Tendler (25).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513534/preview-69c0acfff5175b5c66a90a56efd39de2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513538/large-a5babb23e976f623f24b65afe76d9980.jpg","alt":"The Trouble Notes_Bajolorian_(c) Stefanie Tendler (28).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513538/preview-9a0723550d586d2256d77d044fce3b86.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513536/large-8bbd7aa0398a868ea86c1c5aa6e4d735.jpg","alt":"The Trouble Notes_Bajolorian_(c) Stefanie Tendler (26).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513536/preview-3174091c49f3364d999eccac580c030e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513539/large-de4a62b9d8905992f79dc4beb0d5bb2e.jpg","alt":"The Trouble Notes_Bajolorian_(c) Stefanie Tendler (40).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513539/preview-afb89c60f49103983adc724066f86380.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513540/large-2828d7c22e8be322be94b287c70c7792.jpg","alt":"The Trouble Notes_Bajolorian_(c) Stefanie Tendler (42).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513540/preview-06c4466f5ab4400ab129dba55bb23021.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513541/large-1a4349768e2126d94a5745307d17aa80.jpg","alt":"The Trouble Notes_Bajolorian_(c) Stefanie Tendler (46).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513541/preview-4e392e45d77d46cc4fc872c86876d551.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513542/large-52bb7abc0c7adcb1b753f26084e567c7.jpg","alt":"The Trouble Notes_Bajolorian_(c) Stefanie Tendler (45).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513542/preview-9201cb3986a61338326de3833379bac2.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>All photos by Stefanie Tendler.</em>"},{"t":"p","html":"With this release, The Trouble Notes are also announcing their return to North America with the ‛<em><strong>More Violins, Less Violence</strong>’</em> tour slated for the fall of 2023. Showcasing songs from their second studio album <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/1Cq3yTrY1ltI1XC1egbwMf?si=S1iIKTuFQvK4qdHwBF2swg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Liberty Awaits</em></a> and spanning 13 dates from October through November, the band is eager to reunite with their Troublemakers in the US and Canada. Carrying a message of “unity in diversity,” their repertoire brings the traditions of Europe and the Americas together, featuring songs like “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/3mXqWdXOkn4Vc4kWWvGpJ3?si=5f1af4c49dd04c60\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grand Masquerade</a>” and “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/7sWmXDHqMhGzLM0r11304J?si=b4DU0QkCSHiEBbWQ7foEew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Never Dream Alone</a>” that have amassed millions of views and listens worldwide. &nbsp;<br><br><strong>As art and music are a force for healing in this world, one dollar of every ticket and five dollars of every <em>‛More Violins, Less Violence’</em> T-Shirt sold will be donated to a charitable cause helping children affected by violence.&nbsp;</strong>"},{"t":"h3","html":"TOUR DATES:"},{"t":"p","html":"Martyrs - Chicago, IL - 10/26&nbsp;<br style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\" id=\"isPasted\">Drom Taberna - Toronto Canada - 10/29 <br style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\">L’Escogriffe, - Montreal Canada - 11/01<br style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\">The Underground - Boston, MA - 11/03 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br>Sultan Room - NYC, NY &nbsp;- 11/04<br>Milkboy - Philadelphia, PA - 11/08<br>Evening Muse - Charlotte, NC - 11/11<br>The Grey Eagle - Asheville, NC - 11/12<br>Muddy Waters - Columbus, MS - 11/17<br>Jig &amp; Reel - Knoxville, TN - 11/18<br>Mag Bar - Louisville, KY - 11/19<br>Theatre at the Centre Munster - Munster, IN - 11/25<br>High Noon Saloon - Madison, WI - 11/26"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7i1WiSQVIHt4bZz8DhuylF?utm_source=generator","height":"380"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Trouble Notes:"},{"t":"p","html":"Sitting between traditional folk, modern classical, and tribal dance music, <a href=\"https://thetroublenotes.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Trouble Notes</strong></a> have traveled across continents in search of musical influences to give listeners the unrivaled music of the generation. The band has proudly built its diverse audience independently, known colloquially as <strong><em>The Troublemakers </em></strong><em>--</em> a testament to their self-made success story that has led to significant festival appearances, multiple film scores, and an extensive tour schedule spanning the globe.&nbsp;<br><br>In 2017, a series of videos of the band performing on the streets in France and Germany went certified viral, amassing more than 100 million views on social media and bringing them international notoriety. They recorded their debut album&nbsp;‛<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/05lK2OB6LAYFranTHTFxoV?si=fcj90-4pShK4szRGbftwtQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Lose Your Ties</em></a><em>’</em> at Riverside Studios in Berlin, Germany working with Lebanese producer, Khalil Chahine. The album was released in February 2018 and peaked in the top 10 of the iTunes charts for their genre in France, Germany, and the USA. Their music has been featured in award-winning films and documentaries, and their headline “<strong>Lose Your Ties</strong>” Tour featured sold-out concerts in Europe and North America. They have performed live on television in the USA, Japan, Brazil, Germany, and France. And in 2019, they toured supporting Rodrigo y Gabriela as a part of their Grammy Award-winning “<strong>Mettavolution</strong>” Tour.&nbsp;<br><br>Currently performing across Europe and gearing up for a North American tour in the fall of 2023, The Trouble Notes allow listeners to travel across oceans and time with the soulful melodies of Bennet’s violin and Carola’s voice as your body pulses with the explosive energy from Florian’s guitar. Worldly percussion rhythms transport the audience across genres with an uplifting spirit for which The Trouble Notes have become world renown.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Trouble Notes:"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/thetroublenotes/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@thetroublenotes","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.thetroublenotes.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.youtube.com/thetroublenotes?cbrd=1&amp;ucbcb=1","img":"","title":"To reduce cultural barriers, The Trouble Notes have made it their mission to create their own cultural universe. Their self-described \"Acoustic Dance Music\" ...","desc":""},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"229423","title":"Read More","date":"2023-03-03","lead":"Jacob McCurdy Takes a Break From Breakup Songs to Release Love Song \"Feels Like Home\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/229423/541b6c0a0b704311bccefa9c1fc91ffb.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Jacob McCurdy Takes a Break From Breakup Songs to Release Love Song \"Feels Like Home\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0sp5yPbOnKUBHDM2l63B62?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Portland, ME (March 3, 2023) - Indie Americana song “<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0sp5yPbOnKUBHDM2l63B62?si=efdb56d122b54b12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Feels Like Home</strong></a>” is the latest single from <a href=\"https://jacobmccurdymusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Jacob McCurdy</strong></a>, which expands his discography beyond his quintessential breakup music and ventures into the world of love songs. A song about falling in love with someone who feels like home, McCurdy wrote “<strong>Feels Like Home</strong>” at a time when he felt like the world could use more love. During the COVID-19 pandemic, McCurdy began growing tired of writing sad songs. Recovering from a breakup, McCurdy craved the warm familiarity of love and companionship once more. Inspired by this desire, McCurdy wrote the song alongside Alex Calabrese and Phil Holub to tell the story of falling in love on a back porch under waning golden rays. In previous years Jacob McCurdy has achieved many accomplishments for his music, including winning second place at Seabrook Idol in 2021, opening for Dzeko, and headlining a regional tour. Starting 2023 on a high note, <strong>Feels Like Home</strong> is expected to generate numerous new opportunities for McCurdy in the near future!"},{"t":"p","html":"Inspired by artists like <strong>Lake Street Drive</strong>, Jacob McCurdy effortlessly blends his take on soulful rock, folk, roots, and indie pop in the Americana track “<strong>Feels Like Home</strong>.” In fact, Jacob McCurdy and his co-writers originally intended to pitch the song to Lake Street Drive. However, after completely falling in love with the lyrical imagery and dynamic instrumentation of the track, McCurdy decided to release it himself. “<strong>Feels Like Home</strong>” is the first of three upcoming singles for McCurdy, and in addition to his new music, McCurdy will be playing a release show on March 3, 2023 at <a href=\"https://www.mideastoffers.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Middle East Upstairs</strong></a> in Cambridge, MA and on March 9, 2023 at <a href=\"https://pressroomnh.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>The Press Room</strong></a> in Portsmouth, NH."},{"t":"h3","html":"See Jacob McCurdy Live:"},{"t":"p","html":"March 3, 2023 - The Middle East Upstairs in <strong>Cambridge, MA</strong>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.ticketweb.com/event/matt-and-the-skeleton-crew-middle-east-upstairs-tickets/12861315?lt_utm_source=lt_share_link","label":"Get Tickets","color":"#000000"},{"t":"p","html":"March 9, 2023 - The Press Room in <strong>Portsmouth, NH</strong>​<br>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/jacob-mccurdy-his-large-adult-sons-tickets-525114089377?lt_utm_source=lt_share_link","label":"Get Tickets","color":"#000000"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513522/large-1ada76a1b855bcbf47617120a367bdce.jpg","alt":"JM&amp;amp;HLAS BandW.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513522/preview-9ceb2061f3c66f1d78863684b94e1e93.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513523/large-0a33a65795b32982b28cbaaf463ead7d.jpg","alt":"j-027.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513523/preview-312b816fc697c7046f807ef23a9b15c9.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513521/large-6a9688f89822927277c1b3813f62afd3.jpg","alt":"j-022.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513521/preview-0e072ca28f660ff032db51a52b382de2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513525/large-701ded4994e25fe859bbed21a9eb7081.jpg","alt":"JM&amp;amp;HLAS-108color.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513525/preview-9d05f37ea1903caaa911565f2cfe5761.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513524/large-99439115b2ee5af81bd3aca4dcc47e32.png","alt":"Feels Like Home 5x4 FINAL.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513524/preview-955d7e1cddf41f9593f42b5016b04701.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513526/large-f36380dbce894c117538414683f97c20.jpg","alt":"j-026.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/513526/preview-094d4a5e6e83ff1ead11c1c5260fcc4c.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Jacob McCurdy:"},{"t":"p","html":"Portland, Maine-based artist <a href=\"https://jacobmccurdymusic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Jacob McCurdy</strong></a> has spent the past three years perfecting a blend of Folk, Rock, and Roots and transforming it into his very own brand of Indie-Americana. McCurdy’s music often displays love, heartbreak, and joy and is an immersive experience that pulls listeners into a lush backdrop of honest harmony. McCurdy wears his heart on his sleeve, using his music to share past traumas with the hope that anyone experiencing them can begin to heal. Releasing music since 2020, McCurdy has found substantial success and opportunity by voraciously performing his original songs live. In 2021 he opened for <strong>Dzeko</strong>, headlined a regional tour, and entered <strong>Seabrook Idol</strong>, where he won second place for his powerful performance and engaging music. McCurdy continues to perform his heartfelt music live to further connect with his rapidly growing audience."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Jacob McCurdy:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0yA6Qdw3Ntzr0zhAo7T5Yx?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/jacobmccurdymusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@jacobmccurdymusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://jacobmccurdymusic.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://facebook.com/jacobmccurdymusicpage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@jacobmccurdymusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"224703","title":"Latin Funk Single “Be Cool” By The Labra Brothers Is All About Staying Calm And Collected In The Face of Challenge","date":"2023-02-25","lead":"The Labra Brothers Encourage Listeners To Always Be Kind To Others In New Latin Funk Single","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/224703/680ad09d58eddcc25f5ddc8cdc697d34.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Labra Brothers Encourage Listeners To Always Be Kind To Others In New Latin Funk Single&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/42KYjgfT8frK7DYE7g7bYB?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Youngstown, OH (February 25, 2023) - The Labra Brothers inspire their listeners to stay poised and persevere through trying times in new single “Be Cool.” The Latin American band set out to spread positivity and encouragement with this danceable bilingual song. The message behind “Be Cool” is that no matter where you are in life, you should always be kind to one another. Everyone is facing their own highs and lows and you never know what someone is really going through behind their facade. When sitting down to write the Latin Funk single, the band wanted to emphasize the importance of being sympathetic, polite, and respectful to the people you encounter throughout the day."},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"228637","title":"Read More","date":"2023-02-24","lead":"Mother-Daughter Duo Cliffs + Caves Display Their Honest and Poetic Voice In New Song \"Sunrise\"","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/228637/c93124500245e82f07eeb2e614339496.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Mother-Daughter Duo Cliffs + Caves Display Their Honest and Poetic Voice In New Song \"Sunrise\""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/NCrZIeanK1I","height":""},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3gd6rfCQjBnNQvQGKNg4me?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Houston, TX (February 24, 2023) - Mother-daughter duo Cliffs + Caves’ new single “<strong>Sunrise</strong>” is a Maggie-Rogers-esque blend of Americana and alternative pop that transforms the feelings of love and longing into a heartfelt song. <strong>Sunrise </strong>is an uplifting and passionate song about young love - a metaphor for duo member Claire Justice's two-year long-distance relationship.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Cliffs + Caves has been a duo for nearly six years and are thrilled to be releasing their latest single <strong>Sunrise&nbsp;</strong>in anticipation of more new music to come in 2023. Duo member Lindsey Justice explains <em>“creating art with your child is a gift. The process changes as your relationship evolves, and it’s difficult at times but so rewarding.”</em> A musical powerhouse and harmonious team, Cliffs + Caves has learned when to step back and give each other the necessary time and space for independent ideas and inspiration, giving the duo a unique synergy that creates a superlative work of art. Comparable to music from Phoebe Bridgers, Lake Street Dive, and Patty Griffin, <strong>Sunrise&nbsp;</strong>by Cliffs + Caves is an engaging love song for people in all stages of relationships.&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1J0Q7piRpWRQHW9IegFT4X?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Cliffs + Caves"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511134/large-0ef13cc915ba33a36777c595d367e1fb.jpeg","alt":"0E8BE187-25A1-4696-97C5-DB4F2C9733D3.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511134/preview-83f6c6eb8edc1dba3daa5aa321efcd55.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511135/large-d3d6e69e74302db8f7bf65ed96b27597.jpeg","alt":"703DEA4C-864F-4220-94FA-F4CA556A676A.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511135/preview-0c116f8fa32dca26319dd863a55bc020.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511136/large-26f3e2ee6489a47f955f3ce8b9178d5b.jpeg","alt":"BD930B70-B3F7-4AD6-821F-9E570A90D9C8.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511136/preview-8e15e8cabe5b6b85e39077de68250bf1.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511137/large-2b31f6c39567695050539eb26be934e9.jpeg","alt":"38588A65-1700-437E-9235-B00C0B9F23F4.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511137/preview-1d0172d9277d8798397c0dce1f491c38.jpeg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<sub><em>Photos by </em></sub><a href=\"https://www.kirbytrapolino.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><sub><em>Kirby Trapolino</em></sub></a><sub><em>.</em></sub><br>"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://cliffsandcaves.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Cliffs + Caves</strong></a>, the mother-daughter duo of Lindsey and Claire Justice, unabashedly share their deeply personal and relatable stories through songs that resonate with listeners of all generations. &nbsp;Best known in their home state of Texas for their unique blend of Contemporary Americana music, the pair showcases the musical ingenuity that is created when artistry runs in the family with intimate lyrics lilting intrinsically over smooth musical progressions. Their previous discography includes their 2017 debut EP, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/3SanUmvSOsrCrv1A4NlXZ2?si=UWYEvR4vSGyJ09KJ5SMfeQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Hold On</em></a> (recorded with Grammy-nominated producer Jamie Candiloro (Ryan Adams, R.E.M., The Eagles) and featuring performances by legendary Willie Nelson’s harmonica player, Mickey Raphael) and sophomore EP&nbsp;<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/4gEhBjWLd5a66JwQRENwNs?si=elCxyGpETSKflNnG8_iZBA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Capsize</em></a> (produced by Chris Jacobie (Penny and Sparrow, Jarrod Dickenson, Duncan Fellows). The original songs are a team effort with the duo individually contributing to the mastery of their lyrics and melodies. Moreover, twenty-year-old Claire being a multi-instrumentalist, not only composes the music for the tracks but also bestows a knack for songwriting. Their newer music further explores the duo's ability to portray life through lyrics as they evolve into a more alternative Maggie-Rogers-esque sound while still maintaining their Americana roots and drawing inspiration from benchmark artists like Phoebe Bridgers, Lake Street Dive, and Patty Griffin. With a love for writing songs and performing them live, Cliffs + Caves is thrilled to be releasing new music which they will be playing at a variety of upcoming shows in 2023!<br style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Cliffs + Caves"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/cliffs_and_caves/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@cliffs_and_caves","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://cliffsandcaves.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://youtube.com/@cliffsandcaves2211\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YOUTUBE</a>&nbsp;"}],"contact":null},{"id":"228819","title":"Alt-Folk-Pop Artist Alec Rose's Debut Single \"Underwater\" Is Inspired By The Subconscious Mind","date":"2023-02-24","lead":"Alec Rose's Debut Single \"Underwater\" Washes Over Listeners With Raw Authenticity and Vulnerability","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/228819/49956c6780e62cb51f8b1fbd513f26cb.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Alec Rose's Debut Single \"Underwater\" Washes Over Listeners With Raw Authenticity and Vulnerability"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/3sEYezu4CcrExwNyF5Md4x?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (February 24, 2023) - Singer-songwriter Alec Rose just released his debut single “<strong>Underwater</strong>.” During a serene writing session on a porch in LA, Rose let his subconscious mind take control as the melodious lyrics of his indie folk-pop track “Underwater” flowed out from deep inside. Rose quickly realized the lyrics were a reflection of his subconscious mind, and drew a direct connection between the song and a recurring dream he had about breathing underwater. Rose successfully tapped into the hidden potential of the subconscious mind to bring his listeners the impassioned and intuitive song."},{"t":"button","href":"https://songwhip.com/alecrose/underwater?fbclid=PAAaa5PkAvMUlQdpJBFgmb84pit665sD2Ka4_ToBjRcOGLvZkstLDNUC3nF7w","label":"LISTEN ON ALL PLATFORMS","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Multifaceted musician and artist Alec Rose created \"Underwater\" alongside his good friend, frequent collaborator &amp; producer, NICOLOSI. Together they were able to build a dynamic song with a soft acoustic intro that erupts into a powerful chorus with hard-hitting drums, ethereal pads, and spacious vocal layers. With Alec Rose’s compelling signature falsetto conveying his deepest sentiments, the melancholic folk-pop song washes over listeners with immense emotion. Rose’s debut single “Underwater” perfectly encapsulates his original and authentic sound and sets the sonic tone for his future releases."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511472/large-45d3db71630636017db6b7415bca14aa.jpg","alt":"the fountain.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511472/preview-40038fb8db4fa1b9ac119ffe8c56579d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511474/large-418ce864ef9f5afcc987235e2e2d25ab.jpg","alt":"Underwater Artwork (Final).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511474/preview-2d9533195162627c20633bffdcbdc3d5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511475/large-53da421ebaa423e4e51060cf866b5425.png","alt":"The Wheel.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511475/preview-d032811b187e09b30a61fcbeb653b9a1.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511473/large-9db75eeb0b04eeed58c4fd9ef8280abb.png","alt":"Rabbit in the Hat.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511473/preview-76e3229a3f6a86ddf4de4b5cdc577eb4.png"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Alec Rose:"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>Alec Rose</strong> is a Los Angeles-based singer, songwriter, musician and producer originally from Chicago, IL. He is happiest when he is making melodies and effortlessly alchemizing incoherent thoughts into articulate and beautiful lyrics. Rose developed his signature sound around his falsetto croon, lower register ramblings, or top-of-his-range rasp. With heavy influence from Bon Iver, Frank Ocean, Alabama Shakes, and Phil Collins, Rose's music is a captivating fusion of alternative, pop, and folk. Rose's debut single \"Underwater\" is set to release in early 2023 and listeners can stay tuned for music to come!"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Alec Rose"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/alecrosemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@alecrosemusic","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100090103134102\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FACEBOOK</a> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/alecrosemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TWITTER</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@alecrosemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@alecrosemusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YOUTUBE</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"230115","title":"ellakate is an alternative pop singer-songwriter making her debut Fall 2022. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way. To keep up with ellakate, check out her Instagram and stay tuned for new music coming soon.","date":"2023-02-24","lead":"Fear not to fall in love without the consequence of time with ellakate's newest single.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/230115/286fd0eac4d4e028cbb116ea1a3c34e0.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Fear not to fall in love without the consequence of time with ellakate's newest single."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0Dxcg2s3vyMwAQaYK5bn12?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"ATLANTA, GA (February 24, 2023) - Ellakate just released her alternative pop single “<strong>I Wanna Fall in Love for the Night.</strong>” The beautiful ballad expresses her longing to experience love yet the fear of being hurt. One of the most touching lyrics reads <em>“I wanna fall in love for the night, without the consequence of time.”</em> The lyric describes the beauty and passion of the beginning of a relationship that after time, can turn into sadness, hurt, or distance. Inspired by her longing to feel a loving coexistence, ellakate also expresses her fear of what time could do to that love. She says that “Whether it turns sour or fizzles away, one thing is for sure, love is at its most pure form in the beginning.”"},{"t":"p","html":"Ellakate’s soft and soulful vocals are incredibly vulnerable and perfectly complemented with a gentle piano and airy backing vocals. Often compared to a “young Amy Winehouse,” ellakate has a honest and sensual quality to her vocals, mixed with the innocence of her years. While some of her songs could be compared to Billie Eilish, “I Wanna Fall in Love for the Night” is more stylistically like the sounds of Lana Del Rey.<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517668/large-b8c36dd755444762d8058e227dac3545.png","alt":"Cover .png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517668/preview-8e1ef21146cd7bbdd790ebbbcac0de97.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517666/large-21e18815f1083e63fb8e635b8a0096e8.jpg","alt":"EllaKateIWTFILWTN-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517666/preview-271324bf8eef4aba66bac20bacf16c69.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517667/large-3f2b1186f82f0aeea7762de08b42919e.jpg","alt":"EllaKateIWTFILWTN-1-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517667/preview-d5a8de19470b3365135e363b4150d92e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517664/large-c2b439635048508e75308bf479349e43.jpg","alt":"EllaKateIWTFILWTN-5-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517664/preview-6d0e06518aee4ead359ff473b7a5c56e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517655/large-5e57b1fc7bd9069f6a47e1200c5d651f.jpg","alt":"EllaKateIWTFILWTN-17-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517655/preview-94576fead999847672d4317d21d605eb.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517652/large-626f8a0c9d5ab46f9d497ee7256e1a4e.jpg","alt":"EllaKateIWTFILWTN-20-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517652/preview-61c1683dadbb9404680982ea9fdd67dc.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517659/large-4bfc355a3acaea43c737f41d88a28321.jpg","alt":"EllaKateIWTFILWTN-10-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/517659/preview-795883559a75515cfbdf98776d50316a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518485/large-ce341e4089dbddda3c989dacd27bb0c9.jpg","alt":"EllaKateIWTFILWTN-6-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/518485/preview-213f1c4cb9dae303c50ac07e3af192e4.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About ellakate:"},{"t":"p","html":"Ella Greenbaum, artistically known as <a href=\"https://www.ellakate.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ellakate</a>, is an alternative pop singer-songwriter born, raised and based in Atlanta, Georgia. Growing up with musical parents and a knack for creating and performing, ellakate found a passion for music that went beyond forcing her brothers to listen to her melodies as a child. “When my dad first explained what the song ‘Brandy’ by Looking Glass was about, I discovered the magic of storytelling in song writing. I have been singing and making up songs for as long as I can remember,” said ellakate about her innate talents.&nbsp;<br id=\"isPasted\">She has written hundreds of songs since her childhood exploring topics that coincide with the journey of growing up and finding love, filling piles of notebooks in her room with song lyrics. ellakate’s songs recount stories and experiences that may have not happened to her, but are inspired by events that have impacted her."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with ellakate:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0t5IrUFo0RQnOfVkhZplHd?utm_source=generator","height":"80"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.ellakate.com/","img":"","title":"ellakate is an alternative pop singer-songwriter making her debut Fall 2022. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way. To keep up with ellakate, check out her Instagram and stay tuned for new music coming soon.","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/ellakatemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@ellakatemusic","post":false}],"contact":null},{"id":"230258","title":"Apoorva Takes Listeners On a Transformative Journey In New Single \"Phoenix Unbound\"","date":"2023-02-24","lead":"\"Phoenix Unbound,\" the Newest Single From Apoorva, Is the Perfect Blend of R&B, Soul, and New Age","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/230258/3de10f88c290e94ed29802a7bd5e9622.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"\"Phoenix Unbound,\" the Newest Single From Apoorva, Is the Perfect Blend of R&amp;B, Soul, and New Age"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1hNi2QZkmpEj1RizV57oUC?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"New York, NY (February 24, 2023) - “<strong>Phoenix Unbound</strong>” was two years of hard work in the making for R&amp;B and soul artist Apoorva. With her main objective being to seamlessly blend R&amp;B, soul, and new age, Apoorva successfully crafted the song to beautifully and eloquently showcase the story behind the lyrics. A song about renewal, “Phoenix Unbound” is meant to transform listeners and inspire them to achieve their fullest potential.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"Apoorva wrote “Phoenix Unbound” during the global pandemic when the world was shut down and everyone was forced into isolation. Determined to find the silver lining, Apoorva used her time in isolation for self improvement and growth. With vivid imagination, she visualized herself as a phoenix being reborn stronger and more radiant than ever. The idea of the Phoenix resonated deeply with Apoorva, and it became the inspiration for the entire song. In true symbolic fashion, Apoorva wants the song to ignite a fire under her listeners that motivates them to go beyond their comfort zone.<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516943/large-6aa5631b7c51d9305b859178fbc448f8.png","alt":"IMG_3366.PNG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516943/preview-8fe726d5b0f53f70a21370bfd1e38a2c.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516944/large-3b8f6569052f2154fd7c5932dd5f28f7.jpg","alt":"2022_9_10_Portraits_ApoorvaTalanki-785-Edit-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516944/preview-7af696e17ce133273a40e19a21f0c680.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516946/large-4810e5edc6f7317d04b8789da6b575a2.jpg","alt":"2022_9_10_Portraits_ApoorvaTalanki-939-Edit_v2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516946/preview-0bb97bb65917f67c774467577c654efa.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516945/large-14335cdbe622fe9616eb38868b41acb2.jpg","alt":"2022_9_10_Portraits_ApoorvaTalanki-944-EditRedBG.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516945/preview-6329f8965361c27323a3b781c1d9452c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516947/large-1def85b4364a11b231fde9b24805c096.jpg","alt":"2022_9_10_Portraits_ApoorvaTalanki-944-Editv3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516947/preview-a7b22e41e1a59c0dee78bdbf75542b33.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"<em><sup>Photos by <strong>Autumn Stein </strong>of </sup></em><a href=\"http://autumnlaynephoto.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em><sup>Autumn Layne Photography</sup></em></a><em><sup>.</sup></em><br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Apoorva:"},{"t":"p","html":"Born and raised in New York, Apoorva is an Indian-American musician whose name means “never before” in Sanskrit. Seeing as Indians in the American music scene is a rarity, Apoorva set out to represent all people who feel like outsiders with her soulful r&amp;b music. She aims to make her listeners feel that, much like her, they belong too. Although music has always been in Apoorva's blood, it wasn’t always the path she pursued. It wasn’t until after she was accepted into a post-baccalaureate program at a prestigious university that she realized her childhood dream of becoming a professional singer had been buried due to social pressure and fears. It was then that she decided to pursue music full-time. Apoorva draws her influences from Enya's ethereal artistry and Sade's sultry beckoning voice. She brings a new edge to the genres of r&amp;b and soul by incorporating new-age elements into them. Hitting the music scene with a new and authentic genre, Apoorva hopes to take her audience on a harmonious listening experience."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Apoorva"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/55wDP0gmqLCkzARAW96rBh?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/this.is.apoorva/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@this.is.apoorva","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/thisisapoorva_\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TWITTER</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@this.is.apoorva\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"226007","title":"Unconditional Love In Chris Bloom's Indie Pop Single \"Peace of Mind\"","date":"2023-02-22","lead":"Chris Bloom Releases Indie Pop Single \"Peace of Mind\" About A Relationship Overcoming Animosity","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/226007/413df3d95142ec18f421dea0e405f79e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Chris Bloom Releases Indie Pop Single \"Peace of Mind\" About A Relationship Overcoming Animosity"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/6k14GmdoO9TXb5VQoKL2Sp?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, CA (February 22, 2023) - Chris Bloom just released his pop single, “<strong>Peace of Mind</strong>,” now available on all platforms. A song about loving someone unconditionally despite their flaws, “Peace of Mind” details Bloom’s experience with overcoming challenges and mistakes in a relationship. After a relationship has been tainted by arguments and animosity, a couple must decide if they want to continue to be together. The song was inspired by the peace of mind that a couple feels after reaching that crossroads and realizing that whether they choose to separate or be together, they will always have love and respect for one another.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"With a background as a singer, songwriter, and producer, Chris Bloom uses his extensive knowledge of music creation to formulate a distinct sound for himself in new single “Peace of Mind.” The song features rhythmic guitars, raw lyrics, harmonious background vocals, and groovy drums. Bloom has a bright airy quality to his vocals that lead him to be compared to John Mayer, Justin Bieber, and Kid Laroi.<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509897/large-d7d77d8a7e9c1d8aaa0cdd28848d78ba.jpg","alt":"Peace_Of_Mind_Rev (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509897/preview-8b92851afeee10b0ff196940e87d9a30.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509899/large-a0430fd14472d490433b1ebffe2a0ed7.jpg","alt":"2 (1).JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509899/preview-22ac34fc9455df88099a3da78d962267.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509900/large-db38c382cdfd63a873c30fcbdae2f456.jpg","alt":"IMG_0981.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509900/preview-eb5ed21dddf0e33ae351575683df7967.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509901/large-50329febb0622d954ee46f29792b200c.jpg","alt":"dsc06097.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509901/preview-eea62449d462e187e99134978aa81956.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509903/large-6677d339706808ed746e2533acb4b77d.jpg","alt":"dsc06129.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509903/preview-009f4046eef82f5360149b7ca00017b8.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509902/large-0feefa21719783de81de20e209c154e2.jpg","alt":"1 (1).JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509902/preview-7efab862019f4eaed5f5b4a7b0dbe42e.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Chris Bloom"},{"t":"p","html":"Chris Bloom, born Christopher Burkich, holds a fluidity in genres and production. From his first two singles “Learning Curve” and “Petals”, to his latest 2020 EP CAFÉ, his sound has ranged from r&amp;b and hip-hop, to pop and acoustic influences. Bloom grew up in Chattanooga TN, in a household where all types of music were celebrated. This, and being a self-taught singer, musician and producer has allowed him to be a comfortable writer with a distinct voice. At the age of seventeen, he dropped out of high school and moved with his siblings to Los Angeles to pursue music. Since then, he has performed on two North American tours and one Australian tour with Scotty Sire, Sonreal, and Bruce Weigner.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7CHhuFCa2PZXtPhXUY4wVy","height":"380"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/_chrisbloom/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@_chrisbloom","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/_chrisbloom?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TWITTER</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@chrisbloom_?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TIKTOK</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ChrisBloommusic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YOUTUBE</a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"229913","title":"Gianfranco Pescetti","date":"2023-02-20","lead":"Ambient House Single \"Clownspunk\" Brings Out The Light And Dark Energy At Once","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/229913/7a6ca7da83e32f4d70fc8616f0839a6e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Ambient House Single \"Clownspunk\" Brings Out The Light And Dark Energy At Once<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2yu3dg7IETDKDLfUzvOXy6?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"MAUI, HI (February 20, 2023) - Gianfranco Pescetti just released his electronic ambient house single “<strong>Clownspunk.</strong>” This is the second single release from his upcoming album this Fall."},{"t":"p","html":"Pescetti masterfully created a piece that is simultaneously danceable and cinematic. Inspired by the juxtaposing happy and sad feelings of a clown, <strong>Clownspunk </strong>has a psychedelic feel and a gradual build that makes it very intriguing. Pescetti says that <em>“I feel that clowns and the circus have an energy that's both light and dark at once.”</em> As part of his collection of new music, Gianfranco Pescetti has been leaning towards instrumental atmospheric electronica with a dance vibe and interspersed elements of modern indie rock."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516069/large-6e4a5a0c560f42956de7151ee03c1fb1.jpg","alt":"Clownspunk Cover.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516069/preview-bfe61c44737e39a79e7d74367da8248b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516060/large-5ece4b828e02e9240f81870da4c67141.jpg","alt":"_C6A9700 (1)squarer.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516060/preview-f0af146b52312e5a869b57e5b714fcea.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516062/large-22bf2c4533d5a5141d6c653a9ed3285a.jpg","alt":"_C6A9656.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516062/preview-0008f458bdd2f534d7942f35f375b17d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516063/large-7e813493d063cc71bf1f8cfc80e3a744.jpg","alt":"_C6A9682r.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516063/preview-b629d004c4fc82e2a45a6d64ccd82429.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516061/large-7262e5558371dd470bceab4ea9ef2e6f.jpg","alt":"_C6A9804r.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516061/preview-2edc5d24fd29fe6ab3c3ffd719c65e02.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516066/large-148e27110094fd14bf33a4398cd90881.jpg","alt":"_C6A9738r.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516066/preview-f66d0897d440b1df6628efe3cb8df7f7.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516068/large-91e51083ddfb8e98c249ca3bd46fbc7c.jpg","alt":"_C6A9687r.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/516068/preview-1af4f62c94dbee4927006912d1c48dd5.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Gianfranco Pescetti:"},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://gianfrancopescetti.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gianfranco Pescetti</a> is a bass player, composer, and producer living on the island of Maui. Born on the Tuscan Island of Capraia, he studied ballet and music and danced professionally at a young age. In his twenties, he decided to put dancing aside, and turned his full attention to writing music. He moved to San Francisco in 1988 to a vibrant music scene and played bass guitar in several bands. Most notably in Alfred which he formed with cellist Zoe Keating and singer/guitar player Jane Woodman. After playing with his last band, 14 Mission, he recorded his first album Love is Rain in 2014. After a hiatus from music during which he went back to college to get a degree in Landscape Architecture, he returned in 2023 with the new single “Sundog” and a new album scheduled to release this Fall."},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Gianfranco Pescetti"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6ysa2Tfi3Ax4u8SyLuhWMw","height":"500"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://fb.watch/iPaN3Sayzb/","img":"","title":"View this post on Facebook","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.facebook.com/gianfrancopescettimusic","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://gianfrancopescetti.com/","img":"https://d10j3mvrs1suex.cloudfront.net/s:bzglfiles/u/675315/b9fe2ecb5a0622c05b8b36499087a97167c560fa/original/love-is-rain-cover.jpg/!!/meta%3AeyJzcmNCdWNrZXQiOiJiemdsZmlsZXMifQ%3D%3D.jpg","title":"Gianfranco Pescetti","desc":"Home page of Gianfranco Pescetti, from Haiku. Somewhere between the dark side of the eighties and a cinematic soundscape evocative of a bygone romanticism lies the music of his first album Love Is Rai"}],"contact":null},{"id":"222084","title":"Home page of Christopher Morse, a songwriter artist from Boulder","date":"2023-02-17","lead":"Christopher Morse Discovers How To Find Closure and Heal Wounds in Country Folk EP Covering Old Scars","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/222084/644fe30cb68168b1656d792525436e0e.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Christopher Morse Discovers How To Find Closure and Heal Wounds in Country Folk EP <em>Covering Old Scars</em>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/1eKiNKodSUhgSYMnARgB2R?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Boulder, CO (February 17, 2023): Colorado-based singer-songwriter and folk artist Christopher Morse just released his second EP, <em><strong>Covering Old Scars</strong>.</em> An EP about tackling self-doubt and anxiety, <em>Covering Old Scars</em> is composed of four unique and vulnerable songs that highlight Morse’s songwriting abilities. Recorded at Cinder Sounds Studios in Longmont, CO, <em>Covering Old Scars</em> was produced by John Mcvey, and mastered by Grammy-award-winning mastering engineer David Glasser. The EP seeks to be a sonic continuation of Morse’s first EP,&nbsp;<em>Escape</em>, and has the commercial viability of pop music while combining elements of folk, country, and americana.&nbsp;<br><br id=\"isPasted\">“Always Been You,” the first single off of <em>Covering Old Scars</em>, was inspired by the marriage of one of Christopher Morse’s friends. After witnessing their wedding, he began to wonder what his friend’s relationship may have been like had the couple met each other earlier in life. Would the couple have found their way back to each other had their relationship failed in their youth? This experience had Morse asking himself if any of his past relationships could have worked out had they given it a second chance. The song became an ode to the one that got away, and perfectly set the stage for the story the EP sets out to tell. With songs like “Never had,” which further dives into Morse’s unresolved relationship, “Silver Lining,” a song about finding happiness and stability in uncertain times, and “Help Me Out,” a vulnerable song dedicated to Morse’s mental health and struggle with anxiety,&nbsp;<em>Covering Old Scars</em> takes listeners on an emotional journey toward finding closure when all hope seems lost.&nbsp;<br><br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500630/large-f33f6da5c55d947b7b4ccc37c7353af9.jpg","alt":"IMG_4143.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500630/preview-3418971fe3a81a100febe5ada03f1888.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500631/large-8a69eeeed31eda60b2a3c169e3bbcc32.jpg","alt":"IMG_3213.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500631/preview-726c71a8595c2de32e0166b3846a7dcd.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500632/large-6c43312fdb794379db520848e794bf5b.jpg","alt":"IMG_3397.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500632/preview-68698fdb6d30ab538ae6147d312f0231.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500633/large-1bb69409939947b5dc649bff62c55417.jpg","alt":"IMG_3785.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500633/preview-4370fb8976f5bdeeb1de803a2d0a2ca6.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Christopher Morse:"},{"t":"p","html":"Colorado Based Folk Artist Christopher Morse began his musical journey when he was only 10 years old. He began touring with the American Boychoir School, and it was during this time that he fell in love with singing. While on tour he performed at Carnegie Hall, a renowned music venue in New York, and became not only a strong singer but a captivating performer as well. After discovering John Mayer’s <em>Room For Squares</em>, Morse began to learn the guitar for the first time. This transformative experience is what inspired Morse to write his own lyrics and melodies. Before long he was playing his original music in local coffee shops. He gradually expanded his reach to playing in larger venues across the United States, including The Tin Angel in Philadelphia, PA and Rockwood Music Hall in New York City, NY. Morse continues to connect with audiences across Colorado through his passionate and heartfelt performances.<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Christopher Morse:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/1yW5ehXJBJ0BXwCNIZDUDO?utm_source=generator","height":"380"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/christophermorsemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@christophermorsemusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://christophermorsemusic.com/","img":"","title":"Home page of Christopher Morse, a songwriter artist from Boulder","desc":""},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"228623","title":"Tele-Novella Inspired Electro-Pop Single \"Rock (Right Now)\" by Gemïny","date":"2023-02-14","lead":"The Twisted Love Story Single to Release on Valentine's Day","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/228623/067e5dc0a0f2b0d551a8f66f41814430.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Twisted Love Story Single to Release on Valentine's Day"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2w7GMyoule4YD5k5vkFNMo?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"COLUMBIA, SC (February 14, 2023) - Electro-pop R&amp;B artist Gemïny is releasing his single \"Rock (Right Now)\" on Valentine's day, February 14th. A precursor to his upcoming EP <em>My Dark Twisted Valentine</em>, which is slated for release in early September."},{"t":"p","html":"Gemïny describes <em>My Dark Twisted Valentine</em> as a TV series type collection, showing his life as a toxic tele-novella. The EP is centered around a series of recurring dreams that have weaved themselves into Gemïny's reality, with \"Rock (Right Now)\" being the most symbolic.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"The single is set in a flooding jail as Gemïny's dream self is stoned by onlookers, being shunned as an imposter and painting him with hue's of red as an exile. His only source of solace is a young dancer elegantly circling in the violent waters; distracting him from his torture.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511115/large-41c0413db38509baf30bd4fc04cd44eb.jpg","alt":"Rock-(Right-Now)-1 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511115/preview-f9391715fa0521f25716ff0342be6f3a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511116/large-24ac7e4efbeb75ab732a7081f45526f3.jpg","alt":"629921E2 v1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511116/preview-c5956ae6812aa96decf277875ecb31a8.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511121/large-83fc727b1fd80db963a71e326ab6cc31.jpg","alt":"IMG_2297.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511121/preview-3ad6179784c823dae1da771c1149cf09.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511123/large-4b305ebd0afcca7a9bb1c260494e01b2.jpg","alt":"C09FFFE3-8506-4197-9377-599345EC2B51 2 (1).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/511123/preview-a69d91eceb99836cb8f8bd83085ae9f1.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Gemïny:"},{"t":"p","html":"Hailing from Raleigh, NC, recording artist Gemïny is a unique mix of raspy rock, smooth jazz and pop-soul that creates a sound distinctly his own. Before taking a brief hiatus from music, Gemïny studied music composition under John Fitz at the University of South Carolina. Gemïny returned to the music scene in 2020 where he began participating in freelance work recording hooks and background vocals for aspiring artists in hopes of raising money for the National Alliance on Mental Illness. Overtime, this grew into gig work in the local Columbia music scene where Gemïny performed as a background vocalist and pianist for a multitude of bands. With recordings reminiscent of a live show, every song feels like a page ripped from a classic love story; a redefined iteration of the Heartbreak Hotel. 15% of Gemïny's streaming revenue is used to support the National Alliance on Mental Illness.<br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3Wm0Khz27xWSexaDJ95RpW","height":"380"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/minime.ge_/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@minime.ge_","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@minime.ge_\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> I <a href=\"https://twitter.com/minimege_\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> I <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/sage-r-wesley?utm_campaign=social_sharing&amp;utm_medium=text&amp;utm_source=clipboard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SoundCloud</a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"225984","title":"J. Matthews Finds Love When He Least Expects It In New Indie Pop Single \"For You\"","date":"2023-02-10","lead":"Indie Pop Artist J. Matthews Releases Single \"For You\" About Finding The One You Always Dreamed Of","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/225984/dbc9123be566b951b53c65c6b1b7d61b.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Indie Pop Artist J. Matthews Releases Single \"For You\" About Finding The One You Always Dreamed Of&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/0W6I1CwBei8Li65x8K0c9a?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"North Haven, CT (February 10, 2023) - J. Matthews is excited to release his indie-pop love song “For You” just in time for Valentine's day. “For You” is the third song on his upcoming four song EP <em>Courage</em> and is about finding love when you least expect it. He was inspired to write the song after having an instantaneous connection with a girl he met. At that point in time, Matthews had given up on looking for love, and that’s when love found him. Matthews explains <em>“Everyone has an image in their heads of what their ideal partner would be, and we hope and pray that we find that person someday. We've already fallen for them, but we don't always get the chance to meet them in real life. I was waiting to fall for her in real life, and I was lucky enough to find her and have that happen.”</em>&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://freshnoise.lnk.to/ForYou","label":"Listen On All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"p","html":"Singer-songwriter J. Matthews worked hard to achieve an instrumentation that not only elevates the lyrical content of “For You” but also stays true to his distinguishable sound. A dynamic song packed full of emotion and love, “For You” has atmospheric guitars, spacious pads, and danceable instrumental breaks. “For You” by J. Matthews is the perfect love song to listen to while spending time with your special someone!"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509895/large-22ae1d491583a4369ecdcf4307c033c8.jpg","alt":"J. Matthews - For You (no glow).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509895/preview-7d1560611c1f31d6e953b7d84d1410fe.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509888/large-dcbf4f5e7c7235d6f9f5dc65ca5cc494.jpg","alt":"JMatt spotify profile pic .jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509888/preview-135df3d744b31a03ae48171805e3ef9f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509890/large-9aed25396051207a26cde33b4af4b812.jpg","alt":"IMG_0115 (1).JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509890/preview-81235fd0a6eab84ad1c165c8a498b7cd.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509887/large-9a77fb70752b513b5af3946d534ae19f.jpg","alt":"EP Cover.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509887/preview-43097450c90a565b3b3996930e0fe2bf.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509889/large-d404d065c45f372c487c01bb02399f00.jpg","alt":"Wanderlust-Distro.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509889/preview-a71d549af10866157f0d170c8c507b39.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509891/large-4707ef477ab6abec8d784b5962dcd61f.jpg","alt":"Courage for Fools Cover Art .jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/509891/preview-c3d6ec1bb565aa2b601852fb9e3605f8.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About J. Matthews"},{"t":"p","html":"A songwriter first, J. Matthews prides himself on his intricate and illustrative lyrics. Matthews started his musical journey spending his days writing poems, songs, and stories to perfect his craft. Storytelling quickly became the centerpiece of his music. Not letting genre define the music he makes, Matthews experiments with an array of genres to create his own unique style. Matthews believes that any story worth telling has its phases, unique chapters, unexpected twists, and his music captures this ideology through an unexpected, yet cohesive, rhapsody. When listening to J. Matthews, you'll feel deep, personal expression to his voice, wrapped around a melody to match, connecting stories that transcend linear genre.<br>"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6LZHdh9JNBz74zevk2t1q6?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/officialjmatthews/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@officialjmatthews","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/officialjmatth3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a>| <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/officialj.matt97\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@official_jmatthews?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TikTok</a> | <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCsxKF-xWmtER7a83Ee4aTEQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>"}],"contact":null},{"id":"222660","title":"The Hidden Gems Illustrates Parenthood in Debut Single “My Favorite Stranger”","date":"2023-02-07","lead":"Debut Alt-Pop Single From The Hidden Gems Featuring Crystal St. John Is Now Out Everywhere","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/222660/f29aada649b4fac36d72110017ecfb84.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Debut Alt-Pop Single From The Hidden Gems Featuring Crystal St. John Is Now Out Everywhere"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/2DolJwWvwbFs9HrwJVjS5W?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/thehiddengems/my-favorite-stranger-feat-crystal-st-john","label":"LISTEN ON ALL PLATFORMS","color":"#000000"},{"t":"p","html":"Los Angeles, CA (February 7, 2023) - The Hidden Gems is making their debut with alt-pop single “My Favorite Stranger” featuring Crystal St. John which is now available on all platforms. A song inspired by the selfless responsibility and unconditional love a parent has for their baby, “My Favorite Stranger” dives into the mind of a first-time parent. Although neither member of the alt-pop duo has had children of their own, members Robert Murphy and Crystal St. John felt compelled to write a candid song that further explores the internal dialogue of a new parent as they realize their baby is a stranger that will grow into an independent person with their own thoughts and opinions. Murphy says, “My favorite line in the lyrics comes from a friend, actress Marci Miller, who once posted on Instagram about her newborn: ‘We see in colors that we never knew existed.’ &nbsp;We sort of adapted it to say ‘If only we all knew what to do, but these colors are so new.’ &nbsp;There is no playbook for being a parent—you really have to fly blind and grow with your baby, and that’s the message we were trying to get across.” The Hidden Gems have created an enthralling story about the realities of parenthood with new single “My Favorite Stranger”.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"“My Favorite Stranger” was made remotely after Robert Murphy put out an open call audition in search of a vocalist for the demo he had created. Murphy was hypnotized by Crystal St. John's vocal performance and St. John explains, “Robert sent me a demo of the song, and I basically had to translate how this would sound with my voice and my own maternal spin on the song, which I'm not a mother, but I do feel like this was very well fitting because I feel like I'm kind of a maternal personality.” After emailing back and forth for weeks, the duo had come up with the catchy melodies and illustrative lyrics that can be heard in the song today.&nbsp;<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>The duo decided to produce “My Favorite Stranger” as an alternative pop song with hints of 90’s brit rock and Motown. As the process began to progress, Robert Murphy brought in top music industry instrumentalists to play on the track. These musicians included drummer Dan Konopka from rock band OK Go, bassist Sean Hurley who has played with John Mayer, Lana Del Rey, and Stevie Nicks, renowned pianist Michael Arrom, Guitarist Leo Abrahams who produced and played guitar on Regina Spektor’s album \"Remember Us to Life,\" Matt DeMerritt on the entire horn section, and pro synth player Beau Golden. With the help of these musicians, The Hidden Gems was able to create a sound unique to themselves. After the song was recorded, the duo brought on professional mix engineer Ghian Wright, who has worked with the likes of Duran Duran, Nine Inch Nails, and John Legend, to mix the track and meld the instruments together. With hard-hitting rock drums, funk-inspired basslines, delicate yet powerful vocals, experimental guitars, and 80’s inspired synth tracks, “My Favorite Stranger” keeps listeners engaged from start to finish.&nbsp;"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/505549/large-d3bbfebf3c4f6d76ae7c1a2df201d428.jpg","alt":"2158-crystal-blue-poster1-no text.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/505549/preview-fa88152429b9b2fb63104353ebc8614f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/505548/large-c12fc41ad776f75ca27a9498b7692bfd.jpg","alt":"2410-crystal-fave-jacket-A2-no text.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/505548/preview-b824d4358a6bb89953da30aa4f57201d.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/505550/large-796b4265008deaa193c9a4cb77432cb1.jpg","alt":"2497-crystal-robert-park--1-no text.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/505550/preview-a0ac3303fd1fdceb87846e7c9e1079d2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506967/large-953514925dca61091e298a834a9a408c.jpg","alt":"2566-crystal-park-A3-no text.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506967/preview-339454e999b77d02064f59e04d1fa650.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506968/large-b8753cb8308f9b36551dace408b0a5f0.jpg","alt":"my favorite stranger cover - crystal color.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506968/preview-bd38fd47a8dc91716fad504eea87c9d7.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506969/large-e42c0b815d8b04be4ac5238bd09796d4.jpg","alt":"2273-crystal-robert-blue-A4-no text copy.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/506969/preview-5f93c6ba0313c26517f7b5b6739db922.jpg"}]},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/CRqyEJLXX3c","height":""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Hidden Gems:"},{"t":"p","html":"Alt-pop duo The Hidden Gems was formed remotely during the COVID-19 pandemic when member Robert Murphy was looking for a vocalist for a demo he created. After coming across a vocal submission from Crystal St. John, Murphy knew he had to work with her. They began communicating back and forth through email before the duo ultimately created a sound unique to them. They look forward to not only sharing new music, but also a music video for their debut single “My Favorite Stranger” in early 2023!"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Crystal St. John"},{"t":"p","html":"At only eight years old, Crystal St. John embarked on her musical journey. At the recommendation of her music teacher, she began classically training her voice. After gaining performance experience from recitals, school events, and church, Crystal St. John began to write and sing her own melodies. Sitting down at the piano to write music became a therapeutic outlet to process difficult emotions for St. John. She decided to use her voice to help people feel less alone and fell in love with how music could help people find beauty and possibility in their challenges. Since then, Crystal has released several singles on music streaming platforms, including her recent single and music video “Sometimes You Gotta Let Go.” In addition to music, Crystal recently starred in the feature film “Little Town” and has written a book on self-empowerment called “How to Be the Main Character: A Workbook for Becoming the Star of Your Own Story.”<br>"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With The Hidden Gems"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/thehiddengemsmusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@thehiddengemsmusic","post":false},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect With Crystal St. John"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/crystalst.john/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@crystalst.john","post":false}],"contact":null},{"id":"219784","title":"View BRII_music’s Linktree. Listen to their music on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music here.","date":"2023-01-20","lead":"Up-and-coming pop artist Brii Elliss showcases a sultry, rich voice and dynamic songwriting in new single \"Bad Idea\".","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/219784/f84cc1c4576b36063a7009741e1fa5c2.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Up-and-coming pop artist Brii Elliss showcases a sultry, rich voice and dynamic songwriting in new single \"Bad Idea\"."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/7MhRHvcFZ8cfrF85ZHzuFE?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"LOS ANGELES, CA (January 20, 2023) - The third single from her highly anticipated EP <em>Solitaire</em>, “Bad Idea” is about Brii’s experiences dating in your twenties; specifically, a past relationship with someone who could never fully commit. Written during a time when she was feeling especially nostalgic, this intimate pop R&amp;B track perfectly encapsulates the feeling of regret that often comes along with revisiting bad decisions made during previous relationships. \"It came to a point where I ended things because he couldn't give me what I needed and he kept trying to change me into someone I'm not,\" says Brii of the song's inspiration. \"'Bad Idea' is all about going back to an ex when you know it's not going anywhere and know they're not good for you. I've learned that even though it may give you instant gratification and temporary warmth to go back to something that was comfortable, it's a better idea to move forward and not look back.\" A smooth, soothing exploration of the experience of being single in the current dating culture - \"Bad Idea\" shows how fragile someone can be when they're blinded by attraction, yet leaves the listener with a feeling of self-empowerment as they make a better choice for themselves. Working with Grammy-winning producer <strong>Synematik</strong>, Brii's sultry rich tone is on full display as the bittersweet lyrics showcase her brilliant ability to weave her stories into a soundscape that captures listeners and keeps them coming back for more.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://orcd.co/nqyb2em","label":"Listen on All Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493573/large-276587b288ad68337779672cb896ff43.png","alt":"Solitaire Album Cover (1) (1).png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493573/preview-52f2715aec70fb0df5553e1273b406cb.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493569/original-0fac4c5e609b66d6ad2650644ecee1f5.jpg","alt":"image1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493569/preview-d2a6069f439b98a6aca929683a013c00.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493572/large-d883208c47a7d4c95818624439f43678.jpg","alt":"image3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/493572/preview-aa31b9efe598fce3f2f7035c4217aaa0.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494963/large-168106205206004a1a9515720f0a1e4a.jpg","alt":"_MG_1165.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494963/preview-e43dc142f9f8c92abe736bfa147849fc.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494964/large-b3639cf8865a92baffc41bb10995f905.jpg","alt":"_MG_1018.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494964/preview-4e89be11b59fb880e172f45f32ee99c3.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Brii Elliss:"},{"t":"p","html":"Up-and-coming pop artist Brii Elliss is a singer-songwriter who brings a certain closeness to her lyrics, giving testament to the power of storytelling in music. With an Irish father and Puerto Rican mother, her voice and life experiences create a unique blend that filters into her songs effortlessly, showcasing a sultry R&amp;B chill-pop soundscape that captivates and entrances listeners. Working with Grammy-winning producer Synematik to create her signature buttery sound, Brii pulls inspiration from artists like Amber Mark, H.E.R., Snoh Aalegra, Jhene Aiko, and Jazmine Sullivan, with a deeply rich tone that is quickly creating a buzz in the music community. A New Jersey native who has been singing since she can remember, Brii was on the path to stardom by the age of 12, having already auditioned for the famed X-Factor show and made it through several rounds. Throughout high school, she continued pursuing this passion by writing new songs and recording them, honing her piano skills, and preparing to move to LA where she attended college at Loyola Marymount University and graduated with her Bachelors degree in music. As she began to record her own music she realized how much she needed music to be center stage in her life. \"I'm in my element when I am recording and surrounded by other creatives. It feels like home to me, and it's still my happy place today.\" Needless to say, her happiness and passion in the studio shines through her work as her debut single garnered over 17K streams upon release while showcasing her authentic songwriting and silky low voice. Fans have already started rallying behind her and eagerly anticipate what's to come next for this budding artist. Lucky for them, Brii has lots of new music up her sleeve for 2023 and plans to share her soulful vibe with the world... one song at a time.<br style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; box-sizing: border-box; border-width: 0px; border-style: solid;\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Brii Elliss:"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://linktr.ee/BRII_music","img":"","title":"View BRII_music’s Linktree. Listen to their music on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music here.","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/brii_elliss/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@brii_elliss","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@brii_elliss\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tik Tok</a>&nbsp;"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"219794","title":"ellakate is an alternative pop singer-songwriter making her debut Fall 2022. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way. To keep up with ellakate, check out her Instagram and stay tuned for new music coming soon.","date":"2023-01-14","lead":"Channeling a Billie Eilish vibe, ellakate's new single \"It's Not My Fault\" is about when romantic feelings get in the way of friendship.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/219794/10a5a277079c4c0aff028f88937d84cc.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Channeling a Billie Eilish vibe, ellakate's new single \"It's Not My Fault\" is about when romantic feelings get in the way of friendship."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/1zUJ9PqwFeSfQ7LSIBqFyU?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/ellakate/its-not-my-fault","label":"LISTEN ON ALL PLATFORMS","color":"#000000"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"ATLANTA, GA (January 13, 2023) - Rising alt-pop star ellakate's newest single \"It's Not My Fault\" is about a situation where a romantic confession gets in the way of a perfectly good friendship. \"I wrote this song after a guy confessed his feelings for me after I had made it clear to him that I wasn't interested in anything more than friendship,\" says ellakate of the song's inspiration. \"When he came to me, I reminded him of how I felt, and he acted shocked and wounded. The song is written to him out of my sheer frustration at his lack of respect for my boundaries.\"&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"ellakate's musical prowess is on full display as the singer-songwriter displays a voice far beyond her years and a musical ingenuity that carries her lyrics in a driving, uptempo melody. With a soundscape akin to the styles of Billie Eilish, \"It's Not My Fault\" shows off the incredible ability ellakate has to write lyrics that explore topics coinciding with the journey of growing up and finding love. A refreshing voice in the music industry, ellakate's mature yet cheeky take on the topics we all face in life brings a fresh dose of honesty to her music set against the backdrop of striking pop melodies and bold production."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494606/large-b34bfd66e7f94755bc80e381da80d181.jpg","alt":"It_s Not My Fault Cover Art.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494606/preview-1fa6031e121158213cb8d5b9f39daf66.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494605/large-70d36cef0134c56f516a0b4710d38dd9.jpg","alt":"IMG_0715.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494605/preview-ac398a2bfd9241536e9658dc820335e3.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494607/large-574fa17ca0dafcb193f89e4bd3d0cc0b.jpg","alt":"IMG_0662.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494607/preview-081ec59633f0ac659d0cbedb96946ceb.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494608/large-851ca0630560bb1c62129691a3d188e5.jpg","alt":"IMG_0643.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494608/preview-7389e38a3ff9e5aeece75f072974bb2c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494609/large-a24b58f7081984783150ad5067d34efa.jpg","alt":"IMG_0991-Edit.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494609/preview-d498cdbc7ddb1452daadb0b46d327b0b.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About ellakate:"},{"t":"p","html":"Ella Greenbaum, artistically known as ellakate, is an alternative pop singer-songwriter born, raised and based in Atlanta, Georgia. Growing up with musical parents and a knack for creating and performing, ellakate found a passion for music that went beyond forcing her brothers to listen to her melodies as a child. “When my dad first explained what the song ‘Brandy’ by Looking Glass was about, I discovered the magic of storytelling in song writing. I have been singing and making up songs for as long as I can remember,” said ellakate about her innate talents. She has written hundreds of songs since her childhood exploring topics that coincide with the journey of growing up and finding love, filling piles of notebooks in her room with song lyrics. ellakate’s songs recount stories and experiences that may have not happened to her, but are inspired by events that have impacted her. Her voice has been compared to a “young Amy Winehouse”, showing her vocal prowess - honest and sensual, with a hint of innocence. Her sultry vocals mixed with her haunting, bold and romantic sound is reminiscent of artists like Billie Eilish, Tove Lo and Lana Del Rey.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with ellakate:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/0t5IrUFo0RQnOfVkhZplHd?utm_source=generator","height":"80"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.ellakate.com/","img":"","title":"ellakate is an alternative pop singer-songwriter making her debut Fall 2022. ellakate is a breath of fresh air in the musical climate, writing exactly what we’re all thinking and spinning it in a mature, yet cheeky way. To keep up with ellakate, check out her Instagram and stay tuned for new music coming soon.","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/ellakatemusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@ellakatemusic","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"222082","title":"Nilka","date":"2023-01-09","lead":"Bedroom Pop Artist Nilka Goes Back to Her Roots With Reggaeton Infused Pop Song “Luna”","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/222082/c10caa4e2fa149de7d959b9b534b69fd.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Bedroom Pop Artist Nilka Goes Back to Her Roots With Reggaeton Infused Pop Song “Luna”"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/10haRw7sXhsgYwra4RypvA?utm_source=generator","height":"380"},{"t":"button","href":"https://hypeddit.com/nilka/comolaluna","label":"LISTEN ON ALL PLATFORMS","color":"#000000"},{"t":"p","html":"Nashville, TN (January 12, 2023) - Singer, songwriter, and producer Nilka has released her new bilingual song “Luna,'' which is the fifth single from her upcoming album, <em>Sacred</em>. Nilka was inspired to write “Luna'' after struggling with the impatience she was experiencing over the instability of life. She longed for control over her life and grew frustrated with the lack thereof. This frustration fueled her impatience, and she decided to write “Luna” to explore a potential explanation as to where she obtained this quality. Nilka half-jokingly theorized that her impatient characteristic came from her Puerto Rican family. After connecting her experiences to her background, she found it fitting to incorporate her Latin roots by writing the bilingual reggaeton infused pop song about practicing patience. The process of writing “Luna” was a cathartic experience for Nilka, and she says, “creating this song felt very much like painting a self-portrait.”"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500626/large-4d94eabb714d45418473a6665ae09d80.jpg","alt":"PhotoByAnnaKaufmann_IMG_3826.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500626/preview-0dcd84b8b96ce7f89f3d989c8cfa07b2.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500627/large-b4061e3ed1c481f14b65035b6a88ebea.jpg","alt":"PhotoByAnnaKaufmann_IMG_3825.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500627/preview-b35d54d6fa386e56b51b5a7e1a83bb6a.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500628/original-a640092beb27259b24efc7660b8f9c8b.jpg","alt":"PhotoByAnnaKaufmann_IMG_3824.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500628/preview-a5ba2b13d38c41f62dfdecffd06f8e22.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500629/large-02f8e975359057b36439ff880be7fb6d.jpg","alt":"5-luna.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500629/preview-0eaf8a7f2090cb9e44b22bda540159eb.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Nilka:"},{"t":"p","html":"Florida-native artist, Nilka, is transcending the soul-pop genre with her fluid vocals and dreamy bedroom production. Nilka fell in love with creating songs as a young girl fusing her thoughts to a string of notes with lyrics originating back to the early age of nine years old. Five years later she taught herself how to play guitar, cementing her melody-lyric combinations and her pensive songs became like entries in a journal. Songwriting was a way for Nilka to confront experiences in her life and music became her outlet. Throughout grade school, she participated in different bands and choirs where she became fascinated with the impression symphonic music could leave on an audience and she has been inspired by a broad spectrum of genres from Motown to Folk music. In 2014 Nilka graduated from Polk State College with an Associate of Arts degree emphasized in music where she studied Classical Voice. During the summer of 2014, Nilka relocated to Nashville, Tennessee to finish her Bachelor of Music degree at Belmont University in Commercial Voice and Songwriting.<br><br>Nilka has been releasing music since 2017 and during that time has gained song placements on HULU’s series “Light as a Feather” as well as the series “Love Island Australia”. Her songs have been released by EDM labels such as NoCopyrightSounds and Magic Records and now in the next 12 months, she is set to release her first self-produced album project consisting of seven songs that reflect on her spirituality and deepest relationships. Nilka’s lyrics undeniably share a message of how powerful and sacrificial true love is and her music captivates listeners with a soul-moving experience revealing a unique and authentic perspective of the human experience.<br><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Nilka:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/3JED4McgKAqYMqDrPStAxg?utm_source=generator","height":"380"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/nilkamusic/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@nilkamusic","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.nilkamusic.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/58c372cf8419c2ae2beac186/t/5eacbe12625c2f2eff896969/1588379157920/RWEPartworkOG.JPG?format=1500w","title":"Nilka","desc":""}],"contact":null},{"id":"220968","title":"Read More","date":"2023-01-06","lead":"New album ‘Azimuth’ by Mighty Brother navigates audiences towards their own North at the time of reawakening.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/220968/c64cf360b34481c8a1323d414a4837d6.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"New album ‘<em>Azimuth’</em> by Mighty Brother navigates audiences towards their own North at the time of reawakening."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"NEW ORLEANS, LA (December 8, 2022) - <b>‘<i>Azimuth’</i></b> is the fourth studio release from Mighty Brother (releasing December 8th), who expertly knows how to sway listeners with the fluidity of rhythm in their new album that transports the hero myth into the modern day. The term <b><i>azimuth </i></b>describes the angle between North and a celestial object, essentially what sailors use to track their course. Hence, the title hints at the album’s themes of navigating difficult times and trying to maintain a sense of your own personal North. Throughout<b> </b>the themes<b> </b>of the album,<b> ‘<i>Azimuth’ </i></b>deals with loss, normalcy, and rebirth."},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/mightybrother/azimuth-2","label":"Listen on All Major Platforms","color":"#4d6eff"},{"t":"p","html":"Written during the pandemic, the writing process for the album began in the summer of 2020 when Nick and Ari took a month-long writing retreat in Oceanside, Oregon. The ocean view of the Bed and Breakfast they stayed at in company with the host’s generosity by bringing them baked goods daily translated into the album’s energy – a blue horizon mixed with homely sweetness. “Throughout the writing, we also imagined what it would be like to play these songs live. Like other bands, we had to cancel full tours for more than a year due to the pandemic and we were really missing the stage. We felt both nostalgic for the road and hopeful for its return, and poured that love for the journey and the friends you make along the way into the tracks,” they said. “Early on, we decided on making a concept album that would reimagine the Hero’s Journey. We’ve always written very narrative and character-based songs, and wanted to expand on that and see what we could do with a wider story arc. We [also] think it’s important to say that the hero of Azimuth is intentionally unnamed and ungendered,” they added. “I was having a ‘trans-awakening’ of sorts throughout the pandemic. You know, lots of downtime for self-exploration. I introduced a few tunes to the band that directly reference that journey – ”The Breakers” especially–and they ran with ‘em. Felt like a true ally moment, and the songs really blossomed further from there,” uttered Ari."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500099/large-fd0f425f22cf949b8a018895e158af54.jpg","alt":"01 - MB-AZ Press - Photo by Ian Wellman.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500099/preview-3fbe8ca821a4e18b3f7a16ab366bb5c9.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500103/large-3ee5bedbdff393bb765c397b834dedd8.jpg","alt":"03 - MB-AZ Press - Photo by Katie Sikora.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500103/preview-e6b5270d469e81e1293ac26fef744725.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500100/large-e5ef3c99daa124ad57b5d4f2c4273812.jpg","alt":"05 - MB-AZ Press - Photo by Ari Strauss.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500100/preview-f42e22bf8365713d0f11480f2a27f394.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500102/large-9765643dda30f5b5b6adf75a6ed1b831.jpg","alt":"02 - MB-AZ Press - Photo by Ian Wellman.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500102/preview-c02c746f0bfe468fe490299619d32fce.jpg"}]},{"t":"p","html":"Indeed, Mighty Brother intends for listeners to feel invited to see themselves as the protagonist. “<strong>Every Drop of Moonlight</strong>” was one of the first songs the band finished, and is the perfect stage-setting song for an adventure album, as it identifies a character who is motivated toward adventuring out of their comfort zone by a mentor who has left on their own. Hereon, it was easy to imagine the character sailing forward to different islands, twisting and turning through adventures of the heart, art, society, and finally shipwreck.&nbsp;Azimuth is not only an auditory experience but also a visual experience. In addition to a traditional music video for “Rubia Marionet,” a single from the album, Mighty Brother has created an AI-generated music video for the second song on the album, \"Weighed Down.\" \"Weighed down\" depicts the beginning of a tale when the protagonist has first set sail. It is here where the protagonist is experiencing doubt and is questioning their decision. The AI-generated video for the song did an excellent job of exhibiting these emotions by signifying the internal turmoil that occurs as a plan actualizes. The video displays images of a dark tower struck by lightning, a grim church choir, a bed-turned-galaxy, spiral staircases, and a bird floating above a blue expanse. William Huster, a friend of the band, created the AI video and used narrative work, mathematical prompting, and manual editing to create the final product that viewers see.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QCZtpYYUrpM","img":"","title":"We told an AI the story of this song, and fed it some lyrics, and here's the result.www.mightybrotherband.comMade with Disco Diffusion in collaboration with ...","desc":""},{"t":"p","html":"By the end of the album, the protagonist finds themselves marooned and hopeless, wondering ‘what was it all for?’. “I think a lot of us felt that way in 2020 when the work we had been doing, art we had been making, and life and career paths we had chosen were suddenly uprooted. In the end, though, the character finds some hope in the idea of sharing their experience with others, and understanding that there is still a future ahead of them. They have this sort of one-ness with everything, the ego-death moment in “Cliffs &amp; The Ghost”, then are able to head back to the sea” expressed Ari.<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"‘<i>Azimuth’</i> is the first album from the band to be available on 12” vinyl. For more information, you may order the vinyl record on <a href=\"http://mightybrother.bandcamp.com/merch\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><b><u>Mighty Brother on Vinyl: Azimuth.</u></b></a>"},{"t":"p","html":"<b><i>Album Credits:</i></b>"},{"t":"p","html":"Recorded at Marigny Studios in New Orleans, LA"},{"t":"p","html":"Engineer: Justin Armstrong"},{"t":"p","html":"Mixing Engineer: Nathan Feler"},{"t":"p","html":"Mastering Engineer: David Farrell<br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/KV0yFN7OibE","height":""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<b>Mighty Brother</b> started as a songwriting duo in 2015, composed of Nick Huster and Ari Kirkman. Eventually growing to a five-piece indie rock outfit to include band members <b>Jonah Devine Tarver (Saxophone)</b>, <b>Quinn Sternberg (Bass)</b>, and <b>Nicholas Solnick (Drums)</b>, Mighty Brother was quick to carve out two musical successes with <b>Jettison, Reprise</b> <b>(2015)</b> and <b>The Vibe EP (2017)</b>. The band, who describes their sound as groovy and flavorful, has been influenced and inspired by the likes of Grizzly Bear, Radiohead, Bon Iver, The Decemberists, Avett Brothers, Alt-J, and several other musical acts. This menagerie of influences led to Mighty Brother’s indie-rock sound that also pays tribute to folk, singer-songwriter, funk, and alternative soundscapes. Having toured the globe on tours spanning from the United States to New Zealand, Mighty Brother performs as if they were actively conversing with the crowd, drawing listeners in for an engaging experience. This energy is translated into their music, proven through the tracks of their double album release <b>The Rabbit </b>and <b>The Owl (2020)</b>. Now, the band is poised for even greater heights with their 2022 return for <b>‘Azimuth’</b>. Stay tuned!&nbsp;&nbsp;"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/5JMMFl90guPresBKQ9Y0To?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://mightybrotherband.com/","img":"","title":"New Orleans Indie Rock Band Mighty Brother, nationally touring 5-piece band with a sound that ranges from avett-americana to radiohead-esque art rock.","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.facebook.com/MightyBrotherBand/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/mightybrotherband/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@mightybrotherband","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://twitter.com/mightybother","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"220972","title":"Masculinity Exposed: John Zdrojeski (as Virgil Wilde) Releases New Rock Album ‘Misters’ Confronting Toxicity Head-On","date":"2023-01-06","lead":"John Zdrojeski (under pseudonym Virgil Wilde) releases blistering new \"rock-worshipping epic\" deconstructing white American masculinity.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/220972/990fded75878f4b035a51f6372bfd09d.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"John Zdrojeski <em>(under pseudonym <strong>Virgil Wilde</strong>)</em> releases blistering new \"rock-worshipping epic\" deconstructing white American masculinity."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"BROOKLYN, NEW YORK (November 17, 2022) - &nbsp;On December 8th, <strong>John Zdrojeski</strong> will release his debut album ‘<strong>Misters</strong>’, and promote it as his alter-ego: <strong>Virgil Wilde</strong>. In the vein of David Bowie as Ziggy Stardust, Virgil is a character from the album, which explores the stifling effects of toxic white masculinity. Inspired by Dante's Inferno, Misters deals with Jack, a man struggling to “sing his song” in the midst of an aggressive, disjointed choir. With a squeal of guitar feedback, a ravaged, rock star channeler named Virgil Wilde appears to Jack. Virgil morphs into each member of the choir, known as <strong>\"The Misters\"</strong>, hoping to dull their power over Jack’s song by doing so. But periodically, Jack is overtaken by the <em>Devil You Know&nbsp;</em>: a polished, mirror image of Virgil, who uses every tactic he can to get Jack to abandon his own unique song. Not shying away from a difficult topic, Zdrojeski hopes Misters contributes to the dialogue about the ill effects of the patriarchy not only on society, but on men themselves.&nbsp;"},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/johnzdrojeski/misters","label":"Listen on All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/5FGEhueYoqCWKvR0GxpsYE?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"Sonically weaving through prog rock, country rock, alternative, glam rock, and classic heavy metal among other different sub-genres, Misters pays homage to rock 'n' roll, exploring Zdrojeski's love of the music itself while tackling the controversial topics. The epic begins with \"In The Weeds\" as our protagonist, Jack, is surrounded on all sides by the toxic voices of the Misters. Following that, Virgil introduces himself in the 70’s-inspired, riff-tastic thunderbolt invocation, \"O Rock N’ Roll.” And finally, &nbsp;the third and final voice - our antagonist - reveals himself in the guise of moody, mysterious industrial rock in \"Devil You Know I\". As the album continues, each “Mister” Virgil channels embodies a different trope: male hypocrisy, male apathy, and performative machismo, with more unconventional themes and archetypes popping up along the way. Overall, ‘<strong>Misters</strong>’ is a rock 'n' roll epic, promising to be a rollicking action movie-musical of the mind."},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500119/large-fce7645c7511ba1573bad0f60b951d77.jpg","alt":"1. Misters Album Cover.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500119/preview-65be6a01ffbbcdb6e08365864bd69e31.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/496793/original-c0ccd9a3604c22162e03fa5ef59e92a5.jpg","alt":"10+Inner+Sleeve+Photo+1.1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/496793/original-c0ccd9a3604c22162e03fa5ef59e92a5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500114/large-0f30bbb3be2dfc6f5e92d3622411cc9f.jpg","alt":"9 Inner Sleeve Photo 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500114/preview-b9daf40e62215455d5a91a2264bf2d7c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500111/large-d7a8a4ab8129ab375f8691122d3413a2.jpg","alt":"2 Virgil Promo 1.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500111/preview-dc22595177cc379b395eb805af12fb4f.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500109/large-edbad98240acf7560624fa0d3160c827.jpg","alt":"4 Virgil Promo Alt 2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500109/preview-f5a061a0cc90d63ee26bffa197fe105e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500112/large-073a432e2c17f01090458ad8b656559e.jpg","alt":"7 Virgil Promo Alt 4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500112/preview-348602ea8713bdd4a75484a66295ad70.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500110/large-d1aca9efed22bf3c8b2fb3a2a65d74b6.jpg","alt":"5 Virgil Promo Alt 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500110/preview-46d89ba4be1b11b86f43d03e4f616232.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"\"Story behind these songs? You try being locked away with the Misters for as long as you can remember and writing about anything else. But see, what I think you’re really asking is: why rock ‘n’ roll? And that’s cuz I had to find a way to tune them out, to cut through their noise, to sing my song despite them to trying to shout me down. I think that’s what we all want to do, right? Sing our songs? You might say it different than me but deep down, you know what I mean. I needed firepower, I needed lightning to come out of my hands, I needed volume that makes you catch your breath. I needed Oasis at Knebworth, Ziggy at the Odeon. I needed the feeling you get when Axl tells you to wake up cause you’re gonna die. And rock ‘n’ roll, despite those who would tear it down, or sully its name, or declare it dead, is nothing if not a divine middle finger to something. In my case, it was to the Misters. And how do you do that? Show 'em off to the world, and tell no lies. In fact, if they ever get me, if the Misters ever do shut me up, let my epitaph be these nine words: &nbsp;<br><br>Sing your song. Tell no lies. Rock ‘N’ roll.\"<br><br>- Virgil Wilde"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"<strong>About John Zdrojeski:</strong>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500119/large-fce7645c7511ba1573bad0f60b951d77.jpg","alt":"\nCover art for Misters by John Zdrojeski as Virgil Wilde."},{"t":"p","html":"John Zdrojeski is a performing artist based out of Brooklyn, NY. An Obie award winning actor as well as a singer/songwriter, <strong>John combines the unapologetic theatricality of David Bowie, the off-beat lyrical bite of Warren Zevon, and the riff-driven, melodic rock 'n' roll of Oasis into one undeniably charismatic package</strong>. John’s first release was the five-song EP Primitive. Chronicling the life cycle of a relationship, its music was heavily influenced by the work of Nick Drake, Joni Mitchell, and Bon Iver. Of “Madness,” Primitive’s climax, The Wild is Calling wrote: <strong>“John patiently weaves his narrative like a maze that only he knows the route through, breaking between lines, dancing around his melody but never repeating it exactly. Without knowing his face, you can see him, alone under the spotlight on the stage, a delivery so natural, you swear he’s writing it on the spot.”</strong>&nbsp;<br><br>For the follow-up, John has taken all the theatrical impulses hinted at on Primitive and turned them up to eleven. Engineered by the <strong>Grammy-nominated Tom Gardner</strong> (Chromeo) and mastered by the <strong>Grammy-nominated Joe Lambert</strong> (The National), Misters, his forthcoming full-length debut, is an exploration of white American masculinity through classic, rollicking, riff-driven rock ‘n’ roll. Blog Given To Rock described \"Snake Oil Strongman,\" as \"having a contagious groove with dynamic vocals.\" Roadie Music described another single, \"Fragile,\" as \"having a pulse you should savor and will make you sweat.\" To promote Misters live, John adopts the persona of Virgil Wilde: the ravaged, muscle-shirt wearing, guitar-slinging rock star. Described by one audience member as <strong>\"part Rocky Horror Picture Show, part Joker, and part Elvis with a heavy dose of 70's glam rock,\"</strong> Virgil Wilde is the main character from the album, and came about when John decided to create the rock show he always wanted to see. Since his official birth in 2022, Virgil Wilde has brought the house down at several iconic venues in New York City, and John plans to debut a one-man show as Virgil in 2023.<br><br>"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/boomerzdr/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@boomerzdr","post":false},{"t":"p","html":"<a href=\"https://www.johnzdrojeski.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><u>Website</u>&nbsp;</a>| <a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/artist/john-zdrojeski/1462979116\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><u>Apple Music</u></a> | <a href=\"https://music.youtube.com/channel/UCcC1_uywzC81zfJJ3aF_ykA?feature=share\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><u>YouTube</u></a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"221694","title":"Elder Grown- Funkalicious Rock'n Roots Music","date":"2023-01-05","lead":"Elder Grown brings unique genre-bending music to the stage at The Sherbino Theater in Ridgway, CO","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/221694/2e063a03cb7941e5dc88bb1b3020a8db.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Elder Grown brings unique genre-bending music to the stage at The Sherbino Theater in Ridgway, CO"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499634/large-33370a47d262f7c14e447b2d5a0d3fe0.jpg","alt":"IMG_8601.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"RIDGWAY, CO (February 4, 2023) - On Saturday, February 4th, Elder Grown will be performing at The Sherbino in Ridgway, Colorado. This unique band blends funk, rock, pop and hip hop into a captivating sound that is sure to get your feet moving. Switching instruments mid-song, you never know what instrument anyone in the band will be playing or who will be singing next! Blending improvisational jams with captivating originals, this band brings an evening of music that breaks all the rules and journeys into the unrecognizable familiar, resulting in a night you won't forget! Tickets are available now at the link below.<br style=\"box-sizing: border-box; border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: rgba(226,232,240,var(--tw-border-opacity)); --tw-border-opacity:1; --tw-shadow:0 0 transparent; --tw-ring-inset:var(--tw-empty, ); --tw-ring-offset-width:0px; --tw-ring-offset-color:#fff; --tw-ring-color:rgba(0,38,234,0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow:0 0 transparent; --tw-ring-shadow:0 0 transparent; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: &quot;Inter var&quot;, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;; font-size: 17.5px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: pre-wrap; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://sherbino.org/event/elder-grown/","label":"Ticket + Event Information","color":"#727070"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499633/large-6d028ee8fd7218c076d3a3ea06d81a45.jpg","alt":"EH3A8810.jpg"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Elder Grown:"},{"t":"p","html":"Family and community are the roots of the band Elder Grown. &nbsp;A band of brothers and sisters. &nbsp;Though the group is made up of five guys from Durango, Colorado, they consider every audience to be their 6th collective member; their heartbeat, medicine, and reason for song.Funk meets Pop, Rock meets Hip Hop, Jazz meets Reggae. &nbsp;Elder Grown uses the freedom of improvisational jams as their foundation to create their captivating, soul-inspired sound. &nbsp;From the set opener to the fourth hour, Elder Grown encourages you to break down your ideas of genre with your hips and heartbeat. &nbsp;The band takes listeners on a genre-bending rollercoaster through a menagerie of rule-breaking sound, often switching instruments mid-song. &nbsp;Start with groovy, funk inspired bass lines reminiscent of Motown meeting the Red Hot Chili Peppers. &nbsp;Then, add screaming soprano guitar and bossy sax lines reflective of Pink Floyd and Maceo Parker. &nbsp;Finish it off with inspiration from Rage Against the Machine, Atmosphere, and Sublime and you are beginning to understand the sound that is Elder Grown. &nbsp;Brothers and Sisters, you are invited to embark on a journey into the unrecognizably familiar.&nbsp;<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Elder Grown:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"http://eldergrownmusic.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/56b56c938259b57383073e49/t/586435aabebafbe2173742ca/1482962346931/EG+Green+CircleTiny.png?format=1500w","title":"Elder Grown- Funkalicious Rock'n Roots Music","desc":"Colorado based professional funk, rock, roots, and soul band. Check Elder Grown's tour schedule and see where they're touring next."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/eldergrown/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@eldergrown","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/ElderGrown\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ElderGrown/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.bandsintown.com/a/1142918?came_from=257\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BandsinTown</a> |<a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/album/elder-grown/1376637581\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> Apple</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"221699","title":"Elder Grown- Funkalicious Rock'n Roots Music","date":"2023-01-05","lead":"Elder Grown brings their unique genre-bending music to the stage in Buena Vista, CO","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/221699/f68477a1264d574eeae4f15b8fde2d21.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"Elder Grown brings their unique genre-bending music to the stage in Buena Vista, CO"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499634/large-33370a47d262f7c14e447b2d5a0d3fe0.jpg","alt":"IMG_8601.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"BUENA VISTA, CO (January 21, 2023) - On Saturday, January 21st, Elder Grown will be performing at The Lariat in Buena Vista, Colorado. This unique band blends funk, rock, pop and hip-hop into a captivating sound that is sure to get your feet moving. Switching instruments mid-song, you never know what instrument anyone in the band will be playing or who will be singing next! Blending improvisational jams with captivating originals, this band brings an evening of music that breaks all the rules and journeys into the unrecognizable familiar, resulting in a night you won't forget! Tickets are available now at the link below.<br style=\"box-sizing: border-box; border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: rgba(226,232,240,var(--tw-border-opacity)); --tw-border-opacity:1; --tw-shadow:0 0 transparent; --tw-ring-inset:var(--tw-empty, ); --tw-ring-offset-width:0px; --tw-ring-offset-color:#fff; --tw-ring-color:rgba(0,38,234,0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow:0 0 transparent; --tw-ring-shadow:0 0 transparent; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: &quot;Inter var&quot;, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;; font-size: 17.5px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: pre-wrap; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://thelariatbv.com/event/elder-grown/","label":"Event Info","color":"#434246"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499633/large-6d028ee8fd7218c076d3a3ea06d81a45.jpg","alt":"EH3A8810.jpg"},{"t":"h3","html":"About Elder Grown:"},{"t":"p","html":"Family and community are the roots of the band Elder Grown. &nbsp;A band of brothers and sisters. &nbsp;Though the group is made up of five guys from Durango, Colorado, they consider every audience to be their 6th collective member; their heartbeat, medicine, and reason for song. Funk meets Pop, Rock meets Hip Hop, Jazz meets Reggae. &nbsp;Elder Grown uses the freedom of improvisational jams as their foundation to create their captivating, soul-inspired sound. &nbsp;From the set opener to the fourth hour, Elder Grown encourages you to break down your ideas of genre with your hips and heartbeat. &nbsp;The band takes listeners on a genre-bending rollercoaster through a menagerie of rule-breaking sound, often switching instruments mid-song. &nbsp;Start with groovy, funk inspired bass lines reminiscent of Motown meeting the Red Hot Chili Peppers. &nbsp;Then, add screaming soprano guitar and bossy sax lines reflective of Pink Floyd and Maceo Parker. &nbsp;Finish it off with inspiration from Rage Against the Machine, Atmosphere, and Sublime and you are beginning to understand the sound that is Elder Grown. &nbsp;Brothers and Sisters, you are invited to embark on a journey into the unrecognizably familiar.&nbsp;<br id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Elder Grown:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/2goH9cMI15q2lSTHCkrZCO?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"http://eldergrownmusic.com/","img":"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/56b56c938259b57383073e49/t/586435aabebafbe2173742ca/1482962346931/EG+Green+CircleTiny.png?format=1500w","title":"Elder Grown- Funkalicious Rock'n Roots Music","desc":"Colorado based professional funk, rock, roots, and soul band. Check Elder Grown's tour schedule and see where they're touring next."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/eldergrown/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@eldergrown","post":false},{"t":"lead","html":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/ElderGrown\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ElderGrown/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"https://www.bandsintown.com/a/1142918?came_from=257\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BandsinTown</a> |<a href=\"https://music.apple.com/us/album/elder-grown/1376637581\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> Apple</a>"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"221993","title":"Read More","date":"2023-01-05","lead":"To Heal Her Too is the long-awaited follow up to previously loved To Heal Her, Diving Inward for Self-Reflection","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/221993/58f4fe63462940b3384f15ceda001049.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"<em>To Heal Her Too</em> is the long-awaited follow up to previously loved <em>To Heal Her</em>, Diving Inward for Self-Reflection"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/4CNIC9X7N4c337djWg6y1s?utm_source=generator","height":"380"},{"t":"button","href":"https://distrokid.com/hyperfollow/haleyharkin/to-heal-her-too","label":"Listen On All Platforms","color":"#67676b"},{"t":"p","html":"FORT COLLINS, CO (January 6, 2023) - Folk singer-songwriter Haley Harkin is excited to announce the release of her new album <em>To Heal Her Too</em>, the long-awaited follow-up to her 2021 album <em>To Heal Her</em>. The album, which will be available exactly one year after the release of its predecessor on January 6th, fearlessly explores the outward experience of self-reflection and the pursuit of finding ways to be of service to the world, earth, and humanity.&nbsp;<br>"},{"t":"p","html":"Just as it's precursor delivered a stunning showcase of vulnerability, <em>To Heal Her Too</em> delves into the pain of being human, while also finding hope and resilience in the face of suffering. Harkin caresses her raw lyricism in a comforting acoustic warmth, creating a playful and whimsical touch with instruments like triangles, tambourine, and conga drums inspiring a lively and energetic feel. The simplicity of her arrangements allows the music’s inherent beauty to shine through with an unfiltered brilliance and draws resemblance to artists like Rising Appalachia, Watchouse, and Ayla Nereo. Harkin is proud to present some of her favorite songs on this new album, including \"I Am The Key\" and \"Teacher,\" which were produced by Vince Cimo, a well-known producer for Ayla Nereo. \"Creating an album is an act of self discovery,\" says Harkin. \"I get to know myself, the songs, and the creative channel more and more. I am really happy with how it turned out, some of my favorite songs are on this album.\""},{"t":"p","html":"Harkin will be celebrating the release of <em>To Heal Her Too</em> with an album release party at Wolverine Farms in Fort Collins on January 7th. She invites all fans to come and celebrate this exciting new release, which touches on themes of nature, Mother Earth, and the connection to nature.<br>"},{"t":"button","href":"https://www.wolverinefarm.org/product/haley-harkin-album-release-concert-doors-6pm/","label":"Event Info","color":"#404040"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500000/original-f81f9420893b267bb31ee88853ff6af5.png","alt":"Untitled Art Cover.png","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/500000/preview-fb28536c1b4f028223af3ce2cf142f06.png"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499999/large-9fab23a69db73b5a249ba6843ecb9a39.jpg","alt":"PC136629.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499999/preview-1c3fc5b2fca4e91d21b4740e6841ce21.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499998/large-231cc3a8f21f177c455c3466865fefad.jpg","alt":"PC136627.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499998/preview-ab6da6b038b21fff8e02b6ba3075e56b.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499997/large-118d7f98d5d3c07f21a81fef108bf695.jpeg","alt":"e75ea9bbb46a806fe596c6780ffa10c8.jpeg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499997/preview-f287b91aa158254ebdc35b5e05157dd7.jpeg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499996/large-563f7a86d3cc62b0059c5a14b3036ac9.jpg","alt":"PC136678.JPG","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/499996/preview-e9a16d050ac2d56eccf63e6852aa8906.jpg"}]},{"t":"h3","html":"About Haley Harkin:"},{"t":"p","html":"Haley was born and raised in Austin, TX, and is currently residing in Colorado. Surrounded by music most of her life, her roots are in folk, while pushing the edges of creativity. With music that feels like \"bare feet on grass\", Harkin describes her style as \"folk medicine\" as her lyrics express her love for nature, humanity, and her desire to make change. Harkin's sultry sounds in previous releases have garnered praise within the folk industry with <em>303 Magazine</em> claiming, “The seven-song album brings the passionate and solemn yet feel-good vibes that are induced from Joni Mitchell’s Blue or something from the Elephant Revival catalog.”"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with Haley Harkin:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/4NVY9moD4gj1RJpVfWgz5S?utm_source=generator","height":"380"},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/haleyharkin/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@haleyharkin","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.haleyharkin.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"lead","html":"FACEBOOK | TWITTER"},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}},{"id":"220974","title":"Read More","date":"2023-01-02","lead":"A song about miracles, STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION’s new track “SPARKLES” is about what we leave behind.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/220974/0e6663df0060f392adfa0ed3a65605bc.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"p","html":"<b><i>A song about miracles, STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION’s new track “SPARKLES” is about what we leave behind.</i></b>"},{"t":"img","src":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/496794/large-49e0beb5e71ed6be416a1fed37ee9e3c.jpg","alt":"SPARKLES.jpg"},{"t":"p","html":"TOKYO, JP (November 15, 2022) - <b>“SPARKLES”</b>,<b> </b>STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION’s song for the movie <b><i>That Time I Got Reincarnated as a Slime</i></b>, is a pop ballad blend of pleasing melodies and creative arrangement that emanates tranquility and leaves SDF audiences in awe. Out November 25th, “SPARKLES” is a tease for fans as SDF tours for his burgeoning US audience, showcasing his vastly growing local roots in the United States. Written about how what we leave behind is more important than what we receive in life, SDF hopes that the song will spark positive emotions that listeners can relate to for various situations in their own lives."},{"t":"button","href":"https://lnk.to/LZC-2285p","label":"Listen on All Major Platforms","color":"#614DFF"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/6yLTrq59HxfE6aTq8r4gVP?utm_source=generator","height":"352"},{"t":"p","html":"With over 217K monthly listeners on Spotify, <strong>STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION (SDF)</strong> is a sound-creating project of songwriter/music producer <strong>RON</strong>, who not only releases music under its own name but also produces various sound contents and music for varieties of popular Japanese artists and top-rated Anime TV series. Known for his Asian-pop vibe, SDF’s music journey began at the young age of 4 when he started playing the piano and that led him to create his own music by the time he reached high school. His audition with Sony in 2001 became a defining moment in his life and changed the trajectory of his music career, which led him to sign with Lantis (and is currently signed with <strong>Lantis</strong>). SDF describes his music as <strong>a mixture of piano and melodic sounds</strong>. And with this crossover, he hopes his creative arrangement will resonate with his US audience. With SDF’s work being 90% anime music and subscription services that provide accessible access to anime, the chance of listening to anime-related music in the US has increased significantly. Currently, on his North American Showcase tour in support of the latest <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/5FW8M5cMPA24iL0TNT2Ojg?si=0vZDMVf9RWO4PuRtMGvmjQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong><em>STEREO DIVE 02</em></strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em>album, SDF hopes that this single will be a pleasing gift for American fans and will further establish his presence in the States."},{"t":"h3","html":"|"},{"t":"p","html":"<b>Connect with STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION:</b>"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://stereodivefoundation.jp/","img":"","title":"STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.youtube.com/c/STEREODIVEFOUNDATIONOfficialChannel?cbrd=1&amp;ucbcb=1","img":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/ytc/AMLnZu8uFUouVcATNbK4o7EURT3xgWWXYxx4zgi9wexS=s900-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj","title":"STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION Official Channel - YouTube","desc":"\"STEREO DIVE FOUNDATION\" is the sound making project of RON, who is also active as a music producer.He is in charge of theme songs of animes popular outside..."},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/ron_sdf/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@ron_sdf","post":false},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://twitter.com/RON_SDF","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":null},{"id":"219933","title":"To reduce cultural barriers, The Trouble Notes have made it their mission to create their own cultural universe. Their self-described \"Acoustic Dance Music\" ...","date":"2022-12-13","lead":"The Trouble Notes’ “Never Dream Alone” is a fantastical folk-pop ode to dreamers inspired by the cosplay community.","hero":"https://prowly-prod.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/landing_page/cover_photo/219933/b7f6dba0de9f6009ddd49ac322566d05.jpg","blocks":[{"t":"lead","html":"The Trouble Notes’ “Never Dream Alone” is a fantastical folk-pop ode to dreamers inspired by the cosplay community.<br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://youtube.com/embed/zzV6pTAZ8sM","height":""},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"p","html":"BERLIN, GERMANY (December 15, 2022) - Sitting between traditional folk, modern classical, and tribal dance music, The Trouble Notes' newest single “Never Dream Alone” is a fantasy-tinged folk-pop anthem. Written for and filmed at the 2022 Summer edition of Elfia, Europe's largest outdoor Cosplay festival, the video showcases the energy of the song with vibrant visuals and eclectic costumes - inspiring listeners to embrace their dreams and imagination.&nbsp;"},{"t":"p","html":"A call to embrace the fantastic, wonderful and weird, “Never Dream Alone” showcases the band’s quintessential classical-cross-over style, holding elements of an epic film score within the structure of a modern Folk Pop song. The fantasy-tinged violin melodies and string arrangements are a nod to the epic scores of the genre, while the operatic vocals of Carola Zerega and Bennet Cerven carry the message of unity in diversity. On full display is the energetic rhythms of the mind-blowing percussionist Oliver Maguire, whose unique hand drumming techniques elevates the listener to new heights. Florian Eisenschmidt’s rock inspired riffs on guitar are the backbone on which pianist Frederic Dubois creates the harmonic soundscapes that shape “Never Dream Alone” and bring the listener into a fairytale realm with unity at its core. “‘Never Dream Alone’ is an epic ode to the dreamer,” says Bennet Cerven, Violinist for The Trouble Notes. “It was an easy song for us to write because we have always identified ourselves as such. We wanted to create a piece of music that captures the fantastic spirit of our favorite films and stories while being inclusive and easy to sing along to!” Overall, this track will take you on an auditory journey through realms unknown - so be sure not to miss it!<br>"},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494611/large-0a4965bcd99f0c5287d2d306250a974f.jpg","alt":"Never Dream Alone_(c) Stefanie Tendler.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494611/preview-0cd46fcdd7536e5d65c98edefc7bc98c.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494612/large-4742b645df6152ea78ce53c2c964fcd1.jpg","alt":"Never Dream Alone_(c) Stefanie Tendler (3).jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494612/preview-bc5730d01e06f22c491461c511e464b5.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494622/large-2196938367b8bfe3435d535fa47b5403.jpg","alt":"Never Dream Alone_(c)Stefanie Tendler-2.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494622/preview-7152f1aab1125df475c4742badb2ad21.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494621/large-0fe21c0d38ba9b75e3421e290c54ab7d.jpg","alt":"Never Dream Alone_(c) Stefanie Tendler 5.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494621/preview-c9197e8120d823d30999ec9d6c43d874.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494620/large-bbcf4eb0020b14753a0095de83bc3fa6.jpg","alt":"Never Dream Alone_(c) Stefanie Tendler 4.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494620/preview-9deffe3353acad2ea266ea29dc1cd40e.jpg"},{"full":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494613/large-7ff4f94c9aa59fe61e032f4d994d7e3d.jpg","alt":"Never Dream Alone_(c) Stefanie Tendler 3.jpg","thumb":"https://prowly-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/56123/assets/494613/preview-1f5679e95b9b78ba7af7668fa5e9baf6.jpg"}]},{"t":"caption","html":"<em>All photos by Stefanie Tendler.</em>"},{"t":"h3","html":"About The Trouble Notes:"},{"t":"p","html":"Sitting between traditional folk, modern classical, and tribal dance music, The Trouble Notes have traveled across continents in search of musical influences to give listeners the unrivaled music of the generation. The band has proudly built its diverse audience independently, known colloquially as “The Troublemakers”-- a testament to their self-made success story that has led to significant festival appearances, multiple film scores, and an extensive tour schedule spanning the globe. In 2017, a series of videos of the band performing on the streets in France and Germany went certified viral, amassing more than 100 million views on social media and bringing them international notoriety. They recorded their debut album “Lose Your Ties” at Riverside Studios in Berlin, Germany working with Lebanese producer, Khalil Chahine. The album was released in February 2018 and peaked in the top 10 of the iTunes charts for their genre in France, Germany, and the USA. Their music has been featured in award-winning films and documentaries, and their headline “Lose Your Ties” Tour featured sold-out concerts in Europe and North America. They have performed live on television in the USA, Japan, Brazil, Germany, and France. And in 2019, they toured supporting Rodrigo y Gabriela as a part of their Grammy Award-winning “Mettavolution” Tour.&nbsp;<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" id=\"isPasted\"><br>"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"h3","html":"Connect with The Trouble Notes:"},{"t":"embed","src":"https://open.spotify.com/embed/artist/7i1WiSQVIHt4bZz8DhuylF?utm_source=generator","height":"380"},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.thetroublenotes.com/","img":"","title":"Read More","desc":""},{"t":"linkcard","href":"https://www.youtube.com/thetroublenotes?cbrd=1&amp;ucbcb=1","img":"","title":"To reduce cultural barriers, The Trouble Notes have made it their mission to create their own cultural universe. Their self-described \"Acoustic Dance Music\" ...","desc":""},{"t":"instagram","href":"https://www.instagram.com/thetroublenotes/?utm_source=ig_embed","handle":"@thetroublenotes","post":false},{"t":"hr"}],"contact":{"name":"Dawn Jones","role":"","email":"dawn@pressedfreshpr.com","phone":""}}];